g their Sales Teams and Service Teams \n\nMy responsibility in the team is\n\nDeveloping the User Interface and Integrating the GUI and Backend using Ajax \n\nAnalysis on Different Types of Reporting Systems JFreeReports, JasperReports.\nAnd developed a reporting system which has ability to generate reports In Different formats like PDF, WORD, Excel and Integrating Graphical Charts in the Reports\nCustomization of the existing software as per the requirements from the clients.\n\n\n\nACHEIVEMENTS\nInitially CRM software is not having good reporting System and Developed a new Reporting System using JFree Reports whith in a few days time\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nProject \n                        \nBeacon IMS\nPlatform\n                       \nJava,J2EE on Windows.\nTechnologies\n               \nJSP,JDBC,JavaScript,Ajax\nDatabase\n                      \nPostgreSQL 8.1\nCompany\n         \n            \nBeacon Business Systems pvt Ltd, Bangalore.\nClient\n                           \nRamsons India Pvt Ltd,Bangalore.Karel Group.\n\nDescription\n\nBeacon IMS is a Inventory Management Software where Companies Can Manage Multiple Stores and Effectively Managing Raw material Stocks and Integrated Bar Coding System bar coding System using different types of bar code fonts like UPC,EAN,PDF417,Linear Bar coding System\n\nMy responsibility in the team is\n\nIntegrating the software with CRM System Providing a Common Library for both the systems and\n\nDeveloping Bar Code System using\nAnalysis on Different Types of Reporting Systems JFreeReports, JsaperReports.\nAnd developed a reporting system which has ability to generate reports In Different formats like PDF, WORD, Excel and Integrating Graphical Charts in the Reports\nCustomization of the existing software as per the requirements from the clients.','Beacon Business Systems Pvt Ltd',9,NULL,'2007-10-15',NULL,'2007-10-15','2010-06-08 12:13:25','2010-06-08',10,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,9,'0',NULL),(34,'Satish ',NULL,NULL,'Banglore','haconscasccey12sccasc1@rediffmail.com',NULL,NULL,'0','9900866199','0',NULL,'0','2008-04-13',7,20,'2010-06-08 12:13:25',12,'0',NULL,'200710/15/ATT8008.html','200710/15/DOC55868.doc','E-id: rijocv@rediffmail\nCURRICULAM VITAE\n\nSATISH \nMobile\n: 9900866199\nEmail: \nhaconscasccey12sccasc1@rediffmail.com\n\n\nSUMMARY\n\n\n         \nWorking at \nNagaraj Technologies Pvt. Ltd\n from October 2005 to till date.\n\n         \nCurrently working onsite at \nHP (Hewlett Packard)\n on a finance project. \n\n         \n2.1 years of experience in the software industry. \n\n         \nExperience in developing \nJava\n and \nJ2EE\n applications using Apache Tomcat server (Tomcat 5.0)\n\n\n         \nExperience on \nOracle \n\nOracle 9i).\n\nTechnical Skills\n\n\n         \nProgramming Skills - \nJava/J2EE\n (Core Java, JDBC, JSP, Servlets), \nSQL\n\n\n         \nServers ? Tomcat 5.0.\n\n         \nDatabase ? Oracle 9i.\n\n         \nTools used: \nEdit plus, TOAD.\n\nEducational Qualification\n\n\n     \nMCA \nfrom REC BAHLKI , passed out in the year 2004.\n\n\nOther Qualification(s)/ Certification(s)/ Programme(s) Attended: \n\n     \nAttended training at STG on Java/J2EE.\n\nSummary of Projects done\n\n\n\nDesignation\nClient\nProject\nUsing\nSoftware Engineer\nHP(Hewlett Packard)\ne-Travel\nJava/J2EE (Core Java, JDBC, JSP, Servlets), \nSQL\nSoftware Engineer\nHP(Hewlett Packard)\nElectronic Claim Processing System (ECPS).\n\nJava/J2EE (Core Java, JDBC, JSP, Servlets), \nSQL\n\nSoftware Engineer\nHP(Hewlett Packard)\nEJoining.\nJava/J2EE (Core Java, JDBC, JSP, Servlets), \nSQL\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nProject details:\n\n1) Project Name\n\ne-Travel\nClient Name: \nHewlett Packard\n\nfrom\n\nDec 2006 to till date.\nTeam size: 6\nLocation: \nBangalore\n\nProfile\n\n\n: E-Travel is a web application, which enables the employee to make travel, Visa requests, and approval from the concerned higher authority, booking of ticket by travel desk (both domestic and international) etc online.This application provides Approval mechanism for managers, travel desk users, and finance users. Automail facility provided in the application facilitates the employees to have online info about the status of their request.\nResponsibilities\n\n\n         \nResponsible for developing process, db and data classes.\n\n         \nResponsible for developing various reports using JSP.\n\n         \nDeveloped Normal Travel Request module.\n\n         \nInvolved in manual unit testing.\n\nEnvironment\n\n Apache Tomcat 5.0 and Oracle 9i using Java/J2EE (Core Java, JSP, Servlets, JDBC), SQL.\n\n\n2) Project Name\n\nElectronic Claim Processing System\n\nECPS\n).\nClient Name: \nHewlett Packard\n\nfrom\n\nMay 2006 ? Oct 2006.\nTeam size: 5\nLocation: \nBangalore\n\nProfile\n\n\nAn Intranet application which processes the different claims (Two Wheeler/Four Wheeler allowance,Special Day Claims etc) made by the employees at HP?s BPO?s and \nDevelopment\nCenters\n. It is being used by the HP employees, finance and accounts section in the respective premises.\nResponsibilities\n\n\n         \nResponsible for developing process, db and data classes.\n\n         \nResponsible for developing various reports using JSP.\n\n         \nDeveloped \n\nClaim?s request module.\n\n         \nInvolved in manual unit testing.\n\nEnvironment\n\n Apache Tomcat 5.0 and Oracle 9i using Java/J2EE (Core Java, JSP, Servlets, JDBC), SQL.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n3) Project Name\n\nEJoining.\nClient Name: \nHewlett Packard\n\nfrom\n\nDec 2005 ? Mar 2006.\nTeam size: 4\nLocation: \nBangalore\n\nProfile\n\n\nA Intranet application which all the new joiners in HP(in the above mentioned centers) have to enter and fill in the forms. It is used to store all the employee information which includes personal, educational, financial and professional details. Only after entering the details in this application will the employee be able to use different internal web applications like ECPS and Employee Payroll.\n\nResponsibilities\n\n\n         \nResponsible for developing process, db and data classes.\n\n         \nIntegration of EJoining and EBS (duration: September 2006).\n\n         \nInvolved in manual unit testing.\n\nEnvironment\n\n Apache Tomcat 5.0 and Oracle 9i using Java/J2EE (Core Java, JSP, Servlets, JDBC), SQL.\n\n\nPersonal Details:\nName\n                               \n\n   \nSatish Kumar Patil\nDate of Birth\n                      \n\n   \n12-07-1978\nGender\n                    \n\n   \nMale\nLanguages\n                        \n\n   \nEnglish and Hindi.\nPermanent Address\n             \n\n   \nC/o Sona Kaur\n                             \n             \n  \nHno 19-1-274,\n                                             \n\nRadhaSoami Nivas.\n                                              \nMahadev Colony,\n                                             \n\nShiv Nagar,\n                                       \n       \nBidar-585401,Karnataka.','Nagaraj Technologies Pvt. Ltd ',1,NULL,'2007-10-15',NULL,'2007-10-15','2010-06-08 12:13:25','2010-06-08',12,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(35,'Satyaban ',NULL,NULL,NULL,'sasccstyaban@gmail.com',NULL,NULL,'0','09916321558','0',NULL,'0','2008-04-29',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-08 12:13:25',12,'0',NULL,'200710/15/ATT8007.html','200710/15/DOC55869.doc','CURRICULUM VITAE\n\n\nSatyaban\nCell Phone: 09916321558, E-mail: scpsc.cs\nsasccstyaban@gmail.com\n\n    \n                                                                                             \n\nObjective\n\n\nSeeking a challenging position in corporate world where my skills and abilities will help in fulfilling the corporate objectives and personal growth\n\n\n\n\nProfessional Summary:\n\n\n         \n2+ years of experience in developing web and client/server applications using \nJava/J2EE\n technology.\n\n         \nStrong emphasis and in-depth knowledge of JDBC, Java Server Pages, Servlets, Struts, XML, Weblogic and Tomcat.\n\n   \n   \nInvolved in Requirement analysis, Design, Implementation, Deployment and Configuration of Client/Server validation and Web Applications using JDBC, Servlets, JSP and STRUTS\n\n\n         \nPrepare the Database to store the details of Project Affected Persons of the above\n    \nupcoming company using SQLServer as a database.\n\n         \nGood analytical skills, hard working and a good learner\n\n\n         \nAbility to adapt new technologies and tight schedules.\n\n   \nWork Experience:\n      \nWorking as a \nSoftware Engineer\n in \nSpan InfoTech (I) Pvt. Ltd, \nBangalore\n from May 2005 \nto till date.\n\n\nEducational Qualification:\n\n   \nB.Tech \nin \nInformation Technology\n from \nBiju\nPatnaik\nUniversity\n of Technology\n\nRourkela\n with \n   \nan aggregate of \n70%.\n\n   \nTechnical Skills:\n\nProgramming Language\n                  \n\n Java \nWeb Technology\n\n                             \n\nHTML, XML\n     \nArchitecture/Design Pattern\n              \n\nMVC, Struts\n\nJ2EE Technology\n                              \n\n JDBC, JSP, Servlets, EJB, JMS\nApplication Server\n                            \n\nBEA?s Weblogic 8.1\nWeb Server\n                                      \n\nTomcat 5.5\nJava IDE?s\n                                         \n\n NetBeans, Eclipse\nDatabase\n                                          \n\nOracle 9i, SQL Server 2000\n\n    \n\n\n\n   \n   \nPROJECT #1\n\nProject Title\n                          \n: Online Banking Transaction(OBT)\nClient\n                                    \n\nBankOne\n\nUSA\nOperating System\n                 \n: Window 2000 Server\nTechnology\n                           \n: JSP, XML, JDBC, STRUTS, EJB\nDatabase\n                              \n: SQL Server 2000\nFront End\n                              \n: MS Front Page, HTML\nApplication Server\n                \n: Web logic 8.1\nDuration\n                                \n: Dec 2006 to till date\n\n\n   \nProject Description:\n\nThis application is to develop an on-line banking system provides customers with the facility to check their accounts and do transactions on-line. The System will provide all the banks facilities to its customers when their authentications matches, including viewing account information, performing transforms, giving the customer an option of changing address, paying bills on-line, password retrievals ,performing transactions and the locations the bank and its branches. The System should also support an online enrollment facility for credit card customer and should allow customer to view their personal accounts and to pay bills online from their account. The system should assign a unique transaction number to every transaction that a user makes. It also generates credit card numbers automatically when administrator inserts credit card customer?s information. This online transaction automates many of these processes, saving time and money.\n\n\n   \nRole & Responsibilities:\n   \nAs a\n Team Member, \nperformed the Following tasks\n\n\n         \nDesign and develop Session Beans, Application Service, Implementation Business logic and deploy them on the Web Logic Application Server.\n\n         \nCreated tile definitions, struts-config files, validation files and resources bundles for this module using Struts framework.\n\n         \nDevelop the User Interface Screens for presentation logic using JSP and HTML..\n\n         \nParticipate in client side and server side data using the Struts Validation.\n\n         \nJBuilder Used as a Java IDE tool for creating EJBs.\n\n         \nDeployed and tested JSPs, Servlets and EJBs in Web Logic Server.\n            \n   \n    \nPROJECT #2\n\nProject Title\n              \n            \n: Customer Resource Management (CRM)\nClient\n                                    \n: In House Product\nOperating System\n                 \n: Window 2000 Server\nTechnology\n               \n            \n: JDBC ,JSP, XML, STRUTS, EJB,JMS\nDatabase\n                              \n: SQL Server 2000\nFront End\n                              \n: MS Front Page, HTML\nApplication Server\n                \n: Weblogic 8.1\nDuration\n                                \n:July2006 to Dec 2006\n\n\n   \nProject Description: \n                     \n\nCRM is a domain independent client request tracking system. It makes the organization to provide the service \n    \nto their customer?s accurately. CRM\n Software gives an extra & flexibility to the consumer. After purchasing of the product consumer is facilitate with the User Id.Afterwards if buyer is facing any problem regarding the product, he can give complaint to the retailer by logging in CRM site. It gives facility to write complaint/problem about the product and to check the status of the complaint. Consumer can also get a proper date for solving out that problem. CRM gives complete satisfaction to its customer by saving the valuable time.\n\n   \n\n\n\nRole & Responsibilities:\n      \nAs a\n Team Member, \nperformed the Following tasks\n            \n\n   \n   \nCreated Config file through XML.\n\n         \nInstall and configure Weblogic Application Server.\n\n         \nIdentified the action and form classes, based on the Struts framework, to handle the pages.\n\n         \nDevelop the User Interface Screen for presenting logic using JSP and HTML.\n\nPROJECT #3\n\n            \n\nProject Title\n                             \n: Efficiency of Drug Analysis (EDA)\nClient \n                          \n            \n\nDamai\nHospital\n\nKulalampur\n\nMalaysia\nOperating System\n      \n\n            \n: Windows 2000\nTechnology \n                             \n: JDBC, Servlets, JSP, XML, SessionBeans\nFramework\n                  \n             \n: Struts, J2EE\nDatabase\n                                 \n: SQL Server 2000\nApplication Server\n                   \n: Weblogic 8.1\nDuration\n                                   \n: Dec 2005 to July 2006\n\nProject Description: \n\nThe department of health is in the process of unifying and expanding their drug treatment database into a\n                  \n      \n  \nsingle national system in order to respond more effectively to their new and developing information needs in the context of the drugs strategy. Critical objectives include:\n\n         \nAbility to collect a revised range of data.\n\n         \nResponding to the needs of a range of stakeholders.\n\n         \nEnhanced support for strategic decision-making.\n\n         \nFlexibility to support future information and analysis needs.\n\nThe key benefits of our solution are\n\n\n\n         \nFamiliarity and ease of use from a web interface.\n\n         \nSimplified data management arising from centralized storage of data, combined with local ownership of data.\n\n         \nCompliance with government?s-GIF strategy via, for example, use of XML\n\n         \nScalability, if the volume of usage turns out to be greater than expected.\n\n         \nEase of management-no difficult pc configuration of software and hardware required.\n\n         \nMinimal infrastructure demands-minimization of requirement for high-speed networking.\n\n         \nFlexibility and future-proofing through adherence to standards.\n\n         \nUse of SQL Server, a robust industry-standard database system.\n\n\nRole and Responsibilities\n\n\nAs a\n Team Member, \nperformed the Following tasks\n\n\n         \nInvolved in developing forms using JSP and performing client-side validations using JavaScript.\n\n         \nWas responsible for coding server side programs in java Servlets and JSP, developed on Web logic Server for Windows 2000.\n\n         \nDesigning and developed session beans.\n\n         \nCreating DTD?s for transferring data from legacy system.\n\n         \nUsed struts framework and coded the project by extending MVC Struts Framework\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nPROJECT #4\n\n\nProject Title\n                            \n: Cardiac\n\nClient\n                                      \n: Medisoft Inc., \nBoston\n\nOperating System\n                   \n: Window 2000 Server\n\n\nTechnology\n                             \n: Struts, JDBC, Servlet, JSP, HTML\n\nWeb Server\n                \n            \n: Tomcat 5.5\n\nDatabase\n                                \n: SQL Server2000\n\nDuration\n                                  \n: July 2005 to Nov 2005\n\nProject Description:\n\nThe cardiac is a medical application package to be used by cardiologists for diagnosis and information office clients. This package consists of various modules catering to patient registration, patient?s case history management, hospital management, drug profile and clinical investigation to help the doctor. The summary of the patient can be taken completely or divided through their follow up. The user edit the report and serves it\n\n\nRole & Responsibilities:\n      \nAs a\n Team Member, \nperformed the Following tasks\n\n\n         \nCoding & Providing Production Support and Maintenance.\n\n         \nInstall and configure Web Logic Application Server.\n\n         \nDeveloped Servlets and Java Server Pages (JSP).\n\n         \nDesigning screens, which includes popup and help screens.\n\n         \nData is stored in appropriate table in organized way.\n\n         \nInvolved in developing the hospital management module.\n\n         \nUse of the Struts Framework for the application based on the MVC design paradigm.\n\n\n\n\nPERSONAL INFORMATION:\n\n\n\nPermanent Address\n                             \n\n\n          \nSCM \n(TATA STEEL)\n, Q.No: 12/6\n                                                                   \n     \nPo\n: Kalrangiatta, Dist: Jajpur\n                                                                        \nPin: 755028\n\n\nGender\n                                                \n\n           \nMale\n\n\nNationality\n                                           \n\n\n         \nIndian\n\n\nLanguages Known\n                                \n\n\n         \nEnglish, Hindi, and Oriya \n                                \n                                                                    \n\n\n\nPlace: \nBangalore\n\nDate:\n                                                                                                   \nSatyaban Pradhan',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-15',NULL,'2007-10-15','2010-06-08 12:13:25','2010-06-08',12,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(36,'Gunasekhar.G',NULL,NULL,NULL,'gvdvuna.sdvdvekhar01@gmail.com',NULL,NULL,'0','9986406110','0',NULL,'0','2008-04-29',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-08 12:13:25',12,'0',NULL,'200710/15/ATT8006.html','200710/15/DOC55870.doc','Curriculum Vitae\n\nGunaSekhar.G\nEmail ID:\n\ngvdvuna.sdvdvekhar01@gmail.com\nMobile No.: \n+91-9986406110\n\n\nObjective\n\n\n                                \nI am looking for a position where I can help the company achieve its targets by utilizing all my expertise, my professional skills and acquiring new ones.\n\n\nProfessional summary\n2+ Years of experience in JAVA and J2EE.\nCurrent Organization\nOsprosys Software Pvt ltd.\nDate \nJun 2005 to Till Date\nDesignation\nSoftware Developer(JAVA)\n\n\nCurrent Job Activities\n\n\nPresently I am working as a Software Engineer. I am responsible for Coding and developing new applications using\n java, j2ee Technologies (JDBC,SERVLETS, JSP, Struts framework)\n .My job includes Software Development, up gradation of new versions, finding the missing functionalities in existing applications and does the necessary modification.\n\n\n\n\nTechnical Summary\n\n\n         \n\nProgramming Languages\n              \n\n\nJava\n\n         \nWeb Technologies\n                        \n\n\n\n\n\nJDBC, JSP, and Servlets\n\n         \nInternet Tools\n                               \n  \n\n\nHTML, JavaScript\n\n         \nApplication Server/Web Servers \n  \n\n\nTomcat5.0,Web logic 8.1\n\n         \nRDBMS\n                                           \n  \n\n Oracle 9i,SQL Server\n\n         \nFrame Work\n                               \n     \n\n\n\nStruts1.1 \n\n         \nIdes\n                                            \n     \n\n\nJCreater, Edit Plus, Eclipse3.0\n\n         \nOperating Systems\n                     \n          \n\n\n\n\n\nWindows98/2000/NT\n\n         \nConfiguration Management Tool\n   \n\n\nVSS, ClearCase\n\n\nQualifications\n\nBachelor of Engineering in Electrical & Electronics(2001-2005)\nFrom Anna University, Chennai passed out in First Division with an aggregate \n          \npercentage of 69.\nIntermediate (1999-2001)\nFrom Board of Intermediate Education, Andhra Pradesh Passed out with an aggregate Percentage of 89.9.\nS.S.C (1999)\nFrom Board of Secondary Education, ,Andhra Pradesh Passed out in First Division with an aggregate Percentage\n\nof 79.\n\n\n\n\nPROJECT DESCRIPTION\nPROJECT #1\n\nProject\n      \n\n\n The Financial Manager\nClient\n        \n\n\n\n\nBanco Penta \nTeam Size \n\n\n\n15 members\nDuration\n    \n\n\n\nJuly 2006 to till date\nDescription:\nThe Financial Manager is a planning tool that helps an Advisor in providing guidance to a customer\'s financial planning, based on the identified needs and risk appetite. Wealth Manager Planner\'s functionality will particularly help banks to increase the sales of the investment products in their product range. \nThe Planner provides features like Knowledge-Based Decision System, Need Analysis, Risk Profiling ,Customer profiling, Goal planning, Goal Coordination, Investment Strategy and Financial Status.\nTechnologies include:\n\n         \nCore Java, JDBC ,Servlets,JSP, Oracle 9i\n\n         \nStruts Framework, VSS\n\nResponsibilities include: \n\n         \nUnderstanding User requirements\n\n         \nDeveloping Action Class for struts frame work.\n\n         \nDeveloping views by using jsp and Unit Testing.\n\n         \nExtensively involved in development of server side modules\nPROJECT #2\n\n\n\nProject\n      \n\n\n\nIDBManager\nClient\n        \n\n\n\nDCSSP (Ind) Pvt Ltd,\nTeam Size \n\n\n\n6 members\nDuration\n    \n\n\n\nJan 2006 to June 2006\n\nDescription:\nA Web-based DBA tool, which is highly helpful to Database administrators. This tool is a J2EE component that can be deployed on J2EE certified application server to develop, administer, tune, and monitor an Oracle database. \nTechnologies include:\n\n         \nCore Java,JDBC, Servlets, JSP\n\n         \nApache/Tomcat\n\n         \nOracle,Windows2000\nResponsibilities include: \n\n         \nUnder Standing the Requirements\n\n         \nDeveloped the access control Functionality to the administrator so that the site administrator can set access controls for the tool after deciding who can access the tool.\n\n         \nDeveloping\n views using jsp and html and unit testing\n\n\nPROJECT #3\n\n\nProject\n   \n   \n\n\n\n\nSMSXpress\nClient\n        \n\n\n\n\nPMK Associates\nTeam Size \n\n\n\n5 members\nDuration\n   \n\n\n\n\nAug 2005 to Dec 2005\n\nDescription:\nSMSXpress is web based application Implemented using MVC architecture that provides facility to send single as well as broadcast SMS messages. This application also includes uploading of excel sheet for sending bulk messages which is having mobile numbers and messages to be sent.\nTechnologies include:\n\n         \nCore Java,JDBC,Servlets, JSP, Struts 1.1\n\n         \nApache/Tomcat\n\n         \nSQL Server,Windows2000\nResponsibilities include: \n\n         \nDeveloped and deployed SMS modules using Apache/Tomcat, used Servlets JSP and JDBC.\n\n         \nDeveloping\n views using jsp and html and unit testing',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-15',NULL,'2007-10-15','2010-06-08 12:13:25','2010-06-08',12,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(37,'J.Kamesh',NULL,NULL,NULL,'kegegamesegsh_m@yahoo.com',NULL,NULL,'0','919884116621','0',NULL,'0','2008-04-29',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-08 12:13:25',12,'0',NULL,'200710/15/ATT8005.html','200710/15/DOC55871.doc','Resume of Kamesh M\n\nPROFESSIONAL EXPERIENCE (2+ Years):\n\n?SENIOR SOFTWARE DEVELOPER?\n\n\n\nName :\nJ.Kamesh\n\n\nEmail:\n\nkegegamesegsh_m@yahoo.com\n\n\n\nContact. No\n.:\n\n+919884116621\n\n\n\n\n\n\nPresent Address:\nNo.26/17, \nPadmanabha Nagar,\nMain Road\n\nChoolaimedu,\nChennai ? 94.\n\n\n\nPersonal Information:\nDate of Birth: \n21\nst\n July 1982\nSex: Male\nNationality: Indian\nMarital Status: Single\n\n\n\n\nObjective\n\nTo obtain a creative and challenging position that enables me to gain good exposure and sound technically knowledgeable for Organizational and personal growth.\n\n\nTechnical Expertise\nProgramming Skills\nJava (JDBC)\n\nJ2EE (JSP, Servlets)\n\nJavaScript, HTML, CSS, \nAJAX\n, XML\nWeb Server\nJboss4.0.3, Tomcat\nDatabase Packages\nOracle, PostgreSQL 8.1.1 \nOperating Systems\nLinux 9.0, \nWindows \nNT/2K/XP \nBuild Tool\nAnt v1.6.5\nVersion Control\nCVS\nModeling Tool\nER - Studio \nIDE\nEclipse\n\nEducation\n    \n\n\n         \nM.C.A\n (Master of Computer Application) from \nVelammal\nCollege\n of Management and Computer Studies, Chennai. \nMadras\nUniversity\n\n Secured 80% \n\n                  \nWork Experience\nProfessional Summary\n\n2+ Years of Professional Experience as Senior Software Developer in Application Development.\nStrong Knowledge in Java \nStrong in \nDatabase design \nGood in leading a team \nGood in Client Interface\n\n\n\n\n\nEmployer Details\n\nOrganization\nDesignation\nDuration\nJai E Technologies\nSenior Software Developer\nNov?2004 ? Till Now\n\n\nProject Experience\n\n\nSHARP [Sheenlac Advance Resource Planning System]\n\nSheenlac is a leader in Wood Finishes and Thinner. They have various branches spread across \nIndia\n. They have strong dealer network. They had their own custom application on D2K. This was replaced by our SHARP ERP system. This includes various modules like Order, Invoice, Purchase, Accounts, Stores etc., It is an web based application using state of the art technologies.\n\nEnvironment\n\nRole \n                             \nSenior Software Developer\nDuration\n                         \n8 months\nOS \n                               \nRed Hat Linux, Windows 2K and XP\nSoftware \n                       \nJava, J2EE\nDatabase \n                       \nOracle \nVersion Control \n              \nCVS\nBuild tool\n                        \nAnt\n\nMy Responsibilities\n            \nImplementation\nDatabase design using ER studio\nHandled team of 4 people to support rollout.\nClient interface\nOptimization\nBug fixing\nUser Training \nDocumentation using Javadoc\n\nSHARP Admin\n\nThis module is used for managing users, user groups and rights. User creation, group creation (Geographical, Functional Level, Custom Groups), Rights Template Creation, Assigning the Rights templates to users, groups, etc can be done using Admin module. All Masters Creation like Dealer, Stock, Discount, Accounts, Price Lists, Credit Schemes, Products, Transporters, Tax Schemes, Locations, Commitment, Bank, Marketing Group and CMS is done. All operations in Admin are rights based.\n\nEnvironment \n\nRole \n                             \nSenior Software Developer\nDuration\n                         \n8 months\nOS \n                               \nRed Hat Linux, Windows 2K and XP\nSoftware \n                       \nJava, J2EE\nDatabase \n                       \nOracle\nVersion Control \n              \nCVS\nBuild tool\n                        \nAnt\n\n\n\n\nMy Responsibilities\n            \nDesigned front end using \nAJAX\nDesigned and developed DB model \nConverted DB model to physical structure.\nSQL Development \nManaged a team of 3 developers\nInterfaced with PM at customer \n\n\nSHARP Data Migration\n\nAll Masters Creation like Dealer, Discount, Price Lists, Credit Schemes, Products, Transporters, Tax Schemes and Bank were migrated from older database structure to new database structure. Order and Invoice were also migrated.\n\nEnvironment\n\nRole \n                             \nDeveloper \nDuration\n                         \n2 months\nOS \n                               \nRed Hat Linux, Windows 2K and XP\nSoftware \n                       \nJava, J2EE, XML\nDatabase \n                       \nOracle\nVersion Control \n              \nCVS\n\nMy Responsibilities\n            \nDeveloped migration plan and executed\nDeveloped scripts for automation\nBug fixing\nDocumentation\n\nSMPP [Sheenlac Marketing promoters package]\n\nSheenlac has large dealer network. To help the dealer network, Sheenlac has developed a custom application to suite all dealers to sell their products. It has integrated billing system. It has various reports to assess the total sales, product wise, brand wise etc.\n\nEnvironment \n\nRole \n                             \nDeveloper\nDuration\n                         \n2 months\nOS \n                               \nRed Hat Linux, Windows 2K and XP\nSoftware \n                       \nJava, J2EE\nDatabase \n                       \nOracle\nVersion Control \n              \nCVS\n\nMy Responsibilities\n            \nDesigned and developed DB model using ER Studio\nDesign and developed back end using Jai Framework\nTrouble shooting online issues\nDocumentation\n\n\n\n\n\n\nProduct Experience\n\nNAGADA\nNagada is a suite of products under one secured shell that helps to manage mail, work, people, events, appointments, and information?s, etc.\nModules,\n\n         \nCalendar\n\n         \nNews\n\n         \nAddress Book\n\n         \nChat\n\n         \nAdmin\nCalendar\nThis is a Web-based Calendar. Multiple Calendars can be created. Calendar is used to set appointments at any date and time. Appointments are Daily events. Notifications can be sent through SMS/E-Mail. Appointments can be scheduled if the appointment repeats on a regular interval. Calendars can be shared. Calendars can be shared public/private/protected. This is an online Diary you can manage your daily events and plan your future.\n    \n\nNews \nThis is a corporate news system. This system is used to publish news in the company. This can be used to publish the achievements, announcements, in formations, etc. This is also a document sharing system.\n\nAddress Book\nAddress Book is used to store addresses. Group Creation (Official, Personal and Vendor), Friends creation in the group, etc can be done with Address Book. Vendor groups can be shared with other users. All operations in Address Book is rights based. \n\nChat\nThis is a Web Chat. One to one chat and Conferencing can be done.\n   \n\nAdmin\nThis module is used for managing users, user groups and rights. User creation, group creation (Geographical, Functional Level, Custom Groups), Rights Template Creation, Assigning the Rights templates to users, groups, etc can be done with this module. All operations in Admin is rights based.\n\nEnvironment\nRole \n                             \nDeveloper\nDuration \n                        \n12 months\nOS \n                               \nRed Hat Linux, Windows 2K and XP\nSoftware \n                       \nJava, J2EE\nDatabase \n                       \nPostgreSQL\nVersion Control \n              \nCVS\n\nContribution\nDesigned and developed DB model \nDesign and developed front end using \nAJAX\nDeveloped middle tier components \nContributed in the design of Jai Framework\nImplementation of the product to client\nCustomizations for the product\nMigration of data\nClient Interface\nUser Training \nDocumentation using Javadoc',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-15',NULL,'2007-10-15','2010-06-08 12:13:25','2010-06-08',12,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(38,'J Ramakrishna',NULL,NULL,'Mumbai','mdvrvasdvmakrishnasv369@gmail.com',NULL,NULL,'0','09920246209','0',NULL,'0','2007-01-12',7,19,'2010-06-08 12:13:25',12,'0',NULL,'200710/15/ATT8004.html','200710/15/DOC55872.doc','J.RamaKrishna\nEmail: mdvrvasdvmakrishnasv369@gmail.com\nPhone: 09920246209\n\nProfessional Summary:\n\n\n         \nHaving 3+ years of experience in software development life cycle in creating solutions for web-based and client server applications using \nCoreJava, Jsp, Servlets, JDBC, Struts\n\n\n\n         \nExperience in object-oriented applications using J2EE (JSP, Servlets, JDBC) and servers like Tomcat and Web Logic Server.\n\n\n         \nClient/Server and Web applications using Java, Jsp, and HTML with backend database as Oracle.\n\n\n   \n    \nExtensively worked on \nServlet, Jsp, and Struts.\n\n\n         \nEffective communication skills, good analytical abilities and zeal in learning new tools.\n\nWork History:\n\n         \nWorking as a \nSoftware Engineer\n for Syntel Mumbai since Sep-06 to Till Date. \n\n\n       \nWorked\n as a \nSoftware Programmer\n for \nCapstone InfoTech pvt Ltd\n\n\nBanglore from July-04 to Aug-06.\n\n\nTechnical Skills:\n\n   \nOperating Systems\n   \n\n               \nMS-DOS and Windows 9X / 2000 / XP.\n   \nLanguages\n                       \n\n               \nJava\n, J2ee, C, C++, \nJavaScript\n, SQL, XML, HTML.\n   \nRDBMS  \n    \n                     \n\n             \nOracle, MS Access\n   \nEnterprise\n Tech\n           \n\n               \nJava, Servlets, Jsp, Jdbc, Struts, and Ejb.\n   \nSERVERS\n   \n                   \n\n\n\n             \nWebLogic7.1, Apache Tomcat5.0.\n\n\nAcademics:\n\n         \nB.Sc (CS) from \nAurora\nDegree\nCollege\n Affiliated to \nOsmaina\nUniversity\n\nHyderabad\n, A.P.\nSoftware Training:\n\n         \nCompleted DAST (Diploma in Advanced Software Technology) from CMC. Computer Maintenance Corporation of \nIndia\n (A GOVT. OF \nINDIA\nENTERPRISE\n). \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nProject 1:\nProject Name:\nSkillBay\nClient\nSyntel Ltd, \nUSA\nRole\nTeam Member\nOrganization\nSyntel\nDuration\n09-2006 to Till Date\nEnvironment\nSoftware\nJ2ee, Struts, JSP, Servlets, JDBC.\nDatabase: Oracle \nTools: Eclipse\nServer: Weblogic7.1\nO/s: Windows2000 and Windows NT.\n\nDescription\n\nSkill\nBay\n is a \nfull-service business-to-business IT Staffing e-Marketplace. It provides a platform to the clients, who are need of skilled resources, to post the requirements online and to the vendors, who are capable of providing skilled resources to fulfill the requirement of client, to place bids for the potential candidates. The portal automates and facilitates the entire process involved in staffing from registration to requirements porting, bidding, interviews, placements, timesheets, billing and invoicing.\n\nRole & Contribution:\n\n         \nInvolved in the development of coding for the controllers, JSPs using Struts MVC Framework\n\n         \n\nInvolved in the development of HTML pages and JavaScript.\nProject 2:\nProject Name:\nStores and Purchase Management System.\nClient\nNippon System ware CO., LTD, \nJapan\nRole\nTeam Member\nOrganization\nCapstone InfoTech pvt Ltd\nDuration\n12-2005 to 08-2006\nEnvironment\nSoftware\nCore Java, JSP, Servlets.\nDatabase: Oracle 8i\nO/s: Windows2000 and Windows NT.\n\nDescription\n\n\n         \nStores and purchase management system was designed and set up on the company\'s intranet to manage and maintain all typical activities related to the inventory applications. The system enables all the users at different warehouse locations to access the information on-line regarding order status, goods marked for picking, goods picked, shipped and dispatched. System keeps track of the stock levels, enables decision-making for raising the purchase order and organizes complete information on the stock-updates. It involves maintenance of Supplier, material and department details. It also involves purchase requisition & order, material receipts & issues processes, Stock availability and transactions. It will allow relevant Queries and generate Reports to the organization.\n\nRole & Contribution:\n\nDeveloped the Servlets, JSP?s, and Beans using MVC Architecture.\n\nProject 3:\n\nProject Name:\nTime Sheet Management System\nClient\n\nNippon System ware CO., LTD, \nJapan\nRole\nTeam member\nOrganization\nCapstone InfoTech pvt Ltd\nDuration\n03-2005 to 11-2005\nEnvironment\nSoftware\nCore Java, JSP, Servlets.\nDatabase: Oracle 8i\n\n         \nServer: Tomcat\n\n         \nO/s: Windows2000 and Windows NT.\n\nDescription:\n        \n         \nThis Web application is for maintaining the Time Sheet Entry. All the Employees in an organization enter their daily work schedules in Time sheet. This Application will be useful in calculating the metrics for a project, to find out which employee is working in which project etc. Each and Every employee is allowed to Login and Fill the Time Sheet. All the security constraints are maintained. This is developed using HTML, Java Servlets, MS Access and Java Script.\n   \nRole & Contribution:\nInvolved in the development of front-end developing part (presentation layer).\nInvolved in Web logic Configurations.\nProject 4:\nProject Name:\nSales Management System\nClient\n\nWilliams Sonama, \nUSA\n      \nRole\nTeam member\nOrganization\nCapstone InfoTech pvt Ltd\nDuration\n07-2004 to 02-2005\nEnvironment\nSoftware:\nJSP, Servlets,\n\nHTML, Java Script \nDatabase: Oracle 8i\nServer: Tomcat\n\n         \nO/s: Windows2000 and Windows NT.\n\nDescription:\n          \nThis project is an order processing system for Cisco Systems. This system helps various branches of Cisco Systems for sales management.\n\nIt provides functionalities like estimation, order placing and follow up, delivery status, inspection and also the details of payment. The details are maintained in an Oracle 8i database. The GUI is developed using JSP and the server side processing is developed using Servlets as well as Java Beans. \n                                                                             \n     \n                                                                                              \n                                                                                                \n                                   \nM.Ramakrishna','Syntel',1,NULL,'2007-10-15',NULL,'2007-10-15','2010-06-08 12:13:25','2010-06-08',12,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(39,'Jilani P',NULL,NULL,'Chennai','jilsvanvdsvibaji.p@gmail.com',NULL,NULL,'0','9986003613','0',NULL,'0','2006-10-13',7,19,'2010-06-08 12:13:25',12,'0',NULL,'200710/15/ATT8003.html','200710/15/DOC55873.doc','jilanibaji\n\njilsvanvdsvibaji.p@gmail.com\ncell: +91 9986003613\n        \n\nJilani p\n\n\nSummary\n\n\n        \nHaving \n3.5 years\n of Software Engineering experience in the field of Development and Implementation for various projects and products for our valuable clients in the areas like Enterprise, Distributed, and Business Intelligence Systems using \nJava, EJB, JSP, XML,Struts,Hibernet, Spring, Servlets, WebSphere Message Broker 6.0 \nand it?s related advanced concepts.\n\nStrengths\n\n\n        \nQuick study who rapidly assimilates into organization and aggressively employs new ideas, concepts, methods and technologies to support business objectives. \n\n\n        \nThrive in both independent and collaborative work environments.\n\nExperience Summary\n\n\n        \nCurrently Working in \nTATA CONSULTANCY SERVICES (TCS), Chennai \nas a \nAssistant Systems Engineer\n\n\n        \nWorked as a \nSoftware Developer\n at \nNeural It Solutions.\n\n        \nWorked as a \nSoftware Developer\n at \nProvidence Technologies Pvt. Ltd., Hyd. \n\nEducational Profile\n\n        \nM.Sc(I.S) from Andhra University with 74%\n\n        \nB.C.A from Nagarjuna University with 70%\n\n        \nIntermediate M.P.C Group from Andhra Pradesh Intermediate Board with 78%\n\n        \nSchooling from Secondary Board with 71%\n\nSkills\n     \nOperating systems\n    \n\n        \nWindows OS Family and UNIX\n     \nLanguages\n               \n\n        \nJava\n     \nInternet Technologies:\n        \nEJB,\n\nServlets, Struts, Hibernet, JSP and XML \n     \nApplications Server\n   \n\n        \nBEA WebLogic\n     \nWeb Server\n             \n\n        \nTomcat\n     \nRDBMS\n          \n\n        \nMySql, Oracle, MS-SQL server\n\n\nProjects Details\n\nProject Title\n\nOIM (Q BMG-DEV-DNVR-POM) \nCustomer\n\nQWEST COMMUNICATION INC., USA\nDuration\n\nDec-2006 to present\nOperating Systems\n\nUNIX, Windows 2000\nRole\n\nDevelopment and Unit Testing.\nRole Description\n\nTo gather requirements, analyzing the GUI\n\ndesign and the implementation for the various modules assigned to me. Got an opportunity to work with the front end (JSP), implementing modules in struts framework J2EE and the back end database work too in oracle. \nCurrently working on few enhancements for this project.\nExtensively have used CVS and Eclipse as part of the project.\nSolution Environment\n\nJava, J2EE, XML, struts, HTML, Oracle 9i database , Web logic Server (WLS) 7.0 , \nHighlights\n\nThe project was severely curtailed by the lack of time. The team successfully gathered requirements (which were ever changing), researched solutions, and developed the application in a very short time frame.\nDescription\n             \n            \n      \nEFLOW is a project that aims to consolidate the inventory systems of Qwest national and Qwest local. The preferred inventory system, called TIRKS (a TELCORDIA application), is being used by Qwest local. EFLOW effort also aims at setting common path for provisioning orders in both national and local side. This brings in multiple advantages of reducing the number of systems used, ease of training, ease of deployment of personnel in either local or national side. Such an effort will be the first in the US telecom industry when it goes live.\n\n               \nEcore is also a project\n\nupdated version of the OIM project,\n\ndeveloped using Spring, hibernate, DWR and Oracle 9i database\n\n\n\nProject Title\n\nBritish Telecom (BT)\nRole\n\nDevelopment, Deployment and Testing.\nTechnologies\n\nIBM WebSphere Message Broker, xmlspy 2006, ESql, Toad and Unix\n\nDescription\n             \n          \n      \nThe CMPAL is an Integration layer based on IBM Message Broker which sits between OneView and OpenReach (the connection with OpenReach is via a B2B Gateway on the Retail side). \n       \nThe Integration Platform will only provide simple routing and translation of messages. Where a message requires more complex handling it will be passed onto another application/platform probably on the COP\n\n\nResponsibilities\n\n   \nInvolved in the development, deployment and Testing modules.\n\n\nProject Title\n\nEpractice ERP\n\nDuration\n\n1 year\nRole\n\nDevelopment\nTechnologies\n\nJava, JSP, Servlets, EJB, XML, HTML, JavaScript, Oracle 8i, Web Logic, Unix\n\nDescription\n             \n               \nEPracticeERP®\n is a state of the art, end-to-end Practice Management Solution that efficiently manages all aspects of any solo or multi-specialty outpatient private practice. \n\n\n            \nEPracticeERP\'s built-in decision support system frees the Practitioner to focus on the care-giving aspect of the encounter. It (behind the scene and real-time) analyses the encounter, recommends optimum level of billing, generates progress-notes that support levels of billing, stores progress-notes in electronic health records format, generates invoices and submits claims to insurance companies for re-imbursement.\n\nStreamlined\n cash flow management.\n\nExponential increases\n in productivity and office efficiencies.\n\nAffordable\n end-to-end solution for any outpatient solo & multi-speciality practice.\n\nOptimize\n billing levels for every encounter\n\nResponsibilities\n\n   \nInvolved in the development and integration of modules using Java, JSP, Servlets.\n\n\n\nProject Title\n\nAlphalitigator\nClient\n\nAlphalitigator Systems, USA\nDuration\n\n1.2 years\nRole\n\nAnalysis, Design and Development\nTechnologies\n\nJava, JSP, Servlets, JDBC,\n\nXML, HTML, JavaScript, Oracle 8i, Tomcat, Windows NT\nDescription\n\nThe Alphalitigator? Litigation Management Portal is a secure web based calendaring and document management solution. Project features Client/Admin/super with Automated Notification / Reminders and Personal / Group Calendar Views with\n\nDiscussion Forum, AVI player, Knowledge Base Representation Extensive and Customized Reports and a Custom Report Tool.\n\nTotal Project developed based on US-Level Standards, Guidelines and Reviews with rigorous testing.\n\n\n\nResponsibilities\n\n\n        \nInvolved in the development and integration of modules using Java, JSP and\n\nServlets.\n\n\n      \nBy\nJilani Baji P','TATA CONSULTANCY SERVICES ',1,NULL,'2007-10-15',NULL,'2007-10-15','2010-06-08 12:13:25','2010-06-08',12,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(40,'John Jayaraj',NULL,NULL,'Chennai','jrherhohn.jayraraj@rediffmail.com',NULL,'04329 293309','0','91 9865315105','0',NULL,'0','2008-04-13',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-08 12:13:25',12,'0',NULL,'200710/15/ATT8002.html','200710/15/DOC55874.doc','RESUME\n          \n                               \nJOHN JAYARAJ\n                              \n                                                                   \n            \n9,\nPatel Street\n\nRazack\nGarden\n\n\nEmail:\n\njrherhohn.jayraraj@rediffmail.com\n              \n                   \nArumbakkam\n, Chennai-600 005\n\nCell: \n+91 9865315105\n                                                            \nTamil \nNadu\n\nIndia\n\n\n\nOBJECTIVE\n\n       \nTo pursue career in an organization which offers tremendous growth potential to my career giving Exposure to latest technologies fully utilizing my skills. \nPROFILE AND EXPERTISE\n\n\n       \nSuccessful software professional with \n2+\n\n\nears of experience\n in the \nweb based development \nand broad knowledge of software development life cycle with an emphasis on client satisfaction. \n\n       \nHaving well built domain experience in Insurance.\nPROFESSIONAL EXPERIENCE\n\n\n       \nWorking as a \nPROGRAMMER\n in \nMAAN SAROVAR Software Private Limited, Chennai\n from \nMay\n 2006 to till date.\n\n       \nWorked as a \nPROGRAMMER \nin \nE-galax technologies, Chennai \nfrom \nMay 2005 to May 2006. \n\nPROFESSIONAL QUALIFICATION\n\nCourse\nInstitution\nYear of Passing\n\nM.Sc Computer Science\nSt.Joseph?s College-Trichy\n2005\n74\nB.Sc Computer Science\nSt.Joseph?s College-Trichy\n2003\n62\nXII Standard\nSt.Peter?s \nHr.Sec\nSchool\n,Viragalur-Trichy\n2000\n74\nX Standard\nSt.Little\nFlower\nHr.Sec\nSchool\n\nSalem\n1998\n62\n\n\nCOMPUTER SKILLS\n\n\n      \nProgramming Languages \n      \n\n\n       \nJava\n\n\n      \nOperating Systems\n\n\n\n         \n\n\n       \nWindows NT/2000\n\n      \nDatabase\n      \n    \n               \n\n\n       \nMYSQL , \nOracle\n\n\n      \nWeb Technologies\n              \n\n       \nJSP ,SERVLETS\n\n      \nIDE\n                                  \n\n       \nNetBeans \n\n      \nWeb Servers\n                      \n\n       \nApache Tomcat\n\n\n\n\nPROJECT PROFILE \n\nProject I\n\nClient\n              \n\n\nRoyal&SunAlliance,(RSA) \nDubai\n\n\nTitle\n                \n\n\nMarine Cargo Policy\n\n                        \n   \nURL:\nwww.valuemycard.com\n\nEnvironment:\n\nJava, JSP, Servlets,Oracle, Tomcat 5.0\n\n\nDescription:\n        \n            \nThis is B2B Insurance policy System. Using this system broker can generate the quote and assign to existing customer or can make new customer. The premium amount is being calculated by based on commodity and its sum insured, mode /place of transit and cover. After generating quote broker need to give additional information to generate the policy. The additional information is Bill/Air details, Bank details and invoice / packing details. Finally the overall summary will display here broker may generate or on-hold or delete the policy. Pending policy holds the list of draft policy broker can edit and finalize any on-hold policy.\n\nResponsibilities:\n          \nPerformed as a Team Member, which includes developing the Modules-Customer information, Policy Information &policy Generation and also handled the Admin rights. \n\nProject II\n\nClient\n              \n\n\nRoyal Sundaram Finance and Insurance\n,(RSA) Chennai.\n\nTitle\n                \n\n\nPowerlink \n\nEnvironment:\n\nJava, JSP, Servlets,Oracle, Tomcat 4.1.7\n\n\nDescription:\n          \nThe purpose of this project is to collect the data?s of motorcar for calculating the insurance premium in online. Motorcar data?s are referred from the insurance application in the form of Tiff image, which was filled by the applicant.\n\n          \nThe three important aspects of this project are,\n\n        \n\n1. \nTiff Files are extracted and Converted to JPEG\n\n   \n2. Data Entry with Image Highlighting is done and stored in Database.\n   \n3. Premium Calculation is done and stored in table.\n\n\n\n\nProject III\n\nClient\n              \n\n\nRoyal \nSundaram Finance and Insurance\n,(RSA) Chennai.\nTitle\n                \n\n\nSMART (Sales Management and Renewal Tracker)\n                        \n   \nURL : \nwww.royalsundaramagent.com\nEnvironment\n\n\n\nJava, JSP, MYSQL,\n\nTomcat 4.1.7\n\nDescription:\nAgency portal serves as \nInformation\nCenter\n, Transaction center and reward scheme tracking system for the agents. The agents can have updated information on the market and also about the policy status of their clients and generate the commission statement. The agents can post their doubts to the departments and responsible persons through this portal clarify them.\n\nResponsibilities:\n          \nDeveloped Modules Pending Policies and also involved as a team member in Admin Rights.\n\nPERSONAL DETAILS \n\n\nFATHER?S NAME\n                           \n\n        \nD.Joseph Benedit Henry\nNATIONALITY\n                              \n\n        \nIndian\nSEX\n                                           \n\n        \nMale\nDATE OF BIRTH\n                            \n\n        \n03-10-1982\nLANGUAGES KNOWN\n                      \n\n        \nEnglish, \nTamil\nPERMENANT ADDRESS\n                   \n\n        \n1/18, \nEast Street\n\n                                                          \nViragalur? 621722, Trichy Dist,\n                                                          \nTamilnadu\n\nIndia\n\n                                                          \nPhone No:04329 293309\n\n\nDate:\n                                                                               \n          \nPlace: Chennai\n                                      \n                                      \n[J John Jayaraj]\n                                                   \n                                 \n     \n       \n                                    \n         \n   \n                        ','MAAN SAROVAR Software ',1,NULL,'2007-10-15',NULL,'2007-10-15','2010-06-08 12:13:25','2010-06-08',12,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(41,'Bhavani .R',NULL,NULL,NULL,'bhavaevgfgnirayaefla@gmail.com',NULL,NULL,'0','9949352883','0',NULL,'0','2007-04-30',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-08 12:13:25',13,'0',NULL,'200710/15/ATT8001.html','200710/15/DOC55875.doc','Praveen Deevela\nBHAVANI .R\n\nMobile\n: 9949352883\n                                                      \n           \nE-Mail: bhavaevgfgnirayaefla@gmail.com\n\nOBJECTIVE\n\nTo pursue a challenging career and be a part of progressive organization that gives scope to enhance my knowledge, skills, which can be better used for the organizational growth and personal growth.\n\nEXPERIENCE IN SUMMARY\n\n\n         \n3+ years\n of extensive experience in software development with proficiency in development of \nWeb\n\nbased\n technologies.\n\n         \n\nyears \nexperience in Design and Development of Web based applications and n-tier applications using \nJAVA, JSP, Struts, Servlets, Java Beans\n and \nJDBC\n\n\n         \nHands-on experience in implementing \nJ2EE applications \nusing \nStruts\n\nnd MVC framework\n\n\n         \nGood experience and exposure on \nTomcat, WSAD, Savvion Business Manager (SBM)\n\n\n         \n2+ years\n of extensive experience in \nJavaScript\n and designing \nHTML\n pages.\n\n         \nDeveloped, tested and deployed applications in \nWindows \nenvironment.\n\n         \nHighly conceptual innovative problem solver with excellent organizational and communication skills.\n\nEDUCATION\n\n\n          \nB.E\n\nAndhra\nUniversity\n, AP in 2004 with 67%.\n\n          \nIntermediate\n, Board of Intermediate, A.P in 1999 with 85%.\n\n          \nS.S.C\n, Secondary School Certificate, A.P in 1997 with 81%.\n\nWORK EXPERIENCE\n\n\n          \nWorking as a \nSoftware Engineer\n in\n Infosys Technologies Ltd\n\nHyderabad\n from \nAug 2006 \nto \nTill Date.\n\n          \nWorked as a \nSoftware Engineer\n in \nE-Wings Solutions, \nHyderabad\n from \nApril\n\n2004\n to \nJuly 2006\n\n\n\n\nTECHNICAL SKILLS\n\nLanguages\nJava, PL/SQL,\n HTML, Java Script and XML\nDistributed computing\nJSP, Servlets, JDBC, Struts\nWeb/App Servers\n\nApache Tomcat, Savvion, WSAD, Web Logic\nRDBMS and Tools\nOracle, DB2, SQL Server\nDesign tools & IDEs\nWSAD, Net Beans, Eclipse, BPM Studio,\n Edit plus \nand Dream\n\nweaver \nOperating Systems\nAll Windows Versions\n\n\n\n\nPROFESSIONAL EXPERIENCE\n\nWachovia\n\nUSA\n                                                                                                \nJun 07 ? till date\nSoftware Engineer\n                                                                                           \n\nProject:\n\nLoan and Lease Operations (Maintenance)\n\nEnvironment\n: Servlets, JSP, WSAD, MQ Workflow, Unix, DB2, XML\n\nLoan and Lease Operations ? LLO is a workflow based web application used to ensure that the collateral for a loan is secured. It is used in the Retail Credit Servicing division of Wachovia. The process of securing collateral begins at the time a loan is booked and continues until either the collateral is secured, or the business has determined that the collateral cannot be secured.\n\nThe Collateral Perfection Group (CPG) based in Roanoke-VA, experts of state laws and loan/ lease agreements, uses this LLO. The LLO system was developed in 2001 with the stated objectives of improving the existing process of collateral follow-up\n\nResponsibilities:\n\n1.\n      \nSDLC process. (Design to Delivery)\n2.\n      \nCreating SDLC documents for every request.\n\n\nCapital One Auto \nFinance\n\nUSA\n                                                                       \nSep 06 ?Apr 07\nSoftware Engineer\n                                                                                           \n\nProject:\n\nCommon Loan Origination System\n\nEnvironment\n: Java, JDBC, JavaScript, Savvion Business Manager (SBM 6.8), BPM Studio, and Oracle9i.\n\nThis project is for the US based finance giant Capital One in the Auto Finance domain. This project basically proposes a process model solution applying the Savvion Business Manager 6.8 as the core, for automation of the Common Loan Origination system.\nDesigned an ?Inbound Communication via Emails? functionality that basically involves capturing all new emails from the Exchange Server received for the System from Capital One Loan Applicants (/ co-Applicants) / Auto Finance Dealers / Lending Partners and automatically process the same.\nCurrently involved in design and build of Business Process Flow components related to ?Fraud Investigation?, ?Termination? and ?Revival of Applications?.\n\n\nResponsibilities:\n\n1.\n       \nDesign and build of business process flow components by using Savvion Business Manager.\n2.\n       \nCoding for all batch job processes.\n3.\n       \nDeveloped the business logic in savvion adapters.\n4.\n       \nCreated the Stored Procedures, which contains the backend logic.\n5.\n       \nCreation of exhaustive Unit test plan and Execution of Unit test cases.\n\n\n\nBGK Engineering & Projects, \nHyderabad\n, AP\n                                                     \nAug? 05 ?Jul 06\nSoftware Engineer\n                                                                                           \n\nProject:\n\nBGK Engineering & Projects\n\nEnvironment\n: Java, JDBC, Struts, Servlets, JSP, JavaScript, Tomcat4.0 and Oracle.\n\nThis is E-procurement and Managing Information System project. The client main aims to construct any type of plants i.e. water plant, power plant and etc. The company has Head Office at one location and Plants at different locations. This project contains five main departments Finance and Administration, Commercial, Project, Procurement and plant departments. According to plants requirement the Plant Manager sends the Material Indent form to procurement Department, which is at Head Office. They will examine which supplier is supplying that material and forward to that supplier as purchase order.\n\nMain Operations are like Enquiry Form, Material Indent Form, Purchase Order Form, Purchase Order Amendment Form, Goods Delivery Note, Stores Issue Voucher, Stores Review Voucher, maintaining stock details and display, maintain the details of suppliers, contractors, products information and generating daily, weekly and monthly reports, salary accounts etc.\n\nResponsibilities:\n\n1.\n       \nDeveloped the whole Account Business Logic.\n2.\n       \nDeveloped programs using Servlets connecting to database.\n3.\n       \nDesigned and Developed JSP?s for front end.\n4.\n       \nInvolved in deploying the Servlets and JSP pages.\n\n\nInner Doorway\n         \n          \n                                                                                       \nOct? 04 ? July?05\nSoftware Engineer\n                                                                                           \n\nProject\n\nOnlineJobs.com\n\nEnvironment\n: Java, JDBC, Servlets, JSP, JavaScript, Tomcat,\n Net Beans IDE\n and Oracle.\n\nOnline Jobs is a web application and resembles any live job site. This portal allows prospective employees and employers to come together. It allows prospective employees and employers to register. Employees can search and apply for jobs that are added by employers. Employers can add and delete jobs and can get the details of applicants. Job Search can be done on the selected criteria. Operations like Login, Logout, Change Password, Change Profile and Forgot Password are common to both types of users.\n   \n\nResponsibilities:\n\n1.\n       \nDeveloped the whole \nserver side components containing business logic\n\n2.\n       \nDeveloped programs using \nServlets\n connecting to database\n\n3.\n       \nDesigned and Developed \nJSP?s\n for front end.\n\n\nE-Wings Solutions\n                                                             \n                                      \nApril? 04 ? Sep?04\nSoftware Engineer\n                                                                                                \nProject\n\nDaily Log Application\n\nEnvironment\n: Java, JDBC, Servlets, JSP, JavaScript, Tomcat,\n Net Beans IDE and\n Oracle.\n\nIt keeps the log details of all the employees along with the timings of activities done on each day. The activity entry includes the project name and the activity name. There is a provision for viewing the work report to the employee. There is provision for applying for the leave and for getting the leave details.\n\nThe administrator will get the work report as well as the total human hours needed for the project during the specified interval. Administrator can sign - up a new employee, can add a new project, allocate members to a project and add activities.\n\nResponsibilities:\n\nDeveloped programs using \nServlets\n connecting to database\n\n2.\n       \nDesigned and Developed \nJSP?s\n for front end.\n\n\nPERSONAL PROFILE\n\nName\n                           \n\nBhavani Rayala\nFather?s Name\n             \n\nMr.R.Venkateswara Rao.\n          \nDate of Birth\n                \n\n28\nth July, 1982\nLanguages Known\n       \n\nEnglish, Telugu and Hindi\nPermanent Address\n     \n\n P.No-162, Avanthi Nagar,Erragadda,Hyderabad-18\n\nREFERENCES\nAvailable on Request.',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-15',NULL,'2007-10-15','2010-06-08 12:13:25','2010-06-08',13,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(42,'Sreedhar Raman',NULL,NULL,NULL,'sd@yahoo.com','sreedhar.g@gmail.com','044 25262257','0','919444222323','0','919444222323','0','2008-04-29',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-08 12:13:25',13,'0',NULL,'200710/15/ATT8000.html','200710/15/DOC55876.doc','                                                            \nResume\n          \nSreedhar Raman\nOld No:34/New No:18, \nSreenivasa Iyer Street\n\n      \n                       \n\nHome ?\n (044)25262257\nParrys,\n                                                               \n           \n  \n\n                            \n\nMobile\n\n- +919444222323\n                                             \nChennai-600001\n                                                 \n   \n        \n\n\n\n\nsd@yahoo.com\nIndia\n            \n                                                                           \n                          \n___________________________________________________________________________\nCareer objective\nTo continue to grow in leadership and knowledge, excel in innovative technology application, interact and share with team members and colleagues, and develop world class solutions to real world challenges. I have a good balance of experience and education in applying effective software engineering methodologies and techniques. Areas that interest me include software & system architecture, requirement specification, software metrics, and Software Development.\n\n\nEDUCATION QUALIFICATIONS\nDegree / Certificate\nUniversity / Institute\nDescription\nYear\nB.E\nMadras\nUniversity\nBachelor of Engineering (E.E.E)\n1999\n\n\n\nTechnical Capabilities \nOperating Systems\n                   \nWindows \nLanguages\n                         \nJava, Servlets, JSP, EJB\nFramework\n                       \nStruts\nDatabases\n                               \nOracle, SqlServer\nMiddleware\n                             \nRMI\nApplicationServer\n        \n            \n\nWeblogic7, JBoss4, Apache\nTools\n                                               \nVSS, ClearCASE\n\nPROJECTS SUMMARY\nCompany: \nNess Technologies Limited, \nIndia\n\n                 \n    \n                    \n(July 2007 - Till Date)\n\nProject:\n\nEbay\n\n       \n                 \n    \n             \n       \n                                    \n(July 2007 ?Till Date)\n\nEbay is one of leading online auction store\n\nWas in the Shipping Team, it is the place where most of the development work happens, put on the project for label printing and also involved in the project for calculating the international shipping calculator.\nEnvironments\n\nJava, Servlets, Jsp, EJB, Oracle, Web Logic\n\nRole & Responsibility: \nSenior Associate.\n\n\n\n         \nCoordinating with onsite for issue resolution.\n\n\n         \nInvolved in the projects International Shipping Calculator and also Label Printing.\n\n\n         \nMaintenance and Enhancement.\n\n\n         \nPreparing the Unit / System test plan and executing the Unit / System testing\n\n\nCompany: \nHexaware Technologies Limited, \nIndia\n\n                     \n    \n(October 2005 - Apr 2007)\n\nProject:\n\nSEB OBM Online Banking\n     \n       \n                 \n\n               \n\n(October 2005 ? Apr 2007)\n\nSEB OBM\n is one of the largest banks in \nEurope\n with over 180 branches. \n\nSEB has different channels of banking namely HBCI (card banking), Ebroker, PinTan and Telebanking. Was involved in enhancement and maintenance of Ebroker, PinTan and Telebanking and tools like Ebroker Test tool.\n\nEbroker is a Brokerage application providing brokerage services in the Ebuisness suite of applications. The major services offered by the Ebroker application are Stock Ordering, Funds, Account Services and Portfolio Services. This application is used by customers who do high volume trading.\n\nSEB provides its customers different forms of Home Banking and Tele-banking is one of the widely used\nCustomers login to the PIN/TAN mode of access by launching \nwww.seb.de\n website and clicking on the link ?PIN/TAN Banking?. The entry point for the digital online banking system using the PIN/TAN mode of access is a via a set of client HTML screens that are part of the portal. The customer has to supply a PIN for logon. There are a set of transactions that would require a unique transaction number (TAN) also to be supplied.\n\nEnvironments\n\nJava, Servlets, Jsp, EJB, Oracle, Struts, Web Logic\n\nRole & Responsibility: Sr. \nSoftware Engineer.\n\n\n         \nAnalyze the current functionality of the system.\n\n\n         \nCoordinating with onsite for issue resolution.\n\n\n         \nPrepare the Analysis & Design document.\n\n\n         \nWent Onsite for a period of 3 months as First Level Support\n\n\n         \nMaintenance and Enhancement.\n\n\n         \nPreparing the Unit / System test plan and executing the Unit / System testing\n\n\nCompany: \nScandent Technologies. \n                   \n                       \n(July 2003 ? October 2005)\n\n\nProject:\n\nMyValueShop\n                                                \n          \n\n          \n(Jan 2005 ? October 2005)\n\n    \nMyValueShop is one of the leading e-commerce sites. Was involved in development and maintenance of this site. Was also involved in developing various reports\n\nEnvironments\n\nJava, Servlets, Jsp, EJB, Oracle, Web Logic\n\nRole & Responsibility: \nSoftware Engineer\n\n\n         \nWas involved in Development and Maintaince of site.\n\n         \nPrepare the Analysis & Design document \n\n         \nPreparing the Unit / System test plan and executing the Unit / System testing \n\nCompany: \nScandent Technologies.\n   \n\nProject:\n\n\nhakti\n                                                                        \n(Feb 2004 ? Jan 2005)\n                                    \nShakti is one of the leading garment portal. This portal has various features like customizing the size and style according to the choice of the customers. The site has various menu contents like the top sellers. Also there was also a back office manager, which was developed, this back office tool, which helps to monitor the status of the order that is placed by the customer. Also various reports are generated based on the customer requirements.\n\nEnvironments:\n Java, Servlets, Jsp, EJB, Oracle, Web Logic\n                                    \nRole & Responsibility: \nProgrammer.\n\n\n         \nInvolved in preparation of detailed design documents (DD) based on conceptual design (CD) produced by Client. \n\n         \nInvolved in coding and maintenance. \n\n         \nThis involves, building functionality within the existing system to enhance the functionality. \n\n         \nCoding & Unit Testing of Online programs.\n\n________________________________________________________________________\n\n\nCompany: \nScandent Technologies.\n\nProject:\n\nZapelle\n\n                                                        \n      \n(July 2003 ? Feb 2004)\n\nZapelle is one of the leading garment portal, which targets the us customers with various Indian Ethnic garments. The customers have the option of the customizing the size and style of the Garments. Also there is tool which maintains track of orders that are placed by the customer.. \n\nEnvironments\n\nJava, Servlets, Jsp, EJB, Oracle, Web Logic\n\nRole & Responsibility: \nProgrammer.\n\n\n         \nInvolved in preparation of detailed design documents \n\n         \nAlso involved in coding and maintaince. \n\n         \nCoding & Unit Testing of Online programs.\n________________________________________________________________________\n\n\nCompany: \nMarrquina Technologies.\n                                               \n(March 2002 ? June 2003)\n\n\nProject:\n\nWhize Cargo\n\n                                                            \n      \n         \n(March 2002 ? June 2003)\n\nThe Warehouse Management Software controls the placement of stock within a warehouse, stock movement with in the warehouse and its dispatch\n\nThe stock holding can be viewed from either the customer/product perspective or from the viewpoint of the physical location within the warehouse. General warehouse management functions. Quarantine - placing stock on hold and releasing stock from hold Enquiries: Including the interrogation of stock holding by product, by customer, by physical location and by pallet number. Stocktaking: Includes the initial warehouse set-up at installation and the perpetual warehouse stock checks.\n\nWith the stock check the physical stock actually held in the warehouse, is compared with the book stock held within the software. This discrepancy report is used to amend the book stock through the Stock Adjustments module within Warehouse Manager. The stock check can be performed by customer/product. Builds and maintains the base information the software needs to operate, including\n   \nCustomers Suppliers Products Warehouse. Financial Accounting: It includes complete customized financial accounting package\n\n\nEnvironments\n\nJava, Swing, RMI, SqlServer \nRole & Responsibility: \nProgrammer.\n\n\n         \nInvolved in preparation of detailed design documents \n\n         \nAlso involved in coding and maintaince. \n\n         \nPreparing the Unit / System test plan and executing the Unit / System testing\n\n\nPERSONAL PROFILE\nName in Full\n                       \n\n           \nG.Sreedhar\nDate of Birth\n                       \n\n           \nMarch 25\nth\n, 1978\nGender\n                               \n\n           \nMale\nNationality \n                         \n\n           \nIndian\nReligion\n                              \n\n           \nHindu\nLanguages Known\n              \n\n           \nEnglish, Hindi, Tamil, Telgu\nEmail\n                                  \n\n           \nsreedhar.g@gmail.com\n, sdrsd@yahoo.com\nTelephone Number\n              \n\n          \n+91 9444222323',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-15',NULL,'2007-10-15','2010-06-08 12:13:25','2010-06-08',13,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(43,'Sushma M',NULL,NULL,'Banglore','su2000@gamil.com','sushmamishra2000@gmail.com',NULL,'0','09341676566','0',NULL,'0','2006-07-14',7,18,'2010-06-08 12:13:25',12,'0',NULL,'200710/15/ATT7999.html','200710/15/DOC55877.doc','Resume\n\nSUSHMA\n\n\n\nEmail: \nsu2000@gamil.com\n\n\nMobile-\n 09341676566\n\nObjective\n\n\nTo make a promising carrier in field of Software Developer Engineering in the organization where my hard work and dedication will take me the pinnacle of success while contributing to growth of the organization\n\nProfessional Summary\n\n\n         \nMore than\n 3+ yrs \nof Experience\n in developing Web Applications Using Java Technologies\n\n         \nExperience\n in developing Web Applications Using Java Technologies\n\n\n         \nExcellent knowledge\n on \nJ2EE\n technology.\n\n         \nHand on experience \nin \nStruts\n\n\n         \nKnowledge in UML. \n\n         \nStrong Knowledge on core java programming\n\n\n         \nExcellent problem solving skills with a strong technical background and good interpersonal skills\n\n\n         \nQuick learner and excellent team player having ability to meet tight dead lines and work under pressure\n\nWork Experience\n\n         \nWorking\n\nas Application Devloper with\n\nSUPERSOFT\n\nSOLUTION\n Banglore from 2004 till date.\n\n         \nWorked as Junior programmer with Pentasoft tech frmJan2004-June2004.\n\n\nTechnical Skills\n\n\n                                               \n                 \nLanguages\n                           \n\nJAVA,J2EE.\nJava Technology\n                   \n\nCorejava,SWINGS,JDBC,JSP,Servlet,Struts.\nServer\n                                 \n\nTomcat4.1,Weblogic,Webspere5.1.\nIDE\n                              \n       \n\nEclipse\nScripting language\n                \n\nHTML,XML.\nDatabase\n                             \n\n Oracle,MS Access.\nOperating Systems\n               \n\n Windows series.\nExposure to\n                          \n\nISO,CMM quality standard.\n\nScholastic Profile\n\nProfessional:\nB.E in Electronics & Telecommunication Engineering with an aggregate of 70% in 2004.\n\nProjects Undertaken\n\nInsurance Management\n\nApplication Software\n\n                 \n\nStruts,Jsp,Servlet\nPlatform\n                                    \n\n WindowXP.\nServer\n                                       \n\nTomcat\n\nDatabase\n                                    \n\nOracle\nDuration\n                           \n        \n\n Mar 2007 till date\n          \nThis project is all about the Insurance Management\n\nfor insurance company.Here the process is improved much in better way\n\nwhich satisfy the client requirment.The purpose of this project to eleminate manual transaction\n\n& establish a easy way accses connection to the normal people .\nResponsibilities: \n\n               \nInvolved in coding\n\n               \nDevoloping \nthe source code for the Struts MVC Component\n                                             \nSanotorium Management System(SMAS)\n          \nClient\n                                       \n\nBeth\nIsarel\nHospital\nApplication Software\n\n                  \n\nStruts,Jsp,Servlet\nPlatform\n            \n                         \n\n WindowXP.\nServer\n                                        \n\nTomcat\n\nDatabase\n                                    \n\nOracle\nDuration\n                           \n        \n\n Aug 2005 to Jan 2007\n     \nBeth Isarel Hosapital is a premier Hospital in USA with numerous branches established to serve the community.SMAS is an integrated Sanotorium Management System(SMAS),which addresses all major functional areas of modern multi-specific hospitals.SMAS enable better patent care, patient safty,efficiency and reduced\n\ncosts.its provides easy access to critical information thru by enabling the management to take better decision on time.\nResponsibilities: \n\n               \nInvolved in coding\n\n               \nDevoloping \nthe source code for the Struts MVC Component\n   \n\n               \nInvolved in Unit testing.\n    \nACCUASYS\n         \n\nClient\n                                        \n\nSupersoft solution\nApplication Software\n\n                  \n\nJ2ee,Jsp,Servlet\nPlatform\n                                     \n\n WindowXP.\nServer\n                                        \n\n Weblogic \nDatabase\n         \n                           \n\nOracle\nDuration\n                           \n        \n\n10-month\n      \nThis project based on ACCOUNTING\n\nOutsourcing. In this project Client want to perform\n\nthe hole client requirement for Indian system. \nThis project is for the associates who will be executing the job in India.The jobs may be accounting,medical,financial etc.This module is for the experts in domains like QuickBook,Sages(Accounting Software?s)\n\nResponsibilities:\n\n         \nInvolved in coding\n\n         \nInvolved in design and analysis discussion. \n\nConstruction Of staging material\n          \nClient\n                                         \n:Mahabir construction\nApplication Software\n\n                  \n:Core java,SWINGS,JDBC,RMI\nPlatform\n                                     \n:WindowXP.\nServer\n                              \n          \n:Weblogic \nDatabase\n                                    \n:Oracle\nDuration\n                           \n        \n: 6-month.\nMahabir is construction is a leading construction company in Orissa, The project based on this construction company. This project aimed at servicing the client in better way.The main purpose of this project is to automate the master requirement of production, how the processing carried out from raw material order. In this project we try to reduce manual work and time. This gives total information about Construction Company.\nNotice Period\n         \n\n20-30days\nCurent CTC\n              \n\n2.96 per Annum\nExpected CTC\n         \n\nAs per company standard\n\nPersonal Summary\n\nName\n                          \n                \n: Sushma Mishra\nAddress\n                     \n                \n\nC/o:-Mr.Ambika Prasad\n\nMishra,\n                   \n          \n\n        \n        \nAt/Po Devinivash,\n                             \n\n        \n        \nH/N114,5\nth\n cross Dinnur,\n                                      \n        \nR.T Nagar Post,\n                                                 \nBangalore-32.\nNationlity\n                                \n\nIndian\n\nEmail\n                          \n                 \n\nsushmamishra2000@gmail.com\nMobile\n                        \n                 \n\n 09341676566','SUPERSOFT SOLUTION',1,NULL,'2007-10-15',NULL,'2007-10-15','2010-06-08 12:13:25','2010-06-08',12,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(44,'Sreepriya T',NULL,NULL,NULL,'sree8378R_tk@yahoo.com',NULL,'91 480 2829488','0','09901062639','0',NULL,'0','2008-04-29',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-08 12:13:25',12,'0',NULL,'200710/15/ATT7998.html','200710/15/DOC55878.doc','SREEPRIYA T\nSREEPRIYA .R\nHouse No: 18,2\nnd\n Cross,\nBalaji Nagar, DRC Post, \nBangalore-560029\nE-mail: sree8378R_tk@yahoo.com\nMobile\n\n\n09901062639\n                                                \n                                             \nObjective:\nAim to be associated with progressive organization that gives me scope in the Software Development to apply my knowledge and skills along with my hard work and patience and to be involved as a part of team that dynamically works towards the growth of the organization.\n\n\nExperience Summary:\n\n2+ years of experience as a Software Developer.\n\nWork Experience:\n\nWorking as \nTechnical Associate\n with \nTech Mahindra Ltd \nfrom 8\nth\n Apr 2005 till date\n\n\nStrengths:\n\n\n          \nGood Communication skills\n\n          \nGood analytical, Presentation skills.\n\n          \nGood knowledge of Software Development Life Cycle (\nSDLC\n).\n\n          \nAn excellent team player as well as an individual contributor.\n\n          \nA fast learner who is flexible and enjoys mastering new job assignments\n\nEducation\n\n\n             \nB.Tech\nin [Computer Science] from \n\nCo-operative Institute Of Technology, Vadakara, \nCalicut\n] with \nAggregate: 65.64%\n of all semesters.\n\n              \nPRE-DEGREE\n Passed in Distinction, [\n81.6%\n] from [\nSt.Joseph?s College, Irinjalakuda, Thrissur\n] in [\n2000 June\n.]\n\n               \nSSLC\n Passed with distinction, \n92%\n] from [\nST.Mary?s H S, Kayamkulam, Alappuzha\n] in [1998 May.]\n\n        \nSoftware Exposure:\nOperating System \n                    \nWin 9X, Windows XP, UNIX\nLanguages \n                               \nC, C++, Java, Sql, Pl/sql, VB\n\nCompany Profile:\n\nTechMahindra\n            \nis a leading Systems Consulting and Integration Organization providing high quality software services to businesses and industry, with specific expertise in Telecommunications. Services are provided in the areas of Requirements Analysis to System Implementation, Application, Maintenance and Support, Internet based Solutions, Software Solutions in Customer Care and Billing etc. \nTechMahindra\n is an ISO 9001-2000 certified organization and is assessed at CMM Level 5.\n\nProfessional Projects:\n\nFLOW STREAM\n                                                                                    \n        \nTechMahindra\n            \n\nRole\n\nSoftware \ndeveloper\nDescription\n\nFlow Stream acts as a mid - tier system targeted at automation of Order handling. It is designed as a fully configurable system allowing new products to be deployed rapidly. It supports multiple client systems and can place component orders across multiple back end systems. FlowStream is focused on problems associated with complex orders, packages and bundles.\n\nThis project uses a java-based tool called E-SCAMP. This tool collects customer data and helps to validate orders for the customer through call sequences developed and this information is passed to eCO system marketed by \nTechMahindra\n to place the orders. The project also uses a tool called Change Synergy for creating Change Request (CR), associating tasks to the respective CRs and resolving them. A tool called Continuus is used for creating objects and tasks.\n\n\nResponsibilities\n\n1)\n       \nDevelop new call sequences using E-SCAMP tool and test for optimized performance.\n2)\n       \nUnit testing and preparation of Unit Test Plans.\n3)\n       \nInvestigation of faults and fixing them.\n4)\n       \nQuery handling and solving them.\n\nProfessional Training:\n\n\nttended 3 months of technical and behavioral training program conducted by \nTechMahindra Ltd\n in Mumbai. \nTechnical training was given on JAVA, VB, SQL, PL/SQL, UNIX, C++, DBMS, Software Engineering and VV&T. Behavioural training mainly concentrated on Presentation Skills, Communication Skills, Business etiquette and Teamwork.\n\nCurriculum Projects:\n\nMain Project:\n\n   \n\nSIMULATION AND PERFORMANCE EVALUATION OF GIGABIT ETHERNET\n?.\nA local area network is simulated in the project, which employs Ethernet based (Bus) topology and makes use of token frame as an arbitration mechanism. Various parameters, which include frame size, bandwidth etc are varied in order to obtain the characteristics of Gigabit Ethernet.\n\nThe graphical user interface is implemented using C language.\n          \n\nMiniProject:\n    \n\nINTERNET CONNECTION SHARING USING PROXY SERVER\n\n\nBy internet connection sharing we enable to configure a computer network to share a single connection to the internet. One computer on the network called the connection sharing computer has an internet connection and provides private IP address and resolution services for the other computers on the network. We used Visual Basic 6.0 to implement the project.\n\n\n\n\nPersonal Profile:\n\n      \n\name:\n                                \nSreepriya T.K\n      \nDate of Birth:\n                      \n20-05-1983.\n      \nFather?s name:\n                    \nKumaran T.K\n      \nSex: \n                                   \nFemale\n      \nMarital Status:\n                   \nMarried\n      \nLanguages:\n                         \nEnglish, Hindi and Malayalam \n      \nNationality:\n                        \nIndian\n      \nPermanent Address:\n      \nLeela Nivas,\n      \nNear Block Office,\n      \nMadayikonam P.O, Irinjalakuda,\n      \nThrissur, Kerala- 680712\n      Ph: +91-480-2829488\n\nHobbies:\n\n\nListening to Music and Drawing.\nReferences:\nAvailable upon request',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-15',NULL,'2007-10-15','2010-06-08 12:13:25','2010-06-08',12,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(45,'Vijay J',NULL,NULL,'Chennai','auv1456@gmail.com',NULL,NULL,'0','9940305015','0',NULL,'0','2008-04-13',10,33,'2010-06-08 12:13:25',12,'0',NULL,'200710/15/ATT7997.html','200710/15/DOC55879.doc','VIJAY KUMAR\n\nB.E Computer science and Engineering\n\nCollege\n of \nEngineering\n Guindy, \nAnna\nUniversity\n\n\n\n\nEmail\n\nauv1456@gmail.com\n\nMobile Number:\n\n\n\n+91-9940305015\n\nCommunication Address\nVIJAY J\nC/O. T.Rajmohan,\n14/9\n\n5th street\n\nGovindasamy nagar,\nKandan chavadi,\nPerungudi,\nChennai-600096\nIndia\n\n\nPersonal Data:\n\nFather\'s Name : \nT.Jayaraman\nDate of\n\nBirth\n\n: 30 MAY 1982\nSex\n                \n: Male\nNationality\n      \n: Indian\nMarital Status : Single\nPassport No\n\n: E6833479\n\nLanguages\n\n: English, Tamil ,Telugu\n\nProfessional Summary\nProfessional with close \nto 3 years of IT experience\n on \nDEVELOPMENT ROLE \nIn leading \ndigital Cable interactive systems for video (Set Top boxes-Embedded)\n & writing test automation tools.\n\n\nCareer Profile\n\n\nWORK EXPERIENCE\nOrganization\n\nScientific \nAtlanta\n, A CISCO Company ? Chennai\nWork Area\nSet Top boxes\n, APPLICATION AND MIDDLEWARE DEVELOPER\n\nDBDS- Digital Broadband Delivery System) \nSA is providing solutions in broadband communication and digital subscriber networks.\nDesignation\nDevelopment Engineer\nDuration\nMarch 2006 ? till date.\nProjects\nJAVA IGUIDE(OCAP-JAVA), NATIVE IGUIDE(MIDDLEWARE-C)\n\n\nOrganization\nORACLE\n\nIndia Limited, \nBangalore\nWork Area\nTest scripts(Automation tools,C,UNIX),PATCH BUILDING,\nTESTING)\nDesignation\nMember Technical Staff\nDuration\nJanuary 2005 ? FEB 2006. (14 MONTHS)\nProjects\nServer Technologies (PATCH BUILDING,TESTING)\n\nEducation\nDegree\nUNIVERSITY/BOARD\n% OF MARKS\n\nState Board\n83%\nXII\nState Board\n83.83%\n\n\nTNEA RANK 112\n\n   \n(STATE LEVEL)\nB.E-CSE\n\nCollege\n Of \nEngineering\n, Guindy, Chennai\nAnna\nUniversity\n         \n7.2 /10\n\n\nSkills\nLanguages\n      \n\n\nC, C++, Java, UML\nOS & DB\n\n        \n\n\nSolaris, Unix, Linux, WINDOWS, Oracle, Ms Access\nTools \n              \n\nRational Rose for OOAD ,Clarify 12.5,\nCable & Broadband Devices :\n\nSA Range of DVR, non-DVR Set top boxes,\n\nKey Projects\n\n1) I-Guide (Implemented in c)\n\nDescription\nI-Guide\nThe all new interactive programming guide from TV Guide. A common UI for both scientific \nAtlanta\n and Motorola head ends.\nFeatures:\nA convenient, time-saving quick menu\nA user friendly enhanced search\nincreased speed\nAnd Mini Guide, a whole new way to watch TV and surf at the same time\nEasy to set reminders, favorites, Parental control and Pay Per View\nRole\n\nDevelopment Engineer\nEnvironment\n\nSA Range of DVRs, non-DVR set top boxes, QAMs, QPSK,\n\nDNCS\n (Solaris Server)\nResponsibilities\n          \n\n\nDESIGNED AND DEVELOPED DDM MODULE(Diagnostic Data Manager)\n\n   \nDiagnostic pages to be determined at run-time rather than compile-time.\n\n   \nDDM is a middleman between components that have diag data to display and a component or components that want to display diagnostic data\n\n   \nMaintains a list of active (registered) pages.\n\n   \nNotifies data providers when diagnostics begin and end.\n\n   \nPasses data requests to data providers on behalf of the data consumer.\nFixing CRS(bugs) and unit testing on other modules\nWorked closely with OS, Drivers, GWS to triage out the CRS that?s related with their layer and suggesting the fix from my analysis.\nDuration\nNOV 2006 ? Till now\nTeam Size\n12\nCompany\nScientific \nAtlanta\n, A Cisco Company\n\n\n2)\n                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                           \nJAVA GUIDE(Implemented in Java)\n\nDescription\n\nThis is Java version of native Iguide. In native iguide APL layer will be different based on the set top (platform dependent). Java iguide running on OCAP (middleware) stack and it will run on any set top. Application developers don?t need to worry about hardware.\n\n\n\n\nRole\nDevelopment Engineer\nEnvironment\nSA Range of DVRs, non-DVR set top boxes.\nResponsibilities\n          \n\n\n\n\n\n\nGiven couple of presentations to new team members\nAt the initial stage of project I am the only member who handled project in Chennai.\nGenerated profiled data for various scenarios\nAnalyzed methods (call sequence) based on time and memory\nOptimized those methods\nUnit testing (comparing performance between old and profiled data)\n\nDuration\nMarch 2006 ? OCT 2006\nTeam Size\n\nCompany\nScientific \nAtlanta\n, A Cisco Company\nClient\nComcast, cable vision, times Warner\n\n\n\n\n3. TESTING AUTOMATION TOOLS \n\nDescription\n\n         \nSORT INPUT SQL FILES (I\nmplemented in c\n\n                 \nThis tool will reduce lot of manual work at the time of patch building and testing.\n\nAfter applying the patch we need to execute some x number of sql files in db. There is some dependency between sql files. So initially we don?t know in which order we have to execute. If we give the incorrect or improper order of sql file names as input, it will give the output in correct order.\n\n\n         \nSEND ALERT MAIL TO DELIVER THE PATCH ON TIME\n (PERL,JAVA,UNIX)\n     \nI have written this tool in perl , java on Linux platform. \n\nOur team contains lot of bugs in centralized queue. It?s difficult to scan the queue frequently in a day. My tool will send the alert mail with list of bugs to my team for every 3 hours that if queue contains high priority or highly escalated bugs. \n     \n\nPerl code will access the bug database and it will filter less priority bugs and write the high priority bugs into file which we need to send through mail. Once the file has been created, java code will read this file and send the mail to my team.\n\nRole\n\nMember Technical Staff\nEnvironment\n\nC,UNIX,JAVA,SOLARIS\nContribution\n\n         \nI have done some couple of test automation tools.\n\n         \nDelivered show stoppers bugs on time, severe CRS\n\nDuration\nJanuary 2005 ? FEB 2006\nTeam Size\n14\nCompany\nORACLE ? \nBangalore','ORACLE  India Limited',1,NULL,'2007-10-15',NULL,'2007-10-15','2010-06-08 12:13:25','2010-06-08',12,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(46,'Suresh Kumar',NULL,NULL,NULL,'sp@rediffmail.com','spsureshkumar79@rediffmail.com','04426841284','0','9940420452','0',NULL,'0','2007-04-30',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-08 12:13:25',12,'0',NULL,'200710/15/ATT7996.html','200710/15/DOC55880.doc','Name:\nSuresh Kumar\n                                                                                                            \n                                                                                                            \nMobile\n:9940420452\n   \n                                                                        \n    \nEmail\n:sp@rediffmail.com\n\nProfessional\n\nSummary\n\n\n3+ years of experience in software industry as a Software Tester\n\nExpertise in \nManual Testing.\nWell Experience in \nBlack Box Testing.\nActively involved in Preparing and executing \nTest Cases\n\nWell versed in \nDefect Tracking & Bug Reporting\nHave good knowledge of methodology followed in the \nSDLC\n and \nSTLC\n\nExtensive work experience on Sanity Testing, Regression Testing, Functional testing, and System Testing, User Interface Testing and Ad-hoc testing.\n\nSkill Set:\n                     \n\nOperating System\n         \n        \n: Windows\nProgramming Language\n     \n: Java\nDatabase\n          \n                    \n: Oracle\nTesting tool\n       \n        \n    \n        \n: Win runner 7.0\n                \nOthers\n   \n                       \n        \n\n\nHTML, Java Script.\n\nEducation Qualifications:\n\n\n          \nMCA (Master of Computer Applications) from\n\nJaya College of Arts and Science.\n\n\nProfessional Experience:\n\n        \nPresently working in \nPolaris Software Lab Ltd \nas a Software Tester from Jan 2006 - till date.\n\n        \nWorked in \nFiducia Technology\n as a Test Engineer from July 2004 to Jan 2006.\n\n\n\nPROJECT SUMMARY\nProject\n\n\n\nProject\n Name\n\nHiCommand NAS Manager GUI\n                     \nClient : \nHitachi\n\nJapan\n\nEnvironment : \nJSP, Servlet , Java Script, Struts\nDuration:\n Jan 2006 - till date\n\nProject Description : \nThe project deals with development a managerial application for administering the Network Attached Storage (NAS) system, a proprietary product of Hitachi. The NAS system enables users in a network to use storage areas that are attached to the network and available to them in the form of shared folders. The storage device is normally a RAID system in which file systems are created and made available to users in the form of shared folders. Access rights and privileges for a particular share can also be specified using the application. The users of this application can be categorized into Account Administrators, System Administrators and End Users.\nThis particular GUI phase deals with development of GUI for the Administrative functions that are currently executed using Command Line Interface (CLI). The current development involves modules such as Shares Management, File Systems Management, Processing Node Management, Users and Permissions etc. Internationalization of the application is also taken into consideration during development\nRole: Software Tester\nTeam size:6\nResponsibilities: \n\n        \nDeveloping and Designing Test Plan.\n\n        \nCreation of detailed test cases by understanding the and user requirements.\n\n        \nVerified fixes and closed bugs during regression test cycle.\n\n        \nBug Report generation.\nProject#2\n                              \nProject Name\n\nSchool Management System\n         \nClient \nGlobal Technology Innovations\nEnvironment \nJSP, Servlets, HTML, JDBC, Java Script\nDuration:\n Feb 2005 - Dec 2005\nProject Description\n\nThis product will automate every activity in the school management like maintaining student, staff details, and other necessary details. Apart from these, this product will provide all needed information about the school activities to the students and staffs online. For Students the details about their graduation status, school calendar, and for Staffs their pay details and both can apply for leave online. Moreover, this product is capable of maintaining the entire accounting system and payroll management system of the school and other activities like Transport maintenance, Library Maintenance. \nRole: Test Engineer\nTeam Size\n   \n\n\n10\nResponsibilities: \n\n        \nInvolved in preparing Test cases.\n\n        \nCreation of test cases and execution of test cases.\n\n        \nDone Test case Review.\n\n        \nPerformed different types of testing like Positive, Negative, Regression, Integration and System Testing.\nProject# 3\nProject Name: \nHuman Resource Management System\n       \nClient\n\nSTADS LTD\nEnvironment\n\nJsp, Servlets, JDB\n\nDuration: \nJuly 2004 - Jan 2005\nProject Description\n\nHRMS allows companies to manage information based on their unique HR structure and needs. Data is entered just once and is shared with the entire HR system ? leaving time to address strategic business issues that support recruiting and maintain a competitive work force.\n\nThe various modules that are handled in this system are:\n\n\nHuman Resource Development, which covers Man, power planning, Man power Requests, Recruitment Management, Advertisements, Interview Process etc.\n\n\nPersonnel management which has the scope of Employee Transfers, Employee Promotions, Employee Separation, Profile Management, Employee PF, ESI, Performance appraisal and Loans and Advances.\n\n\nAttendance System, which helps in recording the daily attendance, maintains a movement register, allows monthly shift and weekly off allocations for the employees, employee over time request and on duty request and helps views the employee work calendar.\n\n\nLeave module, which manages all the leave eligibility, leave carry over, and leave monthly balance.\n\n\nLibrary module covers the books receipt / Issue, books lost register, Books availability, advance reservation, current day dues.\n\n\nTraining Management unit describes the various training schemes, training participants, training budget, training plan, training status and training calendar.\n\n\nAdmin module, which is used for the user creation and user management.\nRole: Tester Engineer\nTeam Size : 8\nResponsibilities: \n\n          \nUnderstanding the requirements and\n\n          \nPreparation of Test cases and Execution of Test cases\n\n          \nDefect logging and tracking\n\nProject# 4\nProject Name: \nE-Shopping Cart\n                                   \nClient \nMaxwin Tech\nEnvironment\n\nJSP, Servlets, HTML, JDBC, Java Script\nDuration:\n Dec 2003 - Jun 2004\nProject Description\n\n\nThis project is dealt with designing a E-shopping which can be applied for a E-Shopping Center. The project has lot of modules such as viewing all the items in the shop, maintaining the stock and maintain the user enter information etc. It has a cart in which all the items purchased by the user can be added to the cart and it can be also deleted from it. There are various payment modes in order to facilitate the user by giving him choices to choose his mode.\nRole: Test Engineer\nTeam Size\n\n\nResponsibilities: \n\n        \nPreparation of Test cases and Review Test cases and \n\n        \nExecution Test cases\n\n        \nDefect Tracking and Publishing the Test results.\n\n\n\n\nPersonal Details:\n\nPresent Address: \n#5 Udaya Suriyan Street,\n                                    \n\nMittanamalli\n                                    \n\nIAF, Avadi\n                                    \n\nChennai\n   \n                                 \n  \nTamil Nadu\n                                                                            \n                                    \n\nPin 600 055\n               \n\nPermanent Address\n\n#5 Udaya Suriyan Street,\n                             \n\nMittanamalli\n                                    \n\nIAF, Avadi\n                             \n\nChennai\n                             \n\nTamil Nadu\n                                                            \n                             \n\nPin 600 055\n\n          \n\nContact Numbers:\n\nResidence - \n04426841284\n                             \nMobile ? \n9940420452\n                             \nEmail Address: \n      \nspsureshkumar79@rediffmail.com\n                             \n                             \nPassport details:\n    \nF 2885211',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-15',NULL,'2007-10-15','2010-06-08 12:13:25','2010-06-08',12,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(47,'Vinod Kumar',NULL,NULL,'Bangalore','vinod1783@yahoo.co.in',NULL,NULL,'0','9916308896','0',NULL,'0','2008-04-13',7,19,'2010-06-08 12:13:25',12,'0',NULL,'200710/15/ATT7995.html','200710/15/DOC55881.doc','Sample Profile Format\n\nName :\n\n\nVinod Kumar\nE-Mail:vinod1783@yahoo.co.in\nPhNo : 9916308896 \n      \n    \n  \n                              \n                                       \n   \n\n\nObjective\n\n\n        \nQuest to work in a professional atmosphere in the field of Information Technology that enables me to cope with the emerging skills as well as the latest technology thus widening the spectrum of my knowledge\n\n\nSummary\n\n\n        \nHave 2 years of experience in JAVA/J2EE as a team member.\n\n        \nHave knowledge in Servlets, JSP, and Struts Framework.\n\n        \nFlexible to work in any kind of environment\n\n        \nDeep desire to learn & constantly upgrade skills.\n\n        \nGood communication skills\n\n\nEducation\n\n\n        \nB.Tech.\n\n(Bachelor of Technology)\n\nin\n\nElectrical and Electronics with \nFIRST CLASS\n from\n\nJNTU, \nHyderabad\n\n\n        \nIntermediate from \nBoard of Intermediate, A.P \nwith First Class\n\n        \nS.S.C from \nBoard of Secondary Education, A.P\n with First Class.\n\n\nWork Experience\n\n\n        \nWorking as Software Developer in \nPrimes IT Solutions, \nBangalore\n\nfrom May?05 to till date.\n\n\nExpertise\n\n     \nOperating Systems\n        \n\n     \nWindows 2000/XP\nLanguages\n                          \n\n     \nJava and HTML\n      \nAdv Java Technologies\n\n\n     \nJDBC, Servlets, JSP\n      \nFrame Work\n                      \n\n     \nStruts\n      \nWeb/Application Servers\n    \n\n     \nTomcat 5.0, Weblogic 8.1\n      \nDatabase\n                            \n\n     \nOracle\n      \nIDE?s\n                                 \n\n     \nEclipse 3.1\n      \nTools\n                                  \n\n     \nTortoise CVS, File Compare\nProjects\n\nPROJECT# 1\n\nCustomer Service Maintenance System\n\nClient\n         \n            \n                  \nSip Micro Systems Inc Pvt Ltd., \nFranklin\nSoftware\n                                  \nJSDK 1.4, JSP?s, Struts and Oracle\nTeam Size\n                                \n\nDuration\n                                   \nSeptember 2006 to till date\nRole\n                                         \nTeam Member\n\nDescription:\n                    \n               \nThis package helps the Customer Service Department of company in providing efficient after sales services for their products. Items are served based on complaints and contract. The allotted service engineer attends the complaint and as such updates the customer card with the required information. In addition, a daily activity form for each service engineer is maintained to keep tracks the performance of the service engineer. Invoices, Customer Card, and daily activity report are also maintained.\n\nResponsibilities:\n\n        \nDevelopment of Screens using JSP.\nInvolved in Unit Testing\n\n\nPROJECT# 2\n\nEnterprise\n Resource Information System\n\nClient\n                                       \nMaruthi-IT, \nBangalore\nSoftware\n                                  \nJSDK 1.4, Servlets, JSP, JavaScript, Oracle\nTeam Size\n                                \n10\nDuration\n     \n                              \nFebruary 2006 to August 2006\nRole\n                                         \nTeam Member\n\nDescription:\n                                  \nIt is a computerized solution for recruiting agencies and software consultants. This application maintains electronic Database compromising of job applications, work stand employers. User of this system can create and access details of all the information using advanced GUI screens compromising of menus, bitmaps toolbars, status bar and many more. This is an intranet application to maintain his clients and employees status and schedule interviews for applicants.\n\nResponsibilities:\nDeveloped applications in java which collects the database of applicants, employers.\nDeveloped Servlets to handle servlet?s request and servlet?s response objects.\n\nPROJECT #3\n\ne- Trucking\n\nClient\n               \n                              \nFreight Desk Technologies Inc.\nSoftware\n    \n      \n                              \nJava, JSP, Servlets, EJB, WebLogic7.0, Oracle8i\nTeam Size\n                                      \n10\nDuration\n           \n                              \nAugust 2005 to Jan 2006 \n   \nRole\n                                               \nTeam Member\n      \nDescription:\n\ne- Trucking is a global freight management system that enables shippers and logistics service providers to manage the complexities of international trade from their customers. This system substantially automates the communication process between multiple parties exchanging many documents and much data. This system aggregate all the data, make intelligent routing recommendations, track the location and status of all cargo and increasing visibility with full data connectivity to all partners and existing applications.\nThis project is developed in J2EE Architecture (MVC Type II Model) using JSP? segmentation in Web Tier and business logic in EJBs with Servlets as controllers.\ne-Trucking is completely vendor and carrier neutral. The applications are mode neutral, i.e., the shipment can move via air, ocean, and surface. The project consists of four modules: i) e-Trans, ii) e-Log, iii) e-Accounts, iv) e-HR\n\nRole and Responsibilities\n\n   \nInvolved in the coding of JSP?s and Java Servlets for e-Trans module.\nInvolved in the Unit testing.\n\n\nPersonal Details\n\nFather?s Name\n       \n: Y. Simhachalam\nDate of Birth\n           \n: 07-01-1983\nSex\n                        \n: Male\nMarital Status\n         \n: Single\nContact Details\n\n: #3, \nMuniappan\nBuildings\n, Pai Layout, Benniganahalli, Bangalore-16.','Primes IT Solutions',1,NULL,'2007-10-15',NULL,'2007-10-15','2010-06-08 12:13:25','2010-06-08',12,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(48,'Sanjeeth Chakravarthi',NULL,NULL,'Hyderabad','samba14589@gmail.com',NULL,NULL,'0','9966009730','0',NULL,'0','2006-06-13',8,24,'2010-06-08 12:13:25',12,'0',NULL,'200710/15/ATT7994.html','200710/15/DOC55882.doc','Resume\nSanjeeth Chakravarthi \nPhone: 9966009730\nLocation: Hyderabad, India\nEmail:\n\nsamba14589@gmail.com\n\n   \nSUMMARY:\n3.8 years\n of experience in Development, Implementation and Testing of web-applications using \nMicrosoft .NET Framework,\n\nASP.NET, C#.NET, VB.NET, SQL Server, \nHTML, \nJavaScript.\nWorked on Object oriented programming\n (OOPS), \nhaving knowledge of \nADO.NET\n\nWorked using Infragistics controls\n\n        \nExperience in creating \nWeb Forms, User Controls, Custom controls \nand\n\n\nvalidating user inputs using\n validation techniques.\nWorked on \nStored\n Procedures,\n\nTriggers and Cursors with SQL Server\n\n\n        \nExperienced in different phases of software development cycle including Programming, Testing.\n\n        \nTeam player with strong interpersonal and communication skills.\n\n\n        \nHolding a valid passport.\n\nTECHNICAL SKILLS:\n\nProgramming Languages \n      \n\n           \nC#.NET, VB.NET.(OOPs Concepts)\nInternet Technologies\n       \n     \n\n\n          \nASP.NET.\nScripts & Mark-up\n    \n     \n       \n\n\n         \nJavaScript, HTML and CSS\n                               \n          \n       \nDatabases\n                  \n     \n       \n\n\n         \nMS-SQL Server 2000.\nDatabase Concepts\n    \n     \n       \n\n\n         \nADO.NET.\nTools\n                           \n     \n       \n\n          \nVS.NET,\n\nInfragistic Controls.\n\nOperating Systems\n    \n     \n       \n\n\n         \nWindows XP / 2000, MS-DOS.\nERP\n                                         \n\n          \nMS Dynamics ? Navision 4.0\n\n\nEDUCATION:\n\n        \nBachelor of Engineering in Computer Science & Engineering\n\n\nCERTIFICATIONS:\n\n        \nMicrosoft Certified Professional Certification.\n\nPROFESSIONAL EXPERIENCE\n\n\n        \nTechnical Associate at\n Tech Mahindra \nfrom\n\nApril 2007 to till date\n\n        \nSoftware Engineer\n\nat\n Computer Solutions and Software International \nfrom Dec? 05 to March? 07\n\n        \nApplication Developer\n\nat\n SugaeTech Solutions from \nMay? 05 to Dec? 05\n\n        \nProgrammer at \nRAM INFORMATICS LTD from \nDec? 03 to Apr? 05\n\n\n\n\n\n\nPROJECTS\n\n1. Computer Solutions and Software International Ltd, Hyderabad, India\nDuration \n        \n\n December 2005 ? March 30 2007\nClient\n              \n\nParagon Metals, USA \nRole\n                \n\n DotNet Developer\nProject \n           \n\n\nParagon Product Management System\n\n\nParagon acts as mediator between customers and vendors. They take the order from their customers and get those parts from their vendors and will release those to their customers. This application is used right from taking the order from customer and involves in all steps like ordering, creating customer requirements, giving the order to vendors, billing, releases and goes on. This whole process is managed using this \nParagon Product Management System.\nResponsibilities\n\n\nExtensively worked with \nWindows \napplication\n, ASP.NET, ADO.NET, \nC#.NET\n\n\nSQL Server.\n\n\n\nUsed \nInfragistic controls\n in developing.\n\n\nWorked on Purchase Order, Order entry edit and search screens.\n\n\nWorked on Customer Requirement and Vendor Release entry, edit and search screens.\n\n\nWorked on Inventory Search screen.\n\n\nWorked on Incident Resolution search screen. \n\n\nWorked on Bill of Lading Screen.\n\n\nWorked on Events,Navigation Screens.\n\n\nWorked on Presentation, Data Access and\n\nBusiness Logic layers of the application.\n\n\nUsed \nDataset\n\nDataTable\n, SQLHelper and other \nADO.NET\n connectivity controls .\n\n\nUsed Validation Controls, Java Script and custom Validation functions for validations.\n\n\nCreated Stored Procedures, Cursors and Triggers for accessing, inserting and updating data.\n\n\nUsed CSS for look and feel approach for Web pages.\n\nEnvironment:\n ADO.NET, Windows\n application\n\nASP.NET\n\nC#.\nNET, JavaScript, Visual SourceSafe, Windows XP, IIS, MS SQL Server 2000 and Infragistic Controls.\n\n\n2. SugaeTech Solutions, Hyderabad, India\nDuration\n         \n\n September 2005- December 2005 \nClient\n              \n\nMEDNET Solutions, USA\n                                                               \nRole\n                \n\nDotNet Developer\nProject\n                        \n\nPatient Demographic and Allergy Survey\n\n\n\n\nThis product involves developing web application for the Asthma Allergy Center in USA. This Application is for Online ?Patient Demographic and Allergy Survey?. Entry \n\nfor New patients and on going patient can view their ?A/C Activity, Statements, Appointments, and Medications and Allergy Shot history. Patients can select their providers by selecting state and practices. Patients can send the messages to the providers in non-emergency conditions.\nResponsibilities\n\n\nExtensively worked with ASP.NET, ADO.NET, C#.NET,\n\nSQL Server.\n\n\n\nWorked on User Registration, Visitor Demographic Details Screens\n\n\nWorked on Patient Allergy Survey screens.\n\n\nWorked on A/C Activity,Appointments,Allergy Shot History Screens.\n\n\nWorked on Presentation, Data Access and\n\nBusiness Logic layers of the application.\n\n\nUsed \nDataset\n\nDataTable\n\nDataAdapter\n\nDataReader\n and other \nADO.NET\n connectivity controls .\n\n\nCreated Stored Procedures for accessing and updating data.\n\n\nUsed CSS for look and feel approach for Web pages.\n\n\nEnvironment:\n C#.NET, ADO.Net, \nASP.Net\n, JavaScript,Visual SourceSafe, Windows XP/NT and MS SQL Server 2000\n\n3. SugaeTech Solutions, Hyderabad, India\nDuration\n                     \n\n July 2005 - September 2005\nClient\n                          \n\nMEDNET Solutions, USA\n                                                               \nRole\n                            \n\nDotNet Developer\nProject\n                                    \n\n Phone Tracking System\n\nThis is a health care product involves developing web application for all the branches of \nDoctor?s Office in USA\n\nto manage their Daily appointments, billing System and the \nMedication to the Patients. The functionality of the PTS is to facilitate the providers and\n\nthe staff of a hospital to keep track of Phone calls / messages received during their \nabsence or unavailability and the subsequent response to those messages.\nResponsibilities\n\n\nExtensively worked with ASP.NET, ADO.NET, C#.NET,\n\nSQL Server.\n\n\n\nWorked on Managing Appointments, Received Messages,Maintain Messages List screens.\n\n\nWorked on Medication Entry, Billing System screens.\n\n\nWorked on Presentation, Data Access and\n\nBusiness Logic layers of the application.\n\n\nUsed \nDataset\n\nDataTable\n\nDataAdapter\n\nDataReader\n and other \nADO.NET\n connectivity controls .\n\n\nCreated Stored Procedures for accessing and updating data.\n\n\nUsed CSS for look and feel approach for Web pages.\n\nEnvironment:\n C#.NET, ADO.Net, \nASP.Net\n, JavaScript, Visual SourceSafe, Windows XP and MS SQL Server 2000\n\n\n4. SugaeTech Solutions, Hyderabad, India\nDuration\n         \n\n May 2005 - July 2005\nClient\n              \n\n MEDNET Solutions, USA\n                                                              \nRole\n                \n\n DotNet Developer\nProject\n                        \n\nClient Activity Tracking System\n\nThe objective of this project is to facilitate the staff of an Adult day care facility to keep track of their client?s activities and to record their involvement in those activities. The CAT is being designed to provide an interface for the personnel working at such a facility to have a user friendly and paperless tracking system for measuring the ?Client Participation Levels? and to generate reports for such Client Activities\nResponsibilities\n\n\nExtensively worked with ASP.NET, ADO.NET, C#.NET,\n\nMySQL,Pocket PC 2003,Mobile Web Forms.\n\n\n\nWorked on Maintaining Client Information and Managing User Information screens,Updating Client details screens..\n\n\nWorked on Daily Client Activity,Client Attendance record,Client Activity History Screens.\n\n\nWorked on Presentation, Data Access and\n\nBusiness Logic layers of the application.\n\n\nUsed \nDataset\n\nDataTable\n\nDataAdapter\n\nDataReader\n and other \nADO.NET\n connectivity controls .\n\n\nCreated Stored Procedures for accessing and updating data.\n\n\nUsed CSS for look and feel approach for Web pages.\n\nEnvironment:\n C#.NET, ADO.Net, \nASP.Net\n, JavaScript, Mobile Web Forms, Visual SourceSafe, Windows XP, Pocket PC 2003 and MSSQL\n\n\n5. RAM Informatics Ltd., Hyderabad, India.\nDuration\n                     \n\n December 2003 ? April 2005\nRole\n                            \n\n DotNet Developer\nProject\n            \n           \n             \n\n\nCentral Silk Board \n\nThis project involves developing web application for the CSB to maintain a centralized data for their quarterly production program at different CSB offices across the country. CSB is a premier organization for overall development of sericulture and silk industry.\nResponsibilities\n\n\nExtensively worked with ASP.NET, ADO.NET, VB.NET,\n\nSQL Server 2000.\n\n\n\nWorked on User Login screen.\n\n\nDeveloped ForgetPassword, User Registration, Change Password screens.\n\n\nWorked on Password Encryption and Automatic Password generation.\n\n\n\n\n\nWorked on the screens which gives the details of the Products available, products distributed.\n\n\nWorked on entriy screens like registration of users and many other.\n\n\nWorked on Presentation, Data Access and\n\nBusiness Logic layers of the application.\n\n\nUsed \nDataset\n\nDataTable\n\nDataAdapter\n\nDataReader\n and other \nADO.NET\n connectivity controls .\n\n\nCreated Stored Procedures for accessing and updating data.\n\n\nUsed CSS for look and feel approach for Web pages.\n\nEnvironment:\n VB.NET, ADO.NET, \nASP.Net\n, JavaScript, Visual SourceSafe and MS SQL Server 2000\n\n      ','Tech Mahindra ',1,NULL,'2007-10-15',NULL,'2007-10-15','2010-06-08 12:13:25','2010-06-08',12,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(49,'Sasikanth Varma',NULL,NULL,'Hyderabad','nagulapalli1256@gmail.com',NULL,NULL,'0','9966993687','0',NULL,'0','2008-04-13',7,19,'2010-06-08 12:13:25',12,'0',NULL,'200710/15/ATT7993.html','200710/15/DOC55883.doc','Sasikanth\nSasikanth Varma\nE-mail: nagulapalli1256@gmail.com\nPhone:\n 9966993687\n\n\nProfessional Summary\n         \n\n2+ years of experience in diversified fields of Application Software Development in Client-Server Environment and 3-tier architecture which includes Development, Documentation, Testing and Bug Fixing.\n\nHaving working knowledge in Struts 1.2\nExposure to OOAD concepts.\nTrained on Documentum 5.3 by Wipro Technologies.\nExposure to Telecom Domain.\n\nExperience\nWorking as a Software Engineer for \nSatyam Computer Services, \nHyderabad\n from \nSep 2007\n to till date.\nWorked as a Project Engineer for \nWipro Technologies, \nBangalore\n from\nOct 2005 \nto \nAug 2007.\n\nEducational Qualification\nMasters of Computer Science\n\nfrom \nAndhra\nUniversity\n in 2003 with an aggregate of \n71%\n\nBachelor of Computer Science from \nAndhra\nUniversity\n in 2000 with an aggregate of \n63%\n\n\n\nTechnical Skills\n\n\nOperating Systems \n\nWindows 2000/ NT/ XP, Unix, Solaris\nDatabases\n\nOracle8i and MySQL4.1\nProgramming Languages\n\n\nJava 2, C and C++\nWeb Technologies \n           \n\nServlets, JSP, Struts1.1, Spring 1.2.6\nDistributed Technologies\n\nRMI, EJB\nServers\n                              \n\nBEA WebLogic 8.1, Tomcat 4.1.29\nTools / IDE?s\n\n\nEclipse3.0, \nWinCVS 2.0, Ant 1.2, Apache Forrest 0.7\nScripting Language\n\nHTML, XML, and JavaScript\nJ2EE Services \n\nJDBC, JNDI.\n\n\nProject?s Details\n\n\n\n#4.\n            \nTitle\n              \n     \n: News&Sports\n           \nClient\n           \n      \n\n\nHutchison3G, \nUK\n\n\n     \n     \nDuration\n      \n      \n\n\nFeb 2007 to till Date\n          \n\nTeam Size\n    \n      \n\n\n\n         \n\n\nRole\n               \n    \n\n\nDeveloper\n        \nSoftware/Tools\n   \n\n\nServlets, JSP, Struts, Spring, SDF, Volantis,Apache Forrest 0.7, Eclipse3.0, log4j, Ant.1.6.0, Jcache, WinCVS, StarTeam, Unix, \nProxomitron.\n         \nEnvironment\n      \n\nSun solaris, Unix PDE Environment\n       \n  \n   \nServer\n              \n\n\n\nBEA WebLogic 8.1\n            \nDescription\n     \n   \n\nThe News, Weather product provides an Internet enabled application that will allow H3G customers to browse for the latest News, and a wide range of weather forecasts. News provides \nRegional\n\nUK\n National, International and Funny News. It will provide links to the Sports and Personal Financial Services products. On the other side, Weather provides atmospheric and environmental forecasts for every place in the \nUK\n, whether it is a city, town, postcode or region\n\n\n            \n#3.\n            \nTitle\n              \n     \n: Dynamic Image Generator-DIG\n           \nClient\n           \n      \n\n\nHutchison3G, \nUK\n\n\n     \n     \nDuration\n      \n      \n\n\nOct\n 2006 to till Date\n          \n\nTeam Size\n    \n      \n\n\n\n          \n\nRole\n               \n    \n\n\nInvolved in development/enhancements and maintenance of \n                                       \n   \nthe application.\n        \nSoftware/Tools\n   \n\n\nServlets, JSP, Struts, SDF, JMS,Volantis,Apache Forrest 0.7, Eclipse3.0, log4j, Ant.1.6.0, StarTeam, Unix, \nProxomitron.\n         \nEnvironment\n      \n\nSun solaris, Unix PDE Environment\n        \n\n   \nServer\n              \n\n\n\nBEA WebLogic 8.1\n            \nDescription\n        \n\nDIG (Dynamic Image Generator) is a java library (.jar file) that generates images for all \nmobile\n devices served by 3. It provides the user with the capabilities to describe images in an XML vocabulary that is then parsed into a DIG Object Model then rendered to the appropriate image file type by the DIG Renderer. DIG has the ability to create static as well as dynamic images using canvas XML and data files. The DIG feature set includes support for Image Manipulation including geometric manipulation (scaling, cropping, rotating), Rich Font and Text Handling, Shapes, Transparency and Antialiasing.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n#2.\n            \nTitle\n              \n     \n\nFAPL ( Football Application)\n           \nClient\n           \n      \n\n\nHutchison3G, \nUK\n\n\n     \n     \nDuration\n      \n      \n\n\nApr\n 2006 to Sep 2006\n          \n\nTeam Size\n    \n      \n\n\n\nRole\n               \n: Worked as a 4th line support engineer for this product. The\n     \nresponsibilities of the 4th line support engineer involves :\n\n        \nAccepting trouble tickets, Analyzing logs, providing solution with in given time, making releases, follow SIT and maintaining the code & documents updated in CVS.\n\n        \nPreparing Root cause analysis reports.\n\n        \n?Answering any queries related to FAPL.\n\n        \nUpdating SMTD (System maintenance technical document), which gives the overview of a product for newcomers.\n\n        \nSoftware/Tools\n   \n\n\nJava 1.4, JSP, Struts, SDF, Volantis, Eclipse3.1, log4j, Ant.1.6.0, StarTeam, UNIX, \nProxomitron.\n         \nEnvironment\n      \n\nSun solaris, Unix PDE Environment\n         \n   \nServer\n              \n\n\n\nBEA WebLogic 8.1\n            \nDescription\n     \n: Football is a product that is developed in house of Hutchison3G. It is designed to render all the football content to SDF (Service Delivery Framework) in the Hutchison3G mark up. This product manages to render all the media and image assets related to Football matches to the mobile end user. FAPL product will maintain its own cashing implementation to serve the content fast. So the product first searches the data in cache and then if data not available it looks into the database to serve the contest. Every product in H3G uses the LAM (live asset management) database as well as SsDF (provides the mobile specific content to the end User). The product interacts also with the DIG image server to get the dynamic images..\n\n#1.\n            \nTitle\n              \n     \n\nLive Streaming\n           \nClient\n           \n      \n\n\nHutchison3G, \nUK\n\n\n     \n     \nDuration\n      \n      \n\n\nNov 2005 to Mar 2006\n          \n\nTeam Size\n    \n      \n\n\n\n          \n\nRole\n               \n    \n\n\nInvolved in development/enhancements and maintenance of \n                                       \n   \nthe application.\n        \nSoftware/Tools\n   \n\n\nServlets, JSP, Struts, SDF, Volantis, Eclipse3.1, log4j, Ant.1.6.0, StarTeam, UNIX, \nProxomitron.\n         \nEnvironment\n      \n\nSun solaris, Unix PDE Environment\n         \n   \nServer\n              \n\n\n\nBEA WebLogic 8.1\n            \nDescription\n     \n\nStreaming is the continuous delivery of media content to the end users? devices. When a customer clicks a link for any live event, the media is streamed real-time and delivered within the handset?s available bandwidth. Live streaming enables users to view the content within a short start-up delay while the handset starts to receive the data. From the user perspective, streaming reduces the wait time required to view content, making it a more immediate and enjoyable experience.\n\n\nPersonal Details\n            \nFathers Name\n               \n\n    \nN.MadhavaRao.\n            \nDate of Birth\n                 \n\n     \n17\nth\n September 1978\n            \nSex\n                              \n\n     \nMale\n            \nMaterial Status\n             \n\n     \nSingle\n            \nLanguages Known\n        \n\n     \nEnglish, Hindi and Telugu.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n(N.SasiKanth)','Satyam Computer Services',1,NULL,'2007-10-15',NULL,'2007-10-15','2010-06-08 12:13:25','2010-06-08',12,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(50,'Shibani P',NULL,NULL,'Bangalore','dhal98756@gmail.com','shibani.p.dhal@gmail.com','996115645','0','91 9986115645','0',NULL,'0','2008-01-12',7,18,'2010-06-08 12:13:25',12,'0',NULL,'200710/15/ATT7992.html','200710/15/DOC55884.doc','CURRICULUM VITAE\n\n                          \n\n\nShibani P\n                                                     \n     \n\nEmail: dhal98756@gmail.com\n                                            \n                                                              \nMobile\n: + 91- 9986115645\n\n\n\n\nExperience Summary\n\n\n\n         \n\n .3 years \nof hands in experience in Java/J2EE.\n\n         \nSound knowledge on Core Java, J2EE Web Server technologies like Servlet 2.4, JSP 2.0, JDBC, JNDI.\n\n         \nExperience in \nJakarta\n Open Source Framework Struts 1.1 \n\n         \nGood exposure to client side technologies like HTML and JavaScript.\n\n         \nKnowledge on Oracle database (procedure, functions).\n\n         \nKnowledge of design patterns like Front Controller, Application Controller, MVC, Data Access Object, and Composite View.\n\n         \nExperience in Weblogic 8.1 application server.\n\n         \nExperience in Eclipse 3.1 IDE.\n\nStrengths\n\n\n          \nGood Domain knowledge of Trade and Finance, Banking and Logistics.\n\n          \nA fast learner with a positive attitude and flair for innovative ideas and ability to meet tight deadlines and work under pressure.\n\n          \nEnjoy new challenges & willing to take on extra responsibilities to get the work done. \n\n          \nAbility to grasp new technology and tools quickly.\n\nProject Synopsis\n\n\n          \nLC Factoring (Core Java, Servlets, JSP, Struts,JDBC, HTML,Java Script, EJB)\n\n          \nSupply Chain Management (Core Java, Servlets, JSP, Struts, JDBC,HTML, Java Script)\n\n          \nCourier Document Tracking \n(Core Java, Servlets, JSP,JDBC, HTML, Java Script)\n\n\nCareer Objective\n\n                    \nTo be part of an esteemed organization, share my technical knowledge in providing creative\n\nsolutions for the advancement of the organization and grow in hand with the organization.\n\n\nWork Experience\n\n             \n\nWorking with \nQuad Scope Solutions\n\nBangalore\n as a \nSoftware Engineer\n since July 2005\n\nto till date\n\n\n\nEducational Qualification\n\n          \nM.Sc.\n in computer science in the year 2005.\n\n          \nB.Sc. in Computer Science in the year 2003. \n\n         \n\n10+2 in the year of 2000.\n          \nMatriculation in the year of 1998.\n\nSkill Summary\n\n\n   \nLanguages\n         \n             \n\n      \n\nCore Java, Advance Java, C, C++, UNIX\n\n\nWeb Technologies\n          \n\n       \nServlets, JSP, JDBC, JNDI, XML\n   \nFramework\n                       \n\n       \nStruts 1.1\n         \nApplication Server\n          \n\n\n     \n\n\nBEA Weblogic 7.0/8.0\nWeb Server\n                    \n  \n\n       \nApache-Tomcat 4.0/5.\n         \nClient Side Technology \n\n\n       \nHTML, JavaScript.\n         \nRDBMS\n     \n            \n             \n\n\n       \nOracle 9i, MS SQL Server 2000, MS Access\n         \nTesting Tools\n                    \n\n       \nJUnit\n         \n       \n  \nOperating System\n          \n  \n\n       \nWindows 95/98/00/XP. \n         \nTools\n       \n                          \n\n       \nMy Eclipse 3.1, JBuilder, and EditPlus\n                         \nProject Details\n   \nOrganization:\nQuad Scope Solutions\n\n     \n1. Project Title\n         \nLC Factoring\n   \nDomain\n               \nTrade and Finance\n   \nModule\n               \nAdministration\n   \nTeam Size\n           \n14\n   \nTechnologies\n      \nCore Java, J2EE, Servlets, JSP, JDBC, JavaScript, EJB.\n   \nDatabase\n           \nOracle 8i\n   \nIDE\n                      \nEclipse 3.1\n   \nFramework\n         \nStruts 1.1\n   \nServer\n                 \nWeblogic 8.1\n   \nDuration\n             \nOct 2006 ? Till Date\n   \nDescription:\n                  \n\n   \n\nLC Factoring\n is a web-enabled application, which automates the process of LC Factoring in a bank. LC is mortgaged by the exporter. The module, \nAdministration\n, which I am currently working in, can add new plans to the existing plans and also can modify the existing plans. This module provides user interface for the administrator for configuring all the new master tables. Also the administrator maintains the dunning process.\n\n                  \n                  \n                  \n\n                  \nThis module is implemented using struts framework and following MVC design pattern. View part consists of JSPs where data is captured, Model part consists of Java Beans and Controller part consists of Action Servlets.\n\n\nRoles and Responsibilities:\n\n         \nInvolved in coding JSP pages, ActionForms, Actions and Model Components.\n\n         \nInvolved in client-side validation using JavaScript.\n\n         \nUnit testing of my module using JUnit.\n\n\n\n\n\n     \n2. P\nroject \nTitle\n         \nSCM\n   \nDomain\n               \nLogistics\n   \nModule\n               \nProcurement\n   \nTeam Size\n           \n18\n   \nTechnologies\n      \nCore Java, J2EE, Servlets, JSP, JDBC, JavaScript, EJB.\n   \nDatabase\n           \nOracle 8i\n   \nIDE\n                      \nEclipse 3.1\n   \nFramework\n         \nStruts 1.1\n   \nServer\n                 \nWeblogic 8.1\n   \nDuration\n             \nFeb 2006 ? Sep 2006\n   \nDescription:\n         \n         \n\n   \nSCM\nis a web-enabled application, which \nmanages the movement of goods into an organization from the vendors. The module which I worked on this application\n-Procurement\n deals with the procurement department which implements seven major functionalities, Requisition for Quote(RFQ), Quote, Vendor Selection, Purchase Order Processing, Reciept Confirmation, Invoice Verification and Transport Planning.\n           \n                  \n\nRFQ takes all the internal requests from within the various departments of the company, after which Quote is being sent by the vendors based on which the Vendor Selection is done. After which Purchase Order is Processed, Reciept is Confirmed, Invoice Verification is done and Transport Planning is done as well.\n           \n       \nThis module is implemented using Struts Framework \nand following MVC design pattern. View part consists of JSPs where data is captured, Model part consists of Java Beans and Controller part consists of Action Servlets.\n\n\nRoles and Responsibilities:\n\n         \nInvolved in coding JSP pages, ActionForms, Actions and Model Components.\n\n         \nInvolved in client-side validation using JavaScript.\n\n         \nUnit testing of my module using JUnit.\n\n     \n\n\nProject\n\nTitle\n         \nCourier Document Tracking (CDT) \n   \nTeam Size\n           \n\n   \nTechnologies\n      \nCore Java, J2EE, Servlets, JSP, JDBC, HTML, JavaScript\n   \nDatabase\n           \nOracle 8i\n   \nIDE\n                      \nEclipse 3.1\n   \nServer\n                 \nWeblogic 8.1\n   \nDuration\n             \nAugust 2005 ? January 2006\n   \n\n\nDescription:\n   \n       \n  \n\n  \nThis is a web application using J2EE technologies, where a courier company can track the documents at different stages during the delivery process. The process starts at the booking agents place, where the document or parcel is booked and a docket number is generated at that time. From then on, the docket number is used as the key, to track the document or parcel. The data is entered at each stage of the courier delivery process. The facility is given for agents and customers to check the status of their documents. Different views are provided to different types of users.\n\n\nRoles and Responsibilities:\n\n         \nInvolved in designing Jsp pages and Servlet programs.\n\n         \nInvolved in client side validation using JavaScript\n\n         \nInvolved in database connectivity.\nPersonal Details\nName\n              \n\n           \nShibani Prasad Dhal\nDate of Birth\n    \n\n           \n29-09-1983\nGender\n            \n\n           \nMale\nMarital Status\n   \n\n           \nUnmarried\nNationality\n       \n\n           \nIndian\nPassport No.\n    \n\n           \nG0594866\nAddress\n            \n\n           \n#467 3\nrd\nMain\n, 1\nst\n B-Cross,\n                                    \nMathikere, Bangalore-54.\nContact No.\n    \n\n           \n996115645\nEmail\n               \n\n           \nshibani.p.dhal@gmail.com','Quad Scope Solutions',1,NULL,'2007-10-15',NULL,'2007-10-15','2010-06-08 12:13:25','2010-06-08',12,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(51,'Shiva Raman',NULL,NULL,NULL,'shiv149863@yahoo.com',NULL,NULL,'0','9900191445','0',NULL,'0','2007-02-28',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-08 12:13:25',12,'0',NULL,'200710/15/ATT7991.html','200710/15/DOC55885.doc','YODLEE INFOTECH PRIVATE LIMITED\nSHIVA RAMAN\nSoftware Engineer\nYODLEE INFOTECH PVT LTD, \nBangalore\nEmail: shiv149863@yahoo.com\nMobile: \n+91\n 9900191445\n\n\nCareer \nObjective\n\nShort term: Desire a position where I can leverage on my technical skills and can be part of a team that works in the latest technologies.\nLong term: To head the IT solutions department of a global IT company.\n\nProfessional \nSummary\n\nAbout 2 years of experience in the software development industry, working on Web based Business and Financial Applications and Knowledge Management solutions.\n\n\nEDUCATION\n\n\n         \n2000-2004 BE in Computers Science Engineering from PDA College of Engineering, \nGulbarga\n, affiliated to VTU, \nBelgaum\n with Distinction (72%).\n\n         \n1998 ? 2000 PUC with an aggregate of 73% with Physics, Chemistry, Biology and Mathematics as the main subjects.\n\n         \n1998 SSLC with first Class (74%)\n\n\nTECHNICAL SKILL SETS\n   \n\nPlatforms\n                                  \n\nWindows 98/2000 professional, LINUX, UNIX\nProgramming Languages\n           \n\nC, C++, Core JAVA\nTechnologies\n                             \n\nJ2EE (JSP, Servlets), XML, HTML\nData Base\n                                \n\nOracle 9i\nGraphical User Interface Tools\n\n\nJava AWT, Swings, Ms FrontPage 2000.\nFinancial Domain Technologies\n\n\nFinancial Data Mining from Web sites and servers using web crawler (program which navigates to web sites and gathers relevant information) and online financial data interchange technologies like XML, OFX, and HTML.\n\n\nYODLEE INFOTECH PRIVATE LIMITED\nPeriod July 2005 till Date\nDesignation Software Engineer \n\nYodlee helps FSPs fully leverage the online channel to drive more satisfying and profitable customer relationships via a suite of solutions that automate and simplify consumers\' financial chores while generating new revenue opportunities for FSPs.\n\nUnlike other financial services, Yodlee\'s solutions are powered by a patented technology - the Yodlee Data Engine - that communicates in real-time with thousands of financial sources to power new and existing applications, such as bill pay, personal financial management (PFM), advisor solutions, etc.\n\nProject Currently Working On\n1) Yodlee?s FT Direct\nClient: Swiss One, Net teller, \nWestern Union\n\nYodlee ?FT Direct?or ?Funds Transfer Direct? is Yodlee?s funds transfer by proxy functionality that allows a customer to effect funds transfers to/from financial institutions where the customer maintains accounts without directly logging into the financial institution sites, via a user interface that sits in front of and normalizes the customer?s experience across the online sites where the customer has funds transfer privileges. As a proxy service, FT Direct interfaces with the functionality of the customer\'s financial institution and is subject to the controls, risk management and limit policies of the customer\'s financial institution.\n\nProject Worked On\n1) Yodlee?s Instant Account Verification\nClient: Pay Pal, E*Trade, Scottrade, Prosper, Swiss One.\nYodlee Account Verification verifies your customers\' and prospects\' external accounts faster and with lower risk than using traditional methods. With 75% coverage for instant account verification, customers are set up for new accounts or funds transfers in seconds, rather than two to three days. The combination of broad instant account verification coverage plus the challenge deposit method means higher conversion rates and higher balances.\nYodlee Account Verification can be seamlessly integrated into your current applications such as funds transfer, bill pay, and account opening.\n\n2) Yodlee?s OnCenter Suite\nClient: Bank Of \nAmerica\nYodlee\'s OnCenter suite is a Personal Finance solution for the masses that automates, simplifies and enhances key PFM tasks while providing unique, value-added capabilities\nMy Role\nDesign and Implementation of Agents (Programs/Web Crawlers) using JAVA, COM and Yodlee?s SDK to navigate and scrape customer relevant financial information from the financial institution sites. Also, understand the quality of Data scraped from these sites by querying databases and testing the agents and improve the quality of data by using various web page data mining techniques. It also includes learning and implementing of Financial Institution Information Exchange protocols like OFX, IFX, XML, and HTML.\n\n3) Yodlee?s BillPay Account Accelerator\nClient: Bank Of America, Wachovia Bank\nYodlee BillPay Account Accelerator Service is an essential component for any financial institution. It minimizes the effort required for a consumer to move bill pay services from one financial institution to another. By providing a fully automated, easy-to-integrate online solution, Yodlee BillPay Account Accelerator enables financial institutions to attract new bill pay users and accelerate profitability.\n\n4) Yodlee?s Bill Manager\nClient: \nAmerica\n On-line (AOL)\nYodlee\'s \nMoney Direct enables Scottrade customers to make online ACH deposits into their Scottrade account from nearly any external bank account. Yodlee supports both challenge deposits and instant account verification methods to authenticate users and ensure secure money movement between financial accounts.\n\n5) Yodlee?s Money Direct - Online Funds Transfer\nClient: Scottrade\nA Personal Financial Management product, which ?presents? the user with the bills (for example: telephone bills, insurance bills, credit card statements etc.), which are due at the end of a billing cycle (usually a month). In other words, this product aggregates all the bills obtained from web sites for a given user and presents it in a single page.\n\n6) Yodlee?s AdvisorView\nClient: Bank Of \nAmerica\nYodlee\'s AdvisorView is the industry\'s first aggregation-enabled wealth management data consolidation solution. AdvisorView uniquely provides advisors with a collaborative environment to import client-permissioned account data held at any financial institution. Powered by Yodlee\'s industry leading technology, AdvisorView bundles a real-time, consolidated view of clients\' financial lives with the tools and export facilities necessary to track all account activity and provide comprehensive, timely investment advice.\n\n\nPersonality Traits \n\n         \nSincere and Efficient with good communication skill\n\n         \nGood team working capabilities and Strong technical knowledge\n\n         \nQuick learning abilities\n\nPERSONAL DETAILS\n\nPermanent Address:\n                  \nBlock - 3, G ? 4, Srivastava Block\n                                                \nPolice Colony, Gulbarga ? 585105,\n                                                \nKarnataka, INDIA\n\nPassport:\n                                  \nF7234455\n\nDate of Birth:\n                            \n20/12/1982',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-15',NULL,'2007-10-15','2010-06-08 12:13:25','2010-06-08',12,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(52,'Someswara Rao Maradani',NULL,NULL,'Hyderabad ','somu789456@rediffmail.com',NULL,NULL,'0','9866898016','0',NULL,'0','2008-08-14',7,19,'2010-06-08 12:13:25',10,'0',NULL,'200710/15/ATT7990.html','200710/15/DOC55886.doc','someswara rao maradani\nSomeswara M.\n\nEmail:\n\nsomu789456@rediffmail.com\nMobile\n\n\n91\n\n9866898016\n\nPROFESSIONAL SUMMARY\n\n       \n\n+ years\n of professional experience in the IT industry\n\n       \nCapability to handle Projects (Development & Implementation).\n\n       \nA motivated team player with excellent communication skills.\n\n       \nWorked on web-based applications and development environments including Java, JSP, Servlets, JDBC, Java Beans, HTML and Java Script.\n\n       \nA responsible software developer, fast learner, good technical abilities and skills. \nTECHNICAL SKILLS\n\nOperating Systems\nWindows 9X/2000, MS-DOS\nLanguages\n                        \nJava , C++, C\n, DBUnit\nInternet\n Technologies\nWeblogic Portal, \nHtml, Java Script\nJ2EE Technologies\nJDBC, Servlets, JSP, EJB, Struts\nDatabases\nOracle 8i, \nDB2\n, SQL Server 7\nWeb/App Servers\nWeblogic 8.1,\n WebSphere 6.0, T\nomcat 5.1\nDevelopment Tools \nIBM Rational Application Developer\n\n Eclipse, \nNet Beans, J\nRun Studio, Jcreator\n\nWORK EXPERIENCE \nWorking as Senior Software Engineer at \nSatyam Computer Services Ltd,\nHyderabad\n from Feb 2006 to till date.\nWorked as \nSoftware\n Engineer at \nParadigm InfoTech\n (ISO 9001-2000\n Certified Company)\n\nSomaji Guda\n\nHyderabad\n from\n\nJuly 2003 to Feb 2006\n\n It is an offshore development center of Paradigm InfoTech Inc., \nUSA\n\n\nEDUCATION\n\n         \nMCA\n\nrom \nNagarjuna\nUniversity\n in 2003 with 70%.\nPROJECTS SUMMARY\n#1 HR Wave-1 Applications\nClient: Pfizer Japan Inc.\nTeam size: 3\nAs the world?s leading research-based pharmaceutical company, Pfizer discovers, develops, manufactures, and markets leading prescription medicines for humans and animals and many of the world\'s best-known consumer healthcare brands.\nPfizer has been doing business in \nJapan\n for more than 50 years and now provides drugs that cover a wide range of disease categories, including cardiovascular system, central nervous system, infections, urology, ophthalmology, cancer and endocrinology in this important market.\nHR Wave-1 Applications support includes below four applications\n\n         \neAIP\n(e-Annual Incentive Plan) application provides automated\n\nmechanism to\n\ndetermine the employee?s annual incentive payable\n\n         \n360 Degree Feedback\n is a web based tool used to evaluate the managers by his Colleagues, Sub-ordinates and Superiors and generates the feedback for each evaluatee.\n\n         \nCBE\n is for non-managers. Appraisee login to the system gives his self evaluation and after that appraisers login to the system and they recommend for the promotion or demotion or continue in same rank for \n\nppraisee.\n\n         \nHR Portal\n is a Portal site for HR Pfizer.\n\nIt contains all the HR information and links any employee needs to access. HR Portal is used to view the web contents displayed in its port-lets.\nResponsibilities\n\nSupport and Maintenance of four applications in production\nEnvironment\n\nASP, JSP, Oracle 9i, Weblogic Portal, Visual Studio\n\n#2 Six Sigma Applications\nClient: Caterpillar \nUSA\nTeam size: 3\nCaterpillar is the world\'s largest manufacturer of construction and mining equipment, diesel and natural gas engines and industrial gas turbines. As one of the fortune 500 companies, Caterpillar and its dealers sell products in nearly 200 countries and sponsor events that promote the company\'s growth oriented high-tech strategy.\nThe Six Sigma Green Belt Test/Certification Process (SSGBTC) is valuable to the corporation in that it automates most of the testing, approval and certification process.\nThe 6 Sigma test/certification process improvements will track the training, testing, and the distribution of training certificates and belts.\n\nThe certification process will gather financial information from FRS to approve the green belt or black belt certificate.\n\nA report will be generated to help black belts and administrators track the training/certification effort.\n The resulting system will be supportable by Global IT Solutions.\n\nResponsibilities\n\n\nxplore the Framework given by client\n\nWriting DBUnit test cases\n\nCoding Java\n\nclasses in DAO layer with DB2 queries\n\ntesting each\n\nfunctional\n scenario\nwith DBunit test cases.\nEnvironment\n\nJava, HTML, JSP, DBUnit\n, DB2, IBM RAD, WebSphere 6.0, TUF framework\n\n#3\n\nCrecon Reporting Systems\nClient: \nHitachi\n Inspharma, \nOsaka\n\nJapan\nTeam size: 4\nCrecon Consulting is a market data research company, which offers market research services corresponding to Pharmaceutical industry. Distribution Promotion Department\'s Dealer Group of Takeda Pharmaceutical Company used to buy market data research analysis report every year from Crecon, which it uses to set targets and improvement of sales. The info offered by Crecon includes sales of all prominent makers (not only Takeda\n\nPharma) and Dealers (not only TakedaPharma\'s Dealers) with respect to monthly sales, area wise sales, prefecture wise (state wise) sales, and countrywide sales.\nResponsibilities\n\nPreparation for Detailed Design Document\n\nPreparation for Unit Test cases Review document\n\nExplore the Framework given by the client\n\nCoding \nin Sumisho Frame work \nusing JAVA,\n\nHTML and JavaScript, Testing - unit testing\nand\n integration testing.\nEnvironment\n\nJava, HTML, JSP, JavaScript, \n\nExcel A\nPI\n\n iText\n\nAPI, Oracle 9i, Eclipse and OC4J \n\n\n\n eWDAC (\nEnterprise\n Web Data Access Control)\nClient: \nthe\n Jockey club technology services Inc. USA\nTeam size: 4\nEnterprise Web Data Access Control is a comprehensive system that enables to conduct regular audits that include nightly process to purge, load, transform and filter web logs. Create audit reports that show up the browser?s activities and handle the client threshold notifications. Apart from the audit and threshold activities the system will handle request exclusion based on the exclusion policies and the system is built with a real time request meter.\nResponsibilities\n\nDesigning and developing user interfaces using struts. Involved in coding of Nightly Process. Testing of application.\nEnvironment\n\nJava, JSP, Struts, Sybase, IntelliJ, Tomcat, Visual SourceSafe, Java Script.\n\n\n\n\nProduct Configuration Tracking (eChecklist)\nClient\n\nGE Transportation Systems, \nUSA\nTeam size: \n\nProduct Configuration Tool is used to track the birth, production and shipment of configured product to designated customers.\n\nThis application includes the tracking of defective product, the repair of defective returned material, and the sales order generation of RMA. The application also allows the administrator to enable different roles to different operators of the application.\nResponsibilities\n\nCoding Java Programs & JSPs Maintenance. Writing Stored procedures in Oracle 8i. Testing the application.\nEnvironment\n\nJava, Servlets, JSP1.1, PL/SQL, HTML, JavaScript, Oracle 8i, Windows 2000, Visual Interdev, Visual SourceSafe, Toad, Weblogic\n\n\n\n eMaterial Shortage Tracking\nClient:\n\nGE Transportation Systems, \nUSA\n\nTeam size: 2\nThis application is used to get an improved visibility of part shortages. This will help to identify and track shortages as well as provide information on the expected delivery date. It improves delivery, improves shortage-tracking time by 75%. It keeps track of the shortages, keeps track of the critical items which may or may not be short, will be able to request promises for short or critical items, include an explanation with any shortage request, make promises for requested items, promise a specific quantity, have promise information carry over from day to day until the job has been completed, store multiple profiles for each user that will each contain a combination of planner codes and critical parts to be tracked\n\nResponsibilities\n\nDesigning the tables required for this project. Developing modules like promising request, promising input, profile maintenance, planner/part maintenance. Writing Stored procedures in Oracle 8\n\n\nEnvironment\n\nJava, JSP, Java Beans, JavaScript, Weblogic, Oracle 8i\n\nVisual Interdev, Visual SourceSafe\n\n\n\n\n\n Part Lead Time Update\nClient: \nGE Transportation Systems, \nUSA\n\nTeam size: 2\nMaintaining accurate part lead-times is essential for GE in ensuring the necessary service levels and making sure that the supply base receives the time necessary to complete open orders. The GE Rail Global Services organization has implemented a web-based tool that will make the updating process simpler and faster. Suppliers and Buyers will get e-mail notifications when the information is posted into Supplier Extranet. Suppliers login with their username/password into Supplier Extranet within their allotted time period and update the lead times. Buyers will be registered in GESMP and will be provided with an account to approve the updated lead times. The registered buyer will get e-mail notification to approve the updated lead times. After the approval of lead times the updated information in the supplier extranet will be moved to source systems. The total cycle takes 6 weeks.\nResponsibilities\n\nInvolved in design, development and testing of server side components like jsps and java beans. Written stored procedures to fetch and store the appropriate data from supplier extranet database.\nEnvironment:\nJava, JSP, Java Beans, JavaScript, Weblogic, \nSQLSERVER.\n\n\n\n Multiple Systems\nClient:\n\nSAFE Operations Inc. \nColumbia\n\nUSA\n\nTeam size: 3\nSafe operations involved in \nmeasure and manage security, which they intend to become standard for information security. \nSafeops is Web-based security assessment product that allows information technology professionals with no information security expertise or limited expertise to determine the extent to which their local computing environment protects its information assets from computer systems and network and Internet security risks. The product presents excellent capabilities for administrators of the system to build their own security assessments. The product can be accessed remotely by means of a standard web browser.\nResponsibilities\n\nDeveloped individual menus like Supervisor Menu, Point Of Contact Menu, Analyst Menu, Assessor Menu and individual modules like User Setup, Module Setup, Group Setup and System Listing Setup using JSP, Java Script and HTML.\nEnvironment\n\nJava, JSP, Servlets, HTML, Java Script, MS-SQL Server, Windows2000.\n\nPersonal Profile:\nName\n                      \n\n        \nM.Someswara Rao\nGender\n          \n\n        \nMale\nDOB\n                       \n\n        \n15\nth\n June 1980\nMarital Status\n          \n\n        \nUnmarried\nLanguages Known\n     \n\n        \nEnglish, Hindi & Telugu','Satyam Computer Services Ltd',9,NULL,'2007-10-15',NULL,'2007-10-15','2010-06-08 12:13:25','2010-06-08',10,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,9,'0',NULL),(53,'Narasimha Rao',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL,'0',NULL,'0','2008-04-29',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-08 12:13:25',10,'0',NULL,'200710/15/ATT7989.html','200710/15/DOC55887.doc','Profile:\n\n\nProfile:\n\nSeeking a challenging career with a progressive organization which will utilize my skills, abilities, experience and education in web based application design, development and testing. Currently working for IBM India Pvt Ltd, \nBangalore\n as System Engineer.\n\n\nProfessional Summary:\n\n\n         \n2 years \nof IT experience encompassing a wide range of skill set, roles.\n\n         \nProficient in Object Oriented Programming using Java, J2EE and strong database skills.\n\n         \nExperienced in implementation of software applications with analysis, design, and development and testing.\n\n         \nGood communication skills, interpersonal skills, self-motivated, quick learner, team player\n\n\nExperience Summary:\n\n         \n2.1 years \nin \nIBM India Pvt. Ltd.\n\n(From \nAug 22, 2005\n to Till Date).\n\n         \nJoined IBM as a Fresher \nSkill Set: \n\n         \nTechnology\n\nCore Java, Java Beans, J2EE 1.4, J2EE 1.5 (Servlet, JSP), C, C++, HTML,\n\nXML, Websphere portal 5.1\n\n         \nDatabases :\n Oracle, DB2\n\n         \nWeb Frameworks: \nStruts, Struts Portal.\n\n         \nPersistence Mechanism:\n Hibernate,EJB\n\n         \nDevelopment IDE?s :\n WSAD 5.0, WSAD 5.1,RAD 6.0\n\n         \nOthers :\n JUnit, Log4j, CVS\n\n         \nConcepts:\n Operating Systems, DBMS Concepts, Object Oriented Concepts\n\nAwards:\n\n         \nReceived Gestner Award from IBM for the year 2006-2007.\n\n         \nReceived Many Appreciations from the Clients.\n\nEducation Summary:\n   \n\n         \nM.Tech\n in Power Electronics\n\nfrom \nJNTU\nUniversity\n\nyear of Post graduation \n2005 \n\n         \nConsistent Academic profile of 75% and above in 10\nth\n(CBSE)\n,12\nth\n,B.tech and M.tech.\n\nTrainings Attended:\n   \n\n         \nOne month in house training on Java technologies, J2EE, UNIX and RDBMS provided by IBM.\n\n         \nInternal training provided by IBM on web sphere application developer.\n\n         \nInternal training provided by AT&T on Client Application for AT&T.\n\n         \nInternal training provided by IBM on communication skills and interpersonal skills\n\n         \nInternal training provided by IBM on Struts, Hibernate, HTML and XML.\n\n\nIntroduction to the Client and Application:\n\nProject Name:\n       \nBRM (BRM-MNS Billing, BRM-GAMS API, BRM-GAMS WEB)\nClient\n\n                   \nAT&T \n\nBRM-MNS Billing\nMNS Billing is a web-based application which MNS users will input and manage customer-billing information in the Global Billing Platform (GBP). MNS Billing is part of the BRM suite of applications and is tightly coupled with GBP.\n\nBRM-GAMS API\nBussys API/GAMS API is a billing application used in the account setup process.\n\nThe main purpose of Bussys API is to supplement the legacy GAMS application.\n\nThe API provides a HTTP interface to other applications to perform account setup related tasks.\n\nThe applications that are currently using this API are CSMIP and USRPFR.\nBRM-GAMS WEB\nIn terms of functionality the GAMS Web application is currently a supplemental application to the mainframe GAMS application.\n   \nThe mainframe Global Account Management System (GAMS) is concerned mainly with account setup of Global accounts.\n   \nSince the GAMS Web application shares a similar architecture with the other applications in the Business Rules Management (BRM) suite of applications, namely MNS Billing and GAMS API, GAMS Web is considered part of BRM.\n\nResponsibilities:\n\n\n         \nPreparing the design document based on the requirements.\n\n         \nImplementation of the code by enhancing the code as per the requirements.\n\n         \nPreparing the system test plan, test execution plan.\n\n         \nTest data preparation and test execution.\n\n         \nDeveloping and Releasing the code.\n\n         \nProduction Deployment Support.\n\n         \nPost production Support and Maintenance Support.\n\n\nProject Summary:\n\nProject #1:\nProject name:\n       \nP8A11- Creation of new feeds to UB \nSize:\n                      \n2 Members (Web/Java technology) + 9 Members (Mainframe) \nRole:\n                     \nApplication Developer \nEnvironment:\n        \nJ2EE (Servlet, JSP), XML/DOM/Parsing, SQL?DB2, Struts, JUnit, Log4J, Hibernate,UNIX, Ant, CVS\nDuration:\n               \nApr 2007-Till Date.\n\nDescription:\n\nModify the logic in the BRM API to check the eBill exclusion criteria for new AVTS accounts.\n\nIf the account qualifies as eligible for eBill, the API will set the eBill indicator for this account.\n   \n                                                \nThe accounts setup via the BRM API which is eligible for eBill must be sent to BBGW just like any other account\n\nProject #2:\n\nProject name:\n       \nPA298-168e Business Case\nSize:\n                      \n2 Members (Web/Java technology) + 9 Members (Mainframe) \nRole:\n                     \nApplication Developer \nEnvironment:\n        \nJ2EE (Servlet, JSP), XML/DOM/Parsing, SQL?DB2, Struts, JUnit, Log4J, Hibernate, UNIX,Ant, CVS. \nDuration:\n                \nNov 2006- Feb 2007\n\nDescription:\n\nReceive mapping transactions from USRP-FR that will create new MCN/SOC/GRC to GAMS ID mappings or which will re-map an existing MCN/SOC/GRC to a different GAMS ID.\n\n\nProject #3:\n\nProject name:\n       \nPA242-UBB 10, 11 ? UBB CRs ? 203L\nSize:\n                      \n2 Members (Web/Java technology) + 9 Members (Mainframe) \nRole:\n                     \nApplication Developer \nEnvironment:\n        \nJ2EE (Servlet, JSP), XML/DOM/Parsing, SQL?DB2, Struts, JUnit, Log4J, Hibernate,UNIX,Ant, CVS. \nDuration:\n                \nAug 2006- Nov\n\n2006\n\nDescription:\nBRM will modify GAMS-API application so that in MapMcnGrcSocToOrganizationAccount request \nSOC value is optional for MNC/GRC/SOC to Charge-to Account mappings for the AVPN service and these values are stored in ORGMCN table instead of CHGMCN table.\n\nBRM needs to modify its mapping for the AVPN service to map the Organization Account to the MCN/GRC, and store the mapping information in ORGMCN table. Since this is the relationship being maintained for the AVPN service.\n\n\nBRM needs to change logic behind map request to populate ORGMCN for AVPN\nMigration program\nAll accounts with SOC blank in CHGMCN will be migrated to ORGMCN as AVPN customers.\n\nProject #4:\n\nProject name:\n       \nPA096-SOC issue for UBB\nSize:\n                      \n2 Members (Web/Java technology) + 9 Members (Mainframe) \nRole:\n                     \nApplication Developer \nEnvironment:\n        \nJ2EE (Servlet, JSP), XML/DOM/Parsing, SQL?DB2, Struts, JUnit, Log4J, Hibernate,UNIX, Ant, CVS. \nDuration:\n               \nMay 2006-Aug 2006\n\nDescription:\nBRM will modify GAMS-API application so that in McnGrcSocToOrganizationAccount request SOC value is optional for SOC to Charge-to Account mappings for the AVPN service.\n\nBRM will accept a new field called ?Service Option?.\n\nBRM will always expect AVPN as the value for the Service Option. BRM will change logic not to expect the SOC when the service option is ?AVPN?\n\nProject #5:\n\nProject name:\n       \nP7839-BRM\nSize:\n                      \n2 Members (Web/Java technology) + 9 Members (Mainframe) \nRole:\n                     \nApplication Developer \nEnvironment:\n        \nJ2EE (Servlet, JSP), XML/DOM/Parsing, SQL?DB2, Struts, JUnit, Log4J, Hibernate, UNIX,Ant, CVS. \nDuration:\n               \nFeb 2006-May 2006\n\nDescription:\nBRM will include the IP addresses in the Property file. It will also read the MCN/GRC/SOC from the upstream application and map these values to CHGACCT in the down stream Application. These values will be stored in the CHGMCN table.\n\n\nProject #6:\n\nProject name:\n       \nTest Simulator Tool.\nSize:\n                      \n3 Members (Web/Java technology) + 9 Members (Mainframe) \nRole:\n                     \nApplication Developer \nEnvironment:\n        \nJ2EE (Servlet, JSP), XML/DOM/Parsing, SQL?DB2, Struts, JUnit, Log4J, Hibernate, Ant, CVS. \nDuration:\n               \nOct 2005-Feb 2006\n\n\nDescription:\nThis is a Web based Portal. This Portal will provide many functions for the management of test data and environment relationships. The following operations can be performed.\nDisplay the test environment attributes for a project that match selection criteria entered by the user. Display a list of Accounts that match selection criteria entered by the user. Display a list of Sites that match selection criteria entered by the user. Display a list of MCN?s that match selection criteria entered by the user. Create a Project for Test Simulator,\n\nView or Update information for an existing Project.\n\nPersonal Details:\n\nFull Name\n                                 \n\n           \nSreekanth Dara\nFather?s Name\n                          \n\n\n         \nNarasimha Rao\nDate of Birth \n                            \n\n           \n10\nth\n Nov 1979\nGender\n                                     \n\n           \nMale.\nLanguages Known \n                   \n\n\n          \nEnglish, Hindi & Telugu.\nMarital Status \n                           \n\n\n          \nMarried.',NULL,9,NULL,'2007-10-15',NULL,'2007-10-15','2010-06-08 12:13:25','2010-06-08',10,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,9,'0',NULL),(54,'S.Sekar   ',NULL,NULL,NULL,'karrp@gmail.com',NULL,'258849 04562','0','09841920444','0',NULL,'0','2008-04-29',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-08 12:13:25',10,'0',NULL,'200710/15/ATT7988.html','200710/15/DOC55888.doc','s.sekar\n                                              \n54, 54\nth\n street, 10\nth\n sector,\n                                                            \n                                    \nKK Nagar west,\n                                                \n                                                \nchennai-600078.\nEmail: - \nkarrp@gmail.com\n\n                                            \nMobile No: 09841920444\n\nPROFESSIONAL SUMMARY:\n\n       \nHaving more than 2.0 year of experience in \nDevelopment\n and \nMaintenance\n of Client Server and n-Tier Architecture.\n\n       \nWorked extensively in \nJava, JSP, Servlets, Oracle and SQL\n\nServer2005.\n\n       \nCurrently working as a Software Engineer for \nTechnomind Ltd\n, Chennai.\n\nSKILL SET:\nOperating Systems\n         \n: Windows 9X/XP, Linux Fedora\nLanguages\n                     \n: Java, C++, C \nFront End Tools\n              \n: Visual Basic 6.0 with seagate crystal Report\nWeb Technology\n            \n: JSP, Servlets, Struts, \nAJAX\n, JavaScript \nDatabases\n                     \n: MS-SQL Server 2005, Oracle 10g, MS-Access\n\nACADEMIC QUALIFICATIONS:\nCourse\nName of the Institution\nYear of pass\nPercentage/Grade\nMCA\nGandhigram Rural Institute -Deemed University Dindigul -624302.\n2005\n8.22 CGPA\nB.Pharm\nP.P.M.M.College of Pharmacy \nTirunelveli.\n2000\n68.17\nHSC\nN.M.Higher\nSecondary School\n Elayiram pannai ?626201\n1996\n83.25\nS.S.L.C\nN.M.Higher\nSecondary School\n Elayiram pannai ?626201\n1994\n81.8\n\nEXPERIENCE:\nOrganization\nDesignation\nDuration \nTechnomind Ltd., Chennai.\nSoftware Engineer\n07/2006? Till Date\nLaunchPD\nSoftware Trainee\n06/2005 ? 07/2006\nNational Informatics Center, Chennai\nProject Trainee\n12/2004 ? 04/2005\nPROJECTS PROFILE:\n#1. \nProject Name : Electronics Medical Record System\nClient\nVijaya Health Centre\n\nRole\nTeam Member\nOrganization\nTechnomind.\nTeam Size\n\nEnvironment\nSoftware\nLanguages : \nJSP,HTML,DHTML,Javascript\nDatabase\n   \n\n\nMS-SQL Server2005\n\nPROJECT DESCRIPTION:\nThis system is used to reduce the task of maintaining the patient?s record in the hospitals.\nBy this system, we convert the Case sheet in to electronic format. We capture the Case sheet in image format by scanning the record. In the database we arranged the case sheet in ascending order according to the Patient?s discharging date.\n\nAs a team member, was \nresponsible\n for\n\n        \nAnalysis\n of the specifications provided by the clients.\n\n        \nCoding\n using HTML pages, Java Script validations and jsp?s.\n\n        \nTesting\n - unit testing & integration testing, preparing test cases and release notes.\n\n#2. \nProject Name : Surabhi\nClient\nAkshaya Agro Informatics Pvt Ltd\nRole\nTeam Member\nOrganization\nTechnomind\nTeam Size\n\nEnvironment\nSoftware\nLanguages : \n\nJSP, Javascript,DHTML, HTML,Linux\nDatabase\n   \n: PostgreSql\n\nPROJECT DESCRIPTION:\n                                                                                                               \nThe SURABHI project was developed for collecting and maintaining the data of the various \n\nAgricultural Commodities from various sources and giving rates to the public for selling or buying the Commodities with actual price .The clients are Mill Owner, Trader, Farmer, and Wholesaler etc. The commodities are Paddy, Rice, Pulses, Wheat, Ground Nut Seed, Moong Dhal etc.\n\nAs a team member, was \nresponsible\n for\n\n        \nAnalysis\n of the specifications provided by the clients\n\n        \nCoding\n using HTML pages, Java Script validations and jsp?s\n\n        \nTesting\n - unit testing & integration testing, preparing test cases and release notes\n\n\n\n#3.\nProject Name : PRO Monitor\nClient\nXcellent scan\nRole\nTeam Member\nOrganization\nLaunchPD\nTeam Size\n\nEnvironment\nSoftware\nLanguages : \n\nJSP, Javascript,DHTML, HTML\nDatabase\n   \n: mysql\n\nPROJECT DESCRIPTION:\n                                                                                                               \nThe PRO Monitor was developed to generate reports of the PRO?s daily activities in the organization. The software maintains all the records of the PRO and their daily activities. The ProMonitor generates reports like weekly Wise, date Wise and month Wise etc.\n\nAs a team member, was \nresponsible\n for\n\n        \nAnalysis\n of the specifications provided by the clients\n\n        \nCoding\n using HTML pages, Java Script validations\n\n        \nTesting\n - unit testing & integration testing, preparing test cases and release notes\n\n\n#4.\nProject Name : \nPATRAM\nClient\nNational Informatics Center(NIC)\nRole\nProject Trainee\nOrganization\nNational Informatics Center\nDuration\n12/2004 ? 04/2005\nTeam Size\n\nEnvironment\nSoftware\nLanguages : \nVisual Basic6.0 \nDatabase\n   \n\nMS-SQL Server 2000\nReport\n        \n:Segate Crystal Report\n\n\nPROJECT DESCRIPTION:\nThe PATRAM stands for Postal Accounts Transaction Maintenance software. The PATRAM Backlog module was developed to carry out over all accounting details in the postal accounts department.\n\nAs a Project Trainee, was \nresponsible\n for\n\n        \nCoding\n using Visual Basic\n\n        \nGenerating Reports \nusing \nSeagate crystal Report\n\n        \nTesting\n - unit testing & integration testing, preparing test cases and release notes\n\n\n\n\nPERSONAL DETAILS:\n            \nFather?s Name\n               \n: Mr.S.Ponnu Swamy\nDate of Birth\n                  \n: 11 May 1978\nNationality\n                     \n: Indian\nGender\n                          \n: Male\nMarital Status\n                \n: Single\nPermanent Address\n        \n: 1/14, North Street,\n\nOld Elayiram Pannai,\n\nVirudhunagar Dt -626201\nPhone Number\n               \n: 258849 (04562)\nLanguages known\n           \n: Tamil and English (Read, Write & Speak)\nDECLARATION:\nI hereby declare that all the above furnished details are true to the best of my knowledge.\n\nPlace:\n                                                                                       \nYours truly,\nDate:\n(P.Chandra sekar)',NULL,9,NULL,'2007-10-15',NULL,'2007-10-15','2010-06-08 12:13:25','2010-06-08',10,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,9,'0',NULL),(55,'Sanjay Krishna',NULL,NULL,'Mumbai',NULL,NULL,'95250 2451231','0','9820761423','0',NULL,'0','2007-10-13',10,33,'2010-06-08 12:13:25',11,'0',NULL,'200710/15/ATT7987.html','200710/15/DOC55889.doc','                                                                                                                                    \nSummary\n________________________________________________________________________\n\nI am Senior software engineer currently having over 39 months of experience in Information technology industry & have worked on exciting projects during this tenure. The project was based on mainly windows platform in Java & Java related technology. I have worked on different phases of SDLC from analysis to implementations stage & am technically sound with SDLC model.\n\n\nSkills\n_______________________________________________________________________\n\nPlatform\n                      \nWindows Platform with J2EE & J2ME technology\n\nLanguages\n                  \nJava & related technology (Servlet & JSP), C, C++, Visual Basic\n6.0 & PL/SQL\n\nDatabase\n                    \nMS-Access, Oracle & HiRDB.\n\nInternet Technology\n\nHtml, Xml, JavaScript & VBScript\n\nTools\n                           \nRational ClearCase, Visual SourceSafe, Eclipse IDE & IntelliJ\nIDEA.\n\nOthers\n                         \nStruts\n\nShell script, JavaMail, etc.\n\n\nProfessional Profile\n________________________________________________________________________\n\nPresent\n                       \nCurrently working with Patni Computer Systems Limited, \nIndia\n                                    \nfrom last 29 months (25\nth\n April ?05) on J2EE platform.\n\nJob Function - \nRequirement Analysis, Design, Implementation, Testing & Application support.\n\nPast\n                 \n            \nWorked for 10 months as a Software Engineer with Indiagames\nLtd, Chembur from 17\nth\n May 2004 to \n22\nnd\n March 2005\n\n          \n\nJob Function ? \nDeveloping mobile game application using J2ME\ntechnology. I have worked on important project for Disney &\nUniversal studio. My work during this tenure include working on\nbranded games like The Day After Tomorrow, Predator, Recess, The Mummy & developing contents for Bollywood movies.\n\nEducational Profile\n________________________________________________________________________\n\nMaster of Science in (Computer Science) in May 2004 with First class distinction from \nMumbai\nUniversity\n\nProject done at PG\n       \nPattern Recognition using neural network\nIt is an AI project used for Handwriting recognition & was developed in Java. The objective of doing this project was to work on some real world application by simulating the behavior of brain functioning. The project was completed within duration of eight months based on intensive research & analysis using SDLC\napproach. It was successful in achieving 78% accuracy in\nrecognizing Human handwriting.\n\nBachelor of Science in (Computer Science) in May 2002 with First class distinction from \nMumbai\nUniversity\n\nProject done \n                \nEmployees Information System.\nThe project was Information tracking system developed using Visual Basic & MS access. It was used for tracking & maintaining information of employees working within the firm & their personal as well as professional details.\n\nThroughout First class grade in studies.\n\n\nContact Detail\n________________________________________________________________________\n\nEmail\n                           \nsanjay13007 @gmail.com\n                                    \nMobile \n                       \n9820761423\n\nTelephone\n                   \n95250 2451231\n\nAddress\n                      \n8, Usha Sadan, 3\nrd\n floor, Golani Complex,\n                                    \nVasai, Valiw (E) ? 401208. \nIndia','Patni Computer Systems ',1,NULL,'2007-10-15',NULL,'2007-10-15','2010-06-08 12:13:25','2010-06-08',11,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(56,'Rudra Kumar ',NULL,NULL,'Bangalore','agyan@yahoo.co.in',NULL,NULL,'0','09886733088','0',NULL,'0','2007-07-15',7,20,'2010-06-08 12:13:25',11,'0',NULL,'200710/15/ATT7986.html','200710/15/DOC55890.doc','Agyan Kumar Prusty\n\nRudra\n Kumar \n\nEmail id: agyan@yahoo.co.in\n                           \nContact Number: 09886733088\n          \nObjective\n          \nTo be associated with a progressive organization that gives scope to apply knowledge and skill and to be a part of a team that dynamically works towards the growth of the organization and the developer community.\nEducational Qualification\nB.Tech. \n(Computer Science and Engineering) with 68.03%, August 2004 from Orissa\n+2 Science \nwith 70.5% From Orissa\n10\nth\n\nFrom Orissa with 83.5%\n\nProfessional Summary:\n\nWorking for approximately 2.9 years in the IT industry. \nWorking with iGATE global Solutions from February 2007 to till date.\nKnowledge of CMM levels and \nSixSigma\n\n\nWas involved in the automation of employee management, quality assurance and employee training at \nFlash InfoTech Pvt Ltd\n from August 2004 to \njanauary\n 2007 to develop a cost effective student evaluation system.\nTechnical Skills\nOperating Systems\nWindows XP, Windows 2000, Windows 9x.\nProgramming Languages\nJava\nJ2EE/Java Technologies\nServlets, JSP, Struts, JDBC\nWeb Technologies\nXML, HTML.\nWeb/App Servers\nApache Tomcat, \nJboss\nDatabase Servers\nOracle 9.0.\nProject Summary\n1.E COMP(Electronic Compensation)\nClients\n                                  \nGE(General \nEletric,USA\n\nDeployment Platform\n           \n  \nWindows2000\nJ2EE Technologies\n                 \nServlets,JSP,JDBC,Struts\nApplication Server\n                  \nJboss\nDatabase\n                                \nToad\nTeam Size\n                              \n20\n\n\n\nDescription\n                   \nE Comp is an employee management project which maintains all the employees working for GE through out the world. It maintains their salary, their experience and all. The project has 14 modules and I worked in 2 modules. One is Employee Report generation and other is creation and modification of Employees.\n\n2. Online Student Evaluation System (OSES)\nClients\n                         \n         \n: Internal \nDeployment Platform\n   \n         \n: Windows 2000\nJ2EE/Web Technologies\n       \n: Servlets, JSP, JDBC, Struts\nApplication Server\n       \n         \n: JBoss\nDatabase\n                     \n         \n: MySQL.\nDevelopment Tools\n      \n         \n: Eclipse\nTeam Size\n                    \n         \n: 3\n\n\n\nDescription\n           \nOnline Student Evaluation System (OSES) is comprehensive examination software capable of testing and grading students, helping trainers to stay focused on teaching. The software was built on the lines of the Employee Performance Monitor (EPM). Major changes/additions from EPM include the use of Struts as the design model and an online tutor that can guide the student in the areas he/she is weak in.\n3. Employee Performance Monitor (EPM)\nClients\n                         \n            \n: Internal \nDeployment Platform\n   \n            \n: Windows 2000\nJ2EE/Web Technologies\n          \n: Servlets, JSP, JDBC\nApplication Server\n                   \n: JBoss\nDatabase\n                                 \n: Oracle 9.0 \nDevelopment Tools\n                  \n: Eclipse\nTeam Size\n                               \n: 4\n\nDescription\n             \nEmployee Performance Monitor (EPM) was designed to test the aptitude and skill-set knowledge of the employees at regular intervals. The software is capable of conducting preset tests or real-time Computer Adaptive Tests similar to the GRE. Employees can log into the software and take the available tests. Objective Test results are displayed right after the test. Managers and Team Leaders can monitor employee performance in various tests. Employees also have the capability to monitor their individual performances. The software also has the capability of managing the computer adaptive test database.\n\n\n\n\n\n4. Employee Management Tool (EMT) \nClients\n                         \n           \n: Internal \nDeployment Platform\n   \n           \n: Windows 2000\nJ2EE/Web Technologies\n         \n: EJB, Servlets, JSP, JDBC\nApplication Server\n       \n           \n: JBoss\nDatabase\n                     \n           \n: Oracle 9.0 \nDevelopment Tools\n      \n           \n: Eclipse\nTeam Size\n                    \n           \n: 4\n\nDescription\n          \nEmployee Management Tool (EMT) is a comprehensive payroll and employee information management tool. EMT. In its first release, it supported automatic generation for payrolls using employee attendance information. Team Leaders and Managers are authorized to maintain the attendance information. It was also designed to dispatch payrolls to the employees at any preset date. It was capable of storing and retrieving general employee information along with Manager/Team Leader comments/reports about individual employees. After the Quality Analysis Tool and the Employee Performance Monitor were developed and deployed, EMT was enhanced to pull out the Quality Assurance and Employee Aptitude test scores thus becoming the swiss knife of the higher management.\nPersonal Information\nDate of Birth: \n              \n23rd, May, 1982\nLanguages Known:\n      \nEnglish, Hindi and Oriya.\nAddress: - Near \nMurthappa\n Garden ,17\nth\n Cross \nJP Nagar 6\nth\n phase\nBangalore-72\n                ','Flash InfoTech Pvt Ltd ',1,NULL,'2007-10-15',NULL,'2007-10-15','2010-06-08 12:13:25','2010-06-08',11,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(57,'Raghu Vamshi',NULL,NULL,NULL,'ram12345@yahoo.com','sb_graghuvamshi@yahoo.com','91 40 24650153','0','09886693538','0','040 24650153','0','2008-04-29',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-08 12:13:25',11,'0',NULL,'200710/15/ATT7985.html','200710/15/DOC55891.doc','Resdex @ naukri.com\nRAGHU RAMAN\n#3-2-371/1, Nimboli Adda, Kachiguda Hyderabad / Secunderabad - 500027 \nram12345@yahoo.com\nTelephone: 09886693538\n(M)\n 91 40 24650153\n(R)\n\nD.O.B\n - 18 Mar 1983 \nModified on\n - 25 Sep 2007 \nAnnual Salary\n - INR 3 Lac(s) 0 Thousand \nTotal Years of Experience\n - 2 Year(s) 10 Month(s) \nCurrent Location\n - Hyderabad \nPreferred Location\n - Anywhere in India \n\nTEXT RESUME \n\nRaghu RAMAN\nH.No: 3-2-371/1,\nNimboli adda,\nKachiguda, E-mail: sb_graghuvamshi@yahoo.com\nHyderabad-027. Phone: 91-9886693538\n040-24650153\nSUMMARY:\nTo associate with an organization which progresses dynamically and gives me a chance to improve my knowledge, enhance my skills in the state-of-art technologies and be a part of the team that work towards the growth of organization.\nTotal years of Experience: 2.10 years\nCurrent Location : Hyderabad\nProfessional Experience:\nWorking in Cyber India Technologies as a Software Engineer from November 2004 to Till Date\nProfessional Summary:\n\n?¢\nHaving 2+ years of experience in design, development and implementation of applications using JAVA, J2EE Technologies.\n\n?¢\nExperience with Servlets, JSP, Java Beans, JDBC, Hibernate, Struts and Java Script.\n\n?¢\nGood understanding of OOPs concepts.\n\n?¢\nAbility to work in group as well as independently with minimal supervision.\n\n?¢\nAbility to learn new languages and tools quickly.\n\n?¢\nStrong Analytical, inter-personal, communication and presentation skills.\nAcademic Qualification:\nB.Tech (ECE) from JNTU in 2004 with an aggregate of 68.57%.\nIntermediate from Board of Intermediate Education in 2000 with an aggregate of 77.6%.\nS.S.C. from Board of Secondary Education in 1998 with an aggregate of 71.8%.\nTechnical Skills:\nJAVA Technologies : JDBC, Servlets, JSP, Hibernate, Struts.\nOperating systems : Windows 9x, NT, 2000, DOS\nRDBMS : Oracle 8i\nWeb Technologies : HTML, Java Script, XML\nServers : WebLogic 8.1, Tomcat 5.0\nProfessional Experience:\nLMS June 2007 to till to date\nLeave Management System (LMS) allows users to apply for leave online and also it allows to approve/decline the leave by the management and as well as add/edit employee details. We can create login id for the new employee, create user types, employee types, add list of holidays.\nTechnical Environment: JDBC, Servlets, JSP, Struts, Hibernate\nRole & Responsibilities:\n\n?¢\nInvolved with a team of three in the Development of Servlets, JSP, Action classes, connecting to SQL Database using Hibernate.\n\n?¢\nInvolved in designing User DAOâ\n??s.\nRAS Remainder November 2006 to May 2007\nThe theme of this project is to automate the manual process of filling up the Resource Availability Sheet (RAS).\nThis application is useful for the person who has a team to send the message to the team members to fill up the RAS every day. It pops up a window at a particular time to fill the RAS by each team member. The window will pop up till the RA Sheet is filled. This application is also responsible for storing the data in the database, generating the excel sheet with the data of all members and sending an e-mail of the spreadsheet to the specified persons at a particular time, automatically.\nTechnical Environment: Swings, JDBC, Servlets\nRole & Responsibilities:\n\n?¢\nInvolved with a team of two in the Development of Swings, Servlets, JSP, connecting to Oracle Database using JDBC.\n\n?¢\nInvolved in Designing User interface.\nReport Track February 2006 to October 2006\nDTE Energy is located in U.S.A is a premier organization for providing gas and power supply. It has many systems like SAP, Maximo, and WBI etc for finance and asset management. It has more than twenty systems to manage the organization. Data need to be transferred among these systems. While message is transferring from source system to destination system there may be a chance to fail it in middle. Administrator need to login to all systems to know where exactly the message is failed any why it is failed. This practice is consuming lot of time for the administrator to get a consolidated picture of message track. To overcome this, they decided to develop an application. Our application tracks the messages and maintains a record for all the systems. Administrator needâ\n??s login to only our appli\ncation to get a consolidated picture of message track instead of login to all the systems.\n\nTechnical Environment: Java, Servlets, JSP, JDBC, Hibernate, Struts\nRole & Responsibilities:\n\n?¢\nInvolved with a team of four in the Development of CronTask, Data Loading\n\n?¢\nInvolved in Designing User DAOâ\n??s, Report generation\nJDE_CRM August 2005 to January 2006\nThis application can be used as an interface between the process of JDE entry and CRM entry of the work order documents for Whataburger. It helps the team who are processing the CRM entry to avoid miscommunication while taking the closed work order numbers manually. The application can also be used as database for storing the numbers of the work order, which are closed in JDE as well as in CRM.\nThe important feature of this application is security. The users are restricted from doing modifications to the data. Only few designated users are allowed to do necessary modifications to the data.\nThe main purpose of this application is to improve the quality of the work by eliminating the manual process of taking numbers from the JDE entry team.\nTechnical Environment: Java Beans, JSP, HTML, Scripts, XML, Oracle8i.\nRole & Responsibilities:\n\n?¢\nInvolved with a team of three in the Development activities using Java Beans, connecting to Oracle Database using JDBC.\n\n?¢\nInvolved in Designing User interface.\nFocus walks December 2004 to July 2005\nThis project keeps track of the Focus Walks Evaluation carried out at various units of Whataburger. Each unit is evaluated thrice, in each quarter, twice by Area Managers and once by Director of Operations. The evaluation scores are recorded in this application. It has a search option on unit basis. The records found in the search can be edited to update the database with the latest scores. If no records are found for a particular unit, the application will automatically prompt the user to enter the details. Each walk scores is assigned a unique integer number which separates it from the rest.\nTechnical Environment: Java (Servlets, JSP and JDBC) and SQL Server\nRole & Responsibilities:\n\n?¢\nDevelopment and Coding according to the specifications provided by the client.\nPersonal Profile:\nLanguages Known : English, Hindi, and Telugu\nDate of Birth : 18 March, 1983\nNationality : India\nGender : Male\nMarital Status : Single\nPassport No : F 3449959\nDeclaration:\nI hereby declare that the information furnished above is true to the best of my knowledge.\nDate:\nPlace: Hyderabad (Raghu Vamshi G)',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-15',NULL,'2007-10-15','2010-06-08 12:13:25','2010-06-08',11,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(58,'Raj  Kumar Behera',NULL,NULL,NULL,'java@gmail.com',NULL,NULL,'0','9945784416','0',NULL,'0','2008-04-29',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-08 12:13:25',11,'0',NULL,'200710/15/ATT7984.html','200710/15/DOC55892.doc','PROFILE\nCurriculum Vitae\nRAJ \n\nKUMAR BEHERA\n#378, MSR Nagar,7th main,6th cross\n                                     \nE-mail : \njava@gmail.com\n\nMathikere\n                                                                             \nMob\n   \n: 91-9945784416\nBangalore-560054.\n                                                   \n\nPROFILE\nObjective:\n\n\n      \nTo seek a challenging environment that encourages continuous learning and creative exposure to new ideas, which stimulates professional growth.\nExperience Summary:\n\n\n      \nHaving \n2+ years\n of exposure in software development in Client-Server, middleware architecture, solution design and implementation for domestic and overseas clients.\n\n      \nHaving good knowledge and working experience on \nUNIX\n (RedHat Linux, AIX, Sun sol) servers\n\n      \nExcellent skills in \nJAVA\n\nSERVLET \n\nJSP\n\nJDBC\n\n JAVABEANS\n\n STRUTS\n\n\n      \nDeveloped application for\nautomating\n\naccounting operation in\n\nthe \nTelecom Domain\n\n Insurance\n, and\n Banking\n\n\n\n      \nKnowledge on \nHTML\n\nJavaScript\n\n\n      \nWell versed in\n\nclient side & server side Scripting.\n\n      \nHaving knowledge in \nSQL\n\n\n      \nWell acquainted with \nselenium Tool\n\nProfessional Qualification:\n\n\n      \nB.E.\n in \nComputer Science & Engineering\n from \nUtkal University in \n2004\n, with\n First\n Class.\nProfessional Skills:\n\nOperating System\nWINDOWS-9X,Windows 2000 ,Window XP,UNIX(AIX 5.1, Linux RedHat 9.0,Sun Solarise 8.0)\nLanguages\nJAVA with J2EE Technology\nRDBMS\nMs Access, Oracle 9i, DB2.\nJava Technology\nCore java\nWeb programming\nJava,Servlet,JSP,JDBC,Java Beans,Struts\nApplication/Web Servers\nBEA Web Logic 8.1,websphere 6.0/Apache Tomcat5.0\nOther Primary Technology\nXML, HTML, DHTML, JavaScript\nIDE\nRSA 7.0, WSAD 5.1, Eclipse 3.2,JCreator,NetBeans4.1\nVersion Control\nClear Case, CVS\n\nCertifications:\n\n\n      \nSun certified Java programmer.\n\n      \nBrain bench Certified java programmer.\n\n      \nIBM AIX Certified.\nCOMPANY\nPOSITION\nDATE HIRED\nIBM Global Services India Pvt Ltd\nSoftware Engineer\nMarch 2006, till date.\nIVector Technologies Pvt.Ltd\nSoftware Engineer\nNov 2004 to March 2006.\nProject details:\nPROJECT #1\nGIOM-Global Integrated Order Management\n(AT&T, USA,\nwww.att.com\n\nTitle\n            \n: Global Integrated Order Management (GIOM)\nDuration\n     \n\nAugust 2007 to Till date \nTeam\n          \n\nGIOM\nTeam size\n   \n\n04\nTechnology \n         \n: JAVA, JSP, Servlet, Java Beans, JDBC, UNIX (sun Solaris)\nTools\n           \n\nIBM Rational Software Architect, Oracle, UNIX, XML, Rational Clear Case.\nInterfaces\n\n\n UNIX (Sun Solaris 8.0), sablime 5.2,\n\niPlanet 6.0,\n worked with \nRSA (Rational Software Architect7.0) and Clear Case integration, webSphere 6.0\nDescription:\nThe Global Integrated Order Manager (GIOM) is intended to provide a common user portal to AT&T Business Services\' service-specific order infrastructures (Voice,port,PVC ,VPN ,Data/IP, LD Voice, and Local Voice) to facilitate customer-centric ordering of both standalone and bundled services.\n\nGIOM provides the capability to place both Express (Flow-through) and the (Flow-to) Orders.\n\nAdditionally, the Linked Provisioning subsystem gives an administrator user the capability to easily provision an GIOM application user for access to GIOM with the authorized customer accounts and service types and finally it comes to a Common shopping cart and delivering to different subsystems\nGIOM would offer a unified portal to order all the services to the customer (internal/external), sanitize the order by performing the required validations thus minimizing fallouts due to order entry, and hand off the service specific orders to the corresponding downstream systems. The downstream would then perform the necessary provisioning, account maintenance, and billing updates in the existing service delivery architecture and provide status back to GIOM, and hence to the customer. GIOM leverages this ?unified? approach to provide a ?Shopping Cart? capability, where a customer can place orders for multiple services in a single shopping cart, and track their delivery in GIOM.\nResponsibilities as Team Member:\n\n        \nInvolved development of our new requirement for new Release.\nInvolved in the design.\nServer side development for the application which included coding (JDBC Connections, java, Servlet, jsp, java Beans, Threads)\nInvolved in the code migration of our generic in to RSA\n\nCapable of sharing knowledge with other team members.\n\nPROJECT #2\n\nMMO2 ? O2 Companion System\n\n(O2, United Kingdom, \nwww.o2.co.uk\n\nTitle\n            \n\n\nElectronic Bill Presentment and Payment (EBPP) \nDuration\n\n    \n\n March 2006 to July 2007\nTeam\n          \n\n EBPP \nTeam Size\n\n\n 05\nTechnology\n   \n: JAVA, JSP, servlet, Struts, Java Beans, JDBC.\nTools\n           \n\n IBM Web Sphere Developer, DB2, Korn shell scripting, XML, CAREX,\n\nGeneva, AMDOCS, Test Director, Rational Clear Case. \nInterfaces\n\n\n UNIX (AIX 5.1),\n\nworked with \nWSAD (Web sphere Application Developer 5.1) and Clear Case integration, web Sphere 6.0\nDescription:\nO2 companion project deals with the development of customer mobile billing software and profile of the customer. This system is developed for one of the top most Mobile service provider called O2 in United Kingdom.\n\nO2 is a leading mobile communications services provider in Europe, which was diverged from BT in 4 Q 2001.\nIt handles more than 3.8 million customers a month and involves all the recent technologies and products .O2 can provide their mobile services to UK\'s mobile user with the help of GENEVA rating and billing engine, CAREX customer care Extension, ABS, Orange, and Kana Response and EBPP.Here EBPP Allows a variety of O2 customers to view/manage their bills online. Allows Care agents to service customers, ?Bill Repository? for the whole of Companion. It work in different phases Bill Preparation (Batch Schedule) and then it will Notifies customers of new bills via emails or SMS.Then it will Displays billed and unbilled usage information relevant to the user?s profile. Allows ad-hoc credit and debit card payments and viewing payment history and also display customers display treatment status. It allows customers to raise a Bill Dispute and download of Call Details.\nResponsibilities as Team Member:\n\n         \nInvolved development in our new Release.\nPersonally involved in coding and understand the functionality, requirement.\nDefect fixing, build generation, edocs pattern mapping (ddf, alf file generation).\nInvolved in Unit Testing and testing with selenium tool.\nPROJECT # 3.\nTitle\n   \n      \n: Centralized Insurance business application (CIBA)\n\n Auto Insurance.\nDuration\n               \n\n 09 Months\nTechnology\n          \n\n\nJava\n\nJSP\n\nJDBC\n\nServlet\n\n JavaBeans, Oracle\n\n9i\n\n Eclipse 3.0\n and\n                     \ndeployed on \nBEA Web Logic Server 8.1\nTeam size\n            \n\n06\n\n\nDescription:\nThis is a web based system provides various insurance services for customers. The customers are provided with\n   \nuser-friendly HTML & JSP pages to submit their proposals or renewal or claim forms. These information?s are collected and inspections are carried out.\nThe system allows inspector to enter inspection details. Accordingly the status of the proposal is displayed using JSP, which contains the status of the proposal (i.e. Accepted or rejected) and reason for rejection. If the proposal is accepted then all the business logic (i.e. calculation premium account, insurance depreciated value (IDV) depending on various parameters of vehicle) is carried out and insurance certificate will be generated in the printable format using Servlets.\n          \nThis system also maintains all the detail related to insurance policy in a database using JDBC and these data are accused by various departments in the insurance company.\nResponsibilities as Team Member:\n\n         \nAs a team member, understood the user requirements and functional specifications.\nDeveloped Web Pages using \nJSP\n and static \nHTML\n pages.\nUsed \njava scripts\n for client side validations.\nUsed \nJSP\n\n Servlet\n for server side validation, Controlling and dynamic processing.\nImplemented and developed \nJava Beans\n\nUsed \nJDBC\n Drivers for communicating the database.\nPROJECT 4 #.\nTitle\n            \n         \n: Banking Analysis System.\nDuration\n               \n\n 06 Months\nTechnology\n\n        \n\n\nJava,JSP, Servlets, JavaBeans, Web Logic 7.0\n\nOracle 8i\n\n Eclipse 3.0\n\n                                                            \nTeam size\n            \n\n 06\n\nDescription:\nThis is a web based application, which helps their customer to make banking transaction through internet or intranet. This system consists of two sections. Client section and Administrative section. The main input of the Client section is manual input that is done by the user. After manual input the account holders or customers are provided with a login ID and password along with their account number. User can get in to the system after user id and password checking and then can enter into his/her account details. Account transactions statement will be provided to a customer on demand and report will be presented to the customer. Administrators have their own user name and password. Through this page administrator can add new users.\nResponsibilities as Team Member:\n\n         \nInvolved in development procedure and coding.\n\n         \nUsed \nJSP\n\nServlet\n for server side validation, Controlling and dynamic processing.\n\n         \nImplemented and developed \nJava Beans\n\n\n         \nWe use \nJDBC\n (Pure java driver used) to retrieve the records from database.\n\nPersonal details:\nPersonality Traits\n   \n: Confident, Team Worker, Patience\nPassport Details\n     \n: G0594167, Place of Issue ? Bhubaneswar',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-15',NULL,'2007-10-15','2010-06-08 12:13:25','2010-06-08',11,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(59,'Raj  Kumar Reddy.M',NULL,NULL,'Bangalore ','Kumarreddy123345@gmail.com',NULL,NULL,'0','9886060553','0',NULL,'0','2008-01-12',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-08 12:13:25',3,'0',NULL,'200710/15/ATT7983.html','200710/15/DOC55893.doc','RAJANIKANTH REDDY\nRAJ \n\nKUMAR REDDY.M\n                                                                          \n      \n       \nKumarreddy123345@gmail.com\n                                                                                                \n      \n    \nPh no: 91-9886060553\n\n\nSUMMARY\n\n\n      \nHaving \n2.2 years\n of experience in IT industry dedicated to Testing client/server applications and web applications.\n\n\n      \nHas good experience on various techniques used in \nManual Testing\n and \nQTP\n\n\n      \nExpertise in Functional Testing, System Testing, Regression and Re Testing\n\n\n      \nProficient in Preparing Test Plan and Designing Test Cases and Test Data.\n\n\n      \nSkill full in Executing the Test Cases and Test Scenarios,\n\n\n      \nHas good experience in Defect Tracking and Reporting.\n\n\n      \nHands in QTP Scripting, automating the scenarios and Writing End-to-End Script.\n\n\n      \nInvolved in Release Management and Preparing Release Notes, Build Installation, Preparing Traceability Matrix and Functional coverage Matrix and Deliverables.\n\n\n      \nExcellent analytical skills and logical programming skills with a good understanding at conceptual level.\n\n\n      \nExcellent interpersonal skills with a strong desire to achieve specified goals.\n\nPROFESSIONAL PROFILE\n\n\n      \nWorking as a Software Engineer for \nMphasiS Limited\n\nBangalore\n From Nov 2006 to Till Date\n\n      \nWorked as a Software Engineer for \nSlash Infotech Solutions, \nBangalore\n\n\nFrom Jun 2005 to Nov 2006\n\nEDUCATIONAL PROFILE\n\nB.Tech \nin\nComputer Science\n from \nJ.N.T\nUniversity\n\nHyderabad\n\nTECHNICAL SKILLS\n\nFunctional Testing Tool \n    \n    \n     \n\nQTP 9.0\nTest Management Tool\n    \n           \n\n\nTest Director 8.0 and MQC \nOperating Systems\n        \n            \n   \n\nWindows and Linux\nProgramming Languages\n            \n\n\nC and Java\nDatabases\n                      \n             \n  \n\nOracle and Sql Server\nScripting Languages\n         \n         \n   \n: VB Scripting\n\nPROJECT PROFILE\n\nProject #1\n      \nZurich\n Financial Services\n\n\nRate Review\n        \nNov 2006 to Till Date\nClient\n        \n   \n\n\n\nZurich\nRole\n           \n    \n: Test Engineer\nTools Used\n    \n: Manual Testing, QTP 9 and \nQuality\nCenter\nEnvironment\n\n\n\nront End\n                   \n\nJava, \nJsp\n                                                                                                                                                                                   \n          \nBack End\n                   \n\n Oracle 9i and Main Frames\n                                                        \nApplication Server \n           \n\nJBoss-3.2.5\n                                                                                       \nOperating system\n\n          \n\n Windows XP and Linux\n                                   \n                                                           \nBrowsers Used\n       \n       \n\n Internet Explorer 6\nDescription: \n        \nZurich\n Financial Services is an insurance-based financial service mainly aimed to help the customers to manage and track their accounts. It also helps for planning the future investments. It \noffers a comprehensive range of general and life insurance products and services for individuals, small businesses, commercial enterprises, mid-sized and large corporations, and multinational companies and also provides services like General Insurance, Personal Line, Life Insurance, Investments, combined protection and savings.\n\nResponsibilities:\n      \nManual Testing:\nUnderstanding the Requirements and its functionalities\nDesigning Test Cases, Reviewing\n\nof Test Cases, Execution of Test Cases\nInstalling Builds, Involved in CFT, Involved in Release Management,\nPreparing Traceability Matrix, Preparing Functional\n\nCoverage matrix\n\nPreparing the\n\nDeliverable\n      \nAutomation (QTP):\n1.\n      \nIdentifying the End to End Regression Test Scenarios and design Test Data\n2.\n      \nDesigning the Business Functions, Generic functions and parameters.\n3.\n      \nResponsible for data interaction with database and application functionality.\n4.\n      \nDesigning the End to End Script and Involved in Review of Functions\n\n5.\n    \nResponsible for identifying Objects in Object Repository\n\n\nProject \n#2\n              \nDigi\nté\n\n\nEnterprise\n                          \nFeb\n 2006 to Oct 2006\nClient\n              \n\n       \nBearing Point, T-Mobile, Deloitte and etc\nRole\n                \n\n        \nTest Engineer\nTools Used\n     \n\n         \nManual testing\nEnvironment\n\n\n        \n\nront End\n                       \n\nJava, \nJsp\n                                                                                                                                                    \n                               \nBack End\n                       \n\n SQL Server 2000, Oracle\n                                                             \nApplication Server \n         \n\nWebLogic-8.1 and JBoss-3.2.5\n                                                                               \n        \nOperating system\n\n          \n\n Windows 2000 and Linux\n                                                                                              \nBrowsers Used\n       \n        \n\n IE 6, Mozilla\n\nFirefox\nDescription:\n        \nDigité is a complete, pre-packaged web-based product for Project Management and Software Lifecycle Management, for Small and Medium IT Services enterprises. The application is pre-configured and is available for Use at the customer\'s site.\n       \nDigite deals with Project Management activities like \nDefect/Issue Tracking, Program Management, Risk Management, Resource Management, Document Management, Software Configuration Management and Collaborative Development activities\nlike Test Management, Service Management and Change Management. It also generates Reports based on request and data.\nResponsibilities:\n1.\n      \nUnderstanding the Requirements and its functionalities\n2.\n      \nDesigning Test Cases, Reviewing\n\nof Test Cases\n3.\n      \nExecution of Test Cases and Defect reporting and Tracking\n4.\n      \nPreparing Traceability Matrix and Doubts documents\n5.\n      \nPreparing the\n\nDeliverable\n\nProject\n # 3\n       \n\n  \n  \nBanking Management System\n          \n    \n\n\nJune\n 2005\n\nto \nJan\n 2006\nClient \n   \n          \n  \n\n\n\n\n\n\nABI Group\n\nRole\n               \n\n\n   \n  \n\n Test Engineer\nTools Used\n       \n   \n\n\n\nManual Testing and Test Director\nEnvironment\n\n\n        \n\nront End\n                       \n\nJava, \nJsp\n                                                                                                                                                                                   \nBack End\n                       \n\n SQL Server 2000, Oracle\n                                                             \nOperating system\n\n          \n\n Windows 2000\n                                                                                               \nBrowsers Used\n       \n        \n\n Internet Explorer\nDescription :\n    \n  \nThis software is used to map the associated branches of a cooperative bank. The Objective of this software is to generate the consolidated Reports as a whole. Based on this we can generate the reports that are needed to submit to RBI. And we can use this consolidated data extracted from the branches and to give the necessary information to Management and RBI for maintaining proper Liquidity, show funds flow business details at any point of date. I worked on the module called GL Transactions\n\nResponsibilities:\n1.\n      \nUnderstanding the Requirements and its functionalities\n2.\n      \nDesigning Test Cases and Execution of Test Cases\n3.\n      \nPreparing Traceability Matrix, Preparing Functional Coverage matrix.\n   \n4.\n      \nPreparing the Deliverable\n\n\n       \nPersonal Strengths\n     \n      \n        \n                  \nSelf-Motivated, Hard Working, Team Player\n\n      \nReferences\nAvailable upon request.','MphasiS Limited',1,NULL,'2007-10-15',NULL,'2007-10-15','2010-06-08 12:13:25','2010-06-08',3,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(60,'Ravi Amit ',NULL,NULL,NULL,'traval@gmail.com',NULL,'020 32501030','0','9822799292','0','265 2510142','0','2006-09-28',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-08 12:13:25',3,'0',NULL,'200710/15/ATT7982.html','200710/15/DOC55894.doc','SHAH RITESH A\nRAVI AMIT \nPh. (M) 9822799292, Email: \ntraval@gmail.com\n\nPresent Address\n                                                             \nPermanent Address\nE-21 Sadhu Waswani Road\n                                              \n36/H Chandranagar Colony,\nBuilding E, Block E - 21\n                                                   \nOPP. Prabhat Coolony, Waghodiaroad,\n    \n   \n   \n2ndFloor (E), Pune 411001\n                                          \nVadodara-390019, \nGujarat\n         \nPh: 020-32501030\n   \n                                                       \nPh: 265-2510142\n\nSeeking assignments in Software Development with a frontline organization in IT Sector.\n\nPROFESSIONAL SYNOPSIS: \n\n3.7 years of qualitative exposure in software development. Presently working as technical co-ordinator with Capsilon Corporation. Proficient in handling projects encompassing conceptualization and module design & development. Have successfully developed EAI project, OSS-BSS system, Rule engine, Pattern Matching, CRM, Cross Platform Application with .NET. \nAn\n\nEffective communicator with honed team leading & management skills. Strong analytical, problem solving & organizational abilities.\n\nI have B1 visa for US valid till 2016.\nTechnical SKILLS\nOperating systems\n         \n: Windows X, Linux 9.0 \nLanguages \n                    \n: C#.net, Asp.net, C, C++ , Visual Basic, Core Java\nDatabases \n                    \n: Inter System Cache[ORDBMS], MS-Access\nApplication server\n          \n: IIS 5.0\nIntegration serve\n\n          \n: Ensamble\nOthers\n                          \n: LLBLGen, GeoCoding [GIS Applocation], LDAP [Novell E ? Directory], MONO,\n\nWeb Services, STL, \n   \nUML, Knowledge \n    \nManagement.\nEDUCATION\nMCA\n from \nB.V.D\nUniversity\n (68.52%) in 2004\nB.Com\n from \nM.S\nUniversity\n\nBaroda\n (64%) in 2001\nH.S.C.\n from G.S.E.B., \nBaroda\n (73%) in 1998\nS.S.C.\n from G.S.E.B., \nBaroda\n (82%) in 1996\nPursuing MBA from TASMAC\nDATE OF BIRTH\n\n 17\nth\n Dec, 1980\n\nORGANIZATIONAL EXPERIENCE\n\nCurrent Employment Status\n\nSince Feb?06 with Avalara \n\n[www.avalara.com]\nAn ASP, providing products for in U.S.Sales Tax Domain.\nAvalara is an SST CSP. Avalara is authorised to calculate sales tax for around 19 states in US by SST govenring body. There are only 3 SST CSP in \nUSA\n, including us. \n\nPast employer \n\nSince Dec?03 with Capsilon Corporation \n\n[www.capsilon.com]\nAn ASP, providing products for in \nU.S.\n Financial Domain.\n\n\n\nKey Result Areas;\n\n         \nFollowing RUP for solving the problems.\n\n         \nInvolved in Geo Coding for US Sales Tax calculation.\n\n         \nInvolved in designing OSS-BSS system for the company?s ASP operation.\n\n         \nProposing solutions to solve complex problems like Pattern Matching, Designing and prototyping own rule Engine, meeting client \nSLA\n for real time Billing and CRM processes.\n\n         \nProject planning, technical review, progress monitoring and ensuring seamless product delivery.\n\n         \nWrite software codes/ programmes as per the planned algorithms/ logic.\n\n         \nEnsure timely execution of projects involving scheduling of tasks and resource deployment for timely completion of projects with quality delivery.\n\n         \nProvide technical leadership ensuring that the project teams deliver an integrated business and technology solution that meets client\'s needs.Has handled team of 4-5 software engineer at Capsilon.\n\n         \nInteract with clients to understand scope for improvements, modifications & additions in modules if required. \nChallenges Handled\n\nCurrent Assignment:\n           \n            \n\nE-Bay Integration\nTeam size:\n\n     \n                                                                                    \nRole: Analysis & Develop\nEnvironment:\n Windows 2000 onwards, C#.net,COM .My SQL,JAVA, LLBLGen\nDesciption: \nThis is themost ambitious project of companywhere we are integrating with E- BayProstore for calculating Sales Tax. I am not supposed to provide more details for this project. Currently in US for this project.\nResponsibilies:\n\n- Understanging E-Bay SDK and provide a feasibility study.\n- Closely work with E-Bay team on first Proff of Concept.\n      \nCurrent Assignment: Avatax SDK\nTeam size:\n\n     \n                                                                                    \nRole: Analysis & Develop\nEnvironment:\n Windows 2000 onwards, C#.net,COM .\nDesciption: \nCurrently I am writing SDK for the AvaTax solution. SDK is the ultimate way for the user to use the webmethods we expose. There have been humdrads of user using SDK and the challenge is to manage the SDK and make it developer friendly. It is exposed as .net assembly as well as COM. There are other SDK which supports JAVA and PHP programmers as well.\nResponsibilies:\n\n- Design and develop code for SDK.\n- Manage backward compatibility train customer support team and possibly end user as well .\n      \n- Draft a meaningful help file.\nTitle: Avatax Web Methods.\nTeam size:\n\n     \n                                                                                    \nRole: Analysis & Develop\nEnvironment:\n Windows 2000 onwards, C#.net,SQL Server2005, LLBLGen, .\nDesciption: \nIt is the heart of the system. It is the mail solution which calculates the TAX, exempt the transaction and some of the complex tasks as Reconciliation. It covers complex programming capability to write such solution.\nResponsibilies:\n\n- Extensively use LLBLGen to generate DB layer.\n- Write Algo and different approaches to solve reconciliation problem.\n      \n- Implementing solution for calculating Tax and exempting transactions.\n\nTitle: Geo Coding for \nUS\n Sales Tax Jurisdiction determination.\nTeam size:\n\n     \n                                                                                    \nRole: Research & Develop\nEnvironment:\n Windows 2000 onwards, C#.net,SQL Server2005, Tatuk GIS.\nDesciption: \nThis is a challenging application which helps customer find their Point of Sale falls under which juricdiction? It is a challenging task to pattern match the address which is not aslways complete and to deal with hundrads of scenario. This is the crusial most application which determines how much TAX should be paid for that Sales transaction?\nResponsibilies:\n\n- Integrating with TatukGIl API.\n- Extensively use LLBLGen to generate DB layer.\n- Write Algo and different approaches to Geo Code the given address.\n      \n\nTitle: \nOSS\n[Operatikon Support System] Framework.\nTeam size:\n\n     \n                                                                                    \nRole: \nTechnical Co-Ordinator\nEnvironment:\n Windows 2000 onwards, Linux, C, C++,C#.net,C# with MONO, xml,ASP.NET Web Service ,\n            \n\nISC[Inter SystemCache], Novell E-Directory,JMS [Fiorano MQ].\nDesciption: \nThis is complete frmework containing 6 components, which will help more than 50 components running 24/7 on more than 3000 mschines in clustered environment. We have to track each and every minute activity happened in the system. Realtime alarm generation and defect fixing system has to be really strong to handle routine operations and the worst case scenario to meet the \nSLA\n\nResponsibilies:\n\n\n- Designing the over all system.\n- Implementing low level system calls for process health monitoring, controlling, process scheduling etc.\n- Implementing real time alarm generation and resolution system.\n- Designing flexible rule based system. \n- Implementing LDAP based authentication mechanism.\n\nTitle: Aktive Messenger.\n            \nTeam Size\n: 2\n                                         \n                                                \nRole\n: Technical Co-Ordinator\nEnvironment\n: Windows 2000 onwards, VB, C#.net, xml,WORD SFTP.\n                                    \nDescription\n: This is the only client facing module of th ewhole product. It deals with uploading the files through SFTP channel to the data centre. Moreover , it acts as CRM module which helps client in solving the querries and tracking the activities. It is tightly bound with the strict \nSLA\n made with client.\nResponsibilities: \n\n\n          \nGet the data for processing from clientside to the data centre using SFTP api.\n\n          \nImplement different ideas and creative usability features to make client?s life easier.\n\n          \nEnsure security, We kept on improving the application to support the GLB norms of the \nUS\n industry.\n\nTitle: Pattern Matching.\nTeam Size\n: 1\n                                                                    \n                    \nRole\n: Research & Development.\nEnvironment\n: C#.net.\nDescription\n: This started with an idea while observing one of the most trivial business problem. It deals with the Auto Doc Identification. I developed some pattern matching algo to recognisethe document from the bunch of lacs of documents. Now it is part of one major module who identifies the documents automatically. \nResponsibilities: \n\n          \nDesigning the algo which can deal with huge number of files within specified time.\n\n          \nTo make the module plugable so that is can be part of major Auto classifiaction system.\n\nTitle: BSS [Business support System] Framework\nTeam Size\n: 4\n                     \n                 \n                                        \n          \nRole\n: Technical Co-Ordinator.\n         \n   \nEnvironment:\n Windows 2000 onwards, C#.net, , xml,ASP.NET Web Service ,Web Logic,\n\n           \nISC[Inter SystemCache], Novell E-Directory,JMS [Fiorano MQ]. JAVA, J2EE, J2ME.\nDescription\n: This is my current assignment. I am involved in designing and implementing the BSS framework which includes 7 components. \n\nIt deals with the client set up, on demand demo, 24/7 helpdesk support,\n\ncustomer setup and service provisioning, Rule Creation for \nSLA\n and schemes etc.\nWe are developing a system which acts as a window between data centre and client. Billing and rating engine are two key components which we have developed. We designed and implement our own Rule engine to support the complex rules for billing . Rule Engine is a generic module which is now used by\n\nmany compnent in the system.\nResponsibilities\n\n\n          \nDesign and prototype own [Generic] Rule Engine.\n\n          \nCapturing requiremtns and designing the BSS framework.\n\n          \nImplementing the Rating enging.\n\n          \nInterating with client to support their dynamic requirements.',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-15',NULL,'2007-10-15','2010-06-08 12:13:25','2010-06-08',3,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(61,'Niraj Kumar',NULL,NULL,NULL,'kumar1234567@rediffmail.com',NULL,NULL,'0','09902579163','0',NULL,'0','2007-04-30',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-08 12:13:25',11,'0',NULL,'200710/15/ATT7981.html','200710/15/DOC55895.doc','NIRAJ KUMAR\nNIRAJ SHARMA\n                             \nMobile:\n    \n09902579163\n                                                                                           \nEmail:\n      \nkumar1234567@rediffmail.com\n\n\n         \nOBJECTIVE\n   \n\n           \n\n          \nTo be part of a dynamic environment that will equip me to develop, sustain and enhance my talents\n\n\n         \nPROFESSIONAL SUMMARY:\n\n\n\nHaving \n3+ \nyears of IT experience in Product Software and Web Applications Development\n\n\n2.0\n years of relevant experience in \nVB, VB.Net, Winforms,\n\nASP.Net and Webforms\n\n\nStrong in \n\nNet framework, Winforms, Webforms, ADO.Net and Crystal Reports\n\n\nGood Knowledge in ADO.Net for all RDBMS\n\n\nStrong Database skills in \nOracle, MS SQL Server\n and \nMS Access\n\n\nHaving good knowledge of object oriented concepts and programming\n\n     \nEXPERIENCE:\n\n\n      \nWorking as Programmer in \nMarlabs Software Private Ltd\n. from Aug 2006 to\ntill date\n\n      \nWorked as Programmer and cooperate trainer in \nSoftware Technologies Groups\n from May 2006 to August 2006.\n\n      \nWorked as Programmer in \nGenius Software Technology \nfrom Jan 2006 to March 2006.\n\n      \nWorked as Programmer in \nSun Infosys Software Development \nfrom Nov 2003 to December 2005.\n\n    \nEDUCATION:\n\n\n      \nMCA\n from \nPeriyar\nUniversity\n in 2003\n                          \n                               \n    \nTECHNICAL SKILLS:\n          \n          \nLanguages\n                  \n\n          \nVB, VB.net, ASP.net, C#\n          \nOperating Systems\n     \n\n          \nMS-DOS, Windows 98, and Windows 2003, Windows XP\n\nInternet Technologies\n   \n\n           \nIIS, HTML\n          \nDatabases\n                   \n\n           \nMS- Access, Oracle 8.0, SQL-SERVER 2000\n\n\n\n\n\nProject Details\n\n\n\nRole\nSoftware developer\nProject\nLivewire 3.0\nTeam Size\n04\nDuration\n06 months\nEnvironment\nVB.Net, SQL SERVER2000\nCompany\nI-Flex Solutions\n\n\n           \nDescription:\n\n                          \n   \nLivewire is a VB.net client server windows application with its database in \nSQL Server 2000. The application generates text and Excel file reports with a variety of \nformats. The application has a reporting engine that comprises of a Reporting Model and\n\nProcess Model using which the developer can generate reports without modifying any stored\n\nprocedure or application components. \n\nProject Details\n\n\nRole\nBug Fixing, coding and Testing\nProject\nTracking Application Support\nTeam Size\n02\nDuration\n06 months\nEnvironment\nVB.Net, Oracle 10.2g,\nCrystal\n report,Perl script\nCompany\nCognizant Technology Solutions\n\n     \n\n\nDescription:\n                           \nThe project Tracking Support Application is one of the Support project.\nAlmost every type of operation, whether an individual or a group of people performs it, requires some sort of tracking procedure for it to succeed. Whenever goals are set, tracking the progress towards these goals is of great importance. By tracking a process, all the people involved can tell what stage the process is in at any given moment, how much work has already been done, and what still remains to be done. Tracking implies not only the ability to record the information about various tasks, but also to search for the information quickly and efficiently. \n\nProject Details\n\n\nRole\nDebugging, code review and coding\nProject\nProvantis 8.0\nTeam Size\n11\nDuration\n06 months\nEnvironment\nVB.Net, Oracle 10.2g\nCompany\nAspire System(\nIndia\n) Private Limited\n\n        \nDescription:\n        \n             \nThis project consists of 5 modules. They are Animal Management, System Libraries, Graphical Palpable Masses, Protocol Definition and In -Life. This project is mainly focusing on the study of animals. In Animal Management; we are defining the source to be taken. In GPM, we can identify particular animal symptoms or changes after giving doses. And it can be represented by graphically. In protocol Definition, we are defining particular study. In InLife, we are making normal representation of animals. In system librarary, we are entering the particular medicine injected to the animals. \n\nProject Details\n\n\nRole\nSoftware Developer\nProject\nGulf Terrace Hotel\nTeam Size\n03\nDuration\n04 months\nEnvironment\nASP.Net, Sql-server2000\nCompany\nGenius Software Technology\n\n       \n\n\nDescription:\n        \n             \nThis project consists of 3 modules. They are Check in, Checkout and HK-clearance. This is hotel, where the person comes to stay here, so we first make a check in. And if they are leaving the room, then checkout is made. HK clearance is nothing but the room is completely vacant and cleared. All the records are kept in track and updated.\n\n     \nProject Details\n\n\nRole\nSoftware Developer\nProject\nInventory Management System\nTeam Size\n04\nDuration\n05 months\nEnvironment\nVB.net, Sqlserver2000\nCompany\nSun infosys software Development\n\n        \nDescription:\n        \n             \nThis project consists of five modules. They are Indent, Inquiry, Purchase Order, Goods Receipt Voucher and Issue-Voucher. First, a particular department raises indent, and then purchase enquiry is made by purchase manager about that product. If particular product doesn?t exist in any department, then purchase order is raised by purchase manager. Purchase manager give order to the supplier to bring the particular product of suitable quantity, quality, price etc. Then supplier brings their product and it is kept in store and noted as GRV. And at last Store department issue the product to particular department.\n\nProject Details:\nRole\nSoftware Developer\nProject\nHRD System\nTeam Size\n05\nDuration\n05 months\nEnvironment\nVB.net,Sql-server2000\nCompany\nSun infosys software Development\n\n\n\nDescription:\n                 \n        \nThis project consist of two module i.e. HRD system, Time office Management. Cochin Shipyad Company has been using this product to automate the HRD system of the organization. System has records of each and every employee, who are entering into the office campus and leave from office. System calculates the leave, salary, refreshment, bonus of employee and it alerts the authority about the promotions /demotions\n   \nof employees.\n\nProject Details\n\nRole\nSoftware Developer\nProject\nBell\n Seafoods\nTeam Size\n05\nDuration\n06 months\nEnvironment\nVB.net,Sql-server 2000\nCompany\nSun Infosys software Development\n\nDescription:\n\n                 \nThis project consists of 3 modules. They are Log Details, Raw materials Management, and Production Management. Here the Raw material is brought to the company by the suppliers of specified quality, quantity and price etc. And starts Production from different raw material to finished products. After the production the products (ie.different size Slabs) is packed in different size Carton. And they are sent to store department and entry is made.',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-15',NULL,'2007-10-15','2010-06-08 12:13:25','2010-06-08',11,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(62,'Radha.Ch.Sah',NULL,NULL,NULL,'SRINIVAS-srinu_noti@yahoo.co.in',NULL,NULL,'0','9902033699','0',NULL,'0','2007-04-30',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-08 12:13:25',11,'0',NULL,'200710/15/ATT7980.html','200710/15/DOC55896.doc','SRINIVAS-srinu_noti@yahoo.co.in\n\nFocus:\nSeeking a position where my experience of software development will add value operations and a dynamic organization where I can learn and contribute to the growth of the organization. I like to work on challenging jobs using \nJAVA\n\nJ2EE\n related technologies and \nWebServices\n\nExperience Summary:\n\n         \nSoftware Professional around 4.0+ years of experience in software development.\n\n         \nExperienced in Internet technologies using Java, J2EE, EJB, Servlets, JSP, Java Beans, JDBC and RMI, WebServices.\n\n         \nEfficient in implementing database concepts, having worked on Oracle.\n\n         \nGood Knowledge of various Design Patterns, Architectures and Frameworks.\n\n         \nExposure of EAI, Banking, Insurance domains.\n\n         \nExposure to OOAD and UML techniques.\n\n         \nPossess good working experience of RAD (Rational Application Developer) /WSAD (WebSphere Studio Application Developer) and WAS (WebSphere Application Server) 6.0/5.x.\n\n         \nExcellent verbal, written/documentation and inter-personal communication skills.\nProfessional Experience:\n\n         \nCurrently working in \nIBM Software Labs\n (since Jan 2006) \n\n         \nWorked as a Software Engineer in Maquis Technologies, \nBangalore\n from July 2003 to till Dec 2005.\nPersonal Achievements:\n\n         \nSUN Certified JAVA Programmer (Java 1.4).\n\n         \nSUN Certified Business Component Developer (EJB 2.0).\n\n         \nSUN Certified Web Component Developer.\n\n         \nSUN Certified Developer for Java WebServices.\nEducational Background:\nBachelor of Engg. (Computer Science), \nSambalpur\nUniversity\n, 2003.\nAreas of Expertise:\nThese are some areas abstracted out of much larger works detailed further down.\n\n         \nJava Component-Based Development\n: Application development based on existing high level components and their interaction patterns, including AWT and Swing Components. \n\n         \nJ2EE\n\nThe Java platform for e-commerce and other enterprise grade systems (JSP1.2, 2.0, Servlets 2.3, EJB 2.0)\n\n         \nAsynchronous Message Systems: \nSystems that pass messages asynchronously (JMS)\n\n         \nSOA: \nService oriented architecture\n\n         \nJava Web Services: \nAn interface that describes a collection of operations that are network accessible.\nTraining Session Delivered:\n\n         \n\nJMS (Java Messaging Service using WebSphere Application Server).\n\n         \n\nWebServices.\nTechnical skills:\nLanguages\nProgramming:\nJava\n\nScript, Markup:\nHTML, JavaScript, XML, ANT\n\n\nDatabases\nRDBMS:\nDB2, Oracle\n\n\nApplication Platforms\nJ2EE:\n\nData Access:\nRemoting:\nWeb Application:\n\nIBM WebSphere Application Server, BEA Weblogic Application Server, Apache Geronimo\nJDBC\nRMI, RMI-IIOP, JMS\nApache Tomcat\n\n\n\nProgramming Model\nArchitecture & Frameworks:\n\nJ2EE, Spring, \n\nSOA, WebServices\n\n\n\nRAD Tools\n\n\n\n\n\nOpen Source\n\nEclipse, IBM Rational Application Developer, IBM WebSphere Studio Application Developer, Borland JBuilder.\n\n\n\n\nApache Geronimo\n\n\nServer Components\n\nEJB, JSP & Servlet.\n\nModeling & Design\n\nUML:\n\nRational Rose\n\n\nOperating system\n\nWinNT, Linux, AIX\n\n\nMiscellaneous\n\nCMVC, CVS\n\n\n\n\n\n\n                                                                                             \nProjects Summary\n# WebSphere Application Server System Management Server (SMS) (IBM ISL) \n  \n01/06 to present\nDomain\n             \n            \n: EAI (WebSphere)\nTeam Size \n        \n            \n: 4 members\nResponsibilities:\nRole: Senior Software Engineer\nDevelopment and Maintenance\nPresentations to higher management\nProject Details:\nSystem Management Server side development and maintenance includes the notification framework, discovery service, Process Monitoring, Synchronization service and File transfer.\n\n# WebSphere Application Server System Management Miscellaneous (SMX) (IBM ISL)\n   \n09/06 to present\nDomain\n             \n            \n: EAI (WebSphere)\nTeam Size \n        \n            \n: 4 members\nResponsibilities:\n\nRole: Senior Software Engineer\n\nDevelopment and Maintenance\n\nPresentations to higher management\nProject Details:\nSystem Management Miscellaneous development and maintenance includes avoiding the scenarios such as OOM and Hangs in WebSphere Application server.\n\n# Vault Automation System (CMS)\n   \n05/05 to 12/05\nDomain\n             \n            \n: Banking\nTeam Size \n        \n            \n: 14 members\nResponsibilities:\n            \nRole : Software Engineer\nInvolved in planning & developing server side component using JSP, Servlets & EJB.\nInvolved in analysis of the project module.\nProject Details:\nThis sub-system automates the Cash transaction at the ATM stations and at cashier stations. This sub-system is entered on by authorized bank personnel to monitor and control the cash status at ATMs and with cashier across the region.\nATM - Transaction monitoring and cash replenishment system.\nAuthorized bank personnel can enter the system using proper authorization (where the log keeps record of who entered the system) and keeps track of the currency distribution, replenishment and status of the cassettes at the ATM, Along with other daily audits.\nTreasury ? Currency distribution and monitoring system:\nCassettes issued to be replenished at the ATM are recorded and \n\nmonitored.\nCashier Station ? Daily audits and Currency roster system.\nImpressed money issued to cashiers is done thru this module.\nModule working under:\n\nVAS Manager\n\n# HI-CIA (Mediclaim)\n   \n09/04 to 03/05\nDomain\n                         \n: Insurance\nTeam Size\n                     \n: Eight members\nResponsibility:\n   \n\n         \nRole: Software Engineer\n\n         \nInvolved in developing server side component using Servlets, JSP, Coding & bug fixing.\n\n         \nInvolved in code review.\nProject Details:\n\nMediclaim is a web-enabled application that automates medical insurance. This sub-system takes care of the medical expenses following Hospitalization/Domiciliary Hospitalization of the insured in respect of the situations such as sudden illness, accident or surgery that is required in respect of any disease which has arisen during the policy period.\n\n         \nAutomated the Claim-sub system:\nThe payment of claim is made through Third Party Administrators Users, who have been empanelled by the Company to provide hassle free admission and discharge from the Network hospital without making any payment.\nThe reimbursement of domiciliary hospitalization claims will also be made through by the TPA.\n\n         \nClaim Application Process:\nThe Details of the claims are recorded with relevant check-list of documents attached.\n\n         \nMO Updates:\nUsed to capture, the remarks and recommendations of the medical officer on the proposer?s Medical History.\nHealth Rating Report (HRR) with remarks prepared by MO about proposer.\n\n         \nMO report Verification:\nHRR report compared with the (Customer HRR) CHRR report for threshold deviation.\nModule worked under: Medical Insurance\n\n# AI-CIA (Automobile Insurance)\n   \n05/04 to 09/04\nDomain:\n                        \nInsurance\nTeam Size:\n                    \nEight members\nResponsibility:\n\n\n         \nRole: Software Engineer\n\n         \nInvolved in developing server side component using Servlets, JSP, Coding & bug fixing.\n\n         \nInvolved in code review.\nProject Details:\n\nAutomobile Insurance is a web-enabled centralized application that automates Automobile insurance. This sub system provides the Registration and Renewal of the Automobile Insurance Policy.\nThe Proposal or Renewal Sub System: The Proposal or Renewal Sub System deals with the Registration of a new Automobile Insurance or Renewal of the existing policies.\n\n         \nThe functionalities handled are: Party Sub-system\n\n         \nCustomer: The sub module is used to register the Customer details.\n\n         \nInsured Objects: This module is used to capture the details and condition of the object to be insured.\n\n         \nFraud Detection VDR (Variation Detailed Report): Used to analyze the previous history of the Customer and the vehicle.\nPolicy sub-system\n\n         \nPremium calculation: Based on parameterized inputs generated thru proposal system, premium amount is \n  \ncomputed.\n\n         \nPolicy Preparation: The policy document containing the perils, validity etc is generated.\n\nModule worked under: Auto Mobile Insurance\n\n\n\n\n# Out Patient Management\n   \n11/03 to 03/04\nDomain\n\n\n                      \nHealth Care\nTeam Size:\n                    \n4 members\nResponsibility:\n\n\n         \nRole: Software Engineer\n\n         \nInvolved in developing server side component using Servlets, JSP, Coding & bug fixing.\n\n         \nInvolved in code review.\nProject Details:\n\n         \nThis is a sub-system of Health care provided for the Out patient; the primary objective of this system is to provide better help to customers and hospital management in terms of:\n\n         \nMaintaining and accessing records of patients, by acquiring proper handling of data. \n\n         \nMaintaining the record of doctor?s, checking for the availability. Need to create, add, delete, modify and view the database of the medical personnel. \n\n         \nDoctors could access the record of the patients, view history, recommend lab test, prescribe medication and fix a follow up appointment.\n\n         \nModule also provides a facility to charge the patients for the consultation, test and the medicines. \n\n         \nThis sub system is also capable of generating daily, weekly and monthly reports.\n\nModule worked under: Reception and Cashier Module\n\nPersonnel Details:\nMarital Status\n                \n: Single\nGender\n                          \n: Male\nMobile no\n                      \n: +91-9902033699\nLanguages Known\n          \n: English, Hindi.\nCurrent Location\n            \n: #871, 22nd Cross, 6th \nMain\n, 7th Sector, HSR Layout \nBangalore\n, Karnataka.',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-15',NULL,'2007-10-15','2010-06-08 12:13:25','2010-06-08',11,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(63,'Nandkishore ',NULL,NULL,'Bangalore','kishor@gmail.com',NULL,NULL,'0','91 9916032757','0',NULL,'0','2007-10-13',7,19,'2010-06-08 12:13:25',11,'0',NULL,'200710/15/ATT7979.html','200710/15/DOC55897.doc','           \n                            \nNANDKISHORE \n                                                                                                                                                                 \n\nMobile: +91-9916032757\n   \n                   \n                   \nEmail: \nkishor@gmail.com\n                                                                                                   \n\n                   \nI foresee myself as a successful Software Professional in an organization in the position of trust and responsibility. This I perceive through hard work, sincerity and zeal to excel.\n\n\n\n         \nHaving \nTwo Plus\n Years Experience on Development of Web based applications using Java/J2EE Technologies\n\n\n         \nGood Knowledge of OOPs Concepts, Java Technologies.\n\n         \nHave Good Knowledge to understand the Technical issues reside in different applications.\n\n         \nHeld with responsibilities such as analysis, coding, security, unit testing.\n\n         \nKnowledge in all phases of software life cycle development.\n\n         \n\nInvolved wholly in debugging. \n\n         \n\nWith Good communication skills and inter personnel skills.\n\n         \nGood Experience in developing Web based applications.\n\n         \nWilling to involve in different aspects of development.\n\n         \nInvolved in designing class diagrams using UML.\n\n\n      \nCurrently Working as Software Programmer IQURA at Bangalore, from September 2006 to till date. \n\n      \nWorked as a junior software programmer at Morphues Technologies from April 2005 To August 2006 at Hyderabad.\n\n      \nTook Training and Worked in the field of Hardware and networking at \nSJINFOTECH\n, from June 2001 to Aug 2002.\n\n          \nMaster in Computer Applications\n from Osmania University.\n\nI worked with the technologies using \nj2se, j2ee (jsp, servlets, jdbc, struts)\n and as back end I used \noracle\n data base, Servers like \nTomcat\n and \nweblogic\n with the IDE as \nEclipse\n. Besides to these aspects, I too possess exposure to advanced skills like \nHibernate\n\nWebservices\n and ERP technology such as \nSAP-ABAP\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nProject #1\n\n               \nTitle\n                     \n\n  \nWork Flow Engine.\n               \nPlatform\n            \n   \n\n   \nWindows Xp professional.\n               \nClient\n                   \n\n   \nEnvision labs\n                                                                         \n               \nSoftware\n               \n\n   \nJsp, Servlets.\n               \n               \nDatabase\n              \n\n    \nOracle\n               \nTeam Size\n            \n\n    \n\n               \nDuration\n               \n\n   \n6 months\n                                                          \n\nDescription:\n                       \nThis web application cum automated system had been developed to implement and follow up system for the current existing system. This project would automate the operations of the management, the specific part of the system is to automate the proposals that are submitted to the various departments include technology, process management.\nProject #2\n                \nTitle\n                  \n\n       \nHealthCare Control System.\n                \nPlatform\n            \n\n      \nWindows XP Professional\n                \nClient\n                \n\n       \nJublie Hospitals.\n                \nSoftware\n           \n\n       \nJSP, Servlets, Weblogic 8.0.\n                \nDatabase\n           \n\n       \nOracle8i\n              \nResponsibility\n     \n\n       \nAnalysis and Coding.\n     \n               \nTeam Size\n          \n\n      \n\n               \nDuration\n             \n\n      \n5 months\n                                             \n   \nDescription:\n                    \nThis System has complete automation of the hospital activities. It comprises of In-patient, Outpatient, Staff, Charges, room & bed allotment, and tests, Reports Modules etc.\nThe Software is comprehensive and time saving and easy to access critical information like billing details, patient information, Doctors information and any analysis with respect to the Hospital Business growth.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nProject #3\n     \n       \n                \nTitle\n                  \n\n       \nElectronic Patient medical Record\n                \nPlatform\n            \n\n       \nWindows XP Professional\n                \nClient\n                \n\n       \nJohn Hopkins Hospital.\n               \n\nSoftware\n           \n\n       \nServlets, Jsp, Jdbc.\n                \nDatabase\n           \n\n       \nOracle8i\n\n              \n\nResponsibility\n   \n\n       \nCoding, Unit Testing\n               \nTeam Size\n          \n\n       \n\n                \nDuration\n            \n\n       \n7 months\n\nDescription:\n                        \nThis Project develops a tool to build to validate the patient?s financial insurance information which is provided during the patient?s initial visit. It enables the Interventional Radiologist with an interactive user interface where he/she can directly generate code by just selecting the diagnostic area on an organ image before he/she actually performs invasive procedures.\n\n              \nEnable automatic comparison of the provided data (patient?s personnel /diagnosis / procedure) to applicable regulations, thus, tracking the billing anomalies and reducing the coding related billing denials, to provide a reliable, portable, reusable, maintainable and secure software.\n                   \nIt is user friendly, which is self ?descriptive, menu driven, a comprehensive user manual.\n\nProject #4\n       \n       \n                \nTitle\n                  \n\n       \nAutomatic Order Generation System\n             \n                \nPlatform\n            \n\n      \nWindows XP Professional\n        \n        \nClient\n                \n\n       \nInpack Fabrications Private Limited\n\n                \nSoftware\n           \n\n       \nStruts Frame Work.\n                \nDatabase\n           \n\n       \nOracle8i\n              \nResponsibility\n     \n\n       \nCoding, Unit Testing, Design\n               \nTeam Size\n          \n\n       \n\n                \nDuration\n            \n\n      \n4 months\n\n\n\nDescription:\n              \nThis application developed to automate the transactions of the management as well as deals with employers of the organization. The employers can interact with organization through this application from remote place. Customers directly approach the organization as per their requirements. The organization will respond to the customers as per their needs and send their introduction letter to customer.\n\n                                                                            ','IQURA',1,NULL,'2007-10-15',NULL,'2007-10-15','2010-06-08 12:13:25','2010-06-08',11,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(64,'Manoj Kumar',NULL,NULL,NULL,'manoj123456@yahoo.co.in',NULL,NULL,'0','9966408796','0',NULL,'0','2006-12-29',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-08 12:13:25',11,'0',NULL,'200710/15/ATT7978.html','200710/15/DOC55898.doc','RESUME\nRESUME\n\n\nNAME\nManoj kumar\n        \n\nmail: \nmanoj123456@yahoo.co.in\n\nMb:\n 91-9966408796\n\nProfile Summary\n\nOver 3.5 years of experience in the Software Industry working with\n\nInfosys Technologies Ltd, \nIndia\n in design and development of applications/tools in web based technologies.\nTechnology Skill-set: \nITIL\n based IT Infrastructure & Service Management tools (HP OpenView Suite), \nCore Java, Servlets, XML, HTML, VB-Scripting, and ASP. \nTrained on HP OVCM (Radia), HP NNM\nEducational Qualification: \nB. Tech.\n (ECE) from \nBharati\nVidyapeeth\nCollege\n of Engineering, \nGGSIP\nUniversity\n\nDelhi\n\nCumulative Performance Index :-\n\n76.34%\nAggregates in \nXII\n (CBSE, \nIndia\n) ? 82.0 %, \n\n(CBSE. \nIndia\n\n\n79.0%.\nEngagement Index\n1.\n      \nDuration: June 07 till date: \nWorking as Team Lead for solution design fro ITSM based implementation of ServiceDesk\nProject\n\n\nDesign of resiliency options for local & geographical fail over\n\nClient\n\n\nBritish \nTelecom\n\nUK\n\nLocation:\nHyderabad\n\nIndia\nTeam Responsibilities:\n1.\n       \nInformation gathering for SD implementation in validation environment\n2.\n       \nCreation of acceptance criterion for resiliency options\n3.\n       \nDesign of resiliency & monitoring options \n4.\n       \nPreparation of Test case documents for the proposed design\n5.\n       \nDesign implementation in test environment\n\n& signoff\n2.\n      \nDuration: Dec 2006 till May 2007: \nWorking as Team Lead with System Integration, Infosys Technologies Ltd. with Accelerate solutions team. Involved in product research, POC, proposal writing and effort estimations. \nDec 07 till Mar 07\n: Solution design for enterprise wide deployment of Windows Vista operating system. Worked on following deployment tools:\n\n          \nBusiness Desktop Deployment (BDD) 2007 for Windows \nVista\n\n          \nVista Deployment using Symantec Ghost\n\n          \nApplication compatibility Toolkit\nApr 07 till Jun 07:\n Product research, POC, proposal writing & solution design for \nEMS\n tools (HP OpenView Products)\n\n          \nHP RADIA Packaging\n\n          \nHP OpenView Service Desk 4.5, HP Service Center 6.2 (Integrated ITSM platform)\n\n          \nHP OVO-W, HP NNM\n\n          \nITIL Process Consultancy\n3.\n      \nDuration: July 2006 till Nov 2006: \nWorking as Team Lead with System Integration, Infosys Technologies Ltd. \n       \nProject\n\n\nWINXP Migration(CA)\n\nClient\n\n\nBank Of \nAmerica\n\nUSA\n\n\nLocation:\nBangalore\n\nIndia\nResponsibilities:\n Beeper Support for CA WINXP rollout, Support Portal design and development, Trainer\nBeeper Support:\n\nBeeper support acts as first escalation point for any support issue which remains unresolved for first 30 min. \nSupport Portal:\n\nSupport Portal is a web based intranet portal for accessing all support related tools and utilities based on user access levels. Design and developed in Java (Servlets), it acts as a one stop shop for all needs of support desk. Apart from providing access to support tool, it also provide access to BOA issue logging application for collating call information. \nTechnologies used: \nVbScript, ASP, HTML\n4.\n      \nDuration: January 2006 to June 2006: \nWorked as Team Lead with System Integration, Infosys Technologies Ltd. \nProject\n\n\nWINXP Migration(Mid-Atlantic)\n\nClient\n\n\nBank Of \nAmerica\n\nUSA\n\n\nLocation:\nBangalore\n\nIndia\nResponsibilities: \nSupport Team Lead for offshore support group (10 associates).\n5.\n      \nDuration: March 2005 To December 2005: \nWorked as a developer with System Integration, Infosys Technologies Ltd. \nProject\n\n\nWINXP Migration(GA, SW)\n\nClient\n\n\nBank Of \nAmerica\n\nUSA\n\nLocation:\nAtlanta\n\nUS\nResponsibilities:\n High and Low level Design for Automated Installation Wizard: Automated installation wizard is a tool used during migration process to automatically install and configure various applications without any manual intervention. \nTechnologies used: \nVBScript, HTML, XML\nAchievements: \nAutomated Installation wizard has been recognized by Bank Of America, LDI department for \nGreen Belt Initiative\n\nGreen belt is an initiative in BOA to recognize any process improvement which leads to huge cost savings to Bank of America. After automated install wizard was introduced in Bank Of America during migration rollout, the average rollout time reduced to 5-6 hrs from 7-8 hrs. \n6.\n      \nDuration: Oct 2004 to Feb 2005: \nWorked as a developer with System Integration, Infosys Technologies Ltd. \nProject\n\n\nWINXP Migration(SCA, Mid-west)\n\nClient\n\n\nBank Of \nAmerica\n\nUSA\n\nLocation:\nAtlanta\n\nUS\nResponsibilities:\n Low Level Design and Coding for Deployment Dashboard: Deployment Dashboard tool is used during migration process to monitor activity status on various banking centre servers for issues/ errors and to raise alerts for taking corrective measures. \nTechnologies used: \nASP,\n\nVBScript, HTML, XML, SQL\n7.\n      \nDuration Feb 2004 to Oct 2004 \nWorked as a developer with System Integration, Infosys Technologies Ltd. \nProject\n\n\nWINXP Migration(Fleet, NCA)\n\nClient\n\n\nBank Of \nAmerica\n\nUSA\n\nLocation:\nBangalore\n\nIndia\nResponsibilities:\n Coding for Data Migration and SPS Scripts, Support during Fleet (merger to BOA) rollout. \nTechnologies used: \nVBScript, HTML\n8.\n      \nDuration Oct 2003 to Feb 2004\nProject Name:\n\nInfosys Training\n                      \nROLE: Software Engineer\nInfosys Training:\n Received training on Web technologies, Core Java & Servlets\n                                                \nPERsonal Details\nPassport :\n                      \nValid till 2013\nDate of Birth:\n                \n5th April 1982\nFather?s Name:\n               \nMr. Krishna Nand Pande\nPermanent Address:\n      \nC-12/243, Yamuna Vihar, Delhi-110053',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-15',NULL,'2007-10-15','2010-06-08 12:13:25','2010-06-08',11,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(65,'Mohan Reddy',NULL,NULL,'Hyderabad','mr123456@yahoo.com',NULL,NULL,'0','91 9908195551','0',NULL,'0','2006-11-12',7,19,'2010-06-08 12:13:25',11,'0',NULL,'200710/15/ATT7977.html','200710/15/DOC55899.doc','CURRICULAM VITAE\n\nCURRICULAM VITAE\n\n\nMohan Reddy\nMobile: +91-9908195551\nE-Mail: \n\nmr123456@yahoo.com\n\n\nProfessional Summary:\n\n\n    \nHas \n3.4 Years\n of work experience in \nDevelopment and Project Implementation.\n\n         \nExpertise in developing Web-based n-tier applications with Object Oriented concepts using \nJava\n\n(JDBC, Servlets, JSP)\n\n\n         \nExperience in implementing applications with Model/View/Controller (\nMVC\n) Framework using \nJakarta\n Struts.\n\n         \nProficient in RDBMS: \nOracle 9i,\n and expertise in developing Functions, Triggers, Stored procedures.\n\n         \nWorking on developing Dynamic Reports Using \nxsql \nand\n xsl\n\nParticipated in \nUAT\n (User Acceptance Test) and \nOAT\n (Operational Acceptance Test) Process for \nNepal\n Electric Authority (NEA) at \nKatmandu\n\n\nWork Experience:\n\nWorking as a \nSr. Software Engineer \n\n\nWIPRO\n\nTechnologies\n\nHyderabad\n, from Jul?2006 to till date.\nWorked as a \nProgrammer\n in \nPhoenix\n IT Solutions Ltd, \nVisakhapatnam\n, from Jan?2005 to Jul?2006.\nWorked as a \nJava\n\nProgrammer\n in Ocean Trade Infotech (P) Ltd, \nVisakhapatnam\n, from May?2004 to Jan?2005.\n\nTechnical Skills:\n\nOperating Systems\n    \n: Windows 2K and Linux.\nLanguages\n               \n: C, C++, Java and J2EE.\nJava Technologies\n     \n: JDBC, Servlets, Java Script, JSP, EJB and Struts.\nRDBMS\n          \n: Oracle 9i.\nServers\n                   \n: Web Logic 8.1, Jboss4.0 and Tomcat 5.x.\nIDE/Tools\n                \n\n\nEclipse 3.0, Toad, DefTool and Composer.\nXML Technologies\n     \n: XSQL, XSL, XSLFO and XML.\n\nAcademic Profile:\n\n\n      \nMaster Of Sciences in Information Systems, Nov? 2003\nSir\nC.R.R\nPost\nGraduate\nCollege\n\nAndhra\nUniversity\n, 69%\n\n      \nBachelor Of Computer Applications, Apr? 2001\nBapatla\nCollege\n of Arts & Sciences, \nNagarjuna\nUniversity\n, 60%\n\n      \nBoard of Intermediate Education (M.P.C), Apr? 1998\nPratibha\n\nJunior College\n, Ongole, 77%\n\n      \nSchool of Secondary Education Apr? 1996\nGovt\nHigh School\n, Tallur, 71%\n\n\nProject Profile:\n\nProject#1\n\nEBILL\n\n- Enhancements\n                                                      \n         \nFeb 2007 ? Till Date\n    \n          \nClient\n            \n\nNSTAR, \nBoston\n\nTechnologies \n\n: Java, JSP, Struts, Oracle9i and Web logic 8.1.\nTeam\n            \n: 2.\nRole\n       \n       \n: Sr.Software Engineer.\nTools\n            \n: Eclipse3.0, Ant, PVCS, DefTool, Composer, FTP Commander and SQL\n\n\nNavigator.\nDescription\n   \n\n                             \nEBILL Enhancements has been developed for NSTAR utility to increase the customers to view and pay the bills online. The basic advantages of these enhancements are easy to use registration process, electronic payment options, and De-enrollment process for CSR\'s. \n\nResponsibilities\n\n\n      \nInvolved in the analysis and design of new enhancements and prepared the various documents required for the same.\n\n      \nCoding and Unit Testing.\n\n      \nCode Deployment into Production Server.\n\n      \nSystem Maintenance and Production Support.\n\n\nProject#2\n\nEBILL\n\n- Bill Redesign\n                                                          \n        \nJul 2006 ? Feb 2007\nClient\n            \n\nNSTAR, \nBoston\n\nTechnologies \n\n: Java, JSP, ejb, Struts, Oracle9i and Web logic 8.1.\nTeam\n            \n: 5.\nRole\n       \n       \n: Java Consultant.\nTools\n            \n: Eclipse3.0, Ant, PVCS, DefTool, Composer, FTP Commander and SQL\n\n\nNavigator.\nDescription\n   \n\n                             \nEBILL application has been developed for NSTAR utility to enable their customers to view and pay the bills online. It is a customized version of EDOCS. The basic advantages of this system are easy to use registration process, electronic payment options, and medium to provide bills in different formats. It has interactions with external systems for the operations regarding payments and file transfers. \n\nResponsibilities\n\n\n      \nInvolved in the analysis and design of Bill Redesign and prepared the various documents required for the same.\n\n      \nHad an effective interaction with the onsite team.\n\n      \nCoding and Unit Testing.\n\n      \nWrote Procedures.\n\n      \nSupported for User Acceptance Test from offshore.\n\n      \nCode Fixing for Post Implementation Bugs and Maintenance.\n\nProject#3\n\nCBP NEA\n         \n\n                                                          \n         \n   \n         \nOct 2005 ? Jul 2006\n(Computerized Billing Project for \nNepal\n Electricity Authority)\nClient\n            \n\nNepal\n Electricity \nAuthority\n\nNepal\n\nTechnologies \n\n: Java, JSP, Oracle9i, XSL, XSQL and Jboss 4.0.\nTeam\n            \n: 10.\nRole\n       \n       \n: Developer.\nTools\n            \n: Eclipse3.0, Edit Plus and Toad.\nDescription\n   \n\n                                     \nCommon Billing Program For Nepal Electricity Authority is built on reliable n-tier architecture allowing Customer Care support and billing solution. It is platform-versatile with the system framework powerful enough to handle any volume of transactions. CBP can be easily customized to provide the entire gamut of \nCall\n\nCenter\n and Customer Service Solution. \n\nCBP Monitoring System is a billing cum management information system facilitating\nGeneration of various analytical reports for decision support and statutory requirements.\n\nThe system integrates all the data pertaining to customer care processes for online publishing of reports.\n\nFacilitates flexible generation of reports, which are self explanatory and easy to understand.\n\nResponsibilities\n\n\n      \nDesigned screens using JSP.\n\n      \nInvolved in JavaScript functions for client side Validations.\n\n      \nCoding and Unit Testing.\n\n      \nWrote Triggers and Procedures.\n\n       \nDesigned MVC framework using Velocity Code Generator.\n\n      \nReport Generation through XSQL, XSL.\n\n      \nImplementation at the Client Side.\n\n\nProject#4\n                                                                              \n        \n\nBilling Management System (BMS) \n                                \n        \nJan 2005 ? Sep2005\nClient\n            \n: Eastern Power Distribution Company of A.P.\nTechnologies \n\n: Java, JSP, Oracle9i, XSL, XSQL and Jboss 4.0.\nTeam\n            \n: 8.\nRole\n              \n: Developer.\nTools\n            \n: Eclipse3.0, Edit Plus and Toad.\nDescription\n   \n\n                        \nBilling Management System (BMS) developed was aimed at automating and standardizing the process of billing and generate statutory and analytical reports for the management. Along with monthly bill processing, revenue collection information would also be processed through the system to ensure seamless integration of metering, billing and collection processes with regard to all the categories of Low tension and High-tension consumers of the power distribution utilities.\n\n                        \nA comprehensive product that puts in place customer centric business processes and enable better management of customer needs with the aim of enhanced revenue generation.\n This enterprise wide application is built on modular fashion, wherein the various modules can be deployed individually and future integration with other modules being a smooth and seamless affair. \nResponsibilities\n\n\n      \nDesigned screens using JSP.\n\n      \nInvolved in JavaScript functions for client side Validations.\n\n      \nCoding and Unit Testing.\n\n       \nDesigned MVC framework using Velocity Code Generator.\n\n       \nReport Generation through XSQL, XSL.\n\n      \nImplementation at the Client Side.\n\nProject#5\n      \n                                                                        \n        \n\nCollections\n                                                                            \n       \nJun 2004 ? Dec 2004\nClient\n            \n\nEastern Power Distribution Company of A.P.\nTechnologies \n: Java, JSP, Oracle9i, XSL, XSQL and Jboss 4.0.\nTeam\n            \n: 3.\nRole\n       \n       \n: Developer.\nTools\n            \n: Eclipse3.0, Edit Plus and Toad.\nDescription\n   \n\n                                     \nThe Collection module plays a vital role in this project as it involves in the Revenue Generation. The consumer has the facility to pay the bill either through offline or through online. The module has the facility to receive any type of collection whether it is for consumer bill or it may be a case for new connection or it may be a title transfer etc., The module has the facility to search for the payments he had done either through receipt number or through consumer number. The Consumer had also got the facility to get the details of his transactions either daily or monthly or yearly. The reports had been done using xsql and xsl.\n\nResponsibilities\n\n\n      \nDesigned screens using JSP.\n\n      \nCoding and Unit Testing.\n\nPersonal Profile:\nFull Name\n                \n: Jagan Mohan Reddy Mallu.\nFather\'s Name \n         \n: M.V. Narasimha Reddy.\nDate of Birth \n           \n: 01 July 1981.\nSex\n                        \n: Male.\nMarital Status \n         \n: Single.\nBlood Group\n    \n       \n   \n\n\nB+.\nPassport \n                \n: Available.\nNationality\n               \n: Indian.\nLanguages Known \n    \n\n\nEnglish, Hindi and Telugu.\n\nPersonal Achievements:\n\n\n         \nAwarded Certificate of Excellence for Implementing the Project Successfully. \n\n         \nParticipated in various camps as a NCC Cadet in 2001 with ?C? Certificate.\n\n\n                                                                             \n(Jagan Mohan Reddy. M)\n  ','WIPRO Technologies',1,NULL,'2007-10-15',NULL,'2007-10-15','2010-06-08 12:13:25','2010-06-08',11,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(66,'Monalisa sahoo',NULL,NULL,'Bangalore','a1982@yahoo.co.in','monalisa_sahoo1982@yahoo.co.in',NULL,'0','9342824727','0',NULL,'0','2007-02-12',7,19,'2010-06-08 12:13:25',11,'0',NULL,'200710/15/ATT7976.html','200710/15/DOC55900.doc','Monalisa Sahoo\nCURRICULUM VITAE\n\n\nMonalisa Sharma\n                                \n#16/34, Thimmaraya Swami Masion,\n                                                                                          \n   \n                                                   \nHosur Road\n\nBangalore\n\n                                        \n                                             \n        \n                                                     \nMobile No: +91-80- 9342824727\n                                                       \nE-mail: a1982@yahoo.co.in\n\n\n\n                                                                                                \n     \nProfile\n\nSummary\n   \n\n               \n2.6 years of experience in the field of\n   \nInformation Technology.\n\n               \nCurrent Organization\n: Working as a Project Engineer in \nWipro\n   \nTechnologies\n\nBangalore\n, from July 2006 to till date.\n   \n\n               \nPrevious Organization\n\n\nWorking as a Software Engineer in\n   \nElbrus Global\n\nBangalore\n, from August 2004 to June 2006.\n\n   \n       \nProficient in Web Based Application Programming with Core\n JAVA, JDBC, JSP, SERVLET, EJB.\n\n               \nWorked on various projects, JDBC, JSP, Servlets, EJB, Java Beans, with MySql database. \n\n\n               \nExposure to HLD \ntechniques.\n\n               \nUsed Web logic as application server.\n\n               \nFunctional knowledge in General/Non Life Insurance Business.\n\n               \nExposure to Banking Domain.\n\n               \nExposure to Medical Domain.\n\n               \nExposure to Agile Methodology.\n\n               \nGreat team player, with excellent communication skill.\n\nObjective\n              \n\nAccept responsibility and new challenges, to develop my potential and achieving the glorious height\n   \nin the field of IT environment, where I can efficiently utilize my IT Skills.\n\nTechnical Summary\n\n\n         \nOperating System:\n           \nWindows 98/2000 Professional\n\n\n         \nDatabase:\n                          \nSQL server 7.0, MS Access\n\n\n         \nLanguage:\n                          \nCore Java\n\n\n         \nJ2EE:\n                                \nServlet2.4, JSP1.2, JDBC, EJB2.0, Java Script.\n                   \n                           \n\n         \nMarkup Language:\n            \nXML, HTML.\n\n         \nIDE:\n                                  \nEclipse 3.0\n\n\n         \nTools:\n                                 \nCVS, Smart Draw tools\n, Ant\n\n         \nApplication Servers:\n        \nWeb-Logic 8.1,JBOSS\n\n         \nWeb Servers:\n            \n      \nTomcat 4.1.\n\n         \nAncillary:\n                           \nVarious Design Patterns. \n\n\n\nEducation summary\n\n                  \nB. E in Computer science and Engineering from BPUT Rourkela.\n\n\nProjects Undertaken\n# PHS-Health Device\n\n         \nDomain:\n                         \n    \nMedical\n\n         \nRole:\n                                \nSoftware Engineer.\n\n         \nTeam Size:\n                         \n20\n\n         \nEnvironment:\n                       \nWindows 2000 Professional\n\n         \nTechnology/Software:\n             \nCore Java\n\nEJB,JSP,Struts,HTML,Java Script\n\n         \nTools:\n        \n                       \nEclipse 3.0,Ant\n\n         \nApplication Server:\n                 \nJBoss\n\n         \nDatabase Server:\n                   \nMySql \n\n\n         \nDescription:\n\nThe purpose of this project is to provide medical facility at home. This device connects to other modules to give the product more reliable. Entire project based on NAS technology. The purpose of the project is to interface between medical devices and NAS, to give the information regarding medical checkup or do the medical checkup. \n\n\n     \n# CMS-Website\nDomain:\n          \n                  \n  \nTelecom\nRole;\n                                 \nSoftware Engineer.\nTeam Size:\n                          \n\nEnvironment:\n                        \n\nWindows 2000 Professional\nTechnology/Software:\n               \nJSP,Struts,HTML,Java Script\n\nTools:\n                                 \nEclipse 3.0\nApplication Server:\n                  \nWeb logic\n 8.1\n\nDescription: \nThe purpose of this project is provide a temporary website to provide Information to the users, when the existing three.com.au, business.three.com.au and care.three.com.au are not available\n\nFunctionalities handled:\n\n1. Involved in doing static pages. \n                                               \n2.\n\nInvolved in testing for both static and dynamic pages.\n\n         \nResponsibility:\n Involved in reviews of coding and testing of the functional modules.\n                         \n\n# Mortgage (Vehicle Loan)\n\n         \nDomain:\n                                      \nBanking.\n\n         \nRole:\n                            \n\nSoftware Engineer.\n\n         \nTeam Size:\n                                 \n14\n\n         \nEnvironment:\n                                    \nWindows 2000 Professional\n\n\n                                                                 \n  \nTechnology/Software\n\n                    \nJSP, Servlet, JDBC, HTML, Java beans.\n\n         \nTools:\n                                \nEclipse 3.0 \n\n         \nApplication Server:\n                 \nWeb logic\n 8.1\n\n\n         \nDescription: \nLoan processing is a web-enabled application which Automates\n                     \n       \n      \nVehicle loan. This sub-system takes care of the whole vehicle loan Process\n\n   \n\n   \n    \nFunctionalities handled: \nLoan adjustment, Loan payment & Loan closure after \nre-payment of loan amount to the bank. Daily review, update of EMIs, PDCs pre-\n closure, post ?closure etc in loan.\n\n                            \n    \nResponsibility:\n Involved in reviews of Various Design, coding and testing of the functional modules.\n              \nInvolved in Peer-reviews and Code-Reviews of modules.\n\n\nCIA-F&SP(Fire and special perils)\n\n\n        \nDomain\n\n                              \nInsurance.\n\n\n  \nRole:\n                      \n\nSoftware Engineer.\n\n        \nTeam Size:\n                       \n\n\n        \nEnvironment:\n                    \n     \nWindows 2000 Professional\n\n\n        \nTechnology/Software\n\n           \nJSP, Servlet, JDBC, EJB, HTML, Java beans, Oracle 8i.\n\n        \nTools:\n                                  \nEclipse 3.0, CVS.\n\n        \nApplication Server\n\n              \nWeb logic 8.1.\n\n\n        \nDescription: \nFire\n and special perils is a web-enabled application that\n\nautomates the fire insurance. This sub-system takes care of following things like collapse, explosion, fire, lightning, weight of ice/snow, windstorm.\n                                                     \n\n        \nFunctionality handled:\n\nThe payment of claim is made through third party\n\nadministrator?s users, who have been empanelled by the Company. The various phases of claims are settlement, cover cheque, payment advice.\n                                                          \n     \n\n\n\n\n# HI-MCT(Mediclaim)\n\n        \nDomain:\n                              \nInsurance.\n\n\n  \nRole:\n                      \n  \nSoftware Engineer\n\n\n        \nTeam Size:\n                         \n\n\n        \nEnvironment:\n                          \nWindows 2000 Professional\n\n\n        \nTechnology/Software\n\n      \n     \nJSP, Servlet, JDBC, EJB, HTML, Java beans, Oracle 8i.\n\n        \nTools:\n                        \n\nEclipse 3.0, CVS.\n\n        \nApplication Server\n\n               \nWeb logic 8.1.\n\n        \nDescription\n\nMedi-Claim is a web-enabled application that automates medical insurance. This sub-system takes care of the medical expenses following Hospitalization/Domiciliary.\n             \nHospitalization is insured in respect of the situation like sudden illness or accident.\n\n\n        \nFunctionality handled:\n The payment of claim is made through third party\n     \n    \nadministrator?s users, who have been empanelled by the Company to provide hassle free admission and discharge from the Network hospital without making any payment. The TPA will also make through the reimbursement of domiciliary hospitalization claims\n\nThe various phases of claims are claim application process, MO verification.\n                               \n                   \n\n        \nResponsibility\n\nInvolved in the Process discussions, in developing the Controller (using Servlet) and View (using JSP) in unit testing.\n\n\n\nPersonal details\n   \n\n                \nGender:\n               \nFemale\n                \nMarital Status:\n    \nSingle\n                \nDate of Birth:\n      \n19\nth\n may 1982.\n       \n                       \nContact Address:\n       \n#16/34, Thimmaraya Swami Masion, \nHosur Road\n\n                                                                     \nBangalore\n\n                                                        \n\n\n                                             \n\n\n          \n\n                                   \n\n\n\n      \n\n                \n          \n\n\n\n       \n             \n  \n                                                                        \n\n    \n           \n                   \n\n      \n              \nCURRICULUM VITAE\n\n\nMonalisa Sahoo\n                               \n    \n#16/34, Thimmaraya Swami Masion,\n                                                                                          \n   \n                                                   \nHosur Road\n\nBangalore\n\n                                                                                     \n        \n                \n                                     \nMobile No: +91-80- 9342824727\n                                                       \nE-mail: monalisa_sahoo1982@yahoo.co.in\n\n\n\n                                                                                                     \nProfile\n\nSummary\n   \n\n               \n2.6 years of experience in the field of\n   \nInformation Technology.\n\n               \nCurrent Organization\n: Working as a Project Engineer in \nWipro\n   \nTechnologies\n\nBangalore\n, from July 2006 to till date.\n   \n\n               \nPrevious Organization\n\n\nWorking as a Software Engineer in\n   \nElbrus Global\n\nBangalore\n, from August 2004 to June 2006.\n\n   \n       \nProficient in Web Based Application Programming with Core\n JAVA, JDBC, JSP, SERVLET, EJB.\n\n               \nWorked on various projects, JDBC, JSP, Servlets, EJB, Java Beans, with MySql database.\n\n\n               \nExposure to HLD \ntechniques.\n\n               \nUsed Web logic as application server.\n\n               \nFunctional knowledge in General/Non Life Insurance Business.\n\n               \nExposure to Banking Domain.\n\n               \nExposure to Medical Domain.\n\n               \nExposure to Agile Methodology.\n\n               \nGreat team player, with excellent communication skill.\n\nObjective\n              \n\nAccept responsibility and new challenges, to develop my potential and achieving the glorious height\n   \nin the field of IT environment, where I can efficiently utilize my IT Skills.\n\nTechnical Summary\n\n\n         \nOperating System:\n           \nWindows 98/2000 Professional\n\n\n         \nDatabase:\n                          \nSQL server 7.0, MS Access\n\n\n         \nLanguage:\n                          \nCore Java\n\n\n         \nJ2EE:\n                                \nServlet2.4, JSP1.2, JDBC, EJB2.0, Java Script.\n                                              \n\n         \nMarkup Language:\n      \n      \nXML, HTML.\n\n         \nIDE:\n                                  \nEclipse 3.0\n\n\n         \nTools:\n                                 \nCVS, Smart Draw tools\n, Ant\n\n         \nApplication Servers:\n        \nWeb-Logic 8.1,JBOSS\n\n         \nWeb Servers:\n                  \nTomcat 4.1.\n\n         \nAncillary:\n                      \n     \nVarious Design Patterns. \n\n\n\nEducation summary\n\n                  \nB. E in Computer science and Engineering from BPUT Rourkela.\n\n\nProjects Undertaken\n# PHS-Health Device\n\n         \nDomain:\n                             \nMedical\n\n         \nRole:\n                                \nSoftware Engineer.\n\n         \nTeam Size:\n                         \n20\n\n         \nEnvironment:\n                       \nWindows 2000 Professional\n\n         \nTechnology/Software:\n             \nCore Java\n\nEJB,JSP,Struts,HTML,Java Script\n\n         \nTools:\n                               \nEclipse 3.0,Ant\n\n         \nApplication Server:\n                 \nJBoss\n\n         \nDatabase Server:\n                   \nMySql \n\n\n         \nDescription:\n\nThe purpose of this project is to provide medical facility at home. This device connects to other modules to give the product more reliable. Entire project based on NAS technology. The purpose of the project is to interface between medical devices and NAS, to give the information regarding medical checkup or do the medical checkup. \n\n\n     \n# CMS-Website\nDomain:\n                            \n  \nTelecom\nRole;\n                 \n                \nSoftware Engineer.\nTeam Size:\n                          \n\nEnvironment:\n                        \n\nWindows 2000 Professional\nTechnology/Software:\n               \nJSP,Struts,HTML,Java Script\n\nTools:\n                                 \nEclipse 3.0\nApplication Server:\n                  \nWeb logic\n 8.1\n\nDescription: \nThe purpose of this project is provide a temporary website to provide Information to the users, when the existing three.com.au, business.three.com.au and care.three.com.au are not available\n\nFunctionalities handled:\n\n1. Involved in doing static pages. \n                                               \n2.\n\nInvolved in testing for both static and dynamic pages.\n\n         \nResponsibility:\n Involved in reviews of coding and testing of the functional modules.\n         \n                \n\n# Mortgage (Vehicle Loan)\n\n         \nDomain:\n                                      \nBanking.\n\n         \nRole:\n                            \n\nSoftware Engineer.\n\n         \nTeam Size:\n                                 \n14\n\n         \nEnvironment:\n                                    \nWindows 2000 Professional\n\n\n                                                                 \n  \nTechnology/Software\n\n                    \nJSP, Servlet, JDBC, HTML, Java beans.\n\n         \nTools:\n                                \nEclipse 3.0 \n\n         \nApplication Server:\n                 \nWeb logic\n 8.1\n\n\n         \nDescription: \nLoan processing is a web-enabled application which Automates\n                     \n       \n      \nVehicle loan. This sub-system takes care of the whole vehicle loan Process\n\n   \n\n   \n    \nFunctionalities handled: \nLoan adjustment, Loan payment & Loan closure after \nre-payment of loan amount to the bank. Daily review, update of EMIs, PDCs pre-\n closure, post ?closure etc in loan.\n\n                            \n    \nResponsibility:\n Involved in reviews of Various Design, coding and testing of the functional modules.\n              \nInvolved in Peer-reviews and Code-Reviews of modules.\n\n\nCIA-F&SP(Fire and special perils)\n\n\n        \nDomain\n\n                              \nInsurance.\n\n\n  \nRole:\n                      \n\nSoftware Engineer.\n\n        \nTeam Size:\n                       \n\n\n        \nEnvironment:\n                         \nWindows 2000 Professional\n\n\n        \nTechnology/Software\n\n           \nJSP, Servlet, JDBC, EJB, HTML, Java beans, Oracle 8i.\n\n        \nTools:\n                                  \nEclipse 3.0, CVS.\n\n        \nApplication Server\n\n              \nWeb logic 8.1.\n\n\n        \nDescription: \nFire\n and special perils is a web-enabled application that\n\nautomates the fire insurance. This sub-system takes care of following things like collapse, explosion, fire, lightning, weight of ice/snow, windstorm.\n                                                     \n\n        \nFunctionality handled:\n\nThe payment of claim is made through third party\n\nadministrator?s users, who have been empanelled by the Company. The various phases of claims are settlement, cover cheque, payment advice.\n                                                               \n\n\n\n\n# HI-MCT(Mediclaim)\n\n        \nDomain:\n             \n                 \nInsurance.\n\n\n  \nRole:\n                      \n  \nSoftware Engineer\n\n\n        \nTeam Size:\n                         \n\n\n        \nEnvironment:\n                          \nWindows 2000 Professional\n\n\n        \nTechnology/Software\n\n           \nJSP, Servlet, JDBC, EJB, HTML, Java beans, Oracle 8i.\n\n        \nTools:\n                        \n\nEclipse 3.0, CVS.\n\n        \nApplication Server\n\n               \nWeb logic 8.1.\n\n        \nDescription\n\nMedi-Claim is a web-enabled application that automates medical insurance. This sub-system takes care of the medical expenses following Hospitalization/Domiciliary.\n             \nHospitalization is insured in respect of the situation like sudden illness or accident.\n\n\n        \nFunctionality handled:\n The payment of claim is made through third party\n         \nadministrator?s users, who have been empanelled by the Company to provide hassle free admission and discharge from the Network hospital without making any payment. The TPA will also make through the reimbursement of domiciliary hospitalization claims\n\nThe various phases of claims are claim application process, MO verification.\n                               \n                   \n\n        \nResponsibility\n\nInvolved in the Process discussions, in developing the Controller (using Servlet) and View (using JSP) in unit testing.\n\n\n\nPersonal details\n   \n\n                \nGender:\n               \nFemale\n                \nMarital Status:\n    \nSingle\n                \nDate of Birth:\n      \n19\nth\n may 1982.\n       \n                       \nContact Address:\n       \n#16/34, Thimmaraya Swami Masion, \nHosur Road\n\n                                      \n                               \nBangalore\n\n                                                        \n\n\n                                             \n\n\n          \n\n                                   \n\n\n\n       \n                \n          \n\n\n\n       \n          \n   \n  \n                                                                        \n\n    \n           \n                   \n\n      \n              \nCURRICULUM VITAE\n\n\nMonalisa Sahoo\n                                   \n#16/34, Thimmaraya Swami Masion,\n              \n                                                                            \n   \n                                                   \nHosur Road\n\nBangalore\n\n                                                                                     \n        \n                                                     \nMobile No: +91-80- 9342824727\n                                                       \nE-mail: monalisa_sahoo1982@yahoo.co.in\n\n\n\n                                                                                                     \nProfile\n\nSummary\n   \n\n               \n2.6 years of experience in the field of\n   \nInformation Technology.\n\n               \nCurrent Organization\n: Working as a Project Engineer in \nWipro\n   \nTechnologies\n\nBangalore\n, from July 2006 to till date.\n   \n\n               \nPrevious Organization\n\n\nWorking as a Software Engineer in\n   \nElbrus Global\n\nBangalore\n, from August 2004 to June 2006.\n\n   \n       \nProficient in Web Based Application Programming with Core\n JAVA, JDBC, JSP, SERVLET, EJB.\n\n               \nWorked on various projects, JDBC, JSP, Servlets, EJB, Java Beans, with MySql database.\n\n\n               \nExposure to HLD \ntechniques.\n\n               \nUsed Web logic as application server.\n\n               \nFunctional knowledge in General/Non Life Insurance Business.\n\n               \nExposure to Banking Domain.\n\n               \nExposure to Medical Domain.\n\n               \nExposure to Agile M