o.in',NULL,NULL,'0','0 92442 16126','0',NULL,'0','2006-11-12',7,19,'2010-06-08 12:13:25',11,'0',NULL,'200710/15/ATT7975.html','200710/15/DOC55901.doc','CV Template\nKarthikeyan S\nFuture Focus Infotech Pvt Ltd.,\nEmail: mdu22222@yahoo.co.in, Phone: (0) 92442 16126\n\nExperience Summary \nI am a Business associate with Tata Consultancy Services for the last 6 months with a total of 3.5 years of work experience. My main area of experience has been project delivery of various workflow Applications. I have worked primarily in the domain of banking. My technological forte is Java Technologies and I am also proficient in Java J2EE. My current role is Backup Project Leader of my Project.\n\nProfessional Experience\n\n       \nFuture Focus Infotech Pvt Ltd., Mumbai as Software Engineer & \n               \nFeb?07 ? Till Date\nBusiness Associate with TCS\n\n       \nIPFOnline Ltd, Chennai as Programmer\n                                                   \nJuly?04 ? Jan?07\n\nQualifications\n            \nDegree and Date\nInstitute\nMajor and Specialization\nPercentage\nMSC Computer Science, May 2004\nHindusthan College of Art?s & Science, \nBharathiar\nUniversity\nComputer Science\n60.85%\nBSC Computer Science, May 2002\nMadurai\nKamarajar\nUniversity\nCollege\n\nMadurai\nKamarajar\nUniversity\nComputer Science\n58%\n\nTechnology\nBelow is a list of important hardware, software products and tools that I have worked with.\nOperating System\n                      \nIBM AIX 5.2 ML 6 on Hardware P570, \nWindows\nTechnical Skills\n                         \nJava, JSP, Struts / SSO Framework\nIBM WAS 5.0 & 6.1\nIBM DB2 Version 8.1 & 8.2\nHTML, Struts HTML, JavaScript\nTibco Staffware Classic Version 9.3 & iPE (upcoming)\nTools Used\n                                \nIBM RAD 7.0\nIBM WSAD 5.1\nMicrosoft Visual Source Safe 6.0 (For Version Control)\nOther Activities\n                          \nUpgradation of IBM WAS Server from 5.0 to 6.1\n                                                \nUpgradation of IBM WAS Applications from 5.0 to 6.1\n                                                \nUpgradation of IBM DB2 from 8.1 to 8.2\n                                                \nUpgradation of Tibco Staffware Classic version to Tibco \n                                                \niProcess (Ongoing Activity)\n                                                \nDeployment of IBM WAS Applications on IBM AIX &\nMicrosoft windows\nReview of Code\n\nProject Thesis \nThe details of the various assignments that I have handled are listed here.\n\nProject\nWorkflow & DMS Applications ? Development, Production Support & Enhancements \nCustomer\nHDFC Bank, Mumbai\nPeriod\nFeb-2007 to Till Date\nDescription\nHDFC Bank has few Custom Applications running in Live Production, few in development Stage and few in Enhancement Stage. All Applications are workflow based and Data Management Applications.\nRole\nBackup PL for the Development Project Refund Processing System.\nSolution Environment\nIBM AIX 5.2 ML 6 on Hardware P570(Live, Backup, UAT)\nWindows\n (Development)\nJava, JSP, Struts / SSO Framework\nIBM WAS 5.0 & 6.1 (Both AIX & Windows)\nIBM DB2 Version 8.1 & 8.2 (Both AIX & Windows)\nTibco Staffware Classic Version 9.3 (Both AIX & Windows)\nTools\nIBM RAD 7.0, IBM WSAD 5.1, Microsoft Visual Source Safe (for source code control), Edit+\nHighlights\nInvolved in the Design, Development, Deployment of Applications in UAT, Backup & Live.\nInvolved in the Support of Applications in UAT, Backup & Live.\nInvolved in Providing Release for these Applications.\nTeam Size\nSix Member to Two Member depends upon the project activity\n\n\nProject\nwww.ipfonline.com\nCustomer\nIPFOnline Ltd, Chennai\nPeriod\nJuly-2004 to January-2007\nDescription\nwww.ipfonline.com is a B2B portal that serves as an interactive medium for users from engineering industry and enables them to locate industrial products of their needs. The website is a veritable storehouse of data on industrial products.\nThe Portal features:\nIndustrial Product Profiles\nIndustrial Storefronts\nE-Product Catalogues\nIPF Magazine Advertisements\nSearch Engine\n\nRole\nProgrammer\nSolution Environment\nIBM AIX 4.3 on RS 6000 Hardware\nWindows\nJava, JSP\nIBM WAS 3.02\nIBM DB2 6.0\nTools\nFront Page 2000, Homesite 4.5, MS-VSS (for source code control)\nHighlights\nInvolved in the Development & Maintenance of \nwww.ipfonline.com\nTeam Size\nFour Members.\n\n\nCareer Profile\n\nDates\nOrganization\nRole\nFebruary 2007 to Till Date\nFuture Focus Infotech Pvt Ltd., Mumbai\nClient: TATA Consultancy Services Mumbai\nSoftware Engineer and Business Associate with TATA Consultancy Services\nJuly 2004 to January 2007\nIPFOnline Ltd Chennai\nProgrammer\n\nPersonal Details\n\nDate of Birth\n22-05-1982\nNationality\nIndian',' Future Focus Infotech Pvt Ltd',1,NULL,'2007-10-15',NULL,'2007-10-15','2010-06-08 12:13:25','2010-06-08',11,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(68,'Kumar Padhan',NULL,NULL,NULL,'padhan12345@gmail.com',NULL,NULL,'0','91 9916197068','0',NULL,'0','2008-04-29',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-08 12:13:25',11,'0',NULL,'200710/15/ATT7974.html','200710/15/DOC55902.doc','CV\n\nKUMAR PADHAN\n                                                  \n\n\n Email ID: padhan12345@gmail.com\n                          \n\nMobile\n: +91?9916197068\n    \nObjective\n                                                          \n\nTo become a successful software professional in the field of IT Industry.\n\n\nProfessional Summary\n                                \n\nTotal IT Experience\n             \n\n      \n\n2+yrs\nJava/J2EE Technologies\n       \n\n        \nCore Java , Servlet , JSP , Struts \n\n                                               \nJDBC, JNDI\nWeb Technologies\n              \n\n        \nXML, HTML, Java Script\nApplication server\n               \n\n        \nWeblogic 8.1\nDatabase\n                          \n\n        \nOracle \nTools\n                               \n\n        \nEclipse \nOthers\n                              \n\n        \nVarious design pattern, Oops concept, SDLC \nStrength\n                           \n\n        \nSincerity, Honesty, Good logical ability, \n         \n                                       \n             \n                                                \nHardworking\n\nOrganizational Details\n                              \n   \n\nCurrent company\n                \n\n        \nVerna Info Solutions, \nBangalore\nEmployment period\n              \n\n        \nJuly 2005 till date\nCurrent Job Designation\n       \n\n        \nSoftware Engineer.\n\n\nEducational Profile\n                                     \n\nBachelor of Engineering in Electronics & Telecommunication from\nBPUT, Orissa in 2005.\n          \n\n\nTechnical Skills\n                                             \n\nOperating Systems\n             \n\n        \nWindows XP/2000\nProgramming Languages\n       \n\n        \nJava\nJ2EE Technologies\n              \n\n        \nServlet , JSP , Struts, JDBC, JNDI\nWeb Technologies\n              \n\n        \nXML, HTML\nApplication server\n               \n\n        \nWeblogic 8.1\nWeb Server\n                       \n\n        \nTomcat \nDatabase\n                          \n\n        \nOracle 9i\nTools\n                               \n\n        \nEclipse \nScripting\n                           \n\n        \nJava Script\nSource control\n                   \n\n        \nCVS\n\n\n\nProjects\n                                                            \n\n#1.Banking Online\n                                                                                                         \n\nDuration\n                            \n\n\nFeb 2007 till date\nTeam Size\n                         \n\n12\nOperating System\n           \n\n Windows 2000\nTechnology\n                       \n\nServlet, JSP, JDBC, Struts 1.1, Weblogic 8.1, Oracle 9i, \n    \n\n         \n  \nEclipse\nSource management\n      \n\ncvs\n\nResponsibilities:\n            \nDesigning JSP pages.\nResponsible for the development of controller.\nCreating Java Beans.\n\nDescription:\n              \n\nBanking information System is a Package developed for\n\nonline banking. \nThis project is developed to handle various transactions involved in the banking system and involves generation of record for the new account holder, updating of database depending on the type of transaction involved and this project effectively handles withdrawals deposits and closing of accounts. \nThe services offered by this bank includes Accessing account details, Bill payments, Funds transfer, Service requests, Credit cards etc., Existing account holders can view their account details\n\nby looking into the site\n\nand new users can apply for an account Online. We will also provide other facilities such as Interest Calculator, Foreign Exchange Calculator etc on this site.\n\nVarious modules in the application are Client Application Entry and Registry, Membership, Transactions, Bill Payment Deposits, Loans, Closing memberships or deposits, Payment and Reports.\n\n\n#2. Web Shopping Application (WSA)\n                                                                       \n\nDuration\n                            \n\n May 2006 to Jan 2007\nTeam Size\n                         \n\n10\n                   \nOperating System\n           \n\n Windows 2000\nTechnology\n                       \n\nServlet, JSP, JDBC, Struts, Weblogic 8.1, Oracle 9i, \n         \n\n         \n  \nEclipse\nSource management\n      \n\nCVS\n\nResponsibilities:\n            \nInvolved in the development of controller. \nInvolved in developing JSP pages.\n\nDescription\n\n                              \n\nThe objective of this product is to provide online shopping to all users i.e. the user can buy any product from home with the help of internet. All information?s about the products are displayed on the web pages. The modules in this project are Shopping, Payment System and Shipping into the address place. To buy a product the customer select the product and see all information about the product i.e. color, size, type etc. After choosing his/her desired options, the customer order for that .For this he has to enter his address, type of payment i.e. by credit card or any other mode.\n\n\n\n#3. Airline Reservation System(ARS)\n                                            \nDuration\n                            \n\n Oct 2005 to Apr 2006\nTeam size\n                          \n\n\n                          \nOperating System\n           \n\n Windows 2000\nTechnology\n                       \n\nJava, JDBC, Servlet, JSP, Struts Framework, Oracle9i,\n          \n      \n  \nApache Tomcat.\nSource management\n      \n\nCVS\n\nResponsibilities:\n            \nInvolved in the GUI creation.\nNormalization of database tables.\nDocumentation of the project\n\nDescription:\n                                                \nThis is an Internet application for Reservation of ticket for Air lines. This consist of reservation, cancellation and query module. For cancellation of ticket the user can request through phone or by email or personally. The system user enter the information about the ticket and the validity is checked by retrieving information?s from the database. Then the request is processed.\n\n\nPersonal Profile\n                                           \n\nGender\n          \n: Male\nDate of Birth\n            \n\n22nd July 1980\nMarital Status\n          \n: Single\nFather?s Name\n\n: Mr. Dasarathi Padhan\nLanguages Known\n     \n: English, Hindi, and Oriya.\nPermanent Address\n   \n: At/PO-Rupra Road, Dist-Kalahandi\n                             \n\nPIN-766101\n                             \n\nOrissa.\n\n\nThe informations furnished above are true to the best of my knowledge.\n\n\n\n                   \nBrajesh Kumar Padhan\n                  ',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-15',NULL,'2007-10-15','2010-06-08 12:13:25','2010-06-08',11,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(69,'Manish Kumar Patel',NULL,NULL,NULL,'patel00ng04@yahoo.com',NULL,NULL,'0','9886016720','0',NULL,'0','2007-08-31',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-08 12:13:25',11,'0',NULL,'200710/15/ATT7973.html','200710/15/DOC55903.doc','Address:\nAddress:\nBTM Layout 2\nnd\n Stage,\n                                             \n     \nMobile\n: 9886016720\nBangalore-560068\n                                     \n               \nEmail-id: patel0004@yahoo.com\n\n                                   \n\nObjective:\n\nSeeking a technically challenging position in the Software industry, providing a highly motivated, progressive, friendly environment, encouraging the pursuit of career advancement and expand my knowledge and skills especially in Software Testing.\n\nExperience Summary:\n\n\n         \nMore than 2.7 years of extensive experience in \nSoftware Development and Testing\n in different Technologies.\n\n         \nMotivated and hardworking individual with the ability and enthusiasm to learn and excel.\n\n         \nWell organized, energetic and creative.\n\n         \nCan effectively work both in a team and individually.\n\n         \nWilling to move towards \nSoftware Testing\n, especially in Automation Testing or White-Box Testing.\n\nExperience Profile:\n\n\n         \nWorking as Programmer Analyst in MindTree Consulting Pvt. Ltd., \nBangalore\n from August 2005 to till date.\n\n         \nWorked as Project Trainee in Pacific IT Solution, \nBangalore\n from January 2005 to July 2005.\n\nProfessional Qualification:\n\n\n         \nBachelor of Engineering (Computer Science) ?2000-2004? from ?\nRungta\nCollege\n of Engineering & Technology?, Bhilai affiliated to \nRaipur\nUniversity\n, Chhattisgarh.\n\nTechnical Skills:\n\n\n         \nTesting Tool:\n           \nWinrunner, QPT, Test-Director\n\n         \nLanguages: \nCore JAVA, PowerBuilder, Oracle-pl/sql\n\n         \nDataBase: \n               \nOracle 8i, ML-SQL 2000/05 Server\n\n         \nReporting Tools: \n     \nCrystal\n Reports, Actuate Reporting Tool\n\n         \nOperating System: \n\nWindows 98/2000/XP/NT\n\n         \nOthers:\n                   \nSiebel, Toad, Microsoft Visio\nPVCS Version Manager, Microsoft VSS\n\nArea of Interest\n\n\nSoftware Testing (Automation and White-Box Testing)\n\n         \nHas sound knowledge in Software Testing, Software testing Life cycle.\n\n         \nExpertise in Unit Testing and good Knowledge in Manual and Automation Testing both.\n\n         \nSince I had exposure to development and enhancement process in various technologies and domain, definitely it will be helpful to me to do root cause analysis while doing testing.\n\nProject Experience:\nProject #1\n                   \n\n           \nEquipment Management Customer One Touch (EMCOT)\nClient\n                            \n\n           \nGE ? \nTFS\n\nUSA\nDuration\n                        \n\n           \nFrom \n\nst\n Aug 2005\n to \n15\nth\n Nov 2005\nPlatform / DB\n                 \n\n           \nSiebel / JAVA / VBScript / JavaScript\n\nDescription\n      \n              \n\n\n                      \n\nEquipment Management Customer One Touch (EMCOT)\n is an application, which enables you to store, retrieves, and manage details of your customers. Using EMCOT, you can store, manage, and retrieve information efficiently. EMCOT has tools that validate and standardize the information that you enter. Hence, there are fewer chances of entering duplicate or incorrect records.\nEMCOT\n deals with two businesses namely TFS (Trailer Fleet Services) and MOD (Modular Spaces).\n\nEMCOT is widely used by Sales Agents, Managers of TFS and MOD.\nGE Modular Space brings you value through convenience, reliability and profitability. GE MOD provides building solutions for Construction, Healthcare, Education and Industrial. Its breath of offering includes mobile offices in a variety of configurations, versatile modular complexes, and fiberglass equipment enclosures. And that?s not all-ease you?re planning process with GE Modular Space?s convenient options such as furniture, steps decks and ramps, wireless security systems, and insurance services.\n\nRole-played:\n      \n1. \nInvolved in Development, Enhancement and maintenance process.\n2.\n       \nInvolved in Unit Testing, and Bug Fixing.\n\nProject #2\n                   \n\n           \nBusiness Performance Compensation (BPC TIP/MOD)\nClient\n                            \n\n           \nGE ? \nTFS\n\nUSA\nDuration\n                        \n\n           \n16\nth\n Nov 2005\n to \n01\nst\n Feb 2006\nPlatform / DB\n                 \n\n           \nOracle 9i, PL/SQL, PowerBuilder\nDescription\n             \n       \n\n           \nBPC\n is a Power Builder and Oracle based system, which takes care of calculating the commission involved in the sales and leases of Modular units based on the information regarding the commission plans and eligibility criteria of sales representatives.\n\nGE Equipment Services TIP/Space (GECTIP/Space)\n is a part of GE Equipment Services, which are the financial services ?arm? of General Electric Corporation (\nGE\n). GE Equipment Services Transport International Pool (\nGECTIP\n) is the industry leader in the renting, leasing, selling and financing of commercial over-the-road, storage and intermodal trailers, with a fleet of around 244,000 trailers and 227 branches in North America, which includes the United States and Canada. GE Equipment Services Modular Space (\nGECMS\n) is the industry leader in the rental, leasing and sales of modular buildings, with a fleet of around 90,000 units and over 100 branches in \nNorth America\n\nRole-played:\n      \n1.\n   \n\nInvolved in Development, Enhancement and maintenance process.\n2.\n       \nInvolved in Unit Testing, and Bug Fixing.\nProject #3\n                   \n\n           \nGE TIP HomeRun Application\nClient\n                            \n\n           \nGE ? \nTFS\n\nUSA\nDuration\n                        \n\n           \nFrom\n\n28\nth\n Nov 2005\n to \n28 June 2006\nPlatform / DB\n                 \n\n           \nOracle 9i, PL/SQL, PowerBuilder\n\nDescription\n             \n       \n\nGE Capital Transport International Pool & ModSpace (GE-TIP ModSpace) is an Industry leader in the rent, lease and sale of Trailers. GETIP has developed a Client/Server HOMERUN Application to serve its operation?s function of the business.\n\nThe HOMERUN application supports the users at several GETIP branches and Devon Service Centre. It caters to the order process of the trailer rent, lease and sale and repair operations.\n TIP system consisting of modules such as Inventory, Reservation, Customer, Lease, Sales and Collections. Enables TIP employees to see different aspects of the job.\nRole-played:\n      \n1. \n  \nInvolved in Development, Enhancement and maintenance process.\n2.\n       \nInvolved in Unit Testing, and Bug Fixing.\n\nProject #4\n                   \n\n           \nDevelopment and\n\nMigration of Actuate Reports\nClient\n                            \n\n           \nANZ, \nAustralia\nDuration\n                        \n\n           \nFrom\n\n10th July 2006\n to \n9th November 2006\nPlatform / DB\n                 \n\n           \nActuate Reporting Tool\n\nDescription\n             \n       \n\n           \nThis project was to develop new reports and to migrate existing Actuate Reports for Murex, high profile financial software used by Banks. Around 180 actuate repots was developed and migrated for ANZ \nBank\n\nAustralia\n\nRole-played:\n      \n1. \n  \nInvolved in Development, Enhancement and maintenance process.\n2.\n       \nInvolved in Unit Testing, and Bug Fixing.\n\n\nProject #5\n                   \n\n           \nSoftrax - Contrax\nClient\n                            \n\n           \nSoftrax\n\nUSA\nDuration\n                        \n\n           \nFrom\n\n28\nth\n Nov 2005\n to till date\nPlatform / DB\n                 \n\n           \nOracle 9i, MS-SQL Server, PowerBuilder, Visual J++, Crystal Report\n\nDescription\n             \n       \n\nSoftrax - Contrax is a flexible, yet powerful tool for managing complex subscription and transaction billing, and for managing associated revenue streams. With it you can easily implement new contract based business models, automate billing and revenue recognition, simplify administration of contracts, and manage critical financial and services information. Completely integrated with Softrax Operations and Financials to ensure efficient end-to-end management, Contrax is a complete billing and business solution.\n\nRole-played:\n      \n1. \n   \nInvolved in Development, Enhancement and maintenance process.\n2.\n       \nInvolved in Unit Testing, and Bug Fixing.\n\nPersonal Profile:\n\nName\n                \n        \n: Manish Kumar Patel\nFather?s Name\n           \n: Shri Hari Narayan Patel\nDate of Birth\n             \n\nJune 04, 1982\nLanguage Known\n       \n: English, Hindi\nMarital Status\n    \n        \n: Single\nPassport Status\n\n        \n: Available\nHobbies\n             \n        \n: Cooking, Light and Romantic music, Playing T.T.\n\nI here by declare that the above information is true to the best of my knowledge & belief.\n\nDate:\n                                                                                                    \n\nManish Kumar Patel\n\nPlace:\n                                           \n                                                          ',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-15',NULL,'2007-10-15','2010-06-08 12:13:25','2010-06-08',11,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(70,'Kamesh  ',NULL,NULL,'Hyderabad','dbk@yahoo.com',NULL,'040 23720511','0','919866558381','0','9246653592','0','2007-02-12',7,19,'2010-06-08 12:13:25',11,'0',NULL,'200710/15/ATT7972.html','200710/15/DOC55904.doc','Resume of\n                                    \n\n\nKamesh\n                                             \n                           \n            \nMobile:+919866558381,9246653592\n[Software Engineer]\n                                \n                  \n                  \n   \nEmail:\ndbk@yahoo.com\n\nA Self-motivated professional with strong analytical, communication and client liaison skills, having an understanding of the value of time, cost and quality of work. Can assure of the best of commitment & productivity. \n3 years \nof IT experience in Software Design & Development. \n\nPROFESSIONAL SUMMARY:\n\n\n       \nHave Strong exposure to Client/Server, Multi-tier and \nEnterprise\n application development using \nJava,\n\nJ2EE, JSP, Servlets, Oracle, JDBC, HTML, and Web Logic\n\n\n       \nExperienced in development, deploying and packaging of different types of software components. \n\n       \nExcellent inter-personal and communication skills and the ability to work as part of a team.\n\n       \nAbility to work in-group as well as independently with minimal Supervision.\n\n       \nAbility to learn new languages and tools quickly.\n\n       \nHaving strong analytical and problem solving skills.\n\nPROFESSIONAL EXPERIENCE:\n\nWorking in \nCogent Software Technologies\n\nHyderabad\n as a \nSoftware Engineer\n from \nAuguest?04 ?Till date\n\n\nEDUCATIONAL QUALIFICATION:\n\n\n       \nM.C.A\n from \nIGNOU.\n\n       \nB.Sc\n from \nAndhra\nUniversity\n\n\nTECHNICAL QUALIFICATION:\n\n\n       \nDiploma in Advanced Software Technology DAST Course from \nCMC\n\n\n       \nBrainbench\n Certified in \nJ2EE Experts.\n\n\nTECHNICAL SKILLS:\n\nOperating System\n                      \n: Windows 9x, Windows XP\n        \n    \nProgramming Languages\n            \n: Java, C++, C\n        \n    \nServer Side Programming\n           \n: JDBC, Servlets, JSP, EJB\n            \nWeb/Scripting Languages\n           \n: HTML\nWeb / Application Servers \n          \n: Tomcat, Web Logic\n        \n    \nDatabase\n                                  \n: Oracle 8i, Ms- Access\n\n\n\n\n\nPROJECT DETAILS:\nPROJECT #1:\n            \nTitle\n                             \n: Schools Resource Planning Software\n            \nDuration\n                       \n\nOngoing from \nDec\'06 \nClient\n                           \n\n\nInfo People corp, \nNew Jersey\n\nUSA\nRole\n                             \n: Team Member\nDescription:\n            \nA Web based application for Schools & Colleges, targets all those Educational Institutes, which would like to automate the entire functioning of the school including all its branches online. This system is being developed to help schools make use of the\n\nnew\n\nemerging\n\ntechnologies\n\nand take the day-to-day management load off the backs of\n\ntheir\n\nadministration and also to provide up to date information to the parents\n\nregarding\n\ntheir wards. Administration, Admission, Fee, Attendance, Exam, Medical, HR, Timetable, Accounts, Library, Inventory, Hostel, Transport & Health. It also takes care of\n\ncollection\n\nof\n\nfines\n\nfor\n\nthe\n\nlate\n\npayments.\n\nThe reports were generated in such a way that the school can\n\nhave\n\n\n\ntrack\n\nof the income on different types of fees.\nResponsibilities:\n\n         \nInvolving in Development of Modules\n\n\n         \nInvolving in Developing screens using HTML.\n\n         \nInvolving in Writing business logic using Servlets and JSP.\n\n         \nInvolving in unit & integration testing\n          \n\nEnvironment:\nDevelopment Environment\n           \n: JDBC, SERVLETS, JAVA-BEANS, JSP,EJB\nWeb Server\n                               \n: WebLogic 8.1\nDatabase\n                  \n    \n            \n: Oracle 8i\n\nPROJECT #2:\n            \nTitle\n                             \n: Doctor Ayurveda\n            \nDuration\n                       \n: Jan?06 to Nov\'06\nClient\n                           \n\n\nRani \nHealth Care\n\nUSA\nRole\n                             \n: Team Member\nDescription:\n           \nA Web based application to help the people who are suffering from chronic diseases online.\n\nFor the first time the user has to register him self with his past health record.\n\nThe data, which has been entered by the patient, will be shown in the form of graph to the doctor.\n\nThe panel of doctors will discuss the health condition of the patient; suggestions of the panel are made available to the patient. One of the features of the site is the student?s forum, where they can have discussions with the experts.\n\nDay to day changes in the field of Ayurveda is reported to the registered users.\n\nThe site also has the facility to order the medicines and health magazines online.\n\nIt also gives elaborate description of yoga and its benefits.\nResponsibilities:\n\n         \nInvolved in Developed of\n\nModules\n\n\n         \nInvolved in Developed screens using HTML.\n\n         \nInvolved in business logic using Servlets and JSP.\n\n         \nInvolved in unit & integration testing.\nEnvironment:\nDevelopment Environment\n           \n: JavaScript, JAVA2.0, HTML, JDBC, JSP \nWeb Server\n                              \n  \n\n: WebLogic 8.1\nDatabase\n                   \n               \n: Oracle 8i\n\nPROJECT #3:\n\n            \nTitle\n                             \n: Online Purchasing\n            \nDuration\n                       \n: April?05 to Dec?05\nClient\n                           \n\n\nSilver Line Industries , \nUSA\nRole\n                             \n: Team Member\nDescription:\nThe application is an online computer product store, which enables customers to buy the computer products online. The user can select the product and quantity. This is a web-based application. It reduces the duplication work, Maintain log information and generates automatic alerts.\n\nResponsibilities:\n\n         \nWeb pages are developed using HTML\n\n         \nDeveloped the Login screen and products screen.\n\n         \nDone server side programming using Servlets.\n\n         \nAccessed Database from Servlets using JDBC API.\n\n         \nResponsibilities for the maintain the application in production.\nEnvironment:\nDevelopment Environment\n           \n: JavaScript, HTML, JDBC, JSP, Servlets \nWeb Server\n             \n                  \n            \n\n\nWebLogic 7.0\nDatabase\n                  \n                \n: Oracle 8i\n\nPROJECT #4:\n            \nTitle\n                             \n: Net Conference\n            \nDuration\n                       \n: Sept?04to March?05\nClient\n                           \n\n\nNEC, \nHyderabad\nRole\n                             \n\n\nTeam Member\nDescription:\nThis project ?Net Conference? is an internet application and developing to transfer the messages between employees through internet in java languages using java as front end .\n   \nThe main aim of ?Net Conference? is to share ideas between the employees. The administrator will add the employees to conference. The primary features of the project entitled ?Net Conference? are high accuracy, design, flexibility and easy availability and also it uses data \n            \nbasetables. Representing entities and relationship between entities.\n\nEnvironment:\nDevelopment Environment\n           \n: HTML, JDBC, JSP, Servlets \nWeb Server\n                               \n: WebLogic 7.0\nDatabase\n                   \n   \n            \n: Oracle 8i\n\nPERSONAL DETAILS: \nFather?s Name\n             \n\n           \nD Kameswara Sarma\nMarital Status\n              \n\n           \nSingle\nLanguages Known\n       \n\n           \nEnglish , Hindi ,Telugu\n    \nPresent Address\n           \n\n           \nD.No :6-3-240/5,Prem Nagar,\n                                                \nBanjaraHills, Road no:1,\n                                    \n\n           \nHyderabad\n\n        \n040 ? 23720511\n\nPlace: \nHyderabad\n                                                           \n         \n\n(D. B. K. KAMESH)\nDate:','Cogent Software Technologies',1,NULL,'2007-10-15',NULL,'2007-10-15','2010-06-08 12:13:25','2010-06-08',11,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(71,'Chandra',NULL,NULL,'Chennai','k81@gmail.com',NULL,NULL,'0','91 9241212829','0',NULL,'0','2007-02-12',7,19,'2010-06-08 12:13:25',2,'0',NULL,'200710/15/ATT7971.html','200710/15/DOC55905.doc','CURRICULUM VITAE\n\nCURRICULUM VITAE\n                                                                                                      \n\n    \n                                                                          \nE-mail : k81@gmail.com\nCHANDRA\n                   \n           \n\nMobile: +91- 9241212829\n       \n\n\n\nProfessional Summary\n\n\n       \nOver 3.1\n\nyears of experience in IT.\n\n       \nExperience in designing, developing and project implementation, support functions and software requirements study.\n\n       \nProficient in writing application using JAVA.\n\n       \nImplemented Connectivity to databases using JDBC API.\n\n       \nKnowledge in writing web-based application using Java Script, HTML and Servlets.\n\n       \nHas comprehensive knowledge of MVC2 Architecture\n\nand has design and development skills in J2EE\n\nFamiliar with Application Servers and databases.\n\n       \nHas strong communication and team building skills and has the exposure to customer IT environments in various projects.\n\n\nWork Profile:\n\nWorking as a Software Development engineer in \nCovansys Corporation Ltd.\n\n\nfrom August 2004 to till date.\n\n\nSoftware Skill Set:\n\nLanguages\n                                  \n: Java, SQL, HTML, XML\nMiddleware Technologies\n               \n: J2EE, JDBC, Servlets, JSP, EJB\nServers\n                                      \n: BEA Weblogic 8.1, Tomcat 4.1\nDatabases\n                                  \n: Oracle 8i\nOperating Systems\n                       \n: Windows 9X/2000/NT/XP.\nIDE / Configuration Tools\n               \n: Eclipse\n\n\nEducational Qualifications:\n\nPost Graduation\n                          \n\n   \nM.Sc(I.T) from \nAnna\nUniversity\n\n\nGraduation\n                                 \n\n   \nB.C.A\n   \nfrom \nOsmania\nUniversity\n\n\nIntermediate\n                              \n\n   \nBoard of Intermediate Education, A.P.\n\nSSC\n                                           \n\n   \nICSE, \nDelhi\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nProjects Profile:\n\nProject # 1\n        \n\n                                                       \n     \nMAR 2007 ? till date\n\nProject Name\n            \n\n\n\nContainer Monitoring System\nClient\n               \n      \n  \n\n\nHyper war U.S.A\nTeam Size\n          \n       \n\n\n\nRole\n                            \n\n\n\nTeam member\nTechnologies\n\n            \n\n\nJava, Servlets, JSP, JDBC, HTML, JavaScript, Oracle 8i.\nEnvironment\n             \n\n\n\nWindows 2000, Web logic Server 8.1. \n\n\n   \n                             \n    \n    \nDescription:\n      \n                             \nCMS system aims at monitoring the container moving from port to depot/port through the consignee place. CMS will have different Liners and customers. Each Liner has containers. The CMS system aims at monitoring only those containers, which are asked by the Liner. Liner with whom CMS has contract will\n   \nsend a flat file providing the information about the containers to be monitored. Sometimes, the container can be loaded with goods for re-exporting and can be sent empty to port instead of depot for repositioning. \n                             \nIf the Customer has held the containers more than the allowable number of days, then detention charges will be incurred for him.\n\nThe customer will be paying the amount for the invoices raised. In case of failure to do so, the system waits for predefined no of days (Credit days), after which the customer will be put under the Black List. The black listed customer will not be allotted any new containers unless he is removed from that Black List. Once the payment is received from the customer (detention charges), a part of it will be reimbursed to the concerned liner.\n\n\nContribution:\n\n       \nDesigned UI Pages\n\n       \nInvolved in Developing\n\nMaster Module at Business logic layer\n\n       \nInvolved in analyzing the PRS(Project Requirements Specification)Coding, Identifying the Primitive test cases\n\n       \nInvolved in Unit Testing.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nProject # 2\n               \n                                                 \n   \nFEB 2006 ? FEB 2007\n\nProject Name\n            \n\n\nAssessment Management System\nTeam Size\n                  \n\n\n\nRole\n                            \n\n\nTeam member\nTechnologies\n\n          \n\n\nJava, Servlets, JSP, JDBC, HTML, JavaScript, Oracle 8i.\nEnvironment\n             \n\n   \nWindows 2000, Web logic Server7.0. \n\nDescription\n\n\nThe Assessment Management Tool is part of the E-tool products. It is an evaluation tool which enables authoring of questions in a wide range of formats. The questions can then be assessable into variety of tests, quizzes, surveys, and questionnaire.\n\n          \nThe AMS supports 21different questions types. Learning objects such as images, videos, clips and audio can be used as part of a question. Mathematical symbols and Chemical formulae are fully supported. As questions are created they are added to a question bank. These then can be shared with other authors and used in variety of test formats.\n                   \nCompany Management System has 6 modules\n\n         \nUser\n\n         \nQuestion Bank\n\n         \nAssessment\n\n         \nRole\n\n         \nSetup\n\n         \nEvaluation\n\n                   \nContribution:\n\n       \nInvolved in \nDesign\n and coding of user and installation modules.\n\n       \nInvolved in writing \nServlets\n and \nJSP?s.\n\n       \nScreen designing using \nHTML\n and \nJSP?s.\n\n       \nInvolved in \ntesting\n and \ndebugging\n of \nServlets.\n\n       \n\n\n\nProject # 3\n                                                   \n          \n         \n  \nMAR 2005 ? JAN 2006\n\nProject Name\n            \n\n\nTransactional Messaging System\n              \n\nClient\n                          \n\n\nBooyah Enterprizes, California.USA\n\nTeam Size\n                  \n\n\n\nRole\n                            \n\n\nTeam member\nTechnologies\n          \n\n\nJava, Servlets, JSP, JDBC, EJB, HTML, JavaScript, Oracle 8i.\nEnvironment\n           \n\n\nWindows 2000, Web logic Server7.0. \n\n\nDescription\n    \n\n                        \nTransactional Messaging System (TMS) will process bi-directional transactional (Incoming and Outgoing) Requests and Responses messages between BOOYAH! Enterprises Inc ADMIN TOOL, which is sub-component of TMS, tool will be built for BOOYAH! to create, process, validate and send (using TMS) out-bound Program\n\nRegistration, Merchant Registration, Terminal Registration, Card Status.\n       \n                 \nIt will process these Registration Requests messages and then will send corresponding Registration Acknowledgement Response XML messages back to BOOYAH! for each Registration Request sent from BOOYAH! These Response messages are then received by TMS at BOOYAH! Will be processed, validated and stored in Oracle (need to Interface compatible with MySql 4.0.18) database at BOOYAH! Using built-in business logic.\n\n\n\nContribution:\n\n       \nDeveloped User interface using JSP.\n\n       \nDeveloped front-end design using html, java script.\n\n       \nParticipated in coding using java and developed components using jsp, servlets.\n\n       \nCoordinated with team members in fixing the bugs with manual testing.\n\n\nProject # 4\n                                                             \n   \nAUG 2004 - FEB 2005\n\nProject Name\n            \n\n\nMedisol Medical Resource Management\n                                                             \nClient\n                          \n\n\nMedisol UAE\nTeam Size\n                  \n\n\n\nRole\n                            \n\n\nTeam member\nTechnologies\n\n          \n\n   \nJava, Servlets, JSP, JDBC, EJB, HTML, JavaScript, Oracle 8i.\nEnvironment\n           \n\n\nWindows 2000, Web Server2.0. \n\nDescription\n          \nThe Medisol is a health service solution for healthcare organizations. It enables practices to maintain complete patient information; manage patient, physician and resource scheduling. Medisol consists of different modules like the Patient module, scheduling, Accounts, pharmacy, lab and employee module.\n\nRequisite procedures of patient admission, storage of his/her medical records, prescription details, bill details etc are maintained in Patient module. The lab module makes available all the various reports along with the diagnostic reports. Furthermore it takes care of Stock, purchase, payments and alarm new order level. Pharmacy module takes care of Stock, purchase, sales, payments, and batch expiry date and alarm new order level. \n\nContribution:\n\n       \nDesigned UI Pages\n\n       \nDesigned and developed database model.','Covansys Corporation Ltd',1,NULL,'2007-10-15',NULL,'2007-10-15','2010-06-08 12:13:25','2010-06-08',2,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(72,'Dhamodharan sriram',NULL,NULL,NULL,'dhamu006@yahoo.com','consul_03@yahoo.com',NULL,'0','9841707250','0',NULL,'0','2008-04-29',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-08 12:13:25',2,'0',NULL,'200710/15/ATT7970.html','200710/15/DOC55906.doc','THAMODHARAN\nDHAMODHARAN SRIRAM\n\nE-Mail:\n\ndhamu006@yahoo.com \nMobile No: +91 9841707250\n\nCAREER OBJECTIVE\n\nA Challenging position in software design and development with the state-of-the-art technology where my managerial, analytical problem solving skills and application knowledge can be put in for the successful execution of the project.\n\nOVERVIEW Software Development\n\n2+ Years\n of experience in \nJava/\nJ2EE Technologies\n. Experience in full software development life cycle involving analysis, design, development, testing, documentation, implementation and maintenance of application software in the three-tier environment.\n\nRamco Systems Ltd\n, Chennai, Working as a Software Engineer from Dec-2006 to Till Date\n\nTATA Consultancy Services Ltd,\n Worked as a Business Associates from July 2006 to Dec 2006.\n\nCubic Systems\n Worked as a Software Engineer from Dec 2005 to July 2006.\n\nPSP Technologies Private Ltd,\n Worked as a Programmer from Feb 2005 to Nov 2005.\n\n\nEDUCATION\n\nMaster of Computer Applications\n\nMadurai Kamaraj University\n\nIndia\n\nBachelor of Science\n\nMadurai Kamaraj University\n\nIndia\n\n\nTECHNICAL SKILLS\n\nOperating System\n                              \n\n          \nWindows 2000, NT,Windows 98.\n           \nLanguage\n                                            \n\n           \nC, C++, Java,\nJava Technology\n                    \n            \n\n           \nJdk1.5, Java Servlts, JSP, JDBC\n                 \n            \n                                                                        \nAnd other J2EE Technologies.\nApplication Server\n                             \n\n           \nWeblogic 8.1, Websphere 5.0\nWeb Technology\n                   \n             \n\n           \nHTML,Java Script, XML\nFramework\n                                         \n\n           \nStruts 1.1, ATG 6.0\nORM\n                                                  \n\n           \nHibernate 3.0\n             \nWeb Server\n                                        \n\n           \nTomcat 5.5\nRDBMS\n                                             \n\n           \nOracle 9.x, MySQL 5.0 , DB2\n\n\n\nTitle\n                              \n\n          \nCoE Portal\nOrganization\n                 \n\n          \nRamco Systems Ltd\n, Chennai.\nLanguage\n                      \n\n          \nJdk1.5, JSP 2.0, Struts 1.1 and Hibernate.\nWeb Server\n                  \n\n          \nTomcat 5.5\nEnvironment\n                 \n\n          \nWindows 2000.\nDataBase\n                     \n\n          \nSQL Server 2000.\nDuration\n                       \n\n          \nDec 2006 to Till Date\nDescription:\nThe CoE Portal for sales and sales support organization of Ramco; including the\nPartner community. Here is the single window for all the information regarding the products and solutions Offered by Ramco; encompassing marketing collaterals, demo applications, product documentation and case studies. In addition this portal shall also give you information regarding latest products roadmaps, releases, happenings and other relevant information.\nThe CoE Portal gives you control of your information. You can update information live on your intranet/internet site, without the need for extensive technical knowledge.\n\nTitle\n                              \n\n           \nItem Management\nOrganization\n                 \n\n           \nTata Consultancy Services Ltd\n, Chennai.\nClient\n                           \n\n           \nwww.target.com\nLanguage\n                      \n\n           \nJdk1.5, JSP, ATG 6.0.\nEnvironment\n                 \n\n           \nWindows 2000.\nDataBase\n                     \n\n           \nDB2.\nDuration\n                       \n\n           \nJuly 2006 to Dec 2006\nDescription:\nIMN is a system that will support the full range of functionalities needed to satisfy the business process of software ventures International and other companies. Feature include the retailer had multiple operating companies each with its own order management process. The initiative was to build a common order\n\nmanagement process to remove functional deficiencies and redundancies for better supply chain management and easier maintenance.\n\nTitle\n                              \n\n           \nMyRoda\nOrganization\n                 \n\n           \nCubic Systems\n, Chennai.\nClient\n                           \n\n           \nECM & Parlo-Malaysia.\nLanguage\n                      \n\n           \nJdk1.5, JSP, Struts 1.1, Hibernate 3.0, Tiles.\nEnvironment\n                 \n\n           \nWindows 2000.\nDataBase\n                     \n\n           \nMySQL 5.0.\nDuration\n                       \n\n           \nDec 2005 to July 2006\nDescription:\nThe system MyRoda is mainly for customer tracking of vehicle in the appropriate positions. The system is placed in different locations of \nMalaysia\n. They are interlinked by a server for tracking the changes that are happening in and around the system. Every customer can book the vehicle corresponding to their requirements for their trip. The booking information for their trip can be done in online basis. The system is authorized by an administrator who takes care of the operations regarding to the newly available vehicle and their trip rate is on day basis. Each location has a start time and an end time. It can be changed according to the customer?s requirements, while starting for their trip.\n\nTitle\n                              \n\n           \nWeb Mail Server\nOrganization\n                 \n\n           \nPSP Technologies Private Ltd\n, Chennai.\nClient\n                           \n\n           \nwww.netkracker.com.\nLanguage\n                      \n\n           \nJdk1.5, JSP, Java Servlet, JavaMail API, Struts 1.1,\nEnvironment\n                 \n\n           \nWindows 2000.\nDataBase\n                     \n\n           \nOracle 9.x.\nDuration\n                       \n\n           \nJuly 2005 to Nov 2005\nDescription:\nThis Electronic mail server provides the facility to send and receive the messages with attachments Java Mail API and JSP handle the front-end GUI and LDAP handle the backend operation. Such as Authorization, Authentication and storing messages, SMTP, POP3 and IMAP protocols are used for sending and receiving messages. Electronic mail server is configured for setting personalization options like managing folders, signature and multilingual support for composing messages.\n\nTitle\n                              \n\n           \nPortal Website\nOrganization\n                 \n\n           \nPSP Technologies Private Ltd\n, Chennai.\nClient\n                           \n\n           \nhttp://digisecy.zeenext.com\n                    \n                                                \nwww.hathway.com\nLanguage\n                      \n\n           \nJdk1.4, Java Servlet, JSP.\nEnvironment\n                 \n\n           \nWindows 2000.\nDataBase\n                     \n\n           \nOracle 9.x\nDuration\n                       \n\n           \nFeb 2005 to May 2005.\nDescription:\nThis portal site offers various features such as Calendar, Virtual Folder, Spider (Homepage maker), Letters, Discussions Forums and NEWS. User can use the Calendar feature as Online Organizer. Using Virtual Folder, user can upload and download the files from anywhere at anytime. Letters module gives specimen business letters and legal letters in various template forms. JSP handles GUI. Developed in Java; the system is platform independent and is designed for easy customization and connectivity to any JDBC/ODBC compliant database.\nResponsibilities:\nInvolved in the interaction with the client as part of System study and analysis of Business Processes and designing and coding of Server side applications and the database Tables residing in the server. Responsible for designing of user interface screens using JSP and HTML, Client Side validation using JavaScript.\n\nPERSONAL DETAILS\n\nAddress for Communication\n\n\n           \nOld No 28, New No 6,\n                                                                        \nNethaji Street\n\n                \n                                                        \nMadipakkam, Chennai- 600 091.\n                                                           \n             \nMobile No +91 9841707250.\nE-Mail\n                                                \n           \n\n            \nconsul_03@yahoo.com\nFather?s Name\n                       \n           \n\n            \nMr\n\nM.Subbiah.\nDate of Birth\n                          \n           \n\n            \n12-05-1975',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-15',NULL,'2007-10-15','2010-06-08 12:13:25','2010-06-08',2,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(73,'Dhana shankar',NULL,NULL,'Chennai','dhana123456@rediffmail.com',NULL,NULL,'0','98417 53314','0',NULL,'0','2009-04-13',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-08 12:13:25',3,'0',NULL,'200710/15/ATT7969.html','200710/15/DOC55907.doc','RESUME\nRESUME\n\n\nDHANA SHANKAR\n                     \n    \n   \n25,Kanchi Natarajar Street,\n   \nVasudevan Nagar(Near Kasi Theatre),\n   \nJafferkhanpet,\n\n\nChennai-600083.\n   \nPh.No\n\n: 98417 53314.\n   \nE-mail : \ndhana123456@rediffmail.com\n\n\nObjective\nTo perceive a challenging career as a Software Engineer in your Esteemed Organization and hence forth contribute to its growth and Development.\n\n\nProfessional Experience\n      \n\n\n      \nAround 1+ yrs of experience in Java and Web Technologies.\n\n      \nGood knowledge in Java, JSP, Servlets and EJB.\n\n\nAcademic Qualification\n\n     \nS.No\nQualification\n         \nInstitution\nYear of \nPassing\n     \nMarks \n\n\n\n\nB.E\n\nSardar\nRaja\nCollege\n of\nEngineering, Alangulam.\n\nApril 2004\n\n      \n72.6%\n\n\n\n\nH.S.C\n\nSt . Michael?s \nHr.\nSecondary School\n,Tenkasi.\n\nApril 2000\n\n      \n74.9%\n\n\n\nS.S.L.C\n\n\nSt. Michael?s \nHr.\nSecondary School\n,Tenkasi.\n\nApril 1998\n\n      \n86.8%\n\n\nTechnical\n\nSkills\n\n\nProgramming Languages\n     \n\n   \nC, C++, Core Java\nMarkup Languages\n               \n\n   \nHTML\nOperating Systems\n                \n\n   \nWindows 9x/NT\nDatabases\n                               \n\n   \nORACLE 8.0, MS ACCESS\n    \nWeb Technologies\n\n   \n            \n\n    \nServlets, JSP, EJB\nWeb Server\n                         \n   \n\n    \nApache Tomcat\n\n\nProfessional Summary\n\nCompany Name\n\n        \n\n   \nSeven Axiom Software Pvt.Ltd.\nDesignation\n                 \n\n   \nDeveloper.\nDuration\n                      \n\n   \nOct 2004 ? Feb 2006.\n\nProject Profile\n     \n\n         \nE-Nominate\n                  \nThis web based application, E-Nominate, is developed for the use of all employees of the concern. This application deals with training activities of Employee Education. Request and Nomination of employees for a course will be done by Manager, Scheduling a batch for course, Allocation of nominees for the batches, recording attendance details of participants will be the activities done by Employee Education. Generation of various reports like skills and training details of employees, ongoing and planned courses etc. are handled by this application. User can know the status of their Requests through the application online at any time.\n\n                        \n\nEnvironment\n    \n            \n: Servlets, JSP, Oracle 8.0 under Windows 2000\n                        \n\nResponsibilities\n            \n: Desiging and Coding\n                        \n\nDuration\n          \n           \n: 4 Months\n                        \n\nTeam Size\n       \n   \n         \n: 5\n\n\n         \nE-Library\n\nE-Library is one of the tools for enriching the knowledge of employees to increase their competency level in various spheres. It is a web-based application, which provides company employees the facility of reading from their desks like news cuttings from newspapers, selected articles from magazines, and contents of books available in the company library. Search option is also available, where the user can enter any text to search and it will retrieve all the documents related to that word.\n          \n                        \nEnvironment\n    \n: JSP, JavaScript\n                        \nResponsibilities\n\n: Desiging and Coding\n                        \nDuration\n           \n           \n: 3 Months\n                        \nTeam Size\n        \n   \n         \n: 4\n\n\n         \nShare Management System\nThis project is an online project\n\n The web site maintained for various Share information such as, broker, exchange, share holder information, transactions etc. Only the administrator can change the share details and enter the transaction details from anywhere at any time.\n            \n            \n\n           \nEnvironment\n    \n: JSP, JavaScript, Oracle\n                        \nResponsibilities\n\n: Desiging and Coding\n                        \nDuration\n           \n           \n: 4 Months\n                        \nTeam Size\n        \n   \n         \n: 5\nAcademic Project\n\n        \nTitle\n                                            \n?Human Resource Administration?\n         \n         \nFirm\n                                           \nObject Frontier Software Pvt.Ltd.,Chennai.\n                                                                                                              \n                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                \n                                                                                                                     \n         \n         \nSoftware used\n                            \nJava, Oracle\n         \n         \nDescription\n                                \nThis project mainly concentrates upon the effective\n\n\n\n               \n                               \ndesign controlling\n\nthe electronic media through\n                \n     \n                               \ncomputer.The main objective of this project is used to\n\n    \n                                \ntrack the phone calls.i.e, both incoming and outgoing\n     \n                                 \ncalls.\n\nPersonal Details\n       \n\n          \nFather?s Name\n             \n        \n\n\nD.Balu\n\n          \nDate Of Birth\n               \n        \n\n\n08-10-1982\n\n          \nSex\n                    \n                    \n\n\nFemale\n\n          \nMarital Status\n              \n        \n\n\nSingle\n\n          \nLanguages Known\n       \n        \n\n\nEnglish, Tamil\n\n          \nNationality\n                    \n        \n\n\nIndian\n\n          \nI here by declare that the above furnished details are true to the best of\n     \n          \nmy knowledge.\n                                                                                \n                                       \n                                           \n(B.DHANA SHANKARI)','Seven Axiom Software Pvt.Ltd',1,NULL,'2007-10-15',NULL,'2007-10-15','2010-06-08 12:13:25','2010-06-08',3,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(74,'Govind sharma',NULL,NULL,NULL,'rma33123@yahoo.com',NULL,NULL,'0',NULL,'0',NULL,'0','2005-04-29',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-08 12:13:25',3,'0',NULL,'200710/15/ATT7968.html','200710/15/DOC55908.doc','GOVIND SHARMA\nGOVIND RAM\nEmail : \nrma33123@yahoo.com\n\nObjective\nA mentally and financially rewarding opportunity with a cutting-edge company that will continually push my skills to the limits\n\nSummary\n\n    \nHaving 5 years & 1 month of in-depth experience in analysis, design\n\n& development of applications based on Java/J2EE Platform\n\n    \nAcquainted with the Quality Processes, as working in CMM Level 5 environment\n\n    \nPossesses good knowledge of Core Java (JDK 1.4), Servlets, JSP, Struts, Threads, JDBC, SQL and Mule\n\n    \nFamiliar with RMI, Spring, XMLMILL, JavaScript and XML Beans, Jasper Reports\n\n    \nPossesses strong analytical and debugging skills\n\n    \nWorking as a Team Lead and Sr. Developer.\n\nExperience\n\n    \nOrganization\n                         \nDesignation\n                    \nFrom\n                \nTo\n                    \nDuration\n\n(2) \n\nKanbay Software (I) Pvt. Ltd.\n          \nConsultant\n                                 \n01-01-2006\n           \nTill-Date\n                 \n42 months\n        \n(CapGemini since 08-02-2007)\n     \nAssociate Consultant\n             \n24-02-2004\n           \n31-12-2005\n        \n(1)\n   \nBabul Technologies Pvt. Ltd.\n         \nFaculty cum Programmer\n      \n03-11-2000\n           \n02-05-2002\n           \n19 months\n\n\nEducation\n\n    \nMCM (secured 68.54%) from NMU (\nMaharashtra\n) in Apr-1999\n\n    \nB.Sc. (Electronics) (secured 58.27%) from KU Kurukshetra (Haryana) in Apr-1997\n\n    \n10+2 (secured 63.8%) from CBSE (\nDelhi\n) in Mar-1994\n\n    \n10th (secured 63.8%) from CBSE (\nDelhi\n) in Mar-1992\n\nCertification\n\n    \nSun Certified Java Programmer (SCJP) in Oct-2000\n\nTechnical\n                \nOperating Systems\n      \nWin XP, Win2K, WinNT, Win98, Linux\n                \nLanguages\n                   \nJava\n                \nDatabases\n                    \nDB2\n                \nTechnology\n                   \nJ2EE (JSP, Servlets), Struts, Spring, Mule, XML, XML Beans, Jasper Reports, UML, ANT \n                \nApplications/Tools\n       \nRAD6, Eclipse, SVN, PVCS, WSAD, JBoss4.0.3, Tomcat 5.0, Clear Case, Clear Quest\n\n                                                        \nProjects\n           \n            \n(7) Trans Union ? \nTuscany\n Invoicing\n\n            \nClient\n                      \nTrans Union, \nChicago\n\nUSA\n                \nOrganization\n         \nKanbay Software (I) Pvt. Ltd., \nPune\n\nIndia\n (now Capgemini)\n                \nRole\n                       \nTeam Lead\n                \nTeam Size\n            \n\n                \nPlatform\n                 \nJDK 1.4, MULE 1.3, Spring 2, DB2\n                \nTools / Utility\n         \nRAD 6, Subversion, Ant 1.6.5\n                \nDuration\n                \n04-2007 to Till Date\n                                                \n                \nDescription\n           \nThe Tuscany Invoicing has functionality of generating report for Credit Bureau. The initially the project includes Hawk and Watch report functionality. The Hawk is High Risk Fraud Alert report available to customers to review the results of all of their enquiries for Hawk family of products. Watch is Individual Monitoring Satisfaction report available to review the results for Watch family of reports. The application fetches data from database, processes it, formats and generates reports in the form of fixed-format printable plain text files.\n            \n                        \n                \n(6) Trans \nUnion\n ? CIBIL Bulk Channel\n\n            \nClient\n                      \nTrans Union, \nChicago\n\nUSA\n                \nOrganization\n         \nKanbay Software (I) Pvt. Ltd., \nPune\n\nIndia\n (now Capgemini)\n                \nRole\n                       \nSr. Developer\n                \nTeam Size\n            \n\n                \nPlatform\n                 \nJDK 1.4, Spring 1.2.2, XMLMILL, ActiveMQ 4, JBoss 4\n                \nTools / Utility\n         \nEclipse 3, SVN, Ant 1.6.5\n                \nDuration\n                \n11-2006 to 04-2007\n\n                \nDescription\n           \nCIBIL enterprise system is for Trans Union and Credit Information Bureau (\nIndia\n) Limited.\n\nThe Bulk Channel is one of the components of this enterprise system.\n\nThe system includes other components like B2B, User Admin, Products Engine and Credit Scoring Engine.\n   \n                                                \nThe Bulk Channel has functionality of accepting the Credit Report requests in various format, parse and convert in Trans Union Enquiry Format and pass those to TUCRS engine for generating Credit Reports.\n\nTUCRS returns report again in TUEF format, hence Bulk Channel again convert these report in different formats like HTML, PDF or TXT formats as required by the requestor.\n                                                \nBulk Channel has administration GUI also, where processing status can be seen and priorities of files being processed can be changed or processing can be stopped, resumed and cancelled.\n\nAlong with report generation, it does create error files for bad input files and places those in configured location.\n            \n                \n(5) TransUnion ICRS \nCroatia\n Credit Reporting System\n\n            \nClient\n                      \nTrans Union, \nChicago\n\nUSA\n                \nOrganization\n         \nKanbay Software (I) Pvt. Ltd., \nPune\n\nIndia\n (now Capgemini)\n                \nRole\n                       \nSr. Developer\n                \nPlatform\n                 \nJava 1.4.2, JBoss 4.0.3, DB2, rational Clear Case, Rational Clear Quest, Eclipse 3.1.\n                \nDuration\n                \n12-2005 to 11-2006\n\nDescription\n           \nThe credit reporting industry has long played an integral role in the American economy. By providing updated consumer information to help credit grantors make fast and accurate decisions for consumer credit transactions, credit reporting agencies help fuel economic growth. \n\nCredit reporting provides significant benefits to the financial system and the economy. Examples of these benefits include:\n\nAllowing consumers with good credit to open and expand credit lines \n\nProviding businesses with reliable data to make sound judgments about credit \n\nDecreasing loan losses and personal bankruptcies by providing crucial information needed for credit \n   \ngrantors to more accurately assess the profile of an individual borrower \n\nReducing risk-assessment costs by accessing the comprehensive information gathered by the credit \n   \nbureau more quickly and accurately \n\nIncreasing borrower privacy protection by providing a systematic basis for lending without the hassle of \n   \nlengthy support documentation \n\nReducing fraud by providing additional information such as invalid addresses and Social Security \n   \nnumbers that allow credit grantors to identify and avoid potentially fraudulent credit applications \n\nSpeeding access to data by allowing consumers to make \n   \nimmediate large-scale purchases such as a car \nTasks carried out includes\n? Development of sequence diagrams and class diagrams for different use cases.\n? Development of use cases.\n? Carried out Unit Testing and Integration Testing of developed modules.\n\n        \n                \n(4) HMS eCare\n\n\n                \nClient\n                      \nHSBC, \nBuffalo\n\nUSA\n                \nOrganization\n         \nKanbay Software (I) Pvt. Ltd., \nPune\n\nIndia\n (now Capgemini)\n                \nRole\n                       \nDeveloper\n                \nPlatform\n                 \nJava1.4, JSP, Servlet, DB2, Execusion Services, WSAD, PVCS\n                \nDuration\n                \n08-2004 to 10-2005\n\nDescription\n           \nThe HMS Mortgage eCare site for HMS customers to access information about their loan accounts. This site will provide a variety of functions to allow mortgage customers to access their mortgage accounts, including viewing loan detail, transaction history, escrow information, payment information, and pending payments; making online payment; registering or modifying/canceling auto pay. BackEnd used in this project is MainFrames. The ESI framework is the highest level of abstraction achieved to access these 3rd level legacy cobol programs. Moreover one requires Java Record Classes to mirror COBOL copybooks for every transaction.\n        \n                        \n\n(3) HSBC eCare\n                        \n                \nClient\n                      \nHSBC, \nBuffalo\n\nUSA\n                \nOrganization\n         \nKanbay Software (I) Pvt. Ltd., \nPune\n\nIndia\n (now Capgemini)\n                \nRole\n                       \nDeveloper\n                \nPlatform\n                 \nJava1.4, JSP, Servlets, Tiles, DB2, Execusion Services, PVCS, WSAD\n                \nDuration\n                \n03-2004 to 08-2004\n\nDescription\n           \nThe HSBC Mortgage eCare is intended to be part of the overall migration of mortgage data and services from Alltel to the Household MortgageServ system. It will be a new online mortgage site for HSBC customers to access within HSBC?s Personal Internet Banking system. This site will provide a variety of functions to allow mortgage customers to access their mortgage accounts, including viewing loan detail, transaction history, escrow information, payment information, tax information and pending payments; making online payment; registering or modifying/canceling auto pay, ordering loan documents and payoff letters, as well as completing a promise-to-pay form. BackEnd used in this project is MainFrames. The ESI framework is the highest level of abstraction achieved to access these 3rd level legacy COBOL programs. Moreover one requires Java Record Classes to mirror COBOL copybooks for every transaction.\n\n\n                \n(2) Materials Requirement & Planning System\n           \n\n                \nClient\n                      \nSoma Textile Pvt. Ltd.\n                \nOrganization\n         \nBabul Technologies Pvt. Ltd.\n                \nRole\n                       \nDeveloper\n                \nPlatform\n                 \nLINUX, Oracle 7.x, JSP, Servlets, JDBC, Tomcat\n                \nDuration\n                \n09-2001 to 05-2002\n\nDescription\n           \nThe application facilitates invoice preparation, maintains Customer Record, inventory record in the go downs & generation of Daily/Monthly reports for the Materials dept. \n                                \n? Development of invoice, customer Records, Inventory of the application\n                                \n? Running the application for tests\n\n                \n(1) Employee Management System\n                        \n                \nClient\n                      \nBabul Technologies Pvt. Ltd.\n                \nOrganization\n         \nBabul Technologies Pvt. Ltd.\n                \nRole\n                       \nDeveloper\n                \nPlatform\n                 \nLINUX, Oracle 7.x, JSP, Servlets, JDBC, Tomcat\n                \nDuration\n                \n11-2000 to 09-2001\n\nDescription\n           \nThe customized application consists of modules on Administration, Search, Report generation & Accounts, and facilitates the maintenance/merging of employee records.\n                                \n? Handling the coding of modules on Report Generation, Search and Total working time calculation of an employee\n                                \n? Testing the application to find code errors & debugging the application\n\nPersonal\n            \nDate of Birth\n          \n1st Feb 1976\n                \nGender\n                  \nMale\n                \nMarital Status\n       \nMarried\n\nUpdated On\n                \nSeptember 15, 2007',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-15',NULL,'2007-10-15','2010-06-08 12:13:25','2010-06-08',3,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(75,'Jayprakash sahoo',NULL,NULL,NULL,'jay45689@gmail.com',NULL,NULL,'0','91 9916448315','0',NULL,'0','2008-04-29',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-08 12:13:25',10,'0',NULL,'200710/15/ATT7967.html','200710/15/DOC55909.doc','            \n            \n                            \n\n\n                                                       \nJAY PRAKASH \n\n\n\n\nEmail: \njay45689@gmail.com\n             \n      \n      \n        \n    \n\n           \nMobile:\n\n+91-9916448315\n\nPROFESIONAL\n\nSUMMARY \n\n\n   \nOver \n2+\n ye\nars of working experience in the field of Software Development having actively \n    \n                 \n\n   \ninvolved in Developing, Deploying and Maintaining application using \njava\n and \nJ2EE\n\n\n   \nGood Experience in Developing Applications using \nHibernate, Servlets\n\nJSP\n\nJDBC\n\nStruts and Oracle.\n\n   \nGood Implementation Knowledge in \nStruts Framework\n and\n XML.\n\n   \nExcellent \ncommitment, dedication\n and \nplanning\n towards goal oriented tasks.\n\nCAREER PROFILE\n\n\n   \nWorking as a\n Software\n Engineer \nfor\n\nVernainfo solution\n\nBangalore\n\nfrom June 2005\n\nto till date.\n\nACADEMIC QUALIFICATION\n\n\n   \nB.E. \n\n   \nSambalpur\nUniversity\n\n(B.P.U.T.,Orissa)\n\n\nSKILL SET\n\nOperating Systems\n                             \n\n\nWindows 9X/NT/XP/\n2000\nLanguages\n      \n            \n         \n               \n\n\nJava, XML \nJ2EE/Web Technologies\n   \n                 \n\n\nJDBC, Hibernate, Servlets, JSP, Struts 1.1\nFrame Work\n             \n         \n                 \n\n\nStruts 1.1\nWeb server\n                         \n                \n\n\nTomcat \nApp Server\n                         \n                \n\n\nWeb Logic 7.1\n                                                \nRDBMS\n          \n            \n         \n               \n\n\nOracle\nMarkup Languages\n           \n                 \n\n\nHtml\nScripting Languages\n   \n                        \n\n\nJavaScript\nIDE/GUI Tools\n                   \n                \n\n\nEclipse\n\n\n\n\nPROJECT 1\n\n                         \n\n# Banking:\n\n   \n                        \n  \nVehicle Loan Application\nType\n                            \n            \nWeb-based Application\nRole\n                                        \nSoftware Developer\nTeam size\n                                \n\nEnvironment\n                           \nWindows 2000 \nTechnology \n                 \n           \nJSP, Servlets, Java Beans, Struts, Oracle 10g\nFramework\n                                \n         \nStruts\nApplication Server \n             \n    \nWeblogic 7.1\nTools\n                                       \nEclipse\n\nProject Description\nVehicle loan approval system comprises various modules. One of the modules is loan appraisal. The result of this module which is a 100 check point system named as Credit Rating Report, mainly supports the key aspect of whole loan sanction process and also enhances the decision making capability of the bank executive. CRR passes through various phases like:\n\n        \nIdentity Verification\n\n        \nAddress Verification\n\n        \nSalary Verification\n\n        \n\nCredit History\n\n        \n\nC.R.R (Credit Rating Report)\n\nRoles & Responsibility\n1)\n      \nResponsible for designing forms using JSP?s and Struts.\n2)\n      \nResponsible for writing Action classes and JSP?s.\n3)\n      \nUsed Struts Tiles and Validation Framework\n\n\nPROJECT 2\n    \n               \n           \nProject name\n           \n    \n             \n\nwebwize\nType\n                            \n            \nWeb-based Application\nRole\n                                        \nSoftware Developer\nTeam size\n                    \n            \n\nEnvironment\n                           \nWindows 2000 \nTechnology \n                 \n           \nJSP, Servlets ,Hibernate, Java Beans, Struts, Oracle 8i\nFramework\n                                \n         \nStruts\nApplication Server\n              \n    \nWeblogic 7.1\nTools\n                                       \nEclipse\n\nProject Description\nIn a nutshell: The major objective of this project is to develop a web portal for bidding system to make business transactions more users friendly. Here the users have to register themselves as buyer or seller for placing up a tender with their requisites and to review them to give their revised quotations before the administrator prepares the auction procedures. Beside online bidding or web auction and also facilities are provided for virtual store where the sellers can directly place their goods for sale the products which are placed in virtual store are available for online shopping. So the proposed system will provide an end-to-end user environment ease to use.\n\nRoles & Responsibility\n\n              \n\n1) Involved in coding of the JSP and HTML pages. \n2) Involved in validation process. \n3) Writing code to access the database.\n\nPROJECT 3\n   \n\nInsurance\n\n\n              \nCIA ? OMP\nType\n                            \n            \nWeb-based Application\nRole\n                                        \nTeam member\nTeam size\n                                \n\nEnvironment\n                           \nWindows 2000 \nTechnology \n                 \n           \nJSP, Servlets, Java Beans, \n\nOracle 8i\nFramework\n                                \n         \nStruts\nApplication Server\n              \n    \nWeblogic 7.1\n\n\n\n\nProject Description\nOverseas Medical Policy is a web-enabled application that automates medical policy. This sub-system takes care of medical expenses following Hospitalization, accident or surgery that is required in respect of any disease which has arisen during the policy period along with the situations like loss of checked baggage, loss of passport for those who are going abroad for specific purpose like Business, Holidays etc for specific time period.\nClaim-sub system\n\nThe Claim Sub System deals with the payment of claims through Third Party Administrators who have been empanelled by the Company and Reimbursement of the claims through Authorized Service Centers after inspection\n\nRoles & Responsibility\n\n1)\n      \nResponsible for writing Servlets and JSP.\n2)\n      \nPage design and implementations through Servlets.\n3)\n      \nDesigning the web pages using Html.\n\nPERSONAL DETAILS\n\nFather?s Name\n                                    \n           \n\n       \n   \n  \nJagannath sahoo\nCommunication Languages\n                \n\n           \nEnglish, Hindi, and Oriya. \nSex\n                                                      \n\n           \nMale\nDOB \n                                     \n                   \n\n            \n08.02.1982\nNationality\n                                           \n\n           \nIndian.\nHobbies\n                                              \n\n           \nplaying badminton, listening to Music, panting\n\nDECLARATION\n\nInformation provided is meant for depicting the work, skill of the candidate. The projects details shown above are the main projects involved. I here by declare that the above information is true to the best of my Knowledge and belief.\n                                    \n                                    \n                                                \n                                 \nJayprakash sahoo',NULL,9,NULL,'2007-10-15',NULL,'2007-10-15','2010-06-08 12:13:25','2010-06-08',10,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,9,'0',NULL),(76,'Boopathi Arun',NULL,NULL,'Chennai',NULL,NULL,'9841388182','0','9884336801','0',NULL,'0','2003-09-12',7,18,'2010-06-08 12:13:25',10,'0',NULL,'200710/15/ATT7966.html','200710/15/DOC55910.doc','Resume of Jayaprakash.R\nPROFESSIONAL EXPERIENCE (3+ Years):\n\n?SOFTWARE DEVELOPER?\n\n\n\nEmail:\n\nboopathi.arumugam@\ngmail.com\n\n\n\n\nContact. No\n.:\n\n9884336801/ \n9841388182\n\n\n\n\n\nPresent Address\nB-1 block, Yes Yes Grace Apartments,\nNo. 12/6, \nFirst Street\n\nTNGO Colony,\nAdambakkam,\nChennai-600088\n\n\nPersonal Information\nDOB: \n11\nth\n June 1979\nSex: Male\nNationality: Indian\nMarital Status: Single\nObjective\n\nTo obtain a creative and challenging position that enables me to gain good exposure and sound technically knowledgeable for Organizational and personal growth.\n\n\nTechnical Expertise\nProgramming\n\nSkills\n     \nJava\n\nJ2EE\n\n\nJDBC\n\nAJAX\n, JavaScript, DOM, HTML, CSS\nDesign Skills\n                \nER-Studio 6.5\n                                             \nWeb Server\n                 \nJboss-3.2.5, Jboss-4.0.3\nDatabase Packages\n      \nPostgresSQL 8.1, Oracle 8i\nOperating Systems\n        \nWindows \nNT/XP, Linux 9.0\nBuild Tool\n                   \n\nAnt v1.6.5\nVersion Control\n           \n\nCVS\n\nEducation\n\n         \nBE\n (Mechanical) \n   \n\nAnnamalai\nUniversity\n (1996 ? 2000) - Secured 63%.\n\n\n         \nHSC\n\n\n  \n                \n\nSt. Paul\n?s \nH.S.\nSchool\n\nSalem\n (1996) - Secured 82%.\n\n\n         \nS.S.L.C\n\n   \n           \n\nG.H.\nSchool\n, Villipalayam, Namakkal Dt.\n\n(1994) - Secured 84%.\n\n\n         \nDJP\n\n                  \n\n\n(Diploma in Java Programming) ? LIBA, \nLoyola\nCollege\n, Chennai \n               \n                 \n\nAug 2000 ? Dec 2000 - Secured 81%.\n\nExperience\nProfessional Summary\n\n         \n3 + Years of Professional Experience as a Software Developer in Application \n     \n      \nProduct Development Companies.\n\n\nPossess expertise in Object-Oriented Analysis/Design and Java Development, \n      \nSkilled at progressing from problem statement to well-documented designs.\n\n\n        \nInvolved in front end design for Applications\n                                                              \n\n\nEmployer Details\nOrganization\nDesignation\nDuration\nJai E Technologies, Chennai\nSoftware Developer\n2005 May \n   \n\n\ntill date\nParadox Technologies, Chennai\n     \nProgrammer\n2004 May \n   \n\n\nApril 2005\nPandian Engineering Tools, Chennai\nQuality Engineer\n2002 June \n\n\n\n\nApril 2004\nKorex Computer Technique, Namakkal\nComputer Training Faculty\n2001 March - \n\nMay 2002\n\n\n\nProject Experience\n\nNAGADA\n\nNagada is a office management tool and it is a suite of products under one secured shell that helps to manage mail, work, people, events, appointments, information, etc.\n\nNagada Chat and News\n\nDescription:\n\n                        \nNagada Chat\n is one of the sub product of Nagada. This is used to communicate with group of people at a time. It provides open chat, one-one chat, many-one chat, one-many chat and offline chat. \n\nAttachment of files and save conversation are also provided with this product. So communication can be easier and faster within all level of people in an organization.\n\n                        \nNagada News\n is one of the sub product of Nagada. This is used to communicate news between groups and used to make conversation with single person or group of members. This product provides alert messages through E-mail and SMS by setting time duration like month-wise, day-wise, year-wise, every Monday, every 1 hour etc.\n\nClient & Build Environment\n\nRole\n                            \n\nSoftware Developer\nOS\n                                \nRed Hat Linux, Windows 2K and XP\nSoftware\n                       \nJava, Servlet, JSP, JDBC, \nAJAX\n, JavaScript, DOM, CSS, HTML\nVersion Control\n              \nCVS\nBuild Tool\n                     \nAnt v1.6.5\n\n\nContribution\n\n\n         \nResponsible for Design & Development\n\n         \nCoding and Testing\n\n         \nWorking on Code Optimization and Bug fixing \n\n         \nEnhancing the features\n\n         \nMaking user interface more interactive\n\n\nNagada Customer Care Manager\n\nDescription:\n\n            \nNagada Customer Care Manager\n is one of the sub product of Nagada. This is useful for customers and testing team to report bugs. The bug is automatically assigned to the relevant person to solve. Then the person can allocate the bug as a task to the next level person. By using this system, we can easily track and status of the bug without confusion and make the customers more satisfactory.\n\nClient & Build Environment\n\nRole\n                            \n\nSoftware Developer\nOS\n                                \nRed Hat Linux, Windows 2K and XP\nSoftware\n                       \nJava, Servlet, JSP, JDBC, \nAJAX\n, JavaScript, DOM, CSS, HTML\nVersion Control\n              \nCVS\nBuild Tool\n                     \nAnt v1.6.5\n\n\nContribution\n\n\n         \nResponsible for Design & Development\n\n         \nCoding\n\n         \nTesting\n\n         \nWorking on Code Optimization and Bug fixing \n\n         \nEnhancing the features\n\n         \nMaking user interface more interactive\n\n\nNagada Report\n\n\nDescription:\n\n                        \nNagada Report\n is one of the sub product of Nagada. A top level Management person is more interested to view the overall performance and\n\nstatus of a project. This product is very much helpful to view all the details of a projects as well as tasks in the projects. He can see the individual performance of a person in a particular project. This system provides tabular view, graphical view and printable view of the report.\n\nClient & Build Environment\n\nRole\n                            \n\nSoftware Developer\nOS\n                                \nRed Hat Linux, Windows 2K and XP\nSoftware\n                       \nJava, Servlet, JSP, \nAJAX\n, JavaScript, CSS, Html, DOM\nVersion Control\n              \nCVS\nBuild Tool\n                     \nAnt v1.6.5\n\nContribution\n\n         \nResponsible for Design & Development of Report.\n\n         \nCoding\n\n         \nTesting\n\n         \nWorking on Code Optimization and Bug fixing \n\n         \nEnhancing the features\n\n\nNagada Project/Task Management\n\nDescription\n\n                       \n\nNagada Project/Task Management\n\nis one of the sub product of Nagada. This system is used to control the inner activities of a project. Allocating resources to tasks, status changing like approval, forwarding a task, setting milestone for a project, setting dependency for a task, file attachment, recording conversation, alerts through E-mail and SMS, timesheet management are the key features of this product. By using this system, handling of a whole project can be easier.\n\nClient and Build Environment\n\nRole\n                            \n\nSoftware Developer\nOS\n                                \nRed Hat Linux, Windows 2K and XP\nSoftware\n                       \nJava, Servlet, JSP, JDBC, \nAJAX\n, JavaScript, DOM, CSS, HTML\nVersion Control\n              \nCVS\nBuild Tool\n                     \nAnt v1.6.5\n\n\n\nContribution:\n\n         \nResponsible for Design & Development\n\n         \ncoding\n\n         \nTesting\n\n         \nWorking on Code Optimization and Bug fixing \n\n         \nEnhancing the features\n\n\nNagada Cross Browser\n\nDescription:\n\n                       \nNagada Cross Browser \nsolving\nis to fix the cross browser compatibility like Internet Explorer, Firefox, Netscape and Opera for Project/Task management, Chat, News, Reports, Customer Care Manager and Dashboard.\n\nClient & Build Environment\n\nRole\n                            \n\nSoftware Developer\nOS\n                                \nRed Hat Linux, Windows 2K and XP\nSoftware\n                       \nJava, Servlet, JSP, JavaScript, DOM, CSS, HTML\nVersion Control\n              \nCVS\nBuild Tool\n                     \nAnt v1.6.5\n\nContribution\n\n\n         \nResponsible for bug fixing and alignment issues\n\n         \nCoding\n\n         \nTesting\n\n\n\nork Allocation and Tracking System \n\nWATS)\n                 \n\nDescription:\n                                                                                                     \n            \n             \nWATS\n is a product and it is extremely useful for work allocation and tracking system. It maximizes efficiency in development teams through optimized team interaction and systematic tracking of tasks in a project. \nWATS\n features project planning, resource allocation, task management, customized team member interaction and bug tracking.\n\nClient & Build Environment\n\nRole\n                            \n\nSoftware Programmer\nSoftware\n                       \nJava, Servlet, JSP, JDBC, JavaScript, HTML, CSS\nDatabase\n                       \nOracle 8i\n                                                                                                             \nOS\n                                \nWindows 2K\nWeb Server\n       \n\n          \nJboss-3.2.5\n\nContribution\n\n\n\n         \nWeb page development based on requirements.\n\n         \nCreation of Java Bean classes and interfaces.\n\n         \nCoding and unit testing\n\n         \nProto type creation\n\n\n\n\nFreight Forwarding System\n   \n(FFS)\n      \n          \n\nDescription\n\n\n                                                                                                    \n\nFFS\n is developed to automate various process of a truck owner.\n\nThis project takes care of truck details like rental, registration, renewal, maintenance etc. By using the software, we can easily track the current hirer, truck-driver details, salary, allowances etc. Then the periodical reports of the truck can also be generated.\n\n\nClient & Build Environment\n\nRole\n                            \n\nSoftware Programmer\nSoftware\n                       \nJava, Servlet, JSP, JDBC, JavaScript, HTML, CSS\nDatabase\n                       \nOracle 8i\n                                                                         \n                                    \nOS\n                                \nWindows 2K\nWeb Server\n       \n\n          \nJboss-3.2.5\nContribution:\n\n\n      \nWeb page development based on requirements.\n\n      \nCreation of Java classes and interfaces.\n\n      \nProto type creation\n\n      \nCoding and Unit testing','Jai E Technologies',9,NULL,'2007-10-15',NULL,'2007-10-15','2010-06-08 12:13:25','2010-06-08',10,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,9,'0',NULL),(77,'Bivash Pandit',NULL,NULL,NULL,'andit@gmail.com',NULL,NULL,'0','9986337448','0',NULL,'0','2008-04-29',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-08 12:13:25',14,'0',NULL,'200710/15/ATT61746.html','200710/15/DOC55911.doc','Sandip Mondal\n\n\nPh no :\n9986337448\nEmail :\nandit@gmail.com\n\n\nBivash\n\nsharma\nK ? 45, Near\n\n43\n\n\n\nBus Stand \nBanashankari\n   \n\nrd\n\nStage\nKathri\n   \nGuppa\n   \nMain\n   \nRoad\nBangalore\n   \n\n\n560085\n\n\n\nKarnataka.\n            \n                                    \n                             \n\nJob Objective \n\n\n       \nTo Work in a Technology Oriented Enterprise to apply my innovative skills to manage the Talent.\n\nExperience\n\n       \n2 Years \nof experience in Java Development in the IT sector.\n\n       \nSkills in Core Java, Struts1 Framework ,Servlets, JSP,\n\nHTML, MySql \n\n\nOrganizational Experience\n\n\n       \nWorking as a Software Engineer in \nTELiBrahma Convergent Communications Pvt\n. Ltd\n\nBangalore \n\nfrom March-2007 till date.\n\n       \nWorked as a Java Trainee in \nIrizon Communications Private Limited\nBangalore from\n         \nJune-2006 to\n\n\nFebruary-2007. and\n\nfrom\n\nOctober-2005 to June-2006 in\n\nSGC PVT LTD Bangalore worked as a trainee.\n\nEducation \n\n       \nBachelor of Technology \nComputer Science & Engg. \nwith 75.6% from Siliguri Institute of Technology under\n\nWEST BENGAL UNIVERSITY OF TECHNOLOGY\n 2005\n\n       \n12th\n Std under \nW.B.C.H.S.E\n with \n56.6% \nin 2000\n\n       \n10th\n Std under \nW.B.B.S.E\n with \n73.25% \nin 1998\n\nIT Skills\n\n       \nOperating System\n        \n\n           \nMSDOS, Windows, Red Hat Linux 8, Fedora\n\n       \nDatabase\n                     \n\n           \nMYSQL 4 , MYSQL 5\n\n       \nLanguages\n                   \n\n           \nJAVA\n\n       \nWeb languages\n           \n   \n         \n\n           \nHTML4.0, JSP, Servlet\n\n       \nFramework\n                   \n\n           \nStruts 1\n\n       \nWeb Server\n              \n    \n\n          \nApache Tomcat 5.5\n\n       \nIDE Tools\n     \n              \n\n\n          \nEclipse , NetBeans\n\n\nKey \nProjects\n Handled\n\n\nProject 1:\nKiZZ-Social networking and content sharing through mobile:\n   \n    \nClient:\n\nStand alone product offered to mobile subscribers in collaboration with mobile network\n   \noperators.\nRole:\n    \nDesign based on requirements\nImplementation of design in a tight schedule\nTesting and fixing of bugs found\nDeployment and maintenance\nConducting code-reviews and walkthroughs as required.\nTechnologies Used:\n    \nJava, Tomcat, Struts, Apache James, ImageMagick/ffmpeg for audio/video/image processing , MySQL 4.1, OpenJMS\nTeam Size:\n      \n     \n\nDescription:\nKiZZ is a social networking, content sharing and network storage portal. KiZZ users have their own keyword, and their personal site. They use their mobile number and password to log on to \nwww.blr.kizz.com\n. They can post content or messages on their site for others to see. Other KiZZ users can post messages or content to a KiZZ user. Content is processed according to its type and sorted onto folders (e.g. videos, images, etc.) Users can browse other peoples postings/content and organize groups and events through KiZZ.\n\nProject 2: \nEasy Modelling :\n      \nRole:\n                \n    \nAnalysis of the problem\n\nDesign \nDevelopment of Struts for different user interfaces\n\nPerforming\n\nvalidations using Struts\nReview and Testing \nPreparation of the required documents.\n\nTechnologies Used:\n    \nJava, Tomcat, Struts,\n\nMySQL 4.1\n\nTeam Size:\n     \n        \n\nDescription:\n                \nEasy Modeling is Web application for modeling industries in all over the globe. EM enables Modeling agencies to handle the requirements of models for a particular event. The web application is a solution for all the parties involving a modeling. The application is a solution for a modeling agency those who are involving with models, agents and modeling events. The web application solution allows users to handling the billing ,event scheduling and event mail option also .\nFor modeling agencies those having to increase their range of operation and those\n\nhaving multiple branches across the globe can use this system to improve performance\n\nwith less cost\n\n\nPersonal Details:\n\n\n       \nName\n                      \n\n   \n     \nBivash Pandit\n\n       \nDate of Birth\n            \n\n   \n     \n13- 03- 1982\n\n       \nGender\n          \n\n       \nMale\n\n       \nLanguages known\n     \n\n\n      \nEnglish, Hindi, Bengali\n\n       \nNationality\n               \n\n\n      \nIndian\n\n       \nPassport Number\n       \n\n    \n    \nF5505934\n\nHobbies\n\n\nWatching Cricket, listening\n\nmusic and Surfing the Internet\n\n\nI hereby declare that the above written particulars are to the\n\nbest of my knowledge and belief.\n                   \n         \n                                                                   \n      \n              \n                                                \n\n(BIVASH PANDIT)',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-15',NULL,'2007-10-15','2010-06-08 12:13:25','2010-06-08',14,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(78,'Arul Kumar Manivannan',NULL,NULL,NULL,'sachin12345@yahoo.com',NULL,NULL,'0','9884190614','0',NULL,'0','2008-04-29',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-08 12:13:25',14,'0',NULL,'200710/15/ATT61745.html','200710/15/DOC55912.doc','ARUL KUMAR MANIVANNAN\n32, Sea Breeze Flats,\nThiruvanmiyur,\nChennai-41.\nPhone:\n\n9884190614 \nMail id: \nsachin12345@yahoo.com\n            \n   \nOBJECTIVE: \n  \nTo work in a challenging and creative environment and effectively contribute towards the goals of the organization. \n\nPROFESSIONAL EXPERIENCE:\n\n2+ Years Experience in Java and j2ee Platforms.\n\n1)\n      \nWorking as an \nApplication Engineer\n in Java/J2ee Developer Team in \nSlash Support India Pvt. Ltd, \nChennai from \nAug 2006 \nto till now.\n\n2)\n      \nWorked as a \nSoftware Developer\n in Java/J2ee platform in \nFemtosoft Technologies Pvt. Ltd, \nChennai\n\nfrom \nJuly 2005\n to \nAug 2006\n\n               \n                               \n   \nEDUCATIONAL QUALIFICATION: \n\n2001-2005 \n              \nB.Tech, Information Technology with 78.3%,\n               \n                \n               \nCrescent\n\nEngineering\n\nCollege\n, Chennai\n               \n                \n2001\n        \n                               \nHigher Secondary Course with 88.67%, \n               \n                \nSrinivasa Higher Secondary School, Melaiyur\n\n1999\n            \n            \nS. S. L. C., with 91.8%, \n               \n                \nSrinivasa Higher Secondary School, Melaiyur \n\nTECHNICAL SKILLS: \n\nLanguages\n               \n\n              \nC, C++, Java, J2EE\nWeb Servers\n           \n\n               \nTomcat 5.5, Weblogic 8.1\nUML Tools\n             \n\n              \nRational Rose\nWeb Languages\n       \n\n              \nHTML, JavaScript, Applets, Servlets, JSP\nFramework\n              \n\n              \nStruts 1.1, MVC 2.0, \nAjax\nReporting Tool\n         \n\n               \nCrystal\n Reports XI, CR for Eclipse \nReport Admin\n          \n\n              \nBusiness Objects \nEnterprise\n XI,\n Crystal Reports Server XI\nIDE\n                        \n\n              \nEclipse\nReporting SDK?s\n     \n\n               \nJRC\n (Java Reporting Component Java/J2EE), \nRDC\n (Report \n                        \n       \n                                             \n    \n\nDesigner Component ASP), \nRAS\n (Report Application Server \n                                                 \n\nJ2EE) and BOE SDK (Business Objects \nEnterprise\n SDK J2EE).\nWeb Design Tools\n   \n\n              \nWeb Page Maker, MS-Front Page Express\nDistributed \nComputing Tools\n      \n\n              \nEJB, RMI, CORBA\nDatabases\n               \n               \n\n              \nOracle 10g, SQL Server, \nMySql\n\nMS\n-Access, FoxPro\nOperating system\n     \n\n             \nWindows 9x/xp/2000, MS-DOS, Linux, Unix\n\n\nPROJECTS:\n\n1. Account Management System\n            \nThe Account management System maintains the day to day transaction of the organization; it deals with the Cash Inflow and Outflow. It gets the details such as Payment Particulars, Amount and Other Details, then it updates the Cash in Hand and Cash in Bank. It maintains a Ledger, Trail Balance and Bank Details of the organization.\n\n\n\nAs a \nSoftware Developer\n, I have contributed for the following activities:\nDesign of HTML Forms and Adding Client Side Scripting.\nWriting Server Side Scripting (JSP and Servlet).\nAlso in System Design.\n\nTools\n   \n: JSP, Servlet, Java Bean, Java Script, HTML, MySql, JDK 1.5 and Tomcat 5.5\n       \nClient\n\n: IT007 InfoTech solutions, Chennai\n      \n\n\n2. Union Purchase and Sales Management System\n\n          \nThis project maintains Purchase and Sales details of the Milk Union. It Calculates the Amount per Liter, taking the FAT content of the Milk as Input and Stores the records of each Purchase and Sales. It also maintains the Payment Register that gives the details of Quantity of Milk given by the entire Union Members and the Amount that has to be paid to them. Daily, Weekly, Monthly and Yearly Reports are added for purpose of maintaining the Profit and Loss Account.\n\nAs a \nSoftware Developer\n, I have contributed for the following activities:\nDesign of HTML Forms and Adding Client Side Scripting.\nWriting Server Side Scripting (JSP and Servlet).\nAlso in System Design.\n\nTools\n   \n: JSP, Servlet, Java Bean, Java Script, HTML, MySql, JDK 1.5 and Tomcat 5.5\n   \nClient\n\n\n\n804 Sullakal Milk Producers, \nMadurai\n\n\n\n\n3.\n\nSchool Management System\n This Project deals the activities involved in a School such as Student Admission, Student Marks, Students/Staff Attendance, Student/Staff Profile, Conducting Examination and Library Management. Monthly Attendance Report, Yearly Attendance Report, Exam-Wise Marks Report are also added.\n\nAs a \nSoftware Developer\n, I have contributed for the following activities:\nDesign of HTML Forms and Adding Client Side Scripting.\nWriting Server Side Scripting (JSP and Servlet).\nAlso in System Design.\n\nTools\n   \n: JSP, Servlet, Java Bean, Java Script, HTML, MySql, JDK 1.5 and Tomcat 5.5\n               \n\n\n       \nClient\n\n\nSherwood\nHall\nMatriculation\nSchool\n, Chennai\n\n\n\n4. Business Objects \nEnterprise\n ? Java/J2ee Developer Support\n               \nThis project basically involves Business Objects Enterprise XI and all its tools. I work on integrating the Business Objects Enterprise XI and Crystal Reports with Java (Desktop) & J2EE (web) applications. I also deal with report administration with Business Objects XI and Crystal Report Server XI. Report Administration involves Report Publishing, Scheduling, Sending generated documents to the various destinations and accessing it through J2EE web application. I do work in CMC, Infoview, Universe Builder, DESKI, WEBI and Business View Manager Etc., and SDK?s like RAS, BOE SDK and REBEAN. The web servers I use are Apache Tomcat 5.0 and BEA Weblogic 8.1.\n\nTools\n\n: JDK 1.4, Tomcat 5.0, Weblogic 8.1, SQL Server 2000, Oracle 10g, MySql 4.1,\nCrystal\n Reports (10, XI and XI Release 2), \nCrystal\n Reports Server XI, \n    \nBusiness Objects \nEnterprise\n XI (and XI Release 2) and Crystal Report for Eclipse (CR4E).\nClient\n\n: Business Objects Customers, \nUSA\n\nDuration\n: Aug 2006 to till now\n\nDECLARATION\n\nI declare that the facts stated here in above are true and correct to the best of my knowledge and belief.\n\nPlace\n    \n\n                                              \n\nDate\n     \n\n\n                                 \n                                                \n(R.ARULMANIVANNAN)',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-15',NULL,'2007-10-15','2010-06-08 12:13:25','2010-06-08',14,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(79,'Arul Vel',NULL,NULL,NULL,'arull123@gmail.com',NULL,'0431 2555681','0','0 94435 91492','0',NULL,'0','2008-04-29',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-08 12:13:25',11,'0',NULL,'200710/15/ATT61744.html','200710/15/DOC55913.doc','bSoft ? business Software\nARUL VEL KUMAR\n5/11, \nIst Street\n, Periyar Nagar,\nNGO Colony,\nAdambakkam,\n\n            \n                          \nMobile\n : (0) 94435 91492\nChennai-600088.\n                                               \nE-mail : arull123@gmail.com\n\n  \n\n\nExperience Summary:\nHaving\n\n2+ years\n of proven experience in software development with strong skills in developing enterprise wide, multi-tier application software.\nExtensively involved in technical activities, including Requirement Analysis, Design, Coding, Debugging and developing client/server application software using J2EE technologies.\nHaving hands of experience and strong knowledge in JDBC, JSP, Servlets and Weblogic Server.\nStrong knowledge in Object Oriented Concepts and it is implementation.\n\nEducational Qualification:\nM.Sc Information Technology \nfrom \nChristhuraj\nCollege\n, Trichy affiliated to \nBharadhidasan\nUniversity\n\n\nB.Sc Computer Science\n from \nUrumu\nDhanalakshmi\nCollege\n, Trichy affiliated to \nBharathidasan\nUniversity\n\n\n\nComputer Skills:\nOperating Systems \nMS-Dos,Windows-98,Windows-2000\nSoftware\nC, C++, Java, J2EE\nRDBMS\nSQL Server, Oracle & MS Access\nPackages Known\nMS Office\n\n\nExperience:\n\nWorking as a Software Engineer in \nPROPUS INFOTECH P LTD., CHENNAI\n from Jan 2004 to till now.\n\n\nProject Details:\n                                              \n                                                                                                                               \n\n1. Material Management System\n\nEnvironment\n                                \nJSP, Servlets, HTML\nWeb server\n                                 \nApache Tomcat 5.0\nDatabase \n                                   \nSQL Server 2000.\n\n?Material Management System \n(MMS)? is designed to provide real time information about material flow and inventory levels across the organisation. Bringing the production facilities, sales offices and purchase offices under a single umbrella, this multiple site warehouse management application integrates the core business processes and ensures the decision making system more accurate and effective.\nThis product manages both the quantity and the value of the materials during the external procurements and internal movements. This can also be implemented as a stand-alone system since it is loosely integrated to the rest of the ERP systems.\n\nRole: \nDetailed study of the problem domain and Requirements Analysis.\n\n         \nRequirements gathering. \nDeveloped Servlet and JDBC.\n\n2.\n\nProject Monitoring System\n                   \n\nEnvironment\n                                \nJSP\nWeb server\n                                 \nApache Tomcat 5.0\nDatabase\n\n                                   \nSQL Server 2000.\n\nThe project entitled ?Project Monitoring System? is as an intranet application developed to maintain the project information for a company. The main aim of the project is to improve the services of the company. The head office will maintain the Central server. This project contains two major modules, which are Employee details and Project details .The employee module maintains employee information, which is having Designation, department, and personal information. The second module has the information regarding project head, project id and project headed by, starting date and ending date. The primary features of the project are high accuracy, design flexibility and easy availability and also it uses database tables representing entities and relationships between entities.\n\nRole:\n   \nDetailed study of the problem domain and Requirements Analysis.\nRequirements gathering. \nDeveloped JSP and JDBC.\n\n3. Purchase Order Generation System (POGS)\n                                \n\nEnvironment\n                      \nJava, Servlets, JSP\nWebServer\n                        \nApache Tomcat 4.1\nDatabase\n                          \nOracle\n\nPurchase Order Generation System (POGS) is an intranet system that enables to generate purchase orders. The application stores the details of their employees, manufacturers and purchase orders in the SQL Server Database 2000.The module is to automate the process of selecting manufacturers and generating purchase orders. Registered employees needs to first authenticate their credentials before generating purchase orders. A list of manufacturers dealing in a particular product can be viewed by selecting a product type. Purchase order can be generated by selecting a manufacturer from the list displayed and by filling a purchase order form.\n\nRole:\nDesign and implementation of registration component to register account department employees with the new system \nImplementation of the login component to check the credentials of registered employees before granting rights to view the manufacturer list and generate purchase order.\nImplementation of the purchase order generation component to generate purchase order.\n4. \nRTSOS\n                               \n\n\nEnvironment\n                      \nJava, Servlets, JSP\nWeb Server\n                       \nApache Tomcat 4.1\nDatabase\n                          \nSQL Server 2000\n\nClient\n\n                              \nISS Technology\n\nDevelopment of a dispatching and scheduling software application using advanced 3-tier client/server architecture. The software application will enable shuttle operation management in real time. The system will have the ability to manage vehicle, drivers and passenger information, define and manage vehicle schedules and fixed routes, and management reporting. In addition to operating a fixed route system, the application also provides scheduled routing for residential and non-fixed hotel routes and variable routing for load balancing.\n\nRole:\n   \nDetailed study of the problem domain and Requirements Analysis.\nDeveloped Servlets and JDBC\n\nPersonal Profile:\n          \n          \nFather?s Name\n                                  \n\n         \nMr. V.LOGANATHAN\n\n          \nDate-Of-Birth\n                                   \n\n         \n15\nth\n January 1981\n\n          \nSex\n                                                     \n\n         \nMale\n\n            \nMarital Status\n                                   \n\n         \nSingle \n\n          \nNationality\n                                        \n\n         \nIndian\n\n          \nPermanent Address\n                        \n\n         \nC3/031, \nBHEL\nTownship\n\n                                                                   \nKailasapuram,\n                                                                   \nTrichy ? 620 014.\n                                                                   \nTamilnadu\n\n          \nPhone No\n                                           \n\n         \n0431 2555681\n\n          \nLanguage known\n                              \n\n         \nEnglish and Tamil\n\nHobbies\n                                             \n\n         \nSurfing,Playing Cricket,\nReading\n                                                                   \nbooks\n\nPassport Details\n\n\nPassport Number\n             \n          \n\n        \nF2763191\n\nDate of Issue\n          \n                   \n\n        \n12\nth\n March 2005\n\nDate of Expiry\n           \n                   \n\n        \n11\nth\n March 2015\n\nPlace of Issue\n         \n                   \n\n        \nTiruchirappalli\n\n\n                                                                                    \nPlace\n\n: CHENNAI\n                                         \n                         \n        \n(L.ARULVEL)\n    \n                                      \n                                                         ',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-15',NULL,'2007-10-15','2010-06-08 12:13:25','2010-06-08',11,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(80,'Debasis Mohapatra',NULL,NULL,'Bangalore','sk12345@gmail.com',NULL,NULL,'0','9900402164','0',NULL,'0','2008-01-12',8,24,'2010-06-08 12:13:25',11,'0',NULL,'200710/15/ATT61743.html','200710/15/DOC55914.doc','Debasis Mohapatra\nASHUTOSH RAM\nE-Mail Id: \nsk12345@gmail.com\nMobile No: +91-9900402164\n\nPROFILE :\n\n\n            \nHaving \n2.2years \nof IT Experience in \nDevelopment of Application Software.\n\n            \nExtensive knowledge in \n.NET Frame Work, C#, ASP.NET, ADO.NET\n\n\n            \nStrong knowledge of Object Oriented concepts.\n\n            \nWorking Knowledge on Database.\n\n            \nWell versed to GUI designing\n\n\n            \nGood command over Exception handling and Debugging.\n\n            \nExcellent analytical and programming skills\n\n\n            \nAbility to Work in-group as well as independently with minimal supervision.\n\n\nSKILL SET:\n\nProgramming Languages\n   \n\n           \nC#.NET, VB.NET, C, C++.\nDatabase\n                               \n\n           \nSQL Server 2000, Oracle9i & MS Access.\nTechnologies\n                        \n\n           \nASP.NET, ADO.NET, HTML, XHTML, Java Script. \n  \nWeb Server\n                           \n\n         \nIIS\nTools\n                                       \n\n           \nVisual Studio 2003/2005\nOperating Systems\n             \n\n         \nWindows 9x, 2K, XP.\n\nQUALIFICATION :\n\n\n            \nB.E \n\nElectronics & Telecom)\n from B.P.U.T, Orissa\n\nin\n\nthe\n\nyear of \n2005\nPROFESSIONAL EXPERIENCE :\n\n\n            \nCurrently Working for \nShellsoft Technologies\n\nBangalore\n\nas a Software\n Engineer\n\n\nPROJECT DETAILS :\n\nProject #1:\n   \nDream Bricks\n\nPlatform\n                  \n: Windows 2000\nLanguage/Tools\n        \n: ASP.NET 1.1, C#.NET, ADO.NET, CSS, Java Script\nDatabase\n                \n: SQL Server 2000\nWeb server\n              \n: IIS 5.0\n                  \nTeam Size\n               \n: 3\nDuration\n                  \n: On going\n\n\nProject Description\nThis is a properties based web project with lots of information regarding properties and services at different sites in \nIndia\n. Here users can buy/sale/or give their properties in lease online. It has properties tools such as EMI, area calculation, city description etc. It also provides information about bank loans. The functional specification of the project is in two parts user and admin. In user module it again divided into sub-modules. In the user area user has to search for properties by property type, price, city, region and location. User can search for real-estate agents as city wise. For searching properties user can register with filling all the necessary details or without registering also. In the Admin it consists with offer management, giving rights to user to perform specific task, change password, banner advertise management.\n\n\nResponsibilities\n\n            \nInvolved in Coding of module.\n\n            \nInvolved in Design of User Interface.\n\n            \nInvolved in Database connectivity.\n\n            \nInvolved in Unit Testing.\n\nProject#2:\n\ne-Cards\n\nPlatform\n                \n: Windows 2000\nLanguage/Tools\n      \n: ASP.NET, C#.NET, ADO.NET, CSS, Java Script\nDatabase\n              \n: SQL Server 2000\nTeam Size\n             \n: 4\nDuration\n               \n: 6 months\n\nProject Description\nThis Web based project is purely shopping of e-Greetings. Where shopping is for user need with online. The Functional specifications of the project are deals in two parts user area, and admin area. In the user area, users have to search for Greetings by category and card name, browse for Greetings by alphabetic name, view Greetings detail page and buy online. In online shopping, each Greetings details page will have functionality to add desired no?s to cart. Checkout shopping which can be edited. Get e-mail address. Give payment detail. Display payment conformation and display order id, simultaneously e-mail of order detail will send to user and a copy to admin. User to enter order id after successful buying session the system will now show the status. Admin area consists of four parts, Greetings catalogue management, order status update, offer management and change password.\n\nResponsibilities\n\n            \nInvolved in Coding and User Interface Designing.\n\n            \nInvolved in Unit Testing.\n\nProject #3:\n   \nTrack Biz Solution\n\n\nPlatform\n               \n: Windows 2000\n\nLanguage/Tools\n     \n: C#, ADO.NET\n\nDatabase\n             \n: SQL Server 2000\n              \n\nTeam Size\n            \n: 5\n\nDuration\n              \n: 8 months\n\n\nProject Description\nThis is completely automated software for an automobile dealer. This is a Window based application. This application is used to keep track of all purchase, sale, enquiry, service, account and attendance of employee. This project is divided into six modules vehicle purchase, inquiry and vehicle sale, spare purchase and sale, service, account, front office and attendance register. I have handled vehicle purchase, spare purchase, sale and inquiry. Once your entry is done it will show you about the stock in report. I have also have worked in account module to keep track of vehicle, spare - purchase and sold.\n       \n\nProject #4:\n   \nLearning Management Systems(LMS)\n\n\nPlatform\n                \n: Windows2000\n\nLanguage/Tools\n      \n: ASP.NET, C#.NET, ADO.NET, Java Script\n\nDatabase\n              \n: SQL Server 2000\n\nTeam Size\n             \n: 5\n\nDuration\n                \n: 7 months\n          \nProject Description\nLMS is web based e-learning management system enabling users to achieve high level of education through Intranet. This e-learning is a mode of instruction that is delivered electronically through web server. The main modules in LMS are admin, register, instructor and learner. The different activities involved are like creating syllabi, assignment entry, mail services, examination schedule.\n\n\nPERSONAL DETAILS :\n\nDate of Birth\n                   \n\n   \n12\nth\n Jun 1982\nFather?s Name\n                 \n\n   \nSusanta Ku. Panda\nNationality\n                      \n\n   \nIndian\nMartial Status\n                 \n\n   \nSingle\n\nPassport\n                         \n\n   \nValid Passport \nSex\n                               \n\n   \nMale\n      \nLanguages Known\n   \n          \n\n   \nEnglish, Hindi, Oriya and Kannada\n\n\nCONTACT DETAILS :\n\n           \n15,17\nth\nMain\n, AGOS Layout, Arehalli,\n           \nB.S.K 4\nth\n Stage, Bangalore-61.','Shellsoft Technologies',1,NULL,'2007-10-15',NULL,'2007-10-15','2010-06-08 12:13:25','2010-06-08',11,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(81,'Azee Zullah',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Ozee@gmail.com',NULL,NULL,'0',NULL,'0',NULL,'0','2007-04-30',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-08 12:13:25',12,'0',NULL,'200710/15/ATT61742.html','200710/15/DOC55915.doc','Executive Summary\nAzee zullah \n                                                                             \nEmail\n   \n\nOzee@gmail.com\n                                                                             \nMobile\n\n: +9 1 9 9 7 2 8 5 0 5 0 5\n\nProfessional Abstract\n\n\n       \n3+ years of IT Experience\n in J2EE Architecture with \nStrong Coding, Debugging and Testing Skills\n. Developed Multi-tier Architecture Applications using JDK 1.4, JSP, Servlets, EJB, and XML\n\n\n       \nExposure to Application Servers like BEA Weblogic, JBoss and Web Servers like Tomcat.\n\n\n       \nExpertise at Process Oriented aspects of Software Development life cycles and Methodologies.\n\n\n       \nKnowledge in Sybase 12.5.\n\n\n       \nInvolved in Requirements gathering, System Analysis and Designing, Testing and Implementation.\n\n\n       \nPossess high end Technical and Analytical Skill Set which makes me better than the best amid extreme competition.\n\nCareer Profile\n\n1.\n      \nWorked as a Programmer Analyst at \nSAMBA\n Technology Group Ltd. \nRiyadh\n\nSaudi Arabia\n since \nMay 2006\n to June 2007.\n      \nSamba Financial Group\n is the largest bank in the Middle-East based in KSA, and ranked 200 among Fortune 500 companies worldwide by Forbes. It was formerly part of Citibank. Samba has the following achievements.\n\n         \nFirst bank in KSA to establish a dedicated Investment Department\n\n         \nBest Investment Bank in the Middle East & Africa\n\n         \nThe Banker Magazine?s 2006 Technology Award in the ?Technology Innovation? category.\n2.\n      \nWorked as a Software Engineer at Technoforte Software Pvt Ltd. \nBangalore\n since\n     \nJanuary 2004 to April 2006.\n     \nTechnoforte Software \nis one of the fastest growing Information Technology Consulting and Services Company headquartered at \nBangalore\n\nIndia\n. Technoforte has global presence in Middle East, Europe and Far East with offices in \nDubai\n\nUK\n and \nJapan\n. Technoforte provides high end enterprise solutions to clients across various industry verticals like manufacturing, automobile and automotive components, finance, warehousing, supply chain management and logistics\n\n3.\n      \nWorked as a Project Trainee in Savant Technologies, Chennai on J2EE Platform from \n          \nDecember 2002\n to \nApril 2003\n\n\n\nTechnical Skill Set\n\nLanguages \n              \n\nC, C++, JAVA, COBOL, VB 6.0\nPresentation Layer\n    \n: JSP, HTML, JavaScript\nBusiness Layer \n        \n\nJ2EE (JDBC, Servlets, JSP, EJB) and Struts\nApplication and \nIntegration Servers\n   \n\nBEA Weblogic, JBoss, Tomcat\nRDBMS\n          \n\nSybase, \nOracle, MS SQL Server 2000, MS Access\n          \nOS\n                \n                   \n\n\nWindows, UNIX\n\nEducational Details\n\nMCA from \nVellore Institute of Technology, \nVellore\n\n\nBSc\n(Computer Science) from \nUniversity\n of \nMadras\n\n\nTraining and Certification\n\nAttended training on ?IBM WebSphere?\nCertificate in Computing from IGNOU, \nNew Delhi\n\n\nEngagement Overview\n\n\n\n\nTitle\n                       \n\n\nConsumer Portal System\n\nClient\n                     \n\n\nSamba Financial Group\n\nDuration\n                  \n\n\nDecember\n 2006 ? June 2007\n\n\nTools\n   \nUsed\n             \n\n\nJava,\nJ2EE, Weblogic, Tuxedo, Java Script, JDBC, Sybase and HTML\n\nRole\n                       \n\n\nCoding, Page Designing and Testing.\n\nDescription:\n             \nToday Samba uses One Step Relationship Opening System (OSRO) to open Customer and his various products like Accounts, ATM Cards, and Cheque Books. OSRO has several disadvantages like:\n1.\n      \nClient Installations\n2.\n      \nNon User Friendly\n3.\n      \nCycle time is more for the Customer Service Representative.\nThe new system is developed to overcome the above mentioned defects. This System was developed using the J2EE architecture. We have integrated with the PIN PAD (which is used to maintain ATM and T-PINs) and external Emboss Card Printer using Applet. The new system is more Interactive and User Friendly. This system searches across all the databases in the bank and displays all his products to the CSR. CPS has been designed to support multi-lingual.\n\n\nTitle\n                       \n\n\nCorporate Account Opening\n\nClient\n                     \n\n\nSamba Financial Group\n\nDuration\n                  \n\n\nMay 2006 ? November 2006\n\nTools\n   \nUsed\n             \n\n\nJava,\nJSP, EJB, Weblogic, Java Script, JDBC, Sybase and HTML\n\nRole\n                       \n\n\nRequirement Gathering, Screen Designing.\n\nDescription:\n             \nThe Objective of the Project is to reduce the Current Account Opening Cycle and to define a clear system based checklist documents for Central Bank (SAMA) requirements. The new system will allow to create difference types of accounts based on the type of institution.\nTitle\n                       \n\n\nTSIN (\nTKM Service Information Network)\n\nClient\n                     \n\n\nToyota Kirloskar Motor Pvt Ltd. (TKML)\n\nDuration\n                  \n\n\nSeptember\n 2004 ? April 2006\n\n\nTools\n   \nUsed\n             \n\n\nJava,\nJ2EE, JMS, Weblogic, Java Script, JDBC, DB2 and HTML\n\nRole\n                       \n\n\nCoding JSPs and Testing\n\nDescription:\n\nThis is a web based defect analysis system between the dealer and the manufacturer (TKM).\n\nThis system maintains a centralized knowledge base system being developed targeting the fastest possible solution delivery for problems encountered at the dealer?s end.\n\nThe dealer reports the defect with images and video files attached to it to the CSD who in turn forwards it to QD for the corrective measures against it.\n\nThese corrective measures are then informed to the dealer through the service bulletin and are stored in the database for future reference.\n\nTitle\n                       \n\n\nUNIFIEX\n\nClient\n                     \n\n\nAndhra Pradesh Government\n\nDuration\n                  \n\n\nJanuary 2004 ? August 2004\n\nTools\n   \nUsed\n             \n\n\nJava,\nJSP, EJB, JMS, Weblogic, Java Script, JDBC, Oracle and HTML\n\nRole\n                       \n\n\nCoding JSPs and EJB, Testing\n\nDescription:\n\nThe UNIFIEX is an architecture suggested to the Government of Andhra Pradesh for automating the services of their various departments. The feature of the system is to integrate Service Access Providers (SAP) and Service Providers. The prototype of the system contains a Caste Certificate Requisition and Primary Health Center Details of a particular citizen. The architecture has been implemented using Web Services, JMS, EJBs and JSP.\n\n\nTitle\n                       \n\n\nCustomer Relationship Management\n\nClient\n                     \n\n\nSavant Technologies, Chennai. Tamil Nadu. \nINDIA\n\n\nRole\n                       \n\n\nDesigning, Coding Servlets, JSPs, Form Validations\nand\n   \nTesting and Report Generation.\nDescription:\n\n        \n   \nCRM, ERP are the major buzzwords in the today?s Business World. Customer Relationship Management is to help the customer in all aspect of the problem with any kind of response. This project focuses on how to manage the customer relationship. Here we analyze the customer request, based on that we should respond to him. Customer may approach the company in different reasons; it may for purchase, enquiry for problem, etc.\n\nIt maintains active information about the entire customer and their purchases.\n\n\nResponsibilities\n\n\n       \nDesign, develop, test and maintain the product and deliver high quality deliverables.\n\n       \nParticipate in the construction and integration of software components into the product to facilitate and maximize functionality and performance.\n\n       \nAssociate with technical teams in design and development of new features and enhancements, manage day-to-day design and development processes, on-going support, make crucial technical decisions pertaining to the assigned area of work.\n\n       \nHelped in managing scope and estimation of release schedules; worked with the development manager and architect to ensure that release schedules are met.\n\n       \nAdhere to standards and use best practices in software development.\n\n       \nPersons leading design and development teams will have the added responsibility to ensure adherence to agreed development standards and provide technical guidance to the team.\n\nPersonal Profile\n\nQualities with me:\n\n\n       \nA Strong Candidature with intellectual horsepower and excellent problem solving skill.\n\n\n       \nCreative Techno Functional achiever with excellent Analytical and comprehension ability.\n\n\n       \nExcellent verbal and written communications skills (both inter and Intra Official) and \nGood Interpersonal Skills.\n\n\n       \nProfessional attitude and Self motivated with strong work ethics of a self-starter.\n\n\n       \nDemonstrated ability to work effectively as a team member as well as individual contributor.\n\n\n       \nStrong technical experience sufficient to administer and configure test environments.\n\n\n       \nSelf-starter, detail oriented, excellent communicator. Good problem solving capabilities.\n\n\n       \nThe ability to learn and provide complex technology solutions.\n\n\n       \nAspiration to take bigger challenges.',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-15',NULL,'2007-10-15','2010-06-08 12:13:25','2010-06-08',12,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(82,'Bhumanna Ram',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL,'0',NULL,'0','2007-04-30',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-08 12:13:25',12,'0',NULL,'200710/15/ATT61741.html','200710/15/DOC55916.doc','Date\nObjective\nTo explore new dimensions and hone my skills to bring innovation and value addition to my organization.\nSummary\n\n\n        \nHaving 3+ years of experience in Web based application development.\n\n     \nProficiency in developing applications using \nJava\n\nJ2EE\n\nOracle 8i\n\n\n     \nHave used technologies such as \nJSP\n\nServlet\n\n JavaScript\n\nJDBC \nand\n EJB\n\n\n     \nHave experience on Application server \nWeb logic\n, Web server \nApache Tomcat\n\n\n        \nConceptual understanding of object oriented software development.\n\n        \nA good team player with strong analytical and problem-solving skills.\n\n        \n\nA fast learner with excellent Oral and Written communication skills.\n\n        \nAdaptability to other technologies.\nOrganizations & work profile\n\n        \nCurrently Working with Imattrix Technology, Hyderabad.\nlanguages known\n\n        \nEnglish, Telugu, Hindi, Marathi.\nEducation\n\n     \nBSC \nfrom Osmania University, Hyderabad.\n\n     \n12\nth\n from Board of Intermediate Education, Hyderabad.\n\n     \n10\nth\n from Board of Secondary Education, Hyderabad.\nSkill Set\nProgramming Languages\n        \n\n           \nC, C++, Java\nDatabases\n                                \n\n           \n\nracle8i \nTechnologies\n                           \n\n           \nServlets, JSP, EJB\nJ2EE Servers\n                            \n\n           \nBEA Web logic, Tomcat\nOperating Systems\n                  \n\n           \nWindows 95,98,2000\nMarkup Languages\n                  \n\n           \nHTML, XML\nScripting Languages\n               \n\n           \nJavaScript \nIDEs\n                                         \n\n           \nEclipse\nFrame Work\n                             \n\n           \nStruts\nKEY PROJECTS - Industry\n\nContract Management System\n             \n\n           \nDecember 2006 - August 2007\nRole\n                                                     \n\n\n         \nDeveloper.\nTeam Size\n                                           \n\n\n         \n\nDescription\n                                          \n\n         \nContract Management System is a user friendly web based application that would be deployed on web logic server.\n\nThe application would be able to provide facilities to the administrators, Project Managers, related Users in entering new contracts, tracking contracting details, modifying contract details, reporting ?etc.\n\nContract Management System application shall provide the following features to the users. \nIt can create a new Contract with Users, Groups and Roles defined which can be modified by the authorized users. It can be used to search different modules of the contract and make modification if necessary. It also provides reports for higher management.\nResponsibilities\n                                   \n\n\n         \nCoding JSP pages for dynamic representation of data.\n\n         \nImplemented core business logic based upon Command and Front Controller design pattern.\n\n         \nWrote local Entity beans and Remote Session beans for database operations.\n\nEnvironment\n                                        \n\n          \nJava1.4, EJB2.0, JSP2.0, Servlets2.4, \n                                                                        \nOracle8i, Web logic 8.1\n\nRailway Ticket Vending Machine (Tickon)\n                   \nJune 2006 - November 2006\nClient\n                                                    \n\n\n            \nWESTERN RAILWAYS, Mumbai, INDIA.\nRole\n                                                      \n\n\n            \nDeveloper.\nTeam Size\n                                            \n\n             \n\nProduct Description\n                              \n\n         \n\nIt is a sophisticated electronic mechanism for dispensing of the Tickets to the Passengers.\n\nhe main idea of this product is to issue tickets through Ticket Vending Machine (TVM). This Product contains three-tier architecture (TVM, Gateway, and Railway Server). This Product contains four Modules/Layers: Application Layer, Component Layer, Embedded Layer and Server Layer. \nRole & Responsibilities\n                        \n\n\n         \nAnalysis of functional requirements associated with the system.\n\n         \nCreated JSP pages for Screens and coded Servlets and JSP?s.\n\n         \nDeveloped the forms using HTML with client side validations using JavaScript.\n\n         \nAltered the design and development of several components to improve the quality of the product.\n\n         \nProvided Technical Support to the Clients and fixed issues reported by the users of the product.\nEnvironment\n                                        \n\n   \n        \nJava Server Pages, Java Servlets, JDBC, \n                                                                        \nHTML, JavaScript,\n BEA Web logic and Oracle 8i.\n\nE-Banking System\n                                \n\n           \nAugust 2005 - May 2006\nClient\n                                                   \n\n           \nHelp-line (USA).\nRole\n                                                     \n\n           \nDeveloper\nTeam Size\n                                           \n\n           \n\nProject Description\n                              \n\n\n         \nThis System is a 3 Tier Architecture which enables Customers to do online banking which includes Transfer Funds (TF), bill clearances (BC), request for stop payment, online trading (OT) and provides online information over the web. The customer info is obtained form the Directory Server (LDAP).\nResponsibilities\n                                   \n\n\n         \nDeveloped JSP?s for Accounts, Bills, Transfers, Requests, and Mail objects.\n\n         \nDeveloped JSP?s for Customer request like Stop payment, chequebook request, Loss of ATM.\n\n         \nDeveloped JSP?s and HTML pages for user interfaces and JavaScript for validation.\n\n         \nCoded Servlets, API?s for Transfer Request Module.\nEnvironment\n                                        \n\n          \nJava Server Pages, Servlets, EJBS, Windows, \n                                                                        \nBea Web logic Server, Oracle8i.\n\n\nCaller Ring Back Tone (CRBT)\n                         \nJune 2004 - July 2005\nRole\n\n          \n                                         \n\n          \nDeveloper.\nClient\n   \n          \n                                      \n\n          \nTataIndicom\nTeam Size\n                                           \n\n          \n\nProject Description\n                              \n\n\n          \n         \nCaller Ring Back Tone (CRBT) system aims at adding a customized ring tone (\nWAV \nfile\n\nfor subscriber. This ring back tone can be different for different people who call the subscriber. That is, the family members hear one ting tone, a colleague can hear another ring tone, and a friend can hear yet another ring tone.\nResponsibilities\n                                   \n\n\n         \nDeveloped GUI using HTML and JSP for dynamic page generation\n\n         \nCreated server-side JAVA architecture using Java Servlets, JSP\n\n         \nInvolved in documentation and producing a user manual for the client.\nEnvironment\n                                        \n\n\n         \nJava\n\nServer Pages, Java Servlets, JMS, \n                                                                        \nJDBC, HTML, JavaScript,\n BEA Web logic and \n                                                                        \nOracle 8i.\n\nPersonal Information\n\nName: Bhumanna Boinwar\nMother Tongue: Telugu\nNationality: Indian\n\n\n\nPlace: Hyderabad\n                                                                                              \n(BHUMANNA BOINWAR)',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-15',NULL,'2007-10-15','2010-06-08 12:13:25','2010-06-08',12,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(83,'Bhuwnendra Vekram singh',NULL,NULL,'Banglore','singh_4519@rediffmail.com',NULL,NULL,'0','09972200677','0',NULL,'0','2006-05-14',7,19,'2010-06-08 12:13:25',3,'0',NULL,'200710/15/ATT61740.html','200710/15/DOC55917.doc','BHUWNENDRA VEKRAM SINGH\nName\n               \nBHUWNENDRA \n\nSINGH\nMailbox\n           \nsingh_4519@rediffmail.com\nMobile\n                        \n09972200677\n\n\nPROFESSIONAL EXPERIENCE ? \n\nIBM India ? (November 2003 till date)\nJob Profile ? \nWorking as Senior System Engineer at IBM, I have over 3.8 years of IT industry\n experience encompassing a wide range of skill set, roles and industry verticals\n. Being lead for the projects and managing project execution activities, my profile includes -\nSuccessful execution of several mid-size projects as System Engineer, Designer and Developer.\nSound knowledge of software development process, database and OOP skills\nExperience in design, development and testing of J2EE/Java projects\nProject resource and productivity estimation, Configuration /Environment management and control\n6 Months Onsite experience with US customers.\n\nTECHNICAL SKILLS \n\nRDBMS\nOracle 9i, Microsoft Access 2000, Pointbase, MySQL 5.0\nLanguages/Technologies\nJava, JDBC, Servlets, JSP, RMI, PL/SQL, XML, JAXB, EJB, Java WEB SERVICES\nO/S\nWindows NT/2000 Server, AIX, Solaris, HP-UX B.11\nIDE\nWebSphere Application Development, ECLIPSE 3.2, Rational Application Software Development 6.0\nProcesses\nIBM QMS (Quality Management System), Software Development Framework Process, AT&T One Process, AT&T Express One Process\nTools\nSablime, Rational Portfolio Manager (RPM), Sterling Connect: Direct, IBM Requirements Mapping Tool (RMT)\nApplication Servers\nIPLANET, WebSphere Application Server 6.0, Sun Java Application Server 8.1\n\nCERTIFICATION ? \nSun Certified Java 1.4 Programmer \n\nIBM INTELLECTUAL CAPITAL SUBMISSIONS (Reusable components)\n\n1.\n         \nWeb-based Modification Request Tracker\n            \nThis Intellectual Capital Idea has been submitted to IBM and has been accepted and approved. The idea of this IC is to have an easy maintenance and tracking of Modification Requests in Source Code Control Versioning System, Sablime.\n2.\n         \nUNIX File System Usage Statistics\nIntellectual Capital Idea has been submitted to IBM and has been accepted and approved. The idea of this submission is to have a statistical report generated when various mounted file systems reach a threshold limit of usage. It informs the system administrators to take corrective action.\n\n3.\n         \nVersion control report for a particular file\nThe idea of this intellectual capital is to provide a detailed report for a version controlled source file. This IC script can be re-used for obtaining the details about a file, which is under version control tool sablime. Script will take three parameters from command line. First will be the generic of sablime in which the query has to be done. Second one will be the name of the file for which details are to be obtained. Third will be the type of report required. (Type can be either SHORT or ALL). This scrip will store this report in the current directory and name will have timestamp in it.\n\n\nAT&T INNOVATIVE SOLUTION PROPOSAL ? \nContract Generation Process Improvement\nThis solution has been proposed to AT&T for improvement of automated contract generation process. It is internally accepted.\nContract Management Tool ? Data, an AT&T system, was taking 4-5 minutes for generating the contract pages for AT&T users, and system was timing out in case AT&T Executives chooses all the possible data services. By implementing the proposed solution, the quantity of data retrieved from the database server is reduced which prevents the user from reaching the threshold limit and hence increases performance of the system.\n\nPROJECT\n\nIntegrated Contract Tool\nClient\n                            \n: AT&T, USA\nSoftware \n                        \n: Java, Servlets, JDBC\nApplication Server\n         \n: Websphere Application Server 6.0\nIDE\n                                \n\n\nRational Software Architect 6.0\nDatabase\n                         \n: Oracle 9i\nRole\n                             \n: Project Lead, System Engineer, Developer, Tester, SME\nDuration\n                       \n: Jan ?04 ? till date\n?Integrated Contract Tool? is a web-enabled application that provides AT&T executives a Common Gateway to Create, Process and finalize the contracts. ICT interacts with 11 external applications.\nI worked in various enhancement projects in this application. \nThe projects in this application do use Model View Controller architecture. Servlets, JDBC classes and dynamic HTML is used to attain this architecture.\n\nPROJECT\n\nData Services Deal Management (CMT-Data)\nClient \n                           \n: AT&T, USA\nSoftware\n                         \n: Java, Servlets, JDBC, RMI\nApplication Server\n         \n: Websphere Application Server 6.0\nIDE\n                                \n\n\nRational Software Architect 6.0\nDatabase\n                  \n       \n: Oracle 9i\nRole\n                             \n: System Engineer, Developer, SME\nDuration\n                       \n: Jan ?04 ? till date\nContract Management Tool - Data is a Web-based contract generation tool that supports the creation of bundled and customized Offers for services offered in the Global markets. The application automates the customized deal development processes including discounting, terms of commitment, and contracts. The system allows the Account Executives and Contract Specialists to negotiate autonomously within pre-defined parameters. Outside of those parameters, the system also provides a controlled escalation path to the Contract Managers for completion of the contract. It includes automation of cross edits and discount calculations.\nI worked in various enhancement projects in this application. \n\n\n\nPROJECT\n\nEnterprise On Line (EOL)\nClient\n                            \n         \n: AT&T, USA\nSoftware\n                                  \n: Cold Fusion 6.1 MX\nApplication Server\n                  \n: Internet Information Server 5.0, CF Server\nDatabase\n                 \n                 \n: MS SQL Server 2000\nRole\n                             \n          \n: Project Lead, System Engineer, Tester, SME\nDuration\n                       \n          \n: Apr ?06 ? till date\nEOL is a tool for viewing enterprise critical data; however, it is different from client-server systems in existence. It is web-based and AT&T employees with an ID and PIN can use it. \nThis system is mainly used for Year to date, Monthly Revenue data and other Sales and Marketing reports which are generated real time.\n\nRESPONSIBILITIES? \n\n        \nBusiness requirement analysis from system perspective and estimation of the projects so as to get required resource funding.\n\n        \nAllocation of work to team members and Execution of the Project as per Project Plan and Quality Plan\n\n        \nInvolved in design and coding of the projects. It involved design to code mapping, actual coding, code review and Unit testing.\n\n        \nMaintaining Quality records and documentation pertaining to projects, Test Management for Life Cycle and Enhancement Projects. Interaction with interfacing applications \n\n        \nReviewing of the project deliverables, Installation plans and Configuration audits for the applications\n\n        \nRight from attending the BRD calls, system requirement review, user acceptance test support, and production stand by support to day ? to ? day interaction with the AT&T customer is being done by me.\n\n        \nReporting the Project status and metrics to the Group Head and Department Head\n\n        \nDirect Client Interaction, AT&T and IBMUS meetings, Funding Issues and related matters\n\nADDITIONAL RESPONSIBILITIES\n\n\n\n         \nI am handling the source code control configuration job in ICT, CMT-Data and CMT-ABN applications. These application use SABLIME tool for code control. I am also executing job of environment management. These environments are Development, System Test, Integration Test environments.\n\n         \nApart from the projects mentioned above, I am dealing the issues reported in production systems of AT&T. Quick analysis and fixing the bugs and preparing install plan are done by me.\n\n         \nThere are small Life Cycle projects apart from regular projects in the applications mentioned above. I am executing such small projects as per the quality plan.\n\nAWARDS AND RECOGNITION at IBM? \n\n\n         \nIBM AT&T Account Performance Award\n ? This is given for contributing significantly to AT&T?s account growth and being critical for the set of applications.\n\n         \nFourth Quarter AT&T Tower Award\n\nFor contribution towards the highly critical project. Performed multiple roles over the project life cycle with complete focus on the quality process, to deliver a successful project with no issues.\n\n         \nCustomer Dedication Award ? \nThis award has been given for continuous customer dedication and working towards client?s success.\n\nTRAININGS ?\n\nTraining \nOrganized by\nQuality Management System\nIBM India Pvt Ltd, Bangalore.\nConfiguration Management\nIBM India Pvt Ltd, Bangalore.\nJava/J2EE Concepts\nIBM India Pvt Ltd, Bangalore.\nWebSphere Application Development IDE\nIBM India Pvt Ltd, Bangalore.\nWeb Services\nIBM India Pvt Ltd, Bangalore.\nOracle 9i\nIBM India Pvt Ltd, Bangalore.\nUnix\nIBM India Pvt Ltd, Bangalore.\nDefect Prevention\nIBM India Pvt Ltd, Bangalore.\nInspection and Reviews\nIBM India Pvt Ltd, Bangalore.\nEstimation Techniques\nIBM India Pvt Ltd, Bangalore.\nPrésentation Skills\nIBM India Pvt Ltd, Bangalore.\n\nEDUCATION ?\nMaster in Computer Applications (With Honors) ? U. P. Technical University, India\nBachelor of Science (Mathematics, Physics, Statistics) ? University of Lucknow, India \n\nPASSPORT/VISA DETAILS ?\n\nPassport Number\n                                  \n\n           \nF0158937\nPassport Issue Date\n                              \n\n           \n30 July 2005\nCountries for which have valid Visa\n        \n\n          \nUnited States of America\nVisa Type\n                                             \n\n          \nL1\nVisa Issue Date\n                                                \n\n           \n20 Apr 2006\nVisa Valid Till\n                                       \n\n           \n31 Jan 2009\n\nCORRESPONDENCE ADDRESS ? \n\n985/1, 12TH MAIN, \n\nst\n CROSS, HAL 2\nnd\n STAGE, \nINDIRANAGAR, BANGALORE ? 560038\n\nPERMANENT ADDRESS ? \n\n214 A, CIVIL LINES, \nK D SINGH BABU ROAD, \nBARABANKI U.P. 225001, INDIA\n\n\n\n(BHUWNENDRA VEKRAM SINGH)','IBM India',1,NULL,'2007-10-15',NULL,'2007-10-15','2010-06-08 12:13:25','2010-06-08',3,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(84,'Arnab sahara',NULL,NULL,'Bangalore','Arnab99999@gmail.com',NULL,NULL,'0','9342567092','0',NULL,'0','2007-08-15',7,18,'2010-06-08 12:13:25',3,'0',NULL,'200710/15/ATT61739.html','200710/15/DOC55918.doc','Sarika_resume\n\nARNAB SAHARA\nMobile No: +91-9342567092\nArnab99999@gmail.com\n\n\nObjective\n\nA Team member with a well experience in Software development. Able to work on own initiative and as part of a team. First-class analytical, design and problem solving skills. Dedicated to maintaining high quality standards.\n Basically a person with very positive attitude and can give its best commitment towards its employer\n\nProficiency in \nServlet, JSP, Struts\n\nJDBC, EJB 2.0, ORACLE 8i, Web Logic 8.0, Tomcat 5.4\n\n\nSummary\n\n\n\n   \n2.6 ye\nars of working experience in the field of Software Development having actively\n                      \n    \nInvolved in Developing, Deploying and Maintaining application using \njava\n and \nJ2EE\n\n\n   \nGood Experience in Developing Applications using \nServlets\n\nJSP\n\nJDBC\n\nStruts and Oracle.\n\nExperience Summary\n\n     \nTotal IT Experience: 2.6 Years\n\n       \nWorking as a\n Software\n Engineer \nfor\n\nVerna Info Solutions\n\nBangalore\n\nfrom Feb 2005\n\nto till date \n\n\nTechnical Skills\n\nJ2EE/\nWeb Technologies\nServlet, JSP, JDBC, EJB 2.0\nLanguage\nJava\nFrame Work\nStruts\nOperating Systems\nWindows 2000/AS\nWeb server\nTomcat 5.4\nApp Server\n                         \nWeb Logic 8.1\nDatabases\n                  \nOracle 8i\nIDE/GUI Tools\nJBuilder\n\n\n\n\nProject:1\n                                                  \n                   \n                     \nFeb-2007\n? Till date\n\nShopemen\n\nClient\nEarthbase Infotech\n, Pune\nType\nOnline Shopping & Bidding Portal\n(B2B)\nRole\nSoftware Engineer\nEnvironment\n\nWindows 2000\nTechnology\nJava, JSP, Servlet, Struts, EJB , JDBC, JTA, Oracle 8i\nFramework\n                              \nStruts\nApplication Server\n              \n                                              \nWebLogic 8.1\nResponsibilities\n\n       \nInvolved in development of Controller part using STRUTS technology. \n\n       \nInvolved in creation of business logic implementation model layer using EJB, JTA, JDBC\nDescription\n: In a nutshell: The major objective of this project is to develop a web portal for bidding system to make business transactions more users friendly. Here the users have to register themselves as buyer or seller for placing up a tender with their requisites and to review them to give their revised quotations before the administrator prepares the auction procedures. Beside online bidding or web auction and also facilities are provided for virtual store where the sellers can directly place their goods for sale the products which are placed in virtual store are available for online shopping. So the proposed system will provide an end-to-end user environment ease to use.\n\nProject:2\n                                                               \n          \n             \nMay 2006 ? Dec 2006\n\nJcafe\n\nClient\nRestored Media Technology\n, Ambarnath East, Maharastra\nType\nOnline Java/J2EE Portal\nRole\nTeam Member\nEnvironment\nWindows 2000\nTechnology\nJSP, Servlet, EJB, Oracle 8i\nApplication Server\nWeblogic 8.1\nResponsibilities\n\n       \nInvolved in developing components for managing efficient data flow using JavaBean.\n\n       \nInvolved in creation of components for interaction between Controller layer, Model layer and Database tier using EJB, JDBC, and JTA.\nDescription\n\n\nThe primary scope of the proposed application was to design, develop, test and deliver a web based application that would enable end users to get and give project guidance through online. Out side cities of this proprietor office, B.E/B.TECH/M.C.A student can get online Project guidance for their final year project, as well as experienced professionals would earn money providing guidance in their corresponding cities to the service seekers, registered with this site. Except guidance students can also do download free related software, demo- project, e-books etc. But they all should be a registered user.\n\n\n\nProject:3\n                                                            \n               \n         \nMay 2005 ? April 2006\n\nGeezemail\n\nClient\nJuniper Info Tech, Pune\nType\nMultilingual Web Mail Application\nRole\nTeam Member\nEnvironment\nWindows 2000, Linux (Fedora Core 4)\nTechnology\nJAF, JavaMail, Servlet, JSP, JavaBean, JDBC, Hibernate\nMail Server\nJames-2.2.0 (\nJava Apache Mail \nEnterprise\n Server), SMTP, POP3\nAntivirus\nclamAV0.88\nWeb Server\n\n\nTomcat-5.0.25\n\nResponsibilities\n\n       \nCode developing.\n\n       \nDebugging and Implementation.\n\nDescription\n\nThis project is a cross browser portable application; developed based on \njava unicode\n to provide the \nmultilingual\n\nfunctionalities\n (Geez, Amharic, Trigna African languages). A user can access the application in these three different languages. The core parts of this project are \n\n.New User creation in the mail server and database. \n\n.Changing password and retrieving forgotten password \n\n. Sending and receiving the mails for the user. \n\n. Sending mail automatically \n\n.Composing the formatted text mail in three different languages based on java unicode.\n\n. Inbox, out box, Draft folder, maintaining the deleted mail in database. \n\n. Address book maintenances, \n\n.Job scheduling. \n\n. User payment maintenance. \n10.\n Blocking particular users and domains.\n\n\nAcademic Credentials\n\nBSc. In Software Systems\n\nfrom \nUniversity\n Of \nNorth Bengal\n\nDarjeeling\n with\n 50.1%\n\n\n\n\nPersonal Information:\n\nFather?s Name\nAdhir Kumer Saha\nMother?s Name\nNamita Saha\nDate of Birth\n10 th January,1981\nSex\nMale\nMarital Status\nSingle\nLanguages Known\nEnglish, Hindi, and Bengali\nCurrent Company\nVerna Info Solution\nURL\nhttp://vernainfo.com/\n\nDECLARATION\n\nInformation provided is meant for depicting the work, skill of the candidate. The projects details shown above are the main projects involved. I here by declare that the above information is true to the best of my Knowledge and belief.\n\nDate\nArnab Saha','Verna Info Solutions',1,NULL,'2007-10-15',NULL,'2007-10-15','2010-06-08 12:13:25','2010-06-08',3,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(85,'Vishnu B',NULL,NULL,'Banglore','visfbfbbhnu2boddu@gmail.com',NULL,NULL,'0','9242805982','0',NULL,'0','2006-12-13',10,34,'2010-06-08 12:13:25',2,'0',NULL,'200710/16/ATT53988.html','200710/16/DOC40070.doc','Vishnu Mohan\nVishnu B\nMobile No : +91-9242805982\n   \n                                        \n       \nvisfbfbbhnu2boddu@gmail.com\n\n\nProfessional Summary:\n\n\n       \nHaving 3+ years of experience in software Development.\n\n       \nExtensively worked on \nInformatica\n Designer.\n\n       \nStrong working experience on Data Warehousing applications, directly responsible for the Extraction, Transformation and Loading of data from multiple sources into warehouse.\n\n       \nExtensive knowledge on SQL.\n\n       \nExtensively worked on Oracle 9i.\n\n       \nExcellent in communication, technical skills.\n\nAcademic Qualification:\n\n\n       \nB.Tech\n\nComputer\n Science and Engineering\n\nfrom Jawaharlal Nehru Technological University, \nHyderabad\n\nAndhra Pradesh\n\nIndia\n\n\nProfessional Experience:\n\n1.\n      \nWorking as a \nData warehouse consultant in \nWipro\n Technologies Ltd,\nBangalore\nfrom March? 2006 to till date.\n\n2.\n      \nWorked as a \nData warehouse consultant in \nASM Technologies Limited\n\nBangalore\n from Jun?2004 to Feb?2006.\n\n\n\nSoftware Skills:\n\nData warehouse Tools\n\n   \n                          \nETL\n                           \n\n           \nInformatica\n\n( Designer\n\n\n\n            \nDatabase packages\n                   \n\n          \nOracle 9i\n      \nOperating Systems\n                    \n\n          \nWindows, UNIX\n      \nProgramming Langages\n\n\n          \nC,C++,SQL\n      \nInternet technologies\n                 \n\n\n          \nHTML.\n      \nData \nmodaling\n tool\n                    \n\n           \nErwin 4.0\n      \nOLAP Tools\n                            \n\n           \nBO?s\n,Cognos\n\n\n\n\n\nPROJECT DETAILS:\nProject #1\nVCA Data Warehouse \nProject\n\n\n Thames Water Utilities, \nUK\n\nPeriod\n\n Feb?2007 \n- Till Date.\n\nDescription\n\nThames Water Utilities is the \nUK\n?s largest water and wastewater services company with over 4,000 employees providing service round the clock to 13 million customers across \nLondon\n and the Southeast of England.\n They provide services such as underground pipeline and networks, integrated waste management solutions and maintenance & facilities management. We built a Data Warehouse solution within the\n Thames Water Utilities\n environment named as \n   \nValue Chain \nAnalysis\n\n The VCA project began with the aim of developing the ability to understand costs at the sub regional level across the \ncompany.The\n aim of the VCA project was to replace the manual extraction with automatic process using \nInformatica\n Power Centre ETL tool. \n\nEnvironment:\n\n\nInformatica\n 7.1, Oracle and Windows NT\n\nResponsibilities:\n\n\n       \nImporting Source/Target Tables from the respective databases and created Reusable Transformations and Mappings using Designer Tool set of \nInformatica\n\n\n       \nExtensively worked in data Extraction, Transformation and Loading from source to target system using power center of \nInformatica\n\n\n       \nWorked on various tools in \nInformatica\n like Source analyzer, Warehouse Designer, Transformation developer, Mapping Designer & \nMapplet\n Designer.\n\n       \nMost of the Transformations were used like the Source Qualifier, Aggregator, Filter, Router, Sequence Generator, Lookup, Joiner and Update strategy\n\n       \nExtensively used \nInformatica\n Power center for loading the data from various source involving flat files and oracle tables.\n\n       \nDoing Development and Unit Testing.\n\n       \nDeveloped mappings to load data into dimension tables and fact tables.\n\n       \nCreated reusable sessions and workflows to load the data into warehouse.\n\n\nProject #2\n\nData Warehouse for \nExel\nOyj\n\nPeriod\n\n April?2006 \n? Jan?2007.\n\nDescription\n\nExel\n\nOyj\n is one of the largest sports good retailer and manufacturer in the world selling athletic footwear, apparel and equipment The client wanted to synchronize its \"Sell\", \"Plan-Buy\", \"Make\" and \"Deliver\" processes and systems with its factories, suppliers, service providers and retailers. To achieve this we \nbiuilt\n a data warehousing solution which address four functional groups - planning, sales, logistics and \nfinance.\n\nInformatica\n is used as an ETL tool to load the data from all the several source systems. Here the input data is in flat files and the target database is DB2.\n\nEnvironment: \n\n            \nInformatica\n 7.1, Oracle and Windows NT\n\nResponsibilities:\n\n\n       \nTranslated Business processes into \nInformatica\n mappings. \n\n       \nDeveloped Complex mappings by extensively using \nInformatica\n Transformations like Lookup, Filter, Expression, Aggregator, Joiner etc.\n\n       \nLoading of data from Source system (Flat Files) to target DB2 Database.\n\n       \nCreated Sessions using the Workflow Manager.\n\n       \nDocumented the existing mappings.\n\n       \nPerforming Unit Testing for Mappings.\n\n       \nPreparation of\n\nuser test plans\n\n       \nPreparation of weekly status reports.\n\n\nProject #3\n\nData Marts for Robert Systems.\n                                                                                  \n            \nPeriod\n\n May?2005 \n? Feb?2006.\n\nDescription\n\nRobert Systems Ltd. is world\'s largest independent supplier of automobile seating and interior systems such as overhead systems and door panels, instrument panels and floor consoles. \nWorked on various departments like Sales & Marketing, Procurement.\n\nEnvironment:\n\n\n            \nInformatica\n 6.1, Oracle and Windows NT\n\nResponsibilities:\n\n\n       \nUnderstanding and analyzing the Requirements.\n\n       \nPreparation of Mapping Documents\n\n       \nMost of the Transformations were used like the Source Qualifier, Aggregator, Filter, Router, Sequence Generator, Lookup, Joiner and Update strategy\n\n       \nDoing Development and Unit Testing.\n\n       \nPreparation of\n\nuser test plans\n\n       \nPreparation of weekly status reports.\nProject #4\n\nData Mart for Sears Robust & \nCo.\n                           \n                                               \n\nPeriod\n\n July?2004 \n? April?2005.\n\nDescription\n\nData marts and Data Warehouse is constructed to stage the retail Sales Analysis and Inventory related data. BO is used to develop various reports like Sales Performance, Regional Sales, Financials reports etc.\n\nEnvironment:\n\n\n            \nInformatica\n 5.1, Oracle and Windows NT\n\nResponsibilities:\n\n\n       \nDevelopment of ETL Process using \nInformatica\n Tool.\n\n       \nCreated and Maintained various mappings and reusable transformations\n\n       \nApplied various transformations to the source data before loading into the staging area.\n\n       \nInvolved in debugging the mappings.\n\n       \nEffectively involved in closing the defects raised by the client during testing.\n\n       \nUsed various transformations like Joiner, Aggregator, expression, Filter, lookup, sequence generator and router in developing the mappings.\n\n       \nCreating Email tasks for sending an email after the session runs.\n\n\n\n                                                                      ','Wipro Technologies Ltd',1,NULL,'2007-10-16',NULL,'2007-10-16','2010-06-08 12:13:25','2010-06-08',2,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(86,'Srikanth',NULL,NULL,NULL,'sriscsackanth.orsccaapps@gmail.com','srikanth.oraapps@gmail.com',NULL,'0','91 9886437369','0',NULL,'0','2007-01-28',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-08 12:13:25',2,'0',NULL,'200710/16/ATT54005.html','200710/16/DOC40071.doc','Resdex @ naukri.com\nsrikanth\nsriscsackanth.orsccaapps@gmail.com\n\nTelephone: 9886437369\n(M)\n\nD.O.B\n - 18 Jun 1982 \nModified on\n - 26 Sep 2007 \nAnnual Salary\n - INR 3 Lac(s) 80 Thousand \nTotal Years of Experience\n - 3 Year(s) 3 Month(s) \nCurrent Location\n - Bangalore \nPreferred Location\n - Anywhere in India \nHaving 3.2 years exp in oracle apps\n\nTEXT RESUME \n\nSrikanth Email: srikanth.oraapps@gmail.com\nTechnical Consultant Phone : +91-9886437369\nOBJECTIVE\nI Strive for Excellence in all my endeavors and I look forward to work in a World-Class team of competent and motivated individuals.\nEXPERIENCE SUMMARY\n\n?3.2 years Experience in IT Industry.\n\n?2+ years of hands on experience in ERP ? Oracle 11i Applications.\n\n?Having Very good exposu\nre to implementation of Oracle 11i Applications.\n\n?Worked on Functional Modules like PO, INV, GL, \nOM\n, AP.\n\n?Development and customization of Reports, Interfaces.\n\n?Good knowledge on SQL * Loader.\n\n?Creation of Value sets in various Modules of the applicat\nion.\n\n?Defining Concurrent Programs, Executables.\n\n?PL/SQL method of submitting Concurrent programs\nWORKING EXPERIENCE\n? Working as a Technical Consultant for Trianz, \nBangalore\n from April 2005 to till date.\n? Worked as Software Trainee for Globus Systems, \nBangalore\n From May 2004 to March 2005.\nTECHNICAL SKILLS\nERP : Oracle Applications 11i (PO, INV, AP)\nProgramming Languages : C, SQL, PL/SQL\nDatabase : Oracle 8i\nOperating Systems : Windows 98/NT/2000 Server\nG.U.I : Forms6i, Reports6i\nTools : SQL* Loader, TOAD\nEducation Qualification:\n\n?B.C.A from \nAcharya\nNagarjuna\nUniversity\n\nGuntur\n\nPROJECT EXPERIENCE DETAILS:\nProject #1\nClient : \nCDL\n\nUK\nRole : Technical consultant.\nEnvironment : Oracle Applications 11.5.9, Reports 6I, PL/SQL,\nSQL*Loader\nDescription:\nCDL is a global leader in reliable portable data storage. CDL solutions help consumers, home and small business customers to manage, preserve, use and share their digital content and data. CDL provides personal storage solutions that help people manage their important information. CDL is the leading manufacturer of smart, portable storage solutions, including drives and disks.\nResponsibilities:\nAs a Team Member, was responsible for:\n\n?Analysis of the specifications provided by the client.\n\n?Involved in customization and development of Reports and Interfaces.\n\n?Have been involved in the Multi language Report Output generation.\n\n?Preparation of Technical Design Documents.\n\n?Validation of staging data before insertion into Oracle base tables \nor Interface tables.\n\n?Registrations of Custom Tables and Concurrent Programs.\n\n?Creation of Value sets in various Modules of the application.\n\n?Preparation of SQL Loader scripts.\n\n?Involved in creating unit test cases.\nInterface development:\n\n?Customiz\ned AP Invoice Import Program to upload Invoices into the Oracle Apps base tables.\n\n?Developed Purchase order inbound Interface to upload the Purchase orders details from the legacy to Oracle Apps base tables.\nReports:\n\n?Developed Standard Purchase Order\n Report.\n\n?Customized Payables Account Analysis Report.\n\n?Developed Internal requisition report.\n\n?Developed Customer Master Report.\n\n?Customized Quotation Action Required Report.\n\n?Developed advance purchase order information.\nProject #2\nClient : Integra, New York, USA.\nRole : Technical Consultant.\nEnvironment : Oracle Applications 11.5.9, SQL, PL/SQL, Reports 6i,\nSQL*Loader\nDescription:\nIntegra Systems is implementing Oracle Applications Suite to meet its E-Business vision. It is carrying out the implementation in a global single instance in a finance &discrete manufacturing environment. The project has been undertaken to streamline its Global business activities covering Financial, Distribution and Manufacturing operations. The objective is to phase out the numerous isolated legacy systems currently in use and to seamlessly integrate all the local business operations worldwide with its global business operation. To achieve this goal, entire system is being implemented in a single instance of database, which will support its global business operations as well as provide real time global data to management for taking appropriate decisions.\nResponsibilities:\n\n?Involved in customizing and Development of the Reports and Interfaces.\n\n?Preparation o\nf Technical Design Documents.\n\n?Validation of staging data before insertion into Oracle base tables or Interface tables.\n\n?Registrations of Custom Tables and Concurrent Programs.\n\n?Creation of Value sets in various Modules of the application.\n\n?Preparation\n of SQL Loader scripts.\n\n?Involved in Client meetings.\nInterfaces:\n\n?Developed Purchase order inbound Interface to upload the Purchase orders details from the legacy to Oracle Apps base tables.\n\n?Developed outbound interface to extract the data from the\n Oracle Apps tables to the Flat file.\nReports:\n\n?Developed total purchased order report (supplier wise).\n\n?Developed approved requisition details.\n\n?Customized Sales order Acknowledgement Report.\n\n?Developed AP invoice payment report.\n\n?Developed blanke\nt purchased order report.\n\n?Developed Purchase Order and Payables analysis report.\nProject #3\nClient : WGT\nRole : Software Developer\nEnvironment : PL/SQL, Oracle 8i, Forms 6i & Reports 6i.\nProject Description:\nThis project is designed to computerize the operations of the client who is involved in bulk sales of pharmaceuticals to various hospitals and medical outlets. Stock details and Products can be viewed using Lov?s. The software developed has been extremely user friendly with messaged boxes guiding the user for navigation. Reports are generated for daily, weekly month sales. An area and company wise report is also generated to keep track of the monthly purchases made.\nResponsibilities:\n\n?Developing Reports and Forms as per Client Requirement.\n\n\nDeveloping Procedures, Functions, Packages\n\n?Writing code for Reports and Forms\n\n?Preparing Technical Documentation.\n\n?Involved in Product demos and Client engagements\nProject #4\nProject Title : vendor systems\nRole : Software Developer.\nEnvironment : PL/SQL, Oracle 8i,Forms 6i & Reports 6i.\nProject Description:\nVendor System is covers the activities of Stores, Purchase and Goods Inwards Functions of a Manufacturing Organization. This Module has provisions to capture Supplier Details (Vendors) required for the Purchase Department. It facilitates Stores to check the stock of the Raw Materials used and System automatically places Purchase Requisitions to the Purchase Department. Purchase Department can place Purchase-Orders and keep track of the Work-orders given to the Vendors. When the raw material is received, corresponding Stock is updated.\nResponsibilities:\n\n?Developing Report and Forms as per Client Requirement.\n\n?Developing Procedures, Functions.\n\n?Writing code for Reports and Forms.\n\n?Prepari\nng Technical Documentation.',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-16',NULL,'2007-10-16','2010-06-08 12:13:25','2010-06-08',2,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(87,'V. Manjunath',NULL,NULL,NULL,'vdfdsivamansdvfdfjunath@gmail.com',NULL,NULL,'0','9884352298','0',NULL,'0','2005-04-29',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-08 12:13:25',2,'0',NULL,'200710/16/ATT54004.html','200710/16/DOC40072.doc','CURRICULAM VITAE\nV. Manjunath\n                                                                    \nMobile:9884352298\nvdfdsivamansdvfdfjunath@gmail.com\n                                                                   \n                                          \n                                                                           \n\n\nSummary:\n\n\n        \nHaving more than 5 years of Strong functional experience in Financial Sector like Mutual funds, Stocks Brokerage.\n\n        \nExperience in Full Life Cycle Implementation of Oracle Financials 11i (GL/AP/AR): Analysis, Development, Testing, Implementation and Support\n\n        \nExperience in Testing and Maintenance Support for O2C Modules.\n\n        \nGood knowledge on system study, Business process modeling and functional design. \n      \n\n        \nStrong skills in Oracle Applications-Financials.\n\n        \nAble to work independently with end-user and with in the IT team.\n\n        \nGood communication and interpersonal skills.\n\n\nQualifications: \n\n\n        \nM.B.A. (Finance) from Jawaharlal Nehru Technological University, \nHyderabad\n. (Jan?1999).\n\n        \nPursuing PG Diploma in Investment Banking(PGDIB)\nFrom \nICFAI\nUniversity\n\n\n        \nB.Sc. (Statistics)\n\nfrom \nSri\nKrishnadevaraya\nUniversity\n, Anantapur.\n\nTechnical skills:\n\n\n        \nERP\n            \n: Oracle Financials 11i Modules AR,AP,GL&FA.\n\n        \nPackages\n     \n: Oracle 8i\n\n        \nTools\n           \n: MS Office\n\n        \nOperating systems: Windows 98,Windows XP.\n\nProject Experience:\n                                            \nProject 1 :\n\nTitle\n                            \n: Maintenance Support\n for O2C Modules.\n\nClient\n\n            \n          \n  \n: PASCI(Pfizer Accelerated \nSolution Center\nIndia\n).\n\nTeam Size\n                   \n: 6\n\nDuration\n                     \n: Aug\'06 ? Till date.\n\nRole\n                          \n\n: Team Member (Pfizer EFSS AD-O2C Team).\n\nAbout The Project\n    \n\nPASCI is a \nSoftware\nService\nCenter\n setup for assisting and developing Pfizer ERP Model.\n\nhe project involved in leading Off-Shore Implementation of Oracle Applications 11i, Application Testing and Off-Shore Support of Oracle Applications for European Financials of Pfizer.\n\n\nResponsibilities:\n\n\n        \nResolving Client Issues related to AR and OM Modules.\n\n        \nCorrecting Auto Invoice Errors and Process the Invoices.\n\n        \nResolving Issues related to Auto Invoice.\n\n        \nResolving Issues related to Imported Order.\n\n         \nUnderstanding the system related and operating issues raised by the users and providing viable solutions based on the priority of the request\n\n         \nActively interacting with the users to understand their requirements.\n\n         \nEducating the user through mails, phone calls about the apps setups and their impact on functionality.\n\n         \nPreparation of Process Documents for any critical issues as mapping of the requirements with Standard 11i functionality.\n\n         \nPreparation of Apps Setup Change documents if any of the issues require change in the existing setup or requires any new features to be setup.\n\n         \nTroubleshooting and Creation of SR?s with Oracle for production support issues and the application of Patches and testing the same in Testing and Development instances.\n\n\nProject 2 :\n\nTitle\n                            \n\nImplementation of Oracle Applications-11i.(AR,AP,GL &FA)\n\nClient\n\n            \n            \n: Commercial Real Estate Company,\n    \n                                  \n(Onsite Project), \nKuwait\n\nDuration\n                     \n: Feb\n\'06 ? Jul?06.\n\nTeam Size\n                   \n: 9\n\nRole\n                          \n\n\nFunctioned as a Team Member.\n\nResponsibilities\n         \n\n\n\n        \nPrepared RD20 and BR30 Documents for AR and AP Modules.\n\n        \nDocumented Application Setup(BR.100) for AR and AP Modules.\n\n        \nInvolved in defining setups for AR,AP, GL and FA.\n\n        \nDeveloped FSG Reports\n\n\nProject 3 :\n\nTitle\n                            \n\nImplementation of Oracle Applications-11i.(AR,AP,GL&FA)\n\nClient\n\n            \n            \n: India Pistons ltd., Sembiam, Chennai.\n\nDuration\n                     \n: May?\n05 ? Dec\'05.\n\nRole\n                          \n\n: Involved in Implementation from Client side.\n\nLine of business of the client: Manufacturers of Pistons, Rings and Gudgeon Pins.\n\nAbout the project\n       \n:The project Aims at Implementing Oracle 11i across all the business units of IPL. IPL intends to consolidate and integrate its various entities, automate the standard Financial functions, and thereby enhance productivity, Customer service and Business growth\n\n\n                                     \nResponsibilities\n          \n\n\n\n        \nDefined AR setups in CRP2.\n\n        \nTested AR Business Cases in CRP2.\n\n        \nTrained and assisted Super user in Understanding Oracle Financials.\n\n        \nPrepared User Training Manuals for all Financial Modules.\n\n        \nDeveloped FSG Reports.\n\n        \nTrained end user after implementation.\n\n        \nPost implementation support for AR and AP modules.\n\n\nWork Experience:\nAug?2006-Till Date\n                                                        \n    \nAs Functional Specialist with ?Thirdware \n      \n              \n        \n      \n  \n                                                                                             \nBusiness Solutions?, Ascendes International\n                    \n                                                                \n\n   \n                         \nTech\nPark\n, Chennai.\n                                                                                                                                                                  \n                                                 \n                                                                             \nMay?2005-Jul?2006\n     \n                                                     \n   \nAs Functional Consultant with\n                                                             \n        \n                    \n\n?Broadgate Technical Services (\nIndia\n) Pvt Ltd?,\n                  \n                                                                                            \n  \nRoyapettah,Chennai.\n          \n       \n\nMar?2004-Sep?2004\n                   \n                                         \nAs Back Office Executive With \n                                                                                             \n?ICICI Two Wheeler Loans?,\n          \n                                                      \n                                       \nBegumpet, \nHyderabad\n\n\n\n        \nAnalyzing Customers capability.\n\n        \nAnalyzing customer?s strengths and drawbacks\n\n        \nPreparing Credit Approval Memorandum (\nCAM\n).\n\nJan?2003-Feb?2004\n                                                        \n       \nAs Supervisor with ?Lokesh Pharma?\n                                                                 \n                               \nL.B.Road,\nHyderabad\n(Super Distributors for\n                         \n                                                   \n              \n                               \nCipla and Sun Pharmaceuticals\n\n\n\n        \nDealing with Customers.\n\n        \nAssisting Accounts Officer.\n\n        \nResponsible for entire dealings.\n\nOct?2000-Dec?2002\n                                                               \nAs Executive-Operations with \n                                                                                                \n?Hanuman sai investments Ltd?, \n                                                                                                \nHyderabad.(Stock Brokerage Firm).\n\n\n        \nReceiving orders from customers.\n\n        \nQuoting Orders in the terminal.\n\n        \nHandling and resolving queries for priority Customer Base.\n\n        \nPreparing Customer Reports.\n\n\nAug?1999-Sep?2000\n                                                               \nAs Executive With \n                                                                                               \n\nKarvy Consultants Ltd?, \nHyderabad\n\n                                                          \n\n        \nFinding NAV value for Birla Mutual Fund.\n\n        \nFinding total Sales and total redemptions for mutual fund.\n\n\nAcademic Projects:\n\n\n        \nFinancial Statement Analysis: A Study of NCL Industries Ltd.\n\n        \nIndustry Analysis of ?Cement Industry?.\n\n        \nCompany Analysis Report on ?Raasi Cements Ltd?.\n\n\n\n                              \n                                                                      ',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-16',NULL,'2007-10-16','2010-06-08 12:13:25','2010-06-08',2,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(88,'Subhankar Bohidar',NULL,NULL,NULL,'scsacsdssc@gmail.com',NULL,NULL,'0',NULL,'0',NULL,'0','2007-11-28',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-08 12:13:25',2,'0',NULL,'200710/16/ATT54003.html','200710/16/DOC40073.doc','RANJAN KUANAR\nSUBHANKAR BOHIDAR\n                                                      \n\n\nEmail ID:\nscsacsc@gmail.com\n                                                      \n\n\nMobile\n\n\n+91?934sac2210060\n\n\n\nObjective\n\n\nA Challenging and responsible position, which provide a platform to use my abilities with functional and technical skills in the field of Information Technology with present technology for the organization using professional approach to contribute towards organization growth.\n\n\nProfessional Expertise\n\n\n\n      \nAbout \n2.5 year?s\n significant experience in the IT industry in \nOracle\n\nApplications 11i \nas \nTechno-Functional Consultant\n\n\n      \nExperience on modules like PO, AP,\n\nGL, \nOM\n\nAR\n and INV for overseas clients. \n\n      \nKnowledge of the development and customization of business applications according to customer requirements.\n\n      \nDomain Knowledge in Oracle \nPurchasing\n and Oracle \nFinance\n\n\n\nEducational Profile\n\n\n\n         \nBachelor of Engineering in \nComputer Science\n from \nBiju\nPattanaik\nUniversity\n Orissa, \nin\n 2004.\n\nEmployment Summary\n\nCompany\nName\nLocation\nDesignation\nStarting\nDate\nEnding date\nCGI Netvorks\nBangalore\nTechno-Functional Consultant\n10/01/05\nTill date\n\n\nTechnical Skills\n\nOperating Systems\nWindows 2000/XP/NT\nLanguages\nSQL, PL/SQL\nERP\nOracle Apps\nDatabase\nOracle 8i/9i\nTools\nToad, SQL Loader, ERP Tool Time Management System\nGUI\nD2K (Form6i, Report6i)\nDomain Knowledge\nOracle Purchasing, Finance\n\n\n\n     \nMajor Projects\n\n\n\n#1.Oracle Apps Implementation\n\nOrganization/Client\nWACHOVIA CORPORATION Ltd., \nUSA\n\nDuration\n     \nOct.2006 to till date\n        \nPosition\nTechno Functional Consultant\n                \nTeam size: 5\nResponsibilities\n\n                     \nWriting SQL Loader Control files to transfer the data from flat files into staging tables.\n\n                     \nWriting Pl/SQL packages & procedures for data validation & data transfer.\n\n                     \nCreating concurrent programs & request sets.\n\n                     \nCustomization / development of oracle apps report.\n   \n\nDescription\n           \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n           \nThis project aims at implementing oracle application modules. As a part of implementation involves transferring their legacy system data\n\ninto Oracle Apps tables as well as developing & customizing the reports to suite their needs.\n\nDETAILS:\n\n         \nVander Evolution Interface\n\n         \nItem loading Interface\nREPORTS:\n\n         \nUn booked sales order report\n\n         \nSales Order status Report\n\n         \nPayment Origination Report\n\nOperating System\nWindows 2000/XP/NT\nDatabase\nOracle 9i, Toad\nGUI\nD2K (Form 6i, Report 6i)\nUtilities\nExport, Import, SQL*Loader\n\n\n\n#2. Oracle Apps Integration\n\nOrganization/Client\nTEXAS MICROSYSTEMS, USA\nDuration\n     \n10Months (Oct.05 to Aug.06)\n   \nPosition\nTechno Functional Consultant\n                \nTeam size: 5\nResponsibilities\n\n      \nThrough SQL loader and control files transfer the flat file data to staging tables.\n\n      \nCreating some transport programs and procedures for data validation and data transfer.\n\n      \nDefining the concurrent programs and request sets.\n\n      \nAnalyze and customizing Oracle Apps Reports.\n   \nDescription\n          \nThe main objective of this project is to implement oracle purchasing module, which comprises improved and efficient handling of operation and to provide upload and download facilities to export and import data to external system. The implementation part involving transferring the legacy system data into Oracle Apps tables as well\n   \nas developing and customizing the reports to suite the needs.\n\nDETAILS:\n\n         \nPO\n Interface\n\nREPORTS:\n\n         \nPurchase requisition for which tender yet to be invited\n\n         \nPurchase requisition for which tender invited but PO/contract yet to be placed\n\n         \nPurchase requisition for which PO/contract placed\n\nOperating System\nWindows 2000/XP/NT\nDatabase\nOracle 9i\nGUI\nD2K (Form 6i, Report 6i)\nUtilities\nExport, Import, SQL*Loader\n\n\nPersonal Profile\n\n           \nDDDDDD DDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDD\n                 \nGender\n                 \n          \n\n       \nMale.\nMarital Status\n      \n          \n\n        \nSingle.\nFather?s Name\n     \n          \n\n        \nMr. J.N.Bohidar.\nLanguages Known\n        \n\n       \nEnglish, Hindi.\n\n\nShould you feel convinced as regards the achievements stipulated, May please contact me to be across your table to justify my worth for the position applied for, I shall be grateful.\n\n\n\n\n\nDate:\n    \n                                                                                                      \nSubhankar Bohidar',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-16',NULL,'2007-10-16','2010-06-08 12:13:25','2010-06-08',2,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(89,'Subhrajyoti B',NULL,NULL,'Bangalore','subhrajyscsacoti_brahscma@rediffmail.com','subhrascsacjyoti.bscsacrahma@gmail.com',NULL,'0','9916084586','0',NULL,'0','2007-03-15',7,18,'2010-06-08 12:13:25',2,'0',NULL,'200710/16/ATT54002.html','200710/16/DOC40074.doc','SUBHRAJYOTI BRAHMA\nSUBHRAJYOTI B\n                                          \nADDRESS:\nsubhrajyscsacoti_brahscma@rediffmail.com\n      \n                                    \nG.V.\nReddy\nBuilding\n\nsubhrascsacjyoti.bscsacrahma@gmail.com\n                                            \nRoom No 19,\n                           \n            \nsdcsc\n                                                                            \nVinayak layout,\n    \n    \n                                        \nOpp.\nSRG\nDental\nCollege\n\nMunekallal,\nMarthahalli, \nBangalore\n -37\n      \n                  \n                                                                        \nMOBILE-91-9916084586\n      \n_______________________________________________________________________\n\nOBJECTIVE:\n\nSeeking a position to utilize my skills and abilities in the Information Technology Industry and nurture my career with consulting challenges that offers professional growth while being\n   \nresourceful,\n   \ninnovative\n   \nand flexible.\n\nTECHNICAL ENVIRONMENT:\n\nOperating System\n   \nWINDOWS 95/98, XP\nDatabase\nORACLE 8i, ORACLE 9i,\n Teradata\nLanguages\nPL\\SQL\n\n SQL\n, BTEQ\nETL Tool\nInformatica 7.1\nReporting Tool\nBusiness Objects 5.1.9\nOther Tools\nTOAD 8.0.0.47\n\nVSS 6.0,\nVisio 2000\nInternational Certification\n       \nCCNA (CISCO ID-CSCO10691264)\n\nEDUCATIONAL QUALIFICATION:\n\n# B.E. in Comp. Sc.& Engg. from \nUtkal\nUniversity\n, In 2003 with avg. 67%.\n# 12th\n\nFrom C.H.S.E Orissa, In 1998 with 67 %.\n# 10th\n\nFrom H.S.C. Orissa, In 1996 with 82 %.\n\nTOTAL IT EXPERIENCE:\n\nOrganization\n      \n                                   \n\nTata Consultancy Limited\n\nBangalore\nDesignation \n                                          \n: Asst. System Engineer.\nDuration\n                                               \n: 3-Jan-2007 to Till Date\n\nOrganization\n      \n                                   \n\nInfosys Technologies Limited\n\nBhubaneswar\nDesignation \n                                          \n: Software Engineer.\nDuration\n                                               \n: 27-Sep-2004 to 15\n-Dec-2006\n\nPROJECTS CARRIED OUT TILL DATE:\n\nTITLE: PROJECT: RTS\nCompany: \nTata Consultancy Ltd, \nBangalore\nDuration: \nJan 2007 to Till Date\nTeam Size: \n21\nClient:\n GEHC (General Electric Health Care)\nAbstract: \nThe project deals with different modules of GEHC like GLA, HR, LCD, AP, AR, OSB, COST, Inventory, Market Maker, CoFe etc.\nDescription:\n General ledger is the main ledger of an organization where the data gets posted from the sub ledgers as well as other non-oracle systems in the form of journal entries. So, all the transactions happening in the sub ledgers like the invoices to the customer, receipts from the customer and invoices from the suppliers can be found here.\nFADB which is used for financial reporting for a long period since 1999 has many stand-alone data marts. But the data here is not global, meaning that data can only be run at a pole level (Asia, Europe and \nAmerica\n).\nGL Analyzer is built in Teradata warehouse. GL Analyzer gets the data loaded from Oracle apps. It stores the data from all the poles. GL Analyzer is slowly replacing FADB and is used for transaction level financial reporting and analysis.\nSince FADB is a reliable system and users have used it for quite a number of years, it is mostly used as a validation system now.\nThis is an enhancement and support project, where in we deliver enhancements requested by client and also solve issues raised by client features to the existing application due to disconnects in the data in FADB and GLA.\nBack End:  \nOracle 9i, Teradata\nLanguages: \nPL\\SQL, SQL, BTEQ\nTools:\n Informatica 7.1\nResponsibilities: \n\n        \nProject Manager\n\n        \nClient Interaction\n\n        \nOnsite offshore co-ordination\n\n        \nCoding.\n\n        \nTesting\n\nTITLE: PROJECT: ABNCDW\nCompany: \nInfosys Technologies Ltd, \nBhubaneswar\nDuration: \nJul 2005 to Till Date\nTeam Size: \n18.\nClient:\n ABN-AMRO (\nNetherlands\n).\nAbstract:\n\nCDW (Commercial Data Warehouse) provides customer and loan based historical data from various source systems and helps ABN Amro to make business decisions. \nCDW is the primary Data warehouse that is extensively used by the ABN Amro business group for key business decision support decisions. The overall CDW architecture centers on the enterprise data warehouse. It is the place where the most granular data resides. The data found in the enterprise data warehouse is detailed, historical and integrated. Due to the nature of this data, data marts are created to represent data in a more user friendly view particular to a business user?s overall needs. CDW stores the historical loan and customer based information, and helps the Business to analyze, understand, review and research the key business trends, profitability, forecasting and make a foundation for the future business decisions.\nCDW is fed from various source systems, eg. DDA, AAD, ABL, AFS, MM, LP, DRV, FMG, BT, FX.\nThe web based Cross-Sell application is used for reporting purpose.\nDescription:\n This is an enhancement project, where in we added new features to the existing application. Project got the \n?Best Project?\n\n ?Spirited Team? \naward. The project has been executed release wise.\nBack End:  \nOracle 8i\nLanguages: \nPL\\SQL, SQL\nTools:\n Informatica 7.1, TOAD 8.0.0.47, VSS 6.0, Visio 2000\nResponsibilities: \n\n        \nLeading Module.\n\n        \nOnsite offshore co-ordination, Process adherence\n\n        \nDesign\n\n        \nDatabase Updations.\n\n        \nCoding.\n\n        \nTesting.\n\nTITLE: PROJECT: \nBASEL\n II\nCompany: \nInfosys Technologies Ltd, \nBhubaneswar\nDuration:\n Nov 2004 to Jun 2005\nTeam Size: \n25.\nClient:\n ABN-AMRO (\nNetherlands\n).\nAbstract:\nBasel\n II involves in managing the Credit Risk, Market Risk and Operational Risk. Experience in developing a data warehousing banking project (BASEL II), tested and implemented successfully. The Client is one of the leading global banks; project involves   fulfilling the client?s needs for establishing a robust Data Warehouse, implementing the BASEL II norms. The project involves building the Financial Reporting Warehouse which is expected to provide the client a sound reporting on its financial status in order to comply with the Basel II norms. The project provided all the challenges which a development project can offer. The project is more of partnership with the client in implementing different business requirements.\nDescription: \nProject got the \n?Best Project?\n\n ?Spirited Team? \naward. The project has been executed release wise.\nTool used:\n Informatica 7.1, TOAD 8.0.0.47, Erwin, VSS 6.0\nLanguages: \nPL\\SQL, SQL\nBack End:  \nOracle 9i\nResponsibilities: \n\n        \nOnsite offshore co-ordination\n\n        \nDatabase Updations.\n\n        \nCoding.\n\n        \nTesting.\n\nPERSONAL DETAILS :\n\nAge & DOB\n    \n     \n                   \n\n 26 years, 14-06-1981\nSex\n                    \n                                  \n\n Male\nMarital Status\n                                     \n\n\n Single\nNationality\n                             \n               \n\n Indian\nLanguages\n   \nKnown\n                   \n           \n\nEnglish, Hindi, Oriya and Bengali\nPassport #\n                                            \n\nF3403273\n\n\nACHIEVEMENTS & HOBBIES:\n\n# Got \n?Spot Award? \nin Infosys in 2006.\n# Awarded school level scholarship 1986 to 1996.\n# Awarded National Rural Talent Scholarship.\n# Solving puzzle books by different authors.\n# Comprehensive problem solving abilities, excellent verbal and written communication skills, ability to deal with people diplomatically, willingness to learn & team facilitator.\n# Good knowledge of the computer internals, hardware and assembling.\n\nDECLARATION:\n\nI hereby declare that the above written particulars are true to the best of my knowledge and belief.\n                                   \n                                                                         \n\nSubhrajyoti Brahma','Tata Consultancy Limited',1,NULL,'2007-10-16',NULL,'2007-10-16','2010-06-08 12:13:25','2010-06-08',2,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(90,'Sudhanshu Bajpai',NULL,NULL,'New Delhi','sudhanshu2006@rediffmail.com',NULL,'09936055312','0','09910343264','0','09334701960','0','2007-06-14',10,34,'2010-06-08 12:13:25',2,'0',NULL,'200710/16/ATT54001.html','200710/16/DOC40075.doc','                                                                                                                                                                                    \n                                                                                    \n                                                                                \nSUDHANSHU BAJPAI\nH No wz -27C? Vishnu Garden Park-1? \nNew Delhi?\n 110018 \nPhone:\n (M) 09910343264 (R) 09936055312\nE-mail:\n sudhanshu2006@rediffmail.com\n\nCareer Objective\n\nSeeking position that would utilize my current skills and challenge my various abilities in Database Administration and various field of Computer Application. Looking for an organization that offers career growth and chance to achieve goals through persistence and hard work.\n\nPROFESSIONAL ACHIVEMENT\n\n\n         \n2.9 years experience in Oracle technology\n\n         \nSound understanding of Oracle database architecture, configuration and administration.\n\n         \nSound knowledge of Backup & Recovery\n\n         \nProficient in backup and recovery with RMAN\n\n         \nGood exposure to Data Guard and Export / Import\n\n          \nGood written and client interaction skills at all management level. Energetic initiator and can learn new technology in short time with proficiency and hardworking in any circumstances\n\n\n\n                                                           \nProfessional Experience\n\n\n         \nWorking for \nJAGRAN PRAKASHAN LIMITED\n, from 1\nst\n Dec -2004 to 30-Apr-2007 as an Oracle Technical.\n\n         \nPresently working as \nSenior Engineer with \n\nIMACHAL \n\nUTURISTIC \n\nOMMUNICATIONS \n\nTD\n   \nposted at \nNew Delhi\n from May-07\n\n\n                                                   \nCURRENT RESPONSIBILITES AND\n\nSKILLS (ORACLE 9I)\n\n\n\nPresently working as \nSenior Engineer with \n\nIMACHAL \n\nUTURISTIC \n\nOMMUNICATIONS \n\nTD\n   \nposted at \nNew Delhi\n. Responsible for maintain the database of MTNL New Delhi & MTNL Mumbai for Sun Solaris OS . \nJob responsibility includes Customer Support & Services, Installation, Maintenance Following is my major responsibility of Oracle 9i Database.\n\n\nInstallation,\n      \nUpgradation, \nMaintenance of Oracle database.\n\nSpace Management (management of tablespaces and datafiles).\n\nManaging backup strategies like cold, hot and logical Proficient in RMAN.\nMaking various customized \nSQL and Discoverer reports\n according to the client?s requirement.\nPrepared all MIS Reports.\nMaintenance of company database.\n\nResponsibilities \n\n\n         \nDesigning & building databases to store information and monitoring performance of the database.\n\n         \nPlanning the capacity of the database and fixing database problems like software failures.\n\n         \nManaging security of the data and ensuring accuracy of the data.\n\n         \nSetting up static and dynamic parameters.\n\n         \nResponsible for planning and performing routine backup and recovery of the databases. \n\n         \nBackup administration of EBS, TAR & ufsdump Backup\n\n         \nFile System administration\n\n\n         \nAllocate system storage and plan for future storage requirements for the database system \n\n         \nInstall the database server and application tools \n\n         \nPlan for backup, recovery of database; back up and restore the database \n\n         \nControl and monitor user access to database; monitor and optimize the performance of database \n\n         \nAllocate system storage and plan for future storage requirements for the database system \n\n         \nCreate primary database storage structures and primary objects \n\n         \nEnroll users and maintain system security, ensuring compliance with database license agreements \n\n         \nDevelop and maintain database standards and conventions; analyze impact of data change \n\n            \nTECHNICAL SKILLS\n\n\nOperating System\n                        \n: Windows 98/ XP\nPackages \n                                   \n: MS Office\nLangages \n                                   \n: C, C++, ASP, JAVA, VC++\nDBMS/ RDBMS\n                    \n: Oracle 9i, MS SQL, \nOracle tools/ Utilities: \n- SQL*PLUS, PL/ SQL\n                    \n- Database Configuration Assistant\n\n- Oracle Enterprise Manager\n\n     \n- ORADIM\n                                      \n- ORAPWD\n                                  \n- ANALYZE\n- DBVERIFY\n                                 \n- Log Miner\n                                 \n- Back up & Recovery Manager\n\n- UMB\n                                                \n- Export/ Import\n                          \n- Explain Plan\n- Oracle Net Manager\n                             \n- TOAD\n\n\n\nTechnical Environment\n\n\nOperating Systems:\n   \n       \nWindows 2000,\n\nSolaris 9\n\nDatabase:\n                  \n            \nSQL, PL/ SQL, iSQL*PLUS, Oracle 8i/9i.Toad\n                                             \nKey Skills as a DBA:\n\nInstalling Oracle Server (9i/8i) on different OS, viz., Windows ,solaris9\nConfiguring the Oracle instance using the Initialization parameters.\nUser management and accessibility.\nDatabase creation and management of logical and physical structure.\nBackup and recovery of database and automation of the same.\nPerforming check for the existence of constraints and indexes to enforce Data Integrity and performance.\nExport, Import, RMAN. (Configuring automated export/ RMAN backups)\nAdministering and securing the database using Roles and Privileges.\nRegular maintenance viz., deleting old core files, cleaning up old trace and log files.\nWriting SQL queries against the database\n\n\nCompany\n          \n\nJagran Prakashan Ltd\n\n          \nwww.jagran.com\nFrom Dec, 04 to Apirl, 07 as Oracle Technical. The job includes\n\nJunior DBA \n\n         \nPlan for backup, recovery of database; backup and restore the database \n\n         \nControl and monitor user access to database; monitor and optimize the performance of database \n\n         \nAllocate system storage and plan for future storage requirements for the database system \n\n\n         \nCreate primary database storage structures and primary objects \n\n         \nEnroll users and maintain system security, ensuring compliance with database license agreements \n\n         \nResponsible for installation, account management, backup/recovery of Oracle 9i databases \n\n         \nResponsible for planning and performing routine backup and recovery of the databases. \n\n         \nProgramming, troubleshooting databases. \n\n\n\nPROJECTS UNDERTAKEN\n\nTitle:\n\nHousekeeping System\n\n                   \nDuration :\n Two months\nTeam Size\n: 2\n                                       \nLanguage :\n Developer ?2k\n\nTools:\n\nOracle9i, Developer 2000, Windows ?NT 4.0, Clients with Windows-98\n\nScope:\n\nHOUSEKEEPING SYSTEM \nsophisticated client server base system. Main function of this project is In hardware level to maintain the inventory of computers and its parts that are purchased for the company and in software Level To records about Severs i.e. how much table spaces we are using in sever .in this software we can trace the size and records of table and rate of increase of database from time to time. This software warns the user that particular table space is going to fill. So we can tune our servers time to time. This Package also gives the all Information about server wise table space used and created, going down up to user wise and each table wise size used and number of rows in a table. This package includes various module i.e. product master, computer master, issue (transaction) module, A.M.C. Module. By this project we can trace about a particular computer and its configuration and where it is located and it has warranty or not and how may times a particular computer got upgraded. My contribution in this package is from system study to Database Designing and then format designing for all Master Tables, Transaction Module and various reports are developed by me in this package.\nCERTIFICATIONS\n\nOracle 9i certified professionals OCP\n\nDatabase Administrator\n\n\n\nEDUCATIONAL QUALIFICATIONS\n\n\n         \nPursuing Oracle 10g certification - DBA Track\n\n         \nMCA from \nNorth\nMaharastra\nUniversity\n Jalgaon\n\nIn Jul-04\n\n         \nBSC (PCM) from \nKanpur\nUniversity\nUniversity\n in Jul-2000.\n\n\n\n\nHobbies:\n\nCricket.\nListening Soft Music.\nLong Driving \nTraveling and interacting with people\n\n            \n\n\n\n\n\n\nPERSONAL DETAILS\n\nFather:\n                                               \nMr. Gokarn Nath Bajpai\nDate of birth:\n\n                            \n\n01-03-1981\nSex:\n                                                    \nMale\nMarital Status:\n\n                          \n\nSingle \nPermanent Address:\n\n                     \n\n30 E/18 Daboli Ratan Lal Nagar \n                      \nKanpur\n -208022\n                              \n                            \n  \nUtter Pradesh.\n\nLanguages known:\n                     \nEnglish, Hindi \nSoft Skills:\n                                  \nQuick Learner, strong communication skills and effective team player.\n\nREFERENCE\n\nName:\n                                       \nMr. Manish Gupta\nCompany:\n                                 \nJagran Prakashan Ltd, \nRanchi\nPhone:\n                                      \n09334701960\n\n                                                                                                  \n\n\nDate:\n\nPlace:\n                                                                                                             \n(SUDHANSHU BAJPAI)','HIMACHAL FUTURISTIC COMMUNICATIONS LTD',1,NULL,'2007-10-16',NULL,'2007-10-16','2010-06-08 12:13:25','2010-06-08',2,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(91,'Secunderabad',NULL,NULL,'Secunderabad','hisiddu@yahoo.co.in','siddu.kamatagi@gmail.com',NULL,'0','91 9849667452','0',NULL,'0','2007-06-14',10,34,'2010-06-08 12:13:25',2,'0',NULL,'200710/16/ATT54000.html','200710/16/DOC40076.doc','Namdev B Jagtap (ID# 25841)\n\nSiddalingesh Kamatagi \nProfessional Summary\nHaving \nTwenty four months experience\n in information technology areas involving \nOracle Apps Database Administration and Oracle 9i Administration.\n I have good experience in \ninstallation and Administration of Oracle Apps on Solaris and HP - UNIX\n, database maintenance, backup & recovery of Oracle database. I also worked in \nC, C++ \nlanguages and well versed with RDBMS like \nOracle\n and \nFront End GUI tool Developer2000.\n\nAs an Oracle DBA, I was involved in installation, configuration and administration of various Oracle Products like Oracle 11i, Oracle Database Server 8.x/9i on window/Solaris/Linux platforms. I have experience in System Administration, Databases Creation, Database Configuration, Space management, User management, Backup and Recovery and Database Maintenance. \n\nEducation\n\nDegree\nUniversity\nYear of Passing\nB.E. (Information Science and Engineering) \nVisveswaraiah Technical\n\nUniversity (Karnataka) \nJuly 2004\nExperience\n\nOrganization\nDesignation\nDuration \nSatyam Computer Services Ltd.\nSoftware Engineer\n27/12/04 - till date\n\nTechnical Skills\n\n\nOperating Systems\nSun Solaris9, Windows95/98/2000/XP, MS-DOS,HP-UX\nLanguages\nC, C++, SQL, PL/SQL, Shell Scripting\nDatabases\nOracle Apps 11i, Oracle 8i/9i\nGUI\nD2K( Forms 6.0, Reports 5.0)\nTools & Utilities\nExp, Imp, Tkprof,\n\nSQL * loader, Toad, \nDBA\nOracle Application 11i\n\n\n\n\nTrainings\n\n\n\nProjects Profile\n\n1. \nProject Name: DBA SUPPORT\nClient\nSatyam\nRole\nDatabase administrator and System administrator\nOrganization\nSatyam Computer Services Ltd.\nDuration\n27/01/05 ?\n\n25/09/05 \nEnvironment\nOracle apps 11i with oracle 9i DB ,HP-UX servers.\n\n\nProject Description \n\nSatyam has a DBA Support Help desk for all internal Development projects. The support Help desk gives 16 X 5 DBA support like installations, space management, schema management, security, performance and backup, to all internal projects in Satyam.\n\nContribution\n\n\n\n        \nApplying various patches.\n\n        \nInstallation of APPS financial module on Sun Solaris 5.8.\n\n        \nDeploying Data guard configuration on oracle 8i\n\n        \nResolution of various online issues.\n\n        \nComplete Database and system administration support.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n2.\nProject ? EAST - GE Power Systems, Atlanta, USA\n\nClient\nGE \nRole\nOracle Application 11i System Administrator\nOrganization\nSatyam Computer Services Ltd.\nDuration\n01/10/05 ?\n\ntill date \nEnvironment\nOracle Apps 11i with oracle 9i DB ,HP-UX servers.\n\n\n\nProject Description \n\nTeam Size - 85, Module Size - 9\nGE Energy, a leading unit with in GE USA. The Project includes analysis of the specifications provided by the clients, troubleshooting and configuring the Oracle Applications.\n The project involves Troubleshooting, Supporting, and implementation of the all the Oracle Applications modules in more than 7 GE Energy Business Environment. Working with various teams and the functional users as a System Administrator for the various modules like Oracle GL, AP, AR, Supply Chain Mngt., CRM, Global HR etc. and various Business environments like Wind Energy, Aero/Hydro, CPG, CMF, FRMT, NRPS etc.\n\nContribution\n\nWorked at Client side and Offshore as a \nSystem Administrator (\nOracle ERP Sys Admin Consultant\n\n, and is responsible for \n\n        \nCustomization of Oracle Applications and Providing System Administrator Support.\n\n        \nPreparing SQL Queries to for various reports.\n\n        \nInteracting with the Client, Analyzing the Case/Issues and Providing the Resolution within the Time Frame. \n\n        \nWorked with Oracle TAR when required. Performing User Training\n\n        \nConfiguring System (Oracle Application Manager, Workflow, Notification Mailer etc.)\n\n        \nParticipating in Business Critical, Serv. 1 TAR, Change Control Board, etc. Meeting.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nPersonal Details\n\nName\nSiddalingesh Kamatagi \nEmail Id \nhisiddu@yahoo.co.in\n ; siddu.kamatagi@gmail.com\nPresent Address\nFlat no 310, Alliance homes,\nS. D. Road , Secunderabad\nPin 500 003\nContact Numbers\n\nMobile: +91- 9849667452','Satyam Computer Services Ltd',1,NULL,'2007-10-16',NULL,'2007-10-16','2010-06-08 12:13:25','2010-06-08',2,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(92,'Madhu sudhan',NULL,NULL,NULL,'bhogfbfbesh8fbfdb88@gmail.com',NULL,NULL,'0','9986688986','0',NULL,'0','2007-01-28',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-08 12:13:25',2,'0',NULL,'200710/16/ATT53999.html','200710/16/DOC40077.doc','Madhu Sudhan\nT. \nBhogeswara\n\n                      \n     \n\n       \nE-Mail\n:bhogfbfbesh8fbfdb88@gmail.com\n         \n                                                \n  \n\n         \nPh: + 91 9986688986\n    \n                         \n   \n                                                                   \n     \nExperience Summary\n\n\n\n\n\n       \nHaving\n\n3 years of Experience in Oracle Back-End programming\n\n       \nGood Programming knowledge of PL/SQL statements\n\n       \nStrong Exposure to SQL queries\n\n       \nInvolved in writing Database Triggers\n\n       \nImplementation of stored procedures and functions\n\n       \nGood Knowledge in writing Cursors\n\n       \nExposure to Packages\n\nObjective\n\n\n\n\n      \n             \n\nSeeking a challenging as a programmer.\n Integrate my technical, analytical software skills and to become a professional in the IT environment and make a career in this profession.\n\nTechnical Profile\n\n\n\n\n\n       \nWorking as a programmer In ADITI Technologies, \nBangalore\n, Since December 2005 to till date.\n\n\n       \nWorked as a programmer in Wipro, \nBangalore\n from\n     \n\nJuly 2004 to November 2005\n\nTechnical Skills\n\n\n\n\n\nOperating Systems\n   \n          \n\n        \nWindows NT/2000/XP.\n\nLanguages\n                       \n\n        \nC, C++, SQL, PL/SQL\n\nRDBMS\n                            \n\n        \nOracle8i, Oracle9i\n\nStrengths\n\n\n\n\n\n       \nHave the motivation to take independent responsibility as well as ability to contribute and be a productive team member\n     \n\n   \nA fast learner with a positive attitude and flair for innovative ideas.\n\n       \nGood communication and interpersonal skills\n\nEducation\n\n\n\n                                  \n\nM.C.A from \nS.K.\nUniversity\n with 78%.\n\nProject Summary\n\n\n\n\nProject 1:\n\n\n\n\nTitle\n             \n: SPIC\nClient\n            \n: Info Space corp.\nDuration\n        \n: December 2006 to Till Date\nTeam Size\n      \n: 12.\nBack End\n       \n: Oracle-9.2.0.4.0, PL/SQL.\n\nDescription:\n\n          \nSPIC is a powerful tool developed for Info Space crop?s Global Equity team. This is a custom-designed, proprietary web-based valuation model and communication platform called Specified platform for internal communication (SPIC). This system enables team members to share information, fundamental research and to function as a cohesive unit. The information in SPIC helps the Managers to gain a comprehensive understanding of the companies and to extract the best investment ideas.\n          \nThe existing data is migrated from Sybase to Oracle through data migration scripts.\n     \n  \n   \nROLE:\n Team Member\nResponsibilities:\n\n      \nPreparation of the Technical Specifications based on the functional specifications received from Client. \n\n      \nDevelopment of Code based on the approved Technical Specifications.\n\n      \nDeveloped Stored Procedures and Functions and Packages.\n\n      \nCreated Views from multiple Tables.\n\nProject 2#\n\n\n\n\n          \nTitle\n             \n\n\ne-O\nSCAR.\nClient\n\n          \n\n\nInfo space corp.\nDuration\n        \n\n\nFrom Dec \n2005\n\nto\n November 2006.\n          \nTeam Size\n     \n\n\n9.\n          \nFront End \n     \n: Asp.NET\n,C\n#.Net,\n          \nBack End \n      \n: Oracle-9.2.0.4.0, PL/SQL, Windows NT.\n\nDescription:\nThe e-OSCAR system is a collection of processes and tools that allows Credit Involved Agencies (\nCIAs\n), otherwise known as the User Community, to communicate through a central system to resolve consumer credit disputes. \nAutomated Consumer Dispute Verification (ACDV)\n.The ACDV process enables \nCRAs\n to submit consumer disputes for verification to \nDFs\n\n\nDFs\n in turn respond to the verification requests from the \nCRAs\n\n\nA DF can modify, misroute, delete, or verify an ACDV as accurate as reported.\n Automated Universal Data (AUD)\n.The AUD are initiated by \nDFs\n to request an out-of-cycle update or deletion of their item on a consumer?s credit \nfile .\n\n\n          \nROLE: Team Member\n\n          \nResponsibilities: \n\n      \nDevelopment of Code based on the approved Technical Specifications.\n\n      \nDeveloped Stored Procedures and Functions and Packages.\n\n      \nWriting code for Database Triggers on Tables.\n\n      \nCreated Views from multiple Tables.\n\n      \nCreated Indexes to improve Performance.\n\nProject 3#\n\n\n\n\nTitle\n          \n\n\n\n\n\nADMIN LOGISTICS\nClient\n\n          \n: NTTF (NETTUR TECHNICAL TRAINING FOUNDATION)\nDuration\n   \n     \n: July 2004 to Nov 2005.\nLanguage(s)\n   \n\n\nSQL, PL/SQL\nGUI\n     \n          \n\n\nVB6.0\nRDBMS\n      \n\n   \n\n\nSQL Server 2000, Oracle 9.1\n\nDescription:\n\n          \nAdmin Logistics is a Students Life Cycle Management Project which covers Students Admissions, Services, Billing Details, Course Details, \nProject\n Details of Students Ledger. This is a special Student \nInformation\n\ntool\n, which helps especially for Education Departments and Accounts Departments\n\n          \nThis was implemented successfully on January 1\nst\n 2006 at Bangalore, Hyderabad ,Vijayawada Chennai Unit covering the areas from Different Places Different students Information to Dispatches including Remote Sheeting, Branch Operations activities etc.\n\n\n\nRole and Responsibilities:\n\n         \nDeveloped Interfaces to the Dispatch System, Base Monitoring System and the Finance System.\n\n         \nImplementation of the system in different units by customizing the requirements.\n\n         \nSupporting the system maintenance after implementation.',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-16',NULL,'2007-10-16','2010-06-08 12:13:25','2010-06-08',2,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(93,'S Rama Krishna.Gorantla',NULL,NULL,NULL,'gorasasxcscntl@gmail.com',NULL,NULL,'0','91 9916597489','0',NULL,'0','2008-04-29',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-08 12:13:25',2,'0',NULL,'200710/16/ATT53998.html','200710/16/DOC40078.doc','Dear Sir(s),\nS Rama Krishna.Gorantla\nrk. gorasasxcscntl@gmail.com\nMobile\n: +91 9916597489\n\n\nPROFILE:\n\nHaving 2+ years of experience in (Oracle SQL/PLSQL, Forms6i, Reports6i) Development. \nExperience in development / customization of Forms and Reports.\nStrong Experience in developing Inbound and Outbound Interfaces using PL/SQL, SQL* LOADER\nWorked in the modules like Order Processing, Purchase Order, and Inventory Systems.\n\nSKILL SET\n\n\nRDBMS\nORACLE 8i,9i\nOS\nMS DOS, Windows 2000, Windows NT & Unix\nLanguages\n\nSQL, PL/SQL\nTools\nForms 6i, Reports 6i ,Toad,SSH Secure Shell\n\n\nACADEMIC DETAILS\n\n\nB.TECH (Electronics & Control Engineering) from J.N.T.U, 2005, Andhra Pradesh.\n\n\nCAREER OVERVIEW\n\n\nworking as Software Engineer for Tavant \nTechnologies from February 2007 to till date.\n\nWorked as \n\nProgrammer\n in Tavas Infotech\n\n\nBangalore\n from August 2005 to January 2007.\n\n\nEXPERIENCE SUMMARY\n\n\nExperience Distribution\nCountry\nNo. of Years - Months\nNo. of Projects\nOffshore\nIndia\n2 Years\n\n\n\nPROJECT#1:\n\nProject Name: \nToyota CDMS\nClient\n\n            \n\nToyota Kirloskar Motors Limited\nPeriod\n\n\n February\n 2007 to till date \nIndustry\n         \n\nManufacturing\nProject Type\n\n\nDevelopement\nLocation\n         \n\nBangalore\nEnvironment\n\n\nOracle 9i(SQL, PL/SQL), \nReports6i\n\nRole\n                \n\nDeveloper\n\n\nDescription:\n\nToyota Kirloskar Motors Limited (TKML) is in the business of manufacturing different type of vehicles. There is a need for automation process of marketing activities for decision-making to increase their sales. The customer database management system (CDMS) enables TKML?s existing customer and prospects data in a single system. The system supports for launching various campaign programs for customer/prospect and maintain customer/prospect feedback of it for better decision-making.\n\nResponsibilities:\n\n         \nDeveloped Reports based on the specification i.e. Campaign Creation, Launch Campaign,\n\n\n         \nDeveloped Program Units in Reports.\n\n\n         \nPreparation of System Requirements Specification\n\n\nPROJECCT#2:\n\nProject Name: \nPharmaceutical Automation & Hr Information System.\nClient\n              \n\nDirectorate of Health Services\nPeriod\n\n\n\nJune 2006 to January 2007\nIndustry\n         \n\nFinance/ Human Resource Management.\nProject Type\n\n\nDevelopment\nLocation\n         \n\nBangalore\nEnvironment\n\n\nOracle 9i (sql,pl/sql)\nRole\n                \n\nDeveloper\n\nDescription:\n\nPharmaceutical Automation\n\n                            \nAIM: This Package is only developed for medicine dealers. It maintains the details of various products available with dealers and details of the supplier and details of the sub dealers. This package maintains the stock that is available with the dealers and details like current stock level, stock received and detail transaction carried out\n\nby the dealer are also recorded. The transaction includes the sales of different products, order date, order receipt date and order delivery date and also to maintain material return details. There is also a provision to see particular date?s sales, sale for a month and for a year also. Provision to show details of medicines that are expires, so that the dealer can exchange. Provision to maintain ledger and see balance in the form of report. Billing system is also maintained.\n   \n\nHR INFORMATION SYSTEM\n\n                            \n\nAIM: The HR Information System Application Software has been designed to keep track of the required details of every Employee working under Directorate of Health Services (DHS), including both Official & Medical Staffs. It provides the necessary Employee related information (such as emp. details, their job history, leaves, trainings, etc.) to the authorities of DHS whenever needed by them.\nResponsibilities:\n\nPreparing the Technical Design Documents\nBuilding the Procedures, Functions\nCarried out Unit Tests for the units\nPROJECT#3:\n\n\nProject Name:\n Goods Inwards System (GIS)\nClient\n              \n\nChidambaram Ship care Pvt Ltd\nPeriod\n\n\nAugust 2005 to May 2006\nIndustry\n         \n\n\nManufacturing\nProject Type\n\n\nDevelopment\nLocation\n         \n\nBangalore\nEnvironment\n\n\nOracle 9i(SQL, PL/SQL)\n and Developer 2000 (Forms 6i,Reports 6i)\nRole\n                \n\nDeveloper\n\nDescription:\n\nGoods Inwards System (GIS) is an integrated Module, which covers the activities of Stores, Purchase and Goods Inwards Functions of a Manufacturing Organization. This Module has provisions to capture Supplier Details (Vendors) required for the Purchase Department. It facilitates Stores to check the stock of the Raw Materials used and System automatically places Purchase Requisitions to the Purchase Department. Purchase Department can place Purchase-Orders and keep track of the Work-orders given to the Vendors. When the raw material is received, corresponding Stock is updated. \n\nResponsibilities:\n\nCreation of database tables \n\nPreparation of Program Specifications\n\nDeveloped Program Units in Reports.\n\nDeveloped program units in forms\n\nDefect removal and Regression testing\n\n\n\nTRAININGS UNDERGONE\n\n    \n                                                            \n         \n           \n\nSoft Skills Training like e-mail etiquettes and Client Interaction\n\nFunction Modules like Order Processing, Purcahse Order\n\n\nPERSONAL DETAILS\n\n\nAddress\n                  \n: HNo: 167/2,\n\n                            \n\nNavaneethnivas,\n                             \n\n\nNear Puttappamath,\n                             \n\nNew thippasandra,\n                                \n\nBangalore\n\n\n                            ',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-16',NULL,'2007-10-16','2010-06-08 12:13:25','2010-06-08',2,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(94,'  singh    ',NULL,NULL,NULL,'pdvsdfval1008fgr@yahoo.com',NULL,NULL,'0','9980981754','0',NULL,'0','2008-01-28',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-08 12:13:25',2,'0',NULL,'200710/16/ATT53997.html','200710/16/DOC40079.doc','CV\n\n\n\n\nSingh\n                                      \n          \nE-mail\n\n\npdvsdfval1008fgr@yahoo.com\n\nC/o Anil gaddi, A-2, campus-1\n\n                   \n\nMobile\n: 9980981754\n    \n\nKristal galena, belandur gate\n\nSarjapur road\n\nBangalore-560037\n   \n      \n                                                                        \n\n\n\nOBJECTIVE\n\n\n\nI would like to see myself working for an organization where I can make use of my potential and analytical attitude for the good of the organization to genuinely contribute in the growth of the organization. I would like to grow with the organization, in which I can gain experience and become a part of decision - making process, to enhance the value of the company. A fun and challenging work environment where my hard work and talent is rewarded. A company where my ideas and expertise in \ndevelopment\n will contribute to high quality, cost effective solutions for the customer\n\n\n\nWORK EXPERIENCE:\n\nOrganization:\n        \nGlobal \nEnterprise\n Infotech Solutions (GEIS), \nBangalore\n\n\nDesignation:\n         \nSoftware Engineer.\n\n\nPeriod:\n        \n          \nFrom July 2005 to till date.\n\nOrganization\n\n\n        \nSolaris energy.\nDesignation:\n          \nAssistant Marketing Manager.\nPeriod:\n                  \nfrom oct 2004 ? april 2005.\n                 \n\n   \n\nALL I KNOW\n1.\n     \nMore than 2+ years of experience in Data Warehousing in the role of ETL developer.\n2.\n     \nExpertise, knowledge and hands on experience with Informatica\n\nPower Center 7.1\n3.\n     \nExtensive experience in Extraction, Transformation, Loading (ETL) data from various Sources into Data Warehouses and Data Marts using \nInformatica\nPower\nCenter\n\n4.\n     \nWorked on\n\nInformatica tools (Source Analyzer, warehouse designer, Mapping\n\nDesigner, Workflow Manager).\n5.\n     \nGood communication, interpersonal, analytical skills, and strong desire and ability to perform as a team member.\n6.\n     \nStrong tendency to learn new concepts and very hard working.\n\n\nTECHNICAL SKILLS\n\n\n         \nETL:\n               \n     \n      \nInformatica 7.1\n\n         \nOperating Systems\n\n   \nWin NT/2000\n\n         \nLanguages:\n    \n           \nSQL & PL/SQL\n         \n\n         \nDatabases:\n     \n     \n      \nOracle 9i\n\n\n\n\nProjects\n\n1. Client\n\n\nCENTRAL PACIFIC BANK, \nHONOLULU\n\nHAWAII\n\nUSA\n\nCentral Pacific Bank is top 50 bank of \nUSA\n, with its headquater at \nHonolulu\n\nHawaii\n\nHawaii\n is an island state of \nUSA\n located almost in the middle of the Pacific Ocean.Data Warehouse is build upon integrated legacy system data feeds received from many divisions of business data sources. This will allow\n\nCentral Pacific Bank\n to continue to analyze the organized data. This Data warehouse would enable both tactical and strategic decision-making and after successfully implementing the customer data at\n Central Pacific Bank\n, GEIS is currently developing the sales data mart as part of the bank?s efforts towards building an enterprise wide data warehouse.\n\n\nDuration:\n                       \nNov 2006- Till Date\nOperating System\n\n\n        \nWindows NT, 2000\nData Base\n\n   \n                  \nOracle9i\nTools used\n\n\n                  \nInformatica 7.1\nTeam Size\n\n           \n         \n16\nRole\n\n            \n                  \nETL Developer\n\n\nResponsibilities:\n\nDeveloped various Mappings, Transformations and Mapplets for migration of data using Informatica Designer.\nUsed various transformations in Informatica.\nDone data cleansing and aggregation while transformation.\nDone performance tuning in Informatica.\n\n\n\n2. Client\n\n\n\nSEARS, ROEBUCK & CO. ? \nENTERPRISE\n DATA \nWAREHOUSE\n\nILLINOIS\n\nUSA\n\nSears, roebuck & co is a leading broadline retailing company, with its headquater at \nILLINOIS\n\nSears, Roebuck & co\n has identified the need for an Enterprise DW strategy with business intelligence & reporting architecture and future roadmap as part of their enterprise architecture implementation to support the information needs appropriate for the goals and anticipated growth of the company. The DW architecture is intended to identify a robust, comprehensive, and enterprise-reporting environment (high-level infrastructure need) that will effectively leverage the investment made in operational systems. This will allow Sears, Roebuck & co to continue to analyze the organized data. This Data warehouse would enable both tactical and strategic decision-making. \n             \nDuration\n\n                       \nJuly 2005 -Oct 2006\nOperating System\n\n       \nWindows NT, 2000\nData Base\n\n     \n               \nOracle8i\nTools used\n\n\n                 \nInformatica 6.1\nTeam Size\n\n                    \n15\nRole\n\n            \n                  \nETL Developer\n\n\nRESPONSIBILITIES:\n\n     \nAs an ETL Devloper was responsible for \n\n1.\n   \nDeveloping various Mappings, Transformations and Mapplets for migration of data\n   \nusing Informatica Designer. \n2.\n   \nValidating the ETL Design and development through Unit Testing, \n3.\n   \nvalidating the data populated in the database and the data that comes up on the reports.\nThe objective is to extract data stored in different databases such as Oracle, SQL Server and to load scheduled finally into a single data warehouse repository, which is in Oracle.\n\neducational profile\n          \nGraduation in Mechanical Engineering from \nNATIONAL INSTITUTE OF TECHNOLOGY (NIT), \nCALICUT\n in\n\nJune 2002 with First division.\n\npersonal profile\n\n\nFather Name\n\n        \n      \nSh. Roop Singh\nMarital Status\n\n       \n   \n  \n\nSingle\nNationality\n\n                  \nIndian\nLanguage known:\n         \nEnglish, Hindi, Punjabi, dogri\n\nstrenGths\n\n\n1.\n\nQuick & continuous desire for learning new technologies.\nA dedicated worker having a practical approach to any problem.\n3.\n\nCapable of handling projects independently.\nAbility to blend in a team.\n\nExtra curricular activities\n\nSports\nWon a number of certificates and trophies in the most popular game of \nIndia\n, cricket. I have represented my college in the inter- college cricket tournaments and university in the inter- university games, also take keen interest in watching other famous international games like lawn tennis, hockey, football as well. \nSchool\nI passed my 10\nth\n level exams with first division and had done exceptionally well in the 12\nth\n standard by securing 82.3% marks. I have also won a number of prizes, while participating in the seminars and debates. \nHobbies:\nWatching cricket from close quarters, in spite of \nIndia\n\'s pathetic performance every now and then \nI do take pride in recognizing singers voice singing Hindi songs and ghazals',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-16',NULL,'2007-10-16','2010-06-08 12:13:25','2010-06-08',2,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(95,'Operating Tools',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Kishore.Agnihotra@gmail.com',NULL,'98850 18487','0','9346327243','0',NULL,'0','2008-04-29',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-08 12:13:25',3,'0',NULL,'200710/16/ATT53996.html','200710/16/DOC40080.doc','CURRICULAM VITAE\n\nCURRICULAM VITAE\n\nS/o \nV.V.Narasimha\n\nRao\n\nPlot no: 321, V Phase, A2 Block\nJanapriya\n Apartments, \nMiyapur\nHYDERABAD\nPh: 9346327243;98850 18487\nKishore.Agnihotra@gmail.com\n\n\nV.A.KISHORE\n          \n\n\n\n\n\n                                                            \n\n\nObjective:\n\nTo gain professional satisfaction by rendering my best skill & experience for the growth of your esteemed organization.\n\nEducational Qualification:\n\nPursuing M.Com. \nOsmania\nUniversity\n (Correspondence)\nB.Com.\nAndhra\nUniversity\n, Vizag (1998 ? 2001)\n\nTechnical Qualification:\n\nTally Graduate from Tally Software Solutions, \nBangalore\nPGDCA from BEST Computers, \nRajahmundry\nTypewriting Higher in English\nTypewriting Lower in Telugu\nTypewriting Lower in Hindi\n\nStrengths and Achievements:\nWell Versed in Tally, Wings, MS ? office.\nCapable to handle all sorts of accounts independently and affectively.\n\nth\n ranker in All India Tally Experts Examination held in 2002. (Tally 5.4 & 6.3).\nReceived 5 times Best Performance Incentive, while working in Siva \nShakhi\n Bio \nPlanttec\n Ltd., \nRajahmundry\n\nReceived twice the Good Achievement Cash Prize in Hutch\nExperience:\nHaving 4 years of experience in various areas of Accounting and Management Information System.\nSummary:\n(a)\n\nOrganisation\n\n\n           \nHutchison \nEssar\n South Ltd, \nHyderabad\n                         \nDesignation \n   \n            \n\n           \nExecutive-Payroll in Finance Department\nPeriod \n                        \n\n           \nSep?05 to till date\nProcessing of All AP Employees Monthly Salaries and as well as settlement of resigned employees within TAT\nAfter processing the payroll account the same in Oracle Finance\nPreparation of monthly Provisions like Leave encashment and Bonus etc.,\nGuide to employees about their tax planning\nTaking care about the remittance of all Statutory Payments\n        \nUpload the \nPayslips\n in URL on every monthly\nPreparation of monthly MIS like Head count \nReconciliation,Gross\n\nReco\n compare with earlier month\nProcessing of all employee Medical & LTA claims as per IT Act\nPreparation of Monthly Schedules of all Payroll related expenses and Liabilities.\n(b)\n\nOrganisation\n\n\n           \nSatyam Computer Services Ltd, \nHyderabad\n                         \nDesignation \n   \n            \n\n           \nOfficer ? Finance in Payroll Department\nPeriod \n                        \n\n           \nMay?04 to till date\n\n\n        \nMaintenance of Payroll Books\n\n        \nProcessing of \nUnited States\n and India Payrolls with using of available tool software (ADP etc,)\n\n        \nAfter Processing the Payroll taking care about the statutory works for payroll related (US, \nIndia\n\nSingapore\n\n\n        \nBased on Payroll reports accounting the same in Oracle Finance (OF)\n\n        \nPreparation of Monthly Schedules and taking care about the statutory returns (yearly and monthly)\n\n\n        \nOperating Tools\n            \n\n           \nADP, GPMS for Payroll Processing\n\n       \nOracle Finance for Accounting\n\n\n        \nAnd also attending the works like Inter Branch Reconciliation, Bank Reconciliation with US Banks, verification of Tax Proofs submitted by the employees in every F/Y and validates those proofs accordingly the Act.\n\n\n        \nAnd as well as developments to be incorporated with Quality work in Payroll processing and bill processing.\n\n\n        \nAnd every month calculation of PF for all employees\n\n\n\nSummary:\n\n(a)\n\nOrganisation\n\n\n           \nGordon \nWoodroffe\n Logistics Ltd, \nHyderabad\n                         \nDesignation \n   \n            \n\n           \nExecutive ?\n\nAccounts\nPeriod \n                        \n\n           \nDec?02 to May?04\n\nMaintenance of Books of Accounts.\nPreparation of MIS reports like Branch performance statement, Age wise Debtors statement, Projected collection and Funds requirement, Billing & collection statements periodically.\nPreparation of budgets like Sales, Expenditure and comparison of actuals with budgets periodically.\nMonitoring Bills raising to customers and Control of Expenditure.\nReconciliation of Debtors account periodically and interacting with customers to get it confirmation.\nPreparation of \nFinalisation\n Statements like Schedules of Accounts etc.,\nPreparation of Debtors above 60days & 180days with remarks\nReporting to GM ? Finance, corporate.\n\n(b)\n\nOrganisation\n               \n\n           \nSiva \nShakthi\n Bio \nPlanttec\n Ltd, \nHyderabad\nDesignation \n   \n            \n\n           \nBr.Executive\n ? Accounts, \nRajahmundry\n Branch.\nPeriod\n                         \n\n           \nJuly?01 to Nov?02\n\n\n        \nMaintenance of daily accounting transactions.\n\n        \nPreparation of monthly bank reconciliation statement (BRS).\n\n        \nPreparation of stock reconciliation statement.\n\n        \nMonthly salaries statement of branch.\n\n        \nInter branch reconciliation statement.\nReporting to Manager ? Finance, corporate.\n\nPersonal Details:\n            \nDate of Birth\n                                         \n\n                       \n26\nth\n October 1980\n\n            \nMarital Status\n                                       \n\n                       \nUn-Married.\n            \nSex\n                                                      \n\n                       \nMale.\n            \nLanguages Known\n                                \n\n                       \nTelugu, English, Hindi.\n            \nDate:\n                                                                                                            \nPlace:\n                                                                                                   \n        \n\nV.A.Kishore',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-16',NULL,'2007-10-16','2010-06-08 12:13:25','2010-06-08',3,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(96,'D Ebizframe',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL,'0',NULL,'0','2007-04-30',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-08 12:13:25',3,'0',NULL,'200710/16/ATT53995.html','200710/16/DOC40081.doc','Objective:\n\nTo combine my project management, planning and execution and oracle financials knowledge to deliver solutions that are efficient, intuitive and long ranging. Continuously improvise existing processes, to make them more effective and results oriented. Motivate people to bring the best out of them.\nProfessional Highlights:\n\n         \nWorked as Functional Lead on 3 \nfull life cycle oracle Financials implementation projects\n and leaded those from concept to delivery.\n\n         \nWorked on 2 oracle financials Support projects. \n\n         \nHave expertise in project management, planning, design, development, QA and support initiatives\n\n         \n8 years experience\n\nimplementing ERP application software?s in Manufacturing, Financial, Service organizations.\n\n         \nAround 4 years in Oracle Financials.\n\n         \nHave good understanding of\n\nOracle?s AIM Methodology.\n\n         \nDemonstrated professionalism as a project Leader, team leader and team member, while continually striving to meet project needs with user requirements\n\n         \nProven ability to communicate with client\n, leading the team, estimate, design and implement projects\n\n         \nLead onsite & offshore teams\n in a matrix environment\n\n         \nWorked on various process definition, standardization and process improvement projects\n that involved defining coding standards, change request management, configuration management, release management\n\n         \nEvaluated different vendors, tools available in the market and managed vendor relationships\n\n         \nExtensive experience as \nsolution provider to the clients\n\n         \nHas worked on various Financials modules of oracle apps11i suit including Oracle General Ledger, Oracle Payables, Oracle Receivables, Oracle Fixed assets, Oracle purchasing.\n\n         \nExposure to other ERP applications\n namely Ebizframe6i enables me to think out of the box when implementing business software?s & \nevaluate solutions from Optimization perspective\n\n         \nTeam player with ability to lead by example and motivate to achieve desired objectives\n\n         \nHighly intuitive, goal-oriented, analytical and go-getter\n with a positive attitude; Always looks for process improvement opportunities and opportunities to add value\n\n         \nGreat listener, assertive but strongly believe in participative management style\n\nEducation: \n\n\n         \nPursuing \nMBA- Finance\n from University of Pondicherry\n\n         \nMaster of Human resource management (MBA- HR)\n from University of Pondicherry ? \n\nyear 2000-2002\n\n         \nBachelor of Commerce\n from University of Agra - \nyear 1995-1998\n\n         \nMasters Diploma in Aptech Computer Education (Duration 3 years) ? year 1994-1998\n\n         \nOracle Applications 11i Training\nfrom \ncomp-u-learn. ? \nYear 2004\n\n         \nMicrosoft Certifications (MCP, MCSD and cleared 4 Windows 4.0 NT Admin exams (core papers of MCSE Curriculum) ? year 1999\nAffiliation: \n\n         \nMember of All India Management Association\nImmigration / Passport Status:\n\nValid Indian Passport is available without any visa.\nLocation Preference:\n\nLimited to opportunities in Gurgaon India, or oversees projects\nAvailability to Join: \nupon 3 month notice.\n\nKey Skills & Knowledge\n\n\n\nBusiness Applications\nOracle Apps 11.5.9, 11.5.8, 11.5.6, 11.5.5, 11.5.3, 10.7 NCA, 10.7 SC\n\nOracle Apps 10.6 CUI\nEbizframe 6i\n\n\n\nOracle Apps Modules\nOracle General ledger, Oracle Payables, Oracle Receivables, Oracle Fixed Assets, Oracle Cash management, Oracle Purchasing\n\n\n\n\nSoftware\nOracle 7.x, 8.x, 9.x, 10g\nOracle Configurator\nOracle Workflow Developer\nOracle Trace, TKPROF\nSQL, PL/SQL, SQL Loader\nDeveloper 2000, 6i, 9i\nC, Unix Shell scripts\n\n\n\n\nPackages\nMicrosoft Project 2000\nProject Tracker\nMicrosoft Office XP\nVisio2000, SQL Navigator\nPVCS, VSS, DBA Studio, Oracle Enterprise Manager\n\n\n\n\nOperating Systems\nWindows XP/ 2000/NT\nLinux/HP-UNIX, Sun Solaris\n\n\n\n\nHardware\nLinux RAC front to back\nIntel *86 m/c?s, Dec Alpha, \nSun Sparc, HP 9000, HCL Magnum\nBusiness & Application Experience\n\nEmployer\n\nSyntel Inc, Mumbai, India\n               \n                                \n                \n12/2006 ? Present\n\nSyntel Inc is a US based SEI CMMi Level5 company present revenue around 300 Million US dollars and I Joined here Senior Project leader and my role in my current project is of senior functional consultant or senior business analyst.\n\nEngagement\n\n\nOracle Financials Implementation at American Express, I am working on this project as senior project lead / senior functional consultant, I am responsible for requirement gathering and analysis, future process designing, helping functional & technical team and testing manger as subject matter expert.\n\nTask and Responsibilities \n\n\n         \nProviding guidance and leadership to team \n\non the functional aspects of the implementations as appropriate\n\n         \nIdentify inbound and outbound feeds related to point of departure (Legacy general ledger) systems.\n\n         \nReviewing High-level documents\nand ensuring it fits the overall architectural plan for build phase.\n\n         \nGuiding functional and technical consultant in preparing design documents\n the inbound and outbound interface requirements\n\n         \nMilestone \nreview and getting deliverables signed offs\n\n         \nParticipation in Change Control Meetings\n\n         \nHelping testing team manager in preparing Testing Strategy and Requirements\n\n         \nCoordinate with testing team manger in making the testing team understand the business process and development requirements\n\n         \nConduct workshops with the client to \nsetting up expectation\n\n         \nConduct \nmeeting\n\nwith the key stake holders for planning the rollout\n\n         \nMeet with Technical leads and development teams at Mumbai / Chennai to \nassure alignment and timely delivery\n\n\n         \nPublishing meeting minutes, issue log and weekly status report.\n\n         \nConsolidate and publish issue list from all tracks on a weekly basis. \nDrive issues to resolution\n\n\n         \nEscalate scope change requests to program management\n\n         \ncoordination with other departments\nlike quality assurance, support and systems departments to \nforecast resource demands\n and work with them when issues arise, so solutions can be worked out as a team. \n\n         \nEnsure fresh hands comply with other proper On-boarding training formalities \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nEmployer: Polaris Software Labs Ltd.\n                             \n                                \n1/2004 ? 12/2006 \n\nPolaris Software Labs Ltd. a SEI CMMi level5 company is very well known in India and across the globe for its Banking Software Solutions and ERP Consultancy present revenue around 300 Million US dollars I worked here for around 3 years in capacity of Oracle Financials Consultant and Executed 2 End to End ERP implementations and worked on 2 support projects. \n\nEngagement\n\n\nOracle Financials11i Implementation at GE Industrial India Pvt. Ltd.\nFull Life Cycle Ownership/Execution Responsibility for Oracle General Ledger, Oracle Receivables, Oracle Payables implementation.\nAs a Functional Lead\n, I was responsible for \nPlanning, Leadership, Coordination, Analyzing requirements, Preparing Specs, managing client relationship and Development. \n\n\n        \nTask and Responsibilities\n\n         \nEnsuring seamless transition from Legacy System to Oracle ERPs 11i. \n\n         \nPreparing Requirement gathering and analysis, conversion strategy, Functional \nSpecifications and setup documents as per AIM methodology\n\n         \nCreation of new responsibilities, request groups.\n\n         \nSetting up new Organizations.\n\n         \nSetting up new COA and Calendar and SOBs for US and India GAAP\n\n         \nPrepared other required setups for Oracle AP, AR and GL.\n\n         \nLooking after SITs and UAT.\n\nEngagement\n\n\nOracle Fixed Assets Implementation at GE Iprocess Pvt. Ltd., Full Life Cycle Ownership/Execution Responsibility for Oracle General Ledger, Oracle Receivables, Oracle Payables implementation.\nAs a Functional consultant, I was responsible for \nAnalyzing Requirements, Preparing Specs, and setting up Oracle Fixed Assets. \n        \n        \nTask and Responsibilities\n\n\n         \nPreparing Requirement gathering and analysis, conversion strategy, Functional \nSpecifications and Setup documents as per AIM methodology\n\n         \nCreation of new responsibilities, request groups.\n\n         \nSetting up fixed assets application to fulfill US and IND GAAP requirements\n\n         \nLooking after SITs and UAT.\n\n\n        \nEngagement\n\n\nOracle Financials11i support and quarterly release testing project for GE Energy Parts, ownership and Responsibility of\n\nall major Oracle Financials modules like Oracle General Ledger, Oracle Receivables, Oracle Payables.\n\nLead the Finance production support team to deliver the solutions as per SLAs. Understand all business processes and provide functional leadership to the team\n\n\n        \nTask and Responsibilities\n\n\n         \nManage the day to day execution of issue resolution and enhancements\n\n         \nResponsible for the 24 x 7 production support for Finance users located in various GEPS geographical \nlocation and time Zones\n\n         \nCoordinate with Finance leaders and understand the various changing business needs and align the \nteam to meet the requirements\n\n         \nUnderstand various interfaces to the Oracle system and coordinate with relevant teams and ensure \nsmooth production support\n\n         \nManage knowledge transfer between various teams \n\n         \nEnergize and motivate the contractor team to deliver their best\n\n         \nMaintain various performance matrices and monitor the support team performance\n\n         \nUnderstand and ensure the adherence to all the laid out production support and related policies\n\n\n         \nIdentify opportunities for improvement and drive improvement through 6 sigma rigor\n\n         \nHandling Oracle Payables Super user Responsibilities \n\n      \nPerforms Rifle shot and complete modular testing for Oracle Payables quarterly releases.\n\n      \nPerforming Inter company Settlement for Hungary and Atlanta sites. \n\n      \nCreation of payment batches for different pay groups. \n\n      \nProviding solutions to client on functional problems related to Oracle payables.\n\n\n        \nEngagement\n\n\nOracle Financials11i support project for GE Advance materials,\n Lead the Finance production support team to deliver the solutions as per SLAs. Understand all business processes.\n\n        \nTask and Responsibilities\n\n\n         \nInteracting with users for business requirement analysis, design and enhancement of reports after migration.\n\n         \nManaging deliverables on time\n\n         \nMigration/Customization of reports using Oracle Reports 3.0\n\n         \nRe-Registration of Concurrent programs using AOL.\n\n         \nPerformance Tuning of the Reports and other batch programs.\n\n         \nWrote technical Specifications based on given Functional Documents.\n\n         \nWrote SQL Script to create a data file for Data Extraction.\n\n         \nOngoing Production supports to Oracle Users.\n\n         \nCreating the Responsibilities, Data Group, Request Group and Users.\n\n         \nCreation of values sets in various modules of the application.\n\n         \nDefining Concurrent Programs, Executables.\n\n         \nGenerated Financial Statements using Financial Statement Generator.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nEmployer: \nEastern Software Systems Ltd. \n\nSEI CMM ? 5 company\n             \n                                \n1/2003 ? 1/2004\n\nEastern Software Systems Ltd. a SEI CMM level5 company is First Indian Company with self made Web based ERP Software named Ebizframe6i. I worked here for around 1 years in capacity of Software Engineer and Executed 3 End to End ERP implementations at prestigious Indian Clients. \n\nEngagement\n\n\nImplementation of ebizframe6i\n suite at \nP.A. Time Industries Ltd.(Maxima Watches)\n, Dharampur H.P., India,\n\nLead the \n\nteam to deliver the solutions as per Project plan. Understand all business processes and provide functional leadership to the team\n\n        \n        \nTask and Responsibilities\n\n\n      \nInstallation of Oracle8i and \nOracle 9iAS 10222 and Ebizfram6i ERP.\n\n      \nStudying the old system with a view to find out the Gaps\n\n      \nThe project mainly involved implementation of implementation of Manufacturing module(Production and production planning) of Ebizfram6i ERP and support of other core modules including Financials, HRPAY, Inventory, sales and purchase.\n\n\n\n      \n\nPrimary responsibility was to collect and analyze user?s requirements and customization of manufacturing module accordingly.\n\n      \nPreparing Data flow diagram, Flow chart and Entity Relationship diagram to ensure the system reliability and robustness.\n\n      \nDeveloped various SQL loader scripts to transfer data from legacy system to Ebizframe6i Production module, Programs include transferring WIP and finished goods details into production module. \n\n      \nDeveloped various new forms and reports as per user requirements.\n\n      \nInvolved in preparing SOPs and user training. \n\n      \nAlso supported Financials, HRPAY, Sales, Purchase and done various enhancements as required\n\nEngagement\n\n\nImplementation of ebizframe6i suite at \nP.A. Time Industries Ltd.(Maxima Watches), Dharampur H.P., India,\n\nLead the \n\nteam to deliver the solutions as per Project plan. Understand all business processes and provide functional leadership to the team\n\n        \nTask and Responsibilities\n\n\n      \nInstallation of Oracle8i and \nOracle 9iAS 10222 and Ebizfram6i ERP.\n\n      \nStudying the old system and designing systems and procedures for new sytem.\n\n      \nThe project mainly involved implementation of implementation of Inventory and Export module\n   \nof Ebizfram6i ERP and support of\n   \nEbizfram6i Financials and HRPAY module.\n\n      \n\nPrimary responsibility was to collect and analyze user?s requirements and development of Export module from the scratch and customization of Inventory module accordingly.\n\n      \nPreparing Data flow diagram, Flow chart and Entity Relationship diagram to ensure the system reliability and robustness.\n\n      \nDeveloped various new forms and reports as per user requirements.\n\n      \nInvolved in preparing SOPs and user training. \n\n      \nAlso supported Financials, HRPAY modules.\n\nEngagement\n\n\nImplementation of ebizframe6i suite at \n\nesmen Ipsen Furnaces Pvt. Ltd.,\n kolkata, India,\nLead the team to deliver the solutions as per Project plan. Understand all business processes and provide functional leadership to the team\n\n\n         \nUnderstand the architecture, security and coding standards of Wesmen.\n\n         \n\nReview technical design documents for the components identified during the planning phase\n\n         \n\nPrepare Application extension strategy\n\n         \nPrepare data-conversion documents and interact with technical lead / client for approval\n\n         \nCreation of technical documents and Coding for interfaces, data-conversions etc\n\n      \nInstallation of Oracle8i and \nOracle 9iAS 10222 and Ebizfram6i ERP.\n\n      \nDeveloped various new forms and reports as per user requirements.\n\n      \nPerform Unit testing, SIT and UAT. \n\n\nEmployer: \nSavvy Information management System(SIMS) Pvt. Ltd. \n           \n                                \n10/1999 ? 1/2003\n\nI started my career with SIMS as Software Engineer and subsequently leaded flagship School management systems software package development apart from School management systems I Have worked on various MIS software solution development.projects. \n\nEngagement\n\n\nDevelopment of School management systems software, Lead the team to deliver the solutions as per Project plan. Understand all business processes and provide leadership to the team.\n\n        \nTask and Responsibilities\n\n\n      \nI was a part of team responsible for designing the \nsystems & procedures from scratch and lead the \n      \nSame team at later stage\n\n      \nDeveloped comprehensive MIS application for schools the product contains This product contains various modules like accounting, payroll, purchase and admission procedure and examinations etc.\n\n\n      \nPreparing Data flow diagram, Flow chart and Entity Relationship diagram to ensure the system reliability and robustness.\n\n      \nDesigning and developing forms and reports, writing PL/SQL Packages, procedures and database triggers and performed modular testing.\n\nEngagement\n\n\nDevelopment of \nIntegrated office management and Information system (IOMIS)\n\nIOMIS has designed and developed on the lines of ERP to facilitate in different operations for the area distributor of camphor allied limited. \n\nI worked in team as oracle developer and ensured deliveries inline with Project plan. Following are the modules specific responsibilities \n\n      \nFinancial Accounting System\n\nIt includes all types of ledgers like General ledger, sub ledger, voucher generation, books like Cash book, Bank book, Sales book, purchase book, Trial balances, Balance sheet Profit & loss A/c, Schedules Reconciliation of Bank entries against Bank statements, interest calculation, control of bank limits etc.\nPass the supplier bills against various purchases, making payment and keeps the track of payment on due date, Printing cheque etc.\nPass the supplier bills against Import purchase, it is linked with the consignments monitoring system, by which we keeps a track of various documents like Commercial invoice, bill of entry, CHA bill, freight bill and making payments against these bills.\nGenerating different kind of work orders for job processing release by the company for contractors and making payment against those.\nCalculate the inventory value at the end of each month by using weighted average rate technique.\nL.C.\'s generated for various Import purchase & sales & Overhead budget monitoring.\nCheck the expense against budgeted expenses assigned to each Cost-Centre monthly/ annually\n\n\nSales and Marketing System\n\nCustomer Registration and Order Entry\nSales Invoice generation, Invoice Printing and Sales Voucher Posting into financial system\nDebit/Credit Advice preparation and Debit/Credit Note generation\nSales Analysis Report, Daily Stock position Report, Customer Outstanding Report\nMaintain different Excise registers i.e. RG23 Part1, Part 2 RG23 C Etc.\n\n         \nInvolved in Development of Forms and reports using forms4.5/Reports2.5 for Financial Accounting module.\n\n         \nInvolved in Creation of Stored Procedures, Database Triggers, Sequences, Indexes, Views, Temporary Tables.\n\n         \nCustomizing forms and reports according to client\'s need\n\n         \nWrote SQL Script to create a data file for Data Extraction\n\n         \nLoading of Data through SQL Loader. Backups through Export Utility\n\nEngagement\n\n\nDevelopment of Export Management systems \nto facilitate in export documentation for the Export oriented industries. \n\nI worked in team as oracle developer and ensured deliveries inline with Project plan. \n\nTask and Responsibilities\n\n\n      \nIt was generic software for Brass Exporters. This package had developed to cater all requirements related to Brass Export. It also kept insurance related information.\n\n      \nDevelopment of export system, which starts with sales order, Performa invoice, insurance detail, goods dispatch till final commercial invoice. \n\n      \nDesigning and developing forms and reports, writing PL/SQL Packages, procedures and database triggers and performed modular testing.\nADDITIONAL INFORMATION:\n\nDate of Birth\n                        \n\n               \n14\nth\n July 1977\nFather?s Name\n                     \n\n               \nLate M.K. Vashistha\nSex\n                                         \n\n               \nMale\nMarital Status\n                      \n\n               \nMarried\nPassport No. \n                        \n\n               \nE2879083.\n\n\nCurrent Place \n                     \n\n\n\n\nDate\n                                       \n\n                                               \n                                                                                                                                                \nTarun Kr. Vashistha',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-16',NULL,'2007-10-16','2010-06-08 12:13:25','2010-06-08',3,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(97,'Siva Krishna N',NULL,NULL,'Hyderabad ','Sivsdcsccakrishnascsdc_nsk@yahoo.co.in',NULL,NULL,'0','9885800379','0',NULL,'0','2008-01-12',10,34,'2010-06-08 12:13:25',3,'0',NULL,'200710/16/ATT53994.html','200710/16/DOC40082.doc','          \n                                              \n             \n             \nSiva \nKrishna\n\nCell ? (+\n91\n) - \n9885800379\n                         \n            \nSivsdcsccakrishnascsdc_nsk@yahoo.co.in\n                             \nMadhapur, Hi-tech city, Hyderabad\n          \n\n\n\nExperience Summary\nAbout 2 years \n(26 months) of diverse experience in Information Technology with focus on \nTechnologies \nlike \nUnix Shell Scripting, SQL/PL-SQL, ORACLE.\n\n         \nExpertise in \nTelecom\n\nDomain \nespecially\n\nin\n Order Management. \n\n         \nWell-organized, creative, self-motivated, result oriented, and a \nTeam Player\n with proven ability to complete given tasks on time.\n\nAchievement / Rewards\n\n         \nCertified as \nOracle Certified Associate\n as PL/SQL developer.\n\n\nTrainings / Memberships\n\n\n         \nMember of ISI (Instrument Society of \nIndia\n) since Aug-2002\n\n         \nDone\nIn-Plant training at Nuclear Fuel Complex (NFC). \nHyderabad\n\nWorking Experience \n\n\n         \nWorking as \nAssistant System Engineer\n in \nTata Consultancy Services-\nHyderabad\n\nIndia\n\nfrom \nJuly 2005 to till now.\n\nEducational Qualification \n\nB.Tech\n from \nVellore\n Institute of Technology-\nVellore\n, Tamilnadu. in 2005 \nwith 85%.\nPlus 2 Exam \nfrom A.P. Board, \nNellore\n,A.P. in 2001 \nwith 89.4%\nSSC Exam \nfrom A.P. Board , Board, \nNellore\n,A.P. in 1999 \nwith 80.2%\n\n\nTechnical Skills\n\n1.\nOperating System\n\nUNIX, DOS, WINDOWS-XP, 9X\n2.\nDatabase\nOracle 9i\n3.\nScripting\nUnix Shell Script,PL/SQL, SQL\n4.\nOthers\nOracle forms, Reports, C, C++, Core JAVA, JSP, SAP BW\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n          \n                                           \nPROJECT DESCRIPTION\n\n1.\n     \nPoint of Sell (TATA Consultancy Services)\n\n\nClient\nTATA Tele-Services Ltd.\nTitle\nPoint of Sell\nPeriod\nOctober 2005 to till now\nPosition\nTeam Member\nThe Project\nTata Tele Services Limited offers telecom services in \nIndia\n. POS is a module of TTSL. POS is that system through which customers information enters into the system. POS is developed by TCS itself for fulfill Business requirement. After entry in POS, information flows to different systems like\n\nMetasolv, Billing, CRM, SAS.\nResponsibilities\n\n         \nResolving customers problems and providing best solution to them.\n\n         \nWriting stored procedures and triiggers.\n\n         \nScheduling of scripts in crontab.\n\n         \nTunning the procedures for better performance.\n\n         \nFixing for bugs\n\nand resolving Discrepencies between different systems like Metasolv,Package and Billing team.\n\n         \nTo give training to new members.\n\n\nOperating Systems\nUNIX, Windows XP\nSoftware used\nOracle,PL/SQL ,Oracle Forms(D2K)\nDatabase\nOracle 9i\nTools\nToad 7.4.03\nWork Location\nHyderabad\n\nIndia\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nProject Thesis \n                \nAs part of University project\n       \n\n                    \n\nProject Title\nDesign of MEMS based Glucose sensor using Intellisuite and Coventorware software?s\nDescription\nIt deals with finding the amount of glucose concentration present in the blood. The design includes the micro needled structure, which is the best-suited structure for finding the amount of glucose concentration. The project also involves the withstanding capability of the micro needled structure.\nRole\nTeam member (team consists of 3 members)\nResponsibilities\nLiterature survey, designing the structure, testing the structure for various pressures and simulation.\n\n\n\nPersonal Details\n\nDate of Birth\n09-06-1985\nGender\nMale\nMarital Status\nSingle\nNationality\nIndian\n\n\n\nPassport Details\n\nName as on passport\nRelationship\nPassport Number\nDate of Issue\nExpiry Date\nPlace of Issue\nSivakrishna Nandimandalam\nMyself\nB5512707\n25-Jun-2001\n24-Jun-2011\nHyderabad\n (AP)','Tata Consultancy Services',1,NULL,'2007-10-16',NULL,'2007-10-16','2010-06-08 12:13:25','2010-06-08',3,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(98,'Sukanta Kumar Jena',NULL,NULL,NULL,'sukant_jena2002@yahoo.com','sukant_jena2002@yahoo.com',NULL,'0','09841930478','0',NULL,'0','2008-04-29',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-08 12:13:25',3,'0',NULL,'200710/16/ATT53993.html','200710/16/DOC40083.doc','Resdex @ naukri.com\nsukanta kumar jena\nsukant_jena2002@yahoo.com RAJGANGPUR - 770017 \nsukant_jena2002@yahoo.com\n\nTelephone: 09841930478\n(M)\n\nD.O.B\n - 18 May 1983 \nModified on\n - 25 Sep 2007 \nAnnual Salary\n - INR 2 Lac(s) 0 Thousand \nTotal Years of Experience\n - 2 Year(s) 2 Month(s) \nCurrent Location\n - Bangalore \nPreferred Location\n - Anywhere in India \nPlsql Developer having 2+ years of expe in Oracle application\n\nTEXT RESUME \n\nSUKANTA KUMAR JENA Mobile no: 09841930478\nMail:sukant_jena2002@yahoo.com\nSUMMARY\nÂ· Having around over 2+years of experience in software development using oracle.\nÂ· Experience in Application Development using oracle tools (SQL,PL/SQL, Reports, Forms) and other related technologies.\nÂ· Experience in development of live projects in Developer 2000 and Oracle 8i.\nÂ· Experience in development of live projects in Ramco ERP (e.Application).\nÂ· Having good domain knowledge and working experience in HRMS product.\nÂ· A self-motivated and results-driven professional with strong analytical ability backed by technical knowledge. Has a strong communication and team skill.\nÂ· Currently Working in Ramco System Ltd as a Programmer\nEDUCTIONAL QUALIFICATION\nBachelors of Engineering in Information Technology, Padmanava College of Engineering, Sambalpur University, Orissa, India\nTECHNICAL SKILLS\nOperating Systems : Windows NT/2000/XP.\nLanguages : PL/SQL\nDevelopment Tools : Developer 2000\nDatabases : Oracle 8i/9i\nReporting Tools : Oracle Reports 6i\nERP : Oracle Applications (PO & AOL) and Ramco e. Applications (HRMS)\nTools : Toad 7.3.0, SQL*Loader, Discoverer, Ramco Virtual Works\nPROFESSIONAL EXPERIENCE\nCurrent Employer: Sheltec Software (India) Pvt ltd, Bangalore July 2005 â\n?? till Date\nContractor: Ramco System Ltd, Chennai, India Oct 2006 â\n?? till Date\nClient : ITC-WELCOMGROUP, (ITC) New Delhi (July 2007 to till date)\nModule : HRMS (APPRAISAL)\nRole : Analyzing, Coding and Debugging\nTools : Ramco HRMS, PL/SQL, RVW\nDescription: ITC Hotel Division is one of top companies in India for Hotels. The project was developed ITC Hotel Div for implementing appraisee appraisal details.Their appraisal are of three types BSC, NBSC and Others. Based on Appraisal type they are maintain their appraisee details. As a programmer I was involved in these following areas.\nResponsibilities:\nÂ· Involved in Writing Procedure, Function for Appraisal Component.\nÂ· Involved in Bug fixing and Testing for the same.\nÂ· Involved in Supporting Work from Offshore.\nClient : Competent Software Ltd, (CSW) New Delhi (Feb 2007 to Jun 2007)\nModule : HRMS (Leave, Payroll, Production Planning)\nRole : Developer, Debugger and Tester\nTools : Ramco HRMS, SQL Server 2005\nDescription: Competent Software Pvt. Ltd. (CSW) incorporated in 1992, is in the Business Process Outsourcing (BPO) space. The company headquartered in New Delhi with full fledged units at Noida and Gurgaon is engaged in the development of electronic databases for clients in North America.CSW provides businesses of all sizes with a complete range of services including data conversion services and data analysis services. These intelligent services allow the customers to maximize the value of their IT expenditure and the unique methodology provides exceptional speed, efficiency, accuracy, and of course a very high returns on investment. I was responsible for these areas.\nResponsibilities:\nÂ· Involved in Writing Procedure, Function for leave Component.\nÂ· Involved in Bug Fixing for payroll, leave, Source to transmission, Production Planning Component.\nÂ· Extensively involved in Review and Testing for the same.\nClient : Singapore Health Services, (Sing Health) Singapore (Sep 2006 to Jan 2007)\nModule : HRMS\nRole : Developer and Debugger\nTools : Ramco HRMS, PL/SQL\nResponsibilities:\nÂ· Involved in Writing Procedure, Function for Employee Induction and leave Component.\nÂ· Involved in Bug Fixing for payroll, leave, Employee Induction, Reimbursement Component.\nÂ· Extensively involved in Review and Testing for the same.\nClient : South India Corporation Limited (Jun 2006 to Aug 2006)\nModule : AOL, PO\nRole : Developed Reports.\nTools : Oracle Applications 11i, Oracle 9i, SQL * Loader\nÂ· Reports Customization of Purchase Order Detail Report in Purchasing.\nÂ· Developed New Report Which give the stock of particular item on a particular date and as well as quantity received only without deliver.\nÂ· AOL activities like Creation of Users, Responsibilities, and Value sets, Enabling Flex Fields etc.\nÂ· Registration of Forms and Reports\nClient : Aurobindo Pharma ltd, Hyderabad (Jan 2006 â\n?? May 2006)\nTools : SQL, PL/SQL, 8i, Reports 6i\nRole : Analyzing, Coding and Debugging\nDuration : 5 months\nTeam Size : 5\nDescription:\nAPL is one of top ten pharmaceutical companies in India in bulk drugs. As a Developer I was Preparating of Reports in accordance with the User requirements, Development of Forms and Reports in Oracle Forms/Reports 6i.\nPayroll system was designed for providing Employee database, Attendance Maintenance, Leaves Maintenance, Loans and Advances, Bonus, Saving Schemes. This was developed on Oracle-8i with developer 2000 as front end.\nResponsibilities:\nÂ· Implemented various packages, PL/SQL procedures.\nÂ· Designed and Developed Forms as per client requirements.\nÂ· Generation of Reports as per requirement.\nClient : Jyoti Pvt Ltd, BBSR (July 2005 â\n?? Dec 2005)\nTools : Oracle 8i, Forms 6i, Report 6i\nRole : Developer\nDuration : 6 Months\nTeam Size : 7\nDescription:\nThe project was developed for Jyoti Pvt Ltd. Before implementing the project they faced problems with legacy system to maintain the inventory details. So this project was to solve all the problems met by the company. Here complete details about the Items and the stocking details were maintained. Depending on the previous months sale and keeping a base month sales the order level and re-order level was calculated so that, they can manufacture the at required level. This data was very helpful for managers and admin departments. Various flexible features which involve Quotation analysis, rising purchasing orders and receiving. It also gives complete information of On-hand-Quantity and on hand avalibilty.\nResponsibilities:\nÂ· Created table in database using Oracle-8i.\nÂ· Writing the procedures,functions,packages,database triggers in PL/SQL\nÂ· Involved for designing various application forms using form 6i.\nÂ· Generating various Reports using report 6i.\nÂ· Extensively involved in review and testing for the same.\nPersonal Details:\nName : Sukanta Kumar Jena\nMail id : sukant_jena2002@yahoo.com\nDate of Birth : 18th May 1983\nSex : Male\nMarital status : Single\nNationality : Indian',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-16',NULL,'2007-10-16','2010-06-08 12:13:25','2010-06-08',3,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(99,'Surendra Kurra',NULL,NULL,NULL,'surendrababukurra@yahoo.com',NULL,'91 20 000000000','0','09923206321','0',NULL,'0','2005-04-29',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-08 12:13:25',2,'0',NULL,'200710/16/ATT53992.html','200710/16/DOC40084.doc','Resdex @ naukri.com\nsurendra kurra\nPlot No 10,BlockB,Balaji Devlopers pune Pune \nsurendrababukurra@yahoo.com\n\nTelephone: 09923206321\n(M)\n 91 20 000000000\n(R)\n\nD.O.B\n - 10 Jul 1979 \nModified on\n - 25 Sep 2007 \nAnnual Salary\n - INR 4 Lac(s) 20 Thousand \nTotal Years of Experience\n - 4 Year(s) 9 Month(s) \nCurrent Location\n - Pune \nPreferred Location\n - Anywhere in South India \nresume of surendrababu kurra\n\nTEXT RESUME \n\nMR.SURENDRA BABU KURRA\nEXPERIENCE SUMMARY\n\n??\n Over 4.9 Years of experience in the analysis, design, development, implementation and management of full life cycle commercial applications.\n\n??\n 2.3 Years of Experience in Oracle,SQL*Loader &UTL Files .\n\n??\n 2.6 years of experience in Oracle 11i Applications in modules like GL, INV, AP and AR\nACADEMICS\n\n??\n Bachelor of Science (Electronics), Nagarjuna University, India.\nTECHNICAL SUMMARY\nSKILLS TOOLS EXPERIENCE LEVEL\nERP Oracle Apps 11.5.9 (AP, AR, GL). 4\nRDBMS Oracle 8 4\nFront-end Tool Forms6I 3\nLanguages SQL, PL/SQL 3\nReports Reports6I, Visual Basic 6.0 3\nTools Toad, SQL*Loader, Oracle Workflow Builder 2.6,EDI Integrator (I4) 4\n\n??\n 1 connotes experience ranging between one month to three months\n\n??\n 2 connotes experience ranging between three to six months\n\n??\n 3 connotes experience ranging to six months to two years\n\n??\n 4 connotes experience ranging to two years and higher\n\n??\n For the experience level section, please highlight the skill with the maximum experience\nWORK HISTORY\nDuration Organization Designation\nFeb-2007 to till date Tech Mahindra LTD. Technical Associate\nAug-2006 to Jan -2007 Satyam Computer Services LTD. Sr Software Engineer\nJul-2004 to Jul-2006 Genisys Software. Sr. Software Engineer\nJan-2003 to Jun-2004 Effexoft Technologies Software Engineer\nWORK EXPERIENCE\nPL. mention all your project details in reverse chronology order for all the companies.\nTech Mahindra Ltd\n1. Apr 2007 - Till date (6 months)\nSupport for BT- British Telecom â\n??Hosartâ??\nEnvironment: Oracle, UNIX, Sql*loader, Html\nDescription\nHoSART application is a web based reporting tool for reporting performance measures for Service Assurance .This tool is basically used for tracking fault life cycle and for improving customer satisfaction.\nThe tool is available in the Client intranet and can be accessed by users who have been granted the access provided the login details\nTech Mahindra Ltd\n2. Feb 2007 - March (2 months)\nSupport for HORIZON - MIS & Forecasting\nEnvironment: Oracle 9i, UNIX, VB.Net, TOAD 8.0.\nDescription\nMIS & Forecasting are the modules in HORIZON. This application was developed for generating various reports which gives the ability to measure the BT performance of various stages in the lead to cash cycle (primarily in the order entry and order validation stages). These reports are generated based on different base feeds, which are loaded to the database using UNIX shell scripts.\nAs a Team Member (with a team size of 4) of the application Group was responsible for the following responsibilities.\n\n?¢\n Regular maintenance of production activities.\n\n?¢\n Executing and modifying UNIX scripts according to the requirement.\nSatyam computer Services Ltd.\n3. Aug 2006 â\n?? January 2007\n (6 months)\nSupport for EA - Electronic Arts US\nInvolved in other activities like:\n\n??\n Specialization In EDI Tools Like EDI Integrator (I4)\n\n??\n Registrations of Tables and Forms for custom applications.\n\n??\n Executing concurrent programs from PL/SQL.\n\n??\n Creation of Value sets in various Modules of the application.\n\n??\n Defining Menu, Reports\n\n??\n Defining Concurrent Programs, Executables.\n\n??\n PL/SQL method of submitting Concurrent programs\nVeritas Ltd.\n4. July 2004 â\n?? July 2006\n (25 months)\nDevelopment & Support For Citi Group (Oracle Apps AOL,GL,AP,AR,PO,INV)\nInterfaces:\n\n??\n Developed interface program to upload items into GL interface tables from\n\n??\n Legacy System in Oracle General Ledger and Used SQL * Loader to upload\n\n??\n data from Flat Files to Pre-interface table and wrote a PL/ SQL Procedure for\n\n??\n all the business validations.\n\n??\n Developed PO Requisition interface program\n\n??\n Developed Customer Interface program\n\n??\n Developed Stock Locaters Interface program for Sub Inventory\nInvolved in other activities like:\n\n??\n Registrations of Tables and Forms for custom applications.\n\n??\n Executing concurrent programs from PL/SQL.\n\n??\n Creation of Value sets in various Modules of the application.\n\n??\n Defining Menu, Reports\n\n??\n Defining Concurrent Programs, Executables.\n\n??\n PL/SQL method of submitting Concurrent programs.\nResponsibilities:\n\n??\n Customization and development Reports and Interfaces. As per client\nrequirements.\n\n??\n Developing MD070 After completion of the Object Development.\n\n??\n Testing the Other Consultant Objects after completion of the Object.\nEffexoft Technologies Pvt Ltd.\n5. September 2003 â\n?? June 2004\n (10 months)\nDevelopment & Support For Mac Mohan Farma (VB and Oracle)\nDescription:\nThis project was to cater the requirements of the management and the administration dept of the company. The project was mainly aimed at the various details of the staff of the company. Data was maintained of the attendance details of the staff. The Login and Logout time of the employee was taken and his pattern of attendance, leave status, numbers of hours worked etc were provided as reports to the admin departments like HR, and also the managers. The company accepts multiple Loginâ\n??s and Logoutâ??s per day and that also flexible timing.\nEffexoft Technologies Pvt Ltd.\n6. January 2003 â\n?? August 2003\n (8 months)\nDevelopment & Support For SG Automobiles (Developer 2000 and Oracle)\nDescription:\nThe project was developed for the SG Automobile Industry. This project caters the requirements of the administration department. The project mainly aims at the various details of the total users of the company. Data was maintained and also it contains master and transactions files and have full details of inventory maintained. This data will be helpful for managers and admin departments. Various flexible features like searching names, sorting data, updating of master files time to time. Various good features of Oracle like triggers, procedures and packages have been implemented in the project.\nPERSONAL PROFILE: ï\n?ª surendrababukurra@Yahoo.com\nName : Surendra Babu .K\nNationality : Indian ï\n?? \n09923206321\nMartial Status : Single\nLanguages Known : English, Hindi, and Telugu\nHobbies : Reading Books, Browsing, playing Chess & Cricket',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-16',NULL,'2007-10-16','2010-06-08 12:13:25','2010-06-08',2,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(100,'Shireesha',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Shisdagsdagreeshedgaa2moedghan@gmail.com',NULL,NULL,'0','9242801202','0',NULL,'0','2007-04-30',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-09 12:13:49',2,'0',NULL,'200710/16/ATT53991.html','200710/16/DOC40085.doc','Kavitha\n\nShireesha\nMobile No: +91- 9242801202\nShisdagsdagreeshedgaa2moedghan@gmail.com\n\n\nProfessional Profile:\n\n\n      \n3+ years of Experience in Software Development.\n\n      \nExtensive knowledge on Data Warehousing concepts.\n\n      \nExtensively used Informatica client tools ? Source Analyzer, Warehouse designer, Mapping designer, Transformations.\n\n      \nExperience in using Oracle 9i Database.\n\n      \nStrong working experience on Data Warehousing applications, directly responsible for the Extraction, Transformation and Loading of data from multiple sources into warehouse.\n\n      \nExcellent in communication, technical skills \n\nEducational Qualification:\n\n\n      \nB.Tech\n\nElectrical and Electronics Engineering\n\nfrom Jawaharlal Nehru Technological University, \nHyderabad\n\nAndhra Pradesh\n\nIndia\n\n\nWork Experience:\n\n1.\n      \nWorking as a Data warehouse consultant in \nHCL\nTechnologies \nLtd\n\nBangalore\nfrom March?2006 to Till date..\n\n2.\n      \nWorked as a \nData warehouse consultant in \nAdea Solutions, \nBangalore\n\nfrom Jun?2004 to Feb?2006.\n\n\n\nSoftware Expertise:\n\nData warehouse Tools\n     \n\n                       \nETL\n                             \n\n           \nInformatica (Designerer)\n\nOperating System\n                  \n\n           \nWindows 2000 Server/professional\nOLAP Tool\n                             \n\n           \nBusiness Objects, Cognos\nMethodologies\n                       \n\n           \nStar Schema, Snow Flake Schema\nData Modeling Tool\n              \n\n           \nErwin 4.0\nDatabase\n                                \n\n           \nOracle 9i\n\n\n\n\n\n\nPROJECT DETAILS:\nProject #1\n\n\n      \nMCD Data Warehouse Project\n ? Lehman Brothers\n\nU.K.\n\nPeriod\n\n Feb?2007 \n- Till Date.\n\nDescription\n\nLehman Brothers, an innovator in global finance, serves the financial needs of corporations, governments and municipalities, institutional clients, and high net worth individuals worldwide. Lehman Brothers acquired 3 Mortgage Business Units (SPML, PML and ELQ) in the \nUK\n and the European geography to strengthen their presence in the mortgage business. We built a Data Warehouse solution within the Lehman Brothers environment, to meet the reporting requirements of various stakeholders within Lehman brothers. Informatica is used as an ETL tool to load the data from all the different source systems. Here the input data is in flat files and the target database is DB2\n\n\n\nTechnologies include:\n\n\n        \nInformatica 7.1, Oracle and Windows NT.\n\nResponsibilities include:\n\nDevelopment of ETL Process using Informatica Tool.\nCreated and Maintained various mappings and reusable transformations\nApplied various transformations to the source data before loading into the staging area.\nLoading of data from Source system (Flat Files) to target DB2 Database.\nInvolved in debugging the mappings.\nEffectively involved in closing the defects raised by the client during testing.\nDeveloped mappings to load data into dimension tables and fact tables.\nUsed various transformations like Joiner, Aggregator, expression, Filter, lookup, sequence generator and router in developing the mappings.\nCreated reusable sessions and workflows to load the data into warehouse.\n\n\nProject #2\n\n\n      \nSales Retails Business Process Management\n\nMorrisons Super Store, \nUK\n\n\nPeriod\n\n April?2006 \n? Jan2007.\n\nDescription\n: The \nUK\n?s fourth largest supermarket group with more than 400 stores across the country, welcoming more than 10 million shoppers each week. The enlarged group?s share of the \nUK\n?s grocery market is over 15 percent and currently employees more than 150,000 members of staff in stores, factories, and distribution centers and head office administrative functions. Data warehouse has many functional and technical groups and ETL is one among them performing the development activities for Data warehouse.\nTechnologies include:\n\n\n        \nInformatica 7.1, Oracle and Windows NT.\n\nResponsibilities:\n\n\n        \nUnderstanding and analyzing the Requirements.\n\n        \nWorked on various tools in Informatica like Source analyzer, Warehouse Designer, Transformation developer, Mapping Designer & Mapplet Designer.\n\n        \nPreparation of Mapping Documents\n\n        \nMost of the Transformations were used like the Source Qualifier, Aggregator, Filter, Router, Sequence Generator, Lookup, Joiner and Update strategy\n\n        \nCreating Email tasks for sending an email after the session runs.\n\n        \nDoing Development and Unit Testing.\n\n        \nPreparation of\n\nuser test plans\n\n        \nPreparation of weekly status reports.\n\n\nProject #3\n\n\n      \nData Marts for \nSutherland Technologies\n\n\nPeriod\n\n May?2005 \n? Feb?2006.\n                                                            \nDescription\n\nST is the leading provider of real time surveillance healthcare information and market research to its global pharmaceutical and healthcare companies. It provides syndicated research intelligence data, which tracks and predicts illness and product sales for Pharmaceutical & Healthcare companies, Marketing & Sales analysts, Consumer product manufacturers and Retailers.\n\nTechnologies include:\n\n\n        \nInformatica 6.1, Oracle and Windows NT.\n\nResponsibilities:\n\n\n        \nTranslated Business processes into Informatica mappings. \n\n        \nDeveloped Complex mappings by extensively using Informatica Transformations like Lookup, Filter, Expression, Aggregator, Joiner etc. \n\n        \nCreated Sessions using the Workflow Manager.\n\n        \nDocumented the existing mappings.\n\n        \nPerforming Unit Testing for Mappings.\n\n        \nPreparation of\n\nuser test plans\n\n        \nPreparation of weekly status reports.\n\n\nProject #4\n\n\n      \nExim \nBank\n\nMalaysia\n\nPeriod\n\n July?2004 \n? April?2005.\n\nDescription\n: Exim Bank was established on August 1995 to provide support to Malaysian exports and investors as well foreign buyers of Malaysian products and services. Exim Bank provides medium to long term credit to promote the export of Malaysian goods and services with emphasis on exports to the non-traditional markets.\nThis project was developed to provide Enterprise Reports for their internal and external use and to support queries for marketing banking decisions based on data available over a period of time. Data from ODS was extracted, transformed and loaded into Data warehouse using Informatica 6.2. This Project describes the high level requirements of the data warehouse systems. It is meant for the use of executives, senior managers and business analysts with access to accurate, consolidated information. \n\nTechnologies include:\n\n\n        \nInformatica 5.1, Oracle and Windows NT.\n\nResponsibilities: \n\n\n        \nTranslated Business processes into Informatica mappings. \n\n        \nDeveloped Complex mappings by extensively using Informatica Transformations like Lookup, Filter, Expression, Aggregator, Joiner etc. \n\n        \nCreated Sessions using the Workflow Manager.\n\n        \nDocumented the existing mappings.\n\n        \nPerforming Unit Testing for Mappings.\n\n        \nExtensively used Informatica Power center for loading the data from various source involving flat files and oracle tables.',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-16',NULL,'2007-10-16','2010-06-09 12:13:49','2010-06-09',2,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(101,'Satya',NULL,NULL,'Bangalore ','sds.tiruscsacnamala@gmail.com','satya.tirunamala@gmail.com',NULL,'0','9886459650','0',NULL,'0','2007-01-12',7,18,'2010-06-09 12:13:49',3,'0',NULL,'200710/16/ATT53990.html','200710/16/DOC40086.doc','Resdex @ naukri.com\nSatya\nSrinagar Bangalore \nsds.tiruscsacnamala@gmail.com\n\nscsc\nTelephone: 9886459650\n(M)\n\nD.O.B\n - 10 May 1978 \nModified on\n - 25 Sep 2007 \nAnnual Salary\n - INR 3 Lac(s) 5 Thousand \nTotal Years of Experience\n - 3 Year(s) 4 Month(s) \nCurrent Location\n - Bangalore \nPreferred Location\n - Anywhere in India \nSatyam.T\n\nTEXT RESUME \n\nSATYAM.T\nsatya.tirunamala@gmail.com Contact: +91-9886459650\nSummary of professional experience:\n\n??\n Having 3+ yrs of professional software experience in the area of Web Application development using Java and J2EE Technologies.\n\n??\n Expert in developing web based applications.\n\n??\n Extensive work experience in Java, J2EE technologies, including JDBC, Servlets, JSP, Struts , SQL and PLSQL\n\n??\n Good expertise in design and development aspects of software projects Using Java.\n\n??\n Ability to learn new things at a brisk pace.\n\n??\n Working as a team player, but can also complete a task of supervision.\n\n??\n Dedicated, conscientious individual with strong sense of responsibility, work flexible and quickly adapt to changing environments professionally and personally.\nProfessional Experience:\n\n??\n Working as a System Analyst in SONATA SOFTWARE LTD, \nBangalore\n from Aug? 2006 to Till Date.\n\n??\n Worked as a Junior Programmer in Nyku Systems, \nBangalore\n from July?2004 to July 2006.\nEducational Qualification:\n\n??\n Master of Computer Applications from Sri Venkateswara University\nSKILLS:\nOperating Systems : Windows98/2000/NT/XP, MS-DOS\nLanguages : JAVA /J2EE\nJava Technologies : JDBC, Servlets, JSP, Struts\nWeb / Application Servers : Tomcat 4.1/5.0, WebLogic7.0/8.1\nDatabase : Oracle 8 (SQL, PLSQL)\nIDE : Editplus, Eclipse 3.1\nTools : VSS\nOthers : HTML, Design Patterns, MVC2\nDetails of Professional Experience:\nSonata Software Ltd.\nA. CRAMER ? TCO and Usability Enhancements\nTCO describes a set of enhancements to be made to Resource Manager in Cramer6 Release 2 to support reduced total cost of ownership (TCO) and increased usability. This has five streams which are as follows, Data Load API which will provide a limited set of operations designed to be used as replacements for the list of existing Cramer API calls which have been identified as performing slowly in a data load environment. Second one is a new Attribute Wizard for Configuration will be designed to ease the specification of wizard attributes. Third stream is system for caching the values of filter parameters; the state of the label set switch and the filter toggle button will be implemented so that when refresh is clicked by the user, the view or web report is displayed in exactly the same way as its previous execution. Fourth stream changes are In order to improve this usability issue it is necessary to reduce the overall width of the routing views while still presenting a useful amount of information. The last stream would involve a new feature will be implemented that will allow users to store filter parameters for subsequent re-use on Cramer objects of the same class.\nAs a Developer for a team of 10 is responsible for\n? Involved in third (History and Caching) and fourth (Filter Sets) streams.\n? Understanding of the existing code and functionality of the all Web Reports and implemented\nHistory, Caching and Filter sets functionality in Resource Manager, Service Catalog, Sync\nEngine and Task Engine modules and also views in Resource Manager\n? Involved writing test cases for Unit and Integration Testing.\n? Involved testing of the all Resource Manager and Service Catalog Web Reports and views in\nResource Manager\n? Post delivery support by analyzing and fixing any ORs related to TCO\nB. CRAMER ? SERVICE CATALOG\nThe objective of the Service Catalog is to decouple the front end; sales and marketing of the telco, from the back end technology chosen to implement it. To support this Cramer?s Service Catalog provides capability where Products can be defined in terms of services components, which are defined from a consistent Service Catalogue of viable, reusable components. All this empowers product managers to better understand the feasibility of product enhancements quickly. Finally, new technologies can be introduced and technology migration implemented.\nI worked in the web content module of the above and being a Team Member was instrumental in following:\n? Implementation of the Order Summary Web report\n? Implementation of the all Homepages in Service Catalog and modified some of the existing Homepages which is included in Service Catalog\n? Involved to implementation of the Service Component Template and Capability Fulfillment Web Reports\n? Involved writing test cases (Homepages and Web Reports) for Unit and Integration Testing\n? Involved Unit and Integration testing of the all Homepages and Web Reports in Service Catalog.\n? Post delivery support by analyzing and fixing any ORs for the Web content of Service Catalog, which consisted of 6 Homepages and 6 Web reports.\nNyku Systems:\nC). Product Management System\nProject : Product Management System\nClient : Rass Groups, U.S.A\nSkills : JDBC,JSP, Servlets, Struts\nDatabase : Oracle\nWeb Server : Tomcat\nDescription:\nProduct Management System allows the customers to place orders online and helps the production department to keep track of the orders placed by customers. Product Management System enables the organization to deliver the products on time by notifying the production department about the orders and their delivery dates. Various reports by product, order, or customer can also be generated.\nRoles and Responsibilities:\n? Involved in coding and development of the Project.\n? Involved in validation of project using Struts frame work.\n? Involved in Unit Testing, Integration testing.\nD. Pharmacy\nProject : Pharmacy\nClient : Medinova, \nSSM\nHospital\n & pharmacies inside Hospitals\nScope : Development\nSkills : JSP, Servlets, JDBC\nDatabase : Oracle\nWeb Server : Tomcat\nDescription:\nProject developed in JAVA. Main objective of Pharmacy management software is to maintain daily transactions in pharmacy. It enables pharmacy people to manage their activity with ease and facility. We have developed entire software using JSP, Servlets and database Oracle.\nRoles and Responsibilities:\n? Involved primarily in the Design and development of the Project.\n? The design involved the presentation of the GUI Interface and development of GUI Front End Prototype.\n? Backend Java programming using JDBC for accessing information from the Oracle database.\n? Communicated with our clients, enquired and validated their business requirements.\nE. Distributed Management System\nProject : Distributed Management System\nClient : Global Leafs, Canada\nScope : Development\nSkills : JDBC, JSP, Servlets, Struts\nDatabase : Oracle\nWeb Server : Tomcat\nDescription:\nThe Distributed Management System is a web-based system designed for US Client., which gives information relating to clients and dealers of the company with respect to its different product launches. This product develops a system that can be used by the company management to keep track of the sales, dealers and its clients. In the existing method of tracking of all the details is tedious and time consuming. Any product survey and launching of the area carried out manually by representatives, which is a time taking task.\nRoles and Responsibilities:\n? Designed Components using the technology Servlets.\n? Involved in development of the interfaces using JSP and HTML.\n? Designed and created components for company?s object framework using best practices and design patterns such as Model-View-Controller (MVC).\n? Involved in the design and development of Presentation Tier using JSP, Tag Libraries and Property files.','SONATA SOFTWARE LTD',1,NULL,'2007-10-16',NULL,'2007-10-16','2010-06-09 12:13:49','2010-06-09',3,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(102,'Syed Idrees Rahamani',NULL,NULL,NULL,'idreesrahamani@yahoo.com',NULL,NULL,'0','91 9885480651','0',NULL,'0','2008-04-29',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-09 12:13:49',3,'0',NULL,'200710/16/ATT53989.html','200710/16/DOC40087.doc','Syed Idrees Rahamani\nSyed\n\nIdrees\n\nRahamani\n\nPhone No: +91-9885480651\n                          \nE-\nmail\n\n\n\nidreesrahamani@yahoo.com\n\nObjective\nTo obtain a challenging role as an Oracle Database Administrator using all the experience gained in the field of Information Technology.\n\nSummary of Qualification\n\nEducational Qualification\nM.Sc\n\nInformation Systems)\n first class Distinction with \n77%\n\nfrom \nOsmania\n University 2005 .\nB.C.A(\nComputers)\n Secured first class with \n65%\n\nfrom \nOsmania\nUniversity\n\n   \n12 \nth\n (Intermediate)\n Board of Intermediate A.P India\n10 \nth\n (SSC)\n Board of Secondary A.P India.\n\nTechnical Expertise\nPrimary Skills\n                           \n\n   \nORACLE 11i APPS DBA.\nOperating systems\n                  \n\n   \nLinux As 3.0/4.0, Win 9x\n,2000,NT,Xp,Unix\n\n\n        \nProgramming Languages\n       \n\n   \nSQL,PL/\nSQL,C,C++,Unix\n Shell Scripts & HTML\nRDBMS\n                                  \n\n\nOracle 8i\n,9i,10g\n\nOther Packages\n                      \n\n   \nMS-\nOffice\n,VB\n 6.0.\n         \n\n                                               \n   \n         \n    \n\nProfessional Summary\nAbove \n2 + years\n of experience in \nthe\n\nInformation\n Technology \nIndustry.\nCurrently working as \nOracle\n\nApplications\n DBA\n. for 2.0 years\nExperience of \nOracle\n   \nDBA\n 9i & 10g.\nExpertise hands on Installation, backup & recovery/ performance tuning of Oracle\n\nDatabase Maintaining & scheduling the Backup & Recovery plans using\n\nRMAN\n\n    \nExpertise hands on Installation of Oracle Apps 11i,\n\ncustom installations, Applying patches, Cloning , using AD utilities and Managing Concurrent Managers and Requests,\nExperience of Linux Advanced Server, Managing\n System Administration and Network Administration,\nExpertise hands on Creating User\n\naccounts assigning Quotas, Groups, Passwords, Access permissions, Scheduling System Tasks, Configuring and & maintaining of \nServers\n DHCP, FTP, NFS, Apache web server, proxy, samba server.\nExcellent communication \nand\n\ninterpersonal\n skills.\n\n\nWork Experience:\n\nWorking as an \nOracle Apps DBA\n since July 2005 to till date in \nSoft \nPearl\n\ninfotech\n Pvt. Ltd. (\nwww.softpearl.com\n\n\nResponsibilities:\n\nOracle Application DBA \nInstallation\n\nand\n\nupgradation\n\nof Oracle\n\nApplications 11i software.\nMonitoring the Instance on daily basis.\nSetting up new \nusers\n and \nProfile\n\nMonitoring\n Application Services and Performing Checks\nManaging \nConcurrent Processing\n\nCloning \nusing\n\nRapid\n Clone\n\nApplying \nPatches\nUsing \nAdpatch\n\nadctlr\n\nadadmin\n\nadconfig\n\nand\n other \nAd utilities\n\nCreation of \nSpecialized Concurrent Managers\n, Assigning \nWorkshifts\n\nAssigning Programs, Reports to Specialized\n Concurrent Managers\n\nUse \nAdpatch\n\nAdctlr\n\nAdadmin\n\nAdsplice\n and other \nAd utilities\nTrouble shooting\n\nOracle DBA\nInstallation \nof Oracle\n\nsoftware\nMonitor\n database and system performance. .\nManaging \nTablespaces\n, rollback segments, Control file, Data file, Log file and\n\nparameter file\nCreating \nUsers\n and allocating Space and\n\nPrivileges to Users\nMonitoring \nalert log\n\nPerform \nhot, cold backups \nof \nthe\n\nOracle\n Database.\nTuning\n Database, Memory for optimal Performance\nRecovery of Database\n from Disk or Instance failure\nUsing \nSQL Loader\nPerform \nhot, cold backups \nof \nthe\n\nOracle\n Database.\n\n        \nPerforming Export and \nImport\n\n        \nCreating a database \nClone.\n\n        \nCreating and Managing \nStandby Database.\n\nLinux Administration\n\nInstallation of Linux Advance Server Operating System,\nManaging System Administration and Network Administration,\nCreating User\n\naccounts\nAssigning \nQuotas\n\nGroups\n\nPassword\n\nSecurity\n\nAccess\n permissions\n to users,\nScheduling System \nTasks,Users\n\nTasks,Backups\n & Recovery Tasks,\nConfiguring & maintaining of \nNETWORKING,\n\nDHCP server\n\nConfiguring & maintaining \nof,\nNFS\n server \n\nConfiguring & maintaining of \nFTP server \n\nConfiguring & maintaining of \nApache web server\n\nConfiguring & maintaining of \nProxy, and Samba server\n\n\nProjects :\n\nPROJECT#1:\n\nProject \n        \n\n           \nMaintenance \nof\n\nOracle\n Applications11.5.9,11.5.10 \nRole\n\n   \n         \n\n           \nOracle Application DBA\n\nResponsibilities\n\n\n\n\nMonitoring the Instance on daily basis.\n\n\nInvolving in Performance/ Trouble shooting Issues.\n\n\nSystem Administration Tasks like Create users, assigning responsibilities.\n\n\nSystem Administration Tasks on Concurrent Manager.\n\n\nMaintaining the instance with AD Administration\n\n\nApplying application patches.\n\n\nAdministration of Oracle Applications.\n\n\nTroubleshooting Oracle Application Issues.\n\n\nCloning Oracle Applications\n                                                                                                                   \n                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                \n                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                \n                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                \n                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                \n                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                \n                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                \n                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                \n                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                \n                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                \n                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                \n                                                                                 \nPROJECT#2\n\nProject\n         \n\n           \nConfiguration and Maintenance of Oracle 9i Database \nRole\n    \n         \n\n           \nOracle DBA\n\nResponsibilities:\n\n\n        \nAdministration of Oracle 9i database including installation, creation and planning the Backup strategy on Linux.\n\n        \nAllocating system storage and planning future storage requirements for \nthe\n\ndatabase\n system.\n\n        \nManaging primary database structure and objects.\n\n        \nPlanning for backup and recovery of database and maintaining Hot Backups and Cold Backups.\n\n        \nCreating users, assigning roles and profiles, maintaining system security through monitoring user access to the database.\n\n\n\nPersonal Details:\n\nFather?s Name\n                         \n\n\nSyed\n\nYaqub\nDate of birth\n                              \n: 30-12-1979.\nGender\n\n                                      \n\n\nMale\nLanguages Known\n                    \n\n\nEnglish, \nHindi\n,Telugu\n\nPostal Address\n                         \n\n: 8-1-143/MB/23,\n    \nMini \nBrindavan\n Colony,\n                            \nTolichowki\n\nHyderabad\n ? 500008,\n       \n                     \nAndhra Pradesh\n\nIndia',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-16',NULL,'2007-10-16','2010-06-09 12:13:49','2010-06-09',3,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(103,'V. Venkat',NULL,NULL,'Bangalore ','vvmohscsacscanbabu@yahoo.com',NULL,NULL,'0','09886189860','0',NULL,'0','2007-09-12',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-09 12:13:49',3,'0',NULL,'200710/16/ATT29561.html','200710/16/DOC40088.doc','V. Venkat \n\n                                                                   \n32/1,3rd Cross,9th A \nMain\nB.T.M\n   \n1st Stage\nBangalore\n - 560029\nPhone: 09886189860\n                                                            \n             \n\nEmail : \nvvmohscsacscanbabu@yahoo.com\nExperience Summary\n2.5 years of experience working in Tibco Product Suite. \nGood client interaction experience.\nStrong knowledge of emerging EAI standards.\nHaving good hands on work experience in XML Technologies (XML, DTD, XSD, XSLT and XPATH, SOAP, WSDL).\nStrong knowledge of TIBCO EMS.\n\nHighlights\n\nExpertise in working with TIBCO BusinessWorks, TIBCO Designer, TIBCO Administrator, TIBCO Rendezvous,TIBCO EMS, MQSeries & MQSeries adapter, File and Adb adapters.\n\nExpertise in working with Oracle and SQL Server Databases.\n\nEducation\n\nBACHELOR OF TECHNOLOGY (MECHANICAL), 2001-05, \nOsmania\nUniversity\n, Hyd.\n\nTechnical Skills\n\nDatabases\nOracle 9i AS, SQL Server\n\nEAI/Integration Tools\nTIBCO Business Works, TIBCO Designer, TIBCO Rendezvous, TIBCO EMS, MQSeries, TIBCO Administrator(\nEnterprise\n Edition) and MQSeries, File and Adb Adapters. \nJ2EE Technologies\nJAVA (Servlet, JSP, JMS, JDBC)\nWeb and Application Servers\nWeb Logic Application Server, Tomcat\nERP/CRM\nSiebel CRM 7.6',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-16',NULL,'2007-10-16','2010-06-09 12:13:49','2010-06-09',3,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(104,'Venkata subba',NULL,NULL,NULL,'suscscbbu.scsc4634@gmail.com',NULL,NULL,'0','09886238096','0',NULL,'0','2007-04-30',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-09 12:13:49',3,'0',NULL,'200710/16/ATT29560.html','200710/16/DOC40089.doc','Responsibilities: -\nVenkata SubbaRao\n                         \n                    \nmail: suscscbbu.scsc4634@gmail.com\nETL Developer\n                                                                      \nVoice:\n\n09886238096\nOBJECTVIE:\n            \nLooking for\n\na challenging and Responsible position in the field of Information Technology and have the flexibility to adapt to any new environment and work on any project wish to utilize this experience in an organization as part of a team.\nPROFILE:\nHaving 3+ years of experience with ETL functioning and dataware housing concepts and 7 months of experience with Oracle database. \n\nSUMMARY:\n\n         \nData warehousing ETL\nexperience using,\n Informatica Power Center 7.1 \n(Source Analyzer, Warehouse Designers, Repository Manager, Server manager\n\nMapping/Mapplet/Transformations, Repository Server, Repository Server Admin Console, Workflow Manager) .\n\n         \nExpertise in \nStar/Snowflake \nSchema Design\n\n\n         \nKnowledge of OLAP reporting tool \nBusiness Objects\n\nSupervisor\n\nDesigner and\n      \nBusiness Objects \nfor building \nEnterprise\n reports. \n\n         \nDatabase experience\n using Oracle 9i/8i.\n\n         \nVery Good Programming skills using \nPL/SQL\n (Coding Procedures, Functions, Database Packages and Triggers).\nExcellent communication and interpersonal skills.\nTECHNICAL SUMMARY\n\nData\n\nWarehousing\nInformatica PowerCenter7.1/6.1/5.1.\nBusiness\n\nIntelligence\n\nBusiness Objects (Designer, Supervisor, Reporter & WEBI).\nData\n\nModeling\nStar-Schema Modeling, Snowflakes Modeling, FACT & Dimensions.\nDatabases\nOracle 9i/8i, MS Access.\nProgramming\nSQL, PL/SQL. \nOperating systems\nWindows95/98/NT/2000.\n\nEDUCATION\nB.Sc (Computer Science)\n from \nUniversity\nof \nNagarjuna\n\nP.G.D.C.A.\n   \nfrom \nIndira Gandhi National Open University.\n\nExperience Profile:\n\nWorking as \nSoftware Engineer\n\nfor Logica CMG\n\n\n\nfrom\n Mar? 2005 \nto\n till date.\nWorked as \nSoftware Engineer\n in\n\nTechy Soft\n from \nDec?2003 to Feb? 2005.\n\nProject Summary:\n\nProject 1\n\n\nTitle \n           \n\n         \n  \n\n: Insurance Warehouse\n                \nJuly 2006 to till date\nClient\n           \n         \n   \n\n\nUnited America Insurance Company \nEnvironment\n\n      \n   \n: Windows 2000/Informatica7.1\n\nOracle9i/8i/\nOverview:\n          \nWith just four employees, United American opened its doors in 1947 to provide life, health and accident coverage to individuals in \nTexas\n. Today, UAIC has over 500 people in the Home Office working to ensure our customers receive outstanding products, service and support every day. This project is basically designed for a centralized warehouse on which managers can draw their analysis easily\nResponsibilities: -\n\n\n         \nInvolved in creating \n\nMappings\n\nMapplets\n in \nInformatica\n\n\n         \nWorked on several transformations such as Filter Transformations, Joiner Transformations, Rank Transformations, \nSequence Generator\n Transformations, \nStored Procedure\n Transformations, Expression Transformations in \nInformatica\n\n\n         \nSetup Procedures to \nExtract, Transform and Load\n (ETL) data from different sources \n\nby Using \nInformatica\n\n\n         \nDefined the \nSource\n databases and \nTarget\n databases in \nInformatica.\n\nProject 2:\n\n\nTITLE\n     \n         \n   \n: Sales Data Mart\n                 \nMarch 2005 to June 2006\n    \nClient\n      \n    \n      \n   \n: Con Agro Foods.\n    \n    \nEnvironment\n   \n   \n: Informatica 6.0, Oracle 8i, Business Objects 5.0/6.5\n\nDescription\n\nThis Project involves the creation of a Data Mart for the Sales Reporting System and \nprovides details of the Work Order, Sales invoice with domestic sales which currently uses transactional processing system. It implements decision support system using data warehouse for forecasting, designing business model, cost and expenses analysis for better utilization of resource distribution of historical sales, financial and Sales information data to brokers, Dealers and financial centers.\n\n\n\n\n\n\nResponsibilities\n\n\n         \nDesign of \nETL\n processes using Informatica tool to load data from Source System and Data Transformations and then load to the target database. Extracted Data from \nOracle\n, Flat files using \nInformatica.\n\n\n         \nInvolved in creating mappings for the source and target definitions.\n\n         \nUsed Debugger for debugging \nMappings\n and \nSessions\n\n\n         \nOptimizing Various \nMappings, Sessions, Source \nand\n Target Databases\n\nProject 3:\nTitle\n            \n          \n: Educational Management system \n          \n   \nJuly\n 2004 ? Feb 2005\nClient\n          \n          \n\nDorset\n cerial ltd\n                   \n           \nEnvironment\n        \n: Informatica 7.1, Oracle 8i.\nDescription:\n\n                   \nThis system is Educational Management Software. It has many outstanding features such as data retrieval, high-speed report generation. The user can define screens and reports etc. It provides a wide range of advanced and easily upgradeable functions covering all necessary requirements of institution. It includes Student Information System, Fee Collection, Financial Accounting and Inventory controlling System, Invoicing and voucher printing, transportation, performance analysis, Timetable, Attendance, Library Automation, Report Designer and M.I.S & Utilities. \nResponsibilities:\n\n\n         \nInvolved mainly in creating mappings for source definitions and target definitions.\n\n         \nCreated transformations like Lookup, Aggregator and Rank...etc.\n\n         \nBug tracking using Debugger.\n\n         \nImplementing SQL Overrides where ever necessary.\n\n\nProject#4:\n                                                                                      \nDec 2003 to June 2004\n\n    \nTitle \n                 \n\nHandling and Transportation System\n     \n    \nClient\n                \n: IFFCO Limited\n    \nEnvironment \n   \n: Oracle-8i, PL/SQL.\nDescription\n\n   \n                     \n\nThis project consists mainly three modules they are master, transactions, reports. Master module handles operations, storage rate master and space reservations segments. In transaction module we are going to handle various transactions such as handling at rake point, dispatch advices, stock releasing order. The report module consisting of preparing reports as per the user requirement normal bill detail, dist wise space reserved bill passing statement and payment details.\nResponsibilities:\n\n\n         \nCreating Views, Synonyms and Sequences.\n\n         \nInvolved in writing user defined Exceptions.\n\n         \nInvolved in creating package specifications and cursors.\n\n         \nInvolved in Writing procedures, functions and triggers.',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-16',NULL,'2007-10-16','2010-06-09 12:13:49','2010-06-09',3,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(105,'Venkatesh P',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL,'0',NULL,'0','2007-04-30',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-09 12:13:49',3,'0',NULL,'200710/16/ATT29559.html','200710/16/DOC40090.doc','Resume - Viraj Patil\nHaving 3.6 years of experience in software development \nsummary\n\n       \nSoftware professional with 3 years 6 months of experience\n\n       \nSound exposure in \n\nSQL SERVER 2000 ,\nORACLE PL\n/SQL\nProfessional profile\n\n         \nWorking as Software Engineer for \nWipro Technologies ltd\n\nBangalore\n from \n26-06-2006\n to till date\n\n         \nWorked as a Analyst Programmer for \nRamco Systems ltd, \nChennai from 24-12-2003 to \n     \n18-05-2006\n\nEducation \n\n       \nBachelor of Engineering (C.S.E), \nMadras\nUniversity\n (Sri Muthu Kumaran Institute of Technology), Chennai, Percentage : 74\n\n       \n12th Std, Sri Ramakrishna Mission Higher Secondary School, Chennai, Percentage : 83\n\n       \n10th Std ,The \nHindu\nSenior\nSecondary School\n, Chennai, Percentage : 69\n\nTechnical Skills\nOperating Systems\nWindows 2000/NT/XP,Unix\nTools\nCrystal\n Reports 9.0.\nRDBMS\n\nMS SQL Server 2000, \nOracle PL\n/SQL,Sybase 12.5.1\n\n\nProject Name\n\n\n                      \n\n\n          \nCorporate Employee Financial services\nProject Description\n                \n\n          \nDevelopment of Stock options for Employees.\nEnvironment\n                           \n\n           \nSybase 12.5.1, \nOracle PL\n/SQL\nRoles and Responsibilities\n     \n\n            \n                        \nAs a software engineer perfomed the following tasks\n\n\n       \nDeveloped and Modified procedures for the plans ESOP, RSA, SAR.\n\n       \nPerformed Technical Design document for RSA product.\n\n       \nInvolved in requirement gathering from client and modifying the reports\n\nProject Name\n\n\n                      \n\n           \nImplementation of Ramco E-Applications\nProject Description\n                \n\n          \nTo design, maintain and develop the screens and Reports.\nEnvironment\n                           \n\n          \nSql server 2000, Oracle PL/SQL\nRoles and Responsibilities\n     \n\n\n       \nInvolved in developing the reports\n\n       \nWriting the Procedures,Triggers,Functions,T-Sql\n\n       \nTaking the Backups of the Databases and restoring it in another server for testing the applications.\n\n       \nDatabase Maintenance and Performance tuning.\n\nProject Name\n              \n\n Base Product Development.\nProject Description\n    \n: Maintenance of the Product Ramco E-Applications\nEnvironment\n               \n\nSql server 2000\nRole:\n\n       \nWriting the Stored Procedures,Triggers,Functions,T-Sql\n\n       \nTaking the Backups of the Databases and restoring it in another server for testing the applications.\n\n       \nDatabase maintenance and performance tuning.\n\nProject Name: Internal CRM Project\nProject Description: Maintaining the customers and sales person details involved in the company\nEnvironment:\n\nSql server 2000\nResponsibilities:\n\n       \nWriting the Stored Procedures,Triggers,Functions,T-Sql\n\n\nPROFESSIONAL PROFILE\n\n\n       \nEnthusiastic, having relevant experience in Programming.\n\n       \nMotivated achiever and problem-solver who will do what it takes to get the job done\n\n       \nEnergetic self-starter who is enthusiastic about learning new technologies, enhancing current technical expertise and applying transferable skill sets.\n\n       \nCongenial to teamwork, innovative and Optimistic.\n\nPersonal Details \n\nName\n                                                   \n\n\nVenkatesh puchakatla\n\nDate of Birth \n                                       \n\n\n09\nth\n Feb 1981\n\nMarital status \n                          \n           \n\n\nSingle\n\nPassport \n                                 \n           \n: Yes\n\nPlace : \nDate\n   \n\n                                                                                                            \nVenkatesh P',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-16',NULL,'2007-10-16','2010-06-09 12:13:49','2010-06-09',3,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(106,'Vibhavari Arya',NULL,NULL,NULL,'vibhaxvaxxri.arya@gmail.com',NULL,NULL,'0','09818579994','0',NULL,'0','2007-04-30',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-09 12:13:49',3,'0',NULL,'200710/16/ATT29558.html','200710/16/DOC40091.doc','Vibhavari Arya\nVibhavari Arya \nMobile No. : 09818579994\nEmail Id: vibhavari.arya@gmail.com\n\n\nProfessional Experience\n: 3 years of experience and extensive knowledge of Oracle 9i,Oracle 10g,SQL,PLSQL, Developer 2000(Forms 6i & Reports 6i) and Developer Suites 10G.\n\nobjective\n\nTo seek a challenging position in the field of Software development to enhance my skills and strengths in conjunction with the organization?s goals and objectives.\nQUALIFICATIONS SUMMARY\n\n\n      \n\nyears of Professional software experience in a development environment.\n\n      \nMasters In Computer Application\n (MCA) from IGNOU. \n\n      \nExperience with Client/Server applications and knowledge of Oracle. \n\n      \nHave excellent analytical, interpersonal and communication skills.\n\n      \n\nexcellent front-end development skills using \nDeveloper 2000 and Developer Suit 10G\n\n\n      \nExcellent \nOracle\n\n8i, Oracle 9i and Oracle 10G\n RDBMS skills on Windows 2000 Platform. \n\n      \nExcellent \nPL/SQL programming\n/Database design.\n\nPROGRAMMING SKILLS\n\n\n      \nLanguages\n                                     \nSQL and PL/SQL, C, FORTRAN, COBOL\n\n      \nRDBMS Tools:\n\n                           \nOracle 8i, Oracle 9i and Oracle 10G \n\n      \nFront End \n     \n                                \nDeveloper 2000 (Forms 6i, Report 6i), Developer Suit 10G\n\n      \nOperating Systems:\n\n                   \nWindows NT/95/98/2000, Linux\n      \nProfessional work summary\n\n\nTAVANT TECHNOLOGIES,\n a sOFTWARE ENGINEER FROM 13 Nov.2006 TO TiLL DATE \n\nFounded in 2000, Tavant has quickly grown to a company of over 1100 professionals delivering global IT solutions and services. Tavant has built a strong foundation of engineering excellence and process maturity that has allowed us to excel in providing enterprise wide software applications with a particular focus on Warranty Management and Mortgage Lending.Tavant is an ISO 27001 compliant and SEI-CMMi level 4 certified organizations. Our high Customer satisfaction & employee satisfaction cores are an indication of the success of our solutions, which are based on a deep understanding of the processes and industries we focus on. We have built significant expertise in highly engineered technologies including workflow and rules engines, constraint-based optimization engines, and document management & imaging solutions, with Service Oriented Architecture (SOA) at its core. Tavant accelerates the development of custom software through modular, configurable and SOA-based solution platforms resulting in quick delivery of reliable custom applications.\n\nRole & Responsibility:\n\nAs a Software Engineer my responsibilities include:\n\n          \nInvolved in making ER Diagrams and Technical Design Documents. \n\n          \nInvolved in development of Forms and reports as per the requirement of client. \n\n          \nInvolved in the Planning for a Timely Delivery. \n\n          \nInvolved in Meeting with the testing team to mitigate all the \n        \nRisks and Potential failures\n\n          \nSmoke Testing.\n\n          \nInvolved in resolving bugs.\n\n          \nDirectly communicating with the client regarding the requirements \n     \n\nCompany name\nTavant Technologies\nProject Name \nMLBAM(Major League Baseball Advanced Media)\nOS: \nWindows\n\n2000,Solaris\nGUI TOOL:\nDeveloper Suit 10G\nDatabase:\nOracle 9i,Oracle 10G\nDescription:\nMLB(Major League Baseball) is highest level of play in professional baseball in the world. MLB refers to entity that operates North America?s two top leagues, the National League and the American League since 1903. \nThe production/multimedia wing of MLB is New York-based MLB Advanced Media (MLBAM), which oversees MLB.com and all 30 of the individual teams\' websites. Its charter states that MLB Advanced Media holds editorial independence from the League itself, but it is indeed under the same ownership group and revenue-sharing \n\n\n\n\nEASTERN SOFTWARE SYSTEMS (ESS) PVT. LTD,\n AS a sOFTWARE ENGINEER FROM \nMay 05 to Nov-06\nESS \nis a software development company in OKHLA PHASE II NEW DELHI. The activities in ESS involve development, QA and Support assignments of customized applications.\nResponsibilities:\n\n      \nProgramming on Oracle 8i and above with Developer 2000 Forms, Reports.\n\n      \nUnderstanding client?s requirement, developing a system according to the requirements and deploying it after completion. \n\n          \nMigration of Existing ERP (Ebizframe) into Oracle 10G and Developer Suit 10G.\n\n\n\n\nASSIGNMENTS UNDERTAKEN \n\n\nCompany name\nM/S. Eastern Software Systems Pvt. Ltd\n\nProject Name \nebizframe\nOS: \nWindows\n\n2000\nGUI TOOL:\nDeveloper 2000 ( Forms 6i, Report 6I),Developer Suit 10G\nDatabase:\nOracle 9i,Oracle 10G\nDescription:\nEbizframe, a mid-range, web-enabled ERP specifically targeted at the Small and Medium Enterprises [SME] segment. Ebizframe works with equal dexterity and robustness across manufacturing, distribution, trading and retail environments.\n ESS Ebizframe software is a fully integrated business solution that gives firms in a variety of\n\nindustries complete control over the planning and management of all facets of their operations, including accounting, manufacturing and distribution\n\n\n\n\n\nCompany name\nM/S. Eastern Software Systems Pvt. Ltd\n\nProject Name\nNexus, UK Project\nOS: \nWindows 2000\nGUI TOOL:\nDeveloper 2000 (Form 6i, Report 6i) \nDatabase:\nOracle 8i\nDescription:\nThis is most popular ERP package in which 16 modules exist for resolving the problem of current business processing. I\n\nimplemented following modules in Nexus:-\n\n          \nSales\n\n          \nPurchase\n\n          \nInventory\n\n          \nProduction Planning\n\n          \nProduction\n\n          \nFinance \n\n          \nHrPay\n\n          \nSystem Admin\n\n          \nShares\n\n          \nCosting\n\n          \nFixed Assets\n\n              \n\n                                  \nHY-TEK PVT. LTD. \n\n as a sOFTWARE DEVELOPER FROM AUG 04 to April 05.\nResponsibilities:\n\n      \nProgramming on Oracle 8i and above with Developer 2000 Forms, Reports.\n\nCompany name\nHY-Tek Pvt. Ltd.,\n\nNew Delhi\n\nProject Name\nGlobal Table System\n\nOS: \nWindows 2000\nGUI TOOL:\nDeveloper 2000 (Form 6i, Report 6i) \nDatabase:\nOracle 8i\nDescription:\nIt is troubleshooting software for customer. It also automates loan processing of the various customers. This application adopted the Horizontal Market Framework and converted it into Vertical Market Framework.\n\n    \nIt had a general and specific implementation and could be adopted to other industry specific applications\n\n                             \n\nEDUCATION AND TRAINING\n\n\nEducation\n        \n\n    \nM.C.A. \nfrom School of Computer & Information Sciences (SOCIS), IGNOU.\n                            \nADCA\n from SOCIS, Indira Gandhi National Open University.\n                            \nPGDCA\n from SOCIS, Indira Gandhi National Open University.\n\nCertification\n   \n\n   \nCertificate In Computing (CIC), \nfrom SOCIS, Indira Gandhi National Open University.\n            \n                   \nDiploma in Computer Software Technology from ET&T\n\n\n\nacademic qualification\n\n\n\nB.Sc\n. (General) from Delhi university.\n\n\nHigher Secondary from C.B.S.E Board.\n\n       \nHigh School from C.B.S.E Board.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nPERSONAL DETAILS\n\nFather?s Name\n                      \n\n\nShri H.C Arya.\nAddress \n                                \n                \n\n\nH.No-261 , Sec-1\n                                           \n\n\nPkt-1 , Dwarka.New Delhi-110075.\n       \n  \n             \nMobile no.\n                             \n\n\n09818579994,\nE-mail\n                     \n                \n\n\nVibhavari.arya@gmail.com\nDate of Birth\n                         \n\n\n14\n\n Jan 1978.\nNationality\n                            \n\n\nIndian.\nStatus\n                     \n               \n\n\nFemale, Single\nLanguage Known\n                \n               \n\n\nEnglish, Hindi.\nPassport Status\n                    \n\n   \nValid Passport with B-1 Visa (Expires in 2017\n\n                                                      \n\n\n\n\nPlace: New Delhi\n                                  \n                                              \n      \n(Vibhavari Arya )',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-16',NULL,'2007-10-16','2010-06-09 12:13:49','2010-06-09',3,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(107,'Saji sukumaran',NULL,NULL,NULL,'sajiscsacc03@yahoo.com',NULL,NULL,'0','91 9945002222','0',NULL,'0','2006-09-28',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-09 12:13:49',3,'0',NULL,'200710/16/ATT29557.html','200710/16/DOC40092.doc','SAJI SUKUMARAN\n\nSAJI SUKUMARAN\nEmail\n\nsajiscsacc03@yahoo.com\nBangalore\n\nINDIA\nPhone\n: +91 9945002222\n\n\n\nSummary: \nBanking & Financial Analyst / Consultant\n\n\n         \nHolding \n3.6 years\n of experience in Business requirement gathering, Development work flow, gap analysis, and Implementation experience in I.T industry (BFSI Domain).\n\n         \nGood understanding of the \nBanking (viz)\n\nCapital Markets-\nsecurities, derivatives, Forex \nconcepts.\n\n         \nCarried out implementation and enhancement of \nFLEXCUBE\n (Core Banking suite of I-flex).\n\n        \nWorked in \nOracle ERP Applications 11.5.9 (\nviz\n) ACCOUNTS & RECIEVABLE\n; Involved in the integration projects.\n\n        \nInvolved in the \nProduct specific requirements gathering & preparation/review of Functional specifications/Use case artifacts.\n\n        \nInvolved in the development of test cases and executing the test cases.\n\n        \nInvolved in Functional, System and Regression Testing;\n\n        \nInvolvement in all stages of Software Development Life Cycle.\n\n        \nTheoritical expertise on OOAD language standards.\n10\n      \nTheoretical knowledge of C/Java/SQL prog.languages & technologies; RDBMS concepts & Software Engineering terminologies\n11\n      \nPossess excellent academic background in Engineering ? \nInformation Technology\n\n\nWork Experience:\nI-flex solutions Ltd (\nwww.iflexsolutions.com\n\n\nBangalore\n\nJune 05 ? Till date\nGE Consumer & Industrial \n\nBangalore\n) (\nContract-Team lease\n\nApril, 04 ?June 05.\n\n\nEducation\nBachelor of Technology\n (B.Tech) ?Information Technology-2003,\nMadras University\nINDIA\n (73%).\n\n\n\n\n\n\nTechnical skills\nDatabase: Oracle 8i, 9i.\nERP: Oracle Application\n\ne- business suite11i\nLanguages:\n\nSQL, PLSQL\nOperating Systems: Windows NT/XP\nFront End: Developer 6i.\nScripts: HTML,Java script\n\nProject Experience:\n\nI-flex Solutions Ltd\n                                                                \nJune 05 ? Till date\n\n    \nProjects & Responsibilities:\n\n         \nSecurities Module Enhancement analysis and implementation ?\nKazakhstan\n\n\n         \nFlexcube Notional Pooling ? Integrated Liquidity Management (\nSouth Africa\n) Analysis and requirement study. \n\n         \nInterface feasibility study and Analysis of RTGS messages to ILM (IBM liquidity Manager) from Flexcube.\n\n         \nUganda RTGS enhancement.(MT103,MT202) \n\n         \nKenya\n Securities Enhancement (Swift 541 and 543).\n\n         \nMorocco\n teller enhancement (Conditional Archiving and Purging).\n\n         \nImplementation: Citibank Nairobi (Kenya-Onsite);Implementation role out of Securities- Fixed Income, T-bills, Zero coupon bonds,\n    \nILFs, Liens.\n\n         \nFlexcube Implementation support for SSA cluster. (Offshore)\n\n         \nFlexcube Securities Implementation support for Citibank \nEGYPT\n, Citibank \nUkraine\n. (Offshore)\n\n         \nImplementation: Citibank Johannesburg(South Africa-Onsite)\n      \nImplementation role out of Securities- Fixed Income, T-bills.\n\n         \nSecurities Module Enhancement analysis (\nPoland\n).\n10\n      \nIntegrated Liquidity Management Enhancement Support (\nPoland\n).\n\nBroad view of responsibilities undertaken:\n\n\n        \nPerfom techno-functional analysis for module development and enhancement.\n\n        \nPerform requirements gathering for modular development/enhancement projects on the Client?s legacy systems\n\n        \nPerform analysis & develop Functional/Design specification documents, based on BRDs sent in by customer\n\n        \nActive involvement in Product design reviews; Put forward technical suggestions on methodology to be deployed for module development \n\n        \nConsults and coordinates with developers to implement automated solutions; Provide assistance from a functional perspective in identifying, evaluating, and developing systems and procedures\n\n        \nPréparation of test case scénarios & perform smoke tests to ensure product requirements. Facilitate issue resolution including communicating end state solutions to business customers\n\n        \nPerform STP analysis to ensure module integration with Client partner systems.\n\n        \nInvolve in preparation of project deliverables, reports & project-related metrics data\n\n        \nParticipate in providing Product presentations/demos & application training at customer sites to end users.\n\n\n\nGE Consumer & Industrial\n - (Team Lease Pvt Ltd)\n             \nApril, 04 ?June 05\n\nProject\n: GLOBAL CUSTOMER MASTER (GCM) ?Oracle Financial-AR customization of forms & Reports, Interfaces and complete Integration.\nEnvironmen\nt: Oracle Applications 11.5.9/Forms 6i/Reports 6i/Oracle 8i\n\n        \nInterface with GCM.\n\n        \nIntegrating GCM with many Business Unit.\n\n        \nCustomer Addition Globally from single entry point \n\n        \nReport & Form Customization for \nOracle\nAR\n modules.\n\n        \nRole out of integration with all business units of GE.\n\nResponsibilities\n\n        \nInterface study of GCM with ERP - AR.\n\n        \nMaintenance Analysis of GCM Bulk data load using SQL * Loader as well online data addition.\n\n        \nInvolved in Legacy Customer Attribute Mapping with Duns Attribute.\n\n        \nUnit Testing performed thoroughly in order to hit proposed match ratio.\n\n        \nMaintenance of Business Management Portal.\n\n        \nDeveloped PLSQL Scripts for Database Manipulation.\n\n        \nInvolved in Designing Database Setup for corresponding portal.\n\n        \nInvolved in Manual Testing, prepared Test Cases.\n\n        \nInvolved in the Maintenance and Support for Production Roll out of GCM with remaining business of GE C&I.\n\n\n\n\nPersonal Details.\nFull Name: Saji Sukumaran\nBirth Date: 03-12-1981\nSex: Male:\nMartial status: Single\nNationality: Indian.\n\nReferences\n\nWill be furnished on request.',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-16',NULL,'2007-10-16','2010-06-09 12:13:49','2010-06-09',3,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(108,'Sakshi Tyagi',NULL,NULL,NULL,'kishtiscscsactyagi@yahoo.com',NULL,NULL,'0','09888496345','0',NULL,'0','2007-04-30',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-09 12:13:49',3,'0',NULL,'200710/16/ATT29556.html','200710/16/DOC40093.doc','Shweta Agarwal\nSakshi Tyagi\nTel: 09888496345 ~ Email: kishtiscscsactyagi@yahoo.com\n\nTo utilize my acquired knowledge and experience for the growth of the organisation that provides opportunities for professional and personal growth\n\nProfessional Synopsis\n\n\n     \nSoftware/hardware Test Engineer having 3 years of exp with Infosys Technologies Ltd.\n\n     \nWorked with client, ABN AMRO in \nAmsterdam\n, The \nNetherlands\n on short term basis from Feb ?07 to Apr ?07.\n\n     \nWorking experience of Regression\n testing, Functional/Non-functional testing, Stress/Performance testing, Test\n planning and strategies and Reports.\n\n     \nAccomplished, flexible and results-driven tester in intense pressure and aggressive timelines.\n\n     \nResourceful team player with good interpersonal skills.\n\nAcademia\n\n\n     \nB. Tech. \nin Chemical Engineering from \nM.J.P\nRohilkhand\nUniversity\n\nBareilly\n in 2003 with 83%.\n\n     \nH.S.C \nfrom \nT.R.M\nPublic School\n, Modinagar in 1998 with 75.4%.\n\n     \nS.S.C \nfrom \nRainbow\nSchool\n\nSaharanpur\n in 1996 with 76.6%.\n\nIT Skills \n\nTesting Tools\n               \n          \n\n            \nTest Director, Win runner\nOthers\n              \n              \n     \n\n             \nUNIX, RDBMS, Sybase, TOAD\n\nOrganisational Experience\n\nClient: ABN AMRO BANK\n      \n          \n              \nTest Engineer\n\n         \n     \n                        \n     \n   \nsince Aug ?06\n\nProject Handled;\n\n     \nAAAMOMGA (OMEGA) \n||\n Minerva Application \n\n   \nMinerva is the Order Management System for new order posting to back offices present in different locations such as \nAmsterdam\n, Luxemburg etc. through Mercator. \n\n    \nTransaction, holdings etc details are taken care by State Street Bank (outsourced to SSB)\n\n\n\n     \nAAAMOMGA (OMEGA) \n||\n FMC Sylvan Application \n\n\nSylvan suite is used to perform performance calculation of portfolio against database.\n   \nThen sylvan reports are generated.\n\n\n\n     \nAAAMOMGA (OMEGA) \n||\n Performance Building Blocks Application \n\n\nA standalone excel VBA application which generates graphical performance building blocks.\n\n\n\n     \nAAAMOMGA (OMEGA) \n||\nEnterprise\n Client Reporting \n- Client reporting is a critical work stream supported by SSB and helps AAM in meeting its client-critical reporting requirements.\n\nThe\n client reports will be made up of smaller units called as Building blocks (including performance building blocks generated from PBB application).\n\nRole;\n\n     \nAnalysis and Documentation.\n\n     \nCreating and maintaining different test scenarios for execution in Minerva.\n\n     \nChecking the different tags sent out from front end application.\n\n     \nPerforming Manual Testing of monthly and quarterly ECR reports.\n\n     \nRegression testing of ECR reports.\n\n     \nGeneration of performance building blocks.\n\n     \nStress testing of PBB application for both quarterly and monthly ECR portfolios.\n\n     \nPerforming manual performance calculation in sylvan application.\n\n\n\nClient: ADIDAS\n          \n       \n                               \n\n    \nTest Engineer\n                                   \n          \nMay?06 ? Jul?06\n\nProject Handled;\n\n\n     \nADHQAPPS (ADIDAS HQ APPLICATION SUPPORT) \n||\n ILS ( International Logistic Systems)\n- Planning engine in the adidas environment and the assignment requires de-linking an existing file based interface from a mainframe (IB) and building an interface to a new Master Data Management application for Supplier information (MDM-S) and then manually testing the whole.\n\nRole;\n\n     \nCreation/modification of Tables and Stored procedures in Sybase. \n\n     \nModifications in Power Builder code.\n\n\n     \nReviewing all business and technical specifications. \n\n     \nIdentify and isolate problems encountered during test execution. \n\n     \nUpdating and maintaining documentation\n\nClient: UBS Investment Bank\n\n     \n          \n     \n     \nTest Engineer\n\n                                 \n     \nMar ?05 ? Arp ?06\n\nProject Handled;\n\n     \nUBQCTM(APAC OFFSHORE QA TESTING) \n||\n Equity Trader(ET) Application\n- The Equity Trader is a Global Client-tool Web-based application for DMA (Direct Market Access) and Worked order flow.\n\nRole;\n\n     \nDaily Build Verification Tests on newly deployed product builds\n\n     \nCreating and maintaining test plans and test cases for the assigned areas\n\n\n     \nDocumenting bugs, Regression testing\n\n     \nStress/Performance testing\n\n     \nDeveloping/Executing Automated Performance\n\nProject Handled;\n\n     \nUBQCTM(APAC OFFSHORE QA TESTING) \n||\n OASIS Application\n- OASIS is UBS Warburg?s global order management system. It?s a key component of the \nEquities Global Execution Engine\n- The system provides complete transparency, life cycle tracking and the ability to handle\n cross border transactions to all Equity sales and trading force across the world.\n\nRole;\n\n     \nDaily Build Verification Tests on newly deployed product builds\n\n     \nCreating and maintaining test plans and test cases for the assigned areas\n\n\n     \nDocumenting bugs, Regression testing\n\n\nExtra-Curricular Activities \n\n\n     \nDeveloped \na POST project on \nLibrary management\n using Visual Basic.\n\n     \nProject in 8\nth\n Semester: \nPlant Design for Manufacturing of Cumene of capacity 2.5 tons/hr \n(Techno-economic feasibility survey) \nMember,\n Seminar:\n\nIndustrial Waste Water Treatment by Solar Detoxification Technology.\n\n\n     \n\nSeminar: Industrial Waste Water Treatment by Solar \nDetoxification\n\nTechnology\n\n\n\nPersonal Profile\n\nDate of Birth\n               \n\n             \n29\nth\n September 1980\nAddress\n                      \n\n             \n256/1 Sector-14, Panchkula, Haryana.',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-16',NULL,'2007-10-16','2010-06-09 12:13:49','2010-06-09',3,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(109,'Sanjeev Kumar sharma',NULL,NULL,NULL,'sascscscnjeev.shscscarma80@rediffmail.com','sanjeesacscv.sscsacharma80@yahoo.com',NULL,'0','91 09999891007','0',NULL,'0','2008-04-29',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-09 12:13:49',10,'0',NULL,'200710/16/ATT29555.html','200710/16/DOC40094.doc','Sanjeev kumar Sharma\nSanjeev kumar Sharma\n                                     \n\nSouth Ganesh\n Nagar, Delhi-92\nPhone:\n +91-09999891007 (M.)\n                                                           \nE-Mail: \nsascscscnjeev.shscscarma80@rediffmail.com\n\nsanjeesacscv.sscsacharma80@yahoo.com\n\nSeeking challenging assignments in the field of Software Programming with a technology oriented organization.\n\nAn Overview\n\n\nA self motivated candidate, possessing an MCA degree, with about \n2 year?s\n experience.\n1) NATIONAL INFORMATICS CENTRE, \nNew Delhi\n\nFrom \n\nth\n Jan 2007\n to Till)\nWorking for N.I.C. from 4\nth\n Jan-2007 as a Software Programmer on Project \n?Indian Customs EDI System (ICES)? as an employee of HCL InfoSystem.\n\n2) VRG ELCETRONICS PVT. LTD, New Delhi.\n(From \n\nst\n Jan 2005\n to \n29\nth\n\nDec 2006\n.)\n\n     \nCurrently associated with HCL InfoSystem. Noida as a Software Engineer.\n\n     \nSuccessfully carried out projects like \nDesigning Web Site for the Popcornfurniture\n\nWeb Site development for KDR Groups\n and \nDesign WAP site for downloading the games via micro browser of mobile phones\n to name a few.\n\n     \nA tech savvy individual, competent in a wide array of skills ranging across Unix, oracle, Java, JSP, Servlets, Tomcat Jakarta 5.0.19 etc.\n\n     \nAn energetic, self-motivated team member with hands on experience in programming skills, client-server infrastructure, requirements gathering and application customization.\n\n     \nA team player with strong interpersonal and communication skills, and capability to deliver to full potential even under high pressure situations.\n\nSkill Set\n\nTechnical \nOperating Systems\n                  \n\n           \nUNIX, Windows 98/NT/ 2000.\nLanguages\n                               \n\n          \nC, C++, JAVA.\nWeb Technologies\n                   \n\n           \nServlet 2.3, JSP 2.0\nDistributed Technologies \n        \n\n          \nBasic knowledge EJB 2.0s, RMI and Struts\nMarkup Languages\n                  \n\n          \nHTML, XML.\nApplication Server \n                   \n\n          \nBEA WebLogic Server 8.1.\nWeb Servers\n                            \n\n           \nTomcat \nJakarta\n 5.0.19, 5.5.\nRDBMS \n                                    \n\n          \nOracle 7.2/9i/10g\n\n\nFunctional \n\n       \nInteracting with the clients for system study, requirements gathering and analysis.\n\n       \nActively involved in designing & development & coding.\n\n       \nDesigning and developing the workflow diagrams. \n\n       \nManaging smooth implementation and testing of the application at client location\n\nProfessional Experience\nNATIONAL INFORMATICS CENTRE, \nNew Delhi\n\nIndia\n\n                   \n(Jan \n?07 ? Till)\n\nDatabase Administrator JAN 2007\n ? Till date\n\n\nEnvironment \nSolaris 5.6, Linux, Windows 2000, Oracle 7.2/9i/10g databases, Unix Shell \nScripts, Pro*C, Oracle Forms/Reports/Menu.\n\nProject \nIndian Customs EDI System (ICES)\n\nClient\n Indian Customs, Government of \nIndia\n\n\n\n\nResponsibilities \n\n         \nCreating and maintaining the database.\n\n         \nCreating database objects like tables, procedures, functions, triggers, indexes, views, constraints.\n\n         \nMonitoring alert log/system log.\n\n         \nPerformance tuning using Oracle diagnostics tools and Unix performance monitor tools.\n\n         \nImplement and maintain database security (create and maintain users and roles, assign privileges).\n\n         \nIdentify and resolve ORA errors, OS and database application issues.\n\n         \nPlan database space needs and growth analysis, and future disk need analysis by adding or resizing Datafiles in the Tablespace.\n\n         \nCreate and maintain Backup scripts.\n\n         \nCold and Hot backups of Production Databases.\n\n         \nRefreshing databases by import/export.\n\n         \nComposing and Maintaining shell scripts for the application.\n\n         \nAnalyze application related bugs, issues and implement application updates.\n\n\n\nVRG-Electronics Pvt. Ltd. \nNew Delhi\n\n                                               \n(Jan ?05- Dec ?06)\n\nAs Software Engineer\n\nKey Highlights:\n\n         \nDesigning and developing the company website and WAP site for micro browsers of cell phones.\n\n         \nContributing in providing e-commerce facilities to the company by utilizing MVC.\n\n         \nCarrying out procedures entailing Coding, Testing, Installation and integration of the different modules of static pages and dynamic pages on eApp server (A virtual Sever ?http://support.eapps.com?).\n\n\nProject Purview:\n\n\n    \nDeveloped Web Site for the Popcornfurniture\n\nClient\n                \n\n           \nPOPCORN Pvt. Ltd., \nwww.popcornfurniture.com\n\n\nDuration\n           \n\n           \nJan ?06- Dec ?06\nTeam Size\n         \n\n           \n\nEnvironment\n     \n\n           \nEclipse 3.1(MyEclipse Entrprise Workbench 4.0), XML, Oracle 8i, Tomcat \n                       \n            \nJakarta\n 5.0.19, Servlets, JSP, JDK 1.3.\n   \n\nSynopsis:\n\n          \nThe project is an online shopping portal operating with credit card interaction and is based on template coding.\n\n          \nThe presentation layer in the front end is coupled with the logical programming which facilitates easy integration of front end themes and fast and easy designing changes.\n\n          \nContributed in developing the ?searching module? (product search by word and price) and ?tell a friend? functionality module (by this customer can send mail to a friend of the particular product).\n\n          \nThe system developed makes provisions for placement of orders online and billing through credit card or cheque.\n\n\n    \nDeveloped Web Site for KDR Groups.\n\nClient\n               \n\n           \nKDR Groups Pvt. Ltd., \nwww.kdrgroups.com\nDuration\n           \n\n           \n5 months\nTeam Size\n        \n\n           \n\nEnvironment\n    \n\n           \nEclipse 3.1(MyEclipse Entrprise Workbench 4.0), XML, Oracle 8i, Tomcat \n                    \n            \nJakarta\n 5.0.19, Servlets, JSP, JDK 1.3.\n\nSynopsis:\n\n\n          \nThe site developed makes provisions for making offers for items in which they can negotiate details for as long as they need and will have the option to accept the trade. \n\n          \nThe system developed shows the trade in pending state if both the parties accept it and contact details will be shown to initiate correspondence.\n\n\n    \nDesign WAP site for downloading the games via micro browser of mobile phones.\n\nClient\n               \n\n           \nVRG-Electronics Pvt. Ltd., \nwww.vrgstudio.com\nDuration\n           \n\n           \n2 months\nTeam Size\n        \n\n           \n\nEnvironment\n    \n\n           \nEditPlus2, XML, WML, MySQL Server-4.1.8a, Servlets, JSP, JDK 1.\n\nSynopsis:\n\n         \nOn this site games can be directly down loaded via mobile?s micro browser from the WAP site of the company with the help of JSP and WML from http:// vrgstudio.com:8080/MOB_APP.\n\n         \nThe site also gives the option of uploading the games on it.\n\n         \nThe system is similar to mobile Portal service where a visitor log is being maintained in the database and logs for the game downloaded is also maintained with complete mobile headers. \n\n\n            \n\n\n\n\nInternships & Training\nXorient Technologies, \nNew Delhi\n\n                                                \n(Duration: 6 months)\n\nAs Trainee\n\n          \nTrained in software development which included procedures like Coding, Testing, Installation and integration of the different modules.\n\nEducation\n\n          \nM.C.A from \nRKGIT, \nGhaziabad\n under \nU.P.\nTechnical\nUniversity\n in 2005 from with 72%.\n\nPersonal Details\nDate of Birth\n                \n\n           \nNovember 14, 1980\nPermanent Address\n     \n\n           \nR-826, Adarsh Colony, \nPachenda Road\n, Muzaffar Nagar (U.P.)\nReferences\n                   \n\n           \nTo be produced on request\n           ',NULL,9,NULL,'2007-10-16',NULL,'2007-10-16','2010-06-09 12:13:49','2010-06-09',10,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,9,'0',NULL),(110,'Sarmista ',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Sscscscarmista09@rediffmail.com',NULL,NULL,'0','9886490757','0',NULL,'0','2007-10-29',10,NULL,'2010-06-09 12:13:49',10,'1','2010-06-21','200710/16/ATT29554.html','200710/16/DOC40095.doc','Sample Resume\n\n\n\n\nSARMISTA\n                                                                 \n     \nSscscscarmista09@rediffmail.com\n    \n                                \n                                                                              \n                 \nCONTACT:+91- 9886490757\n         \n                                                                             \n                  \nSummary\n2.5 yrs of exp in IT industry. Currently working with Accenture Services Pvt. Limited, \nBangalore\n as Software Engineer.\nHave experience in Oracle 9i (SQL, PL/SQL), Shell Scripting on Sun Solaris UNIX 5.8.0.\nProficient on UNIX Commands.\nGood understanding of Software Development Life Cycle and involved in understanding the functionality.\nCoordinating and interacting with team members and development team.\nExcellent Communicator with the ability to deal with issues with precision & accuracy.\nTechnical Expertise\nOperating System\nUnix (Sun Solaris 5.8.0), Windows XP/2000/NT\nLanguages\nC/C++, PL/SQL.\nTechnology\nUnix shell scripts,\nDatabases\nOracle 9i\nTools\nToad\nProfessional Experience\nAccenture Services\n\nPvt. Ltd.\n                                      \nSept 2005 ? Till date\nSoftware Engineer\nProject # 1\nProject Title\n              \n\nRisk Reporting Warehouse\n Managed Services\nClient\n\nUnion Bank of \nSwitzerland\n (Investment Bank).\nDuration\n                    \n\nAug?06 ? Till Date\nTechnologies\n\n9i, SQL, PL/SQL, UNIX, \nAUTO\n_SYS, Informatics, java\nTeam Size\n\n12\n\n\n\nProjects Scope\n   \nUBS and Accenture are working together to create a Managed Service for the Risk Reporting Warehouse (RRW).\n\nThe aim is to create responsive and reliable delivery of Maintenance and Innovation, as well as Level 3 Support for the existing platform.\n\nInvestigation and resolution of production issues that cannot be addressed by Level 1 and Level 2 Support team.\n    \nRole\nCreating Packages, B-tree index, Bitmap Index and using hints FULL, INDEX_JOIN.\nHandling Mutating Table Errors. (Create DML Triggers row level and statement level).\nOptimizing the SQL statements for better performance.\nInvolved in unit testing.\n\nProject # 2\nProject Title\n              \n\nOASIS\nClient\n\nUnion Bank of \nSwitzerland\n\nLondon\n\nUK\nDuration\n                    \n\nOct? 05 ? Jun? 06.\nTechnologies\n\nOracle 9i, SQL, PL/SQL, UNIX, C, C++\nTeam Size\n\n\n\nProject Scope\nThe purpose of this project is to define the role of pre production in managing the prep environment, source code management and automation of prep environment.. The main issues to be highlighted in managing prep environment are processes running in each system, Cron tab files and the processes kicked-off by cron(demon process), Log files and log information, managing command post messages, everyday and weekly systems check list, Debugging the problems, supporting to the development team.\nRole\n\n\n      \nClient requests come as emails, chats, or through phones.\nConstant monitoring of these channels and taking up requests and doing appropriate. Escalation based on criticality and feasibility.\n\n\n      \nMonitoring housekeeping jobs on weekends and making sure they are complete.\n\n\n\n\n\nDSRC Chennai,\n                               \n                             \nFeb 2005 ? Aug 2005\nSoftware Engineer\nProject # 3\nProject Title\n      \n        \n\nCLCP\nOrganization\n\nDSRC\nDuration\n                    \n\nFeb?05 ? Aug?05\n\nTechnologies\n\nOracle, UNIX, Shell Script, C, html\nTeam Size\n\n10\n\nProject Scope\n\nThis project compares the \"last\" and \"close\" prices of all the securities to make sure that the vendor properly process data overnight and makes correct last and close price available for next business day. If the close prices are not correct, applications that use change (= last - close)\n\nwill provide wrong change prices as well as all other calculations dependent on previous day?s close will be wrong. This project makes use of a script which runs at 7:30 AM EST and will report differences between previous day?s last and today?s last/close prices of the security. When there are mismatch securities more than 10 or when the Traded Volume of any of the mismatch securities is greater than a specific value a message is sent to the concerned teams (so as to alert the vendor and get the value corrected before start of Market hrs).It also maintains a record of last 8 weeks with the number of mismatch securities for each day and shown on the front-end using a browser.\nRole\nTeam member involved in analysis, requirements gathering, coding, testing.\n\nInvolved in writing stored procedures.\nWorked in 12 change requests and enhancement modules Privacy Act.\nEducation Qualification\n\n      \nB.E in Electrical & Electronics From NIST,\nBerhampur\nUniversity\n (2003)\n\n      \n+2 SC C.H.S.E Board \n\nfrom \nChrist\nCollege\nCuttack\n\n      \n10\nth\n I.C.S.E Board from \nSunabeda\nPublic School\n, Sunabeda.\n                                          \n      \n                                                                        \nSarmista\n                                                                        \nDate:\n                                             \n                           \nPlace:',NULL,9,NULL,'2007-10-16',NULL,'2007-10-16','2010-06-09 12:13:49','2010-06-09',10,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,9,'0',NULL),(111,'Saroj Kant Nayak',NULL,NULL,NULL,'skansscsctnayscak@gmail.com','skantnayak@gmail.com',NULL,'0','09868626052','0',NULL,'0','2007-04-30',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-09 12:13:49',10,'0',NULL,'200710/16/ATT29553.html','200710/16/DOC40096.doc','SAROJ KANT NAYAK\nSaroj kant Nayak\nmail:skansscsctnayscak@gmail.com\ncell@09868626052\n                               \n\nObjective\n\nTo be an invaluable IT resource for a well respected organization that will provide an atmosphere conductive to my professional and personal growth.\n\nMy technical expertise is in\n\n       \nORACLE 9i, 10g\n\n       \nDevelopment & Production Support using PL/SQL, Unix.\nEDUCATION (ACADEMIC & PROFESSIONAL)\n\n\n       \nMCA\nwith 76 % from \nUTKAL\nUniversity\n, Orissa.\n\nEmployment\n\nJuly 2005 ?\n\nTILL DATE \nOrganization \n\n- ERP Solution \nAsia\nLocation \n         \n- Noida\n            \nPosition \n          \n- Software Engineer\n\nSKILL PROFILE\n\nLanguages & Tools\n                          \n\n           \nPL/SQL, SQL, TOAD\nOperating Systems\n                           \n\n           \nUnix, Windows NT \nRDBMS\n                                              \n\n           \nOracle 9i/10g\nMAJOR PROJECT EXPERIENCE\n1. E-Topup(Mobile Recharging)\n     \n      \nE-Topup(mobile recharging) is a software is developed in a client server architecture. With its current installation sites at Vodafone Essar Teleservices New Delhi. Through this system customer recharge their prepaid mobile through retailor mobile or internet banking\n\nRole/Responsibility:\n\nMy sponsibility domain were monitoring daily NetBackup and full database export and managing customer queries and desolving in specific timeframe, Managing and scheduling cronjobs . Maintenance, analyzing and developing Pl/Sql procedures, functions and database triggers also performing daily, weakly, monthly database maintenance activities. Performing CPU performance, diskspace and background process also.\n\n\n\n\nSkills/Tools/Environment Used:\n\nHardware\n                     \nSunMicrosystem\nOperating System\n        \nSunSolaris UNIX, Windows XP\nLanguage\n                     \nOracle Sql, Pl/Sql\nDatabase\n                      \nOracle 10g\nClient\n\n                          \nVodafone Essar Teleserves\nPeriod\n\n                         \nSince March 2006\n\n          \n  \n2.\n\nSubscription Management System (SMIT), \nIndia\n Today\n       \nSubscription management system is software for India Today. Our project will deal with all the aspects of Subscriber Management starting from Subscriber enrolment, processing, delivery, tracking as well as complaint resolution. \nThe objective of this project is: -\n1)\n      \nTo process subscriber details starting from the entry of the subscriber?s particulars to auto generation of a unique subscriber?s number.\n2)\n      \nThe system will generate customized reports that will help Management take decisions regarding business promotional process improvement and product enhancements.\n3)\n      \nMaster Forms will be created which are generated predefined masters maintaining unique\n   \ndata to avoid redundancy.\n4)\n      \nThere will be a concept of POD (Proof of Delivery) according to which the subscriber on receiving the product will confirm so to the organization by signing a Proof of Delivery slip.\n5)\n      \nData security is maintained to relatively high level by implementing it at Database level, so as to ensure that only authorized users have access to confidential client information.\n\nRole/Responsibility:\nDeveloping data-entry forms for master tables. Writing PL/SQL code for triggers and stored procedures.\nSkills/Tools/Environment Used: \n\nOperating System\n       \nWindows NT\nLanguage\n                     \nOracle Sql, Pl/Sql,\nClient\n                           \n\nIndia\n Today\nPeriod\n                          \n\nJuly 2005-Feb 2006\nPosition\n\n                      \nOracle Developer\n\n            \n\n\n\n\n\nPERSONAL DETAILS\n\nNationality\n      \n: Indian\nDate of Birth \n\n: 10-04-1982\nFather?s Name \n            \n: Shri G S Nayak\nMarital Status\n\n: Unmarried\nLanguages\n        \n: Hindi, Oriya and English.\nEmailid\n           \n\nskantnayak@gmail.com\nMobile\n            \n: 09868626052\nLocation\n          \n\nNew Delhi\n\nSTRENGTHS\n\n\n       \nSincere, hard working, determined and quick learner.\n\n       \nBelieve in teamwork.\n\n       \nHighly motivated, proven results oriented achiever.\n\n\n\nI am very confident to undertake any kind of desirable responsibilities and assure successful completion of the same.\n      \n                                                                                    \n\n\n\n                                                                                                \nSaroj Kant Nayak',NULL,9,NULL,'2007-10-16',NULL,'2007-10-16','2010-06-09 12:13:49','2010-06-09',10,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,9,'0',NULL),(112,'Mehta sachin',NULL,NULL,NULL,'myhemscsdcsdcsdccdangi@rediffmail.com',NULL,NULL,'0','91 9987267316','0',NULL,'0','2005-04-29',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-09 12:13:49',10,'0',NULL,'200710/16/ATT29552.html','200710/16/DOC40097.doc','CV\n\n\nSUM\n\n\nMEHTA SACHIN RAJNIKANT\n\nE-mail: \nmyhemscsdcsdcsdccdangi@rediffmail.com\n                  \n          \n\n     \nCell: \n+ 91 9987267316\n\n\nCarrier Objective :\n\n\n          \nTo work in a competitive and challenging work environment which fully utilizes my interpersonal and academic skills and to contribute to the best of my abilities towards the growth and development of progressive company and to pursue a challenging and rewarding career.\n\n\nWork Experience: \n[59 Months]\n\n\n          \nCurrently working with \nZicom Electronic Security Systems Ltd\n., Andheri (E), Mumbai, as \nSr. Engineer ? Software Development\n (from April 11, 2005 till date) \n\n\n\n          \nHad worked with \nAnurag Electronics (\nGujarat\n) Pvt. Ltd\n., Andheri (E), as an EDP Supervisor - (Sep 24, 2004 to Apr 9, 2005)\n\n\n\n          \nHad worked with \nAtul Reprographics\n, Dadar (W), as a VB Programmer ? (Oct 1, 2002 to \nSep 23, 2004\n\n\n\nTechnical Skills:\n\nLanguages\nVisual Basic 6.0\n\nWeb Technologies\nHTML, CSS\n\nOperating System\nWindows XP/2000/2003/98\n\nDatabases\nSQL Server 2000, Oracle, MS Access 2000,Sybase\n\nEducational Qualification:\n\nDegree\nUniversity\nYear\nPercentage\nClass\nB.E. (Computers)\nLokmanya\nTilak\nCollege\n of Engg., Vashi, Navi Mumbai.\n2001\n52%\nSecond\nH.S.C.\nS.I.E.S.\nCollege\n, Sion, Mumbai.\n1996\n77.87%\nDistn.\nS.S.C.\nOur Lady of \nSalvation\nHigh School\n, Dadar, Mumbai.\n1994\n85.28%\nDistn.\n\nMAJOR PROJECTS UNDERTAKEN\n\n#1. ?DEMS\n\n\n\nClient:\nAtul Reprographics.\nProject name:\nData Entry Management System.\n     \nTeam Size:\n\n       \nDuration:\n2 Months\nTechnologies:\nVisual Basic 6.0, MS Word (Visual Basic Editor)\n\nDetails of the Project:\n\n\n          \n\nData Entry Management System contains ?\n                       \n1. \nText formatting\n         \n2. \nTable formatting\n                        \n3. \nImage formatting\n     \n4. Conversion of .doc to .pdf.\nRole\n\n\n\n       \nProject Requirement Specification and Analysis\n\n\n       \nPlanning and Risk Analysis\n\n       \nDevelopment and Coding\n\n       \nDocumentation\n\n       \nBug fixing\n\n       \nUnit & Integration testing\n\n\n\n#2. ?\nHCFA\n\n\n\nClient:\nAnurag Electronics (\nGujarat\n) Pvt. Ltd.\nProject name:\nHealth Insurance Claim Form Application\n     \nTeam Size:\n\n       \nDuration:\n3 Months\nTechnologies:\nVisual Basic 6.0, Oracle 8.0.\n\nDetails of the Project:\n\n          \nThis project was developed for entering data of various people who applied for Insurance claim.\n\n          \nThe basic idea behind this was to fill the details of the people in such a way that the soft copy looked exactly like the hard copy that is the Insurance Claim Form.\n\nRole\n\n\n\n       \nDevelopment and Coding\n\n       \nDocumentation\n\n       \nBug fixing\n\n       \nUnit & Integration testing\n\n\n\n#3. ?Universal 4.0? \n\n\nClient:\nZicom Electronics Systems Ltd.\nProject name:\nUniversal 4.3 Time and Attendance Software\n     \nTeam Size:\n\n       \nDuration:\n3 Months\nTechnologies:\nVisual Basic 6.0, MS Access 2000/SQL Server/Oracle\nDetails of the Project:\n\n\n          \nUniversal 4.0 System Contains \n1.\n      \nMaster setup\n2.\n      \nData Entry module\n3.\n      \nLeave module\n4.\n      \nShift Setup\n5.\n      \nReports module\nMaster module\n\nThe master module will consist of forms for\n\n          \nLocation setup\n\n          \nDepartment setup\n\n          \nGrade entry\n\n          \nEmployee Type details\n\n          \nTeam Name details\n\n          \nCompany setup\nThe Data Entry module consists of\n1.\n      \nMaster Data Entry\n2.\n      \nTour Data Entry\n3.\n      \nManual Data Entry\n4.\n      \nOutdoor Duty Entry\nThe Leave Module consists of\nA.\n      \nLeave codes setup\nB.\n      \nLeave configurations\nC.\n      \nLeave applications\nD.\n      \nCarry forward of leaves\nThe Shift Setup consists of \n1.\n      \nShift Creation\n2.\n      \nShift Pattern Creation\nThe Reports module consists of\na.\n      \nAttendance Report\nb.\n      \nIn/Out Report\nc.\n       \nMuster Report etc.\n\n\n\nPersonal Information:\n\nName:\nMehta Sachin Rajnikant\nD.O.B:\n27\nth\n February 1979\nAge:\n28 years\nGender:\nMale\nNationality:\nIndian\nReligion:\nHindu (Jain)\nMother Tongue:\nGujarati\nAddress:\n42, Ganesh Bhuvan, II Floor, Khed Gully, K.G. Road, Dadar (W), Mum-25\nResidence No:\n+91 22 2431 1668\nCell No:\n+91 \n99872 67316\nLanguages:\nGujarati, English, Hindi, Marathi\n\nCurrent CTC:\n                \nRs. 26,000/- p.m.\n\nCurrent Designation: \n\nSr. Engineer, Software Development.\n\nExpected CTC:\n\nRs. 35,000/- p.m. (negotiable)\n\nNotice Period: 1 month.\n\nReady for Relocation (Y/N): Y.\n\nDate: \n\n20/09/2007\nPlace: \n\nMumbai.\n                                                                                               \n(Mehta Sachin Rajnikant)',NULL,9,NULL,'2007-10-16',NULL,'2007-10-16','2010-06-09 12:13:49','2010-06-09',10,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,9,'0',NULL),(113,'V.A.Kishore   ',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Kishfbfbore.Agnihbfbotra@gmail.com',NULL,'98850 18487','0','9346327243','0',NULL,'0','2006-04-29',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-09 12:13:49',10,'0',NULL,'200710/16/ATT17835.html','200710/16/DOC40098.doc','CURRICULAM VITAE\n\nCURRICULAM VITAE\n\nS/o V.V.Narasimha Rao,\nPlot no: 321, V Phase, A2 Block\nJanapriya Apartments, Miyapur\nHYDERABAD\nPh: 9346327243;98850 18487\nKishfbfbore.Agnihbfbotra@gmail.com\n\n\nV.A.KISHORE\n          \n\n\n\n\n\n                                                            \n\n\nObjective:\n\nTo gain professional satisfaction by rendering my best skill & experience for the growth of your esteemed organization.\n\nEducational Qualification:\n\nPursuing M.Com. \nOsmania\nUniversity\n (Correspondence)\nB.Com.\nAndhra\nUniversity\n, Vizag (1998 ? 2001)\n\nTechnical Qualification:\n\nTally Graduate from Tally Software Solutions, \nBangalore\nPGDCA from BEST Computers, \nRajahmundry\nTypewriting Higher in English\nTypewriting Lower in Telugu\nTypewriting Lower in Hindi\n\nStrengths and Achievements:\nWell Versed in Tally, Wings, MS ? office.\nCapable to handle all sorts of accounts independently and affectively.\n\nth\n ranker in All India Tally Experts Examination held in 2002. (Tally 5.4 & 6.3).\nReceived 5 times Best Performance Incentive, while working in Siva Shakhi Bio Planttec Ltd., \nRajahmundry\n\nReceived twice the Good Achievement Cash Prize in Hutch\nExperience:\nHaving 4 years of experience in various areas of Accounting and Management Information System.\nSummary:\n(a)\n\nOrganisation\n\n\n           \nHutchison Essar South Ltd, \nHyderabad\n                         \nDesignation \n   \n            \n\n           \nExecutive-Payroll in Finance Department\nPeriod \n                        \n\n           \nSep?05 to till date\nProcessing of All AP Employees Monthly Salaries and as well as settlement of resigned employees within TAT\nAfter processing the payroll account the same in Oracle Finance\nPreparation of monthly Provisions like Leave encashment and Bonus etc.,\nGuide to employees about their tax planning\nTaking care about the remittance of all Statutory Payments\n        \nUpload the Payslips in URL on every monthly\nPreparation of monthly MIS like Head count Reconciliation,Gross Reco compare with earlier month\nProcessing of all employee Medical & LTA claims as per IT Act\nPreparation of Monthly Schedules of all Payroll related expenses and Liabilities.\n(b)\n\nOrganisation\n\n\n           \nSatyam Computer Services Ltd, \nHyderabad\n                         \nDesignation \n   \n            \n\n           \nOfficer ? Finance in Payroll Department\nPeriod \n                        \n\n           \nMay?04 to till date\n\n\n        \nMaintenance of Payroll Books\n\n        \nProcessing of \nUnited States\n and India Payrolls with using of available tool software (ADP etc,)\n\n        \nAfter Processing the Payroll taking care about the statutory works for payroll related (US, \nIndia\n\nSingapore\n\n\n        \nBased on Payroll reports accounting the same in Oracle Finance (OF)\n\n        \nPreparation of Monthly Schedules and taking care about the statutory returns (yearly and monthly)\n\n\n        \nOperating Tools\n            \n\n           \nADP, GPMS for Payroll Processing\n\n       \nOracle Finance for Accounting\n\n\n        \nAnd also attending the works like Inter Branch Reconciliation, Bank Reconciliation with US Banks, verification of Tax Proofs submitted by the employees in every F/Y and validates those proofs accordingly the Act.\n\n\n        \nAnd as well as developments to be incorporated with Quality work in Payroll processing and bill processing.\n\n\n        \nAnd every month calculation of PF for all employees\n\n\n\nSummary:\n\n(a)\n\nOrganisation\n\n\n           \nGordon Woodroffe Logistics Ltd, \nHyderabad\n                         \nDesignation \n   \n            \n\n           \nExecutive ?\n\nAccounts\nPeriod \n                        \n\n           \nDec?02 to May?04\n\nMaintenance of Books of Accounts.\nPreparation of MIS reports like Branch performance statement, Age wise Debtors statement, Projected collection and Funds requirement, Billing & collection statements periodically.\nPreparation of budgets like Sales, Expenditure and comparison of actuals with budgets periodically.\nMonitoring Bills raising to customers and Control of Expenditure.\nReconciliation of Debtors account periodically and interacting with customers to get it confirmation.\nPreparation of Finalisation Statements like Schedules of Accounts etc.,\nPreparation of Debtors above 60days & 180days with remarks\nReporting to GM ? Finance, corporate.\n\n(b)\n\nOrganisation\n               \n\n           \nSiva Shakthi Bio Planttec Ltd, \nHyderabad\nDesignation \n   \n            \n\n           \nBr.Executive ? Accounts, \nRajahmundry\n Branch.\nPeriod\n                         \n\n           \nJuly?01 to Nov?02\n\n\n        \nMaintenance of daily accounting transactions.\n\n        \nPreparation of monthly bank reconciliation statement (BRS).\n\n        \nPreparation of stock reconciliation statement.\n\n        \nMonthly salaries statement of branch.\n\n        \nInter branch reconciliation statement.\nReporting to Manager ? Finance, corporate.\n\nPersonal Details:\n            \nDate of Birth\n                                         \n\n                       \n26\nth\n October 1980\n\n            \nMarital Status\n                                       \n\n                       \nUn-Married.\n            \nSex\n                                                      \n\n                       \nMale.\n            \nLanguages Known\n                                \n\n                       \nTelugu, English, Hindi.\n            \nDate:\n                                                                                                            \nPlace:\n                                                                                                   \n        \n(V.A.Kishore)',NULL,9,NULL,'2007-10-16',NULL,'2007-10-16','2010-06-09 12:13:49','2010-06-09',10,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,9,'0',NULL),(114,'Tarun V',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL,'0',NULL,'0','2007-04-30',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-09 12:13:49',10,'0',NULL,'200710/16/ATT17832.html','200710/16/DOC40099.doc','Objective:\n\nTo combine my project management, planning and execution and oracle financials knowledge to deliver solutions that are efficient, intuitive and long ranging. Continuously improvise existing processes, to make them more effective and results oriented. Motivate people to bring the best out of them.\nProfessional Highlights:\n\n         \nWorked as Functional Lead on 3 \nfull life cycle oracle Financials implementation projects\n and leaded those from concept to delivery.\n\n         \nWorked on 2 oracle financials Support projects. \n\n         \nHave expertise in project management, planning, design, development, QA and support initiatives\n\n         \n8 years experience\n\nimplementing ERP application software?s in Manufacturing, Financial, Service organizations.\n\n         \nAround 4 years in Oracle Financials.\n\n         \nHave good understanding of\n\nOracle?s AIM Methodology.\n\n         \nDemonstrated professionalism as a project Leader, team leader and team member, while continually striving to meet project needs with user requirements\n\n         \nProven ability to communicate with client\n, leading the team, estimate, design and implement projects\n\n         \nLead onsite & offshore teams\n in a matrix environment\n\n         \nWorked on various process definition, standardization and process improvement projects\n that involved defining coding standards, change request management, configuration management, release management\n\n         \nEvaluated different vendors, tools available in the market and managed vendor relationships\n\n         \nExtensive experience as \nsolution provider to the clients\n\n         \nHas worked on various Financials modules of oracle apps11i suit including Oracle General Ledger, Oracle Payables, Oracle Receivables, Oracle Fixed assets, Oracle purchasing.\n\n         \nExposure to other ERP applications\n namely Ebizframe6i enables me to think out of the box when implementing business software?s & \nevaluate solutions from Optimization perspective\n\n         \nTeam player with ability to lead by example and motivate to achieve desired objectives\n\n         \nHighly intuitive, goal-oriented, analytical and go-getter\n with a positive attitude; Always looks for process improvement opportunities and opportunities to add value\n\n         \nGreat listener, assertive but strongly believe in participative management style\n\nEducation: \n\n\n         \nPursuing \nMBA- Finance\n from University of Pondicherry\n\n         \nMaster of Human resource management (MBA- HR)\n from University of Pondicherry ? \n\nyear 2000-2002\n\n         \nBachelor of Commerce\n from University of Agra - \nyear 1995-1998\n\n         \nMasters Diploma in Aptech Computer Education (Duration 3 years) ? year 1994-1998\n\n         \nOracle Applications 11i Training\nfrom \ncomp-u-learn. ? \nYear 2004\n\n         \nMicrosoft Certifications (MCP, MCSD and cleared 4 Windows 4.0 NT Admin exams (core papers of MCSE Curriculum) ? year 1999\nAffiliation: \n\n         \nMember of All India Management Association\nImmigration / Passport Status:\n\nValid Indian Passport is available without any visa.\nLocation Preference:\n\nLimited to opportunities in Gurgaon India, or oversees projects\nAvailability to Join: \nupon 3 month notice.\n\nKey Skills & Knowledge\n\n\n\nBusiness Applications\nOracle Apps 11.5.9, 11.5.8, 11.5.6, 11.5.5, 11.5.3, 10.7 NCA, 10.7 SC\n\nOracle Apps 10.6 CUI\nEbizframe 6i\n\n\n\nOracle Apps Modules\nOracle General ledger, Oracle Payables, Oracle Receivables, Oracle Fixed Assets, Oracle Cash management, Oracle Purchasing\n\n\n\n\nSoftware\nOracle 7.x, 8.x, 9.x, 10g\nOracle Configurator\nOracle Workflow Developer\nOracle Trace, TKPROF\nSQL, PL/SQL, SQL Loader\nDeveloper 2000, 6i, 9i\nC, Unix Shell scripts\n\n\n\n\nPackages\nMicrosoft Project 2000\nProject Tracker\nMicrosoft Office XP\nVisio2000, SQL Navigator\nPVCS, VSS, DBA Studio, Oracle Enterprise Manager\n\n\n\n\nOperating Systems\nWindows XP/ 2000/NT\nLinux/HP-UNIX, Sun Solaris\n\n\n\n\nHardware\nLinux RAC front to back\nIntel *86 m/c?s, Dec Alpha, \nSun Sparc, HP 9000, HCL Magnum\nBusiness & Application Experience\n\nEmployer\n\nSyntel Inc, Mumbai, India\n               \n                                \n                \n12/2006 ? Present\n\nSyntel Inc is a US based SEI CMMi Level5 company present revenue around 300 Million US dollars and I Joined here Senior Project leader and my role in my current project is of senior functional consultant or senior business analyst.\n\nEngagement\n\n\nOracle Financials Implementation at American Express, I am working on this project as senior project lead / senior functional consultant, I am responsible for requirement gathering and analysis, future process designing, helping functional & technical team and testing manger as subject matter expert.\n\nTask and Responsibilities \n\n\n         \nProviding guidance and leadership to team \n\non the functional aspects of the implementations as appropriate\n\n         \nIdentify inbound and outbound feeds related to point of departure (Legacy general ledger) systems.\n\n         \nReviewing High-level documents\nand ensuring it fits the overall architectural plan for build phase.\n\n         \nGuiding functional and technical consultant in preparing design documents\n the inbound and outbound interface requirements\n\n         \nMilestone \nreview and getting deliverables signed offs\n\n         \nParticipation in Change Control Meetings\n\n         \nHelping testing team manager in preparing Testing Strategy and Requirements\n\n         \nCoordinate with testing team manger in making the testing team understand the business process and development requirements\n\n         \nConduct workshops with the client to \nsetting up expectation\n\n         \nConduct \nmeeting\n\nwith the key stake holders for planning the rollout\n\n         \nMeet with Technical leads and development teams at Mumbai / Chennai to \nassure alignment and timely delivery\n\n\n         \nPublishing meeting minutes, issue log and weekly status report.\n\n         \nConsolidate and publish issue list from all tracks on a weekly basis. \nDrive issues to resolution\n\n\n         \nEscalate scope change requests to program management\n\n         \ncoordination with other departments\nlike quality assurance, support and systems departments to \nforecast resource demands\n and work with them when issues arise, so solutions can be worked out as a team. \n\n         \nEnsure fresh hands comply with other proper On-boarding training formalities \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nEmployer: Polaris Software Labs Ltd.\n                             \n                                \n1/2004 ? 12/2006 \n\nPolaris Software Labs Ltd. a SEI CMMi level5 company is very well known in India and across the globe for its Banking Software Solutions and ERP Consultancy present revenue around 300 Million US dollars I worked here for around 3 years in capacity of Oracle Financials Consultant and Executed 2 End to End ERP implementations and worked on 2 support projects. \n\nEngagement\n\n\nOracle Financials11i Implementation at GE Industrial India Pvt. Ltd.\nFull Life Cycle Ownership/Execution Responsibility for Oracle General Ledger, Oracle Receivables, Oracle Payables implementation.\nAs a Functional Lead\n, I was responsible for \nPlanning, Leadership, Coordination, Analyzing requirements, Preparing Specs, managing client relationship and Development. \n\n\n        \nTask and Responsibilities\n\n         \nEnsuring seamless transition from Legacy System to Oracle ERPs 11i. \n\n         \nPreparing Requirement gathering and analysis, conversion strategy, Functional \nSpecifications and setup documents as per AIM methodology\n\n         \nCreation of new responsibilities, request groups.\n\n         \nSetting up new Organizations.\n\n         \nSetting up new COA and Calendar and SOBs for US and India GAAP\n\n         \nPrepared other required setups for Oracle AP, AR and GL.\n\n         \nLooking after SITs and UAT.\n\nEngagement\n\n\nOracle Fixed Assets Implementation at GE Iprocess Pvt. Ltd., Full Life Cycle Ownership/Execution Responsibility for Oracle General Ledger, Oracle Receivables, Oracle Payables implementation.\nAs a Functional consultant, I was responsible for \nAnalyzing Requirements, Preparing Specs, and setting up Oracle Fixed Assets. \n        \n        \nTask and Responsibilities\n\n\n         \nPreparing Requirement gathering and analysis, conversion strategy, Functional \nSpecifications and Setup documents as per AIM methodology\n\n         \nCreation of new responsibilities, request groups.\n\n         \nSetting up fixed assets application to fulfill US and IND GAAP requirements\n\n         \nLooking after SITs and UAT.\n\n\n        \nEngagement\n\n\nOracle Financials11i support and quarterly release testing project for GE Energy Parts, ownership and Responsibility of\n\nall major Oracle Financials modules like Oracle General Ledger, Oracle Receivables, Oracle Payables.\n\nLead the Finance production support team to deliver the solutions as per SLAs. Understand all business processes and provide functional leadership to the team\n\n\n        \nTask and Responsibilities\n\n\n         \nManage the day to day execution of issue resolution and enhancements\n\n         \nResponsible for the 24 x 7 production support for Finance users located in various GEPS geographical \nlocation and time Zones\n\n         \nCoordinate with Finance leaders and understand the various changing business needs and align the \nteam to meet the requirements\n\n         \nUnderstand various interfaces to the Oracle system and coordinate with relevant teams and ensure \nsmooth production support\n\n         \nManage knowledge transfer between various teams \n\n         \nEnergize and motivate the contractor team to deliver their best\n\n         \nMaintain various performance matrices and monitor the support team performance\n\n         \nUnderstand and ensure the adherence to all the laid out production support and related policies\n\n\n         \nIdentify opportunities for improvement and drive improvement through 6 sigma rigor\n\n         \nHandling Oracle Payables Super user Responsibilities \n\n      \nPerforms Rifle shot and complete modular testing for Oracle Payables quarterly releases.\n\n      \nPerforming Inter company Settlement for Hungary and Atlanta sites. \n\n      \nCreation of payment batches for different pay groups. \n\n      \nProviding solutions to client on functional problems related to Oracle payables.\n\n\n        \nEngagement\n\n\nOracle Financials11i support project for GE Advance materials,\n Lead the Finance production support team to deliver the solutions as per SLAs. Understand all business processes.\n\n        \nTask and Responsibilities\n\n\n         \nInteracting with users for business requirement analysis, design and enhancement of reports after migration.\n\n         \nManaging deliverables on time\n\n         \nMigration/Customization of reports using Oracle Reports 3.0\n\n         \nRe-Registration of Concurrent programs using AOL.\n\n         \nPerformance Tuning of the Reports and other batch programs.\n\n         \nWrote technical Specifications based on given Functional Documents.\n\n         \nWrote SQL Script to create a data file for Data Extraction.\n\n         \nOngoing Production supports to Oracle Users.\n\n         \nCreating the Responsibilities, Data Group, Request Group and Users.\n\n         \nCreation of values sets in various modules of the application.\n\n         \nDefining Concurrent Programs, Executables.\n\n         \nGenerated Financial Statements using Financial Statement Generator.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nEmployer: \nEastern Software Systems Ltd. \n\nSEI CMM ? 5 company\n             \n                                \n1/2003 ? 1/2004\n\nEastern Software Systems Ltd. a SEI CMM level5 company is First Indian Company with self made Web based ERP Software named Ebizframe6i. I worked here for around 1 years in capacity of Software Engineer and Executed 3 End to End ERP implementations at prestigious Indian Clients. \n\nEngagement\n\n\nImplementation of ebizframe6i\n suite at \nP.A. Time Industries Ltd.(Maxima Watches)\n, Dharampur H.P., India,\n\nLead the \n\nteam to deliver the solutions as per Project plan. Understand all business processes and provide functional leadership to the team\n\n        \n        \nTask and Responsibilities\n\n\n      \nInstallation of Oracle8i and \nOracle 9iAS 10222 and Ebizfram6i ERP.\n\n      \nStudying the old system with a view to find out the Gaps\n\n      \nThe project mainly involved implementation of implementation of Manufacturing module(Production and production planning) of Ebizfram6i ERP and support of other core modules including Financials, HRPAY, Inventory, sales and purchase.\n\n\n\n      \n\nPrimary responsibility was to collect and analyze user?s requirements and customization of manufacturing module accordingly.\n\n      \nPreparing Data flow diagram, Flow chart and Entity Relationship diagram to ensure the system reliability and robustness.\n\n      \nDeveloped various SQL loader scripts to transfer data from legacy system to Ebizframe6i Production module, Programs include transferring WIP and finished goods details into production module. \n\n      \nDeveloped various new forms and reports as per user requirements.\n\n      \nInvolved in preparing SOPs and user training. \n\n      \nAlso supported Financials, HRPAY, Sales, Purchase and done various enhancements as required\n\nEngagement\n\n\nImplementation of ebizframe6i suite at \nP.A. Time Industries Ltd.(Maxima Watches), Dharampur H.P., India,\n\nLead the \n\nteam to deliver the solutions as per Project plan. Understand all business processes and provide functional leadership to the team\n\n        \nTask and Responsibilities\n\n\n      \nInstallation of Oracle8i and \nOracle 9iAS 10222 and Ebizfram6i ERP.\n\n      \nStudying the old system and designing systems and procedures for new sytem.\n\n      \nThe project mainly involved implementation of implementation of Inventory and Export module\n   \nof Ebizfram6i ERP and support of\n   \nEbizfram6i Financials and HRPAY module.\n\n      \n\nPrimary responsibility was to collect and analyze user?s requirements and development of Export module from the scratch and customization of Inventory module accordingly.\n\n      \nPreparing Data flow diagram, Flow chart and Entity Relationship diagram to ensure the system reliability and robustness.\n\n      \nDeveloped various new forms and reports as per user requirements.\n\n      \nInvolved in preparing SOPs and user training. \n\n      \nAlso supported Financials, HRPAY modules.\n\nEngagement\n\n\nImplementation of ebizframe6i suite at \n\nesmen Ipsen Furnaces Pvt. Ltd.,\n kolkata, India,\nLead the team to deliver the solutions as per Project plan. Understand all business processes and provide functional leadership to the team\n\n\n         \nUnderstand the architecture, security and coding standards of Wesmen.\n\n         \n\nReview technical design documents for the components identified during the planning phase\n\n         \n\nPrepare Application extension strategy\n\n         \nPrepare data-conversion documents and interact with technical lead / client for approval\n\n         \nCreation of technical documents and Coding for interfaces, data-conversions etc\n\n      \nInstallation of Oracle8i and \nOracle 9iAS 10222 and Ebizfram6i ERP.\n\n      \nDeveloped various new forms and reports as per user requirements.\n\n      \nPerform Unit testing, SIT and UAT. \n\n\nEmployer: \nSavvy Information management System(SIMS) Pvt. Ltd. \n           \n                                \n10/1999 ? 1/2003\n\nI started my career with SIMS as Software Engineer and subsequently leaded flagship School management systems software package development apart from School management systems I Have worked on various MIS software solution development.projects. \n\nEngagement\n\n\nDevelopment of School management systems software, Lead the team to deliver the solutions as per Project plan. Understand all business processes and provide leadership to the team.\n\n        \nTask and Responsibilities\n\n\n      \nI was a part of team responsible for designing the \nsystems & procedures from scratch and lead the \n      \nSame team at later stage\n\n      \nDeveloped comprehensive MIS application for schools the product contains This product contains various modules like accounting, payroll, purchase and admission procedure and examinations etc.\n\n\n      \nPreparing Data flow diagram, Flow chart and Entity Relationship diagram to ensure the system reliability and robustness.\n\n      \nDesigning and developing forms and reports, writing PL/SQL Packages, procedures and database triggers and performed modular testing.\n\nEngagement\n\n\nDevelopment of \nIntegrated office management and Information system (IOMIS)\n\nIOMIS has designed and developed on the lines of ERP to facilitate in different operations for the area distributor of camphor allied limited. \n\nI worked in team as oracle developer and ensured deliveries inline with Project plan. Following are the modules specific responsibilities \n\n      \nFinancial Accounting System\n\nIt includes all types of ledgers like General ledger, sub ledger, voucher generation, books like Cash book, Bank book, Sales book, purchase book, Trial balances, Balance sheet Profit & loss A/c, Schedules Reconciliation of Bank entries against Bank statements, interest calculation, control of bank limits etc.\nPass the supplier bills against various purchases, making payment and keeps the track of payment on due date, Printing cheque etc.\nPass the supplier bills against Import purchase, it is linked with the consignments monitoring system, by which we keeps a track of various documents like Commercial invoice, bill of entry, CHA bill, freight bill and making payments against these bills.\nGenerating different kind of work orders for job processing release by the company for contractors and making payment against those.\nCalculate the inventory value at the end of each month by using weighted average rate technique.\nL.C.\'s generated for various Import purchase & sales & Overhead budget monitoring.\nCheck the expense against budgeted expenses assigned to each Cost-Centre monthly/ annually\n\n\nSales and Marketing System\n\nCustomer Registration and Order Entry\nSales Invoice generation, Invoice Printing and Sales Voucher Posting into financial system\nDebit/Credit Advice preparation and Debit/Credit Note generation\nSales Analysis Report, Daily Stock position Report, Customer Outstanding Report\nMaintain different Excise registers i.e. RG23 Part1, Part 2 RG23 C Etc.\n\n         \nInvolved in Development of Forms and reports using forms4.5/Reports2.5 for Financial Accounting module.\n\n         \nInvolved in Creation of Stored Procedures, Database Triggers, Sequences, Indexes, Views, Temporary Tables.\n\n         \nCustomizing forms and reports according to client\'s need\n\n         \nWrote SQL Script to create a data file for Data Extraction\n\n         \nLoading of Data through SQL Loader. Backups through Export Utility\n\nEngagement\n\n\nDevelopment of Export Management systems \nto facilitate in export documentation for the Export oriented industries. \n\nI worked in team as oracle developer and ensured deliveries inline with Project plan. \n\nTask and Responsibilities\n\n\n      \nIt was generic software for Brass Exporters. This package had developed to cater all requirements related to Brass Export. It also kept insurance related information.\n\n      \nDevelopment of export system, which starts with sales order, Performa invoice, insurance detail, goods dispatch till final commercial invoice. \n\n      \nDesigning and developing forms and reports, writing PL/SQL Packages, procedures and database triggers and performed modular testing.\nADDITIONAL INFORMATION:\n\nDate of Birth\n                        \n\n               \n14\nth\n July 1977\nFather?s Name\n                     \n\n               \nLate M.K. Vashistha\nSex\n                                         \n\n               \nMale\nMarital Status\n                      \n\n               \nMarried\nPassport No. \n                        \n\n               \nE2879083.\n\n\nCurrent Place \n                     \n\n\n\n\nDate\n                                       \n\n                                               \n                                                                                                                                                \nTarun Kr. Vashistha',NULL,9,NULL,'2007-10-16',NULL,'2007-10-16','2010-06-09 12:13:49','2010-06-09',10,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,9,'0',NULL),(115,'Siddalingesh K',NULL,NULL,'Secunderabad','hisdviddvvdu@yahoo.co.in','siddvdudv.kadvdvmatagi@gmail.com',NULL,'0','91 9849667452','0',NULL,'0','2007-06-14',10,34,'2010-06-09 12:13:49',10,'0',NULL,'200710/16/ATT17831.html','200710/16/DOC40100.doc','Namdev B Jagtap (ID# 25841)\n\nSiddalingesh K \nProfessional Summary\nHaving \nTwenty four months experience\n in information technology areas involving \nOracle Apps Database Administration and Oracle 9i Administration.\n I have good experience in \ninstallation and Administration of Oracle Apps on Solaris and HP - UNIX\n, database maintenance, backup & recovery of Oracle database. I also worked in \nC, C++ \nlanguages and well versed with RDBMS like \nOracle\n and \nFront End GUI tool Developer2000.\n\nAs an Oracle DBA, I was involved in installation, configuration and administration of various Oracle Products like Oracle 11i, Oracle Database Server 8.x/9i on window/Solaris/Linux platforms. I have experience in System Administration, Databases Creation, Database Configuration, Space management, User management, Backup and Recovery and Database Maintenance. \n\nEducation\n\nDegree\nUniversity\nYear of Passing\nB.E. (Information Science and Engineering) \nVisveswaraiah\nTechnical\n\nUniversity\n (Karnataka) \nJuly 2004\nExperience\n\nOrganization\nDesignation\nDuration \nSatyam Computer Services Ltd.\nSoftware Engineer\n27/12/04 - till date\n\nTechnical Skills\n\n\nOperating Systems\nSun Solaris9, Windows95/98/2000/XP, MS-DOS,HP-UX\nLanguages\nC, C++, SQL, PL/SQL, Shell Scripting\nDatabases\nOracle Apps 11i, Oracle 8i/9i\nGUI\nD2K( Forms 6.0, Reports 5.0)\nTools & Utilities\nExp, Imp, Tkprof,\n\nSQL * loader, Toad, \nDBA\nOracle Application 11i\n\n\n\n\nTrainings\n\n\n\nProjects Profile\n\n1. \nProject Name: DBA SUPPORT\nClient\nSatyam\nRole\nDatabase administrator and System administrator\nOrganization\nSatyam Computer Services Ltd.\nDuration\n27/01/05 ?\n\n25/09/05 \nEnvironment\nOracle apps 11i with oracle 9i DB ,HP-UX servers.\n\n\nProject Description \n\nSatyam has a DBA Support Help desk for all internal Development projects. The support Help desk gives 16 X 5 DBA support like installations, space management, schema management, security, performance and backup, to all internal projects in Satyam.\n\nContribution\n\n\n\n        \nApplying various patches.\n\n        \nInstallation of APPS financial module on Sun Solaris 5.8.\n\n        \nDeploying Data guard configuration on oracle 8i\n\n        \nResolution of various online issues.\n\n        \nComplete Database and system administration support.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n2.\nProject ? EAST - GE Power Systems, \nAtlanta\n\nUSA\n\nClient\nGE \nRole\nOracle Application 11i System Administrator\nOrganization\nSatyam Computer Services Ltd.\nDuration\n01/10/05 ?\n\ntill date \nEnvironment\nOracle Apps 11i with oracle 9i DB ,HP-UX servers.\n\n\n\nProject Description \n\nTeam Size - 85, Module Size - 9\nGE Energy, a leading unit with in GE \nUSA\n. The Project includes analysis of the specifications provided by the clients, troubleshooting and configuring the Oracle Applications.\nThe project involves Troubleshooting, Supporting, and implementation of the all the Oracle Applications modules in more than 7 GE Energy Business Environment. Working with various teams and the functional users as a System Administrator for the various modules like Oracle GL, AP, AR, Supply Chain Mngt., CRM, Global HR etc. and various Business environments like Wind Energy, Aero/Hydro, CPG, CMF, FRMT, NRPS etc.\n\nContribution\n\nWorked at Client side and Offshore as a \nSystem Administrator (\nOracle ERP Sys Admin Consultant\n\n, and is responsible for \n\n        \nCustomization of Oracle Applications and Providing System Administrator Support.\n\n        \nPreparing SQL Queries to for various reports.\n\n        \nInteracting with the Client, Analyzing the Case/Issues and Providing the Resolution within the Time Frame. \n\n        \nWorked with Oracle TAR when required. Performing User Training\n\n        \nConfiguring System (Oracle Application Manager, Workflow, Notification Mailer etc.)\n\n        \nParticipating in Business Critical, Serv. 1 TAR, Change Control Board, etc. Meeting.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nPersonal Details\n\nName\nSiddalingesh Kamatagi \nEmail Id \nhisdviddvvdu@yahoo.co.in\n ; siddvdudv.kadvdvmatagi@gmail.com\nPresent Address\nFlat no 310, \nAlliance\n homes,\nS. D. Road\n , Secunderabad\nPin 500 003\nContact Numbers\n\nMobile\n: +91- 9849667452','Satyam Computer Services Ltd',9,NULL,'2007-10-16',NULL,'2007-10-16','2010-06-09 12:13:49','2010-06-09',10,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,9,'0',NULL),(116,'Siva K',NULL,NULL,'Hyderabad  ','Sivadvdkrisdvsdhna_ndvsk@yahoo.co.in',NULL,NULL,'0','9885800379','0',NULL,'0','2008-01-12',10,35,'2010-06-09 12:13:49',10,'0',NULL,'200710/16/ATT17829.html','200710/16/DOC40101.doc','          \n                                              \n             \n             \nSiva K\nCell ? (+\n91\n) - \n9885800379\n                         \n            \nSivadvdkrisdvsdhna_ndvsk@yahoo.co.in\n                             \nMadhapur, Hi-tech city, \nHyderabad\n          \n\n\n\nExperience Summary\nAbout 2 years \n(26 months) of diverse experience in Information Technology with focus on \nTechnologies \nlike \nUnix\n Shell Scripting, SQL/PL-SQL, ORACLE.\n\n         \nExpertise in \nTelecom\n\nDomain \nespecially\n\nin\n Order Management. \n\n         \nWell-organized, creative, self-motivated, result oriented, and a \nTeam Player\n with proven ability to complete given tasks on time.\n\nAchievement / Rewards\n\n         \nCertified as \nOracle Certified Associate\n as PL/SQL developer.\n\n\nTrainings / Memberships\n\n\n         \nMember of ISI (Instrument Society of \nIndia\n) since Aug-2002\n\n         \nDone\nIn\n-Plant training at Nuclear Fuel Complex (NFC). \nHyderabad\n\nWorking Experience \n\n\n         \nWorking as \nAssistant System Engineer\n in \nTata Consultancy Services-\nHyderabad\n\nIndia\n\nfrom \nJuly 2005 to till now.\n\nEducational Qualification \n\nB.Tech\n from \nVellore\n Institute of Technology-\nVellore\n\nTamilnadu\n\nin\n 2005 \nwith 85%.\nPlus 2 Exam \nfrom A.P. Board, \nNellore\n,A.P\n. in 2001 \nwith 89.4%\nSSC Exam \nfrom A.P. Board , Board, \nNellore\n,A.P\n. in 1999 \nwith 80.2%\n\n\nTechnical Skills\n\n1.\nOperating System\n\nUNIX, DOS, WINDOWS-XP, 9X\n2.\nDatabase\nOracle 9i\n3.\nScripting\nUnix Shell Script,PL/SQL, SQL\n4.\nOthers\nOracle forms, Reports, C, C++, Core JAVA, JSP, SAP BW\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n                    \n                                 \nPROJECT DESCRIPTION\n\n1.\n     \nPoint of Sell (TATA Consultancy Services)\n\n\nClient\nTATA Tele-Services Ltd.\nTitle\nPoint of Sell\nPeriod\nOctober 2005 to till now\nPosition\nTeam Member\nThe Project\nTata Tele Services Limited offers telecom services in \nIndia\n. POS is a module of TTSL. POS is that system through which \ncustomers\n information enters into the system. POS is developed by TCS itself for fulfill Business requirement. After entry in POS, information flows to different systems \nlike\n\nMetasolv\n, Billing, CRM, SAS.\nResponsibilities\n\n         \nResolving customers problems and providing best solution to them.\n\n         \nWriting stored procedures and triiggers.\n\n         \nScheduling of scripts in crontab.\n\n         \nTunning the procedures for better performance.\n\n         \nFixing for bugs\n\nand resolving Discrepencies between different systems like Metasolv,Package and Billing team.\n\n         \nTo give training to new members.\n\n\nOperating Systems\nUNIX, Windows XP\nSoftware used\nOracle,PL/SQL ,Oracle Forms(D2K)\nDatabase\nOracle 9i\nTools\nToad 7.4.03\nWork Location\nHyderabad\n\nIndia\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nProject Thesis \n                \nAs part of University project\n       \n\n                    \n\nProject Title\nDesign of MEMS based Glucose sensor using \nIntellisuite\n and \nCoventorware\n software?s\nDescription\nIt deals with finding the amount of glucose concentration present in the blood. The design includes the micro needled structure, which is the best-suited structure for finding the amount of glucose concentration. The project also involves the withstanding capability of the micro needled structure.\nRole\nTeam member (team consists of 3 members)\nResponsibilities\nLiterature survey, designing the structure, testing the structure for various pressures and simulation.\n\n\n\nPersonal Details\n\nDate of Birth\n09-06-1985\nGender\nMale\nMarital Status\nSingle\nNationality\nIndian\n\n\n\nPassport Details\n\nName as on passport\nRelationship\nPassport Number\nDate of Issue\nExpiry Date\nPlace of Issue\nSivakrishna\n\nNandimandalam\nMyself\nB5512707\n25-Jun-2001\n24-Jun-2011\nHyderabad\n (AP)','Consultancy Services',9,NULL,'2007-10-16',NULL,'2007-10-16','2010-06-09 12:13:49','2010-06-09',10,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,9,'0',NULL),(117,'Sudhanshu Bajpai',NULL,NULL,'New Delhi ','sudvdvdhavdsvnshu2006@rediffmail.com',NULL,'09936055312','0','09910343264','0','09334701960','0','2007-05-15',7,19,'2010-06-09 12:13:49',10,'0',NULL,'200710/16/ATT17826.html','200710/16/DOC40102.doc','                                                                                                                                                                                    \n                                                                                    \n                                                                                \nSUDHAN BAJPAI\nH No wz -27C? Vishnu Garden Park-1? \nNew Delhi?\n 110018 \nPhone:\n (M) 09910343264 (R) 09936055312\nE-mail:\n sudvdvdhavdsvnshu2006@rediffmail.com\n\nCareer Objective\n\nSeeking position that would utilize my current skills and challenge my various abilities in Database Administration and various field of Computer Application. Looking for an organization that offers career growth and chance to achieve goals through persistence and hard work.\n\nPROFESSIONAL ACHIVEMENT\n\n\n         \n2.9 years experience in Oracle technology\n\n         \nSound understanding of Oracle database architecture, configuration and administration.\n\n         \nSound knowledge of Backup & Recovery\n\n         \nProficient in backup and recovery with RMAN\n\n         \nGood exposure to Data Guard and Export / Import\n\n          \nGood written and client interaction skills at all management level. Energetic initiator and can learn new technology in short time with proficiency and hardworking in any circumstances\n\n\n\n                                                           \nProfessional Experience\n\n\n         \nWorking for \nJAGRAN PRAKASHAN LIMITED\n, from 1\nst\n Dec -2004 to 30-Apr-2007 as an Oracle Technical.\n\n         \nPresently working as \nSenior Engineer with \n\nIMACHAL \n\nUTURISTIC \n\nOMMUNICATIONS \n\nTD\n   \nposted at \nNew Delhi\n from May-07\n\n\n                                                   \nCURRENT RESPONSIBILITES AND\n\nSKILLS (ORACLE 9I)\n\n\n\nPresently working as \nSenior Engineer with \n\nIMACHAL \n\nUTURISTIC \n\nOMMUNICATIONS \n\nTD\n   \nposted at \nNew Delhi\n. Responsible for maintain the database of MTNL New Delhi & MTNL Mumbai for Sun Solaris OS . \nJob responsibility includes Customer Support & Services, Installation, Maintenance Following is my major responsibility of Oracle 9i Database.\n\n\nInstallation,\n      \nUpgradation, \nMaintenance of Oracle database.\n\nSpace Management (management of tablespaces and datafiles).\n\nManaging backup strategies like cold, hot and logical Proficient in RMAN.\nMaking various customized \nSQL and Discoverer reports\n according to the client?s requirement.\nPrepared all MIS Reports.\nMaintenance of company database.\n\nResponsibilities \n\n\n         \nDesigning & building databases to store information and monitoring performance of the database.\n\n         \nPlanning the capacity of the database and fixing database problems like software failures.\n\n         \nManaging security of the data and ensuring accuracy of the data.\n\n         \nSetting up static and dynamic parameters.\n\n         \nResponsible for planning and performing routine backup and recovery of the databases. \n\n         \nBackup administration of EBS, TAR & ufsdump Backup\n\n         \nFile System administration\n\n\n         \nAllocate system storage and plan for future storage requirements for the database system \n\n         \nInstall the database server and application tools \n\n         \nPlan for backup, recovery of database; back up and restore the database \n\n         \nControl and monitor user access to database; monitor and optimize the performance of database \n\n         \nAllocate system storage and plan for future storage requirements for the database system \n\n         \nCreate primary database storage structures and primary objects \n\n         \nEnroll users and maintain system security, ensuring compliance with database license agreements \n\n         \nDevelop and maintain database standards and conventions; analyze impact of data change \n\n            \nTECHNICAL SKILLS\n\n\nOperating System\n                        \n: Windows 98/ XP\nPackages \n                                   \n: MS Office\nLangages \n                                   \n: C, C++, ASP, JAVA, VC++\nDBMS/ RDBMS\n                    \n: Oracle 9i, MS SQL, \nOracle tools/ Utilities: \n- SQL*PLUS, PL/ SQL\n                    \n- Database Configuration Assistant\n\n- Oracle Enterprise Manager\n\n     \n- ORADIM\n                                      \n- ORAPWD\n                                  \n- ANALYZE\n- DBVERIFY\n                                 \n- Log Miner\n                                 \n- Back up & Recovery Manager\n\n- UMB\n                                                \n- Export/ Import\n                          \n- Explain Plan\n- Oracle Net Manager\n                             \n- TOAD\n\n\n\nTechnical Environment\n\n\nOperating Systems:\n   \n       \nWindows 2000,\n\nSolaris 9\n\nDatabase:\n                  \n            \nSQL, PL/ SQL, iSQL*PLUS, Oracle 8i/9i.Toad\n                                             \nKey Skills as a DBA:\n\nInstalling Oracle Server (9i/8i) on different OS, viz., Windows ,solaris9\nConfiguring the Oracle instance using the Initialization parameters.\nUser management and accessibility.\nDatabase creation and management of logical and physical structure.\nBackup and recovery of database and automation of the same.\nPerforming check for the existence of constraints and indexes to enforce Data Integrity and performance.\nExport, Import, RMAN. (Configuring automated export/ RMAN backups)\nAdministering and securing the database using Roles and Privileges.\nRegular maintenance viz., deleting old core files, cleaning up old trace and log files.\nWriting SQL queries against the database\n\n\nCompany\n          \n\nJagran Prakashan Ltd\n\n          \nwww.jagran.com\nFrom Dec, 04 to Apirl, 07 as Oracle Technical. The job includes\n\nJunior DBA \n\n         \nPlan for backup, recovery of database; backup and restore the database \n\n         \nControl and monitor user access to database; monitor and optimize the performance of database \n\n         \nAllocate system storage and plan for future storage requirements for the database system \n\n\n         \nCreate primary database storage structures and primary objects \n\n         \nEnroll users and maintain system security, ensuring compliance with database license agreements \n\n         \nResponsible for installation, account management, backup/recovery of Oracle 9i databases \n\n         \nResponsible for planning and performing routine backup and recovery of the databases. \n\n         \nProgramming, troubleshooting databases. \n\n\n\nPROJECTS UNDERTAKEN\n\nTitle:\n\nHousekeeping System\n\n                   \nDuration :\n Two months\nTeam Size\n: 2\n                                       \nLanguage :\n Developer ?2k\n\nTools:\n\nOracle9i, Developer 2000, Windows ?NT 4.0, Clients with Windows-98\n\nScope:\n\nHOUSEKEEPING SYSTEM \nsophisticated client server base system. Main function of this project is In hardware level to maintain the inventory of computers and its parts that are purchased for the company and in software Level To records about Severs i.e. how much table spaces we are using in sever .in this software we can trace the size and records of table and rate of increase of database from time to time. This software warns the user that particular table space is going to fill. So we can tune our servers time to time. This Package also gives the all Information about server wise table space used and created, going down up to user wise and each table wise size used and number of rows in a table. This package includes various module i.e. product master, computer master, issue (transaction) module, A.M.C. Module. By this project we can trace about a particular computer and its configuration and where it is located and it has warranty or not and how may times a particular computer got upgraded. My contribution in this package is from system study to Database Designing and then format designing for all Master Tables, Transaction Module and various reports are developed by me in this package.\nCERTIFICATIONS\n\nOracle 9i certified professionals OCP\n\nDatabase Administrator\n\n\n\nEDUCATIONAL QUALIFICATIONS\n\n\n         \nPursuing Oracle 10g certification - DBA Track\n\n         \nMCA from \nNorth\nMaharastra\nUniversity\n Jalgaon\n\nIn Jul-04\n\n         \nBSC (PCM) from \nKanpur\nUniversity\nUniversity\n in Jul-2000.\n\n\n\n\nHobbies:\n\nCricket.\nListening Soft Music.\nLong Driving \nTraveling and interacting with people\n\n            \n\n\n\n\n\n\nPERSONAL DETAILS\n\nFather:\n                                               \nMr. Gokarn Nath Bajpai\nDate of birth:\n\n                            \n\n01-03-1981\nSex:\n                                                    \nMale\nMarital Status:\n\n                          \n\nSingle \nPermanent Address:\n\n                     \n\n30 E/18 Daboli Ratan Lal Nagar \n                      \nKanpur\n -208022\n                              \n                            \n  \nUtter Pradesh.\n\nLanguages known:\n                     \nEnglish, Hindi \nSoft Skills:\n                                  \nQuick Learner, strong communication skills and effective team player.\n\nREFERENCE\n\nName:\n                                       \nMr. Manish Gupta\nCompany:\n                                 \nJagran Prakashan Ltd, \nRanchi\nPhone:\n                                      \n09334701960\n\n                                                                                                  \n\n\nDate:\n\nPlace:\n                                                                                                             \n(SUDHANSHU BAJPAI)','HIMACHAL FUTURISTIC COMMUNICATIONS LTD   ',9,NULL,'2007-10-16',NULL,'2007-10-16','2010-06-09 12:13:49','2010-06-09',10,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,9,'0',NULL),(118,'Srikanth',NULL,NULL,NULL,'srikdvvandvdth.ovdaadpps@gmail.com','srikanscth.oraascscpps@gmail.com',NULL,'0','91 9886437369','0',NULL,'0','2008-04-29',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-09 12:13:49',10,'0',NULL,'200710/16/ATT17825.html','200710/16/DOC40103.doc','Resdex @ naukri.com\nsrikanth\nsrikdvvandvdth.ovdaadpps@gmail.com\n\nTelephone: 9886437369\n(M)\n\nD.O.B\n - 18 Jun 1982 \nModified on\n - 26 Sep 2007 \nAnnual Salary\n - INR 3 Lac(s) 80 Thousand \nTotal Years of Experience\n - 3 Year(s) 3 Month(s) \nCurrent Location\n\nBangalore\n\nPreferred Location\n - Anywhere in \nIndia\nHaving 3.2 years exp in oracle apps\n\nTEXT RESUME \n\nSrikanth Email: srikanth.oraapps@gmail.com\nTechnical Consultant Phone : +91-9886437369\nOBJECTIVE\nI Strive for Excellence in all my endeavors and I look forward to work in a World-Class team of competent and motivated individuals.\nEXPERIENCE SUMMARY\n\n?3.2 years Experience in IT Industry.\n\n?2+ years of hands on experience in ERP ? Oracle 11i Applications.\n\n?Having Very good exposu\nre to implementation of Oracle 11i Applications.\n\n?Worked on Functional Modules like PO, INV, GL, \nOM\n, AP.\n\n?Development and customization of Reports, Interfaces.\n\n?Good knowledge on SQL * Loader.\n\n?Creation of Value sets in various Modules of the applicat\nion.\n\n?Defining Concurrent Programs, Executables.\n\n?PL/SQL method of submitting Concurrent programs\nWORKING EXPERIENCE\n? Working as a Technical Consultant for Trianz, \nBangalore\n from April 2005 to till date.\n? Worked as Software Trainee for Globus Systems, \nBangalore\n From May 2004 to March 2005.\nTECHNICAL SKILLS\nERP : Oracle Applications 11i (PO, INV, AP)\nProgramming Languages : C, SQL, PL/SQL\nDatabase : Oracle 8i\nOperating Systems : Windows 98/NT/2000 Server\nG.U.I : Forms6i, Reports6i\nTools : SQL* Loader, TOAD\nEducation Qualification:\n\n?B.C.A from \nAcharya\nNagarjuna\nUniversity\n\nGuntur\n\nPROJECT EXPERIENCE DETAILS:\nProject #1\nClient : \nCDL\n\nUK\nRole : Technical consultant.\nEnvironment : Oracle Applications 11.5.9, Reports 6I, PL/SQL,\nSQL*Loader\nDescription:\nCDL is a global leader in reliable portable data storage. CDL solutions help consumers, home and small business customers to manage, preserve, use and share their digital content and data. CDL provides personal storage solutions that help people manage their important information. CDL is the leading manufacturer of smart, portable storage solutions, including drives and disks.\nResponsibilities:\nAs a Team Member, was responsible for:\n\n?Analysis of the specifications provided by the client.\n\n?Involved in customization and development of Reports and Interfaces.\n\n?Have been involved in the Multi language Report Output generation.\n\n?Preparation of Technical Design Documents.\n\n?Validation of staging data before insertion into Oracle base tables \nor Interface tables.\n\n?Registrations of Custom Tables and Concurrent Programs.\n\n?Creation of Value sets in various Modules of the application.\n\n?Preparation of SQL Loader scripts.\n\n?Involved in creating unit test cases.\nInterface development:\n\n?Customiz\ned AP Invoice Import Program to upload Invoices into the Oracle Apps base tables.\n\n?Developed Purchase order inbound Interface to upload the Purchase orders details from the legacy to Oracle Apps base tables.\nReports:\n\n?Developed Standard Purchase Order\n Report.\n\n?Customized Payables Account Analysis Report.\n\n?Developed Internal requisition report.\n\n?Developed Customer Master Report.\n\n?Customized Quotation Action Required Report.\n\n?Developed advance purchase order information.\nProject #2\nClient : \nIntegra\n\nNew York\n\nUSA\n\nRole : Technical Consultant.\nEnvironment : Oracle Applications 11.5.9, SQL, PL/SQL, Reports 6i,\nSQL*Loader\nDescription:\nIntegra Systems is implementing Oracle Applications Suite to meet its E-Business vision. It is carrying out the implementation in a global single instance in a finance &discrete manufacturing environment. The project has been undertaken to streamline its Global business activities covering Financial, Distribution and Manufacturing operations. The objective is to phase out the numerous isolated legacy systems currently in use and to seamlessly integrate all the local business operations worldwide with its global business operation. To achieve this goal, entire system is being implemented in a single instance of database, which will support its global business operations as well as provide real time global data to management for taking appropriate decisions.\nResponsibilities:\n\n?Involved in customizing and Development of the Reports and Interfaces.\n\n?Preparation o\nf Technical Design Documents.\n\n?Validation of staging data before insertion into Oracle base tables or Interface tables.\n\n?Registrations of Custom Tables and Concurrent Programs.\n\n?Creation of Value sets in various Modules of the application.\n\n?Preparation\n of SQL Loader scripts.\n\n?Involved in Client meetings.\nInterfaces:\n\n?Developed Purchase order inbound Interface to upload the Purchase orders details from the legacy to Oracle Apps base tables.\n\n?Developed outbound interface to extract the data from the\n Oracle Apps tables to the Flat file.\nReports:\n\n?Developed total purchased order report (supplier wise).\n\n?Developed approved requisition details.\n\n?Customized Sales order Acknowledgement Report.\n\n?Developed AP invoice payment report.\n\n?Developed blanke\nt purchased order report.\n\n?Developed Purchase Order and Payables analysis report.\nProject #3\nClient : WGT\nRole : Software Developer\nEnvironment : PL/SQL, Oracle 8i, Forms 6i & Reports 6i.\nProject Description:\nThis project is designed to computerize the operations of the client who is involved in bulk sales of pharmaceuticals to various hospitals and medical outlets. Stock details and Products can be viewed using Lov?s. The software developed has been extremely user friendly with messaged boxes guiding the user for navigation. Reports are generated for daily, weekly month sales. An area and company wise report is also generated to keep track of the monthly purchases made.\nResponsibilities:\n\n?Developing Reports and Forms as per Client Requirement.\n\n\nDeveloping Procedures, Functions, Packages\n\n?Writing code for Reports and Forms\n\n?Preparing Technical Documentation.\n\n?Involved in Product demos and Client engagements\nProject #4\nProject Title : vendor systems\nRole : Software Developer.\nEnvironment : PL/SQL, Oracle 8i,Forms 6i & Reports 6i.\nProject Description:\nVendor System is covers the activities of Stores, Purchase and Goods Inwards Functions of a Manufacturing Organization. This Module has provisions to capture Supplier Details (Vendors) required for the Purchase Department. It facilitates Stores to check the stock of the Raw Materials used and System automatically places Purchase Requisitions to the Purchase Department. Purchase Department can place Purchase-Orders and keep track of the Work-orders given to the Vendors. When the raw material is received, corresponding Stock is updated.\nResponsibilities:\n\n?Developing Report and Forms as per Client Requirement.\n\n?Developing Procedures, Functions.\n\n?Writing code for Reports and Forms.\n\n?Prepari\nng Technical Documentation.',NULL,9,NULL,'2007-10-16',NULL,'2007-10-16','2010-06-09 12:13:49','2010-06-09',10,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,9,'0',NULL),(119,'Syed  Rahamani',NULL,NULL,'Hyderabad ','idefereesraefewfhamani@yahoo.com',NULL,NULL,'0','91 9885480651','0',NULL,'0','2008-01-12',10,33,'2010-06-09 12:13:49',10,'0',NULL,'200710/16/ATT17824.html','200710/16/DOC40104.doc','Syed Idrees Rahamani\nSyed Rahamani\n\nPhone No: +91-9885480651\n                          \nE-mail\n\n\nidefereesraefewfhamani@yahoo.com\n\nObjective\nTo obtain a challenging role as an Oracle Database Administrator using all the experience gained in the field of Information Technology.\n\nSummary of Qualification\n\nEducational Qualification\nM.Sc(Information Systems)\n first class Distinction with \n77%\n\nfrom Osmania University 2005 .\nB.C.A(Computers)\n Secured first class with \n65%\n\nfrom \nOsmania\nUniversity\n\n   \n12 \nth\n (Intermediate)\n Board of Intermediate A.P India\n10 \nth\n (SSC)\n Board of Secondary A.P India.\n\nTechnical Expertise\nPrimary Skills\n                           \n\n   \nORACLE 11i APPS DBA.\nOperating systems\n                  \n\n   \nLinux As 3.0/4.0, Win 9x,2000,NT,Xp,Unix.\n\n        \nProgramming Languages\n       \n\n   \nSQL,PL/SQL,C,C++,Unix Shell Scripts & HTML\nRDBMS\n                                  \n\n\nOracle 8i,9i,10g.\nOther Packages\n                      \n\n   \nMS-Office,VB 6.0.\n         \n\n                                               \n   \n         \n    \n\nProfessional Summary\nAbove \n2 + years\n of experience in the\n\nInformation Technology \nIndustry.\nCurrently working as \nOracle\n\nApplications DBA\n. for 2.0 years\nExperience of \nOracle\n   \nDBA\n 9i & 10g.\nExpertise hands on Installation, backup & recovery/ performance tuning of Oracle\n\nDatabase Maintaining & scheduling the Backup & Recovery plans using\n\nRMAN\n\n    \nExpertise hands on Installation of Oracle Apps 11i,\n\ncustom installations, Applying patches, Cloning , using AD utilities and Managing Concurrent Managers and Requests,\nExperience of Linux Advanced Server, Managing\n System Administration and Network Administration,\nExpertise hands on Creating User\n\naccounts assigning Quotas, Groups, Passwords, Access permissions, Scheduling System Tasks, Configuring and & maintaining of \nServers\n DHCP, FTP, NFS, Apache web server, proxy, samba server.\nExcellent communication and\n\ninterpersonal skills.\n\n\nWork Experience:\n\nWorking as an \nOracle Apps DBA\n since July 2005 to till date in \nSoft \nPearl\n infotech Pvt. Ltd. (\nwww.softpearl.com\n\n\nResponsibilities:\n\nOracle Application DBA \nInstallation\n\nand \nupgradation\n\nof Oracle\n\nApplications 11i software.\nMonitoring the Instance on daily basis.\nSetting up new \nusers\n and \nProfile\n\nMonitoring\n Application Services and Performing Checks\nManaging \nConcurrent Processing\n\nCloning using\n\nRapid Clone\n\nApplying \nPatches\nUsing \nAdpatch\n\nadctlr\n\nadadmin\n\nadconfig\n\nand other \nAd utilities\n\nCreation of \nSpecialized Concurrent Managers\n, Assigning Workshifts.\nAssigning Programs, Reports to Specialized\n Concurrent Managers\n\nUse \nAdpatch\n\nAdctlr\n\nAdadmin\n\nAdsplice\n and other \nAd utilities\nTrouble shooting\n\nOracle DBA\nInstallation \nof Oracle\n\nsoftware\nMonitor\n database and system performance. .\nManaging \nTablespaces, rollback segments, Control file, Data file, Log file and\n\nparameter file\nCreating \nUsers\n and allocating Space and\n\nPrivileges to Users\nMonitoring \nalert log\n\nPerform \nhot, cold backups \nof the\n\nOracle Database.\nTuning\n Database, Memory for optimal Performance\nRecovery of Database\n from Disk or Instance failure\nUsing \nSQL Loader\nPerform \nhot, cold backups \nof the\n\nOracle Database.\n\n        \nPerforming Export and \nImport\n\n        \nCreating a database \nClone.\n\n        \nCreating and Managing \nStandby Database.\n\nLinux Administration\n\nInstallation of Linux Advance Server Operating System,\nManaging System Administration and Network Administration,\nCreating User\n\naccounts\nAssigning \nQuotas\n\nGroups\n\nPassword Security\n\nAccess permissions\n to users,\nScheduling System Tasks,Users Tasks,Backups & Recovery Tasks,\nConfiguring & maintaining of \nNETWORKING,\n\nDHCP server\n\nConfiguring & maintaining of,\nNFS server \n\nConfiguring & maintaining of \nFTP server \n\nConfiguring & maintaining of \nApache web server\n\nConfiguring & maintaining of \nProxy, and Samba server\n\n\nProjects :\n\nPROJECT#1:\n\nProject \n        \n\n           \nMaintenance of\n\nOracle Applications11.5.9,11.5.10 \nRole\n\n   \n         \n\n           \nOracle Application DBA\n\nResponsibilities\n\n\n\n\nMonitoring the Instance on daily basis.\n\n\nInvolving in Performance/ Trouble shooting Issues.\n\n\nSystem Administration Tasks like Create users, assigning responsibilities.\n\n\nSystem Administration Tasks on Concurrent Manager.\n\n\nMaintaining the instance with AD Administration\n\n\nApplying application patches.\n\n\nAdministration of Oracle Applications.\n\n\nTroubleshooting Oracle Application Issues.\n\n\nCloning Oracle Applications\n                                                                                                          \n                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                \n                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                \n                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                \n                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                \n                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                \n                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                \n                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                \n                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                \n                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                \n                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                \n                                                                                          \nPROJECT#2\n\nProject\n         \n\n           \nConfiguration and Maintenance of Oracle 9i Database \nRole\n    \n         \n\n           \nOracle DBA\n\nResponsibilities:\n\n\n        \nAdministration of Oracle 9i database including installation, creation and planning the Backup strategy on Linux.\n\n        \nAllocating system storage and planning future storage requirements for the\n\ndatabase system.\n\n        \nManaging primary database structure and objects.\n\n        \nPlanning for backup and recovery of database and maintaining Hot Backups and Cold Backups.\n\n        \nCreating users, assigning roles and profiles, maintaining system security through monitoring user access to the database.\n\n\n\nPersonal Details:\n\nFather?s Name\n                         \n\n: Syed Yaqub\nDate of birth\n                          \n    \n: 30-12-1979.\nGender\n\n                                      \n\n\nMale\nLanguages Known\n                    \n\n\nEnglish, Hindi,Telugu.\nPostal Address\n                         \n\n: 8-1-143/MB/23,\n    \nMini Brindavan Colony,\n                            \nTolichowki, \nHyderabad\n ? 500008,\n                            \nAndhra Pradesh\n\nIndia','Soft Pearl infotech Pvt Ltd',9,NULL,'2007-10-16',NULL,'2007-10-16','2010-06-09 12:13:49','2010-06-09',10,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,9,'0',NULL),(120,'Subhankar B',NULL,NULL,NULL,'subhadzsdavvdnkarbohdvvdvdvidar@gmail.com',NULL,NULL,'0','91 9342210060','0',NULL,'0','2007-09-28',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-09 12:13:49',10,'0',NULL,'200710/16/ATT17822.html','200710/16/DOC40105.doc','RANJAN KUANAR\nSUBHANKAR B\n                                                      \n\n\nEmail ID:\nsubhadzsdavvdnkarbohdvvdvdvidar@gmail.com\n                                                      \n\n\nMobile\n\n\n+91?9342210060\n\n\n\nObjective\n\n\nA Challenging and responsible position, which provide a platform to use my abilities with functional and technical skills in the field of Information Technology with present technology for the organization using professional approach to contribute towards organization growth.\n\n\nProfessional Expertise\n\n\n\n      \nAbout \n2.5 year?s\n significant experience in the IT industry in \nOracle\n\nApplications 11i \nas \nTechno-Functional Consultant\n\n\n      \nExperience on modules like PO, AP,\n\nGL, \nOM\n\nAR\n and INV for overseas clients. \n\n      \nKnowledge of the development and customization of business applications according to customer requirements.\n\n      \nDomain Knowledge in Oracle \nPurchasing\n and Oracle \nFinance\n\n\n\nEducational Profile\n\n\n\n         \nBachelor of Engineering in \nComputer Science\n from \nBiju\nPattanaik\nUniversity\n Orissa, \nin\n 2004.\n\nEmployment Summary\n\nCompany\nName\nLocation\nDesignation\nStarting\nDate\nEnding date\nCGI Netvorks\nBangalore\nTechno-Functional Consultant\n10/01/05\nTill date\n\n\nTechnical Skills\n\nOperating Systems\nWindows 2000/XP/NT\nLanguages\nSQL, PL/SQL\nERP\nOracle Apps\nDatabase\nOracle 8i/9i\nTools\nToad, SQL Loader, ERP Tool Time Management System\nGUI\nD2K (Form6i, Report6i)\nDomain Knowledge\nOracle Purchasing, Finance\n\n\n\n     \nMajor Projects\n\n\n\n#1.Oracle Apps Implementation\n\nOrganization/Client\nWACHOVIA CORPORATION Ltd., \nUSA\n\nDuration\n     \nOct.2006 to till date\n        \nPosition\nTechno Functional Consultant\n                \nTeam size: 5\nResponsibilities\n\n                     \nWriting SQL Loader Control files to transfer the data from flat files into staging tables.\n\n                     \nWriting Pl/SQL packages & procedures for data validation & data transfer.\n\n                     \nCreating concurrent programs & request sets.\n\n                     \nCustomization / development of oracle apps report.\n   \n\nDescription\n           \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n           \nThis project aims at implementing oracle application modules. As a part of implementation involves transferring their legacy system data\n\ninto Oracle Apps tables as well as developing & customizing the reports to suite their needs.\n\nDETAILS:\n\n         \nVander Evolution Interface\n\n         \nItem loading Interface\nREPORTS:\n\n         \nUn booked sales order report\n\n         \nSales Order status Report\n\n         \nPayment Origination Report\n\nOperating System\nWindows 2000/XP/NT\nDatabase\nOracle 9i, Toad\nGUI\nD2K (Form 6i, Report 6i)\nUtilities\nExport, Import, SQL*Loader\n\n\n\n#2. Oracle Apps Integration\n\nOrganization/Client\nTEXAS MICROSYSTEMS, USA\nDuration\n     \n10Months (Oct.05 to Aug.06)\n   \nPosition\nTechno Functional Consultant\n                \nTeam size: 5\nResponsibilities\n\n      \nThrough SQL loader and control files transfer the flat file data to staging tables.\n\n      \nCreating some transport programs and procedures for data validation and data transfer.\n\n      \nDefining the concurrent programs and request sets.\n\n      \nAnalyze and customizing Oracle Apps Reports.\n   \nDescription\n          \nThe main objective of this project is to implement oracle purchasing module, which comprises improved and efficient handling of operation and to provide upload and download facilities to export and import data to external system. The implementation part involving transferring the legacy system data into Oracle Apps tables as well\n   \nas developing and customizing the reports to suite the needs.\n\nDETAILS:\n\n         \nPO\n Interface\n\nREPORTS:\n\n         \nPurchase requisition for which tender yet to be invited\n\n         \nPurchase requisition for which tender invited but PO/contract yet to be placed\n\n         \nPurchase requisition for which PO/contract placed\n\nOperating System\nWindows 2000/XP/NT\nDatabase\nOracle 9i\nGUI\nD2K (Form 6i, Report 6i)\nUtilities\nExport, Import, SQL*Loader\n\n\nPersonal Profile\n\n           \nDDDDDD DDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDD\n                 \nGender\n                 \n          \n\n       \nMale.\nMarital Status\n      \n          \n\n        \nSingle.\nFather?s Name\n     \n          \n\n      \n  \nMr. J.N.Bohidar.\nLanguages Known\n        \n\n       \nEnglish, Hindi.\n\n\nShould you feel convinced as regards the achievements stipulated, May please contact me to be across your table to justify my worth for the position applied for, I shall be grateful.\n\n\n\n\n\nDate:\n\n   \n                                                                                                      \nSubhankar Bohidar',NULL,9,NULL,'2007-10-16',NULL,'2007-10-16','2010-06-09 12:13:49','2010-06-09',10,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,9,'0',NULL),(121,'Rajesh K',NULL,NULL,NULL,'rksscscscscsc04@gmail.com',NULL,NULL,'0','09393709371','0',NULL,'0','2006-04-29',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-09 12:13:49',11,'0',NULL,'200710/16/ATT17833.html','200710/16/DOC40106.doc','Resdex @ naukri.com\nRajesh K\nrksscscscscsc04@gmail.com\n\nTelephone: 09393709371\n(M)\n 91 \n(R)\n\nD.O.B\n - Not Specified \nModified on\n - 26 Sep 2007 \nAnnual Salary\n - INR 5 Lac(s) 40 Thousand \nTotal Years of Experience\n - 4 Year(s) 10 Month(s) \nCurrent Location\n - Hyderabad \nM. Sc (IT), GNIIT with 4.7 yrs of IT exp. in System Admin, Networking Oracle DBA, Oracle Apps DBA in Unix Solaris & Linux\n\n\nTEXT RESUME \n\nInstallation of Oracle Application 11.5.9 and 11.5.10 on Red Hat Linux AND Release 12 as well.\nUpgrading Oracle Application 11.5.7/11.5.8 to 11.5.10\nGood experience in Patching\nExperience in Autoconfig management\nExperience in Cloning Oracle Application\nManaging Concurrent Manager and concurrent requests.\nUser management and assigning responsibilities to the users in Oracle Applications\nDuplicating (Cloning) a RAC database to a single node database.\nGood knowledge of Recovery Manager (RMan) scenarios for database backup, restore & recovery.\nImplementing of 9i RAC & 10g RAC (Real Application Cluster) on RH Linux AS 3.0\nCreation of database, Managing Tablespaces and Undo Management, user/role management.\nDuplicating (Cloning) a RAC database to a single node database.\nStrong knowledge in Oracle 10g new features. Such as Sysaux tablespace, automated storage management (ASM), automatic workload repository (AWR), space management- locally managed tablespace, transportable tablespace and undo tablespace.\nWorked as a windows administration & support executive.',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-16',NULL,'2007-10-16','2010-06-09 12:13:49','2010-06-09',11,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(122,'Ashish s sawant',NULL,NULL,NULL,'rascscsc@gmail.com',NULL,'0712 2742380','0','098220 61728','0',NULL,'0','2008-04-29',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-09 12:13:49',11,'0',NULL,'200710/16/ATT17830.html','200710/16/DOC40107.doc','Ashish S Sawant\nRahul K\n\nEmail \n?rascscsc@gmail.com\nCell\n   \n--098220-61728 , 0712-2742380\n               \n\nObjective:\n\n\nTo work in a challenging and enriching environment where I can upgrade my current skills and apply them at their best for optimum benefit of the company\n\n\nSummary:\n\n\n       \n2.7+ years of experience in Database management,\n Evaluate SQL statement\nperformance using utilities like explain plan, tkprof and sqltrace\n\nDetermining Tablespace free space and managing growth (TABLESPACE,DATAFILE, maintenance).Configured the service on oracle client using\n\nNet configuration assistance.\n\nManaging all Daily database maintenance issues.\n\nLoading data between databases (Export and Import, SQL Loader).\n\nImproving performance by creating appropriate indexes.\n\n\n       \nExperience in \nInstallation of ORACLE9iand oracle 10GR2 RAC (server & client) on LINUX Solaris as well as WINDOWS platform.Shell Scripting like Startup,Shutdown.Maintains Password for sys,system and Users.Deploying backup (hot and cold) mechanisms and Recovery procedures. RMAN for Backup & Recovery.\n\nTuning and configuring the Oracle\n\nserver for Maximum performance (Statspack).\n\n\nSkill Set: \n\nRDBMS\n: Working Knowledge of Oracle 8i-9i-10G\nLanguage\n: SQL,PL/SQL\nOperating Systems\n: Sun Solaris8,LINUX 7.1, Windows 9X XP, 2000.\nApplication \n: MS-Office.\nConcepts, Techniques\n\nConcepts of Information Processing, Structured Systems Analysis and Design, LAN, Internet.\n\n\nCertification:\n\n\n         \nOracle9i Database Administrator Certified Associate.(\nTest ID: SR2074358\n\n        \nReg.No. M4ESYD5073\n\n\n\n         \nAchievement certification of PL/SQL Programming and database administration.\n\n\n                                 \nEducation:\n\n\n         \nBachelor of Electrical Engineering with 64.77% from YCCE.PT.NAGPUR .\n\n         \nDiploma in electrical Engg. from Shri Datta Meghe Polytechnic\n\nNGP.\n\n\n\n\n\nWork Experience:\n\n\nTotal Experience:-2.7years\n\n1) \nTECH MAHINDRA LTD. SHARADA CENTRE PUNE\n         \nAPR2007- Till Date\n\n\nJob Profile:-\nworking as Technical associate. Provide\n\ndatabase support to 24*7 Production \nenvironment\n Sun solaris 8.Daily maintance of all oracle database environment.Troubleshooting user queries for slow performance using explain plan, sqltrace ,explain plan.Patching for upgradation of database and application\n\nSpace management.etc\n\n\n   \n\n2)\n   \nPrabhudas Lilladher Pvt. Ltd. Worli.MUMBAI\n\nJune2006 ?APR2007\n\nJob Profile:- \nWorking as a Database Administrator.Job involved application of archieved log to synchronise standby database,Maintain Backup policy,monitor Database performance.\n\nPeriodic Maintenance and upgradation of Applications as per the requirements.\n\nTuning and configuring the Oracle\n\nserver for Maximum performance (Stats pack).\n\n\n\n\n\n2)\n\nACES e-solutions Pvt.Ltd.STP \nNagpur\n     \nFrom NOV 2004 ? june 2006\n\nJob Profile:-\n Working as a Asst. Database administrator. Job Involve \nCreate user logins Query and user to respective database and Manage security task.like granting and revoking permissions \nCreate profile and assign users, maintain tablespace(like providing space for enoughData)Performing Backup (Logical & Physical) & Recovery automation, logical incremental backup on daily basis &full logical Backup on weekly\n\nbasis, Physical\n\nBackup using RMAN.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n3)\n\nAS A FACULTY ON ORACLE 9i DBA IN RAMIFY SYSTEMS, MAHAL, NAGPUR\n\n\n         \nPerformed onsite Installation,provide trainning on pl/sql programming and Database administration.\n\n         \nConceptual Model design\n\nEstimated sizes of storage structures and growth projection.\n\n         \nWrote scripts for creation of tables, views and indexes\n\n         \nWrote program units in PL/SQL - Packaged Procedures, DML, System and Schema Triggers.Evaluating queries for performance.\n\n         \nDeveloped some Data Entry Screens (GUI interface development)\n\n         \nTransferring some tables\' data from legacy system (Foxbase) to Oracle.\n\n         \nCreating user accounts and roles; managing security related issues.\n\n         \nMaintaining Backup (logical and OS level)\n\nExtracurricular activities\n\n\n         \nActive participation in events like Quizzes, Elocution, at the school & college levels.\n\n         \nDid some social works in school.\n\n         \nOne of the best players in college cricket squad\n\nInterests:\n\n         \nComputers, Reading books, Listening Music and Gossiping\n               \n\n\nPersonal Details:\n\nName \n                                  \n\n\nRahul V. Katturwar\n          \nDate Of Birth\n                  \n\n\n3rd-Nov-1977\nGender\n                                \n\n\nMale.\nPassport No.\n                      \n\n\nF6962724 (Passport Office Nagpur)\nLanguage Spoken\n             \n\n\nMarathi,English & Hindi\nCurrent Address\n             \n: Rahul Vijay Katturwar\n                                             \n\n\nA\\4,c/o A. V Pawar.\n                              \n                                         \nAnurag socity.Opp. Kokan Express\n                                   \n      \nRestonrent , Kothrud Stand ,karve Road .\n         \n       \n                                      \n  \nKothrud. Pune.\n         \n       \nPermanent Address\n         \n: Rahul Vijay Katturwar\n                                             \n\nPlot No.3,14\nth\n street\n                                             \n\nVishwakarma Nagar\n                                             \n\nNagpur-440027\n                                                                                    \n                                                         \n    \n\n                   \n\n\n\n\nPlace:PUNE\n                                                                                                   \nDate:\n              \n                                                                         \n(Rahul\n\nV. Katturwar)',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-16',NULL,'2007-10-16','2010-06-09 12:13:49','2010-06-09',11,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL);
INSERT INTO `tp_applicants` VALUES (123,'Rajasekar M',NULL,NULL,NULL,'asccppscscs@yahoo.co.in',NULL,NULL,'0','9940383930','0',NULL,'0','2006-11-28',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-09 12:13:49',11,'0',NULL,'200710/16/ATT17828.html','200710/16/DOC40108.doc','Muniyandi Elayaraja\nRajasekar\n     \n\n                           \nMobile:9940383930\n            \n        \n                                                                            \nEmail : asccppscscs@yahoo.co.in\n                    \nOracle \nApps\n 11i Techno Functional Consultant\n        \n\nEXPERIENCE SUMMARY:\n\nHaving\n   \n3.4\n   \nyears of\n   \nIT experience\n   \nin Oracle Applications with technical expertise in Oracle Apps (11.5.9, 11.5.10)\n\n\n       \nExcellent Oracle Applications Techno Functional Knowledge and working as Techno Functional Consultant \n\n       \nHas undergone complete \nimplementation life cycle\n\n       \nCurrently working in \nTata Consultancy Services\n\nMODULES\n\n         \nInventory \n\n         \nBills of Material\n\n         \nGeneral Ledger\n\n         \nPurchasing\n\n         \nOrder management\n\n         \nWork in Process\n\n         \nSystem Administration\n\n         \nAOL\n\nSUMMARY\n\n       \nHas been involved in\n\nimplementation, customization, maintenance , conversions\n           \ninterfaces and user training Document Preparation\n\n       \nStrong in Forms 6i, Reports 6i, Sql*loader, SQL*plus, PL/SQL, packages, procedures, functions and triggers\n\n       \nDevelopment and customization of \nReports, Forms, custom.pll\n and \nInterfaces\n\n       \nConfiguring Value sets, DFF for various requirements\n\n       \nDefining Concurrent Programs, Executables\n\n       \nExcellent Programming experience in PL/SQL\n\n       \nExcellent Inter-Personal, Communication, Coordination\n\n       \nExcellent trouble shooter\n\n       \nGood Team player\nSKILLS\n\n       \nUnderstanding the Technical Requirements \n\n       \nDetailing the design to the team\n\n       \nProvide support to existing applications\n\n       \nRapid Knowledge transfer for support\n\n       \nIntegrate Custom Applications to the system\n\n       \nProviding Daily Status updates to the Onsite Team\n\n       \nImplementation knowledge of Oracle Applications\n\n       \nResolving System issues\n\n       \nUnderstanding the functionality of custom.pll\n\nEDUCATIONAL QUALIFICATION\n\n       \nBachelor of Engineering from \nMadras\n university\n\nTECHNICAL SKILLS\n\nOperating System\nLinux, Unix, Win XP/NT/2000\nLanguage\nPL/SQL\nFront-end\nDeveloper 2000(Forms & Reports 6i)\nTools\nSQL * Plus, Toad, PVCS\nDatabase\nOracle 9i\nApplication\nOracle Applications 11i \n\n\nTECHNICAL ACTIVITIES: \n\n\n       \nFollow the Functional Documentation and prepare Tech Specification Document\n\n       \nDevelopment of conversions and Interfaces for the Data Migration from Legacy to Oracle Apps\n\n       \nExperienced in designing interfaces\n\n       \nDeveloped SQL Loader, PL/SQL Procedures to do custom validation\n\n       \nRegistering the programs as Concurrent Programs for Interfaces\n\n       \nSequential Execution of the programs to migrate from legacy to Apps\n\n       \nError reporting at each stage and getting concurrence from the user\n\n       \nMenu registration for the newly created forms\n\n       \nCreation of Form functions to handle the view only Functionality of Secured forms\n\n       \nCreation of responsibility and assigning appropriate Data Group, Menu, Request group\n\n       \nCustomization of Forms and reports\n\n\n\nWORK EXPOSURE \n\nOracle\n E-Business\n Suite 11.5.10\n Production Support\nProject\nEnvironment :\nOracle\n\n\n-Business Suite 11.5.10 residing on Linux Server. Modules involved Inventory (INV), Bills \nOf\n Material (BOM), Purchasing (PO), General Ledger, Order Management (OM), Accounts Receivable (AR)\nDuration\n      \n\nFrom Feb 2005 ? Till Date\nCompany\n     \n\nTCS\nClient\n             \n\nMotorola\nRole\n\n\n           \n\nTechno Functional Consultant\n\nThis Project includes\n\n\n       \nSupporting \nBom\n interface\n\n       \nSupporting routing interface\n\n       \nSupporting OTC cycle\n\n       \nOpen a SR with oracle and resolved the ticket \n\n       \nDaily updating the TAR/SR and finally resolved the ticket \n\n       \nGetting feedback from the user after resolving the ticket\n\n       \nAssigning the ticket based on the priority\n\n       \nPrepared PRD and send it to built team\n\n\n       \nGetting feedback from the user before closing the ticket critical ticket\n\n       \nInteracting with the clients for any updates\n\n\nEnvironment :\nOracle\n\n\n-Business Suite 11.5.10 residing on Linux Server. Modules involved Inventory (INV), Bills \nOf\n Material (BOM), Purchasing (PO), General Ledger, Order Management (OM), Accounts Receivable (AR)\nDuration\n      \n\nFrom Dec 2005 ? Feb 2007\nCompany\n     \n\nArleen Technologies\nClient\n             \n\nArvin Meretor\nRole\n\n\n           \n\nTechno Functional Consultant\n\nThis Project includes\n\n\n       \nDevelopment of Requisitions interfaces for Purchase Requisitions\n\n       \nDevelopment of Purchase Order Interface\n\n       \nUnderstanding the functionality of Requisitions \n\n       \nGood functional understanding of RFQ and Quotation\n\n       \nTechnical design review with Onsite to cross check any dependency and got approved \n\n       \nDeveloping PL/SQL procedure to validate and move data to interface tables\n\n       \nDefining Concurrent programs, Request Sets and Request Group\n\n       \nCustomized purchase order print report\n\n       \nExecution and Error reporting after Import process\n\n       \nEnhancing the programs based on new user requirements\n\n       \nRegistering Forms and reports in the front end\n\n       \nDiscussing the technical details with onsite team \n\n       \nProviding test support during user testing phase \n***********************************************************************************************\n\nOracle\n E-Business\nSuite 11.5.9\n Implementation and Support\n Project \n\nEnvironment :\nOracle E-Business Suite 11.5.10.\n Modules involved Inventory (INV), Bills \nOf\n Material (BOM), Purchasing (PO), General Ledger, Order Management (OM), Accounts Receivable (AR), Work in Process (WIP)\nDuration\n       \n\nFrom Feb 2005 ? Nov 2005\nCompany\n        \n\n Arleen Technologies\nClient\n              \n\nPower One\nRole\n                \n\nTechnical consultant\n\nResponsibility includes\n\n\n       \nDeveloped Bill of Materials Interface for Standard BOM\n\n       \nGood functional knowledge in routing and types of BOM\n\n       \nEnabled DFF for miscellaneous stock locator\n\n       \nDeveloped on hand quantity report to display cycle count stock locator\n\n       \nCreation of GL Source and GL Categories for new Legacy sources\n\n       \nDevelopment of GL Interface\n\n       \nUnderstanding and configuring Recurring Journal\n\n       \nConfigured security rule and cross validation rule for month end process security\n\n       \nEnabling Account Alias for frequently used accounts\n\n       \nDeveloped Routing interface \n\n       \nDevelopment of Item Interface Error Correction form\n\n       \nLogging the resolution and send for approval\n\n       \nFollow up of Issue Tickets with respective users and proper closure after user testing\n\n       \nMigrating code after unit testing and user acceptance testing in test instance\n\n       \nMonitoring the migrated program for a weeks time for any further issues\n***************************************************************************\n\nOracle\n E-Business\n Suite 11.5.9 \nEnvironment : \nOracle E-Business Suite 11.5.9 implementation on Unix Server, Inventory(Inv), Bills Of Material (BOM), Purchasing (PO), General Ledger, Order Management (OM), Accounts Receivable (AR),\nDuration\n        \n\nFrom June 2004 ? Jan 2005\nCompany\n      \n\n\nArleen Technologies\nClient \n    \n        \n\n\nAgilent Technologies\nRole\n             \n\nTechnical Consultant\n        \n\nResponsibility includes\n\n\n       \nProvided support for the existing 11i manufacturing modules as a support Analyst\n\n       \nUnderstanding the existing support guides for the applications\n\n       \nTaking knowledge transfer from the onsite team\n\n       \nMaintained On hand Quantity conversion Interface\n\n       \nMaintained item import interface \n\n       \nMatching the standard functionality with custom code\n\n       \nInterface error checking, status reporting\n\n       \nData Fix for data issues based on user feedback /approval\n\n       \nCode fix for code issues\n\n       \nCustomized forms based on user inputs\n\n       \nCustomized vendor report\n\n       \nReports modification and migration of reports to respective directory\n\n       \nResolving assigned open tickets\n\n       \nRegistration of forms and reports\n\n       \nDefining Request sets for Interface programs',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-16',NULL,'2007-10-16','2010-06-09 12:13:49','2010-06-09',11,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(124,'Ratheesh',NULL,NULL,'PUNE','vscgcscscc@yahoo.com',NULL,NULL,'0','91 9850832361','0',NULL,'0','2007-11-12',10,34,'2010-06-09 12:13:49',11,'0',NULL,'200710/16/ATT17823.html','200710/16/DOC40109.doc','Curriculum Vitae\nCurriculum Vitae\n\n\n\n                                               \n     \n                                               \n                                               \n\n\nFLAT NO 7\n           \nRATHEESH \n                         \nNASSEB\nPARK\n                     \n                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   \n     \n                       \n                                                                                \nSALUNKE VIHAR\n                             \nWANOWIRE\n    \n                                                  \nPUNE \n? 411048\n                                                         \n  \n                                            \nEmail: vscgcscscc@yahoo.com\n                                                          \n                                            \n\nMobile: +91- 9850832361\n         \n\n\nObjective:\n\n   \n            \nMy Professional Goal is to\n\nexcel in the application of innovative technology, and develop world-class solutions to real world challenges and use my professional skills as the foundation for building a unique combination of technical aptitude with business development.\n\n\nWork Experience:\n\nAMDOCS Business Services India Pvt Ltd, Pune \n\nPosition: SME (Subject Matter Expert)\nDuration: Jan 2007- Till Date\n\nProject Name: Telecom Billing \nClient: \nBELL\nCanada\n\nKey Areas:\n\n      \nTelecom Billing systems\n\n      \nOracle \n\n      \nSQL\n\n      \nUNIX\n\n      \nEnsemble\n\n      \nClarify\n\nProject Details: \nAmdocs is using Ensemble for Billing.\nWorking platform is HP-UNIX.\nRunning Bill cycles & \nMonitoring Cycles\n for all the LOBs (Line Of Business).\nIdentifying the error by checking log file for the jobs& Sort out it through the Clarify Tickets.\n\n         \nHandling UAT team for the billing conversion activity from legacy billing system to Ensemble.\n\n         \nProviding Level 3 support for defects and production issues related to Billing Systems.\n\n         \nPlayed important role in Generation and Resolving Tickets in Clarify.\n\n         \nCoordinating with Clients and business user for new requirements / enhancements.\n\n         \nCoordinating with the Quality Assurance team related to ISO and SAS 70.\n\n         \nExecution and Monitoring the customer \nSLA\n (Service Level Agreement). \n\nOrient Technologies Pvt Ltd, Mumbai\n           \nPosition: \nSupport Engineer \nDuration:\n\nMay 2006\n-Jan 2007\n\nJob Location:\n\nTATA CONSULTANCY SERVICES\nProject Name:\n\nCorporate Telecom Billing\nClient: VSNL\n\n\n\nProject Details: \nGeneva Billing Software is used for billing& its of Converges which is the heart of our application.\nTCS is customized \nGeneva\n for VSNL\nDatabase is Oracle 9 i\nSQL is used for accessing Data Base\n\n\nWorking platform is Unix\nMediation Server collects these CDR and converts them to text files. These text files are processed by us and stored into oracle database. We can define various rate plans. We can also set various cost bands for a particular code.\nPlayed an important role from creation of customers to bill production\nBusiness Objects (BO) is used for generating reports as per requirement. \n\nJob Profile: \nWorking in on \nGeneva\n, Telecom billing software. We are doing billing for corporate customers for the services like CIT, Vciplc, and Inmarast etc.\n\n\nPosition: System Engineer\nCompany: Advanced Photonics Pvt Ltd, Mumbai\nDuration: \nMay 2005-May 2006\n\nSome of the key areas relating to my job include:\n\n      \n\nTroubleshooting technical problems of PC \n      \n\n\nInstallation of different softwares &hardware peripherals\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n Overall control& Maintenance of all computers\n\nCertifications:\n\n     \nCCNA (Cisco Certified Network Associate) CSCO11054524\n\n\n\nTraining Completed:\n                                                                                                                            \n\nP.G.C.A (Post Graduate Diploma in Computer Applications)\nECIT, Hydrabad\n\nDiploma in Computer Hardware\nLogic Software Solutions, \nCochin\n, Kerala\n\n\nSoftware Exposure:\n\nOperating System: WIN 98, XP\nPackages: MS Office\nLanguage: C\n   \n\nEducational Qualifications:\n       \n\nM.Sc Industrial Electronics\n\nfrom [\nBharathidasan\nUniversity\n, Thiruchirappalli, Tamilnadu] in \n[April 2004] with First Class (16\nth\n Rank in University)\nAggregate: 77.53%\n\nB.Sc Electronics\n\nfrom [\nMahatma\nGandhi\nUniversity\n, Kottayam, Kerala] in\n[June 2001] with First Class\nAggregate: 70.25%\n\nPDC\n\nfrom [\nMahatma\nGandhi\nUniversity\n, Kottayam, Kerala\n] in\n[April 1998] with First Class\nAggregate: 74.6%\n\n\nSSLC\n\nfrom [Department Of General Education, Kerala] in \n[March 1996] with First Class\nAggregate: 63.5%\n\nCurriculum Project:\n\nTitle\n\n      \n\nPC Interfaced Speed Monitoring System \n\n\nBrief Overview of Project\n\n\nThis Project leads to measure the speed of any rotating object with high accuracy at low cost. It also gives the facility of capturing and storing the file and also can view the graph. The circuit is directly interfaced to PC through parallel port. Software program is written in C++. It was carried out at Travancore-Cochin Chemicals Ltd. Kerala. \n\nPersonal Profile:\n\n    \n      \nDate of Birth\n                        \n\n\n20-04-1981\n      \nFather?s Name\n                     \n\n\nGOPALAKRISHNAN E.T\n      \nSex\n                                    \n\n\nMALE\n      \nMarital Status\n                      \n\n\nSINGLE\n      \nLanguages Known\n                \n\n\nENGLISH, HINDI, MALAYALAM & TAMIL\n      \nNationality\n                           \n\n\nINDIAN\n      \nPermanent Address\n             \n\n\nVADAKKEMANDOPPILLIL HOUSE\n                                                \n   \nALLAPRA POST, PERUMBAVOOR\n                                                \n   \nERNAKULAM KERALA - 683 553.\n                                                                                \n                        \n\n     \nPassport Details:\n\nPassport No:\n   \nF0551346\nDate of Issue:\n\n4/10/2004\nDate of Expiry: 3/10/2014\nPlace of Issue: \nCochin\n                        \n                   \nExtra Achievements:\n\nWon Best Team member &full attendance awards from Amdocs.\nWon prizes in Quiz Competitions.\nWon prizes in Technical sensoriom.\n\nReferences:\n\nAvailable upon request.\nDeclaration\n\nI here by declare that the information furnished above is true to the best of my knowledge.\n\n                                                                                    \nPlace: Pune\n                                                                                           \n  \n   \n\nRATHEESH','AMDOCS Business Services India Pvt Ltd',1,NULL,'2007-10-16',NULL,'2007-10-16','2010-06-09 12:13:49','2010-06-09',11,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(125,'Raghavendra T',NULL,NULL,'Bangalore ','r0vxzvxv86@hotmail.com',NULL,'080 2 674 4241','0','98454 50495','0',NULL,'0','2008-09-11',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-09 12:13:49',11,'0',NULL,'200710/16/ATT17820.html','200710/16/DOC40110.doc','Raghavendra H\nRaghavendra T\n44, 12\nth\n Cross, 19\nth\n Main, Muneshwara Block, Banashankari 3rd stage, Bangalore ? 560 026\nMob: 98454 50495, Tel.: 080 2 674 4241, Email:xv r0vxzvxv86@hotmail.com\n\nSummary of Experience\nAbout \n1.8 years\n of functional and technical \nOracle ERP\n experience, plus 5+ years of application development experience using Microsoft Technologies and 7+ years in the IT field.\n\nTechno-Functional consultant\n for Oracle Human Resources, Oracle Learning Management(earlier called OTA), Employee Self-Service, Manager Self-Service and knowledge of AME.\nProficient in using Oracle Apps tools - \nAME\n\nDiscoverer\n and third party tools including \nTOAD\n\nMethodologies & Documents: Oracle?s \nApplications Implementation Methodology\n (AIM), Oracle documents including: RD020, BP080, BR010, MD050, BR100, CV030, CV040, TE040 and DO070\nProductivity Applications: MS Office, MS Visio and MS Project \nPast experience in Client Server Applications & Web based Applications development using Microsoft ASP.net, C#, Web Services, ASP, Java script and others.\nHandled legacy system Data migration, rapid modifications & interfacing with Oracle E\n\nP systems.\nCountry visited - \nBahrain\n\nand\nSaudi Arabia\n\nRiyadh\n\n for on-site implementations.\n\nOracle Apps Skills and Tools\nStudy of Current Business Processes, Future Business Flow and identification of GAP/Workaround\n\nBusiness Requirements Mapping for the various HR processes\n\nDesigning and Setting up \nOracle Core HR\n - Business Groups, Key Flexfields, Descriptive Flexfields, Recruitment model, Competency management, Payroll Definition, Security Profile, etc.\n\nSetup of SSHR and OLM (OTA\n\nas per requirements\nCustomizing/Formatting \nDiscoverer\n Reports\n\nConducting UAT ? Prepare \nTest Scripts\n and \nUsers Acceptance Test (UAT)\nConduct \nKey User Training\nLog, view, monitor, follow-up and close Technical Assistance Requests \n(TARs)\n on \nOracle Metalink\n\nOn Job Associations \n\n\n          \nCurrently working with Arowana Consulting Ltd. as \nOracle HRMS\n\nTechno-Functional Consultant \nsince Aug 2005 till date.\n\n          \nWorked as Senior Software Engineer from July 2002 to Aug 2005 with JGI-Information Services.\n\n          \nWorked as Software Engineer from May 2000 to June 2002 with MIIT.\n\nProjects\n\nProject: \nOracle HR 11i Implementation\nClient: Arab National Bank, \nRiyadh\n (KSA)\n                                                                                                                                                  \nDuration: \nJanuary, 2007 to till date\nRole:\n Oracle HCM Consultant\nTeam Size:\n\nDescription: \nArab National Bank (a Saudi Joint Stock Company) is the 4\nth\n largest Bank in the \nKingdom\n of \nSaudi Arabia\n, Headquartered in \nRiyadh\n\n\nImplementation of \nOracle HR , Payroll, OLM(OTA), iRec, SSHR and OTL version 11i being implemented in Riyadh Headquarters office \nto carryout the business responsibilities efficiently to act as a strong business enabled to deal with human resources department requirements.\nRoles and Responsibilities:\n\n          \nImplemented Oracle HR 11i (11.5.10) and OLM (OTA.J), ESS & MSS. \n\n          \nStudy of Current business processes, future business flow & identification of GAP/Workaround.\n\n          \nAnalyzing user needs, conferring with users to improve procedures and identifying and solving problems.\n\n          \nBusiness Requirements Mapping for HR and OLM (OTA) modules.\n\n          \nInstance and modules testing for inconsistencies and missing steps.\n\n          \nCustomizing/Formatting Discoverer Reports.\n\n          \nCarrying out Conference Room Pilots (1 & 2) and Users Acceptance Test (UAT).\n\n          \nProvided end-user Training & User Guides \nEnvironment\n: Windows XP, HP Tru64 UNIX, Modules: HR, SSHR and OLM (OTA.J)\n\nProject: \nProject Easy\nClient: Gulf \nAir\n\nBahrain\nDuration: \nFebruary, 2006 to December, 2006\nRole: \nOracle HR Consultant\nTeam Size:\n\nDescription: \nGulf Air is a major international airline serving 46 destinations worldwide, \ncomprised of a corporate headquarters in \nBahrain\n and about 50 locations worldwide. \nImplementation of \nOracle HR, Payroll, iRec, OTL, SSHR, OTA and Finance version 11i t\no have an accessible and common HR module to capture data, adopting the best business practices/processes and provide self-service reporting direct to desktops. \nRoles and Responsibilities:\n\n          \nImplemented Oracle HR and OTA 11i, Discoverer 4i.\n\n          \nSetting up HR system ? Design and Development \n\n          \nDeveloped test plans, test scripts and did unit testing on after each setup.\n\n          \nInstance and modules testing for inconsistencies and missing steps\n\n          \nDeveloped Training materials and conducted Training sessions for end users.\n\n          \nDid post-production support.\nEnvironment\n: Windows XP, HP Tru64 UNIX, Modules: HR, OTA\n\nProject: \nStaff Travel Management System\nClient:\n\nGulf \nAir\n\nBahrain\nDuration:\n September, 2005 to Jan 2006\nRole:\n Project Lead\nTeam Size:\n\n\nProject Description: \nStaff Travel Management Application is a web based client-server application which facilitates Gulf Air to manage Staff Travel needs. The application consumes a 3\nrd\n party web service (booking engine) to carry out live air bookings and search for flight schedules and availability. The application is interfaced with the Oracle Apps to share & synchronize employee HR data.\n\nRoles and Responsibilities:\n\n          \nHandling Project Management activities of the team.\n\n          \nDefine and analyze requirements\n\n          \nSystem Study, HLD, Database Designing, Code \n\neview & Project Planning. \n\n          \nDesign, Development and Onsite Implementation including client interactions.\nEnvironment:\nLanguages & Platform\n: ASP.NET 2.0, C#, Visual Studio .Net 2005\nDatabase:\n SQL Server 2000\nOperating System:\n Windows XP/2000, Windows 2003 Server\n\nProject:\nCore Fund Management System ? Prototype development\nClient:\n\nNational Social Security Fund, Govt. of \nTanzania\n\nEast Africa\nDuration:\n Aug 2005 to Sep 2005\n\nole:\nTeam Lead\nTeam Size:\n 10\nProject Description: \nNational Social Security Fund (NSSF) is a leading provider of social security in \nTanzania\n. NSSF Core Fund Management System (NSSF-CFMS) is web-based intranet application, developed to manage and monitor the activities of NSSF. Some of the main modules are \nCompliance, Benefits and SHIB.\n\noles and \n\nesponsibilities:\n\n          \nProject Planning, Handling Project Management activities of the team.\n\n          \nDefine and analyze requirements.\n\n          \nSystem Study, HLD and Database Designing. \nEnvironment:\nLanguages & Platform\n: ASP.NET 2.0, C#, Visual Studio .Net 2005\nDatabase:\n SQL Server 2000\nOperating System:\n Windows XP/2000, Windows 2003 Server\n\nProject: \nMATSnet (Intranet Application)\nClient:\n\nMATS\nUniversity\n\nRaipur\nDuration:\n October, 2004 to February, 2005\nRole:\n Team Lead\nTeam Size:\n\n\nProject Description: \nMATSnet is an Intranet application which facilitates faculty and staff of \nMATS\nUniversity\n to manage daily activities such as Travel allowance, Leave application, Memos, Circulars and host of other services. \n\nRoles and Responsibilities:\n\n          \nHandling Project Management activities of the team.\n\n          \nDefine and analyze requirements\n\n          \nSystem Study, HLD, Database Designing, Project Planning. \n\n          \nDesign, Development and Testing.\nEnvironment:\nLanguages & Platform\n: ASP.NET, C#, Visual Studio .Net 2003\nDatabase:\n SQL Server 2000\nOperating System:\n Windows XP/2000, Windows 2003 Server\n\nProject: \nOnline Parents Corner Ver 1.2 \nClient: Jain International Residential School (JIRS), \nBangalore\nDuration:\n May, 2004 to August, 2004\nRole: \nSenior Software Engineer\nTeam Size:\n\n\nProject Description:\n\nParents Corner is a web-based application intended to give parents up to date information on the progress of their children studying at \nJain\nInternational\n\nesidential\nSchool\n\nBangalore\n\n\nRoles and Responsibilities:\n\n          \nHandling Project Management activities of the team.\n\n          \nDefine and analyze requirements\n\n          \nSystem Study, Database Designing, Project Planning.\n\n\n          \nDesign, Development, Testing, Deployment and Implementation.\nEnvironment:\nLanguages & Platform:\n ASP.NET, C#, Visual Studio .Net 2003\nDatabase:\n SQL Server 2000,\nOperating System:\n Windows XP/2000, Windows 2003 Server\n\nProject: \nAdmission Process Management Application \nClient: Jain International Residential School (JIRS), \nBangalore\nDuration:\n January, 2004 to April, 2004\nRole:\n Senior Software Engineer\nTeam Size:\n\n\nProject Description: \nThis application facilitates the management to record and maintain the caller information for further follow up, analysis and future references. This application also enables to share the information between the school and the corporate office.\n\nRoles and Responsibilities:\n\n          \nSystem Study, Database Designing\n\n          \nDefine and analyze requirements\n\n          \nDesign, \n\nDevelopment, Testing, Deployment and Implementation\nEnvironment:\nLanguages & Platform:\n ASP.NET, C#, Visual Studio .Net 2003\nDatabase:\n SQL Server 2000\nOperating System:\n Windows XP/2000, Windows 2003 Server\n\nWebsites Developed\nVarious websites of type static and dynamic were developed for Jain Group of Institutions, \nBangalore\n\nDuration:\n June, 2000 to October, 2003\nRoles and Responsibilities:\n\n          \nUnderstand Requirements, conceptualizing, Database Designing\n\n          \nDesign, Development, Testing, Deployment, Implementation and Search Engine optimization\nEnvironment:\nLanguages & Platform:\n ASP, HTML, Java Script, Dream weaver / Home site,\nDatabase:\n MS Access 2000, SQL Server 2000\nOperating System:\n Windows XP/2000, Windows 2000 Server\n\nWorkshops attended\n\n          \nOracle Apps Training \n\n          \nIntel seminar on web technologies\n\n          \nMicrosoft seminar on .Net and Embedded system\n\n\n          \nAdobe Creative Suite seminar\n\nAcademic Qualification and Certifications\n\n          \nMasters of Science (Information Technology), M.Sc. (IT)\nCurrently pursuing final semester, \nKuvempu\nUniversity\n\n          \nBachelor of Science in Electronics, B.Sc. \nApril 2000, \nSri\nBhagawan\nMahaveer\nJain\nCollege\n\nBangalore\nUniversity\n\n          \nProfessional diploma in Network Centered Computing from NIIT\nNovember 1999, NIIT, Jayanagar\n\nPersonal Information\nDate of Birth\n         \n\n\n              \n08 June 1977\nGender\n                 \n\n\n              \nMale\nMarital Status\n       \n\n\n              \nSingle\nPassport No\n         \n\n\n              \nG0742784\n\nStrengths\n\n          \nPossess good communication, interpersonal, intuitive, technical, organizational skills with the ability to adapt in changing environments.\n\n          \nEnergetic and self-motivated team player. Proven ability to work in both independent and team environments.\n\n          \nExcellent analysis of business processes and legacy systems.\n\n          \nCan learn new technologies quickly as and when required.\n\nExtra Curricular Activities\n\n          \nTrekking and Adventure sports (Go-karting, River Rafting, Mountain Climbing, Bungee Jump etc.,)\n\n          \nSports\n\n         \nRepresented \nSri\nBhagawan\nMahaveer\nJain\nCollege\n in Cricket for all 3 Years. Team Captain at Inter-college and University Tournaments.\n\n         \nRepresented ?Bangalore Cricketers? at various state level tournaments and was part of the club for 5 years.\n\n          \nVolunteer at Blood Donation, Health and Eye Camps besides taking part in a host of social service initiatives conducted by SBMJC and Public Relations, JGI.\n\n          \nPlayed an active role in a host of events in college and at work.','Arowana Consulting Ltd',1,NULL,'2007-10-16',NULL,'2007-10-16','2010-06-09 12:13:49','2010-06-09',11,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(126,'Ramesh N',NULL,NULL,NULL,'rnaldccdcdcdcem@gmail.com','amesh.nalem@sify.com',NULL,'0','091 9848863665','0',NULL,'0','2007-04-30',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-09 12:13:49',11,'0',NULL,'200710/16/ATT40689.html','200710/16/DOC40111.doc','RESUME\nRESUME\nCURRENT ADRESS:\nRamesh.N\nH.No. 2-3-64/5/C,\nOpp.Amberpet Police Station,\nThirumala Nagar\n                                                                   \nE-mail: \nrnaldccdcdcdcem@gmail.com\nHyderabad\n\n                                                                           \n            \n\namesh.nalem@sify.com\n\n\n                                                                                               \nPhone No: +091-9848863665.\n\nOBJECTIVE:\n\n                \nTo pursue a challenging long-term career in ORACLE APPS. To be a part of winning team of a professionally managed organization and to use my knowledge and experience in leading and implementing innovate and quality oracle ERP products and to continuously update my self with the latest ERP new dimensional products.\nSUMMARY:\n\n\n         \nAround 3 years \nof functional experience in Oracle Financial- 11i\n\n\n         \nGot ?Best Performance year of the Award? from Genpact\n\n         \nHolding B1 Visa from Genpact.\nFunctional responsibilities have included business process analysis, requirements gathering and Analysis.\nExperience in developing statements of functional overviews, business processes, and other documentation to facilitate users? acceptance.\n\nGood Analytical, Problem-Solving skills.\nGood leadership and project management skills.\nGood exposure to interacting with clients.\nAbility to learn new skills quickly.\nHave good team spirit, which has helped me understand the group requirements, and plan the project accordingly. My analytical skills also helped me analyzing problems and faster decision-making.\nACADEMIC QUALIFICATIONS:\nMBA- with the specialization of IT-Finance in International Institute of Information Technology, Pune\nBachelor of Science in \nS.R.R.Govt\nDegree\nCollege\n\nKakathiya\nUniversity\n\nWarangal\n, and AP.\nIntermediate- Alphores Jr.\nCollege\n, Board of intermediate, Andhra Pradesh.\nS.S.C- Z.P.S.S, Regadimaddikunta, Karimnagar.\nTECHNICAL EXPOSURE:\n                \n                                                                \nFunctional: \n                           \nOracle Financial Applications 11i (\nGL\n\nAR\n, AP). \nPlatforms:\n          \n    \nWindows 98/XP, Unix.\n   \n                                                     \n                                                                      \nDBMS: \n            \n   \n                \nOracle 8i, PL/SQL\n                              \n                   \n                \n                         \n       \n      \nOperating Systems:\n             \nWindows 95 & 98, Windows NT.\n                                                     \n                                \nIT Tools: \n                               \nMS Project 2000.\n\n                \n\nWORK EXPERIENCE:\n\nORACLE FINANCIALS:\n\nAssociated with Genpact, \nHyderabad\n, as Oracle 11i Apps. Associate Functional Consultant from May 2006 to till date.\n\nProject #1:\n             \n                                                                                                               \nDec?06-Cont.\n\nProject: \n                \nSupporting\n of Oracle Financials 11i\n\nClient:\n   \n                \nGE Commercial Finance.\n\nEnvironment\n\n        \nOracle Applications 11i ?GL, AP and \nSQL.\n\nRESPONSIBILITIES:\n\nI have defined the COA in all instances of Oracle Applications.\nCreated Financial Statement Generator (FSG) reports for the company. Developed FSG reports on Balance Sheet, Combined and departmental Statement of Operations/Income Statement and other reports.\nProvided Post implementation support in GL, AP\nProject work that involves co-ordination with the TCS&Project teams for data conversions, interfaces, data extraction etc.\nI ran the Discoverer reports and tallied with the FSGs\nI ran the FRS Program and Interface reports.\nDefine Accounting Flexfield Structure, Define Security Rules, Assign Security Rules Setup, Define Cross-Validation Rules, Define Period Type.\nUploaded the journals by using the Web-ADI Templates\nDeleted, Posted, reversed the Journals as per the client reuquest.\nRun the Auto Approval journal program to the approve the journal batches.\nSet up the Auto post.\nProject #2:\n                                                                                                                            \nMay?06-Dec?06.\n\nProject: \n                \nImplementation of Oracle Financials 11i (GL)\nClient:\n   \n                \nE*Trade Financial Services, \nUSA\n\nURL:\n      \n                \nhttp://\n www.us.etrade.com..com\nEnvironment\n\n        \nOracle Applications 11i (GL, AP, AR)\n, SQL.\n\nE*Trade has\n online trading since 1983. E*TRADE FINANCIAL is an S&P 500 company. $187 billion in 4.3 million accounts worldwide. One of the industry\'s highest levels of security, including our E*Trade Complete Protection Guarantee.\nRESPONSIBILITIES:\n\nResponsible for the implementing Oracle General Ledger.\nConducted thorough analysis of the relevant required process flows using Oracle Application Implementation Methodology (AIM) Ver. 3. It included preparing deliverables such as Current business Baseline and Current Architecture etc. to ascertain the existing problems, future business needs and multi-organization issues.\nWorking closely with users to get the requirements and mappings during conversion\nSetting up of cross validation rules between accounting flex field segments, value sets.\nTraining of the users as a part of implementations so that they can use all the available features.\nDefining Set of Books consisting of Chart of Accounts, Calendar and Currencies,\n Combination of accounting flex field Structures, Qualifiers, Segments, Values and Value Sets.\nDefining Calendar Period Types like Monthly, Quarterly, and Yearly.\nAssigning Set of Books for Setting up financial Controls.\nDefining Currency Exchange Rate Types and Rates.\nDefining Journal Categories, Sources for accounting Transactions.\nDefining Mandatory Accounts for Set of books for Suspense Accounts, Retained Earnings. \nDefining roll-up Groups, Summary Accounts and cross validation rules.\nDefining Document Sequences for transaction sequence purpose.\nThe standard tasks performed Oracle General Ledger like Mass Allocation, Mass Budgeting, Recurring journals, reversal of journal entries, foreign currency journals, translation, revaluation, creation of roll-up groups, setting up of cross validation rules \nCreation & Generation of Financial Statement Generator (FSG) Reports like Actual vs. Budgets Reports, Comparative Income Statements, Balance Sheet Reports, etc.\nAssociated with Lance Soft Inc, as Oracle 11i Apps. Functional Consultant from Nov 2004 ?April2006.\nProject #1:\n                                                                                                                            \nOct?05\n-Apr?06.\nProject:\n   \nSupport of\n\nOracle Apps 11i Implementation (AP)\nClient:\n            \n         \nDeserent Books, US.\nEnvironment:\n        \nOracle Applications 11i (AP)\nProfile-Desert Books operates business to customer and business to-business distribution center for books.\n\nRESPONSIBILITIES:\n\nSetting up Financial and Payable Options\nSetup Various Suppliers, Suppliers Sites, bank accounts, pay groups\nSetup various distribution Sets. \nGenerating Vendor Audit Report to get the duplicate suppliers information and merging the duplicate suppliers.\nRunning the unaccounted transaction program to identify the unaccounted entries.\nInvolved in the month end process activities. \nProject #2:\n                                                                                                                            \nNov?04-\n\nSep?05\n                                                                                                                \n\nProject:\n\nSupporting\n of Oracle Financials 11i.\nClient:\n   \n                \nGATI Cargo Management Services, Secunderabad.\nURL:\n      \n                \nhttp://www.gati.com\nGati Limited is a leader in the Express Cargo movement and a pioneer in Distribution and Supply Chain Management solutions in \nIndia\n since 1989. Today its turnover is Rs.3613 million, thanks to the strong team of 6400 dedicated professionals. \n\nRESPONSIBILITIES:\n\n         \nSetting up system options\n\n         \nDefining Invoicing and Accounting rules\n\n         \nDefining Receipt classes and Sources\nDefining Transaction Types, Transaction Sources, Collectors, Approval Limits.\nDefining Statement Cycles, Standard Messages, Dunning Letter Sets, Territories and Salespersons.\nDefining Customer Profile Classes, Customers, remit-to address and customer Relationships.\nEntering manual receipts and applying them to Multiple Invoices. \nCreation of Adjustments against an Invoice.\n\nPERSONAL STRENGTHS:\n\nGood Communication Skills.\nAbility to Work Collaboratively.\nPersistent and\n\nGoal Oriented.',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-16',NULL,'2007-10-16','2010-06-09 12:13:49','2010-06-09',11,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(127,'Ramana M',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL,'0',NULL,'0','2007-04-30',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-09 12:13:49',11,'0',NULL,'200710/16/ATT40688.html','200710/16/DOC40112.doc','Srinivas Resume\nExperience Summary\n\n\n\n       \n3+ years of experience in information technology (IT). \n\n       \nExpertise in manufacturing domain and experienced in modules Order Management (OM), Purchase order (\nPO\n) and Oracle Inventory.\n\n       \nExperience in Customizing Oracle seeded Reports in Oracle Inventory, Purchase Order (PO) and Order Management (OM).\n\n       \nExpertise in Interfaces, Conversions and Data Migration from legacy systems to Oracle Inventory. \n\n       \nExpertise in System Administration and Application Object Library (AOL) to manage concurrent managers, application user setup, defining responsibilities, values sets, flex fields, reports, concurrent programs.\n\n       \nExpertise in using tools like TOAD, SQL*Loader and Reports builder. \n\n       \nExcellent command over SQL, PL/SQL, Oracle Reports. \n\n       \nStrong programming experience in creating Procedures, Packages, Functions, Triggers using SQL and PL/SQL. \n\n       \nAlso experienced in fine-tuning code for better performance. Commitment to excellence proven by an outstanding career track.\n\nDomain expertise: \nManufacturing\n\nTechnical Expertise:\nERP:\nPackages (Incl Versions)\nOracle Applications ? Release 11.5.10, 11.5.5\nModules\nOrder Management (OM), Oracle Inventory (Inv) and Oracle Purchasing (\nPO\n).\nLanguage\nProgramming\n                        \n\nSQL, PL/SQL, \nUNIX-Shell Scripts\nDatabase\nOracle 8i,9i\nGUI\nDeveloper/2000\n(Forms 6i & Reports 6i)\nTools\nTOAD, SQL* LOADER, SQL* Plus, Oracle Forms Builder, Reports Builder, Schema Builder, Procedure Builder, WS-FTP\nMethodology \nAIM ( Application Implementation Methodology)\n\n\nEducation:\n\nDegree/Qualification\nInstitution Name\nB. Tech (Computer Science Engineering)\nS.\nV.\n University, Tirupati, A.P passed in 2003 \n\nEmployment History\n\nCompany Name\nDesignation\nStart date ? End date\nBirla Soft\n\nAssociate Consultant\n\nSep?05\n\nto Till Date\niGate\nSoftware Engineer\nAug?04 \n\nto Aug?05\n\n\n\n\n\n\nProject Details: \n\n1. \nAvago Technologies\n\nProject Description\nAvago Technologies is a spin off company of Agilent Technologies. They are manufacturers of semiconductor products. Avago is aiming at maintaining its own system and database by separating out all data and programs from the current Agilent system to its own. It also aims to implement 11.5.10 instead of the existing 11.5.5 for Agilent. This project aims in migrating objects from 11.5.5 instance to 11.5.10 instance. The project involves compiling of Forms, Interfaces and Reports. \nClient\nOracle \nIndia\nStart and End Date\nNov?06 to Till Date\nRole\nTechnical\nContribution\nDevelopment and Customization of Reports and Conversions \nInvolved in unit testing for Concurrent Programs \nInvolved in unit testing for Database Objects\nInvolved in performance testing of reports\n\nEnvironment\nOracle 11.5.5,11.5.10\nOperating System\nUNIX, Windows XP\nTeam Size\n20\n\n\n\n\n2.\n Oracle Apps Maintenance\n\nProject Description\nMaintenance Project ? As a t\nechnical Consultant, provided post implementation support\nClient\niGate\nStart and End Date\nSep?05 \nto Oct?\n06\nRole\nTechnical\nContribution\nApplication User creation and assigning responsibilities & permissions.\nInterfaces, Forms and Reports registration.\nConcurrent program definitions and executable, creating value sets, registration of forms, reports.\nCreation of Value sets of Independent/Dependent/None and table type.\nRegistering the newly created tables with APPS using API?s AD_DD PACKAGE.\n\nDeveloped various Packages & Procedures.\n\nEnvironment\nOracle apps11i(11.5.8) , Oracle8i\nOperating System\nUNIX, Windows NT\nTeam Size\n10 \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n3.\n Business Model for Retail Banking\n\nProject Description\nBanking, like any other business model has a master business process (i.e. Retail Banking), which is supported by a number of sub processes. The retail banking consists of sub processes like savings account, current accounts, loans, fixed deposits and demat accounts. The project has been developed to deal with all retail banking operations and the external Customer?s services.\n\nClient\nSolar Softech\nStart and End Date\nAug?04 \nto \nAug?05\nRole\nProgrammer\nContribution\n\n         \nDevelopment of Stored Procedures and Functions\n\n         \nWriting code for Data base triggers on Tables\n\n         \nInvolved in creating Tables\n\n         \nDeveloped Reports using Reports 6i\n\n         \nInvolved in unit testing for Database Objects\n\nEnvironment\nSQL, PL/SQL, Forms6i, Reports6i\nOperating System\nWindows 2000\nTeam Size\n20',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-16',NULL,'2007-10-16','2010-06-09 12:13:49','2010-06-09',11,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(128,'S Rama Krishna',NULL,NULL,NULL,'goedefranefeftl@gmail.com',NULL,NULL,'0','91 9916597489','0',NULL,'0','2008-04-29',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-09 12:13:49',11,'0',NULL,'200710/16/ATT40687.html','200710/16/DOC40113.doc','Dear Sir(s),\nS Rama \nKrishna\nefrefk. goedefranefeftl@gmail.com\nMobile\n: +91 9916597489\n\n\nPROFILE:\n\nHaving 2+ years of experience in (Oracle SQL/PLSQL, Forms6i, Reports6i) Development. \nExperience in development / customization of Forms and Reports.\nStrong Experience in developing Inbound and Outbound Interfaces using PL/SQL, SQL* LOADER\nWorked in the modules like Order Processing, Purchase Order, and Inventory Systems.\n\nSKILL SET\n\n\nRDBMS\nORACLE 8i,9i\nOS\nMS DOS, Windows 2000, Windows NT & Unix\nLanguages\n\nSQL, PL/SQL\nTools\nForms 6i, Reports 6i ,Toad,SSH Secure Shell\n\n\nACADEMIC DETAILS\n\n\nB.TECH (Electronics & Control Engineering) from J.N.T.U, 2005, Andhra Pradesh.\n\n\nCAREER OVERVIEW\n\n\nworking as Software Engineer for Tavant \nTechnologies from February 2007 to till date.\n\nWorked as \n\nProgrammer\n in Tavas Infotech\n\n\nBangalore\n from August 2005 to January 2007.\n\n\nEXPERIENCE SUMMARY\n\n\nExperience Distribution\nCountry\nNo. of Years - Months\nNo. of Projects\nOffshore\nIndia\n2 Years\n\n\n\nPROJECT#1:\n\nProject Name: \nToyota CDMS\nClient\n              \n\nToyota Kirloskar Motors Limited\nPeriod\n\n\n February\n 2007 to till date \nIndustry\n         \n\nManufacturing\nProject Type\n\n\nDevelopement\nLocation\n         \n\nBangalore\nEnvironment\n\n\nOracle 9i(SQL, PL/SQL), \nReports6i\n\nRole\n                \n\nDeveloper\n\n\nDescription:\n\nToyota Kirloskar Motors Limited (TKML) is in the business of manufacturing different type of vehicles. There is a need for automation process of marketing activities for decision-making to increase their sales. The customer database management system (CDMS) enables TKML?s existing customer and prospects data in a single system. The system supports for launching various campaign programs for customer/prospect and maintain customer/prospect feedback of it for better decision-making.\n\nResponsibilities:\n\n         \nDeveloped Reports based on the specification i.e. Campaign Creation, Launch Campaign,\n\n\n         \nDeveloped Program Units in Reports.\n\n\n         \nPreparation of System Requirements Specification\n\n\nPROJECCT#2:\n\nProject Name: \nPharmaceutical Automation & Hr Information System.\nClient\n              \n\nDirectorate of Health Services\nPeriod\n\n\n\nJune 2006 to January 2007\nIndustry\n         \n\nFinance/ Human Resource Management.\nProject Type\n\n\nDevelopment\nLocation\n         \n\nBangalore\nEnvironment\n\n\nOracle 9i (sql,pl/sql)\nRole\n                \n\nDeveloper\n\nDescription:\n\nPharmaceutical Automation\n\n                            \nAIM: This Package is only developed for medicine dealers. It maintains the details of various products available with dealers and details of the supplier and details of the sub dealers. This package maintains the stock that is available with the dealers and details like current stock level, stock received and detail transaction carried out\n\nby the dealer are also recorded. The transaction includes the sales of different products, order date, order receipt date and order delivery date and also to maintain material return details. There is also a provision to see particular date?s sales, sale for a month and for a year also. Provision to show details of medicines that are expires, so that the dealer can exchange. Provision to maintain ledger and see balance in the form of report. Billing system is also maintained.\n   \n\nHR INFORMATION SYSTEM\n\n                            \n\nAIM: The HR Information System Application Software has been designed to keep track of the required details of every Employee working under Directorate of Health Services (DHS), including both Official & Medical Staffs. It provides the necessary Employee related information (such as emp. details, their job history, leaves, trainings, etc.) to the authorities of DHS whenever needed by them.\nResponsibilities:\n\nPreparing the Technical Design Documents\nBuilding the Procedures, Functions\nCarried out Unit Tests for the units\nPROJECT#3:\n\n\nProject Name:\n Goods Inwards System (GIS)\nClient\n              \n\nChidambaram Ship care Pvt Ltd\nPeriod\n\n\nAugust 2005 to May 2006\nIndustry\n         \n\n\nManufacturing\nProject Type\n\n\nDevelopment\nLocation\n         \n\nBangalore\nEnvironment\n\n\nOracle 9i(SQL, PL/SQL)\n and Developer 2000 (Forms 6i,Reports 6i)\nRole\n                \n\nDeveloper\n\nDescription:\n\nGoods Inwards System (GIS) is an integrated Module, which covers the activities of Stores, Purchase and Goods Inwards Functions of a Manufacturing Organization. This Module has provisions to capture Supplier Details (Vendors) required for the Purchase Department. It facilitates Stores to check the stock of the Raw Materials used and System automatically places Purchase Requisitions to the Purchase Department. Purchase Department can place Purchase-Orders and keep track of the Work-orders given to the Vendors. When the raw material is received, corresponding Stock is updated. \n\nResponsibilities:\n\nCreation of database tables \n\nPreparation of Program Specifications\n\nDeveloped Program Units in Reports.\n\nDeveloped program units in forms\n\nDefect removal and Regression testing\n\n\n\nTRAININGS UNDERGONE\n\n    \n                                                            \n         \n           \n\nSoft Skills Training like e-mail etiquettes and Client Interaction\n\nFunction Modules like Order Processing, Purcahse Order\n\n\nPERSONAL DETAILS\n\n\nAddress\n                  \n: HNo: 167/2,\n\n                            \n\nNavaneethnivas,\n                             \n\n\nNear Puttappamath,\n                             \n\nNew thippasandra,\n                                \n\nBangalore\n\n\n                            ',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-16',NULL,'2007-10-16','2010-06-09 12:13:49','2010-06-09',11,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(129,'Sachin Rajnikant',NULL,NULL,NULL,'myhedfbgsdfbvdfvgmangi@rediffmail.com',NULL,NULL,'0','91 9987267316','0',NULL,'0','2005-04-29',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-09 12:13:49',11,'0',NULL,'200710/16/ATT40685.html','200710/16/DOC40114.doc','CV\n\n\nSUM\n\n\nSACHIN RAJNIKANT\n\nE-mail: \nmyhedfbgsdfbvdfvgmangi@rediffmail.com\n                   \n          \n\n     \nCell: \n+ 91 9987267316\n\n\nCarrier Objective :\n\n\n          \nTo work in a competitive and challenging work environment which fully utilizes my interpersonal and academic skills and to contribute to the best of my abilities towards the growth and development of progressive company and to pursue a challenging and rewarding career.\n\n\nWork Experience: \n[59 Months]\n\n\n          \nCurrently working with \nZicom Electronic Security Systems Ltd\n., Andheri (E), Mumbai, as \nSr. Engineer ? Software Development\n (from April 11, 2005 till date) \n\n\n\n          \nHad worked with \nAnurag Electronics (\nGujarat\n) Pvt. Ltd\n., Andheri (E), as an EDP Supervisor - (Sep 24, 2004 to Apr 9, 2005)\n\n\n\n          \nHad worked with \nAtul Reprographics\n, Dadar (W), as a VB Programmer ? (Oct 1, 2002 to \nSep 23, 2004\n\n\n\nTechnical Skills:\n\nLanguages\nVisual Basic 6.0\n\nWeb Technologies\nHTML, CSS\n\nOperating System\nWindows XP/2000/2003/98\n\nDatabases\nSQL Server 2000, Oracle, MS Access 2000,Sybase\n\nEducational Qualification:\n\nDegree\nUniversity\nYear\nPercentage\nClass\nB.E. (Computers)\nLokmanya\nTilak\nCollege\n of Engg., Vashi, Navi Mumbai.\n2001\n52%\nSecond\nH.S.C.\nS.I.E.S.\nCollege\n, Sion, Mumbai.\n1996\n77.87%\nDistn.\nS.S.C.\nOur Lady of \nSalvation\nHigh School\n, Dadar, Mumbai.\n1994\n85.28%\nDistn.\n\nMAJOR PROJECTS UNDERTAKEN\n\n#1. ?DEMS\n\n\n\nClient:\nAtul Reprographics.\nProject name:\nData Entry Management System.\n     \nTeam Size:\n\n       \nDuration:\n2 Months\nTechnologies:\nVisual Basic 6.0, MS Word (Visual Basic Editor)\n\nDetails of the Project:\n\n\n          \n\nData Entry Management System contains ?\n                       \n1. \nText formatting\n         \n2. \nTable formatting\n                        \n3. \nImage formatting\n     \n4. Conversion of .doc to .pdf.\nRole\n\n\n\n       \nProject Requirement Specification and Analysis\n\n\n       \nPlanning and Risk Analysis\n\n       \nDevelopment and Coding\n\n       \nDocumentation\n\n       \nBug fixing\n\n       \nUnit & Integration testing\n\n\n\n#2. ?\nHCFA\n\n\n\nClient:\nAnurag Electronics (\nGujarat\n) Pvt. Ltd.\nProject name:\nHealth Insurance Claim Form Application\n     \nTeam Size:\n\n       \nDuration:\n3 Months\nTechnologies:\nVisual Basic 6.0, Oracle 8.0.\n\nDetails of the Project:\n\n          \nThis project was developed for entering data of various people who applied for Insurance claim.\n\n          \nThe basic idea behind this was to fill the details of the people in such a way that the soft copy looked exactly like the hard copy that is the Insurance Claim Form.\n\nRole\n\n\n\n       \nDevelopment and Coding\n\n       \nDocumentation\n\n       \nBug fixing\n\n       \nUnit & Integration testing\n\n\n\n#3. ?Universal 4.0? \n\n\nClient:\nZicom Electronics Systems Ltd.\nProject name:\nUniversal 4.3 Time and Attendance Software\n     \nTeam Size:\n\n       \nDuration:\n3 Months\nTechnologies:\nVisual Basic 6.0, MS Access 2000/SQL Server/Oracle\nDetails of the Project:\n\n\n          \nUniversal 4.0 System Contains \n1.\n      \nMaster setup\n2.\n      \nData Entry module\n3.\n      \nLeave module\n4.\n      \nShift Setup\n5.\n      \nReports module\nMaster module\n\nThe master module will consist of forms for\n\n          \nLocation setup\n\n          \nDepartment setup\n\n          \nGrade entry\n\n          \nEmployee Type details\n\n          \nTeam Name details\n\n          \nCompany setup\nThe Data Entry module consists of\n1.\n      \nMaster Data Entry\n2.\n      \nTour Data Entry\n3.\n      \nManual Data Entry\n4.\n      \nOutdoor Duty Entry\nThe Leave Module consists of\nA.\n      \nLeave codes setup\nB.\n      \nLeave configurations\nC.\n      \nLeave applications\nD.\n      \nCarry forward of leaves\nThe Shift Setup consists of \n1.\n      \nShift Creation\n2.\n      \nShift Pattern Creation\nThe Reports module consists of\na.\n      \nAttendance Report\nb.\n      \nIn/Out Report\nc.\n       \nMuster Report etc.\n\n\n\nPersonal Information:\n\nName:\nMehta Sachin Rajnikant\nD.O.B:\n27\nth\n February 1979\nAge:\n28 years\nGender:\nMale\nNationality:\nIndian\nReligion:\nHindu (Jain)\nMother Tongue:\nGujarati\nAddress:\n42, Ganesh Bhuvan, II Floor, Khed Gully, K.G. Road, Dadar (W), Mum-25\nResidence No:\n+91 22 2431 1668\nCell No:\n+91 \n99872 67316\nLanguages:\nGujarati, English, Hindi, Marathi\n\nCurrent CTC:\n                \nRs. 26,000/- p.m.\n\nCurrent Designation: \n\nSr. Engineer, Software Development.\n\nExpected CTC:\n\nRs. 35,000/- p.m. (negotiable)\n\nNotice Period: 1 month.\n\nReady for Relocation (Y/N): Y.\n\nDate: \n\n20/09/2007\nPlace: \n\nMumbai.\n                                                                                               \n(Mehta Sachin Rajnikant)',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-16',NULL,'2007-10-16','2010-06-09 12:13:49','2010-06-09',11,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(130,'Saji sukumaran',NULL,NULL,NULL,'sasvjvsdavsdavi03@yahoo.com',NULL,NULL,'0','91 9945002222','0',NULL,'0','2006-09-28',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-09 12:13:49',11,'0',NULL,'200710/16/ATT40686.html','200710/16/DOC40115.doc','SAJI SUKUMARAN\n\nS. SUKUMARAN\nEmail\n\nsasvjvsdavsdavi03@yahoo.com\nBangalore\n\nINDIA\nPhone\n: +91 9945002222\n\n\n\nSummary: \nBanking & Financial Analyst / Consultant\n\n\n         \nHolding \n3.6 years\n of experience in Business requirement gathering, Development work flow, gap analysis, and Implementation experience in I.T industry (BFSI Domain).\n\n         \nGood understanding of the \nBanking (\nviz\n\n\nCapital Markets-\nsecurities, derivatives, \nForex\n\nconcepts.\n\n         \nCarried out implementation and enhancement of \nFLEXCUBE\n (Core Banking suite of I-flex).\n\n        \nWorked in \nOracle ERP Applications 11.5.9 (\nviz\n) ACCOUNTS & RECIEVABLE\n; Involved in the integration projects.\n\n        \nInvolved in the \nProduct specific requirements gathering & preparation/review of Functional specifications/Use case artifacts.\n\n        \nInvolved in the development of test cases and executing the test cases.\n\n        \nInvolved in Functional, System and Regression Testing;\n\n        \nInvolvement in all stages of Software Development Life Cycle.\n\n        \nTheoritical expertise on OOAD language standards.\n10\n      \nTheoretical knowledge of C/Java/SQL prog.languages & technologies; RDBMS concepts & Software Engineering terminologies\n11\n      \nPossess excellent academic background in Engineering ? \nInformation Technology\n\n\nWork Experience:\nI-flex solutions Ltd (\nwww.iflexsolutions.com\n\n\nBangalore\n\nJune 05 ? Till date\nGE Consumer & Industrial \n\nBangalore\n) (\nContract-Team lease\n\nApril, 04 ?June 05.\n\n\nEducation\nBachelor of Technology\n\nB.Tech\n) ?Information Technology-2003,\nMadras University\nINDIA\n (73%).\n\n\n\n\n\n\nTechnical skills\nDatabase: Oracle 8i, 9i.\nERP: Oracle \nApplication\n\n\n- business suite11i\nLanguages:\n\nSQL, PLSQL\nOperating Systems: Windows NT/XP\nFront End: Developer 6i.\nScripts: \nHTML\n,Java\n script\n\nProject Experience:\n\nI-flex Solutions Ltd\n                                                                \nJune 05 ? Till date\n\n    \nProjects & Responsibilities:\n\n         \nSecurities Module Enhancement analysis and implementation ?\nKazakhstan\n\n\n         \nFlexcube\n Notional Pooling ? Integrated Liquidity Management (\nSouth Africa\n) Analysis and requirement study. \n\n         \nInterface feasibility study and Analysis of RTGS messages to ILM (IBM liquidity Manager) from \nFlexcube\n\n\n         \nUganda RTGS enhancement.(MT103,MT202) \n\n         \nKenya\n Securities Enhancement (Swift 541 and 543).\n\n         \nMorocco\n teller enhancement (Conditional Archiving and Purging).\n\n         \nImplementation: Citibank Nairobi (Kenya-Onsite);Implementation role out of Securities- Fixed Income, T-bills, Zero coupon bonds,\n    \nILFs\n, Liens.\n\n         \nFlexcube\n Implementation support for SSA cluster. (Offshore)\n\n         \nFlexcube\n Securities Implementation support for Citibank \nEGYPT\n, Citibank \nUkraine\n. (Offshore)\n\n         \nImplementation: Citibank Johannesburg(South Africa-Onsite)\n      \nImplementation role out of Securities- Fixed Income, T-bills.\n\n         \nSecurities Module Enhancement analysis (\nPoland\n).\n10\n      \nIntegrated Liquidity Management Enhancement Support (\nPoland\n).\n\nBroad view of responsibilities undertaken:\n\n\n        \nPerfom\n techno-functional analysis for module development and enhancement.\n\n        \nPerform requirements gathering for modular development/enhancement projects on the Client?s legacy systems\n\n        \nPerform analysis & develop Functional/Design specification documents, based on \nBRDs\n sent in by customer\n\n        \nActive involvement in Product design reviews; Put forward technical suggestions on methodology to be deployed for module development \n\n        \nConsults and coordinates with developers to implement automated solutions; Provide assistance from a functional perspective in identifying, evaluating, and developing systems and procedures\n\n        \nPréparation\n of test case \nscénarios\n & perform smoke tests to ensure product requirements. Facilitate issue resolution including communicating end state solutions to business customers\n\n        \nPerform STP analysis to ensure module integration with Client partner systems.\n\n        \nInvolve in preparation of project deliverables, reports & project-related metrics data\n\n        \nParticipate in providing Product presentations/demos & application training at customer sites to end users.\n\n\n\nGE Consumer & Industrial\n - (Team Lease \nPvt\n Ltd)\n             \nApril, 04 ?June 05\n\nProject\n: GLOBAL CUSTOMER MASTER (GCM) ?Oracle Financial-AR customization of forms & Reports, Interfaces and complete Integration.\nEnvironmen\nt: Oracle Applications 11.5.9/Forms 6i/Reports 6i/Oracle 8i\n\n        \nInterface with GCM.\n\n        \nIntegrating GCM \nwith many Business Unit.\n\n        \nCustomer Addition Globally from single entry point \n\n        \nReport & Form Customization for \nOracle\nAR\n modules.\n\n        \nRole out of integration with all business units of GE.\n\nResponsibilities\n\n        \nInterface study of GCM with ERP - AR.\n\n        \nMaintenance Analysis of GCM Bulk data load using SQL * Loader as well online data addition.\n\n        \nInvolved in Legacy Customer Attribute Mapping with Duns Attribute.\n\n        \nUnit Testing performed thoroughly in order to hit proposed match ratio.\n\n        \nMaintenance of Business Management Portal.\n\n        \nDeveloped PLSQL Scripts for Database Manipulation.\n\n        \nInvolved in Designing Database Setup for corresponding portal.\n\n        \nInvolved in Manual Testing, prepared Test Cases.\n\n        \nInvolved in the Maintenance and Support for Production Roll out of GCM with remaining business of GE C&I.\n\n\n\n\nPersonal Details.\nFull Name: \nSaji\n\nSukumaran\nBirth Date: 03-12-1981\nSex: Male:\nMartial status: Single\nNationality: Indian.\n\nReferences\n\nWill be furnished on request.',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-16',NULL,'2007-10-16','2010-06-09 12:13:49','2010-06-09',11,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(131,'Sakshi T',NULL,NULL,NULL,'kishtcvsacityagi@yahoo.com',NULL,NULL,'0','09888496345','0',NULL,'0','2009-02-27',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-09 12:13:49',11,'0',NULL,'200710/16/ATT40684.html','200710/16/DOC40116.doc','Shweta Agarwal\nSakshi T\nTel: 09888496345 ~ Email: kishtcvsacityagi@yahoo.com\n\nTo utilize my acquired knowledge and experience for the growth of the organisation that provides opportunities for professional and personal growth\n\nProfessional Synopsis\n\n\n     \nSoftware/hardware Test Engineer having 3 years of exp with Infosys Technologies Ltd.\n\n     \nWorked with client, ABN AMRO in \nAmsterdam\n, The \nNetherlands\n on short term basis from Feb ?07 to Apr ?07.\n\n     \nWorking experience of Regression\n testing, Functional/Non-functional testing, Stress/Performance testing, Test\n planning and strategies and Reports.\n\n     \nAccomplished, flexible and results-driven tester in intense pressure and aggressive timelines.\n\n     \nResourceful team player with good interpersonal skills.\n\nAcademia\n\n\n     \nB. Tech. \nin Chemical Engineering from \nM.J.P\nRohilkhand\nUniversity\n\nBareilly\n in 2003 with 83%.\n\n     \nH.S.C \nfrom \nT.R.M\nPublic School\n, Modinagar in 1998 with 75.4%.\n\n     \nS.S.C \nfrom \nRainbow\nSchool\n\nSaharanpur\n in 1996 with 76.6%.\n\nIT Skills \n\nTesting Tools\n               \n          \n\n            \nTest Director, Win runner\nOthers\n                             \n     \n\n    \n          \nUNIX, RDBMS, Sybase, TOAD\n\nOrganisational Experience\n\nClient: ABN AMRO BANK\n      \n          \n              \nTest Engineer\n\n         \n     \n                        \n     \n   \nsince Aug ?06\n\nProject Handled;\n\n     \nAAAMOMGA (OMEGA) \n||\n Minerva Application \n\n   \nMinerva is the Order Management System for new order posting to back offices present in different locations such as \nAmsterdam\n, Luxemburg etc. through Mercator. \n\n    \nTransaction, holdings etc details are taken care by State Street Bank (outsourced to SSB)\n\n\n\n     \nAAAMOMGA (OMEGA) \n||\n FMC Sylvan Application \n\n\nSylvan suite is used to perform performance calculation of portfolio against database.\n   \nThen sylvan reports are generated.\n\n\n\n     \nAAAMOMGA (OMEGA) \n||\n Performance Building Blocks Application \n\n\nA standalone excel VBA application which generates graphical performance building blocks.\n\n\n\n     \nAAAMOMGA (OMEGA) \n||\nEnterprise\n Client Reporting \n- Client reporting is a critical work stream supported by SSB and helps AAM in meeting its client-critical reporting requirements.\n\nThe\n client reports will be made up of smaller units called as Building blocks (including performance building blocks generated from PBB application).\n\nRole;\n\n     \nAnalysis and Documentation.\n\n     \nCreating and maintaining different test scenarios for execution in Minerva.\n\n     \nChecking the different tags sent out from front end application.\n\n     \nPerforming Manual Testing of monthly and quarterly ECR reports.\n\n     \nRegression testing of ECR reports.\n\n     \nGeneration of performance building blocks.\n\n     \nStress testing of PBB application for both quarterly and monthly ECR portfolios.\n\n     \nPerforming manual performance calculation in sylvan application.\n\n\n\nClient: ADIDAS\n          \n       \n                               \n\n    \nTest Engineer\n                                   \n          \nMay?06 ? Jul?06\n\nProject Handled;\n\n\n     \nADHQAPPS (ADIDAS HQ APPLICATION SUPPORT) \n||\n ILS ( International Logistic Systems)\n- Planning engine in the adidas environment and the assignment requires de-linking an existing file based interface from a mainframe (IB) and building an interface to a new Master Data Management application for Supplier information (MDM-S) and then manually testing the whole.\n\nRole;\n\n     \nCreation/modification of Tables and Stored procedures in Sybase. \n\n     \nModifications in Power Builder code.\n\n\n     \nReviewing all business and technical specifications. \n\n     \nIdentify and isolate problems encountered during test execution. \n\n     \nUpdating and maintaining documentation\n\nClient: UBS Investment Bank\n\n     \n          \n     \n     \nTest Engineer\n\n                                 \n     \nMar ?05 ? Arp ?06\n\nProject Handled;\n\n     \nUBQCTM(APAC OFFSHORE QA TESTING) \n||\n Equity Trader(ET) Application\n- The Equity Trader is a Global Client-tool Web-based application for DMA (Direct Market Access) and Worked order flow.\n\nRole;\n\n     \nDaily Build Verification Tests on newly deployed product builds\n\n     \nCreating and maintaining test plans and test cases for the assigned areas\n\n\n     \nDocumenting bugs, Regression testing\n\n     \nStress/Performance testing\n\n     \nDeveloping/Executing Automated Performance\n\nProject Handled;\n\n     \nUBQCTM(APAC OFFSHORE QA TESTING) \n||\n OASIS Application\n- OASIS is UBS Warburg?s global order management system. It?s a key component of the \nEquities Global Execution Engine\n- The system provides complete transparency, life cycle tracking and the ability to handle\n cross border transactions to all Equity sales and trading force across the world.\n\nRole;\n\n     \nDaily Build Verification Tests on newly deployed product builds\n\n     \nCreating and maintaining test plans and test cases for the assigned areas\n\n\n     \nDocumenting bugs, Regression testing\n\n\nExtra-Curricular Activities \n\n\n     \nDeveloped \na POST project on \nLibrary management\n using Visual Basic.\n\n     \nProject in 8\nth\n Semester: \nPlant Design for Manufacturing of Cumene of capacity 2.5 tons/hr \n(Techno-economic feasibility survey) \nMember,\n Seminar:\n\nIndustrial Waste Water Treatment by Solar Detoxification Technology.\n\n\n     \n\nSeminar: Industrial Waste Water Treatment by Solar \nDetoxification\n\nTechnology\n\n\n\nPersonal Profile\n\nDate of Birth\n               \n\n             \n29\nth\n September 1980\nAddress\n            \n          \n\n             \n256/1 Sector-14, Panchkula, Haryana.',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-16',NULL,'2007-10-16','2010-06-09 12:13:49','2010-06-09',11,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(132,'Sanjeev  sharma',NULL,NULL,NULL,'sanjedvdev.shardvdvmadvdv80@rediffmail.com','sanjedvdvev.shardvdvma8v0@yahoo.com',NULL,'0','91 09999891007','0',NULL,'0','2008-04-29',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-09 12:13:49',10,'0',NULL,'200710/16/ATT40683.html','200710/16/DOC40117.doc','Sanjeev kumar Sharma\nSanjeev \n\nSharma\n                                      \n\nSouth Ganesh\n Nagar, Delhi-92\nPhone:\n +91-09999891007 (M.)\n                                                           \nE-Mail: \nsanjedvdev.shardvdvmadvdv80@rediffmail.com\n\nsanjedvdvev.shardvdvma8v0@yahoo.com\n\nSeeking challenging assignments in the field of Software Programming with a technology oriented organization.\n\nAn Overview\n\n\nA self motivated candidate, possessing an MCA degree, with about \n2 year?s\n experience.\n1) NATIONAL INFORMATICS CENTRE, \nNew Delhi\n\nFrom \n\nth\n Jan 2007\n to Till)\nWorking for N.I.C. from 4\nth\n Jan-2007 as a Software Programmer on Project \n?Indian Customs EDI System (ICES)? as an employee of HCL InfoSystem.\n\n2) VRG ELCETRONICS PVT. LTD, New Delhi.\n(From \n\nst\n Jan 2005\n to \n29\nth\n\nDec 2006\n.)\n\n     \nCurrently associated with HCL InfoSystem. Noida as a Software Engineer.\n\n     \nSuccessfully carried out projects like \nDesigning Web Site for the Popcornfurniture\n\nWeb Site development for KDR Groups\n and \nDesign WAP site for downloading the games via micro browser of mobile phones\n to name a few.\n\n     \nA tech savvy individual, competent in a wide array of skills ranging across Unix, oracle, Java, JSP, Servlets, Tomcat Jakarta 5.0.19 etc.\n\n     \nAn energetic, self-motivated team member with hands on experience in programming skills, client-server infrastructure, requirements gathering and application customization.\n\n     \nA team player with strong interpersonal and communication skills, and capability to deliver to full potential even under high pressure situations.\n\nSkill Set\n\nTechnical \nOperating Systems\n                  \n\n           \nUNIX, Windows 98/NT/ 2000.\nLanguages\n                               \n\n          \nC, C++, JAVA.\nWeb Technologies\n                   \n\n           \nServlet 2.3, JSP 2.0\nDistributed Technologies \n        \n\n          \nBasic knowledge EJB 2.0s, RMI and Struts\nMarkup Languages\n                  \n\n          \nHTML, XML.\nApplication Server \n                   \n\n          \nBEA WebLogic Server 8.1.\nWeb Servers\n                            \n\n           \nTomcat \nJakarta\n 5.0.19, 5.5.\nRDBMS \n                                    \n\n          \nOracle 7.2/9i/10g\n\n\nFunctional \n\n       \nInteracting with the clients for system study, requirements gathering and analysis.\n\n       \nActively involved in designing & development & coding.\n\n       \nDesigning and developing the workflow diagrams. \n\n       \nManaging smooth implementation and testing of the application at client location\n\nProfessional Experience\nNATIONAL INFORMATICS CENTRE, \nNew Delhi\n\nIndia\n\n                   \n(Jan \n?07 ? Till)\n\nDatabase Administrator JAN 2007\n ? Till date\n\n\nEnvironment \nSolaris 5.6, Linux, Windows 2000, Oracle 7.2/9i/10g databases, Unix Shell \nScripts, Pro*C, Oracle Forms/Reports/Menu.\n\nProject \nIndian Customs EDI System (ICES)\n\nClient\n Indian Customs, Government of \nIndia\n\n\n\n\nResponsibilities \n\n         \nCreating and maintaining the database.\n\n         \nCreating database objects like tables, procedures, functions, triggers, indexes, views, constraints.\n\n         \nMonitoring alert log/system log.\n\n         \nPerformance tuning using Oracle diagnostics tools and Unix performance monitor tools.\n\n         \nImplement and maintain database security (create and maintain users and roles, assign privileges).\n\n         \nIdentify and resolve ORA errors, OS and database application issues.\n\n         \nPlan database space needs and growth analysis, and future disk need analysis by adding or resizing Datafiles in the Tablespace.\n\n         \nCreate and maintain Backup scripts.\n\n         \nCold and Hot backups of Production Databases.\n\n         \nRefreshing databases by import/export.\n\n         \nComposing and Maintaining shell scripts for the application.\n\n         \nAnalyze application related bugs, issues and implement application updates.\n\n\n\nVRG-Electronics Pvt. Ltd. \nNew Delhi\n\n                                               \n(Jan ?05- Dec ?06)\n\nAs Software Engineer\n\nKey Highlights:\n\n         \nDesigning and developing the company website and WAP site for micro browsers of cell phones.\n\n         \nContributing in providing e-commerce facilities to the company by utilizing MVC.\n\n         \nCarrying out procedures entailing Coding, Testing, Installation and integration of the different modules of static pages and dynamic pages on eApp server (A virtual Sever ?http://support.eapps.com?).\n\n\nProject Purview:\n\n\n    \nDeveloped Web Site for the Popcornfurniture\n\nClient\n                \n\n           \nPOPCORN Pvt. Ltd., \nwww.popcornfurniture.com\n\n\nDuration\n           \n\n           \nJan ?06- Dec ?06\nTeam Size\n         \n\n           \n\nEnvironment\n     \n\n           \nEclipse 3.1(MyEclipse Entrprise Workbench 4.0), XML, Oracle 8i, Tomcat \n                       \n            \nJakarta\n 5.0.19, Servlets, JSP, JDK 1.3.\n   \n\nSynopsis:\n\n          \nThe project is an online shopping portal operating with credit card interaction and is based on template coding.\n\n          \nThe presentation layer in the front end is coupled with the logical programming which facilitates easy integration of front end themes and fast and easy designing changes.\n\n          \nContributed in developing the ?searching module? (product search by word and price) and ?tell a friend? functionality module (by this customer can send mail to a friend of the particular product).\n\n          \nThe system developed makes provisions for placement of orders online and billing through credit card or cheque.\n\n\n    \nDeveloped Web Site for KDR Groups.\n\nClient\n               \n\n           \nKDR Groups Pvt. Ltd., \nwww.kdrgroups.com\nDuration\n           \n\n           \n5 months\nTeam Size\n        \n\n           \n\nEnvironment\n    \n\n           \nEclipse 3.1(MyEclipse Entrprise Workbench 4.0), XML, Oracle 8i, Tomcat \n                    \n            \nJakarta\n 5.0.19, Servlets, JSP, JDK 1.3.\n\nSynopsis:\n\n\n          \nThe site developed makes provisions for making offers for items in which they can negotiate details for as long as they need and will have the option to accept the trade. \n\n          \nThe system developed shows the trade in pending state if both the parties accept it and contact details will be shown to initiate correspondence.\n\n\n    \nDesign WAP site for downloading the games via micro browser of mobile phones.\n\nClient\n               \n\n           \nVRG-Electronics Pvt. Ltd., \nwww.vrgstudio.com\nDuration\n           \n\n           \n2 months\nTeam Size\n        \n\n           \n\nEnvironment\n    \n\n           \nEditPlus2, XML, WML, MySQL Server-4.1.8a, Servlets, JSP, JDK 1.\n\nSynopsis:\n\n         \nOn this site games can be directly down loaded via mobile?s micro browser from the WAP site of the company with the help of JSP and WML from http:// vrgstudio.com:8080/MOB_APP.\n\n         \nThe site also gives the option of uploading the games on it.\n\n         \nThe system is similar to mobile Portal service where a visitor log is being maintained in the database and logs for the game downloaded is also maintained with complete mobile headers. \n\n\n            \n\n\n\n\nInternships & Training\nXorient Technologies, \nNew Delhi\n\n                                                \n(Duration: 6 months)\n\nAs Trainee\n\n          \nTrained in software development which included procedures like Coding, Testing, Installation and integration of the different modules.\n\nEducation\n\n          \nM.C.A from \nRKGIT, \nGhaziabad\n under \nU.P.\nTechnical\nUniversity\n in 2005 from with 72%.\n\nPersonal Details\nDate of Birth\n                \n\n           \nNovember 14, 1980\nPermanent Address\n     \n\n           \nR-826, Adarsh Colony, \nPachenda Road\n, Muzaffar Nagar (U.P.)\nReferences\n                   \n\n           \nTo be produced on request\n           ',NULL,9,NULL,'2007-10-16',NULL,'2007-10-16','2010-06-09 12:13:49','2010-06-09',10,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,9,'0',NULL),(133,'Sarmista ',NULL,NULL,'Bangalore ','Sarmisdaffedfsta09@rediffmail.com',NULL,NULL,'0','9886490757','0',NULL,'0','2009-04-13',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-09 12:13:49',11,'0',NULL,'200710/16/ATT40682.html','200710/16/DOC40118.doc','Sample Resume\n\n\n\n\nSARMISTA\n                                                                 \n     \nSarmisdaffedfsta09@rediffmail.com\n\n                                \n                                                                              \n                 \nCONTACT:+91- 9886490757\n         \n                                                                             \n                  \nSummary\n2.5 yrs of exp in IT industry. Currently working with Accenture Services Pvt. Limited, \nBangalore\n as Software Engineer.\nHave experience in Oracle 9i (SQL, PL/SQL), Shell Scripting on Sun Solaris UNIX 5.8.0.\nProficient on UNIX Commands.\nGood understanding of Software Development Life Cycle and involved in understanding the functionality.\nCoordinating and interacting with team members and development team.\nExcellent Communicator with the ability to deal with issues with precision & accuracy.\nTechnical Expertise\nOperating System\nUnix (Sun Solaris 5.8.0), Windows XP/2000/NT\nLanguages\nC/C++, PL/SQL.\nTechnology\nUnix shell scripts,\nDatabases\nOracle 9i\nTools\nToad\nProfessional Experience\nAccenture Services\n\nPvt. Ltd.\n                                      \nSept 2005 ? Till date\nSoftware Engineer\nProject # 1\nProject Title\n              \n\nRisk Reporting Warehouse\n Managed Services\nClient\n\nUnion Bank of \nSwitzerland\n (Investment Bank).\nDuration\n                    \n\nAug?06 ? Till Date\nTechnologies\n\n9i, SQL, PL/SQL, UNIX, \nAUTO\n_SYS, Informatics, java\nTeam Size\n\n12\n\n\n\nProjects Scope\n   \nUBS and Accenture are working together to create a Managed Service for the Risk Reporting Warehouse (RRW).\n\nThe aim is to create responsive and reliable delivery of Maintenance and Innovation, as well as Level 3 Support for the existing platform.\n\nInvestigation and resolution of production issues that cannot be addressed by Level 1 and Level 2 Support team.\n    \nRole\nCreating Packages, B-tree index, Bitmap Index and using hints FULL, INDEX_JOIN.\nHandling Mutating Table Errors. (Create DML Triggers row level and statement level).\nOptimizing the SQL statements for better performance.\nInvolved in unit testing.\n\nProject # 2\nProject Title\n              \n\nOASIS\nClient\n\nUnion Bank of \nSwitzerland\n\nLondon\n\nUK\nDuration\n                    \n\nOct? 05 ? Jun? 06.\nTechnologies\n\nOracle 9i, SQL, PL/SQL, UNIX, C, C++\nTeam Size\n\n\n\nProject Scope\nThe purpose of this project is to define the role of pre production in managing the prep environment, source code management and automation of prep environment.. The main issues to be highlighted in managing prep environment are processes running in each system, Cron tab files and the processes kicked-off by cron(demon process), Log files and log information, managing command post messages, everyday and weekly systems check list, Debugging the problems, supporting to the development team.\nRole\n\n\n      \nClient requests come as emails, chats, or through phones.\nConstant monitoring of these channels and taking up requests and doing appropriate. Escalation based on criticality and feasibility.\n\n\n      \nMonitoring housekeeping jobs on weekends and making sure they are complete.\n\n\n\n\n\nDSRC Chennai,\n                               \n                             \nFeb 2005 ? Aug 2005\nSoftware Engineer\nProject # 3\nProject Title\n      \n        \n\nCLCP\nOrganization\n\nDSRC\nDuration\n                    \n\nFeb?05 ? Aug?05\n\nTechnologies\n\nOracle, UNIX, Shell Script, C, html\nTeam Size\n\n10\n\nProject Scope\n\nThis project compares the \"last\" and \"close\" prices of all the securities to make sure that the vendor properly process data overnight and makes correct last and close price available for next business day. If the close prices are not correct, applications that use change (= last - close)\n\nwill provide wrong change prices as well as all other calculations dependent on previous day?s close will be wrong. This project makes use of a script which runs at 7:30 AM EST and will report differences between previous day?s last and today?s last/close prices of the security. When there are mismatch securities more than 10 or when the Traded Volume of any of the mismatch securities is greater than a specific value a message is sent to the concerned teams (so as to alert the vendor and get the value corrected before start of Market hrs).It also maintains a record of last 8 weeks with the number of mismatch securities for each day and shown on the front-end using a browser.\nRole\nTeam member involved in analysis, requirements gathering, coding, testing.\n\nInvolved in writing stored procedures.\nWorked in 12 change requests and enhancement modules Privacy Act.\nEducation Qualification\n\n      \nB.E in Electrical & Electronics From NIST,\nBerhampur\nUniversity\n (2003)\n\n      \n+2 SC C.H.S.E Board \n\nfrom \nChrist\nCollege\nCuttack\n\n      \n10\nth\n I.C.S.E Board from \nSunabeda\nPublic School\n, Sunabeda.\n                                        \n        \n                                                                        \nSarmista\n                                                                        \nDate:\n                                             \n                           \nPlace:','Accenture Services Pvt. Ltd',1,NULL,'2007-10-16',NULL,'2007-10-16','2010-06-09 12:13:49','2010-06-09',11,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(134,'Padarthi',NULL,NULL,'Noida','jhsd@yahoo.com','Padefewfarthi.Prefewfasad@birlasoft.com',NULL,'0','09971134289','0',NULL,'0','2007-07-15',10,33,'2010-06-09 12:13:49',11,'0',NULL,'200710/16/ATT40681.html','200710/16/DOC40119.doc','RESUME\nNAME: Padarthi\nContact No:\n 09971134289\nE-mail\n:jhsd@yahoo.com\n   \nOfficial E-mail :Padefewfarthi.Prefewfasad@birlasoft.com\n       \nOracle Apps11i\n Technical Consultant\n______________________________________________________________________________________\n   \n\nExecutive Summary:\n\nHaving 3 \nyears \nof total IT experience, which includes Around \n2 years\n on \nOracle 11i\n\nApplications \nand \n1 Year\n on D2k, Oracle.\n\n\n         \nConversant with modules like Purchase Order. \nAccount Payables, General Ledger, Account Receivables, Order Management. \n\n         \nExtensive experience in writing stored procedures, triggers and very strong in \nPL/SQL. \n\n         \nExtensively worked on \nForms6i, Reports6i.\n\n         \nCapable of working independently and \nas well as a part of a team.\n\n         \nPossess very good communication and interpersonal skills. \n\n         \nSelf-motivated, quick learner, zealous, and diligent.\n\nKey Strengths in Oracle Applications\n\n\n\n         \nDevelopment and customization of \nReports\n and \nInterfaces,\n Forms.\n\n         \nCreation of Value sets in various Modules of the application.\n\n         \nDefining Concurrent Programs, Executables.\n\n         \nPL/SQL method of submitting Concurrent programs.\n\n         \nConcurrent programs, PL/SQL API?s.\n\nEducation \n               \n\n         \nMaster of Computer Applications \nM.C.A\n\nrom\nMadras\nUniversity\n\n\n         \nBachelor of Computer Applications \nB.Com (Computers ) \n\nFrom\n       \nS.V\nUniversity\n\n\n\nTechnical Skills\n\nERP\n\nOracle Apps 11.5.9.(PO,AP,\nOM\n,GL)\nRDBMS\n\nOracle 8i\nFront-end Tool\n\nForms6i\nLanguages\n\nSQL, PL/SQL, C, C++\nReports\n\nReports6i\nTools\n\nToad, SQL*Loader\n\n\n\nEXPERIENCE HISTORY\n\n\n       \nWorking with Birlasoft ,\n\nNoida (From Oct?2006 to Till date) \n\n       \nWorked with Accenture, Chennai (From Jan?2005 to Sep?06) \n\n\n\n\nProjects Profile:\n\nProject #1\n\nClient: Juniper Networks(US)\n   \nTechnical- Consultant (Offshore)\nIn Juniper Networks inside sales creates quote for renewals of IPG and SPG services in SCMC and send it to the customer. In case customer accepts it, customer sends PO to \nOM\n admin. On receiving the PO, Order admin retrieve the quote in pre-entered screen and Verifying line information, changes the bill to, ship to and end user at header level to match the \nPO\n. And push the order in \nOM\n as enter status.\nThe other information in the \nPO\n is based on the quote. As per the PO the Order is created in the \nOM\n and quote id information is also maintained with the Order to relate the Order with Quote\n\n\nWorked on data conversion, interface development and reports development implementing Oracle Applications 11i \nWorked on the interface customization and reports (6i and SQL). Developed several \nOM\n reports using SQLPLUS. \n\n\nReports:\n\n\n         \nDeveloped Goods Receipt Report.\n   \n\n         \nDeveloped Purchase order and Payables analysis report\n\n         \nDeveloped Purchase order and receipts detail report.\n\n         \nCustomized RFQ report.\n\n         \nDeveloped\n\nCustomer analysis report.\n\nOutbound Interfaces:\n\nDeveloped Items On-Hand quantity outbound interface to transfer the data from Oracle Apps base tables to the flat file using the UTL_FILE Package.\n\nInbound Interface:\n\nDeveloped requisitions Interface to import the data from flat file to the Oracle Apps Requisitions base tables using the SQL*LOADER.\n\n\nProject\n #2\n\nClient: Pfizer (Efss)\n       \n(Accenture)\nTechnical- Consultant (Offshore)\n\nPfizer are the largest Pharmaceutical company in the world with a strategy to go ?beyond number one?.Provide Pfizer with a more flexible option for merger integration.The EFSS (European Financial Shared Services) involves creation of single service centre for Europe based in \nDublin\n. Pfizer have build a green-field site in \nDublin\n with mostly new employees\n\nPfizer is currently in the process of \nOracle 11i ? PO, AP,GL, \nOrder Management\n, Inventory, HRMS : Application Interfacing Solution, Concur : Travel & Expenses,Automatic Call Distribution and Call Logging, Document Imaging Tool .\n\n\n\n\nResponsibilities:\n\nThis is Developing and Supporting\n   \nProject in the \nProvided support in day-to-day software issues and developments of new requirements. \nInvolved in customizing Reports and Interfaces.\nCreation of Responsibilities ,Creation of new Users\nCustomizing DFF as per client requirement.\nCustomizing report Formatting and assigning Value Sets\n\nReports:\n\n\n         \nDeveloped \nPO\n Analysis Report.\n\n         \nDeveloped Inventory Valuation Report.\n\n         \nDeveloped Material Receipt Data \n\n         \nDeveloped\n\nNew Customer Statement Report.\n\n         \nDeveloped Vendor Delivery Report.\n\n\n   \nInbound Interface:\nDeveloped requisitions Interface to import the data from flat file to the Oracle Apps Requisitions base tables using the SQL*LOADER\nProject # 3\n\nClient\n            \n: Novartis-Rekha Corps\nRole\n              \n: Software Engineer\nEnvironment: Oracle, D2k\n\nDescription\n      \nDesigning and developing the Ebiznet warehouse Manager System for Novartis-Rekha Corps. This system delivers the basic functionality of an integrated WMS specifically suited to manufacture operations with an integrated Manufacture Billing Module. These functions include\n\nResponsibilities\n\nDeveloping and Debugging of Forms and Reports.\nDeveloping and Debugging of Triggers and Packages.\nCustomization of Reports.\nData Conversion using SQL * Loader.\nProject # 2\n\nTitle\n                  \n: MATERIAL ACCOUNTING SYSTEM\nRole\n                  \n: Software Engineer\nEnvironment\n    \n: Oracle, D2k \n\nThis system monitors the material movements at different stages. The material storage details such as location bin card details are provided by the system for proper control and co ordination. Further this system generates the following reports.\nWork Order and department wise material consumption report.\nA B C classification report. Receipt and Issues during the month and year & Stock Status report. Summary Ledger for the year which is also used for audit purpose.\n\nResponsibilities\n\nInvolved in the design and development of Issues module. Created views, database triggers and PL/SQL programs to validate and maintain stock status.','Birlasoft',1,NULL,'2007-10-16',NULL,'2007-10-16','2010-06-09 12:13:49','2010-06-09',11,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(135,'Ramesh sonkusre',NULL,NULL,NULL,'sosdcsace@gmail.com',NULL,NULL,'0','731 9893175181','0',NULL,'0','2007-04-30',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-09 12:13:49',2,'0',NULL,'200710/16/ATT40680.html','200710/16/DOC40120.doc','Resume\n\nC/O Mr. Mohan Roy, 19-Giridhar Nagar\nIndore\n(Madhya Pradesh) -\nIndia\nTelephone: (Res.) 91+731+9893175181\nEmail: sosdcsace@gmail.com\n\n\n\nObjectives\n\n\n       \nAttain a challenging position in Web Promotional activities.\n\n\n       \nBring out the best within me and utilize it to serve the Industry.\n\n\nProfessional Summary\n\n\n       \nSEO Experience: 3 years.\n\n\n       \nCurrent Designation: Sr. Internet Marketing Specialist\n\n\nEducation\n\n\n       \nM.Sc.\n\nMathematics from \nAmravati\nUniversity\n\nMaharashtra\n (Pursuing).\n\n\n       \nB.Sc.\n\n(Computer Science)\n   \nfrom \nAmaravati\nUniversity\n\nMaharashtra\n in 2004.\n\n\n\nProfessional Experience\n\nCurrently working as \nSr. Internet\n Marketing Specialist\n in \nGatesix Technologies India Pvt. Ltd\n. ,\n Based in \nIndore\n (Madhya Pradesh).\n\nWorked as \nSEO Expert\n in\n\nD?zine Garage Pvt Ltd.\n based in Chennai (Tamilnadu).\n\n\nEmployment History\n\nDecember 2005 to still the date as a \nSr.\n\nInternet Marketing Specialist.\n\n\nJuly 2005 to December 2005 as a \nSearch Engine Optimization Expert\n\n\n\n\nResponsibilities\n                                                                                                                                                                            \nResponsible for all search engine optimization related activities along with other Internet marketing activities like Pay per Click Campaigning, email campaigning, web analytic reports, Post-launch activities, Manual site submissions to different search engines and other industry specific Directories, Link Exchanges, Interlinking strategy, keyword research and Inbound linking.\n\n\n\n\nProjects\n         \n\n       \nAmCheck\nURL- \nhttp://www.amcheck.com/\n\nCountry-\nUnited States of America\n\nDescription- Company is providing the Human Resource solutions and Payroll Services\n\nRole - Optimize the site, blogs submission, article submission, directory submission, reciprocal link exchanges, forums and group?s discussions, web analytics, Pay per Click campaigning, custom IM reporting.\n\nAchievement- Site is ranking on #1 position for the keyword ?Payroll Services? , good conversion rate according to Pay per click campaigning.\n\n\n\n\n       \nBusiness ware Services Inc.\nURL- \nhttp://www.bwsi.com/\n\nCountry-\n\nnited States of America\n\nDescription- Company is providing staffing agency software for Employment\n\nRole - Optimize the site, directory submission, reciprocal link exchanges, forums, web analytics, and custom IM reporting.\n\n\nAchievement- Strong back links and site is ranking on top 10 positions for main keywords.\n\n\n\n\n       \nLuminati\nURL- \nhttp://www.luminati.net/\n\nCountry-\nUnited States of America\n\nDescription- Company is related to \nTours\n and Travels\n\nRole - Optimize the site, search engine submission, directory submission, and reciprocal link exchanges.\n\n\nAchievement- Site is ranking good on the entire top search engine.\n\n\n\n\n       \nRoyal \nEnfield\nURL- \nhttp://www.royalenfield.com/\n\nCountry - \nIndia\n\nUnited Kingdom\n\nDescription- Company is dealing with bikes for leisure riding.\n\nRole - Optimize the site, search engine submission and directory submission.\n\nAchievement- Site is ranking good on every keyword.\n\n\n\n       \nAshok Leyland\nURL - \nhttp://www.ashokleyland.com/\n\nCountry ? \nIndia\n\nDescription- the Company is manufacturer of trucks, buses and Auto.\n\nRole - Optimize the site, search engine submission and directory submission and web analytics.\n\nAchievement- Site is ranking good on every keyword.\n\nGot the conversions through the site.\n\n\n\n\n       \nICICI Bank \nUK\nURL- \nhttp://www.icicibank.co.uk/\n\nCountry-\nUnite