00\nOperating systems:\n\n                         \nWindows (XP, 2000, Server 2003)\n                          \nLinux\n Red hat, \nRHES 3.0\n\n\nHardware & Networking:\n                        \nAssembling, Troubleshooting & Maintaining PC\n\n                       \nAble to design, plan, implement and manage a small\n                                                                               \n                        \nNetwork of 100 nodes. \n\n\n\n\nPersonal Information:\n\nName\n                         \n            \n\n\nMahammed Amir.A.G\n\nFather?s Name\n                       \n\n Abdul Aziz\n\nAge & Date of Birth\n               \n: 21\n years, 3\nrd\n Sep 1986.\n\nLanguages known\n                 \n\n English, Kannada, Hindi, Tamil, Urdu.\n\nHobbies & Interests\n              \n\n Listening Music, Chatting, Volleyball.\n\nNationality\n                             \n\n Indian\n\nPermanent Address:\n\nMahammed Amir .A.G\n                                             \n     \nEmail ID:\naamir63@gmail.com\nS/O Abdul Aziz\nNo-21/16 3\nrd\n cross \nChristian colony Ghantikery\nHubli-560020\nPh: 0836-2261332\n   \n                                 \nKarnataka.\n\n\n\nI here by declare that information furnished above is true to best of my knowledge and belief.\n\nPLACE:\nBangalore\n\nDate:\n                                                          \n\n                                                                 \n       \nSignature\n\n(MahamedAmir.A.G)','NTTF Industries Limited ',1,NULL,'2007-10-17',NULL,'2007-10-17','2010-06-09 12:13:49','2010-06-09',12,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(139,'Neelima  K',NULL,NULL,NULL,'knefbfdbelima.sfbfbiebel@gmail.com','kneelima.siebel@gmail.com',NULL,'0','9986453868','0',NULL,'0','2007-04-30',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-09 12:13:49',2,'0',NULL,'200710/17/ATT22606.html','200710/17/DOC15313.doc','Resdex @ naukri.com\nNeelima\n\n\nknefbfdbelima.sfbfbiebel@gmail.com\n\nTelephone: 9986453868\n(M)\n\nD.O.B\n - 05 Aug 1980 \nModified on\n - 26 Sep 2007 \nAnnual Salary\n - INR 3 Lac(s) 75 Thousand \nTotal Years of Experience\n - 3 Year(s) 1 Month(s) \nCurrent Location\n\nBangalore\n\nPreferred Location\n - Anywhere in \nIndia\nBsc with 3+ years exp. as Siebel Configurator\n\nTEXT RESUME \n\nNeelimaReddy Kola E-mail: kneelima.siebel@gmail.com Call-me@ 91-9986453868\nExperience Summary:\nA strongly motivated professional having 3 years as total IT Experience and\n2 years of experience in Seibel with\nØ Experience in configuring Siebel 7.7/7.8 Versions.\nØ Hands on Experience in Siebel configuration, Scripting.\nØ Knowledge in EIM.\nØ Good communication and presentation skills.\nØ High motivation in learning and mastering new technologies in short span.\nØ Performing Unit testing involved in functional testing.\nØ Good Team Player with interpersonal skills.\nEducation:\nBSc (Computers) from \nS.V.\nUniversity\n with 82% in 2003.\nSkill \n? Set Summary:\nØ Siebel Tools Configuration (V7.7, 7.8)\nØ Siebel Scripting.\nØ EIM\nApplication Worked \n? On:\nØ Siebel Financial Services 7.8 (Technical)\nØ Siebel Emedia v7.8\nSkills:\nCRM Package : Siebel 7.7X, Siebel 7.8X.\nLanguages : C, C++, JAVA, COBOL\nWeb Technologies : JAVA Script, XML, HTML and DHTML\nOperating Systems : Windows 9x/NT/2000/XP/2003\nDatabases : Oracle, SQL Server and MS Access.\nOOAD Languages : UML Using Rational Rose\nWork Experience:\nWorking as a Siebel Consultant in IBM, \nBangalore\n since August 2005 till date.\nWorked as a Java Developer for Imbue Consulting Services from May 2004 till May 2005\nProject Experience:\n1. Current Project : Reuters - \nUK\nClient : IBM.\nDuration : 7 months\nProduct : Siebel Media\nTeam Size : 30\nTechnologies : Siebel 7.8, Oracle\nRole : Siebel Configurator\nProject Description:\nReuters is a global information company providing indispensable information tailored for professionals in the financial services, media and corporate markets. Millions of consumers see and hear news from Reuters in the world\'s media and over 300,000 financial professionals across the globe each day receive market data, in-depth news, quotes, statistics and analytics on financial and commodities markets from Reuters. We are the largest financial information provider in the world\nRoles and Responsibilities:\n1. Configured Joins, Links and Pick lists.\n2. Created User Properties at Applet and BC level.\n3. Configured and modified Screens, Views, and List Applets, Toggle Applets.\n4. Configured Dynamic, Static Drill downs\n5. Extending Data Base Schema by creating custom extension columns.\n6. Created User Properties in Applet and BC level.\n7. Performed Unit testing.\n2. Project : Rabobank - \nNetherlands\nClient : IBM\nDuration : 12 Months\nProduct : Siebel Financial Services\nTeam Size : 12\nTechnologies : Siebel 7.8, SQL Server\nRole : Siebel Configurator\nProject Description:\nRabobank, Centralized bank in, \nNetherlands\n, having 218 member banks, which does co-operative banking and act as a banker\n?s bank in \nNetherlands\n, of dealing with Payment and Savings Products. The main objective is to have a high Customer value\nRoles and Responsibilities:\n1. Configured Joins, Links and Pick lists\n2. Configured Hierarchical Pick List, Toggle Applets\n3. Configured MVG\n?s\n4. Created User Properties at Applet and BC level\n5. Configured and Customized Screens, Views, and Applets\n6. Configured Dynamic, Static Drill downs\n7. Written Script at Applet, Business Component Level\n8. Implementation of Data Validation manager as part of validating the fields without writing the script.\n9. Implemented Assignment manager.\n10. Implemented Workflow Manager.\n11. Defined organization hierarchy and created responsibilities and positions using Application Administration.\n12. Performed Unit testing.\n3. Project: Distributed Channel Management\nClient : Propest Company Ltd\nOrganization : Imbue Solutions Pvt Ltd\nDuration : 6 Months\nTeam Size : 9\nTechnologies : Tomcat, JSP, Html, Java Script and Oracle.\nRole : Developer\nDescription:\nThe Distribution Channel Management system is a web-based system, designed for Propest Co. ltd, which gives information relating to the clients and dealers of the company with respect to its pesticides product launches. This product develops a system that can be used by the company management to keep track of the sales, dealers and its clients. In the existing method of tracking of all the details is tedious and time consuming. Any product survey and launching of the area carried out manually by representatives, which is a time taking task.\nIt fulfills different requirements of management, client and dealers of the company. The specific purpose of the system is to automate the communication between the management, clients and the dealers of the organization. The key entities of this system are company management / administration department, employees, dealers and clients. The activities relating to this system are listing of various dealers of the company, its branches, its clients and providing expertise suggestion on the usage of the product, update product, providing instructions to the dealers and many additional tasks, which supplement the above functions.\n4. Project : Insurance Management System\nDuration : 3 Months\nTeam Size : 2\nTechnologies : J2EE, JSP, JDBC and Oracle 9i.\nRole : Designing, Coding & Documentation.\nProject Description:\nThis Project has 3 Modules, which are the Heart of the Insurance Management Company. They are Agent, Administrator and Policy Holders.\nAgent is the person who acts like a Bridge between the People and Insurance Company. Administrator is responsible, for the events that go in the company. Policy Holder takes Policies from the Insurance Company to him/ his Family /his Things etc.\nPersonal Details:\nName : NeelimaReddy Kola\nFather\n?s Name\n : K.P.Reddy\nDate of Birth : 08-05-1983\nGender : Female\nMarital Status : Un-Married\nLanguages Known : English, Telugu, and Hindi.\nNationality : Indian.',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-17',NULL,'2007-10-17','2010-06-09 12:13:49','2010-06-09',2,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(140,'Ramesh.Nalem',NULL,NULL,NULL,'rasscsacmesacsh.nalem@gmail.com','amesh.nscscscalem@sify.com',NULL,'0','091 9848863665','0',NULL,'0','2007-04-30',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-09 12:13:49',12,'0',NULL,'200710/17/ATT22605.html','200710/17/DOC15314.doc','RESUME\nRESUME\nCURRENT ADRESS:\nRamesh.Nalem\nH.No. 2-3-64/5/C,\nOpp.Amberpet Police Station,\nThirumala Nagar\n                                                                   \nE-mail: \nrasscsacmesacsh.nalem@gmail.com\nHyderabad\n\n                                                                           \n            \n\namesh.nscscscalem@sify.com\n\n\n                                                                                               \nPhone No: +091-9848863665.\n\nOBJECTIVE:\n\n                \nTo pursue a challenging long-term career in ORACLE APPS. To be a part of winning team of a professionally managed organization and to use my knowledge and experience in leading and implementing innovate and quality oracle ERP products and to continuously update my self with the latest ERP new dimensional products.\nSUMMARY:\n\n\n         \nAround 3 years \nof functional experience in Oracle Financial- 11i\n\n\n         \nGot ?Best Performance year of the Award? from Genpact\n\n         \nHolding B1 Visa from Genpact.\nFunctional responsibilities have included business process analysis, requirements gathering and Analysis.\nExperience in developing statements of functional overviews, business processes, and other documentation to facilitate users? acceptance. \n\nGood Analytical, Problem-Solving skills.\nGood leadership and project management skills.\nGood exposure to interacting with clients.\nAbility to learn new skills quickly.\nHave good team spirit, which has helped me understand the group requirements, and plan the project accordingly. My analytical skills also helped me analyzing problems and faster decision-making.\nACADEMIC QUALIFICATIONS:\nMBA- with the specialization of IT-Finance in International Institute of Information Technology, Pune\nBachelor of Science in \nS.R.R.Govt\nDegree\nCollege\n\nKakathiya\nUniversity\n\nWarangal\n, and AP.\nIntermediate- Alphores Jr.\nCollege\n, Board of intermediate, Andhra Pradesh.\nS.S.C- Z.P.S.S, Regadimaddikunta, Karimnagar.\nTECHNICAL EXPOSURE:\n                \n                                            \n                    \nFunctional: \n                           \nOracle Financial Applications 11i (\nGL\n\nAR\n, AP). \nPlatforms:\n          \n    \nWindows 98/XP, Unix.\n   \n                                                     \n                                                                      \nDBMS: \n            \n   \n                \nOracle 8i, PL/SQL\n                          \n    \n                   \n                                         \n       \n      \nOperating Systems:\n             \nWindows 95 & 98, Windows NT.\n                                                     \n                                \nIT Tools: \n                               \nMS Project 2000.\n\n                \n\nWORK EXPERIENCE:\n\nORACLE FINANCIALS:\n\nAssociated with Genpact, \nHyderabad\n, as Oracle 11i Apps. Associate Functional Consultant from May 2006 to till date.\n\nProject #1:\n             \n                                                                                                               \nDec?06-Cont.\n\nProject: \n                \nSupporting\n of Oracle Financials 11i\n\nClient:\n   \n                \nGE Commercial Finance.\n\nEnvironment\n\n        \nOracle Applications 11i ?GL, AP and \nSQL.\n\nRESPONSIBILITIES:\n\nI have defined the COA in all instances of Oracle Applications.\nCreated Financial Statement Generator (FSG) reports for the company. Developed FSG reports on Balance Sheet, Combined and departmental Statement of Operations/Income Statement and other reports.\nProvided Post implementation support in GL, AP\nProject work that involves co-ordination with the TCS&Project teams for data conversions, interfaces, data extraction etc.\nI ran the Discoverer reports and tallied with the FSGs\nI ran the FRS Program and Interface reports.\nDefine Accounting Flexfield Structure, Define Security Rules, Assign Security Rules Setup, Define Cross-Validation Rules, Define Period Type.\nUploaded the journals by using the Web-ADI Templates\nDeleted, Posted, reversed the Journals as per the client reuquest.\nRun the Auto Approval journal program to the approve the journal batches.\nSet up the Auto post.\nProject #2:\n                                                                                                                            \nMay?06-Dec?06.\n\nProject: \n                \nImplementation of Oracle Financials 11i (GL)\nClient:\n   \n                \nE*Trade Financial Services, \nUSA\n\nURL:\n      \n                \nhttp://\n www.us.etrade.com..com\nEnvironment\n\n        \nOracle Applications 11i (GL, AP, AR)\n, SQL.\n\nE*Trade has\n online trading since 1983. E*TRADE FINANCIAL is an S&P 500 company. $187 billion in 4.3 million accounts worldwide. One of the industry\'s highest levels of security, including our E*Trade Complete Protection Guarantee.\nRESPONSIBILITIES:\n\nResponsible for the implementing Oracle General Ledger.\nConducted thorough analysis of the relevant required process flows using Oracle Application Implementation Methodology (AIM) Ver. 3. It included preparing deliverables such as Current business Baseline and Current Architecture etc. to ascertain the existing problems, future business needs and multi-organization issues.\nWorking closely with users to get the requirements and mappings during conversion\nSetting up of cross validation rules between accounting flex field segments, value sets.\nTraining of the users as a part of implementations so that they can use all the available features.\nDefining Set of Books consisting of Chart of Accounts, Calendar and Currencies,\n Combination of accounting flex field Structures, Qualifiers, Segments, Values and Value Sets.\nDefining Calendar Period Types like Monthly, Quarterly, and Yearly.\nAssigning Set of Books for Setting up financial Controls.\nDefining Currency Exchange Rate Types and Rates.\nDefining Journal Categories, Sources for accounting Transactions.\nDefining Mandatory Accounts for Set of books for Suspense Accounts, Retained Earnings. \nDefining roll-up Groups, Summary Accounts and cross validation rules.\nDefining Document Sequences for transaction sequence purpose.\nThe standard tasks performed Oracle General Ledger like Mass Allocation, Mass Budgeting, Recurring journals, reversal of journal entries, foreign currency journals, translation, revaluation, creation of roll-up groups, setting up of cross validation rules \nCreation & Generation of Financial Statement Generator (FSG) Reports like Actual vs. Budgets Reports, Comparative Income Statements, Balance Sheet Reports, etc.\nAssociated with Lance Soft Inc, as Oracle 11i Apps. Functional Consultant from Nov 2004 ?April2006.\nProject #1:\n                                                                                                                            \nOct?05\n-Apr?06.\nProject:\n   \nSupport of\n\nOracle Apps 11i Implementation (AP)\nClient:\n            \n         \nDeserent Books, US.\nEnvironment:\n        \nOracle Applications 11i (AP)\nProfile-Desert Books operates business to customer and business to-business distribution center for books.\n\nRESPONSIBILITIES:\n\nSetting up Financial and Payable Options\nSetup Various Suppliers, Suppliers Sites, bank accounts, pay groups\nSetup various distribution Sets. \nGenerating Vendor Audit Report to get the duplicate suppliers information and merging the duplicate suppliers.\nRunning the unaccounted transaction program to identify the unaccounted entries.\nInvolved in the month end process activities. \nProject #2:\n                                                                                                                            \nNov?04-\n\nSep?05\n                                                                                                                \n\nProject:\n\nSupporting\n of Oracle Financials 11i.\nClient:\n   \n                \nGATI Cargo Management Services, Secunderabad.\nURL:\n      \n                \nhttp://www.gati.com\nGati Limited is a leader in the Express Cargo movement and a pioneer in Distribution and Supply Chain Management solutions in \nIndia\n since 1989. Today its turnover is Rs.3613 million, thanks to the strong team of 6400 dedicated professionals. \n\nRESPONSIBILITIES:\n\n         \nSetting up system options\n\n         \nDefining Invoicing and Accounting rules\n\n         \nDefining Receipt classes and Sources\nDefining Transaction Types, Transaction Sources, Collectors, Approval Limits.\nDefining Statement Cycles, Standard Messages, Dunning Letter Sets, Territories and Salespersons.\nDefining Customer Profile Classes, Customers, remit-to address and customer Relationships.\nEntering manual receipts and applying them to Multiple Invoices. \nCreation of Adjustments against an Invoice.\n\nPERSONAL STRENGTHS:\n\nGood Communication Skills.\nAbility to Work Collaboratively.\nPersistent and\n\nGoal Oriented.',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-17',NULL,'2007-10-17','2010-06-09 12:13:49','2010-06-09',12,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(141,'Malli M',NULL,NULL,NULL,'malflsdfsdafi.idednformatica@gmail.com',NULL,NULL,'0','09921107133','0',NULL,'0','2007-04-30',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-09 12:13:49',2,'0',NULL,'200710/17/ATT22604.html','200710/17/DOC15315.doc','Resdex @ naukri.com\nMalli.m\nmalflsdfsdafi.idednformatica@gmail.com\n\nTelephonse: 09921107133\n(M)\n\nD.O.B\n - 06 Aug 1983 \nModified on\n - 26 Sep 2007 \nAnnual Salary\n - INR 3 Lac(s) 50 Thousand \nTotal Years of Experience\n - 3 Year(s) 2 Month(s) \nCurrent Location\n - Pune \nPreferred Location\n - Anywhere in \nIndia\nMalli Informatica 3+ Yrs Of Exp',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-17',NULL,'2007-10-17','2010-06-09 12:13:49','2010-06-09',2,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(142,'Mahua Ghosh',NULL,NULL,'Kolkata','mahdvdsvua_g25dvgd@yahoo.com',NULL,NULL,'0','09331261894','0',NULL,'0','2007-09-12',10,34,'2010-06-09 12:13:49',12,'0',NULL,'200710/17/ATT22602.html','200710/17/DOC15316.doc','                                                \n           \nMahua Ghosh \n                                                \n\nEmail: \nmahdvdsvua_g25dvgd@yahoo.com\n                                                \n         \nPhone: 09331261894\n\n\n\nSUMMARY:\nMahua works as a Programmer Analyst with \nCognizant Technology Solutions\n on Sybase PL/SQL in the Banking and Financial Service (BFS) Domain and has a professional experience of \n2.5\n\nyears plus\n. She is also an \nOracle Certified Associate (OCA)\n on the Developers Track.\nHer experience profile includes: \nSystem Analysis\n\nCoding, Unit Testing, System Test planning and testing. \nProject Management, Quality Initiatives \n\nEMPLOYMENT HISTORY: \n\nName of the Company\nDesignation\nAddress of the employer\nFrom\nTo\nDuration \n\nCognizant Technology Solutions\n\nProgrammer\nAnalyst\nGN 34/3, \nSalt\nLake\n, Sector 5, Kolkata? 91\nMarch 2005\nPresent\n30 months + \n\nTECHNICAL SKILLS\n\nDatabases \nPL ?\nSQL\n\nMS\n-SQL ,ORACLE 9i,SYBASE \nBug tracking tool\nE-Tracker, \nProlite\nOperating System\n            \n2003 Server, DOS, Basic Knowledge of Linux\nProgramming Languages\nC++, Java, Advanced Java, HTML\n\nEXTRA QUALIFICATION\n\n1 Yr Diploma (DIT) on GNIIT track\nSoftware Engineering, NIIT\n\n\nEDUCATIONAL QUALIFICATION\n\nMCA\nPursuing 6\nth\n Semester\n\nfrom \nSikkim\n\nManipal\n\n2007\nBachelor of Science(Chemistry Major)\nSt. Xavier?s College, Kolkata.\n                 \n57.4%\n2004\nHigher Secondary Examination(\nXIIth\n\nCBSE, \nDELHI\n74%\n2001\nSecondary Examination(\nXth\n\nCBSE,\nDELHI\n83%\n1999\n\n\n\n\n\nProject Profile\nProject Title\nHealth & Welfare Business Analysis\nVertical\nBanking & Financial Services\nClient\nACS HRIS(\nAffliated\n Computer Services Human Resources & Investor Services)\nDuration\nMarch 2005 till present\nRole\nModule lead.\n\nPROJECT DESCRIPTION: \nACS HRIS (ACS Human Resources & Investor Services) is engaged in the Benefits Administration domain where it gives services to its various clients like Lockheed Martin, Morgan Stanley, Chevron, Delta Airlines, \nPriceWaterHouse\n Coopers etc. \nThe engagement scope for the project involves Business & System analysis for the Health & Welfare sub-domain in the Benefits Admin area where Cognizant is engaged in new client implementation, existing client servicing and implementing strategic technical initiatives.\nROLES AND RESPONSIBILITIES IN THE PROJECT: \n\nDesign and construction of applications\n: Designing the application according to customer business requirement for new client implementation. Develop technical specifications involving Health & Welfare discipline (translate high level requirements into detailed technical requirements. \n\nDeveloping the code in \nSybase :\n\nApplication is coded in Sybase. We are involved in updating the application as per client requirements which involves writing Stored Procedures, Cursors and other PL/SQL units. We do this for new client as well as for existing clients. \n\nManaging all\n\nquality related work:\n Includes invoice generation for billing to client using tools like \nEtracker\n , project planning where we do resource planning and also preparing effort estimation for\n\ntimed delivery and preparing documents for quality audits for the account.\n\nSystem Test planning and execution. \nWe are involved in Unit test and System test case preparation where we do test case scenario identification, Data preparation. After Code is developed we also do system testing and integration testing.\n\n               \nAchievements in Cognizant Technology \nSolution\n\nand\n others\n1.\n       \n  \nCognizant Certified Professional (CCP) in Banking and Financial domain\n2.\n          \nOracle Certified Associate OCA\n\n(Developers Track)\n    \nPersonal Profile\nDate of Birth\n   \n     \n   \n\n            \n    \n: 25-Dec-1982\nSex \n                                        \n   \n\n: Female.\nMarital Status\n                     \n    \n: Unmarried','Cognizant Technology Solutions ',1,NULL,'2007-10-17',NULL,'2007-10-17','2010-06-09 12:13:49','2010-06-09',12,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(143,'Naveen C D',NULL,NULL,NULL,'navscvdacveenchanvdsdrad@gmail.com',NULL,NULL,'0','91 9840850007','0',NULL,'0','2007-11-28',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-09 12:13:49',12,'0',NULL,'200710/17/ATT4915.html','200710/17/DOC15317.doc','                                                \nNaveen C D\n                                               \n   \nMobile\n: +91-9840850007\n                             \n          \n     \n     \n     \n     \n\n      \nEmail: \nnavscvdacveenchanvdsdrad@gmail.com\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nObjective:\n\n\no be associated with a progressive organization that gives me scope to update my knowledge and skills in accordance with latest trends and be a part of team that dynamically works towards the growth of the organization and gains satisfaction.\n\nProfessional Experience (27+ Months):\n\nWorking as Software Consultant at 3i-Infotech (formerly called as ICICI INFOTECH), Chennai from Dec 2006 to Till Date.\nWorked as Technical Consultant at Arral Technologies, \nHyderabad\n from Jul 2005 to Nov 2006.\n\n\nTechnical Skills:\n\nProgramming Languages\n       \n: SQL, PL/SQL \nDatabase Utilities\n               \n: SQL* Loader, SQL*Plus and TOAD\nDatabase\n                          \n: Oracle 8i,9i and 10i \nGUI\n                                  \n: Oracle Developer 2000 (Forms 10g, Reports 6i)\n\n         \nERP Applications\n                 \n: Oracle Applications 11i\n\n         \nOracle 11i Modules\n              \n: GL, SA and AOL \nOperating Systems\n             \n: Windows XP/2000/NT/9xs and MS-DOS, UNIX.\n\n\nProfessional Profile:\n\n\n         \nFunctional proficiency in the Insurance domain (Level -Beginner).\n\n         \nComprehensive experience in Oracle technologies and Oracle Applications 11i.\n\n         \nTechnical proficiency in Oracle Applications 11i (11.5.x Modules -\n\nGL).\n\n         \nExperienced in Application Object Library, Coding Standards Oracle Applications.\n\n         \nWorked with standard interfaces of GL module of Oracle Applications.\nProficient in \nPL/SQL programming\n and developing the Client-server applications.\n\n         \nExperienced in development of custom interface programs.\nTeam Player with excellent Technical, communication and Inter personnel skills. Exceptional ability to master new concepts.\nComprehensive knowledge in Data warehousing (INFORMATICA)\n\n\nAcademic Profile:\n\nB.Tech-IT \nfrom \nGuru\nNanak\nEngineering\nCollege\n, J.N.T.U passed with 64%.\nIntermediate from \nGowtham\nJunior College\n passed with 81%.\nS.S.C from The \nKodad\nPublic School\n with 81%.\n\nProject Experience:\n\n\nProject 1:\n            \n            \nProject Title\n   \n\n        \nLV\n (Liverpool \nVictoria\n\n          \nTeam Size\n      \n\n        \n15\n          \nRole\n              \n\n        \nDeveloper\nEnvironment\n   \n\n        \nWindows XP, Oracle 10i, Forms 10g\n            \nDescription:\n               \nThe Liverpool Victoria group of companies is the \nUK\n\'s largest Friendly Society (Association of Friendly Societies Yearbook 2006/2007), which offer a broad range of products and services including: Savings, Investments, Life Insurance, Home and Motor Insurance, Banking and Financial advice. At present the Liverpool Victoria group of companies manages more than £8 billion on behalf of its members and customers. The Society does not have any shareholders and, as a mutual organization, exists wholly for the benefit of its members.\n             \nResponsibilities:\n\n\n          \nDevelopment of Forms using Forms 10g.\n\n          \nSupporting various QC calls\n\n          \nWriting extensive PL/SQL code for customizations as needed\n\n\n\nProject 2:\n            \n            \nProject Title\n   \n\n        \nNMIC (Nevada Mutual Insurance Company)\n          \nTeam Size\n      \n\n        \n10\n          \nRole\n              \n\n        \nDeveloper\nEnvironment\n   \n\n        \nWindows XP, Oracle 10i, Forms 10g\n            \nDescription:\n\n                \nNMIC is the only doctor-owned insurer domiciled in \nNevada\n and insures only \nNevada\n doctors. Nevada Mutual is the largest insurer of medical professional liability coverage for physicians, surgeons and allied healthcare providers in \nNevada\n. To meet the demands of its growing membership, NMIC needed a modular and scalable solution to optimize its data processing capabilities and enable greater user efficiency, which helps NMIC to utilize a single platform solution that supports rating and quoting, policy administration, claims, reinsurance and billing.\n\nResponsibilities:\n\n\n          \nDevelopment of Forms using Forms 10g.\n\n          \nSupporting various QC calls\n\n          \nWriting extensive PL/SQL code for customizations as needed\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nProject 3:\n            \n            \nProject Title\n   \n\n        \nHGA (Hallmark General Agency)\n          \nTeam Size\n      \n\n        \n12\n          \nRole\n              \n\n        \nDeveloper\nEnvironment\n   \n\n        \nWindows XP, Oracle 10i, Forms 10g\n            \nDescription:\n               \nHallmark General Agency (HGA) is a provider of standard commercial lines insurance products that are marketed through the independent agency system. It is the commercial division of Hallmark Financial Services.\n\nHGA markets commercial insurance products through agents in the independent agency system.\n\nIt is focused on writing all of the coverages for an account. The majority of the business is written as either a CPP (Commercial Package Policy) or Commercial Advantage (BOP) Policy. CPP policies includes: Property, General Liability, Crime, Inland Marine and Auto.\n\nResponsibilities:\n\n\n          \nDevelopment of Forms using Forms 10g.\n\n          \nSupporting the calls\n\n          \nWriting extensive PL/SQL code for customizations as needed\n\n\n\n\nProject 4:\n            \n            \nClient\n\n          \n\n        \nSriven Multi-Tech Limited\n          \nTeam Size\n      \n\n        \n12\n          \nRole\n              \n\n        \nTechnical Consultant\nEnvironment\n   \n\n        \nMS Windows 2000, Oracle Applications 11.5.9\n\n            \nDescription:\n                   \nSriven Multi-Tech Limited is a publicly traded company in \nIndia\n. It has its registered office, development centers and studios in \nHyderabad\n, Mumbai and \nBangalore\n\n\nSriven has widely implemented various modules of Oracle Applications. \nImplementation process involves data conversion, customization and development of reports.\n\nResponsibilities:\n\n\n          \nDevelopment/Customization of Reports using Reports 6i.\n\n          \nDevelopment/Customization of Forms using Forms 6i.\n\n          \nData Conversion and Interface (From TALLY to Oracle Applications)\n\n          \nWriting extensive PL/SQL code for customizations as needed\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nProject 5:\n            \n            \nClient \n          \n\n        \nImpact Plastics Ltd\n          \nTeam Size\n      \n\n        \n\n          \nRole\n              \n\n        \nDeveloper\nEnvironment\n   \n\n        \nMS Windows 2000, Oracle 9i, Developer 2000\n            \nDescription:\n\nThe Sales Order System Captures Order Data. The Data includes the Terms & Conditions of \nSale\n, Credit Worthiness of Customers, Delivery Schedules, and Source of Orders. The Meta Data so captured is used to validate and process the Transaction Data, which is entered on a Daily Basis.\n\nThe System also captures the Returns of Sales from Customers. The System is used to Review the Status of any Specific Order Online.\n\nThe System is used to View and Generate Daily, Weekly, Monthly, Delivery and various Reports and maintaining the data about employees, stock, sales, daily expenses .The System also helps in Forecasting of Sales for the Future.\n\nResponsibilities:\n\n\n          \nDevelopment of Reports using Reports 6i.\n\n          \nDevelopment of Forms using Forms 6i.\n\n          \nWriting extensive PL/SQL code for customizations as needed\n\n\n\n\n\nPersonal Profile:\n\n            \nName\n                      \n\n        \nNaveen Chandra D\n          \nFather?s Name\n\n\n        \nPandu Ranga Rao [Late]\n          \nDate of Birth\n            \n\n        \n17\nth\n March, 1984\n          \nPassport No\n             \n\n        \nF4455851\n          \nLanguages Known\n     \n\n        \nEnglish, Telugu and Hindi\n\nDeclaration:\nI hereby declare that the information furnished above is true to the best of my knowledge\n\n\nPlace: Chennai\n                                                            \n          \n(Naveen Chandra D)',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-17',NULL,'2007-10-17','2010-06-09 12:13:49','2010-06-09',12,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(144,'Raghavendra H',NULL,NULL,'Bangalore','ragscvcvvdv086@hotmail.com',NULL,'080 2 674 4241','0','98454 50495','0',NULL,'0','2003-04-14',9,30,'2010-06-09 12:13:49',12,'0',NULL,'200710/17/ATT4914.html','200710/17/DOC15318.doc','Raghavendra H\nRaghavendra H\n44, 12\nth\n Cross, 19\nth\n Main, Muneshwara Block, Banashankari 3rd stage, Bangalore ? 560 026\nMob: 98454 50495, Tel.: 080 2 674 4241, Email: ragscvcvvdv086@hotmail.com\n\nSummary of Experience\nAbout \n1.8 years\n of functional and technical \nOracle ERP\n experience, plus 5+ years of application development experience using Microsoft Technologies and 7+ years in the IT field.\n\nTechno-Functional consultant\n for Oracle Human Resources, Oracle Learning Management(earlier called OTA), Employee Self-Service, Manager Self-Service and knowledge of AME.\nProficient in using Oracle Apps tools - \nAME\n\nDiscoverer\n and third party tools including \nTOAD\n\nMethodologies & Documents: Oracle?s \nApplications Implementation Methodology\n (AIM), Oracle documents including: RD020, BP080, BR010, MD050, BR100, CV030, CV040, TE040 and DO070\nProductivity Applications: MS Office, MS Visio and MS Project \nPast experience in Client Server Applications & Web based Applications development using Microsoft ASP.net, C#, Web Services, ASP, Java script and others.\nHandled legacy system Data migration, rapid modifications & interfacing with Oracle E\n\nP systems.\nCountry visited - \nBahrain\n\nand\nSaudi Arabia\n\nRiyadh\n\n for on-site implementations.\n\nOracle Apps Skills and Tools\nStudy of Current Business Processes, Future Business Flow and identification of GAP/Workaround\n\nBusiness Requirements Mapping for the various HR processes\n\nDesigning and Setting up \nOracle Core HR\n - Business Groups, Key Flexfields, Descriptive Flexfields, Recruitment model, Competency management, Payroll Definition, Security Profile, etc.\n\nSetup of SSHR and OLM (OTA\n\nas per requirements\nCustomizing/Formatting \nDiscoverer\n Reports\n\nConducting UAT ? Prepare \nTest Scripts\n and \nUsers Acceptance Test (UAT)\nConduct \nKey User Training\nLog, view, monitor, follow-up and close Technical Assistance Requests \n(TARs)\n on \nOracle Metalink\n\nOn Job Associations \n\n\n          \nCurrently working with Arowana Consulting Ltd. as \nOracle HRMS\n\nTechno-Functional Consultant \nsince Aug 2005 till date.\n\n          \nWorked as Senior Software Engineer from July 2002 to Aug 2005 with JGI-Information Services.\n\n          \nWorked as Software Engineer from May 2000 to June 2002 with MIIT.\n\nProjects\n\nProject: \nOracle HR 11i Implementation\nClient: Arab National Bank, \nRiyadh\n (KSA)\n                                                                                                                                                  \nDuration: \nJanuary, 2007 to till date\nRole:\n Oracle HCM Consultant\nTeam Size:\n\nDescription: \nArab National Bank (a Saudi Joint Stock Company) is the 4\nth\n largest Bank in the \nKingdom\n of \nSaudi Arabia\n, Headquartered in \nRiyadh\n\n\nImplementation of \nOracle HR , Payroll, OLM(OTA), iRec, SSHR and OTL version 11i being implemented in Riyadh Headquarters office \nto carryout the business responsibilities efficiently to act as a strong business enabled to deal with human resources department requirements.\nRoles and Responsibilities:\n\n          \nImplemented Oracle HR 11i (11.5.10) and OLM (OTA.J), ESS & MSS. \n\n          \nStudy of Current business processes, future business flow & identification of GAP/Workaround.\n\n          \nAnalyzing user needs, conferring with users to improve procedures and identifying and solving problems.\n\n          \nBusiness Requirements Mapping for HR and OLM (OTA) modules.\n\n          \nInstance and modules testing for inconsistencies and missing steps.\n\n          \nCustomizing/Formatting Discoverer Reports.\n\n          \nCarrying out Conference Room Pilots (1 & 2) and Users Acceptance Test (UAT).\n\n          \nProvided end-user Training & User Guides \nEnvironment\n: Windows XP, HP Tru64 UNIX, Modules: HR, SSHR and OLM (OTA.J)\n\nProject: \nProject Easy\nClient: Gulf \nAir\n\nBahrain\nDuration: \nFebruary, 2006 to December, 2006\nRole: \nOracle HR Consultant\nTeam Size:\n\nDescription: \nGulf Air is a major international airline serving 46 destinations worldwide, \ncomprised of a corporate headquarters in \nBahrain\n and about 50 locations worldwide. \nImplementation of \nOracle HR, Payroll, iRec, OTL, SSHR, OTA and Finance version 11i t\no have an accessible and common HR module to capture data, adopting the best business practices/processes and provide self-service reporting direct to desktops. \nRoles and Responsibilities:\n\n          \nImplemented Oracle HR and OTA 11i, Discoverer 4i.\n\n          \nSetting up HR system ? Design and Development \n\n          \nDeveloped test plans, test scripts and did unit testing on after each setup.\n\n          \nInstance and modules testing for inconsistencies and missing steps\n\n          \nDeveloped Training materials and conducted Training sessions for end users.\n\n          \nDid post-production support.\nEnvironment\n: Windows XP, HP Tru64 UNIX, Modules: HR, OTA\n\nProject: \nStaff Travel Management System\nClient:\n\nGulf \nAir\n\nBahrain\nDuration:\n September, 2005 to Jan 2006\nRole:\n Project Lead\nTeam Size:\n\n\nProject Description: \nStaff Travel Management Application is a web based client-server application which facilitates Gulf Air to manage Staff Travel needs. The application consumes a 3\nrd\n party web service (booking engine) to carry out live air bookings and search for flight schedules and availability. The application is interfaced with the Oracle Apps to share & synchronize employee HR data.\n\nRoles and Responsibilities:\n\n          \nHandling Project Management activities of the team.\n\n          \nDefine and analyze requirements\n\n          \nSystem Study, HLD, Database Designing, Code \n\neview & Project Planning. \n\n          \nDesign, Development and Onsite Implementation including client interactions.\nEnvironment:\nLanguages & Platform\n: ASP.NET 2.0, C#, Visual Studio .Net 2005\nDatabase:\n SQL Server 2000\nOperating System:\n Windows XP/2000, Windows 2003 Server\n\nProject:\nCore Fund Management System ? Prototype development\nClient:\n\nNational Social Security Fund, Govt. of \nTanzania\n\nEast Africa\nDuration:\n Aug 2005 to Sep 2005\n\nole:\nTeam Lead\nTeam Size:\n 10\nProject Description: \nNational Social Security Fund (NSSF) is a leading provider of social security in \nTanzania\n. NSSF Core Fund Management System (NSSF-CFMS) is web-based intranet application, developed to manage and monitor the activities of NSSF. Some of the main modules are \nCompliance, Benefits and SHIB.\n\noles and \n\nesponsibilities:\n\n          \nProject Planning, Handling Project Management activities of the team.\n\n          \nDefine and analyze requirements.\n\n          \nSystem Study, HLD and Database Designing. \nEnvironment:\nLanguages & Platform\n: ASP.NET 2.0, C#, Visual Studio .Net 2005\nDatabase:\n SQL Server 2000\nOperating System:\n Windows XP/2000, Windows 2003 Server\n\nProject: \nMATSnet (Intranet Application)\nClient:\n\nMATS\nUniversity\n\nRaipur\nDuration:\n October, 2004 to February, 2005\nRole:\n Team Lead\nTeam Size:\n\n\nProject Description: \nMATSnet is an Intranet application which facilitates faculty and staff of \nMATS\nUniversity\n to manage daily activities such as Travel allowance, Leave application, Memos, Circulars and host of other services. \n\nRoles and Responsibilities:\n\n          \nHandling Project Management activities of the team.\n\n          \nDefine and analyze requirements\n\n          \nSystem Study, HLD, Database Designing, Project Planning. \n\n          \nDesign, Development and Testing.\nEnvironment:\nLanguages & Platform\n: ASP.NET, C#, Visual Studio .Net 2003\nDatabase:\n SQL Server 2000\nOperating System:\n Windows XP/2000, Windows 2003 Server\n\nProject: \nOnline Parents Corner Ver 1.2 \nClient: Jain International Residential School (JIRS), \nBangalore\nDuration:\n May, 2004 to August, 2004\nRole: \nSenior Software Engineer\nTeam Size:\n\n\nProject Description:\n\nParents Corner is a web-based application intended to give parents up to date information on the progress of their children studying at \nJain\nInternational\n\nesidential\nSchool\n\nBangalore\n\n\nRoles and Responsibilities:\n\n          \nHandling Project Management activities of the team.\n\n          \nDefine and analyze requirements\n\n          \nSystem Study, Database Designing, Project Planning.\n\n\n          \nDesign, Development, Testing, Deployment and Implementation.\nEnvironment:\nLanguages & Platform:\n ASP.NET, C#, Visual Studio .Net 2003\nDatabase:\n SQL Server 2000,\nOperating System:\n Windows XP/2000, Windows 2003 Server\n\nProject: \nAdmission Process Management Application \nClient: Jain International Residential School (JIRS), \nBangalore\nDuration:\n January, 2004 to April, 2004\nRole:\n Senior Software Engineer\nTeam Size:\n\n\nProject Description: \nThis application facilitates the management to record and maintain the caller information for further follow up, analysis and future references. This application also enables to share the information between the school and the corporate office.\n\nRoles and Responsibilities:\n\n          \nSystem Study, Database Designing\n\n          \nDefine and analyze requirements\n\n          \nDesign, \n\nDevelopment, Testing, Deployment and Implementation\nEnvironment:\nLanguages & Platform:\n ASP.NET, C#, Visual Studio .Net 2003\nDatabase:\n SQL Server 2000\nOperating System:\n Windows XP/2000, Windows 2003 Server\n\nWebsites Developed\nVarious websites of type static and dynamic were developed for Jain Group of Institutions, \nBangalore\n\nDuration:\n June, 2000 to October, 2003\nRoles and Responsibilities:\n\n          \nUnderstand Requirements, conceptualizing, Database Designing\n\n          \nDesign, Development, Testing, Deployment, Implementation and Search Engine optimization\nEnvironment:\nLanguages & Platform:\n ASP, HTML, Java Script, Dream weaver / Home site,\nDatabase:\n MS Access 2000, SQL Server 2000\nOperating System:\n Windows XP/2000, Windows 2000 Server\n\nWorkshops attended\n\n          \nOracle Apps Training \n\n          \nIntel seminar on web technologies\n\n          \nMicrosoft seminar on .Net and Embedded system\n\n\n          \nAdobe Creative Suite seminar\n\nAcademic Qualification and Certifications\n\n          \nMasters of Science (Information Technology), M.Sc. (IT)\nCurrently pursuing final semester, \nKuvempu\nUniversity\n\n          \nBachelor of Science in Electronics, B.Sc. \nApril 2000, \nSri\nBhagawan\nMahaveer\nJain\nCollege\n\nBangalore\nUniversity\n\n          \nProfessional diploma in Network Centered Computing from NIIT\nNovember 1999, NIIT, Jayanagar\n\nPersonal Information\nDate of Birth\n         \n\n\n              \n08 June 1977\nGender\n                 \n\n\n              \nMale\nMarital Status\n       \n\n\n              \nSingle\nPassport No\n         \n\n\n              \nG0742784\n\nStrengths\n\n          \nPossess good communication, interpersonal, intuitive, technical, organizational skills with the ability to adapt in changing environments.\n\n          \nEnergetic and self-motivated team player. Proven ability to work in both independent and team environments.\n\n          \nExcellent analysis of business processes and legacy systems.\n\n          \nCan learn new technologies quickly as and when required.\n\nExtra Curricular Activities\n\n          \nTrekking and Adventure sports (Go-karting, River Rafting, Mountain Climbing, Bungee Jump etc.,)\n\n          \nSports\n\n         \nRepresented \nSri\nBhagawan\nMahaveer\nJain\nCollege\n in Cricket for all 3 Years. Team Captain at Inter-college and University Tournaments.\n\n         \nRepresented ?Bangalore Cricketers? at various state level tournaments and was part of the club for 5 years.\n\n          \nVolunteer at Blood Donation, Health and Eye Camps besides taking part in a host of social service initiatives conducted by SBMJC and Public Relations, JGI.\n\n          \nPlayed an active role in a host of events in college and at work.','Arowana Consulting Ltd',1,NULL,'2007-10-17',NULL,'2007-10-17','2010-06-09 12:13:49','2010-06-09',12,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(145,'Packiyaseelan',NULL,NULL,NULL,'seeladsn_c@yahoo.com','sejhghjelan_c@rediffmail.com','91 0462 2351694','0','919444276315','0',NULL,'0','2006-04-29',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-09 12:13:49',2,'0',NULL,'200710/17/ATT4910.html','200710/17/DOC15319.doc','Resdex @ naukri.com\nPackiyaseelan \nseeladsn_c@yahoo.com sejhghjelan_c@rediffmail.com Chennai - 600064 \nseelsdvdsvan_dvc@yahoo.com\n\nTelephone: 919444276315\n(M)\n 91 0462 2351694\n(R)\n\nD.O.B\n - 28 Feb 1978 \nModified on\n - 25 Sep 2007 \nAnnual Salary\n - INR 1 Lac(s) 50 Thousand \nTotal Years of Experience\n - 5 Year(s) 1 Month(s) \nCurrent Location\n - Chennai \nPreferred Location\n - Chennai \nB.Sc with 4 years Payroll Experience\n\nTEXT RESUME \n\nI\'m seelan. Now i am working as a Sr.Executive HR & Administration in Twinstar metal products pvt. ltd- chennai. I handling all HR & Administration activities of 250 workers.',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-17',NULL,'2007-10-17','2010-06-09 12:13:49','2010-06-09',2,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(146,'Varma M Rajanikanth Raju',NULL,NULL,'Banglore','rajanikdvvadvdnth.raju@gmail.com','rajanikanth.raju@gmail.com','09916329532','0','09916329532','0',NULL,'0','2007-05-15',7,19,'2010-06-09 12:13:49',2,'0',NULL,'200710/17/ATT4909.html','200710/17/DOC15320.doc','Resdex @ naukri.com\nrajanikanthvarma\nrajanikdvvadvdnth.raju@gmail.com\n\nTelephone: 09916329532\n(M)\n\nD.O.B\n - 28 Dec 1982 \nModified on\n - 26 Sep 2007 \nAnnual Salary\n - INR 3 Lac(s) 40 Thousand \nTotal Years of Experience\n - 3 Year(s) 5 Month(s) \nCurrent Location\n\nBangalore\n\nPreferred Location\n - Anywhere in \nIndia\nHaving 3.5 Years of Experience in IT with 2.3 years of experience in Data Stage.\n\nTEXT RESUME \n\nRAJANI KANTH VARMA.M rajanikanth.raju@gmail.com\nMobile: 9916329532\nTo be a part of challenging projects in a progressive Organization that gives scope to put my experience and skills for the growth of the Organization and to achieve career goals in synchronization with organization goals.\n?X 3.5 Years of Experience in IT with 2.3 years of experience in Data Stage.\n?X Experience in designing, developing of data stage jobs.\n?X Accustomed to work in a team environment with tight schedules and capable.\n?X Good communication and Interpersonal skills and Team player.\n?X Working as Software Engineer with Target Services \nIndia\n from DEC 2006 ?V Till Date.\n?X Worked as Software Engineer in Span Systems \nBangalore\n, from Nov 2004 to OCT 2006.\n?X BSc Computers from \nSri\nVenkateswara\nUniversity\n, Tirupati, Passed out in Year 2004.\n?X ETL Tools : DataStage 7.1/7.5\n?X Languages : C,C++\n?X Operating System : Windows (XP, 98,NT/2000 ).\n?X BI Concepts : OLTP, OLAP, Slowly changing dimensions\n?X Data base : Oracle 8i/9i\n?X Testing Tool : Win Runner 7.01.\n# Project 1:\nProject : \nENTERPRISE\n DATA WAREHOUSE-CREDIT\nTechnology : Ascential Data Stage 7.5, ORACLE 9i, Windows Xp.\nClient : TARGET.\nRole : Team member.\nDuration : DEC 2006 to Till Date\nDescription:\nTarget Services Enterprise Data Warehouse (EDW-C) is an Integrated Data Warehouse based on IBM??s Retail Enterprise Data Warehouse (REDW) model. The transformed and validated data related to Target credit cards from multiple sources is loaded into Enterprise wide data warehouse. This Data Warehouse is used to populate the subject specific Datamarts. The warehouse gives details of the various customer accounts, the credit scores of the customer, the transactions carried out by customer and also describes about the billing cycle periods of the credit cards.\nResponsibilities:\n?X Extensively used Ascential Data Stage designer to develop Jobs for extracting, transforming, loading data into data warehouse tables.\n?X Used Data Stage Director to run and monitor the Data Stage jobs. Developed jobs in Ascential Data Stage for loading data from source to target.\n?X Used Data Stage Manager to import metadata, new job categories as well as to export and import jobs\n?X Used most of the Stages in Datastage, such as Hash file stage, Transformer Stage, pivot stage, aggregator stage and Sequential stage.\n?X Involved in Unit Testing\n# Project 2:\nProject : Insurance Data Warehouse\nTechnology : Ascential Data Stage 7.5, ORACLE 9i, Windows 2000.\nClient : Alliance Insurance, U.K\nRole : Team member\nDuration : April 2006- Oct 2006\nDescription:\nThis Insurance Company is a one of the biggest insurance company that offers insurance for automobiles, home fire protection, and personal liability. This insurance data warehouse contains two major production data sources. They are, all transactions relating to the formulation of policies And all transactions involved in processing claims. This data warehouse has been built from many different sources for information about coverage??s, covered items, employee, insured party, and this data warehouse enables to the company to see which coverage??s most are most profitable, which are least profitable, to measure profit over time by covered item and want to understand what happens during life of a policy, particularly when a claim is processed.\nResponsibilities:\n?X Developed Datastage applications (Jobs) based on the Design and Mapping Documents\n?X Used most of the Stages in Datastage, such as Hash File Stage, Transformer Stage and Sequential Stage.\n?X Involved in Unit Testing\n# Project 3:\nProject : Sales and Marketing Data Warehouse\nTechnology : Ascential DataStage 7.5, ORACLE 9i, Windows 2000.\nClient : Polo Ralph Lauren, USA\nRole : Team member\nDuration : Sep 2005- Mar 2006\nDescription:\nPolo Ralph Lauren (Polo) is a major player in fashions and designer ware. This system has been developed to take care of all sales and marketing of the products. The main objective of this project is to provide integrated information on retail sales and promotional sales data for better decision making. The objective of this project is to provide complete historical information, related with Polo\'s product mix includes sportswear, men??s wear, jewelry, fragrances, fashion accessories and couture. They have all the data of their products, vendors and customers in various Data Bases and certain data in the form of flat files.\nResponsibilities:\n?X Developed Datastage applications (Jobs) based on the Design and Mapping Documents\n?X Used most of the Stages in Datastage, such as Hash File Stage, Transformer Stage and Sequential Stage, Link partitioner, Link Collector.\n?X Involved in Unit Testing\n\n# Project 4:\nProject : EduQuest.\nEnvironment : Java, Java Script, Oracle and Windows NT.\nClient : UK Government\nRole : Software Test Engineer\nDuration : Nov 2004- Aug 2005\nDescription:\nThis project is for maintaining the UK government??s schools information. For this all schools information stored in oracle database. In this project user can analyze the student??s information and growth. User can see all schools information and nearest schools information from their residence. They estimate the performance of the students through performance chart. User can apply for new admissions.\nResponsibilities:\n?X Identified test requirements based on client requirements.\n?X Prepared test cases according to SRS Docs.\n?X Involved in functional testing, User interfacing testing, regression testing and other system testing.\n?X Analyzing and writing weekly/Monthly review documents.','Target Services India ',1,NULL,'2007-10-17',NULL,'2007-10-17','2010-06-09 12:13:49','2010-06-09',2,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(147,'Mansi Mittal',NULL,NULL,NULL,'madvdvfvvnsimiddvttal11@gmail.com','Mansimittal11@gmail.com',NULL,'0','91 9899051865','0',NULL,'0','2008-04-29',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-09 12:13:49',12,'0',NULL,'200710/17/ATT4908.html','200710/17/DOC15321.doc','Ashish Bhardwaj Resume\n       \nmadvdvfvvnsimiddvttal11@gmail.com\n\n                                                                                                                               \n       \nMobile\n: +91-9899051865\n\nMANSI \n\nObjective\n\nTo embark a career path of growth and new challenges and to utilize my potential and skills to evolve consistently with the organization. \nI hold a positive outlook and attitude so that I can tackle any situation with reason and intellect.\n\nBrief Profile\n\nWork experience of 2+ years as on July 2007, with Perot Systems Noida, mostly worked on SQL and VB\n\n         \nCurrently working as a Team Lead for a team of 6 members.\n\n         \nConstant Client interaction, and receive appreciation mails from client.\n\n         \nAbility to take up challenging tasks and deliver beyond the expectations of my Institution and the Client.\n\nOrganization Profile\n\nPerot Systems Technology Services, NOIDA is well known global IT, PCMM?5 company, having spread its development centers all over the world. It develops software in all domains for its clients from every part of the world. It works on mostly on all popular technologies such as Microsoft .Net, Java, Mainframe etc.\n\nWork Experience And Projects\n\n\nExperience\n\n2+ years\n\nOrganization\n\n\nPerot Systems Technology Services\n\nDuration\n\n\nJuly 2005 - till date\n\n\n\nProject Name\n\nSHL-RIT (Regional Implementation Team)\n\n\nClient\n\nSHL\n\nUK\nDuration\n\nFrom Jan 2006 till date\n\n\nProject Description:\nThe project basically deals with creation and management of online psychometric tests for the client. The client handles these tests to their clients which includes some universities. These psychometric tests are undertaken by various candidates under those universities. Our client has its own well developed sites, and all the tests run on those sites.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nRole\n\n\n\n         \nThe project includes direct interaction with the client. Being a \nTeam Leader\n\nI make direct calls to the client, and have received many appreciation mails from the client for all my work.\n\n         \nMy work includes working on database and VB, for creating psychometric tests, according to the specifications provided by the clients.\n\nThese tests are taken by various candidates under various institutes.\n\n         \nMy work also includes data extraction work, which is writing and executing SQL queries according to the data required by the client as mentioned in the specifications. These extracts are used by the client for analysis of the scores obtained by different candidates in various tests.\n\n         \nMy work also includes manipulation of various images using Adobe Photoshop, Macromedia Flash and Fireworks. These images are used in the psychometric tests.\n\nTools, Languages & Components\n\nVSS, SQL2000, VB, Adobe Photoshop, Macromedia Fireworks, Macromedia Flash.\n\n\n\nSkill Set\n\nLanguages and Technologies\n                                           \n: C, C++, C#, VB.net, ADO.net, ASP.net,\nAdobe Photoshop, Macromedia Fireworks, Macromedia Flash.\nFramework\n                                                    \n: .NET Framework 1.1.\nRelational Database Management System\n        \n: MS SQL Server 2000\nDevelopment Tool\n   \n                                       \n: Visual Studio .Net 2003\nOperating Environment\n                                               \n: Windows 2000/XP\n\n\nAcademics\nExamination\nBoard/University\nYear \nCGPA/ %\nMajor Subjects\nB.Tech.\nIndira Gandhi Institute of Technology(IGIT), \nDelhi\n2005\n    \n74.1\nComputer Science & Engineering\n12th\nCBSE, \nRyan International, \nDelhi\n2001\n    \n87.8\nScience Group\n10\nth\nCBSE, \nRyan International, \nDelhi\n1999\n     \n80.6\nMatriculation\n\n\n                        \nAcademic Training And Projects\n\n1. Developed projects using SQL and VB.Net at SQL Star International Ltd. during B.Tech.\n2. Developed web application?s in ASP.NET using C# at \nPerot\nAcademy\n, Perot Systems Tech. Services during professional training.\n3. Developing projects using SQL and VB at \nPerot\nAcademy\n\n\n\n\n\n\nCertifications\n\nMCP (70-315): \nDeveloping web application?s in ASP.NET using C# and .Net Framework 1.1\n\nCleared \nStandards & Ethical Principles \ntraining in Perot Systems.\n\n\n\n\n\nAchievements And Awards\n\n1. Awarded \nPat on the Back Award\n for high productivity and accepting challenges by Managing Director of PSTS.\n2. Awarded \nAppreciation Mails\n by client, \nSHL\n\nUK\n\n            \n\n\n\n\n\n                        \nStrengths \n\nDiligence, sincerity and hard work have been instrumental in shaping my life so far. A strong aspect of my personality is \ncontinuous desire to move up on the learning curve\n, ability to take on responsibilities and work with efficiency and involvement.\n\nPersonal Information\n\nName\n\nMansi Mittal\n\nDesignation\n\nAssociate\n\nDate Of Birth\n\nApril 11\nth\n, 1984\n\nSex\n\nFemale\n\nPermanent Address\n\nB-61, Ram Puri, P.O. Chandar Nagar. Distt. \nGhaziabad\n, U.P. 201011\n\nPresent Address\n\nB-61, Ram Puri, P.O. Chandar Nagar. Distt. \nGhaziabad\n, U.P. 201011\n\nEmail\n\nMansimittal11@gmail.com\n\nmansimittal11@yahoo.co.in\n\nPassport\n\nValid till 2015\n\nContact Number\n\n+91-9899051865\n\n\nReferences:\n   \nAvailable upon Request.\n\n\n                                                                                                                                                                                    \n                                                                        \n   \nMansi Mittal\n\nAs on date: 25\nth\n September 2007',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-17',NULL,'2007-10-17','2010-06-09 12:13:49','2010-06-09',12,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(148,'Padarthi',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Padarthffsi.Prasdssbvad@gmail.com','Padarthi.Prasad@birlasoft.com',NULL,'0','09971134289','0',NULL,'0','2007-04-30',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-09 12:13:49',12,'0',NULL,'200710/17/ATT4907.html','200710/17/DOC15322.doc','RESUME\nNAME: Padarthi\nContact No:\n 09971134289\nE-mail\n\n\nPadarthffsi.Prasdssbvad@gmail.com\n   \nOfficial E-mail :Padarthi.Prasad@birlasoft.com\n       \nOracle Apps11i\n Technical Consultant\n______________________________________________________________________________________\n   \n\nExecutive Summary:\n\nHaving 3 \nyears \nof total IT experience, which includes Around \n2 years\n on \nOracle 11i\n\nApplications \nand \n1 Year\n on D2k, Oracle.\n\n\n         \nConversant with modules like Purchase Order. \nAccount Payables, General Ledger, Account Receivables, Order Management. \n\n         \nExtensive experience in writing stored procedures, triggers and very strong in \nPL/SQL. \n\n         \nExtensively worked on \nForms6i, Reports6i.\n\n         \nCapable of working independently and \nas well as a part of a team.\n\n         \nPossess very good communication and interpersonal skills. \n\n         \nSelf-motivated, quick learner, zealous, and diligent.\n\nKey Strengths in Oracle Applications\n\n\n\n         \nDevelopment and customization of \nReports\n and \nInterfaces,\n Forms.\n\n         \nCreation of Value sets in various Modules of the application.\n\n         \nDefining Concurrent Programs, Executables.\n\n         \nPL/SQL method of submitting Concurrent programs.\n\n         \nConcurrent programs, PL/SQL API?s.\n\nEducation \n               \n\n         \nMaster of Computer Applications \nM.C.A\n\nrom\nMadras\nUniversity\n\n\n         \nBachelor of Computer Applications \nB.Com (Computers ) \n\nFrom\n       \nS.V\nUniversity\n\n\n\nTechnical Skills\n\nERP\n\nOracle Apps 11.5.9.(PO,AP,\nOM\n,GL)\nRDBMS\n\nOracle 8i\nFront-end Tool\n\nForms6i\nLanguages\n\nSQL, PL/SQL, C, C++\nReports\n\nReports6i\nTools\n\nToad, SQL*Loader\n\n\n\nEXPERIENCE HISTORY\n\n\n       \nWorking with Birlasoft ,\n\nNoida (From Oct?2006 to Till date) \n\n       \nWorked with Accenture, Chennai (From Jan?2005 to Sep?06) \n\n\n\n\nProjects Profile:\n\nProject #1\n\nClient: Juniper Networks(US)\n   \nTechnical- Consultant (Offshore)\nIn Juniper Networks inside sales creates quote for renewals of IPG and SPG services in SCMC and send it to the customer. In case customer accepts it, customer sends PO to \nOM\n admin. On receiving the PO, Order admin retrieve the quote in pre-entered screen and Verifying line information, changes the bill to, ship to and end user at header level to match the \nPO\n. And push the order in \nOM\n as enter status.\nThe other information in the \nPO\n is based on the quote. As per the PO the Order is created in the \nOM\n and quote id information is also maintained with the Order to relate the Order with Quote\n\n\nWorked on data conversion, interface development and reports development implementing Oracle Applications 11i \nWorked on the interface customization and reports (6i and SQL). Developed several \nOM\n reports using SQLPLUS. \n\n\nReports:\n\n\n         \nDeveloped Goods Receipt Report.\n   \n\n         \nDeveloped Purchase order and Payables analysis report\n\n         \nDeveloped Purchase order and receipts detail report.\n\n         \nCustomized RFQ report.\n\n         \nDeveloped\n\nCustomer analysis report.\n\nOutbound Interfaces:\n\nDeveloped Items On-Hand quantity outbound interface to transfer the data from Oracle Apps base tables to the flat file using the UTL_FILE Package.\n\nInbound Interface:\n\nDeveloped requisitions Interface to import the data from flat file to the Oracle Apps Requisitions base tables using the SQL*LOADER.\n\n\nProject\n #2\n\nClient: Pfizer (Efss)\n       \n(Accenture)\nTechnical- Consultant (Offshore)\n\nPfizer are the largest Pharmaceutical company in the world with a strategy to go ?beyond number one?.Provide Pfizer with a more flexible option for merger integration.The EFSS (European Financial Shared Services) involves creation of single service centre for Europe based in \nDublin\n. Pfizer have build a green-field site in \nDublin\n with mostly new employees\n\nPfizer is currently in the process of \nOracle 11i ? PO, AP,GL, \nOrder Management\n, Inventory, HRMS : Application Interfacing Solution, Concur : Travel & Expenses,Automatic Call Distribution and Call Logging, Document Imaging Tool .\n\n\n\n\nResponsibilities:\n\nThis is Developing and Supporting\n   \nProject in the \nProvided support in day-to-day software issues and developments of new requirements. \nInvolved in customizing Reports and Interfaces.\nCreation of Responsibilities ,Creation of new Users\nCustomizing DFF as per client requirement.\nCustomizing report Formatting and assigning Value Sets\n\nReports:\n\n\n         \nDeveloped \nPO\n Analysis Report.\n\n         \nDeveloped Inventory Valuation Report.\n\n         \nDeveloped Material Receipt Data \n\n         \nDeveloped\n\nNew Customer Statement Report.\n\n         \nDeveloped Vendor Delivery Report.\n\n\n   \nInbound Interface:\nDeveloped requisitions Interface to import the data from flat file to the Oracle Apps Requisitions base tables using the SQL*LOADER\nProject # 3\n\nClient\n            \n: Novartis-Rekha Corps\nRole\n              \n: Software Engineer\nEnvironment: Oracle, D2k\n\nDescription\n      \nDesigning and developing the Ebiznet warehouse Manager System for Novartis-Rekha Corps. This system delivers the basic functionality of an integrated WMS specifically suited to manufacture operations with an integrated Manufacture Billing Module. These functions include\n\nResponsibilities\n\nDeveloping and Debugging of Forms and Reports.\nDeveloping and Debugging of Triggers and Packages.\nCustomization of Reports.\nData Conversion using SQL * Loader.\nProject # 2\n\nTitle\n     \n             \n: MATERIAL ACCOUNTING SYSTEM\nRole\n                  \n: Software Engineer\nEnvironment\n    \n: Oracle, D2k \n\nThis system monitors the material movements at different stages. The material storage details such as location bin card details are provided by the system for proper control and co ordination. Further this system generates the following reports.\nWork Order and department wise material consumption report.\nA B C classification report. Receipt and Issues during the month and year & Stock Status report. Summary Ledger for the year which is also used for audit purpose.\n\nResponsibilities\n\nInvolved in the design and development of Issues module. Created views, database triggers and PL/SQL programs to validate and maintain stock status.',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-17',NULL,'2007-10-17','2010-06-09 12:13:49','2010-06-09',12,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(149,'Murali T',NULL,NULL,NULL,'masadvddi.mdvurali@gmail.com','Masai.murali@gmail.com',NULL,'0','9840244453','0',NULL,'0','2008-04-29',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-09 12:13:49',12,'0',NULL,'200710/17/ATT4906.html','200710/17/DOC15323.doc','Resume\nMurali T\n                                    \n                                             \n   \n+91 9840244453\n                        \n                                       \nmasadvddi.mdvurali@gmail.com\n\nSummary:\n\n         \nHaving\n\nover\n 4 years \nof extensive Professional \nIT\n experience. \n\n         \nIT consultant with over \n3 years\n dedicated experience in Development and Production of Data warehousing solutions using \nInformatica, Oracle, \nand\n Teradata\n based systems.\n1+\n years of experience in the areas of \nASP\n\nOracle Database Administration, SQL.\nExperience in Data Warehouse/Data Mart Development Life Cycle.\nExpertise in ETL (Extraction Transformation Loading) using \nInformatica\nPower\nCenter\n tools like Designer, Workflow manager, Workflow monitor and Repository manager.\nCreated reusable ETL components using Informatica. \nExtensive experience in building Client Server Applications using Oracle, PL/SQL, stored Procedures, Packages and Database Triggers. \nSQL Tuning and creation of indexes for faster database access and better query performance in Terabyte level database.\nProgramming Skills using PL/SQL, C, C++.\nInstallation of Informatica Server and Informatica Repository Server in Windows-NT operating Systems.\nParticipated in a Decision Support Project team to develop views necessary for structured and ad-hoc reporting.\nFamiliarity with Business Objects 7.0.\nExcellent communication and interpersonal skills, demonstrated ability to quickly grasp new concepts, both technical and business related and utilize as needed.\n\nEducation\n\n\n         \nBachelor of Computer Science, \nSri\nVenkateswara\nUniversity\n\nProfessional experience:\nCurrently working as assistant engineer in, \nCaterpillar\n India (P) Ltd., Chennai, from Aug 2005 to till date.\nWorked as a software engineer for Atrix soft technologies, \nBangalore\n, from May 2003 to July 2005.\n\nTECHNICAL SKILLS:\n\nData Warehousing\n      \n\n\nInformatica\nPower\nCenter\n 6.x/7.x \n(Source Analyzer, Warehouse\n   \n   \nDesigner, Mapping Designer, Mapplet Designer, Transformation \n   \nDeveloper). \nBusiness Intelligence\n            \n\n\nBusiness Objects Designer 6.0\nDatabases\n                   \n\n\nOracle 9i, MS SQL Server, MS Access\n\nProgramming\n              \n\n\nC, C++, Visual Basic 6.0, SQL, SQL*Plus, PL/SQL\nEnvironment\n   \n            \n\n\nWin XP, NT 4.0\nWeb Technologies\n      \n\n\nASP, HTML, DHTML\nProject#1:\n\nCaterpillar Inc., \nIL\n                                                                 \n            \nJan? 07 ? Till Date\n     \n                         \nParts illustration and control management system\n\nCaterpillar is one of the world\'s largest consumer companies for earth moving equipments products manufacturing and services. Caterpillar is one of the finest companies, which implements 6 sigma technologies in all its success factors. Caterpillar products are sold in nearly 200 countries\n\nProject was to develop data warehouse for material management and inventory control, focusing on achieving optimum Business solution for supply chain management involving component materials, inventory management and dealer sales across the country.\n\nThe company does a high volume of business, so it runs business statistics reports to aid in decision support. Many of these reports are time-based and nonvolatile. That is, they analyze past data trends. The company loads data into its database and then into its data warehouse regularly to gather statistics for these reports. \n\nResponsibilities:\n\nDeveloped various mappings in Informatica to populate the data mart.\nResponsible for material and product detail extraction from flat files and various databases such as MS SQL Server, Oracle and Teradata.\nDesigned mappings to implement complex business logic using multiple sources and targets in different databases.\nUsed various transformations such as unconnected lookup, connected lookup, aggregator, rank, joiner, and stored procedure.\nDid \nperformance tuning\n on targets, sources, mappings and sessions to improve system performance.\nDesigned mappings to implement \ntype 2 slowly changing dimensions\n\nCreated partitions for concurrent loading and processing of data.\nUsed shortcuts for sources and target.\n\nEnvironment: Informatica PowerCenter 7.1.2, PL/SQL, ODBC, Oracle 9i, \nTeradata V2R5,\n\nWindows 2000/NT\n\n\nProject#2:\n\nCat logistics, \nBangalore\n\nIndia\n\n         \n     \n                                           \nJun?06 ? Dec?06\nSales Data mart \n\nCat logistics is an Asia Pacific based servicing retail and manufacturer. The purpose of the warehouse is to provide business analysts and senior management of Marketing Specialists with an ability to analyze company?s sales data and the market data to learn how their performance compares with the competition and take decisions to improve the company?s bottom-line.\nWhen the company runs special promotions on its products, it analyzes the impact of these promotions on sales. It analyzes the\n annual, quarterly, monthly, and weekly sales figures by product. \nIt also analyzes sales by geographical area.\n\nResponsibilities:\n\n\n         \nCreated a set of mappings to integrate internal data with market data to map product?s internal and market categories.\n\n         \nUsed \nvarious transformations\n like Lookup, Update Strategy, Router, Filter, Sequence Generator, Source Qualifier/Joiner on data and extracted according to the business rules and technical specifications.\n\n         \nCreated reusable Mapplets using \nMapplet Designer.\n\n         \nUsed workflow manager for session management, database connection management and scheduling of jobs.\n\n         \nExpertise in using \ndifferent tasks\n\nSession, Assignment, Command, Decision, Timer, Email, Event-Raise, Event-Wait, Control\n) of Informatica 7.\n\n         \nDeveloped ETL mappings using Informatica.\n\n\n         \nInvolved in developing end-user training guide, performance optimization and troubleshooting.\n\nEnvironment:\n\nInformatica\nPower\nCenter\n 7.1.2, Oracle 9i, UNIX, Windows 2000\n\n\n\nProject#3:\n\nCat EDC ? \nIndia\n                                                        \n                   \nSep?05 to May?06\nGlobal Communication System. \n\nThe purpose of this project is to create an Integrated Distribution Management System. This system uses the Internet as the primary channel for communication between different warehouses as well as central office. In this system, a central office is connected to different warehouses using the Internet. The Central office contains the marketing, sales, manufacturing and accounts departments. These departments provide forecasting, pricing, Monitoring and Administration request to the Warehouses. It therefore, essentially behaves as a host system.\n\n\nThe host system provides the real time status for all warehouses. This data on the host will be used for inventory and sales analysis. The warehouse contains information about customers/dealers, orders and dispatches, as well as invoice & stocks. Standard templates are used to facilitate communication between host and warehouses.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nResponsibilities\nDeveloped data transfer strategy to move the data from various legacy data sources to current warehouse.\nDeveloped mappings/sessions using Informatica power center for data loading.\nDeveloped mappings to load the data in to slowly changing dimensions.\nUsed Unconnected Stored Procedure for look up on target table.\nUsed Aggregate, Expression, Lookup, Update Strategy, Router and Rank transformations.\nDeveloped Joiner transformation for extracting data from multiple sources.\nPreparation of technical specification for the development of Informatica Extraction, Transformation and Loading (ETL) mappings to load data into various tables in Data Marts and defining ETL standards.\nDesign and Development of data validation, load processes, test cases, and error control routines using PL/SQL, SQL.\nMethodology with confirmed and granular dimensions and FACT tables.\nDesign and Development of pre-session, post-session routines and batch execution routines using Informatica Server to run Informatica sessions.\nUsed Informatica Server Manager to create, schedule, monitor and send the messages in case of process failures.\nWrote PL/SQL stored procedures and Functions for data manipulation.\nEnvironment:\nInformatica\nPower\nCenter\n 7.1.2\n, Windows 2000/NT, MS Access, Oracle.\n\nProject#4:\n\nBankers Life and Casualty, IL\n                                                         \nJune ?04 ? Apr ?05\n\nEstablished in 1879, Bankers Life and Casualty Company is today one of the largest and most respected insurance companies in the \nUnited States\n focused exclusively on the needs of Senior Americans. Banker?s services the needs of the seniors through a broad portfolio of quality, competitive insurance products including long-term care, life and annuities and Medicare supplement.\n\n\n\nResponsibilities:\nWorked closely with the Business users to understand business needs, define requirements and implement solutions within the Data Warehouse.\nExtensively used ETL and \nInformatica\n to load data from different sources like flat files, Excel spreadsheets, and Oracle into the Oracle data marts and Oracle staging areas.\nInvolved in ETL process design in development, test and production environments.\nCreated reusable transformations and mapplets to be used in multiple mappings.\nConfigured the session properties and target options for better performance.\nImplemented \nPipeline Partitioning\n as a part of Performance Tuning.\nPerformed Unit Testing and tuned the mappings for the better performance.\n\nEnvironment\n\nInformatica\nPower\nCenter\n 6..2/7.1.1, Oracle 9i, \nPL/SQL, \nWindows XP.\n\n\nProject#5:\n\nData System Solutions, \nIndia\n                                 \n                           \nJul? 03 to Mar? 04\nProject Management System\n\n\nData System Solutions is a\n\nconsulting service in Information Technology. Developed and implemented Purchase Order and Sales, account request and database maintenance system for an engineering firm.\n\nThis system also takes care of all the project details. Operational leads will enter the project information and time sheets. This system also contains the customer requirements and contact details. Backend used was oracle 9i.\n\nResponsibilities:\n\n\n   \n   \nInvolved in writing code for front-end design using HTML, ASP.\nInvolved in writing \nSQL stored procedures\n to access data from Oracle9i.\nDeveloped \nSQL queries\n to check the database.\nCreation of \nTriggers\n\nStored Procedures\n\nTables\n\nIndexes\n, Rules.\nCoordinate with clients as needed for on-going system support and troubleshooting.\n\nEnvironment:\n\nOracle9i\n, PL/SQL, Developer 2000, \nWindows NT\n\n\nCertification: \n\nCertified 6 Sigma \nGreenbelt\n from Caterpillar. \n\n         \nOne of the \nGreenbelt\n in establishment of new Caterpillar Engineering design center at Chennai.\n\n         \nOne of the \nGreenbelt\n in implementing license optimization project, which saves $70\nthousand per year.\n\n         \nPAC2/web time coordinator for CAT EDC-India, to take care of the billing and project reporting.\n\n\nEmail id:\n                       \nMasai.murali@gmail.com\nMasai_murali@cat.com\n            \n\n\n\n\n                                   ',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-17',NULL,'2007-10-17','2010-06-09 12:13:49','2010-06-09',12,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(150,'Munavvar Khan',NULL,NULL,'Mumbai','murtcbxfbuza.khbxan@yahoo.com','murtuza.khan@yahoo.com','91 731 2478769','0','9967887800','0','9324937022','0','2008-04-13',10,33,'2010-06-09 12:13:49',2,'0',NULL,'200710/17/ATT4905.html','200710/17/DOC15324.doc','Resdex @ naukri.com\nM Khan\nR No. 1,Grnd Flr, Chandan Nivas Chetanya Nagar, IIT Powai Mumbai - 400076 \nmurtcbxfbuza.khbxan@yahoo.com\n\nTelephone: 9967887800\n(M)\n\nD.O.B\n - 02 Dec 1979 \nModified on\n - 25 Sep 2007 \nAnnual Salary\n - INR 2 Lac(s) 50 Thousand \nTotal Years of Experience\n - 2 Year(s) 5 Month(s) \nCurrent Location\n - Mumbai \nPreferred Location\n - Bangalore, Mumbai, Pune \n2(+)Years,MCA 71% exp. in Oracle,UNIX,Finacle\n\nTEXT RESUME \n\nCurriculum Vitae\nMurtuza Khan R No. 1,Grnd Flr, Chandan Nivas\nChetanya Nagar, IIT Powai,\nMumbai - 76\n( : +91 9324937022\nmurtuza.khan@yahoo.com\nProfile summery:\nA dedicated Software Professional with 2+ years of technology development and functional experience. Worked with technologies like Oracle, Unix.\nHave good exposure over banking worked with product like Finacle core banking solution.\nProficient in writing SQL and PL/SQL programs, developed oracle stored procedures, functions, triggers etc based on technical and functional specification documents\nProficient in writing Unix shell programming, awk, vi editor, embedding pl/sql code in to Unix scripts for automation.\nClarified the requirements by talking to the user groups and accordingly modified the functional and technical specifications\nKnowledge over Database Design, Normalization & Performance Optimization, Good knowledge over ORDBMS concepts\nAnalyze performance problems & recommend actions to alleviate problems\nAttend day-to-day Database related, network related problems and troubleshoot to resolve\nProfessional Experience:\nPresently working as Software Engineer Technology Solutions at 3i Infotech Ltd. Mumbai, from Feb 07 till date.\nWorked as Functional Analyst for Tech Process Solutions Ltd. Mumbai, from July 06 - Feb 07\nWorked as PL/SQL Developer for Infobeans Systems Ltd Indore, March 05 - May 06\nEducational Credentials:\nMaster of Computer Application (MCA) A three year full time degree program From Ragiv Gandhi Technical University, Bhopal MP (2002-2005) with 71%\nBachelor of Science ( Comp.Sc [Hons.] ) From Davi Ahilya Vishva Vidyalaya, Indore MP (1998-2001)\nSkill Set:\nLanguages : SQL, PL/SQL, C, C++\nScripting Languages : Shell Script, awk, Vi\nRDBMS : Oracle 8i/9i\nOperating Systems : UNIX, Windows NT/2000\nProjects:\n1) MIS for Finacle Core Banking System\nClient : ICICI Bank Ltd.\nEnvironment : UNIX, Oracle\nRole : Requirement Analysis, Development\nThe System involves wide range of MIS report generation for different business groups of ICICI bank at international level. System is dedicated to improve performance with highest security, but at most accuracy level, as it involves transactions of Retail & Corporate sectors of bank. Managing the resolution of support service issues, queries and enhancements Fix errors in data for various clients by using PL/SQL scripting . Investigate for possible reasons of errors by studying backend code, and scripting as needed to resolve issues.Communicate and discuss with client and support team in order to research and resolve a perceived issue or problem.\n2) Billing System\nClient : ICICI Bank Ltd.\nEnvironment : UNIX, Oracle\nRole: : Logic building, Transactions upload\nIt includes different billing for various product of the bank, which includes Debit card charging, QAB charging, RCA charging etc. arriving on the customers which need be charged on that particular cycle & excluding high value customers & than finally upload of transactions. Post upload reporting for customer care department & calculation of earning etc.\n3) Report Management System (rptmgr)\nClient : ICICI Bank Ltd.\nEnvironment : UNIX, Oracle\nRole: : Development, Maintenance\nA menu driven user friendly system which uses complexity like multiple parallelization to do database extraction, at the same time ensuring completeness of each process. It has been implemented globally, reports under rptmgr are very critical it includes raw data which gets uploaded in other important systems of bank like CCM, Perform, Billing, Audit etc systems.\n4)Dynamic Creation Of Crontab (popcron)\nClient : ICICI Bank Ltd.\nEnvironment : UNIX, Oracle\nRole : Development & Enhancement\nAll corporate sector reporting is being done over MIS server, which contain data till last day EOD, everyday data get transfer from production server to MIS server. The popcron starts execution of reports accordingly. It fully customization of Unix crontab utility for scheduling. It creates cronjobs dynamically according to database uptime.\n5) Enterprise Sales & Material Management System\nClient : Yash Corporation, \nRNT Road\nIndore\nEnvironment : D2k,Oracle 8i, HTML, Windows NT\nRole : PL/SQL Packages/Triggers, Reports\nSynopsis: The System has the functionality and process of SD, MM & QM modules of an organization from raw material purchase to shop floor dispatch. A large number of Reports were the part of the system to support decision making of the organization. It was flexible enough for future up gradation.\nCorporate Trainings:\nUndergone traning from ICICI Bank in Essentials of Core Banking.\nFinacle I-Core system (an Infosys organized program)\nTraning from 3i infotech ltd for SAS reporting tool.\nOther Key Assets:\nGood interpersonal skills & Decent command on English\nFocused and skilled to meet deadlines\nQuick in adapting to new work culture\nTeam sprite and flexible attitude\nOpen For relocation\nExtra Curricular Activities:\nWorked as Hardware Engineer at leading H/W consultancy\nTaken Classes at various IGNOU centers\nParticipated in Various Commercial Exhibitions including\n(Fonocom, inside/outside shows)\nWon prizes in table tennis at college level sports\nPersonal Details:\nFather : Mr. A.R. Khan (Retd. Gazetted Officer)\nResidence No. : 91 731 2478769\nDate Of Birth : 2nd Dec 1979\nSex : Male\nMarital Status : Unmarried\nPassport No. : F4081163\nNationality : Indian\nLanguages Known : English, Hindi, Urdu\nHobbies : Photography , \nReading\n , Listening Music\nAlternate Email : murtuza.khan@3i-infotech.com\nReferences:\n1. Munavvar Khan [Senior Project Manager at Wipro Technologies]\nEmail: munavvar.khan@wipro.com, Cell: +919342494989\n2. Zarin Khan [ Project Leader at Flextronics (Hughes) ]\nEmail: zarin.khan@flextronicssoftware.com, Cell: +919242411404\nI hereby declare that above mentioned details are correct and complete to the best of my knowledge.\nPlace: Mumbai (Murtuza Khan)','3i Infotech Ltd',1,NULL,'2007-10-17',NULL,'2007-10-17','2010-06-09 12:13:49','2010-06-09',2,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(152,'Rajesh Kumar sahu',NULL,NULL,'Hyderabad','vdvdv@gmail.com',NULL,NULL,'0','09393709371','0',NULL,'0','2005-07-14',7,19,'2010-06-09 12:13:49',2,'0',NULL,'200710/17/ATT4902.html','200710/17/DOC15326.doc','Resdex @ naukri.com\nRajesh Kumar Sahu\nvdvdv@gmail.com\n\nTelephone: 09393709371\n(M)\n 91 \n(R)\n\nD.O.B\n - Not Specified \nModified on\n - 26 Sep 2007 \nAnnual Salary\n - INR 5 Lac(s) 40 Thousand \nTotal Years of Experience\n - 4 Year(s) 10 Month(s) \nCurrent Location\n - Hyderabad \nM. Sc (IT), GNIIT with 4.7 yrs of IT exp. in System Admin, Networking Oracle DBA, Oracle Apps DBA in Unix Solaris & Linux\n\nTEXT RESUME \n\nInstallation of Oracle Application 11.5.9 and 11.5.10 on Red Hat Linux AND Release 12 as well.\nUpgrading Oracle Application 11.5.7/11.5.8 to 11.5.10\nGood experience in Patching\nExperience in Autoconfig management\nExperience in Cloning Oracle Application\nManaging Concurrent Manager and concurrent requests.\nUser management and assigning responsibilities to the users in Oracle Applications\nDuplicating (Cloning) a RAC database to a single node database.\nGood knowledge of Recovery Manager (RMan) scenarios for database backup, restore & recovery.\nImplementing of 9i RAC & 10g RAC (Real Application Cluster) on RH Linux AS 3.0\nCreation of database, Managing Tablespaces and Undo Management, user/role management.\nDuplicating (Cloning) a RAC database to a single node database.\nStrong knowledge in Oracle 10g new features. Such as Sysaux tablespace, automated storage management (ASM), automatic workload repository (AWR), space management- locally managed tablespace, transportable tablespace and undo tablespace.\nWorked as a windows administration & support executive.',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-17',NULL,'2007-10-17','2010-06-09 12:13:49','2010-06-09',2,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(153,'Malaya Das',NULL,NULL,NULL,'malsvdvaya.ddvdvas9@gmail.com','malaya.das9@gmail.com','919916452835','0','09916452835','0',NULL,'0','2008-04-29',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-09 12:13:49',2,'0',NULL,'200710/17/ATT4901.html','200710/17/DOC15327.doc','Resdex @ naukri.com\nMalaya Das\nmalsvdvaya.ddvdvas9@gmail.com\n\nTelephone: 09916452835\n(M)\n\nD.O.B\n - 28 Jan 1981 \nModified on\n - 25 Sep 2007 \nAnnual Salary\n - INR 3 Lac(s) 20 Thousand \nTotal Years of Experience\n - 2 Year(s) 4 Month(s) \nCurrent Location\n - Bangalore \nPreferred Location\n - Anywhere in India \nOracle Application(SCM)\n\nTEXT RESUME \n\nMalaya Das\nE-mail: malaya.das9@gmail.com\nMobile\n: +919916452835\nSummary:\n\n?¢\n Having 2+ years of experience in Oracle Supply Chain Management as a Functional Consultant.\n\n?¢\n Having experience in One full life cycle implementation.\n\n?¢\n Hands on experience in Functional applications in Purchasing, Inventory and Order Management modules.\nEducational Qualification:\n\n?¢\n B.E Information Technology from BPUT in 2005.\nWork Experience:\n\n?¢\n Working as a Functional Consultant in Satyam Computer Services Ltd., since May 2005 to till date.\nProject #1\n\n?¢\n Project Profile: Implementation of SCM modules (INV, \nPO\n, ONT)\n\n?¢\n Duration: Jan07 to Till Date.\n\n?¢\n Team Size: 9 Members.\n\n?¢\n Role: Team Member.\nResponsibilities:\n\n?¢\n Oracle Applications 11i implementation experience in Oracle Applications E-Business Suite consulting role, which encompasses Business Process Flow analysis.\n\n?¢\n Functional setup/configuration.\n\n?¢\n Oracle Applications module configuration.\nOracle Inventory:\nSetting up Organization parameters, Receiving Parameters, Freight Carriers, Sub-inventory Attributes, UOM conversions, Category assignments, Item Templates and attribute controls, shipping parameters, transaction types, descriptive flex fields, profile options etc.\nOracle Purchasing:\nSetting up Profile Options, Financial and Purchasing Options, Approval Limitations through groups, Assignments, Responsibility Assignments, Handling Menu Exclusions, request groups, Supplier management, modification for Lookup Codes, ASL Assignments and Sourcing Rules and Set Assignments, Descriptive Flex field Settings etc.\nOrder Management:\nSetup of selling items, Defining Customers and Credit Limits, Defaulting Rules, Processing Constraints, Item Validation Orgs, Profile Options, Transaction Types, Customer Items, Maintaining Price list etc.\nSales order entry, shipping, RMA, Drop ship, & ISO.\nProject#2\n\n?¢\n Project Profile: Supporting of Oracle E-Business Suite 11i (11.5.9)\n\n?¢\n Duration: Oct05-Dec06\n\n?¢\n Team Size: 5 Members\n\n?¢\n Role: Team Member\nResponsibilities:\n\n?¢\n Supporting Users in solving their regular day-to-day problems in the Oracle Applications\n\n?¢\n Provide functional support and Trouble shoot the issues\n\n?¢\n Prepared change request documents\n\n?¢\n Application training to new joiners\n\n?¢\n Updated other documents as per the requirements\n\n?¢\n Prepared training manuals and Conducted training program for end users\nProject Description\nAs a member of Oracle Applications Release 11.5.9 Functional Support Team, I was involved in 24Ã\n?7 solution support for the end-users day-to-day transaction troubles referred as Trouble Ticket (TT) solutions. TTs are prioritized according to their criticality as High \nPriority, Medium Priority, and Low Priority and are solved accordingly in their given period of time. Its all about providing solutions to the trouble tickets for functional as well as technical issues raised by the users and making documentation for the issues and solutions for future reference purposes.\nOther Skills:\nOracle general ledger\n\n?¢\n Entering/Posting Journals, manual JE (batch and journal entry), JE additions to an existing batch.\n\n?¢\n Reversing JE, Recurring JE (Standard, Skeleton, and Formula), posting JE\n\n?¢\n Defining the set of books, Defining the rate types, Enabling the currency.\nAccounts payable\n\n?¢\n Procure to pay (P2P)\n\n?¢\n Manage invoices, credit and debit memos\n\n?¢\n Matching invoices to the purchase orders\n\n?¢\n Maintain Expense reports\n\n?¢\n Enter and maintain the recurring invoices\n\n?¢\n Other Invoice Functions [Invoice inquiry, hold to invoice, manual batch invoices]\n\n?¢\n Maintain pre-payments\nAccount Receivables\n\n?¢\n Order to cash cycle (OTC)\n\n?¢\n Enter and Process Receivables Transactions\n\n?¢\n Enter and Process Credit Memos\n\n?¢\n Enter and Process Receipts\n\n?¢\n Perform Receivables Inquiry\n\n?¢\n Receivables Print Statements\n\n?¢\n Entering/Posting Journals\nSystem Administrator:\n\n?¢\n Responsibilities\n\n?¢\n Menus\n\n?¢\n Profile Options\n\n?¢\n Value Sets etc',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-17',NULL,'2007-10-17','2010-06-09 12:13:49','2010-06-09',2,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(154,'M Murugesan  ',NULL,NULL,'Bangalore','murugdfdfvanvsavdfsvmy@gmail.com',NULL,NULL,'0','91 9886463206','0',NULL,'0','2006-01-11',10,34,'2010-06-09 12:13:49',3,'0',NULL,'200710/17/ATT4900.html','200710/17/DOC15328.doc','Harshad Bhimani\n                                                                                                \n    \nM.Murugesan\n\n#10 1\nst\n Main, 1st Cross\n                                            \nAdugodi post, Vinayaka nagar\n                                                               \n     \nMobile\n: +91 9886463206\n                                            \n                \n              \n\n\nBangalore-560030\n                            \n                   \n         \n          \n              \n     \n  \nEmail \n  \n\nmurugdfdfvanvsavdfsvmy@gmail.com\n\n                   \n         \n                    \n              \n     \nObjective \n\nSeeking a challenging and responsible position to excel in the field of Oracle Database Administration with the latest technological developments and productively contribute towards the growth of the organization\n\n\nCareer Summary\n\n\nHave around 2+ years of experience on Oracle Database Administration.\n\nExperience Summary\n\nWorking as a \nSoftware Engineer\n\n\nin \nSYNERGY i SOFTWARE SOLUTION\n\nBangalore\n\nfrom Jan?05 to till date.\nWorked as an Engineering\n\nTrainee in Millennium Motors, \nBangalore\n from July 2003 to Nov 2004.\n\nCERTIFICATIONS\n\n         \nOracle Certified Professional (OCP) in Oracle 9i from \nORACLE\nUniversity\n\n\nEducation Details\n\nB. Tech\n from \nPondicherry\nUniversity\n, Karaikal during 2000-2003 and acquired 64\n %.\nDME \nfrom Annamalai Polytechnic, Chettinad\n\nduring 1997-2000\n\nand acquired 65%.\nS.S.L.C\n at A.M.H.S.S, Karaikudi, during 1996-1997 and acquired 53%\n\n\n   \nSkill Set\n\nOS Environment\nUnix, Linux (Redhat, SuSe),Windows NT,Sun Solaris 9\nRDBMS\nOracle 8i ,Oracle 9i \n                                      \nLanguages\nC,C++ , SQL\nTools\nNet Manager, OEM, RMAN\nOracle Utilities\nSQL Trace, TK Prof, Explain-plan,\n\nStatspack report, Cloning Database, Log miner\n\n\nOracle Skills:\n\nOracle 9i Server Installation.\n               \nReorganization and resizing of Data files, Table spaces and segments.\nStatspack Installation and analyzing Statspack report.\nMonitoring daily hot backups and\n\nweekly cold backups\nIndex rebuilding to improve query performance and Index usage monitoring.\nManaging Database Structure, Storage Allocation, Constraints, Database Access, \n       \nRoles and Privileges.\nManaging Undo segments, Table/Index segments. Monitoring Fragmentation and resolving them.\nCarried out Monthly/Weekly Maintenance of Database such as Rearrangement of segments in \n       \ndifferent Disks based on disk I/O and Identification of Chained / Migrated Rows.\n\n         \nMonitoring of Space Allocation, Temporary Tablespace Usage, CPU Usage, Shared Pool Area,\n       \nHit Ratios, etc \nLogical backup using Export and Import utility.\nExposure to logminer utility.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nResponsibilities:\n\nPerform overall health checks on the database at regular intervals to ensure smooth operation.\nCloning of Database for Test Purpose.\nApply database patches and fixes as per Client requirements\nRoutinely review database logs to review alerts and take corrective actions as deemed necessary.\nExecute backups for all databases and take corrective actions for failed backups.\nManage and maintain database security and database configuration\nAnalyzing objects (DBMS_STATS) for the performance of the database.\nReorganizing the database to avoid defragmentation and sizing the existing segments.\nDatabase performance monitoring and tuning.through STATSPACK reports.\nSolving online problems by query tuning through OEM Topsql, autotrace, SQL_TRACE, TKPROF.\nScheduling of jobs by using CRONTABS.\n\n\nPERSONAL:\n\nDate of Birth\n      \n: 01/07/1980\nPassport no\n       \n: E6013793\nMarital Status\n    \n: single\nNationality\n         \n: Indian\nLanguages \n       \n: English, Tamil, Kannada\n\n\n\nReferences:\nWill be submitted on request.','SYNERGY i SOFTWARE SOLUTION',1,NULL,'2007-10-17',NULL,'2007-10-17','2010-06-09 12:13:49','2010-06-09',3,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(155,'Napolean Nivas',NULL,NULL,'Chennai','naefpoeefnivas@gmail.com',NULL,NULL,'0','9840473656','0',NULL,'0','2007-11-12',10,34,'2010-06-09 12:13:49',12,'0',NULL,'200710/17/ATT4899.html','200710/17/DOC15329.doc','SENTHIL KUMAR\n                                                                                                                        \n     \n\n\n                 \nNapolean. M\n                                                                                      \n                        \nC-10,DR Flats\n                        \n                                                                                                                        \nNB Road, T.Nagar\n                    \n                        \n                                                                                   \n   \n           \nChennai ? 600017\nnaefpoeefnivas@gmail.com\n\n                                                                                                          \n91-44-9840473656\n\n\nObjective\n\n        \n    \nSeeking challenging position in Software Industry, which encourages my growth along with the organization.\n\nSummary\n\nA total of above 2 years of experience in IT Industry involved in Analysis, Design, Enhancement, Testing and Maintenance of Distributed applications in Manufacturing domain. Proficient in Enhancement\n\nand Maintenance of applications and have been dynamically involved in most of the phase in SDLC and client coordination. Possesses excellent communication and inter-personal skills.\n\n\nProfessional Summary\n            \nS.No\nOrganization\nDesignation\nFrom Date\nTo Date\n1.\nElectronic Data Systems\nSoftware Engineer\nMay 2005\nTill Date\n\n\nEducation Qualification\n\n        \n    \nCompleted \nB.Tech (I.T)\n from \nUniversity\n of \nMadras\n in 2004 ranked with Distinction.\n\nAdditional Qualification\n            \n\n         \nCompleted \nAccelerated NIIT\n from NIIT in 2005\n\n         \nCompleted \nOCA \nin Aug 2007\n\nTechnical Summary\n\nLanguages\n                  \n\nOracle PL\n/SQL\n, C / C++, Pro*C\nOperating System\n        \n\nSUN OS\n\nUNIX\n, Windows 98 / 2000 / XP\nDatabase\n                     \n\nOracle 9i\n, MS SQL Server 2000\nTools\n                           \n: Toad 8.0.0\n\nPersonal\n\nInformation\n\nName\n                     \n      \n: Napolean Nivas .S.M\nDOB\n            \n           \n      \n\n05-Sep-1981\n                         \nMarital Status\n         \n      \n: Single\nPassport Number\n   \n      \n: E9156494 ( Valid till\n\n07/05/2014)\n\n\nProject Summary\n   \n\nProject Title\n     \n            \n: VOMS\nOrganization\n\n\n            \n: Electronic Data Systems (I) Pvt. Ltd\nClient \n              \n            \n: General Motors\nDuration\n           \n            \n: Oct?06\n\n- Till Date\nTeam size\n        \n            \n\n\n\nRole \n                \n            \n: Team Member\nSkill\n                  \n            \n: Unix,Oracle,Pro*C, C++\nDescription\n      \n            \n\n           \n: Vehicle Order Management System (VOMS) is a GM application to manage their vehicle orders, generation of orders, specification of vehicles, sales, and security of the system. Order Management (OM) comprises of subsystems like Order Generation (OG), Vehicle Specifications (SPECS), Sales Planner Allocation (SPA) and Vehicle Maintenance Application (VMA). It provides the dealers to use the application in requesting their orders. Once the orders are placed the approval will be done by GM Authorized personal. The vehicle order generation will takes place after the approval of the orders and also based on the requirements by the dealer, their eligibility, allocation of vehicles to a dealer, sales of vehicles by the dealer. VOMS will provide all features to the client in giving secured services like authorized access, authorized user?s to use the application through VMA. \n\nResponsibilities\n\n         \nInvolved in change requirements based on client requirements\n\n         \nTo study and analyze user requirements and design the required Input/ Output formats\n\n         \nValidating and verifying the orders during batch process run.\n\n         \nPresent the proposed system to the user, designing of tables and program units, construction, unit test, plan activities\n\n         \nPreparing process related documents\n\n         \nInvolved in issue fixing to avoid the delay in production/batch cycle\n\n\nProject Title\n                 \n: RIMS \nOrganization\n\n              \n: Electronic Data Systems (I) Pvt. Ltd\nClient \n                          \n: General Motors\nDuration\n                       \n: Aug?05 ? Sep?06\nTeam size\n                    \n: 5\nRole \n                            \n: Team Member\nSkill\n                              \n: Unix, Oracle, Pro*C\nTool\n                             \n: Toad 8.0.0\nDescription\n             \n     \n\n\nRemarketing Information Management System (RIMS) application is used by the General Motors (GM) Fleet operations Remarketing organization which is currently responsible for the acquisition of used vehicles and the subsequent remarketing of those vehicles throughout the United States and Canada. RIMS supports a common business process for GM to account for their used vehicles. The common system provides for maintaining, accessing, retrieving, reporting and analyzing used vehicle information for GM.\n\nThe system has the ability to track remarketing vehicles from their return to GM control to their sale at auction. RIMS assists GM suppliers in improving their work processes and eliminating unnecessary efforts.\n\nAdditionally, RIMS is a decision support tool for the organization with functionality to assist in managing the increasing business, enabling valuable data to be more readily accessed through more effective and efficient means.\n\nResponsibilities\n            \n\n         \nInvolved in analysis and change process \n\n         \nInvolved in issue fixing to avoid the delay in production\n\n         \nInvolved in Data changes for the application\n\n         \nInteracting with the client effectively and ensure their satisfaction.','Electronic Data Systems',1,NULL,'2007-10-17',NULL,'2007-10-17','2010-06-09 12:13:49','2010-06-09',12,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(156,'Zafir A',NULL,NULL,'Banglore','khfbdfban0569fbb83@rediffmail.com',NULL,'06722 220131','0','91 9916387648','0',NULL,'0','2008-04-13',8,24,'2010-06-09 12:13:49',2,'0',NULL,'200710/18/ATT54653.html','200710/18/DOC16280.doc','Zafir A\n          \n                           \n         \nContact No\n\n\n+91-9916387648\n                        \n                                                  \n          \nEmail\n: khfbdfban0569fbb83@rediffmail.com\n\n\n                                                    \n________________________________________________________________________\n\nOBJECTIVE:\nI present myself with a strong desire to achieve the organizational goal with abounding self-confidence keeping in mind every kind of objection, resistance and obstacle as a challenge. I look forward towards a progressive and challenging career.\n\nPROFESSIONAL SUMMARY :\n\n\n        \nHaving\n 2+ years\n\nof Experience\n in \n.NET & SQL Server 2000.\n\n        \nKnowledge in \n.net Remoting.\n\n        \nKnowledge in \nweb Services\n\n\n        \nKnowledge in \nOOPs\n Concepts..\n\nEXPERIENCE:\n\n       \nCurrently working as a software engineer in \nLOGICA CMG \nthrough\n MM Softwares\n\n\nTECHNICAL EXPOSURE:\n\nProgramming Language\n\n      \n\n      \nC, C++, pl/sql\nDatabases\n                              \n\n      \nOracle9i,SQL Server 2005\n\nProducts / Projects participation\n\n\n        \nProject Synopsis # 1\n\nProject Title\n    \n    \n\nMaterial\n\nMovement For Large Scale Industry\nClient\n              \n     \n\nRockman Cycle Industries Limited (Group Of Hero Cycles), \nLudhiana\nEnvironment\n   \n     \n\nWindows2000, C#, Sqlserver2005, Crystal Report\nTeam Size\n       \n     \n\n\n\nResponsibilities\n\n\nDesign and develop code, Unit Test \n                   \n                             \n                                \nThe aim of the project is to implement the concept of material\nmovement and management, which is nothing but LOGISTIC. Logistic is \"the process of planning, implementing and controlling the efficient, effective flow and storage of raw material in-processinventory, finished goods, services and related information right from the point of origin to the point of consumption (including inbound, outbound, internal and external movement) in order tosatisfy customer\'s requirement. The main objective is\n\nto develop amaterial movement system for large industry to handle the complement movement of material\n\n\n\n\n\n\nProject Synopsis # 2\nProject Title\n                \n\n   \nStock Management System. \n            \nTechnology Used\n       \n\n   \nC#.net,Crystal Report 8.0 & SQL\n\nServer 2000.\nPlatform\n                      \n\n   \nWindows 2000\nTeam Size \n                  \n\n   \n\n            \nRole\n                            \n\n   \nCoding\n\n                                                    \nStock Management System will work as a stock\nmanagement system for an organization. It will deal with the stock in, stock storage and the stock out. It will generate the daily, weekly, fortnightly, monthly, item wise, department wise and custom based reports. With the help of this report the stock manager can decide which item stock are sufficient, which items are to be purchased.\n\nProject Synopsis # 3\nProject Title\n                \n\n   \nCRM. \n            \nTechnology Used\n       \n\n   \nASP.Net & SQL\n\nServer 2000.\nPlatform\n                      \n\n   \nWindows 2000\nTeam Size \n                  \n\n   \n\n            \nRole\n                            \n\n   \nCoding\n                                       \n    \nIt is a web based project. It can be used across\n\nthe internet or intranet. This will help customer located in remote location to interact with the company. The customers interaction with the company are in the form of registering himself. The supplier?s interaction\n\nwhich is the business to business relationship. Here supplier can register themselves and then apply tenders. It will deal with business to business and business to customer relationship.\n\nProject Synopsis # 4\nProject Title\n                \n\n   \nCall Reporting\n\n            \nTechnology Used\n       \n\n   \nAsp.net, Datagrid & SQL Server 2000.\nPlatform\n                      \n\n   \nWindows 2000\nTeam Size \n                  \n\n   \n\n            \nRole\n                            \n\n   \nCoding\n                                                    \nCall Reporting system will work as a system for\n            \ncomplain registration and their handling within an organization. It is a user-friendly and intranet application. The application is divided into main three parts.\n1. Registration of a new complain by a user and enter his remarks after the complain is solved.\n2. Accepting the new complain and assigning a technician or reassigning the problem to another technician if one whom, it is already assigned can?t solve it.\n3.Accepting the new complain and adding the remark after the problem is solve or informing the supervisor to assign the problem to next higher level technician.\n\n\n\n\n\n        \nProject Synopsis #\n\n   \nProject Title\n                \n\n       \nOnline Shopping Cart\n      \n\n\nTechnology Used\n       \n\n       \nASP.net & SQL Server 2000.\nPlatform\n                      \n\n       \nWindows 2000\nTeam Size \n                  \n\n       \n\nRole\n                                     \n\n       \nCoding \n                  \nIt is a server based application for purchasing the product\n          \nonline by placing order by Clint and also it works like ECommerce basedapplication such that the various products from various dealers can be maintained as per as it can be sold.\n\n\nACEDEMICS\n\nCompleted 4 years B.E program from Orissa engg. College, \nBhubaneswar\n in the year\n   \n2005 with Information Technology as the specialization and secured 66%.\n\nPERSONAL PROFILE:\n\n             \n           \nDate of Birth\n                 \n      \n\n      \n\nth\n June 1983.\nSex \n                             \n      \n\n      \nMale.\nNationality\n                    \n      \n\n      \nIndian.\nMarital Status\n                    \n\n      \nSingle\nLanguage Proficiency\n    \n      \n\n      \nEnglish, Oriya, Hindi.\n\nPERMANENT ADDRESS\n   \n\n                        \nS/O \n                                   \n: Mr. Abdul Hakim Khan\n                        \nQr.NO\n                               \n: NB-181\n                        \nPhone NO\n                         \n\n\n06722-220131\n                        \nCITY\n                            \n     \n: Paradip\n                        \nSTATE\n                              \n: Orissa\n                        \nPIN\n                                     \n: 754142\n\n\n\n\n                                                                                               \nPlace:\n\nBangalore\n                                                        \n_________________________\nDate\n\n\n                                                                                     \n              \nSignature\n                                                       \n                                    \n                                                                                                \n                                                \n    \n                    ','LOGICA CMG ',1,NULL,'2007-10-18',NULL,'2007-10-18','2010-06-09 12:13:49','2010-06-09',2,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(157,'Amit D',NULL,NULL,'Bangalore','dearrfgregargregmitdubrgey@gmail.com',NULL,NULL,'0','91 9880237152','0',NULL,'0','2008-04-13',10,34,'2010-06-09 12:13:49',2,'0',NULL,'200710/18/ATT54652.html','200710/18/DOC16281.doc','CV Template\nAmit D\nProject Engineer, \nWipro Technologies\nEmail: \ndearrfgregargregmitdubrgey@gmail.com\n   \n                                                               \nPhone:\n +91-9880237152\n\nExperience Summary\nTotal Experience: - 2 \nyrs\nRelevant years of experience: 1 yr 11 months\nWipro Technologies \nLocation: - \nBangalore\n(Karnataka)\nDuration: - October\n 05 ? till date\nResponsibilities: - Team member and Module lead\n\nAfter my campus recruitment from Wipro Technologies below are the details about my personal and professional information.\n\nQualifications\nDegree and Date\nInstitute\nMajor and Specialization\nBachelor of Engineering jun-2005\nMadhav Institute Of technology and Science Gwalior (M.P.)\nElectronics 69%\n\nfirst division\nHigher Secondary (state Board of M.P.) April-1999\nGovt high secondary school no.-1 ,Tikamgarh(M.P.)\nPhy, Chem., Math, English, Hindi \n67% first division with distinction in three subject\nHigh School ( state Board of M.P April-1997\nPushpa christian High School Tikamgarh (M.P.)\nAll Subjects\n   \n81% first division with distinction with national scholarship from Ministry of HRD Govt of India.\n\n\n\nTechnology\nBelow is a list of important hardware, software products, tools and methods that I have worked with.\n1.Project undertaken for Wipro Technologies\nBorland software configuration Management Project\nClient\nGlaxoSmithKline\nDescription\nThis project is a Borland?s Star Team tool for software configuration management system\nRole\nTeam member \nTeam Size\n\nResponsibilities\nSoftware configuration and management \nTools/Languages/OS\nBorland?s Starteam for Software config management.\nDuration \n4 months\n\n\n\n\n\n2.Project undertaken for Wipro Technologies\nRedirect media gateway controller\nClient\nNortel Networks\nDescription\nThis project is a C based project which is made to identify the registered as well as the non registered gateways. \nRole\nModule prime\nTeam Size\n\nResponsibilities\nCode approval and inspection ,development\nTools/Language/OS\nC , HP-Unix, also clarify AND clearcase and clearsupport for Change request related issues\nDuration\n16 months\n\n\n\n3.Project undertaken for Wipro Technologies\nLawful interception\nClient\nNortel Networks\nDescription\nThis project is basically deals in PROTEL language and to resolve the issues related to the interception of the calls made by the criminals, it involves support various markets of the world which are using this product.\nRole\nTeam Member\nTeam Size\n17\nResponsibilities\nTeam member\nTools/Language/OS\nC, HP-UNIX and Clarify clear support for defect control system.\nDuration\n16 months\n\n4.Project undertaken for Wipro Technologies(Currently working project)\nSoft Interactive voice response system\nClient\nNortel Networks\nDescription\nThis project is basically deals with the interactive voice Response system based on DIAMETER protocol and Uses My SQL for database and VC++ for GUI interaction.\nRole\nTeam Member\nTeam Size\n\nResponsibilities\nDevelopment \nTools/Language/OS\nVC++/My SQL for Developing the new application called Soft interactive voice response system.\nDuration\n\nFrom july?07 till this date.\n\n\n\nProject Documentation tools for development and Support\nProject-1\nBorland?s Star team\nClient\nGlaxoSmithKline\nDescription\nThis project is a Borland?s Star Team for software configuration management; The Documentation involves MSWORD for Technical installation reports and Technical installation Plan.\nRole\nTeam member \nTeam Size\n\nTool used \nMS-\n word\n\n\n\n\n\n\nProject-2\nGateway controller and Softswitch design enhancement documentation.\nClient\nNortel Networks\nDescription\nThis project involved documentation for the new design and enhancement in Softswitch ?gateways controller interaction messages.\nRole\nTeam member \nTeam Size\n\nTool used\nAdobe Frame maker\n\nOther Projects\n\nVisitor information and control system (submitted as Final year project to M.I.T.S. Gwalior)\nDescription\nThe project made in C ++ and had hardware integration in real time system which not only gives the information about the user but also controls the power supply also.\nRole\nTeam Leader\nTeam Size\n\nResponsibilities\n\nDesigner, coding, Testing\nTools/Language/OS\nC++\nDuration\n3 Months\n\nTechnical expertise\nHaving good networking knowledge of the OSI and communication protocols i.e. in gateway controller protocol like MGCP, MEGACO, and h.323 also good knowledge of SIP, SDP, RTP, TCP, UDP, SCTP and other VOIP related protocols\n, apart from this have a good exposure to MS-SQL server 2005 and other languages i.e. ASP.NET, C# ,HTML,VC++ with MFC and VB and good knowledge of .NET framework,OOAD with UML and My SQL with C API programming.\n\nHardware Projects (At College Level)\nFM Transmitter and Receiver\n - won 2nd prize in working model science exhibition held in 2002.\n\nSoftware Projects (At College Level)\nAirline ticketing and Management System\n - A software project developed in Visual Fox pro.\n\nPersonal Details\nDate of Birth\n10-08-1982\nNationality\nIndian\nPermanent Address\nPeeli kothi Tikamgarh (M.P.)-472001\nCurrent Address\nHouse no-22,ST bed layout, near Balaji greens apartment ,Koramangla -1\nst\n block, \nBangalore\nPassport\nF3127515 valid till 05/05/2015\n\nProfessional Memberships / Certifications \nWipro Hallmark certified in VOIP technology which includes H.323, SIP, MEGACO, RTP, MGCP etc. protocols.\nOne year Diploma in system management form APTECH computers.\nBrainbench certified in DATABASE concepts.\nE-commerce certification for ethical hacking is in progress.\nLife time member of IETE society \nNew Delhi\n\nLife time member of IEC.\nOther significant technologies knowledge\nGood knowledge of data communication and protocols, along with RFC details.\nGood knowledge of Gateway controller and gateway protocol and architecture.\n\nInterests and Activities \nSports, reading, traveling, Blog writing.\n\nAchievements \nWon govt of \nIndia\n scholarship for high school examination.\nGot the Best Team Member Award in Wipro Nortel CS2k international team, I was the Team member of the same.\n\nElected as the Secretary of IETE Student Forum M.I.T.S.\nWon second prize in working model competition for two consecutive years the school level\nWon Prize in Talent Search Exam conducted Ministry of HRD.\nWon third Prize in essay writing competition organized by department of forest govt of M.P.\nElected as a best cadet in the national service scheme camp for two consecutive years.\n   \n\nI hereby declare that the above information is true and correct to best of my knowledge.\n\n\nDate:\n    \nPlace:\n\nBangalore\n                                                                                            \nAmit Dubey','Wipro Technologies',1,NULL,'2007-10-18',NULL,'2007-10-18','2010-06-09 12:13:49','2010-06-09',2,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(158,'Sathakkathul  M  ',NULL,NULL,'Chennai','jmc_hfgdfgfgfdgaq@hotmail.com',NULL,'99452 40080','0','99411 79632','0',NULL,'0','2006-11-12',8,24,'2010-06-09 12:13:49',2,'0',NULL,'200710/18/ATT54651.html','200710/18/DOC16282.doc','CURRCULAM VITAE\n\n                                                                                       \n\n\nB5,Lakshmi Apartment,\n                                                                      \n                           \n#195,Choolamimedu High Road,\n                  \n                                                                               \nChoolaimedu,\n                                                                                                 \nChennai-600 094. \n                                                 \n                                                                 \nMobile No:+91-99411 79632(TN)\n                                                                                                                     \n+91-99452 40080\n                   \n\n  \nSATHAKKATHUL \n\n\n                        \n                   \n   \n\n     \nEmail\n\njmc_hfgdfgfgfdgaq@hotmail.com\n  \n\n                       \n     \nCARRIER OBJECTIVE:\n\nTo be associated with a progressive organization that would give me scope to apply my knowledge and skills and to be in a challenging role in software management field. \n\n\n\n      \nSUMMARY:\n\n\n         \nA Master of Computer Application graduate from \nBharathidasan\nUniversity\n\n\n         \nCreate and develop new functionalities using full software development process.\n\n         \nAbility to learn quickly and work under pressure in a fast moving environment.\n\n         \nAble to comprehend and incorporate quantitative concepts quickly and easily.\n\n         \nStrong interpersonal, communication, and organizational skills.\n\n      \nWORKING EXPERIENCE:\n\n\n         \n\norking as a Software Engineer for \nEmmoSys Technologies Pvt. Ltd,\n#30E, 2\nnd\n Floor,\nC.S.A\nPlaza\n, Ramamurthy Nagar Main Road,\nBangalore-560 016.\nWebsite: \nwww.emmosys.com\n(Apr?07 ? Till Date)\n\n\n         \n\norked as a Software Engineer for \nCAL-INFO\n(The Business Solutions Company)\n#174, Nagavarapalya Road\n,C.V RamanNagar Post,\nBangalore-560 093.\nWebsite: \nwww.cal-info.com\n(May?04 ? Mar ?07)\n\n\n         \n3+ years of experience in Software Development.\n\n         \nDeveloping controls and components\n\n         \nWorking Exposure in ASP. Net 2003&2005, C#, VB, Sql Server 2000&2005, Ms-Access.\n\n         \nWorking Exposure in designing web pages.\n\n         \nWorking Exposure in coding in C#.Net and VB.Net\n\n         \nWorking Exposure in creating stored procedures, Triggers etc,\n\n\n\n\nEDUCATIONAL QUALIFICATION:\n\n\n         \nM.C.A in \nBharathidasan\nUniversity\n (2001 - 2004) with aggregate of 71.78%\n\n         \nB.Sc., in \nBharathidasan\nUniversity\n (1998 - 2001) with aggregate of 75.86%\n(With Distinction)\n\n\n  \nTECHNICAL PROFICIENCY:\n\nOPERATING SYSTEM\n   \n\n      \nWindows NT 4.0, WIN95/98/2000/2003 Server\nDATA BASE\n                  \n\n      \nSQL Server 2000&2005, MS-Access 2000\nLANGUAGE\n             \n    \n\n\n   \nC, C++, C#\nWEBTECHNOLOGIES\n   \n\n     \nVBScript,JavaScript,HTML,\nCSS\n\nASP,ASP.Net,VB.Net,C\n#.Net,ADO.Net\n                  \n   \n\n   \nPROJECT EXPERIENCE:\n\nPROJECT # 1\n       \nTitle\n             \n        \n  \n\n        \nDispute Online Tracking System\nClient\n                          \n\n           \nWashington\n mutual \nCard\n Services (WMCS)\nPosition\n                      \n\n           \nSoftware Engineer\nRole Played\n            \n\n        \nCoding and Designing\nTeam Size\n    \n         \n\n        \n\nDurations\n               \n\n        \nMay 2007 to\n\ntill date\nSoftware\n      \n          \n\n        \nASP.Net, C#.Net,JavaScript,SQL Server 2000\nOS\n                         \n\n        \nWindows-2000 Server\nDescription\n       \n     \n   \n\n     \n   \n   \nWAMU Credit card Business is an American based leading credit card Issuer Company. DOTS is an internal application used by the dispute representatives of WMCS for resolving the disputes raised by its customer. DOTS centralizes the business rules for resolving the disputes, provides tools for users to work on cases efficiently. It increases the productivity by resolving some of the cases by the system without presenting to the user to work on the case. \n\n          \nThe system uses TSYS (Total system which has all the Information about the credit card account) for retrieving the transaction information and for updating the customer information when working on a dispute case and it also updates the status of the disputes on TSYS. Since resolving a dispute case needs the merchant bank and Association, the system will interact with VISA and MasterCard interfaces for transferring the information to Merchant Bank and to receive some information from merchant bank. \n\n          \nCommunity Integration is\n\na software platform for building web communities quickly and easily. It includes an integrated suite of all community applications such as Blogs,Forum,Review,Group and Photos. \n\nMy Responsibilities:\n\n        \nStudy of Requirement Specifications and data flow Analysis.\n\n        \nInvolved in Coding and creating for Blog,Review modules.\n\n        \nCreating stored Procedures for various tables.\n\n        \nDoing Unit test for Review,EmserverComponents module.\n\n\nPROJECT # 2\n\n     \nTitle\n             \n        \n\n\n\n        \nHospital Supervision Scheme\nClient\n                    \n\n        \nAl\n-Ameen\nMedical\nCollege\n and Hospital\nPosition\n                 \n\n        \nProgrammer\nRole Played\n            \n\n        \nCoding\nTeam Size\n    \n         \n\n        \n\nDurations\n               \n\n        \nAugust 2006 to Mar 2007\nSoftware\n      \n         \n\n\n       \nASP.Net, C#.Net,JavaScript,SQL Server 2005\nOS\n                         \n\n        \nWindows-2000 Server\nDescription \n          \n\n\n         \nThis Project does the Automation of Hospital Management System. It includes the Modules like patient Module, Billing Module, Inventory Module, Employee Module, Pharmacy Module and Reception Module. The main objective of project is to interact with the Patients and the Doctors of the hospital. Through this is web-based application hence Patients and Doctors may take information about their schedule from any sphere of world.\n\n\n\nMy Responsibilities:\n\n        \nStudy of Requirement Specifications and data flow Analysis\n\n        \nInvolved in Coding for Patient Module, Reception, Pharmacy Billing, and Tests Modules.\n\n        \nInvolved in Developing Web Pages for Patient Module, Reception.\n\n        \nInvolved in coding and creating web pages for Employee Module.\n\n        \nInvolved in coding ward and Bed details.\n\n\n\nPROJECT # 3\n\nTitle\n   \n                  \n\n\n\n        \nCal-Scribe Artifact\nClient\n                    \n\n        \nCal-Info\nPosition\n                 \n\n        \nProgrammer\nRole Played\n            \n\n        \nDesign and Development\nTeam Size\n    \n         \n\n        \n\nDurations\n               \n\n        \nAug 2005 to June 2006\nSoftware\n                \n\n        \nASP.Net, VB.Net,JavaScript,SQL Server 2000\nOS\n                         \n\n        \nWindows-2000 Server\nDescription\n     \n     \n\n    \nTh\nis Application is mainly used in medical industry during Transcription Process. CALSCRIBE is an excellent medical transcription site. It provides good security. Main idea behind this project is to enable practitioners and transcribers upload and download the voice files respectively in a sophisticated way. Practitioner initially creates voice files (.DSS, .WAV files), which will be uploaded to the location allocated by Administrator. Transcriber then wills downloads voice files and prepare document files for them, which will be used in future for reference. Administrator is responsible for maintaining users information and account information.\n\nMy Responsibilities:\n\n        \nStudy of Requirement Specifications and data flow Analysis\n\n        \nInvolved in Coding for various Modules.\n\n        \nInvolved in Developing Web Pages.\n\n\n    \nACADEMIC ACHIEVEMENTS\n\n\n\n        \nFirst class\n in SSLC, HSC, MCA\n\n        \nFirst class with \nDistinction\n in \nB.Sc\n.,\n\n        \nReceived \n\nthe certificate from the \nChief Minister \nof TamilNadu\n\n        \nDemonstrated various projects during \nSWAP-X-BIT 2002(Exhibition)\n\n    \nPERSONAL DETAILS\n\n\nName \n           \n          \n\n        \nM. Sathakkathul Haq\n\nFather Name\n\n          \n\n        \nNisa. M. Mohideen Pichai\n\nDate of Birth\n\n          \n\n        \n27-10-1979\n\nLanguages Known \n    \n\n        \nEnglish, Tamil \n\nMartial Status\n\n        \n\n        \nSingle\n\nPermanent Address\n    \n\n        \n#67,Elanthadi St\n\n                                         \nThopputhurai-614 809,\n                                         \nTamil Nadu','EmmoSys Technologies Pvt. Ltd',1,NULL,'2007-10-18',NULL,'2007-10-18','2010-06-09 12:13:49','2010-06-09',2,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(159,'Vivek s',NULL,NULL,'Delhi','sridffbvf5fbvfb4698545@yahoo.co.in',NULL,NULL,'0','9873887263','0',NULL,'0','2007-07-15',8,24,'2010-06-09 12:13:49',2,'0',NULL,'200710/18/ATT54650.html','200710/18/DOC16283.doc','Gaurav_CV\n\n                                                                                                                           \nResume\n\nVivek S\nA-65, Pandav Nagar\nDelhi\n\nMobile\n - 9873887263\nEmail- \n  \nsridffbvf5fbvfb4698545@yahoo.co.in\n     \n\n\n\nCareer Objective\n\nI am seeking a challenging technical position in a pleasant working environment, which will permit me to continue practicing and expanding my skill set and knowledge base. I am equally comfortable for a working on any Programming position. \nAs a result of my developed analytical problem solving skills and ability to learn new tasks and concept abstractions quickly, I am also more than willing to accept a position in an exciting new field that I have not yet had the opportunity to work in. \n\nSummary\n   \n\n\n         \nTotal \nExperience ? 2.6\n year as S/W Developer in .NET\n\n         \nCurrently working as \nS/W Developer\n with \nCPFR Solution\n\n         \nTechnology used - \n\nASP.Net2.0, C#,\n\nSQL Server 2000/2005, ADO.Ne\nt, crystal\n\nreport\n\nSOAP, WCF, WPF, SOA,\n\nInfragistics Framework\n).\n\n             \nKey Skills:\n\n        \nSelf organized and hard working\n\n        \nTeam player with good communication skills\n\n        \nConversant with technical to non technical translation\n\n        \nFlexible and willing to relocate anywhere in \nIndia\n and abroad\n\nDomain Knowledge\n\nDatabase\nSQL 2000/2005,\n Oracle8i,\nFramework\n.Net 1.1/2.0, Infragistics\nProgramming Language\nC#, HTML, XML,\n C, C++,Java\nScript\nJavaScript \n\nProjects handled/Training Summary\n\nCurrently working on eNurseries\nClient: Capita System (\nLondon\n, u.k.)\nPeriod: \nCurrently Working\n\neNurseries provides\n nurseries of all sizes with a wide range of capabilities and was developed to achieve 5 primary goals:\nManage the admission, registration, attendance and waiting lists of children attending nurseries, Manage staff, staff ratio, availability and scheduling \nAutomatically produce a wide range of reports Manage invoicing and payments\neNurseries allows individual nursery places and vacancies to be monitored and made available to 1 or more nurseries, to help alleviate long waiting lists and ensure that available spaces are quickly filled. The entire accounting requirements of nurseries are also addressed allowing fees to be calculated on an hourly, half day or daily basis, with accounts managed on a child or family basis. Various payment schemes can be handled, and invoices can be automatically generated. \nNurseries can also undertake a wide range of forecasting including Expected Income and Required Staffing Levels as well as reports for current NNI, future Early Years, Children?s Centre and Sure Start data submissions.\n This web site is developing in \nASP.Net2.0 /C# (Sharp) / ADO.NET/SQL-Server 2005/Infragistics\n\n                   \nPosition\n                 \n\n\n         \nTeam Member \n   \nResponsibility:\n         \n\n         \nPreparation of System Requirement Specification \n         \n\n         \nDevelopment of Forms and Objects Coding \n         \n\n         \nFinding and Fixing the Defects\n\n              \n      \nTeam Size: \n         \n\n\n\n2. \nTitle:\n\nCASHX (Power Office)\n\n   \nPeriod\n           \n\n\n4 months\n\n   \nProject\n          \n: CASHX \nis also designed as a fully functioning Business Accounting package with a comprehensive list of accounting features, including the generation of an unlimited number of Accounts and Ledgers, Trial Balancing Facilities, Bank Reconciliation, Cost Centre Analysis, Financial Projection details and Cash Flow Analysis. All these functions are supported with a graphical report generator, which gives you a clear and concise indication of the financial health of your business instantly. It brings you the power to help you keep in complete control of your business. It has a comprehensive on-line help system which contains pictures, demonstrations and a context-sensitive drag and drop facility which enables you to\n\nuse the system proficiently within hours. All of this is supplemented with the full support of a local help-desk.\nVarious Modules are:\n\n\nClient Profile\n\n\nPax Profile\n\n· Airline Master\n. Receipts Module\n\nTicket Stock Entry\n\nCheque Tracking system\n\nVoucher\n                 \nPosition\n                     \n\n           \nTeam Member\n   \nResponsibilities\n\n         \nPreparation of System Requirement Specification \n\n         \nDevelopment of Forms and Objects Coding \n\n         \nFinding and Fixing the Defects\n\n\nOperating System\n        \n  \n\n\nWindows 2000\n\nLanguages\n                     \n\n\n  \nC#.Net 2005 with Xml\n\nDatabases\n                       \n\n   \nSQL Server 2000\n\nSoftware Used\n            \n\n   \nC#.Net 2005 with Xml, Crystal Reports 9.0, SQL Server \n                           \n               \n2005, \n\n\nTeam Size\n                       \n\n\n\n3. Real Estate Online: \n\nwww.realestateonline.com\n\n Is a Commercial web site developed for Customer User Interactions, This website is developed to facilitate real estate industry professionals in the sale, purchase and leasing of all types of property located across the length and breadth of India. This web site is developing in \nASP.Net /C#(Sharp) / ADO.NET/SQL-Server 2000/\n\n   \nResponsibility:\n          \nDevelopment of user section, Database Design, and Analysis of few modules\n     \n\nTeam member:\n         \n\n\n4. \nMAXNEWYORK INSURANCE\n\nThe main objective of this project is to develop a system to efficiently monitor and manage the policy status and perform functionality at the website on-line and provide information about the various policy details agent details commissions, and the relevant information regarding the company details.\n\n      \nTools\n                        \n\nASP.NET with C#, HTML, Style Sheet, JavaScript, UML and OMT\n      \nBackend\n                   \n: SQLServer 2000\nServer\n       \n            \n   \n: IIS\n\nTeam Size\n             \n   \n\n\n\nDuration\n                \n   \n: 4 months\nResponsibilities\n    \n   \n: As a team member I was involved in designing and writing codes\n                                  \n\nfor this project.\n\n\n\nQualification\n\nQualification\nUniversity\nYear of Passing\nB.Tech \n\nUP Technical\nApr, 2005\n\nPersonal Detail\n\nDate of Birth\nApril 30, 1982\nMarital Status\nSingle\nLanguages Known\nEnglish, Hindi\nNationality\nIndian\nCorrespondence Address\nA-65, Pandav Nagar\nDelhi\n\nMobile\n - 9873887263\n\n\n\n\nDate:\n                                                     \n                                               \n           \n(Vivek Srivastava)','CPFR Solution',1,NULL,'2007-10-18',NULL,'2007-10-18','2010-06-09 12:13:49','2010-06-09',2,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(160,'Satyabrata Pradhan',NULL,NULL,'Bangalore ','mfefail2sefeatyfefeabrata@gmail.com',NULL,NULL,'0','9986959071','0',NULL,'0','2007-12-13',8,24,'2010-06-09 12:13:49',3,'0',NULL,'200710/18/ATT54649.html','200710/18/DOC16284.doc','     \n      \n                                                             \n\n\nEmail:\n mfefail2sefeatyfefeabrata@gmail.com\n\nSatya Pradhan\n                               \nMob:\n +91-9986959071 \n\n           \nCareer Objective\n\nAim to be associated with a Progressive organization that gives me the scope to share my knowledge and skills in accordance with the latest trends and be a part of team that dynamically works towards the growth of organization and gives the satisfaction thereof.\n\nWork Experience\n\nWorking as a \n.NET Developer\n for \nWipro Technologies\n\nBangalore\n from June 2005 till\n\ndate.\n\nProfessional Summary\n\n2.4 years\n of\n professional IT experiences \nin \nDevelopment, Integration \nand \nImplementation\n of\n web based architecture systems.\nCurrently working for Wipro Technologies, \nBangalore\n\n\n         \nExperienced Developer in .\nNet\n Technologies (ASP\n.NET\n, VB\n.NET\n, ADO\n.NET\n\nC#, .NET\n Framework, MS Visual Studio \n.NET\n, IIS application server)\n\n         \nExtensive experience in \nVB.NET,ASP.NET,C#, JavaScript, HTML, XML\n\n         \nExperienced in \nSDLC Concepts\n, which includes Requirement Gathering, Object Oriented Analysis, Design, Development, Testing and Documentation\n\n         \nInvolved in writing \nStored Procedures\n and \nT-SQL\n Statements. \n\n         \nExcellent analytical, communication and inter-personnel skills with exceptional ability to learn new concepts\n\n         \nA good team player, problem solver, and quick learner with analytical Skills. Ability to perform at\n high level to meet deadlines, adaptable to ever changing priorities\n\n\n\nEducational Summary\n\nB.E (Electronics & Telecommunication.)\n From \nF.M.\nUniversity\n with \n74%\n\n2005\n10+2th\n From Council of Higher Secondary Education, Orissa\n\nwith \n75%,2001\n10\nth\n From Board of Secondary Education, with \n72%, 1999\n\n    \n                                                                                             \n  \n                   \nTechnical Skills Summary\n\n\n       \n. NET Technologies\n            \n\n\nVB.NET, ASP.NET, Visual Studio.\n\nNet\n, C#\n\n       \nDatabases\n                             \n\n   \nSQL Server 2000/2005, Ms-Access\n\n       \nProgramming Languages\n\n\n   \nC.C++,HTML, XML\n\n       \nReporting Tools\n                  \n\n\nCrystal Report\n\n      \nOperating Systems\n             \n\n\nWindows 2000/XP\n\n\nProject Description\n\nProject\n   \n: 1\n\nTitel\n\n                    \n\n   \nContent Management System\nTeam size\n           \n\n\n    \n12\nRole\n                       \n\n\n    \nProgrammer\nEnvironment\n      \n\n\n   \n.C#.Net, Asp.Net.\nDuration\n              \n\n    \nAugust 2005\n\nto April 2006\nProject Description:\nContent Management System: \nCMS provides a structured mechanism of building the new content or managing existing content of your website. It also provides us a testing area where the created content is being hosted. The entire content is grilled through various phases before being made available for the website. This Project consists of five Modules.\nResponsibilities:\n\n      \nUser Interface Design and Coding\n\n      \nEffectively used ADO.NET to perform database operations\n\n      \nUsed strongly typed datasets to select, insert and update of the database.\n\n\n      \nTo provide a system for uniquely identifying the contents of baselines for multi concurrent projects.\n\nProject\n   \n: 2\n\nTitel\n                     \n\n    \nClinic Management:\nTeam size\n           \n\n    \n12\nRole\n                       \n\n    \nProgrammer\nEnvironment\n      \n\n   \nC#.Net, Asp.Net\nDuration\n            \n\n    \nJune 2006 to April 2007\n\nProject Description\n\nClinic Management:\nThis project is developed for Computer based Management of Dental Clinics.This Project Handles all the front end Management of Dental Clinics like patient Informations,Visiting doctor informations,treatment given to patient, Last OPD Date, Next OPD Date, Bill Details & finally Analysis through a number of Reports that help Management in taking Critical Decisions.\nResponsibilities:\n\n\n       \nInvolved in documenting, designing and implementing data driven, multi-tiered applications using ASP.NET and VB.NET.\n\n       \nInvolved in developing \nASP.net, C#\n pages.\n\n       \nEffectively used ADO.NET to perform database operations\n\n       \nInvolved in designing and normalizing databases, created tables, indexes, stored procedures\n\n       \nUsed strongly typed datasets to select, insert and update of the database.\n\nInvolved in designing and normalizing databases, created tables, indexes, stored procedures\nInvolved in the Creation and Maintenance of Database.\n\n\nProject\n   \n: 3\n\nTitle\n                       \n: Customer Management System\nTeam size\n           \n\n 12\nRole\n                       \n\n Programmer\nEnvironment\n      \n\nC#.Net, Asp.Net \nDuration\n             \n\n\nJune 2007 to Tilldate\n\nProject Description:\nCustomer Management System: \nThis\n\nis a user friendly, intranet application developed to maintain clean data of customer?s world wide from different systems like Files, Xmls Based and oracle systems. The application also provides the facilities of Mail Merge, Email Blasting, Template Creation, Email Status Reports and Import /Export Customer?s Lists of the customers from or to different system along with the Cleansing Activities of the customer?s database to the users based on their roles.\nResponsibilities:\n\n\nInvolved in documenting, designing and implementing data driven, multi-tiered applications using ASP.NET and VB.NET.\n\n\nInvolved in developing ASP.net,\n C#\n pages.\n\n\nEffectively used ADO.NET to perform database operations\n\n\nUsed strongly typed datasets to select, insert and update of the database.\n\n\n\nInvolved in designing and normalizing databases, created tables, indexes, stored procedures.\n\n\nInvolved in the Creation and Maintenance of Database. .\n\n\nInvolved in Analysis and Design of the Application.\n\n\nInvolved in preparation of High Level Design Document, Low Level Design Document and Design Review Checklist Templates.\n\n\nInvolved in the Overall System Documentation.\n\n\nInvolved in the Resolving Design and Technical Issues\n\n\nPrepared Detail Design Documents for various Use Cases.\n\nPersonal Summary\n\nName\n    \n                        \n   \n\n    \nSatyabrata Pradhan\nPresent Address\n            \n  \n\n    \n# 49, 8\nth\n main, 9\nth\n Cross\n                                                \nSBM colony, Mathikere\n                                                                                   \n                                                \nBangalore-54\nDate of Birth\n                 \n\n\n    \n  \n\nth\n jan.2007\nMarital Status\n    \n            \n\n\n      \nSingle\nLanguages Known\n         \n\n     \nEnglish, Hindi and Oriya.\nNationality \n                      \n\n     \nIndian\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n(Satyabrata Pradhan)','Wipro Technologies',1,NULL,'2007-10-18',NULL,'2007-10-18','2010-06-09 12:13:49','2010-06-09',3,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(161,'Vishwanath Darshan',NULL,NULL,NULL,'sagar.raste@gmail.com',NULL,NULL,'0','9892671929','0',NULL,'0','2008-04-29',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-09 12:13:49',3,'0',NULL,'200710/18/ATT54648.html','200710/18/DOC16285.doc','Summary\nI am a Developer with Patni Computer Systems with 4.5 years of total experience. I have been with Patni for 2.5 years having worked on various phases of SDLC such as Requirements and Analysis, Design and Construction & Testing. My core skills include design and development using Active Server Pages 3.0, Visual Basic 6.0, SQL Server 2000, HTML, and JavaScript, .NET, C#.\nPrior to joining Patni, I have worked in Essar Constructions Ltd. For 2 years in Import / Export department as a Purchase Executive.\n\nSkills\n\nInternet Technology\n        \nASP .Net\nTools\n                               \nVisual Source Safe\nDatabase\n                         \nSQL Server 2000\nLanguage\n                         \nActive Server Pages 3.0, Visual Basic 6.0, C #, VB.Net\nJob Functions\n                 \nRequirement Analysis, Design, Coding, Testing, Configuration Management\nOthers\n                          \n   \nAutoCAD 2000, Mechanical Desktop, Ideas, Msc / Nastran.\n\nProfessional Profile\n\nPatni Computer Systems Limited, Senior Software Engineer, May 2005 till date\n\nIntegrated front end\n\nDevelopment (Team Leader)\n                                     \nMay\n 07 till date\nFor enrolment and claims\n                      \nSoftware\n                       \n: ASP, .NET, C# and VB.NET and SQL Server 2005\n\nUniversal American Financial Corporation \nis a specialty health and life insurance holding company, with an emphasis on providing a broad array of health insurance and managed care products and services to the growing senior population. \n\n\nRoles and Responsibilities in the Project:\nHeading team of 10 members\nWork allocation and monitoring\nImplementing CMMI 5 level processes \nHigh level design\nClient communication and status reporting\n\n\n\nHeritage Today?s Options (Team leader)\n   \n                                \n                  \nJuly 06 to Apr 07\nFront End Development\nSoftware:\n ASP, HTML,\n\nJava Script, \nVB Script\n, VB, COM, DCOM & \nMS SQL Server 2000\n\nHeritage Health Systems Inc. is a Medicare Managed Care and Medical Management Organization. \nBuilding on a long history of mutually beneficial physician partnerships, Heritage aligns itself with excellent physician groups to provide outstanding quality and financial results.\n\nThe objective of the project is to develop a front end process for Today?s Options enrollment and thereby cater to the MA/MAPD business for FY ?06 and ?07. Broadly, the application will capture the enrollment information, validate information using Business in-built rules and route to corresponding Qs Queue, interface with internal/external entities, provide interface for correction, generate and track front end letters and send details to the backend.\n\nRoles and Responsibilities in the Project:\nAnalysis, design of functionality and Preparing technical specification of the same\nCoding the new modules, which would implement the functionality\nSystem testing of the various functionalities.\nProject related document preparation.\nCo-ordination with team. \n\n\nMedicare Part-D Application (Programmer)\n                        \n      \n                  \nJune 05 to July 06\nSoftware\n: ASP, HTML,\n\nJavaScript, \nVB Script\n, VB, COM, DCOM and \nMS SQL Server 2000\n\nUniversal American Financial Corporation \nis a specialty health and life insurance holding company, with an emphasis on providing a broad array of health insurance and managed care products and services to the growing senior population. \n\nThe objective of this project is to provide an interface to enter data for Medicare Part-D enrollments. The application broadly captures data from the Medicare-D enrollment forms, sends the data for validation to a central agency and then further forwards the data to the administration system at UAFC. The Patni developed application handles Paper & electronic enrollments. Various MIS reports generated out of the system help facilitate process and tracking & Performance.\n\nRoles and Responsibilities in the Project:\nAnalysis, design, code and Test functionality\nProject related document preparation.\nProcess all Group enrollments and provide support for BPO.\n\nEssar Constructions Ltd, \nIndia\n, Logistic Engineer\n                    \n                     \nJune 03 to May 05\n\nRoles and Responsibilities in the Project:\n\n\n          \nConducting Imports through Sea / Air consignments.\n\n          \nApplying for Export Promotion (like EPCG) and import licenses (like Negative list licenses) in the office of Director General of Foreign Trade (DGFT).\n\n          \nDealing with Marine Cargo Insurance companies for arranging for Cargo Insurance.\n\nAchievements\n\n\n       \nRated as an ?Excellent? performer with ?Tremendous growth potential?\n\n\n       \nGot quarterly ?Knowledge Star? award from Patni knowledge forum.\n\n       \nReceived ?Letter of appreciation? from Patni Computer Systems Ltd.\n\n       \nConducted session in ?Communities of Practices? forum.\n\nPersonal & Academic \nBachelor of Engineering (B.E) in Mechanical engineering ? 2002 ? First Class, \nBharati\nVidyapeeth\nCollege\n of Engineering,\nMumbai University\n\nIndia\n\nEmail: sagar.raste@gmail.com\n   \n, Contact: +91-9892671929\nDate of Birth: 04-Nov-1980\nResidential Address ? A/14, Vishwanath Darshan, Dombivli, Thane ? 421201',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-18',NULL,'2007-10-18','2010-06-09 12:13:49','2010-06-09',3,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(162,'Shyam sunder',NULL,NULL,'Noida','shyfbfdbbam.rishfbfbikesh@gmail.com',NULL,NULL,'0','91 9953309328','0',NULL,'0','2008-04-13',8,24,'2010-06-09 12:13:49',3,'0',NULL,'200710/18/ATT54647.html','200710/18/DOC16286.doc','RESUME\nCURRICULUM - VITAE\n\n\nSHYAM SUNDER\n         \n           \n                     \n\nE-mail:\n\nshyfbfdbbam.rishfbfbikesh@gmail.com\n\n                                                                        \n  \nMobile:\n\n+91-9953309328\nCurrent Address:\n                             \n                 \n       \n     \nF-47, Sector-27\nNoida (U.P)\n                    \n                                                                                                         \n\nExperience(1.3 Year)\n            \nEmployer\n                   \n:- \n        \nRM Infotech\n          \nWork Experience\n\n    \n:-\n\n      \nSince July2006 till Date.\n          \nDesignation\n            \n:-\n\n        \nJr. Software Engineer \nCurrent CTC\n              \n:-\n       \nRs. 9,6000/- per annum\nExpected CTC\n           \n:-\n       \nRs. 1,20000/- per annum\nInterview avail\n         \n:-\n       \nWeekends \nNotice Period\n            \n\n\n       \nAt least 15 days.\n\n\n\nObjective\n                        \nSeeking a position to utilize my skills and abilities in the Information Technology Industry that offers professional growth while being resourceful, innovative and flexible.\n\n\nPersonal Skills\n          \nExcellent verbal and written communication skills, ability to gel in a team, willingness to learn, hard working and committed to excellence.\n\n\nProfessional Qualification\n\n         \n?A? Level from DOEACC SOCIETY.\n\n\n   \nPursuing M.C.A. from M.D. University Rohtak (Haryana).\n\n\nEducational Qualification\nM.Sc.\n       \nP.T.L.M.S. College, Rishikesh\n     \nGarhwal University\n\n2004)\n     \nB.Sc.\n       \nP.T.L.M.S. College, Rishikesh\n     \nGarhwal University\n\n2002)\n     \n12\nth\n         \nS.B.M Inter College, Rishikesh \n   \nU.P. Board (1999)\n                 \n10\nth\n         \nP.S.K Inter College, Rishikesh \n   \nU.P. Board (1997)\n                 \n\n\nTechnical Skills\n          \n   \n       \nLanguages\n                        \n\n\nC++, Asp.net, C#\n          \nOperating System\n       \n     \n\n\nMS-Windows-9x/2k/xp, Unix.\n   \n       \nDatabase\n                    \n      \n\n\nSqlserver 2005, Oracle 9i (Sql concept)\n    \n     \n    \nApplication/Packages\n     \n\n\nMS?Office-2000, Office-XP \n    \n       \n   \n\n     \nWeb Technology:\n\n\n      \nClient Side\n                    \n\n    \nJava Script\n\n      \nServer side\n                 \n\n    \nAsp.Net\n\n      \nDesign Tool\n                  \n\n    \nDreamweaver 8.0, HTML.\n\n\nProject Details\n\n\nProject 1\n        \n\n\n       \nLibrary Management System\nTeam size\n      \n\n\n       \n\nDuration \n        \n\n     \n    \n6months\nFront End\n       \n\n           \nC#.net 2005\nDatabase\n      \n\n         \nSqlserver2005\nClient\n            \n\n        \nInfo Institute Of Information Technology\n\nBrief Profile\n          \nIts keeps records of the books available, issued, penalty on the late return of the book. It also shows the books details category wise\nand student details who has taken the books and various features. \n\n         \n      \nInvolved in Development. \n\n         \n      \nCreation of objects and data types for all objects.\n\n\n\nProject 2\n        \n\n\n       \nComputer Resource Management System\nTeam size\n      \n\n\n       \n\nDuration \n        \n\n    \n\n    \n6months\nFront End\n       \n\n           \nC#.net 2005\nDatabase\n     \n\n\n         \nSqlserver2005\nClient\n            \n\n        \nCompany itself\n\nBrief Profile\n          \nIts keeps track of the resources in the company, software as well as hardware, which are\n    \nplaced in various departments and in various locations of the company\n\n\n         \n      \nInvolved in Design, coding and unit testing. \n\n         \n      \nCreation of objects and data types for all objects.\n\n\n\n\nExtra Curricular Activities\n\n\n        \nAchieved\n First Prize in Essay Writing at School Level.\n\n        \nOrganized \nmany\n\nCultural Programs at school and college level.\n\n        \nAttended \nmany Seminars of IT.\n\n\nPersonal Profile\n    \nFather?s Name\n             \n\n     \n   \nShri M.R.Singh\nDate of Birth\n                      \n\n    \n  \n\n6-06-1982\n          \nPermanent Address\n   \n         \n\n\n\n   \n   \n\nShyam Sunder Singh\n                   \n     \n    \n   \n   \nP.W.D inspection House\n                        \n    \n   \n  \n\nRishikesh(U.T)\nNationality\n                        \n\n     \n  \nIndian\nMarital Status\n                    \n\n\n   \n   \nSingle\nLanguage Known\n                \n\n\n   \n   \nEnglish & Hindi.\nHobbies\n                            \n\n\n      \nSwimming, Net Surfing, listening music\n          \nPlace of Birth\n                     \n\n\n      \nRishikesh\n\n\nArea of Interest \n\n\n       \nC#.net, ASP.net, Sql Server\n\n\nDeclaration:\n\n                       \nI hereby declare that the above-mentioned information is correct up to my knowledge and I bear the responsibility for the correctness of the above-mentioned particulars.\n\nPlace: Noida\nDate:\n                                                                     \n\nShyam Sunder Singh','RM Infotech          ',1,'9,6000/- p','2007-12-14','1,20000/- ','2007-12-14','2010-06-09 12:13:49','2010-06-09',3,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(163,'Saleem Mohammad',NULL,NULL,NULL,'salvvdvem.saledvdvem.m@gmail.com',NULL,NULL,'0','91 9342775753','0',NULL,'0','2007-04-30',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-09 12:13:49',3,'0',NULL,'200710/18/ATT54646.html','200710/18/DOC16287.doc','Saleem Mohammad\n\nS Mohammad\n       \nMobile\n\n+91 9342775753\n          \nMail to: \nsalvvdvem.saledvdvem.m@gmail.com\n\n\n\nWork Experience\n\n\nHaving 3+ years\n\nof Software Development Experience in \n.Net\n Technology.\n\n          \n\nWorking as a Software Developer in \nWIPRO\n\nTechnologies ,\n\nBangalore\n\nsince\n    \nAugust\n\n2006 to Till date\n\n\n         \nWorked as Software Associate in \nCERULEAN Infotech\n\nBangalore\n from July 2004 to July 2006.\n\nSoftware design, Development and Maintenance.\nExtensively developed applications using \nASP. Net, VB.Net, \nand\n C#. Net \nwith backend\n                        \nas \nSQL Server\n\nGood Knowledge in \nADO.Net\n\n.Net Framework\n\nXML\n\nKnowledge in Creation of \nStored Procedures\n, Writing Complex Queries in SQLServer2000.\n\n\nEducational Details:\n\nB.Tech (Electronics & Communications)\n From \nJNT\nUniversity\n\nHyderabad\n in 2004\n\n\nTechnical Expertise:\n\nOperating System\nWindows 98/2000.\nProgramming Languages\nC#. NET, VB.NET\n, C.\nBack-End\nSQL Server\n\nInternet Tools\nASP.NET\n\nADO.NET\n, IIS, HTML.\nScripting Languages\nJavaScript\n\n\nNET Framework\nGood knowledge in\n\n.NET framework\n\n\n\n\nProject Profile:\n\n1. \nProject Name\nGlobal Holistic.\nClient\nWellness International, \nUSA\n\nRole\nAnalysis, Designing & Coding.\nDuration\n02/2007 ? Till Date.\nSoftware & Tools\nIIS, C#. NET, ASP. NET, \nADO\n. NET, HTML, SQL Server.\n\nProject Description:\n\nGlobal Holistic Inc is a \nChicago\n based \nAyurvedic\nHospital\n. This web site is an online Diagnosis and e-commerce application where customers (Patients) can approach physicians online and also patients can shops the Ayurvedic products through website\n\nFor this customer can buy online diagnosis form. Patients can participate in Discussion forum. Admin can view the diagnosis form and forward to physician and then\n   \nphysician response to the diagnosis form. Patients can participate in discussion forums, where Patients can post their queries.\n\nResponsibilities:\n\nInterpreting the analysis by the client team and converting it into the low level design.\nAnalyzing the requirements of the individual use cases and coded the same.\nDeveloping User Interfaces.\nInvolving in the development.\n\n\n2. \nProject Name\nVirtual Slabs.\nClient\nGlobal \nE-Sourcing\n\nUSA\n\nRole\nAnalysis, Designing & Coding.\nDuration\n07/2006 ? 01/2007.\nSoftware & Tools\nIIS, C#. NET, ASP. NET, ADO.NET, Java Script, HTML, SQL Server.\n\n\nProject Description:\n\nThe Purpose of this project is to develop a web site which will enable users to search different types of stones, Slabs, Marbles, Granites and Blocks on the bases of various properties of these items like color, supplier name, manufactured at, stone origin, thickness etc.\nThis site will also enable suppliers to bye license online using Skipjack Financial Services for adding there products into the sites catalogue.\n\nResponsibilities\n\nDesign front view screens of the applications and maintaining database connections.\nInvolved in developing business logic, developing data operations using ADO.NET.\nInvolved in developing request process operations using .NET Framework and dynamic content generation and presentation using ASP.NET.\n          \n\n3. \nProject Name\nLeads Express.\nClient\nGlobal \nE-Sourcing\n\nUSA\n\nRole\nAnalysis, Designing & Coding.\nDuration\n07/2005 ? 06/2006.\nSoftware & Tools\nIIS, C#. NET, ASP. NET, ADO.NET, HTML, SQL Server.\n\nProject Description:\n\nThe Purpose of Leads Express is to provide consumers with an easy to understand, efficient means of querying a large consumer list database, and then purchasing only those records they feel will bring profits for their marketing effort. Consumers can use this web site to select demographic, geographic or other criteria that will act to filter this large online consumer database and receive a specifically targeted data file. \nThe main functionality of this site is enable consumer to query a large database to get the count of records satisfying the search query then pay online to get the actual address of the searched records.\n\nResponsibilities:\n\nDesign front view screens of the applications and maintaining database connections.\n            \n4. \nProject Name\nGranite Liquidators\n\nClient\nGlobal E-sourcing.\nRole\nAnalysis, Designing & Coding.\nDuration\n09/2004 ? 06/2005.\nSoftware & Tools\nIIS, C#. NET,ASP. NET, \nADO.NET, SQL Server. \n\nProject Description:\n\n              \nThis application is an E-business and Search engine site to Search for Blocks. The application has 3 modules 1.adminstator 2.supplier 3.user. \n   \nAdmin part can edit/add new categories, subcategories, addresses and Licenses to suppliers. Suppliers can add new items to site and they can buy the License for categories, which are added to the given site. \n\nThe application will allow users with an account to purchase such product by size, color, Zip, address and etc. The application will make use of an e-commerce system to clear funds transfer for the purchase. The application will allow the user to choose from some predefined delivery methods. The application will deliver the product (data file) to the end user.\n\n\nResponsibilities:\n\nDeveloped individual menus like supervisor menu, point of contact menu, and accessor menu. Developed database operations using ADO.NET.',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-18',NULL,'2007-10-18','2010-06-09 12:13:49','2010-06-09',3,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(164,'Vibha Grover',NULL,NULL,NULL,'vibhahfghhhghgro@gmail.com',NULL,'9911114283','0','9891900262','0','09254320540','0','2008-04-29',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-09 12:13:49',2,'0',NULL,'200710/18/ATT54645.html','200710/18/DOC16288.doc','Vibha Grover\nVibha G\nJ3-263, DDA Flats, KalkaJi, New Delhi-110019 (\nIndia\n\nTel. Nos. +91 ? 9891900262, 9911114283, 09254320540\nEmail: \nvibhahfghhhghgro@gmail.com\n\nTotal Experience :- 2+ Years\nPassport : Ready (Valid up to Feb. 2015)\nRelocation : Willing to relocate\nProfile:\n\n\nHaving \n2+\n years exp. and seeking a challenging career that will utilize my professional skills and give me an opportunity for creativity, self-improvement.\nWork Experience:\n\n\n\n\n\nOrganization: Trisoft Global Pvt Ltd. \n\nNew Delhi\nDuration: \n20.July.2\n007 - till date\nJob Profile: \nCurrently\n\nWorking as a A\nssociate Software Engineer \nProject Parikrama.\nProject Parikrama that enables any entity in tourism to get real-time integration with agents and generate better revenues that ever before\n\n\n\nOrganization: \nAlien Softnet Technology Pvt. Ltd., \nNew Delhi\nDuration: \n\n1.Sep.\n2006 ? 19.July.2007\nJob Profile: \n\norked on the Indo Gulf Pest Control Management System project as a Team Member. It is an ERP based three-tire architecture application. This Project maintains all the information of Client Contacts, Stock, Payroll, and Invoices & Reports. This software can handle so many clients at a time & it works within the organization.\n\n\n\nOrganization: \nGraffiti IT Services Pvt. Ltd., \nNew Delhi\nDuration: \n10.\nOct.05 \n\n- 25.Aug.06 \nJob Profile: \nWork experience of 1-year (app.) in media domain. The main area of expertise includes \nAccounts, Campaign, Non-Campaign, Release Order CRM using \nXpertMedia \n(Application fulfilling the needs of Ad agency),\n a product by Graffiti Media Group, implemented successfully across the leading Ad-Agencies throughout \nIndia\n\n\n\n\nQualifications:\nDegree\nInstitute \n\n& University / Board\n\nYear of Passing\nPercentage\nMCA\nSSJITM, Sirsa\n\nKurukshetra\nUniversity\n, Kurukshetra)\n2005\n73.5\nB.Com\n\nSSJGS, Sirsa\n\nKurukshetra\nUniversity\n, Kurukshetra)\n2002\n60.6\n12\nth\nDurga\nVidya\nMadir\nGirls\n\n\nSchool\n, Tohana\n(HSEB, Bhiwani)\n1999\n51.8\n10\nth\nGovt.\nGirls\nS.\nS.\nSchool\n, Tohana\n(HSEB, Bhiwani)\n1997\n47.6\n\n\n\n\nSkills:\nLanguages\nVisual Basic, C#.Net\nWeb Technologies\nASP.Net, ADO.NET, XML, HTML\nBrowser Scripting\nJava Script \nDatabase\nMS SQL 2000, Oracle 9i\n\n\nProjects Details:\nClient:\n    \nUttranchal Govt.\nProject : Parikrama\nProject Parikrama enables an entity in tourism to get real-time integration with agents and generate better revenues that ever before. This Product found customers and vendors at the conceptual stage through haridwar online this product gained investment from uttranchal Govt.Through Parikrama a person can book his entire trip from booking a room in a hotel or booking a seat in a restaurant to book a cab etc. It has domain like Search a Facility, Book a Facility and Package and Maintenance etc I \n\nhave worked on Search a Facility, Book a Facility and Maintenance and actively participated on all other domains too. In Search a Facility one can search a available room by giving some criteria in Book a Facility one can book that a Room, which\n\nis available on these dates and if it so one can book it. In Package a hotel owner can add, update and delete a tourism package a user can search package and book it. This Product uses Web Services and XML.\nDuration\n:20th July 2007-till date\nTechnology: \nASP.net, Java Script, C#, SQL Server 2000\nRole:\n Team Member\nResponsibilities: \nI have involved in Maintenance Module of Project Parikrama.\nMaintenance:\nCreate Maintenance\nMaintenance Schedule\nMaintenance Task\nMaintenance Transaction\nMaintenance Scheduled Information\n\nClient: \nIndo\nGulf\n, Noida\nProject: \nIndo\nGulf\nPest\n Control \n\nManagement System\nIndo Gulf Pest Control is a \nDelhi\n based Company works for government and private sector pest controlling. Companie?s most of the work was a manual one but they were facing problem for their track records their, in all the sectors, so they were in a requirement a one man show for its maintenance.\n\nThat?s why they wanted software to handle all the sectors. This project gives more functionality to handle problems like Client contacts, their stock, payroll, invoices, and inventories. \nDuration\n: 1.Sep.2006 ? 19.July.2007\nTechnology: \nASP.net, Java Script, C#, SQL Server 2000\nRole: \nTeam Member \nResponsibilities\n: I am involved in Enquiry Management, Payroll System and Stock Maintenance.\n\n\n\nClient: \nImpact Advertising Agency, \nNew Delhi\nProject: \nXpertMedia \nDuration\n: Jun ?06 ? Aug? 06\nTechnology: \nASP.net, Java Script, C#, SQL Server 2000\nDescription:\n Web based application\n\nfor Estimates, Release Orders, Inventory, Scheduling, Finance, Reports, and Customer Relationship Management. \nRole: \nModule Lead for Accounts Module. \nResponsibilities:\n\n       \nMentored the team in functional and technical implementation of Accounts module.\n\n       \nRequirements review and design preparation.\n\n       \nSuccessfully worked on forms Account Creation, Journal Voucher, Cheque Dishonor, Payments,\n    \n\nReceipt and Billing Status.\n\nClient: \nMak Ad-Agency, Pune \nProject: \nXpertMedia \nDuration\n: Oct? 05- Aug? 06\nTechnology: \nVisual Basic 6.0, SQL Server 2000, Crystal Report\nDescription: \n\nesktop application\n for the ad-agencies in \nIndia\n\n All the processes of ad-agency can be handled by using online version of \nXpertMedia\n. Different modules are Estimates, Release Orders, Creative, Inventory, Scheduling, Finance, Reports, Customer Relationship Management.\nRole: \nTeam Member \nResponsibilities:\n\n       \nWorked in different modules of \nXpertMedia\n product. These are CRM, Release Orders, Accounts and Campaign. \n\n       \nSuccessfully created Reports using Crystal Reports.\n\nAcademic Project:\n\n\nClient: \nMinistry of Communication & Information Technology, \nNew Delhi\nProject: \nOnline Evaluation System\nDuration\n\n\nst\n Jan 2005\n-30\nth\n June 2005\nDescription: \nThis project is for National Level Computer Literacy Excellence Award. ?Online Evaluation System? is automation of the National School Computer Literacy Excellence Award. In this award, marks are allotted to schools according to online forms filled. There are six forms named General Information, Activity, Faculty, Infrastructure, Social Responsibility, and Teach Method. The forms contain all the information about schools as infrastructure, software, hardware, computer labs, availability of computers/facilities to the students etc. \n\nRole: \nTeam Member \n\nResponsibilities:\n\n       \nRequirements reviewed and prepared designs.\n\n       \nSuccessfully \nCreated database schemas and tables.\n\n\n\nAchievements:\n\n       \nOrganizer\n of IT\n Quiz held in SSJITM, Sirsa. \n  \n\n       \nParticipation \nin KSHITIJ of C.S.E. Department? \nGuru\nJambeshwar\nUniversity\n, Hisar.\n\n       \nParticipation\n in Annual\n Fete\n (cultural event) in SSJITM, Sirsa.\n\n\n\nPersonal Details:\nFather?s Name\nMr. Krishan Kumar Grover\nMother Name\nMrs. Usha Rani\nDate of Birth\n\nrd\n Aug, 1983\nNationality\nIndian\nMartial status\nSingle\nLanguage Known\nEnglish, Hindi and Punjabi',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-18',NULL,'2007-10-18','2010-06-09 12:13:49','2010-06-09',2,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(165,'S B. Kondewar',NULL,NULL,NULL,'skodbfbndefbfwar@yahoo.com','saffbfchdfbin.kofdbfbndewafbr@gmail.com',NULL,'0','9849687297','0',NULL,'0','2008-04-29',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-09 12:13:49',3,'0',NULL,'200710/18/ATT54644.html','200710/18/DOC16289.doc','Curriculum Vitae\nS B. Kondewar\n\nEmail Id:- \nskodbfbndefbfwar@yahoo.com\n               \nsaffbfchdfbin.kofdbfbndewafbr@gmail.com\nMobile No:-+91-9849687297\n\nSUMMARY\n\n\n\n          \n2+ years of experience in the area of Application Software development.\n\n          \nSound knowledge of Application development Asp.net,C#.net,ADO.net,\nAjax\n\n\n          \nWeb Services , Remoting Concepts ,Certification.\n\n          \nSound knowledge of RDBMS, OOP?s Concepts, \n\n          \nStored Procedures ,Functions , Triggers.\n\n          \nSound Knowledge of\n\nDesigning\n\nComponents\n\n          \n2 Tier,3 Tier ,n Tier Architecture\n\n          \nUnderstand and contribute to business strategy.\n\nPROFESSIONAL EXPERIENCE:\n\n\n          \nPresently Working as \n\nSoftware Engineer in I-Nest Solutions , \nHyderabad\n. From \n18 March 2005\n to till date.\n\nSKILL SET:\n\n\n          \nLanguages :\n C#.NET,ADO.NET\n\n          \nDatabase Related :\n Sql-Server2000, Sql-Server2005.\n\n          \nOperating Systems :\n Microsoft Windows 98/2000/NT/XP,Win2k VPC\n\n          \nWeb Technologies :\n ASP.Net, \nAjax\n,HTML,XML,Java Script,Web Certificates.\n\n          \nReport Tools : \nCrystal\n Reports.\n\nEDUCATIONAL PROFILE:\n\n\n          \nMaster of Computer Applications (M.C.A) \nFrom \nPoona\nUniversity\n,Pune,\nMaharashtra\n\n\n\n          \nB.Sc.(Maths) \nFrom \nShivaji\nUniversity\n\nKolhapur\n\nMaharashtra\n\n\nPROJECT DETAILS:\n\nProject \n\n\n\n\n       \n                     \n\nTitle: Asset Management System\n\nDescription: Asset Management System\n\nis one of the\n\nmain and Important module of\n\nWeb Application Smart Help Desk\n   \nManagement System shortly termed as SHDMS.It is backbone of the SHDMS.It has been developed to get the information of each\nand particular System in Huge N/w.so It helps technician to detect the problems also It helps to get the Information of particular \nsystem in Huge N/w.so by getting this Information\n\nso user can underastand easily which systems are working properly in the N/w \nor which devices are get enabled or disabled so He can forward the problem to the technician.ADSI and WMI is key concepts in this Application.Using ADSI we get total information about Users,Computers,Devices etc.\nWMI is giving particular and\n\ndetail Information of each and every system e.g How many S/w were Installed,What is Configuration of System,Devices Information of Keyboard,Mouse,USB port etc.What is Configuration of Processor,Information about Hard Disk etc.\n\nRole\nDeveloper\nTeam Size\n\nPlatform/Tools\nMicrosoft VS.Net 2.0v.,windows 2000 server and\n\nWin2k Virtual PC\nFront End Tool\nAsp.net,\nAjax\n using C#.net\nTool\nWeb Certification\nDatabase\nSQL Server2000\nResponsibilities\n\n        \nPreparing the web applications and queries for accessing the database.\n\n        \nInvolved in Discussions on Project Analysis\n\nin Design Phase.\n\n        \nInvolved in coding modules according to the Microsoft standards.\n\n        \nInvolved in Writing Stored Procedures.\n\n        \nCreating Web Service,Windows Service,Use of Threading Concepts in Application.\n\n        \nStudying and Analysing WMI and ADSI Concepts to Use in Application.\n\nProject 2\n\n\n                          \n\nTitle: Exports Tracking\n\nSystem\n\nDescription: \nExports System is a web application that has been developed for exporting the goods to nationalized and internationalized customers(Esp. Dealers,Wholesalers,Retailers).The customer orders the specific quantity of the goods and the way of transportation. Based on the customer?s requirements the company estimates the total cost needed to export the goods. If the customer has satisfied with the cost and the features then the agreement will be established between them.\n\nOnce the agreement has been established then the company will starts the process and the customer has no rights to modify the agreement. The major idea is to provide a series of services to the customer through the internet, and make the customer feel flexible in calling out simple tasks faster instead of making contact to the company several times.\n\nRole\nDeveloper\nTeam Size\n\nPlatform/Tools\nMicrosoft VS.Net 1.1v.,windows 2000 server\nFront End Tool\nAsp.net using C#.net\nReport Tool\nCrystal Report\nDatabase\nSQL Server2000\nResponsibilities\n\n        \nPreparing the web applications and queries for accessing the database.\n\n        \nInvolved in Discussions on Project Analysis and Assisted as technical\n\nmember in Design Phase.\n\n        \nInvolved in coding modules according to the Microsoft standards.\n\n        \n<nvolved in generating reports for User Responses\n\n        \nInvolved in Writing Stored Procedures,Functions.\n\nProject 3\n\n                \n            \n\nTitle: Retail Products Information System\n\nDescription: Retail Products Information System\n\nis a web application that has been developed for\n   \ncustomized shopping\n\nthe goods to nationalized and internationalized customers.The wide variety of all\n   \nbranded products The customer orders the specific quantity of the goods/products & through visa card or cheque/DD. they can buy the product online easily. Based on the customer?s requirements If the customer has satisfied with the cost and the features then has to register as user or if existing user then they can buy the product directl.\nThe major idea is to provide a series of services to the customer through the internet, and make the customer feel flexible in buying the product at ease with same price or low price depend on products with better service at home .\n\nRole\nDeveloper\nTeam SIze\n\nPlatform/Tools\nMicrosoft VS.Net 1.1v\nFront End Tool\nAsp.net using C#.net\nReport Tool\nCrystal Report\nDatabase\nSQL Server2000\nRole\n\n        \nPreparing the web applications and queries for accessing the database.\n\n        \nInvolved in Discussions on Project Analysis ,\n Domain knowledge \nand Assisted as technical\n\nmember in Design Phase.\n\n        \nInvolved in coding modules according to the Microsoft standards.\n\n        \n<nvolved in generating reports for User Responses\n\n        \nInvolved in Writing Stored Procedures,Functions.\n\nProject 4:\n\n                           \n\nTitle: Accounting Package\n\nDescription: \nThis is The Accounting application module of the ERP Software.It Contains Master,Transaction,Reports sub module.It facilitate all\n\nthe functionality of daily,weekly,monthly,yearly accounting transactions of the company and capability of handling\nvoluminous and very imp. data for daily transactions in safe & secure manner for those who are authorised & authenticated user\n\nonly so strong security is key point in this package.\n\nRole\nDeveloper\nTeam Size\n\nPlatform/Tools\nMicrosoft VS.Net 1.1v.\nFront End Tool\nC#.Net\nDatabase\nSQL Server2000\nReport Tool\nCrystal Report\nRole\n\n        \nThe sub module i was working most is Master,Transaction,Designing Reports.\n\n        \nI was helping more in transactions like purchase,sales,cash voucher,cash receipt etc. & in generating trial balance reports,day book reports,register,income statement and\n\nqueries for accessing the database.\n\n        \nInvolved in Discussions on Project Analysis and Assisted as technical\n\nmember in Design Phase.\n\n        \nInvolved in coding modules according to the Microsoft standards.\n\n        \n<nvolved in generating reports for User Responses\n\n        \nInvolved in Writing Stored Procedures,Functions\n\nProject 5:\n                            \n\nTitle: Human Resource Management System\n\nDescription: \nThis is The Human Resource Management System module of the ERP Software.It maintains \nall the employee data of the company, from daily to monthly sal transactions of employee,also maintains all employee activities like leave,bonus,allowances expenditure for the company like that. It maintains all employee data in Hierachical manner from Top Level management to Bottom Level Management.\n\n\nRole\nDeveloper\nTeam Size\n\nPlatform/Tools\nMicrosoft VS.Net 1.1v\nFront End Tool\nC#.Net\nDatabase\nSQL Server2000\nReport Tool\nCrystal Report\nRole\n\n        \nInvolved in Discussions on Project Analysis and Assisted as technical\n\nmember in Design Phase,\n in analyzing the data in hierarchical manner and help to design & implement RDBMS concept in designing database.\n\n        \nThe sub module i was working\n\nmostly on generating Reports.\n\n        \nI was helping more in generating reports for monthly income statement of the employees. & expenditure that have done for company purpose by the employees like visiting to the client side etc. \n\n        \nInvolved in Writing Stored Procedures,\n\n\n                                                                                 ',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-18',NULL,'2007-10-18','2010-06-09 12:13:49','2010-06-09',3,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(166,'Sankalan Panda',NULL,NULL,NULL,'sasvsvnkalan.pansvsvda@hotmail.com',NULL,NULL,'0','91 9861140003','0',NULL,'0','2006-02-11',8,24,'2010-06-09 12:13:49',2,'0',NULL,'200710/18/ATT54643.html','200710/18/DOC16290.doc','SANKALAN PANDA\n\nSANKALAN PANDA\nEmail: \nsasvsvnkalan.pansvsvda@hotmail.com\nPhone No: \n+91-9861140003\n\n\nPROFESSIONAL EXPERIENCE:\n\n         \nIn my total \n3 Years 9 months of IT experience\n, I have worked on many projects in .NET 2003 and ColdFusion (7.0.0, 7.0.2, 8.0).\n\n         \nWorked with\n\ntwo IT firm\n\nsince August 2003. Presently working with \nMindfire Solutions\n\nwww.mindfiresolutions.com\n\n\n         \n\n\nB.Tech\n graduate with specialization in \nComputer Science & Engineering\n\n\n         \nStrong programming skills in implementing algorithms for implementation of business logic in effective and efficient manner.\n\n         \nExpertise in developing web application and CMS software in ColdFusion.\n\n         \nAlso have expertise in developing both desktop and web application software in VB.NET, C#.NET.\n\n         \nHave good knowledge in Flash ActionScript and also implementing Flash Remoting with both ColdFusion and .NET.\n\n         \nExpertise in design and development of database architecture for projects in SQL 2000, SQL 2005 and MySQL. \nExperience in using SQL/PLSQL, Indexes, Functions, Stored Procedures and Triggers\n\n         \nActive participation in Adobe ColdFusion Forum (senior member). Also have got community activities in some popular communities like DotnetSpider and \nExperts Exchange.\n\n         \nOutstanding communication and interpersonal skills, ability to learn quickly, good analytical reasoning and high compliance to new technologies and tools.\n\nEDUCATIONAL QUALIFICATION:\n\n1.\n   \nB.Tech \ngraduate in \nComputer Science & Engineering\n from KIIT, \nBhubaneswar\n\n\nOrissa\n2.\n   \n10+2\nth\n from \nGovernment\nCollege\n, Orissa\n3.\n   \n10\nth\n from \nTTPS\nHigh School\n, Orissa\n4. Currently pursuing \nMS in Software Systems, 3\nrd\n semester\n (MSSS, a master degree program) from \nBITS Pilani\n, Rajasthan.\n\nPERSIONAL DETAILS:\n\nDate of Birth:\n26\nth\n December 1979\nGender:\n Male\nMarital Status:\n Single\nPassport Number:\n F1699815\nNationality:\nIndian\n\nSOFTWARE SKILLS:\n\nProgramming Language\nVB 6.0, VB.NET, C#.NET, ColdFusion, ActionScript 2.0\nDatabase\nMSSQL Server, MySQL\nOperating System\nWindows 98, ME, 2000, XP\nVersion Control\nVSS, CVS, AccuRev, Perforce\nOthers\nColdfusion Report Builder, SQL Reporting Service, Fusebox 3.0/4.0, Flash MX 2004 Pro, Flash Remoting, XML, HTML, SQL programming, Javascript, CSS\n\n\nPROJECT EXPERIENCE:\n\n# Project 1 : \n\nDuration\n\n Nov 06 ? till date \nProject\n\n Content Management System\nTechnical Details\n\n ColdFusion MX 7.0, XML, JavaScript, MS SQL 2005\nTeam Size\n\n18\nDetails\n\nThis is a Content management System, which basically provides services Creating websites, subsites under main sites and also managing the websites and contents of the websites, those are created already.\n\nThe application is a CMS product having almost all the common and advanced features of a Content Management System product. There are basically two modes to login to the application, Admin and User. \n\nUsers have to purchase the license of the product and will get access to User mode. In User mode users can manage their contents by creating sites and subsites and modifying the sites/subsites contents. \n\nIn Admin mode, there is full control of the Users and user features can be manipulated in Admin mode. There is also a module in admin mode, called ?automation section?. This section basically takes care of all the user and admin functionalities (that UI provides to all users) in an automatic fashion. Admin can log into this mode and check the status of all the functionalities at a particular time (by running the individual test scripts or all scripts at a time), and from the generated report Admin can figure out if any method is having any errors. The scripts run at the backend and use the methods used by the main application to get the status of a particular functionality and status report is generated accordingly.\nRole\n\n Interaction with client. Involved in now features implementation for product features enhancement and bug fixing for two new version releases. Also involved in designing, making the specifications for the automation scripts of the CMS product, coding for the automation scripts.\n\n# Project 2 : \n\nDuration\n\n May 07 ? June 07 \nProject\n\n Document Management Solution\nTechnical Details\n\n ColdFusion MX 6.1, ColdFusion Framework (Fusebox 4.0), MSSQL 2000\nTeam Size\n\n\nDetails\n\nThis is a document management solution to manage PDF and WORD documents (MSDS documents) online for different types of users (Admin, User, Client and Viewers).\n Document management solution with various levels of access to manage users, customers, and customer documents as well as restrict customer access to view documents or document descriptions only.\n\nCustomers wishing to obtain full view access to their assigned documents will pay a subscription fee by credit card.\n\nUsers with full rights are Admins (manages Users, Clients and Viewers), with limited Admin rights are Users (manages Clients and Viewers), paid users with document content view access are Clients and finally non-paid users with only document title view permission are Viewers.\n\nRole\n\n Interaction with client. Involved in requirement analysis, complete database design, UI design, Fusebox 4.0 setup and coding in the application. Also worked on a support tool for this applications to migrate thousands of existing data (in for of CSV file) for documents to the application database.\n\n# Project 3 : \n\nDuration\n\n July 06 ? Oct 06 \nProject\n\n Content Management System\nTechnical Details\n\n ColdFusion MX 7.0, ColdFusion Framework (Fusebox 3.0), Flash MX 2004 Pro, FlashRemoting, XML, ActionScript, JavaScript, MY SQL 4.1.11\nTeam Size\n\n\nDetails\n\nThis is a Content management System, which basically provides services like Generating online funds for various organizations, creating websites and also managing the websites, those are created already.\n\nThe online Website creation section, where a user can create websites of their choice. There are various templates provided to the uses, and uses can select templates, can change the fonts (colors and texts) of their choice and submits the samples. Internally the application creates the CFMs and CSS files (by taking the fonts and templates from the page) and stores in a particular folder for future use. Later users can modify the templates (if needed) and finally submits. After finalizing one template the user can go to the home page of the website. Each time the user access the site the files are picked from the existing contents (CFMs and CSSs created earlier) and output is thrown to the browser which user sees.\n\nThe application also has one Online Fundraising includes various forms by which one user can donate money, and by which the site owners can raise money. The mode of payment includes Credit Card and. The application includes Credit Card validation and verification as a major portion. It also includes many other validations like phone number, zip code, e-mail etc.\n\nThis application uses Fusebox(ColdFusion Framework) and all the requests and routed through fusebox. The framework checks the states of a page requested (like page preview state or page validate stage etc.) and depending on the state it routes to the respective CFCs\n\nRole\n\n Interaction with Client. Involved in designing and coding the Online Fundraising application. And also designed and developed Websites managing tool like designing and storing the contents of the templates.\n\n# Project 4 : \n\nDuration: \nApr 06 ? June 06\nProject:\n Centralized Database hosting\nTechnical Details:\n VB.NET, .NET Remoting, SQL Server 2000\nTeam Size\n\n\nDetails:\n This is an application where multiple remote client databases feeds to one centralized remote database by using .NET remoting. There is a central database which holds data for multiple logistic companies, the central web site hosts the database for all the companies. The application has two main parts, one is client service and other is remote server service. The remote client sends the data to the server in form of XML, and the XML is being parsed by the server application and does the insert/update/delete as per the conditions specified. The client application also sends Images to server in encoded format, and the images are used by the central website for different companies. This entire application runs automatically as it is a service, the entire application is a database driven architecture and the data shuttle is guided by the timer at client end. After the data feeding operation, both client and server sends email notifications to their clients with updates as a status, so the clients are informed about the data is being hosted or not.\nRole:\n Interaction with Client. I was involved in DB design both for client and server, and also creating the business logic layers through which the data transaction was taking place.\n<o:p>\n\n# Project 5 : \n\nDuration\n\n Dec 05 ? Mar 06 \nProject\n\n\nDatabase Synchronization (A Many-to-Many)\nTechnical Details\n\n C#, Web Services, XML, SQL 2000\nTeam Size\n\n\nDetails\n\nThis is basically multiple database synchronization for Logistic companies. The database servers get regularly updated with the latest data and the data flow is bidirectional. The system has two main sections, one is Client and other is Server (WebService). The remote webservice has some objects exposed to internet and the client calls those remote objects for communication. The Client application selects records from the Local database and sends to server database in XML format by calling the webmethods of webservice. The webmethod also replies back with the new records (meant for client database) from server database in XML format. The records are being manipulated (inserted or updated) as per the requirement.\nRole\n\n I was involved in DB design both for client and server, and also creating the central webservice through which the data transaction was happening between client and server. I was also a part of creating the business logic for data synchronization. \n\n# Project 6 : \n\nDuration\n\n Jan 05 ? till date \nProject\n\n Online Training Systems\nTechnical Details\n\n VB.NET, ColdFusion 7.0, ColdFusion Report Builder, Flash MX (Later migrated to Flash MX 2004 Pro), FlashRemoting, ActionScript, XML, MSSQL Server, SQL Reporting Service\nTeam Size\n\n\nDetails\n\nThis is basically an Online training system for regular pilots, taking course online, tracking their progress etc. The system has three sections (SuperAdmin, Admin and User). SuperAdmin creates Companies (Admins), Courses, and assigns courses to companies. Company\n\nAdmin\n\nassigns the courses to it\'s registered users, monitor their progress and manage users. In User section users can takes their courses, appear for the exams and scores calculated accordingly. According to Government Aviation rules, a professional Pilot has to take the course at regular intervals. So this is the complete procedure for training of regular Pilots. \n\nThe Application has three layers, UI that consists of Flash design and all UI logics were coded in ActionScript 2, Application Layer that is developed in VB.NET mainly class libraries and it interacts with UI with an interface called Flash Remoting, and the third layer is DB layer where we have Stored procedures, triggers, views. The middle layer which is in VB.NET where the main business logic is implemented. Also at front end the reports were generated through the ColdFusion report builder (now migrating the reports to SQL Reporting), and the data between UI and Application layer were exchanged in XML format through custom web publishing.\nRole\n\n Interaction with Client. Involved in analysis, DB Design and coding for the Flash UI Layer (except design), .NET application layer and SQL Stored Procedures. Also involved in creating ColdFusion Reports using ColdFusion Report Builder and SQL Reporting Services.\n\n# Project 7 : \n\nDuration\n\n Aug 03 ? Aug 04 \nProject\n\n Data Maintenance tool for ISO Certification\nTechnical Details\n\n VB.NET 2003, MSSQL Server 2000\nTeam Size\n\n\nDetails\n\nThis is a desktop VB.NET tool used by various Engineering & Construction industries (mainly large factories) to maintain their data for ISO certification. Through this tool companies can store their data related to different fields/areas and during ISO audit the ISO team can gather information from this tool as well before certifying for ISO.\n\nThis tool has many sections like: Management information, Employee data, Employee skills, Factory facilities, Safety majors in Factories, Factory production details (past and present), Turn over history for past 5 years etc. Companies install this tool at their each factory end to maintain data and assemble the entire data at the end to generate the centralize database for ISO audit.\n\nRole\n\n Involved in analysis, DB Design, SQL programming (stored procedures) and VB.NET coding for the employee?s data maintenance section, facilities and safety majors provided in factories sections.','Mindfire Solutions ',1,NULL,'2007-10-18',NULL,'2007-10-18','2010-06-09 12:13:49','2010-06-09',2,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(167,'Vikas Bhati',NULL,NULL,'Bhubaneswar','vikgngnas.bfdngdnhati@gmail.com',NULL,'0129 2304258','0','09938374183','0','09891479228','0','2006-10-13',8,24,'2010-06-09 12:13:49',3,'0',NULL,'200710/18/ATT54642.html','200710/18/DOC16291.doc','Vikas B\nVikas B\nPhone\n: 09938374183\nE-mail\n\nvikgngnas.bfdngdnhati@gmail.com\nAddress\n: D-1, Defence Colony, Niladri Vihar, \nBhubaneswar\n, Orissa\n\nProfile:\nAs a committed and enthusiastic IT professional with 3 years & 4 months experience in Software Development and keenness to acquire any additional skills that may be required.\nTechnical Profile:\n\n        \nMicrosoft Technologies\n          \n\n           \nVisual Basic.Net, Visual Basic 6.0, ASP.Net, ASP, C#\n\n        \nMarkup Languages\n               \n\n           \nXML, HTML\n\n        \nScripting Languages\n             \n\n           \nVBScript, JavaScript\n\n        \nDatabases\n                           \n\n           \nSQL Server 2000, Oracle \n\n        \n3GL\n                                     \n\n           \nC, C++\n\n        \nApplication\n                           \n\n           \nMS Office, VBA (Word & Excel)\nEducational Qualifications:\n\n        \nBachelor of Engineering (Honours)\n in \nInformation Technology\n completed with \n70.22\n% from Hindu College of Engineering (Affiliated by \nMaharshi\nDayanand\nUniversity\n, Rohtak), Sonepat in 2004.\n\n        \nClass 12\nth\n passed with \n69.0\n% from \nD.A.V.\nPublic School\n (C.B.S.E.), Ballabgarh in 2000. \n\n        \nClass 10\nth\n passed with \n81.6\n% from Nehru Public School (C.B.S.E.), \nGhaziabad\n in 1998.\nWorking Experience:\n\n        \nWorking as a Software Engineer with Infosys Technologies Ltd., \nBhubaneswar\n since October 2006 to till date.\n\n        \nWorked as a Software Developer with Thomson Digital, Noida since October 2005 to October 2006.\n\n        \nWorked as a Software Engineer with Sakshay Tradelinks Pvt. Ltd., \nNew Delhi\n since May 2004 to October 2005.\nProjects Undertaken:\nCycle Count Application\nLanguage used\n- Visual Basic.Net, ASP.Net, ADO.Net, JavaScript\nDatabase used\n- SQL Server 2000\nPosition\n- Team Leader\nResponsibilities\n- Analysis, Coding & Testing\nProject Location\n- Infosys Technologies Ltd., \nBhubaneswar\n\nE-Requisition\nLanguage used\n- Visual Basic.Net, ASP.Net, ADO.Net, JavaScript\nDatabase used\n- SQL Server 2000\nPosition\n- Team Leader\nResponsibilities\n- Analysis, Coding & Testing\nProject Location\n- Infosys Technologies Ltd., \nBhubaneswar\n\nTravel & Expenses Application\nLanguage used\n- Visual Basic.Net, ASP.Net, ADO.Net, ASP, JavaScript, VBScript \nDatabase used\n- SQL Server 2000\nPosition\n- Team Leader\nResponsibilities\n- Analysis, Coding & Testing\nProject Location\n- Infosys Technologies Ltd., \nBhubaneswar\n\nShopping Cart\nLanguage used\n- C#.Net, ASP.Net, ADO.Net, JavaScript\nDatabase used\n- SQL Server 2000\nPosition\n- Team Leader\nResponsibilities\n- Analysis, Coding & Testing\nProject Location\n- Infosys Technologies Ltd., \nBhubaneswar\n\nThomson Quality Control System\nLanguage used\n- Visual Basic.Net\nDescription\n- According to 175 Wiley Publisher?s specifications, this application checks the final XML file of production of Book section.\nPosition\n- Team Member\nResponsibilities\n- Analysis, Coding & Testing\nProject Location\n- Thomson Digital, Noida\n\nThomson Metadata Management System\nLanguage used\n- Visual Basic 6.0, XML, XSL\nDescription\n- This application generates DART Metadata XML file on the basis of 3B2, XML and PDF files. It checks naming conventions of folders, subfolders and files according to Wiley Publisher?s specifications. It has facility to parse, validate & browse metadata & message XML files.\nPosition\n- Team Member\nResponsibilities\n- Analysis, Coding & Testing\nProject Location\n- Thomson Digital, Noida\n\nQuick Index\nLanguage used\n- Visual Basic 6.0, XML, XSL\nTools used\n- MS Word 2000, Acrobat Reader (5.0)\nDescription\n- This application search out the page numbers of index terms in the PDF & Word files. It generates XML file for final index terms with page numbers.\nPosition\n- Team Member\nResponsibilities\n- Analysis, Coding & Testing\nProject Location\n- Thomson Digital, Noida\n\nAutomated Electronic Product System\nLanguage used\n- C#.Net, MS Access 2000\nTools used-\n Acrobat Reader & Distiller (4.0 & 5.0), Enfocus Pitstop Server (1.61)\nDescription\n- This application converts PS files to PDF files, put cross-linking between Authors? Queries. It takes prints of PDF Files after checking of Enfocus Pitstop Server, if there is no error. If there is any error, then it takes print of those pages, which have errors. After checking of PDF files, the files are uploaded to the FTP locations depending upon locations. In this application, users have to drop the PS files in the hot folders and the remaining process is done by automated way. In this application, there is facility of sending emails at each and every completion of process and error, if any error may occur.\nPosition\n- Team Member\nResponsibilities\n- Analysis, Coding & Testing\nProject Location\n- Thomson Digital, Noida\n\nSmart e-Book\nLanguage used\n- Visual Basic.Net\nTools used\n- Acrobat Reader & Distiller (4.0)\nDescription\n- This application converts PS files to PDF files, and then creates bookmarks and links on the basis of table of contents of book. After completion of process, it also make one final PDF file of book in the sequence of table of contents.\nPosition\n- Team Member\nResponsibilities\n- Analysis, Coding & Testing\nProject Location\n- Thomson Digital, Noida\n\nInvestment Record-Keeper\nLanguage used\n- Visual Basic.Net\nTools used\n- MS Excel & Access 2000\nDescription\n- This application calculates 18 formulas and stores values in Excel Files. It gives the facility to add new stock and fund managers, edit and deletes stock and fund managers.\nPosition\n- Team Member\nResponsibilities\n- Coding & Testing\nProject Location\n\nSakshay Tradelinks Pvt. Ltd., \nNew Delhi\n\nPayroll Management System\nLanguage used\n- Visual Basic 6.0, SQL Server 2000\nDescription\n- This application maintains all payroll activities of the company.\nPosition\n- Team Member\nResponsibilities\n- Coding & Testing\nProject Location\n\nSakshay Tradelinks Pvt. Ltd., \nNew Delhi\nPersonal Profile:\nFather?s Name\n    \n            \n\n           \nMr. Shishupal Singh.\nMother?s Name\n   \n            \n\n           \nMrs. Manorama Singh\nGender\n              \n            \n\n           \nMale\nDate of Birth\n      \n            \n\n           \n22-March-1983\nNationality\n         \n            \n\n           \nIndian\nMarital Status\n     \n            \n\n           \nSingle\nPassport\n                        \n            \n\n           \nYes (#: G1063140)\nPermanent Address\n         \n\n           \n533, Adarsh Nagar-II, Ballabgarh,\n                                                \nFaridabad\n, Haryana. PIN-121004\nPhone\n                           \n\n           \n0129 - 2304258, 09891479228\n\nDate: \n17 October 2007\nPlace:\nBhubaneswar\n(Vikas Bhati)','Infosys Technologies Ltd',1,NULL,'2007-10-18',NULL,'2007-10-18','2010-06-09 12:13:49','2010-06-09',3,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(168,'Trivedi',NULL,NULL,'Gurgaon','triveewfgwerdi56gr85687@rediffmail.com',NULL,NULL,'0','91 9911306937','0',NULL,'0','2007-04-14',8,24,'2010-06-09 12:13:49',2,'0',NULL,'200710/18/ATT54641.html','200710/18/DOC16292.doc','Anjali Mishra\n\nTrivedi\n                                                       \nEmail: \ntriveewfgwerdi56gr85687@rediffmail.com\nMobile\n: 91-9911306937\n                                                \n\nAssignments in Software Development & implementation with a technology driven organisation of repute\n\nProfessional Synopsis\nMasters in Computer Applications\n with 2.8 years of experience in the areas of Software Development & Implementation. Presently working with \nHanu Software Solutions Pvt Ltd.\n\n\nas Software Engineer\n\n Through understanding of the SDLC with proficiency in mapping client / business requirements, documentation, application design, development, integration & testing and troubleshooting for complex information systems management. Holds the distinction of executing numerous software design, development & implementation projects in web technologies. Possess excellent problem solving, analytical, communication and team building skills with proficiency at grasping new technical concepts quickly & utilise the same in a productive manner.\n\nAreas of Expertise\n\nFunctional;\n\n     \nMapping business/client?s requirements and translating these requirements into functional specifications and detailed test plans.\n\n     \nConducting system study and coordinating with team members for System Design & Integration.\n\n     \nHandling various technical aspects like product documentation, software designs, coding of modules.\n\n     \nVerifying change requests and defects, tracking and reviewing test plans, test results and unresolved problems, reviewing test reports & taking corrective actions. \n\n     \nDelivering and implementing the project as per scheduled deadlines, extending post-implementation and maintenance support to the technical support team and client.\n\nTechnical;\n\nMicrosoft Technologies\n   \n: Dot Net Technologies in (C#. net), VB 6.0, and Microsoft Visual\n\n                                       \n   \nSource Safe\n\nTools\n                         \n    \n: VSS (Visual source safe) \nWeb Technologies\n         \n    \n: ASP. Net, XML, JAVA Script, \nAjax\n, PHP, HTML 4.0. \nMiddle Wares\n       \n        \n\nADO\n. Net, Active X Data Objects \nDatabases\n                \n   \n: SQL Server 2000/2005, My Sql, and Access 2000.\nConcepts\n                      \n: System Analysis & Design, DBMS, Data Structures, Networking, Software Engineering, Artificial Intelligence, Compiler Design, Web Technologies, Graphics & Animations, Designs & Analysis of Algorithms. \n\n\n\nCareer Highlights\n\n\n\nHanu Software Solutions, Gurgaon \n                  \n                                    \n       \nDec?06 to till now\nAs a Software Engineer\n\nKey Projects Handled;\nTitle: \nBaidansWebMixer\n                                               \nClient: \nBrice Carrington (http://\nwww.Baidansmixer.com/BaidansMixer\n).\nTeam Size: 6\n\n\n     \n                                                                                 \n    \nRole: Team Member\nTechnologies:\n\nAsp.net 2.0, C#, sqlserver 2000, \nAjax\n, JavaScript.\n\nScope: BaidansMixer web site is the collection of original creation of SoundFX files. These sounds are natural and demanding into feature films, video games and software. Website has one Audio Mixer, which supports these natural sounds. Any Guest or Registered User can mix these rarely available sounds with applying several audio effects with the help of online Mixer and can set that customized sound as a ring tone to his/her cell phone via payment facility while preview option is freely available. This project implements Cybersource payment gateway, Clickatell API to send sms and ring tone, ComponentSpace Email Verification.\n\nAll the available SoundFX files can be purchased through available full-featured shopping cart. This Project has been categorized into three modules Mixer, SoundFx and WAP. In Mixer module user can create or mix the ring tone with sound effects. In SoundFX module user can purchase pre stored sound files in default format or in user selected format. User can view Purchase History and can recover sound file. The WAP module is dedicated to cell phone user where they can download the ring tone by entering their credentials.\n\nResponsibilities:\n        \nTeam member\n\n          \nUnderstanding requirements\n\n          \nCoding using C#\n\n          \nImplementing SSL and Payment Gateway.\n\n          \nDeployment and Delivery\n\n\n\nHanu Software Solutions, Gurgaon \n                  \n                            \n     \n          \nMay?06 to Nov?06\nAs a Software Engineer\n\nKey Projects Handled;\nTitle\n\nBrice Carrington\n (http://www.bricecarrington.com/bricecarrington/index.aspx)\nClient: \nBrice Carrington\nTeam Size: 3 \n   \n     \n                                                                                 \n    \nRole: Team Member\nTechnologies:\n\nAsp.net 2.0, C#, Sql Server 2000, Javascript, Photoshop.\n\nScope: \nBricecarrington.com website will be developed using flash and .net programming. The website will contain the biography of sound designer Brice Carrington. It will also contain the case studies, photos of Brice Carrington, press articles, content of print interviews, TV interview.\n\nMy role is to create the admin section who handle or the users activity, create user Id and password to login into the site. Once user enters the site his account deleted and he has to request again for the login ID. Website will not be open for public access. Only authorized access will be permissible.\n\nResponsibilities:\n   \nTeam member\n\n          \nUnderstanding requirements\n\n          \nCoding using C#\n\n          \nDeployment and Delivery\n\n\nHanu Software Solutions, Gurgaon \n         \n                                       \n            \nNov?05 to\n\nMay?06\n                                  \nAs a Software Engineer\n\nKey Projects Handled;\nTitle: \nRayMarine \n(https://webportal.raymarine.com/wcts/frmLogin.aspx)\n                   \n                            \nClient: \nRayMarine\n\nTeam Size: 5\n\n\n     \n                                                                                 \n    \nRole: Team Member\nTechnologies:\n\nAsp.net 2.0, C#, sqlserver 2000, \nAjax\n, JavaScript.\n\nScope: \nThe Project has been categorized into two major modules Dealer and Admin. Both modules has same login with different authorization role. The Login process has been implemented with SSL and web service. The Dealer has functionalities to add technician, certify them and make installation over the vessels. Admin has functionality as a super admin should have but it also has authorization of process which dealer has.\nResponsibilities:\n        \nTeam member\n\n          \nUnderstanding requirements\n\n          \nCoding using C#(Membership and Role Management)\n\n          \nImplementing SSL\n\n          \nDeployment and Delivery\n\n\nHanu Software Solutions, Gurgaon \n                  \n   \n                               \n\n        \nJun?05 to \n\nOct?05\nAs a Software Engineer\n\nKey Projects Handled;\nTitle: \nWahIndia\n                                                \nClient: WahIndia.inc\n                                       \nTeam Size: 6 \n  \n\n     \n                                                                                 \n    \nRole: Team Member\nTechnologies:\n\nAsp. net, C#, Sqlserver, JavaScript.\nResponsibilities :\n\nDocumentation,Coding and Testing.\n\nScope: Wah \nIndia\n is an online community that connects people through a network of trusted friends. We are committed to providing an online meeting place where people can socialize, make new acquaintances and find others who share their interests\n\n. This is a Social Networking site where you can create your profile, you can search people, You can add them to your profile as friend, family or as an extended network, You can create and join groups and fan clubs, You can create Photo Albums and Video Albums, You can also send message and reply to message of the user and many more functionality like Admin Panel, Birthday Reminder, Account Expiration reminders.\n                           \nResponsibilities:\n        \nTeam member\n\n          \nUnderstanding requirements\n\n          \nCoding using C#\n\n\nNetzone Software, \nDelhi\n            \n                                                              \nOct?04 to May? 05\nAs a Software trainee\n\nKey Projects Handled;\nTitle: \nOfficeGT Company Info\n                                                \nClient: BCA Technologies, Inc\n                                        \nTeam Size: 3\n        \n     \n                                                                                 \n   \nRole: Team Member\nTechnologies:\n\nAsp.net, C#, sqlserver 2000.\n\nScope: OfficeGT is a web application project that was designed for use in a network environment so information will flow to all users to increase office productivity.\n\nEngineers, architects, attorneys, accountants, or other organizations that track people and projects can use OfficeGT to organize information such as time, expenses, contacts, sales, marketing and project information.\n\nResponsibilities:\n        \nTeam member\n\n          \nUnderstanding requirements\n\n          \nCoding using C#\n\n          \nUnit and Manual testing\n\n\n\n                                 \nEducation\n\n\n     \nMCA from \nUtkal\nUniversity\n (BPUT), \nBhubaneswar\n in 2004.\n\n     \nB-Sc (Hons.) from \nBJB\nCollege\n\nUtkal\nUniversity\nBhubaneswar\n\nin 2000. \n\n\nProfessional Courses\n\n\n     \n. Net from Pentasoft Technology Pvt. Ltd in 2002. \n\n\n\nPersonal Details\nContact Address\n       \n\n             \n1213, Rail Vihar, Sector-15,\n\nPart\n   \nII,Gurguon. Haryana\nDate of Birth\n              \n\n             \n23\nrd\n Aug?1978\nLanguage\n                  \n\n             \nEnglish and\n\nHindi\nHobbies\n                     \n\n             \nMusic, Travel & Cooking\nMarital Status\n            \n\n             \nSingle\n\n\n\nDeclaration:\nI consider myself familiar with all Software Development and Functional Testing aspects. I am also confident of my ability to work in a team.\nI hereby declare that the information furnished above is true to the best of my knowledge.\n\n\n\nDate:\n    \n                                                                                                          \nPlace:\n   \nGurgaon\n      \n                                                                            \n      \nYogendra Trivedi','Hanu Software Solutions Pvt Ltd',1,NULL,'2007-10-18',NULL,'2007-10-18','2010-06-09 12:13:49','2010-06-09',2,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(169,'Sangram Keshari R',NULL,NULL,'Ghaziabad','sangradvdvm_indvdvdia@hotmail.com',NULL,'0120 4110517','0','9818400517','0',NULL,'0','2002-11-12',9,29,'2010-06-09 12:13:49',3,'0',NULL,'200710/18/ATT54640.html','200710/18/DOC16293.doc','SANGRAM KESHARI R\nSANGRAM KESHARI R\n1242, Adarsh Apartment, Sec-4C, Vasundhara, \nGhaziabad\n\n\nsangradvdvm_indvdvdia@hotmail.com\nMob: \n9818400517\nRes\n: 0120-4110517\n                                                                        \n                                          \n\nSUMMARY\n\n7+ years of work experience in Design, Development, Integration and Implementation of software applications using\n Microsoft Technologies i.e. DOT NET, SQL Server, Visual Basic, ASP, IIS, COM, XML etc. and other tools like Installshield, Satellite Forms, Seagate Crystal Reports. Extensive knowledge of SDLC, Database and commercial applications including conceptualization, layout designing, user interface planning with programming & managing development cycle. Key strength lies in solving complex design, understanding specification and system analysis. \nEDUCATION\nM.Sc. (IT) \nfrom KSOU, Mysore (Given final exam, awaiting result).\n2.5 Years Diploma Course \nfrom NIIT, M-5, South Extn-II, New Delhi.\nB.Com \nfrom Utkal University.\n\nTECHNICAL/ FUNCTIONAL (Application) SKILLS\nSkills\nDetails\n\nOperation System / Hardware\n\nDOS, \nWindows 95/98/NT/2000/XP/2003/SBS, Unix.\n\nLanguages\n\nVB.NET, C#, ASP. Net, VB 6.0, VC++.\n\nWeb Technology\n\nHTML, JavaScript, XML, CSS.\n\nThird Party Tools\n\nInstallshield 5.5/10.5, Satellite Forms 4.1/5.1,\n\nSeagate Crystal Reports 8.0/10, MS Visio.\n\nDatabase \n\nSQL Server 2000, MS-Access, Sybase, Oracle 7\n\nOffice Management Tools\n\nMS Word, MS Excel, MS PowerPoint, MS\n\nProject, MS Outlook.\n\nVersion Control\n\nMicrosoft VSS.\n\nQuality\n\nKnowledge of CMMI process.\n\n\nWORK EXPERIENCE\n1) \nMindmill Software Ltd, C-37, Sector-58, Noida, U.P\n                   \nMay?00 ? Till Date\n\nPROJECT SUMMARY\n\nProject# 1\nProject Name:\n\nCallScheduler (CS)\n                                               \nNov?04 - till date \nClient:\n            \nSPS (Sales Partner Systems Inc.), USA\nEnvironment:\n\nC#, SQL Server 2000/MSDE, InstallShield 10.5, Crystal Report 9. \nTeam Size:\n      \n\nProject Description:\n\nA customized CRM windows application where sales representatives can schedule daily, weekly, monthly calls for customers. A daily call scheduling facility to view a list of customers that is to be called and/or visited during a specific week. The Call Scheduler shall group customers by their order days, establish a call sequence by time of day, mark calls completed, rescheduled, or cancelled. The a\npplication manages call history; call forwarding, rescheduling, customer notes, reporting etc.\n   \nRole: Project Leader \n\nResponsibilities: \n\n       \nAnalyze client requirements and estimation\n\n       \nPlanning project implementation and performing task breakdown\n\n       \nDesigning & coding some part of the Schedule module and to support OLE method calls \n\n       \nCoordinating team activities to meet software delivery deadlines\n\n       \nSolving technical problems of team members\n\n       \nInvolved in Application Setup\n\n\nProject# 2\nProject Name:\n\nCARAVAN\n                                                  \nNov?04 - till date \nClient:\n            \nSPS (Sales Partner Systems Inc.), USA\nEnvironment:\n\nC#, SQL Server 2000, InstallShield 10.5, Crystal Report 10. \nTeam Size:\n      \n\nProject Description:\n\nCaravan consists up of three sub-applications, Caravan Control Center (CCC), Caravan Messaging System (CMS) and Caravan Document System (CDS).\n\nCaravan Control Center (CCC) \nis a web-based application to manage the distribution network of the client. This includes management of routes, drivers, trucks, trailers and tablet PCs.\n\nCaravan Messaging System (CMS) \nconsists of a Web-based and Windows-based interface to manage the various communications that have to be made to customers and other concerned people regarding the status of routes and other information by communication modes like email, fax and pager.\n\nCaravan Document System (CDS) \nis a windows-based application to generate documents required for CCC.\n   \nRole: Project Leader \n\nResponsibilities: \n\n       \nAnalyze client requirements and estimation\n\n       \nPlanning project implementation and performing task breakdown\n\n       \nCoordinating team activities to meet software delivery deadlines\n\n       \nSolving technical problems of team members\n\n       \nInvolved in Application Setup\n\n\nProject# 3\nProject Name:\n\nDATAWAREHOUSE\n                                                \nJan?07 - till date \nClient:\n            \nSPS (Sales Partner Systems Inc.), USA\nEnvironment:\n\nC#, SQL Server 2000, InstallShield 10.5 \nTeam Size:\n      \n\nProject Description:\n\nDatawarehouse is a web-based application that seeks to integrate Call Scheduler, Caravan, NetLink and other applications of the client. Currently, we are working on application/admin user creation, organization creation module, maintaining their respective hierarchies. Datawarehouse creates logins for the different application databases and assigns appropriate database roles to the users created.\n   \nRole: Project Leader \n\nResponsibilities: \n\n       \nAnalyze client requirements and estimation\n\n       \nPlanning project implementation and performing task breakdown\n\n       \nCoordinating team activities to meet software delivery deadlines\n\n       \nSolving technical problems of team members\n\n       \nInvolved in Application Setup\n\n\nProject# 4\nProject Name:\n\nShip Traders Enquiry Processing System\n (STEPS)\n    \nMar?06 ? Sep?06 \nClient:\n            \nGI GROUP, UK\nEnvironment:\n\nC#, SQL Server 2000/MSDE, InstallShield 10.5, Crystal Report 9. \nTeam Size:\n      \n\nProject Description:\n\nThis is a web based application manages the shipments for the customer. User can receive the customer enquiry, customer order, customer payment, supplier enquiry, and supplier quotations and prepares the order placed to supplier, collection advice, dispatch advice, customer invoice, and dispatch details for customer and delivery to forwarder. It also helps to get reports for item/part information, customer?s pending enquiry/quotation, and delivery due, order performance, order status, payment due and daily stock and sales analysis information.\n\nRole: Project Leader \n\nResponsibilities: \n\n       \nStudy the old FoxPro based application and estimation\n\n       \nDesigning architecture and database \n\n       \nPlanning project implementation and performing task breakdown\n\n       \nCoordinating team activities to meet software delivery deadlines\n\n       \nSolving technical problems of team members\n\n       \nInvolved in Application Setup\n\n\nProject# 5\nProject Name:\n\nICPS\n                                                                   \nSep?04 ? Feb?06 \nClient:\n            \nTraffic Support Ltd (TSL), UK\nEnvironment:\n\nVB.NET, ASP.NET, VB.NET Compact Framework, VB6.0, SOAP, SQL Server 2000 \nTeam Size:\n      \n\nProject Description:\n\nICPS consist of small different projects, which consist web applications, windows applications, SOAP, Web Services and handheld applications.\n\n1.\n     \naMember\nThis is an ASP.Net application that allows the ?public? to self-register their name, address and credit card details and then to purchase \"licenses\" to enter a city.\n\n2.\n     \nHire & Lease\nThis is an ASP.Net application that allows hire and lease companies to register with the local council as users of the web site, and the web site allows them to key in the name and address of the driver and the hire agreement reference and then update the councils system directly. The councils system will then create the replacement notice automatically.\n\n3.\n     \nExemption\nThis is an ASP.Net application that allows individuals who believe they should be exempt from licenses to apply for an exemption via a web page.\n\n4.\n     \nFleet License Management\nThis is an ASP.Net application that\nallows vehicle fleet owners to make a request for a fleet license and to view details of their license charges and to modify their vehicle fleet details.\n\n5.\n     \nHandheld Tickets Application\nIt is a smart Device application developed for the usage of Parking Attendants who carry the application on devices with them to perform various activities like issuing a PCN, observing vehicles, recording a location, Fault reporting etc.\n\n6.\n     \nDBSync Application \nIt is a smart Device application developed to synchronize the data between the device used by parking attendants and server data. At the end of the day when the attendants submit their devices, the DBsync application is executed that reads the data from the device and synchronize the server data and the device data.\n\n7.\n     \nDevice Engineering\nIt \nis a smart device Program that is run on Embedded Devices that support WinCE. It is the program that maintains an inventory of street assets that are located on a street within a council?s borough. The program also maintains, directs and records the maintenance effort for those assets. Each asset will have its own set of attributes and may have parts and sub-parts associated with it. \n\n8.\n     \nSuspension HHT\nThe SuspensionHHT is a smart device based reporting program. The application downloads the data using queries from the ICPS database, saves the data in XML documents and then uses those XML documents as data-source. \n\nRole: Project Leader \n\nResponsibilities: \n\n       \nAnalyze client requirements and estimation\n\n       \nPlanning project implementation and performing task breakdown\n\n       \nCoordinating team activities to meet software delivery deadlines\n\n       \nSolving technical problems of team members\n\n\nProject# 6\nProject Name:\n\nProspector\n                                                 \nJun?04 ? Sep?04 \nClient:\n            \nSafety Media Ltd, UK\nEnvironment:\n\nVB 6.0, MS Access, InstallShield 5.5, Crystal Report 8.5. \nTeam Size:\n      \n\nProject Description:\n\nThis is a window-based application, is used by sales representatives of Safety Media Ltd. for managing clients contact details and for forecasting potential sales. The application runs in two modes, for sales representatives and for administrators. The program is the same for both types of users but with additional options available to the administrator. The user has the ability to export their sales information. There is a facility to FTP the data from the sales representatives to the main head office is also be available. \nThere are also various reports in the application.\n\nRole: Project Leader \n\nResponsibilities: \n\n       \nAnalyze client requirements and estimation\n\n       \nDesigning architecture and database \n\n       \nPlanning project implementation and performing task breakdown\n\n       \nInvolved in Application Setup\n\n\nProject# 7\nProject Name:\n\nAsset Controller\n                                          \nOct?03 ? Dec?03 \nClient:\n            \nSafety Media Ltd, UK\nEnvironment:\n\nVB 6.0, MS Access, InstallShield 5.5, Crystal Report 8.5. \nTeam Size:\n      \n\nProject Description:\n\nThis is a window-based application, which helps to maintain assets in an organization. Users can create/edit asset details. \nThe Asset History will maintain all of the actions the Asset has experienced. There are other master forms through which user can enter master details to create an asset. There are also various reports in the application.\n\nRole: Project Leader \n\nResponsibilities: \n\n       \nAnalyze client requirements and estimation\n\n       \nDesigning architecture and database \n\n       \nPlanning project implementation and performing task breakdown\n\n       \nInvolved in Application Setup\n\n\nProject# 8\nProject Name:\n\nVisitor Controller\n                                        \nApr?03 ? Jul?03 \nClient:\n            \nSafety Media Ltd, UK\nEnvironment:\n\nVB 6.0, MS Access, InstallShield 5.5, Crystal Report 8.5. \nTeam Size:\n      \n\nProject Description:\n\nThis is a window-based application, which allows a receptionist to log visitors in and out of a building and to print badges for them. It uses a webcam to capture an image of a person to be printed on their badge. It displays the output from the camera to the user of the software, then allow them to take a \"snapshot\" and add it to the badge to be printed. There are other features like design the badge, reports, etc.\n\nRole: Project Leader \n\nResponsibilities: \n\n       \nAnalyze client requirements and estimation\n\n       \nDesigning architecture and database \n\n       \nPlanning project implementation and performing task breakdown\n\n       \nInvolved in Application Setup\n\n\nProject# 9\nProject Name:\n\neTS?\n                                                                  \nNov?02 ? Sep?04 \nClient:\n            \nGrantlun Corporation, USA\nEnvironment:\n\nVB 6.0, Satellite Forms 5.1, MS Access, InstallShield 5.5, Crystal Report 8.5. \nTeam Size:\n      \n\nProject Description:\n\neTS? is an electronic time sheet system that runs on any PDA using the Palm operating system. It serves as a friendly and powerful data collection tool that enables field personnel to accurately report labor employment, equipment employment, and work progress. The Product has two parts PC side and Palm Side.\n\neTS? File Manager (PC Side)\n\nStores Company data and enables creation of data subsets by Job and by Time Keeper so Time Keepers are not burdened with data they do not need. Transmits Time Keeper datasets three ways: email, synchronization, memory stick. Imports/exports ALL data in text or XML format. \n\neTS? Time Keeper (Palm Side):\n\nStores specific Job data: employees, machines, crews, activities, accounts, tags and special code data so time sheet data input is fast and accurate.\n\nRole: Project Leader \n\nResponsibilities: \n\n       \nAnalyze client requirements and estimation\n\n       \nDesigning architecture and database \n\n       \nPlanning project implementation and performing task breakdown\n\n       \nCoding for Palm device application and Synchronization process between Palm and PC \n\n       \nPC and Palm Application Setup\n\n\nProject# 10\nProject Name:\n\nTIME\nTM\n                                                      \nApr?02 ? Nov?02 \nClient:\n            \nHard Dollar, USA\nEnvironment:\n\nSatellite Forms 5.1, VB 6.0, and InstallShield 5.5 \nTeam Size:\n      \n\nProject Description:\n\nTIME is a PDA based application that serves as an electronic ?time sheet?. TIME application is used by foremen to record actual labor, equipment, resource employment hours, work progress quantities, and to take notes. TIME transmits that data electronically to PXS application. \n\nRole: Developer \n\nResponsibilities: \n\n       \nCoding for Palm device application\n\n       \nPalm Application Setup\n\n       \nCoding for Synchronization process between Palm and PC \n\n\nProject# 11\nProject Name:\n\nInspection Manager Palm \n                                     \nNov?01 ? Mar?02 \nClient:\n            \nTISCOR, USA\nEnvironment:\n\nSatellite Forms 4.1, InstallShield 5.5 \nTeam Size:\n      \n\nProject Description:\n\nInspection Manager is designed for those who conduct inspection tours of facilities and critical equipment. Safety inspections, hazardous material inspections, and quality control audits are just a few areas where Inspection Manager can make your facility run smoothly and efficiently. With Inspection Manager, your inspector records information by scanning bar code labels and keying information directly into a palm. The device prompts your technician for information about the equipment or the process of operations in your facility. The PC software maintains data on technician, inspection checkpoints, equipment history and question and keeps a history of all entries made through the device. Using the PC generates work-order and management reports.\n\nRole: Developer \n\nResponsibilities: \n\n       \nCoding for Palm device application\n\n       \nPalm Application Setup\n\n       \nCoding for Synchronization process between Palm and PC \n\n\nProject# 12\nProject Name:\n\nFacility Manager\n\n                                     \nApr?01 ? Nov?01 \nClient:\n            \nTISCOR, USA\nEnvironment:\n\nVB 6.0, Satellite Forms 4.1, CrystalReports 8.5, InstallShield 5.5, Oracle, SQL, Access\n\nTeam Size:\n      \n\nProject Description:\n\nFacilityManager is a paperless computerized maintenance management system (CMMS) software application that controls maintenance management operations. FacilityManager schedules routine inspections; schedules detailed work orders for preventive maintenance tasks, and performs unscheduled maintenance in the field. Using software, hand-held computers, and bar codes, the system are used to plan, schedule and track maintenance management activities, including resources, materials, labor hours and cost. FacilityManager provides enterprise back-end connectivity to MS Access, SQL, and Oracle databases.\n   \nThe Project involves around 20 Master and Transaction forms, 25 Reports, Wizards etc.\n\nRole: Developer \n\nResponsibilities: \n\n       \nCoding for Synchronization process between Palm and PC \n\n       \nWorked on master forms like Inspector, Location, etc.\n\n       \nWorked on various reports\n\n\nProject# 13\nProject Name:\n\nTour Watch\n         \n                                               \nAug?00 ? Mar?01 \nClient:\n            \nTISCOR, USA\nEnvironment:\n\nVB 6.0, Crystal\n Reports 8.5,\n\nInstallShield 5.5, Oracle, SQL, Access\n\nTeam Size:\n      \n\nProject Description:\n\nTourWatch is a computerized guard-tour management system that records tours and inspections performed by security officers. Officers use portable data collection devices to document all security checkpoints visited. Simply scanning a bar code label or touching a metal tag records the date, time, and location of each checkpoint. TourWatch provides a variety of reports showing where your officers were, when, their observations, and the actions taken. Available reports include: Route Report, Summary Route Report, Exception Report and Missed-Checkpoint Report. TourWatch works with a variety of hand-held devices like \nDENSO BHT-8000, \nProTouch, ProScan DR, Dolphin, PDT 6100 and PDT6800, giving customers the option of selecting a device that meets their needs and budgets.\n\nRole: Developer \n\nResponsibilities: \n\n       \nWorked on various master forms\n\n       \nImport and export data module\n\n       \nVarious Reports\n\n\nProject# 14\nProject Name:\n\nChargeBackSysystem\n                                   \nMay?00 ? Sep?00 \nClient:\n            \nMckinsey, India\nEnvironment:\n\nVB 6.0, \nCrystal Reports, \nInstallShield\n 5.5, SQL Server6.5 \nTeam Size:\n      \n\nProject Description:\n\nIt?s a windows based application to maintain the uses of various resources in 3 different way, i.e. a) Per Login, b) Duration and c) Per Article for different users. It provides reports to analyze the uses of resources per user.\n\nRole: Developer \n\nResponsibilities: \n\n       \nRequirements gathering & Design Database\n\n       \nWorked on all forms\n\n       \nVarious Reports\n\n\n\nPERSONAL DETAILS\n\nDate of Birth\n          \n           \n\n        \n12\nth\n May 1974.\nMailing Address\n   \n        \n\n     \n1242, Adarsh Apartment,\n                                      \nSector ? 4C, Vasundhra,\n                            \n       \n             \nGhaziabad, U.P. \nMarital Status\n             \n\n      \nMarried.\nPassport Number\n      \n          \n\n        \nA6262472.\nPAN \n                         \n\n      \nAGRPR0527Q\n\nLanguages Known\n      \n\n      \nEnglish, Hindi and Oriya.\n\n\n\nPERSONAL TRAITS\n\nPatient Listener, Responsible, Ability to handle different tasks simultaneously, Ability to adapt fast to dynamic situations\n\n\n\n\n\nDATE:\n                                                                    \nSANGRAM KESHARI ROUT','Mindmill Software Ltd',1,NULL,'2007-10-18',NULL,'2007-10-18','2010-06-09 12:13:49','2010-06-09',3,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(170,'T Kishore',NULL,NULL,'Bangalore ','dasdfgmosdsddara_1983@yahoo.com','damodara_1983@yahoo.com','09341492478','0','09341492478','0',NULL,'0','2007-09-12',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-09 12:13:49',2,'0',NULL,'200710/18/ATT54639.html','200710/18/DOC16294.doc','Resdex @ naukri.com\nT.Kishore\ndasdfgmosdsddara_1983@yahoo.com\n\nTelephone: 09341492478\n(M)\n\nD.O.B\n - 30 Jul 1983 \nModified on\n - 26 Sep 2007 \nAnnual Salary\n - INR 2 Lac(s) 0 Thousand \nTotal Years of Experience\n - 2 Year(s) 5 Month(s) \nCurrent Location\n\nBangalore\n\nPreferred Location\n\nBangalore\nB.Tech with 2.5 years of exp. in .NET\n\nTEXT RESUME \n\nName: Thangella Kishore\nE-Mail: damodara_1983@yahoo.com\nPhNo: 9341492478.\nObjective\n\n Quest to work in a professional atmosphere in the field of Information Technology that enables me to cope with the emerging skills as well as the latest technology thus widening the spectrum of my knowledge\nSummary\n\n Have 2.5 years of experience in .NET as a team member.\n\n Have knowledge in C#, ASP.NET, SQL Server 2000 and WinForms.\n\n Flexible to work in any kind of environment\n\n Deep desire to learn & constantly upgrade skills.\n\n Good communication skills\nEducation\n\n B.Tech (ECE) from JNTU University, A.P with an aggregate of 65.3%.\n\n Intermediate from Board of Intermediate, A.P with an aggregate of 80.3%.\n\n S.S.C from Board of Secondary Education, A.P with an aggregate of 76.6%.\nWork Experience\n\n Currently Working as Associate Software Engineer in Infinite Computer Solutions India Pvt Ltd, \nBangalore\n from March\n?07\n to till date\n\n Worked for Primes IT Solutions Pvt Ltd, Banglore from May\n?05 to March? 07.\n\n Worked as a project trainee from Jan\n?05 to Apr?05 in Primes IT Solutions Pvt Ltd\nExpertise\nLanguages : C#, C, SQL, XML, XSL, Java2.0, HTML4.0.\nWeb Technologies : Microsoft .NET Framework1.1, ASP.NET1.1, ASP.NET2.0, Web Services.\nDatabases : SQLSERVER2000, MSACESS and SQLSERVER2005.\nIDE : Microsoft Visual Studio.NET2003\n.NET Tools : FxCop1.32, Nunit, FxCop, and Microsoft Visio\nScripting Languages : Java Script1.2\nOperating Systems : Windows 2000, Windows XP.\nReporting Tools : MS Reporting services\nProjects\nProject #1:\nTitle : Netwerkes\nClient : Netwerkes\nRole : Developing Reports.\nSoftware : ASP.Net, C#, SQL Server 2005, SQL Server 2005 Reporting Services.\nDescription:\nNetwerkes is an acquired part of AIM healthcare. The primary business of Netwerkes is to act as a clearinghouse and a liaison between healthcare provider and the payer. This Project is mainly for Generate reports that are unique within the industry and demonstrate the value that Netwerkes brings to its customers. This mainly consists of two kind of users and based upon their login respective pages should be displayed. Features & Functionality of this project will include a payer reporting portal where the payers, Netwerkes executive staff & sales personnel will log on to view the summary roll up reports as a dashboard where they can further drill down to granularity of an individual claim based on the roles & privileges.\nResponsibilities:\n\n Generating Reports\n\n Involved in creating reusable user controls\nProject #2:\nTitle : ICS Pharmacy\nClient : Nova\nRole : Design and Developing pages.\nSoftware : ASP.Net, C#, ADO.Net, SQL Server 2005.\nDuration : 5 months\nDescription:\nThis Project is mainly for storing details of patient during his visit to a clinic. This project helps to maintain the details of patients and also maintaining the past visit information like which doctor Patient consulted previously and what are all the prescriptions for that patient. We can also edit patient information or we can remove that patient. This project also maintains allergy details for a patient so that the doctor won\n?t prescribe the same for the patient an\nd act accordingly.\nResponsibilities:\n\n Developed Coding for webforms.\n\n Implementing validations and verifications on all pages.\n\n Involved in designing WebPages\n\n Involved in creating reusable user controls\n\n Designed & implemented database connectivity to send, fetch data from database.\nProject #3:\nTitle : Job portal\nRole : Design and Developing pages.\nSoftware : ASP.Net, C#, ADO.Net.\nDuration : 4months\nDescription:\nThis web site is to help the job seekers for finding processes such as processing the people request, search for resumes from databases, induction, training and the security system. User sign up via customer facing website. Fill the profile form on the web to get username and password approve and the system will issue the individual account id. The member status given at this stage will be normal member. The user will proceed to fill up the rest of the particular in the web site. User will need to follow the payment procedure stated to pay the membership fees.\nResponsibilities:\n\n Developed Coding for webforms.\n\n Implementing validations and verifications on all pages.\n\n Involved in designing WebPages\nProject #4:\nTitle : DMS.\nRole : Team member.\nDuration : 3months.\nSoftware : C#, ASP.NET, ADO.Net, MS-SQL Server 2005.\nDescription:\nDocument Management System is a routing document that sends documents from one section to another section with in that particular orgination.Documents are first received in hand first and then user of record section or admin section has rights to forward that document in that organization. The system is designed in such a way that a section can receive, or send a document internally or to the outward unit\nResponsibilities:\n\n Involved in coding of all crucial web forms.\n\n Designing web pages.\n\n Designing Reports using Reporting services.\nProject #5:\nTitle : EasyCinema .\nRole : Team Member.\nSoftware : ASP.NET, ADO.NET, C#, XML, .NET Framework, SQL Server 2000.\nDuration : 6 months\nDescription:\nEasyCinema is the latest venture from easyGroup to meet the customer needs in booking for various screens. EasyCinema system incorporates many of the successful features of the easyGroup companies, including yield management, internet ticket sales with high levels of automation to avoid unnecessary frills. The customised easyCinema manages scheduling, pricing, booking, payment of easyCinema business.\nResponsibilities:\n\n Designed & implemented database connectivity to send, fetch data from database.\n\n Involved in designing WebPages.\n\n Involved in creating reusable user controls\nProject #6:\nTitle : Insurance Management system.\nRole : Team member.\nDuration : 5 months.\nSoftware : C#, ASP.NET, ADO.Net, MS-SQL Server 2000.\nDescription:\nInsurance Management system is an intranet based private web application, which is designed by a group of insurance Agent agents, to make their application work of insurance policies and claims process easier and flexible. The web based application is used within their organization under the distributed accessibility to check the status of the customers who have taken new policies and their proper track and reminding of policy premium payments and claim conditions. The system is actually developed to cater to the process speed up in their Business process such that the customer satisfaction rates increase and the generic flow of customers into this domain follows a smooth and steady fashion. The major problem under the manual process is to keep track of the existing insurance policy holders, and remaining them at regular intervals about their policy premium payments. In order to render the ordinary services also it takes a great lot of time in just searching through the registers for the existing customers base. . If the process of data storage can be automated and follow up of search can be increased, there is always a heavy chance of getting extra customers in turn, which can increase the profits ratio upon the organization.\nResponsibilities:\n\n Involved in coding of all crucial web forms.\n\n Designing web pages.\nT.Kishore.\n(Signature)','Infinite Computer Solutions India Pvt Ltd',1,NULL,'2007-10-18',NULL,'2007-10-18','2010-06-09 12:13:49','2010-06-09',2,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(171,'Vikas B',NULL,NULL,'Bhubaneswar','vikgngbvfbvnas.bfdbvngdnhati@gmail.com',NULL,'0129 2304258','0','09938374183','0','09891479228','0','2006-11-12',8,24,'2010-06-09 12:13:49',3,'0',NULL,'200710/18/ATT24648.html','200710/18/DOC16295.doc','Vikas B\nVikas B\nPhone\n: 09938374183\nE-mail\n\nvikgngnas.bfdngdnhati@gmail.com\nAddress\n: D-1, Defence Colony, Niladri Vihar, \nBhubaneswar\n, Orissa\n\nProfile:\nAs a committed and enthusiastic IT professional with 3 years & 4 months experience in Software Development and keenness to acquire any additional skills that may be required.\nTechnical Profile:\n\n        \nMicrosoft Technologies\n          \n\n           \nVisual Basic.Net, Visual Basic 6.0, ASP.Net, ASP, C#\n\n        \nMarkup Languages\n               \n\n           \nXML, HTML\n\n        \nScripting Languages\n             \n\n           \nVBScript, JavaScript\n\n        \nDatabases\n                           \n\n           \nSQL Server 2000, Oracle \n\n        \n3GL\n                                     \n\n           \nC, C++\n\n        \nApplication\n                           \n\n           \nMS Office, VBA (Word & Excel)\nEducational Qualifications:\n\n        \nBachelor of Engineering (Honours)\n in \nInformation Technology\n completed with \n70.22\n% from Hindu College of Engineering (Affiliated by \nMaharshi\nDayanand\nUniversity\n, Rohtak), Sonepat in 2004.\n\n        \nClass 12\nth\n passed with \n69.0\n% from \nD.A.V.\nPublic School\n (C.B.S.E.), Ballabgarh in 2000. \n\n        \nClass 10\nth\n passed with \n81.6\n% from Nehru Public School (C.B.S.E.), \nGhaziabad\n in 1998.\nWorking Experience:\n\n        \nWorking as a Software Engineer with Infosys Technologies Ltd., \nBhubaneswar\n since October 2006 to till date.\n\n        \nWorked as a Software Developer with Thomson Digital, Noida since October 2005 to October 2006.\n\n        \nWorked as a Software Engineer with Sakshay Tradelinks Pvt. Ltd., \nNew Delhi\n since May 2004 to October 2005.\nProjects Undertaken:\nCycle Count Application\nLanguage used\n- Visual Basic.Net, ASP.Net, ADO.Net, JavaScript\nDatabase used\n- SQL Server 2000\nPosition\n- Team Leader\nResponsibilities\n- Analysis, Coding & Testing\nProject Location\n- Infosys Technologies Ltd., \nBhubaneswar\n\nE-Requisition\nLanguage used\n- Visual Basic.Net, ASP.Net, ADO.Net, JavaScript\nDatabase used\n- SQL Server 2000\nPosition\n- Team Leader\nResponsibilities\n- Analysis, Coding & Testing\nProject Location\n- Infosys Technologies Ltd., \nBhubaneswar\n\nTravel & Expenses Application\nLanguage used\n- Visual Basic.Net, ASP.Net, ADO.Net, ASP, JavaScript, VBScript \nDatabase used\n- SQL Server 2000\nPosition\n- Team Leader\nResponsibilities\n- Analysis, Coding & Testing\nProject Location\n- Infosys Technologies Ltd., \nBhubaneswar\n\nShopping Cart\nLanguage used\n- C#.Net, ASP.Net, ADO.Net, JavaScript\nDatabase used\n- SQL Server 2000\nPosition\n- Team Leader\nResponsibilities\n- Analysis, Coding & Testing\nProject Location\n- Infosys Technologies Ltd., \nBhubaneswar\n\nThomson Quality Control System\nLanguage used\n- Visual Basic.Net\nDescription\n- According to 175 Wiley Publisher?s specifications, this application checks the final XML file of production of Book section.\nPosition\n- Team Member\nResponsibilities\n- Analysis, Coding & Testing\nProject Location\n- Thomson Digital, Noida\n\nThomson Metadata Management System\nLanguage used\n- Visual Basic 6.0, XML, XSL\nDescription\n- This application generates DART Metadata XML file on the basis of 3B2, XML and PDF files. It checks naming conventions of folders, subfolders and files according to Wiley Publisher?s specifications. It has facility to parse, validate & browse metadata & message XML files.\nPosition\n- Team Member\nResponsibilities\n- Analysis, Coding & Testing\nProject Location\n- Thomson Digital, Noida\n\nQuick Index\nLanguage used\n- Visual Basic 6.0, XML, XSL\nTools used\n- MS Word 2000, Acrobat Reader (5.0)\nDescription\n- This application search out the page numbers of index terms in the PDF & Word files. It generates XML file for final index terms with page numbers.\nPosition\n- Team Member\nResponsibilities\n- Analysis, Coding & Testing\nProject Location\n- Thomson Digital, Noida\n\nAutomated Electronic Product System\nLanguage used\n- C#.Net, MS Access 2000\nTools used-\n Acrobat Reader & Distiller (4.0 & 5.0), Enfocus Pitstop Server (1.61)\nDescription\n- This application converts PS files to PDF files, put cross-linking between Authors? Queries. It takes prints of PDF Files after checking of Enfocus Pitstop Server, if there is no error. If there is any error, then it takes print of those pages, which have errors. After checking of PDF files, the files are uploaded to the FTP locations depending upon locations. In this application, users have to drop the PS files in the hot folders and the remaining process is done by automated way. In this application, there is facility of sending emails at each and every completion of process and error, if any error may occur.\nPosition\n- Team Member\nResponsibilities\n- Analysis, Coding & Testing\nProject Location\n- Thomson Digital, Noida\n\nSmart e-Book\nLanguage used\n- Visual Basic.Net\nTools used\n- Acrobat Reader & Distiller (4.0)\nDescription\n- This application converts PS files to PDF files, and then creates bookmarks and links on the basis of table of contents of book. After completion of process, it also make one final PDF file of book in the sequence of table of contents.\nPosition\n- Team Member\nResponsibilities\n- Analysis, Coding & Testing\nProject Location\n- Thomson Digital, Noida\n\nInvestment Record-Keeper\nLanguage used\n- Visual Basic.Net\nTools used\n- MS Excel & Access 2000\nDescription\n- This application calculates 18 formulas and stores values in Excel Files. It gives the facility to add new stock and fund managers, edit and deletes stock and fund managers.\nPosition\n- Team Member\nResponsibilities\n- Coding & Testing\nProject Location\n\nSakshay Tradelinks Pvt. Ltd., \nNew Delhi\n\nPayroll Management System\nLanguage used\n- Visual Basic 6.0, SQL Server 2000\nDescription\n- This application maintains all payroll activities of the company.\nPosition\n- Team Member\nResponsibilities\n- Coding & Testing\nProject Location\n\nSakshay Tradelinks Pvt. Ltd., \nNew Delhi\nPersonal Profile:\nFather?s Name\n    \n            \n\n           \nMr. Shishupal Singh.\nMother?s Name\n   \n            \n\n           \nMrs. Manorama Singh\nGender\n              \n            \n\n           \nMale\nDate of Birth\n      \n            \n\n           \n22-March-1983\nNationality\n         \n            \n\n           \nIndian\nMarital Status\n     \n            \n\n           \nSingle\nPassport\n                        \n            \n\n           \nYes (#: G1063140)\nPermanent Address\n         \n\n           \n533, Adarsh Nagar-II, Ballabgarh,\n                                                \nFaridabad\n, Haryana. PIN-121004\nPhone\n                           \n\n           \n0129 - 2304258, 09891479228\n\nDate: \n17 October 2007\nPlace:\nBhubaneswar\n(Vikas Bhati)','Infosys Technologies Ltd',1,NULL,'2007-10-18',NULL,'2007-10-18','2010-06-09 12:13:49','2010-06-09',3,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(172,'Yogendra Trivedi',NULL,NULL,NULL,'triveewfgwerdi56gr85fgb687@rediffmail.com',NULL,NULL,'0','91 9911306937','0',NULL,'0','2006-04-29',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-09 12:13:49',2,'0',NULL,'200710/18/ATT24647.html','200710/18/DOC16296.doc','Anjali Mishra\n\nTrivedi\n                                                       \nEmail: \ntriveewfgwerdi56gr85687@rediffmail.com\nMobile\n: 91-9911306937\n                                                \n\nAssignments in Software Development & implementation with a technology driven organisation of repute\n\nProfessional Synopsis\nMasters in Computer Applications\n with 2.8 years of experience in the areas of Software Development & Implementation. Presently working with \nHanu Software Solutions Pvt Ltd.\n\n\nas Software Engineer\n\n Through understanding of the SDLC with proficiency in mapping client / business requirements, documentation, application design, development, integration & testing and troubleshooting for complex information systems management. Holds the distinction of executing numerous software design, development & implementation projects in web technologies. Possess excellent problem solving, analytical, communication and team building skills with proficiency at grasping new technical concepts quickly & utilise the same in a productive manner.\n\nAreas of Expertise\n\nFunctional;\n\n     \nMapping business/client?s requirements and translating these requirements into functional specifications and detailed test plans.\n\n     \nConducting system study and coordinating with team members for System Design & Integration.\n\n     \nHandling various technical aspects like product documentation, software designs, coding of modules.\n\n     \nVerifying change requests and defects, tracking and reviewing test plans, test results and unresolved problems, reviewing test reports & taking corrective actions. \n\n     \nDelivering and implementing the project as per scheduled deadlines, extending post-implementation and maintenance support to the technical support team and client.\n\nTechnical;\n\nMicrosoft Technologies\n   \n: Dot Net Technologies in (C#. net), VB 6.0, and Microsoft Visual\n\n                                       \n   \nSource Safe\n\nTools\n                         \n    \n: VSS (Visual source safe) \nWeb Technologies\n         \n    \n: ASP. Net, XML, JAVA Script, \nAjax\n, PHP, HTML 4.0. \nMiddle Wares\n       \n        \n\nADO\n. Net, Active X Data Objects \nDatabases\n                \n   \n: SQL Server 2000/2005, My Sql, and Access 2000.\nConcepts\n                      \n: System Analysis & Design, DBMS, Data Structures, Networking, Software Engineering, Artificial Intelligence, Compiler Design, Web Technologies, Graphics & Animations, Designs & Analysis of Algorithms. \n\n\n\nCareer Highlights\n\n\n\nHanu Software Solutions, Gurgaon \n                  \n                                    \n       \nDec?06 to till now\nAs a Software Engineer\n\nKey Projects Handled;\nTitle: \nBaidansWebMixer\n                                               \nClient: \nBrice Carrington (http://\nwww.Baidansmixer.com/BaidansMixer\n).\nTeam Size: 6\n\n\n     \n                                                                                 \n    \nRole: Team Member\nTechnologies:\n\nAsp.net 2.0, C#, sqlserver 2000, \nAjax\n, JavaScript.\n\nScope: BaidansMixer web site is the collection of original creation of SoundFX files. These sounds are natural and demanding into feature films, video games and software. Website has one Audio Mixer, which supports these natural sounds. Any Guest or Registered User can mix these rarely available sounds with applying several audio effects with the help of online Mixer and can set that customized sound as a ring tone to his/her cell phone via payment facility while preview option is freely available. This project implements Cybersource payment gateway, Clickatell API to send sms and ring tone, ComponentSpace Email Verification.\n\nAll the available SoundFX files can be purchased through available full-featured shopping cart. This Project has been categorized into three modules Mixer, SoundFx and WAP. In Mixer module user can create or mix the ring tone with sound effects. In SoundFX module user can purchase pre stored sound files in default format or in user selected format. User can view Purchase History and can recover sound file. The WAP module is dedicated to cell phone user where they can download the ring tone by entering their credentials.\n\nResponsibilities:\n        \nTeam member\n\n          \nUnderstanding requirements\n\n          \nCoding using C#\n\n          \nImplementing SSL and Payment Gateway.\n\n          \nDeployment and Delivery\n\n\n\nHanu Software Solutions, Gurgaon \n                  \n                            \n     \n          \nMay?06 to Nov?06\nAs a Software Engineer\n\nKey Projects Handled;\nTitle\n\nBrice Carrington\n (http://www.bricecarrington.com/bricecarrington/index.aspx)\nClient: \nBrice Carrington\nTeam Size: 3 \n   \n     \n                                                                                 \n    \nRole: Team Member\nTechnologies:\n\nAsp.net 2.0, C#, Sql Server 2000, Javascript, Photoshop.\n\nScope: \nBricecarrington.com website will be developed using flash and .net programming. The website will contain the biography of sound designer Brice Carrington. It will also contain the case studies, photos of Brice Carrington, press articles, content of print interviews, TV interview.\n\nMy role is to create the admin section who handle or the users activity, create user Id and password to login into the site. Once user enters the site his account deleted and he has to request again for the login ID. Website will not be open for public access. Only authorized access will be permissible.\n\nResponsibilities:\n   \nTeam member\n\n          \nUnderstanding requirements\n\n          \nCoding using C#\n\n          \nDeployment and Delivery\n\n\nHanu Software Solutions, Gurgaon \n         \n                                       \n            \nNov?05 to\n\nMay?06\n                                  \nAs a Software Engineer\n\nKey Projects Handled;\nTitle: \nRayMarine \n(https://webportal.raymarine.com/wcts/frmLogin.aspx)\n                   \n                            \nClient: \nRayMarine\n\nTeam Size: 5\n\n\n     \n                                                                                 \n    \nRole: Team Member\nTechnologies:\n\nAsp.net 2.0, C#, sqlserver 2000, \nAjax\n, JavaScript.\n\nScope: \nThe Project has been categorized into two major modules Dealer and Admin. Both modules has same login with different authorization role. The Login process has been implemented with SSL and web service. The Dealer has functionalities to add technician, certify them and make installation over the vessels. Admin has functionality as a super admin should have but it also has authorization of process which dealer has.\nResponsibilities:\n        \nTeam member\n\n          \nUnderstanding requirements\n\n          \nCoding using C#(Membership and Role Management)\n\n          \nImplementing SSL\n\n          \nDeployment and Delivery\n\n\nHanu Software Solutions, Gurgaon \n                  \n   \n                               \n\n        \nJun?05 to \n\nOct?05\nAs a Software Engineer\n\nKey Projects Handled;\nTitle: \nWahIndia\n                                                \nClient: WahIndia.inc\n                                       \nTeam Size: 6 \n  \n\n     \n                                                                                 \n    \nRole: Team Member\nTechnologies:\n\nAsp. net, C#, Sqlserver, JavaScript.\nResponsibilities :\n\nDocumentation,Coding and Testing.\n\nScope: Wah \nIndia\n is an online community that connects people through a network of trusted friends. We are committed to providing an online meeting place where people can socialize, make new acquaintances and find others who share their interests\n\n. This is a Social Networking site where you can create your profile, you can search people, You can add them to your profile as friend, family or as an extended network, You can create and join groups and fan clubs, You can create Photo Albums and Video Albums, You can also send message and reply to message of the user and many more functionality like Admin Panel, Birthday Reminder, Account Expiration reminders.\n                           \nResponsibilities:\n        \nTeam member\n\n          \nUnderstanding requirements\n\n          \nCoding using C#\n\n\nNetzone Software, \nDelhi\n            \n                                                              \nOct?04 to May? 05\nAs a Software trainee\n\nKey Projects Handled;\nTitle: \nOfficeGT Company Info\n                                                \nClient: BCA Technologies, Inc\n                                        \nTeam Size: 3\n        \n     \n                                                                                 \n   \nRole: Team Member\nTechnologies:\n\nAsp.net, C#, sqlserver 2000.\n\nScope: OfficeGT is a web application project that was designed for use in a network environment so information will flow to all users to increase office productivity.\n\nEngineers, architects, attorneys, accountants, or other organizations that track people and projects can use OfficeGT to organize information such as time, expenses, contacts, sales, marketing and project information.\n\nResponsibilities:\n        \nTeam member\n\n          \nUnderstanding requirements\n\n          \nCoding using C#\n\n          \nUnit and Manual testing\n\n\n\n                                 \nEducation\n\n\n     \nMCA from \nUtkal\nUniversity\n (BPUT), \nBhubaneswar\n in 2004.\n\n     \nB-Sc (Hons.) from \nBJB\nCollege\n\nUtkal\nUniversity\nBhubaneswar\n\nin 2000. \n\n\nProfessional Courses\n\n\n     \n. Net from Pentasoft Technology Pvt. Ltd in 2002. \n\n\n\nPersonal Details\nContact Address\n       \n\n             \n1213, Rail Vihar, Sector-15,\n\nPart\n   \nII,Gurguon. Haryana\nDate of Birth\n              \n\n             \n23\nrd\n Aug?1978\nLanguage\n                  \n\n             \nEnglish and\n\nHindi\nHobbies\n                     \n\n             \nMusic, Travel & Cooking\nMarital Status\n            \n\n             \nSingle\n\n\n\nDeclaration:\nI consider myself familiar with all Software Development and Functional Testing aspects. I am also confident of my ability to work in a team.\nI hereby declare that the information furnished above is true to the best of my knowledge.\n\n\n\nDate:\n    \n                                                                                                          \nPlace:\n   \nGurgaon\n      \n                                                                            \n      \nYogendra Trivedi',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-18',NULL,'2007-10-18','2010-06-09 12:13:49','2010-06-09',2,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(173,'S K Pallai',NULL,NULL,'Bangalore','skdvdvvpallai@gmail.com',NULL,NULL,'0','9916217932','0',NULL,'0','2007-08-15',8,23,'2010-06-09 12:13:49',3,'0',NULL,'200710/18/ATT24641.html','200710/18/DOC16297.doc','Personal Summary\n\n\nName:\n S.K. Pallai\nEmail ID:\n\nskdvdvvpallai@gmail.com\nCell phone:\n (0)-9916217932 \n\nExperience Summary\n\n          \nHaving 2+ years of experience on Microsoft Technologies(\nC#, ASP.NET, MSSQL\n).\n\n          \nExcellent knowledge on \nObject Oriented analysis, design, development and implementation\n of applications.\n\n          \nExtensively worked on enterprise, web and client/server applications.\n\nProfessional Experience\n\n          \nWorking as Software Engineer in \nThinkways Software Technologies\n\nBangalore\n\nIndia\n from February 2005 to till date.\n\nEducational Summary\n\n          \nBachelor of Engineering in Computer Science & Engineering from Visveswaraiah Technological University, \nBelgaum\n\n\n          \nDiploma in Computer Science & Engineering from Board of Technical Education, Karnataka.\n\n\nTechnical Skills\n\nWeb Technologies\nASP.NET, HTML, CSS, JavaScript\nLanguages\nC#, XML\nServers\nWindows 2000 Server, IIS\nOS\nWinXP/2000/WinNT/Win98 and MS-DOS \nDatabases\nMS SQL Server 2000, MS Access\nSoftware Engineering Technologies\n.NET Framework\n\nProjects Summary\n1. Web Portal\nClient\n            \n: Vaayoo Inc.\nRole\n           \n\n: Developer\nTeam Size\n      \n\n\n\nProject Description:\nThis project is mainly divided into 3 parts: portal, web services and device. This project?s main theme is interacting with web application and devices by using web services. Portal contains two parts: User Module and Provider Module. While user subscribing for this site needs to mention his/her mobile number. User needs to select community, channels and services from the site. Channels and services are created by the providers and communities are created by the user.\n\nHere user subscribed communities, channels and services are displayed in user device. User can download or upload images, text, audio and video to any community he/she has subscribed. Uploading and downloading an image, text and video is transferred from the web service.\n\nSkills:\n.Net Framework, C#, ASP.Net, MSSQL Server-2000, \nJavaScript\nResponsibilities:\n\n     \nAs a project engineer I was involved in the following activities: \n               \n              \n                               \nDesigning & Coding the web pages for user module.\nWriting the SQL queries for various database operations. \nInvolved in database designing.\n\n2. Job Portal\nClient\n            \n: JobJunctionIndia.\nRole\n           \n\n: Developer\nTeam Size\n      \n\n\n\nProject Description:\nIt is a job search site for a manpower consultancy based on \nBangalore\n which helps job seekers advance their careers and get jobs easily and help employers to fulfil their recruitment needs. It contains four modules i.e. Jobseeker, Employer, Recruiter and Administrator.\nSkills:\n\n        \nVisual Studio.NET,C#,.NET Framework,MSSQLServer, JavaScript, HTML, CSS\nResponsibilities:\n\n    \n\nAs a project engineer I was involved in the following activities: \n                             \nDesigning various web Forms\nWriting Database Queries and Stored procedures\nCoding and Testing of various modules\n\n3. On Line Quotation Processing \nClient\n            \n: Creative Engineering\nRole\n           \n\n: Developer\nTeam Size\n      \n\n\n\nProject Description:\nThis is a web-based application providing facilities to process the quotations for the products of that manufacturer unit. The customer can access the engineering product details through its web site and can send order to the company. The company administrator enters the cost details, which will be forwarded to the customers email id automatically. The Sales executives of the company appointed in different locations can view the quotation details and can contact the customer at the time of need.\nSkills:\n.Net Framework, C#, MSSQL Server-2000, ASP.Net, IIS \nResponsibilities:\n\n     \nAs a project engineer I was involved in the following activities: \n                               \nDesigning various web Forms\nWriting Database Queries and Stored procedures\nCoding and Testing of various modules','Thinkways Software Technologies',1,NULL,'2007-10-18',NULL,'2007-10-18','2010-06-09 12:13:49','2010-06-09',3,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(174,'Anand sudeer',NULL,NULL,'Gurgaon','sadadvdvnand_sudvdeer@hotmail.com',NULL,'124 2219272','0',NULL,'0',NULL,'0','2006-08-14',9,30,'2010-06-09 12:13:49',2,'0',NULL,'200710/18/ATT24640.html','200710/18/DOC16298.doc','Resdex @ naukri.com\nanand sudeer\nA-11 South City 2 Sohna Road Gurgaon - 122101 \nsadadvdvnand_sudvdeer@hotmail.com\n\nTelephone: 9810\n(M)\n 1 124 2219272\n(R)\n\nD.O.B\n - 02 Apr 1977 \nModified on\n - 25 Sep 2007 \nAnnual Salary\n - INR 10 Lac(s) 55 Thousand \nTotal Years of Experience\n - 7 Year(s) 0 Month(s) \nCurrent Location\n - Gurgaon \nPreferred Location\n - No preference \nMCA + 7 Years of Experience in Microsoft Technologies and J2EE platform\n\nTEXT RESUME \n\nRESUME\nNAME Sadanand Sudeer\nQUALIFICATION Master in Computers Application\nHARDWARE x86, Pentium\nOPERATING SYSTEM Windows 9x, Windows NT, Unix\nLANGUAGES C#, VB.Net, Java, Javascript, C, C++\nRDBMS/GUI/TOOLS Oracle 7.x / 8.0, MS SQL Server 2000, MS Access,\nWEB TECHNOLOGIES ASP.Net, ASP, JSP, HTML, DHTML,\nJava Script, Servlets, XML, XSL, SOAP.\nWEB TOOLS Visual Studio .Net, Visual Interdev, IIS\nB2B & EAI Tools Tibco Businessworks, Extricity 4.0\nSUMMARY\nFive years and Four months of experience in the areas of Internet Technologies, RDBMS, and GUI Tools. Proven Expertise on technologies like .Net, C#, VB .Net, VB 6.0, ASP, COM/DCOM, Oracle 7.x / 8.0 and SQL Server 2000.\nPROJECT DETAILS\n1 SECnet Feb-2004 - Till Date\nSECnet is an in-house application maintained by CCH. SECnet system is used by securities law firms to search for information filed with the Securities and Exchange Commission (SEC) or information sent by the SEC in response to a company request. Changing customer requirements, functionalities offered by competitor products, aggressive revenue targets given to business users and most importantly the cost involved in maintaining and enhancing the existing CGI Perl based application, impelled CCH to migrate the application to .Net.. The project also involved adding several functional and non-functional enhancements to the capabilities of the existing system.\nSECnet system also interacts with many third party systems such as Lexis Nexis search engine, EDGAR filing feed and uses many other 3rd party tools like convert-online, Active PDF Doc Converter and Web-Grabber etc. to provide easy-to-use functionalities to end users.\nIn addition to the above system a Tools was also developed to convert HTML documents to RTF on the fly and was integrated with the above mentioned system.\nResponsibilities\n* Project Lead\n* Full System Requirements Gathering\n* Use Case Analysis\n* Use Case Design\n* Architecture Design\n* Development and Testing.\nEnvironments\nVisual Studio .NET, C#, .Net Remoting, SQL Server 7.0, Windows 2000 Server, JavaScript, IE 5.5, Morzila, Netscape\nTeam Size 10\nDuration 14 Months\n2 EDI Transmission System Dec-2003 to Jan 2004\nThis system was developed for Southern California Edison company for electronically transmitting Workers Compensation Data to Division of Workers Compensation (DWC) of California. This transmission earlier was being done on paper and required intensive manual effort in extracting and consolidating the data and sending it through mail. The client required this system to be built so as to automate the above process.\nThe system hence developed had functionalities like extracting data from SCE Workers Compensation Repository called Pyramid, validating the data based on the rules set by DWC, formatting the data into EDI X12 format, transmit the data to DWC, accept acknowledgements from DWC and Notifying Users if DWC reports any error\nResponsibilities\n* Team Lead\n* Full System Requirements Gathering\n* Use Case Analysis\n* Use Case Design\n* Architecture Design\n* Development and Testing.\nEnvironments\nVisual Studio .NET, C#, Oracle 9.0.2, Rational XDE for .Net, Windows 2000, XP, JavaScript, IE 5.5.\nTeam Size 5\nDuration 2 Months\n3 Enterprise Inventory System Jun-2003 to Nov-2003\nThis project was aimed at complete automation of the Business Processes the client has with its business partners. This project involved change in the enterprise inventory system of the client from Promis to SAP. This affected all the existing systems, their integration and B2B processes. The detailed flow is as follows:\n* Business partners send data through TIBCO, which is inserted into SQL Server database using TIBCO ADB Adapter.\n* Validations are done upon this data according to the client\'s business processes by a threaded Console application and events are generated and maintained in a Queue.\n* These generated events are then sent to SAP using Tibco Database Adapter.\n* Changes in the SAP system trigger IDOCS, which, using TIBO SAP Adapter is sent to the planning system.\n* A Web based GUI was provided to give complete transparency and control over the Data-Flow and to manage error and recovery for the whole system\nResponsibilities\n* WEB Interface part of the project\no Full System Requirements Gathering\no Use Case Analysis\no Use Case Design\no Architecture Design\no Development and Testing\n* Other Modules\no Development of TIBCO BusinessWorks Processes using TIBCO SAP Adapter and TIBCO ADB Adapter.\no Development of C# Console Application for Data validation and Event generation, and PL./SQL.\nEnvironments\nVisual Studio .NET, C#, Tibco BusinessWorks, Tibco ADB Adapter, Tibco SAP Adapter, SQL Server 2000, Rational XDE for .Net, Windows 2000, JavaScript, IE 5.5.\nTeam Size 4\nDuration 11 Months\n3. Stock Info Web Application Jan-2003 to May-2003\nThe Client is a share brokerage firm in United Kingdom, providing share analysis data as a value added service to their clients. The project is to create a web application that provides the information to the business users of client in a fast and friendly manner without exposing any of the proprietary information to non-business users.\nResponsibilities\n* Full System Requirements Gathering\n* Use Case Analysis\n* Use Case Design\n* Architecture Design\n* Development and Testing\nEnvironments\nASP, JavaScript , VB Script, SQL Server 2000, Rational Rose, Windows 2000, IE 5.5.\nTeam Size 5\nDuration 3 Months\n4. Cognos Dashboard Development & Maintenance Aug-2002 to Dec-2002\nThis project involved replacing the existing Essbase based dashboard by a Cognos based Dashboard providing the reports in-line with existing system.\nResponsibilities\nDesigning and developing Database schema to derive optimum performance from Cognos\nMapping the existing reports to the reporting features available in Cognos\nDesigning and developing Cubes on Cognos\nPreparing the test plan and test cases\nTesting and deployment\nEnvironments\nCognos - Series 7(Impromptu, PowerPlay), Oracle 8i\nTeam Size 2\nDuration 6 Months\n5. Hyperion Essbase Dashboard Maintenance Feb-2002 to Jul-2002\nAs a member of Dashboard support and maintenance team, I was involved Building Cubes and generating reports as per the requirements of the client. I was also responsible for maintaining the cubes and trouble shooting the cubes in case of data inconsistency.\nResponsibilities\nAnalysis of the specification provided and studying the requirements\nCube Design and development\nPreparing the test plan and test cases\nModule level testing and integration testing\nEnvironments\nHyperion Essbase OLAP-Server, EIS Tool, Hyperion Analyzer (for reporting), Oracle 8i\nTeam Size 2\nDuration 6 Months\n6. Letter Template Tool Jan-2002 to Jan-2002\nLetter Template Admin is a letter template generation/editing tool. The tool helps the user design letter templates with images and text on it, further the user can define place holders for text/ part of text/ Images and associate them with any database field using a inbuilt query builder. The tool has the capability to fill in the contents (text/images) from any associated database and produce a complete document. The tool also provides for storing images & text contents into the database.\nResponsibilities\n* Full System Requirements Gathering\n* Use Case Analysis\n* Use Case Design\n* Architecture Design\n* Development and Testing\nEnvironments\nVisual Basic 6.0, Com+, ActiveX, SQL Server 2000\nTeam Size 6\nDuration 1 Months\n7. Campaign Management System Jan 2000 to Dec 2001\nThe Campaign Management System is a comprehensive solution for any Out-Bound & In-bound Telephonic-Campaign. The solution provides for dialing (Manual/Power/Predictive as provided by the underlying Call-Center Solution) to multiple cities across continents, with any number of campaigns running. The system displays data of the customer being dialed out to the agent before the call gets matured so that the agent addresses the customers only after knowing his background. The system provides for host of regular telephony controls like hold, transfer, disconnect and release, and agent-to-agent Communication and agent to supervisor text messaging. It also provides for features like Recorded-Script playback to agent as well as the customer, automatic verifier Call Barging, Monitoring, Coaching and Remote supervision of calls.\nThe Unique features of CMS are as follows\n1. The unique feature of Coaching where the agents supervisor could speak to the agent while agent is in conversation with the customer without the customer knowing about it\n2. The ability of the software to run multiple campaigns across continents and all time zones simultaneously.\n3. The system is independent of the underlying Call-Center Software and Database Management System.\n4. Manipulating the resource allocated to the running campaigns on the fly so that the call-center operation is not halted for any reason.\n5. An Interactive Voice Response (IVR) system generator to develop any IVR/Welcome messages on the fly. This tool gives the customer all the features to develop any IVR of any complexity\n6. A Script (User Screen) Designer. This tool gives the customer features to design/Modify the user/Agent screen dynamically according to the requirements of the Campaign being run by the system.\nResponsibilities\n* System requirement Study team\n* High level design of the system\n* Design and Development of enhancements required in the Call-Center Server (Mars-Server - A Real-time OS) using C.\n* Design and Development of front-end GUI for Agent Machine.\n* Design and Development of the IVR Generator\nEnvironments\nC, Visual Basic 6.0, HTML, VB Script, ASP, Java Script, Visual Interdev 6.0, MS SQL Server 7.0, IIS 4.0, and Windows-NT.\nTeam Size 45\nDuration 36 Months','SECnet',1,NULL,'2007-10-18',NULL,'2007-10-18','2010-06-09 12:13:49','2010-06-09',2,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(175,' v Kumar',NULL,NULL,'Bangalore','viv@yahoo.co.in',NULL,NULL,'0','09868475807','0',NULL,'0','2007-07-15',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-09 12:13:49',3,'0',NULL,'200710/18/ATT24637.html','200710/18/DOC16299.doc','CURRICULUM ? VITAE\n\nCURRICULUM ? VITAE\n\n\nKUMAR\nDOB: 1st march 1979\nE-mail: viv@yahoo.co.in\nPhone: 09868475807\n\n\n\n\n\n\n           \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nExperience Summary\n\n\n2 years and 9 months of experience in object oriented programming and Web based applications in ASP.NET(C#) and Java script. RDBMS experience is on SQL-Server, Oracle, Postgres and MS Access. Currently working at Nagarro Software Pvt. Ltd. as \nAssociate Technical Lead\n\n\nObjective\n\n\nTo achieve a better position in a software industry with better opportunity of responsibility.\n\nAcademic Qualifications\n\n\nDegree\nInstitute\nUniversity/Board\nPercentage/CGPA\nMCA (2005)\nSC&SS\nJNU, \nNew Delhi\n\n7.44/9.0 (82.67%)\nB.Sc (Maths. Hons.)\nA.N.\nCollege\n\nPatna\nMagadh\nUniversity\n66.62%\nIntermediate \nGovt. Queens Inter College,\nVaranasi\nUPSEC\n70.6%\n10\nth\nDayanand Vidyalaya, \nPatna\nBSEB\n79.67%\n\nAreas of Interest\n\n\n\n         \nData Structure\n\n         \nAlgorithms\n\n         \nC, C++, C#, Java Script\n\nTechnical Skills\n\n\n\n         \nMain\n                      \n\n           \nC#, ASP.NET, Java Script.\n\n         \nLanguages\n\n            \n\n           \nC#, C\n\n         \nE-Commerce\n          \n\n           \nASP.NET, HTML, XML, JavaScript.\n\n         \nDatabase\n   \n            \n\n           \nMS Access, SQL Server 2000.\n\n         \nOS worked on\n        \n\n           \nWindows 2000, Windows 98 and Windows XP Professional.\n\n         \nTechnologies\n         \n\n           \nWorking knowledge of Microsoft .Net 2003 and Microsoft .Net 2005.\n\nCo-curricular Activities\n\n\n\n         \nGot 4\nth\n rank in JNU entrance examination.\n\n         \nOthers selections: \n   \nM.P. M.C.A. Entrance\n\n-9\nth\n Rank\nH.C.U. M.C.A. Entrance -3\nrd\n Rank\nCochin\nUniversity\n M.C.A. Entrance ? 1\nst\n Rank\nSelection in D.U M.C.A. Entrance (Written)\nCompany Projects \n\n\n\n         \nUAL \nClient\n    \n            \n: United Aluminum Limited\nDuration\n            \n: February 2007 onwards\nEnvironment\n      \n: Microsoft Visual Studio.NET 2005, SQL Server 2000.\nDescription\n        \n: The software deals in maintenance of alloy, metals etc. to reconstruct new alloys on basis of percentage allotment of alloys. \n\nAlso it deals in constructing process of item templates.\nContribution\n       \n: Currently I am looking into Standard Manufacturing process, Freight Reconciliation,\n    \nLook up admin, Shipping, Tolling Manager, Machines, UA Dashboard, IQR and Login module.\n\n\n\n         \nUNIVERSAL\nClient\n    \n            \n: Coke Universal\nDuration\n            \n: November 2005 to March 2006.\nEnvironment\n      \n: Microsoft Visual Studio.NET 2003, SQL Server 2000.\nDescription\n        \n: At CokeUniversal.com you can book your ticket requests, hotel requests, meeting requests, VIP tour requests and trip package requests. Here admin can add users and delete users.\n\nContribution\n       \n: Handled the team of four members, three developers and one quality analyst and involved in developing the login page and all security aspects.\n\n\n         \nFHI \nClient\n    \n            \n: FHI\nDuration\n            \n: November 2005 to March 2006.\nEnvironment\n      \n: Microsoft Visual Studio.NET 2003, SQL Server 2000.\nDescription\n        \n: FHI is a site for handling its customers, where they can ask questions and find the possible solutions of their questions. Also there are some users and distributors who can collect various information from the sites posted by admin users.\nContribution\n       \n: I handled the team of three members, two developers and one quality analyst and involved in developing the login page and all security aspects.\n\n\n         \nProjistics \nClient\n    \n            \n: Projistics\nDuration\n            \n: March 2005 to February 2007\nEnvironment\n      \n: Microsoft Visual Studio.NET 2003, SQL Server 2000.\nDescription\n        \n: Projistics is a web-based collaboration and project management software for managing entire project lifecycles and logistics seamlessly, by facilitating collaboration in distributed teams.\nContribution\n       \n: I had worked on Discussion Board, Gadgets, Requirement Database, Dashboard, earned value reports and make R & D for fire fox support.\n\nDiscussion Board is an interface where we can send mail to group users by using either outlook, Projistics UI or any other mailing tool.\n\nIn our project management software we have a facility of dashboard where we can add gadgets. Gadgets are the way to show the information to user in a quick view format.\n\nCurrently I am working on earned value reports, where we can create reports on the basis of tasks and resources.\n\n\n\n         \nPortal \nClient\n    \n            \n: Portal\nDuration\n            \n: October 2005 onwards.\nEnvironment\n      \n: Microsoft Visual Studio.NET 2003, SQL Server 2000.\nDescription\n        \n\nPortal is in house software to handle all the internal interactions of employees.\nContribution\n       \n: I had made Discussion Board and create framework for mail notification.\n\n\n         \nTask Schedular Service \nClient\n    \n            \n: Nagarro\nDuration\n            \n: January 2005 to February 2005.\nEnvironment\n      \n: Microsoft Visual Studio.NET 2003.\nDescription\n        \n: By using t\nask schedular service one can schedule tasks daily, monthly, weekly or monthly or yearly. \nUsage\n   \n            \n: Now a day?s t\nask schedular service has been used in various projects.\n\nAlso I had worked in the development of Data Base Services and entity framework. Data base service is used by most of the ASP.NET Projects in Nagarro. \nEntity framework generates 7 class files for each entity selected by us from database. These classes help us for inserting, deleting, updating and retrieving useful information from database. \nIn the Data base service, I have done the functions, which accepts parameterized SQL query and returns the desired results. \nAlso I enhanced it by giving the functions, which execute the user-defined functions.\n\nCourse Project Undertaken\n\n\n\n         \nCar Show Room Management System\nCourse: RDBMS \nTool Used: SQL. (Oracle 8i)\nDescription: We implement the real world by using ER diagrams, making tables, normalizing them and then running our query by using SQL.\n\n\n         \nJNU Chess 2004 Software \nCourse: Software Engineering\nTool used: Java\nDescription: This Project has been developed under full phase of software development.\n\n\n         \njnutravels.com\nCourse: IT Management\nTool used: Java Servlets\nDescription: We developed our website jnutravels.com by using java Servlets and apache tomcat server.\n\n\n\n         \nObject Oriented Analysis and Design\nCourse: OOPS\nReal World:\n\nCar Show Room Management System\nTool Used: UML\nDescription: We did object oriented analysis and design. That was achieved by use case diagrams, class diagrams, refined class diagram, collaboration diagram, sequence diagram and activity diagram. Further\nthis was implemented in JDBC (course: Dap) using Java.\n\nPassport Details\n\n\nPassport no.\nDate of issue\nDate of expiry\nIssued by\nPlace\nF0331686\n6-9-2004\n5-9-2014\nGovt. Of \nIndia\nNew Delhi\n\n\nI affirm that the above information is true to the best of my knowledge\n\nDate:\n                                  \n                                                                                          \nPlace:\n                                                                                                                            \nVivek Kumar','Nagarro Software Pvt. Ltd.',1,NULL,'2007-10-18',NULL,'2007-10-18','2010-06-09 12:13:49','2010-06-09',3,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(176,'Thomas J',NULL,NULL,NULL,'v.thomasjoseph@gmail.com',NULL,'91 4868 264609','0','91 9947774609','0',NULL,'0','2008-04-29',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-09 12:13:49',2,'0',NULL,'200710/18/ATT24635.html','200710/18/DOC16300.doc','CURRICULAM VITAE\n\nTHOMAS J\n                                                      \nAddress for Correspondence\nValiyamattam (H),\nThopramkudy.P.O.\n                                                                   \nIdukki (Dist.), \nKerala\n\nIndia\n\nPin ? 685515\n                                                                   \nPhone: + 91 9947774609\n\n(Mobile)\n\n+ 91 4868 264609\n (Res.)\n                                                                   \nEmail:\n\nv.thomasjoseph@gmail.com\n\n\n\n\nCAREER OBJECTIVE\n\nTo continue exerting my passion for software development while learning new software engineering practices to obtain a key position in the information systems division of a major corporation or consulting firm, so as to use my skills and abilities to support the company?s mission and vision.\n\n\nPROFESSIONAL SUMMARY\n\n2+ years of experience in software industry in developing wide range of solutions using Client-Server and Web applications. Problem solving and analysis complement my abilities.\n\n\n\nTECHNICAL SKILLS\n\nLanguages\n                   \n\n        \nC#, VB, C, C++\nFront end Tools\n\n          \n\n        \nASP.Net and VB.6\nRDBMS\n                        \n\n        \nSQL Server 2000, Oracle, MS Access\n\nReporting Tools\n            \n\n        \nSeagate Crystal Reports\n\nOthers\n                        \n\n        \nXML\n\n\nPROFESSIONAL EXPERIENCE\n\n\n       \nHolsoft Systems Pvt. Ltd. \nKochi\n\nIndia\n\n    \n\nJan 2005 - Present\n\nDesignation\n: Sr. Programmer\n\n\nEDUCATION\n\n\n       \nMaster of Computer Application M.K .University, \nMadurai\n\n       \nBachelor of Computer Application M.K .University, \nMadurai\n\n\n\n\n\nPROJECTS\n\n\n1.\n\nDECISIONS plus Time And Attendance\nRole: Programmer\nEnvironment: \nASP.Net, C#, Visual Basic, SQL Server 2000, \nCrystal\n reports\n\nDescription\n\n     \nThis is an integrated online attendance processing and monitoring system based on smart card and biometric technology (fingerprint recognition based). This system has been developed as fully web-based and also desktop-based solution for managing employee?s time and attendance of one location or multiple locations in real time basis. It includes the registration, punching, verification, online batch processing and leave processing, shift scheduling and produces attendance reports, time utilization, employee status reports and department wise performance ratio reports.\n\nMy responsibilities: \n      \nInvolved in developing the application in ASP.NET and C#.Used ADO.NET extensively for data retrieving, querying, storage and manipulation. \nReport generation using crystal reports, performed testing on every new version, \ndocumentation of the application. \nInvolved in the implementation of the system, and user training.\n\n\n2.\n\nA self service portal for IPO Management \nRole: Programmer\nEnvironment: \nASP.Net, C#, SQL Server 2000\n\nDescription\n\n     \nThe is an online, multiuser system. It provides clients facility for applying for shares of the company and online customer support in share market.\n\nMy responsibilities: \n\n     \nInvolved in development of the application in ASP.NET using C#. Used ADO.NET extensively for data retrieving, querying, storage and manipulation. \nPerformed testing on every new version before sending it. \nDocumentation of the application and other details. \nInvolved in the implementation of the system and training of user representatives.\n\n\n3.\n\nDecisions Plus Car Care\nRole: Programmer\nEnvironment: \nASP.Net, C#, SQL Server 2000\n\n\n\n\nDescription\n\nThe is an On-line,Multi User System. \nThis system has been developed as fully web-based solution for updating and managing vehicle dealings information from multiple branches.\n It provides facility for create and edit sourcing details, upgradation details and sales details. The system generates stock aging \nreports, vehicle history reports, debtors reports, creditors reports, sourcing monthly reports, sales monthly reports etc.\n\n\nMy responsibilities: \n     \nInvolved in developed the application in ASP.NET and C#. Used ADO.NET extensively for data retrieving, querying, storage and manipulation. \nPerformed testing on every new version before sending it and d\nocumentation on the application.\n\n\n4.\n\nDECISIONS plus MIS\n\nRole: Programmer\nEnvironment: \nVisual Basic, SQL Server 2000, \nCrystal\n reports\n\nDescription\n\n         \nThe system keeps track of all transactions that taking place in an organization. It automates the complete process of purchase, sales and production modules. It deals with the production of floor coverings and exporting them using shipment process. Mainly consists of Purchase Order, Factory Order, Work Order and generates different kinds of reports purchase register, sales register and Pending reports that will meet requirements of all types of users.\n The system is having a very good user friendly interface.\n\n\n\nMy responsibilities: \nInvolved in Coding, \nReport Generation using crystal reports, \nDeveloped SQL stored procedures and views for data manipulation and querying data from SQL Server 2000, \nCode Reviewing, Correction of errors, \nTechnical Documentation for end users,\n Involved in the implementation of the system, Involved in user training.\n\n\nPERSONAL PROFILE\n\nDate of Birth\n                \n\n        \n9th\n\nAug 1978\nGender\n                       \n\n        \nMale\nMartial status\n              \n\n        \nSingle',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-18',NULL,'2007-10-18','2010-06-09 12:13:49','2010-06-09',2,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(177,'Sangram K',NULL,NULL,'Ghaziabad','sangreggadvdvm_indvdvdia@hotmail.com',NULL,'0120 4110517','0','9818400517','0',NULL,'0','2002-11-12',9,28,'2010-06-09 12:13:49',15,'0',NULL,'200710/18/ATT24646.html','200710/18/DOC16301.doc','SANGRAM KESHARI R\nSANGRAM KESHARI R\n1242, Adarsh Apartment, Sec-4C, Vasundhara, \nGhaziabad\n\n\nsangradvdvm_indvdvdia@hotmail.com\nMob: \n9818400517\nRes\n: 0120-4110517\n                                                                        \n                                          \n\nSUMMARY\n\n7+ years of work experience in Design, Development, Integration and Implementation of software applications using\n Microsoft Technologies i.e. DOT NET, SQL Server, Visual Basic, ASP, IIS, COM, XML etc. and other tools like Installshield, Satellite Forms, Seagate Crystal Reports. Extensive knowledge of SDLC, Database and commercial applications including conceptualization, layout designing, user interface planning with programming & managing development cycle. Key strength lies in solving complex design, understanding specification and system analysis. \nEDUCATION\nM.Sc. (IT) \nfrom KSOU, Mysore (Given final exam, awaiting result).\n2.5 Years Diploma Course \nfrom NIIT, M-5, South Extn-II, New Delhi.\nB.Com \nfrom Utkal University.\n\nTECHNICAL/ FUNCTIONAL (Application) SKILLS\nSkills\nDetails\n\nOperation System / Hardware\n\nDOS, \nWindows 95/98/NT/2000/XP/2003/SBS, Unix.\n\nLanguages\n\nVB.NET, C#, ASP. Net, VB 6.0, VC++.\n\nWeb Technology\n\nHTML, JavaScript, XML, CSS.\n\nThird Party Tools\n\nInstallshield 5.5/10.5, Satellite Forms 4.1/5.1,\n\nSeagate Crystal Reports 8.0/10, MS Visio.\n\nDatabase \n\nSQL Server 2000, MS-Access, Sybase, Oracle 7\n\nOffice Management Tools\n\nMS Word, MS Excel, MS PowerPoint, MS\n\nProject, MS Outlook.\n\nVersion Control\n\nMicrosoft VSS.\n\nQuality\n\nKnowledge of CMMI process.\n\n\nWORK EXPERIENCE\n1) \nMindmill Software Ltd, C-37, Sector-58, Noida, U.P\n                   \nMay?00 ? Till Date\n\nPROJECT SUMMARY\n\nProject# 1\nProject Name:\n\nCallScheduler (CS)\n                                               \nNov?04 - till date \nClient:\n            \nSPS (Sales Partner Systems Inc.), USA\nEnvironment:\n\nC#, SQL Server 2000/MSDE, InstallShield 10.5, Crystal Report 9. \nTeam Size:\n      \n\nProject Description:\n\nA customized CRM windows application where sales representatives can schedule daily, weekly, monthly calls for customers. A daily call scheduling facility to view a list of customers that is to be called and/or visited during a specific week. The Call Scheduler shall group customers by their order days, establish a call sequence by time of day, mark calls completed, rescheduled, or cancelled. The a\npplication manages call history; call forwarding, rescheduling, customer notes, reporting etc.\n   \nRole: Project Leader \n\nResponsibilities: \n\n       \nAnalyze client requirements and estimation\n\n       \nPlanning project implementation and performing task breakdown\n\n       \nDesigning & coding some part of the Schedule module and to support OLE method calls \n\n       \nCoordinating team activities to meet software delivery deadlines\n\n       \nSolving technical problems of team members\n\n       \nInvolved in Application Setup\n\n\nProject# 2\nProject Name:\n\nCARAVAN\n                                                  \nNov?04 - till date \nClient:\n            \nSPS (Sales Partner Systems Inc.), USA\nEnvironment:\n\nC#, SQL Server 2000, InstallShield 10.5, Crystal Report 10. \nTeam Size:\n      \n\nProject Description:\n\nCaravan consists up of three sub-applications, Caravan Control Center (CCC), Caravan Messaging System (CMS) and Caravan Document System (CDS).\n\nCaravan Control Center (CCC) \nis a web-based application to manage the distribution network of the client. This includes management of routes, drivers, trucks, trailers and tablet PCs.\n\nCaravan Messaging System (CMS) \nconsists of a Web-based and Windows-based interface to manage the various communications that have to be made to customers and other concerned people regarding the status of routes and other information by communication modes like email, fax and pager.\n\nCaravan Document System (CDS) \nis a windows-based application to generate documents required for CCC.\n   \nRole: Project Leader \n\nResponsibilities: \n\n       \nAnalyze client requirements and estimation\n\n       \nPlanning project implementation and performing task breakdown\n\n       \nCoordinating team activities to meet software delivery deadlines\n\n       \nSolving technical problems of team members\n\n       \nInvolved in Application Setup\n\n\nProject# 3\nProject Name:\n\nDATAWAREHOUSE\n                                                \nJan?07 - till date \nClient:\n            \nSPS (Sales Partner Systems Inc.), USA\nEnvironment:\n\nC#, SQL Server 2000, InstallShield 10.5 \nTeam Size:\n      \n\nProject Description:\n\nDatawarehouse is a web-based application that seeks to integrate Call Scheduler, Caravan, NetLink and other applications of the client. Currently, we are working on application/admin user creation, organization creation module, maintaining their respective hierarchies. Datawarehouse creates logins for the different application databases and assigns appropriate database roles to the users created.\n   \nRole: Project Leader \n\nResponsibilities: \n\n       \nAnalyze client requirements and estimation\n\n       \nPlanning project implementation and performing task breakdown\n\n       \nCoordinating team activities to meet software delivery deadlines\n\n       \nSolving technical problems of team members\n\n       \nInvolved in Application Setup\n\n\nProject# 4\nProject Name:\n\nShip Traders Enquiry Processing System\n (STEPS)\n    \nMar?06 ? Sep?06 \nClient:\n            \nGI GROUP, UK\nEnvironment:\n\nC#, SQL Server 2000/MSDE, InstallShield 10.5, Crystal Report 9. \nTeam Size:\n      \n\nProject Description:\n\nThis is a web based application manages the shipments for the customer. User can receive the customer enquiry, customer order, customer payment, supplier enquiry, and supplier quotations and prepares the order placed to supplier, collection advice, dispatch advice, customer invoice, and dispatch details for customer and delivery to forwarder. It also helps to get reports for item/part information, customer?s pending enquiry/quotation, and delivery due, order performance, order status, payment due and daily stock and sales analysis information.\n\nRole: Project Leader \n\nResponsibilities: \n\n       \nStudy the old FoxPro based application and estimation\n\n       \nDesigning architecture and database \n\n       \nPlanning project implementation and performing task breakdown\n\n       \nCoordinating team activities to meet software delivery deadlines\n\n       \nSolving technical problems of team members\n\n       \nInvolved in Application Setup\n\n\nProject# 5\nProject Name:\n\nICPS\n                                                                   \nSep?04 ? Feb?06 \nClient:\n            \nTraffic Support Ltd (TSL), UK\nEnvironment:\n\nVB.NET, ASP.NET, VB.NET Compact Framework, VB6.0, SOAP, SQL Server 2000 \nTeam Size:\n      \n\nProject Description:\n\nICPS consist of small different projects, which consist web applications, windows applications, SOAP, Web Services and handheld applications.\n\n1.\n     \naMember\nThis is an ASP.Net application that allows the ?public? to self-register their name, address and credit card details and then to purchase \"licenses\" to enter a city.\n\n2.\n     \nHire & Lease\nThis is an ASP.Net application that allows hire and lease companies to register with the local council as users of the web site, and the web site allows them to key in the name and address of the driver and the hire agreement reference and then update the councils system directly. The councils system will then create the replacement notice automatically.\n\n3.\n     \nExemption\nThis is an ASP.Net application that allows individuals who believe they should be exempt from licenses to apply for an exemption via a web page.\n\n4.\n     \nFleet License Management\nThis is an ASP.Net application that\nallows vehicle fleet owners to make a request for a fleet license and to view details of their license charges and to modify their vehicle fleet details.\n\n5.\n     \nHandheld Tickets Application\nIt is a smart Device application developed for the usage of Parking Attendants who carry the application on devices with them to perform various activities like issuing a PCN, observing vehicles, recording a location, Fault reporting etc.\n\n6.\n     \nDBSync Application \nIt is a smart Device application developed to synchronize the data between the device used by parking attendants and server data. At the end of the day when the attendants submit their devices, the DBsync application is executed that reads the data from the device and synchronize the server data and the device data.\n\n7.\n     \nDevice Engineering\nIt \nis a smart device Program that is run on Embedded Devices that support WinCE. It is the program that maintains an inventory of street assets that are located on a street within a council?s borough. The program also maintains, directs and records the maintenance effort for those assets. Each asset will have its own set of attributes and may have parts and sub-parts associated with it. \n\n8.\n     \nSuspension HHT\nThe SuspensionHHT is a smart device based reporting program. The application downloads the data using queries from the ICPS database, saves the data in XML documents and then uses those XML documents as data-source. \n\nRole: Project Leader \n\nResponsibilities: \n\n       \nAnalyze client requirements and estimation\n\n       \nPlanning project implementation and performing task breakdown\n\n       \nCoordinating team activities to meet software delivery deadlines\n\n       \nSolving technical problems of team members\n\n\nProject# 6\nProject Name:\n\nProspector\n                                                 \nJun?04 ? Sep?04 \nClient:\n            \nSafety Media Ltd, UK\nEnvironment:\n\nVB 6.0, MS Access, InstallShield 5.5, Crystal Report 8.5. \nTeam Size:\n      \n\nProject Description:\n\nThis is a window-based application, is used by sales representatives of Safety Media Ltd. for managing clients contact details and for forecasting potential sales. The application runs in two modes, for sales representatives and for administrators. The program is the same for both types of users but with additional options available to the administrator. The user has the ability to export their sales information. There is a facility to FTP the data from the sales representatives to the main head office is also be available. \nThere are also various reports in the application.\n\nRole: Project Leader \n\nResponsibilities: \n\n       \nAnalyze client requirements and estimation\n\n       \nDesigning architecture and database \n\n       \nPlanning project implementation and performing task breakdown\n\n       \nInvolved in Application Setup\n\n\nProject# 7\nProject Name:\n\nAsset Controller\n                                          \nOct?03 ? Dec?03 \nClient:\n            \nSafety Media Ltd, UK\nEnvironment:\n\nVB 6.0, MS Access, InstallShield 5.5, Crystal Report 8.5. \nTeam Size:\n      \n\nProject Description:\n\nThis is a window-based application, which helps to maintain assets in an organization. Users can create/edit asset details. \nThe Asset History will maintain all of the actions the Asset has experienced. There are other master forms through which user can enter master details to create an asset. There are also various reports in the application.\n\nRole: Project Leader \n\nResponsibilities: \n\n       \nAnalyze client requirements and estimation\n\n       \nDesigning architecture and database \n\n       \nPlanning project implementation and performing task breakdown\n\n       \nInvolved in Application Setup\n\n\nProject# 8\nProject Name:\n\nVisitor Controller\n                                        \nApr?03 ? Jul?03 \nClient:\n            \nSafety Media Ltd, UK\nEnvironment:\n\nVB 6.0, MS Access, InstallShield 5.5, Crystal Report 8.5. \nTeam Size:\n      \n\nProject Description:\n\nThis is a window-based application, which allows a receptionist to log visitors in and out of a building and to print badges for them. It uses a webcam to capture an image of a person to be printed on their badge. It displays the output from the camera to the user of the software, then allow them to take a \"snapshot\" and add it to the badge to be printed. There are other features like design the badge, reports, etc.\n\nRole: Project Leader \n\nResponsibilities: \n\n       \nAnalyze client requirements and estimation\n\n       \nDesigning architecture and database \n\n       \nPlanning project implementation and performing task breakdown\n\n       \nInvolved in Application Setup\n\n\nProject# 9\nProject Name:\n\neTS?\n                                                                  \nNov?02 ? Sep?04 \nClient:\n            \nGrantlun Corporation, USA\nEnvironment:\n\nVB 6.0, Satellite Forms 5.1, MS Access, InstallShield 5.5, Crystal Report 8.5. \nTeam Size:\n      \n\nProject Description:\n\neTS? is an electronic time sheet system that runs on any PDA using the Palm operating system. It serves as a friendly and powerful data collection tool that enables field personnel to accurately report labor employment, equipment employment, and work progress. The Product has two parts PC side and Palm Side.\n\neTS? File Manager (PC Side)\n\nStores Company data and enables creation of data subsets by Job and by Time Keeper so Time Keepers are not burdened with data they do not need. Transmits Time Keeper datasets three ways: email, synchronization, memory stick. Imports/exports ALL data in text or XML format. \n\neTS? Time Keeper (Palm Side):\n\nStores specific Job data: employees, machines, crews, activities, accounts, tags and special code data so time sheet data input is fast and accurate.\n\nRole: Project Leader \n\nResponsibilities: \n\n       \nAnalyze client requirements and estimation\n\n       \nDesigning architecture and database \n\n       \nPlanning project implementation and performing task breakdown\n\n       \nCoding for Palm device application and Synchronization process between Palm and PC \n\n       \nPC and Palm Application Setup\n\n\nProject# 10\nProject Name:\n\nTIME\nTM\n                                                      \nApr?02 ? Nov?02 \nClient:\n            \nHard Dollar, USA\nEnvironment:\n\nSatellite Forms 5.1, VB 6.0, and InstallShield 5.5 \nTeam Size:\n      \n\nProject Description:\n\nTIME is a PDA based application that serves as an electronic ?time sheet?. TIME application is used by foremen to record actual labor, equipment, resource employment hours, work progress quantities, and to take notes. TIME transmits that data electronically to PXS application. \n\nRole: Developer \n\nResponsibilities: \n\n       \nCoding for Palm device application\n\n       \nPalm Application Setup\n\n       \nCoding for Synchronization process between Palm and PC \n\n\nProject# 11\nProject Name:\n\nInspection Manager Palm \n                                     \nNov?01 ? Mar?02 \nClient:\n            \nTISCOR, USA\nEnvironment:\n\nSatellite Forms 4.1, InstallShield 5.5 \nTeam Size:\n      \n\nProject Description:\n\nInspection Manager is designed for those who conduct inspection tours of facilities and critical equipment. Safety inspections, hazardous material inspections, and quality control audits are just a few areas where Inspection Manager can make your facility run smoothly and efficiently. With Inspection Manager, your inspector records information by scanning bar code labels and keying information directly into a palm. The device prompts your technician for information about the equipment or the process of operations in your facility. The PC software maintains data on technician, inspection checkpoints, equipment history and question and keeps a history of all entries made through the device. Using the PC generates work-order and management reports.\n\nRole: Developer \n\nResponsibilities: \n\n       \nCoding for Palm device application\n\n       \nPalm Application Setup\n\n       \nCoding for Synchronization process between Palm and PC \n\n\nProject# 12\nProject Name:\n\nFacility Manager\n\n                                     \nApr?01 ? Nov?01 \nClient:\n            \nTISCOR, USA\nEnvironment:\n\nVB 6.0, Satellite Forms 4.1, CrystalReports 8.5, InstallShield 5.5, Oracle, SQL, Access\n\nTeam Size:\n      \n\nProject Description:\n\nFacilityManager is a paperless computerized maintenance management system (CMMS) software application that controls maintenance management operations. FacilityManager schedules routine inspections; schedules detailed work orders for preventive maintenance tasks, and performs unscheduled maintenance in the field. Using software, hand-held computers, and bar codes, the system are used to plan, schedule and track maintenance management activities, including resources, materials, labor hours and cost. FacilityManager provides enterprise back-end connectivity to MS Access, SQL, and Oracle databases.\n   \nThe Project involves around 20 Master and Transaction forms, 25 Reports, Wizards etc.\n\nRole: Developer \n\nResponsibilities: \n\n       \nCoding for Synchronization process between Palm and PC \n\n       \nWorked on master forms like Inspector, Location, etc.\n\n       \nWorked on various reports\n\n\nProject# 13\nProject Name:\n\nTour Watch\n         \n                                               \nAug?00 ? Mar?01 \nClient:\n            \nTISCOR, USA\nEnvironment:\n\nVB 6.0, Crystal\n Reports 8.5,\n\nInstallShield 5.5, Oracle, SQL, Access\n\nTeam Size:\n      \n\nProject Description:\n\nTourWatch is a computerized guard-tour management system that records tours and inspections performed by security officers. Officers use portable data collection devices to document all security checkpoints visited. Simply scanning a bar code label or touching a metal tag records the date, time, and location of each checkpoint. TourWatch provides a variety of reports showing where your officers were, when, their observations, and the actions taken. Available reports include: Route Report, Summary Route Report, Exception Report and Missed-Checkpoint Report. TourWatch works with a variety of hand-held devices like \nDENSO BHT-8000, \nProTouch, ProScan DR, Dolphin, PDT 6100 and PDT6800, giving customers the option of selecting a device that meets their needs and budgets.\n\nRole: Developer \n\nResponsibilities: \n\n       \nWorked on various master forms\n\n       \nImport and export data module\n\n       \nVarious Reports\n\n\nProject# 14\nProject Name:\n\nChargeBackSysystem\n                                   \nMay?00 ? Sep?00 \nClient:\n            \nMckinsey, India\nEnvironment:\n\nVB 6.0, \nCrystal Reports, \nInstallShield\n 5.5, SQL Server6.5 \nTeam Size:\n      \n\nProject Description:\n\nIt?s a windows based application to maintain the uses of various resources in 3 different way, i.e. a) Per Login, b) Duration and c) Per Article for different users. It provides reports to analyze the uses of resources per user.\n\nRole: Developer \n\nResponsibilities: \n\n       \nRequirements gathering & Design Database\n\n       \nWorked on all forms\n\n       \nVarious Reports\n\n\n\nPERSONAL DETAILS\n\nDate of Birth\n          \n           \n\n        \n12\nth\n May 1974.\nMailing Address\n   \n        \n\n     \n1242, Adarsh Apartment,\n                                      \nSector ? 4C, Vasundhra,\n                            \n       \n             \nGhaziabad, U.P. \nMarital Status\n             \n\n      \nMarried.\nPassport Number\n      \n          \n\n        \nA6262472.\nPAN \n                         \n\n      \nAGRPR0527Q\n\nLanguages Known\n      \n\n      \nEnglish, Hindi and Oriya.\n\n\n\nPERSONAL TRAITS\n\nPatient Listener, Responsible, Ability to handle different tasks simultaneously, Ability to adapt fast to dynamic situations\n\n\n\n\n\nDATE:\n                                                                    \nSANGRAM KESHARI ROUT','Mindmill Software Ltd',1,NULL,'2007-10-18',NULL,'2007-10-18','2010-06-09 12:13:49','2010-06-09',15,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(179,'Selvaraju N',NULL,NULL,NULL,'sesdvdsvlvandfv.it@gmail.com','selvan.it@gmail.com','91 80 66267000','0','91 9986004511','0',NULL,'0','2007-10-29',8,24,'2010-06-09 12:13:49',2,'0',NULL,'200710/18/ATT24631.html','200710/18/DOC16303.doc','Resdex @ naukri.com\nSelvaraju N\n#111/1, Flat#10, #3rd Floor, Opp Govt School Taverekere, B.T.M I Stage Bengalaru / Bangalore - 560029 \nsesdvdsvlvandfv.it@gmail.com\n\nTelephone: 9986004511\n(M)\n 91 80 66267000\n(R)\n\nD.O.B\n - 15 May 1983 \nModified on\n - 26 Sep 2007 \nAnnual Salary\n - INR 2 Lac(s) 40 Thousand \nTotal Years of Experience\n - 2 Year(s) 6 Month(s) \nCurrent Location\n - Bangalore \nPreferred Location\n - Anywhere in South India, Bangalore, Chennai \nC#, ASP.NET Developer with 2.5 Years Experience in Banking/Finance and Insurance Domains\n\nTEXT RESUME \n\nObjective\n\n?¼ To associate with an organization which gives me a chance to update my knowledge and enhance my skills where I can use my experience towards the goals of the organization.\nProfessional Summary\n\n?¼ 2.5 Years of Experience in Dot Net Technologies (C#, ASP.NET), Involved in the Development of Client / Server Application and Web Based Application.\n\n?¼ Exposure to SQL Server 2000.\n\n?¼ Understanding of UML and SDLC.\n\n?¼ Knowledge and\n Experience in Banking/Finance and Insurance Domains.\n\n?¼ Knowledge in Unit Testing and Functional Testing.\n\n?¼ Proven Problem Solving and Analytical Skills.\n\n?¼ Committed to learning new technologies.\nWork Experience\n\n?¼ Presently working as a Software E\nngineer in HCL Technologies, Bangalore.\nQualification\n\n?¼ B.Tech (Electronics\n & Communication Engineering) from National Institute of Technology (NIT, Formerly REC) Tiruchirappalli, Tamilnadu - 620015\nSkill Sets\n\n?¼ .NET Technologies :C#, ASP.NET, ADO.NE\nT, VB.NET\n\n?¼ RDBMS :SQL Server 2000\n\n?¼ Web Software :Java Script, HTML, IIS\n\n?¼ Operating System :Windows XP/98/2000\n\n?¼ Tools :NUnit Testing, VSS, Sourcegear, eManager\nAchievements\n\n?¼ Received Best Performer Award from the previous employer.\n\n?¼ Secur\ned District First in TNPCEE (Engineering Entrance Exam) - 2001 for 95.24%.\n\n?¼ Received Best Outgoing Student Award and School Topper in higher secondary.\n\n?¼ Won Gold in KABADI-2005, an intra college sports meet and College Team Captain.\nProject Details:\nTitle:- Banking/Finance- Scheduling of MortgageIT Business (Calendar Service)\nTechnology : C#, ASP.NET.\nRDBMS : SQL Server 2000.\nPlatform : Windows XP SP2.\nRole : Developer.\nDuration : 5 Months.\nTeam Size : 5.\nClient : Deutsche Bank - Mortgage IT, US.\nDescription:\nCalendar Service web application allows branches under MortgageIT to control their hours of operation for different automated services provided online like locking of loans, pricing of loans and underwriting. It includes the following modules: Daily Operations, Exceptional Day, Initiation/Termination, Day/Week/Month View and Transaction History. Daily Operation sets default operation hours for services and Exceptional Day sets the exception for services.\nRoles and Responsibilities:\n\n?¼ Involved\n in requirement gathering and analysis through con-call from onsite.\n\n?¼ Understanding of Functional Requirements from SRS.\n\n?¼ Involved in Peer Code Review and Development.\n\n?¼ Created Classes and Objects to write the Business Logic in a separate Assembly\n to Isolate Business from User Interface.\n\n?¼ Worked extensively with DataSet and other web controls.\nTitle:- Banking/Finance: Recurring Deposit (RD)\nTechnology : C#, ASP.NET.\nRDBMS : SQL Server 2000.\nPlatform : Windows 2000.\nRole : Developer.\nDuration : Sep-06 to Feb-07.\nTeam Size : 14.\nDescription:\nIBS-RD web application automates the process of managing the Term Deposit Process. It includes Application System, Deposit Processing System, Payment System and Closure System. The Deposit Processing System Module calculates interest over the period for whatever the payment made towards the RD account based on the type of RD selected by the customer and generates the deposit receipts for the customer.\nRoles and Responsibilities:\n\n?¼ Involved in analysis and \ndevelopment.\n\n?¼ Involved in Peer Code Review.\n\n?¼ Understanding of Functional Requirements from SRS.\n\n?¼ Created Classes and Objects to write the Business Logic in a separate Assembly to Isolate Business from User Interface.\n\n?¼ Worked extensively with Da\ntaGrid and other web controls.\nTitle:- Centralized Insurance: Overseas Medi-Claim (OMPI)\nTechnology : C#, ASP.NET.\nRDBMS : SQL Server 2000.\nPlatform : Windows 2000.\nRole : Developer.\nDuration : Feb to Aug-06.\nTeam Size : 14.\nDescription:\nOverseas Medi-Claim Policy Insurance (OMPI) subsystem deals with the expenses with respect to the Hospitalization/Domiciliary Hospitalization of the insured in situation like sudden illness, accident, or surgery that is required in respect of any disease that has arisen during the policy period along with the situation like loss of checked baggage, baggage delay on outbound flights or loss of passport etc. This application handles the claim for the Person Going Abroad. OMPI core modules are Policy Processing System, Premium System, Claim System and Closure System. Claim System captures the details of claim entry, claim generated, claim document, claim verification, claim settlement and claim settlement report.\nRoles and Responsibilities:\n\n?¼ Understanding of functional re\nquirements from SRS.\n\n?¼ Involved in analysis and development.\n\n?¼ Involved in Peer code review and Unit Testing.\n\n?¼ Worked extensively with DataGrid and other web controls\nTitle:- Miscellaneous Insurance (MI)\nTechnology : C#, ASP.NET.\nRDBMS : SQL Server 2000.\nPlatform : Windows 2000.\nRole : Developer.\nDuration : Aug-05 to Jan-06.\nTeam Size : 14.\nDescription:\nMiscellaneous Insurance (MI) encompasses a large variety of crime coverage forms available to protect against losses of money, securities, or property by such causes of loss as: employee dishonesty, forgery, theft, burglary, robbery, kidnap, fraud, and extortion. Product Administration is a module of MI which is used to list, update, edit or delete the products available under MI. It?s one of the important modules of MI since all the calculations are based on the products available at the particular time.\nRoles and Responsibilities:\n\n?¼ Understanding of functional requirements from SRS.\n\n?¼ Involved in project discussion and development.\n\n?¼ Involve\nd in Peer code review and Unit Testing.\n\n?¼ Design and development of C#/Web Forms.\nAcademic Project\nTitle : Embedded System Control Applications through Hard Wired TCP/IP & 8031 Micro Controller.\nDuration : Jan to May-05.\nRole : Micro Controller Programming & Interfacing, Without Using OS.\nDescription : Stand Alone System providing user with Ready Internet Connectivity, easy low cost solution for High Speed internet connectivity and Automated Control through internet where man cannot reach.\nContact Details\nCommunication Address:\n#111/1, Flat#10, 3rd Floor,\nOpposite to Govt School,\nThavarekere Bus Stand,\nBTM 1st Stage,\nBangalore - 560 029.\neMail : selvan.it@gmail.com\nMobile : +91 9986004511',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-18',NULL,'2007-10-18','2010-06-09 12:13:49','2010-06-09',2,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(180,'Sapna G',NULL,NULL,NULL,'sapndsvsdagodvdsvsdvwami2006@gmail.com',NULL,'0121 2767471','0','9818529742','0','09897302618','0','2007-12-29',8,NULL,'2010-06-09 12:13:49',3,'1','2010-06-21','200710/18/ATT19250.html','200710/18/DOC16304.doc','CURRICULUM VITAE\nCURRICULUM VITAE\n\n\nSapna G\nE-mail:\n\nsapndsvsdagodvdsvsdvwami2006@gmail.com\nContact: 9818529742, 09897302618\n                                                                                                \nObjective\nTo establish myself as a successful person with excellence in terms of teamwork, creativity and dedication.\n\nSo as to join an organization that provides opportunities to do task in healthy and challenging environment and to learn, grow and improve the scope for implementing my skills thereby contributing to the growth of organization\n\nExperience Summery\n\nCurrent Employer : Magic Solv Pvt. Ltd.\nDesignation: \nSoftware Developer\nExperience Summery\n\n        \nI have \nTotal\n\n2.3 years\n of experience in the\n\nfield of Information Technology as a Software Programmer\n\nwith emphasis on complete Application Life Cycle Development of Object-Oriented methodologies.\n\n        \nApprox 2 Years\n of Software Development Experience of working with \ndesign & development client-server application using \nASP.NET, C#, java script, HTML and SQL Server.\n\n        \nAround 6 months of exposure in VB.Net, Oracle and ASP in Ministry of information Technology, \nNew Delhi\n\nTechnical Skills\n\n\nLANGUAGES\nC#,\n C,C++\nDBMS\nSql Server\n. ORACLE 8i, MS-Access\nWEB TECHNOLOGIES\nASP.NET\n, HTML, JavaScript, VBScript.\nOPERATING SYSTEMS\nWindows 95/98/2000/XP, Windows NT, Linux\n\n\n\n\n\n\nProfessional Experience\n\n        \n1.\n\nOrganization\n       \n        \nMagic Solv Pvt. Ltd. \nProjects Name\n       \n      \nCall Management System\n\nDetails\n                          \nThis Project handles the call management of the center of KentRo Water purifier, How a person contact to the call center for any problem in the water purifier, and then call center search his/her details and send for further processing. \n\nTeam Size\n                 \n   \n\nLanguage\n      \n                \nASP.Net , C#, Java Script, SQL Server.\n\n           \nRole\n                             \nworked as a Team Member involved in developing the project and Database designing as per the requirement\n\n\n\nOrganization\n        \n       \nMagic Solv Pvt. Ltd.\n      \nProject Name\n      \n         \nHotel Information System\n      \n      \nDetails\n                \n          \nIt?s a Website of a Hotel, Which contain the information about the rooms available, rent of these rooms based on the type of rooms, food facilities and other necessary information.\n            \n      \nLanguage\n           \n           \nASP.NET With C#, SQL Server\n      \nRole\n                    \n         \nworked as a Team Member involved in developing the project and Database designing as per the requirement\n\n       \n\n3.\n\nOrganization\n               \nMagic Solv Pvt. Ltd.\n           \nProjects\n                \n       \nStudent Cell.\nDetails\n                  \n        \nThis is the application running on Intranet prepared by keeping in mind to provide students the facility to get information about the faculty, their batch timings, their registration information etc. Application has different forms to be used by Administrator and for the end users. It contains one form having all information about the different courses provided by the institute. Same way the application provides the functionality to the faculty also like their lecture timings, batch of the day and their skill set. \n\n      \nTeam Size\n            \n        \n\nLanguage\n              \n        \nASP.NET With C#, SQL Server\n\n      \n\n\n   \nOrganization\n               \nMagic Solv Pvt. Ltd.\n\n            \nProjects\n           \n    \n\n       \nHR Management System.\nDetails\n                  \n        \nHR Management System is a Tool designed to perform different activities like creation and modification of employee record, Appraisal, Resignation, Termination change status & designation, view reports. Its objective is to provide such an interface for HR department so that they can manage their employee details at a glance\n\n      \nTeam Size\n            \n        \n\nLanguage\n              \n        \nASP.NET With C#, SQL Server\n\n\n\n\n\n\n      \n5.\n   \nOrganization\n   \n            \nMinistry of Information Technology, \nNew Delhi\n\n            \nProjects\n           \n    \n\n       \nOffice Automation & mail System \nDetails\n                  \n        \nIt is a mailing application having function of sending, receiving, forwarding, it also have an address book and opens \n\n        \nOutlook express or Microsoft Outlook automatically. \n      \nTeam Size\n                   \n\n                                                           \n\nLanguage\n              \n        \nVB.Net ,C#,Oracle\n\n            \n       \n\nProfessional/Academic Qualification.\n\n         \nMCA. From \nU.P\n\nTech\nUniversity\n Luknow \n\n2001-2004.\n\n         \nBachelor of Science(PCM), \nMeerut\nCollege\n\nMeerut\n\n\n         \nIntermediate , U.P Board-1998.\n\n         \nHigh School, U.P Boared-1996.\n\n\n\nPersonal Details\n\nName\n    \n           \n       \n     \nSAPNA GOSWAMI\nGender\n             \n       \n     \nFemale\nDate of Birth\n     \n       \n     \n2 July 1981\n        \nFather?s Name\n       \n  \n     \nSri Brahma Nand Goswami\nCurrent Address\n            \nE-103, Amar Colony, Lajpat Nagar, \nNew Delhi\n\nPermanent Address\n       \nHno.1396 sec-3 Shastri Nagar \nMeerut\nPhone\n               \n        \n    \n0121-2767471\nNationality\n               \n     \nIndian\n\nDeclaration\n\nI hereby declare that the foregoing information is true, correct and complete to my Knowledge and belief.\n\nDate:\nPlace:\n                                                                                      \nSignature: \n(Sapna Goswami)\n\n\n\n\n\n                             ',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-18',NULL,'2007-10-18','2010-06-09 12:13:49','2010-06-09',3,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(181,'Vinod K',NULL,NULL,NULL,'vingfgnodk.yadgngnav@yahoo.com',NULL,'011 25055385','0','91 9871581360','0',NULL,'0','2008-09-27',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-09 12:13:49',3,'0',NULL,'200710/18/ATT19248.html','200710/18/DOC16305.doc','CURRICULUM VITAE\nVINOD K\n                                                                                      \nMobile\n\n          \n\n\n+91-9871581360\nEmail Id\n   \n\n\nvingfgnodk.yadgngnav@yahoo.com\n                         \nPermanent #\n\n\n       \n011?25055385\nOBJECTIVE\nA position as a \nSoftware Engineer\n where I can use my potential to achieve organizational goals through persistent development of vocational and analytical skills.\nWORK EXPERIENCE\nCompany\nRole\nDuration\nSysmatic InfoTech P Ltd., \nNew\n\nDelhi\n\nSoftware Engineer\nJuly 2005 to Till date\nNCNL Infomedia Pvt. Ltd., \nNew\n\nDelhi\n\nJunior Software Engineer\nJan. 2005 to June 2005\nCAREER PROFILE\nMCA \nwith more than \n1.5 yrs\n experience in Software Development on \nWeb ? Based Application\n and \nClient ? Server Solutions\n\nMore than \none ? year \nof experience on \nASP.NET \nwith\n C#\n\nEight ? months on \nClient ? Server \nDevelopment on \nMicrosoft Technology\n\nOne and a half year on \nSQL Server/Oracle \nin backend.\nCOMPUTER SKILLS\nDatabases\n                             \nMicrosoft SQL Server 2000, Oracle 9i.\nLanguages\n                            \nC#, C++, C, VB.NET, T-SQL.\nInternet Technology\n           \nASP.NET, D/HTML, XML, JavaScript.\nReporting\n                               \nCrystal Report.\nWeb Server\n                           \nIIS 5.0.\nPROJECT DETAILS\nProject Name\n      \nGlobal Sourcing - MIT\nPlatform\n               \nVisual Studio .NET 2003, ASP.NET, C#, COM+, SQL Server 2000, IIS 5.0.\nDuration\n               \nAugust 2006 to till date.\nDescription\n          \nGlobal Sourcing-MIT (Margin Improvement Tool) is an Internet business solution to automate the process of procurement of goods & services. It also tracks the milestones of the project. This Internet business solution generates matrices on the performance of projects.\nProject Name\n      \nHR Management Solution\nPlatform\n               \nVisual Studio .NET 2003, ASP.NET, C#, JavaScript, Oracle 9i, IIS 5.0.\nDuration\n               \nFeb. 2006 to July 2006.\nDescription\n          \nHR Management Solution is a Web based comprehensive Application Software that covers Back-Office operations of an organization. The complete Human Resource Management functions, including Payroll Processing & placement process of an organization are handled by this application. The core product can be customized for various organizations for their specific needs.\nProject Name\n      \nMaterial Requirement Planning\nPlatform\n               \nVisual Studio .NET 2003, ASP.NET, C#, SQL Server 2000, Crystal Report, IIS 5.0.\nDuration\n               \nSep. 2005 to Jan. 2006.\nDescription\n          \nThis is a web-Tier application working for Intranet. The client was facing problems with the supply of material required for production due to lack of sufficient information of the inventory and the orders to be fulfilled. The application was designed to capture the current inventory of the materials, track the purchase orders in pipeline and provide information for planning the requirement for material. The system was made intelligent to break up a purchase order in terms of different spares required to fulfill the order.\nProject Name\n      \nEngineering Management System\nPlatform\n               \nDeveloper 2000 & Oracle 9i.\nDuration\n               \nJuly 2005 to Aug. 2005.\nDescription\n          \nEngineering Management System is a tool to cater to the day-to-day requirements of the engineering.\n\nThe basic day to day of engineering activities involve monitoring the following:\n\n         \nFlow of documents\n\n         \nEngineering Activities\nEMS\n enables to capture and monitor the above processes of engineering. The main aim of the system is to provide and store reliable data that is consistent throughout. The system also aims at generating timely and reliable MIS reports.\nProject Name\n      \nMIS - Electricity Distribution\nPlatform\n               \nVisual Studio .NET 2003, VB.NET, SQL Server 2000, Microsoft Excel, Crystal Report.\nDuration\n               \nJan. 2005 to June 2005.\nDescription\n          \nThe application is a complete automation of electricity distribution activity and mass meter replacement activity. It is designed to keep information about Contractors & their Employee, and also storing Information about meter change with their digital image for record and which contractor?s employee changed that meter, and captures the current inventory of the materials, track the inventory status in pipeline and provide information for planning the requirement for material. \nEDUCATION\nQualification\nBoard\nDuration\nMCA\nMaharshi\nDayanand\nUniversity\n, Rohtak.\n2002 ? 2005\nBCA\nChoudhary\nCharan\nSingh\nUniversity\n\nMeerut\n\n1999 ? 2002\nIntermediate\nCentral Board of Secondary Education, \nDelhi\n\n1997 ? 1998\nMetric\nCentral Board of Secondary Education, \nDelhi\n\n1995 ? 1996\nPERSONAL INFORMATION\nDate & Place of Birth\nAugust 15\nth\n, 1980\n. (\nDelhi\n).\nFather\'s Name\nMr. Kanwar Pal Yadav.\nPassport\nAvailable, valid till 2015.\nGender\nMale.\nLanguage\nEnglish & Hindi.\nPermanent Address\nRzf - 188, Street No. 31c, Sadh Nagar - II, \nPalam Colony, \nNew Delhi\n - 110045.\nDate\n\n\n\n?????\nPlace\n\n\n\nNew Delhi\n\n                                                                                \n(Vinod Kumar)',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-18',NULL,'2007-10-18','2010-06-09 12:13:49','2010-06-09',3,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(182,'S Fatima',NULL,NULL,NULL,'fatidvdvma.sdvdvadaf@gmail.com','sf_vsadvdvfy@yahoo.co.in',NULL,'0','91 9899469904','0',NULL,'0','2007-09-28',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-09 12:13:49',3,'0',NULL,'200710/18/ATT19246.html','200710/18/DOC16306.doc','BARKHA GUPTA\nS Fatima\n                                                                                   \n                     \n            \nDeveloper Consultant,\n                                                                                                \nMobile\n\n\n+91-9899469904\nVisnova Solutions Pvt. Ltd.,\nNoida\n                \n                                                \n            \n      \n                           \n  \n       \n\nE-mail:\n\nfatidvdvma.sdvdvadaf@gmail.com\n                                                                                                            \n   \n         \n    \nsf_vsadvdvfy@yahoo.co.in\n       \n                                                                                                                                      \n\nCareer Objective\n\nAspire to be associated with an organisation wherein I can apply my knowledge and skills in developing business applications and thereby contribute towards the growth of the organization in lieu with ?Self Development? with ?Self Control?; under supremacy of ?Ethics?.\n\nProfessional Summary\n\nHaving more than \n2.6 Years of \nexperience of working project involving \nMicrosoft Dot Net Technologies.\nCurrently working as a \nDeveloper Consultant\n with \nVisnova Solutions Pvt. Ltd\n\nNoida \nsince September 2006\n\nWorked as a \nSoftware Engineer\n with \nPlasma Softech Pvt. Ltd\n\nNoida, \nfrom March 2005 to September 2006\n\n\nCompany Profile\n\nCompany Name\n          \n: Visnova Solutions Pvt. Ltd\n                    \n\nWorking as a team member and involved in software development of\n ERP Implementation\n\nExecution of projects from design to implementation stage.\n\n\nTechnical Skills\n\nProgramming Languages\n           \n     \n: ASP.Net, ADO.Net, C#\nDatabases\n                                       \n: SQL Server 2000.\nServer\n                                             \n\n: IIS \nTool\n                                               \n  \n\n: SAP business one tool\nRecent Projects\n\nProject Name\n               \n\nAnand group ERP\n    \n        \nClient\n                           \n: Anand group, \nIndia\n\n    \n        \nTeam Size\n                   \n: 10\n       \n     \n\nTechnology Used\n        \n: C#, SQL Server 2000, XML\n\n            \n\nDescription\n       \n     \n    \n: The Company is a manufacturer of spare part of automobile engine assembly. The project is aimed at facilitating the production department to do better planning by providing information on line. The system is divided in various modules stated as Administration, Purchase, Inventory, Sales, Buisness partner, Production, Banking, Human Resources, and Reports. Each module is further categorized in sub-modules.\n\n          \n\n\n\nProject Name\n               \n\nPhotoG\n    \n        \nClient\n                           \n\nNational Access Group, \nUSA\n\n    \n        \nTeam Size\n                   \n: 5\n            \nTechnology Used\n         \n: C#, ASP.NET, SQL Server 2000\n            \n            \nDescription\n                    \n\n             \n\n\nThe PhotoG website allows the registered freelancers to login in and then search for active projects (related to their specialization) using geographic region as one of the search criteria. They can then competitively bid on the project through an open bid process. The projects are time sensitive and require the freelancer to complete the project before the due date. The registered user can also go in and check all the projects, which are assigned to them and not completed yet as well as all the projects, which have been previously completed by them. They can also check all the projects, which are being actively bid by them.\n\n\nProject Name\n               \n\nCustomer Support System\n    \n        \nClient\n                           \n: Allcom Inc. \nUSA\n\n    \n        \nTeam Size\n                   \n: 6\n            \nTechnology Used\n         \n: C#, ASP.NET,SQL Server 2000.\n             \n                   \n            \nDescription\n                    \n\n             \n\n            \nThis is a Customer Support System developed for Allcom (USA).This system has three modules: Trouble ticketing, RMA and Download center. This System is for the user of a telecom company, The users of this systems are the client of Allcom and Vendors providing the products to Allcom. Trouble Ticket is for submitting the problems related to the operating products. RMA is for the returning the product to the company and download center is providing the facility to download the useful stuff for the client of company.\n\n         \n\nProject name \n           \n\nKingdom Flooring\n             \nClient\n              \n           \n: Kingdom \nFlooring\n\nUSA\n\n            \nTeam Size\n      \n         \n: 3\n            \nTechnology Used\n      \n: C#, ASP.NET, SQL Server 2000,\n            \n             \nDescription\n                \n\n\nKingdom Flooring.com is a complete e-Commerce solution that includes the Shopping cart system, Online Credit card processing powered by Authoize.net Shipping Solution with UPS Online, along with the dynamic content manager o incorporate the changes in the website dynamically.\n\nThe project has following modules - Main Website, Clearance Items, Dynamic Content Manager, Reporting, Shipping and Online Credit Card processing.\n            \n                    \n     \nProject Name\n   \n            \n\nPushpanjali Construction\n           \n  \nClient\n              \n            \n: Pushpanjali Construction\nTeam Size\n                 \n\n: 6\n             \nTechnology Used\n         \n: C#, ASP.NET, JavaScript, SQL Server 2000, \n            \n                                                     \n\nDescription\n               \n\n   \n\n\nProject is made for office automation of a construction company. It is a small erp system. The project has following modules ? Admin, CRM, Sales, Purchase, payroll, Customer Registration and Reporting.\n            \n\n\n\n\nProject Name\n   \n            \n\nDynamic Content Manager\n    \nClient\n               \n            \n: Plasma Computing\nTeam Size\n                 \n\n: 2\n            \nTechnology Used\n        \n\n\n: C#, Web Forms, ASP.Net\n            \nDuration\n             \n          \n: 1 Month.\n\nDescription\n\n                \n\n\n\n\nDynamic content manager provides users with easy-to-use web interface for developing new template based web pages and total content management solutions. With DCM implementation webmaster gets equipped with an ability to modify the website contents through user interface with minimal efforts.\n\n\nProfessional Qualifications\nMaster of Computer Applications \n(MCA) \nfrom \nAligarh\nMuslim\nUniversity\n\nAligarh\n with \n77%\n marks. \nBachler of Science (\nBSc)\n from \nCSGM\nUniversity\n\nKanpur\n with \n65%\n marks. \n\n\n\nPersonal Information:\n\nFather?s Name\n               \n\n           \nMr. Wahid Ullah\n\nDate of Birth\n                  \n\n           \n\nst\n January, 1983\nSex\n                              \n\n           \nFemale\nMarital Status\n                \n\n           \nUnmarried\nNationality\n                     \n\n           \nIndian\n\nPersonality\n\nThe most important aspects of my personality are my positive attitude towards life, openness towards learning new skills and my ability to work hard in adverse circumstances to meet the targets without loosing patience.\n\n\n\n\n\nDate:\n   \nPlace:\n\nNoida (UP) \n                                                                   \n                            \n        \n[Sadaf Fatima]',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-18',NULL,'2007-10-18','2010-06-09 12:13:49','2010-06-09',3,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(183,'Srinivas B',NULL,NULL,'Bangalore','srsacinivassdacass0322@gmail.com',NULL,NULL,'0','919920973348','0',NULL,'0','2007-04-14',8,24,'2010-06-09 12:13:49',2,'0',NULL,'200710/18/ATT19245.html','200710/18/DOC16307.doc','Resdex @ naukri.com\nSrinivas.B\nBangalore - 5600068 \nsrsacinivassdacass0322@gmail.com\n\nTelephone: 919920973348\n(M)\n\nD.O.B\n - 31 Aug 1982 \nModified on\n - 25 Sep 2007 \nAnnual Salary\n - INR 4 Lac(s) 60 Thousand \nTotal Years of Experience\n - 3 Year(s) 0 Month(s) \nCurrent Location\n - Bangalore \nPreferred Location\n - Anywhere in India \nMCA with 3+ years of Experience as Software Engineer with knowledge of Microsoft .Net Technologies.',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-18',NULL,'2007-10-18','2010-06-09 12:13:49','2010-06-09',2,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(184,'Surendran',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Susafrendasefsearan.it@gmail.com',NULL,'080 66231671','0','9980033380','0',NULL,'0','2008-04-29',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-09 12:13:49',2,'0',NULL,'200710/18/ATT19247.html','200710/18/DOC16308.doc','BHANU PRASAD\nSurendran\n\nSusafrendasefsearan.it@gmail.com\n    \n                                                            \n      \n91-9980033380\n                                                \n                                                                       \n080- 66231671(Off)\n         \n\nProfessional Experience Summary:\n\n2+\n years of experience in \n.net \nusing C# \n\n       \nGood exposure in developing Web Application using C# .Net and ASP\n\n       \nGood Knowledge in \nSQL, PL/SQL\n\nWork Experience Summary:\n\n       \nWorked as Developer in \nAztec Software, \nBangalore\n\nfrom Feb 2005 ? Jan 2007.\n\n       \nTransferred from Aztec Softwares to Dendrite from Feb 2008.(internal)\nCareer Achievements:\n\n       \nWorking for worlds No 1 Pharmaceutical Company.\n\n       \nGood working knowledge in SFA Data Model\n\n\n       \nGood Working Knowledge in CRM Domain.\n\n       \nAwarded as Performance champion (2005 3\nrd\n quarter)\n\n       \nB1 Visa holder.\nEducation Profile:\n\n\n       \nBE (Information Technology)\n from \nSethu Institute of Technology, \nMadurai\n\n\nwith 66\n\n during 2000-?04\n\nTechnical Skills:\n\n\nLanguages\nC, C++, C#\nDatabases\nOracle 8i/9i\nInternet Apps\nHTML, Java Script, ASP.Net\nOperating Systems\nMs-DOS, Windows 2000, Windows NT\n\nProject Details:\n\nProject #1:\n\nClient \n               \n\n Sanofi ? \nAventis\n\nUSA\n            \nTitle\n                  \n\n Quest Baseline Upgrade\n            \nRole\n                  \n\n Developer\nEnvironment\n      \n\n Visual C++\n            \nTeam size \n        \n\n\n            \nDuration\n            \n\n 5 months\n            \nWebsite\n            \n\n\nwww.sanofi-aventis.com\nDescription:\nQuest is SFA solution for Sanofi?Aventis field force. Basically it automates the sales promotion of products manufactured by Sanofi?Aventis with the filed force of Sanofi?Aventis. The Quest \n- that would manage making calls on prescribers, sample distribution, electronically capture physicians? signatures, record and analyze prescriber data, prepare reports, and better communicate with the home office using tablet computers\nThis Project Involves of adding new modules to the existing Quest Application used by the sanofi-Aventis field force such as medical Inquiry and adding new functionalities in the existing call module adding new profiles.\n\nContribution:\n\n         \nUnderstanding existing business model and customer requirements\n\n         \nPreparation of\n\nHigh Level Design Document\n\n         \nPreparation of\n\nLow Level Design Document\n\n         \nAdding new functionalities in the call page and validations.\n\n         \nPreparation and Execution of Unit Test Cases\n\n         \nPreparation and Execution of Integration Test Cases\n\nProject #2:\n\nClient \n               \n\n Sanofi ? \nAventis\n\nUSA\n            \nTitle\n                  \n\n EQuest\n            \nRole\n                  \n\n Developer\nEnvironment\n      \n\n ASP\n            \nTeam size \n        \n\n\n            \nDuration\n            \n\n 4 months\n            \nWebsite\n            \n\n\nwww.sanofi-aventis.com\nDescription:\nEQuest is the web based application which duplicates the windows based Quest Applications used by the Sanofi-Aventis field force with minimal functionalities to help the field users in case of emergency.\nEquest comes with the minimal functionalities which allow the reps to create the calls and view the reports in case if they are not able to use their laptops.\n\nContribution:\n\n         \nUnderstanding existing business model and customer requirements\n\n         \nPreparation of\n\nLow Level Design Document\n\n         \nDeveloping Call module in ASP\n\n         \nPreparation and Execution of Unit Test Cases\n\n         \nPreparation and Execution of Integration Test Cases\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nProject #3:\n\nClient \n               \n\n Sanofi ? \nAventis\n\nUSA\n\n            \nTitle\n                  \n\n Merge Manager\n            \nRole\n                  \n\n Developer\nEnvironment\n      \n\n Oracle 9i\n            \nTeam size \n        \n\n\n            \nDuration\n            \n\n 5months\n            \nWebsite\n            \n\n\nwww.sanofi-aventis.com\n\nDescription:\nSanofi ? Aventis Group manufactures pharmaceutical products. Their respective SFA teams promote those products.\nThe objective of this project is to merge the loser customer entity with the winner customer. Client provides the data with the loser customers ID and Winner Customers ID, we are responsible for creating the procedure which will merge all loser customer information with the winner customer and inactivates the loser customer profile\nContribution:\n\n\n         \nUnderstanding existing business model and customer requirements\n\n         \nPreparation of\n\nHigh Level Design Document\n\n         \nPreparation of\n\nLow Level Design Document\n\n         \nCreating the procedure to merge the loser customer with winner \n\n         \nPreparation and Execution of Unit Test Cases\n\n\nProject #4:\n\nClient \n               \n\n Sanofi ? \nAventis\n\nUSA\n\n            \nTitle\n                  \n\n OncQuest\n            \nRole\n                  \n\n Developer\nEnvironment\n      \n\n Asp.Net using C#\n            \nTeam size \n        \n\n\n            \nDuration\n            \n\n 9 months\n            \nWebsite\n            \n\n\nwww.sanofi-aventis.com\n\n\nDescription:\nThis is an Oncology-Specific Account-Based Customer Relationship Management Tool (CRM), built For the User by the User. This system will provide you with all of the necessary tools to successfully manage your customers and business. Oncology-Specific data has been incorporated into the OncQuest System while simultaneously providing flexibility to independently manage information pertinent to your individual territory\nOncQuest is the Full Implemetation project which over rides the existing products with the new web based products released by dendrite. This involves migration of data to the new compatible schema and upgrading entire field force with the new product. This also involves adding new modules to the existing product based on the client?s requirements and adding new validation in the various modules.\n\n\nContribution:\n\n\n         \nUnderstanding existing business model and customer requirements\n\n         \nPreparation of\n\nLow Level Design Document\n\n         \nDeveloping the Medical Inquiry Module and adding new functionalities to the existing call module. \n\n         \nPreparation and Execution of Unit Test Cases\n\n         \nExecution of Integration Test Cases\n\n\nPersonal Profile:\n\nName\n                \n\n           \nSurendran.R\nFather?s Name\n   \n\n           \nRadhakrishnan\nMarital Status\n    \n\n           \nSingle\nDate of Birth\n      \n\n           \n07-Jan-1983\nAddress\n            \n\n           \n17G,1\nst\nfloor\n     \nChalagatta, \nYemalur, \nBangalore\n ? 37',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-18',NULL,'2007-10-18','2010-06-09 12:13:49','2010-06-09',2,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(185,'Srikanth R',NULL,NULL,'Hyderabad','msconsegwergultant.rikanhgkchgth@gmail.com','msconsultant.srikanth@gmail.com','99599 14448','0','91 99599 14448','0',NULL,'0','2002-07-14',9,29,'2010-06-09 12:13:49',3,'0',NULL,'200710/18/ATT19244.html','200710/18/DOC16309.doc','Srikanth R\nSrikanth R\nIndia\n, +\n91 99599 14448\n\nmsconsegwergultant.rikanhgkchgth@gmail.com\n\nSolutions Architect \nSUMMARY\nDecisive, action-oriented and result-focused professional offering more than \n7.5\n years of experience in IT software development industry with \n\n years focused on Software Architecture, project management and IT teams leaderships. Highly skilled with object oriented architectures and patterns, systems analysis, software design, effective coding practices, databases and servers. Capable of delivering a project from a concept through deployment. Experienced with capturing and documenting requirements from business users, managing project expectations and scope, planning, forecasting, budgeting, negotiation, leadership, and organizational skills. Progressed through software developer to Senior Consultant positions and offer strong technical leadership.\nEMPLOYMENT OBJECTIVE\nA position as a Solutions architect that will allow me to apply my technical and managerial skills and experience in production of leading-edge information solutions.\nACHIEVEMENTS\n\n         \nDelivered series of software solutions including windows applications, web applications, \nB2B\n exchanges, e-commerce solutions. Broad technical expertise\n\n         \nPart of VSTS Rangers Team in Microsoft to develop various tools / features for VSTF\n\n         \nAn MCAD (.Net) with over \n7.5\n years experience providing full life cycle solutions as a lead in designing and developing architectures for complex systems with Microsoft technology\n\n         \nProject experience includes web-based and client-server applications with budgets in excess of \n$1\n million\n\n         \nExpert at bringing clarity and ease of use to complex systems and developing guidelines and frameworks for system development\n\n         \nWorked closely with onsite clients to document requirements by conducting interviews\n\n         \nDevelop multi-tiered object-oriented system architectures utilizing use cases, UML diagrams, Visio and VSTS\n\n         \nManaged teams of up to \n10\n developers and outside consultants\n\n         \nPossess excellent communication skills and proven consulting skills\nSKILLS\n\n         \nArchitecture : Good Awareness and understanding about Enterprise Architecture Methods, frameworks and very good knowledge about SDLC Methodologies, best practices and stronghold in .Net enterprise technologies\n\n         \nProject Management : Microsoft Project Server, Microsoft SharePoint Server 2003 / 2007\n\n         \nDevelopment/Productivity Tools : Microsoft Team Foundation Server, Microsoft Visual Studio \n2008 / 2005\n\n         \nFrameworks\n\n- .\nNet 3.5 / .Net 2.0 / 1.1\n\n         \nWeb Technologies\n\n- ASP.NET, Silverlight , WCF / WPF , Web Services, ADO.NET, XML, IIS, COM+\n\n         \nProgramming Languages - C#, C++, VB.NET,VC++\n\n         \nSoftware Engineering Methodologies/Tools/Technologies - Microsoft Visio / VSTS for Architects, UML, TFS / MS Visual SourceSafe, OOAD\n\n         \nDatabases MS SQL Server \n2000\n, MS SQL Server \n2005\n\nEMPLOYMENT EXPERIENCE\nMicrosoft R&D, \nIndia\n\n                                                                                              \nOct 2006 to Present\nDevelopment Lead\nProvided software architecture services and was part of Application Lifecycle Management Team (ALM) to deliver\nBest practices and patterns guide across ALM practice areas (Architecture & Design, SDLC process, Governance, Project Management, Requirement Management, Code Quality, Quality Assurance, Deployment & operations, Data Management).\n\nProvided technical consultancy on new technologies like Silverlight, WCF / WPF ,Microsoft office sharepoint Services , Microsoft SharePoint Server 2003 \n\nand helped the teams in implementing these features\n\nInitiated , anchored and participated in developing tools for VSTF as part of VSTS Rangers team\n\nLeading the team in OEM COE to dog-food Microsoft Visual Studio \n2008\n Beta 2 (Orcas) and suggest improvements to Microsoft Visual Studio product team\n\nRecognized as SME in Team foundation Server and provided technical consultancy in implementing TFS across distributed locations\n\nInfosys Technologies, \nIndia\n                                                                                   \nApril 2005 to Sep 2006\nTechnical Architect\nProvided software architecture and project management services. Managed a team of up to \n10\n software engineers. Successfully completed several mission critical-projects.\n\n\nSupervise and conduct architecture and design activities across projects\n\nConduct code reviews; participating in coding activities as leader software developer\n\nDesigned and participated as Technical Architect in implementation of client-server rule engine framework for a leading online shopping site with more than 6,00,000 lines of C# code\n\nWorked for leading customers of Infosys like JCPenney\n\nProject tracking and reports created using VSTF, MS Project, Visio and PowerPoint\n\nWipro Technologies, \nIndia\n                                                                                      \nJuly 2003 to Mar 2005\nTechnical Lead\nInvolved in proposing the design and architecture for various RFPs across business verticals and involved in effort estimations and proposal presentations\n\n\nDesigned and led programming and test efforts to develop online decision-making portal for Shell Aviation Supply Database\n\nDesigned and developed C# framework, which was reused in other company projects\n\nNegotiated international software development contracts\n\nDemonstrated leadership skills and led a team of 12 developers\n\nCognizant Technology Solutions, \nIndia\n                                                                    \nJuly 2002 to July 2003\nProgrammer Analyst\n\nProvided object-oriented design, programming and implementation for Web-based clinical trial data collection and management software, written in VC++\n\nDeveloped plans for QA/User acceptance test\n\nOpus Software Solutions, \nIndia\n\n                                                                            \nJune 2000 to July 2002\nSoftware Engineer\n\nInvolved in development of communication middleware product that provides the most powerful and comprehensive application-level communication platform for high-speed distributed transaction processing applications using windows socket programming in VC++.\n\nInvolved in development of online equities stock trading website for a brokerage house in \nHong Kong\n\n\nEDUCATION\nUniversity\n of \nMadras\n\nChennai\n\nIndia\n                                                                                         \nMay 2000\nB.E., Computer Science\n\nCERTIFICATIONS AND TRAININGS\n\n\n         \nMCAD in .Net Application Development Foundation\n\n         \nAdvanced C#, Training by \nJeffrey Richter\n (at Microsoft)\n\n         \nAdvanced Threading in C#, Training by \nJeffrey Richter\n (at Microsoft)\n\n         \nRegular attendee of IASA Conference ( International Association of Software Architects)\n\n         \nSOA web services training and workshop\n\nPERSONAL INFORMATION\n\n         \nAge \n28.\n Married\n\n         \nLanguages: fluent English.\n\n         \nCountry of residence: \nIndia\n\n         \nEmail ? \nmsconsultant.srikanth@gmail.com\n\n         \nPhone \n  \n\n91 99599 14448\n\n         \nCitizenship: Indian','Microsoft R&D',1,NULL,'2007-10-18',NULL,'2007-10-18','2010-06-09 12:13:49','2010-06-09',3,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(186,'Vikas s',NULL,NULL,'Gurgaon','Vikadvdvs121saasd280@gmail.com',NULL,'0751 2366178','0','9999334721','0',NULL,'0','2007-12-13',8,24,'2010-06-09 12:13:49',2,'0',NULL,'200710/18/ATT19243.html','200710/18/DOC16310.doc','Mohit S yadav\nVikas S\nVikadvdvs121saasd280@gmail.com\n\nMobile\n 9999334721\n\nQ-305 Sector 40\nSouth\nCity\n-I\nGurgaon\n\n\nCareer Objective\n:-\n\nIntend to build a career with efficient organization with committed & dedicated people, which will help me to explore myself fully and realize my potential. Willing to work as a key player in challenging & creative environment.\n To give my best to every task I undertake and learn continuously for my growth. Interested to work in such an environment, where my horizons of expertise could extend and reach to the utmost point of satisfaction.\n\nWORK EXPERIENCE\n\n        \nHaving good experience in Software Design and Development for various projects and products for the organization?s valuable clients in the following areas of \nEnterprise\n and Distributed Computing and Business Intelligence Systems.\n\n        \nImplemented the projects in the above domain involving .NET Framework, C# VB6.0, ASP, VB.NET, COM, Web Services and various databases.\n\n        \nAdvance Knowledge in converting databases from Oracle to SqlServer or MSAccess to Sql Server and Vice Versa.\n\n        \nGood Exposure in .NET framework based programming\n\n        \nSound knowledge Of Manual and Automated Testing\n\n\n\nProfessional Experience: Having 2.1 year of Exp.\n\n        \nWorking as Software Programmer in \nProtel InfoServe PVT LTD (\nIndia\n) Gurgaon\n, since \nJan 2007\n. Job profile includes requirement gathering, designing and implementation of WEB DEVELOPMENT. Projects for BPO Industry, DEBT Collection. I have also been involved in\n   \ndatabase design.\n\n         \nWorked as a Software Developer in Scancom Solutions Pvt. Ltd., Noida from \nJun, 2005\n till \nDec, 2006.\n Job profile included designing and implementation of WEB\n\nDEVELOPMENT\n\nProjects for Finance, \nMobile\n. I have also been involved in\n   \ndatabase design.\nProfessional Qualifications:\n\n\n         \nMCA\n from Indira Gandhi National Open University New \nDelhi\n\n\n         \nBCA\n from Indira Gandhi National Open University New \nDelhi\n\n\nAcademic Qualification:\n\n         \nBachelor Degree in Commerce from \nJiwaji\nUniversity\nGwalior\n\n\n         \nIntermediate (10+2) from M.P. Board.\n\n         \nHigh School (10) from M.P Board\n\nKey Skills:\n\nTechnology\nTools\nMonths Worked\nOperating Systems\nMS\n\nWindows 2003, XP, 2000\n24\n\nProgramming Languages\nVisual Basic\n10\n\nC#,VB.Net\n25\nDatabase Technologies\nSQL Server\n25\n\nOracle\n10\n\nMS Access\n\nWeb Technologies\nASP.NET,\n25\n\nHTML\n22\n\nASP\n14\nWeb Servers\nInternet Information Server\n10\nMethodologies\nRDBMS\n15\n\nPROJECT DETAILS\n:-\nProject-1\nProject Title:\n      \n        \n         \nOnline \nSale\n Tracking\nProject description\n\nThis website fulfils the requirement of a \nCall\nCenter\n which run different mortgage campaign. This website consists basically four modules, first one for the calling agent who take the details of a customer who need mortgage according to their requirement, second one is the call center admin module in which call center admin can check the status of lead made today and as well as check the status of the lead reject by client and he can check the lead?s state status means how many leads he made in which campaign and which state too. Third one is the Client User module in which client user can view the all leads made by all the call center all over India and as well as he can view the number of leads made in a particular state, fourth one is the client admin module in which client admin have all the right to make new call center, new campaign, user name and password for the call center, and he also set the daily target\n\nOf each call center.\n\nTeam Size\n\n        \n            \n\n   \n\nPlatform & Skills\n           \n\n   \n\nASP.Net, C#, SQL Server 2000\nRole and Responsibility: \n\nMy role as a\n Programmer is\n to design and to deliver \n  \nthe project in a correct time. My responsibility includes gathering requirements, analyze, designing database, coding, unit testing the modules I have developed and integrated all the modules. I am also responsible for supporting product and fixing the issues from the customers through technical person\n\n\nProject-2\nProject Title\n       \n\n               \nFinance Accounting System\nProject description\n\nThis is an accounting system deal with the financial transaction and generates\n   \n\nreport, Balance Sheet, Trail balance and Different Schedules and also shows the flow of funds.\nTeam Size\n\n        \n        \n   \n\n    \n\nPlatform & Skills\n\n         \n\n\n  \nASP.Net, C#, SQL Server 2000\nClient\n         \n              \n       \n\n       \nIndian Council of medical research center (I.C.M.R)\nRole and Responsibility: \n\nMy role as a\n Programmer is\n to design and to deliver\n   \nthe project in a correct time. My responsibility includes gathering requirements, analyze, designing database, coding, unit testing the modules I have developed and integrated all the modules. I am also responsible for supporting product and fixing the issues from the customers through technical person\n\n\n\nProject-3\nProject Title\n                 \nMobile\n Showroom\nProject description\n\nThis System keep track of daily sale & purchase, also maintain customer?s data As well as this system also have the stock management, there is a small module of payroll as well\n\nTeam Size\n\n        \n           \n\n    \n\nPlatform & Skills\n           \n\n\nC#\n.Net, C#, SQL Server 2000\nClient\n         \n                     \n\n       \nJain \nMobile\n Showroom\nRole and Responsibility: \nMy role as a\n Programmer is\n to design and to deliver\n   \nthe project in a correct time. My responsibility includes gathering requirements, analyze, designing database, coding, unit testing the modules I have developed and integrated all the modules. I am also responsible for supporting product and fixing the issues from the customers through technical person\n\nProject-4\nProject Title\n       \n                \nDistributed System integration\n (DSI)\nProject description\n\nThis is a distributed system integration of different processes and departments.\nThis includes the process of distributors, vendors and manufacturers. Manufacturers places the manufactured products and different distributors are responsible to sale the products to their vendors. Distributors can avail the facility of comparing the cost and availability to get the maximum benefits. Lots of reports are given for better comparison\nTeam Size\n\n        \n            \n\n   \n\nPlatform & Skills\n           \n\n   \n\nVB\nNet, ASP.NET, SQLServer 2000\nRole and Responsibility: \nMy role as a\n Programmer is\n to design and to deliver\n   \nthe project in a correct time. My responsibility includes gathering requirements, analyze, designing database, coding, unit testing the modules I have developed and integrated all the modules. I am also responsible for supporting product and fixing the issues from the customers through technical person\n\n\nArea of Interest:-\nProgramming, Designing \nStrength,\n Ability to work hard under any kind of situation and adapt to any kind of environment.\nEagerness to achieve in my life.\nAbility to understand anything quickly.\nHobbies:-\nPlaying Cricket \n\nand chess. \nStudying some books related to subjects. \n\nPersonal Details\nName:\n                         \nVikas Shrivastava\n\nDate of Birth \n               \n12.12.1980\n\n\n       \n\nMarrital Status\n     \n      \nSingle\n\nFather?s Name\n   \n          \nSh. M.N Shrivastava\n\nLanguages known\n      \nEnglish, Hindi, \n\nAddress For Communication \n        \nPermanent Address\nS/o : Mr. M.N Shrivastava \nKrishna\n Puri Morar Gwalior\n   \n\nHome Phone No 0751-2366178\nI hereby declare that the above information is true to the best of my knowledge.\nYours faithfully\n                                               \n                                                                                     \nVikas Shrivastava','Protel InfoServe PVT LTD ',1,NULL,'2007-10-18',NULL,'2007-10-18','2010-06-09 12:13:49','2010-06-09',2,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(187,'Sreehari P',NULL,NULL,'Bangalore','psreehasdgdvdsri@rediffmail.com','psreehdvdsvari84@gmail.com',NULL,'0','98863 41691','0',NULL,'0','2007-09-12',10,34,'2010-06-09 12:13:49',3,'0',NULL,'200710/18/ATT19242.html','200710/18/DOC16311.doc','Curriculum Vitae\nCURRICULUM VITAE\n\nSreehari P\n\n#647, 10th \nMain\n, MEI Layout,\n                           \n              \n         \n               \n       \n\nE-mail: \npsreehasdgdvdsri@rediffmail.com\nBagulgunte, \nBangalore\n\n                \n                      \n             \n        \n   \n\n                                  \npsreehdvdsvari84@gmail.com\nKarnataka - 560073.\n\n                                                      \n            \n          \n              \n\n         \npsreehdsvdsvari84@yahoo.com\nIndia\n\n                \n                        \n         \n           \n                \n          \n              \n        \n\nhone: +\n91-98863 41691\n   \nObjective\nTo contribute to the growth of a progressive organization, through hard work, technical expertise and strong work ethics. \nProfessional Summary\nExperience: 2 Years and 5 Months.\n\n2 Years of Experience in Design, Development, Testing and Support for Front End, Middle ware & Back End embedded Windows applications.\nExperience in Developing Distributed Applications for Windows Operating Systems.\nExperience in Design and Development of Industrial Protocol stacks like BACnet & ModBus.\nGood Knowledge in Microsoft technologies like VC++, MS C#, MFC etc.\nGood Knowledge in development and debugging multi-threaded real time applications for Real Time Operating Systems, like VxWorks.\nFamiliar with Embedded C and Assembly programming for Micro-Controllers.\nGood communication and interpersonal skills.\nGood analytical, debugging and problem solving skills.\nExperience in Technical & Project Management.\nCurrently working as Technical Lead Engineer in \nSunlux Technologies Ltd\n\nBangalore\n\nTechnical Expertise\nWindows Programming\n\nPrimary Skill Set:\n\n         \nDistributed Applications development in MS C#.\n\n         \nCommunication Protocol Stacks Design and Development in C, C++ & VC++.\n\n         \nMulti-Threaded Middle ware applications.\n\n         \nData Base Applications using MS SQL Server.\n\n         \nLibraries Development in C++ & VC++ for use in other applications.\n\n         \nFront End applications development using MFC & C#.\n\n         \nDevelopment of Windows based Hardware Simulators and automated test Applications.\n\nReal Time Systems\n\n   \nI) Real time Operating Systems\na) VxWorks/Tornado from \nWind River\n Systems.\n            \n            \n- General Multitasking Real-time application development\n            \n            \n- Use of Tornado Tools for dev/debugging (WindView, Debugger etc.)\n            \n            \n- Design and development of communication protocols\n\nSecondary Skill Set:\n      \nb) Familiar with Programming of OS-less micro-controller based systems with tools like \n                        \n\nKiel\n \'C\' Compiler\n                        \n\nDynamic \'C\' Compiler\nTypical Projects\nSr. Software Engineer, Sunlux Technologies - India Ltd, \nBangalore\n (12th Aug 2005 ? till Date)\n\nTitle:\n     \n\n          \n   \nUniEye SCADA System.\nClient:\n   \n   \n         \n   \nUniveyor \nDenmark\n\nTools:\n   \n   \n         \n   \nVisual C# 2005\nDescription:\n     \n\n   \nUniEye is a set of tools developed for Visual Studio C# 2005, allowing Univeyor developers to \n\n   \ndevelop conveyor SCADA applications quickly. These tools were implemented as C#\n\n                        \n   \nUser controls\n represent each physical entity in a conveyor system, are able to communicate \n   \nwith the server using distributed technologies like \nDot Net Remoting\n and \nWeb Services\n\nRole:\n                 \n   \nResponsible in Leading a team of four, design and implementation.\n\n\nTitle:\n     \n\n          \n   \nTracking RADAR System.\nClient:\n   \n   \n         \n   \nLarsen & Toubro\n, Povai\nTools:\n   \n   \n         \n   \nWind River\n tornado ? \nVxWorks\nDescription:\n     \n\n   \nReal-time\ncontrol software for each of the four VME based sub-systems that are used to \n   \ntrack and monitor the launch of satellite launch vehicles. This also provides post-mission \n   \nactivities like off line analysis, mission replay, calibrations etc. \nRole:\n              \n   \n   \n\nResponsible for design, implementation and testing modules involved with data accumulation \n   \nand communication between the different sub systems. Implementation was done \n   \nin VxWorks Real time Operating System, using Wind River Tornado.\n\nTitle:\n     \n   \n         \n   \nProtocon -\n\nModBus - BACnet Protocol Converter\nClient:\n   \n   \n         \n   \nSunlux\n\nProduct\nTools:\n   \n   \n         \n   \nDynamic C. Rabbit c\nore\nDescription:\n    \n   \n   \nProvides a convenient way for two or more devices / host understanding different \n                           \nprotocols\n   \nfor communicating between each other. Namely ModBus and BACnet. As\n                           \nspecified by the user in the configuration mode, protocon converts services offered by a \n                           \nModBus device as services understood by BACnet devices, hence enabling both these \n                           \ndevices to transfer data among themselves. \n                           \nRole:\n              \n            \nResponsible for managing, scheduling activities for a team size of two. Also responsible for \n                                          \ntechnical design and review of the project.\n\nTitle:\n     \n\n          \n   \nBACnet Master Protocol Stack SCL (Source Code Library).\nClient:\n   \n   \n         \n   \nDATS (Chennai)\nTools:\n   \n   \n         \n   \nVisual Studio 6, C++\nDescription:\n     \n     \nBACnet is a Data Communication Protocol for Building automation and Control networks. \n                           \nThis protocol SCL allows host computers to track and monitor BACnet devices.\nRole:\n                 \n   \n\nResponsible for leading a team of three, technical design, implementation & Testing.\n\nTitle:\n     \n\n          \n   \nBACnet Slave Protocol Stack SCL (Source Code Library).\nClient:\n   \n   \n         \n   \nDATS (Chennai)\nTools:\n   \n   \n         \n   \nVisual Studio 6, C++\nDescription:\n     \n     \nBACnet is a Data Communication Protocol for Building automation and Control networks. \n                           \nThe primary aim of this protocol SCL is to allow users to create BACnet compatible devices \n                           \neasily by interfacing their devices registry maps with the BACnet Slave SLC.\nRole:\n                     \nResponsible for leading a team of three, technical design, implementation & Testing. \n\nTitle:\n     \n   \n         \n   \nTCP/IP Proprietary Protocol\nClient:\n   \n   \n         \n   \nFuel Automation India Ltd\nTools:\n   \n   \n         \n   \nVisual Studio 6, C++\nDescription:\n    \n   \n   \nThis protocol stack defines rules for the Host to communicate and control multiple Petrol \n                        \n   \npumps on the Run. Enables a Real time monitoring of the pump sets like capturing the \n                        \n   \nindicator reading etc.\nRole:\n              \n      \nResponsible for technical Design, implementation, testing and Support. \n\n\nTitle:\n     \n\n          \n   \nReal - time Tracking and Monitoring system.\nClient:\n   \n   \n         \n   \nIndian Railways, Chittaranjan. \nTools:\n   \n   \n         \n   \nVisual Studio 6, C++\nDescription:\n     \n\n   \nThis Application was developed for real time Fault detection and location tracking of \n   \nLocomotives. Once a fault has been detected, the positional coordinates are retrieved from \n   \nthe GPS and are communicated to the server. A string-based protocol was used for \n   \nCommunication. The faults messages formed were SMSed to the server using the GSM \n   \nmodem.\nRole:\n                  \n   \nResponsible for Implementation, Support and testing. Implemented Libraries for GSM\n   \nand GPS in C++. PHP scripting for MySQL database storage.\n\nTitle:\n     \n   \n         \n   \nRobotic Arm Controller.\nClient:\n   \n   \n         \n   \nIndira\nGandhi\nCenter\n for Atomic Research (IGCAR, Kalpakkam). \nTools:\n   \n   \n         \n  \n\nVisual Studio 6, VC++, \nKeil.\nDescription:\n    \n   \n   \nThis Application controls five robotic arms that give capabilities to a remote user. These\n    \n                           \nRobotic arms perform operations like Sample handling, Pippetting, Capping and De-\n                           \nCapping of Bottles containing Plutonium or Uranium. \nRole:\n              \n      \nResponsible for Implementation, Support and testing. Assembly language module implementation. Support for front end developed using MFC.\n\nTitle:\n     \n\n          \n   \nModBus Protocol Stack\n\nClient:\n   \n   \n         \n   \nSunlux\n\nProduct\n\nTools:\n   \n   \n         \n   \nVisual Studio 6, C++\nDescription:\n     \n\n   \nModBus is an application layer Protocol that provided client server communication between \n   \nDifferent devices connected on different types of busses or networks\nRole:\n                  \n   \nResponsible for Optimization & support of the Existing C Libraries.\n\nOther Experiences:\n\n\n         \nSimulators:\nDeveloped in-house simulator applications to devices in VC++, MFC. \n\n         \nInstalled Programming:\nDeveloped applications to be toggled between Evaluation/Full versions during the final build. using the system registry, timed versions etc.\nOther Work Experiences\n\n         \nWorked for 4 Months as Customer Service Representative (CSR) ? Technical support for Client Logic ITC Infotech India Ltd. (CLi3L).\nEducation\n      \n        \nBachelor of Engineering (Computer Science) from \nVisveshvariah technological university \nin 2005 with an overall aggregate of 61%.\n\nExtra Curricular Achievements\nCaptain of my school and College Basketball teams. \nLead my school basketball team to All Kerala Zonal and also participated in the All India CBSE meet.\nHave also participated in Badminton both in the \nKerala\nState\n and District levels\nPersonal Details\nBorn on 18\nth\n of February 1984\nProficient in English, Hindi, Kannada, Malayalam, and Tamil.\nReferences\nMr. Krishnaraj, Project Manager, Sunlux technologies India Ltd, \nBangalore\n\nG.D Rama Reddy, Sr Software Engineer, Robert Bosch \nIndia\n\nBangalore\n\nProf. Doddegowda, Dept. of Computer science, Acharya Institute of Technology, \nBangalore\n\nProf. Vasuki, Dept. of Mathematics, Acharya Institute of Technology, \nBangalore\n\nDeclaration\nI solemnly declare that all the statements made above are true to the best of my knowledge and belief.\n\n\n\n\nSREEHARI .P','Sunlux Technologies Ltd',1,NULL,'2007-10-18',NULL,'2007-10-18','2010-06-09 12:13:49','2010-06-09',3,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(188,'Sai Pradeep Kumar',NULL,NULL,NULL,'sadfbdfsbiprdfbdfadeep.ch@gmail.com',NULL,NULL,'0','9885883229','0',NULL,'0','2008-04-29',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-09 12:13:49',2,'0',NULL,'200710/18/ATT19241.html','200710/18/DOC16312.doc','RE?SUME?\nSai Pradeep Kumar Reddy. Ch\nC/o A. Ganga Raju,\nH.no-63, Salarjung colony,\nMehdipatnam,\nHyderabad\n ? 500008\nPhone no\n: 9885883229\n\nSai Pradeep\n                   \n    \ne-mail id\n\nsadfbdfsbiprdfbdfadeep.ch@gmail.com\n\n\nCareer objective:\nTo work for a professional organization, assume responsibility and strive for collective growth and development to the best of my ability, helping the company to reach new heights.\n\n\nEducational Qualification: -\n\nBachelor of Engineering \nfrom\nAnna\nUniversity\n\nChennai. \nPassed out in\n 2005. \nSecured 75% with Distinction.\n\n\nSkill Set: -\n\nOperating systems\n\n            \n\nWindows 2000 & 2003, Windows XP.\nLanguages\n                \n            \n: C#.NET, JAVA (Up To Servlets).\nInternet Technologies\n        \n: ASP.NET, \nAJAX\n, Servlets, HTML.\nDatabases\n                 \n            \n: SQL Server 2000/2005.\nReporting Tools\n        \n            \n\nCrystal\n Reports 7.0.\n\n\nExperience Summary: -\n\nA professional graduate with 2+ years of experience in IT Industry in the areas of Development of Business application software based on Internet and GUI based multi-tier architecture and Client/Server technologies.\nHave played the roles of Programmer in time during the course of the career.\nExposure to all aspects of software development, troubleshooting, testing and maintenance.\nHave good communication and interpersonal skills, ability to work as a team member and also an individual.\nExcellent ability to learn and adapt to new tools.\n\nSoftware profile: -\n\n\n         \nCurrently working with \nINFO GENEX TECHNOLOGIES PVT. LTD\n\nas a Software Engineer.\n\nProfessional Summary: -\n\nProject#1\nTitle\n                            \n\nFleet Management\nClient\n                          \n\nSreeven Infocom\nTeam Size\n                  \n: 6\nDuration\n                     \n: December 2006 to till date\nRole\n                             \n: Team Member\nEnvironment\n    \n            \n: C#.Net, ASP.NET, IIS, SQL SERVER 2000, WINDOWS XP.\n\nProject Scope\n\n\nThe objective of the project is to help the users maintain the information of all the vehicles, customers, client details, employees, as well as owners of the vehicles. The various modules in this project help us for each specific use. Some of the features of this product are various maps to track their vehicles, booking details, Map details, return form, invoice generation, payments, reports, etc.\n\nThis project is a single point solution for transportation maintenance.\n\nBooking Details\nVehicle Details\nPersonnel Details \nClient Details\nReports\n\nResponsibilities: \n\nActively Participated in Presentation part of the Project.\nDesigning and Coding using C#.net and Ado.Net.\nResponsible for writing SQL Queries and Stored Procedures\n\nProject#2\nTitle\n                            \n\nITRACK\nClient\n                          \n\nAERCOM TEC\nTeam Size\n                  \n: 4\nDuration\n                     \n: June 2006 to November 2006\nRole\n                            \n: Team Member\nEnvironment\n             \n: C#.NET, ASP.NET, IIS, Win2000, ADO.NET, SQL SERVER 2000\n                                                                                                                                  \n                                                         \n                        \nProject Scope:\n\nThis project is mainly based on the solving the problem?s of AVL of the customers who registered their vehicles with the AERTRAX system. AVL is an abbreviation for Automatic Vehicle Location System. With major advances in technology, \"Car 54, where are you?\" is no longer a question without an answer. AERTRAX System is an innovative, dependable and cost-effective AVL system with an entry level of one unit and no capacity limit. This system can serve a company with four vehicles as easily as a company with four thousand.\n\nThis project deals with the maintenance of the Database of the customers problems, the employee who are working on the problems and maintain the time limiting to solve the problem and assigning the problem based on the level hierarchy. It includes 2 modules.\n\n1.\n      \nsearch module\n2.\n      \nAssign module\n\nResponsibilities: \n\nActively Participated in Presentation part of the Project.\nDesigning and Coding using C#.net and Ado.Net.\nResponsible for writing SQL Queries and Stored Procedures\n\n\nProject#3\nTitle\n                            \n\nAERTRAX\nClient\n                          \n\nAERCOM \nTEC\n\nUSA\n\nTeam Size\n                  \n: 8\nDuration\n                     \n: September 2005 to May 2006\nRole\n                            \n: Team Member \nEnvironment\n             \n: C#.Net, ASP.NET,IIS, SQL SERVER 2000, WINDOWS XP.\n\nProject Scope:\n\n     \nAERTRAX is mainly based on the AVL system which is for tracking the vehicle.\n\nThe main purpose of AERTRAX is to retrieve the location of vehicle.\n\nThe normal process is Aries retrieves the information from unit which retrieves the information directly from the GPS (Global Positioning System) and stores it in Aries database. The genex retrieves the information from the Aries database and create a GUI (Graphical User Interface) for that.\n\n          \nThe Online Vehicle Tracking System has considerable benefits over the manual form of handling. The most obvious advantage is that there is no wastage of time. The whole process will be accurate and reliable, devoid of any human errors. Above all, ease-of-use is enhanced with the online system. Also, we can integrate the existing history into the database for easy access. Aertrax includes 2 important modules which includes so many sub modules.\n\n1.\n      \nRoot Module\n2.\n      \nCust Admin Module.\n\nResponsibilities:\n\nMainly involved in Root module for the entire project\n\n         \nResponsible for relevant documentation.\n\n\n\n\nSai Pradeep Kumar Reddy. Ch',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-18',NULL,'2007-10-18','2010-06-09 12:13:49','2010-06-09',2,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(189,'Sachin T',NULL,NULL,'Jaipur','Sdfgdfgachindsgsdraggtayal05@gmail.com','Sachint@iin.com',NULL,'0','09829593485','0',NULL,'0','2007-07-15',8,23,'2010-06-09 12:13:49',3,'0',NULL,'200710/18/ATT19239.html','200710/18/DOC16313.doc','Full Name :\n\nAddress of Correspondence\n97, Printer?s Colony,\n        \nSitabari Area, \nTonk Road\nJaipur ? 302011\n                       \n\n\nSACHIN T\nSdfgdfgachindsgsdraggtayal05@gmail.com\nSachint@iin.com\nMobile\n: 09829593485\n\nOBJECTIVE\n                                    \n\nIntend to build a career with leading corporate of hi-tech environment with committed & dedicated people, which will help me to explore myself fully and realize my potential. Willing to work as a key player in challenging & creative environment.\n\nEXPERIENCE\n\n\n         \nWorking with Compucom Software Limited, Jaipur, as a \nSoftware Engineer\n\nsince Jan 2005 till date. During this period I have worked extensively in various overseas, domestic and in house projects covering various industry domains in Software Testing.\n\nEDUCATIONAL QUALIFICATION\n\n\n         \nB.Tech \nfrom \nAnand\nEngineering\nCollege\n, Agra(U.P.) affiliated to \nU.P.\nTechnical\nUniversity\n\nLucknow\n in \nJuly 2004 \n\n         \nHSC \nfrom \nRajasthan Board\n in year \n1998 \n\n         \nSSC \nfrom \nC.B.S.E Board\n in year \n1996 \n\nTECHNICAL SKILLS\n\n\n       \nOperating Systems\n\n    \nDOS, Windows 98/NT/2000/XP\n\n       \nDBMS/RDBMS \n        \n\n    \nMS-Access, MS-Sql Server-2000\n\n       \nLanguages \n         \n   \n   \n\n    \nC,\n\nHTML, Core Java, C#.Net, ASP.NET\n\n       \nTesting Tools\n      \n      \n\n   \nQuick Test Professional 9.0, Test Director 8.0, WinRunner\n\n\n\n\n\nPROJECTS UNDERTAKEN\n\n\n      \nProject Title 1 - \nKnowlagent r8\n     \nClient\n                   \n\n\n      \nKnowlagent Inc, \nUSA\n (www.knowlagent.com)\n       \n     \nRole\n                   \n\n\n      \nTest Engineer\n     \nDuration\n       \n        \n  \n\n       \n10 Months\n     \n          \n     \nEnvironment\n      \n\n\n      \nC#. Net, MS SQL Server 2005, IIS (Web server\n\n     \nDescription\n       \n  \n\n       \nThis Software is used primarily in Call centers. Bank of \nAmerica\n, T-Mobile, Coca Cola are some of knowlagent clients in \nUSA\n\nContent Builder \nis an application that is used to create Content e.g. Courses, Reviews. \nThe \nJob Match Process\n is used in recruiting process of Call Center Personnel. The \nInitial Training & Classroom Curriculum \napplication is used for providing skills training to the new recruits specific to their job requirements. Knowlagent is integrated with \nAutomated Call Distribution\n (ACD) System to deliver learning sessions without adversely impacting the ACD service levels. The \nKPI ? Scorecard \napplication is used for evaluating the performance of an agent based on Key Performance Indicators (KPI) e.g. \nAverage Call Handle Time\n\n    \nResponsibilities:\n   \n   \nInvolved in Testing of all the modules of software. Smoke Test, Functional Testing, Manual Testing, Automated Testing, Regression Testing\nCreated Test Plan for SCRs. \nDefect Reporting and Tracking through TFS (Team Foundation Server)\nKnowledge Transfer, Setting-up Test Labs\nInteracting with Clients\n\n\n      \nProject Title 2 - \nPrevisor Contact Management System\n\n   \nClient\n                     \n\n\n      \nTekmark Global Solutions, \nUSA\n(www.tekmarkinc.com)\n      \n     \nRole\n                   \n\n\n      \nTest Engineer\n     \nDuration\n       \n      \n  \n\n      \n4 Months\n       \n          \n     \nEnvironment\n      \n\n\n      \nHTML, ASP,\n MS OutLook 2000,\n MS SQL Server 2000\n     \nDescription\n           \n\n\n       \nThis application comprises of following modules: \n    \nContact Management, Project Information Management & Call/Meeting Information \n    \nManagement. Contact Management System stores the contacts of Employees, tracks the\n                 \n    \ndetails of projects, and maintains the details of any Call/Meeting specific to official purpose.\n   \n    \nThe application is based\n\non three-tier architecture to make it available everywhere & also \n    \nto make it System-Independent.\n\n    \nResponsibilities\n      \n\n       \n   \nDeveloped Test Cases by analyzing functional & system requirements.\nExecuted Test Cases and defect analysis\n\n\n\n\n      \nProject Title 3 ? \nInternet Based Customer Assistance, Reporting And\n     \nExpediting(iCARE)\n     \nClient\n            \n          \n\n      \nTekmark Global Solutions, \nUSA\n(www.tekmarkinc.com)\n      \n     \nRole\n                   \n\n\n      \nTest Engineer\n     \nDuration\n       \n      \n  \n\n      \n10 Months\n     \n          \n     \nEnvironment\n      \n\n\n      \nJava Servlets, JSP, JavaScript, HTML, MS SQL Server 2000,\n        \n     \nDescription\n           \n\n\n        \niCARE is a Web based, and SMS enabled eCRM solution developed using\n\nJava Server-side and networking technologies. It caters to the needs of any customer support organization. It allows customers to report their problems through a Web, SMS, WAP or IVRS based interface. It serves the complete reporting and information needs pertaining to a customer problem and maintains the whole life cycle of trouble shooting i.e. problem reporting, assignment of tasks to respective personnel, giving investigation comments, escalation of problem tickets and resolution, till the problem is resolved. This system allows its users to do the following tasks:\n·Generate iCARE tickets.\n·Generate Automatic Email Notifications.\n·Generate Alarm Emails.\n·Read and Update Tickets.\n·Generate History and Performance.\n·Escalation of Tickets.\nResponsibilities\n       \n\n         \n   \nDeveloped Test Cases by analyzing functional & system requirements.\nExecuted Test Cases and defect analysis\n\n\n\n      \nProject Title 4 ? MerckDesk\n     \nClient\n         \n             \n\n     \nMerck Pharmaceuticals, \nUSA\n\nwww.merck.com\n\n     \nRole\n                   \n\n\n      \nSystem Operations\n     \nDuration\n       \n      \n  \n\n      \n4 Months\n       \n          \n     \nEnvironment\n      \n\n\n      \nHTML, ASP,\n MS Outlook 2000,\n MS SQL Server 2000\n     \nDescription\n           \n\n\n\n       \nPrepare reports as required from Merck database To create classes for meetings for the customer and to add enrollees who are going to attend the meeting for the class and finally provide the technical support while conducting the meeting.\n      \nResponsibilities\n\n   \n\n   \nPreparing reports, arranging online meetings for the Centra training.\nProviding technical support while Centra meeting is in process.\n\nPERSONAL DETAILS\n\nDate of Birth\n            \n\n      \n5 March 1982\nGender \n          \n          \n  \n\n     \nMale\nMarital Status\n           \n\n\n      \nSingle\nLanguages Known\n   \n\n       \nEnglish, Hindi, \nNationality\n             \n\n      \nIndian\nPassport \n                   \n\n        \nValid Upto 2017\n\n\n\n\n                                    \n                                                                                                          \nSachin Tayal','Compucom Software Limited',1,NULL,'2007-10-18',NULL,'2007-10-18','2010-06-09 12:13:49','2010-06-09',3,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(190,'Ritesh Nigam',NULL,NULL,NULL,'ritdfbvfdveshvsdfnigam14@gmail.com',NULL,'98711 78168','0','91 9336108956','0',NULL,'0','2006-12-29',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-09 12:13:49',2,'0',NULL,'200710/18/ATT19238.html','200710/18/DOC16314.doc','Curriculum Vitae\nRitesh Nigam\n                                                                                                          \n+91-98711 78168\nC-35 B, Pandav Nagar, Near Mother Dairy\n                                  \nritdfbvfdveshvsdfnigam14@gmail.com\nDelhi\n ? 110 092 \nINDIA\n\nObjective\nSeeking a challenging position in software development with a growth oriented organization, where my skills will be utilized to ultimate potential and also achieve a position where I can grab technical knowledge.\n\nExperience Profile\nPresent Employer\nOrganization\n     \n\n           \nContata Solutions Pvt. Ltd., Noida\n            \nDuration\n               \n\n           \nDecember\n 20,2005\n ? T\nill\n\nate\n            \nDesignation\n                    \n\n           \nSr.\n\nSystem Analyst\n\nPrevious Employer\n      \nOrganization\n     \n\n           \nWebcraft Technologies, \nDelhi\n            \nDuration\n               \n\n           \nJuly 6\n, 2004\n\nDec 16,2005\n\n            \nDesignation\n                    \n\n           \nWeb Developer\n            \nTotal Experience\n   \n\n           \n3 years 2 months\n\nQualification\n      \nProfessional\n            \nMaster in Computer Applications (M.C.A.) with 65.11% (2004)\n\nthers\n              \n            \nDiploma in Computer Programming and Application from Tata Infotech Education\n            \nShort Term Course on C++ and Oracle 8i from Tata InfoTech Education\n            \nThree years article ship for Chartered Accountant (C.A.) course\n            \nBachelor of Science from \nKanpur\nUniversity\n with 65.48%\nTechnical Skills\n      \nOperating Systems\n           \n\n           \nWindows 2000/98\n      \n\nNET\n        \n                        \n\n           \n.Net Frame Work, C#, ASP.\nNET\n\nADO\n\nNET\n      \nOthers\n                          \n\n           \nAjax\n\nXML, Visual B\nasic\n 6.0\n      \nOpen Source\n              \n\n           \nNhibernate, log4Net\n      \nScripting Languages\n       \n\n           \n\nava\n\ncript, \nVB S\ncript\n      \nRdbms\n                           \n\n           \nSQL Server 2000, Oracle 9i, MySql\n      \nReporting Tool\n      \n\n           \nCrystal\n Reports 8\n      \n\nools\n                             \n\n           \nJIRA, SVN\n      \n\nroject\n\netails\n          \n\n                      \nTitle\n   \n                             \n\n   \nWired For Travel (\nApr\n 2006 ? Till Date)\nTeam\n Size\n               \n\n       \n\n\nnvironment\n     \n\n       \nC#, ASP.\nNET\n, SQL Server 2000, NHibernate\n\nole\n                         \n\n       \nSoftware Developer\n          \nClient\n                     \n\n       \nAccredited Only Inc (\nUSA\n\n\nWired For Travel\n\nis a complete web solution for traveling and hotel booking. This website provides the facility of hotel searching and booking to the user. User can search and book a room in a registered hotel worldwide. The main features of this website are as below ?\n\nAjax\nAffiliate\nMultilingual\nGoogle Maps\nSecurity\n\n\nForm Authentication\n\n\nRole Based Authentication\n\n\nIP \n\n\nSSL\n\nAjax\n provides rich user interface without page refreshing. User feels the windows application experience on web.\nAffiliate is one of the three main sections of the website. Affiliate section is for the affiliate registration and user interface of the website will be changed dynamically as per affiliate?s requirements.\nMultilingual is another very good feature of the website. Currently this website supports two languages English and Spanish.\nGoogle maps is one of the very interesting feature of the website. When a user will click on a link\n?View map? the map of the hotel will be displayed on the screen with zoon in and zoom out feature.\nAs for security is concerned the entire website is running on the Secured Socket Layer (SSL) protocol. Form Authentication has been implemented for registered user to access the website. In admin section Role Based Authentication and IP security has been implemented.\nThe other two main section of the website are member and admin. Member section deals with the user registration, hotel searching and booking etc. Admin section is for the administrator to manage the website. \n\nResponsibilities\n       \n\n              \n\nImplemented \nAjax\n, hotel booking module and embedded URL facility. Designed and implemented affiliate section. Affiliate module includes cosmetic changes of the website as per affiliate?s requirements dynamically, affiliate registration etc. Implemented multilingual feature of the website and hotel search facilities through the banner images. Implemented Role Based authentication in admin section and out proc session state. Implemented google map feature, which shows the position of hotel.\n\n\n\n\nProject Details\n\n                      \nTitle\n   \n                             \n\n   \nSunCountryVIP\n\n(Jan 2006 ? \nApr\n 2006)\nTeam\n Size\n               \n\n       \n\n\nnvironment\n     \n\n       \nC#, ASP.\nNET\n, SQL Server 2000, NHibernate\n\nole\n                         \n\n       \nSoftware Developer\n          \nClient\n                     \n\n       \nSun\n Country (\nUSA\n\n\nSun\n COUNTRY \nis a website for hotel and flight reservation. It includes modules like hotel search, hotel reservation, flight reservation and admin. User can search and book a room in a hotel worldwide. User can do reservation by flight reservation module and will get discount if he is a member of Sun Country \nVIP\n club. I have implemented flight reservation module.\n\n\n\nProject Details\n\n                      \nTitle\n   \n                             \n\n   \nEQUIZ\n\n(July 2005 ? Dec 2005)\nTeam\n Size\n               \n\n       \n\n\nnvironment\n     \n\n       \nC#, ASP.\nNET\n, SQL Server 2000\n\nole\n                         \n\n       \nProgrammer and Database Developer\n       \n\nEquiz\n is\n\nan\nonline quiz model. It is very effective to assess student?s performance. It includes \nQuestion Bank, Paper Creation and Analysis. Question Bank module includes various types of \nquestions such as Simple, Fill in the blank, Descriptive, Match case and Antonym Synonym. \nPaper created subject wise. The main module is Analysis. When the student submits the paper \nhe/she can see his/her result, right and wrong answers immediately in Preview Page. \n\n\nProject details\n\n                      \nTitle\n   \n                             \n\n   \nSchool Management\n\n(Feb 2005 ? June 2005)\nTeam\n Size\n               \n\n       \n\n\nnvironment\n     \n\n       \nC#, ASP.\nNET\n, SQL Server 2000\n\nole\n                         \n\n       \nProgrammer and Database Developer\n       \n            \nThis website includes several modules like Students Registration and HR module. Students can \nregister with the use of registration module. HR module deals with the online registration for any \nopenings in teaching and administration. There is various search option to get information based \non a specific criteria. The other main features of the website are Popup, News, Photo Gallery and \nFolder Management. With Folder management we can create folders and sub folders through the \nuse of GUI.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nProject Details\n                        \n                      \nTitle\n   \n                             \n\n   \nCatering Management (July 2004 ? Jan 2005)\nTeam\n Size\n               \n\n       \n\n\nnvironment\n     \n\n       \nVB 6.0, Oracle 9i and \nCrystal\n Reports\n\nole\n                         \n\n       \nProgrammer and Database Developer\n       \n            \n\nThis project was developed for Jeet caters. The main aim was to develop a system to automate the\nwhole functioning of the company. This software includes various modules like Purchase, Stock\nParty booking, Menu, Supplier, Login and Reports.\nPurchase module includes various sub modules like Order, Challan, Invoice, Return and Payment.\nStock module includes Stock Details, Item Receive and Item Issue. Menu includes Food Details, Plate Details and Extra Effects. Through supplier module we register supplier with their supply material. Party Booking module is for the customer register and menu booking. Through Login module we can create new user and edit the information of the existing users. There is a Search module. With the use of this module a user can get the information about various modules and sub modules. He does not need to go to various modules. This feature is very user friendly. Report module is to get the reports like Purchase Order, Purchase Invoice, Purchase Return, Item and Party Booking.\n\n\nPersonal Details\n      \nDate of Birth\n                       \n\n           \nJune 14, 1975\n      \nPermanent Address\n         \n\n           \n104A/321-B, Ram Bagh,\n                                                            \nKanpur\n ? 208 012\n      \nNatioanality\n                        \n\n           \nIndian\n      \nPassport\n                                  \n\n           \nYes\n      \nPhone\n                            \n\n           \n+91-9336108956 (Residence)\n\n      \nReferences\n    \n            \n\n           \nAvailable on request\n\n\n                                                                                                                        \n                                                                                                                        \n\nRitesh Nigam',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-18',NULL,'2007-10-18','2010-06-09 12:13:49','2010-06-09',2,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(191,'Vishal singhania',NULL,NULL,'Chandigarh ',NULL,NULL,'99992447674','0','919988177760','0','919818485717','0','2009-03-14',8,23,'2010-06-09 12:13:49',3,'0',NULL,'200710/18/ATT19237.html','200710/18/DOC16315.doc','hello\nQUALIFICATIONS SUMMARY\n\n\n         \n2.3+ Years \nof extensive experience in Professional software development environment.\n\n         \nMaster of Computer Application (MCA)\n from \nU.P\nTechnical\nUniversity\n\nLucknow\n in July, 2005. \n\n         \nHave good analytical, interpersonal and communication skills.\n\n         \nGood development skills using \nC#, \nVB.NET (2.0)\n, ASP.NET (2.0), \nAJAX\n and \nSQL Server 2X\n\n\n         \nEfficient in database designing, creating procedures and writing queries.\nPROGRAMMING SKILLS\n\n\n\n         \nLanguages\n                  \n\n\nC#\n\nVB.NET.\n\n         \nTechnology\n                 \n\n\n.NET Framework(1x, 2.0), ASP.NET(1.x, 2.0),ADO.NET(1.x, 2.0),\nAjax\n, Web Services \n                                              \nAnd .NET Remoting (Basics)\n\n         \nMethodology\n             \n\n\nObject Oriented Programming (OOPs)\n\n         \nRDBMS Tools\n           \n\n\nMS SQL Server 2X\n\nMS Access\n\n         \nWeb Tools\n               \n\n\n   \nJAVA Script,HTML\n\n         \nOperating Systems\n\n\n\nWindows 2000/XP/2003\nwork summary\n\npresent Employee:\nA-1 Technology Pvt. Ltd., Chandigarh as Dot Net Developer from 25\nth\n September 2006 to till date:\n\nA-1 Technology, Inc\n\na New York(NY) based company, provides offshore software development software outsourcing, offshore outsourcing ,web design and web application development services to client globally. Some of our focus industries include financial services, eCommerce health care and media.\nWebsite:\n\n\nwww.a1technology.com\n\nPROJECTS\n AT A-1 Technology, INC\n\n\n\n   \nADMatch \nLanguages\n\n                         \n\n\nC# and Java Script\nTechnology\n           \n              \n\n\nASP.NET 2.0, Ajax.NET Toolkit 1.0 and Data Access Application Block v 2.0\nRDBMS Tool\n     \n               \n\n\nSQL Server 2005\nEnvironment\n          \n            \n\n Windows NT \nDesignation\n                     \n\nTeam Member\nTeam Member\n       \n           \n\n\nTwo\nTesting URL\n              \n\n\nhttp://68.178.200.90:4049/searchnew.aspx\nDescription\n\n\n  \nAgency Marketing Match (\nAdMatch\n) is an \nadvertising website\n for clients who want to free themselves from the hassles of hours of search to find a suitable agency. It helps companies of all sizes to find right marketing partners. Desiring registered agencies can place their advertisement on the web and the customers or clients can search the agencies according to their needs and use their services. The users can access, edit and post information of the company and their samples of work like ads, displays etc. Provide a user friendly environment to clients, for searching the companies of its choice. This is done by adding various Search features like selecting various categories or do a free form search. \nAdMatch is the most comprehensive, up-to-date and powerful directory of marketing communications agencies on the Web. The searchable directory includes the world?s leading advertising, public relations; direct marketing, interactive, design, sales promotion, yellow pages, recruitment and media buying agencies. Information that can be found on agencies includes in-depth profiles, work samples and case histories.\n\nWith just a keyword you can find agencies or select the search by criteria ?option that includes variables such as clients or personnel, or location, fee billing, and industry experience, services, compensation fee.\nIn addition to that there are various options providing flexible environment to the administrator. He can add, edit or delete awards, regions, industries and perform many such tasks according to the various options provided. The various options are as follows:\na) Agencies\n     \nb) Users\n     \nc) Add/Edit Section\n     \nd)\n                \nUtilities\n     \ne) Sign out\nResponsibilities Included:\n\n         \nHave developed the complete search Engine using the features of \nAJAX\n\n\n         \nHave developed the stored procedure to carry out effective search.\n\n         \nDeveloped the admin module and carried out user based authentication and authorization.\n\n\n   \nAnythingWeather.Com \nLanguages\n\n                         \n\n\nC#, VB.NET and Java Script\nTechnology\n           \n              \n\n\nASP.NET (1.1) and Microsoft Enterprise library (Data Access Application Block)\nRDBMS Tool\n     \n               \n\n\nSQL Server 2000\nEnvironment\n          \n            \n\n Windows NT \nDesignation\n                     \n\nTeam Member\nTeam Member\n       \n           \n\n\nTwo\nClient\n                         \n       \n\n\n\nwww.anythingweather.com\nDescription:\n\nThis is a\n\nweather forecasting based site for \nmaintenance\n and \ndevelopment\n according to client?s requirements. It is providing real\nweather data available in the country and also offering weather information from more locations than any other public source for quick and easy display and dissemination. \nhttp://www.anythingweather.com/clients/airevac/airevac.aspx\n\nhttp://www.anythingweather.com/douglascounty.aspx\n\n\n   \nTunaverse Portal \nLanguages\n\n                         \n\n\nC#, JAVA Script \nTechnology\n           \n              \n\n\nASP.NET (2.0) \nRDBMS Tool\n     \n               \n\n\nSQL Server 2005\nEnvironment\n      \n    \n            \n\n Windows NT \nDesignation\n      \n               \n\nTeam Member\nTeam Member\n       \n           \n\n\nFour\nClient\n\n                       \n       \n\n TUNAVERSE\nSite URL\n                           \n\nwww.tunaverse.com\n\nURL (Working On Test Server\n\n\nhttp://68.178.200.90:2095/default.aspx\n                                                      \n   \nhttp://68.178.200.90:2095/admin/admin_AdminProfile.aspx\n\nDescription:\n This project is concerned with downloading software on mobile as tunes/movies/songs. It has seven modules: ? \nHome ? My Tuna\n\n? Top Tuna \n\n? Support ? Download \n\n\n News Letter\n\n\n? Join. \nThe sub modules present are: ? \nChat application ? Blogs ? News Letter ? Media Library ? Play list(Ring Tone/gift card/games/cell phone service/merchandiser) .\n\nResponsibilities Included:\n\n         \nWorked on ?\nHome\n? and ?\nMy Tuna\n? Modules and have created Login, Forgot password page, Registration Page and created \nMailbox\nCenter\n in which Compose mail, Inbox, Sent Mail(s), Junk Mail(s) and Trash.\n\n         \nWorked on \nAdmin Section\n\n\nand \n\nBlog Section\n (Create/Update/View/Delete Blog(s)) and User Section [Update Users and View/Delete Users] and News Section [Create News/Update News/View/Delete News].\n\n\n   \nTopDot \nLanguages\n\n                         \n\n\nC#, JAVA Script \nTechnology\n           \n              \n\n\nASP.NET (1.1) \nRDBMS Tool\n     \n               \n\n\nSQL Server 2000\nEnvironment\n          \n            \n\n Windows NT \nTeam Member\n       \n           \n\n\nThree\nClient\n\n                      \n       \n\n\n\n\nTopdot (A & B GIO)\n\n  \n\n\nwww.topdot.com\nURL (Working On Test Server\n\n\n                             \n\nhttp://68.178.200.90:2015/Login.aspx\n\n                          \n\n      \n                   \n      \n   \n                       \nhttp://68.178.200.90:2060/topdot/Login.aspx\nDescription:\n This is a Lead Management System, designed for the extranet and also designed an application, which is for the employees to search for Leads. It has four sections: ? Admin ? Manager ? Loan Officer ? Reception\n\nResponsibilities Included:\nDeveloped a smart search in reception section using AJAX Functionality.\nDeveloped admin section, which handles all users, various reports generated for Manager/Loan Officers and searching for leads.\n\nprevious Employee:\nOne Card Solution, \nDELHI\n\nAS A PROGRAMMER FROM January 06 to 20\nth\n September 06:\n\n\nBased in \nNew Delhi\n\nIndia\n One Card Solution is the leading provider in ERP, Data Intergration, Smart card Solutions Business Intelligence solutions and services. We Deliver product engineering & IT Services and develop Business and Technology solutions to enable our clients gain a competitive advantage. \nWebsite:\n\nwww.1cardsolution.com\nProjects Done AT One Card Solution\n\n\n\n      \nSarvodaya Online Business Marketing\nLanguages\n\n                         \n\n\nVB.NET\nTechnology\n           \n              \n\n\nASP.NET\nRDBMS Tool\n     \n               \n\n\nSQL Server 2000\nEnvironment\n          \n            \n\nWindowsXp-05\nTeam Member\n       \n           \n\n\nFive\nURL\n                                       \n\n\nwww.sobmbusiness.com\nDescription:\n Sarvodaya Online Business Marketing Software maintains a chain, \nWarehouse\n\nDepot\n\nPickup\nCenter\n (PUC) \n\nAuthorized Center (ADC) or from Warehouse \n\nWalking Customer and also promotes \nMulti Level Marketing\n (MLM). This project is running at ?\nSarvodaya Online Business Marketing, Bhilwara, Rajasthan as a Central Server and Over 250 Locations in India as a Depot?s, PUC?s and ADC?s\n\n                                \n\nResponsibilities Included\n\nInvolved in creating ADC/PUC/DEPOT for Download Section of the Site.\nInvolved in analysis, designing and coding of the project.\nHave worked on major forms like Warehouse, Depot, PUC, and ADC that contains master forms like Company Registration, Product, Vendors, Employee, Price,\n\nCategory, Tax, Sub Category, Unit Master, Parent and Child Unit Relation Master, Order Request, Making Challan against Order Request, Order Dispatch , Generate Purchase Order, Generate Invoice against PO , Billing.\nImplemented on Client Site and also given training to end users about its use and functionality.\n\n\n   \nIndian Tobacco Company limited\nLanguages\n\n                         \n\n\nVB.NET \nTechnology\n           \n              \n\n\nASP.NET \nRDBMS Tool\n     \n               \n\n\nSQL Server 2000\nEnvironment\n          \n            \n\n Windows NT \nTeam Member\n       \n           \n\n\nTwo\nClient\n                                \n\n\nIndian Tobacco Company Limited (ITC)\n\nNew Delhi\n\nDescription: \nThis\n Application maintains all the details of Purchase Order, Invoice Generation and Inventory like Stock, Challan, and Billing. It is a multiple user application where multiple clients interact with central server via Web Server.\nResponsibilities Included\n\nHave maintained the data on both of the servers viz, Web Server and Central Server.\nHave working on major forms like Product Registration, Vendors, Employee, Price, Category, Sub Category, Tax, Unit Master, Unit Relation Master; Order Request, Order Dispatch, Generating Bill, Throughput, Expenditure Master and Details.\nImplemented on Client Site and also have given training to end users about its use and functionality.\n\nprevious Employee:\nS.R Infotech, GURGAON \nAS A PROGRAMMER FROM april 05 to December 05\n\n\nProjects Done AT S.R Infotech\n\n\n\n      \nCampus Pro- Institute Management Application\nLanguages\n\n                         \n\n\nC#, VB.NET \nTechnology\n           \n              \n\n\nASP.NET \nRDBMS Tool\n     \n               \n\n\nSQL Server 2000\nEnvironment\n          \n            \n\nWindowsXp-05\nTeam Member\n       \n           \n\n\nFive\nDescription:\n\nIt?s an Institute Management Application that maintains the details regarding the students studying in the school, their fee structure, faculty teaching in the school and every other details regarding school management. It contains 19 modules like Admission,fee,acadmic,timetable, test papr,transport,hostel, Inventory,libray,payroll,accounting,mess,store,alumni,dispensary,dak management, security, student interface.\n\n\nResponsibilities Included:\n    \nInvolved in developing modules, Admission, Fees, Academic, separately in ASP.NET with C# as code behind language, and VB.NET. \nDesigned major forms in the modules.\nInvolved in testing and formatting of the modules.\nDeveloped the stored procedures used by the applications. \nEDUCATION AND TRAINING\n\nEducation\n                            \n\n\nM.CA\n from \nU.P\nTechnical\nUniversity\n\nLucknow\n in July, 2005.\n                                            \n: B.Sc. \n\nMath?s, Physics, and Chemistry\n) Graduate from \nM.J.P.\nRohilkhand\nUniversity\n                                               \nBareilly\n, Uttar Pradesh. \n                                          \n\n\n\n\n12\nth\n\nfrom U.P. Board \nAllahabad\n\n                                            \n\n\n10\nth\n\nfrom U.P. Board \nAllahabad\n\n\nTraining\n     \n                      \n\n\nDone Industrial Training at\n CMC Limited \nNaveen Shahdara, \nNew Delhi\n\n            \n                                                                                                                   \nPERSONAL DETAILS\n\n\n         \nAddress\n                       \n\nC-506, Street No-11, \nMajlish\nPark\n,Azadpur, New Delhi-110033\n                                                                           \n\n         \nDate of Birth\n              \n\n\n\nst\n May 1980\n\n         \nLanguages\n               \n\n\n\n   \nEnglish, Hindi \n\n         \nPassport No\n             \n\n\nG0480356\n\nReferences\n\n\n          \nMr.\nRajneesh Raturi\n     \n\nA1 Technology Inc.\n\nChandigarh\n(TL)\n    \n   \nMob:\n\n+919988177760,\n99992447674\n\n          \nMs. Megha Bansal\n      \n  \n\nQ3 Technologies, Gurgaon(Friend)\n     \nMob\n\n\n +919818485717\n\n          \nVishal Singhania\n          \n\n Wipro Technologies, Gurgaon (Friend)\n            \nMob\n\n\n +91\n\n9810064341\n\n\n\nThe above information published is the best to my knowledge.\n\n\nRavi\n kumar','A-1 Technology Pvt. Ltd',1,NULL,'2007-10-18',NULL,'2007-10-18','2010-06-09 12:13:49','2010-06-09',3,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(192,'Ravi G',NULL,NULL,'Banglore','rgyvdvdvdvani@yahoo.com',NULL,NULL,'0','91 9886646752','0',NULL,'0','2006-04-13',8,24,'2010-06-09 12:13:49',2,'0',NULL,'200710/18/ATT19236.html','200710/18/DOC16316.doc','[FIRSTNAME LASTNAME]\nRavi G\nEmail: \nrgyvdvdvdvani@yahoo.com\nPhone : +91 9886646752\nWebsite: \nhttp://www.knocks-solutions.com\n\n\nSummary\nB.E from NSIT, \nDelhi\n. Having 4+ years of experience in C# Winforms.\n\nCurrently operating personal Company, KNOCKS Solutions.\nWORK EXPERIENCE\n                                                                                                                                              \nKnocks Solutions (April?2006 ? Current)\nFounded Knocks Solutions Pvt. Ltd. For Development of C#.NET components\nProteans Software Solutions\n\n(May?2005 ? April?2006)\nWorked with Proteans Software, \nBangalore\n as a Senior Software Engineer\nCoreObjects\n\n(Oct? 2004- May?2005)\nWorked with CoreObjects, \nBangalore\n as Software Engineer.\nHCL Perot Systems \n(Oct? 2003 ? Oct? 2004)\nWorked with Perot Systems, Noida as Software Engineer.\nEducation\nNetaji Subhas \nInstitute\n of \nTechnology\n\nDelhi\n. (Formerly \nDelhi Institute of Tech\n.), 2003.\n    \n         \nBachelor of Engineering (Instrumentation & Control) Aggregate: 66%.\nAwards, Publications and Professional Affiliations\nPredefined Software Design Contest VC/C++;\nInnovision 2002 (Technical Festival of NSIT and IEEE)\nOvernight Programming 2nd Prize \nC++\n\n\nInnovision 2002 (Technical Festival of NSIT and IEEE)\nOvernight Programming 1st Prize \nC++\n\n\nInfoXpression 2002 (Technical Festival of GGSIPU, \nDelhi\n\nOvernight Programming 2nd Prize C++;\nDitech 2002 (Technical Festival of NSIT, \nDelhi\n\nSelected in \nIITJEE\n\nand various other Engineering Entrance Examinations\nAssociate Performance Award \nby HCL Perot Systems, for Bdellium, BdTools Project\nSkill Set\nProgramming Languages: \nC#, .NET Platform, Compact Framework, XNA\nRDBMS/DBMS: \nSQL Server, ORACLE 8i\n\nTools: \nCrystal\n Reports 9.0, Component One Studio, DevStudio.NET, DotImage, Nunit framework, MSMQ and others\n\n\nProject Details\n\nKnocks Solutions (April?2006 ? Current)\nFounded and operating Knocks Solutions, catering to the Visual Studio.NET third party components market.\n\nPROJECT: \nKNOCKS Windows Components (April?2006-Current)\nEnvironment: Pentium S/w: C#.NET 2.0, SQL Server\nTeam Size: 2\nKNOCKS Product range contains high-quality, customizable UI controls for developers and enterprise software teams working on Microsoft® Visual Studio? development environment. KNOCKS components allow you to quickly create professional and authentic looking applications using the latest controls. \nKNOCKS WinControls\n contains Powerful Grids, Calendars, Tab Strip, Docking Managers, Outlook Bar, SpellChecker, Super ToolTip, etc to meet all UI requirements for enterprise WinForm applications.\nKNOCKS ShellControls\n mimic all standard Windows Explorer features like Thumbnail, Group and Details/Report View, icons, context menus, drag drop, renaming, info tips and many others.\nKNOCKS Instrumentation Suite\n is a set of components built to display numeric values in a graphical manner. The components can be customized and combined to present many different kinds of appearances. One can build and control almost any kind of meters, dials, or gauges using these controls.\nKNOCKS Skinner\n component is a simple drop-in component that helps in building skinnable WindowForms application, like the ever popular WinAmp UI.\nKNOCKS RibbonControls\n helps build MS Office 2007 style application user interface. It proposes to be a complete replacement for the current menus and toolbars for simpler design and discoverability..\nKNOCKS Sql-Sense\n, in its BETA release, aims to provide VS.Net type intelli-sense style help when authoring SQL Statements in a variety of Editors like Microsoft Query Analyzer, SQL Server 2005 Management Studio, Visual Studio 2005 and Visual Studio .NET 2003.\nKNOCKS VS2005 Addins\n is an \"all-in-one\" add-in that integrates with Visual Studio .NET 2005 and provides features to improve developer productivity while coding and designing and debugging.\nWeb Site: \nhttp://www.knocks-solutions.com\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nProteans, (May?2005 ? April?2006)\nWorked as a Senior Software Engineer; also involved in Training and Mentoring of freshers recruited in the company.\n\nPROJECT: \nMobileTEC (October?2005- April?2006)\nClient: \nWennSoft, Inc \nEnvironment: Pentium S/w: C#.NET 2.0, Compact Framework 2.0, MSMQ, SQL Server\nTeam Size: 4\nWennSoft MobileTEC wirelessly connects remote technicians to a host system. Technicians are able to receive and update appointments as they are created on the host system. The system is designed to work on portable devices like laptops and Pocket PCs and uses Microsoft Message Queuing to transmit the data. \nRole: Senior Software Engineer. The responsibilities included requirement study, designing, coding.\nPROJECT: \nEyeBatch (May?2005- October? 2005)\nClient: \nAtalasoft, Inc \nEnvironment: Pentium S/w: C#.NET\nTeam Size: 5\n\nAtalasoft EyeBatch is a batch image processor for automating image processing by applying image commands to a \nset of multiple images. The image commands are pipelined in a very user-friendly UI with preview options for command effects. The application was created using .NET concepts like reflection, XML, Collections and the UI was a complete redistributable User Control.\n\nRole: Senior Software Engineer. The responsibilities were requirement study, designing, coding.\n\n\nCoreObjects, (Oct? 2004 ? May?2005)\nWorked as a Software Engineer\n\nPROJECT: \nProto Portfolio Analysis System (October ?2004- March?2005)\nClient: Proto Software, Inc \nEnvironment: Pentium S/w: C#.NET Tools: Component One.\n\nProto is a .NET based Windows application. It has a very user friendly UI in the shape of Assembler and the \nControl\nCenter\n. These UI elements allow user to capture data from Word, Excel or any conventional database and perform operations on the data. The data can further be displayed in charts, graphs for analysis.\n\nRole: Team Member, Development/Implementation.\n\n\n\n\nPerot Systems, TSI; formerly HCL Perot Systems (Oct? 2003 ? Oct? 2004)\nWorked as a Software Engineer\n\nPROJECT: \nBdellium Portfolio Analysis System (December?2003- October? 2004)\nClient: \nBdellium Inc. \nHonolulu\n\nHI\n. US\nEnvironment: Pentium S/w: C#.NET Tools: \nCrystal\n Reports, SQL Server 2000.\n\nThe project was aimed at developing a client-server application called ?BdTools System? on Microsoft .NET Framework that would automate the statistical & analytical decision making that helps people in making investment decisions. The main Functional Core modules are BdImport, PAM Correlation, Universe Manager, Grouping, Scoring and Analysis Result Generation. BdImport and PAM Correlation are used to populate BdWarehouse, which is a Centralized Data Warehouse for whole system.\n\nThe other modules allow the user to manipulate the data in BdWarehouse. This is a Web-Service based delivery platform built in Microsoft?s .NET development environment using Enterprise Services that is flexible enough to support multiple product offerings and scalable to serve a global customer base.\n\nRole: Team Member, Development/Implementation. As a member of the implementation team, the responsibilities were requirement study, designing, coding, unit testing, unit-test case preparation, system testing.\nWas awarded ?Associate Performance Award? for this project\n\n\nPROJECT: \nElan Capsule Automation System (Oct?2003- December?2003)\nClient: \nElan Pharmaceutical Operations, \nDublin\n\nIreland\nEnvironment: Pentium S/w: C#.NET Tools: \nCrystal\n Reports, Oracle 8i\n\nThe project was aimed for developing a desktop application called ?Capsule Automation System? on Microsoft .NET Framework that would automate the encapsulation documentation process to the maximum extent possible. The system should cater to substantially reducing the manual data entry and batch paperwork by reducing manual calculations on paperwork and hence verification steps. It also should also eliminate manual event log tracking and link events to running/not running machine and hence simplify requirement for operator scrutiny of data to determine efficiency of process centering.\n\nRole: Team Member, Development/Implementation. As a member of the implementation team, the responsibilities were requirement study, designing, coding, unit testing, unit-test case preparation, system testing.','KNOCKS Solutions',1,NULL,'2007-10-18',NULL,'2007-10-18','2010-06-09 12:13:49','2010-06-09',2,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(193,'Ratheesh P',NULL,NULL,NULL,'iratheefefeeshfefankar@yahoo.com','iratheeshankar@yahoo.com','9945562250','0','9740153165','0',NULL,'0','2008-04-29',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-09 12:13:49',15,'0',NULL,'200710/18/ATT19235.html','200710/18/DOC16317.doc','              \n    \n            \n                                                                                            \nAddress: No 4 ,4th cross,Lbs Nagar\n                                                                                            \nIndira Nagar 2\nnd\n\nstage\n                                                                                            \nBangalore-37\nEmail: iratheefefeeshfefankar@yahoo.com\n                                                                                                              \nPhone :9740153165\n\n         \n     \n       \n                     \n\n           \n                      \n                                                         \nRATHEESH \n\n\n\n\nOBJECTIVE\n\n\nTo\n acquire a job that helps in tapping of my talents\n and to work in a creative environment with effectively contributing towards the goals of the organization\n\n\nTECHNICAL SKILLS\nLanguages\n                      \n: .NET (ASP.NET,C#.NET,ADO.NET) VB.NET.\n\nDatabase\n                \n\n                       \n\n\nMicrosoft SQL sever, XML.\n        \nMultimedia knowledge :\n Macromedia flash ,Flash action scripting,3D Max,Photoshop .\nDevelopment Platform\n\n: Windows 98/xp, UNIX, LINUX.\n                             \nEXPERIENCE: (2\n\nyears)\n1)Working ATS(Allied Tech Solutions) \nBangalore\n,as dot net programmer from Aug 2005 to till date.\n\n2) Worked as project trainee at HAL Bangalore(Aircraft Research and design centre for academic project)Nov 2004 to\n\nMar 2005.\n\nEDUCATIONAL QUALIFICATION\nBachelor of Technology \n\nB.Tech\n\nComputer Science\nFrom \nGovernment\nEngineering\nCollege\n, Srekrishmapuram, 2005 \nCalicut\nUniversity\n12\nth\n\n\nCBSE\n) AISSCE From \nKendriya Vidyalaya\n, 2001\n10\nth\n\n\nCBSE\n) AISSCE From \nKendriya Vidyalaya\n, 1999\n\nCERTIFICATION\n1)\n MCP\n (Microsoft certified Professional) in\n\n070-315\nMicrosoft certified in developing and implementation of web applications with Visual C#.Net\nAnd Microsoft visual studio .NET.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nPROJECTS\n1) Image Viewer Application (IVA) :\nScope\n                                       \n:This is an application developed mainly for transfer of daily news\n        \n                               \n                   \npaper articles as XML file .A day?s newspaper is being scanned\n\n                                                  \nand converted as an XML\n\nfile and stored. This application is\n\n                                                 \nbeing used to get the articles and\n\nimages as per the date and \n                                                  \nArticle No etc.\n                                                                                     \nLanguage\n                                 \n:VB.NET, XML.\nRole\n                                   \n   \n:As team member.\nPlatform\n                                   \n:Windows XP/2000.\nDuration\n                                  \n:3 months.\nTeam Size\n                               \n:3\n\n          \n  \n                                                            \n     \n2)E-school:\nA software to manage school activities and student\n Profile,teacher profile,Donations etc.\nLanguage\n                                 \n:VB.Net,Asp.Net with SQL Server 2000.\nRole\n                                   \n   \n:1)Database creation and stored procedures 2)Form designing for\n    \n                                                 \nall pages like Student information, Parent information etc.\nDuration\n                                  \n:6 months\nPlatform\n                                  \n:Windows XP/2000.\nTeam Size\n               \n                \n:5\n\n3)E- hospital:\n A software useful in managing various modules \n                                                 \nlike IP(In patient),OP(Out patient),Lab, Pharmacy etc.\nLanguage\n                                 \n:C#.Net with SQL Server 2000.\nRole\n                                \n      \n:As a team member :1)Database creation and stored procedures\n   \n                                                 \n2)Designing forms for IP ,Create Patient, Corporate Patient, Create\n\n                                                 \nDoctor .\nDuration\n                                  \n:6 months\nPlatform\n                                  \n:Windows XP/2000.\nTeam Size\n                               \n: 5\n\n4)Allied Reality:\n              \nA site for real estate and property management where the seller\n    \n                                             \ncan register and the admin certifies his property and puts\n\nthe site \n                                                 \nfor display .Includes\n                                                                       \n           \n                                                 \nmodules like letting ,mortgage etc.\nLanguage\n                                 \n:C#.Net,Asp.Net with SQL Server 2000.\nRole\n                                   \n   \n:As a team member: 1)Database Table Creation\n    \n                   \n                              \n2)Adminpage,3)Buyer part, 4)Property configuration\nPlatform\n                                   \n:Windows XP/2000.\nDuration\n                                   \n:4 months.\nTeam Size\n                                \n:5\n\n\n\nACADEMIC PROJECTS\n1) MAIN PROJECT\n    \n:Single Projection System for Visual simulation(A multimedia\n\n                                            \nproject)\n                                            \n(Flight simulator module).\n   \nDone for\n                         \n\nAircraft research and design center \nat HAL Bangalore.\n   \nTools\n             \n       \n         \n:Visual Basic,3D Max , Macromedia flash MX 2004. \n   \nScripting tool\n                 \n: Flash action scripting. \n   \nPlatform\n          \n     \n         \n: Windows XP. \n   \nTeam Size\n         \n   \n         \n: 1 \n   \nDuration\n          \n     \n         \n: 3 months \n   \nDescription\n     \n      \n         \n: One of the six modules of flight simulator, this uses update dynamics \n                                            \nand helps in finding out whether the visual scene is with in the view of\n   \n                                   \n  \npilot for a given set of parameters.\n\nPersonal Strengths: \n* Excellent problem solving skills and a self-starter \n* Takes initiative and works independently or as part of a group. \n* Well organized. \n\nTeam spirit, Hardworking nature.\n\nPersonal Details\nName\n                                       \n: Ratheesh P\n                                \nSex\n                                          \n: Male\nMarital Status\n                           \n: Single\nNationality\n                                \n: Indian\nMobile No\n                               \n: 9740153165\nE Mail\n                                      \n:iratheeshankar@yahoo.com\n                                   \nCommunication skill\n                  \n: English, Hindi, Malayalam, Tamil.\n\nReference\nMr. Santhosh\nYahoo\nBangalore\nEmail: \n\nsanjux2@gmail.com\nPhone: 9945562250\nAll the statements made above are correct to best of my knowledge.\n\nPlace:\n\nBangalore\n                                                                           \n       \n                  \n\n                      \n                     \nDate:\n                                                                                                                 \nRatheesh P\n      ',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-18',NULL,'2007-10-18','2010-06-09 12:13:49','2010-06-09',15,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(194,'Rakesh ',NULL,NULL,NULL,'rakesscccshrasacscjan1978@gmail.com','Rakeshrajan1978@Gmail.com',NULL,'0','09891097846','0',NULL,'0