RDL and connectiong it to the front end and writing various Stored Procedures and Triggers as per the Clients needs.\nI am greatly involved in the design and development of Statistical Server , a totally scalable component which uses Message Queuing to deliver the statistical data from sender to the receiving system.\nPrevious Experiences Summary :\n1.\nEmployer: Galgotias Systems,Greater Noida.\nDesignation: Software Developer.\nTechnologies: ASP.Net 2.0,\nAJAX\n,C#,Sql Server 2005Crystal Report.\nDuration: 11-Nov-2005 to 26-Dec-2006\nJob Profile:\nERPS (Eeducational Resource Planning Systems) was a web based Software solution which automates the whole process of any Engg. College.It has various modules like-\nStudent,Fee,Library,Exam and HRMS.\nMy Role was to design and develop BLL(Business Logic Layer) and DAL(Data Access Layer) in ERPS.Also writing of various Stored Procedures and Triggers,designing of various reports.\n2.\nEmployer: CLC Technologies Ltd Okhla.\nDesignation: Software Developer.\nTechnologies: VB6,Sql Server 2000,Crystal Report 8.0.\nDuration: 10-Nov- 2004 to 4-Nov- 2005\nJob Profile:\nParidhan was a window based ERP Solution solution which automates the whole process of any Garment Export Co.\nParidhan has the following modules â\n??\nMerchandising , (MM)Material Management, HR , and Documentation.\nMerchandising has the following featurs\nWell designed Dashboard for analysing the whole data at a center place.\nBPO(Buyer Purchase Order)\nBOM(Bill of Material)\nMM module has the following featues\nRS (Requirement Slip)\nPR (Purchase Requisiotion)\nPO (Purchase Order)\nGRN (Goods Receipt Note)\nStore Issue.\nMy Role was to customize the code, writing Stored Procedure, designing various reports and connecting it to the front end.\nDesired Job Details\nPreferred Location: Delhi/NCR.\nJob Type: Permanent.\nEmployment Status: Full Time.\nPersonal Details\nDate of Birth: 15 Mar, 1978\nGender: Male\nMarital Status: Single.\nMailing Address: 335/4 Govindpuril Kalka G, New Delhi .\nRakesh Kumar Shrivastava',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-18',NULL,'2007-10-18','2010-06-09 12:13:49','2010-06-09',2,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(195,'Siddharth',NULL,NULL,NULL,'mrsidvsdvddhdvvarth8@gmail.com',NULL,NULL,'0','9916325803','0',NULL,'0','2008-04-29',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-09 12:13:49',2,'0',NULL,'200710/18/ATT24632.html','200710/18/DOC16319.doc','NAME\nSiddharth\n                                                                                           \nClassic Hostel\nMobile.No:\n9916325803.\n                                                       \nGayathri Building, \nE-mail:\n\nmrsidvsdvddhdvvarth8@gmail.com\n                                  \n         \n5th A Cross,Triveni Raod\n                                                                                            \nYeshwantpur,Banglore-560022\nObjective\nAspiring to seek a challenging opportunity in the corporate world giving my\n               \n                          \nservices through sheer hard work & dedication and professionally by pursuing\n                       \nstrengthening my Technical & Analytical skills.\n\nWork Experience\n          \nHaving \n\n Year\n total experience/\n1.1 year\n of experience in the \nASP.NET\n\ndevelopment.\n\n         \nWorking as\n\na Web Developer in\n Peri Dot Consulting Services Pvt. Ltd. \nfrom\n\nJuly-2006 to Aug-2007 \n\n         \nWorking with \nJSS PRAYAS\n\nNGO\n), \nNew Delhi\n as a Computer Faculty from Aug-2005 to April-2006\n         \nAcademics\n\n         \nMCA in Computer Science from RGPV, \nBhopal\n with \n69.2% in 2005.\n          \n\n         \nB.sc. in Maths (Hons) from \nTNB\nCollege\n\nTMB\nUniversity\n with 78.5% in 2000.\n\n         \n12\nth\n from BIEC, \nPatna\n with 51.5% in 1996.\n\n         \n10\nth\n from BSEB, \nPatna\n with 72.4% in 1994.\nSkill Set\n\n       \nLanguages\n                              \n\n C# and VB.NET\n\n       \nWeb Technologies\n\n         \n\n         \n\n ASP.NET , HTML, XML\n\n       \nData Base Connectivity\n    \n         \n\n SQL Server\n\n       \nRDBMS\n                                   \n\n SQL,MS Access\n\n       \nOperating System\n                     \n\n\nWindows NT/2000/XP/9x, MS-Dos.\n\nProject Details\n1 > \nSALASAR RETAIL (SR)\nTitle\n                                         \n\n\nSalasar Retail (SR)\nClient\n                               \n\n\nSalasar International Pvt. Ltd.\nEnvironment\n   \n                     \n\n\nASP.NET,HTML,Flash,Sql Server\nDuration\n                           \n\n\nJan\n-07\n\nto Aug-07.\nTeam Size\n                         \n\n\n12\nRole\n                                   \n\n\nSoftware Engineer\n\nDescription:\nThe \nSalasar International Pvt. Ltd\n. is a conglomeration of companies with a highly\n           \nsuccessful chain of mega stores in \nIndia\n. Led by Insight and foresight of a dedicated team the company started its first store at \nRaipur\n, Chattisgarh in the year 2002.One Success paves the way for another, subsequently we have added a chain of seven stores\n\n\nResponsibilities:\n\n\n         \nWorking as Web Developer who involves capturing client Requirements and \nChange request analysis\n for the client specific issues.\n\n         \nTechnical solution, Developing and managing the services from Development and Go live.\n2 > \nOnline Shopping\n\nTitle\n                                         \n\n\nOnline Shopping\nClient\n                               \n\n\nKhanna InfoTech (\nNew Delhi\n\nEnvironment\n   \n                     \n\n\nASP.NET,C#,SQL Server,HTML.\nDuration\n                           \n\n\nOct\n-06 to Dec-06.\nTeam Size\n                         \n\n\n\nRole\n                                   \n\n\nWeb Developer\n\nDescription:\n        \nThis project basically developed for Purchase the different items through\nInternet via credit card. Online Shopping is basically a website develop by our company\n    \nfor EDM Mega Mart located in East Delhi (\nNew Delhi\n). In this site User can registered, create a user ID and proceed to shopping\nResponsibility\n\n\n         \nWorking as Web Developer who involves capturing client Requirements and \nChange request analysis\n for the client specific issues.\n\n         \nTechnical solution, Developing and managing the services from Development and Go live.\n\n\n\nPersonal Details\nName\n               \n      \nSiddharth\nFather?s Name\n        \nDr. S.K.Mishra\nNationality\n       \n      \nIndian\nDate of Birth\n    \n      \nFeb 2, 1980.\nGender\n             \n      \nMale\nMarital Status\n\n      \nSingle\nLanguages \n      \n      \nHindi & English\nHobbies\n                 \nPlaying cricket, Activity participate in Cultural Activities at School and College.\n\nI hereby declare that the above information is true to the best of my knowledge\n\n                                                                                                       \n        \n                                                                                        \nSiddharth',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-18',NULL,'2007-10-18','2010-06-09 12:13:49','2010-06-09',2,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(196,'Suresh',NULL,NULL,NULL,'suredvvssdvsdah806@gmail.com','suresh806@gmail.com',NULL,'0','919871307969','0',NULL,'0','2007-04-30',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-09 12:13:49',3,'0',NULL,'200710/18/ATT19249.html','200710/18/DOC16320.doc','Resdex @ naukri.com\nSuresh\nsuredvvssdvsdah806@gmail.com\n\nTelephone: 919871307969\n(M)\n\nD.O.B\n - 15 May 1979 \nModified on\n - 25 Sep 2007 \nAnnual Salary\n - INR 3 Lac(s) 60 Thousand \nTotal Years of Experience\n - 3 Year(s) 0 Month(s) \nCurrent Location\n - Gurgaon \nPreferred Location\n - Anywhere in India \nMCA with 3 years exp in Microsoft Technologies\n\nTEXT RESUME \n\nSURESH \nMobile\n: +919871307969.\nPROFILE SUMMARY E-Mail:suresh806@gmail.com\n\n Having 3 yrs of experience in Microsoft Technologies ASP.Net, C#, VB.Net, SQL Server.\n\n Developing Web applications using ASP.NET, C#.NET and ADO.NET\n\n Understanding, Designing and coding the middle-tier by implementing the business logic.\n\n Good interpersonal skills and effective team member with motivating skills.\n\n Good Knowledge in Web services, SQL/XML , XML\nTECHNICAL PROFICIENCIES\n\n Languages : C#.Net, VB.Net.\n\n Web Related : ASP.Net, JavaScript, HTML ,XML, web services\n\n Database : SQL- Server, Oracle.\n\n Hardware Skills : Familiar with the basic set up\nPROFESSIONAL EXPERIENCE\n\n Working with InterGlobe Technologies Gurgaon as Software Engineer from Nov 2006 to till Date\n\n Worked in Soft Merchants Pvt Ltd, As Software Programmer from July 2004 to Oct 2006.\nEDUCATIONAL QUALIFICATIONS\n\n MCA (Master of Computer Applications) from Osmania University, Hyderabad.\n\n BCom (Computer Applications) from Kakatiya University.\nPROJECT EXPERIENCE\nProject Name : TCIL\nClient : Thomas Cook\nDuration : Nov 2006 to till Date\nEnvironment : C#, ASP.Net, Web services, XML, JavaScript, SQL Server.\nDescription : The scope of the project is to create Internet booking engine through which users can book flights, Hotels and cars through a secured payment gateway. This Internet booking engine would display results from GDS and ADS.\nUser can search for flights and best available fare using Quick Search option. Registered users would also be able to make customized booking according to their preferences. System would also provide the facility to save search results as a template. User can see and use these templates later. The system should be integrated to secure payment Gateway through which users can make payments online. System would also provide the facility of e-Tickets in addition to the physical tickets.\nResponsibilities:\n\n Involved in Implementation of Flight Module\n\n Coding of business logic Using C# and SQL.\n\n And modifying existing Coding.\n\n Used XMLManager to access the data from (Galileo Distribution System) GDS\n\n Developing User Controls.\n\n Used web services to catch the availability from GDS\n\n Developing XML Validation And Java Script\n\n Unit testing done for the coding of the application\nProject Name : UsaMadeCigs\nClient : Hemi Group Inc. USA\nDuration : Dec 2005 to Oct 2006\nEnvironment : C#, ASP.Net, ADO.Net and SQL Server\nDescription : This website is designed to make online Cigarette Cigar shopping experience convenient and secure. Also provides purchasing of various brands of cigarettes using web through out \nUnited States\n. Any one can Browse thru this site and check out information, incase customer needs to purchase products and add to Basket, once he completes the shopping, then he can check out, at this stage it prompts for Email and password, if that customer is valid it shows the amounts and providing entry for delivery address new features includes \n?Piggy Banking?, repeat orders, offers, order history .Also new customer can click on signup to fill the details. Complicated part in this is with admin interface, as that is the place of \ndoing lot many things such as offers entries, tracking orders, maintaining stock details, sales order report, purchase order report, user report, bar code generation on invoices .Administration can add or delete products which are visible to users, raising orders to manufacturers, invoices, call center user registration etc.\nResponsibilities:\n\n implemented business logic Using C# and SQL\n\n Involved in Admin and User Interface Module\n\n Used ADO.Net to access the data from database in a Web application\n\n Involved in Unit Testing\nProject Name : HOSTELMANIA\nClient : HOSTELMANIA, LONDON\nDuration : Dec 2004 to Nov 2005\nEnvironment : Windows 2000, ASP. Net, VB.Net, SQL- Server, ADO.Net\nDescription:\n\n Online Reservation System for hostels booking through out world.\n\n Allow hostels to maintain their own Availability/Prices/Bookings, along with the relevant information to their properties.\n\n Allow site Administrators to review / authorize hostels, to produce reports on revenue and maintain information held on the site.\nThe Application operates with state of the art security and we use an International Authorizing Company associated with some of the largest companies in the world, ensuring you are completely secure in booking with your credit/debit card online. Hostel Mania Reservations operates using 128 bit SSL encryption. I was involved in Add Hostel\n?s module. The main purpose of this module is to maintain the details of the hostels. The users who wish to add their hostels to the site enters the details of the hos\ntels, which includes the user details, hostel description,location,directions etc. The user can also upload the images and maps related to the hostel. The user can also can also enter information about the room details which include Room Type, No of Beds, Weekday Price, Weekend price and other facilities provided by the hostel.\nResponsibilities:\n\n Involved in Business Logic Using C# and SQL\n\n Design and Implementation\n\n Unit Testing and maintenance of the project\n\n Creating Stored Procedures in SQL Server 2000.\nProject Name : TMT\nClient : Soft Merchants\nDuration : Aug 2004 to Nov 2004\nEnvironment : ASP.Net, C#, SQL- Server\nDescription:\nTalent Management Tool is an application developed for HR department to handle the resource requirement, recruitment and other related functionalities. It takes care of employee recruitment through direct candidate apply or employee referral, or consultants referral. This product consists of different modules viz., Candidate, Admin, Recruiter, Employee and consultant.\nCandidate module can be used by outside candidates; with this candidate can register their resume with details like educational qualification, experience and skills and also can apply for jobs. They can view their status against the job applied or interview taken. Employee, Admin, Recruiter modules are for internal use. With the use of employee module, employees can refer outside people\'s resume for employee referral scheme, once the referred employee gets selected and joins Soft merchants Pvt Ltd then the details goes to HR for benefits. In admin module, the administration of the product done. This product is role based and roles are set by admin.Recruiter module is for HR People, to search resume, arrange interviews and panel etc. In all the modules there are defined reports available to view the entire details specific to the particular functionality.\nResponsibilities:\n\n Participating in Application Design process.\n\n Coding of business logic Using C# and SQL.\n\n Unit testing done for the coding of the application.\n\n Creating Stored Procedures in SQL Server 2000.',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-18',NULL,'2007-10-18','2010-06-09 12:13:49','2010-06-09',3,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(197,'Sachin G',NULL,NULL,NULL,'sacsdvdvhidvvnkotian@hotmail.com','sacdvdhin_kdvdotian@yahoo.com','2628 3074','0',NULL,'0',NULL,'0','2008-04-29',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-09 12:13:49',3,'0',NULL,'200710/18/ATT19240.html','200710/18/DOC16321.doc','Resume of Sachin Kotian\nRésumé \n\nName \nSachin G \nAddress \n28, Raghukul, Near \nLallubhai\nPark\n, Andheri (W),\nMumbai ? 400058.\nTelephone \n2628 3074.\nEmail ID\nsacsdvdvhidvvnkotian@hotmail.com\n   \nsacdvdhin_kdvdotian@yahoo.com\n\n\nObjective\nSeeking to pursue a global career by working in a professional growth oriented organization, with an emphasis on future growth prospects. I want to work in an environment that promotes teamwork, provides challenges and where one can make significant contributions to the success of the organization.\n\n\nSummary\nGood Experience in the IT Industry (5.06 years), including User requirement study, analysis, design and development, including development of Web Applications on Microsoft platforms with good hands on experience in Project development and implementation.\n\n         \nInvolved in implementation of CMM Level 5 and CMM - I quality standards.\n\n         \nExpertise in Database systems and Workflow based applications.\n\n         \nGood knowledge of Banking processes and systems.\n\n\nQualifications\nPost Graduate Diploma in Management Studies (PG DMS) from Welingkar Institute of Management, University of Mumbai. (Underway)\n\nPost Graduate Diploma in Computer Applications (PG DCA) from \nMadurai\nKamaraj\nUniversity\n\n\nBachelor of Commerce from Chetana`s Hazarimal Somani College of Commerce, University Of Mumbai.\n\nProfessional\nMicrosoft Certified Professional\n (MCP) in Designing and Implementing Databases with Microsoft Sql Server 2000 \nEnterprise\n Edition.\n\nTechnical\nDiploma in Programming in MS FoxPro, Oracle and D2k from Concourse Information Technology Ltd.\n\n\n\nSoftware Skills:\n\nOperating Systems\nWindows 2000 Server\nWindows 95/98\n\n\n\nRDBMS/DBMS:\nMS SQL Server 7.0 / 2000\nOracle 8.0\nMS Access\n\n\nLanguages:\nMS Visual C# .NET (Learning)\nMS Visual Basic 6.0\nMS Visual Basic .NET(Learning)\nMS FoxPro 2.6\nTransact SQL\nVB Script\nPL/SQL\nJavaScript\n\nPackages:\nMacromedia Dreamweaver 3.0\nMS Visual Interdev 6.0\nMS Office XP\nMS Visual SourceSafe 6.0\n\n\nTechnologies:\nMS .NET Framework\nActive Server Pages 3.0/ ASP .NET\nHTML/CSS\n\nActiveX Data Objects/ COM\n\nTools:\nStaffware Business process management tool\n\n\n\nWork experience\n\n3i Infotech Ltd. (Formerly known as ICICI Infotech Ltd.) ? Mumbai.\n3i Infotech Ltd. is a SEI CMM Level 5 certified company that specializes in software development and providing other IT Services such as Enterprise Solutions, IT Infrastructure, Support services etc. For details please visit http://www.3i-infotech.com\n\nDesignation\n          \nSoftware Engineer \nDuration\n                \nJune 2003 ? till date\nResponsibilities\nWorking as a Software Engineer in Application Design, Development and providing Project Support. Responsibilities include Design, Development and Implementation of solutions for web based applications and database backend, developing new modules for existing applications, handling change requests and making enhancements, providing support to critical real time applications, troubleshooting of problems in live applications etc. Responsibilities also include ensuring adherence to CMM Level 5 and CMM? I processes and documentation for the same. Also involved in Client side on-site application support requiring frequent client interaction.\n\nMediline Equipments & Computer Systems (I) Ltd. ? Mumbai\nMediline, a Microsoft Certified Solution Provider and an Enterprise Solutions Partner of Microsoft is\n\na company based in India, specializing in development, training and consultancy on Microsoft platforms. For details please visit http://www.mediline.co.in/\nDesignation \nProgrammer/Developer\nDuration\nFebruary 2000 ? September 2001.\nResponsibilities\n\nWorked as a Developer. The duties included\n  \n\nUnderstanding and analyzing client requirements.\n  \n\nVisualizing and deriving a solution architecture\n  \n\nPrototyping \n  \n\nCoding and Development\n  \n\nMaintaining Code of existing applications\n    \nProviding post deployment support\nResponsibilities also included Designing of prototype based on Client requirements, writing Func Specs, making dfd`s, Coding and Documentation , writing Test cases, writing Database Queries and Stored Procedures and optimizing existing code.\n\nProject Work\n\nDatacenter Workflow Automation \n(DC Workflow)\nClient\nICICI Bank.\nDuration\nJune 2005 ? till Date.\nTeam Size\n4 Members\n\nThe system is built to automate the various workflows currently being followed at the Datacenter and manage inventory data relating to datacenter assets. The datacenter is the central repository of critical systems for the Bank and all activities related to datacenter are critical and time bound with defined TaT?s. The application involves capturing of details relating to assets of datacenter as well as capturing process execution requests i.e. induction of a new server, change management, problem requests, pivoting on different viewpoints viz. Application, Asset, etc. I am also the Quality Leader for the project and am responsible for maintaining the CMM Quality documentation for the project.\n\nEnvironment /Tools\n\nStaffware 9.0, MS SQL Server 2000, ASP 3.0, Visual Interdev 6.0, XML, JavaScript and HTML.\n\nCorporate Infopool with Vendorization \n(Capiti - Corporate Account Opening System for ICICI Bank)\nClient\nICICI Bank.\nDuration\n8 months\nTeam Size\n5 Members\n\nThe system was developed for ICICI Bank Ltd. and is used for automating the account opening process of corporate clients of ICICI Bank. Infopool is a Workflow based system which uses Staffware for defining the workflow process. The system is used for tracking/processing of the cases through the various steps as defined within the Staffware system.\n\nEnvironment /Tools\n\nStaffware 9.0, MS VB 6.0, MS SQL Server 2000, ASP 3.0, Visual Interdev 6.0, HTML, OmniDocs (Document management system)\n\n\n\n\nICICI Markets Projects\n\n\nClient\nICICI Bank.\n\nDuration\n4 months\n\nTeam Size\n2 Members\n\nLeadership Survey Questionnaire\n\nThe system is used for appraisal of senior management of ICICI Bank. The system uses complex calculations and formulas to compute the ratings of the employee being appraised, based on the feedback/ratings received for the employee from the respondents who may be superiors, peers or subordinates. The processed reports are then generated in MS Excel.\n\n\nCheque Protect System (CPS) and \nHigh Value Alerts (HVA)\nThe CPS system captures the Account numbers of some of the premium corporate customers of the Bank, whose cheques can be honoured, even when funds in their accounts are insufficient, up to a certain limit specified in the CPS. The system is also used for uploading/adding new accounts and honouring/rejecting of cheques of the premium customers.\n The HVA System is used for sending alerts to the relationship managers of ICICI Bank whenever there is insufficient balance in the account for a corporate that is handled by the relationship manager, giving details of the cheque and the amount required to be credited.\n\nEnvironment /Tools\n\nVB 6.0, MS SQL Server 7.0, Visual Interdev 6.0, HTML, JavaScript and ASP 3.0, \nADO\n 2.6, IIS 5.0, CSS.\n\n\nPayable at Par (PAP)\nClient\nICICI Bank.\nDuration\n5 months\nTeam Size\n4 Members\nThe system is used for online validation of the cheque (warrant) details for making payments for dividend warrants which are issued by the clients of ICICI Bank to its Customers. The Client issues dividend warrants to its customers as per the different schemes for the issues of the company with an arrangement with ICICI Bank to pay the amount to the customers of the client on presentation of warrants for payment The system provides the facility for uploading of cheque details which are validated with the dividend warrant details provided by the client companies.\n\nEnvironment /Tools\n\nMS Sql Server 2000, JSP, JRun.\n\n\n\nwww.jkaindia.org\nSite made for the Japan Karate Association of India\nTeam Size\nIndividual\nThis site was designed and developed for the Japan Karate Association of India (JKAI), one of the largest and oldest Karate clubs in \nIndia\n. The website is one of the biggest websites in \nIndia\n on Karate-do and provides comprehensive details and information regarding Karate-do and the activities of the JKAI. For details please visit \nhttp://www.jkaindia.org\n\n\nAlso maintained the website \nwww.karateindia.com \nwhich is the w\nebsite of the All India Karate-do federation (AIKF).\nThe website provides details of the AIKF and its activities regarding Karate-do in \nIndia\n. For details please visit \nhttp://www.karateindia.com\n\nThese were done as part of my Freelancing project work.\nEnvironment /Tools\n\nVisual Interdev 6.0, Dreamweaver 3.0, HTML, JavaScript and CSS.\n\n\nOtis E2H (Enquiry to Handover)\nTitle\nIntranet Workflow Application for Otis Elevators India Ltd. \nClient\nOtis Elevators India Ltd.\nDuration\n7 Months\nTeam Size\n6 Members\nThe system was a Workflow based intranet application that was developed for Otis Elevators, which is one of the largest manufacturers of elevators and escalators in the world. This system was built to automate the entire process ? right from the time an Enquiry for an Elevator is received to the time the Elevator is made and erected at the client?s site, thus eliminating the tedious paperwork which was in existence previously. The system was login based with users and roles defined for each region, and integrated data coming in from all four regions i.e. Northern, Eastern, Western and Southern as well as the manufacturing units Kandivali works and \nBangalore\n Works. The application supplemented the existing systems by integrating the data coming in from the existing systems by preparing complex reports, generating alerts and notifications and task definitions. The application proved to be a complex system, with options for role definition, task definition, escalation of tasks, generating alerts and dynamically adding new roles\n\nThe system was a browser based thin client application with Sql Server 7.0 as the backend database.\n\nEnvironment /Tools\n\nVB 6.0, MS SQL Server 7.0, MS Access, Visual Interdev 6.0, COM+, HTML, DHTML, Dreamweaver 3.0, Platinum Erwin ERX, JavaScript and ASP 3.0, ADO 2.6, IIS 5.0, IE 5.0, CSS, XML/XSL With SAX, MSXML2.0, Visual Source Safe and MS Remote Scripting.\n\n\nLeave And Travel Workflow Application\nTitle\nIntranet application for Leave And Travel Application. \nClient\nIndian Oil Corporation Limited.\nDuration\n5 Months\nTeam Size\n2 Members\nThis Workflow based application reduces the paper work and manual interaction. All Employees submitted their leave and tour applications by logging into the Intranet Web site. This site uses the employee?s windows credentials for authentication. Once authenticated, the employee can check the status of leave balance applicable to him/her. The information is picked up from the \nOracle Database\n. Application submitted by the employee is sent to an approving authority for approval. This goes up to three levels of escalations. After the approving authority?s approval the request is sent to the next department or authority for further processing.\n\nEnvironment /Tools\n\nOracle 7.0/8i on Unix Platform\n\nMS SQL Server 7.0 with Link Server and Sql Mail\n, Visual Interdev 6.0, HTML, DHTML, VB Script, ASP 3.0, ADO 2.6, IIS 5.0, Microsoft Remote Scripting 2.0.\n\n\nIPRS (Integrated Personnel Recruitment System)\nTitle\nB2B extranet solution for a recruiting firm \nClient\nInetgen Inc., \nIrvine\nCA\n\nUSA\nDuration\n9 Months\nTeam Size\n8 Members\n\nwww.\nalchemus\n.com?\n is a \nB2C Portal \ndeveloped for the Inetgen Company, which is a \nUS\n based recruiting Company. The site provides various options like job posting, job search etc.\n\nProject is a B2B/B2C proposal for recruiter business.  The primary objective is to analyze and develop a web application, which is a complete business within itself.  The clients of this website are large scale recruiters and staffing business organizations who can manage their entire business operations from their profile based business logins to the extent that they should be able to create profiles and logins of their client organizations and staff.  These client organizations in turn should be able to create role-based profiles of their personnel.  There is a three way billing flow and also many other features such as time sheets and expense sheets for candidates.\n\nEnvironment /Tools\n\nVB 6.0, MS SQL Server 2000, MS Access, Visual Interdev 6.0, COM+, HTML, DHTML, JavaScript and ASP 3.0, ADO 2.6, IIS 5.0, IE 5.0, CSS, XML/XSL With SAX, MSXML2.0, Visual Source Safe\n\n\n\nTDS Package \nTitle\nInternal TDS System.\nClient\nInternal Package (Mediline Equipments & Computers (I) Ltd.)\nDuration\n1 Month.\nTeam Size\n1 Member/Individual.\nThis was an existing package which was made on FoxPro 2.5, which needed some Functional changes and modifications. Also certain enhancements were made to the package for the generation of reports. The package is used by the company for the purpose of deducting tax at source before making payments to vendors, clients and individuals.\n\nEnvironment /Tools\n\nFoxPro 2.5 for Dos.\n\n\nPayroll System (Mediline Equipments and Computers (I) Ltd.)\nTitle\nPayroll System\nClient\nInternal Package (Mediline Equipments & Computers (I) Ltd.)\nDuration\n1 Month \nTeam Size\n2 Members\nThis was an existing package and was designed and coded according to the needs of the client, but was also implemented internally. The payroll process is decentralized and processed separately at individual locations. Further it is sub-divided for Executives and for Other Employees (Staff, Factory Workers, Subordinates etc.). The application requires the processing of a lot of complex formulas. These formulas are subjected to various parameters/variables & lookup tables which differ across locations.\nSome of the basic functionalities provided by the application are monthly payroll records including printing of pay slips, periodic/yearly summary slips, Formula processing (D.A, P.F, P.Tax Calculations etc.), help in Income tax calculations, Leave balances and leave records, Overtime calculations, providing the necessary reports etc.\nThe system also provides other utilities like Login based security, Reorganizing/Restoration/Backup of the database, user role creation, internal system security check and sending/receiving mail. The system is also flexible to incorporate changes in Company and payment policies.\n\nEnvironment /Tools\n\nFoxPro 2.6 for Dos.\n\n\nMaruti Manuals Project\nTitle\nMaruti Manuals.\nClient\nMaruti Udyog Limited, \nIndia\n\nDuration\n2 Months\nTeam Size\n4 Members\nThis was a browser based application developed for Maruti Udyog Limited ? a leading manufacturer of cars. The project involved conversion of the manuals of different models of cars manufactured by Maruti, into browser based, searchable html format. These manuals are supplied along with the car models to the various distributors of Maruti across \nIndia\n. The application simulates a web-like interface environment with CSS formatting for good presentation and ease of use along with text search facility.\n\nEnvironment /Tools\n\nMS Word, MS FrontPage, MS Html Help Workshop, Adobe Acrobat Reader.\n\n\nPersonal Qualities/Traits\nOptimistic and prefer to work in teams for achievement of common objective.\nExcellent oral and written communication skills.\nInnovative and Dedicated.\nAbility to work under pressure to achieve deadlines.\nFlair for learning and using new tools and technologies.\n\n\nReferences \nAvailable on request.\n\nEnd of Resume',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-18',NULL,'2007-10-18','2010-06-09 12:13:49','2010-06-09',3,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(198,'Rajnish K',NULL,NULL,NULL,'DevelopdvdsverRaj@Gmail.com','uriousdvdsvsRaj@Gmail.com','011 25484771','0','9818082996','0',NULL,'0','2008-04-29',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-09 12:13:49',3,'0',NULL,'200710/18/ATT19233.html','200710/18/DOC16322.doc','RESUME\nRajnish K\nE-mail: \nDevelopdvdsverRaj@Gmail.com\n\n\nuriousdvdsvsRaj@Gmail.com\n\nMobile\n\n9818082996\n\nCAREER SUMMARY\n2+ years of overall work experience in Analysis, Requirement Estimation, Project Planning, Design, Development and Implementation of commercial web projects using ASP.NET, C#.NET, VB.NET, SQL Server, JavaScript, XML, AJAX, CSS and HTML. Possess excellent skills in Object Oriented Technologies. \n\nSKILL SET AND PROFICIENCY\nLanguages\nC#.NET, VB.NET\nWeb Tech\nASP.NET, \nAJAX\n, XML, JavaScript, CSS, HTML\nRDBMS\nMicrosoft SQL Server 2000\n\nPROFESSIONAL QUALIFICATIONS\n\n         \nMCSD.NET\n From Microsoft Corporation, \nUSA\n\n         \nMCAD.NET \nFrom Microsoft Corporation, \nUSA\n\n         \nMCA \nfrom \nMaharshi\nDayanand\nUniversity\n\n Rohtak [2006]\n\n         \n?A? Level \nfrom\n DOEACC Society of \nIndia\n\nNew Delhi\n [2004]\n\nWORK EXPERIENCES\n\n1. Nov 06 to Present: ASP.NET Developer, Annik Technology Services, Gurgaon\n\nAbout the Company\n\nAnnik is one of the largest providers of Market research related support, data analysis, data management and programming support to clients around the world. It is \nISO 27001 \ncertified and implementing \nCMMi Level-3\n. It has been working with clients in the \nUS\n, Europe, and parts of Asia Pacific, including \nJapan\n. Areas of expertise of Annik include Data Processing and Tabbing, Data Cleaning, Online Survey Programming, Coding of Open Ends, CATI programming, Data Entry, Web Applications and portals to support data collection and data delivery, Automated Reporting Systems, Data Warehousing, Mining and Analysis, Intelligent Reports and Analytical Transaction Processing.\nResponsibilities\n\nI am working on Intranet Web Applications as a programmer. We strictly follow SDLC steps. For each project, I have to perform following tasks:\n\n         \nGoing through \nSRS\n\nTechnical Specifications\n\nPrototype \nand \nSOW \nfor the project\n\n         \nDevelop library classes for common use, user controls and the web pages as per the requirement of the project\n\n         \nServer side programming in \nASP.NET\n\nC#.NET / VB.NET \n\n         \nWriting Stored Procedures using Microsoft SQL\n\n         \nMaking Database Tables, Triggers and Views\n\n         \nJavaScript\n programming for implementing \nAJAX\n and client side functions\n\n         \nChanges in \nHTML\n created by Designer if needed\n\n         \nChanges in \nStyles\n and \nCSS\n created by Designer if needed\n\n         \nPreparing \nMOM\n after each meeting held during various Phases of the project\n\n         \nUnit Testing\n of self created modules\n\n         \nPeer Review\n of modules created by other programmers involved in the project\n\n         \nMaintaining \nRTM\n for self created modules\n\n         \nMaintaining list of Stored Procedures, Database Tables, Views etc. used on each page created\n\nMajor Projects done at Annik:\nPR Insight Management Effectiveness System (Prime UI)\nClient:\n\nMicrosoft Corporation, \nUSA\nTeam Size:\n10\nTools used:\n\nC#.NET, ASP.NET, \nAJAX\n, Java Script, \n\nSQL Server 2000\nOS:\n\nWindows XP\nDuration:\n\n3 Months\nURL:\n\nhttp://primeui.anniktechnology.com\n\nProject Description: \nThis is an intranet web application. This application is being used by Business team leaders of Microsoft as a new global measurement system. This application provides a user interface based on Microsoft?s UI requirements which shows the prime score, prime score trend and data of Microsoft & its competitors in the form of graphs and reports with much simplicity, using API provided by Cymfony. Orchestra database for user interface is being managed and hosted by Cymfony. We are using the API interface provided by Cymfony to extract data from the Orchestra database. The data is being made available in the form of arrays. We put these data in database using a scheduler on daily basis. Our application uses these data in various modules. There are many filters which a user can apply to view data, make report & display as graphs.\nResponsibilities\n\nI worked on Graph, User Preferences, User Profile and Reporting module. Market Trends are depicted in the form of images and collapsible panel in tree form (using client side scripting) for much detail. Data from Orchestra database is manipulated and passed to flash file which generates graph. These graphs are clickable to view more details on another page. Also there is facility to export graphs to Power Point.\n\nConcept Value Normative Database (CVNDB)\nClient:\n\nMicrosoft Corporation, \nUSA\nTeam Size:\n10\nTools used:\n\nVB.NET, ASP.NET, \nAJAX\n, XML, Java Script, \n\nSQL Server 2000\nOS:\n\nWindows XP\nDuration:\n\n2 Months for Version 1.0 and 1 Month for Version 2.0\nURL:\n\nhttp://74.205.95.74/cvndb\n\nProject Description: \nThis is an intranet web application. This is being used to maintain central repository that contains data for all Concepts. Concepts are various products of Microsoft. This repository data is being used to generate reports of scores of different Concepts and Norms on the basis of Key Measures.\n Key Measures are the measures which a customer keeps in mind at the time of purchasing or evaluating a product. Scores are the satisfaction level of a customer out of 100 for a particular product.\nEarlier this database was maintained by Vantis-ipsos skews towards consumer electronics and durable goods, which was not always relevant to Microsoft. Microsoft wanted that Application should maintain data in a fashion that is more relevant to Microsoft.\nAs the number of Microsoft Concept Values keeps on continually increasing, a requirement arose to establish a Microsoft normative database.\nResponsibilities\n\n            \nI worked on Reporting module of this project. There are some Norms generated by user to compare various products on some key measure. I had to generate report on this user created Norms (called Customized Norm) and some predefined norms (called Microsoft Norm) provided by Microsoft on the basis of various Key measures. Generated Report provides option to be saved on user?s machine in excel format.\n\nI also worked on Version 2.0 of this application. In this version there are some new features which are added to the currently running project. Now in Reporting module, Generated Report provides option to be saved on user?s machine as well as on the server in Report Library in excel format. The reports which are saved in report library can be viewed or deleted by user anytime. There is a new Help section now which was not provided in Version 1.0.\n\nAnnik Information Management System\nClient:\n\nIn-House project\nTeam Size:\n\n10\nTools used:\n\nVB.NET, ASP.NET, \nAJAX\n, Java Script, SQL Server 2000\nOS:\n\nWindows XP Professional\nDuration:\n\nContinuously In Process\n\nProject Description: \nThis is an intranet application, which is being used by management and each individual of the organization. The purpose of the application is to help management to apply business policies and make effective decision. \nCMMi\n policies are also implemented using this application. The management can keep track of the progress of individual job. It helps in generating invoices for various jobs. Also, it helps admin/leader to calculate time spent by each employee on a particular job for the day. The admin can generate various reports to analyze the efficiency of the individual.  \nResponsibilities\n\n            \nThis project is in continuous improvement. I worked on Leave module, Effort Capture module & Client Satisfaction Score Collection module of this project which were not added in Version 1.0 of the project. I did the following tasks in these modules:\n\n\n        \nDevelop related classes, user controls and the web pages as per the logic needed\n\n        \nServer side programming in VB.NET\n\n        \nWriting stored procedures and queries using SQL Server 2000\n\n        \nProgramming in JavaScript for implementing \nAjax\n and client side functions\n\nCurrently I am providing support to all employees of Annik for any problem they face. I am also providing some secure data from database to users which are not allowed by application, on the approval of senior persons. If there is any error in any module then I find out it and correct it.\n\n2. \nJan 06 to Nov 06: ASP.NET Developer,\n\nVRI Software Pvt. Ltd, \nDelhi\n\n\nAbout the Company\n\n\nVRI provides affordable design and technology services to organizations. Leveraging leading edge technologies and its talented delivery team, VRI Software enables companies to gain greater value from their business assets and frees organizations to focus on their core competencies. \nResponsibilities\n\nProgramming for Web Applications using \nVB.NET, C#.NET, ASP.NET\n\nSQL Server\n\n2000\n\nAJAX\n\nJavaScript \netc.\n\nMajor Projects done at VRI Software:\n\nCareer Site (\nwww.Jobsgala.com\n\n\nClient:\n\nIn-House project\nTeam Size:\n\n\nTools used:\n\nVB.NET, C#.NET, ASP.NET, \nAJAX\n, Java Script, SQL Server\nOS:\n\nWindows XP Professional\nURL:\nhttp://www.jobsgala.com\n\nProject Description: \nThis is a jobsite for online recruitment, there are two sections First one is Employer section in which an employer can post a job, search a candidate and Second one is the Jobseeker Section in which a candidate can upload resume, search a job and apply for a job.\nResponsibilities\n\n\n        \nDesign pages using HTML as per the design provided by designer using Photoshop and Visual Studio\n\n        \nDevelop related classes, user controls and the web pages as per the logic needed\n\n        \nServer side programming in VB.NET and C#.NET\n\n        \nCreating database tables using SQL Server 2000 and writing queries to interact with these database tables\n\n        \nCreate windows applications for managing database tables used by the websites\n\nHum Online (\nwww.humonline.com\n\n\nClient:\n\nIn-House project\nTeam Size:\n\n\nTools used:\n\nVB.NET, C#.NET, ASP.NET, Java Script, \nAJAX\n, SQL Server\nOS:\n\nWindows XP Professional\nURL:\nhttp://www.humonline.com\n\nProject Description: \nHum Online is an online business directory that enables companies and organizations to establish an online presence. It gives clients the feature to register with the business directory and get their business card online and also can opt for the other membership schemes in which they get a webpage or a website according to the schemes.\n\nBesides the business directory it has other sections for users to watch.\nResponsibilities\n\n\n        \nDesign pages using HTML as per the design provided by designer using Photoshop and Visual Studio\n\n        \nDevelop related classes, user controls and the web pages as per the logic needed.\n\n        \nServer side programming in VB.NET and C#.NET\n\n        \nCreate database tables using SQL Server 2000 and writing queries to interact with these database tables\n\nHum Online Banners (\nwww.humonline.com/Banner\n\n\nClient:\nIn-House project\nTeam Size:\n\n\nTools used:\n\nVB.NET, C#.NET, ASP.NET, Java Script, SQL Server 2000, \nAJAX\nOS:\n\nWindows XP Professional\nURL:\nhttp://humonline.com/Banner\n\nProject Description: \nThis project is for administrators of VRI S/W only. We generate script to place advertisement of our websites as well as that of Clients of our Company. The generated script is to put at any website; it displays advertisements of different categories randomly. We pay the Website for placing these Advertisements, as per our Calculation. After clicking advertisement, website related to that advertisement is opened in new browser window. To calculate amount to be paid to the owner of the website and to Charge our Clients for displaying their Advertisements we keep track of following things: \n\n         \nWhat was the Category of the image clicked by user\n\n         \nImage Id of the image clicked for an Advertisement\n\n         \nURL of the website on which user clicks that Advertisement\n\n         \nWhat is the IP Address of the Computer on which user clicks an advertisement, so that we know the location of user.\nResponsibilities:\n\n        \nDesign pages using HTML as per the design provided by designer using Photoshop and Visual Studio\n\n        \nDevelop related classes, user controls and the web pages as per the logic needed.\n\n        \nServer side programming in VB.NET and C#.NET\n\n        \nCreate database tables using SQL Server 2000 and writing queries to interact with these database tables.\n\n        \nWrite codes in JavaScript for .js file. \n\n4. Shopping Site (\ngifts.humonline.com\n\n\nClient:\n\nIn-House project\nTeam Size:\n\n\nTools used:\n\nVB.NET, C#.NET, ASP.NET, Java Script, SQL Server 2000\nOS:\n\nWindows XP\nURL:\nhttp://gifts.humonline.com\n\nProject Description:\nGifts.humonline.com is an online shopping site within the humonline.com. It displays products according to categories and sub-categories. Users can select products and add to their shopping cart, register and order products online. The users? gives their credit card number which gets verified by a merchant account before the products they selected gets processed further. \nAlso has an admin section to upload the products and the images with various reports for the sales and the admin team.\nResponsibilities:\n\n        \nDesign pages using HTML as per the design provided by designer using Photoshop and Visual Studio\n\n        \nDevelop related classes, user controls and the web pages as per the logic needed.\n\n        \nServer side programming in VB.NET and C#.NET\n\n        \nCreate database tables using SQL Server 2000 and writing queries to interact with these database tables.\n\n3. Sep 05 to Jan 06: Faculty,\n\nNIIT, \nDilshad\nGarden\n Centre, \nDelhi\n\n\nResponsibilities\n: Teaching ASP.NET, VB.NET, C#.NET, MS SQL and C++ for GNIIT Course as well as CATS Course.\n\n4. Aug 05 to Dec 05: Faculty,\n\nCMC\n\nComputer Education, Laxmi Nagar Centre,\nDelhi\n\nResponsibilities\n\n Teaching ASP.NET, VB.NET and C#.NET as well as guiding students in their projects.\n\nPERSONAL INFORMATION\nFather?s Name\n      \n: Shree Janardhan Tiwary \nAddress\n     \n            \n: B-14, Deep Vihar (Near Rohini Sec-24), \nPrahladpur Road\n\nDelhi\n-41\nPhone\n        \n            \n: 011-25484771\nDate of Birth\n          \n: 08-01-1980\nMarital status\n         \n: Never married\nLanguages known\n\n: Fluent English & Hindi\n\nHOBBIES\n\n         \nListening to music\n\n         \nReading self improvement and technology related books\n\n         \nSurfing internet for reading articles, writing blogs and replying to forums related to web technologies\n\nDate:\n\n\n\nPlace:\n            \n                                                                                   \nRAJNISH KUMAR',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-18',NULL,'2007-10-18','2010-06-09 12:13:49','2010-06-09',3,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(199,'Anand shah',NULL,NULL,NULL,'shah123456@yahoo.co.uk',NULL,NULL,'0',NULL,'0',NULL,'0','2002-10-29',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-09 12:13:49',13,'0',NULL,'200710/18/ATT61735.html','200710/18/DOC16323.doc','Resume of Anand Shah\nAddress: \n9/10, Ganesh Niwas, Plot 115/116,\n           \n     \n\nRoad No. 5, Prabhat Colony,\n                \n\nSantacruz (East),Mumbai 400055.\n                \n\nMaharashtra\n\nIndia\n\n\n\n\n\nmail\n\n\n\nshah123456@yahoo.co.uk\n\n   \nAnand\n\n\nExperience Summary \n\nHaving \n7.2 years\n of IT experience.Sound knowledge of Banking and Insurance domain, strengths in \nObject Oriented Design and Programming, client-server and web-based applications\n. Knowledge of system designing tools like \nRational Rose\n\nConfiguration\n\ncontrol and database design tools\n\nCertified CA Clarity 8.0 PPM tool Functional Professional\n\n\nTechnical Proficiencies\n\nOperating Systems\n       \nWindows XP/2000/NT/Linux\n\nLanguages\n                      \nJava\n\nRDBMS\n                           \nOracle 10.0, MS SQL.\n\nInternet\n\nTechnologies\n\nStruts,JSP,Servlets, Java\n\nScript,XML,CSS,DOM,HTML\n\nComponent Technologies\n                          \nEJB, Java Beans, COM\n\nOthers\n                             \nHibernate, webMethods (Basic Overview), XDoclet\n\nDesign Tools\n\n                \nUML, TogetherJ, Rational Rose, ERWin, TOAD, MS Visio\n\nVersion Control Tools\n\n                             \nSubversion, Rational Clearcase, Perforce, MS Visual Source Safe\n\nDefect and Issue Tracking\n                        \nRational ClearQuest\n\nApplication/Web Servers\n\nWebsphere 5.1, Weblogic 8.1, JRun, Tomcat\n\nPortal\n                               \nVignette Application Portal (Trained)\n    \n\nIDEs\n                                 \nEclipse, WSAD\n\nTools\n                                \nCA Clarity PPM Tool (Certified CA Clarity 8.0 Functional Professional)\n\nExperience\n\nCompany: \n                             \nAccenture Services Pvt Ltd\nDesignation:\n         \n               \nSenior Software Engineer\nDuration: \n                              \nDec 2004 ? Till Date\n             \n\nCompany: \n                             \nTata Consultancy Services Ltd\nDesignation:\n         \n               \nAssistant Systems Engineer\nDuration: \n                              \nMay 2004 ? Nov 2004\n          \n\nCompany: \n                             \nICICI Infotech Ltd (\nnow 3i Infotech Ltd\n\n         \nDesignation:\n         \n               \nExecutive\nDuration: \n                              \nMar 2003 ? May 2004\n          \n\nCompany: \n                             \nHOC India Pvt Ltd.\nDesignation:\n         \n               \nSoftware Engineer\nDuration: \n                              \nAug 2000 ? Mar 2003\n\n\n\n\nProjects\n\n\n1.\n                                              \nBSkyB-eSales\nCompany\n                                 \nAccenture Services Pvt Ltd\nClient\n                                        \nA leading broadcasting company in \nUK\n\nEnvironment\n       \n                    \nVigenette Application Portal, Vignette Content Management\nRole\n                                          \nAnalysis, Design, Configuration, Reviews.\nDuration\n                                  \nAug 2007 ? Till Date\n\n2.\n                                              \nClarity\nCompany\n                                 \nAccenture Services Pvt Ltd\nClient\n                                        \nOne of the world?s leading Credit Card Company\nEnvironment\n       \n                    \nCA Clarity 8.0 \nRole\n                                          \nFuntional Lead, Analysis, Design, Configuration, Reviews.\nDuration\n                                  \nMar 2007 ? Aug 2007\nDescription\n                             \nCA Clarity PPM 8 couples top-down portfolio planning and analysis with bottom-up project, programme, financial, and process management. The result is a seamlessly integrated Project Portfolio Management system. The solution gives executives a real-time view into the organisation?s investments, initiatives, and resources, allowing managers to deliver controlled and predictable execution of projects, and programmes.\n\n3.\n                                              \nCRS\nCompany\n                                 \nAccenture Services Pvt Ltd\nClient\n                                        \nFinancial Services division of a leading automobile manufacturer in \nGermany\n\nOnsite\n\nEnvironment\n       \n                    \nJSP, UTCSA-Struts, CA2-EJB, Javabeans, Weblogic 8.1, Oracle10, Synergy, XDoclet \nRole\n                                          \nDesign, Development, Code Review, Testing. Involved in Reviews and Financials modules.\nDuration\n                                  \nJul 2006 ? Feb 2007\nDescription\n                             \nCredit Risk Rating Web application to analyze financial status of automobile dealers in order to provide them with credits to purchase cars.\n\n4.\n                                              \nECB Data Integration\nCompany\n                                 \nAccenture Services Pvt Ltd\nClient\n                                        \nOne of the Leading Bank in \nGermany\n\nOnsite\n\nEnvironment\n       \n                    \nWeb Methods EAI Platform\nRole\n                                          \nDevelopment\nDuration\n                                  \nMay 2006 ? Jun 2006\nDescription\n                             \nThis project scoped to prepare a demo to demonstrate the integration of the tender bidding system between ECB and NCB on the WebMethods EAI platform. Was involved in coordinating with webMethods team to develop the demo. \n\n\n5.\n                                              \nRegulatory Employee Profile System\nCompany\n                                 \nAccenture Services Pvt Ltd\nClient\n                                        \nOne of the leading Financial Institution\nEnvironment\n       \n                    \nJSP, Struts, Weblogic, DB2, Clearcase\nRole\n                                          \nDesigner, Developer, Testing\nDuration\n                                  \nSep 2005 ? Feb 2006\nDescription\n                             \nOnline application to increase cost efficiency of GS through common portal to manage business processes for employees.\n\n6.\n                                              \nVitalExpress\nCompany\n                                 \nAccenture Services Pvt Ltd\nClient\n                                        \nVital\nEnvironment\n       \n                    \nJSP, Struts, EJB, Hibernate, Informix, WSAD 5.1, Rational Clearcase, ClearQuest\nRole\n                                          \nDesign, Development, Testing\nDuration\n                                  \nDec 2004 ? Aug 2005\nDescription\n                             \nOnline management tool that gives acquirers the ability to automate their credit review and enrollment operations of new merchant accounts. It provides straight-through processing of a new merchant application, from credit review and approval, to boarding accounts on terminal management and merchant accounting systems.\n\n\n7.\n                                              \nSBI Life\nCompany\n                                 \nTata Consultancy Services Ltd\nClient\n                                        \nSBI Life Insurance Company Ltd.\nEnvironment\n       \n                    \nGraphTalk, JSP, Servlets, Weblogic Portal 4.0, Java Script, Oracle 8i.\nRole\n                                          \nModule Lead\nDuration\n                                  \nMay 2004 ? Nov 2004\nDescription\n                             \nPolicy Management System used by SBI Life Insurance Company.\n         \n\n\n\n\n8.\n                                              \nNon Resident Indian Speed Remittance\nCompany\n                                 \nICICI Infotech Ltd\nClient\n                                        \nICICI Bank\nEnvironment\n       \n                    \nJSP, Java Beans, Java Script, DOM, HTML, CSS, Tomcat Oracle 8i & Linux.\nRole\n                                          \nModule Lead, DPC. Responsibilities include interacting with Client, understanding requirements, estimation, implementation and testing.\nDuration\n                                  \nApr 2003 ? May 2004\nDescription\n                             \nIt?s a web based system, which is being used by ICICI Bank and its Foreign Exchange Houses/Banks to transfer remittance from a foreign country to an Indian bank.\n\n    \n                                             \n    \n9.\n                                              \nProject Pulse\nCompany\n                                 \nHOC India Pvt Ltd\nClient\n                                        \nHOC India Pvt Ltd\nEnvironment\n       \n                    \nJSP, Java Beans, Java Script, JRun, Oracle 8i & Rational Rose\nRole\n                                          \nDesign, Development. Involved in analysis, design and implementation of DWF module.\nDuration\n                                  \nApr 2002 ? Mar 2003\nDescription\n                             \nThis web-based Intranet system has two modules document workflow management (DWF) and knowledge management (KMS). The DWF module automates the routing of documents to users responsible for working on them with secure access and ensures that documents move along at prescribed pace and appropriate person processes in the correct order.\n\n10.\n                                           \nSDI Web\nCompany\n                                 \nHOC India Pvt Ltd\nClient\n                                        \nShah Diamonds, Inc, \nUSA\nEnvironment\n       \n                    \nJSP, EJB, Java Beans, Java Script, TomCat & SQL Server 7.0.\nRole\n                                          \nDevelopment.\nDuration\n                                  \nAug 2001 ? Mar 2002\nDescription\n                             \nTrading website-involving Customer trading like jewelry search, shopping, sales order invoice and memo generation, vendor management, administration and automated email.\n\n11.\n    \nClient Service Management System\nCompany\n                                 \nHOC India Pvt Ltd\nClient\n                                        \nSun Management Systems, \nUK\nEnvironment \n                          \nVB 6.0, COM, Oracle8i, System Architect, ERWin\nRole\n                                          \nModule Lead, Testing Coordinator\n                                                  \nDeveloped a full module ?Order Management ? of the system. . Created Analysis diagrams, class diagrams & ER diagrams using System Architect.\nDuration\n                                  \nAug 2000 ? Jul 2001\nDescription\n                             \nThis is a data migration project from Ingress to Oracle 8i. The front end used was Visual Basic 6.0. The project completely automates the business transaction of a company.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nPersonal\n\nDate of Birth\n                         \n20\nth\n July 1976\nNationality\n                            \nIndian\nPassport No.\n                         \nE7224082 ? Expiry in \n28-10-2013\nLanguages \n                           \nEnglish, Hindi, Gujarati, Marathi, Kutchi and German (very basic)\n\nQualifications\n\nFeb 2000-July 2000\n                                                                                                                           \nPGDAC\n                                                                 \nYCP-AIT, Mumbai\nCDAC, \nPune\n\nIndia\n\n1996-1999\nB.E (Computer Engineering) \n                           \nRGI\nT, Mumbai\nMumbai University\n\nIndia\n\n1992 ? 1996\nDiploma in Industrial Electronics\n    \n                \nBVIT, New Mumbai\nM.S BTE, \nMumbai\n\nIndia\n\n1981- 1992\nSSC \n                                                       \n                \nFr \nAgnel\nTech\nHigh School\n\nMumbai\n\nIndia\nBoard of Secondary Education\n\n\n\nI hereby declare that the information is correct and true to the best of my knowledge\n           \n                 \n           \n               \n\nAnand Shah',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-18',NULL,'2007-10-18','2010-06-09 12:13:49','2010-06-09',13,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(200,'Amita Kumar',NULL,NULL,NULL,'nandy21567@gmail.com',NULL,NULL,'0','91 9986785628','0',NULL,'0','2008-04-29',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-10 12:14:22',13,'0',NULL,'200710/18/ATT61736.html','200710/18/DOC16324.doc','                        \n\nAMITA KUMAR\n\n\nPhone No.: +\n91 9986785628\n                                             \n     \nE-mail: nandy21567@gmail.com\n\n\n\nObjective:\n                                        \n\n\nTo excel professionally, gaining experience in a growth oriented organization where I can enhance my knowledge base and contribute towards the success of the organization.\n\n\n\nExperience Summary:\n\n\n\n         \nAbove \n2+ years\n of professional experience in \nJava\n and \nJ2EE\n platform.\n\n         \nExperience in Core Java.\n\n         \nFirm Programming skill in \nJSP\n\nServlet\n, Hibernate and EJB. \n\n         \nWorking Knowledge on MVC architectures.\n\n         \nExposure to \nStruts\n framework & Design Patterns.\n\n         \nWell versed in using Application server such as BEA Weblogic.\n\n         \nProficiently worked on various projects using Eclipse IDE.\n\n         \nDatabase Knowledge of Oracle and PL/SQL.\n\n         \nExposure and knowledge of Banking and Insurance domains.\n\n         \nAbility to perform development tasks with minimal supervision.\n\n         \nExceptionally well organized with strong work ethics and willing use my skill-set to achieve project/team objective.\n\n\n\n\nWork Experience:\n\nWorking as a\n Software\n Engineer \nfor\n\nQualiband\n Technologies\n\nBangalore\n\nfrom June 2005\n\nto till date.\n\n\n\nTechnical Skills Sets:\n\n\nProgramming Languages\n\nJava\nPlatform \nJ2EE 1.4\nComponent Technologies\nJSP 1.3, Servlet 2.4\nService Technologies\nJDBC 3.0, JNDI, Hibernate\nFramework\nStruts 1.2, EJB\nApplication Server\nBEA Weblogic 8.0, Apache Tomcat 4.0\nIDE \nEclipse, \nMyEclipse\n\nOperating Systems \nMS Windows 2000, \nXP\n\nNT\n\n\n\n\nProfessional Qualification:\n\n\n\n          \nB.E.(\nElectronics and \nTelecomunication\n\n\n\n          \nSambalpur\nUniversity\n\n\nB.P.U.T.,Orissa\n\n\n\nProjects Summary:\n\n\n\n                                                                       \n\nDTS\n\n\n\nRole\nTeam member\nDescription of Project\n\n\nDTS is a complete collection system for Remedial Management of Customer receivables of any type like Loan installments, Current Account \noverdues\n; etc. DTS is a web-enabled system. It has an interface to accept feed on Customer Information from any product processor. The system also allows Business to follow up with Customers on expected receivables to preserve the Customer Credit Worthiness. DTS provides the ability to\n\nhandle the differentiated follow-ups with Customers of different profiles & at different levels of delinquencies ranging from Customers with Temporary Difficulties & Customers who require a Legal action to realize the Outstanding amounts from them.\n\nTeam Size\n\nDomain\nBanking\nPlatform &Framework \nJ2EE 1.4 ,Struts1.2\nOS & Database\nMS Windows 2000, \nOracle 9i\nTechnologies\nServlet, JSP ,Hibernate\nTools\nMyEclipse\n, BEA Weblogic\nPeriod\nNovember 2006 Till Date\n\nRoles & Responsibilities:\nCoding server- side components.\nDeveloping and Testing of controller & view.\nPeer reviews & Code reviews.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n                                                                       \n\ne@\nBIZZ\n\n\n\n    \nRole\nTeam member\nDescription of Project:\n\nIn a nutshell: The major objective of this project is to develop a web portal for bidding system to make business transactions more users friendly. Here the users have to register themselves as buyer or seller for placing up a tender with their requisites and to review them to give their revised quotations before the administrator prepares the auction procedures. Beside online bidding or web auction and also facilities are provided for virtual store where the sellers can directly place their goods for sale the products which are placed in virtual store are available for online shopping. So the proposed system will provide an end-to-end user environment ease to use.\n\nTeam Size\n\nDomain\nWeb-based Application\nPlatform &Framework \nJ2EE 1.4 ,Struts1.2\nOS & Database\nMS Windows 2000, \nOracle 9i\nTechnologies\nServlet, JSP \nTools\nMyEclipse\n, BEA Weblogic\nPeriod\nMar 2006 ? Sep 2006 \n\nRoles & Responsibilities:\nCoding server-side components.\nCode reviews & Peer-to-Peer reviews.\n\n\n\n\n\n(MI-PPS)\n\n    \nRole\nTeam member\nDescription of Project:\n\nMarine Insurance (MI) is a sub system of CIA application. \n\nPolicy Processing subsystem (PPS) is a sub-module of Marine Insurance.\n\nPolicy Processing subsystem provides all functions necessary to fully automate administration of a policy throughout its life cycle e.g. Automatic calculation of premiums and discounts, Future- and back dated adjustments, cancellation, lapsing and reinstatement with all necessary cash-flow calculations, on-line or batch printing of documents, collection of premiums, matching of payments, etc. \nHandling of cover notes and certificates.\nHandling all communication with Interested Parties.\n\nTeam Size\n\nDomain\nInsurance\nPlatform &Framework \nJ2EE 1.4 ,Struts1.2\nOS & Database\nMS Windows 2000, Oracle \nTechnologies\nServlet, JSP \nTools\nMyEclipse\n, BEA Weblogic\nPeriod\nJuly 2005 ?Jan 2006\n\nRoles & Responsibilities:\n\n         \nCoding Servlet & JSP pages.\n\n         \nCode reviews & Peer-to-Peer reviews.\nDeveloping and Testing of controller & view\n\n\n\n\n\n            \n\n\n\nPersonal Profile:\n\n\nName\n\nAmita\n\nNandy\n\n\nDate of Birth\n\n\n11-May-1982\n\n\nFather?s Name\n\n\nShri\n\nAtul\n Kumar \nNandy\n1-May-19823and Telecomunication)\n\nGender\n\n\nFemale\n\n\nPermanent Address\n\n\nQr.No-G/66,Sector-2,Rourkela-769006,Orissa\n\n\nCurrent Address\n\n\n\n# 23,17\nth\n Cross,26\nth\nMain\n\nMurthappa\nGarden\n\nJ.P.Nagar\n\nth\n Phase,Bangalore-560078.\n\n\n\n\n\n\nDate:\n             \n                                                                     \nAmita\n\nnandy',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-18',NULL,'2007-10-18','2010-06-10 12:14:22','2010-06-10',13,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(201,'Anil sreeram',NULL,NULL,NULL,'anil200@gmail.com',NULL,NULL,'0','9908210508','0',NULL,'0','2002-04-29',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-10 12:14:22',13,'0',NULL,'200710/18/ATT61737.html','200710/18/DOC16325.doc','ANIL SREERAM\n\nanil200@gmail.com\n      \n                                                                        \n+91-9908210508\n                                                            \n    \n                                            \n           \nSummary of Experience\n8 years of experience in the areas design, development and testing of software applications using \nJAVA, J2EE, XML, EAI and WebServices.\n\n         \nGood experience in design, development and implementation of n-tier client-server, B2B, E-commerce and M-commerce applications using \nJava, J2EE, WebServices-SOA, XML, XSL, Tibco, MQSeries, MySQL, Oracle, etc\n\n\n         \nExpertise includes Object Oriented Analysis and Design; Design Patterns and in UML using \nJBuilder Enterprise Studio, StarUML, TogetherJ \nand\n Rational Rose\n\n\n         \nWide Industry experience in \nBanking\n (Clearing and Custody), Financial, Electronic Device Automation and \nNetworking\n (CMS-Centralized Management System, VPN, Firewall) domains.\n\n         \nPrimary programming skill set includes Java, J2EE (EJB, JAXP, JAXB, Java Mail, JSP, Servlets and JDBC), EAI (Tibco, MQSeries), SOA-Webservices, Oracle, Swing, XUI, Multi-Threading, Networking, Struts, XML, XSD, XSL, XSLT, XSL-FO, HTML, JavaScript and CSS.\n\n         \nGood experience in \nOnsite-Offshore Coordination\n, Technical Leadership, Project Management and Team Management skills\n\n\n         \nGood communication and interpersonal skills. Work with \nCMM level 5\n and BS7799 certified companies.\nTechnical Skills:\nProgramming Languages \n\nJava, SQL, PL/SQL, Visual Basic\nIDEs \n\nVisual Basic 5.0, VisualStudio6.0, JDeveloper, TOAD, PL/SQL Dev. XMLSpy, Homesite, Intellij IDEA, JBuilder, Eclipse\nMethodologies/Tools\n\nAgile Software Methodology, UML, Rational Rose 2000, TogetherJ, JBuilder Enterprise Studio, \nEnterprise\n Architect, StarUML\nJ2EE and Internet Technologies\n\nEJB, JAXP, JMS, Java Mail, JSP, JDBC, Servlets, HTML, JavaScript, CSS, XML, XSL, XSLT, Swing, Applets, PKI, Smart Card, JSSE, WebServices\nEAI Technologies\n\nTibco-IM/BW, Adapters-(EJB, File, SWIFT, ADB), MQSeries, jffp parser, JMS\nApplication/Web Servers\n\nJBoss, Weblogic, Websphere, Oracle 9i AS, Orion App. Server, Voyager, Tomcat, Apache, JServ\nPortal Technologies\n\nOracle 9i AS Portal, JPDK, SSOSDK\nOpen Source Frameworks and Tools\n\nAxis, xmlbeans, XUI, JUnit, Hibernate, Checkstyle, Cactus, Avalon, Struts, FOP, PMD, Maven, Ant, Cruise Control, FindBugs\nOther Tools\n\nVisual Source Safe, CVS, Starteam, Jikes, PCAnywhere, Mercury Test Director, Rational XDE Tester, JProfiler, \n\nMicrosoft Projects\nDatabases \n\nOracle 7.x, 8.x, 9.x Ms-Access, MySQL\nOperating Systems\n\nFedoraCore Linux 4, Sun Solaris, Windows NT 4.0 and Windows 95/98/2000/XP.\n\n\nProfessional Experience:\n\nCMS ? Centralized Management System, \nIntoto Software\n\nIndia\nParent Company: Intoto Software Inc, \nSanta Clara\n\nCA\n\nUSA\nCustomer: Redback Networks Inc. \n(An Ericsson Company), \nSan Jose\n\nCA\n\nUSA\n         \n     \n     \n       \n\n            \n(Oct?06 ? Present)\nTeam Leader\nCMS - Centralized Management System eases the management and monitoring of network devices by centralizing the configuration of the physical devices. CMS maintains a logical representation of the physical devices like VPN, Firewall, Anti-Virus, etc; and, allows controlling the devices through CMS. CMS is a SOA-based layered multi-tiered system, allowing different CMS clients to access different webservices to manage, configure and monitor the physical devices in a secure manner. \n\nContributions:\n\n         \nWork as a Team Leader for the Clienttier Framework, VPN and Certificate Manager Application Development. Responsibilities include exploration, estimation, Designing, Planning and execution of the project tasks.\n\n         \nExploration of the Clienttier Design and Architecture for gaps. Designed the Session Management mechanism and Exception Handling Mechanism. Modified the Client App to deploy it as a WebStart Application.\n\n         \nEnhanced the Architecture of the Clienttier and XUI Framework using Swing Custom Components and Business Components.\n\n         \nProposed and implemented the changes in the GUI Framework to increase the Developer Productivity.\n\n         \nRefactoring of the code to make the code more Object-Oriented and Reusable.\n\n         \nPerformance tuning using JProfiler. Profiling the Clienttier and WebServices Layer for finding various memory leaks and Java methods in classes which need to be optimized for performance.\n\n         \nCode Review for the performance bottlenecks and w.r.t the Java Best Practices.\n\n         \nIntroduced various tools like PMD, FindBugs; for simplifying the Code Review Process.\n\n         \nStandardized the Java Coding standards with the help of Jalopy and Checkstyle.\n\n         \nProvide technical and Design solutions to other teams.\n\n         \nManage a team of about 7-12 Team Members for Clienttier framework, VPN, Certificate Manager and some Firewall Modules.\n\n\nnvironment:\n\nWindows, Linux, Solaris, J2Sdk1.5.0, XUI, JBoss, WebServices-SOA, Axis, StarUML, Eclipse, JProfiler, Findbugs, PMD, Jalopy, Checkstyle, XML, XSL, XSD, Ant\n\nCHS ? Capital Harness System, \nMentor\nGraphics\n\nIndia\nParent Company : Mentor Graphics Corporation, \nWilsonville\n\nUSA\n                 \n(Apr?06 ? Sept?06)\nSenior Software Engineer - Team Lead/Java Architect\nCHS provides a set of tools to design the wire harnesses and chip designs. The Software Testing Automation code base built on using the Rational XDE tool. The Automation team?s goal is to make a shift in terms of its role from being a ?Script Generator? to an ?Automation Tool provider?. An Automation framework, loosely coupled with the Rational XDE tool has to be Architected, Designed and Developed to provide a comprehensive solution to the Manual Testing Team to facilitate them in writing Automation Scripts without much programming background. \n\nContributions:\n\n         \nWork as a Java Architect/Technical Lead for the Automation team.\n\n         \nPropose solutions to redesign and to refactor the existing Software Test Automation.\n\n         \nRedesign a flexible framework to separate the automation framework from the Automation Tool.\n\n         \nPropose Continuous build Architecture for Automation Set-Up suing Maven, Abbot, JUnit and Cruise Control.\n\n         \nEvaluation of different Java based GUI tools for Software Testing Automation.\n\n         \nDevelop different Automation Scripts for CHS tool functionality.\n\n         \nContinuously monitor and run the Regression Script Suite for different releases of the Software.\n\n         \nContinuously interact with Manual Testing team to get their inputs on Automation for Architecting the Automation framework \n\n         \nCode Review for the performance bottlenecks and w.r.t the Java Best Practices.\n\n\nnvironment:\n\nWindows XP, J2Sdk1.4.2, Rational XDE, Capital Harness System, \nEnterprise\n Architect, IntelliJ IDEA, Find bugs, Abbot, XML, Cruise Control, Maven.\n\nBNP Paribas Security Services, \nParis\nAceTP Global Re-engineering Project-Milan\n                                       \n(Jan?05 ? Mar?06)\nTeam Lead/Technical Leader ? Onsite Coordinator\nAceTP Global Re-engineering Project is aimed at re-engineering the legacy Security Services to J2EE. AceTP is based on Model Driven Architecture for n-tier applications and is an iterative development process. BNP Paribas being the leading provider of Security Services in \nEurope\n and hence, the AceTp system covers the Clearing and Custody activities of BP2S ? BNP Paribas Security Services.\n\nContributions:\n\n         \nWork as Onsite Coordinator for the Offshore-team, Onsite Team Leader and Technical Lead.\n\n         \nCommunication facilitation: Give continuous feedback to the Offshore-team for the improvement areas and customer feedback. Participate in weekly Management and Technical Conf. Calls with both Onsite and Offshore.\n\n         \nTransfer knowledge to offshore team and increase their knowledge base.\n\n         \nProvide right visibility to both onsite and offshore teams in a neutral manner.\n\n         \nSupport Offshore-team by directly involving in the development and defect fixing to ensure timely delivery with proper quality.\n\n         \nWork with the Users to help the Offshore-team clarify the functional requirements and also support the User during testing.\n\n         \nInvolved in the Development of Non-Regression Test Cases for different Use Cases and also for performing the End-to-End Tests.\n\n         \nMentor\n, Manage and Lead an onsite team of 3-4 Developers. Responsible for the Development and Testing of various Clearing Comms. Layer flows (both Inbound and Outbound) to interact with other systems using Java, Tibco (Integration Manager and Custom Adapters) and MQ-Series. Inbound flows involved mainly Flat file loading and some SWIFT Injection. Responsible for design and development of Duality management software for Milan Clearing flows.\n\n         \nContinuous involvement in the quality related activities like providing Checkstyle checks to make the application multi-branch by removing hard coding, suggesting new tools and technologies for improving the code quality.\n\n         \nProvide frameworks to Automate the Non-Regression Testing.\n\nAutomation for the SWIFT injection and Flat File loading to cater for Non-Regression End-to-End tests\n\n\n\nnvironment:\n\nWindows XP, JBoss, J2Sdk1.4.8, Tibco ? IM, Custom EJB Adapter, ADB, File Adapter, MQ Adapter, MQSeries, Hibernate, JUnit, Checkstyle, Pl/SQL Developer, Swing (Whirl), Ant, Maven, Log4j, Starteam, IntelliJ IDEA, JBuilder Enterprise Studio\n\nBNP Paribas Security Services, \nParis\nAceTP Global Re-engineering Project-Frankfurt/Milan\n                                  \n(Apr?03 ? Jan?05)\nSystems Manager - Technical Leader\nAceTP Global Re-engineering Project is aimed at re-engineering the legacy Security Services to J2EE. AceTP is based on Model Driven Architecture for n-tier applications and is an iterative development process. BNP Paribas being the leading provider of Security Services in \nEurope\n and hence, the AceTp system covers the Clearing and Custody activities of BP2S ? BNP Paribas Security Services.\n\nContributions:\n\n         \nWork as Technical Leader and \nMentor\n to Development Team members. Work in the Custody and Reference Data Modules. \n\n         \nDeveloped plug-ins for TogetherJ 6.0 and merge tool to help complex merging of Java files with different views in Starteam.\n\n         \nInvolved in the Exploration and Detailed Design of the Use Cases using JBuilder Enterprise Studio.\n\n         \nInvolved in the estimation, code reviews, client communication and in the Delivery Process.\n\n         \nInvolved in the Training of New Team members and Mentoring Junior and Senior Developers.\n\n         \nInvolved in Modeling and Code generation of Data Accessor classes, Business Classes and EJB files from Rational Rose.\n\n         \nInvolved in the development of Test Cases for Data Accessor and Business classes using JUnit and integrating the same with DBUnit.\n\n         \nInvolved in the Development of Swing GUI using Custom Framework (Whirl)\n\n         \nInvolved in the development and testing of the Use Cases.\n\n         \nDeveloped the stateless EJBs and deployed the Enterprise Archive on JBoss Application Server.\n\n\nnvironment:\n\nWindows 2000/NT, JBoss, J2Sdk1.4.2, JDBC, DBUnit, JUnit, Rational Rose 2000, TOAD, Swing, Ant, Maven, Log4j, Starteam, JBuilder, Intellij IDEA, JBuilder Enterprise Studio\n\nBarron McCann, \nDerby\n\nUnited Kingdom\n\nBACSESS-II & BACS-IP\n                                                                                    \n(Oct?02 ? Apr?03)\nTechnical Leader ? Java Specialist\nBACSESS-II is an electronic payments system, which provides link into BACS for a fast and secure means of transferring funds electronically for both payments and collections. The System provides a secure link into BACSTEL (BACSTEL-IP) for Crediting, Debiting, Direct Crediting, Direct Debiting, Multi-day Crediting, Multi-day Debiting and AUDDIS. The system provides configurable Profiles enabling users to have different authorization levels and pre/post transmission procedures and reports. The System tightly integrates into all major Accounting systems handling different formats of the Data File.\n\n\nContributions:\n\n         \nInvolved in the Design of the Architecture of the System and provided XML based messaging solutions.\n\n         \nDesigned and developed Data File Editor, Report viewer using Swing and FOP.\n\n         \nUsed HTTP tunneling to communicate with Servlets from the Applet.\n\n\n         \nConverted the Applet based web application into a Standalone application and a Local Applet.\n\n         \nInvolved in the development of HTML front-end using Struts, JSPs, HTML, CSS and JavaScript.\n\n         \nAuthentication using PKI (Public Key Infrastructure), Smart Card, SSL, Digital Certificates and Applet/JAR Signing.\n\n         \nChecking and Storing Digital Certificates in the Keystore for enabling inter-server communication over SSL.\n\n         \nUsed Java API for XML Binding to generate Java source from XML Schemas; and to marshal and un-marshal the XML messages transported over the network.\n\n         \nDesigned and developed the FOP viewer module to generate ?pdf? reports using JSP, XML, XSL, XSL-FO and FOP.\n\n         \nDesign and partial Conversion of Applet Based web Application to Struts based web Application, using Webcream, Homesite, CSS, HTML, JSP, Struts-Console (to convert HTML pages to struts based JSPs) and Struts-Apache framework (to generate the ActionForm and Action classes).\n\n         \nDesigned Swing-to-HTML/Struts converter. Did R&D on Swing-to-Struts converter.\n\n         \nAutomated the build and unit test process using JUnit, Ant, Cruise Control and CVS.\n\n         \nDeveloped a Bug Tracking System using MS-Access\n\n\nnvironment:\n\nWindows 2000, Apache, Tomcat, Struts, J2sdk1.4.1, Java Plug-In, Smart Card, JAXB, PKI, IIAK, XML, XSL, XSLT, XSL-FO, FOP, JSP, Servlets, HTML, CSS, JavaScript, Swing, Applets, Ant, Cruise Control, JUnit, CVS, Webcream, Homesite, Enterprise Architect, Jikes, Intellij IDEA, log4j and Ms-Access\n\nKPIT \nCummins Infosystems\n\nIndia\n\n(ICOM \nMobile\n\nUK\n\nEverest-ICOM \nMobile\n                                                                                       \n(Apr?02 ? Sept?02)\nSenior Software Engineer\nIcom is an M-Commerce application, which provides secure, authorized, cardholder-present payments by any mobile telephone, linked to purchases.\n\nCustomers are provided with a means of identifying themselves and authorizing purchases and payments using their mobile phone. Customers are provided with Icom ?cash accounts? from which to make and receive payments. The mobile phone stands in place of a conventional payment card. It becomes the payment token, and Icom adds the payment authentication and authorization processes to enable this. The Icom service is used for payment transactions as well as to sell products directly to consumers on behalf of merchants, and will provide merchants with a tightly integrated loyalty product, with the benefits of rich marketing data through the data warehouse services.\n\n\nContributions:\n\n         \nInvolved in the development of Login, Partial and Complete Registration, View and Modify Customer Profile, Make Purchases, Make Payment, Close Customer and Close Customer Account Use Cases.\n\n         \nInvolved in the development of Container Managed Entity Beans and Stateless Session Beans.\n\n         \nDeveloped Messages, Message Handlers, Avalon Components and Services for Using Avalon Framework.\n\n         \nDeveloped the persistence layer components using JDBC.\n\n         \nDeveloped and Tested Unit Test Cases using JUnit framework for different Messages.\n\n         \nDeveloped and Tested Integration Test Cases (in container test cases) using Cactus framework.\n\n         \nIntegration Testing and Functional Testing of the Use Cases on Weblogic Application Server.\n\n\nnvironment:\n\nWindows 2000, Weblogic, Oracle 8i, SQL, JDK 1.3.1, Jikes, Intellij IDEA, TogetherJ, JMS, EJB, JDBC, Avalon, Cactus, JUnit, Ant, AspectJ and TOAD\n\nKPIT \nCummins Infosystems\n\nIndia\n (Qatar Petrochemical Company, \nQATAR\n\nInvestment Proposal System\n                                                             \n(Mar?02 ? May?02)\nSenior Software Engineer\nInvestment Proposal System is a Data-Entry and Budget Control Module for Capital Budgeting and computerization of the Investment Proposal Form. The System provides user-friendly interfaces for data-entry of Investment Proposal Form and other master screens, which are deployed as Portlets on Oracle Portal.\n\nContributions:\n\n         \nCreated Web Provider using XML and registered the same with Portal Server.\n\n         \nDeveloped Portlets using JSPs and JavaBeans.\n\n         \nUsed the Single Sign On Authentication feature to authenticate the User?s Login.\n\n         \nProvided the Access-rights based on User Type.\n\n         \nDeveloped the User Interfaces using HTML and provided client side validations using JavaScript.\n\n         \nDocumented the Deployment process.\n\n         \nUnit Testing and System Testing of the Application\n\n         \nAssisting the Client in Application Deployment on Sun Solaris\n\n\nnvironment:\n\nSun Solaris, Windows NT, Oracle 9i AS, Oracle Portal, Oracle 8i/9i, SQL, JDK 1.3, Jikes, JSP, JPDK, JDBC, SSOSDK, XML, HTML, JavaScript, JServ, Apache, JCreator and Rational Rose 2000\n\nCedar Software Solutions, \nIreland\neProcurement-II\n                                                                                             \n(Aug?01 ? Feb?02)\nSoftware Engineer\nThe Cedar eProcurement product set builds on the strengths of the underlying business processes available in eFinancials Requisitioning and Purchase Order Processing. Users can order products and services from a user-friendly web interface taking advantage of on-line web catalogs. Its a B2B application, where purchase orders and invoices are sent and received automatically through E-mail and uploaded into the system. It helps reduce the time and money spent on processing requisitions. The Users Basket is raised to a requisition and approved. The approved requisition is then processed into a purchase order and sent as a BASDA compliant XML file\n\n\nContributions:\n\n         \nWorked as a mentor to some of the development team members. \n\n         \nInvolved in the development of system modules under a full life cycle. This involved Object Orientated Analysis and Design, Database Design, Implementation and Unit Testing of modules.\n\n         \nInvolved in the proto-typing of the new GUI using the JSP, HTML, JavaScript and CSS. Integrated the code from phase I with the new GUI.\n\n         \nDesign and Implementation of Servlets and JSPs\n\n         \nDeveloped Stateless Session Bean and generated Bean Managed Entity Beans using Entity Bean Generator. \n\n         \nDesigned and Implemented Object Caching and sharing mechanism with passivation and activation. \n\n         \nUsed Ant & Jikes to do builds and deploy the same on customer?s machine.\n\n         \nAdministered and deployed EJBs on various Application Servers.\n\n\nnvironment:\n\nWindows 2000, Weblogic, Websphere, Orion, Voyager and JBoss Application Servers, Apache, Tomcat, JDK 1.3.x, EJB, XML, Servlets, JSP, HTML, JavaScript, CSS, XML, JAXP, Ant, Jikes, Intellij IDEA, Homesite, XMLSpy, Oracle8i, VSS, UML and TogetherJ\n\nCedar Software Solutions, \nIreland\neProcurement-I\n                                                                                  \n(Sept?00 ? Aug?01)\nSoftware Engineer\neProcurement is an intranet based purchase requisitioning and procurement system. It?s an EDI-Electronic Data Interchange system, where purchase orders and invoices are sent and received automatically through E-mail and uploaded into the system. It helps reduce the time and money spent on processing requisitions. The Users Basket is raised to a requisition and approved. The approved requisition is then processed into a purchase order and sent as a BASDA compliant XML file.\n\nContributions:\n\n         \nInvolved in the Design of the Architecture of the System and in the development of modules of the system under a full system life cycle. This involved Object Orientated Analysis and Design, Database Design, Implementation and Unit Testing of modules. \n\n         \nDeveloped Dynamic HTML pages using JSP, Servlets, HTML and JavaScript. \n\n         \nDesigned the eProcurement Basket and Basket Lines using TogetherJ in UML.\n\n         \nDesigned and implemented the session tracking mechanism to manage the user?s sessions. \n\n         \nGenerated and Deployed Bean Managed Entity beans and involved in the development of Stateful Session Beans for the Basket and Basket Lines.\n\n         \nInvolved in the development of BASDA specific API using JAXP to generate the Invoice Purchase Order XML Files from Java Beans and convert the same into Java Beans. \n\n         \nInvolved in the study of Internationalization of applications. \n\n         \nDeveloped client-side scripts using JavaScript for Data Grabbing and to perform the client side validations. Used Java Mail API to send XML Purchase Orders.\n\n\nnvironment:\n\nWindows 2000/NT, Orion, Voyager and JBoss Application Servers, Apache, Tomcat, JDK 1.3, EJB, XML, Java Mail API, Servlets, JSP, HTML, JavaScript, CSS, XML, JAXP, Oracle JDeveloper, Homesite, XMLSpy, Oracle8i, VSS, UML and TogetherJ.\n\nInformation Transfer and Monitoring System\n            \n                                      \n                      \nSoftware Engineer\nThe System is an Intranet application, which helps the user to send circulars across various departments.\n\nNetwork Security System\n                   \n                                                                             \n       \nSoftware Engineer\nThe System provides security in the network by monitoring the incoming and out-going traffic from the network.\n\nBusiness Transaction Management System\n                                      \n                         \n\nSoftware Engineer\nThe System processes the Business Transactions of a leading company in Industrial Engineering based in \nIndia\n\n\n\nEducation:\nBachelor of Technology\n\nProfessional Training/ Certifications/Awards: \nFoundation Certificate in Software Testing\n from ISEB/ISTQB.\nCertificate Course in Software Engineering, \nfrom Complete Business Solutions of \nIndia\n\nBest Senior Developer Award, \nfrom BNP Paribas, Paris and KPIT Cummins Infosystems.\nCertificate of Appreciation for Outstanding performance as Onsite Coordinator in achieving the Customer Satisfaction\n from BNP Paribas, Paris and KPIT Cummins Infosystems Ltd.\nReceived training in Microsoft Projects at KPIT Cummins Infosystems LTD.',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-18',NULL,'2007-10-18','2010-06-10 12:14:22','2010-06-10',13,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(202,'Anil Reddy',NULL,NULL,'Hyderabad','reddy12345@yahoo.co.in',NULL,NULL,'0','9849434458','0',NULL,'0','2007-12-13',7,19,'2010-06-10 12:14:22',13,'0',NULL,'200710/18/ATT61738.html','200710/18/DOC16326.doc','MR\n\nANIL\n\nreddy\nE-mail:reddy12345@yahoo.co.in\nmobile:\n91-9849434458\nOBJECTIVE\nSeeking a challenging career in software development with a definite career path that makes the best use of my design and development skills.\n\nTo acquire a career in to excel as an efficient Employee, developing self and the Team work with.\n\nHaving good knowledge in implementing software using programming languages.\n\nEXPERIENCE SUMMARY\n\n\n          \nHaving \n2+\n years of experience in software development with an earned reputation for meeting deadlines and delivering critical solutions.\n\n          \nStrong knowledge in server side programming with java using \nServlets\n and\n JSP. \n\n          \nGood knowledge in \nMVC Architecture \n\nimplementing \nStruts.\n\n          \nGood Exposure to \nOracle 8i \nand\n MySQL.\n\n          \nGood Konwledge in Deploying applications in \nTomcat Web Server.\n\n          \nKnowledge in\n WebLogic Application Server, JBOSS.\n\n          \nKnowledge in \nCore\n\nJava, J2EE Technologies.\n\n\nACADEMICS \n\n          \nB.Tech (\nCSIT) \nin\nGudlavalleru\nEngineering\nCollege\n\nGudlavalleru under\nJNTU\nUniversity\n\n\nProfessional\nExperience\n\n\n         \nWorking as a \nSoftware Engineer\n in \nIndotronix International Corporation\n Systems (IIC) Private Limited,\nHyderabad\n\n                                \n                                                \nhttp://www.iic.com/\n\n\nTechnical Summary\n\nProgramming Lang?s & Scripts\nCore Java\nOperating System\n\nMS-Dos, Windows 9.x/2000.\nDBMS & RDBMS\nSql,Oracle,MySql.\n\n\nEE\n\n/ Web Technologies\nServlets, JSP, JDBC, Struts, HTML,ISPL Framework(Our Company FrameWork).\nApplication/Web Servers\nTomcat 5.0, Weblogic 8.1, JBOSS. \nIDEs\nEclipse 3.1 IDE, VSS(Visuval Source Safe)\n\n\n\nWORK HISTORY\n\nIIC Systems Pvt Ltd.\n1.\n       \nDec \n2006\n ? till date\nBEACON CUSTOMER INTERACTION MANAGEMENT\nThe BCIM is a CRM product which is used by various users like agent, supervisor, quality and admin working with the call center. The application is feature-rich, Agent friendly and easily manageable. The aim of this application is to reduce the maintenance cost of the Beacon. The project contains four modules namely Admin, Agent,Manager and Quality modules and we have used JSP and Struts Framework to develop this application.\n\nAdmin Module: Admin Manager is the module that allows the administrator to define overall functionality for a call center. The specific set-up provided by the administrator determines an agent?s role.Agents are grouped into workgroups by the skills they posses. Each group is assigned to a supervisor for effective supervision. This Admin Manager module will provide the components that enable to define campaigns, Workgroups, and Agents.\n\nAgent Module: Incoming Interactions originating from various media sources including telephone, e-mail,and the web can be received with the help of Agent Manager. This module provides fully integrated contact management so all the information needed to offer personal attention to the callers is instantly accessible.\n\nManager Module: The Supervision Manager provides a visual means for monitoring \nCall\nCenter\n agents via an Internet browser and workstation/personal computer. With the Supervision Manager,Supervisor can supervise agents from any computer connected to call center over the company?s network or the Internet.\n\nQuality Module: Quality Manager is the module that allows the quality team to monitor the calls attended by the agents. Here they can search for voice files that are recorded by the dialer and can listen to them based on various criteria.\n\n\n\nAs a \nTeam Member\n was responsible for the follows -. \n         \n\n          \nDeveloped Application using \nStruts\n Framework .\n\n          \nDeveloped Action Classes and JSP?s for my\n\nmodule.\n\n          \nUnit-tested the Application.\n\n          \nInvolved in Writing Database queries. \n\n\nEnvironment\n: IBM PC, \nWindows, Struts, JDBC, JSP, JBoss 3.2.1, Sql Server 2000\n, Eclipse \n3.1\n\n\nClient : Beacon Global IT services Private Limited, \nUSA\n\nwww.beaconglobalservices.com\n).\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n2.\n      \nMay \n2006\n ? Dec 2006\nTime Sheet Application\n       \n                        \n\nThe Timesheet is a web-based application which is used by the Consultants, of a particular organization, working at different locations with different Clients to report their work hours on the projects assigned to them. All consultants should submit their total work hours spent on their projects for every 2 weeks based on the Pay Period type of the Client. This web application overcomes the necessity to fill the timesheets manually as Excel sheets and is an automation process. After the consultants submit the Timesheets their Marketing Manager approves the same and based on these the accounting department prepares the monthly billing to the client for the services rendered by the consultants and paying salaries to the consultants.\n\n\nAs a \nTeam Member\n I am responsible for the following development -. \n         \n\n          \nDeveloped Application using \nStruts\n Framework\n\n\n\n          \nDeveloped Client side validations using Java Script.\n\n          \nAction classes and Form Bean classes.\n\n          \nUnit-tested the Application.\n\n          \nInvolved in Writing Database queries.\n\n\nEnvironment\n: IBM PC, \nWindows, Struts, JDBC, JSP, JBoss 3.2.3, MySql5.1 \n\nClient : \nAPOLLO\n\nUSA\n\n\n\n3.\n      \nNov \n2005\n ? Apr 2006\nSree Mohan Auto Service Application (SMAS)\n\nThis\n is a highly interactive web application to reduce the maintenance difficulty of the Organization.\n\nThis is useful for easy maintenance of organization for the tasks like storing information about Customers, Vehicles, Services, Technicians and also send Reminders like servicing dates and personal reminders like Birthdays, Marriage days etc by E-Mail. Also Generate reports on basis of Time interval, names, and monthly etc. Also billing section also be automated according to that services. This is mainly for Automation of services for all vehicles, generating reports, and sending reminders. \n\nIt has five modules\n\n\n          \nCustomer/Vehicle Module\n\n          \nServices Module\n\n          \nReminders Module\n\n          \nReports Module \n\nTo achieve this, complete design and drawing of different flow diagrams has been made under guidance of team lead\n\n\nAs a \nTeam Member\n I am responsible for the following development -. \n         \n                \n\n          \nDeveloped Application using \nStruts\n Framework .\n\n          \nDeveloped Client side validations using Java Script.\n\n          \nWriting Appropriate backend Programming & Functunolity for Mysql.\n\n          \nUnit-tested the Application.\n\n          \nInvolved in Writing Database queries.\n\n\nEnvironment\n: IBM PC, \nWindows, Servlets, JSP with JSTL, JDBC,\n\nTomcat \n5.0\n\n\nMysql.\n\nClient : \nSree Mohan Auto Service, \nHyderabad\n, AndhraPradesh\n\n\n\n\n4.\n      \nJun \n2005\n ? Nov \n2005(Maintenance Project)\n\n\nResource Information Management System (RIMS) \n\nThe \nRIMS\n package provides the tool that effectively manages the organization human resources. It is very simple to process the employee detailed information (recruitment to retirement stage). The purpose of the overall \nRIMS\n Project is to create and implement a new vision for processing employee lifecycle information. \n\n\nAs a \nTeam Member\n\nwas responsible for the follows -. \n        \n\n          \nDesigned the User Interface of the system\n\n          \nDeveloped Application using Servlets & JSP\n\n          \nDeveloped Client side validations using Java Script\n\n          \nWriting Appropriate backend Programming & Functunolity for Mysql.\n\n          \nUnit-tested the whole Application.\n   \n\nEnvironment\n: IBM PC, \nWindows, Servlets, JDBC, JSP, Tomcat 5.0, \nOracle 8i.','Indotronix International Corporation Systems (IIC) Private Limited',1,NULL,'2007-10-18',NULL,'2007-10-18','2010-06-10 12:14:22','2010-06-10',13,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(203,'Gangadhar Isetty',NULL,NULL,NULL,'padhar@yahoo.com',NULL,NULL,'0','91 94403 57192','0',NULL,'0','2007-12-29',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-10 12:14:22',13,'0',NULL,'200710/18/ATT40677.html','200710/18/DOC16327.doc','RESUME\nGANGADHAR ISETTY\n\n(Mobile)\n\n91-94403-57192\n       \n(Email)\n\npadhar@yahoo.com\n                                                                                      \nCareer objective\n\nWith the knowledge in the field of Databases coupled with my Exposure of Commercial Software applications as Database Administrator\n\nseek a long-term career in the field of Database management in a professional organization.\n\nProfessional Summary \n\nHaving\n    \n2 .2 years of industry experience in Database Administration support through \nflorinsa\n technologies\n   \nunder Unix, NT environments.\n\nSpecific expertise in \n\nCloning ,storage \nmanagement,user\n management and backup?s Powered by Oracle systems.\n\nExperience Summary\n\n\n      \nResponsible for\n\nAdministration of Oracle 9i database including installation, creation and planning the Backup strategy on Linux AS 3.0. \n\n      \nCreated and maintaining oracle database in customized manner\n\n      \nTablespace\n\ncreation,space\n allocation and Management of space and Rollback segments\n\n      \nCreating \nusers,roles,profiles,assigning\n roles and profiles to users.\n\n      \nTroubleshooting the space management errors\n\n      \nTaking \nlogical backups\n\nand physical backups\n periodically\n\n      \nImplemented multiple archive log destinations to archive \nredologs\n to the production server to support immediate database recovery\n\n      \nReorganisation\n of \ntables,fragmented\n\ntablespaces\n and database using \nexport\n and \nimport \ntools\n\n      \nTransporting the \ntablespaces\n from one database to another database using import\n\nand export tools\n\n      \nPlanning for backup and recovery of database and maintaining \nHot Backups and Cold Backups.\n\n      \nConfiguration of SQL*NET using \nHOSTNAME, TNSNAMES\n and troubleshooting oracle networking issues.\n\n      \nCreating database links and materialized views\n\n      \nDataupload\n using \nsqlloader\n oracle utilities\n\n      \nEnabling the users operation using \nresumable\n\ntablespace\n\n\n      \nInvolved in \ncloning\n for generating reports and for testing\n\n      \nAnalyzing tables and computing statistics\n\n      \nImplementation knowledge on \nRecover manager\n utility(\nRMAN\n) for easier and well managed recovery operations\n\n      \nKnowledge of \nDATAGUARD \nconcepts for high \navilability\n solutions\n\n      \nKnowledge of generating reports using \nSTATSPACK\n\n      \nKnowledge of application level tuning using oracle \nutilities:\nTKPROF,EXPLAIN\nPLAN\n\n      \nKnowledge of tracing a \nsql\n query\n\n\n\n\nTechnical skills\n\n                      \nDatabases\n                 \n\n     \nORACLE\n     \n9i/10G\n\nDBA\n                       \nP/L\n                       \n     \n\n     \nPL/SQL\n            \n           \nOperating Systems\n   \n\n     \nWindows95, 98, NT 2000XP,UNIX\n            \n           \nPackages\n                  \n\n     \nMS-Office\n\n\n            \n\nIndustry Experience \n\n\nPROJECT # 1:\n\n    \nTitle\n                                    \n\n       \nGlobal Merchandising systems\n    \nClient\n                                  \n\n       \nGlobal Technologies U.K.\n    \nProject Execution\n               \n\n       \nSONATA SOFTWARE Ltd. ,Hyderabad\n    \nRole\n                                    \n\n      \nDatabase Administrator\n\nDESCRIPTION:\n\nIt facilitates the customer to browse the site and shop various items \nonline.the\n list of items and their prices are stored in the database. customers will be able to order products online. \n\nREPONSIBILITIES:\n\n\n            \nInstalled oracle 9i on Linux\n\n            \nCreating and maintaining of\n\nthe Oracle database\n\n            \nManaging Database Structure and Storage Allocation\n\n            \nCreating users, roles and assigning roles to users\n\n            \nTablespace\n, table creation and their space allocation\n\n            \nManagement of space and Rollback segments\n\n            \nBackup scheduling and monitoring\n\n            \nLogical backups (Exports and Imports)\n\n            \nPhysical backups(Cold backup & \nHotbackup\n\n\n            \nUsed SQL Loader, Export/Import, Database Links\n\n            \nSetting multiple archive destinations on requirement\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nPROJECT # 2:\n\n    \nTitle\n                     \n                \n\n       \nThomson Holiday Packages\n    \nClient\n                                   \n\n      \nThomson, U.K.\n    \nProject Execution\n                     \n\n       \nSONATA SOFTWARE Ltd. ,Hyderabad\n   \n\nRole\n                                          \n\n       \nDatabase Administrator\n\nDESCRIPTION:\n\n\nIs an U.K based company and working on Travel projects on\n\ndifferent stages of software development\n\nLife cycle \n\nREPONSIBILITIES:\n\n\n            \nInstalled oracle 9i on Linux\n\n            \nCreating and maintaining of\n\nthe Oracle database\n\n            \nManaging Database Structure and Storage Allocation\n\n            \nCreating users, roles and assigning roles to users\n\n            \nTablespace\n, table creation and their space allocation\n\n            \nManagement of space and Rollback segments\n\n            \nBackup scheduling and monitoring\n\n            \nLogical backups (Exports and Imports)\n\n            \nPhysical backups (Cold backup & Hot backup)\n\n            \nUsed SQL Loader, Export/Import, Database\n Links\n\n            \nSetting multiple archive destinations on requirement\n\n\n                                   \n\n\nPersonal data\n\n\nName\n                              \n      \nV.GANGADHAR PINISETTY.\nMarital Status\n                \n       \nUnmarried\nSex\n                                   \n       \nMale\nNationality\n                    \n       \nIndian\nDate of Birth\n         \n           \n       \n03-08-1983\nAcademic Qualification\n     \nBachelors Degree in Computer Science,\n                                                                                 \nAndhra \nUniversity,india\n          \n                      \nMailing Address\n                  \nAchiahnagar,Hno\n 1-8-597,Hyderabad-44\n\n                                                          ',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-18',NULL,'2007-10-18','2010-06-10 12:14:22','2010-06-10',13,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(204,'P singh',NULL,NULL,NULL,'pdsdvdsvgvsd@yahoo.com',NULL,NULL,'0','9980981754','0',NULL,'0','2008-01-28',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-10 12:14:22',13,'0',NULL,'200710/18/ATT40678.html','200710/18/DOC16328.doc','CV\n\n\n\nP Singh\n                                    \n          \nE-mail\n\n\npdsdvdsvgvsd@yahoo.com\n\nC/o Anil gaddi, A-2, campus-1\n\n                   \n\nMobile\n: 9980981754\n    \n\nKristal galena, belandur gate\n\nSarjapur road\n\nBangalore-560037\n   \n      \n                                                                        \n\n\n\nOBJECTIVE\n\n\n\nI would like to see myself working for an organization where I can make use of my potential and analytical attitude for the good of the organization to genuinely contribute \nin\n the growth of the organization. I would like to grow with the organization, in which I can gain experience and become a part of decision - making process, to enhance the value of the company. \nA fun and challenging work environment where my hard work and talent is rewarded.\n\nA company where my ideas and expertise in \ndevelopment\n will contribute to high quality, cost effective solutions for the customer\n\n\n\nWORK EXPERIENCE:\n\nOrganization:\n        \nGlobal \nEnterprise\n\nInfotech\n Solutions (GEIS), \nBangalore\n\n\nDesignation:\n         \nSoftware Engineer.\n\n\nPeriod:\n        \n          \nFrom July 2005 to till date.\n\nOrganization\n\n\n        \nSolaris energy.\nDesignation:\n          \nAssistant Marketing Manager.\nPeriod:\n                  \nfrom \noct\n 2004 ? april 2005.\n                 \n\n   \n\nALL I KNOW\n1.\n     \nMore than 2+ years of experience in Data Warehousing in the role of ETL developer.\n2.\n     \nExpertise, knowledge and hands on experience with Informatica\n\nPower Center 7.1\n3.\n     \nExtensive experience in Extraction, Transformation, Loading (ETL) data from various Sources into Data Warehouses and Data Marts using \nInformatica\nPower\nCenter\n\n4.\n     \nWorked on\n\nInformatica tools (Source Analyzer, warehouse designer, Mapping\n\nDesigner, Workflow Manager).\n5.\n     \nGood communication, interpersonal, analytical skills, and strong desire and ability to perform as a team member.\n6.\n     \nStrong tendency to learn new concepts and very hard working.\n\n\nTECHNICAL SKILLS\n\n\n         \nETL:\n               \n     \n      \nInformatica\n 7.1\n\n         \nOperating Systems\n\n   \nWin NT/2000\n\n         \nLanguages:\n    \n           \nSQL & PL/SQL\n         \n\n         \nDatabases:\n     \n     \n      \nOracle 9i\n\n\n\n\nProjects\n\n1. Client\n\n\nCENTRAL PACIFIC BANK, \nHONOLULU\n\nHAWAII\n\nUSA\n\nCentral Pacific Bank is top 50 bank of \nUSA\n, with its \nheadquater\n at \nHonolulu\n\nHawaii\n\nHawaii\n is an island state of \nUSA\n located almost in the middle of the Pacific \nOcean.Data\n Warehouse is build upon integrated legacy system data feeds received from many divisions of business data sources. This will allow\n\nCentral Pacific Bank\n to continue to analyze the organized data. This Data warehouse would enable both tactical and strategic decision-making and after successfully implementing the customer data at\n Central Pacific Bank\n, GEIS is currently developing the sales data mart as part of the bank?s efforts towards building an enterprise wide data warehouse.\n\n\nDuration:\n                       \nNov 2006- Till Date\nOperating System\n\n\n        \nWindows NT, 2000\nData Base\n\n   \n                  \nOracle9i\nTools used\n\n\n                  \nInformatica 7.1\nTeam Size\n\n              \n      \n16\nRole\n\n            \n                  \nETL Developer\n\n\nResponsibilities:\n\nDeveloped various Mappings, Transformations and Mapplets for migration of data using Informatica Designer.\nUsed various transformations in \nInformatica\n\nDone data cleansing and aggregation while transformation.\nDone performance tuning in \nInformatica\n\n\n\n\n2. Client\n\n\n\nSEARS\n, ROEBUCK & CO. ? \nENTERPRISE\n DATA \nWAREHOUSE\n\nILLINOIS\n\nUSA\n\nSears, roebuck & co is a leading broadline retailing company, with its headquater at \nILLINOIS\n\nSears, Roebuck & co\n has identified the need for an Enterprise DW strategy with business intelligence & reporting architecture and future roadmap as part of their enterprise architecture implementation to support the information needs appropriate for the goals and anticipated growth of the company. The DW architecture is intended to identify a robust, comprehensive, and enterprise-reporting environment (high-level infrastructure need) that will effectively leverage the investment made in operational systems. This will allow Sears, Roebuck & co to continue to analyze the organized data. This Data warehouse would enable both tactical and strategic decision-making. \n             \nDuration\n\n                       \nJuly 2005 -Oct 2006\nOperating System\n\n       \nWindows NT, 2000\nData Base\n\n        \n            \nOracle8i\nTools used\n\n\n                 \nInformatica\n 6.1\nTeam Size\n\n                    \n15\nRole\n\n            \n                  \nETL Developer\n\n\nRESPONSIBILITIES:\n\n     \nAs an ETL Devloper was responsible for \n\n1.\n   \nDeveloping various Mappings, Transformations and Mapplets for migration of data\n   \nusing \nInformatica\n Designer. \n2.\n   \nValidating the ETL Design and development through Unit Testing, \n3.\n   \nvalidating\n the data populated in the database and the data that comes up on the reports.\nThe objective is to extract data stored in different databases such as Oracle, SQL Server and to load scheduled finally into a single data warehouse repository, which is in Oracle.\n\neducational profile\n          \nGraduation in Mechanical Engineering from \nNATIONAL INSTITUTE OF TECHNOLOGY (NIT), \nCALICUT\n\nin\n\nJune\n 2002 with First division.\n\npersonal profile\n\n\nFather Name\n\n        \n      \nSh. Roop Singh\nMarital Status\n\n       \n   \n  \n\nSingle\nNationality\n\n                  \nIndian\nLanguage known:\n         \nEnglish, Hindi, Punjabi, dogri\n\nstrenGths\n\n\n1.\n\nQuick & continuous desire for learning new technologies.\nA dedicated worker having a practical approach to any problem.\n3.\n\nCapable of handling projects independently.\nAbility to blend in a team.\n\nExtra curricular activities\n\nSports\nWon a number of certificates and trophies in the most popular game of \nIndia\n, cricket. I have represented my college in \nthe inter\n- college cricket tournaments and university in the inter- university games, also take keen interest in watching other famous international games like lawn tennis, hockey, football as well. \nSchool\nI passed my 10\nth\n level exams with first division and had done exceptionally well in the 12\nth\n standard by securing 82.3% marks. I have also won a number of prizes, while participating in the seminars and debates. \nHobbies:\nWatching cricket from close quarters, in spite of \nIndia\n\'s pathetic performance every now and then \nI do take pride in recognizing \nsingers\n voice singing Hindi songs and \nghazals',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-18',NULL,'2007-10-18','2010-06-10 12:14:22','2010-06-10',13,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(205,'Ram Reddy',NULL,NULL,NULL,'mddvode.jydvdvothi@yahoo.co.in',NULL,'040 23055285','0','9912159038','0',NULL,'0','2007-04-30',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-10 12:14:22',13,'0',NULL,'200710/18/ATT40122.html','200710/18/DOC16329.doc','Resdex @ naukri.com\nmddvode.jydvdvothi@yahoo.co.in\n\nTelephone: 9912159038\n(M)\n 040 23055285\n(R)\n\nD.O.B\n - 12 Jul 1980 \nModified on\n - 25 Sep 2007 \nAnnual Salary\n - INR 3 Lac(s) 20 Thousand \nTotal Years of Experience\n - 3 Year(s) 1 Month(s) \nCurrent Location\n - Hyderabad \nPreferred Location\n - Anywhere in South India \nworking as ERP Developer',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-18',NULL,'2007-10-18','2010-06-10 12:14:22','2010-06-10',13,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(206,'Ravi L',NULL,NULL,NULL,'jvdvdvainz@rediffmail.com',NULL,NULL,'0','9833566308','0',NULL,'0','2005-04-29',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-10 12:14:22',13,'0',NULL,'200710/18/ATT40123.html','200710/18/DOC16330.doc','Resdex @ naukri.com\njvdvdvainz@rediffmail.com\n\nTelephone: 9833566308\n(M)\n\n(R)\n\nD.O.B\n - 20 Mar 1975 \nModified on\n - 25 Sep 2007 \nAnnual Salary\n - INR 7 Lac(s) 0 Thousand \nTotal Years of Experience\n - 5 Year(s) 0 Month(s) \nCurrent Location\n - Mumbai \nPreferred Location\n - No preference \nMBA ( Mktg, Systems ), BE ( EnC ), 1.5 yrs of SAP Experience',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-18',NULL,'2007-10-18','2010-06-10 12:14:22','2010-06-10',13,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(207,'A Bezawada',NULL,NULL,NULL,'anil.bgddvdvvvfezawada@gmail.com',NULL,NULL,'0','91 9346234675','0',NULL,'0','2005-01-27',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-10 12:14:22',14,'0',NULL,'200710/18/ATT40124.html','200710/18/DOC16331.doc','101, Sweet Home Venus Appts,\n101, Sweet Home Venus Appts,\nPlot #4, Megha Hills, Madhapur,\nHyderabad\n - 530081\nA Bezawada\nPhone +91-9346234675\nE-mail anil.bgddvdvvvfezawada@gmail.com\nEducation\nB.\n\nTech. - May 2001\nManufacturing\n\nScience\n\n\n\nEngineering\n           \nIIT \nDelhi\n6.7/10\n Cumulative Grade Point Average\n12\nth\n ? CBSE \nDelhi\n -1997 ? \n80%\n10\nth\n ? CBSE \nDelhi\n 1995 ? \n86.4%\nExperience\nTotal: 5+ Years\nAlliance\n Consulting \nIndia\n\nas\n Architect \nfrom\n Feb 07\n\n- till Date\nIvy Comptech \nas \nSystems Analyst \nfrom \nJul 05 \n\nFeb 07\nOracle Hyderbad\n as\n Applications Engineer\n from\n Nov 03 ? Jun 05\nWipro Technologies\n as \nSystems Engineer\n from \nFeb 02 ? Oct 03\n\nSoftware Exposure\nDevelopment \nExposure\n           \n              \nPL\n/SQL\nFunctional Domain\n       \n                          \nGaming, SCM/P, Manufacturing, Utilities\nOra Apps\n                  \n                            \nAPS, EAM.\nCurrent Project\nHAVI ROP\nDescription:\n HAVI ROP is the deployment part of the Mc Donald?s Supply Chain Implementation. \n\nRole:\n\nLeading\n\nthe 4 Member HAVI ROP Off shore team.\n Analysis, Database Design, Development of the DB Assets.\nSkills:\n   \nPL/SQL, Informatica\n\nKey Projects\n\nVirtual Racing ? Ivy Comptech\n\nDescription:\n Virtual Racing is the online gaming site. It?s a part of the Party Gaming Integrated gaming Platform and offers players to play Virtual Horse races and Grey Hound Races.\n\nRole:\n Analysis, Database Design, Development of the DB Assets.\nSkills:\n   \nPL/SQL\n\nContribution:\n I was completely responsible for the analysis and database design. Also I was responsible to deliver all the stored procedures that were needed to communicate between the Java Gaming Server and the DB which included all the transaction handling,\n\nretrieval of data for each player, storing and retrieving each players gaming information. My role included leading a team of 2 people to deliver all these DB assets. I was responsible for code review and tuning of the above deliverables.\n\n\n\n\n\nParty Bingo ? Ivy Comptech\n\nDescription:\n Party Bingo is the online gaming site. It?s a part of the Party Gaming Integrated gaming Platform and offers Bingo style games.\n\nRole:\n Analysis, Database Design, Development of the DB Assets.\nSkills:\n   \nPL/SQL\n\nContribution:\n I was completely responsible for the analysis and database design. Also I was responsible to deliver all the stored procedures that were needed to communicate between the Java Gaming Server and the DB which included all the transaction handling,\n\nretrieval of data for each player, storing and retrieving each players gaming information. My role included in coordinating with junior resources for the development of Reports and Other Utilities.\n\n\nParty Casino ? Ivy Comptech\n\nDescription:\n Party casino is the online gaming site. It?s a part of the Party Gaming Integrated gaming Platform and offers Casino style games.\n\nRole:\n Analysis, Database Design, Development of the DB Assets.\nSkills:\n   \nPL/SQL\n\nContribution:\n I was completely responsible for the analysis and database design. Also I was responsible to deliver all the stored procedures that were needed to communicate between the Java Gaming Server and the DB which included all the transaction handling,\n\nretrieval of data for each player, storing and retrieving each players gaming information. Also I was responsible for delivering the html based reports written using Oracle HTP package.\n\n\n\nMeter Hierarchy ? EAM (Oracle Apps)\n\nDescription:\n EAM (Enterprise Asset Management) helps customer in the Preventive and Reactive Maintenance of Assets in an Organization. The preventive maintenance involves raising work orders for maintenance based on usage or some other track-able attribute of the usage. This tracking is done using entities called meters. PM schedules are generated based on the meter readings. As a part of this project the meter functionality is being enhanced to allow user to create a hierarchy in meters where a source counter can feed readings for a set of target meters.\n\nRole:\n Analysis, Requirements gathering, Impact Analysis and Development.\nSkills:\n   \nPL/SQL, D2K \n\nContribution:\n I was completely responsible for the analysis, technical design and development of the entire project. Also the project complexity is greatly increased as there is a simultaneous shift in schema from EAM Meters to IB (Install Base) Counters Schema.\n\n\nDetail Scheduling ? APS\n (Oracle Apps)\n\nDescription:\n This product is a part of the Advanced Supply Chain Planning Solution. This product gives user the flexibility to do a detail level (Operation level) planning. It takes the solution generated by HLS (High Level Scheduler) and returns a Detailed Schedule.\n\nRole:\n    \nDeveloper \nSkills:\n   \nC/C++\n\nContribution:\n   \nI was involved in the development and unit testing of one module of the above products relating to Sequence Dependent Setups.\n\nTransportation Planning ? APS\n (Oracle Apps)\n\nDescription:\n Transportation Planning is a product which would help customer plan all the transportation needs of a customer. It will let user to plan and optimise all transportation from Suppliers Org as well as all the transportation to customers. \n\nRole:\n    \nDeveloper \nSkills:\n   \nD2K Forms, PL/SQL \nContribution:\n   \nI was involved in the very first release of this product. I was responsible development and unit testing of few forms. Also worked on several issues which were raised during system testing.\n\nGemini - Data Migration ? Entry Capacity (Wipro)\nDescription:\n Gemini was a re write of a D2K application\n\n(RGTA) in J2EE. This was being rewritten to make it flexible so that it can accommodate the rapidly changing regulations scenario\nRole:\n Analysis, Requirements gathering, Mapping/Profiling and Developing.\nSkills:\n   PL/SQL \nEnvironment:\n   Oracle 8i (Source) Oracle 9i (Target).\nClient:\n\nUK\nTRANSCO\n\nUK\n Gas Transporter.\nContribution:\n I was involved in the analysis of the existing system ? its Data model and mapping it to the new framework. I was responsible for writing the scripts to migrate data from the old application DB to the new application DB. The critical aspect of this project was tuning of these scripts fit them into narrow down time window. \n\n\nLTA - CBB Build and Implement LTSEC\n/ECBB (Wipro)\n\nDescription:\n RGTA-It stands for Reformed Gas Trade Agreement. As a part of this project LTSEC and ECBB -- Long Term Auctions for selling and Buy Back auctions for buying back capacity were being developed. The development was done in D2K as the front end and Oracle 8i at the back end.\n\nRole:\n    \nDeveloper \nSkills:\n   \nD2K Forms, PL/SQL \nEnvironment:\n   \nWindows NT, HP-UNIX Operating System, Oracle 8i database.\nClient:\n\nUK\nTRANSCO\n\nUK\n Gas Transporter.\n\nContribution:\n   \nI was involved in the development and unit testing of forms for LTSEC and ECBB modules of this project in Oracle-D2K.\n\nOther Achievements \nIIT JEE Rank ? \n869 \n(1997)\nJunior Science Talent Search Scholarship, Department of Science and Technology, \nDelhi\n\nAll \nIndia\n 66\nth\n Rank in National Science Talent Search Examination, Level 5, Universal Trust, Trivendrum.\nAdditional Activities\nRunners up in the Intra Ivy TT Singles and Doubles Tournament.\nActively involved in various sports at Oracle. \n\n         \nCaptain of the APS Cricket Team in the Intra Oracle Cricket Tournament 2005. Member of IDC cricket club.\n\n         \nMember of Oracle Volley Ball Team.\n\n         \nOne of the Organisers for the Intra Oracle Badminton Championship 2005.\n\nVolunteer Project Udaan (2004) ? A major initiative by Ora Volunteers to arrange uniforms for the local primary school.\nActively involved in organising Trans-Sangam ? Bi Annual - Cultural Event of Transco ODC at Wipro.\nEvent Head for Silhouette (Photography Contest) in Tech forum 2003(Annual Tech Event of Wipro technologies) at Hyderabad Development Centre.\nClass representative for Manufacturing Science and Engineering in years 1998, 1999, 2000.\nDOB\nSeptember 20\nth\n 1980',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-18',NULL,'2007-10-18','2010-06-10 12:14:22','2010-06-10',14,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(208,'Kiran.M',NULL,NULL,NULL,'msnrfbfbfdbfbakiran@gmail.com','msnrakiran@gmail.com','91 0884 2359824','0','09908213279','0','09908213279','0','2007-04-30',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-10 12:14:22',14,'0',NULL,'200710/18/ATT40125.html','200710/18/DOC16332.doc','Resdex @ naukri.com\nkiran.\n\nkiran.m 6-114,krishna nagar,yousaf guda Hyderabad / Secunderabad \nmsnrfbfbfdbfbakiran@gmail.com\n\nTelephone: 09908213279\n(M)\n 91 0884 2359824\n(R)\n\nD.O.B\n - 18 May 1979 \nModified on\n - 26 Sep 2007 \nAnnual Salary\n - INR 3 Lac(s) 20 Thousand \nTotal Years of Experience\n - 3 Year(s) 2 Month(s) \nCurrent Location\n - Hyderabad \nPreferred Location\n - Anywhere in India \nBSc(computers) with 3 years experience in oracle Appsdba\n\nTEXT RESUME \n\nRESUME\nM.S.N.R.A.kiran\nmsnrakiran@gmail.com\nORACLE APPSDBA . CELL.NO :(+91)9908213279\nProfessional ExperienceSummary:\nHaving 2+ years experience in Oracle Database / Applications Administration using Oracle 9i and Applications 11i DBA on Linux (3.0).\nEducational Profile:\nBachelor of Science(Computers) from ANDHRAUNIVERSITY\nProfessional Experience:\nWorking as an Apps DBA with SYNTEL CORPORATION, \nHyderabad\n from Nov 2004 to till date.\nTechnical Profile:\nOperating System : Linux (3.0)\nRDBMS : ORACLE 9i\nDBA Tools : EXP, IMP, RMAN, TKPROF, EXPLAN PLAN\nERP Systems : Oracle Business Suite 11i\nLanguages : SQL, PLSQL\nExperience Summary:\n\n Having 2+ years of total experience as Oracle Apps DBA.\n\n Experience includes both 9i DBA & Oracle Applications 11i DBA.\n\n Installations of Oracle Ebusiness Suite11i (Single & Multi Nodes)\n\n Cloning the Oracle 11i production instance for test environment and vice versa using Rapid clone utility.\n\n Patching on 11i instance (RDBMS , Applications) for the product enhancements, Resolving bugs etc\n\n Maintaining the Oracle Applications using adutilities such as adadmin, adpatch, adcontroller etc.\n\n Managing concurrent manager activities.\n\n Performing sysadmin tasks such as creating and managing users, responsibilities.\n\n Changing passwords using FNDCPASS utility.\n\n Oracle 9i Installation on Red Hat Enterprise Linux as Release 3.0.\n\n Creating Databases according to clients need by generating scripts or by Database Configuration Assistant\n\n Maintaining Tablespaces, Control file, Redo log file, Data files..\n\n Creation of oracle roles, granting privileges and profiles etc.\n\n Performing physical, logical Backup and also Recovery:\n\n Monitoring the database by collecting statistics of instance by SQL trace, TKPROF, STATSPACK, EXPLAN PLAN to find ways to improve the database\n?s performance.\n\n Database upgradation from 9.2.0.4 to 9.2.0.7\n\n Documenting Database activities.\nProject Summary:\nProject:1\nProject : Maintenance of Oracle applications (11.5.9)\nPlatform : Linux 3.0\nEnvironment : Oracle Applications 11.5.9\nDesignation : Apps Database Administrator\nRole : Managing OracleE-Business Suite 11i in 24 X 7 days environment\nthis includes cloning for test environment, Patching for bugs.\nResponsibilities:\n\n Interacting with the customer to understand their requirements and their Technical queries.\n\n Installation of Oracle Apps 11.5.9 (single/dual node) on Linux 3.0.\n\n To check Oracle Application services like Form Server, Report Server, Concurrent Manager to ensure availability at specific scheduled times and generating reports.\n\n Maintaining the Oracle Applications using adutilities such as adadmin, adpatch, adcontroller etc.\n\n Applying Database/Application Patches using Opatch and adpatch utilities.\n\n Cloning the applications for test purpose using Rapid Clone.\n\n Changing the oracle users, apps passwords using FNDCPASS utility.\n\n Refreshing / Cloning the Test and Development database as per user\n?s request.\n\n Creating users assigning responsibilities as a sysadmin task.\n\n Managing concurrent manager activities\n\n General trouble shooting like removing yellow bar, Jinitiator Problems.\n\n Backup and Recovery management of Application and Database.\n\n General Dba tasks such as managing tablespaces, controlfiles, redofiles, and datafies.\n\n Collecting the database statistics using statspack, explain plan, tkprof.\nProject:2\nProject : Installation and Maintenance of Oracle applications (11.5.9)\nPlatform : Linux 3.0\nEnvironment : Oracle Applications 11.5.9\nDesignation : Apps Database Administrator\nRole : Managing OracleE-Business Suite 11i in 24 X 7 days environment\nthis includes cloning the applications for test environment, patching\nactivities for the issues, refreshing the database.\nResponsibilities:\n\n Interacting with the customer to understand their requirements and their Technical queries.\n\n Installation of Oracle Apps 11.5.9 (single/dual node) on Linux 3.0.\n\n Checking Oracle Application services like Form Server, Report Server, Concurrent Manager.\n\n Maintaining the Oracle Applications using adutilities such as adadmin, adpatch, adcontroller etc.\n\n Applying Database/Application Patches using Opatch and Ad patch utilities.\n\n Cloned the production database for test/dev.\n\n Database cloning and renaming the database using controlfile.\n\n Day to Day activities of dba such as maintaining control files, redolog files, data files.\n\n Performing logical, physical backups and recovery.\nProject:3\nProject : Upgradation of database from 9.2.0.4 to 9.2.0.7 and Maintanence\nOf database 9.2.0.7\nPlatform : Linux 3.0\nEnvironment : Oracle Database 9.2.0.7\nDesignation : Apps Database Administrator\nRole : Managing Oracle Database 9.2.0.7 in 24 X 7 days environment this\nincludes refreshing the database for test environment, maintaining the\ndatabase.\nResponsibilities:\n\n Maintenance of Oracle Databases as per the requirement.\n\n Managing the logical objects of the Databases.\n\n Monitoring and Analyzing the Index for segment fragmentation.\n\n Checking Alert Log file for errors and making necessary actions to rectify them.\n\n Managing the roles and privileges.\n\n Killing unwanted user sessions or processes.\n\n Monitoring the database growth.\n\n Creation of schema with quota maintenance.\n\n Refreshing the database.\n\n Upgraded the database from 9.2.0.4 to 9.2.0.7.\n\n Performing database activities such as creating and maintaining tablespaces, redo log files, datafiles.\n\n Collecting the statistics of the database using STATSPACK, TKPROF, EXPLAIN PLAN.\n\n Backup : Cold Back, Hot Backup and Logical Backup\n\n Recovery : Complete & Incomplete recovery',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-18',NULL,'2007-10-18','2010-06-10 12:14:22','2010-06-10',14,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(209,'Harmanpreet',NULL,NULL,'Ludhiana','hfbar_jdfbfbas@rediffmail.com','har_jas@rediffmail.com','91 0161 2464077','0','9888512412','0','0175 2370305','0','2007-12-13',10,34,'2010-06-10 12:14:22',14,'0',NULL,'200710/18/ATT40128.html','200710/18/DOC16333.doc','Resdex @ naukri.com\nharmanpreet \n50 ff h.i.g flats rajguru nagar Ludhiana - 141001 \nhfbar_jdfbfbas@rediffmail.com\n\nTelephone: 9888512412\n(M)\n 91 0161 2464077\n(R)\n\nD.O.B\n - 24 Jun 1982 \nModified on\n - 25 Sep 2007 \nAnnual Salary\n - INR 1 Lac(s) 60 Thousand \nTotal Years of Experience\n - 2 Year(s) 6 Month(s) \nCurrent Location\n - Ludhiana \nPreferred Location\n - No preference \nMCA with 1 year , 6 months of experience as an instructor,counselor, administrator\n\nTEXT RESUME \n\nCurriculum Vitae\nHarmanpreet Kaur\n50 ff, h i. g flats, Rajguru Nagar Ph.:(R) (0161) 2464077, \nMobile\n: 9888512411\nLudhiana\n\nPunjab\n e-mail: har_jas@rediffmail.com\nObjective To emerge as a successful team leader with hard work, dedication, high motivation, and dynamism, through the integration of personal goals with organizational goals.\nProfileExperience Result-focused, sincere and hardworking, skilled at completing work on time under stressed conditions, both individually and as a team member. Recognized for:§ Strong analytical & Communication skills with problem solving ability.§ Quick grasping nature.§ Worked as a web trainer for a year in trading company\nEducational Qualification § Masters of computer applications 2002 \n? 2005\n Shri Guru Harkrishan College of Management and Technology, Patiala, Affiliated to Punjabi University, Patiala, Punjab, with aggregate of 72%§ Bachelor of Computer Applications (B.C.A)1999 \n? 2001\n Punjab College of Technical Education, Ludhiana, Affiliated to Punjab Technical University, Jalandhar, Punjab, India.\nComputer Proficiency · MS-Office (\nMS-Word\n\nMS\n-Excel, MS-PowerPoint)· Internet Applications· Languages (C, C++, Java, V.B)· Database (SQL Server)\nSpecialization § Database, doing course in database administration\nOrganizational Skills § Co-operative, hardworking, Team spirit , Self-Motivating , Good Communication Skills\nStrength § Confident, Honest, Optimistic\nReferences § Mr. S.R Sahni, Director, S.G.H.C.M.T Patiala. Phone: 0175 2370305\nPersonal Details § Date of Birth : 24th June , 1982§ Gender : Female§ Father\n?s Name\n : S. C.K.S Brar§ Marital Status : Single§ Proficient in written and spoken : English, Hindi & Punjabi\nDate:\nPlace: \nLudhiana\n, India Harmanpreet Kaur.','Not Mentioned',1,NULL,'2007-10-18',NULL,'2007-10-18','2010-06-10 12:14:22','2010-06-10',14,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(210,'Abhishek Midha',NULL,NULL,NULL,'abhirtregshek.midhrgrega@yahoo.co.in',NULL,'09871107682','0','09891975643','0','91 9871107682','0','2008-04-29',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-10 12:14:22',14,'0',NULL,'200710/18/ATT40126.html','200710/18/DOC16334.doc','RESUME\nRESUME\n\nABHISHEK \nFlat No. 431,4r\nth\n Floor,\nGaur Galaxy Apartments,\nSector-5, Vaishali,\nGhaziabad\n\n(U.P.)-201010\n              \n                                               \nE-mail: abhirtregshek.midhrgrega@yahoo.co.in\n                                               \nPhone:\n\n91-9871107682.\n                                    \n    \n        \nObjective :\nTo work efficiently and effectively as well as grow with a prestigious organization. A position of responsibility, where I can contribute substantially to the organization and to myself in the process.\n\nTechnical Skills:\n\n\n\n        \nScripting Languages\n                    \nShell Script, Perl & Ant.\n\n        \nDatabases\n                          \n        \nOracle 8i/9i & \n10\n\n\nDB2 UDB\n   \n                                                                    \n8.x &\n\nDB2 9.0 (Viper), Informix 7.x- 9.x,\n                    \n                                                \nInformix 10.x.\n\n        \nWeb Technologies \n        \nHTML, XML.\n\n        \nO/S and H/W Platforms\n            \nWindows NT, SCO UNIX, AIX, Linux,\n                                                        \nSolaris 9, Windows 2000, MS-DOS, Sun &\n      \n                                                        \nPentium Server.\n\n        \nLanguages\n                          \n        \nSQL, PL/SQL\n      \n    \n\n        \nOthers\n                                       \nToad, Quest central, Server Studio JE, Aqua\n\nData Studio, AQT, Load Runner, Humming Bird, Star Team, VSS,Websphere.\n\nWork Experience:\n\n\n        \nCurrently working as a \nDB2 DBA\n in \nConnectiva Systems, \nDelhi\n since \n19\nth\n\nMarch?2007.\n\n        \nWorked as a\n\nSoftware Engineer (DBA Team)\n in \nManhattan\nAssociates,\nBangalore\n from 1\nst\n August?2005 to 16\nth\n March?2007.\n\n        \nWorked as a \nProject\n\nTrainee\n\nin Datanet Systems Private Limited\n\nBangalore\n from Feb?2005 to May?2005.\nPROJECT DETAILS:\nCompany Name\n: Connectiva Systems (\nIndia\n) Pvt., \nDelhi\nDesignation\n: Junior DB2 DBA\nDuration\n: 19\nth\n March 2007 to till date\nTeam Size\n: 4 Members\nProjects Description\n\nConnectiva is a leading Telecom software organization providing Revenue Assurance Solutions, Integration Solutions and Service Delivery Solutions to leading telecom Operators across the world.In India the organization is involved in Revenue Assurance project for Bharti?s Wireline (Infotel) and Wireless (Airtel) business (in association with IBM).\nClient\n: IBM,\nDelhi\n (Airtel Bharti Project)\n\nResponsibilities Held\n\n     \n\n        \nEvaluate the Database Server Hardware.\n\n        \nInstall the DB2 software. \n\n        \nPlan the Database\n\n\n        \nTune Database Performance (SQL Tuning as well as DB Tuning)\n\n\n        \nTo do RUNSTATS at regular intervals as & when required\n\n\n        \nTo create new objects (Tables, Views etc) & to modify existing objects if required based on requests on daily basis\n\n\n        \nTo do space calculations & to monitor for the file systems space usage\n\n\n        \nUse of db2load for data loading, db2expln, db2advis, db2 autoconfigure for database tuning\n\n\n        \nDB Configuration, Database Maintenance.\n\n        \nBackup & Restore of Databases.\n\n        \nDeveloping Migration Strategies.\n\n        \nDatabase support to Development and QA team (Onsite/Offshore).\n          \nBrief Description\n\nThis project is basically a telecom project on DB2 DB based on RAS (Revenue Assurance System). The main objective of this project is to prevent the revenue loss of the various telecom service providers. The size of the Production DB here is currently around 20 Terabytes. It is a DPF environment with total of 37 nodes on 8 servers.\n\nCompany Name\n\nManhattan\n Associates, \nBangalore\nDesignation\n: Software Engineer\nDuration\n: 1\nst\n August 2005 to 16\nth\n March 2007.\nTeam Size\n: 5 Members\nProjects Description\n: The various Project Releases on which I have worked in \nManhattan\n Associates, \nBangalore\n are listed below:\nClient\n: HOME DEPOT, \nKROGER\n\nVENTURA\n\nUSA\nResponsibilities Held\n\n     \n\n           \nOracle database setup on sun Solaris/AIX and win2000 & creation of ORACLE databases on AIX boxes, creating table spaces, buffer pools & users. \n\n           \nDB2 Database (DB2 V8.x/Viper) setup on AIX, Win2000 & creating DB2 databases on AIX boxes, creating buffer pools & users.\n\n           \nDB Configuration, Database Maintenance\n\n           \nBackup & Restore of Databases \n\n           \nResponsibilities for tuning of Databases and Applications\n\n           \nDeveloping Migration Strategies\n\n           \nDatabase support to Development and QA team (Onsite/Offshore)\nBrief Description\n\nThe scope of the project was to provide support to the Development and QA Team for different releases of\n\nTMS (Transportation Management System) on Supply Chain Management domain on different databases\n\nflavours like ORACLE and DB2 8.x/Viper and involved on database migration for different releases of TMS product on DB2 database.\nEnvironment\n: Oracle9i/10G, DB2 8.x/Viper, AIX, Solaris & Win2K\nClient\n\nWALMART\n\nUSA\nResponsibilities Held\n\n     \n\n           \nInformix database setup on AIX.\n\n           \nDB Configuration, Database Maintenance\n\n           \nBackup & Restore of Databases \n\n           \nResponsibilities for tuning of Databases and Applications\n\n           \nDeveloping Migration Strategies\n\n           \nDatabase support to Development and QA team (Onsite/Offshore)\nBrief Description\n\nThe scope of the project was to provide support to the Development and QA Team for release of\n\nTMS (Transportation Management System) on Supply Chain Management domain on Informix Database. The release was called as Falcon BU Gap.\nEnvironment\n: Informix 10.x, AIX.\n\nCompany Name\n: Datanet Systems Private Limited, \nBangalore\nDesignation\n: Project Trainee\nDuration\n: 4 Months(February?2005 to May?2005)\nTeam Size\n: 2 Members\nTechnology\n: Java, J2EE, JSP, DB2\nProject Description\n: It was a pure JAVA related development project.The project work was related to CPRO, Datanet?s Proprietary Workflow Automation System. The first part of the project pertained to development of modules for change of Password & Re-Setting of Password. The second part of the project was towards incorporating Files Upload features in CPRO.\n\n\nEducation:\n\n\n      \nMCA \nfrom \nAlliance Business Academy College\n affiliated to \nBANGALORE\nUNIVERSITY\n\nBangalore\n in 2005 (Aggregate 70%).\n\n\n      \nB.S.C. ELECTRONICS (Honours) \nfrom \nDeen Dayal Upadhaya College\n affiliated to \nDELHI\nUNIVERSITY\n\nDelhi\n in 2002. (Aggregate 65%).\n\n\n      \nHSC\n Passed in \nFirst Class\n from \nIngraham English Institute, \nGhaziabad\n in \n1998-99\n affiliated to \nI.S.C. Board (Aggregate 75.6%).\n\n\n      \nSSC\n\nPassed\n in \nFirst Class\n from \nMercy\nMemorial\nSchool\n\nKanpur\n in \n1996-97\n affiliated to \nI.C.S.E. Board (Aggregate 82.2%).\n\nExtracurricular Activities:\n\n\n        \nHas been an active member for the \n?ARYA BHATT?\n\nScience Society\n in \nDeen\nDayal\nUpadhaya\nCollege\n\nDelhi\n and has conducted various \nCultural Events and Educational Trips.\n\n        \nInitiated an \nIT event ?VOYAGE?\n at \nAlliance\nBusiness\nAcademy\n\nBangalore\n\n\n        \nGood Team Player & a keen & a fast learner of latest technologies.\n\n\n        \nHave \nClear Communication Skills\n with ability to interact with \nGlobal Teams.\n\n        \nStrong trouble shooting, problem solving, analytical and design skills.\n\n        \nAttended 5 days workshop for DB2 TRAINING from 20\nth\n June 2006 to 24\nth\n June 2006 given by IBM. \n   \nPersonal Profile:\n\n      \n\name:\n                                \nAbhishek Midha.\n      \nDate of Birth:\n                      \n25-03-1980.\n      \nPassport No.\n                      \nG2668662\n      \nFather?s name:\n                    \nMr. Vippin Midha\n      \nSex: \n                                   \nMale\n      \nMarital Status:\n                    \nSingle\n      \nLanguages Known:\n             \nEnglish, Hindi\n      \nNationality:\n                         \nIndian\n      \nPermanent Address:\n           \nFlat No. 431, 4r\nth\n Floor, Gaur Galaxy,\n                                                \nSector-5, Vaishali, \nGhaziabad\n(U.P)\n                 \n      \nPhone Numbers:\n                 \n09891975643, 09871107682.\n  ',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-18',NULL,'2007-10-18','2010-06-10 12:14:22','2010-06-10',14,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(211,'A. Krishnan',NULL,NULL,NULL,'ravsdvmkidvdvvd25y@yahoo.com',NULL,'022 27711675','0','9869439515','0',NULL,'0','2005-04-29',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-10 12:14:22',14,'0',NULL,'200710/18/ATT40127.html','200710/18/DOC16335.doc','Pradeep Kumar\nA. KRISHNAN\n\n\nIn quest of Project implementations in ERP -Oracle Apps 11i \n\nSupply Chain, Business Process Outsource with a leading IT organization\n\n\nSUMMARY\n\n    \nA technocrat having the following experience \n\n          \n5 years of experience in the field of Information Technology with 3 years of intense experience in Oracle 11i Functional Supply Chain ? Purchasing\n\n          \n2 years of Purchasing domain experience in \nNew York\n\nUSA\n on L1 Visa.\n\n          \n5 years of Purchasing and Inventory Domain experience with Air \nIndia\n, an International Air line\n\n          \n8 years of Purchasing and Inventory Domain experience with Coal \nIndia\n ? the largest Mining Company.\n\n    \nDisplayed proficiency in setup, design and implementation of iProcurement, iSupplier portals, Sourcing, Procurement and Inventory modules in Oracle 11i.\n\n    \nProficient in mapping business requirements, understanding business process, study and analyze workflow to design solutions and preparing functional specifications.\n\n    \nDesigned, developed and implemented Web based Purchasing System in \nNew York\n\n    \nDesigned, developed and implemented\n   \nWeb based Cargo Tracking System in \nNew York\n\n    \nCertified Purchase Manager from \nInstitute\n of\n\nSupply\n Management, \nUSA\n\n    \nUniversity Rank Holder\n\n    \nGold medalist in School and College\n\n    \nEffective communicator with excellent negotiation skills with strong leadership qualities\n\n\nSOFTWARE CERTIFICATIONS\nDegree\nIn Subject\n      \n      \nInstitute / Company\n\nState, Country\nMonth & Year of Passing \n\nOracle Course Certificate \nEssentials for Implementers for\n\nE-Business Suite\n\nOracle\nUniversity\n, Chennai\nIndia\nMarch \n\n2007\n     \nDo\n\nOracle 11i Inventory\nOracle\nUniversity\n, Chennai\nIndia\n\nMarch 2007\n     \nDo\nOracle 11i Purchasing\nOracle\nUniversity\n, Chennai\nIndia\n\nMarch \n\n2007\n     \nDo\nORACLE 10g\n\nDISCOVERER\nOracle\nUniversity\n, Mumbai\nIndia\n\nMarch \n\n2006\nAptech Certified Global Skills \nOracle and Developer 2000 \nAptech Computer Education \nIndia\nDecember 1999\nDiploma in Information and System Management \nFoxPro, C Language\nAptech Computer Education \nIndia\nDecember 1998\n\n\n\nPROFESSIONAL CREDENTIALS\nDegree\nIn Subject\n      \n     \nFrom University\n\nState, Country\nMonth & Year of Passing \nCertified Purchasing Manager (CPM)\nPurchasing\n\nInstitute\n of \nSupply\n Management, \nUSA\n\nNew York\n\nUSA\nDecember, 2006\n\n\nMaster of Business Administration (MBA)\nMarketing, Financial Accounting \nBharathiar\nUniversity\n\nCoimbatore\n\nIndia\nMay \n\n1986\nBachelor of Business Administration \n(BBA)\nFinancial Management, Management Accounting \nMadurai\nKamaraj\nUniversity\nIndia\nApril 1983\n\nUS JOB TRANSFER VISA \n\nStatus\n\nValidity \nWork in US (Months) \nB1\n11-SEP-2000\n\nUPTO\n   \n10-MAR-2001\n3 months\nL1\n05-JAN-2001\n\nUPTO\n   \n20-DEC 2002\n\n\nyear &\n          \n9 months\nPresently holding 10 years multiple entries B1/B2 Visa.\n\nKEY PROJECTS HANDLED\n\nProject\n           \n: ERP implementation in Purchasing and Inventory\n\nClient\n\n          \n: Air \nIndia\n- An International Airline\n            \nDuration\n       \n: Oct 2004 ? Sep 2007\nEnvironment\n\n: Oracle 11.5.10.2\nScope\n           \n: Project SMART involves implementation of Oracle 11i application within the Materials Management Division of Air \nIndia\n. The software application automates and drives the revised processes that have been evolved for MMD. The project aims to:\n\n       \nSeamless Supply Chain by creating Blanket Purchase Agreements and automatic approvals of Blanket Purchase Releases\n\n       \nElectronic approvals\n\n       \nElectronic storage &retrieval of documents reducing the need for repeated copying & printing\n\n       \nTransparency and traceability in the tendering process\n\n       \nDifferent types of tendering based on Approved supplier list and value\n\n       \nAutomated process to stimulate and facilitate repeat orders\n\n       \nStandard, and publicly available,\n\nterms and conditions for tenders\n\n       \nSelf registration of vendors; followed by technical valuation\n\nModules worked on:\n\n       \nCore Purchasing, Inventory, iProcurement, iSupplier Portal, Sourcing.\n\nRole: \nAs \nChange Manager\n involved in\n\ndesigning \nMulti?Org\n environment in Oracle Applications, \nSet Up\n parameters of different Inventory and Sub-Inventory Organizations, defined Lot and Serial Controls for Items during Data Migration, designed Position Approval Hierarchy, defined Concurrent Managers,\n\nProfile Options, Assisted creating\n\nBlanket Purchase Agreements Supplier User Registration, Created Requisition Templates, RFQ Templates, Contract Templates.\n\nKey responsibilities include:\n\n    \nCreating functional requirements as an input to application design\n\n    \nSupervising process and functional design activities\n\n    \nSupervising the Development of the detailed functional designs for business solution components and prototypes\n\n    \nTesting detailed functional designs for business solution components and prototypes\n\n    \nMap with Oracle E-Business Suite\n\n    \nGap Analysis\n\n    \nApproving Standard Operating Procedures\n\n    \nSupervising application build, test, and deploy activities\n\n    \nPlanning and executing data conversion activities\n\n    \nDriving test planning and execution\n\n    \nTraining the end users such as Requisitioners, Buyers, Approvers, Suppliers\n\n    \nDefining support procedures\n\nProject Worth\n\nRs. 6 Crores\n\nOTHER KEY PROJECTS HANDLED\n\n    \nPlayed a vital role in designing, developing and implementing the following \nWeb based Purchasing System in \nNew York\n\nUSA\n\nDatabase:\n\nMS ? SQL Server. HTML User Interface hosted on Microsoft Internet Information Server.\nDesigned the Indent registration page for the Mumbai Users for capture of Indents, which shall be visible in \nNew York\n for the Buyers to process. Worked out the complete business process for converting the Indent into Purchase Orders. Designed the Supplier registration page which shall be accessible to Buyers in \nNew York\n as well as Buyers in Mumbai. Designed the Reporting parameters so that the Indentors in Mumbai shall be able to track their Indent status and see the Purchase Order details on the web page.\n\nWeb based Cargo Tracking System in \nNew York\n\nUSA\n\nDatabase:\n\nMS ? SQL Server. HTML User Interface hosted on Microsoft Internet Information Server.\nDesigned an FTP so that Purchase Orders generated in Mumbai are migrated into this Web based system so that it shall be visible to the cargo staff working in \nNew York\n. Worked out the business process by which the Airway Bills are created from the system for the flight departures of a particular date. Designed the Reporting parameters so that the staff in Mumbai shall be able to see the AWB details for a given \nPO\n\n\nCAREER HIGHLIGHTS\n\nSep 1995 to Sep 2007with Air \nIndia\n\n\nlast served as Senior Manager ? Oracle 11i ERP.\n\n\nCareer Path\nSep 1995:\n      \nJoined as \n      \nManager- Purchase IT Procurement, \nMumbai\n\nIndia\nSep 2000:\n      \nPromoted as \n\nPurchasing Manager, \nNew York\n\nUSA\nOct 2002:\n      \nPromoted as \n\nSenior Manager\n- MM\nOct 2004 to Sep 2007:\n        \nSenior Manager\n- Oracle11i ERP\n\nJul?87 to Aug?95 with SECL as a Senior Stores/ Purchase Officer, \nMadhya Pradesh\n\nIndia\n\nA Subsidiary of Coal India Ltd \nResponsible for managing and supervising the purchasing sections of Electrical Equipments, mining equipments for the coal mines\n\nCareer Path \nJul?87 to Jul?88\n                   \nJunior Executive (T) - Purchase\nAug?88 to Jun?92\n                 \nPurchase Officer\n       \nJul?92 to Nov?92\n                  \nSenior Purchase Officer\nDec?92 to Jul?94\n                  \nSenior Stores Officer\nAug?94 to Aug?95\n      \n          \nSenior Purchase Officer\n\nPERSONAL DETAILS \nDate of Birth:\n\n          \n21-03-1963\nAddress:\n\n               \n\npartment # D3/ 504, \n\nenyadri CHS 47/1, Sector 19A, Nerul, NAVI MUMBAI 400706, \nINDIA\n\nPhone: \n         \n          \n022- 27711675(Res), +91 9869439515(M)\nEmail: \n                    \n\nravsdvmkidvdvvd25y@yahoo.com\nNotice period :\n         \nNIL (Obtained VRS)',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-18',NULL,'2007-10-18','2010-06-10 12:14:22','2010-06-10',14,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(212,'Jibanendu Dash',NULL,NULL,'Bangalore ','jidvdfvbavdsvvn_dash@yahoo.com',NULL,NULL,'0','9886382490','0',NULL,'0','2007-12-13',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-10 12:14:22',14,'0',NULL,'200710/18/ATT40129.html','200710/18/DOC16336.doc','2+ years of professional experience in Database Programming\n\n\n2+ years of professional experience in Client Server Technology.\n                                                                                    \n        \ne-mail :- \njidvdfvbavdsvvn_dash@yahoo.com\n\nJibanendu D\n         \n                                                              \n  \n   \n\n\nobile\n:-91-9886382490\n                                    \n\n\nObjective\n                   \n                        \nTo work in an organization where every assignment is a challenge, that gives me an opportunity to learn and improve and secure position in modern IT Organization utilizing my professional experience that provide platform for my skills to scaffold and contribute to the growth of the organization in an environment conductive to continual advancement of knowledge and skills to prove my inherent creativeness, innovativeness and natural leadership qualities.\n\n\n\nProfile Summary\n\n           \n    \n\nI have been working with \nANZ IDC (\nIndia\n Development center),\nBangalore\n\nas an Consultant Associate from July 2006 to till date.\n\nI was working at \nCaltech Infosystems, \nBangalore\n from June 2005 to July 2006 as a\nSoftware Engineer.\n\nInvolved with active participation in Code enhancement according to the client?s requirement and having excellent skills in database programming.\n\n\nAble to interpret functionality of existing scripts at a glance.\n\n\n\n\n  \ntechnical skills \n            \nLanguages\nC, VB6.0, Core Java\nPlatforms\nWindows & Sun Solaris Unix 5.8\nFront end tools\nHTML, Visual Studio 6.0\nBackend tools\nOracle 9i(SQL, PL/SQL)\n, SQL Server, MS Access\nScripting Languages\nShell Scripting\nDatabase Tools\nToad, PL/SQL developer\nReporting Tools\nCrystal Report\n\n\n\nEducational Qualification\n\n\n       \nI have completed \nMCA\n with 79% from BPUT, \nUtkal\nUniversity\n\nBhubaneswar\n   \n     \nin 2005\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nProject Details\n\n#1\nProject Name\nTS (Trading System)\nProject \nType\nFinance\nClient\nANZ (\nAustralia\n and New Zealand Bank)\nAbout The \nProject\nDescription:\n\nThe Order Management application allows the user to Create, Route, Trade and Allocate orders. The business administration module allows the user to change static data in the application. The static data drives \nRouting Logic, Asset Information, Expense/Commission calculation and Client Information\n. The application is also the primary way in which access to the various functions within OASIS is controlled. The business administration can be used against European server only from where the information is replicated to other OASIS servers.\nDuration\nAug 2006 to Till date\nContribution\nResponsible for solving user queries from various medias like interchange chat channel, mails and on telephone.\nResponsible for monitoring all the feed load status and if any delays need to inform feed owner as well as business rule user.\nResponsible for escalating issues to level2 and coordinating with users.\nResponsible for loading all the Manual loads, through the scripts\n\nTechnologies \nUsed\nRDBMS ORACLE 9.2.02 , PL/SQL, UNIX, SHELL Scripting \n#2\nProject Name\nATT (Asset Tracking Tool)\nProject Type\nProcess automation\nClient\nAltair Engineering, \nDetroit\n\nUSA\nAbout The Project\nDescription:\n\nThis is a web-based application designed for the client?s facility center. For tracking products allotted to dealers\nThose maintain a steady relation with the organization. The application incorporates a central repository of all the products and their movements inside and outside the organization. It allows dealers to view the products owned by them, status of a request to avail new products to the facility center. It allows managers to view all the products for their department. It also has a reporting module which allows multiple reports to be generated including individual product status report, dealer wise product report that shows the entire product owned by the dealer. Daily product movement report and product summary sheet that shows all the product status for given date range.\nDuration\nDec 2005 to July 2006\nContribution\n    \n\n   \nHandling Enhancement Requests\n\n\n         \nCoding.\n\n         \nQuerying the database, writing procedures \nfunctions.\n\n\n         \nCode review maintaining the client?s standards.\n\nTechnologies Used\nRDBMS \nORACLE 9.2.02 , PL/SQL\n\n\n\nProject Name\nDSS\n - Distributed Software Systems \nClient\nCaltech Infosystems\nAbout The Project\nDescription: \nDSS is a list of interfaces, which facilitates the communication between the hosts of different types, such as Mainframe and UNIX.\n\nThe interface Green Dragon acts as the middle-layer between SSE (mainframe) and other Unix hosts, which inputs data into SSE. The interface Red Dragon system gets data from SSE and inputs to other Unix hosts\n\nDuration\nJuly 2005 to Nov 2005\nContribution\nAs a Team member involved in doing change requests. Change requests involve code changes to UNIX scripts, Perl scripts and Sybase store procedures.\n\nI was also monitoring Red Dragon and Green Dragon systems as support activity.\n\nTechnologies Used\nRDBMS ORACLE 9.2.02, PL/SQL, Toad\n\n\n#3\n\n\n\nPersonal profile\n\nDate of Birth\n15-Feb-1978\nSex\nMale\nNationality\nIndian\nMartial Status\nSingle\nContact Address\n201/5, 8\nth\n cross, Doddanekkundi, \nBangalore\nLanguage Proficiency\nEnglish, Hindi, Oriya\nPassport Status\nAvailable\n\n\n\nPersona\n\n         \nDynamic team player \n\n         \nHighly inquisitive \n\n         \nCreative and resourceful \n\n         \nExcellent skills in communication and collaboration\n\n         \nTo work under pressure\n\n         \nLike to take initiative in complex and challenging tasks\n\n\n\n\n\nI do hereby declare that the information made here in is correct to the best of my knowledge and belief.\n\n\n                                                                                                          \n                                                                                                \nJibanendu Dash','ANZ IDC ',1,NULL,'2007-10-18',NULL,'2007-10-18','2010-06-10 12:14:22','2010-06-10',14,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(213,'Jitin J',NULL,NULL,NULL,'jitivndvdsvjain@yahoo.com',NULL,'09416147002','0','9968228658','0','01275 251951','0','2007-04-30',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-10 12:14:22',14,'0',NULL,'200710/18/ATT40130.html','200710/18/DOC16337.doc','RESUME\n                                                       \nRESUME\n\nJITIN J\nHOUSE NO. C-2, Kailash Apartments\n                        \nHome - 01275 - 251951\nAgra\n Chowk, Palwal \n                                                   \nMobile\n no: 9968228658,09416147002\nHARYANA ? 121102 \n                                                \nE-mail: \n- jitivndvdsvjain@yahoo.com\n                                                                        \nSUMMARY:\n3+ years of extensive industry experience in Implementation, Configuration and Troubleshooting of Standard and Enterprise Network Systems. ? IT experience in various Customer Support activities including Desktop Management, hardware testing, hardware installations, hardware maintenance, networking and System administration. ? Excellent experience in installation, configuration and troubleshooting of Linux ? System Administration (as a Team Member in RPRS site)\n\n\nWorking Experience\n\n\nAug 2005 to present CMC Limited, \nNew Delhi\n\nI am working in CMC Limited as a IT Engineer. I have 2 years\n of IT experience in various kind of Hardware Maintenance and Operating Systems, Network Installations, and Peripherals. I have Presented and proved CMC Ltd. as the most robust maintenance company in front of assigned customers. I have good working experience in heterogeneous environment.\n\nAssigned Customer\n\nNorthern Railways(Railways Passenger Reservation System),New-\n                                                  \n\n                                   \nDelhi\n\nResponsibilities\n            \n      \nSystem Engineer for Open VMS System,Unix Adminstration.\n                                    \nUptime of more than 95% for complete heterogeneous system.\n                                   \nAll kinds of payment follow-ups for CMC, the AMC value at\n                                    \nRPRS(NR) was Rs.20000000 and the payments were released\n                                    \non quarterly basis on producing PM reports. \n\n                                   \nMaintaining healthy relations with customer\n\n\nHardware\n         \n    \n      \nHP Alpha DS20E,ES40,ES45 Servers,Hsz80 Array Controller,\n                                  \nCompaq RA 8000 Storage,Terminal Servers(HCL,Equinox)\n\nOperating System\n    \nOpenVMS system,Linux\n\nAssigned Customer: \nNorthern Region Marketing Division of Indian Oil Corporation Limited. \nMy Responsibilities\n\n\n1. I did System Administration for Novell Netware 5.0,Windows NT\n                    \n4.0 servers\n                                    \n2. I have Configured proxy servers and network printers.\n3. I have follow-ups for all kinds of payments to CMC\n4. Maintaining healthy relations with customer\n\n\nHardware: \nIntel Based PCs, Comapq\n\nServers, \nHP LC2000 servers, IBM Netfinity Servers. Acer 1100E, 900k\n\nservers, Printronix P-4280 Line Matrix Printers,LIPI MT-691 Line Matrix Printer,SYNOPTICS\n\nSwitch and Hubs, LAN cable and I/O outlets.\n\nOperating Systems\n    \nWin95-98, WindowsNT4.0, Windows 2000 Professional,\n                                    \nNovell NetWare 5.0\n\nDec 2003 to Jun 2005\n   \nHAVELL?S INDIA LTD, ALWAR ( Rajasthan)\nI have worked in the cable division. My main jobs and responsibilities are:\n1. Maintenance of Windows based systems. \n2. Setup Local Area Network (LAN) using Hub/Switches.\n3. Expertise over Hardware Installation, Maintenance and Troubleshooting including\n   \n    \nPrinters (DeskJet & Laser Printers).\n4. Video Conferencing with the ISDN Line.\nTECHNICAL PROFILE\n\nHardware\n        \nIBM Compatible PCs, Compaq PCs, Acer PCs, IBM Netfinity Servers, IBM x-series 236 Server,Compaq ML330 Server,HP LC2000 Server.HP Alpha ES40,DS20,ES45 Servers,Terminal Servers,RA8000 Storage,HSZ80 array Controller\nPeripherals: \nLine Matrix printer LiPi MT-691, Printronix P-4280,HP DeskJet Series , Lexmark Colorjet series\nOperating System:\nWin95-98,Windows 2000 Professional, Windows Xp,Windows NT 4.0, MS DOS, Novell Netware 5.0,Unix Fundamentals,OpenVMS System.\nSoftware:\nC,ORACLE 8i,VB 6\n\nTRAINING:\nAttended 4 month plant training in \nHCL INFOSYS LTD, \nNOIDA\n\nINDIA\n. I got following hands-on experiences:\n\nHardware Maintenance of\n\nCeleron & P-III Systems based systems.\nAssembling of\n\nCeleron & P-III Systems.\nOperating System and software installation on above systems.\n\nEDUCATIONS:\nExamination\nBoard/University\nYear Of Passing\nCollege/School\nGRADE\nB.E.\n(Computer Science)\nMaharishi\nDayanand\nUniversity\n, Rohtak\nMay, \n2003\nCITM \nInstitute\n Of \nEngineering\n\nFaridabad\n\nst\n division\nDiploma\n(Computer Science)\nS.B.T.E. Chandigarh\nDec? 1999\nH.I.T., Sonipat\n\nst\n division\n\n\n\nACHIEVEMENTS\nGot First prize in Cricket Quiz in Diploma.\n\nnd\n prize in 100mt. Athlete tournament during school time. \nPart of team securing 2\nnd\n position in \nBadminton\nCollege\n tournament.\n\nPERSONAL DETAILS:\nFather?s Name:\n             \nSh. A.K.Jain\nDate of Birth:\n                            \n15\nth\n September, 1980\nSex:\n                                          \nMale\nMarital Status:\n                          \nMarried\nCurrent CTC:\n                           \n2.2Lac.\nExpected CTC:\n                        \n4Lac\nNotice Period: \n             \n15 Days\nTotal Experience: \n                     \n3 Years\nPassport Details :\n                      \nE3025567\n\n                        \n                                                                        \n\n\n\n\n\n\nJITIN JAIN)',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-18',NULL,'2007-10-18','2010-06-10 12:14:22','2010-06-10',14,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(214,'Jogendra Das',NULL,NULL,'Banglore','jogebbncbnndrbnbvna.das@gmail.com',NULL,NULL,'0','91 9886090122','0',NULL,'0','2007-02-12',10,34,'2010-06-10 12:14:22',14,'0',NULL,'200710/18/ATT40131.html','200710/18/DOC16338.doc','JOGENDRA DAS\nJOGENDRA \nEmail\n\njogebbncbnndrbnbvna.das@gmail.com\n\n            \n                        \n    \nPhone\n\n\n(+91)9886090122\n_______________________________________________________________________\n\nProfessional Summary:\n\n3+ years of experience in \n\noftware \nDevelopment and Production Support\n\nPrimary technical experience in \nOracle\n\n\nPL/SQL\n\nCurrently working with \nHCL Technologies Ltd.\n in Banking Domain.\nHaving good Knowledge in \n\nhell\n\nScripting\n\nGood knowledge in\n Unix/Windows \nenvironment.\nHaving good Knowledge in \nSDLC \nand \nTesting\n\nWorking Experience:\n\nCurrently Working as a \nSoftware Engineer\n with \nHCL Technologies Ltd\n\nBangalore\n from Nov 2006 to till date.\n\nWorked as a \nSoftware Engineer \nwith\n Securyes Pvt. Ltd., \nBangalore\n from Aug 2004 to Oct 2006.\n      \nTechnical Skills:\n\nLanguages\n                                \n\n PL/SQL.\nDatabase\n                                  \n\n Oracle 8i/9i.\nScripting Languages\n                  \n\nShell Scripting.\nTools\n                                        \n\nSQL Navigator\n\nTOAD, \nPutty, \nControl-M.\nOperating Systems\n                    \n\n Windows 9x/2000/NT, Linux, \nUnix.\nEducational Qualification: \n\nMaster in Computer Application (MCA) from I.G.I.T Sarang (Govt. Engg. College) Under \nUtkal\nUniversity\n\nMaster in Science (M Sc. in Maths.) from \nUtkal\nUniversity\n\nB.Sc in Mathematics from \nUtkal\nUniversity\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nPROJECT PROFILE: \n\nProject # 1\n\nGlobal Cash\n management\n System\nProduction Support At\n           \n: HCL Technologies Ltd., \nBangalore\n\nEnvironment/Software\n           \n\n\nJava\n\nOracle 9i, \nUnix-Sun/Solaris\n\n\nTeam Size\n                               \n\n\n9.\nProject Duration\n                     \n: Continuing from Nov. 2006\n\nDescription\n\nThis is \nDeutsche\n Bank application. By capturing real-time cash flow information GCMS provides an accurate picture of daily funding requirements. This is backed up by a daily reconciliation process which allows the operations to deal with any irregularities such as delayed payment or receipts. It also provides the ability to cross-charge for late arrival of cash flows, which results in more expensive borrowing of money or lost opportunity costs for investing the extra funds for a better return. It manages cash globally based on cash position for each Accounts at the cut off time that means the Account which having positive balance do not bear high interest rates and negative balances can mean significant charges. If any one of the Account face any negative balance in the same region it will borrow the money from the money market and will pay the interest for that. The overall requirement is to maintain zero balances in these accounts.\nMy Role:\nMonitor batch and interface processes and take remedial action where necessary according to pre-defined \nSLA\nProduction Support Incident Logging and Tracking.\nIncident report Preparation.\nRun Book Updating and SLA Report preparation.\n\nProject # 2\n      \nWarehouse Management System. \n      \n\nDeveloped At\n                         \n: Securyes Pvt. Ltd., \nBangalore\n\nEnvironment/Software\n           \n\nLinux\n, Oracle 9i , C++, Java.\n          \nTeam Size\n                               \n\n\n8.\nProject Duration\n                     \n: 10 months.\n\nDescription\n\n\nThis Project is based on warehouse management system It automate the warehouse business process. The application maintains a repository of all the items and their movements inside and outside the warehouse. There are total seven modules in this project. These are Order Entry Module, Receiving Module, Stocking Module, Shipping Module, Purchasing Module, Invoicing Module and Planning Module. Order Entry module responsible for taking customer orders and for responding to customer queries about the status of an order. Receiving module is responsible for accepting stock from Suppliers, tracking supplier shipments and for accepting stock from suppliers. Stocking module takes care of placing new inventory in stock and retrieving inventory in support of filling customer orders. Shipping module responsible for preparing packages for shipment in support of filling customer orders. Invoicing module deals with tracking customer payments as well as for paying suppliers for orders from purchasing. Planning module responsible for generating reports to management and studying trends in inventory levels and customer activity. Purchasing module is responsible for ordering stock from suppliers.\n\nMy Role:\n\n        \nCreating functions, Procedures, Packages, Triggers etc.\nInvolved in understanding the Application and implementing the business logic.\n\n        \nCoding and Unit Testing.\n\nProject # 3\n    \nAsset Tracking System\n\nDeveloped At\n                         \n: Secureyes Pvt Ltd., \nBangalore\n\nEnvironment/Software\n           \n\nLinux,\n\nOracle 9i(PL/SQL).\nDuration\n                                 \n: 9 months.\nTeam Size\n                               \n: 6\nDescription : \n           \n      \n              \nIt is a web based application, designed for tracking of assets which are\n                                                  \n  \nallotted to the employees within the organization. The application maintains a central repository of all the assets and their movements inside and outside the organization. It allows employees to view the assets owned by them, status of a request made for new assets to the Organization. It allows the managers to view all the assets for their department. The reporting module allows multiple reports to be generated including individual asset status report, employees wise asset report that shows all the assets owned by an employee. Daily assets movements report and assets summery sheet that shows all the assets status for given date range or asset category or department.\n\nMy Role:\n\n        \nCreating functions, Procedures, Packages, Triggers etc.\n\n        \nCoding and Unit Testing.\n\nProject # 4\n    \nPharbase\n\nDeveloped at\n              \n            \n: Secureyes Pvt Ltd., \nBangalore\n\nEnvironment/Software\n           \n: Windows NT Server, Oracle 9i\n(PL/SQL).\nTeam Size\n                               \n: 7.\nProject Duration\n                     \n: 7 months. \n\nDescription:\n    \n    \n                                \n\n                                                                                               \n\nThis project is concerned with enhancement, maintenance, and Support of the pharbase product, mainly dealing with the pharmaceuticals data. This maintains the detail transaction of the company for the better decisional purpose of the upper management level. An entry is made for every transaction and its being extracted to the wire house after performing some ETL process. We have implemented our PHARBASE for the client in \nUK\n\nUSA\n\nAUSTRALIA\n\n\nMy Role:\nData Loading.\nAnalysis and Implementing the Business logic.\n\n        \nCoding and Unit Testing.\n\n\nPersonal Detail: -\n\nFather?s Name: -\n                       \nSridhar Das.\nMarital Status: -\n                        \nUnmarried\nAddress: -\n                                  \nNCR\nTower\n, Room No-10,\n                                                  \nPlot No-152/1, \nDoddanekkundi Main Road\n\n                                                  \nMarthahalli, Bangalore-560037','HCL Technologies Ltd',1,NULL,'2007-10-18',NULL,'2007-10-18','2010-06-10 12:14:22','2010-06-10',14,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(215,'Kaustav G',NULL,NULL,NULL,'kaudvdfvstav_75dvdfv@rediffmail.com','buvdv75van@yahoo.co.in','091 033 25443578','0','093432 19113','0',NULL,'0','2001-03-30',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-10 12:14:22',13,'0',NULL,'200710/18/ATT4912.html','200710/18/DOC16339.doc','                                   \n                                                     \n           \nRESUME:\n                                              \n    \n\nName:\n\nKaustav G.\n\nWorking Experience:\nPresent Employer:\n WNS Global Services Pvt.Ltd.\nPosition: SME.\nResponsibility:\n** Went for a transition for AP project. I was responsible for learning the invoice process in\n      \nOracle. I prepare Process flow in Visio and Process Manual in PowerPoint.\n** Process and audit of Accounts Payable invoices.\nJoining Date: 4 \nTh\n\nJune 2007. \nCurent CTC:RS.2, 30,000 pa.\nExpected CTC: Negotiable\nNotice Period:\n\n30\n Days\n\nPrevious Employers\n\nOrganization:\n Accenture Services Pvt. Ltd.\nPosition: Sr. Process Associate.\nResponsibility:\n** Matching the Sales data with Bank statement for a particular day for all the FSC of a\n     \nclient. The process is known as Deposit verification.\n** Performing period end process which includes running Missing Sales & Sales Edit\n     \nReport, Deposit correction in the system and over/ (short) research.\n** Preparation of Cash Position Report.\n** Preparation of AP & PR Check lists. It means how many new checks are issued\n     \nand how many checks are cleared by the client.\n** Provide on the job training.\n\nOrganization\n\n    \nAcclaris Business Solutions Pvt. Ltd\nPosition\n\nProcess Associate (Period: March 2005 to Nov 2006)\nResponsibility:\n** Process and audit Accounts Payable invoices.\n** Provide on the job training.\n\nOrganization:\n    \nBOSCO \nEnterprise\n\nPosition: Office Clerk (Period: Jan 2002 to Feb 2005)\nResponsibility:\n** Computerization of Sales (Cash) and Purchase (Cash) bills.\n    \nOrganization:\n    \nG.Agarwal & Associates\n\nPosition: Article Clerk (Period: 1998 September 2001 September)\nResponsibility:\n** Comparing bills, invoices with computer generated statement (Vouching part)\n\n\n\n\n\n\nEducational Qualification:\n** CA (Intermediate) GR.1 qualified from ICAI in the year 2003 Nov.\n   \n  \nMarks obtained: 51%\n      \n** B.COM (H) from \nCalcutta\nUniversity\n in the Year 1998.\n    \n\nMarks obtained: 60.5%.\n\n** Higher Secondary (10+2) Level from \nHindu\nSchool\n in the Yr. 1994.\n    \n\nMarks obtained: 52.2%.\n\n** Secondary (+10) Exam from \nHindu\nSchool\n in the Yr. 1992.\n     \nMarks obtained: 76%.\n   \nTechnical Qualification:\n** Three years certified diploma course from (HDSE) Aptech Computer Education Pvt \n     \nLtd.\n     \nDatabases: SQL Server, MS-ACCESS.\n     \nLanguage: VB 6.0, Java Script, HTML.\n     \nOthers: MS-Office\n** Six months course from Oracle.\n     \nDatabase: Oracle 8i.\n          \n\nPersonal Information:\nPassport No: F8575867\nDate of Birth:\n    \n27\nTh\n June 1975.\nAddress: \n8 R.N.Tagore Road\n\nPO\n: Dakshineswar;\n              \nDistrict- North 24 Parganas;\n             \n\nKolkata?700076\nContact Number: 093432 19113 (M)\n                      \n\n\n     \n091-033-25443578 (R)\nMail-id: \nkaudvdfvstav_75dvdfv@rediffmail.com\n or \nbuvdv75van@yahoo.co.in\n   \n            \n\n\nDated:\n                                                                \n               \n\nKaustav\n Ghosh)\n\n\n\n\n\n                                                   \n                                                      ',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-18',NULL,'2007-10-18','2010-06-10 12:14:22','2010-06-10',13,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(216,'K. Meyyappan',NULL,NULL,NULL,'meyyarthtrhppan_vettrhrthha@yahoo.co.in',NULL,NULL,'0','9449670247','0',NULL,'0','2008-04-29',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-10 12:14:22',14,'0',NULL,'200710/18/ATT22608.html','200710/18/DOC16340.doc','Mukund M\nK. Meyyappan\n                                                   \nC/O Megaraj,\n                                                                                    \n25, S.N.T.Road Cross,\n                                                                                    \nUlsoor,\n                                                                                    \n                                                            \nBangalore\n\n    \n                                                                                    \nMobile\n: 9449670247\nE-mail:\n\nmeyyarthtrhppan_vettrhrthha@yahoo.co.in\n\n\n\n\nTitle: PL/SQL Developer\nPrimary Skills: Oracle 8i/9i, SQL, PL/SQL\nSecondary Skills: VB, Crystal Report 8.0\n\n\nSummary\n                    \n    \nHaving 2+ years of experience in Oracle, PL/SQL and in the areas of a\npplication software development.\nDesigned and developed PL/SQL functions, stored procedures, cursors, packages and triggers.\n   \nInvolved in writing complex queries to generate reports.\nEffective resourceful problem solver, capable of identifying & meeting needs.\nHave a vision to quickly identify and understand the business benefits of new technologies.\nStrong computational, analytical problem solving, and design skills. \nHighly organized and dedicated with positive attitude. \n\n\nWork Experience\n\nWorking as a Senior Software programmer in Hard Soft Solutions from Aug 2006 to present.\nWorked as a Software Engineer in Common Entrance Test (CET) Cell from May 2005 to Aug 2006.\n\n         \nWorked as a Software Developer in National Informatics Centre Services Incorporated (NICSI) from Oct 2004 to Apr 2005\n\n\n\nEducation Qualification\n\nM.Sc., (CS) - \nV.H.N.S.N\nCollege\n, Virudhunagar.\nB.Sc., (CS) - \nA.P.S.A\nCollege\n, Tirupattur.\n\nTechnical Skills\nOperating Systems\n                         \n\n         \nWindows NT/2003 server\nRDBMS\n                \n           \n            \n            \n\n           \nOracle 7/8i/9i \nWeb Based Technologies\n                        \n\n           \nJavaScript\nProgramming Languages\n             \n\n           \nVB 6.0, \n\nava\nFront-End Tools\n               \n           \n\n         \n\nCrystal Report 8.0\n\n\nProjects\n\nProject Title\n      \n          \n   \n         \n\n\n         \n\nCane Management System\nClient \n     \n        \n\n           \n            \n\n          \n\nChamundeswari Sugars Ltd .K.M.Dhoddi.\nDuration\n                                 \n\n           \nAug 2006 ?Till Date\nOS & DB\n                                   \n\n           \nWindows 2003 & Oracle 9i\nSoftware\n          \n                       \n\n          \n\nOracle 9i \n(SQL, PL/SQL)\n, Crystal Report 8.0\nRole & Responsibility \n         \n\n\n          \n\nDeveloper, Coding & Implementation\n\n\nDescription: \nFormulated coding guidelines for the application are being targeted towards the efficient management Cane Management system. Main aspect of this project is to maintain the sugar factory transaction flow. It is having three main modules,\n\n1.Cane Monitoring: This system helps monitor the growth of the cane with the help of various\n      \nDocuments - \nDoc 10, Doc 20 and Doc 30,\n\nthat are used the sugar factory monitor the crop\n. This\n                 \n      \nModule \nstrong of monitoring the process of registering plots for cane cultivation and subsequent\n      \ngrowth.\n2.Cane Weighment:\n\nThis module handles the all operation starting from the harvest of cane and the\nactual weighment of the cane. The transaction is start with the issue of the cutting order from the\nfactory and the regulation of supply of harvested cane through trip sheets issued by the filed staff. The movement of field staff enters the Trip sheet the records get updated in the database. This \nmonitoring module having the Gate entry, Gross weight and Tare weight to weight the cane .The cane\nweighment process is completely automated.\n3.Cane Accounting: This module mainly used for factory accounting the Ryot loan amount for cultivation. Various loans given to the ryot after cultivating the factory captures the amount done by these modules various report generated by this system. Payment card, Bill processing daily wise report etc.,\nProject Title\n                            \n\n           \nHall Ticket & Rank Generation and Seat Allotment\nClient\n\n                                    \n\n           \nCommon Entrance Test Cell, \nBangalore\n, Karnataka.\nDuration \n                                \n\n           \nFrom May 2005 ? Aug 2006\nOS & DB\n                            \n           \n       \n\n           \nWindows & UNIX, Oracle 8i\nSoftware\n                     \n            \n\n           \nOracle 8i \n(SQL, PL/SQL)\nRole\n                                        \n\n           \nDeveloper\nResponsibilities\n                      \n\n\n\n         \nCreation of PL/SQL Functions, Cursors, Packages, Stored procedures. Database triggers.\n\n         \nCreated stored sub programs with Dynamic SQL at both Client and Server side.\n\n         \nSupport in the area of technical Writing/Editing by reviewing the grammar, writing styles and syntax of quality materials and technical report.\nDescription:\n    \n\nHall Ticket & Rank Generation process is running on Windows 2000 Server with Oracle 9i. Seat Allotment process is running on UNIX Server with Oracle 7.\nHall Ticket Generation\nis a process of assigning CET Number, which is unique number for each candidate, assigning \nExam\nCenter\n and issuing the Hall Tickets to candidates, who are all appearing for the CET Exam.\nRank Generation\n is assigning ranks to students based on their merit in both medical and engineering disciplines. And also separate sequence of ranks is generated for Karnataka and Non-Karnataka students in both disciplines. Karnataka ranking is based on the performances in both CET and qualifying exams. Non-Karnataka ranking is based on CET performance alone. There is also a Provision to provide a new merit based Spot-rank on sufficient grounds of change of particulars.\nSeat Allotment\n is allotment of seats to candidates on the basis of their ranks. There are five stages in allotment process namely (i) Registration, (ii) Verification, (iii) Seat Selection, (iv) Bank Payment and (v) Getting Admission Order. Rank Generation and Seat allotment ensures that no candidate is able to bypass any of these stages any point of time.\n\n\n\nProject Title\n                       \n\n    \n\n        \n\nPersonal Information System (PIS)\nClient\n                                      \n\n         \nNICSI (National Informatics center, Karnataka)\nDuration\n                                 \n\n         \nFrom Oct 2004 ? Apr 2005\nOS & DB\n                                   \n\n        \nWindows 2003 Server, Oracle8i\nSoftware\n                                 \n\n         \nVB 6.0, Oracle 8i \n(SQL, PL/SQL), \nPostgre sql\nRole \n                           \n      \n      \n\n        \n\nDeveloper\nResponsibilities\n                      \n\n\n\n         \nDesigning and developing customized \nOracle Pl\n/sql Client/Server environment.\n\n         \nCreation of PL/SQL Functions, Cursors, Packages, Stored procedures. Database triggers.\n\n        \nUsed Database trigger for making history of insertion, updating, deletion.\n\nDescription\n\n    \n\nTo collect various details from all the colleges like built area, staff strength, facilities, workload etc.\nTo collect various details of staff from all the college like place served, deputation, disciplinary action, promotion, training attended etc.\nWeb based query system to query all the details and generate various reports based on the statistics collected from the college.\n\nPersonal Details\n\n\nDate of Birth\n                 \n\n   \n22-06-1981\nMarital Status\n                \n\n   \nSingle\nGender\n                         \n\n   \nMale\nPermanent Address\n       \n\n   \nNo 7, Meyyappan Illam,\n                                           \nMahilambu Street\n\n    \nKaraikudi,\n                                    \n    \nTamil Nadu.\nLanguages Known\n        \n\n   \nTamil, English\n\n\nI hereby declare that the information provided above is true to the best of my knowledge. \n\n\nPlace\n\nBangalore\n          \n                                                           \n     \n                    \nYours Sincerely,\n\nDate\n\n                    \n                                                                                             \n(N.Meyyappan)\n                         ',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-18',NULL,'2007-10-18','2010-06-10 12:14:22','2010-06-10',14,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(217,'Hareesh   Ram                                                                      ',NULL,NULL,NULL,'htrharethhtrhesh512@gmail.com',NULL,NULL,'0','91 9916513712','0',NULL,'0','2007-04-30',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-10 12:14:22',14,'0',NULL,'200710/18/ATT40132.html','200710/18/DOC16341.doc','HAREESH\n\n\nHAREESH\n   \nRAM\n                                              \n      \n      \n              \n\nmail\n\nhtrharethhtrhesh512@gmail.com\nSoftware Test Engineer\n\n                                    \n      \n           \n   \n\nMobile\n\n 91+9916513712\n\nSUMMARY\n\n\n                    \n3+ years\n of experience in Software Testing.\n\n                    \nGood knowledge of \nSDLC\n and \nSTLC.\n\n                    \nWorking experience in \nManual testing\n and \nautomation\n\n\n                    \nExpertise in designing test cases using various \nBlack Box testing techniques\n\n\n                    \nHands on experience in automation tool on \nQTP\n\n\n                    \nInvolved in \nFunctional\n\nSystem\n and \nRegression testing\n\n\n                    \nExperience in \nAd-hoc \nand\n Sanity Testing\n\n\n                    \nWorking experience in Bug tracking tools.\n\n                    \nAbility to work independently and in team environments.\n\n                    \nGood Team player and having excellent communication Skills.\n\nEXPERIENCE\n\n\n        \nWorking as Sr. Software Test Engineer for \nWipro,\nBangalore\n from October 2006 to till date.\n\n        \nWorked as Software Test Engineer for \nREEVETECH SYSTEMS\n\nHyderabad\n from May2004 to Sep2006.\n\nEDUCATIONAL QUALIFICATIONS\n\n\n        \nMSc (IT)\n from \nMadras\nUniversity\n\n\n        \nBCA\n from \nOsmania\nUniversity\n\n\nTECHNICAL SKILLS\n\n          \nTesting Tools\n               \n   \n\n\n    \nQTP.\n          \nBugTracking Tool\n   \n         \n\n   \nMercury\nQuality\nCenter\n\n          \nOperating System\n        \n   \n\n\n   \nWin 98/2000, Win XP,\nUnix\n         \n          \nLanguages\n                    \n   \n  \n\n   \nC, C++, Core Java.\n          \nDatabase\n                      \n   \n  \n\n   \nOracle.\n         \nWeb Technologies\n        \n   \n  \n\n   \nHTML, ASP.\n         \nScripting Language\n       \n   \n  \n\n   \nVB Script.\n\nPROFESSIONAL EXPERIENCE\n\nProject Profile #1\n                                                   \nTitle\n                  \n\n\nWestpac\n\nClient\n   \n            \n\n\nWestpac \nBank\n\nAustralia\n\nEnvironment\n     \n\n\nJava, JSP, Struts, Oracle and Unix.\nTesting tools\n     \n\nQTP , \nMercury\nQuality\nCenter\n\nRole\n                 \n\n\nTest Engineer.\nDescription:\n            \nThis suite will provide Westpac?s customers the ability to perform management functions through the internet. This suite will provide the bank customers to make their payments online quickly and securely, and also this suite provides services like transfer balance, view payment history, mail alerts, adding customers to value services etc. This mainly consists of four modules, they are Bank Information Module, finance module, customer module and report module.\nResponsibilities:\n\n\n      \nUnderstanding the Business requirements and Functionality.\n\n      \nInvolved in Manual, Functionality Testing and Regression Testing.\n\n      \nInvolved in Automation Testing.\n\n      \nPreparation and Execution of test cases by going through Specifications.\n\n      \nDeveloped and executed the Test Procedures and Test scripts by using QTP.\n\n      \nReport defects using Bug Tracking Tool.\n\nProject Profile #\n\n                                                                      \n\nTitle\n                  \n\n   \nMedical Report System.\nClient\n               \n\n   \nSt.Thomas Global Hospitals, \nChicago\n\nEnvironment\n   \n\n   \nJSP, Servlets, HTML, Oracle, Windows\n\nTesting tools\n   \n\n   \nQTP, TestDirector.\nRole\n                 \n\n   \nTest Engineer.\nDescription:\n             \nThe \nSt.Thomas\nGlobal\nHospital\n has a medical plan to promote the health of its employees and their Customers called as participants. Medical Report System is a healthcare system, a tool for the medical plan. It measures participants? health, identifies health risks, identifies health & lifestyle behaviors that could be improved, allows the medical staff to develop plans for health improvement and measures Progress/success in following that plan.\nResponsibilities:\n\n\n      \nUnderstanding the Business requirements and Functionality.\n\n      \nPrepared and executed test cases.\n\n      \nInvolved in Manual and Automation Testing.\n\n      \nPerformed Functional Testing and Regression Testing using QTP.\n\n      \nCreated and maintained automated test cases using QTP. \n\n      \nDefect Reporting using MercuryIntaractive.\n\nProject Profile #\n\n                                                                      \n             \n                                                                                   \n  \nTitle \n     \n          \n\n    \n\n\nInsurance Management System(IMS)\nClient\n               \n  \n\n\n\nState Farm Insurance, \nBelgium\n\nEnvironment \n    \n    \n\n\nVB 6.0, Oracle 8i, Windows2000\n\nRole\n     \n     \n       \n  \n  \n\n\nTest Engineer.\nTesting Tools\n      \n\n\nManual, TestDirector.\n\nDescription:\n\nIMS, European online insurer. IMS is an interactive insurer in Europe and is a national provider of Life and Long Term Care insurance in \nBelgium\n and have branches in \nFrance\n\nNetherlands\n and Germany etc., this contains the Data Forms, Requirements, Underwriting, Policy and Product in the form of detailed Use Cases to develop web based automated insurance system.\nResponsibilities:\n\n\n      \nUnderstanding the Business requirements and Functionality.\n\n      \nInvolved in Functionality Testing and Regression Testing.\n\n      \nInvolved in Manual testing.\n\n      \nDeveloped and executed the Test Procedures.\n\n      \nReport defects using Bug Tracking Tool.\n\n\n\n\n\nProject Profile #\n\n                                                                     \n\nTitle \n              \n       \n\nSales Information System\nClient \n           \n       \n\n\nExport Process Zone Development Authority (\nMauritius\n).\nEnvironment\n       \n\n\nJava, JSP and Oracle\nRole\n              \n      \n\n\nTest Engineer.\nTesting Tools\n      \n\n\nManual, TestDirector\n\n\nDescription:\n                     \nThis software was developed for Export Process Zone Development Authority of Mauritius. The activities will be mainly B2B (Business-to-Business). The aim is to provide easy access to information on suppliers of raw materials and to automate the procurement process such as placing orders for raw materials, accessories and equipment. The Sales Information System will also allow customer from abroad to contact local manufacturers to carry out business.\n\nResponsibilities:\n\n\n      \nUnderstanding the Business requirements and Functionality.\n\n      \nWriting and execution of test cases.\n\n      \nInvolved in Functional Testing and Retesting.\n\n      \nReport bugs using bug tracking tool.\n     ',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-18',NULL,'2007-10-18','2010-06-10 12:14:22','2010-06-10',14,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(218,'Divish J',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL,'0',NULL,'0','2006-09-28',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-10 12:14:22',13,'0',NULL,'200710/18/ATT40133.html','200710/18/DOC16342.doc','Divish J\nObjective\n          \n    \n\nSeeking a challenging and responsible position in the field of Oracle Administration as DBA, where I can contribute and exploit my DBA skills to the fullest extent of my potential. \n\n\nTechnical Environment\n\nDatabase - Oracle 9i\nOperating - Windows NT / 2000/XP, Linux.\nLanguages -SQL\nApplications / Tools:- \n\n|SQL*Loader, SQL*Plus, Exp/Imp, RMAN\n\n\nProfessional Experience\n\nPresently working in IBM India Pvt. Ltd. as Senior Executive (Database & Application Support ) Since Sep 2006 ? Till date \nWorked as\n\nTechnical Support Executive in Mainstay CRM from March 2004 -April 2006\n\nIBM India Pvt. Ltd.\n          \n                                      \n                   \nCompany:\n\nIBM\n Global Services India Ltd\n\n\n                  \nLocation: \nBangalore\n\nDesignation:\nSenior CSA-Lead CRM.\n          \n                          \nDuration:\n September?06 till date.\n\nCompany Profile\n\n\nIBM Global Services is the world?s largest information technology services provider, with revenues of approximately $35 billion. Services are the fastest growing part of IBM, with more than 141,000 professionals operating in 160 countries. IBM Global Services (\nwww.ibm.com/in\n) integrates all of IBM?s capabilities ? services, hardware, software and research ? to help companies of all sizes realize the full value of information technology.\n\n\nJob Profile:\n\nDatabase Analyst\n\nMy Responsibilities\n\n\n\n               \nSupport of Risk Assessment Manager (Financial Application) and its equivalent web based application.\n\n               \nHand in installation and maintenance of application and its backend.\n\n               \nBackend support includes installation & maintenance of databases in RDBMS like Sybase, MSSQL and Oracle. \n\n               \nMonitoring index usage.\n\n               \nPerforming Cold and Hot Backups and restored the databases from the Backup\n\n               \nKnowledge on \nRMAN\n to take the backups and restore the databases\n\n               \nData loading using \nSQL * Loader\n from flat files.\n\n               \nIdentifying areas to improve like adding space to datafiles.\n\n               \nProvided backup ORACLE DBA support to Senior DBA in the development, test and production environments.\n\n\nMainstay CRM \n      \n                                      \nMarch 2004 ? April 2006\nSenior Technical Support Executive\n\nRoles & Responsibilities:- \n   \nTroubleshooting\n\nhardware (Desktop, Laptops and Printers) and\n\nISP?s (dial-up and broadband) \nInstallation of Operating System and databases.\nWriting SQL queries.\nCoordinating with the Clients & Customers ( Queries)\n\n\n\n\nAcademic Profile\n\n          \nB com graduate from \nBangalore\nUniversity\n?55%\n          \nPursuing MSc in IT from Manipal University\n    \n\nCertification / Training:- \n\nOracle 9i Certified Database Administrator Professional ( OCP)\nMCP (Microsoft Certified Professional)\nTraining Program attended\n\n      \nOracle 9i DBA ? SQL STAR International, \nBangalore\n\nIndia\n\nSkill Sets\n\n\n        \nPerformed RMAN backups and recovery\n\n        \nCreating RMAN\n\nrecovery catalog\n\n        \nMigrating data using Import and Export utilities\n\n        \nLoading data using SQLLDR from flat files.\n\n        \nCreating tables and indexes as per the requirements.\n\n        \nTuning SQL statements.\n\n        \nMonitor database performance using STASPACK and Performance Views\n\n\nSTRENGTHS\n\n\n        \nStrong belief that everything is possible through hardwork and positive Attitude \n\n        \nDesire for innovation and continuous learning & Ability to blend into a team\n\n\n\n\nPersonal Detail \nDate of Birth \n        \n\n03/04/1980\nSex\n              \n          \n: Male\nMartial status \n       \n: Single\n          \nNationality\n            \n          \n: Indian\n          \nAddress\n       \n          \n: #31 5\nth\n main 8\nth\n cross \n                   \n                  \n   \n  \nKrishnappa block,Ganaganagar,\n                  \n                   \n  \n  \n\nBangalore-560032\n\n\n\n\n\n      \n\n\n(DIVISH J)\n     ',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-18',NULL,'2007-10-18','2010-06-10 12:14:22','2010-06-10',13,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(219,'Gaurav  G',NULL,NULL,NULL,'gauragnnv_soutgfndgh@yahoo.co.in','gauravgangfnggfndhi4all@gmail.com','0 93221 34034','0','9427526747','0','93221 34034','0','2008-04-29',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-10 12:14:22',13,'0',NULL,'200710/18/ATT40134.html','200710/18/DOC16343.doc','RESUME\nGaurav B. Gandhi\n                   \n\nMobile\n: - \n0 93221 34034 (Primary), 0 94275 26747\n\n\n       \nSummary\n\nGAURAV\n\n\n\nSkill Set: Oracle DBA, PL\\SQL, ORACLE TOOLS ? OEM, TOAD\nExperience: 25 Months \nPresent Employer: Tata Consultancy Services Ltd., Mumbai\nPresent Location: Mumbai\nBachelor Of Engineer - Computer Engineer\n\n\n\n       \nExperience\n\nDuration: -\nJune 2007 ? Continue?.\nCompany\n: - \nTata Consultancy Services Ltd., Mumbai\nDesignation: -\nAssistant System Engineer / Oracle DBA\nJob Profile:- \nBackup Configuration \n\n\n\nDuration: -\nFeb 2007 ? June 2007?.\nCompany\n: - \nHDFC Bank Ltd., Mumbai\nDesignation: -\nAssistant Manager-IT / Oracle DBA\nReal Time \nProjects: -\nBranch setups (production Server) on Oracle 9i Database.\nTools & Technology: - \n\nool for \n\nracle \n\npplication \n\neveloper (\nTOAD\n),\n\nracle \n\nnterprise \n\nanager (\nOEM\n), SQL Monitor.\nOracle 9i, D2K, Report 6i,\n Remote Diagnostic Agent (RDA).\nProject \nDescription: -\n\nCreation of Branch Level Database. \nJob Profile: -\nAs an Oracle DBA, I have done/am doing following activities\n\n\n Oracle 9i installation.\n\n Database Creation on oracle server.\n\n Establishment of client-server architecture.\n\n Management of TNSNAMES.ora\n\n Creation and Management of pfile and spfile\n\n Monitering Alert and Trace files in udump,bdump,cdump for\n   \ndatabase dartabase troubleshooting.\n\n Creating and Altering Tablespaces; Adding,Resizing,Renaming and Relocating Datafiles.\n\n Creation and Management of Indexes.\n\n Creation and Management of User and Roles and Privileges.\n\n ORA Error Solution.\n\n Daily Backup through Export.\n\n Performance Tuning of branch database\n\n\n\n\n\nDuration: -\nAug 2005 ? Feb 2007\nCompany\n: - \nSai Info System (\nINDIA\n) Pvt. Ltd., Ahmedabad.\nType of firm: - \nIT Solutions, Database Solutions to BSNL, \nIndia\n\nDesignation: -\nAssistant Manager -Software/ Oracle DBA\nReal Time \nProjects: -\n(1)\n   \nBharat Sanchar Nigam Ltd. (\nBSNL\n), \nNagpur\n\n(2)\n   \nBharat Sanchar Nigam Ltd. (\nBSNL\n), \nMysore\n\nTools & Technology: - \n\nool for \n\nracle \n\npplication \n\neveloper (\nTOAD\n),\n\nracle \n\nnterprise \n\nanager (\nOEM\n), SQL Monitor.\nOracle 9i, D2K, Report 6i.\nProject \nDescription: -\n\nDotSoft\n-Integrated Software for Commercial, Telephone Revenue Accounting (TRA), Directory Enquiry, Fault Resolving System (FRS) of BSNL, \nIndia\n\n    \nJob Profile: -\nAs an Oracle DBA, I have done/am doing following activities\n\n\n Oracle 9i installation.\n\n Database Creation on oracle server.\n\n Purify the data as per database needs.\n\n Establishment of client-server architecture.\n\n Management of TNSNAMES.ora\n\n Creation and Management of pfile and spfile\n\n Monitering Alert and Trace files in udump,bdump,cdump for\n   \ndatabase dartabase troubleshooting.\n\n Creating and Altering Tablespaces; Adding,Resizing,Renaming and Relocating Datafiles.\n\n Creation and Management of Indexes.\n\n Creation and Management of User and Roles and Privileges.\n\n ORA Error Solution.\n\n Daily Backup through Export.\n\n Weekly Cold Backup (Offline Backup).\n\n Backup through RMAN.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n       \nSkill Set\n\nDatabase technologies: -\nOracle 9i,Ms-Access\nProgramming Languages: -\nPL/SQL, VC++, C++, C, Shell Script\n\n\n\n       \nEducation, Concepts\n\nOperating System: \n\nUnix, Linux, Windows, AIX (IBM)\nEducation: -\n\nB.E.\n\nComputer Engineer - May 2005, \nDharmsinh\nD