ment and documentation.\n             \nPresently Working as a Consultant as a Business Objects Developer for Polaris \nSoftware\n,Mumbai\n from Jan-2007 to Till Date.\n\n\n\n\nQUALIFICATION (Education) \n\n\n       \nMIT (\nMasters In Information Technology Collaboration with IBM) From I.B.M.R \n  \ncollege\n,Pune\n\n\n       \nBachelor?s Degree in \nScience(\nComputer Science) from \nBhopal\nUniversity\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nTECHNICAL/ FUNCTIONAL (Application) SKILLS\n\nSkills\nDetails\n\n\nOperation System / Hardware\n\n\nWindows 95/98/NT/2000/XP,Unix(Solaris)\n\nLanguages\n\nC, C++,VB,SQL,PL/SQL\n\nWeb Technology\n\nHTML\n\nWeb Application & Server\n\n\n\nMiddleware\n\n\n\nDatabase \n\nOracle 9i,\n Oracle10g,MS-Access\n\nDataWareHouse\n\nETL(Datastage 7.1),BO-XI-Release2(Business Objects)\n\n\nOthers\n\nTOAD6,\n\nCosort\n 8.1.3\n\n\nReports,MS-Access,VBA\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nPROFESSIONAL EXPERIENCE\n\n\n\nCompany \nDesignation\nDuration\n\nPolaris Software Lab, Mumbai\n\nConsultant\n\nJan?07 till Date\n\n\nReliance Communications, Mumbai\n\nL3\n\n\nOct?03 ? Jan?07\n\n\n\nPROJECT SUMMARY\n\nProject# 1\n\n                                                 \nPolaris Software Lab, Mumbai\nProject Name: \nBestInClass\n\n         \nSince\n Jan?07 till date \nClient\n                     \nCitiGroup\n\nUk\n\nBrazil\n\nEnvironment\n\n       \n  \nBusiness ObjectsXI-R2\n,Oracle10g,Toad,Unix\nProject Description:\n\nI am under \nBestInClass\n Project which \nis\n\n\n\nCitiBank\n Project ,based on FRS(Financial Reporting\n\nSystems)for \nUK\n and \nBrazil\n. T\nhe Functional Solution for accessing data in the Country Core Reporting Warehouse staged as data marts and/or cubes.\nThe reporting out of the country core can be categorized into the following broad categories:\n\n         \nTraceability from Reporting to Local Level\n\n         \nFRS FDL Cube Reporting\n\n         \nLocal Regulatory Reporting for \nBrazil\n\n\nI am \nalso\n\nlook\n after\n\nInstallation of BusinessObjectsXIRelease2 on Unix\n\n& Windows (\nCilient\n & Server both).\n\nRole:\n\nConsultant\n\nResponsibilities: \n\n\n       \nDesign for product enhancements\n\n       \nResponsible for creating \nUniverse,Review\n the \nUniverse,Creating\n & formatting\n\nthe \n\nWebi\n reports in \ninfoview,doing\n\nthe \n  \nInstallation of BusinessObjectsXI-Release2 on Unix\n\n& Windows (\nCilient\n & Server both) with\n\nWeblogic\n & Tomcat & CMS on oracle10g/My SQL\n\n       \nTesting\n\nthe\n\nUniverse into Development\n\n       \nImplemented \nPOC?s\n (Proof of Concept), and prepared approach documents for the same\n\n\n\nProject# 2\n                                          \nReliance Communications,\n\nMumbai\n\n\nProject Name: CRM \n          \nSince\n Apr?05 to Dec?06\nClient\n                     \nReliance \nCommunications\n\nIndia\nEnvironment\n\n       \nETL(\nDatastage 7.1), \nCosort\n 8.1.3\n, Toad6\n,Unix\nProject Description:\n\n\nI see the entire ETL applications development process in CRM, ensuring that development, QA \nand\n\nthen\n\nProduction & the business side all work together and business application is developed on time & on task. Taking the \nData\n\nfrom\n different sources & \nTransfrom\n it according to business requirements & Load into the Target through \nETL(Datastage 7.1) \ntool.Creating\n charts using Visio s/w.\n\n\nRole:\n\nETL Developer\n\nResponsibilities: \n\n\n       \nDesign for product enhancements\n\n       \nResponsible for \nExtraction,Transformation,and\n Loading of\n\ndata from multiple Sources into Data Warehouse\n\n       \nTesting\n\nthe Jobs into \nDevelopment,QA\n\n& then \nProductionised\n\n       \nPromoting the Job from \nDevelopment\n,to\n QA\n\n& then \nProductionised\n through Version Control.\n\n       \nImplemented \nPOC?s\n (Proof of Concept), and prepared approach documents for the same\n\n\nProject# 3\nProject Name: CRM \n          \nSince\n Jan?05 to Mar?05\nClient\n                     \nReliance \nCommunications\n\nIndia\nEnvironment\n\n    \n\nBussinessObjects\n 6.5, Toad6\n,Unix\nProject Description:\n\n\n       \n      \n\n\nsee\n\nthe\n\nReporting Formatting\n\n\n\ndeveloping reports on\n    \nCustomer, Payment, Ageing, Adjustment, Churn. To seeing the Reports ,\nThe Business users can get a clear picture \nofthe\n revenue generated by customers, details of defaulter, details of ageing of customers and take actions/plan business rules according to ensure loss in revenue.\n\nResponsibilities: \n\n       \nUnderstand the \nCustomer\n\nApplication\n developed \n\nReport at the \nReliance Communications\n\nDatawarehouse\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nProject# 4\n\nProject Name: CRM\n\nJan?04 to Dec?04\n    \nClient\n\n                   \nReliance \nCommunications\n\nIndia\nEnvironment\n           \nOracle(\nsql,pl/sql\n),Toad 6,Unix\nProject Description:\n\nTo \nCapture\n the customers data related to Adjustment & Customer details \nfor\nAnalysis.\n   \nThis application primarily used for decision making by the business users.\n\nThe Business users can get a clear picture \nofthe\n revenue generated by customers, details of defaulter, details of ageing of customers and take actions/plan business rules according to ensure loss in revenue.\n\nRole:\n\nOracle Developer\n\nResponsibilities: \n\n       \nUnderstand the \nCustomer\n\nApplication\n developed at the \nReliance Communications\n\nDatawarehouse\n\n\n       \nWriting Ad-hoc Queries, Function, Procedure, Cursor, Tuning Queries, Finding Cost of the Queries, Analyze Data and also generate reports.\n\n       \nDeveloped standard Queries, Function, and Procedure for Business Object & ETL \nDatastage.Primarily\n developing reports on Customer, Payment, Ageing, Adjustment, \nChurn\n\n\n\n\nProject# 5\nProject Name: Voice & SMS\n\n       \nJan?04 to Dec?04\nClient\n                     \nReliance \nCommunications\n\nIndia\nEnvironment\n           \nOracle(\nsql,pl/sql\n),Toad 6,Unix\nProject Description:\n\nTo Capture the Voice & SMS usage data at a centralized location, \nwhich is used for usage analysis.\n\n\nThis application primarily used for decision making by the business users.\n\nBusiness users can analyze the trends in the usage details and plan for new Rate/Tariff plan based on usage pattern.\n\nBusiness users can come up with marketing strategy to increase customer acquisition, increase usage in areas where the usage is less as compared to the average country usage figures.\n\nRole:\n\nOracle Developer\n\nResponsibilities: \n\n       \nUnderstand the Voice & SMS developed at the Reliance Communications \nDatawarehouse\n\n\n       \nWriting Ad-hoc Queries, Function, Procedure, Cursor, Tuning Queries, Finding Cost of the Queries, Analyze Data and also generate reports.\n\n       \nDeveloped standard Queries, Function, and Procedure for Business Object & ETL \nDatastage.Primarily\n developing reports on Customer, Payment, Ageing, Adjustment, \nChurn\n\n\n\nProject# 6\n\nProject Name: R-Connect & R-World\n      \nJan?04 to Dec?04\nClient\n           \nReliance \nCommunications\n\nIndia\n     \nEnvironment\n\nOracle(\nsql,pl/sql\n),Toad 6,Unix\n\nProject Description:\n\n\nTo Capture the R-Connect & R-World usage data at a centralized location, \nwhich is used for usage analysis.\n\nThis application primarily used for decision making by the business users.\n\nBusiness users can analyze the trends in the usage details and plan for new Data plan based on usage pattern.\n\nBusiness users can come up with marketing strategy to increase usage in areas where the usage is less as compared to the average country usage figures.\n\nRole: Oracle Developer \n\nResponsibilities: \n\n       \nUnderstand the R-Connect & R-World developed at the Reliance Communications \nDatawarehouse\n\n\n       \nWriting Ad-hoc Queries, Function, Procedure, Cursor, Tuning Queries, Finding Cost of the Queries, Analyze Data and also generate reports.\n\n       \nDeveloped standard Queries, Function, and Procedure for Business Object & ETL \nDatastage.Primarily\n developing reports on Customer, Payment, Ageing, Adjustment, \nChurn\n\n\n\nProject# 7\nProject Name: Data Dictionary\n              \nFrom\n Oct?03 to Dec?03\nClient\n                     \nReliance \nCommunications\n\nIndia\nEnvironment\n           \nMs-access, VBA\n\nProject Description:\n\nThis System is designed for Data Analyst, which provides services like\n1) Information of\n   \nTables\n2) Easy to use and no need to go \nthrough\n\ndocument\n3) \nProgrammer\n\neasily\n make Query using\n\nthis tools.\n\nRole: Developer\n\nResponsibilities: \n\n       \nInvolved through Information Gathering Phase to development Phase. \n\n       \nData dictionary \nDesigning,\nImplementation,testing','Polaris Software',1,NULL,'2007-10-18',NULL,'2007-10-18','2010-06-10 12:14:22','2010-06-10',14,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(221,'Gyana sahoo',NULL,NULL,'Bangalore','gyanfbhfdbhfdba20@gmail.com',NULL,NULL,'0','91 9343826585','0',NULL,'0','2008-07-14',10,34,'2010-06-10 12:14:22',13,'0',NULL,'200710/18/ATT40136.html','200710/18/DOC16345.doc','PRASANTA SAHU\n\n\ngyana sahoo\n\nEmail: \ngyanfbhfdbhfdba20@gmail.com \n\n   \nCell:\n +91-9343826585\n                               \n                                                                                                                                                                        \n\nObjective\n\nTo pursue a career full of challenges which provides me ample opportunities to learn and grow. At the same time I want to fully utilize my capabilities to dedicate myself to the organization and add value to it by my sincere efforts. \n\n\nSummary\n\n\n      \n3+ yrs \nof \nIT experience\n in all the phases of SDLC.\n\n      \n2.5 yrs\n in \nData Warehousing\n, using \nInformatica &\n Business\n Objects\n\n\n      \n1 yr \nexperience in \nOracle SQL \nand\n PL/SQL \n\nProgramming.\n\n      \nGood experience in \n\n\nInformatica 7.x\n\nOracle 8i, 9i\n\n\n      \nKnowledge of \nBussiness Objects 6.x\n\n\n      \nExposure in both \nClient Server\n\n\nStand-alone\n\n\napplications. \n\n      \nExcellent Analytical and Programming skills.\n\n      \nGood team member providing innovative support.\n\n      \nExcellent written and verbal communication skill.\n\n      \nQuick learner and have diverse technical skills.\n\n\n\nWork Profile\n\n\n      \nWipro Technologies\n\nBangalore\n\n  \n\n            \n            \n\n           \nFeb 2006 ? Till Date\n\n      \nZippy Infotek, \nDelhi\n                                  \n\n           \nDec 2003 - Jan 2006 \n\n\n\n\nProfessional \n\nQualification\n\n\n      \nMaster in Computer Application (\nMCA\n), from \nUtkal\nUniversity\n\nBhubaneswar\n , Orissa\n\n       \nwith \n75%\n\n\n\n\nSkills Summary\n\nETL Tools\n\n\nInformatica 6.X, 7.x\nOLAP Tools\nBusiness Objects 6.x \nData Modeling Tool\nERWin \nLanguages\n\nC,C++, PL\n/SQL\nRDBMS\nMS Access, Oracle 8i/9i\nOperating System\nDOS, Windows NT 4.0, Windows 2000/98/XP, Unix\n\n\n\n\nProject: #1\nTITLE\n\n                       \n\nPhoenix\nOrganization\n         \n\n     \n: Wipro Technologies\nClient\n                          \n: J.P. Morgan Chase & Co.\nEnvironment\n               \n: Informatica 7.1, Oracle 9i, \n\nB.O. 6.1,\n\nWindows XP\nRole\n                            \n: Team member\nTeam Size\n       \n            \n: 6\n\n\nDescription: \n                \nThis project was developed for capturing, measuring, managing operational risk of \nJ.\n\nP. Morgan Chase & Co. \nduring the transaction. This project included three modules:\n\n1)\n      \nRED\n2)\n      \nSA\n3)\n      \nCA\n\n1) Risk Event Database (RED): The different types of risks already happened in the organization are collected from flat files maintained by the organization for last 10 years. Data loaded to the database using Informatica through different transformations like source qualifier, filter, joiner, lookup, update strategy, stored procedure, rank, sequence generator etc.\n\n\n2) Self Assessment (SA): The purpose of this module is to provide a means for the firm?s manager to document the process and activities performed within their organization, building the operational risk faced in performing those activities and evaluate the effectiveness of controls that have been put in place to mitigate and manage such risks. For each issue identified, risk managers have the ability to either institute and track action plans to address the issue and deficiencies in the risk environment or accept the risk faced through what is known as ?Risk Acceptance?. \nThis self assessment includes: \n(i)\n    \nIntegration of general auditing department \n(ii)\n   \nDynamic assessment Capabilities \n(iii)\n\nHistoric tracking of action plan \n(iv)\n\nHorizontal analysis across the firm.\n\n\n3) Capital allocation: Both RED and SA will utilize the same underlying organization and\n    \nprocess hierarchy to determine Capital allocation.\n\n\nResponsibility:\n\n\n      \nInvolved in ETL mapping using Designer\n\n      \nCreation of Unit Test cases and execution of Unit Test cases.\n\n      \nResponsible for Data Loading in Testing Schema and target Schema.\n\n      \nDefect fixing and closing of defects in MQC.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nProject: #2\nTITLE\n\n                       \n\nTEXAS\n IMEX DATAMART\nOrganization\n         \n\n     \n\n\nZippy Infotek\nClient\n                          \n\nTexas\nImex\n\nUSA\nEnvironment\n               \n: Informatica 6.1, Oracle 8i, B. O. 5.1, Windows XP\nRole\n                            \n: Team member\nTeam Size\n       \n            \n: 5\n\n\nDescription: \n\n             \nTexas Imex\n is a leading trading corporation in \nTexas\nState\n of \nUSA\n which deals with the medical supplies to domestic and international customers. The data warehouse is developed to analyze Sales and financial data for the company owned stores on a periodical basis.\n Data for analysis was received from a flat file and then converted to tables in Oracle database using Informatica tool. Flat file Sources were stored in Informatica repository, which was designed as staging area for transformation purpose. Depending on the dimensional data model implemented on oracle 8i, data was segregated, fine-tuned and transformed using Informatica features like Source Qualifier, Filtration, Aggregation, Joiner, Expression and Stored Procedure.\n\n\nResponsibilities:\n\n      \nInvolved in the Preparation of BA test plans, test cases\n\n      \nPredictions and execution of test cases\n\n      \nDefect log in MQC and sign-off for productions.\n\n\n\nProject: #3\nTITLE\n   \n             \n         \n\n\nCBT\nOrganization\n          \n     \n: Zippy Infotek\nClient\n             \n            \n: Floret Solutions, \nSingapore\nEnvironment\n               \n\n\nVB 6.0, Oracle 8i, Crystal Report 6.x, Windows 2000\nRole\n                            \n: Team member\nTeam Size\n                   \n\n\n\n\n\nDescription:\n\nThe CBT was developed with an objective, to help the students, grab the course content in a new exiting way. The course content is assisted with audio, image and video clippings. At the end of each session the student can test his/her efficiency by answering the questions (Subjective and Objective) at the end of each chapter. Reports on student?s performance are generated at the end of each exam session. The CBT too maintains a student?s database basing on the student?s performance, and is highly suited for educational institutions. In addition to it the teacher/professors can add to the course content without changing to the Base Content. This application can run on any stand alone PC and also on a LAN.\n\n\nResponsibility:\n\n\n      \nDesigning and Coding.\n\n      \nCreating reports for Quiz and Exam performance.\n\n\n\n\nEducational Qualifications\n\n\n\n      \nB.Sc. CHEMISTRY (Hons) from \nUTKAL\nUNIVERSITY\n, ORISSA in 1997 with 77%\n\n      \n+2 Sc. from C.H.S.E, ORISSA in 1994 with 72%\n\n      \n10\nth\n from BSE, ORISSA in 1992 with 77%\n\n\n\n\nFather?s Name\n\n            \n\n Mr. Babaji Charan Sahoo\nDate of Birth\n                 \n\n20-02-1977\nMarital Status\n                \n\n Single\nLanguage Known\n          \n\n English, Hindi, Oriya\nGender\n             \n            \n\n Male\nAddress \n                       \n\n # 684/A, 5\nth\nMain\n, 8th Cross\n                                        \n  \nTriveni Road\n, Yeshwantpur\n\n                                          \nBangalore-560 022\n\n                                                                                                \n                                                                                                             \n\n                                                                                                \n               \n\n\n                         \n  \nGyana Ranjan Sahoo','Wipro Technologies',1,NULL,'2007-10-18',NULL,'2007-10-18','2010-06-10 12:14:22','2010-06-10',13,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(222,'Madhurendra K',NULL,NULL,NULL,'madhudvdvrendrakdvumar@gmail.com','madhurendrakumar@gmail.com','09910169024','0','09910169024','0',NULL,'0','2005-04-29',7,NULL,'2010-06-10 12:14:22',14,'1','2010-06-21','200710/18/ATT40137.html','200710/18/DOC16346.doc','Ritesh Kumar\n\nA-1, C-253\n\nPandav Nagar, \nDelhi\n -110 092\nMobile\n\n09910169024\n   \nEmail:\n\nmadhudvdvrendrakdvumar@gmail.com\n\nMadhurendra K\n                                                              \n\n                \n\n\nTo secure a challenging and stimulating career, this provides me with opportunity for analytical thinking and learning, an exposure to enhance my analytical and technical skills.\n\n\n\n\n          \n5+ years experience in project analysis, design, development and execution with last 2 year as project lead.\n\n\n          \nSuccessful project execution experience.\n\n\n          \nWorking as Project Leader at ASTIN SOFTECH PVT. LTD., Noida.\n\n\n          \nExcellent power domain knowledge.\n\n\n          \nHaving good exposure to different SDLC processes.\n\n\n\n\n\nSkill Category\n    \nSkill Name\nBackend:\n     \nOracle 10g (SQL and PL/SQL)\nJava Skills:\n\n    \nJ2EE - General Knowledge\n     \nJ2EE ? JSP 2.0, Servlets 2.4, JDBC 3.0, JNDI\n     \nJava ? Applications\nApplication and Web Servers:\n\n     \nOracle 10g AS\n     \nApache Tomcat 5.5\nOther skills:\n\nKnowledge of UML\n\nBusiness Modeling\n\nJavaScript\n\nVisual Basic 6.0\n\nTOAD\n\n\n\n\n\n\nUtilities Sector (Power) ? Billing, Process Automation\nSystem Automation\nAttendance & Payroll (HR)\nAccounting\nMobile Computing\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nFeb, 2006 to Till Date\nCurrently working as \nProject Lead\n in \nASTIN Softech Pvt. Ltd\n., Noida (ASTIN has \nMobineers Info System Pvt. Ltd\n as its partners in \nIndia\n). ASTIN is an Indo-US based engineering economic systems company, basically working in electrical power industry.\nResponsible for:\n\n        \nStudy and analysis of tender document/ technical specification\n\n        \nProject effort estimation\n\n        \nSRS preparation\n\n        \nProject planning, monitoring and control\n\n        \nTeam building & resource management\n\n        \nClient interaction\n\n        \nBusiness process modeling, development (Using PL/SQL) and providing technical support to Java & Oracle team\nNov, 2003 to Feb, 2006\n\n\n\nWorked as a consultant to \nReliance Energy\n\nDelhi\n\n\nOn the roll of \nMobineers Info System Pvt. Ltd\n., \nDelhi\n as Senior Software Engineer\n\nResponsible for:\n     \nProcess study and providing the solution as automated process using IT\n\n     \ninfrastructure \n     \nAnalysis/ Design\n     \nDeveloping software using\n         \n  \nJSP, \nServlets, Visual Basic\n         \n  \nOracle 9i\n     \nManaging Software Development Team\nDomain:\n     \nUtilities Sector (Power)\n     \nAutomation\n     \nMobile Computing\n\nMarch, 2003 to November, 2003\nWorked as Software Engineer\nTime Technologies India Pvt. Ltd\n., Patparganj, \nDelhi\n\nResponsible for:\n       \nDeveloping software using\n         \n  \nJSP, Visual Basic 6, ASP\n         \n  \nSQL Server, Oracle\n           \nMs Access\n           \nDesigning database and module\n\nDomain:\n      \nAttendance & Payroll (HR)\nJanuary2003 to February 2003\nFreelancer \nFor BABA GLOBAL INC., Noida\nDeveloped a software in Visual Basic 6 & Ms Access\n\nFebruary 2002 to December 2002\nTeam Member\nAMTECH SOFTWARES\n, Kapoorthala, \nLucknow\n\nResponsible for:\n    \nDeveloping software using\n          \nVisual Basic 6\n          \nOracle, SQL Server\n          \nASP\n          \nDesigning database and module\n          \nHandling Accounting module\nDomain:\n         \nAccounting\n\n                \n\n\n\nMaster of Computer Applications\n         \nFirst Class\n\nB.Sc. (MATH)\n          \nFirst Class\n\n\n\n\n\n#1\nSpot Billing System (SBS)\nTeam size\n10\nTechnologies\nJSP, Servlets, JDBC\n     \nBackend: Oracle 10g (On Linux) AS: Oracle 10g AS\ndescription\n\n\nSpot Billing System (SBS) is an electricity billing project being developed for Jaipur Viduat Vitran Nigam Limited (JVVNL). \ncontribution\nContributing as project leader and billing logic implementation using PL/SQL.\n\n#2\nOnline Billing System (OBS)\nTeam size\n12\nTechnologies\nJSP, Servlets, JDBC\n     \nBackend: Oracle 10g (On HP-UX) AS: Oracle 10g AS\ndescription\n\n\nOnline Billing System (OBS) is a comprehensive project developed for Uttranchal Power Corporation Limited (UPCL). A web based application that maintains complete commercial database consisting entire data of Consumer, Metering, Billing, Collections, Closing balances, Disconnections, Customer complaints received from call centers, service requests customer service/call centers through LAN/ WAN network/ internet. With this system UPCL is generating consumer bills.\n\ncontribution\nContributed as project leader and implemented business logic using PL/SQL.\n\n#3\nEnergy Auditing\nTeam size\n\nTechnologies\nJSP, Servlets, JDBC, JNDI, Struts, MVC-2\n                              \nBackend: Oracle 9i\ndescription\n\n\nReliance Energy (BSES)\n\nDelhi\n has around 1800 feeders for this energy auditing was being done manually, through this system the whole auditing system is being automated. The system generates different types of reports.\ncontribution\nAs team leader for analysis, design using MVC three-tier applications development approach as well as execution of energy audit process for process refinement.\n\n\n#4\nDTMS \n(Distribution Transformer Management System)\nTeam size\n\nTechnologies\nJSP, Servlets, JDBC, JNDI, MVC-2\n            \n                              \nBackend: Oracle 9i\ndescription\n\n\nThe project is developed to monitor the distribution transformers the status of power and overloads, in which a intelligent energy meter with memory, processor and GSM modem being installed at site, the application running at server end receives SMS of different events and passes these information to Outage Management System for further action. Developed for BSES (\nReliance Energy\n).\n\ncontribution\nPresentation of technical big picture to top management, lead the project on technical front as well as system design and development.\n\n\n#5\nAMR \n(Automatic Meter \nReading\n\nTeam size\n\nTechnologies\nJSP, Servlets, JDBC, JNDI\n               \n         \n                       \n     \n\nBackend: Oracle 9i\ndescription\n\nA joint activity with Siemens Metering Group \nto monitor load profile and different parameters of 120 Power Distribution Grids of Delhi\ncontribution\nAnalysis, design and implementation of the AMR, which allows the grid staff and system control staff to monitor the load profile, events status as well as provides online data of voltage, current and power factor of whole electricity distribution network of \nDelhi\n. Designed as 3-tier client-server architectures, functions are separated into presentation, business application and data components.\n\n\n#6\nData Loader Module \nTeam size\n\nTechnologies\nJava\n                              \n                         \n             \nBackend: Oracle 9i\ndescription\n\n\nA multithreaded application developed to run on Linux AS 3. The application transfers data by unzipping and filtering the received files on the FTP server to Oracle server using SQL Loader Utility. The software is designed to run 24 x 7 environments it processes as on average 120 files per minute with proper logging of each event.\n\ncontribution\nDesign, development and Testing.\n\n#7\nSuspense Clearing Module\nTeam size\n\nTechnologies\nJSP, Servlets, JDBC, JNDI\n\n                                           \nBackend: Oracle 9i\ndescription\n\n\nThe project is developed to provide access to Suspense account data over intranet, and clear account based on details provided by Consumer. It is being used for BSES consumers.\ncontribution\nDevelopment of module\n\n\n#8\nBAM\n (Bill Amendment Module)\nTeam size\n\nTechnologies\nJSP, Servlets, JDBC, JNDI\n                        \n                             \nBackend: Oracle 9i\ndescription\n\n\nTo Amend Bills of Consumer, this S/w is running from 33 districts of \nDelhi\n where Oracle 9i database is located at \nNehru Place\ncontribution\nAs a team member for development of online reporting part using JSP/ Servlet, as well as design of user security management and PL/SQL Procedure development\n\n#9\nOnline Leave Management System\nTeam size\n\nTechnologies\nJSP, JDBC, and SERVLETS \ndescription\n\n\nThis system is developed by taking consideration of three levels.\n\nEmployee Level, Management Level and Administration level in an Organization.\n\nAt Employee level, an Employee can see its leave schedule. He/she can apply online for their leaves. Also they can see their leave status by checking online. At HR level, a manager can see all the leave applications and grant leaves to the appropriate applications.\n      \n                                                                                                                                            \nThe function of Administrator is to grant rights and permissions to different levels.\n\ncontribution\nHandled design and development.\n\n\n#10\nSMS Server \nTeam size\n\nTechnologies\nVisual Basic 6.0\n                              \ndescription\n\n\nServer Component developed for BSES (Reliance Energy) to send SMS through AT Commands set. It is being used with many applications like Outage Management, DTMS and Key Consumer Billing Information.\n\ncontribution\nDesign and development.\n\n#11\nMeter Management Module\nTeam size\n\nTechnologies\nVisual Basic 6.0\n                              \nBackend: Oracle 9i\ndescription\n\n\nA module developed to tracks meter for the life cycle form installment to removal which is issued by SAP inventory to Meter Management Group\ncontribution\nAs a team member for development of module\n\n\n#12\nARMS \n(Attendance Recording and Management System)\nTeam size\n\nTechnologies\nVisual Basic \n                                      \nBackend: Ms Access, SQL Server, Oracle\ndescription\n\n\nThis software transfer?s attendance machine (Punching Machine) produced data in DAT or DBF format to local database and generates different MIS reports. It is complete HR module.\ncontribution\nWorked as team member for front end development, back design and stored procedure development\n\n\n\n\n\n#1\nE-Business Solution & Web Based Market\n        \nDESCRIPTION\nFor partial fulfillment of MCA Program\nTechnologies\nHTML and JAVA 1.3\nJava Server Pages\nJavaScript, XML\nResign Web server on Win NT 4.0\nOracle 8i\n\ncontribution\nFull Project Design & Development\n\n#2\nRailway Reservation System\nDESCRIPTION\nFor partial fulfillment of BCA Program\nA simple simulation of Railway Reservation System\nTechnologies\nVisual Basic, Ms Access, Windows 98\ncontribution\nFull Project Design & Development\n\n\n\n                \nServed classmates as lab instructor for Oracle, UNIX, Assembly Programming and COBOL, also helped in designing their projects. \nIn leisure, working as project guide.\n\n\n\nName\nMadhurendra Kumar\nDate of Birth\n3rd February 1977\n            \nFather?s Name\nLate S. Narayan\nAddress\nA-1,C-253,\nPandav Nagar, Delhi-92\nMobile\n9910169024\nEmail Id\nmadhurendrakumar@gmail.com\n, madhurendra_kumar@rediffmail.com\n\n\n\n\n\n\nDate:\n                            \n                                                                                                \n        \nSignature \n\n                                                                                                                                \n                  \n\n   \nMadhurendra Kumar',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-18',NULL,'2007-10-18','2010-06-10 12:14:22','2010-06-10',14,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(223,'M Padmaja ',NULL,NULL,NULL,'padsafsdafdfmafsdja.dba@gmail.com',NULL,NULL,'0','91 9885 115 099','0',NULL,'0','2008-03-30',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-10 12:14:22',13,'0',NULL,'200710/18/ATT40138.html','200710/18/DOC16347.doc','Padmaja Manchana\n\n                                          \nM.Padmaja\nE-mail:padsafsdafdfmafsdja.dba@gmail.com\nMobile\n : (+91)9885-115-099\nHyderabad\n ? 11\n\n\nObjective\n\nResponsible position as an \nOracle Database Administrator\n where proven decision-making, managerial and software engineering abilities will be used for improving organisational productivity.\nLong term objective : To become a successful Database administration consultant.\n            \nSummary\n\n\n     \n2.1 Years of experience as Oracle DBA in 8i,9i and 10g DATABASE ACTIVITIES\n\nOracle DBA\n\n     \nAnalyzing and development of database using Oracle\n\n     \nDeep knowledge of architecture of Oracle.\n\n     \nClear concepts of RDBMS. \n\n     \nStrong interpersonal skills , an excellent team player and customer liaison \n\n     \nAbility to delegate and execute work assigned and excel in it. \n\n     \nAbility to keep cool under demanding conditions\n\nEducation:\n\n\n     \nB.Tech (CSIT) from JNTU ? \nHyderabad\n ? 2005 with 61.2%\n\n     \nIntermediate from Board of Intermediate (AP) in April 2001 with 66.8%\n\n     \nSSC from Board of Secondary Education in March 1999 with 72%\n\nTechnical Training:\n\n\n     \nDatabase\n\nadministration at \nXXXXXXXXXXXXXX,Bangloore\n\n     \nOracle Recovery Manger from \nXXXXXXXXXXXXXX, \nHyderabad\n\n\nTECHNICAL SKILLS\n                                                                \n\nRDBMS\n                                  \n\n\nORACLE\n\n9i, 8i\n      \nLanguages\n                               \n\n\nSql, Pl / Sql\nTools\n                                       \n\n\nSql*loader\n      \n   \n           \nOracle Enterprise Manager and RMAN\nOperating System\n                   \n\n\nWindows9x, Win NT, Windows 2K, Unix\n\n\nPROFESSIONAL EXPERIENCE SUMMARY\n\nWorking as a Software Engineer Since July 2005 to till date with \nXXXXXXXXXXX, \nHyderabad\n\n\n\n     \nInstalling Oracle server Enterprise Edition & oracle client software on windows\'98, windows NT & windows 2000 workstations by configuring SQL*Net.\n\n     \nAutomating Startup & Shutdown of Oracle Database in Multi User mode for normal operations and in Single User mode for database maintenance & housekeeping.\n\n     \nCreation of new databases and database storage objects like tablespaces, rollback segments, tables, indexes by estimating the space needed for the objects & assigning the storage parameters accordingly. \n\n     \nCreation and maintenance of other database objects like views, synonyms, sequences, database link, snapshots.\n\n     \nCreating database roles & assigning privileges to the roles.\n\n     \nCreating database users and by setting the default & temporary tablespaces, assigning quotas, roles, privileges and profiles to users. \n\n     \nMaintaining the security & integrity of the database.\n\n     \nPlan, test & implement the database Backup & Recovery strategy depending on the database size. Checking the daily, weekly, monthly backup status.\n\n     \nAutomating Daily Logical & Physical Backups.\n\n     \nManaging hot backups using Oracle Recovery Manager and Exports.\n\n     \nMaking tablespaces available to users, adding datafiles to the tablespaces and resizing of datafiles \n\n     \nChecking for fragmentation and apply de-fragmentation as necessary in Tablespaces.\n\n     \nMaking rollback segments online/offline, monitoring the growth of rollback segments, and shrinking the rollback segments to its optimal size if it is over grown.\n\n     \nDaily monitoring the database alert log files & trace files for any error messages, periodic checking tablespaces, rollback segments & index status. Checking the status of triggers, procedures, packages & compiles them if needed.\n\n     \nDaily Checking Database buffer cache hit-ratio, Library cache hit-ratio, Data Dictionary Cache hit-ratio and resize SGA if necessary.\n\n     \nChecking RBS content, Shared pool content, redo log content and apply the necessary actions.\n\n     \nDocumenting the database setup & updating the document whenever there is a change in the database struture, backup strategy etc.\n\n     \nCreation and Maintenance of Standby Database in managed recovery mode.\n\n     \nCoordinating with the application development team & fulfill their requirements at database level.\n\n\n    \nAreas of Expertise:\n\n\n     \nDatabase Creation. \n\n     \nUser administration ? add/modify/delete users.\n\n     \nMaintaining users level security\n\n     \nManaging user accounts and their updations\n\n     \nData files and Tablespace space managements\n\n     \nManaging initialization files\n\n- PFILE and SPFILE\n\n     \nManging Control files and Online Redo logs \n\n     \nTable layout design, table space management and user maintenance.\n\n     \nMonitoring and analysis of Oracle log files, background processes and jobs etc.\n\nPersonal Information:\n      \n      \n   \nFull Name\n                   \nPadmaja manchana\n         \nGender\n    \n                    \nFemale.\n         \nMarital Status\n              \nSingle.\n         \nAddress\n                       \nFlat:209,\n            \n                                   \n\nSri\nSai\nGalaxy\nPalace\n\n            \n                          \n         \n\nVijayapuri colony,Tarnaka,\n                                      \n        \n\n\nSecundrabad-500003.',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-18',NULL,'2007-10-18','2010-06-10 12:14:22','2010-06-10',13,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(224,'M Jeethendra',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Medgukasdfweakera43sdf@yahoo.co.in',NULL,NULL,'0','9986925439','0',NULL,'0','2006-11-28',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-10 12:14:22',14,'0',NULL,'200710/18/ATT40139.html','200710/18/DOC16348.doc','MUKKERA JEETHENDRA\n\n\n\nJEETHENDRA\n                                 \nMedgukasdfweakera43sdf@yahoo.co.in\n / +91 9986925439\n\nProfessional Summary:\nHaving \n3.4 years\n of experience in Data Warehousing as OLAP developer in \nCognos EP7 & Cognos ReportNet 1.1 \nand ETL developer in \nAscential Data stage.\nDeveloped OLAP applications using Cognos suite of tools and extracted data from the enterprise data warehouse to support the analytical and reporting for all Corporate Business Units.\nHaving Knowledge Over \nBusiness Objects 6.5\n and \nCognos 8 BI\nGood Knowledge on \nOracle9i ?SQL\n\nExtensive Knowledge of \nData warehousing\n and \nDBMS\n Concepts\n\nExperience:\nWorking as a Software Engineer in \nPLANETiSOFT,\nBangalore\n from \nJan 2006 to Till date.\nWorked as a Consultant in\n\nBiztune Software Pvt Ltd.,\nHyderabad\n from \nMay 2004 to Dec 2005.\nTechnical Skills: \n         \nOLAP Tools\n    \n\n   \nReportNet 1.1, Cognos EP Series 7, Business Objects 6.5\n    \n     \nETL Tools\n       \n\n\nData Stage\n   \nLanguages\n       \n\n\nSQL, PL/SQL\n   \nDatabases\n        \n\n\nOracle, SQL server, MS access\nEducation :\n\n        \nBachelors Degree from \nAcharya\nNagarjuna\nUniversity\n (2004).\nCertifications :\n\n        \nOracle Certified Associate (OCA) in Oracle9i \n\n\nProject # 1\n\n      \n\nProject\n                     \n\n           \nMatadox diagnostics\n      \n\nClient\n                        \n\n           \nMatadox diagnostics, \nMalaysia\n      \n\nDuration\n                   \n\n      \n     \nDec 2006 to Till date\n      \n\nRole\n                          \n\n           \nReport Developer\n\nProject Description\n\nIt is a Malaysia Government Organization. This has different modules developed for different departments like MIDA (Malaysia Industrial Development Association), MATRADE (Malaysia Trade Ministry) and MITI (Malaysia International Trade and Industries) and in turn MITI has 3 sub modules IIS (Industrial Information System), TFIS (Trade Facilitation Information System) and EIS (Executive Information System). EIS Module has only reports that can be viewed by different departments of the Malaysian Government.\n    \n\nResponsibilities\n\n\n        \nUnderstanding the business requirements and designing applications to meet their needs.\n\n        \nGenerating the Multilingual reports using report studio.\n\n        \nUsed Report Studio & Query Studio to develop various types of reports like List Reports, cross tab Reports, Chart Reports & Master/Detail reports.\n\n        \nCreated Query Prompts, Cascading Prompts, Calculations, Conditions & Filters.\n\n        \nScheduled and Distributed reports through Schedule Management in Cognos Connection.\n\n        \nCreated Reports Using Drill through according to the Business requirements.\n\n        \nPerformed Unit testing and Performance testing.\nEnvironment \n\n\nCognos Report Net 1.1 , Oracle 9i. and Windows 2000 Advanced server\nProject #2\nProject\n\n          \n             \n\n\n        \nData warehouse for Motor Insurance\nClient\n        \n      \n             \n\n         \nAbbey \nNational\n\nUK\n   \n\nDuration\n                      \n\n         \nJan 2006- Nov 2006\nRole\n                            \n\n\n         \nReport Developer\n\nProject Description:\n     \n                                      \n             \n                   \nAbbey National is \nUK\n based Insurance Company, is one of the largest insurance providers for\n   \nHome insurance, Motor insurance, and Travel insurance and Card insurance. This project involves building of\n   \ndata warehousing for Motor insurance.\nThe source data, which includes\n\nTypes of policies\nInformation about policy holder\nPolicy covered item details\nPremium Payment details\nTypes of claims like fast claim payments, fast repairs claim\n\nResponsibilities:\n\n        \nCreated Standard filters, calculations in Report Studio in report development.\n\n        \nDeveloped list reports, Cross tab Reports, Charts, Drill through Reports using Report studio and query studio.\n\n        \nCreated Standard and ad hoc Reports using Report Studio and Query Studio.\n\n        \nCreated Prompts, Filters & calculations to customize the data.\n\n        \nPerformed Unit testing and Performance testing.\n\n        \nScheduled and Distributed reports through Schedule Management in Cognos Connection.\n\nEnvironment \n\n\nCognos Report Net 1.1 , Oracle 9i. and Windows NT server\nProject # 3\n\n     \nProject Name\n             \n\n           \nHealth care Benefit plans.\n     \nClient\n                          \n\n          \nAnthem Health Care Inc,\nDuration\n                     \n\n\n         \nApril 2005 to Dec 2005\nRole\n                            \n\n          \nReport developer\n\nProject Description\n\nAnthem health care is one of the nations leading health care benefits companies, providing innovative health benefit plans, dental and vision benefits, pharmacy management services, life insurance and workers compensation, benefit management. Participated in the development of a system with decision making support solutions, giving mainstream users the ability to access, analyze and share information in Company?s database. The system generated reports to analyze referral trends ,waiting list for patients, activity for Doctors and patients, payroll ,gross profit analysis ,head count and financial reports on personal.\n\nResponsibilities\n\n\n        \nCreated standard and Ad hoc reports using Cognos Impromptu.\n\n        \nCreated Lists, Groups and Cross-tab reports with Drill-through functionality.\n\n        \nCreated multidimensional models using Transformer.\n\n        \nImplemented Drill-up and drill ?down paths in Power play reports.\n\n        \nCreated user Prompts, Conditions and Filters in the report generation. \n\n        \nGenerated reports using data from multiple databases.\n\n        \nCreated Prompts, Filters & calculations to customize the data.\n\n        \nCreating hot files, Snapshots, IMR reports based on Client Requirement.\n\nEnvironment \n\nCognos Impromptu, Oracle 8i and windows 2000 professional.\nProject # 4\n\n     \nProject Name\n             \n\n           \nBusiness Intelligence Solutions.\n\n\n     \nClient\n                          \n\n          \nAndersons\n Stores \nUSA\n     \nDuration\n                     \n\n\n         \nMay 2004 to March 2005\nRole\n                            \n\n          \nETL Developer\n            \nProject Description\n\n\nThe Retail Group operates six large stores in \nOhio\n that offer \"More For Your Home® - a full range of products for maintaining and improving the home and landscape - plus a variety of other offerings ranging from house wares and automotive supplies to fresh-baked breads and fine wines. According to the increasing customers demand it has opened new plants, sales offices and stores and has its own sales outlets. Data was extracted from Oracle data sources and flat files, cleansed, Transformed & Loaded in a separate database using Data Stage. The project objective is to create a Data warehouse to facilitate the analysis of cost and revenue data for products manufactured and sold by \nAndersons\n stores. \n\nResponsibilities:\n\n\n        \nUnderstanding existing business model and customer requirements\n\n        \nDeveloped jobs using various stages like Transformer Stage, Aggregator Stage, Hashed File Stage and Sequential File Stage.\n\n        \nParameterizing Jobs.\n\n        \nUnit Testing and Integration Testing.\n\n        \nStore metadata, reuse metadata and define routines using Manager\n\n        \nInvolved in Extraction, Transformation and Loading of the data from Oracle based Enterprise Data warehouse to the Data Mart\n\n        \nOptimizing Job Performance.\n\nEnvironment\n   \n            \n\n          \nData Stage 7.0, Oracle 9i , Windows 2000',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-18',NULL,'2007-10-18','2010-06-10 12:14:22','2010-06-10',14,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(225,'Akhil B ',NULL,NULL,NULL,'abatlasefgfentis@gmail.com',NULL,NULL,'0','9989924908','0',NULL,'0','2007-04-30',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-10 12:14:22',13,'0',NULL,'200710/18/ATT40140.html','200710/18/DOC16349.doc','Ravi Krishna Prasad\n\nAkhil B\n                                                           \n         \nabatlasefgfentis@gmail.com\n             \n        \n                                     \n            \n\nPh: +91-9989924908\n\nSummary:\n\nOver 3+ years\n of cutting-edge development and administration experience with main emphasis on \nOracle Application Development.\nMainly involved in various \nApplication Development \nactivities like creating of tables writing sub-programs (functions, procedures, triggers) and designing of reports, and tuning the databases at SQL level.\nWell versed in database programming concepts, packages, triggers & sub-programs.\n\nProfessional Experience\nPresently working as \nSoftware Developer\n at \nBeetel Business Solution, \nHyderabad\n from August 2004 to till date.\n\nTechnical Skills:\nDatabases\n                             \n\n Oracle 9i/10g.\nGUI\n                 \n            \n           \n\n Forms 9i, Reports 9i/10g.\nOther Tools\n                \n           \n\n TOAD 7.6/8.6,PL/SQL developer.\nLanguages\n      \n                      \n\n: C, SQL, PL/SQL.\nOS/Operating Platform\n       \n\n Windows Xp, Red hat Linux 9, Fedora Core 3&4 and Unix.\n                       \n                                \nProject Experiences\n\n\nProject #1:\nTitle\n                        \n: Vivra Atlanta\n\nOrganization\n         \n\n: Harvest Software Solutions, \nHyderabad\nClient\n         \n             \n: Vivra\n Health Insurance Corporation - \nUSA\n\nDuration\n                 \n: December 2006 ? Till Date\nDesignation\n            \n: Developer\n     \n\nTeam Size\n\n              \n: 4\n      \nModule \n                 \n\n: Claims \nTechnologies\n         \n\n: Oracle 9i and Internet Developer Suite.\n\nDescription:\nThe Vivra Atlanta project plays a significant role for the insurance company. This project is mainly meant for computerizing different manual activities in the insurance company. This project deals with managing the customer registration, policy plan, installment payments, and claims of the customers. The principal advantage of the system well formatted reports and effective storage, and maintenance of information. This project also facilities efficient searching.\n\nRoles and Responsibilities:\n\nAs a team member, was responsible for\n\nDeveloped Custom\n\nComponents using Packages, stored procedures, functions and triggers\nReports using Developer\nDesigned menus so that the application will be menu driven easy for navigation\nLoaded Product data using SQL*Loader\n\n\n\n\nProject #2\n\n    \nTitle \n   \n  \n        \n   \n\nHealth Information System\n    \nClient\n           \n   \n\nMCKKASAN\n\nUSA\n    \nOrganization\n\n: Harvest Software Solutions, \nHyderabad\n   \n\nTeam Size\n    \n   \n: 4\n    \nDesignation\n   \n\n: Developer\n    \nDuration\n       \n   \n: March 2006 ? November 2006\n    \nTechnologies\n   \n: oracle 9i and 9i Developer suite\n\nDescription\n\n        \n     \n             \nThe proposed HIS used for the processing and tracking of the Requests for Medical Reports and the associated functionality like billing and payment, Management reports. The request for the Medical report maintained in the system and routed through the departments and Doctors by a workflow engine in HIS. An email notification sent to the Doctors when a new report request is assigned to them. The HIS has a scheduler which execute daily once for fetching the outstanding tasks and sending an email notification to all departments/doctors about their outstanding tasks.\nAs a team member, was responsible for\n\nDeveloped Custom\n\nComponents using Packages, stored procedures, functions and triggers\nDeveloped \n\nReports using Developer\nDesigned menus so that the application will be menu driven easy for navigation\nLoaded Product data using SQL*Loader\n\nProject #3\n\n    \nTitle \n     \n        \n    \n\nPayroll Package\n    \nClient\n           \n    \n\nIndigo Soft, US\n    \nOrganization \n\n\n: Harvest Software Solutions, \nHyderabad\n    \nDesignation\n   \n\n\n: Developer\n   \n\nTeam Size\n    \n    \n: 3\n    \nDuration\n       \n    \n: May 2005 ? Feb 2006\n   \n\nTechnologies\n   \n: oracle 9i and 9i Developer suite\n\nDescription:\n\n              \nPayroll Package meant for Salary Calculation with earnings and deductions. Details to the banks, Provident fund information, Loan information were accurately calculated and dispatched through the reports on timely manner. The Main nature of reporting is financial reports importantly Salary slips, Banking reports, PF reports, Earnings and deduction reports.\n\nAs a team member, was responsible for\n\nDeveloped Custom\n\nComponents using Packages, stored procedures, functions and triggers\nDeveloped \n\nReports using Developer\nDesigned menus so that the application will be menu driven easy for navigation\nLoaded Product data using SQL*Loader\n\n\n\n\nProject#4\n                    \n\nTitle\n                        \n: Material Management System\nClient\n                     \n: Mathura Group of Companies\nOrganization\n          \n: ESN Technologies, \nHyderabad\nDesignation \n            \n\n\nSoftware Programmer.\nTeam Size\n              \n: 3\nEnvironment\n           \n: Oracle9i, PL/SQL, Developer Suite\nDuration \n                \n\n: Jan 2005 to April 2005\n\nDescription: \n\n                 \nMaterial management system is used for the manufacturing company\n\nto manage the raw material for production. Material management system works for planning, organizing and controlling the materials in the organization. The main function modules are supplier registration, RFQ generation and dispatch ,quotation receive and verification, purchase order generation to the suppliers, GRN generation, issue the raw materials, raw materials stock updation and generate the corresponding reports.\nAs a team member, was responsible for\n\nDeveloped Custom\n\nComponents using Packages, stored procedures, functions and triggers\nDeveloped \n\nReports using Developer\nDesigned menus so that the application will be menu driven easy for navigation\nLoaded Product data using SQL*Loader\n\n\n\n#Project 5\n\nTitle\n                  \n\nAttendance Certification System.\nClient\n               \n: Merril Lynch & CO, \nNew York\nOrganization\n    \n: ESN Technologies, \nHyderabad\n            \nRole\n                 \n: Software Programmer\n      \nTeam Size\n        \n: 3\n            \nDuration\n           \n: August 2004 to Dec 2004\n            \nPlatform\n           \n: Oracle, Forms and Reports\n\n\n\nDescriptions:\n             \nAttendance maintenance of employees is vital to any organization. It is very useful to check the punctuality and movements of personal. Moreover, it also forms the basis for employee payrolls and other benefits (like VL encashment, Special leave sanction, Incentive calculation etc.,). Maintenance of records on paper is a tedious task. To overcome from the above difficulties an \'On Line Attendance Certification System (OLACS)\' is developed.\n\nAs a team member, was responsible for\nDeveloped Custom\n\nComponents using Packages, stored procedures, functions and triggers\nDeveloped \n\nReports using Developer\nDesigned menus so that the application will be menu driven easy for navigation\nLoaded Product data using SQL*Loader\n\n\n\n\nProfessional Trainings:\nUndergone training at ?\nSQL* International Hyderabad\n? in Oracle Application Developer 9i.\nUndergone training for 45 days at ?\nMICO BOSCH\n\nBangalore\n as a part of academic curriculum in 3\nrd\n year.\nUndergone training for 30 days at ?\nINSTRUMENTATION LIMITED\n\nDelhi\n as a part of academic curriculum in 2\nnd\n year.\n\n\n\nEducational and Professional Credentials:\nHave done B.Tech. in Electrical engineering from\n Malaviya\n\nNational Institute of Technology,\n\nJaipur,Rajasthan \n\nin the year 2003 in Second Division.\nPassed 10+2 Examination from \nAISSCE\n in the year 1998 Second Division.\nPassed 10\nth\n class Examination from \nAISSE\n in the year 1994 in First Division.\n\n\nProfessional Membership:\nStudent Member Of Indian Society For Technical Education(ISTE)\nStudent Member of \nInstitute\n of \nElectrical Engineers\n (IEE).\n\n\nExtra curricular Activities:\nWas A Member Of College Runners Up Football Team In \nB.O.S.M-2002 \nAt\n     \nB.I.T.S (Pilani).\nWas An Active Member Of College Sports Executive Committee To \nConduct\nCollege\n Sports Meet- 2002.\nOrganize \nTecwit-2001\n, A State Level Paper Presentation Contest At College As A Part of \nI.E.E\n Chapter Of M.N.I.T, Jaipur.\nWas an Executive Member of \nI.E.E\n\n2001, 2002, 2003 \nchapter of M.N.I.T, Jaipur.\nWas an active member in conducting Electrical Feast \nSPARK-2002\n at M.N.I.T, Jaipur. \nHold an \nN.C.C\n certificate for excellence for conducting various social activities in rural areas of Mahadevpur, Arunachal Pradesh.\nHold a \nBrow Belt\n in \nKENPO\n Martial Art under 50 kg weight\n\n\nProjects and Seminar?s:\nDeveloped and designed an ?\nAutomatic Petrol Dispensing Machine\n? as a part of academic curriculum in the final year.\nDesigned an ?\nAutomatic Railways Traffic Control System\n? at \nCamaraderie-2001\n a national symposium conducted by dept. of Computer Engineering, M.N.I.T, Jaipur.\nPresented a seminar on ?\nEthnicity, Alienation and Violence in the North-East\n? organized by dept. of Political Science at \nUniversity\n of \nRajasthan\n\nPresented a paper on ?\nPower Optimization in Real Time Embedded System\n? as a part of academic curriculum in the final year.\nPresented a seminar on ?\nNeural Networks\n? at \nMirage-2001\n a national symposium conducted by dept. of Electronic and Communication, M.N.I.T, Jaipur.\n\n\nHobbies:\n       \nNet surfing and listening to music.\n\n\n\n\nPersonal Data:\nFather?s Name\n           \n: late D.N Borah.\nDate of Birth\n              \n\n01/06/1979\n\nNationality\n                 \n: Indian\nLanguage Proficiency: English, Hindi, Assamess and Bengali.\nPresent\n\nAddress\n        \n\n\nB-403,Bhavaya?s Anandam\n                                            \nNizampet Road\n, Hydernager\n                                            \nKukutpally, Hyderabad-72\n      \n                 \n                    \nReferences:\n1)\n     \nMr\n\n\nBiswajit Bhuyan.\n\nSoftware Engineer, \nMotorola India Pvt. Ltd.\nHyderabad\n\n2)\n     \n\nMr\n\nSukurut Usgaonkar.\nSenior Software Engineer, \nC.S.C India Pvt. Ltd.\nHyderabad',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-18',NULL,'2007-10-18','2010-06-10 12:14:22','2010-06-10',13,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(226,'Ani sadan',NULL,NULL,NULL,'jogrgrgb4argni@gmail.com',NULL,NULL,'0','9916031221','0',NULL,'0','2007-07-31',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-10 12:14:22',14,'0',NULL,'200710/18/ATT40141.html','200710/18/DOC16350.doc','Rubin Luke\nAni \nSadan\n                                                                    \n    \nLocation: \nBangalore\n                                                     \nEmail:\njogrgrgb4argni@gmail.com\n     \n              \n                        \n                        \n  \n  \n        \n     \n    \n                 \nMobile\n\n9916031221\n                          \n                                       \n                                                          \n\n\nCareer Objective\n\nTo pursue a challenging career and reach new peaks as an \nSAP BW Consultant\n\n To be a source of strength and dedication to whomsoever I may be working with, in the filed of \nSAP\n and Leading to organization growth.\n\nSummary\n\n         \nA post graduate in computer science (\nMsc\n) with \n2 years and 10 Months\n of experience in database administration (Production Support) ? Oracle 9i,10g, SQL Server 2000.\n\n         \nUndergone \nSAP BW\n Training from \nIDOSAP ,\nBangalore\n ( A \nCanada\n Based Company).\n\n         \nProficiency of designing and building number of InfoCubes, ODS Objects, InfoSets, MultiProviders, InfoObjects, Hierarchies, DataSources, InfoSources, Update Rules, Transfer Rules, InfoSpokes and Process Chains. Expertise in maintenance of Process Chains, Monitoring, Open Hub Service, Performance Tuning, Aggregates and BW Transports\n\n\n         \nWorked in Windows (Windows 2000\n,2003\n) and Unix Flavors (Linux, Solaris).\n\n         \nOCP \ncertified.\n\n         \nWorking knowledge of database administration, troubleshooting and maintenance.\n\n         \nEasygoing personality, hardworking and ability to perform under pressure.\n\nTechnical Skills \n\nSAP BW: SAP BW 3.5\nData Modeling: Involved in Activating the Business Content, Creating Custom cubes and DSO/ODS, \nDTPs\n and Transformations. Involved in creation of Basic Cubes, Multi Cubes and Remote Cubes.\nData Extraction: Involved in extraction from MM, SD and Generic Extractors, LO-Cockpit, Flat file Extraction, Data extraction from Oracle database using \nDBconnect\n\nDatamart\n, and Open Hub Extraction. \nCustomized Business Content, InfoSources and ODS Objects. \nDeveloped Material Movements Cube and Purchasing data Cube and developed reports on MM Cubes. \nLoaded Master and Transactional data from SAP R/3 via data staging to PSA, ODS and InfoCubes. \nDeveloped Queries using filters, navigational attributes, variables, conditions, calculated key figures and restricted key figures. \nWorked Extensively on Data Analysis tool - \nBEx\n Analyzer (RRMX) to create Queries on ODS objects, Info Cubes, MultiProviders, \nInfo\n Sets and published Web reports. \nCreated \nInfoPackages\n for both master data and transaction data InfoSources and scheduled those using \nInfoPackage\n groups. \n\nOperating system\n                       \n: Microsoft Windows, Sun Solaris, Linux\nDatabases\n             \n                     \n: Oracle 9i\n,10g\n, SQL Server 2000.\n\nExperience\n\n1.\nIBM INDIA PRIVATE LIMITED\n   \n(Nov 2006 ? Present)\nPresently working as a Senior DBA with \nIBM INDIA PRIVATE LIMITED\n\nBangalore\n as a contract employee of \nDatacore\n Technologies\n\nBangalore\n for the last 8 months.\n Doing production support for 60 database servers (\nClient :\n British Petroleum).\n\n2.\nMACS\n INFO SOLUTION PRIVATE LIMITED ( Dec 2004 to Nov 2006)\n           \nWorked as a Junior DBA with \nMacs Info Solution Private \nLimited\n\n Erode from Dec 2004 to Nov 2006. \nHandled SQL Server and Oracle Databases.\n Was part of a 20 member team which implemented Dealership Management System Project for TVS Motor Company, \nHosur\n\n\nProjects Handled\n1. \nCompany:\n IBM INDIA PRIVATE LIMITED\n    \nClient\n      \n\n British Petroleum\n    \nDatabase :\n Oracle 9i/10g, \nSql\n Server 2000\n    \nOperating System:\n Sun Solaris, Windows 2000/2003\n      \n              \nHandled over 60 database servers with more than 350 databases.\n\n2. \nCompany:\n Macs Info Solution Private Limited\n    \nClient\n      \n\n TVS Motor Company, \nHosur\n    \nDatabase :\n Oracle 9i, \nSql\n Server 2000\n    \nOperating System: \nWindows 2000, \nSuse\n Linux\n                    \nWas\n\npart\n of a 25 member team to support database activities in Dealer Management System project.\n\nCurrent Job Profile:\nDatabase Administrator having 2 years 10 months of experience.\n\nResponsibilities Include: \n\n      \nMonitoring \ntablespace\n growth and disk space.\n\n      \nChecking Alert log file.\n\n      \nOracle Server Installation, & Configuration of Database Server.\n\n      \nCreation of Users and Management.\n\n      \nBacking up database.\n\n      \nPerforming various change requests as customer needs.\n\n      \nMigration and Patching.\n\n      \nDatabase refresh.\n\n      \nPrompt resolution for user problems by ensuring compliance to Service Level Agreements.\n\n      \nHandling Problem tickets.\n\n      \nProviding \noncall\n support on weekends.\n\n      \nHandling SQL Server related activities.\n\nInternational Certification\nOracle Certified Professional from \nOracle\nUniversity\n\n\nEducation Details\nM.Sc\n Computer \nScience\n\n with \n71%.\nB.Sc\n Computer \nScience\n\n with \n70%.\nT.H. \nS.E\n\n\n\nXII) with \n60%.\nI.C.S.E\n\n\n\nX) with \n61%.\n\n\n              \n     \nAni K \nSadan\n\n                                            \n                           \n                                               \n               ',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-18',NULL,'2007-10-18','2010-06-10 12:14:22','2010-06-10',14,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(227,'Bhoopathy s',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Suresh_bhoopathy@satyam.com',NULL,NULL,'0','91 9966351170','0',NULL,'0','2005-04-29',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-10 12:14:22',13,'0',NULL,'200710/18/ATT4887.html','200710/18/DOC16351.doc','Resume Standard Format\nProfessional Summary\nHaving \nfive plus years\n of experience in IT industry of which nine months in US and one year in \nTaipei\n and three months in \nHamburg\n\n\n\nHaving good experience in Oracle Applications implementation and Support in different roles including Module Leader, Team Leader and functional experience in Order Management, Teleservices and Shipping domains.\n\nWorked extensively in RDBMS like Oracle, Forms6i, and Reports6i and OS concepts.\n\nHe has worked on Windows NT, 95, CE, SCO-UNIX and Linux platforms. \nEducation\nDegree\nUniversity\nYear of Passing\nMCA\nIGNOU\n(04/2005)\nBA\nMadras\nUniversity\n(04/2000)\nHDSE\nAPTECH\n(04/2000)\nExperience\nOrganization\nDesignation\nDuration \nSatyam Computer Services Ltd., \nSystems Analyst\n(03/2007) ? Till Date\nCovansys Global Services., \nAssociate Projects\n(08/2006) ? (03/2007)\nInformation Dynamics Ind Pvt Ltd\nProject Coordinator\n(05/2004) ? (08/2006)\nLambent Soft Systems Ind Pvt Ltd\nProgrammer\n(03/2002) ? (04/2004)\nTechnical Skills\nHardware\n1*5 GB RAM, SCSI Hard Drive\nOperating Systems\nWindows NT, XP,2000(server), Unix, TRU Unix64, SCO Unix\nLanguages\nPL/SQL, SQL\nDatabases\nORACLE\nGUI\nForms 6i, 10g, Reports 6i \n\nDesigner 2000\nCase Tools\nVSS\nWeb Related\n\nTools & Utilities\nPL/SQL Developer, TOAD, SQL Navigator, Remedy Tools, VSS\nDomain Knowledge\nShipping\nTrainings\nSl#\nTitle\nLocation\nOrganized by\nDuration\n\nDBA\nIndia\nLambent Soft Systems\n2 Weeks\n\nProjects Profile\n\n\n4. \nProject Name : Tele Services Customization(Oracle Applications Rel.11.5.10)\nClient\nCisco Systems, Inc. \nUSA\nRole\nTeam Leader\nOrganization\nSatyam Computer Services Limited, \nIndia\nDuration\n(03/2007) ? Till date\nTeam Size\nProject :5\nModule : 1\nEnvironment\n(with skill versions)\nOracle 10g, Forms 10g with Unix and Windows\nSoftware\n\nLanguages : PL/SQL, SQL\nDatabase : Oracle 11.5.10\nTools : Toad, PL/SQL Developer\nO/s : Unix, Windows NT and XP\n\n\n\nProject Description\nOracle TeleService automates whole problem resolution process from the time a customer calls in, sends an e-mail, or enters a service request on the Web. Agents can use Oracle TeleService to update customer records, validate product ownership and contract coverage, provide proactive and personalized customer service, and resolve many problems during the initial contact using a knowledge base.\n\nThe Oracle Forms-based module of the Oracle TeleService encompasses the widest\nrange of features of all the modules. Its robust technology and integration with inbound\ntelephony and Oracle Order Management for the processing of service charges makes\nthis module ideal for high-volume call centers.\n\nOracle TeleService is composed of the following modules:\n\n          \nCustomer Care\n\n          \nService Request\n\n\nContribution\nAs a team leader, was responsible for \n\n        \nGathering the enhancements and requirements for Customization.\n\n        \nBRD Analysis\n\n        \nGap Analysis between the BRD and Oracle Standard Teleservices\n\n        \nDesign and Development of back-end applications using PL/SQL / Forms10g.\n\n        \nTesting - unit testing and integration testing\n\nResponsible for overseeing the Quality procedures related to the project.\n\n\n3. \nProject Name : DTS ColorTrax\nClient\nWashington Mutual Bank\nRole\nTeam Leader\nOrganization\nCovansys India Limited \nDuration\n(08/2006) ? (03/2007)\nTeam Size\nProject :\nModule : \nEnvironment\n(with skill versions)\nOracle 9i with Unix and Windows\nSoftware\n\nLanguages : PL/SQL, SQL\nDatabase : Oracle 9i\nTools : PL/SQL Developer, Remedy\nO/s : Unix, Windows NT and XP\n\nProject Description\nDTS ColorTrax project deals with home loans section developed and maintained for Washington Mutual bank to the clients Fildelity, Capital Markets, Accupost, Alltel and Wincms. This project is used for data transformation in Oracle 9i and UNIX. This project is developed to handle Teradata transactions which need to be transferred on daily basis from flat files to Oracle DB. \nContribution\nAs a team leader, was responsible for \n\n        \nGathering the enhancements and requirements.\n\n        \nDesign and Development of back-end applications using PL/SQL.\n\n        \nUTL file handling technique is used to transfer the data to Oracle.\n\n        \nTraveled onsite for implementation at client site,\nUSA\n and was single point control for maintaining this module. \n\n        \nTesting - unit testing and integration testing\n\n        \nResponsible for overseeing the Quality procedures related to the project. \n\n2. \nProject Name : Afsys+\nClient\nYang Ming Line Shipping Corporation\nRole\nProject Coordinator\nOrganization\nInformation Dynamics India Private Limited, \nIndia\nDuration\n(05/2004) ? (08/2006)\nTeam Size\nProject :\nModule : \nEnvironment\n(with skill versions)\nOracle 9i with Developer 2000 and Windows\nSoftware\n\nLanguages : PL/SQL, SQL\nDatabase : Oracle 9i\nTools : PL/SQL Developer\nO/s : Sun Solaris\nProject Description\nAfsys+ is the core project of shipping module in Forms6i, Reports6i and oracle9i. It Covers the total shipping domain and it includes Equipment Control, Booking, Export Documentation, Import Documentation, CIS, Accounts etc., \n\nContribution\nAs a project coordinator, was responsible for \n\n        \nGathering the enhancements and requirements.\n\n        \nDesign and Development\n\n        \nSingle point control for implementation and requirement gathering for this module to the locations \nUSA\n\nTaipei\n\nand\nHamburg\n\n\n        \nTesting - unit testing & integration testing\n\n        \nResponsible for overseeing the Quality procedures related to the project. \n\n        \nClient site for implementation and user training. \n1. \nProject Name : Direct and Indirect Purchase Module (DIPM)\nClient\nRane Engine Values\nRole\nProgrammer\nOrganization\nLambent Soft Systems India Private Limited, \nIndia\nDuration\n(03/2002) ? (04/2004)\nTeam Size\nProject :\nModule : \nEnvironment\n(with skill versions)\nOracle 8i with Developer 2000 and Windows\nSoftware\n\nLanguages : PL/SQL, SQL\nDatabase : Oracle 8i\nTools : PL/SQL Developer\nO/s :Windows NT and XP\n\nProject Description\nThis project is a development of Purchase module in Forms 6i and reports 6i. This module has the following sub-modules such as Item creation, Indent creation, Purchase order creation & Mrir Generation etc. \n\nThis module was developed to facilitate the operations of Direct and Indirect Material departments.\nI was also involved in the conversion of this module from Forms 3.0 to Forms 6.0 and Reports 1.1 to Report 6i. \n\nContribution\nAs a programmer, was responsible for \n\n        \nGathering the enhancements and requirements.\n\n        \nDesign and Development\n\n        \nClient site for implementation and user training. \n\nPersonal Details\nName\nSuresh\n Bhoopathy\nID No. (\nIndia\n & US)\n\n58175\nEmail Id \n(i.e., Satyam?s email id)\nSuresh_bhoopathy@satyam.com\nPassport No.\n\nE0886929\nValid Upto: \n(03/02/2012)\nType of Visa holding (if any)\nB1\nValid Upto : \n(10/06/2016)\nLocation\n\nUS\nContact Numbers\n\nMobile\n: +91 9966351170',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-18',NULL,'2007-10-18','2010-06-10 12:14:22','2010-06-10',13,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(228,'Anil R',NULL,NULL,NULL,'arjudgdldsvgsdaanil@gmail.com',NULL,NULL,'0','91 99165 88929','0',NULL,'0','2007-04-30',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-10 12:14:22',14,'0',NULL,'200710/18/ATT4888.html','200710/18/DOC16352.doc','ghgfhbgfhgfh\nANIL R\n                                                                          \nE-Mail : \narjudgdldsvgsdaanil@gmail.com\n                      \n                           \n                                             \n                        \nMobile : +91 99165 88929\n\n\nOBJECTIVE:\nTo work in a quality driven technical environment, that enhances my knowledge , skills and\n\nallows me to use my experience for my personal , professional\n\nand organization growth.\n\nPROFESSIONAL PROFILE:\n\n      \nI have over 3+ years of IT experience in implementing Data Warehouse applications\n\n      \nI have participated on various data warehouse assignments in the Development database\n\n      \nExperience in implementation of Data warehouse applications mainly \nExtraction, Transformation and Loading\n process using ETL tool \nINFORMATICA\nPOWER\nCENTER\n\n      \nExtensive k\nnowledge in \nData Warehousing concepts\n\n      \nExtensive experience in \nINFORMATICA\nPOWER\nCENTER\n\n           \nExcellent written and verbal communication in corporate environment and the Ability to perform independently as well as in team environments.\n\n\nPROFESSIONAL SUMMARY:\n\n\n      \nWorking as a ETL Developer for \nCovansys\n Global Technology Services\n from Dec 2005 to till date.\n\n      \nWorked as a ETL Developer for \niGATE\n\nGlobal Solutions Ltd\n from Mar 2004 to Nov 2005.\n\nPROFESSIONAL QUALIFICATION:\n\n\n      \nBCA \nfrom\nKakatiya\nUniversity\n\nAndhra Pradesh\n\nIndia\n\n\n\nTECHNICAL SKILLS:\n\nOperating Systems\n                 \n\n           \nWindows\n\n2000, Windows NT and UNIX\nRDBMS\n                                   \n\n           \nOracle 9i, MS-ACESS.\nETL Tool\n                                 \n\n           \nInformatica 7.1\nOLAP Tool\n     \n       \n          \n       \n\n           \nBusiness Objects XI\nWeb-Based\n                              \n\n           \nHTML, XML. \n\n\n\nPROJECT SUMMARY\n\nProject 1\n                                 \nUNION BANK OF \nCALIFORNIA\nType\n                                        \nDevelopment - Business Applications - GUI\nRole\n                                        \nETL Developer\nPlatform\n                                 \nClient/Server, UNIX, Windows\nTechnology\n                             \nData Warehousing\nTools\n                                       \nInformatica 7.1\nRDBMS\n                                  \nOracle 9i\nClient\n\n                           \n         \nUNION BANK OF \nCALIFORNIA\n\nUnion Bank of \nCalifornia\n has implemented a centralized data warehouse (CDW) on Oracle 9i, from different source systems. The bank has taken an initiative to increase the performance of the loads so that data will be available within the next working day in Data marts for analysis and decision-making purposes. The data warehouse built will serve as a firm foundation for Business Intelligence and Data Analytics subsequently. \n\nResponsibilities: \n\n\n      \nMainly involved in ETL Developing\n\n      \nUnderstanding the Business rules completely and implemented data Transformation methodologies.\n\n      \nCreated mapping using the transformations such as the Source qualifier, Aggregator, Lookup, Filter, Router, Sequence Generator and Update Strategy.\n\n      \nDesign a mapping Transforming one record into the multiple data records.\n\n      \nInvolved in designing the mapplet and reusable Transformation according to the business needs.\n\n      \nAnalyzed the specifications and identifying the source data that needs to be moved to the data warehouse\n\n      \nDesign a mapping with multi file loading using File Repository.\n\n      \nInvolved in designing the bottle necks at the mapping level and session level.\n\n\nProject 2\n                                 \nGLIC DATA MART\nType\n                                        \nDevelopment - Business Applications - GUI\nRole\n                                        \nETL Developer\nPlatform\n                                 \nClient/Server, UNIX, Windows\nTechnology\n                             \nData Warehousing\nTools\n                                       \nInformatica 6.2\nRDBMS\n                                  \nOracle 9i\nClient\n\n                           \n         \nGuardian Life Insurance Corporation, \nUSA\n\nGuardian Life Insurance Company is the fourth largest Insurance & Mutual fund Company located in \nNew York\n\nUSA\n. Guardian and its subsidiaries today provide almost three million people with life insurance, retirement services, and investment products. \nThe data mart is built to store summarized data about customers, agents, policies, premiums, climes and region wise, to analyze the performance of the company. The ETL process developed using Informatica and various business reports developed using Business Objects. \n\nResponsibilities:\n\n\n      \nAnalyzed the sources, targets, transformed the data, mapped the data and loading the data into Targets using Informatica\n\n      \nCreating the mappings and transformations using Informatica\n\n      \nScheduling ETL process on weekly basis\n\n      \nUsing ETL Process to Extract, Transform and Load the data into stage area and data warehouse\n\n      \nUsing Transformations to clean the data from staging area as per the data warehouse requirements\n\n      \nCreating reusable transformations and using in mapping\n\n      \nCreating Mapplets and using in mapping\n\n      \nResolving if any issues in transformations and mappings\n\nProject 3\n                                 \nENTERPRISE\n DATA WAREHOUSE\nType\n                                        \nDevelopment - Business Applications - GUI\n      \nRole\n                                  \n      \nETL Developer\nPlatform\n                                 \nClient/Server, UNIX, Windows\nTechnology\n                             \nData Warehousing\nTools\n                                       \nInformatica 6.2\nRDBMS\n                                  \nOracle 9i\nClient\n\n              \n             \n         \nPartminer Inc, NY\n\nPart miner is a unique portal which provides B2B E-commerce Application Where buyers can send request for quotations for electronic Parts, and Vendors can respond back to the buyers with quotations and buyers can issue purchase orders if they are satisfied with supplier\'s quotations. All this buyers information come from various sources like SQL Server and Oracle are bought together every night in the warehouse that is the one and only source of consolidated data. Analyzed, interpreted the business requirement to design and developed complex reports\n\nResponsibilities:\n\n\n      \nData Extraction, Transformation and Loading from Source to Target using Power Center of Informatica\n\n      \nExtracted source definitions from various databases like oracle and SQL\n\nServer into the \nPower\nCenter\n repository.\n\n      \nImporting Source/Target tables from the respective databases and created reusable transformations and\n   \nmappings using Designer Tool set of Informatica.\n\n      \nDeveloped Informatica mappings.\n\n      \nResolving if any issues in transformations and mappings\n\n      \nInvolved in the Performance Tuning.\n\n      \nWorked with Worklets for batch processing.\n\n      \nDesign the mapping with re-usable workflow schedules.\n\n\n       \nProject 4\n                          \nBANKING OF ROBUST INFORMATION MANAGEMENT\n\nType\n                  \n                 \nDevelopment - Business Applications - GUI\n\nRole\n                                    \nETL Developer\n       \nPlatform\n                          \nClient/Server, UNIX, Windows\n       \nTechnology\n                     \nData Warehousing\n       \nTools\n                                \nInformatica 6.2\n       \nRDBMS\n                           \nOracle 8i\nClient\n\n   \n                              \nFifth Third Bank\n\nUSA\n\nThe main aim of the Data warehouse is to maintain and enhance competitive position, and to predict the market scenarios. This project deals with the finance details for different products in each branch of the bank, like Personal Loans, Credit Cards, Home Loans, Deposit A/C, and Vehicle Loan. \nThe Company requires different levels of analysis regarding loan amount, type of payment Schedules, and Interest Calculations. Each product has its own business process for each product the product dimension will be changed and the measures too. The transactions can be captured into the corresponding fact tables. The Data Warehouse basically is a Data Mart, as it covers only one domain of the business and captures data from their Transactional Database.\n\n\n      \nMainly involved in ETL developing\n\n      \nCreating the mappings and transformations using Informatica\n\n      \nScheduling ETL process on weekly basis\n\n      \nUsing ETL Process to Extract, transform and load the data into stage area and data warehouse\n\n      \nResolving if any issues in transformations and mappings \n\n      \nScheduling the sessions & Batches to load the data into the target',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-18',NULL,'2007-10-18','2010-06-10 12:14:22','2010-06-10',14,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(229,'Ashish ',NULL,NULL,NULL,'assffsghish_pdffsdurwar12@rediffmail.com','ashifgfsh_purwfgfggar79@yahoo.co.in','0512 2400486','0','09811902486','0','9415736060','0','2007-12-29',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-10 12:14:22',13,'0',NULL,'200710/18/ATT4897.html','200710/18/DOC16353.doc','Pragati Pundir\nRésumé\n\nAshish \n\nB-315, 1\nst\n Floor, \nSector ? 20 \nNoida,U.P.\nMobile No. : 09811902486\nE-mail\n   \n     \n: assffsghish_pdffsdurwar12@rediffmail.com,ashifgfsh_purwfgfggar79@yahoo.co.in\n\n\nObjective\nTo work in a growth oriented organization where my skills could be effectively utilized and contribute to the success of the organization.\n\nExperience Summary\nMaster in Computer Application with 2.4 years of Experience as a Programmer in Software Development Industry, Designing of S/W, Analysis of S/W, Forms 6i, Reports 6i as Front-end and Oracle 8i & 9i ,PL/SQL Programming as Back-end.\n2.4 years of IT experience in database (SQL Server & oracle 8i/9i SQL/PLSQL)\nExtensively worked on oracle and D2k.\nWork experience in SQL-SERVER 2000, VB (6.0), and Oracle database and good conceptual knowledge of RDBMS.\nSelf motivated with initiatives towards fast learning and efficiency/ quality assurance.\nGood team player with excellent communicational and interpersonal skills.\n\nProfessional Qualifications \n\nMaster in Computer Application in 2005 from \nU.P.\nTechnical\nUniversity\n\nLucknow\n ? 73.3%.\nBachelor in Computer Application in 2002 From Dr.B.R.A.University, \nAgra\n ? 60.5%\n\nEducational Qualification \n\n12th with 59% in 1997 from U.P. Board, \nAllahabad\n10th with 62.5% in 1994 from U.P. Board, \nAllahabad\n\nWork Experience: 2.4 yrs\n\nPresent\n   \nExperience\n: from (1 June -07 to till date)\nOrganization:\n Eastern Software System Pvt. Ltd. (CMM Level 5 Company, ISO 9001:2000)\nJob Title: \nSoftware Engineer\nJob Profile: \nPresently I am working in ERP module (MY Company ERP name is Ebizframe which is running in \nIndia\n and abroad, my company client in 28 countries). I have the responsibility of customization of the company product called Ebizframe at the client side, which is an in house developed ERP for SME (Small and Medium Enterprise). As a software engineer, I have worked as team member in the implementation and customization team.\n\nPrevious Experience:\n\n\nFrom (14 March 2005 to 14 May 2007)\n               \nOrganization:\n MDA Softwares Ltd\nJob Title:\n Software Engineer\nJob Profile:\n My job profile is to write Basic Query, Stored Procedure, and Trigger and manage Database on SQL Server 2000,Ms Access platform and designing form and preparing report using (Visual Basic 6.0 and Crystal Report).\n\n\n\n\n\n\nProjects undertaken\n1 June\n\n2007 to Till Date\nCompany\n         \n: Eastern Software System Pvt. Ltd.\n\nFrom 15 June \n\n2007 to Till Date\nProject\nEbizFrame\nClient\n   \nIn house development/enhancement\nRole\nEnhancements, coding and testing of EbizFrame\nEnvironment\nForms 6i, Reports 6i and Oracle 9i\n\n14 March 2005 to 14 May 2007\nCompany\n         \n\n MDA Softwares Ltd\n\nProject\nHr & Payroll System\nDescription\nHRD system contains several modules like \nAll related masters\nShort-listed candidates module\nCV bank\nNew employees, Grades of Employees\nLeave Absentees\nTransfer, Promotions & Increment\nSalary components\nHR Related report & MIS Reports\nPayroll System contains several modules like \nAll related masters\nAdvance / Deduction\nI.T Savings\nAttendance process\nPf Module\nOverstay module\nSalary Reports & MIS reports\nRole\nAnalysis, Design, Coding and Testing\nEnvironment\nForms 6i, Reports 6i and Oracle 9i\n\n\nProject\nPortfolio Management System\nProject Description\nMaintain all the share and debenture details regarding their sells and purchase.\nRole\nAnalysis, Design, Coding ,Testing and Implementation \nEnvironment\nForms 6i, Reports 6i and Oracle 9i\n\nProject\nLibrary Management System.\nProject Description\nThis System deals with the complete Library Management system.\nIt deals with the Book Details, Issue detail, Staff Detail, Penalty Details and Staff Payroll. It contains six canvases and ten Reports.\nRole\nAnalysis, Designing, Developing, Testing & Implementation\nEnvironment\nOracle 8i with Developer 2000 (Forms & Reports 6i ),\n\n\n\nProject\nAddress book\nDescription\nAddress Book is easy to use software that makes keeping track of contacts simple. It organizes contacts to one or more groups or categories for selected listings. It has importing capabilities to quickly import from other programs such as Excel. It can print the addresses in a tabular list format or as detailed records.  Envelope and label printing is also included. \n\nRole\nDesigning, Coding and implementation.\nEnvironment\nV.B. 6.0, Ms Access, Crystal Report 8.0\nProject\neRETURN\nDescription\nThis module maintains all the information for the submission of Form 16 and Form16A. \nIt also generates various reports including Form 16, Form 16A and Form 27A. \nIt generates various flat files for the electronic submission of tax to e-TDS intermediary appointed by the board.\nRole\nDesigning, Coding and implementation.\nEnvironment\nV.B. 6.0, Ms Access, Crystal Report 8.0\n\nKey Competencies & skills\n\n         \nForms 6i and Reports 6i\n\n         \nPL/SQL\n\n         \nSQL Plus\n\n         \nOracle 9i & 8i.\n\n         \nToad\n\n         \nVisual Basic 6.0\n\nTechnical Experience\nOperating platform\n      \n\n           \nWindows NT server Windows/95/98/2000, \nRDBMS\n            \n            \n\n           \nOracle 8.0, 8i, 9i, MS-Access, SQL-SERVER 2000\nFront ?end Tools\n          \n\n           \nVisual basic 6.0, Developer 2000(forms 6i/report 6i).\nLanguage\n                    \n\n           \nV.B. 6.0 and PL/ SQL\nWeb Technology\n         \n\n           \nHTML, HTML, ASP, VB Script, Front Page 2000.\nReporting Tool\n             \n\n           \nCrystal Report 8.0, Reports 6i\n\nPersonal Details\nFather?s Name\n             \n:Sh. O.N. Gupta\nDate of Birth\n                \n:20th Dec. 1979\nLanguage Known\n        \n:English and Hindi\nMarital Status\n\n            \n:Unmarried\nPermanent Address\n\n    \n:18E/21, \nRajeev Gandhi Lane\n\nShiv Katra Road\n, Lal Bunglaw, Kanpur-7\nPhone No\n         \n            \n:(0512)2400486,9415736060, 9451426194\nPassport\n                       \n:G4449970 ( Valid till 13 Aug 2017)\n\nDeclaration\nI hereby declared that all the above information is true and best of my knowledge. I feel that this demonstrates the ability of dedication and enthusiasm for a project over a long period of time.\nThanking you.\n\nDate:\n\n\nPlace:\n              \n                                                                                                \n           \n(Ashish Purwar)',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-18',NULL,'2007-10-18','2010-06-10 12:14:22','2010-06-10',13,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(230,'Anilkumar V',NULL,NULL,NULL,'anilvidhani@gmail.com',NULL,NULL,'0','91 9921972696','0',NULL,'0','2006-07-30',10,NULL,'2010-06-10 12:14:22',14,'1','2010-06-21','200710/18/ATT4903.html','200710/18/DOC16354.doc','Alaykumar Barochia\n\n\n\nAnilkumar .v\n       \n( B.E.E.C.,OCP)(Exp. 3.10+ Years)(DBA)\n      \nE-Mail: \nandvdsvilvdvdsvidhani\n@gmail.com\n\n                 \n                            \n\n        \nContact No\n\n\n+91 9921972696\n\n                               \n     \n                                            \n                                \n\n\n\nOBJECTIVE\n      \n                                                                                         \n           \n     \n                     \nTo pursue a challenging and satisfying career and to be a part of a progressive and growth oriented organization that give me scope to enhance my knowledge and skills to cope up with the latest technological changes.\n\n\n\n\n\nKEY SKILLS\n\n\n       \nKnowledge of Oracle Database Administration on Linux and Windows Platform.\n\n       \nInstallation, maintenance and upgrades of oracle database.\n\n       \nSupport of backup and recovery strategies.\n\n      \nCreating and Managing of tablespaces, datafiles, schema objects and users.\n\n       \nMonitoring and Optimizing (SGA) the performance of database.\n\n       \nMaintaining the Standby Database.\n\n       \nKnowledge of detecting and resolving Row Chaining and Row Migration.\n\n       \nKnowledge of Database Cloning.\n\n       \nKnowledge of implementing Data Guard environment.\n\n\n\nTECHNICAL SKILLS\n\nOperating Systems\n\nRed Hat Linux, Windows NT/2000\n\nLanguages\n\nSQL, PL/SQL, C, \nC++\n\nDatabases\n\nOracle 8i and Oracle 9i\n\nOracle Tools/Utilities\n\nExport/Import, Oracle Enterprise Manager, SQL Trace, Explain Plan, RMAN, STATSPACK, UTLBSTAT, UTLESTAT,\n      \nTKPROF, ORADIM, ORAPWD, TOAD.\n\n\n\n\n                                                                                                \n            \n\n\nPROFESSIONAL WORK EXPERIENCE\n\n1. Company Name\n: Virtual Effects Software solutions, Ahmedabad\n    \nPeriod ofEmployment\n: July 2005 to Till Date\n    \nDesignation\n: Associate Engineer ? Database Administration \n    \nSite Handling\n\n    \n(1) Omni Lense Pvt. Ltd.\n          \nSite Setup:\n\n       \nDell Power Edge 6650\n\n       \nWindows 2000\n\n       \nOracle 8i\n          \nJob Description:\n\n       \nInstallation, configuration and administration of oracle 8i on windows 2000 platform.\n\n       \nCreating and maintaining of database users, profiles. Checking Alert log.\n\n       \nTaking Database backup.\n\n       \nPL/SQL programming.\n          \nProject: \nSales Management Information System(\nC,Oracle8i(PL/SQL),Windows2000)\n\n\n       \nThe Objective of this application is to provide information to the managers about the day-to-day status of the sales operations as well as integrity of the inventory. \nThis system manage all details like order details, items information, payment details like the payment paid by either Credit Card or Cash. This system provide very user-friendly interface.\n\nThe marketing executives to their seniors also use this utility for the reporting of the work.\n\nMy Role:\n\n       \nDeveloped procedures, functions and triggers and dealt with complex SQL queries.\n\n       \nSupport and Maintenance.\n\n       \nProvide support at the time of delivery of Beta version.\n\n   \n(2)\n\nNetcare Infosys Pvt. Ltd.\n          \nRole: \nOracle DBA\n          \nSite setup: \n\n       \nDell Power Edge 6650\n\n       \nWindows 2000\n\n       \nOracle 9.2.0.4\n          \nJob Description:\n\n       \nData migration of non-standard data into oracle database\n\n       \nCreation, configuration and maintenance of databases and management servers\n\n       \nConsulting and support for Data extraction, loading, optimizing queries\n\n       \nPL/SQL scripts for automating and speeding up certain tasks\n\n       \nHandling issues related to Oracle Architecture, Backup, recovery, networking, and database performance, etc\n\n       \nMonitoring of Alert Log file.\n          \n          \nProject:\n\n\nMedical Transcription System( PL/SQL, Toad, C, OEM)\n\n\n       \nAs a Software Development Consultancy, virtual effect solutions has developed an application for Netcare Infosys, Ahmedabad for their Medical Transcription Business. Netcare Infosys is Medical Transcription Firm having more than 200 Employees and had more than 46 hospitals as client in US for whom they were doing Transcription. And transcribed documents were delivered to the respective Physician with the help of Delivery Application\n\n2. Company Name\n: Rangwa Solutions, \nSurat\n    \nPeriod of Employment\n: September 2003 to June 2005\n    \nDesignation\n: Design Enginner\n    \nSite Setup:\n\n       \nFlying Probe CNC Machine\n\n       \nWindows NT/2000\n\n       \nBARCO U-CAM 6.0\n\n    \nJob Description:\n\n       \nFabrication of Single, Double and Multi layer printed circuit board.\n\n       \nPrepare Routing programmes, Electrical test programmes.\n\n       \nQuality Assurance for PCB\n\n       \nC Programming, CNC programming & Design Rule Check\n\n    \nMy Role:\n\n       \nTaking gerber files of PCB from customers and preparation of single and panel images with production boarder. \n\n       \nSupport and Maintenance.\n\n       \nSupervision of Front?End & Production Department.\n\n       \nEditing PCB as per the Design Rule Check and net compare and also photo plot.\n\n       \nDeveloping Routing\n\n& Electrical test programmes for flying probe CNC machine.\n\n       \nKeeping Records of\n\nthe Customer details & their Payment & Order Details & Schedule timetable for all production operations in the Database of the Company.\n\n\n                                                                                                \nACADEMIC PROJECT\n\nTitle\n48-bit I/O DC Using USB \nat Sahajanand Laser Tech,Gandhinagar\n\nDeveloped Using\nC, MPLAB, Pic Controller, Oracle 8i(\nPL/SQL\n), Window 2000 professional\nDescription\nIn general term 48-bit I/O DC Using USB means Bulk of available machines work according to one single PC so that the process can continue. In this project for Sahajanand Laser we have to make I/O Digital Card Using USB Which handle machine (approx. 48) with the help of single PC running throughout the year. & also With the available resources like raw material, workers, machines and time we have to schedule timetable for all the production operations.\n\n\n\nEDUCATIONAL QUALIFICATION\n   \n                                                        \n    \n\nExamination\nBoard/University\nMonth & Year of\n    \nPassing\n\n     \n\n\nGrade\nB.E. \n(Electronics\n\n& Communication Technology)\n\nS.P.\nCollege\n of Eng,\nVisnagar\n\nJune 2003\n\n64.60\n\nFirst\nH.S.C.\nGujarat\n Secondary Education Board\nMarch 1999\n77.55\nDistinction\nS.S.C.\nGujarat\n Secondary Education Board\nMarch 1996\n76.86\n\nDistinction\n\n\n\nPERSONAL DETAILS\n\n\nName\nAnilkumar Lilaram Vidhani\n\nAddress\nA/9,Guru Angad society, \nOpp.\nL.I.C\nBuilding\n\nAundh Road\n\nPune ? 411 020\n\nMEENA\nMANSION\n? 106,\nSHIV GANESH BUNGLOWS,\nS.G.ROAD,\nAHMEDABAD-380059\n\nDate of Birth \n10-June-1981\n\nGender\nMale\n\nMarital Status\nUnmarried\n\nNationality\nIndian\n\nN.C.F.M\nCapital Market Dealers Module\n\nLanguage Known \nEnglish, Hindi, Gujarati, Sindhi\n\nEmail\nanilvidhani@gmail.com\n\nContact No \n9921972696\n\nHobbies\nEnjoy Traveling, Learning new things, Listening to music,\n\nMaking friends.',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-18',NULL,'2007-10-18','2010-06-10 12:14:22','2010-06-10',14,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(231,'Anu Agarwal',NULL,NULL,NULL,'andfvdvnuagdvdvarwal_2000@yahoo.com','annu.addvdgarwaldvv@gmail.com','0124 4141277','0','9811485462','0','0581 3092350','0','2003-09-28',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-10 12:14:22',13,'0',NULL,'200710/18/ATT4911.html','200710/18/DOC16355.doc','CURRICULUM VITAE\nCURRICULUM VITAE\n\nANU AGARWAL\n1264, Sector-10A\nGurgaon-122001\nPh: 9811485462,0124-4141277\ne-mail: \nandfvdvnuagdvdvarwal_2000@yahoo.com\n\nannu.addvdgarwaldvv@gmail.com\n\n\nObjective\nTo Synergize Professional Integrity with the Passion for Path Breaking Growth & Success\n\nProfile\n\n       \nHighly motivated, creative I.T. Professional with 6.5+ Years of experience in Project Management, ERP Implementation, Software Development in Oracle & Developer 2000. \n\n       \nA talent for analyzing problems, developing and simplifying procedures and finding innovative solutions.\n\nWork Experience\nWorking with \n3i\n\nInfotech Ltd. (CMMI Level 5) \nas\n Senior Software Engineer \nfrom\n August 2006.\n\nJob Profile\n\n      \nResponsibility of an Account Manager, accountable for client interaction, implementation, acceptability with product and solution offering with client, sign off and project management.\n\n      \nManaging a team of 3 Members for implementation of \nOrion \n(A Web Based ERP)\n\n      \nBrief the Delivery Head-India about progress of the Implementation\n\n      \nPreparation of SRS for New Requirement and Interact with Development Team for Solution Development\n\n      \nIdentification of Improvement Areas in order to make System more reliable \n\n      \nTraining the development team members to make the business functionality clear to them\n\n      \nDevelopment of Reports as and when required using Oracle 9i and Developer 2000\n\nProject Undertaken\n\nClient: \nSRF Polymers Ltd\n is a part of SRF Group having total turnover of approx 4000 Crores. The Group have 9 different businesses with 16 manufacturing facilities. \n\nRole:\n\nImplementation of Orion at 2 Facilities and Corporate Office.\n\nAchievements and Honours\n\n      \nReceive Appreciations from \n\nVice Vertical Head of 3i Infotech\n\n      \nReceive Appreciations from CEO, Vice President and Associate Vice President of Client from last Two Consecutive Months for Timely and Successful Month Closure\n\n      \nSuccessful Month Closure of Inventory and Finance from Last Four Months \n\nWorked with \nExa Infotech \nas\n Manager-Implementation \nfrom\n June 2005 to July 2006.\n\nJob Responsibilities\n\n      \nManaging a team of 10 Members for implementation of \n\nErpro\n{Manufacturing, Trading,CRM and Construction) in \nIndia\n and Overseas at 30 Clients\n\n      \nPreparation of Project Plan and Schedule and to ensure timely delivery \n\n      \nWorking as Co-coordinator between clients and technical team\n\n      \nSystem study/ analysis for designing & developing the workflow program\n\n      \nGap Analysis in terms of requirement generation \n\n      \nDevelopment of Reports as and when required using Oracle 9i and Developer 2000\n\n      \nMaintenance of Documents as per ISO Standards\n\nBrief of Leading Projects Undertaken \n\nClient: \nMagna Steels, \nKarachi\n is a \nKarachi\n\nPakistan\n) based leading Company in TOR and TMT Bar having worth around 700 Crores\n\nRole:\n\nSystem Study, System Analysis and Implementation of Erpro Manufacturing with all Statutory Requirement related to Taxation\n\nClient: \nAnsal Buildwell Limited\n is Leading Company in Construction Business \n\nRole:\n\nSystem Study/Analysis, Preparation of DFDs, Implementation of Erpro CRM \n\nClient: \nVatika Group\n is a Pioneer Company in Construction Industry with \n\nits presence in Commercial, Residential, Hotels Construction, having worth around 3200 Crores\n\nRole:\n\nSystem Study, System Analysis, DFD Preparation and Implementation of Erpro Construction with Purchase and Contract Managemt Modules at Gurgaon Unit. \n\nClient: \nAtlas Cycles\n is a Leading Cycle Maker in \nIndia\n with Sales in \nIndia\n and Export to Various Countries\n\nRole\n: System Study, System Analysis, Preparation Of DFD and Implementation of AtlasSoft\n\nClient: \nWheels \nIndia\n is a TVS Group Company with makes Tyre Rim for Two Wheeler as well as Four Wheelers\n\nRole:\n\nSystem Study, System Analysis, Preparation Of DFD and Implementation of Erpro Production, Erpro PPC.and Erpro QMS.\n\nClient: \nSpeedy Hot Water,Australia\n\n\nis a leading Electrical Equipment Manufacturer \n\nRole:\n\nSystem Study/Analysis, Preparation of DFDs, Implementation of Erpro CRM \n\nClient: \nSudhir Gensets\n is Indian Market Leader in Silent Genset Manufacturing with Turnover of Approx. 900 Crores\n\nRole:\n\nImplementation of Erpro Manufacturing\n\nat Gurgaon and Athal Units\n\nClient\n\nAvon\n Tubetech\n is Leading Company in Steel Tube Manufacturing with Turnover of Approx. 100 Crores\n\nRole:\n\nImplementation of Erpro Manufacturing\n\nat \nFaridabad\n Unit\n\nClient: \nThreebond \nIndia\n\n\nSubsidiary of Threebond, Singapur) is a M.N.C. with units in several countries. It manufactures Industrial and Domestic Adheshive Items and Coating Material with clients like Maruti Udyog Limited, Honda Scooters and several others.\n\nRole:\n Implementation of Erpro Manufacturing and Trading at Gurgaon Unit\n\nWorked with \nOmax Fusions Ltd. (Omax Auto Group Company) \nas\n Asstt. Manager ?I.T. \nfrom Feb ?2004 to May 2005\n\nJob Responsibilities\n\n       \nDesign & Development of Client-Server application using Oracle and Developer 2000.\n\n       \nImplementation & Support an ERP using \nOracle 9i\n for Database management and Developer\n 2000\n for Graphical User Interface\n\n       \nInstallation of Oracle 9i and Developer 2000 on server\n\n       \nDatabase creation and uploading of data files through SQL Loader, Import.\n\n       \nUser Training \n\n       \nAdoption of new measures for cost saving and paper less office\n\n       \nTroubleshooting end user problems includes Hardware, Networking, Oracle ERP Application\n\n       \nGenerate & maintain MIS & reports for facilitating decision making by the management\n\n       \nSuggesting required software and hardware for purchase (or development)\n\nAdditional Responsibilities\n\n       \nWorked as TPM Secretary which includes-\n1.\n       \nDocumentation of TPM, \n2.\n       \nTPM Audit, \n3.\n       \nTo establish co-ordination between the Teams and Management\n\n       \nWorked as Team Leader of 5?S \n\nWorked with \nTexim Computers Pvt. Ltd. \nas\n Team Member (Software Development) \nfrom July ?2000 to Jan ?2004 \n\nClient:\n\nMark Auto Industries Ltd. \n\nMark Auto is a joint venture company of Maruti Udyog Ltd. with leading supplier of Fuel Tanks \n\nRole:\n\nSystem Study/Analysis, Preparation of DFDs, Documentation, Software Development \n\n\nProjects Undertaken \n\nFinancial Control & Review System \nwith the purpose of bringing discipline in Vendor Payment and thus helping the company in improving its relationship with the vendors. It consists of Modules like Cheque Printing, Bank Reconciliation, TDS, ST38 Reconciliation, Excise Reconciliation and Vendor Payment.\n\nPersonnel Information System \nwith the purpose of bringing transparency and control in manpower movement and cost. It consists of modules like`Online Attendance recording and reporting system, shift planner.\n\nControl MIS System\n with the purpose of generating transparency in the system by facilitating process benchmarking of Material and document movement process.\n\nProfessional Qualification\nMBA (Information Systems) [Full Time] from Bharati Vidyapeeth\'s \nInstitute\n of \nManagement\n and Research (\nPune\nUniversity\n), \nNew Delhi\n Campus (Result First Class with Distinction, Aggregate-70%)\n\n3 Years Advance Diploma in Software Engineering from Aptech Limited\n\nEducational Qualification\nB.Sc. (Physics, Statistics, Maths) from \nBareilly\nCollege\n\nBareilly\n under \nRohilkhand\nUniversity\n with 63% marks in 1995\n\nIT Skills \nArea\nSkills\nLanguage\nPL/SQL\nRDBMS\nOracle 8,8i,Oracle 9i Database\nGUI\nDeveloper 2000 (Form 5/6/6i, Report 3.0/6.0/6i), Architecture & DBA\nNetworking\nData Communication & Networking\nConcepts\nSoftware Engineering, O.S.\nOperating System\nDOS, Windows NT, Windows 2000,95,98,XP\n\nPersonal Profile\nDate of Birth\n                \n\n           \n\nth\n Feb\' 76\nPermanent Address\n     \n\n           \n26-A, UTSAV, Mahanagar\n                                                \nBareilly-243001,\n\n(U.P.),Ph- (0581) 3092350\nLanguage Known\n        \n\n           \nHindi & English\nPassport Details\n           \n\n\n         \nHas a valid Indian Passport.\n\nMiscellany\nIn addition to being an extremely diligent worker, I am good at learning new technologies. I am a good team player and posses a strong leadership quality which reflects in my ability to take initiative and channalize not only my but others effort for the desired outcome.',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-18',NULL,'2007-10-18','2010-06-10 12:14:22','2010-06-10',13,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(232,'Barundev Kar',NULL,NULL,NULL,'barundev_kar@rediffmail.com','barundev_kar@yahoo.com','033 26270403','0','9232651657','0',NULL,'0','2005-04-29',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-10 12:14:22',13,'0',NULL,'200710/18/ATT4913.html','200710/18/DOC16356.doc','Synopsis\n\nPro- active and result oriented with nearly \n\n\nyears Industrial experience.\n\nProficient in implementing high-speed solutions and providing optimized solutions to meet the client needs. Effectively communicate direction and commits people to action. An effective communicator with exceptional relationship management skills with the ability to relate with the people at any level of business and management\n\n\nExperience Summary\n\nA Diploma in Electrical Engineering from Jalpaliguri Polytechnic Institute, a premier Technical Institute of India. Previously working as Technical Consultant in \nTCGIVEGA Software Services Pvt. Ltd. \nKolkata that has achieved \nISO 9001:2000 Certified and SEI CMM Level 5,\n\nheadquartered in \nBangalore\n. Presently working as Consultant Programmer (Technical Lead & Team Lead) in \nTathya Dot Com Pvt. Ltd (ISO 9001:2000), \nheadquartered in Kolkata\n\n\n\n         \n5 years of experience in which 4.6 years in IT industry.\n\n         \nExpert Skill in Oracle 10g/9i/8i\n\n         \nProficient Programming Skills\n in Forms 6i and Reports 10g/9i/6i.\n\n         \nHave knowledge about different Financial Instrument and Stock Market.\n\n         \nHave knowledge about Insurance Product and Marketing.\n\n         \nExperience in various phases of software development including Development and Implementation.\n\n         \nExperience in EPR-Three-Tier Client Server architecture based projects like CoalNet.\n\n        \n1.6 years experience in Team Leading.\n\n\n\nTechnical Skill\n\nLanguage:\n                               \nGW Basic, C, C++, Java, Forms 6i, JSP\nMarkup Language:\n                  \nHTML\nScripting Language:\n                \nJava Script, VB Script\nRDBMS:\n                                  \nOracle 8i, Oracle 9i & Oracle 10g\nReports Builders:\n                    \nReports 6i, Reports 9i & Reports 10g\nOperating System:\n                  \nDOS, Windows 95/98, Windows NT/2000, Linux\n\n\nApplication / Areas\n\nOracle PL/SQL Coding.\nOracle Reports\nJavaScript, JSP\n\n\n\nEXPERIENCE: Project worked on\n\n\n\n\n\nBima Chakrya (Corporate Agent LICI)\n                   \nJanuary, 2003 - December 2004\n\nClient:\nLife Insurance Corporation of \nIndia\nDescription:\nWork with Forms and Report 6i in Client Server Architecture.\nResponsibilities:\nPL/SQL Coding, Data Maintenance, Application Modification, Reports Developments Web-site maintenance, System maintenance day-to-day, IT Operation Management.\nExperience in RAMCO, (Finance), an ERP Package.\nEnvironment:\nOracle 8i, Forms and Report 6i.\n\n\n\nCoalNet\n                                                                      \nDecember 2004-Till Date\nClient :\n\nCoal India Limited (www.coalindia.nic.in)\n\nDescription:\nCoalNet is an ERP system developed for Coal India Limited. This application covers all the functionality to run the business process smoothly and efficiently. This application is scaled and designed to fulfill the intense requirement of Enterprise Computing of an Organization like Coal India having eight large Subsidiary situated at different dispersed location of India. Functionalities covered in this Application are Finance, Production, Personnel, Project, Materials, Payroll, and Sales & Marketing, Equipment and customized modules like VVIP, Grievance and Parliament Affairs. This application also provides a B2B portal and Geographical Information System.\nPreviously posted at \nSystem Departments, Northern Coalfields Ltd, Singrauli, MP\n\nResponsibilities:\nLeading a team of 10 members in Talcher Area, MCL\nClient handling\n\nCreating and modifying the business logic in the source code in Oracle (packages/procedures/functions/triggers/reports) to match the business rules of the respective.\nResponsible for Phase II Implementation (Implementation in Talcher Area of MCL).\nProject Management ? Scheduling, Job allocation, Monitoring.\nEnvironment:\n\nOracle 10g, Oracle Report 10g, JSP, JDK, J2EE\n\nOthers Experience\n\nWorking as a Marketing Executive under Allecrity Electronics for marketing of Heavy Electrical Measuring Instrument.\nWorking as a stock dealer under Spectra Financial Services in NSE, BSE and CSE.\nWorking as a Insurance Advisor under LICI\nConducted training programs on Oracle 8i in different office of BSNL, in different district town in West Bengal & Sikim like Krishnanagar (Nadia), Raigunj (U/Dinajpur), Bardwan (Bardwan), Gangtok (Sikim), Suri (Birbhum) etc.\n\n\n\n\nEducation\n\nMadhyamik from W.B.S.E in the year 1993 (78%)\nHigher Secondary from W.B.C.H.S.E. in the year 1995 (62.6%)\nD.E.E. from W.B.S.C.T.E. in the year 2000 (81.8%)\n\nDiploma in Computer Operation (GW Basic, MS DOS, Word Star)\nCertificate Course in Office Computing under Windows 95 in Production & Operation.\nADVANCE DIPLOMA IN SOFTWARE TECHNOLOGY\n                        \n[Course Content : Preparatory Module: Turbo C, Module I: Oracle 8i, Module II: \nC++]\n\n\n\n\nDomain Knowledge\n\nKnowledge in Personnel Information System.\nKnowledge in Equipment Monitoring System.\nKnowledge in Production Monitoring System.\nKnowledge in Financial Information System.\nKnowledge in Project Monitoring System.\nKnowledge in Payroll Processing System.\nKnowledge in Material Management System.\nKnowledge in Sales Monitoring System.\nKnowledge in Capital Market Services.\nKnowledge in Insurance Industry.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nPERSONAL DETAILS\n\nFull Name\n                               \n\n           \nBARUNDEV KAR\n\nFather?s Name\n                       \n\n           \nLate Buddhadev Kar\n\nPermanent Address\n             \n\n           \n12/2, \nMohesh Paul Lane\n\n                                                            \nHowrah-711104.\n\nPostal Address\n                      \n\n          \nSystems Department,\n\nTalcher Area,\n                                                            \nMahanadi CoalFields Limited,\n                                \n                            \nP.O.- Dera, Dist.- Angul,\n                                                            \nState - Orissa \n\nDate of Birth\n                          \n\n           \n02/08/1977\n\nSex\n                                         \n\n           \nMale\n\nCurrently Employed as\n        \n\n\n          \nConsultant Programmer (Technical Lead)\n\nCurrently Employed in\n         \n\n\n          \nTathya Dot Com Pvt. Ltd.\n                                                            \nSwastik, 4\nth\n Floor, \nV.I.P. Road\n\n                                                            \nKolkata ? 700059.\n\nCurrently Posted At\n          \n    \n\n\n          \nMCL,Talcher for implementation of CoalNet\n\nNationality\n                              \n\n           \nIndian\n\nMarital Status\n                        \n\n           \nUnmarried\n\nE-Mail (Personal)\n                  \n\n           \nbarundev_kar@rediffmail.com\n\nbarundev_kar@yahoo.com\n\nContact No.\n                           \n\n           \n(033) 26270403 / 9232651657\n\nFluent in\n                                 \n\n\n          \nEnglish, Hindi and Bengali\n\nPresent CTC\n                         \n\n           \n2.4 lac\n\nExpected CTC\n                      \n\n           \n4 lac (Negotiable)\n\nJoining Period Required\n     \n\n           \n1 Month (Negotiable)\n\n\n\nDeclaration\nI hereby declare that all the above-mentioned details are true to the best of my knowledge.\n\n\n\nDate:\n   \n04/07/2007\n                                                    \n                         \nSIGNATURE\n\nPlace:\n\nKolkata\n                                                                      \n        \nBARUN DEV KAR',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-18',NULL,'2007-10-18','2010-06-10 12:14:22','2010-06-10',13,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(233,'Dhayanithy K',NULL,NULL,'Bangalore','dhdgdgayanegseithy.k@hotmail.com',NULL,NULL,'0','9916041579','0',NULL,'0','2007-12-13',10,34,'2010-06-10 12:14:22',14,'0',NULL,'200710/18/ATT4916.html','200710/18/DOC16357.doc','DHAYANITHY.K\nMobile No: \n91- 9916041579\n                             \ndhdgdgayanegseithy.k@hotmail.com\n\nOBJECTIVE\nAmbitious and diligent dude and throwing efforts on\n\nproviding efficient value addition to the organization while effectively upgrading myself in the area of Database administration.\n\nPROFESSION AND PROFICIENCY- AN OVERVIEW\n\n    \n\nPossessing \n2.2 years\n of experience in Oracle 9i database administration in orientation with unix exposure.\n\n      \nHaving strong focus in maintaining testing as well as production databases, planning strategies for backup and recovery\n\n      \nFamiliar in Oracle DBA Activities like Monitoring of Database, Performance Monitoring, Backup & Recovery, Database Security, User\n\nand database Management\n\n      \nHaving high caliber to upgrade new technologies and possess excellent interpersonal skills.\n\nEXPERTISE\n\n\n      \nHaving sound knowledge in manual backup & recovery strategies.\n\n\n      \nAll the backup scenarios.\n   \n\n      \nAdept in logical backups (Export/Import) for different levels of tables (Full, Partition), Schemas and Full system levels.\n\n      \nEncountered different levels of refreshments from PROD to UAT & DEV box (schema level, table level). \n\nPROFESSIONAL EXPERIENCE\n             \nWorking as a \nDatabase Administrator\n in \nTryocen Software, \nBangalore\n from \nJune