ng solution.\n\nAchievement ? Good ranking for every keyword of the site.\n\n\n\n       \nCactus Country Property\nURL- \n\nhttp://www.cactuscountryproperty.com/\n\nCountry ? \nUnited States of America\n\nDescription- Real Estate related Services.\n\n\n\n       \nExind Fabrics\n\nURL- \nhttp://www.exindfabrics.com/\n\nCountry ?\nIndia\n\nDescription- the Hand woven Fabrics\n\n\n       \n\nApple country Resorts\n\nURL- \nhttp://www.applecountryresorts.com/\n\nCountry ?\nIndia\n\nDescription- Honeymoon vacation resorts\n\n\n       \nTrails India\n\nURL- \nhttp://www.trailsindia.com/\n\nCountry ?\nIndia\n\nDescription- Tours and Travels Company\n\n\n       \nSaffola Life\nURL- \nhttp://www.saffolalife.com/\n\nCountry ?\nIndia\n\nDescription- Healthy lifestyles and Weight Management Control\n\n\n\n       \nTruedata Online\nURL- \nhttp://www.truedataonline.com/\n\nCountry ?\nUnited States of America\n\nDescription- Dialogic PC boards and Televantage Related Products\n\n\n\n\n\nSEO Tools\n\nUrchin, Google analytics, Dream weaver, keyword generation tools, \n\n.svn , Optilink , Arelis tools, Meta Tag Generation Tools, Internet Business Promotor 8(IBP 8), and Web Position Gold etc., \n  \n\nOther Qualification(s)/ Certification(s)/ Programme(s) Attended\n\n\n       \nMAINFRAME.\n   \n\n       \nCCCO (Certificate course in computer operation).\n\n\nLanguages Known\n\n\n       \nEnglish\n\n\n       \nHindi\n\n\n       \nMarathi\n\n\n       \nTamil\n\n\nPersonal Details \n\n\nDate of Birth\n                  \n\n           \n\nth\n April 1982.\n\nFather?s Name\n               \n\n           \nMr. Ramesh Sonkusre\n\nSex \n                 \n\n           \n\n          \nMale\n\nMarital Status\n                \n\n           \nMarried\n\nHobbies\n                        \n\n           \nCricket',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-18',NULL,'2007-10-18','2010-06-10 12:14:22','2010-06-10',3,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(238,'Gangadhar Pinisetty',NULL,NULL,NULL,'pvganvdvdvdvvdvgadhar@yahoo.com',NULL,NULL,'0','91 94403 57192','0',NULL,'0','2007-12-29',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-10 12:14:22',2,'0',NULL,'200710/18/ATT4890.html','200710/18/DOC16362.doc','RESUME\nV.GANGADHAR PINISETTY\n\n(Mobile)\n\n91-94403-57192\n       \n(Email)\n\npvganvdvdvdvvdvgadhar@yahoo.com\n                                                                                      \nCareer objective\n\nWith the knowledge in the field of Databases coupled with my Exposure of Commercial Software applications as Database Administrator\n\nseek a long-term career in the field of Database management in a professional organization.\n\nProfessional Summary \n\nHaving\n    \n2 .2 years of industry experience in Database Administration support through florinsa technologies\n   \nunder Unix, NT environments.\n\nSpecific expertise in\n\nCloning ,storage management,user management and backup?s Powered by Oracle systems.\n\nExperience Summary\n\n\n      \nResponsible for\n\nAdministration of Oracle 9i database including installation, creation and planning the Backup strategy on Linux AS 3.0. \n\n      \nCreated and maintaining oracle database in customized manner\n\n      \nTablespace creation,space allocation and Management of space and Rollback segments\n\n      \nCreating users,roles,profiles,assigning roles and profiles to users.\n\n      \nTroubleshooting the space management errors\n\n      \nTaking \nlogical backups\n\nand physical backups\n periodically\n\n      \nImplemented multiple archive log destinations to archive redologs to the production server to support immediate database recovery\n\n      \nReorganisation of tables,fragmented tablespaces and database using \nexport\n and \nimport \ntools\n\n      \nTransporting the tablespaces from one database to another database using import\n\nand export tools\n\n      \nPlanning for backup and recovery of database and maintaining \nHot Backups and Cold Backups.\n\n      \nConfiguration of SQL*NET using \nHOSTNAME, TNSNAMES\n and troubleshooting oracle networking issues.\n\n      \nCreating database links and materialized views\n\n      \nDataupload using \nsqlloader\n oracle utilities\n\n      \nEnabling the users operation using resumable tablespace.\n\n      \nInvolved in \ncloning\n for generating reports and for testing\n\n      \nAnalyzing tables and computing statistics\n\n      \nImplementation knowledge on \nRecover manager\n utility(\nRMAN\n) for easier and well managed recovery operations\n\n      \nKnowledge of \nDATAGUARD \nconcepts for high avilability solutions\n\n      \nKnowledge of generating reports using \nSTATSPACK\n\n      \nKnowledge of application level tuning using oracle utilities:\nTKPROF,EXPLAIN PLAN\n\n      \nKnowledge of tracing a sql query\n\n\n\n\nTechnical skills\n\n                      \nDatabases\n                 \n\n     \nORACLE\n     \n9i/10G\n\nDBA\n                       \nP/L\n   \n                         \n\n     \nPL/SQL\n            \n           \nOperating Systems\n   \n\n     \nWindows95, 98, NT 2000XP,UNIX\n            \n           \nPackages\n                  \n\n     \nMS-Office\n\n\n            \n\nIndustry Experience \n\n\nPROJECT # 1:\n\n    \nTitle\n                               \n     \n\n       \nGlobal Merchandising systems\n    \nClient\n                                  \n\n       \nGlobal Technologies \nU.K.\n    \nProject Execution\n               \n\n       \nSONATA SOFTWARE Ltd. ,\nHyderabad\n    \nRole\n                                    \n\n      \nDatabase Administrator\n\nDESCRIPTION:\n\nIt facilitates the customer to browse the site and shop various items online.the list of items and their prices are stored in the database. customers will be able to order products online. \n\nREPONSIBILITIES:\n\n\n            \nInstalled oracle 9i on Linux\n\n            \nCreating and maintaining of\n\nthe Oracle database\n\n            \nManaging Database Structure and Storage Allocation\n\n            \nCreating users, roles and assigning roles to users\n\n            \nTablespace, table creation and their space allocation\n\n            \nManagement of space and Rollback segments\n\n            \nBackup scheduling and monitoring\n\n            \nLogical backups (Exports and Imports)\n\n            \nPhysical backups(Cold backup & Hotbackup)\n\n            \nUsed SQL Loader, Export/Import, Database Links\n\n            \nSetting multiple archive destinations on requirement\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nPROJECT # 2:\n\n    \nTitle \n                                    \n\n       \nThomson Holiday Packages\n    \nClient\n                                   \n\n      \nThomson\n\nU.K.\n    \nProject Execution\n                     \n\n       \nSONATA SOFTWARE Ltd. ,\nHyderabad\n   \n\nRole\n                               \n           \n\n       \nDatabase Administrator\n\nDESCRIPTION:\n\n\nIs an U.K based company and working on Travel projects on\n\ndifferent stages of software development\n\nLife cycle \n\nREPONSIBILITIES:\n\n\n            \nInstalled oracle 9i on Linux\n\n            \nCreating and maintaining of\n\nthe Oracle database\n\n            \nManaging Database Structure and Storage Allocation\n\n            \nCreating users, roles and assigning roles to users\n\n            \nTablespace, table creation and their space allocation\n\n            \nManagement of space and Rollback segments\n\n            \nBackup scheduling and monitoring\n\n            \nLogical backups (Exports and Imports)\n\n            \nPhysical backups (Cold backup & Hot backup)\n\n            \nUsed SQL Loader, Export/Import, Database\n Links\n\n            \nSetting multiple archive destinations on requirement\n\n\n                                   \n\n\nPersonal data\n\n\nName\n                              \n      \nV.GANGADHAR PINISETTY.\nMarital Status\n                \n       \nUnmarried\nSex\n                                   \n       \nMale\nNationality\n                    \n       \nIndian\nDate of Birth\n         \n           \n       \n03-08-1983\nAcademic Qualification\n     \nBachelors Degree in Computer Science,\n                                                                                 \nAndhra\nUniversity\n\nindia\n                                \nMailing Address\n                  \nAchiahnagar,Hno 1-8-597,Hyderabad-44\n\n                                                          ',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-18',NULL,'2007-10-18','2010-06-10 12:14:22','2010-06-10',2,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(239,'Mohammed A',NULL,NULL,'Pune','mohadvsdvmmed.ayvsdfvaz8dfv2@gmail.com',NULL,NULL,'0','919860238668','0',NULL,'0','2007-10-13',10,34,'2010-06-10 12:14:22',2,'0',NULL,'200710/18/ATT4891.html','200710/18/DOC16363.doc','Mohammed Ayaz\nOracle 11i Apps DBA \n\nMohammed A\nEmail: \nmohadvsdvmmed.ayvsdfvaz8dfv2@gmail.com\n\nContact no. +91-9860238668\n         \n\n\n\nOBJECTIVE:\n\nTo work in a challenging environment where I can enhance and deliver my technical skills to the best of my capabilities and talent.\n\n\nSUMMARY:\n\n2.4 year of experience as an Oracle \n\nApps DBA and Core Dba consultant.\n2 years of experience as an Oracle Application Database Administrator in Linux.\n\n\n\nSPECIALIZATION\n\n\n\n\n\nInstallation of databases such as Oracle 8i, Oracle 9i on, Linux A.S 3.\n\n   \nInstallation of Oracle Apps11i (single/multi node) on Linux,.\n\n   \nInstallation of Oracle 11.5.9, 11.5.10., 11.5.10.2 on Linux, Windows.\n\n   \nInstallation of Oracle Developer 6i, Discoverer, Workflow, Toad on Client systems on Windows.\n\n   \nSysadmin, Cloning, Patch application and concurrent manager activities on Apps 11i environment. \n\n  \nConfiguration & connectivity of Forms & Reports servers.\n\n   \nDatabase level patching, OS level patching on Linux.\n\n   \nDatabase Cloning, Application cloning.\n\n   \nConsidering future growth, reorganization of database and space management of database as per \n      \nneed.\n\n\n\nTECHNICAL SKILLS:\n\nOracle Applications\n    \n: Oracle 11i (11.5.9, 11.5.10) Administration.\nDatabase\n                \n          \n\nOracle 8i/9i\nOperating System\n    \n: Linux,AIX, Windows 98/NT/2000.\nLanguages \n              \n: C, C++, java.\nSpecialization\n\n          \n: Oracle Application 11i\n\n\nEDUCATIONAL QUALIFICATION:\n\n\nB.Sc (Comp. Sci.) from \nPune\nUniversity\n\n\n\nWORK EXPERIENCE:\n\nCurrently working in ERP Business Solutions as a Jr.Consultant.\n\nThe company is a software company and is mainly into consulting and technology.\n\n\n\nFrom\n\nSeptember 2006 \ntill date\n\nwith\n\nERP Business Solutions\n\nPune as\n Oracle 11i APPS DBA, Junior Consultant\n\nProject\n\n                           \n\nKotak Mahindra\n\nBANK , Pune\nRole\n    \n                            \n\nOracle Applications DBA \nEnvironment\n          \n         \n\nOracle Applications 11.5.10, Linux As-4.\n\nResponsibilities  \n\nMaintenance of installed Oracle Applications Release 11.5.10 suite and Troubleshooting.\n\nSysadmin, Database cloning, Patch applying, concurrent manager related troubleshooting and other Apps DBA functions\n\nChecking the concurrent manager and concurrent related activities and troubleshoot them.\n\nCloning of production instance on regular basis\n\nBackup maintenance and scheduling and standby server troubleshooting.\n\nTroubleshooting the performance related activities.\n\nCoordinating with Oracle support for logging tar and knowledge based search to find solution to the problems that are occurring in the live server and while applying patches (tar, Bug search, and User forum participation)\n\n\n\n\nFrom\n\nAugust 2005 \ntill \nSeptember 2006\n with\n\nERP Business Solutions\n\nPune\n as\n Oracle 11i APPS DBA,Junior Consultant\n\nProject\n\n                           \n\nShopper?s Stop , Pune\nRole\n    \n                            \n\nOracle Applications DBA \nEnvironment\n          \n         \n\nOracle Applications 11.5.10, Linux AS-3\n\nResponsibilities  \n\nMaintenance of installed Oracle Applications Release 11.5.10.2 suite and Troubleshooting.\n\nApplied patches on different instances (development, test and production).\n\n Performed pre patch analysis.\n\n Creation of tablespaces and users and granting privileges.\n\n Handle various issues while patching.\n\nSystem administration functions like creating users, creating responsibilities and menus.\n\nApplied patches on application and database.\n\nPerform health check up of instances regularly.\n\n Check Workflow Notification Mailer regularly.\n\n\nDatabase Cloning.\n\nFrom\n\nApril 2005 \ntill\n August 2005\n with\n\nERP Business Solutions\n\nPune as\n Oracle DBA, \nTrainee\n\n\n         \nInitial System Study\n\n         \nDatabase Backup and routine maintenance activities\n\n         \nCreating and managing users, granting privileges and roles\n\n         \nCreating and Managing of tablespaces, undo segments, data files. \n\n         \nSpace Management \n\n         \nChecking of all the log files and trace files on regular basis \n\n         \nCreation of tablespaces, rollback segments, users and granting/revoking roles to them. \n\n         \nDevelopment of proper Backup and Recovery strategies.\n\n\nPersonal information\n\nNAME\n                               \n\n\n      \n          \nMohammed Ayaz\nDATE OF BIRTH\n                  \n\n       \n          \nOctober 25, 1982\nSEX\n                                 \n\n       \n         \n\nMALE\nMARITAL STATUS\n               \n\n                 \nSINGLE\nLANGUAGE KNOWN\n    \n          \n\n       \n          \nENGLISH & HINDI.\n\n\nPERMANENT ADDRESS:\n\n2167,\nNew Modikhana,\nCamp,\nPune.\nPin- 411001\nPHONE No.\n\n+919860238668.\n\n\n(References on Request)','ERP Business Solutions',1,NULL,'2007-10-18',NULL,'2007-10-18','2010-06-10 12:14:22','2010-06-10',2,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(240,'Prashanti ',NULL,NULL,NULL,'dvdvdv@gmail.com',NULL,'9979021269','0','09985418489','0',NULL,'0','2007-04-30',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-10 12:14:22',2,'0',NULL,'200710/18/ATT4892.html','200710/18/DOC16364.doc','Resdex @ naukri.com\ndvdvdv@gmail.com\n\nTelephone: 09985418489\n(M)\n 91 80 9979021269\n(R)\n\nD.O.B\n - 10 Jul 1982 \nModified on\n - 25 Sep 2007 \nAnnual Salary\n - INR 3 Lac(s) 80 Thousand \nTotal Years of Experience\n - 3 Year(s) 2 Month(s) \nCurrent Location\n - Bangalore \nPreferred Location\n - Anywhere in India, Anywhere in South India \nMCA with 3+exp in IT field\n\nTEXT RESUME \n\n?«\n Have 10 months of experience in clinical domain (Clinical Industry for drugs), software development, database designing in Oracle 9i, pl/sql, VB by using CRF\'s, Labvalues and follows MeDRA, WHO Dictionaries for Clinical Test material.\n?«\n Have 2.4 years of experience Banking and clinical domain, developing Audit Trail by using Triggers, Database Documentation(database validation, database designing, database capture, database closure) for BIO-MEDICAL CARE AND CCRM.\n?«\n Have excellent skills in systems integration, data migration, business intelligence/reporting, analysis, design, interfacing, and database application development. Current experience in SQL, PL/SQL, Oracle database.\n?«\n Have excellent and broad knowledge of various computer technologies, software/web development, mobile technologies, banking, clinical, pharma relational databases, object-oriented, client-server, and UNIX operating systems.\n?«\n Database Designing for WHO dictionary database to Every Project (spending weekends).\n?«\n Generating Oracle and \nCrystal\n, Data Reports.\n?«\n Understanding and experience in SDLC and QA procedures.\n?«\n Have great motivation to learn new skills/technologies, excellent analytical/problem-solving skills, fast-learner in any skills, resourceful, committed, hard-worker, and self-initiative.\n?«\n Able to coordinate and communicate with project team. Currently I am working independently and as part of team.\n?«\n Able to communicate in Telugu (native), English (fluent), Hindi, Tamil (fluent), Kannada & Gujarati.',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-18',NULL,'2007-10-18','2010-06-10 12:14:22','2010-06-10',2,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(241,'Prashant Kumar Penumatsa',NULL,NULL,NULL,'prashant.p.dba@gmail.com',NULL,'040 23042223','0','9959433320','0',NULL,'0','2007-04-30',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-10 12:14:22',2,'0',NULL,'200710/18/ATT4893.html','200710/18/DOC16365.doc','Prashant Kumar Penumatsa\n                                                                                          \nPrashant\n Kumar Penumatsa\n              \n                                                                                                                          \nPlot-No.54,\n                                                       \nEmail: \nprashant.p.dba@gmail.com\nMayuri\n\nnagar\n\nMiyapur\n\n                                    \nCell: 9959433320.\nHyderabad-560032.\n                \n                                \n040-23042223.\nCareer Objective:\n\nSeeking assignments with a technology-driven organization of repute.\n\nSummary of Experience and skills:\n                                 \n\n\n          \n3+ years of experience in IT industry.\n\n          \nWorking as \nSoftware Engineer \nfor\n HSBC Software Development, \nHyderabad\n\n\n          \nWorked for\n\nIflex\n\nBangalore\n from OCT2006-May2007.\n\n          \nWorked as\n\nSoftware Engineer for \nZisys\n-IT solutions since Jan 2004- Oct 2006.\n\n          \nWorked on Oracle 9i, SQL Server2000 as Developer, \nUnix\n and shell scripting.\n\n          \nWorked as a Back-end developer on database operations as DML, DDL, DCL and TCL, Data Modeling, Creating Procedures, triggers, functions, Packages, Indexes. Exception Handling, Writing Cursors, Tuning of SQL statements.\n\n          \nInstallation, configuration and up gradation of Oracle server software.\n\n          \nExperience in Physical database design & creation. Managing the database?s storage structures and schema objects. Creation of table spaces, rollback segments, database security imposition by creation and granting of roles and privileges. Starting up and shutting down the database. Performance Tuning.\n\n          \nAble to work and communicate across culture and different people. Willingness to learn all the time. Good communication skills, adaptable to surroundings and confident to take up problems.\n\nScholastic Details:\n\n\n          \nBachelor of Technology (B.tech)\n in Computer Science and Information Technology from J.N.T.U, Hyderabad 2003.\n\n          \nMBA-Information Technology\n from \nManipal\nUniversity\n, Bangalore.(pursuing part-time) \n\n\nAdditional Qualifications:\n\n\n          \nOracle Certified\n\nAssociate\n for oracle9i DBA (SQL & Fundamentals-1).\n\n          \nMicrosoft certified\n\nprofessional\n for SQL-Server2000(Installing, configuring & administering)\n\n          \nOracle9i DBA\n from SQL * International, \nBangalore\n\n\n          \nIBM Mainframes from Signon Technologies, \nHyderabad\n\n\n          \nSQL-server UNIX from NIIT.\n\n\nIT skills:\n       \n     \nO/S\nWIN NT, MVS, \nUNIX\nLanguages\nSQL, Pl/SQL, T-SQL, COBOL\n, JCL\nRDMBS\nORACLE 9i, SQL-Server, DB2\n, VSAM.\nTools\nSql*, TOAD, Pro*c\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nProject profile:\n\n\n\nProject: 1 \nTitle\n                                    \n: BEN Support\nClient\n                                  \n\nDeutshe Bank\n\nEnvironment\n                        \n: XML, Oracle9i. \nDescription\n\nI flex\n, Business Enterprise Network (BEN) is a web-based financial project of Deutsche bank which records all the information related to it. It maintains the Database of users, employees, financial issues, Budget and costing activities.\nRole & Responsibilities:\n\n          \nAs the Central administrator am responsible for creating new DB users, \nMaintaining\n existing User records.\n\n          \nResponsible for resolving technical issues related to Database, writing queries in SQL/PLSQL.\n\n        \nUp gradation of project version.\n\n\nProject: 2\nTitle\n                                   \n: ERP, Automation of Distribution and Supply chain.\nClient\n                                 \n: DRL Hydraulics India Ltd\nEnvironment\n                       \n: V.B .NET, Oracle 9i.\nDescription\n\n Project is divided into 12 modules order Management, Designs, Material\nPlanning, indenting, Production, Sub-Contracts, QCD, Assembly, Stores, Purchase, \nMarketing & Dispatch, Tools and HRD modules.\n The system provides the facility to \nMonitor and control the production and inventory of items. It provides the common\nIndenting, order maintenance, purchase, order maintenance and stores modules. It \nEnables the management to streamline the flow of information among the \nDepartments to give the optimum results.\n This provides the features which allow the \nUses to find out the current stock level, purchases and indent details. \nRole & Responsibilities\n\n\n          \nWorked as a pl/sql developer on Order management, stores, QCD (Quality control division) & purchase modules. Menus are designed as per user need. Menu level security is also provided Development of Program Specifications & member of the team to study the existing system. \n\n\nProject :\n\nTitle\n                                   \n\nEnterprise\n Resource Information Systems.\nClient\n                                 \n: IDS Software solutions, \nBangalore\n\nEnvironment\n                       \n: UNIX, Java, Servlets, JDBC and HTML, Oracle9i.\nDescription\n\nENTERPRISE\n RESOURCE INFORMATION SYSTEMS (ERIS) is a computerized solution for recruiting agencies and software consultant?s. This application maintains electronic database comprises of job applicants, employees and clients. User of this system can enter and access details of all the information. The main aspect is to provide good user interface, security, validation, replication of data and auditing, if required. To reduce the load of traffic database packages are also used. Various types of reports like tabular, master-detail, \nmatrix\n are generated accordingly. \nRole & Responsibilities:\n\n          \nInvolved as a Back-end developer in Designing Normalized tables and provided Coding, also involved in some of the database administration tasks.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nProject :4\nName\n                                      \n: UCS (Unified Contract System)\nClient\n         \n                             \n: Deutsche Leasing, \nGermany\nType of Project\n                         \n: Development & Enhancement\nEnvironment\n                            \n: IBM, S/390, JCL, COBOL, VSAM, DB2.\nTeam Size \n                   \n   \n         \n\n: 15\nDescription:\n    \nUCS is the process of Re-Hosting their IBM mainframe applications. We are involved in redesigning, re-engineering & development of UCS. Our Aim is to provide a single source for accessing Customer, Supplier and Prospect information for Offerings, Contracts and other core information about customer. The information is maintained in VSAM files. The system has a mix of Mainframe, Client Server, Web and proprietary Technologies. \nRole & Responsibilities:\n\n          \nDevelopment, Enhancement and Maintenance support (On-line and Batch) Coding related to Archive of Financial related Tables, analysis and Modification of impacted programs in DB2. \n\nPersonal profile:\n\nFather name\n                            \n: Sesha Vardhana Rao\nD-O-B\n                                       \n: 19 November 1981\n\n\n\n\n\nP.Prashant\n Kumar)',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-18',NULL,'2007-10-18','2010-06-10 12:14:22','2010-06-10',2,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(242,'Ramanamurthy',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL,'0',NULL,'0','2007-04-30',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-10 12:14:22',3,'0',NULL,'200710/18/ATT4894.html','200710/18/DOC16366.doc','Srinivas Resume\nExperience Summary\n\n\n\n       \n3+ years of experience in information technology (IT). \n\n       \nExpertise in manufacturing domain and experienced in modules Order Management (OM), Purchase order (\nPO\n) and Oracle Inventory.\n\n       \nExperience in Customizing Oracle seeded Reports in Oracle Inventory, Purchase Order (PO) and Order Management (OM).\n\n       \nExpertise in Interfaces, Conversions and Data Migration from legacy systems to Oracle Inventory. \n\n       \nExpertise in System Administration and Application Object Library (AOL) to manage concurrent managers, application user setup, defining responsibilities, values sets, flex fields, reports, concurrent programs.\n\n       \nExpertise in using tools like TOAD, SQL*Loader and Reports builder. \n\n       \nExcellent command over SQL, PL/SQL, Oracle Reports. \n\n       \nStrong programming experience in creating Procedures, Packages, Functions, Triggers using SQL and PL/SQL. \n\n       \nAlso experienced in fine-tuning code for better performance. Commitment to excellence proven by an outstanding career track.\n\nDomain expertise: \nManufacturing\n\nTechnical Expertise:\nERP:\nPackages (Incl Versions)\nOracle Applications ? Release 11.5.10, 11.5.5\nModules\nOrder Management (OM), Oracle Inventory (Inv) and Oracle Purchasing (\nPO\n).\nLanguage\nProgramming\n                        \n\nSQL, PL/SQL, \nUNIX-Shell Scripts\nDatabase\nOracle 8i,9i\nGUI\nDeveloper/2000\n(Forms 6i & Reports 6i)\nTools\nTOAD, SQL* LOADER, SQL* Plus, Oracle Forms Builder, Reports Builder, Schema Builder, Procedure Builder, WS-FTP\nMethodology \nAIM ( Application Implementation Methodology)\n\n\nEducation:\n\nDegree/Qualification\nInstitution Name\nB. Tech (Computer Science Engineering)\nS.\nV.\n University, Tirupati, A.P passed in 2003 \n\nEmployment History\n\nCompany Name\nDesignation\nStart date ? End date\nBirla Soft\n\nAssociate Consultant\n\nSep?05\n\nto Till Date\niGate\nSoftware Engineer\nAug?04 \n\nto Aug?05\n\n\n\n\n\n\nProject Details: \n\n1. \nAvago Technologies\n\nProject Description\nAvago Technologies is a spin off company of Agilent Technologies. They are manufacturers of semiconductor products. Avago is aiming at maintaining its own system and database by separating out all data and programs from the current Agilent system to its own. It also aims to implement 11.5.10 instead of the existing 11.5.5 for Agilent. This project aims in migrating objects from 11.5.5 instance to 11.5.10 instance. The project involves compiling of Forms, Interfaces and Reports. \nClient\nOracle \nIndia\nStart and End Date\nNov?06 to Till Date\nRole\nTechnical\nContribution\nDevelopment and Customization of Reports and Conversions \nInvolved in unit testing for Concurrent Programs \nInvolved in unit testing for Database Objects\nInvolved in performance testing of reports\n\nEnvironment\nOracle 11.5.5,11.5.10\nOperating System\nUNIX, Windows XP\nTeam Size\n20\n\n\n\n\n2.\n Oracle Apps Maintenance\n\nProject Description\nMaintenance Project ? As a t\nechnical Consultant, provided post implementation support\nClient\niGate\nStart and End Date\nSep?05 \nto Oct?\n06\nRole\nTechnical\nContribution\nApplication User creation and assigning responsibilities & permissions.\nInterfaces, Forms and Reports registration.\nConcurrent program definitions and executable, creating value sets, registration of forms, reports.\nCreation of Value sets of Independent/Dependent/None and table type.\nRegistering the newly created tables with APPS using API?s AD_DD PACKAGE.\n\nDeveloped various Packages & Procedures.\n\nEnvironment\nOracle apps11i(11.5.8) , Oracle8i\nOperating System\nUNIX, Windows NT\nTeam Size\n10 \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n3.\n Business Model for Retail Banking\n\nProject Description\nBanking, like any other business model has a master business process (i.e. Retail Banking), which is supported by a number of sub processes. The retail banking consists of sub processes like savings account, current accounts, loans, fixed deposits and demat accounts. The project has been developed to deal with all retail banking operations and the external Customer?s services.\n\nClient\nSolar Softech\nStart and End Date\nAug?04 \nto \nAug?05\nRole\nProgrammer\nContribution\n\n         \nDevelopment of Stored Procedures and Functions\n\n         \nWriting code for Data base triggers on Tables\n\n         \nInvolved in creating Tables\n\n         \nDeveloped Reports using Reports 6i\n\n         \nInvolved in unit testing for Database Objects\n\nEnvironment\nSQL, PL/SQL, Forms6i, Reports6i\nOperating System\nWindows 2000\nTeam Size\n20',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-18',NULL,'2007-10-18','2010-06-10 12:14:22','2010-06-10',3,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(243,'Rahul V. Katturwar',NULL,NULL,NULL,'rahulkvxczvvdvatturwar@gmail.com',NULL,'0712 2742380','0','098220 61728','0',NULL,'0','2008-04-29',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-10 12:14:22',3,'0',NULL,'200710/18/ATT4898.html','200710/18/DOC16367.doc','Ashish S Sawant\nRahul v. Katturwar\n     \nEmail \n?rahulkvxczvvdvatturwar@gmail.com\nCell\n   \n--098220-61728 , 0712-2742380\n               \n\nObjective:\n\n\nTo work in a challenging and enriching environment where I can upgrade my current skills and apply them at their best for optimum benefit of the company\n\n\nSummary:\n\n\n       \n2.7+ years of experience in Database management,\n Evaluate SQL statement\nperformance using utilities like explain plan, tkprof and sqltrace\n\nDetermining Tablespace free space and managing growth (TABLESPACE,DATAFILE, maintenance).Configured the service on oracle client using\n\nNet configuration assistance.\n\nManaging all Daily database maintenance issues.\n\nLoading data between databases (Export and Import, SQL Loader).\n\nImproving performance by creating appropriate indexes.\n\n\n       \nExperience in \nInstallation of ORACLE9iand oracle 10GR2 RAC (server & client) on LINUX Solaris as well as WINDOWS platform.Shell Scripting like Startup,Shutdown.Maintains Password for sys,system and Users.Deploying backup (hot and cold) mechanisms and Recovery procedures. RMAN for Backup & Recovery.\n\nTuning and configuring the Oracle\n\nserver for Maximum performance (Statspack).\n\n\nSkill Set: \n\nRDBMS\n: Working Knowledge of Oracle 8i-9i-10G\nLanguage\n: SQL,PL/SQL\nOperating Systems\n: Sun Solaris8,LINUX 7.1, Windows 9X XP, 2000.\nApplication \n: MS-Office.\nConcepts, Techniques\n\nConcepts of Information Processing, Structured Systems Analysis and Design, LAN, Internet.\n\n\nCertification:\n\n\n         \nOracle9i Database Administrator Certified Associate.(\nTest ID: SR2074358\n\n        \nReg.No. M4ESYD5073\n\n\n\n         \nAchievement certification of PL/SQL Programming and database administration.\n\n\n                                 \nEducation:\n\n\n         \nBachelor of Electrical Engineering with 64.77% from YCCE.PT.NAGPUR .\n\n         \nDiploma in electrical Engg. from Shri Datta Meghe Polytechnic\n\nNGP.\n\n\n\n\n\nWork Experience:\n\n\nTotal Experience:-2.7years\n\n1) \nTECH MAHINDRA LTD. SHARADA CENTRE PUNE\n         \nAPR2007- Till Date\n\n\nJob Profile:-\nworking as Technical associate. Provide\n\ndatabase support to 24*7 Production \nenvironment\n Sun solaris 8.Daily maintance of all oracle database environment.Troubleshooting user queries for slow performance using explain plan, sqltrace ,explain plan.Patching for upgradation of database and application\n\nSpace management.etc\n\n\n   \n\n2)\n   \nPrabhudas Lilladher Pvt. Ltd. Worli.MUMBAI\n\nJune2006 ?APR2007\n\nJob Profile:- \nWorking as a Database Administrator.Job involved application of archieved log to synchronise standby database,Maintain Backup policy,monitor Database performance.\n\nPeriodic Maintenance and upgradation of Applications as per the requirements.\n\nTuning and configuring the Oracle\n\nserver for Maximum performance (Stats pack).\n\n\n\n\n\n2)\n\nACES e-solutions Pvt.Ltd.STP \nNagpur\n     \nFrom NOV 2004 ? june 2006\n\nJob Profile:-\n Working as a Asst. Database administrator. Job Involve \nCreate user logins Query and user to respective database and Manage security task.like granting and revoking permissions \nCreate profile and assign users, maintain tablespace(like providing space for enoughData)Performing Backup (Logical & Physical) & Recovery automation, logical incremental backup on daily basis &full logical Backup on weekly\n\nbasis, Physical\n\nBackup using RMAN.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n3)\n\nAS A FACULTY ON ORACLE 9i DBA IN RAMIFY SYSTEMS, MAHAL, NAGPUR\n\n\n         \nPerformed onsite Installation,provide trainning on pl/sql programming and Database administration.\n\n         \nConceptual Model design\n\nEstimated sizes of storage structures and growth projection.\n\n         \nWrote scripts for creation of tables, views and indexes\n\n         \nWrote program units in PL/SQL - Packaged Procedures, DML, System and Schema Triggers.Evaluating queries for performance.\n\n         \nDeveloped some Data Entry Screens (GUI interface development)\n\n         \nTransferring some tables\' data from legacy system (Foxbase) to Oracle.\n\n         \nCreating user accounts and roles; managing security related issues.\n\n         \nMaintaining Backup (logical and OS level)\n\nExtracurricular activities\n\n\n         \nActive participation in events like Quizzes, Elocution, at the school & college levels.\n\n         \nDid some social works in school.\n\n         \nOne of the best players in college cricket squad\n\nInterests:\n\n         \nComputers, Reading books, Listening Music and Gossiping\n               \n\n\nPersonal Details:\n\nName \n                                  \n\n\nRahul V. Katturwar\n          \nDate Of Birth\n                  \n\n\n3rd-Nov-1977\nGender\n                                \n\n\nMale.\nPassport No.\n                      \n\n\nF6962724 (Passport Office Nagpur)\nLanguage Spoken\n             \n\n\nMarathi,English & Hindi\nCurrent Address\n             \n: Rahul Vijay Katturwar\n                                             \n\n\nA\\4,c/o A. V Pawar.\n                              \n                                         \nAnurag socity.Opp. Kokan Express\n                                         \nRestonrent , Kothrud Stand ,karve Road .\n         \n       \n                                      \n  \nKothrud. Pune.\n         \n       \nPermanent Address\n         \n: Rahul Vijay Katturwar\n                                             \n\nPlot No.3,14\nth\n street\n                                             \n\nVishwakarma Nagar\n                                             \n\nNagpur-440027\n                                                                                    \n                                                         \n    \n\n                   \n\n\n\n\nPlace:PUNE\n                                                                                                   \nDate:\n              \n                                                                         \n(Rahul\n\nV. Katturwar)',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-18',NULL,'2007-10-18','2010-06-10 12:14:22','2010-06-10',3,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(244,'Saravanan M',NULL,NULL,'Chennai','saravansdvvvdvanm_19vdv83@yahoo.co.in',NULL,'91 044 26864139','0','99402 58506','0',NULL,'0','2007-12-13',8,23,'2010-06-10 12:14:22',3,'0',NULL,'200710/18/ATT24644.html','200710/18/DOC16368.doc','Saravanan.M_.NET_Developer_Resume\nSARAVANAN.M\n                                 \n                                                                            \n#94, 3\nrd\n Avenue\n\n                                  \n          \n\n        \n    \n            \n\nsaravansdvvvdvanm_19vdv83@yahoo.co.in\n      \n\nBanu Nagar, Pudur,\n     \n                                             \n               \n\nMobile:\n\n99402-58506\nAmbattur,\n           \n                                                      \n             \nPhone\n: +91 044 26864139\n                                                  \n       \nChennai ? 600 053,\nTamil Nadu, INDIA\n    \n_______________________________________________________________________\n                                                  \n\nObjective: \n\nTo join an esteemed software organization, which will be an opportunity for me to gain professional experience in application development with quality procedures, to enhance my technical skills as well as learn project management skills.\n\n\nExperience Summary:\nI have around 2.3 Years of Experience in projects from June 2005 till Date. I have worked in different challenging projects in .NET platform.\n    \n    \nJan 07 ? Till Date:\n   \nBlueshift India (P) Ltd.\n                                    \n\nSaidapet, Chennai\n\n    \nJune 05 ? Jan 07:\n   \nChennai Interactive Business \n(P) \nLtd (ChennaiOnline)\n                                    \n\nT.Nagar, Chennai\n\n\nThe projects that I developed are Web Applications using Asp.net, C#.Net using SQL Server 2000 as Database.\n\n                        \nComputer Proficiency:\n\n.NET technologies\n\n                  \n\n\n          \nASP.NET, C#\nOperating Systems\n                 \n\n           \nWindows, MS?DOS\nWeb Technologies\n      \n            \n\n\n         \nHTML, XML, Java Script, XSLT\nPackages\n                                \n\n           \nMS - Office \nTools\n                                       \n\n           \nMS.NET Framework\nDatabases\n                               \n\n           \nMS Sql Server 2000\n            \nEducation:\n\n\nCourse\n\n\nInstitution\nBoard /\nUniversity\nYear of Completion\n\nMarks\n\n\nB.E (CSE)\nKCG College of technology\n(Formerly,\nNational Institute of Technology & Science)\nMadras\nUniversity\n2000-2004\n72\nXII\nEbenezer Marcus Matriculation Higher Secondary School\nState Board\n1999-2000\n82\n\nEbenezer Marcus Matriculation Higher Secondary School\nMatriculation\n1997-1998\n80\n\nProfessional and Project Experience:\n\nProject #1\n\nProject Name\nRMS (RECRUITMENT MANAGEMENT SYSTEM)\nSoftware\nAsp .Net Web Application, C# .Net, JavaScript, Html, SQLserver2000.\nOrganization\nBlueshift India (P) Ltd.\nClient\nFidelity\nTeam Size\n\nRole in the Project\nDevelopment of Admin module, HR, Interview Panelists, Offer Management and Candidate modules.\nProject Description\nA company?s strength lies in its human resources.\n\nThe best companies consider recruitment extremely important, and a lot of resources are spent on it.\n\nIn the recruiting process, many milestones are crossed from the time the requisition is made to the time an employee is\nHired; many tasks are performed; much time is taken; many players are involved.\n\nWhile paper and pen methods work, they are pointless when sophisticated systems perform the same task effortlessly.\n\nThe Recruitment Management System (RMS), intelligently automates many of the tasks in recruitment, and makes recruiting a pleasure.\nRMS has several modules. Its modules are divided into two groups Extranet & Intranet.\nExtranet Modules: Candidate, Vendor and Campus modules.\nIntranet Modules: Administrator, Human Resource, Requirement recommender, Approver, Hire Approver, Requirement Creator, Recruiter, Interview Panelists, Employee referral.\nThe RMS is a customizable product which does it all from creating requirement vacancies to match requirements with candidates, Schedule interviews, search, shortlist candidates, Make offers, authenticate campuses and vendors, see statuses, Evaluate candidates, upload parse resumes and view reports.\nThe process from Submission of resume by the candidate to handling offer letter to the candidate is taken care by the RMS.\n\n\nProject #2\n\nProject Name\nProperty Search\nSoftware\nASP.NET, C#, JavaScript, Windows 2000\nOrganization\nChennai Interactive Business Services (P) Ltd\nClient\nCloserLook Search Services Inc\n Canada \nTeam Size\n\nRole in the Project\nProgramming, Testing\nProject Description\nProperty Search is to determine the assets of an individual as well as for property reporting. By providing the input such as Last Name, Street Name, City, State, Parcel Number, etc., application provides with the details of the property. The results are categorized according to Basic Details, Tax Info, Residence Info, Sales Info etc. This application searches the entire US Country according to the respective County\'s specified by the user.\n\nProject #3\n\nProject Name\nGotcha\nSoftware\nASP.NET, C#, JavaScript, Windows 2000\nOrganization\nChennai Interactive Business Services (P) Ltd\nClient\nCloserLook Search Services Inc \nCanada \nTeam Size\n\nRole in the Project\nDefining functional specifications of the system. Screen design, Coding and testing\nProject Description\nGotcha is a Skip-Tracing Tool that traces a new address and phone number for an individual in Canada and US. This skip tracing tool will take one or more of the following as inputs: last name, first name, address, last known home and/or work phone number as well as phone numbers of friends or family members under the ?Other Phone?. The tool will then search for and match a current address and phone number to the record and present the best results.\n\nProject #4\n\nProject Name\nARP (Automated Recruitment Process)\nSoftware\nASP.NET, C#, MS-SQL Server 2000, JavaScript, Windows 2000\nOrganization\nChennai Interactive Business Services (P) Ltd\nClient\nMafoi\nTeam Size\n\nRole in the Project\nRequirement Gathering and System Study\n. Screens design, Coding and testing\nProject Description\nThis System is used to automate the Consultancy Process. This System has role based authentication through which various roles can be provided. This System has the functionality to manage the Client. Manage the advertisement for a Client, Posting the Job for an advertisement. Managing the Candidate resume for a Job, from Selecting the Candidate for test, interview, offer etc... Reports can be generated for Advertisements, Candidates, and for Job.\n\nProject #5\n\nProject Name\nProperty Search Daily Monitoring Application\nSoftware\nASP.NET, C#, Windows 2000\nOrganization\nChennai Interactive Business Services (P) Ltd\nClient\nCloserLook Search Services Inc \nCanada\nTeam Size\n\nRole in the Project\nRequirement Gathering ,\n Coding and testing\nProject Description\nOur Search Engine involves the concept of Invincible Web. It is therefore essential to check all the sites that are used for developing search engine. This process is done through our application. If our application reports a site change, then we manually check the site for any Site Change or any Regular Expression change and if there is any change then it is reported to our client for further action.\nProperty Search Daily Monitoring Application is used to detect any site change. This application retrieves the previous day result (Xml formatted Result) and current day result (Xml formatted Result), compares it, if there is a site change it informs the user through a mail. This system is run on daily basis and checked for any Site change\n\nKey Values and Achievements:\nInvolved in Client Handling\nRMS (RECRUITMENT MANAGEMENT SYSTEM)\nOrganization: Blueshift India (P) Ltd.\nClient: MphasiS (EDS)\nResponsibilities: Involved in direct Client handling at MphasiS, Perungudi for one month. Provided technical support for RMS at MphasiS. Managed the Master Data of RMS from identifying the Master Data and updating the RMS System with the Master Data through Database (Sqlserver2000) and configuring the RMS System according to the MphasiS environment.\n\nPersonal profile: \n\n\nDate of Birth\n                          \n\n           \n12\nth\n April 1983 \n\nGender\n                                   \n\n           \nMale\n\nMarital status\n\n            \n            \n\n           \nSingle\n\nNationality\n                             \n\n           \nIndian\n\nPassport \n                               \n\n           \nAvailable\n\nLanguages Known\n                 \n\n           \nEnglish and Tamil\n                     \n\nTotal Experience\n                    \n\n           \n27 months.\n\nNationality\n                             \n\n           \nIndian\n\nFather?s Name\n                       \n            \n\n           \nK. Manickavasagam\n\nPermanent Address\n               \n\n           \nNo 94, 3 rd Avenue,\n                                                            \nBanu Nagar, Pudur, Ambattur, Chennai ? 53.\n\nAddress for Comm.\n                \n\n           \nNo 94, 3 rd Avenue,\n                                                            \nBanu Nagar, Pudur, Ambattur, Chennai ? 53.',' Blueshift India (P) Ltd',1,NULL,'2007-10-18',NULL,'2007-10-18','2010-06-10 12:14:22','2010-06-10',3,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(245,'Prasad Athrayil',NULL,NULL,NULL,'dvdvsdvds@gmail.com',NULL,NULL,'0','09860077170','0',NULL,'0','2003-07-31',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-10 12:14:22',2,'0',NULL,'200710/18/ATT19231.html','200710/18/DOC16369.doc','Resdex @ naukri.com\nPrasad Athrayil\ndvdvsdvds@gmail.com\n\nTelephone: 09860077170\n(M)\n\nD.O.B\n - 16 Nov 1977 \nModified on\n - 26 Sep 2007 \nAnnual Salary\n - INR 6 Lac(s) 70 Thousand \nTotal Years of Experience\n - 6 Year(s) 11 Month(s) \nCurrent Location\n\nBangalore\n\nPreferred Location\n\nBangalore\n.Net Team Lead having MCSD, MCAD and a total of 6.11 exp',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-18',NULL,'2007-10-18','2010-06-10 12:14:22','2010-06-10',2,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(246,'Rajesh Atikela',NULL,NULL,'Hyderabad','arajdferesh_ms@yahoo.com','arajergregesh_ms@hotmail.com',NULL,'0','9948109063','0',NULL,'0','2006-11-12',8,24,'2010-06-10 12:14:22',3,'0',NULL,'200710/18/ATT19232.html','200710/18/DOC16370.doc','Rajesh Atikela\n+91 \n\n9 9 4 8 1 \n\n0 9 0 6 3\narajdferesh_ms@yahoo.com\narajergregesh_ms@hotmail.com\n______________________________________________________________________________\n\nProfessional Summary:\n      \nHave 3+ years of Experience in Web Server, Web Services and Windows development.\n\n         \nA highly motivated and committed Software Engineer with 3+ years experience in various Technologies.\n\n         \nExperience and Expertise in Asp.Net, C#.Net, VB.Net, \nAJAX\n, JavaScript, XML and HTML\n\n         \nExperience in SQL Server.\n\nProfessional Experience:\n\n         \nWorking with eSoft Consulting Ltd, \nHyderabad\n as a Software Engineer since May 2005 to till date. \n\n         \nWorked for BRIX Consulting Inc, Secunderabad as a Software Engineer From May 2004 to April 2005.\n\nClient Location Experience:\n\n         \nDevelop and Implemented the Enterprises Security System (ESS) at the Police Control Room (PCS) in Direct General of Police Office (DGP Office) the Head Quarters of Andhra Pradesh Police, \nHyderabad\n\n\n         \nDevelop and Implemented the Truck and Weighbridge Monitoring System (TWBMS) at the Rajashree Cements, a unit of Grasim Industries, Group of Aditya Birla.\n\n         \nDeveloped\n\nthe RFID Batch reader Control Software to ?VESTIGE? Hardware for Controlling the Wagon Monitoring System at the Rajashree Cements, a unit of Grasim Industries, Group of Aditya Birla.\n\n         \nDeveloped the Control Software for ?\nAVERY\n? (Digital Weighbridge) Weigh Bridges and ?SUNMARS? Swipe Card Readers for the Controlling of the Truck and Weighbridge Monitoring System (TWBMS) at the Rajashree Cements, a unit of Grasim Industries, Group of Aditya Birla.\n\n         \nImplemented the Court Trial Monitoring System (TRLMS) at the Police Control Room (PCS) in Direct General of Police Office (DGP Office) the Head Quarters of Andhra Pradesh Police, Hyderabad.aaa\n\n         \nImplemented World Class Manufacturing (WCM) at the Rajashree Cements, a unit of Grasim Industries, Group of Aditya Birla.\n\nEducational Qualification:\nMaster of Science in Information Systems from \nAndhra\nUniversity\n in November 2003\nBachelor of Computer Applications from \nAndhra\nUniversity\n in November 2001.\nDiploma in Electronics and Communications Engineering, from SBTET in November 1997.\n\nTechnical Summary: \nDot Net Technologies\n\n                    \n\n\nAsp.Net, C#.Net, VB.Net\nDatabases\n                                            \n\n\nSQL-Server 2000.\nLanguages\n                                           \n\n\nC & T-SQL.\nWeb Technologies\n                             \n\n\nAJAX\n, JavaScript, Html, Xml\nProjects Summary:\n# Project 6\nEnterprise\n Security System\nClient\nAndhra Pradesh Police Department, \nHyderabad\nDuration\nMay 07 to Till date\nEnvironment\nAsp.Net, C#.Net with Sql-Server 2000\n\n                \nTo create an Enterprise Security System (ESS) that will enable security staff to control entry of authorized visitors and monitors their movement within the organization. This project works with integration of System Camera and Bar-Code generation. The project is implemented as Intranet Web Application with Web-Services and \nAJAX\n. Provided ?\nUser Controls \n\noading? dynamically.\n\nResponsibilities:\n\n         \nHandling the Team (Acting as a Team lead)\n\n         \nCaptured the requirements for ESS.\n\n         \nInvolved in the Product Coding and Unit Testing.\n\n         \nInvolved in the implementation.\n# Project 5\nTruck and Weighbridge Monitoring System\nClient\nAdithya Birla, Grasim Industries, \nMalkhed Road\nDuration\nSep 06 to April 07\nEnvironment\n\nAsp.Net, C#.Net with Sql-Server 2000\n\nThe Truck Monitoring system \n(TWBMS)\n will keep track of the movements of trucks which are Coming IN & Going OUT with the factory premises. This application is developed in two different modules. \n1)\n. Integrated Control Software (This module has developed as the windows services, working at client machine where Swiping and Weighbridge Hardware were installed)\n2)\n. Web based application (This module provides data entry and reports where they require through browser)\n                \nThe project is implemented as Intranet Web Application with Web-Services and \nAJAX\n\nProvided ?\nUser Controls \n\noading? dynamically.\nResponsibilities:\n\n         \nHandling the Team (Acting as a Team lead)\n\n         \nCaptured the requirements for TWBMS.\n\n         \nInvolved in the Product Coding and Unit Testing.\n\n         \nInvolved in the implementation.\n# Project 4\nRadio Frequency Identification\n\nClient\nACG, VESTIGE\nDuration\nMay 06 to Aug 06\nEnvironment\nC#.Net with Sql-Server 2000\n\nThe Main Objective of RFID is a method of remotely storing and retrieving data based on the Reader IP Address. Read and Write operations are possible on mifare cards which has 1024 x 8 bit EEPROM memory. This product is working as the Windows Services.\n\nResponsibilities:\n\n         \nCaptured the requirements for RFID.\n\n         \nInvolved in the Product Coding and Unit Testing.\n\n         \nInvolved in the Implementation.\n\n#3\nCourt Trial Monitoring System\nClient\nAndhra Pradesh Police Department, \nHyderabad\nDuration\nJan 06 to April 06\nEnvironment\nAsp.Net, C#.Net with Oracle\n\nThe Main Objective of Trial Monitoring system (TRLMS) is to provide quality service in line with the objectives of the Trial in the Court of law to expedite the trial process and to provide information to the key stake holders like Investigating officers, Monitoring officers, Prosecutors and Police Constable Officers attending the court duties. Mainly enhancing the cases submitted in the courts and tracking of Adjournments. The project is implemented as Intranet Web Application. Provided ?User Controls loading? dynamically.\n\nResponsibilities:\n\n         \nInvolved in the Product Coding and Unit Testing.\n\n         \nInvolved in the implementation.\n\n#2\nWorld Class Manufacturing\nClient\nAdithya Birla, Grasim Industries, \nMalkhed Road\nDuration\nMay 05 to Dec 05\nEnvironment\nAsp.Net, C#.Net with Sql-Server 2000\n\nWorld Class Manufacturing\n (WCM)\n is a competitive strategy that aims for shareholder?s value creation through focus on sustainable and superior QCDIP performance and other parameters. The objective of our WCM initiative is to successfully compete with any organization in which every employee from top to bottom is working towards making that organization the best in its particular field. \nThe project is implemented as Intranet Web Application. Provided ?User Controls loading? dynamically.\n\nResponsibilities:\n\n         \nInvolved in the Product Coding and Unit Testing.\n\n         \nInvolved in the implementation.\n\n#1\nMeteorological Database Maintain System\nClient\nCentral Tobacco Research Institute, \nRajahmundry\n\nDuration\nSep 04 to April 05\nEnvironment\nAsp.Net, C#.Net with Sql-Server 2000\n\nObject of this application is maintain the details of weather parameters information namely Weather Temperature, Soil Temperatures, Vapour Presser, Relative Humidity, Sunshine in hours, Total Evaporation, Daily Rain-fall, Number of Rainy-days, Wind Velocity in hours. \nThe project is implemented as Intranet Web Application.\n\nResponsibilities:\n\n         \nInvolved in the Product Coding and Unit Testing.\n\n\n\nDate: \n17-Oct-07','eSoft Consulting Ltd',1,NULL,'2007-10-18',NULL,'2007-10-18','2010-06-10 12:14:22','2010-06-10',3,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(247,'Suresh K',NULL,NULL,'Bangalore','rajcdvdvu.k.sdsvdsvuresh@gmail.com',NULL,NULL,'0','91 9916223869','0',NULL,'0','2009-01-11',8,24,'2010-06-10 12:14:22',2,'0',NULL,'200710/18/ATT24630.html','200710/18/DOC16371.doc','SURESH K\n\nSURESH K\nMail: \nrajcdvdvu.k.sdsvdsvuresh@gmail.com\nContact No: +91 9916223869\n                                                           \n                                                                  \n\nCareer Objective:\n\n         \nTo excel in the industry that offers challenge, excitement and freedom to grow with the power of drive to keep frequently updating with new emerging trends in technology.\n\nWork Experience:\n\n\n       \nWorking as Software Engineer in \nWIPRO TECHNOLOGIES\n\nBangalore\n from July-06 to till date. \n\n       \nWorked as Software Engineer in \nCOVANSYS\n\n\nBangalore\n from July-04 to June-06. \n\n       \nTrained in \nSharePoint\n\n2007\n in \nXIAMEN\n\nCHINA\n\nFrom May-07 to July-07.\n\nProfessional Summery:\n         \n\n       \nGood Knowledge in \nSharepoint\n server 2007\n\n\n       \nKnowledge in how to develop \nWEB PARTS \nand \nDeployee\n in \nShare Point Server 2007\n\n\n       \n3+ Years\n\nof experience\n in development of Windows based Applications and Web Applications. \n\n\nWorked with \n.Net framework, VB.NET, ASP.NET, ADO.NET \nand\n C#\n\n\n\nVery strong in Microsoft Development Technologies like \nAsp.Net ,C#\n\n\n\nAbility to work in-group as well as independently with minimal Supervision.\n\n\nQuick ability to master new languages and tools.\n\nTechnical Skill Set:\n\nOS\n      \n                   \n: Windows Server 2003,\n\nWin XP.\n          \nLanguages\n              \n: VB.NET and C#.NET\n          \nWeb Technologies\n    \n: HTML, ASP.NET, XML Web Services.\n          \nTechnologies\n           \n: .NET framework 1.1\n,2.0\n\n\n         \nDatabases\n               \n: MS SQL Server 2005.\n\nAcademic -Profile:\n\n\n\nM.C.A From I.G.N.O.U\n\n\nB.Sc (Computer Science) \nfrom \nS.V.University\n\nStrengths:\n\n\nCommitted to work in different technologies to drive the organization and myself to the greater heights.\n\n\nConfident in accepting any kind of work which suits my skill set.\n\n\nHardworking and Self-Learning as per the needs of the project.\n\n\nGood analytical skills.\n\nProfessional Experience:\n\nPROJECT\n 1:\n\nTitle\n                       \n\n\nNeoBrand\nClient\n                     \n\n\nPhoenix\n\nUS\nDuration\n                  \n\n\nFebruary-07 to till date\nEnvironment\n          \n   \n\n\nASP.NET, C#, SQL Server 2005\nRole\n                       \n\n\nDeveloper\n\nDescription\n\n\n                  \nDeveloped an application for the United States Open University which facilitates online registration,fee payment etc. The application allows the candidates to know about the different programs and courses , to register the courses and to pay the fee in online . The Sql sever database holds the personal and educational details of candidates, which the administration staff can edit , view and delete the inforamation by logging in. \n\nResponsibilities: \n\n\n      \nDesigned the front end using ASP.NET and\n   \nHTML.\n\n      \nDatabase connectivity using ADO.NET\n\n      \nHandling the issues of front-end and apply proper validation.\n\nPROJECT 2:\n\nTitle\n                       \n\nSITE4GIFTS.\nClient\n                     \n: BEST CASH ADVANCE, INC. (\nDelaware\n\nUSA\n\nDuration\n                  \n: August-06 to \n\nJanuary-07\nEnvironment\n             \n: C#, ASP.NET, SQL Server 2005\nRole\n                       \n: Developer\n\nDescription\n\nThis is an Online shopping for sending gifts to relatives, friends & client, etc., This Online Gift Store is developed very user friendly, end users can select gifts based on different Criteria?s like Occasion, Recipients (Father, Mother, Friends, etc.,). End User can search the gift services availability for Recipients location.\n\n\nOnline Gift Store Provides Advanced Search Option for searching the best suitable gifts for the Occasion & Recipient, it allows to search on price range also. The Major Module in this Online Store is Admin Control Panel where the Store Owner \n\nResponsibilities: \n\n\n\nInvolved in the designing of web forms using C#.\n\n\nInvolved in the database interaction using ADO.NET.\n\n\n\n\nPROJECT\n 3:\n\nTitle\n                       \n\n\nHotel Management (HM).\nClient\n                     \n\n\nHotel Mayur, \nMeerut\n\nIndia\n\nDuration\n                  \n\n\nOctober-05 to May-06\nEnvironment\n                 \n\n   \nC#, MS SQL Server 2000.\nRole\n                             \n\n   \nDeveloper\n\nDescription\n\n\nThis project was a complete hotel management system including modules for Lodging, Restaurant, Bar and Kitchen Maintenance in Hotel Mayur. The project provides functionality for customer reservation, customer registration, restaurant orders, kitchen inventory, and laundry. It includes printing of various templates like lodging bill, restaurant bill, kitchen order ticket, reservation/registration form, and other services bills. \n\nResponsibilities: \n\n\n       \nInvolved in the designing of windows forms using C#.\n\n       \nInvolved in the database interaction using ADO.NET.\n\nPROJECT\n 4:\n\nTitle\n                              \n\n\nFreight Logistics System (FL System)\nClient\n                           \n\n\nABX LOGISTICS, \nBelgium\n   \nDuration\n                       \n\n\nOctober-04 to August-05\nEnvironment\n     \n\n          \n\n\nVB.NET, ASP.NET and SQL Server2000.\nRole\n                             \n\n   \nDeveloper\nProject Description\n\n   \n      FL System is a web-based B2B logistics system for international freight shipments. The system enables the shipper and their partners (like exporter, importer, Export Forwarder, Import Forwarder, Customs House Broker etc.) to exchange information regarding the transportation requirements pertaining to an international ocean container shipment. Through the system, the shipper and other participants can track the physical location of the shipment. Participants can also collaborate in creating and exchanging the necessary shipping documentation required by the importer and the importing country\'s Customs authorities & thereby dramatically improving visibility, productivity, and overall supply chain economics. The system records all interactions in a transaction log.\n\nResponsibilities: \n\n\n       \nInvolved in the designing of web forms using ASP.Net.\n\n       \nInvolved in the database interaction using ADO.NET.\n\n\n\nPersonal Details:\n\n\n        \nGender\n                           \n\n      \nMale\n           \n\n                                                                                                   \n       \n\n\nFather?s Name\n                \n\n       \nK.V.SUBBA RAJU\n        \n   \n                                                  \n        \nMarital Status\n                 \n\n        \nUnmarried\n         \n        \nNationality\n                   \n\n  \n\n       \nIndian\n        \n        \nLanguages Known\n         \n\n\n\n       \nEnglish, Telugu and Hindi\n   \n     \n        \nPassport\n                         \n\n       \nAvailable\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nDeclaration:\n\n                       \nI here by assure that the information furnished above is true to the best of my knowledge and belief.\n\nPlace\n\nBangalore\n                        \n                                           \nyours sincerely,\n\nDate:\n                                                                                      \nSURESH K','WIPRO TECHNOLOGIES',1,NULL,'2007-10-18',NULL,'2007-10-18','2010-06-10 12:14:22','2010-06-10',2,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(248,'June 2005',NULL,NULL,'Noida','vingngnodkufggmar1000@sify.com','tovinodtiwari@gmail.com',NULL,'0','9968054949','0',NULL,'0','2007-12-13',8,23,'2010-06-10 12:14:22',3,'0',NULL,'200710/18/ATT24633.html','200710/18/DOC16372.doc','OBJECTIVE\n             \n                                            \n                                  \n\n      \nvinod k t\n                                                                                                                  \n      \nEmail ID: \nvingngnodkufggmar1000@sify.com\n                                                                                                        \n                 \ntovinodtiwari@gmail.com\n                                           \n                                                                       \n      \n\nContact No: 9968054949\n                                                                                                               \n    \n      \nTotal Years of Experience: 2.3 \n\n\n                                                                                                                    \n                                                                                                                  \n\n                       \n                                                                                            \nOBJECTIVE\n\nIntend to build a career in IT Field with leading corporate of hi-tech environment with committed & dedicated\n   \npeople, which will help me to explore myself fully and realize my potential\n\n\nSeeking to provide top-quality IT supports to ensure a competitive advantage in the global marketplace. Understanding of organizational strategies to meet corporate objectives.\n\n                                          \n                                                                       \n                                                                                                                \n  \nEXPERIENCE\n\n\n         \nMore Than \n2.3 years Experience in Jiyoun System Software Pvt. Ltd., Noida as a Software Developer\n in \nWeb-based application development using ASP.Net, C#.Net ADO.Net (Microsoft Technology), IIS, and SQL Server.\n\n         \nExcellent inter-personal skills. Ability to work under pressure.\n\n\n                                   \n                                                 \nQUALIFICATIONS SUMMARY\n\n\nMCA from ALAGAPPA UNIVERSITY KARAIKUDI (Tamilnadu) with \n63.2%\n(2002-2005)\n\nM.Sc. (Maths) from Dr. R.M.L Avadh University Faizabad(UP) with \n56.5%\n(1999-2001)\n\nB.Sc.(Maths) from Dr. R.M.L Avadh University Faizabad(UP) with \n55.5%\n(1996-1999)\nIntermediate from G.I.C.Sultanpur with \n62.3%\n in (1993-1996)\n10\nth\n\nfrom B.P.I.C. Kurwar Sultanpur (U.P.) with \n64%\n in (1991-1993).\n\n                                                                        \n                     \nPROGRAMMING SKILLS\n\n\n\n         \nWeb Technologies\n    \n\n\nASP.Net, HTML, Web Services, .NET Remoting\n\n\n         \nLanguages\n                   \n      \n\n      \nC, C++, C#,Asp.Net 2.0\n                                \n\n         \nRDBMS Tools\n                \n      \n\n      \nSQL Server 2005, Oracle, ADO.Net. \n\n\n         \nOperating Systems\n   \n\n\nWindows 95/98/2000 and XP.\n\n                                                               \n                                                                   \n                                                                    \n\n\nProfessional Experience(2.3 Years)\n\nJiyoun System Software Pvt. Ltd., Noida\n    \n  \n(June 2005 to till date)\n\nDesignation: \nSoftware Engineer\n\nCurrently involved developing various E-Commerce application and Web Application Using C#, ASP.Net, Web Services and SQL Server as Backend.\n\nPROJECT DETAILS:\n1.\nProject Name\nMediProductEShop \nmODIULE-aSSIGNED\nCustomer Module: Registration Details, Select Categories & Product List, Add to Shopping Cart, List in Shopping Cart, place order,Implementing Different Types of Caching .\nCLIENT\nClonegen Biotechnology\n\nUSA\nduration\nAug 2006 to Jan 2006\nOS\nWindows 2003 Server\nTOOLs used\nC#, ASP.Net 2.0 ,ADO.Net SQL Server 2000\nROLE\nTeam Member\nDescription\nThis is a E-Commerce Site i.e. Business to Business Site through \nwhich online pharmaceutical products will be selling and shown to the client and client generate business by providing online placement of Orders. The System will be web-based catalog sales site. User can browse the Catalog, add item in their personal shopping cart, and finish shopping. After that user check out and finalize the sale. To purchase items, Users must be registered as authenticated users by Providing account information: an Email address and Password. Authenticated users can take advantage of two things, to create orders remotely and a component that allows them to track orders remotely. These Two features illustrate Web Services. The ASP.Net facility that allows you to publish a component that is accessible using a web protocol such as SOAP or HTTP.\nResponsibility\nAnalyzing the Module and Development.\nPreparing program spec. and detailed design.\nCoding for ASP.Net page using c#.\n2.\n\nProject Name\nReal Estate Management System\nmODIULE-aSSIGNED\nDataBaseDesign,ModuleAnalysis,ContactDetails,Emailing, Authorization and Authentication, state Management\nduration\nFeb 2006 to July 2006\nOS\nWindows 2003 Server\nTOOLs used\nC#, ASP.Net 2.0 ,ADO.Net SQL Server 2005\nROLE\nTeam Member\nDescription\nReal Estate Management is a system of managing Employee, Customer and relationship with them and how can client interact with REM System. This project is developed for providing Scheduler and Assigns Task to client?s employee and also maintains records of customers and employees. In this system customer registration is maintained by employee and employee registration is maintained by employer which is finally registered by Admin. Admin can update all master records. Employer can login to REM system by providing Authenticated UserID and Password and can perform various tasks like creating Company Profile, Contact creation, Dealing, Task Assignment, Customer details and Searching. This project also provides facility of Messaging and Emailing between company employees and maintains daily Enquiry, Follow-ups, Task and Employee target performance reports\n\nResponsibility\nAnalyzing the Module and Development.Writing queries for data access.\nPreparing functional spec. and detailed design\nCoding for ASP.Net page using c#.\n2.\nProject Name\nFuture Bajar.com\nmODIULE-aSSIGNED\nDataBaseDesign,ModuleAnalysis,ProductDetais, and Authentication, state Management,Providing Links and Payment Gateway\nduration\nJuly 2006 to Feb 2007\nOS\nWindows XP Professional.\nTOOLs used\nC#, ASP.Net 2.0 ,ADO.Net SQL Server 2005\nROLE\nTeam Member\nDescription\nThis is On Line Shopping Cart Application used for shopping different kind of electronic products such as Mobile phones and Computers and other different products available in cart.Using On Line Payment Gateway ?Paypal.com? we manage the online Transactions Visitors can bye products and they can pay using credit cards. When user makes a online shopping\n\nwe register him by providing userid and password of a particular user as he can securely enter his credit card information. Using Secure Socket Layer we maintain Secure Transaction.\nResponsibility\nAnalyzing the Module and Development.Writing queries for data access.\nPreparing functional spec. and detailed design,Cookie Management,server side stateManagement\nCoding for ASP.Net page using c#.\n3.\nProject Name\nCustomer Relationship Management (On Going)\nmODIULE-aSSIGNED\nAdmin Module: login,RoleManagement,BuildsStoredProceedures Contact details, Employee details,state Management. \nduration\nMarch 2007 till Now\nOS\nWindows 2003 Server\nTOOLs used\nC#, ASP.Net 2.0 ,Validation Controls, SQL Server 2005\nROLE\nTeam Member\nDescription\nCustomer Relationship Management is a system of Managing relationship with customers. This project is developing for providing physical and online shopping to customers and also maintains records of customers and employees. Basically this project is developing in two faces. First internal face and second external face. In Internal face of projects limited between employer, employees and customers that physically interact with company points. External face of project is online selling of products. Here two types of registration for customer?s first online registration second physical registration. User must be registered as authenticated user for order placement providing by user Id and Password. In the physical registration, customer comes at physical point of customers. It maintains records of employees and customers. It gives also facility for Phone, mail and sms services.\nResponsibility\nAnalyzing the Module and Development. Preparing functional specification and detailed design .Writing queries for data access.\nPreparing functional spec. and detailed design coding using C# and Asp.net 2.0.\n\n                                                                                        \n                                    \n                                                      \n                                                                                          \narea of interests\n\nWeb Development, Internet Surfing, Programming, Watching TV. \n\n\n                            \n                                        \n                      \n                                                                                          \n\nperSONAL DETAILS\n                                                                                      \n             \n\n                                                                                                                                                                    \n\nFather?s Name: Mr. Heera Lal Tiwari\nDate of Birth:\n   \n20 June 1978\nSex:\n      \n          \nMale\nNationality:\n      \nIndian\nAddress:\n     \n     \nB-194, New Ashok Nagar, New Delhi-110096\nLanguages:\n      \nEnglish, Hindi','System Software Pvt. Ltd',1,NULL,'2007-10-18',NULL,'2007-10-18','2010-06-10 12:14:22','2010-06-10',3,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(249,'Yash',NULL,NULL,'New Delhi','ya7sdvsdvdsv85.it@gmail.com','yashwant.it@gmail.com','91 11 2245983','0','9811984784','0',NULL,'0','2008-01-12',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-10 12:14:22',2,'0',NULL,'200710/18/ATT24634.html','200710/18/DOC16373.doc','Resdex @ naukri.com\nyash \nC/o Shahab Singh,F-35/1 katwadria sarai hauz khaz new delhi New Delhi - 110016 \nya7sdvsdvdsv85.it@gmail.com\n\nTelephone: 9811984784\n(M)\n 91 11 2245983\n(R)\n\nD.O.B\n - 02 Apr 1984 \nModified on\n - 26 Sep 2007 \nAnnual Salary\n - INR 1 Lac(s) 40 Thousand \nTotal Years of Experience\n - 2 Year(s) 2 Month(s) \nCurrent Location\n - Delhi \nPreferred Location\n - Anywhere in India \n.Net Professional having 2 years of experience and experties in ASP.Net, C#, ADO.Net, XML and SQL server\n\n\nTEXT RESUME \n\nCURRICULUM VITAE\nYashwan kumar Present Address:\n+91-9811984784 F-35, katwariasarai,HauzKhas\nyashwant.it@gmail.com New Delhi \n? 110006\nProfessional Summary\n\nAround 2 Yrs. of experience in developing web based and Client Server applications using ASP.Net Technologies.\n\nProficient in Asp.Net, C#, SQL Server 2000.\n\nKnowledge on SDLC concepts.\n\nEffective communication skills, good analytical abilities, and zeal in learning new tools.\nOBJECTIVE\nLooking for a responsible and challenging career with a growth-oriented company where I can learn and improve my skills, where my talent and knowledge will significantly contribute to the company\n?s future growth and profitability\nA challenging position as a Software Engineer and the possibility of career advancement. Willing to work as a key player in challenging & creative Environment.\nEXPERIENCE\nI am working with SOFT TECH WORLD Pvt. Ltd Noida as an S/W Developer from October-2005 to till date.\nEDUCATIONAL QUALIFICATION\n\nM.C.A. from School of Computer & Information Sciences (SOCIS), IGNOU,(Pursuing)\n\nBCA. From School of Computer & Information Sciences (SOCIS) IGNOU\nTECHNICAL SKILLS\nOperatin System : Windows 98/XP/2000 Professional\nLanguage : C,C++,C#,ASP.Net2.0-1.1,C#2005-2003,Crystal Report.\nMarkup Language : Html, Xml\nDomain Knowledge : Educational\nDatabases : SQL Server 2005-2000,MS Access 2003\nPROFESSIONAL EXPERIENCE\nPROJECT : KwikTrig 2.1\nTechnical Skills Used : .NET (asp.net, c#)\nDesignation : Developer.\nBack End : SQL Server 2000.\nRole : Developer\nTeam size : 4\nDescription:\nKwikTrig is a suite of applications designed to help manage all aspects of a business organization\'s activities, from customer acquisition to order entry to warehouse, inventory, and manufacturing to invoices, accounting, and financial statements. It can bring together online and physical stores, integrate your direct sales force with your warehouse and manufacturing information, and provide up-to-the-minute financials results.\nPROJECT :Online Recruitment System (OLRS)\nTechnical Skills Used : .NET (asp.net, c#)\nDesignation : Developer.\nBack End : SQL Server 2000.\nRole : Developer\nTeam size : 4\nDescription:\nOnline Recruitment System is a web based Project which will deliver a new public website and an updated recruitment system. It will enable the Administrator and recruitment Consultant staff to process client, job and candidate data more efficiently.\nCONTRIBUTION\nAs a Software Developer, I was responsible for:\n\nAnalyzing and understanding the requirement of the system.\n\nCoding of candidate area.\n\nDevelopment of module Design.\nInvolved in the development of user Interface\nPROJECT : E-Shopping\nTechnical Skills Used : .NET (asp.net, c#)\nDesignation : Developer.\nBack End : SQL Server 2000.\nRole : Developer\nTeam size : 3\nDescription:\nThis project is based on the E-Shopping system for world Wide. An E-Shopping is a multifunctional integrated computer based system that allows many activities to be performed in an electronics mode.\nIt is done in the HTML, VB Script, Java Script, and Active Server Pages (ASP.NET), which is friendly with MS-SQL as database query language, which has also some important features in this Screenland Technology age. It compromises thirteen modules, user can search and retrieve any queries related to any of these modules.\nThe system is superior to the manual system in that it has speed, reliability, portability and flexibility, which has been fulfilled by our project.\nPROJECT : AIRCHORD ON-LINE AUDIO VIDEO (Working)\nTechnical Skills Used :.NET (asp.net, c#)\nDesignation :Developer.\nBack End : SQL Server 2000.\nRole : Developer\nTeam size : 3\nDescription:\nThis project is online audio video gallery in which any register user can upload own audio and video for shell or for free. User can also buy other\n?s audio or video and can add it to own favorites list and can also download it.\nPERSONAL DETAILS:\nDATE OF BIRTH : 2 April 1984\nNATIONALITY : Indian\nMARITAL STATUS : Single\nLANGUAGES KNOWN : English, Hindi\nDECLARATION:\nI hereby declare that the above written particulars are true to the best of my knowledge and belief.\nDate:\nPlace: (Yashwant Kumar)','SOFT TECH WORLD Pvt. Ltd ',1,NULL,'2007-10-18',NULL,'2007-10-18','2010-06-10 12:14:22','2010-06-10',2,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL);
INSERT INTO `tp_applicants` VALUES (250,'Vipul s',NULL,NULL,'Mumbai','Vipujhsjhjhrimjhali@yahoo.com',NULL,'91 22 28186875','0','9819777500','0',NULL,'0','2003-03-15',9,30,'2010-06-10 12:14:22',3,'0',NULL,'200710/18/ATT24636.html','200710/18/DOC16374.doc','Vipul Shrimali\nVipul S\n\n\n           \n303-A Kadamgiri, Near Dena Bank\nStation Road, Bhayandar (West),\nDist. Thane. Pin - 401101.\nMaharashtra\n\nIndia\n\n\n     \n   \nVipujh,lsjh,jhrimjh,ali@yahoo.com\n\n     \n\n\n     \n\n\n      \n   \n+91-22-28186875\n   \n+91-9819777500\n\n\nObjective\nI am seeking a challenging position with a company that is rapidly expanding and offers good potential. I would like a position with a strong emphasis on leading web-based projects.\n\n\nQualifications\nAcademic\n            \nDetails\n                                      \nClass\n                \nYear\n\n                \nBoard / University\nSSC\n                                         \nII\n                       \nMarch?94\n           \nMaharashtra\n Board\n            \nHSC\n     \n                                    \nII\n                       \nMarch?96\n           \nMaharashtra\n Board\n            \nCommerce Graduation \n               \nII\n                       \nApril?99\n             \nMumbai\nUniversity\n\nMBA in Information Management (MIM) from Welingkar Institute of Management and Research. (Semester-6)\n\nSoftware\nNIIT\n                                           \ne-Commerce course, Java\nOthers\n            \nQuality\n                                      \nCertification by Philip Crosby & Associates \n\n\nCareer Summary\n\nCurrently working as Project Leader with 3i Infotech Ltd. managing development team and coordinating with client for delivering unique web-based solutions for banking & insurance sector.\n\nWorked as Senior Software Engineer with Aurionpro Solutions Ltd. offering customized web-based solutions for banking and logistics industry from June 2005 to August 2006.\n\nWorked as Module Leader with OFS Software, a division of OFS Group involved in developing web-based applications and customized software packages for public & private sector clients from September 2000 to June 2005.\n\nSkill Sets\n           \n\nTechnical\nOperating Systems \nWindows NT 4.0 / 2000, Windows 9x / XP\nWeb Technologies\nASP.Net, C#, ASP, HTML, Java Script, XML\nDatabases\n          \nOracle 9i, SQL 2000\nDevelopment Tools\nDreamweaver MX, VB 6.0, Visual Studio.Net 2005\nDesigning Tools\nPhotoshop 7.0\nProjects\n\nProject Name\nE-Provisions\nClient\nICICI Prudential, Mumbai\nDuration\nJune 2007 to present\nPlatform/Technology\nWindows XP, ASP.Net, C#, Java Scripting\nTools\nVisual Studio .Net 2005\nBackend\nOracle 9i\nSummary\nAn extension to existing claims management system for Finance department. E-Provisions is designed to monitor and track the expenses budgeted and utilized by various departments within the organization on monthly basis.\nRole & Responsibilities\n\n          \nRequirement analysis\n\n          \nSystem design\n\n          \nProject execution\n\n          \nImplementation\n\n\nProject Name\nETravel - Online Travel Management System\nClient\nICICI Prudential, Mumbai\nDuration\nSep 2006 to June 2007\nPlatform/Technology\nWindows XP, ASP.Net, C#, Java Scripting\nTools\nVisual Studio .Net 2005\nBackend\nOracle 9i\nSummary\nA web based intranet/internet application to effectively manage corporate Travel requirements of the client. The system enables users to:\n1. Raise Travel Indents\n2. Approval as per defined Approval Matrix\n3. Booking by Travel desk\n4. Vendor (Travel desk) Reimbursement\n5. Employee Reimbursement\n6. Generate MIS reports\nRole & Responsibilities\n\n          \nRequirement analysis\n\n          \nSystem design\n\n          \nProject execution\n\n          \nImplementation\n\n\nProject Name\nDealer Pad (Phase II)\nClient\nHDFC Bank Ltd., Mumbai\nDuration\nMay 2006 to till date\nPlatform/Technology\nWindows 2000, ASP.Net, Java Scripting\nTools\nVisual Studio .Net 2003\nBackend\nSQL 2000\nSummary\nThe system is a tool for managing the Nostro Accounts (Accounts between two different banks) with Clearing Houses at Non-RBI locations. To maintain the consistency of the Nostro Accounts recorded in the System the Nostro Account entries are compared with another existing system, which helps in carrying out the reconciliation. \n\nThe exposure of HDFC bank to other banks are also recorded in the System and the transactions breaching the limit can also be identified.\nRole & Responsibilities\n\n          \nRequirement analysis\n\n          \nSystem design\n\n          \nProject execution\n\n          \nImplementation\n\n\nProject Name\nInsightz Explorer\nClient\nInsightz Explorer, \nBangalore\nDuration\nDecember 2005 to May 2006\nPlatform/Technology\nWindows 2000, ASP.Net, C#, Java Scripting\nTools\nVisual Studio .Net 2003\nBackend\nSQL 2000\nSummary\nA web portal where students and professionals can upload their research projects online. After registration, projects details can be uploaded along with project report and data sheet in .pdf format. Corporate in need of market data, can search projects across categories/ industries and download these projects by paying online. Student and portal are part of the revenue sharing model. Unique features of the system include Student scheduler and Push & Pull research.\nRole & Responsibilities\n\n          \nRequirement analysis\n\n          \nSystem design, development & implementation\n\n          \nInvolved in compiling SRS and User Requirement Specification\n\n\nProject Name\nIssue Management\nClient\nHDFC Bank Ltd., Mumbai\nDuration\nNovember 2005 to December 2005\nPlatform/Technology\nWindows 2000, ASP.Net, C#, Java Scripting\nTools\nVisual Studio .Net 2003\nBackend\nSQL 2000\nSummary\nAn intranet application to log, monitor, manage and analyze issues pertaining to systems implemented at HDFC Bank. The applications keeps a track of pending issues, alerts for long pending issues, lead time to resolve, analyzes types issues arising frequently. Dashboard is provided to view the project wise status of various issues at different stages.\nRole & Responsibilities\n\n          \nSystem design, development & implementation\n\n\nProject Name\nSupply Chain Management Solution\nClient\nBDP International, \nSingapore\nDuration\nSeptember 2005 to November 2005\nPlatform/Technology\nWindows 2000, ASP.Net, Java Scripting\nTools\nVisual Studio .Net 2003\nBackend\nSQL 2000\nSummary\nDevelopment of Order Management module (Cyber-ORDER) of an integrated supply chain solution which helps to manage the logistics of demand fulfillment seamlessly across all geographies and transport modes for a logistics organization.\nRole & Responsibilities\n\n          \nSystem design, development & implementation\n\n          \nInvolved in UAT\n\n\nProject Name\nCounterparty Registry\nClient\nHDFC Bank Ltd., Mumbai\nDuration\nJune 2005 to September 2005\nPlatform/Technology\nWindows 2000, HTML, DHTML, VB Scripting\nTools\nVisual Studio .Net 2003\nBackend\nSQL 2000\nSummary\nA unique system developed for HDFC Bank (Treasury operations) that serves as a centralized registry for all the Counterparties (Banks/ Financial Institutions) with respective dealers. The overall system integrates with other three independent systems of HDFC namely ITMS (Integrated Treasury Management System), PAN (Panorama), TT (Treasury Trader).\nRole & Responsibilities\n\n          \nRequirement analysis\n\n          \nSystem design, development & implementation\n\n          \nInvolved in preparing the SRS and User Requirement Specification\n\n\nProject Name\ne-Office\nClient\nOFS Group (In-house Project)\nDuration\nFebruary 2002 to May 2003\nPlatform/Technology\nWindows 2000, IIS 5, ASP, Java Scripting, DHTML, HTML\nTools\nDreamweaver 6.0/ MX, Photoshop 6\nBackend\nSQL 7.0\nSummary\nAn Intranet application for executives of a company to co-ordinate with other executives and update them on daily activities from any location. This system is applicable to any organization having offices at different locations as well as for executives traveling for business activities.\nRole & Responsibilities\n\n          \nSystem design, development & implementation\n\n\nProject Name\nWebsite development for OFS Group ? ofsindia.com\nClient\nOFS Group (In-house Project)\nDuration\nOctober 2000 to January 2001\nPlatform/Technology\nWindows 2000, ASP, VB Scripting, Java Scripting\nTools\nDreamweaver 6.0/ MX, Photoshop 6\nBackend\nMS Access\nSummary\nA corporate & informative website designed & developed for OFS Group. The website provides features such as ? Easy navigation, Feedback form, Downloadable Product/Service Brochures in .pdf format.\nRole & Responsibilities \n\n          \nSystem design, development, implementation, search engine optimization and hosting of web site\n\n\nProject Name\nWeb site development for \nMaharashtra\n Maritime Board ? mmbmumbai.com\nClient\nMaharashtra Maritime Board (MMB), Mumbai - \nMaharashtra\nState\n Government\nDuration\nOctober 2004 to March 2005\nPlatform/Technology\nWindows 2000, ASP, VB Scripting, Java Scripting\nTools\nDreamweaver 6.0/ MX, Photoshop 7.0\nBackend\nSQL 2000\nSummary\nAn informative web site for MMB giving organizational details. An important part of the project is a ?Tender Management Module? wherein an authenticated user may post, edit or delete tenders online. The tenders may be in Text/ Image format.\nRole & Responsibilities\n\n          \nRequirement analysis\n\n          \nSystem design, development & implementation\n\n          \nInvolved in preparing the SRS and User Requirement Specification\n\n          \nInvolved in UAT and support\n\n\nProject Name\nPay bill and Pay Slip generation.\nClient\nMercantile Marine Department (MMD), Mumbai under Ministry of Surface Transport, Government of \nIndia\n\nDuration\nNovember 2001 to June 2002\nPlatform/Technology\nNT4.0, VB6.0\nBackend\nSQL 7.0\nSummary\nA user friendly, graphical user interface integrated software application to generate and effectively enable processing of all personal claims and bills regarding Pay & Allowances, salary details. Generating multilingual enclosures and reports.\nRole & Responsibilities\n\n          \nRequirement analysis\n\n          \nSystem design, development & implementation\n\n         \nInvolved in preparing the SRS and User Requirement Specification\n\n\nProject Name\nExam Booking.\nClient\nMercantile Marine Department (MMD), Mumbai.\nDuration\nJuly 2002 to December 2002\nPlatform/Technology\nNT4.0, VB6.0\nBackend\nSQL 7.0\nSummary\nCandidates joining the navy need to appear for certain MMD exams, seats for which have to be booked by paying fees. A fee collection application, which is integrated with Syndicate Bank where the fee is collected for exams, certificates and upgradation. The application calculates and enters the amount of fees to be collected as per the exam or certificate. A unique ?Backup & Restore? facility is provided to update the records from the Bank to MMD?s Exam Centre.\nRole & Responsibilities\n\n          \nRequirement analysis\n\n          \nSystem design, development & implementation\n\n          \nInvolved in UAT and support\n\n\nPersonal Details\nName: \n                          \nVipul Shrimali\nDate of Birth: \n                \n15\nth\n November 1978.\nMarital Status: \n              \nMarried\nLanguages Known:\n       \n\nEnglish, Hindi, Gujarati, Marathi.\nEmail Address:\n              \nvipulshrimali@yahoo.com','3i Infotech Ltd',1,NULL,'2007-10-18',NULL,'2007-10-18','2010-06-10 12:14:22','2010-06-10',3,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(251,'Shailendra D',NULL,NULL,'New Delhi','Dewgwegfgeivedi.shargrgilendra@gmail.com',NULL,NULL,'0','9899655215','0',NULL,'0','2008-04-13',8,23,'2010-06-10 12:14:22',2,'0',NULL,'200710/18/ATT24638.html','200710/18/DOC16375.doc','Resume\nShailendra D\nEMAIL: \nDewgwegfgeivedi.shargrgilendra\n@gmail.com\nCONTACT NO:\n9899655215\n\n\nOBJECTIVE\n\nTo work in an environment that provides me a challenging job, encourages me & helps me to build my career as well as to give my best to the organization.\nEDUCATION\n\nMaster of Computer Application\n with 68%\n2002 - 2005\n       \nNice \nManagement\nCollege\n\nMeerut\n, Uttar Pradesh.\nBachelor Of Science (PCM)\n with 68%\n1999 -2001\n      \nBrahamma\nNand\nDegree\nCollege\n\nKanpur\n\nIntermediate (PCM) \nwith 62% in 1998 from U.P. Board.\nHigh School\n   \nwith 63%\n   \nin 1996 U.P. Board.\nEXPERIENCE\n\nCurrently working with A1 Technology as Software Developer for last 6 months on .Net Technology (Asp.Net with C# & Sqlserver2000). \n\nWorking experience with Nucleus Microsystems P. Ltd. is 1.9 years as Software Developer on .Net Technology (Asp.net with Vb.net & Sqlserver2000).\n6 months of IT experience as a Trainee Programmer in I.I.T. Kanpur.\nSKILLS ACQUIRED\nOS\nWindows 2003, Windows 2000\nLanguages\nVb.net, C#.net.\nDatabase\nMS-Access, SQL Server 2000, SQL Server 2005,MSDE\nIDE\nAsp.net 1.1, 2.0 \nReporting Tool\nHTML Report\nTechnologies\nADO\n. Net, XML\nScript Languages\nJava Script, VB Script\n\nPROJECTS\n\n\n1.\n       \nProfessional Social Networking\n\nhttp://68.178.200.90:4020/business/Index.aspx\n\n\nThis site is currently under construction. It?s a social networking site. It contains all the basic features like (profile management, friends interactions, photos and video sharing, notes, groups management, messages,\n\nEvent Management, account management etc). User can maintain their diary, News. We have also implemented CMS (Content management system) wherever it?s needed. This site contains most of the functionality of www.orkut.com. www.facebook.com. \n                             \n                                                \nTitle\n                                        \nProfessional Social Networking\n                                                \n                                                \nRole\n                                                        \nCoding\n   \n& Analysis\n                                                \nOrganization\n                                     \n    \nA1 Technology P. Ltd. (Gurgaon)\n                                                \nClient\n                                                  \n    \nCountless Business\n                                                \nTeam Size\n                                          \n    \n\n                                                \nUsed Technology & Language\n     \n    \nAsp.Net with C# and SQL Server 2000, JavaScript\n\n2.\n       \nFanPage TimeOut (\nhttp://fanpage.com/folder2/frmlogin.aspx\n\n\nThis site is currently under construction. It?s a gamming site. In this we can create Teams, Players .and Rivals of teams. we can give the ranking to teams , players and rivals according to your choice of teams , players and rivals\n\n                                                                                 \nTitle\n                                        \nFanPage TimeOut\n                                                \n                                                \nRole\n                                                        \nCoding & Analysis\n                                                \nOrganization\n                                         \nA1 Technology P. Ltd. (Gurgaon)\n                                                \nClient\n                                                      \nSalman Ebrahin\n                                                \nTeam Size\n                                              \n\n                                                \nUsed Technology & Language\n         \nAsp.Net with C# and SQL Server 2005, JavaScript\n\n\n3.\n\nLuchHourSale\n\nwww.lunchhoursale.com\n\n\nIt?s an e-commerce site were the user can purchase one item in a speculated time. Which displays the product for a particular time? With in speculated time you have to place an order for that particular product. If either of the limits is over (time or product) accordingly the status is displayed. It also displays the next product to be sold. Apart from that this site is having the feature of Free Day where all remaining items are available for sale.\n\nAll the basic securities are implemented.\n\n                        \n            \nTitle\n                                      \n    \n            \nLunchHourSale\n.com\n                                \n                \nRole\n                        \n                  \n\n     \n        \nCoding, \nDesigning\n                                \n              \nOrganization \n        \n\n          \n      \nNucleus Microsystems P. Ltd., \nNew Delhi\n                                                \nClient\n                                      \n          \n      \nAkiva Tauber\n                                \n                \nTeam Size\n                              \n          \n      \n\n                                \n                \nUsed Technology & Language\n         \nAsp.Net with C# and SQL Server 2000, JavaScript\n4. Payroll Management System (PMS), \nNew Delhi\n\nThe objective is to design and develop a Time Attendance & Payroll Management System, which will be used by companies. HR personal for different activities like making presents, absent, sanctioning leave, maintaining Holidays of the employees of a company.\n            \n    \n            \n            \n            \nTitle\n    \n                                    \nPayroll Management System (PMS)\n            \n                        \nRole\n                         \n    \n         \n   \n\nCoding, Designing \n            \n            \n            \nOrganization \n                             \nNucleus Microsystems P. Ltd., \nNew Delhi\n                        \n            \nClient\n                                        \nHID-Bangalore & Tricolite ? Sahibad\n            \n                        \nTeam Size\n                     \n            \n\nUsed Technology & Language\n       \nAsp.Net with Vb.net and SQL Server 2000, \n\navaScript\n\n5.\n       \nTime Attendance Mgmt System\n\nThis is a complete attendance software. Basically this\n\nsoftware\n\nis used to provide the automation of the attendance system .This software can be linked to various kind of Biometric devices through the IP or the serial port.This is a complete web application by which one can easily access the software\n\nanywhere from the world.\n   \n\nTitle\n                                        \nTime Attendance Mgmt System\n            \n                        \nRole\n                         \n    \n             \nCoding, Designing \n                                    \nOrganization \n                             \nNucleus Microsystems P. Ltd., \nNew Delhi\n                                    \nClient\n                                        \nTricolite- Sahibabad\n                                    \nTeam Size\n                     \n            \n\nUsed Technology & Language\n       \nAsp.Net with Vb.net and SQL Server 2000, \n\navaScript\n\n\n6.\n\nOnline Banking Transaction Management System\n\nThis is Transaction Management software. Basically this software is used for manage the money transaction. With the help of this software we can remove the maximum manual work of any bank and provide the maximum facilities of end users.\n          \n\n\n            \n            \n            \nTitle\n                            \n          \nOnline Banking Transaction Management System\n            \n            \n            \nRole \n                \n            \n        \n\n\nCoding & Designing\n            \n            \n            \nOrganization \n                 \n          \nI.I.T. Kanpur\n            \n            \n            \nTeam Size\n                     \n         \n\n            \n            \n            \nClient\n                            \n     \n     \nin House\n            \n            \n            \nUsed Technology & Language\n     \nAsp.Net with Vb.net and SQL Server 2000\n\nPERSONAL DETAILS:\n\n                        \n            \nFather?s Name\n\n            \n           \nLate Santosh Kumar Dwivedi\n      \n            \n            \n            \nData of Birth \n\n\n           \n           \n22 March 1982\n            \n            \n            \nAddress\n                        \n           \nRoad No. 4, Building No.-7, Flat No.- 5, MahipalPur, \n                   \n                                                \n           \nNew Delhi\n            \n            \n            \nHobbies\n                       \n          \nSinging, Listening to Music\n\n\nSIGNIFICANT STRENGTHS\n\nSelf-motivation, proactive, willingness and confidence to take on new responsibilities.\n\n\n\nI hereby declare that the information given above is mentioned true and correct to the best of my knowledge and belief.\n   \n    \n                                                                                            \n   \n\n\n\n    \nShailendra Dwivedi\n                                                                                    \n                   \n\n\n       \n\nSignature\n                   \n          \n                             \n                                                                              ','A1 Technology',1,NULL,'2007-10-18',NULL,'2007-10-18','2010-06-10 12:14:22','2010-06-10',2,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(252,'S Trivedi',NULL,NULL,NULL,'sandfbkfbdfbet.trifbvedi@gmail.com',NULL,NULL,'0','09990574891','0',NULL,'0','2010-01-27',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-10 12:14:22',3,'0',NULL,'200710/18/ATT24639.html','200710/18/DOC16376.doc','Miss\n\n\nS TRIVEDI\n        \n                \n                                    \nTel: 09990574891\nE-mail: \nsandfbkfbdfbet.trifbvedi@gmail.com\n\n\n\nJob Objective: Seeking assignments in Asp.Net, C#.Net and Vb.Net in IT industry with a Growth oriented organization.\n\nWork Experience \n\n          \nCurrently I am working in \nOpelin Laboratories Pvt. Ltd\n\nGurgaon\n As a Software Engineer, Since July 2007. \n\nProfessional Synopsis\n\n          \nM.C.A from \nNSVKMS\nMCA\nCollege\n\nGujarat\n in 2005 securing 69%.\n\n          \nCIC form IGNOU with Distinction.\n\nStrengths\n\n       \nUnderstanding of SDLC \n\n       \nProven strength in problem solving, coordination and analysis\n\n       \nStrong communication, interpersonal, learning and organizing skills matched with the ability to manage stress and time effectively\n\nSkill Set\n\nTechnical\nMicrosoft Technologies\n\n\nASP.NET 2.0, C#.NET\n, ADO.NET, VB.NET\n             \nWeb Technologies \n   \n   \n: ASP.Net, HTML, JavaScript, VBScript\nDatabase \n                 \n   \n\nSQL Server 2000\n, MS-Access, Oracle\nWeb / App Server\n     \n   \n\nIIS 5.0\nIDEs /Tools\n               \n   \n\nVisual Studio.Net 2005\n, Visual Basic 6.0,VSS\nOS\n                                \n: Window 2000/XP, Linux\n\nKnowledge Domain\n\n          \nClient interaction for system study, requirements gathering and analysis.\n\n          \nDesigning, Developing and Coding\n\n          \nDebugging and troubleshoot the application.\n\n          \nManaging smooth implementation and testing of the application at client location.\n\n          \nExtending post go-live and application maintenance support to the client.\n\n\nEducational Credentials\nMaster in Computer Application (MCA)\n , From 2002 to 2005 securing 69%.\nNorth\nGujarat\nUniversity\n, Gujarat - \nIndia\n\nBachelor of Computer Application (BCA),\n From 1999 to 2002 securing 59%. \nNorth\nGujarat\nUniversity\n\nGujarat\n\nIndia\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nEducational Credentials\nReliance\nData\nCenter\n                         \n   \nDuration:\n\nJuly 2007 to till date\n                                                     \n   \nTools and Technologies:\n\nASP.Net 2.0, C#, SQL Server\nProject Brief :\nReliance\nData\nCenter\n is Web based application. In that application Reliance employess and its Customers can uploads files and uploaded files can download from anywhere. That application can handle by Administrator, \nEnterprise\n Customers & its users depend on the given permission. That application is\n\nGlobalization.\nResponsibilities: \n\n          \nInvolved in coding and problem solving\n\n          \nInvolved in development of Business logic\n\n          \nInvolved in database operations\n\n\nPay Roll System\n                                 \n   \nDuration:\n\nMar 2006 to June 2007\n                                                            \n   \nTools and Technologies:\n\nASP.Net 2.0, C#, SQL Server\nProject Brief :\n Pay Roll System is Intranet Web based application .This system automates almost all payroll task for particular organization. It includes muster creation, leave module, loan module, payroll generation, promotion module etc. The main feature of this system is that it includes all the details of the Employees.\nResponsibilities: \n\n          \nAnalyzing / Understanding the specifications Requirement\n\n          \nInvolved in development of Business logic\n\n\nEmployee Tracking and Scheduling System\nDuration:\n\nJune 2005 to Fabruary-2006\n                                        \n   \nTools and Technologies:\n\nVB.Net, Oracle, WinForm\nProject Brief :\n\nEmployee Tracking and Scheduling System is WinForm based application. The application is operated by System Manager. In this System manager can get readymade information to decide about the placement of the manager and where it is require most. This will be useful in human resources development and the mobility of the personnel of the company at central point for effective utilization of manpower.\n     \nResponsibilities: \n\n          \nAnalyzing / Understanding the specifications Requirement\n\n          \nInvolved in coding and problem solving\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nNetwork Intrusion Detection System (NIDS)\nDuration:\n\nJan 2005 to May-2005\n                                      \nTools and Technologies:\n\nC#, SQL Server, WinForm\nProject Brief:\n\nThe project entitled ?Network Intrusion Detection System? is an IDS where it monitors packets on the network wire and attempts to the discovery of hacker/cracker who is attempting to break into system. This discovery is being performed by comparing the captured packet with the intruder details stored in the database .If the packet is found to be an intruder it is then forwarded to the firewall with the respective message for blocking. \nResponsibilities: \n\n          \nInvolved in database operations\n\n          \nInvolved in coding and problem solving\n\n\nDate of Birth\n\n\n16\nth\n May 1981\n\n\nContact Details: \n#7 Laxminagar, Rajiv Chok, Gurgaon.',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-18',NULL,'2007-10-18','2010-06-10 12:14:22','2010-06-10',3,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(253,'Vivek sharma',NULL,NULL,'Delhi','viewfewfvs_200efwef5@yahoo.com','vivs_2005@yahoo.com',NULL,'0','09818966130','0',NULL,'0','2008-02-12',8,25,'2010-06-10 12:14:22',2,'0',NULL,'200710/18/ATT24643.html','200710/18/DOC16377.doc','Resdex @ naukri.com\nVivek Sharma\nAshok Nagar New Delhi - 110096 \nviewfewfvs_200efwef5@yahoo.com\n\nTelephone: 09818966130\n(M)\n\n(R)\n\nD.O.B\n - 19 Jul 1980 \nModified on\n - 26 Sep 2007 \nAnnual Salary\n - INR 1 Lac(s) 10 Thousand \nTotal Years of Experience\n - 2 Year(s) 2 Month(s) \nCurrent Location\n - Delhi \nPreferred Location\n - No preference \nMCA,MCSD(Microsoft Certified Solution Developer, SQL,Dotnet) Experienced professional for dotnet. Assignment in Software Development.\n\nTEXT RESUME \n\nVIVEK KUMAR SHARMA\nPh : 09818966130\nA 388, Ashok Nagar, New Delhi-96\nEmail : vivs_2005@yahoo.com, vr_net2000@yahoo.com\nTITLE\nSKILLS\nMICROSOFT CERTIFIED PROFESSIONAL ( MCP)\n( .NET , SQL SERVER )\nASP.NET, C#, VB.NET, SQL\nEXPERIENCE\n26 MONTHS\nCURRENT\nORGANIZATION\nRENSOFT TECHNOLOGIES\n\nDELHI\nSERVICE INDUSTRY\nIT/COMPUTERS : SOFTWARE DEVELOPMENT\nHIGHEST DEGREE\nHELD\nMCA ? 1st Division ( 65 % )\nUP \nTECHNICAL\nUNIVERSITY\n\nLUCKNOW\n\nWORK EXPERIENCE\nPresent Organization : Rensoft Technologies, South Ex 2, New Delhi\nDuration : November 2006 - till Date\nRole : Team member\nTeam size : 1\nWork location : New Delhi, India\nPrevious Organization: GetIT Infomediary Ltd, ITO, New Delhi\nRole : Team member\nTeam size : 6\nWork location : ITO New Delhi, India\nPROJECTS\nONEMYC\nThis project is a community site. This project has various sections like Audio, Video, Photography, Browse, Literature, Blog etc. It provides various facilities like listening\nand downloading various songs. Similarly you can view video clips. One can upload photos\nor make its own album and then upload Photos in that Album, thus making a Photo Album. This site gives the facility to view profiles of various persons, who are having their profiles on the site,\nThus inviting them to make friends or sending them message.\nOperating System: Windows XP\nDatabase SQL\nTechnology : ASP.Net, C#\nSUPER POWER MUSIC\nThis project is related to music, images and Albums. This project is\ndivided into three layers - Data Access layer, Common Helper class and\nMain Project (User Interface). Users can listen to the music, download\ntheir favorite music, rate the Music.Similarily Users can view the\nPhotos download their favorite Photos. Artists can upload their music which\ncan be listened by Users. Music can be searched by selecting the Artist,\nOr any favorite music like Rock-Pop,Jazz,Hip-Hop etc. artists and\nUsers have to be registered to upload pr download music or images\nOperating System: Windows XP\nDatabase SQL\nTechnology : ASP.Net, C#\nSHOPPING CART\nCurrently working on Shopping Cart. It is a project which deals with Online buying and selling of Products. This project is divided into 3 parts: Vendor, Customer and Administrator. Customer has the facility to go through various Categories, Sub-Categories and Products. If the Customer has to buy a Product It is necessary for the Customer to be registered. If the Customer Logs in , he can add the product to the cart and then view the selected products. if he is confirm with the selected Products, he can order those product. Similarly Information will be stored about Vendors, Product they will be supplying, charges for the Products, handling Charges etc. Administrator will be handling only the Master Pages, like Adding Updating ? Vendors, Categories for Products, Products, Location Master, VendorLocation, Currency, Role etc.\nOperating System: Windows XP\nDatabase : MS SQL\nTechnology : ASP.Net, C#\nDIGIWAX\nThis Program is divided into three parts - Data Access layer, Common Helper and main Project (User Interface).This project is related to music, images and Albums.This project includes Artists, User and Administrator.Artist can register and upon their registration can upload their music files. Alternatively there can be uploading through Administrator also, who has been given the facility of Power Uploading. User can listen to the music, download their music and rate the music\nOperating System: Windows XP\nDatabase : SQL\nTechnology : ASP.Net, C#\nJOBS MIRACLE\n. It provides an end-to-end web-based automatic solution for job hunting candidates in searching their desired jobs as well as for the employers to post their vacancies and search respective candidates.\nThis Project is divided into three modules ? Applicant, Employer and Administration.\nThe Applicant is allowed to search jobs according to his qualification, experience and skills, also facilitating to post and update the resume.\nThe Employer will get a unique registration in order to post his job vacansies. The Employer is allowed to search Applicant?s resume according to his qualification, skills and experience.\nThe Administration will be doing the Employee registration and updates of Master tables.\nRESPONSIBILITIES PERFORMED\nDeveloped Master forms for Master tables.\nDeveloped Customize Email\nDeveloped Login Form\nOperating System: Windows 2000 server\nDatabase : SQL\nMOBILE APPLICATION - IQ7070\nMobile Application IQ7070 for MTNL?s Trump. It includes facilities like sms for logo, Ringtones, Astrology, Cricket score etc.\nApplication for Cricket score worked on the recent triseries between \nIndia\n, SriLanka and WestIndies (2005-06). Through this Application, the service provider company continuously gives live updates of the match while the match is in progress. At the end of the match the application provide final scores as well as result of the match.\nThis is a flexible application, which can be also modified for the future cricket series comprising any number of teams and countries.\nIn the ringtone Application there are various ringtones in the centralized database with a unique code. The application provides the ringtone either on the basis of the code given by the user or by selecting such a code that it has not been sent to that particular mobile earlier (the later option used as an ad).\nSALES FORCE MANAGEMENT APPLICATION\nThis application was developed to track the activities of Sales Person, Sales Manager etc of a respective department.\nThis project was divided into 3 parts ? Admin, Customer and Users.\nVarious forms developed are :\nShowAssignIssueAllExecutive\nShowActivitiesAllExecutives\nSearchIssueAssign\nActivityInsert\nActivityShow\nSalesManagerActivityShow\nSalesManagerSearchIssueAssign\nSalesManagerShowIssueAssign\nReportToManager\nAREAS OF INTEREST\n? Web Development\n? Programming\n? Spiritual Reading\nPersonal Profile\nFather\'s Name Mr. Harendra Prasad Sharma\nPhone number\n09818966130\nCurrent Address Ashok Nagar, New Delhi-96\nPermanent Address Ghaziabad (U.P.) PIN-245101\nDate of Birth 19 july, 1980\nSex Male\nMarital status Single\nLanguage Known English, Hindi\nI hereby declare that above information are true to best of my knowledge.\nDate: -\nPlace: - \nDelhi\n VIVEK KUMAR SHARMA','RENSOFT TECHNOLOGIES',1,NULL,'2007-10-18',NULL,'2007-10-18','2010-06-10 12:14:22','2010-06-10',2,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(254,'Veeraswamy',NULL,NULL,NULL,'veerdfsgsdfgaswrfhrfamy59@gmail.com',NULL,'91 99 40 58','0',NULL,'0',NULL,'0','2008-04-29',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-10 12:14:22',3,'0',NULL,'200710/18/ATT24642.html','200710/18/DOC16378.doc','Dale F\nVEERASWAMY\nMobile\n: +91-99 40 58 25 47\nEmail:veerdfsgsdfgaswrfhrfamy59@gmail.com\n\n\n\nOBJECTIVE\n\nPosition requiring innovative and challenging employment that will utilize my education and professional skills in the field of Information Technology as a Software Engineer.\nSUMMARY\n\n       \n2+ years\n of Experience in development of software applications using Microsoft technologies. \n\nSTRENGTHS\n\n\n       \nExtensively worked in \nASP.NET, C#. NET and\n\nADO.NET \n\n       \nExtensively worked in \nMS SQL Server 2000\n\n\n       \nKnowledge on \nWeb Services\n\n       \nExcellent analytical and programming skills and proactive problem ? solving approach.\n\n       \nGood communication skills along with patience, perseverance and flexibility adds to my problem solving capabilities\n\n       \nGood Software skills with qualified technical education and background.\n\nACADEMIC QUALIFICATION\n\n       \nB.Tech\n from \nJ.N.T.U\n with aggregate of \n68%,\nHyderabad\n, Andhra Pradesh \n\n       \nMPC\n from \nChaithanya\n\nBharathi\n with aggregate of \n78%\n,Suryapet Andhra Pradesh\n\n       \nSSC\n from \nA.V.M\nHigh School\n with \nAggrigate\n of \n88%\n\nNakrekal\n\nAndhraPradesh\n\nWORK PROFILE\n\n\n       \nPresently working as a \nSoftware Engineer \nin \nISoft\n\n Chennai (Sep 2006-Till Date). \n\n\n       \nWorked as a \nProgrammer \nin\n\nIVision\n Solutions Ltd.,\nHyderabad\n (Sep 2005-Aug2006)\n\n\nTECHNICAL SKILLS\n\n.NET Technologies\nASP.NET , C#.NET and ADO.NET\nDatabase\nMS-SQL Server\n\nProgramming Languages\nC, C++\nOperating Systems\nMS Windows NT/2000/XP/2003\nWeb server\nIIS 5.0\n\n\nPROFESSIONAL EXPERIENCE\n\n\n\nPROJECT PROFILE # \n1 :\n\nTitle\n                 \n\n\n\ne-Logistics\n                                                                        \n          \nClient\n               \n\n\n\nKWE\n\nUSA\nEnvironment\n    \n: C#\n.NET, ASP.NET, SQL Server 2000 and \nWindows 2003 Server\nTeam Size\n       \n: 3\nRole\n                 \n: Team Member\n\nDescription\n\nThis business process makes it possible for to deliver a specific product /Item and quantity, or to provide a service at a specific time. During Shipment order processing, a sales organization accepts the order and is responsible for fulfilling the \norder.Cusotomers\n can order the required items at their end itself through KWE portal login provided to them.\n Warehouse business process makes it possible for you to support all goods movements and in managing stock in the warehouse complex. The system shall support scheduled and efficient processing of all logistics processes within the warehouse.\n\nShipping as the central object of the goods issue process, the outbound delivery supports all shipping activities including picking, packing, transportation and goods issue. \n\n\nResponsibilities:\n\n       \nDesigning and Development \n\n       \nUnit Testing\n\n\nPROJECT PROFILE # 2\n\nTitle\n                 \n\n\nCommercial Business Unit \nClient\n               \n\n\nNHT, \nIndia\n\nEnvironment\n    \n: C#\n.NET, ASP.NET and SQL Server 2000\n\nTeam Size\n       \n\n\n\nRole\n                 \n: Team Member\n\nDescription\n            \nNew \nHolland\n Tractors ? \nIndia\n, here after referred to as NHT is involved in the manufacturing \nand sales of tractors. It is selling their tractors through a Dealership network and their sales \nteam manages this network where the frontline representative is called the Commercial \n           \nBusiness Unit or CBU. Scope of the project is to automate this sales process, taking into \n            \naccounts the business processes accomplished by the CBU and the Dealers. This Project is \n         \ndeveloped in latest web-based technology \nASP.NET \nusing \nC# \nhaving SQL-Server 2000 as \n      \nback-end on Windows 2003 Server.\n\nResponsibilities:\n\n       \nDesigning and Development \n\n       \nUnit Testing\n\n\n\nPROJECT PROFILE #\n\n\nTitle\n                 \n\n\n\nAREA COUNSELLOR (AC) & SCHOOL\n\nClient\n               \n\n\n\nNagase Corporation, \nJapan\nEnvironment\n    \n: C#\n.NET, ASP.NET and SQL Server 2000 \nTeam Size\n       \n: 5\nRole\n                 \n: Team Member\n\n\nDescription\n\n            \nThis project consists of three modules i.e. NHQ, \nAreaCounsellor\n and School. NHQ module helps Nagase Head Quarter users to see all the performance statistics of all schools operated by Nagase as well as the performance of individual students belongs to the schools. This is purely a statistical tool i.e. the logged in user can only view the statistics and it?s not possible for the user to update anything using this application. In Same way \nAreacounsellor\n applications is also useful for viewing the statistics of all schools as well as the students belongs those schools under the direct control of the particular user. School application is also just like a statistical tool and this application is also useful to register the courses for the students and give permissions for the students to give tests against the respected courses \n\nResponsibilities\n\n      \nGUI design and Development.\n\n\n\nPROJECT PROFILE #4\n\n\nTitle\n                 \n\n\nNAGASE EMPLOYEE MANAGEMENT SYSTEM \n\nClient\n               \n\n Nagase Corporation, \nJapan\nEnvironment\n    \n: C#\n.NET, ASP.NET and SQL Server 2000\nTeam Size\n       \n: 5 \nRole\n                 \n: Team Member\n\n\n\nDescription\n\nThe Nagase Employee Management System will consist of Two Modules: HS Coach and FS Coach. This system will be useful to manage employee / coach master maintenance for both High Schools (HS) Franchise Schools (FS).The roles of every employee in this application will be managed through Active Directory structure.\n\nIt is built under the umbrella of ?Single Sign On?. The user interface has multilingual support. The product will be launched in English and Japanese language\n\nResponsibilities:\n\n      \nGUI design and Development.',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-18',NULL,'2007-10-18','2010-06-10 12:14:22','2010-06-10',3,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(255,'Narasimha',NULL,NULL,NULL,'murtfefefhymnefwef_2000@yahoo.com',NULL,'98866 72639','0','91 98866 72639','0',NULL,'0','2006-04-29',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-10 12:14:22',15,'0',NULL,'200710/18/ATT4896.html','200710/18/DOC16379.doc','Business Analyst\nNarasimha \n\n - +91 98866 72639\nEmail: \nmurtfefefhymnefwef_2000@yahoo.com\n\n                                    \n            \n        \n    \n\nSummary\n\n4+ Years\n of Experience in \nRisk Management/ IT / Training Experience\n\n         \nImplementation of Asset and Liability Management \n\nApplication(Oracle Risk Manager)\n\n         \nImplementation of Funds Transfer Pricing Application(Oracle Transfer Pricing)\n\n         \nKnowledge of Wallstreet Treasury(Formerly TremaOne)\n\n         \nExposure to Investment Banking\n\n         \nMortgage Backed Securities ? Bond Calculations and Processing \n\n\n         \nKnowledge of Value at Risk, Shortfall at Risk BackTesting, Interest Rate Models and Analysis of Bonds\n\n         \nPerformed User Acceptance Testing\n\n         \nCo-ordination with Development Team and End Users\n\nEducation \n\nMaster of Science (Mathematics and Computing)\nUniversity\n of \nHyderabad\n\n\nWork Experience Summary\n\nWorking as \nBusiness Analyst\n with \nHCL Technologies Ltd\n\nBangalore\n (From June 2006 to Till Date)\n\nWorked as \nFinancial Analyst\n for Corporate Trust and Agency Services, Deutsche Bank with \nHCL Technologies Ltd\n., \nBangalore\n (From Aug 2005 to May 2006)\n\nWorked as \nSoftware Engineer\n for Financial Engineering Group with \nHCL Technologies Ltd\n., \nBangalore\n (From Feb 2005 to Aug 2005)\n\nWorked as \nAssistant Professor\n in Mathematics with Scient Institute of Technology (From Jul 2002 to Jan 2005)\n\n\nAreas of Interest\n\nEnterprise\n Risk Management,\n   \nHedge Funds\n\n\n\n\nTools/Applications\n\nOFSA ? Oracle financial Services Applications\n viz\nOracle Risk Manager\nOracle Transfer Pricing\nOracle Rate Manager\nOracle Balance and Control Oracle FDM Administration\n\nTremaOne\nExcel \nPL/SQL \nQuIC Script\n\nMATLAB\n\n\n\n\n\nClients\nDeutsche Bank\n\nSmall Industries Development Bank of \nIndia\n\nWallstreet Systems\n\nMoody?s Corporation\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nRole(s) \nBusiness Analyst\nCompany\nHCL Technologies Limited\nLocation\nBangalore\nDuration\nJanuary 2007 to till Date\nAreas :\n Cash Management , Risk Management, Treasury Management\n\nTasks/Functions :\n\n\n          \nProviding Business Intelligence to Developer?s for development of Interfaces used for uploading Statement files with various File formats (BAI2).\n\n          \nCoordinating the Development and Functional Testing\n\n          \nTraining the Development team on generation of different types of Pay methods using TremaOne Application \n\nClient :\n Moody?s Corporation\n\n\n          \nUp gradation of Documentation of all Modules viz. Cash Management, Deal Management, Risk Management from Version 2.XX.XXX to 3.XX.XXX.\n\nClient : \nWallstreet Systems\nKnowledge of TremaOne\n\n          \nSetup of User profiles, Access Rights , Configure Authorization/Verification\n\n          \nDecide on Static data structure\n\n          \nSetup System wide defaults\n\n          \nSetup of Interest Rate Curves / Currencies/ Forecast Periods\n\n          \nElectronic/Manual Reconciliation\n\n          \nCreate, amend and verify deals, Setup of default instructions \n\n\n     \n   \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nRole(s) \nAssociate Business Analyst\nCompany\nHCL Technologies Limited\nLocation\nBangalore\n, Mumbai \nDuration\nJune 2006 to December 2006\nAreas :\n Asset and Liability Management, Risk Management, Transfer Pricing \n\nTasks/Functions :\n\n\n          \nProviding Business Intelligence to Developer?s for Database level Mapping from Legacy System to Oracle Financial Data Manager\n\n          \nSetup of ID?s in the Oracle Risk Manager for various specific calculations like Value at Risk, Earnings at Risk and Market Value \n\n          \nSetup of Transfer Pricing Method to the Individual Products depending on the Characteristics of type of Product\n\n          \nSetup of Interest Rate Curves / Yield Curves/ Transfer Pricing Curves\n\n          \nProduct Modeling/Processing of various Instruments in the Bank?s Portfolio\n\n          \nSetup of Users, provide access rights depending on the\n\n, Configure Authorization/Verification\n\n\n          \nPerformed UAT for Various Products after the Data being completely migrated from Legacy System to Oracle Financial Data Manager.\n\nClient : \nSmall Industries Development Bank of \nIndia\n\nMumbai\n\nIndia\nRole(s) \nFinancial Analyst \nCompany\nHCL Technologies\nLocation\nBangalore\n\nIndia\nDuration\nAugust 2005\n\nto May 2006\n\nAreas : \nMortgage Backed Securities\n\nTasks/Functions :\n\n\n          \nBond Calculation and Reporting of Mortgage Backed Securities\n\n\n          \nProvide support and maintenance of existing Cash Flow Model Applications\n\n\n          \nReporting the Loss Information on the Mortgage Backed Securities\n\n\n\n          \nProviding Manual and Electronic Data Input\n\n\n          \nValidation of Financial Model output through Statistical Analysis \n\nClient : \nCorporate Trust and Agency Services,\n\nDeutsche Bank, \nSanta Ana\n\nUSA\n\n\n\nRole(s) \nSoftware Engineer \nCompany\nHCL Technologies\nLocation\nBangalore\n\nIndia\nDuration\nFebruary 2005\n\nto August 2005\n\nAreas : \nDerivatives, Risk Analysis\n\nTasks/Functions :\n\n\n          \nStochastic Volatility Model for Equity \n\n\n          \nValue at Risk, Shortfall at Risk \n\n\n          \nBackTesting of Value at Risk \n\n\n\n          \nMonte Carlo\n Simulation \n\n\n  \nall the above were Coded and Designed in QuIC Script \n\nClient : \nProof of Concepts done for the Partner Company Quadrus Technologies, \nVancouver\n\nCanada\n\n\n\n\nPersonal Details\nName\nNarasimha Murthy. M\nFather?s Name\nJangaiah.M\nDate of Birth\n24-Apr-1979\nMarital Status \nSingle\nPassport No\nF2741773\nVisa Details\nHolding B1 ? Business Visa (USA) valid till 2017\nAddress\nNarasimha Murthy. M\nH.No.24-33/1,\nVishnupuri Colony,\nMalkajgiri,\nHyderabad ? 500 047\nPhone No : +91 98866 72639',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-18',NULL,'2007-10-18','2010-06-10 12:14:22','2010-06-10',15,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(256,'Abinash Panda',NULL,NULL,NULL,'abindvdshpdvvanda05@gmail.com','abinashpanda05@gmail.com',NULL,'0','91 99860 19146','0',NULL,'0','2008-04-29',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-10 12:14:22',15,'0',NULL,'200710/18/ATT16380.html','200710/18/DOC14011.doc','Resume\n\nAbinash Panda\nMobile: +91-99860 19146\neMail: \nabindvdshpdvvanda05@gmail.com\n\nC/O. H.R.V Reddy, plot no-61/22, 1st Cross, LaxmiLayout, Munnekolala, Marathali, Bangalore - 560 \n037.\n\n\nExperience Summary\n\n\n       \nOver 2 years of progressive experience in Microsoft Technologies with process acumen of Finance, Health Care industry.\n\n       \nProficient in Web Based Application Programming with ASP.Net, C#, ADO.Net ,Crystal Report.\n\n       \nGood understanding\n on N-tier Architecture.\n\n       \nGood Knowledge in Databases SQL Server 2000, Oracle 9i.\n\n       \nGreat team player, with excellent communication skills.\n\n       \nFlexible to learn new technology and tools quickly.\n\n       \nExposed to different processes involved in the Software Development Life Cycle(SDLC).\n\n       \nGood knowledge in OOPS concept.\n\n       \nknowledge \nin Java script.\n\n       \nExposure to DICOM.\n\nObjective\n\nA challenging and progressive Career with an organization where my technical knowledge along with my creative thinking will contribute to the organization?s achievements and my growth.\n\nScholastic Career\n            \nB.E in Computer Science and Engineering from College Of Engineering, Bhubaneswar, Orissa \n\nwith first Division.\n\n\nExposure to IT Skills\nOperating System\n          \n            \n\n\nMS-DOS, Windows98, 2000, and XP\nTechnology\n                    \n            \n\n\nMicrosoft .Net Framework 1.1,2.0\nLanguages\n                     \n            \n\n\nC# ,VB.Net\nMarkup Languages\n         \n            \n\n\nHTML, XML\nScripting Language\n                    \n\n\nJava Script\nDatabases Known\n           \n            \n\n\nOracle 9i, SQL Server 2000\nWeb Technologies\n          \n            \n\n\nASP.NET\nWeb Server\n       \n            \n            \n\n\nIIS 6.0\nVersion Control Tool\n       \n            \n\n\nMicrosoft VSS\nProtocols\n      \n   \n                          \n\n\nHTTPS,HTTP,SOAP\n\n\n\n\n\nWork Experience\n\nWorking as a Software Engineer in \nQuadscope Solutions\n, Bangalore since July?05.\n\n\n\n\nProjects undertaken \n\nThe details of the various projects that I have worked under are listed here in chronological order.\n\n\n# Mortge\nDomain\n                                     \n\nFinance\nModule working under\n     \n           \n\nAPR?Finance\nRole\n                                          \n\n Team Member\nTeam size\n                                 \n\n 14\nEnvironment\n                              \n\n Windows 2000 Professional\nTools\n                                        \n\n Microsoft .NET Framework 2.0 \nTechnologies\n                             \n\n C#, ASP.NET\nRDBMS\n                          \n            \n\n Oracle 9i\nVersion\n                                     \n\n11.00,11.01\nDuration\n                                    \n\n Ongoing.\n                     \nDescription:\n\nA financial revolving credit\n\nwith multiple balance segments each at a different interest rate, possibly with a single umbrella credit limit, or with separate credit limits applicable to the various balance segments\n\n\nMortge-APR, a workflow, that captures, maintains, verifies and validates customer creditworthiness defining credit score in credit Rating report, thus setting a credit Line\n\nResponsibilities:\n\n    \nDevelopment for the application as per design documents, specified coding standards and documented best practices\n\n    \nFollowed the configuration management process as specified in the Project Configuration Plan\n\n    \nResolving defects related to the developed components with quick-turnaround time\n\n    \nInvolved in Peer Review\n\n# Care PM Suite\n            \nDomain\n\n                                  \n\n\n Health Care \nModule working under\n    \n            \n\nCare PMS LMIS\nRole\n                                          \n\n Team Member\nTeam size\n         \n                        \n\n 14\nEnvironment\n                              \n\n Windows 2000 Professional\nTools\n                                        \n\n Microsoft .NET Framework 1.1\nTechnologies\n                             \n\n C#\nRDBMS\n                          \n            \n\n SQL Server 2000\nVersion\n                               \n\n     \n\n7.88,7.89\nDuration\n                                    \n\n 10 Months.\n\n                \nDescription:\n\nCare PMS: LMIS, a sub-system which handles receiving, processing and storing information generated by medical laboratory processes interfacing with instruments and other information systems such as hospital information systems (HIS) etc., \nDisciplines of laboratory science supported by LMIS include hematology, chemistry, immunology, blood bank (Donor and Transfusion Management), surgical pathology, anatomical pathology, flow cytometry and microbiology. \n\nModules handled covers clinical lab which encompasses hematology, chemistry and immunology.\n\n                 \n\nFunctionality handled are Point of Request, Scheduling, Bill generation,Check ? in, \n\n  \n              \nSample collection, \n\nOrdering, \n\nEntry & Report Generation etc.\n\nResponsibilities:\n\n    \nDevelopment for the application as per design documents, specified coding standards and documented best practices\n\n    \nFollowed the configuration management process as specified in the Project Configuration Plan\n\n    \nInvolved in Peer Review\n\n\n# FMS \n\n       \n  \nModule working under\n    \n            \n\nAdmin FMS\nRole\n                                          \n\n Team Member\nTeam size\n                                 \n\n\nEnvironment\n                              \n\n Windows 2000 Professional\nTools\n                                        \n\n Microsoft .NET Framework 1.1,MS VSS\nTechnologies\n                             \n\n C#, ASP.NET \nRDBMS\n                                      \n\n SQL Server 2000\nDuration\n                                    \n\n 4 Months.\nDomain\n                                     \n: Facility\nVersion\n                                     \n: 2.1\n\nDescription:\nFacility management manages information about services provided by the facility providers to members. System provides the centralized access to service details.\n\nSystem admin manages the system and the devices connected to network.Inventory of users and log are tracked by the system admin i.e \nUser\n Log tracking, Mail alert messages to users and report generation.\n\nResponsibilities:\n\n\n    \nDevelopment for the application as per design documents, specified coding standards and documented best practices\n\n    \nFollowed the configuration management process as specified in the Project Configuration Plan.\n\n    \nInvolved in Peer Review\n\nAchievements:\n\n\n\n       \nAwarded Best Team Player of the year 2006\n\nPersonal Profile: \n\nDate of Birth\n                 \n: 23\nrd\n June 1984\nGender\n              \n          \n\n: Male\nLanguage Known\n            \n: English, Hindi, Oriya\nNationality\n                    \n: Indian\nAlternate eMail\n              \n: abinashpanda05@gmail.com\nPermanent Address\n        \n: At-Champati, Po-Padmapur,\n                                      \n            \nDist-Cuttack,Orissa,Pin-754200',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-18',NULL,'2007-10-18','2010-06-10 12:14:22','2010-06-10',15,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(257,'Alok Kumar sinha',NULL,NULL,'Delhi ','alodvdsvk.sdvsdvinha@hotmail.com','alok.sinha@hotmail.com','09999658257','0','91 99 99658257','0','06540 285340','0','2008-01-12',10,35,'2010-06-10 12:14:22',15,'0',NULL,'200710/18/ATT16381.html','200710/18/DOC14012.doc','Resdex @ naukri.com\nAlok Kumar Sinha\nB-45,Gopalpura Colony, Post Office Mugma, Dhanbad - 828204 \nalodvdsvk.sdvsdvinha@hotmail.com\n\nTelephone: 09999658257\n(M)\n 91 99 99658257\n(R)\n\nD.O.B\n - 26 Mar 1983 \nModified on\n - 26 Sep 2007 \nAnnual Salary\n - INR 2 Lac(s) 20 Thousand \nTotal Years of Experience\n - 2 Year(s) 2 Month(s) \nCurrent Location\n - Delhi \nPreferred Location\n - Anywhere in India, Anywhere in Northern India, Anywhere in South India \nB.Tech(CSE) having 2 years of experience in .Net and Microsoft Technology\n\nTEXT RESUME \n\nCURRICULUM VITAE\nAlok Kumar Sinha (B. Tech)\nCorrespondence Address: Email: 1) alok.sinha@hotmail.com\nRoomNo-k/301, HNo-14 , 2) meetalok_2004@yahoo.co.in\nBer Sarai, Oppsite Old JNU Campus,\nNew Delhi-16 Tel #: - 09999658257\nObjective: To associate with the reputed industry and work for the organization\n?s growth\n & progress with my whole energy, ability, knowledge, dedication and sincere efforts.\nSkills: C, C++, Vb.Net, C#, Java Script and \nADO\n. Net, Asp. Net, Sql Server 2000 and 2005 , \nCrystal\n report, PL\\SQL, Oracle 9i.\nExperience: 2 year and 2 months as Software Engineer and getting the requirements from the clients for developing the software and develops the projects. I take care of the timely delivery of quality software.\nI am presently working as Web Developer in Nethuesindia- futuristic software solutions, NN Mall, Rohini Sector-3, \nNew Delhi\n since 10th August 2007.\nI was previously working as Software Engineer in Dwon Technologies, \nBehind\nBhikaji\nCama\nPalace\n, and \nNew Delhi\n since 5th July 2005 to 9th August 2007\nEducation:\nB. Tech from Dehradun Institute of Technology in Computer Science & Engineering (2001-05) from \nU.P\nTech\nUniversity\n with 63%.\n12th from De Nobili School, Mugma, (affiliated to ICSE) in the year 2000 with 75.5%\n10th from De Nobili School, Mugma, (affiliated to ICSE) in the year 1998 with 82.5%\nProjects:\n1)Project Name: www.123supercart2.com\nSite : www.123supercart2.com\nResponsibilities: Designing of database, Coding and development of the software.\nTechnical Skills used: C#, ASP. Net 2.0, SQL Server2005, and \nAdo\n. Net.\nDescription of the project: It deals with the online shopping of products and placing their orders. User gets logins to view their orders placed and their status. The project is of n tier architecture. It is built in C# , ASP.Net, Ado.Net and SQLServer2005.\n2)Project Name: Quality Control Forum\nSite : www.qcforum.in\nResponsibilities: Designing of database, Coding and development of the software.\nTechnical Skills used: C#, ASP. Net , SQL Server2000, and Ado. Net.\nDescription of the project: It deals with the quality standards present in different industries. User gets logins to view the queries posted by different members and their solutions. In this quality related jobs are displayed and members can apply to the different jobs posted. It is a system which increases the efficiency of the management by searching the different quality standards prevailing in the different organization.. The project is of n tier architecture. It is built in C# , ASP . Net, Ado. Net and SQLServer2000.\n3)Project Name: www.onslogistics.in\nSite : www.onslogistics.in\nResponsibilities: Designing of database, Coding and development of the software.\nTechnical Skills used: C#, ASP. Net , SQL Server2000, and Ado. Net.\nDescription of the project: It deals with the ONLINE tracking of goods and cargo of customers and their updated status of the goods forwarded. It deals with online tracking of customer orders and maintain the details of the goods and their shipments. User gets logins to view the shipment of the goods and their updated status. It is an automated system, which increases the efficiency of the management. The project is of n tier architecture. It is built in C# , ASP . Net, Ado. Net and SQLServer2000.\n4)Project Name: Project Management System\nResponsibilities: Designing of database, Coding, Testing and documentation of the Software\nTechnical Skills used: C#, ASP. Net , SQL Server2000, Crystal Report and Ado. Net.\nDescription of the project: It deals with the project handling and maintenance of the projects in the Company. It also deals with establishing the milestone for the project and jobs completed by the developers in given time and schedule. It is an automated system, which increases the efficiency of the management. The project is of n tier architecture. It is built in C#, Ado. Net , Crystal Report and Sql Server2000.\n5)Project Name: ONSLOGISTICTS ACOUNTING AND BILLING SOFTWARE\nResponsibilities: Designing of database, Coding, Testing and leading the team of the software developer to deliver a quality product.\nTeam Size: Three (3) members.\nTechnical Skills Used: Vb.net, Sql Server2000, Crystal Report and Ado. Net.\nDescription of the project: It deals with Acounting and billing system of the company and Tracking the transactions of goods and cargo. The project is of n tier architecture. It is built in Vb. net, Ado. Net , Crystal Report and Sql Server2000.\n6)Project Name: IMS (Inventory Management System)\nTeam Size: Three (3) members.\nResponsibilities: Designing, Coding, Testing and documentation of the IMS.\nTechnical Skills used: VB.Net2003, Sql Server2000, Crystal Report and Ado. Net.\nDescription of the project: It deals with the Inventory Management System. The project is of n tier architecture. It is built in VB. Net, Ado. Net, Crystal Report and Sql Server2000\nComputer skills\nProgramming Languages - C, C++, C#, Vb.Net, Ado.Net, Asp.Net, Crystal\nReport , SQL Server, Oracle, PL\\Sql, Microsoft Visio.\nSubjects -Software Engineering, Database, Operating System\nConcepts and data structure.\nOperating Systems - MS-DOS, Windows 2k, 9X Series and XP\nPackages - MS Word, MS PowerPoint, MS Access, Ms Excel\nExtra Curricular Activities\n§ Member of Indian Society for Technical Education.\n§ Lead the CSE team in cricket tournament in college.\nHobbies\nMy hobbies are reading books on computer concepts, playing cricket, football, badminton, chess & video games.\nStrengths\nPositive attitude.\nI am eager to learn new things and try to implement in the project only if the quality of the project gets improved.\nI am a good team member and a good team leader.\nI am ready to accept challenges.\nPersonal Details\nFather\n?s name\n : Late: Anil Kumar Sinha\nDate of Birth : 26TH March 1983.\nPermanent Address : Village+PO: Lalpur, Dhanbad \n? 828129\nPhone (residence) : 06540 285340\nAlok Kumar Sinha','Nethuesindia- futuristic software solutions',1,NULL,'2007-10-18',NULL,'2007-10-18','2010-06-10 12:14:22','2010-06-10',15,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(258,'Anjali Yadav',NULL,NULL,'Noida ','yarfgergrdav.anergregjali@gmail.com','ydvdsvadav.anjrgrgali@gmail.com',NULL,'0','9911357006','0',NULL,'0','2007-04-14',8,23,'2010-06-10 12:14:22',15,'0',NULL,'200710/18/ATT16382.html','200710/18/DOC14014.doc','Resdex @ naukri.com\nanjali\nyarfgergrdav.anergregjali@gmail.com Noida - 201301 \nydvdsvadav.anjrgrgali@gmail.com\n\nTelephone: 9911357006\n(M)\n\nD.O.B\n - 11 Nov 1980 \nModified on\n - 25 Sep 2007 \nAnnual Salary\n - INR 3 Lac(s) 50 Thousand \nTotal Years of Experience\n - 2 Year(s) 9 Month(s) \nCurrent Location\n - Noida \nPreferred Location\n - No preference \nMCA with abt 3 year exp in healthcare & finance domain with .net, asp.net, vb.net, ado.net, c#, progress, sql server 2005\n\nTEXT RESUME \n\nAnjali Yadav\nSYNOPSIS OF EXPERIENCE\nSoftware professional with 2.8 years of experience in Information Technology with expertise in analysis, design and development of multi-tier web based application using formal software engineering and project management methodologies. These client-server, internet/intranet applications are developed for Healthcare & Finance domain using .NET Framework (ASP.net & VB.net), ASP, Visual Basic, COM/DCOM, VBScript, JavaScript, SQL Server, IIS, VSS and Crystal Reports\nI have always been an active Team member with Excellent Communication, Interpersonal and Team Building skills.\nOBJECTIVE\nSeeking a position in an IT services company that nurtures and develops talent and provides a facilitating environment to foster performance. I am looking for challenging and exciting opportunities in team-oriented environment, which calls upon one\'s abilities and gives a considerable degree of independence and responsibility, along with the personal, professional and financial growth of individual.\nEXPERIENCE Details\nOct \n?05 ? Till Date\nKeane Ltd. (Noida) as Software Engineer\nIn business since 1965, Keane, Inc. is a leading business process and IT services firm. It delivers highly synergistic application and business process services, including Application Development and Integration Services, Architecture Services, Application Outsourcing, Program Management, and Testing, as well as Business Transformation Services including Business Process Outsourcing.\nI am serving as an active team member for a Healthcare domain project of HSD (Healthcare solution division) which provides a total Healthcare Management solution to its customers across \nUSA\n\nJuly \n?04 ? Sept ?05\nMotherson Sumi InfoTech & Designs (\nIndia\n) Ltd. (Noida) as Software Engineer\nMIND InfoTech Ltd. is a CMM level 5 co. It is a subsidiary \nCo.\n of Sumito Wiring Systems Ltd. (Japanese) which a 500 fortune co. of manufacturing wiring harness. It caters to the software needs of the clients based in U.S.A, \nGermany\n\nJapan\n and other domestic clients like the manufacturing units of Motherson Sumi Systems Ltd. by delivering process and technology solutions.\nI have served as a Finance domain team member for the project Information Management System (IMS). Its objective is to keep records of the funds flowing in and out of the business and to do funds flow analysis. It is running successfully in the units of MSSL spread across NOIDA, Pune, Banglore and Sharjah.\nSKILLS SUMMARY\nSpecial skills Client interaction for requirement analysis. Design & development.\nOperating System WIN-9X/2000,Windows NT & MS -DOS\nLanguages VB.NET, C, C++, JAVA (2.0), VB (6.0) COM & DCOM, ASP, Progress\nDatabase SQL Server 2000, Sybase SQL Server, MS-Access\nWeb Technology HTML, ASP.NET, JavaScript, VbScript\nPackages Visual Studio framework\nSoftware/IDE Visual Studio .Net, Visual Studio 6.0, HTML Help, Crystal Report 8.5./9.5/10/11, JBuilder 4.0 and Rational Rose\nEnterprise Server Apps Internet Information Services (IIS)\nTools Used Visual source safe and Seagate Crystal Reports\nACADEMIC QUALIFICATION\n1. Post Graduation M.C.A.\nInstitute and University Banasthali Vidyapith, Rajasthan.\nYear of Passing 2001-2004\nPercentage 71.71%\n2. Graduation B.Com\nInstitute and University M.D.U., Rohtak\nYear of Passing 1998-2001\nPercentage 54.88%\n3. AISSCE-98 10+2\nInstitute and University Halwasiya Vidya Vihar, Bhiwani\nYear of Passing 1997-1998\nPercentage 62.80%\n4. AISCE-96 10th\nInstitute and University Public School Bal Bhawan, Bhiwani\nYear of Passing 1995-1996\nPercentage 68.40 %\n5 Honors Diploma in \n?Network centered computing? from NIIT (1-Year) in September (1999-2000)\nPROJECTS (In reverse chronological order)\n1) Project \n? HSD-LAB\nHSD is the Healthcare Solutions Division of KEANE Inc., and it provides solutions for Hospitals and other medical areas. LAB solution is offered on \n?Progress? technologies. It?s a Character User Interface (CUI) based product on UNIX, written in ?Progress? language. Project is migration of already existing LAB application, written in Progress language, to Web Ap\nplication. This web application needs to be integrated with two other applications EzAccess and iMed that works on .Net and Java platform. It provides business solutions for areas like Laboratory, Microbiology, Pathology and Cytology.\nThe application caters to the laboratory requirements of a hospital like that of patient records, specimen collections, requisition, inquiry, result entry, secondary approval and diagnosis. The cycle that follows is : Register the visit of the patient and allocate an account number, requisition for the test is generated and accession# are assigned for each of them, collect the samples of the patient, perform tests on the sample, result entry is done from instruments or manually for the tests performed, generate reports for the test & their results for the patient and his accounts, update billing, providing inquiry facility to surf through the history data on the basis of patient/account/accession#. Architecture of the project came out as a wonderful and innovative task as it merger of two technologies i.e. Microsoft Dot Net and Sun Java by the use Service Oriented Architecture (SOA). Secondly the both technology use same business layer for their business logic, which gave birth to loosely coupled implementations of different tiers. Architecture includes lot of common code implementation such as runtime screen generation and runtime code execution through reflection. Business layer & Reports will be used commonly from both environments.\nClient : Keane Inc Ltd, USA\nRole : Team Member (Team Size- 25)\nDuration : Oct \n?05 ? Till Date\nDBMS : SQL Server 2000 and AS/400-DB2\nEnvironment : VB.Net, ASP.Net, IIS, Crystal Reports 11, XML, J2EE, WebSphere, Web Service,\nMidd-Cor, JNI Bridge,\nResponsibility : Acting as a Team Member and responsible for following activities -\n· Reverse Engineering of the existing progress application\n· Discussion on the approach Document being provide from the client side\n· Prototype creation for the client approval\n· Design, Development & Integration of screens \n? Construction(.net) and testing of interfaces, components, Reports\n· Coding the front-end of the application using asp.net , XML, JavaScript & business layer using vb.net\n· Peer review & code review of screens developed by other team members\n· Preparation of UTP documents for the testing of the screens\n· Testing of the screens being developed as a part of application\nLocation : Keane India Ltd, Noida.\n2) Project \n? eBizSol\ne-BizSol is a ASP.NET based application. Its Finance domain fills in the gap of various accounting and after\n?the?operation information ?anything that is found in the chart of the accounts, journal entries or historic transactions. This allows consistency between operational, off-site or outsourced systems, back office accounting and repo\nrting systems. Along with each transaction, finance entity i.e. project or location are identified and a new channel is designed to trounce the inefficiencies of non-integrated financial systems. It collects General Ledger and after-the-fact receivables, payables, inventory and other financial facts, and then permits the representation of that information using traditional summaries and flexible links for reporting. An organization can define its accounting structure as per its requirements a level of defined accounting structure like General Ledger and Sub Ledger can be further allocated to costs centers, projects and employees. This versatile accounting structure offers infinite potential to classify information for an origination\n?s need. In addition to th\nis, consolidated reports can be produced to show details across multiple units\nClient : Motherson Sumi InfoTech & Design Ltd\nRole : Team Member\nDuration : Jan \n?05 ? Oct ?05\nDBMS : SQL Server 2000\nEnvironment : VS.Net, ASP.NET, C#, VB.NET, SQL Server 2000, XML, Crystal Reports\nResponsibility : As a Team Member responsible for following activities -\n· Conversation with the client to understand the requirements for development or enhancement\n· Do the feasible study for the proposal along with the DB changes expected\n· Preparation of specification documents & prototype screen\n· Development of the screens as per the approach finalized\n· Perform Unit, Integration and Functional testing of the Application\n· Providing maintenance and support to the client after development &deployment\nLocation : Motherson Sumi InfoTech & Designs Ltd., Noida.\n3) Project \n? Material Management\n & Control System\nThe MMCS automates the material handling process of Manufacturing Industry. This application keeps track of all the materials and vendors of the company. The user is facilitated to view and print different kinds of reports on all the incoming & outgoing material with the help of Crystal Reports.\nClient : Sagar Auto Linker, NOIDA\nDuration : 1st Oct\n?04 ? Dec ?05 (3 months)\nDBMS : SQL Server 2000\nEnvironment : VS.Net, ASP.NET, C#, VB.NET, SQL Server 2000, XML. \nCrystal\n Reports\nResponsibility : Acting as a Team Member and responsible for following activities -\n· Part of the team designing and developing the framework for application development, by preparing required documents.\n· Development of various applications and services for the system\n· Perform Unit, Integration and Functional testing of the Application\n· Providing maintenance and support to the client after development &deployment\nLocation : Motherson Sumi InfoTech & Designs Ltd., Noida.\n4) Key Review Area Application to CMM Level \n?5 process management.\nApplication keeps online track of training requirements & appraisal throughout the company, by performance appraisal cycle. Employee code determines access level to various web pages, which provides the security throughout the application. Proper security is maintained by doing authentication and validations of users at different levels\nClient : MIND, NOIDA\nRole : Data Base designing, Coding and Unit testing\nDuration : 1st Sept\n?04 ? Oct?04 (2 months)\nDBMS : SQL Server 2000\nEnvironment : ASP.NET, VB.NET, C#, HTML, XML.\nLocation : Motherson Sumi InfoTech & Designs Ltd, Noida.\n5) Monthly Reporting System\nMonthly Reporting System is an online Enterprise Resources Planning Solution, which caters to the need of combining the efforts of all the manufacturing units (scattered at different geographical locations) of a big manufacturing firm. It has functionalities like analysis & recording of monthly data, generation of charts in MS Access, activation & deactivation of users, data consolidation and currency conversion for the data collected from various manufacturing units.\nM.C.A. DISSERTATION\n1) Design and development of front-end federates for battlefield simulation (MCA 6th sem)\nObjective of the project was to provide map based Front-end for Wargame playable on High Level\nArchitecture (HLA) based distributed simulation. It provides GIS based functionality required for Wargame Simulation. The software is integrated with other dummy prototype subsystems like Simulation Engine and the Controller. UML was used to prepare class diagrams and sequence diagrams\n2) Simulation of loaders & its tutorial\nThe Objective of the project was to simulate the working of loader and to provide an easy way for its user to learn about loaders, its type and working with the help of a tutorial. It graphically represents loading of a program written in C language and the position in memory after loading of instructions.\n3) Video library management\nThe objective of this Project was to automate the recording of customers, movies and the transaction of a Video Library. The monthly transaction report is generated in the end. It helps in easy management of accounts, and keeps tracks of movement of objects moving in and out of the store.\nExtra-Curricular Achievements\nMember of the team which got award for \n?Exceptional Quality? at Keane level\nHobbies\nListening to music, cooking, playing games & traveling\n[Anjali Yadav]','Keane Ltd.',1,NULL,'2007-10-18',NULL,'2007-10-18','2010-06-10 12:14:22','2010-06-10',15,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(259,'Ajit saha',NULL,NULL,'Pune','ajitsabfbbfbffbfha020@gmail.com',NULL,NULL,'0','09326696400','0',NULL,'0','2009-04-13',10,35,'2010-06-10 12:14:22',15,'0',NULL,'200710/18/ATT16383.html','200710/18/DOC14015.doc','RESUME\nAjit Saha\nPhone: \n09326696400\nEm\n\nil:\n\najitsabfbbfbffbfha020@gmail.com\nAddress: \nFlat No 1, Ajad nagar, Sibaji Nagar,\n                \nPune- 411038, \nMaharashtra\n\nIndia\n                       \n                                                                                           \n\nPROFESSIONAL EXPERIENCE:\n\n     \n      \n\n2.5 +\n years experience in IT Industry\n\n1. BMC Softw\n\nre Indi\n\n Pvt. Ltd\n\n\n\n\nR & D Technic\n\nl Associ\n\nte\n\nfrom\n 18-Dec-2006\n    \n\n\n\nhttp://www.bmc.com/\n\n\n. Worked in \nSTPI\n, Orissa as Software Engineer from 23rd May 2005 to 31st Oct 2006\n            \n\nCurrent Responsibilities\nResolving customer technic\n\nl issues rel\n\nted to Product.\nConsulting with the development te\n\nm for fixing the bugs in the Service Desk Express product. And Submitting the defects \n\nnd Request for enh\n\nncement for the product to the development te\n\nm.\nSupporting product through Remedy (An enterprise ticketing system) \nDisp\n\ntching c\n\nses to the te\n\nm members when required.\nDiscuss the defects in the product with the QA team.\nProducts:\n\n\n   \n   \nBMC \nService Desk Express Suite\n is an easy-to-use and easy-to-implement browser-based service desk tracking automation tool. It offers a flexible architecture, which makes it an ideal service desk tracking software for the service needs of many departments. Powerful workflow delivers superior service and reduces operational expenses, while interactive graphical reporting displays the data you need to make informed business decisions.\n\n\n         \nBMC \nKnowledge Management Express\n (formerly Magic Knowledge Management) helps building an effective knowledge management system by plugging easily into the existing BMC \nService Desk Express Suite \nimplementation. With BMC, organizations can protect and extend their investments, harvest information from most skilled, knowledgeable workers, identify information needs, and resolve issues faster. The separate self-service module can be added to empower end users and customers to find solutions to common problems, further reducing costs and improving customer satisfaction.\n\n         \nThe BMC \nService Desk Express Integration Engine\n provides an interface through which you can define data integration (data sources, data transformation, importing, and exporting) with BMC SDE. You can also define the actions that BMC SDE takes after importing the data, such as creating an incident record. The BMC Service Desk Express Integration Engine supports a variety of data sources, including other BMC applications.\n           \nTECHNICAL PROFICIENCY\n\n\n   \nLanguages\n                  \n\n\nC, C++, C#.Net\n   \nOperating Systems\n    \n: Windows, Linux, MS-DOS\n   \nFront-End\n      \n             \n: VB 6.0, VB.NET\n   \nBack-End\n                    \n\n\nSQL Server 2000/2005\n   \nScripting Language\n     \n: JavaScript, VBScript\n   \nWeb Technology\n         \n: HTML, ASP, ASP.NET\n   \nWorking knowledge\n   \n: MS Word, MS Excel, MS Power Point.\n\n\nProfessional Qualification:\n\n\nBE \n\nComputer Science & Engineering\n.) from \nBCET, Balasore, Orissa\n with 68%. \nYear : 2001 to 2005\n\nProfessional Experience:\n\nProject # 1 -\n\n\nClient\n                  \n: Vie InfoTech.\nProject\n           \n    \n\n: Employee Management System\nDuration\n              \n: Nov 2005 ? April 2006.\nPosition\n               \n: Software Engineer\nEnvironment\n        \n: VB6.0, SQL Server 2000. \nRole\n                    \n: Developer\nTeam size\n                        \n: 3\n\nDescription:\n\nThis is an enhancement project to keep track of employees in the office, their attendance, their payroll, projects in which they are involved etc. The employee will meet the operator while entering the office. Then he will be checked in. Before going out he will meet him again. The employee?s holidays will be adjusted as he takes leave. The applications of the employees will be maintained. His payment details is also stored, whether he was paid check or DD, date of issuing the check or DD, issuing bank etc.\n\nThe employee will be involved in the projects according to his/her skill set. We can know the project status i.e. it is finished or continuing. \n\nRoles & Responsibilities:\n\nAs a team member I was involved in\n\n\nAnalysis of programs or low-level design documents provided for the work\n     \n       \nRequest.\n\n\nAdding and removing fields from the application and their Impact analysis.\n\n\nChanging Screens and the Maps.\n\nProject # 2 -\n\n\nClient\n                  \n: Padmalaya Book Store,BBSR,Orissa\nProject\n             \n: Book store Automation\nDuration\n              \n: July 2005 ? Nov 2005.\nPosition\n               \n: Software Engineer\nEnvironment\n        \n: VB6.0, SQL Server 2000. \nRole\n                    \n: Developer\nTeam size\n                        \n: 4\n\nDescription:\n\nPadmalaya Book Store is one of the leading dealer as well as seller in \nBhubaneswar\n, Orissa\n\nThis was a small development project for Padmalaya Book Store. The first development project from Scratch for Vie InfoTech. The project was very simple development with less complexity about their process. They wanted an Application for their small book store comprising of more than 10,000 books with 3 Locations especially for their in house tracking.\n\nBook store Automation is software made for automating their book store. This is a software which keeps record for ordering the books. First all the book details available from the book catalogue is stored in the database. Then administrator will order the books from their distributors. After receiving the order he can verify the order accordingly. If some of the books are not received then he can reorder them. This software keeps the record of the accounts. There is a section that maintains employee record. This software also maintains \nSale\n of books and keeps details of the regular customers.\n\nRoles & Responsibilities:\n\nAs a team member I was involved in\n\n\nAnalysis of programs or low-level design documents provided for the work\n     \n      \nRequest.\n\n\nPreparing design documents for the requirements. \n\n\nCoding and designing\n\n\nInteracting with the client.\n\nProject # 3 -\n\n\nClient\n                  \n: Jan Shikshyan Sansthan(JSS),\nRourkela\n,Orissa\nProject\n            \n\n\nOffice automation software\nDuration\n              \n: June 2006 ? August 2006.\nPosition\n               \n: Software Engineer\nEnvironment\n        \n: VB6.0, SQL Server 2000. , \nCrystal\n reports 8.5\nRole\n                    \n: Developer\nTeam size\n                        \n: 3\n\nDescription:\n\nThe Jan Shikshan Sansthan (JSS) is an innovative educational scheme in the field of non-formal and continuing education and training for adults started by the Government of India in the year 1967. (This was formerly known as Shramik Vidyapeeth). \n\n\nThis is a project to keep records of all the candidates taking admission in various courses. Provision is there to add new courses .All details of the candidates such as their personal details as well as their professional details are stored in the data base. This software keeps record of the instructors who are there to teach the students. This organization performs some activities at remote places. Those details are also stored in database. The authorized person takes a printout of all the details of activities and students for sending it to the Government as annual report.\n\nRoles & Responsibilities:\n\nAs a team member I was involved in\n\n\nAnalysis of programs or low-level design documents provided for the work\n     \n   \nRequest.\n\n\nPreparing design documents for the requirements. \n\n\nCoding, designing and report making\n\n\nInteracting with the client.\n\nPERSONAL DETAILS\n\nNmae\n                    \n\n           \nAjit Saha\n           \nFather?s Name\n      \n\n           \nHemant Saha\nDate of Birth\n           \n\n           \n02-02-1984\nNationality \n\n          \nIndian\nReligion \n                 \n\n          \nHinduism\nLanguage known \n   \n\n          \nEnglish, Hindi, Oriya\n\nDeclaration:\n\n            \nI hereby declare that the information furnished above as per my knowledge is true.\n\n\n\n\nDate:\nPlace: \n                                                                                                        \nSignature','BMC Software India Pvt. Ltd',1,NULL,'2007-10-18',NULL,'2007-10-18','2010-06-10 12:14:22','2010-06-10',15,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(260,'Ashish Ranjan',NULL,NULL,'Bangalore ','ashishrwefefeanjan_efefmcaefewf@yahoo.co.in','ashishranjan_mca@yahoo.co.in','234 8073385643','0','9900519830','0',NULL,'0','2008-04-13',8,24,'2010-06-10 12:14:22',15,'0',NULL,'200710/18/ATT16384.html','200710/18/DOC14016.doc','Resdex @ naukri.com\nAshish Ranjan\nSrinivas Complex Chunchugatta Main Road, New Bank Colony, Bangalore - 560062 \nashishrwefefeanjan_efefmcaefewf@yahoo.co.in\n\nTelephone: 9900519830\n(M)\n\nD.O.B\n - 02 Feb 1983 \nModified on\n - 26 Sep 2007 \nAnnual Salary\n - INR 3 Lac(s) 50 Thousand \nTotal Years of Experience\n - 2 Year(s) 3 Month(s) \nCurrent Location\n - Bangalore \nPreferred Location\n - Bangalore \n2+ years on hand experience in .Net and T24 ( GLOBUS )\n\nTEXT RESUME \n\nAshish Ranjan Tel # (Mobile): +234-8073385643\nSrinivas Complex E-mail: ashishranjan_mca@yahoo.co.in\nNew Bank Colony\nChunchugatta Main Road\nBangalore-560 062\n-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nJob Objective:\nChallenging work environment, Application of skills, Enhancement of knowledge levels and Major contribution towards organizational goals\nProfessional Summary:\n\n?¢\n Gained 2+ years in depth experience on .Net Technology with Banking Domain via implementation of web Application, Services as well as Banking Applications\n\n?¢\n Gained 7+ months of Onsite experience in East Africa.\nI Technical Skills:\nTechnology : .Net Framework, ASP.Net, ADO.Net,\nWeb-Services, AJAX, XML\nProgramming Language : C#.Net, VB.Net, C, C++, VB6.0, Info Basic\nDatabase : SQL SERVER, Oracle, jBASE, Universe\nScripting Language : JavaScript, VBScript, HTML\nUtility Packages : MS-FrontPage, Dream waver\nBanking Product : GLOBUS / T24 (Temenos)\nII Work Experience:\nA) Organization : Sepit Softech Pvt Ltd ( Bangalore )\nTenure : January 2006 till date\nRole : Technical Consultant\nProjects Handled:\n1) Title - GSS, Intraday, Deposit and Lending Solution\nClient - Central Bank of Nigeria\nWork Place - Abuja, Nigeria (Onsite)\nDuration - 20th June 2007 to 15th September 2007\nTools - C#, ASP.NET, mv.NET, Java Script, TCServer, TCClient\nDatabase - jBASE (Temenos - T24) ,Sql Server 2000\nRole - Developer\nGist:\n\n??\n Developed some of local application for GSS, Intraday and Deposit\n\n??\n Coordinated with the CBN users for designing the above application.\n\n??\n Defines the Parameter table for the above local application\n\n??\n Developed the E- Solution for the above local application\n\n??\n Developed a separate control panel for the user to control the parameter value if required by the Bank.\n\n??\n Developed the interfaces between RTGS and T24 system\n\n??\n Given training to the users regarding the administration of the above development.\n\n??\n Documentation and Implementation\n2) Title - E- Banking Solution\nClient - AfriBank, South-Africa\nWork Place - Bangalore (India) + Johannesburg ( RSA )\nDuration - 12th November 2007 to 30th May 2007\nTools - C#, ASP.NET, mv.NET, Java Script, TCServer, TCClient\nDatabase - Universe (Temenos - T24), SqlServer\nRole - Developer\nGist:\n\n??\n Successfully implemented the database Integration with the T24 system and .Net Technology using mv.NET via TCServer and TCClient.\n\n??\n Developed a complete E-Solution for Retail & Corporate Customer.\n\n??\n Developed the Online Trade Financial services for their customers.\n\n??\n Implemented the Online Portfolio and Security details for the Afribank customer.\n\n??\n Developed SMS Banking for notification of transactions initiated by the AfriBank customers.\n\n??\n Documentation and Implementation.\n\n??\n Given Administration training to the Internet Admin ( Bank User )\n3) Title - Data Migration\nDuration - 13th April 2006 to 30th October 2007\nTools - C#, Win-Form, JDK, PLSORA DRIVER, XML\nRole - Developer\nGist:\n\n??\n It converts the multi-value database into a relational table based format ( In case of Oracle )\n\n??\n Developed and designed interfaces for data migration from jBASE to Oracle.\n\n??\n Developed the local Interface which first converts the jBASE database into CSV format using JDK Driver\n\n??\n Later automatically it Converts the CSV data into XML\n\n??\n Finally it writes the XML data into Oracle Table Using PLSORA driver.\n\n??\n Migrated T24 database into ORACLE using JEDI ( jBASE External Device Interfaces )\n4) Title - Retail Banking Module\nDuration - 5th January 2006 to 27th March 2006\nTools - ASP.NET, C#, mv.Net, JavaScript\nDatabase - SQL Server 2000, jBASE\nRole - Developer\nGist:\n\n??\n Successful Integration of T24 Database with .NET Technology\n\n??\n Developed a complete Demo Solution for implementing E- Services for any bank using ASP.NET\n\n??\n It places online request in to T24 system.\n\n??\n It can generate online enquiry and reports on Live T24 system\nIII Technical Achievements\n\n?¶\n Delivered live presentation on Temenos and E- Banking in Equatorial Trust Bank \nSwitzerland\n and PHB Bank Lagos \nNigeria\n\n\n?¶\n Data Migration from a file based Multi-value format to a relational table format ( from jBASE to Oracle using C#)\n\n?¶\n Integration of .Net with T24\n\nIII Academic Qualifications:\n\n?¶\n MCA - G.G.D University, Bilaspur\n\n?¶\n BCA - G.G.D University, Bilaspur\nIV Academic Achievements:\n\n?¶\n University Topper in MCA (2nd Semester)\n\n?¶\n District Topper in 12th Std\nV Personal Details:\nPassport No : F6965742\nDate of Birth : 02-02-1983\nMarital Status : Single\nLanguages Known : Hindi, English, Maithali\nHobbies : Cricket, Reading\nDate :\nPlace : Bangalore (Signature)','Sepit Softech Pvt Ltd ',1,NULL,'2007-10-18',NULL,'2007-10-18','2010-06-10 12:14:22','2010-06-10',15,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(261,'Ashish Kumar',NULL,NULL,'New Delhi','aewfgwefghish_soegwergft@rediffmail.com',NULL,NULL,'0','9871124950','0',NULL,'0','2005-04-13',9,28,'2010-06-10 12:14:22',15,'0',NULL,'200710/18/ATT16385.html','200710/18/DOC14017.doc','Ashish Kumar Sinha\n\n\n                                                                                                         \nASHISH K \n\nSINHA\n\n                              \n                                                                                                   \n                               \naewfgwefghish_soegwergft@rediffmail.com\n\n                                                                                                         \nM.No. 9871124950\n                                                                                                         \nF-146/B, Katwaria sarai,\n                                                                                                            \nNew Delhi\n -16\n      \nCareer Objective\n\n\nI am seeking an opportunity to work with motivated and ambitious team of people with whom I can make a significant contribution for organization and its customers to meet their objectives and also to participate in the process of knowledge sharing and wealth creation.\nCORE STRENGTH:\n\n\n       \nWorked for \n5+ Years\n on Web & Desktop Projects. \n\n       \nSound knowledge of C#,\n ASP.NET, VB.NET, ADO.NET.\n\n       \nStrong in\n   \nCrystal Report\n 9.0, 10.0, NET.\n\n       \nGood Working Knowledge of \nWEB SERVICES, \nREMOTING\n, XML. \n\n       \nSound in Object Oriented Concepts and SDLC.\n\n       \nSound Knowledge of \n\n\nSQL\n   \n2000\n\n       \nSound in RDBMS Concepts. \n\n       \nSound knowledge about Data structures.\n\n        \nGood knowledge In Oracle.\n\n        \nGood knowledge In Informix 8.0(Database).\n\n        \nStrong knowledge \nin Java Script\n\n        \nGood knowledge of\nAJAX\n\n        \nGood Knowledge of\n ?SQL Reporting Servicing?.\nPROFESSIONAL SUMMARY:\n   \n\n       \nWorking with NIIT TECH. LTD. As Senior Soft.Engg, \nMohan\nCooperative\nState\n 18. Since Oct. 2006.\n\n       \nWorked with\n\n DIMENSION \nINDIA\nAs a \nSenior\n\nSoft.Engg\n, Noida from Apr. 2005 to Sep 2006.\n\n       \nWorked with. MKT. PVT. LTD.\n   \nAs Developer\n\nfrom March 2002 to March 2005\nPROFESSIONAL QUALIFICATION:\n\n\n       \nMASTER OF COMPUTER APPLICATION\n\nADDITIONAL QUALIFICATION:\n\n\n       \n?O? & ?A? level from DOEACC\n\n       \nPGDCA \n(Post Graduate Diploma In Computer Application) \n\n       \nTECHNICAL QUALIFICATION / CERTIFICATION\n\n       \nHIGHER DIPLOMA IN SOFTWARE ENGINEERING\n from \nAPTECH LTD\n\n\n\n\nSOFTWARE SKILL SET:\n\nOperating System\n    \n         \nDOS, Windows 9x, Windows-NT, UNIX\nProgramming Language\n     \nC with (Data structure), C++, Java\nGUI (Environment)\n            \nASP.NET(C#),\n VB.NET (Desktop Application, Remoting, Crystal Report) \nADO\n. Net, Web services, XML.\n\nVB-4.0, 5.0, 6.0\n (Active Control, Active EXE, \nDLL\n\nADO\n, RDO, DAO, \nCOM\n\nDCOM\n, MTS (NT), COM+ (2000)), \nOracle Work Bench (Migration Tool).\n      \nWeb Server (OS)\n    \n           \nIIS, PWS \nPackage\n                   \n         \nMs-office\nDatabase\n                 \n         \nOracle-7.0, 8.0, 8i, 9i, MS-Access, SQL server 7.0,2000\nScripts (Client Side)\n\n         \nJava scripts, Vb scripts.\nOthers Tools Used\n\n         \nCrystal\nreport\n   \n8.0, 9.0.10, Work Bench (Database Migration Tool).\nMAJOR PROJECTS:\n\nProject \nPrime West (Decommission)\n     \nFinancial\n\nDomain\nSoftware Used\nASP.NET WITH C#, Framework \n\n2.0\nDatabase\n\nOracle 9i.Informix 8.0\n\nRole\nSoft Developer, Unit Testing, Unit Test Cases.\n\nClient\n\n\nING (Neetherland).\n\nProject \nCharles River\n\n                              \nFinancial\n\nDomain\nSoftware Used\nASP.NET WITH C#, Framework 2.0\nDatabase\nOracle 9i.\n\nRole\nSoft Developer, Unit Testing, Unit Test Cases.\n\nClient\n\n\nING (Neetherland).\n\nProject \nNetpromoworld.com\nSoftware Used\nASP.NET WITH C#, Framework 2.0\nDatabase\nSQL SERVER 2000.\n\nReports.\nCrystal\n report 9(Server Side)\n\n\nOther Tools \n\nXML, Web service. \nRole\nCreate Business logic, implement Business Logic, coding, debuging\nClient\n\nHolcim (\nUSA\n).\nModule\n\nAdmin Control panel, Vendor, Front End, client, Employee, Item.\nDescription\nhttp://www.netpromoworld.com\n\nIt is a complete ecommerce web site solution that provides all you need to build, operate, and maintain an online store. It includes easy-to-use shopping cart software forms for managing product information, built-in interfaces to Link Point, Your Pay and Authorize.Net payment gateways, and a special version that interfaces with Innovative Gateway Solutions.\n\nProject Name\n\nWWW.MyStarDvd.com\nSoftware Used\nASP.NET (C#)\nDatabase\nSQL SERVER 2000\nDescription\nOn Line DVD Rental, Purchase.\n\n\n       \nDvd Rental.\n\n       \nFront End (Searching, ShopingCart, Review)\n\n       \nOrder.\nMember Registration.\n\n\nProject Name\n\nWWW.Marcindia.com (On Line Reporting Website)\nSoftware Used\nASP.NET WITH C# ( ver .1.1) \nDatabase\nSQL SERVER 2000\nDescription\nThis application has been developed for \nFare\n\n& Finance Pvt Ltd.\n\n\nProject \nNetwork Based\n   \nFinancial Software (Stock market).\nSoftware Used\nC# 2003.\nDatabase\nSQL SERVER 2000.\n\nReports.\nCrystal\n report 9.\n\n\nOther Tools\n\nRole\n\n\nMS Excel (Macro Programming for Porfolio analyzer with help of Omega software.) \n\n\nProgrammer (Coding, Functional Testing).\nDescription\nThis Network based application being developed for \nStock market.\n\n\n\n       \nDeveloped day trading systems for high volume stocks listed\n      \nOn NSE.\n\n       \nDeveloped position trading system for high volume stocks listed \n      \nOn NSE.\n\n       \nDeveloped strategy.\n\n       \nDevelop indicator\n\n       \nData Simulation (SQL SERVER 2000)\n\n       \nGenerate system (Data simulation)\n\n       \nReport for Carry forward ,Intraday\n\n       \nReports\n\n\n1.\n      \n\nDay wise\n   \nStrategy, Signal, Portfolio.\n2.\n      \n\nDay wise Pl, Stop losses, Target hit.\n3.\n      \n\nAnalyst wise no. win, loss trades.\n4.\n      \n  \nMax Consecutive loss.\n     \n5.\n      \n\nTop 5 Draw Down.\n6.\n      \n\nDay wise Open, Close trades.\n7.\n      \nSignals Performance.\nThis system is partially dependent on\n\n\nNSE (National stock exchange) data. Which is available on line in \nAd hoc manner and we are operating & manipulating the data to \nGenerate report and take crucial decision to generate our profitability.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nProject \nIEMS(Invoice Enquiry Management System)\n\nSoftware Used\nVB.NET 2003.\nDatabase\nSQL Server 2000.\nReports.\nCrystal\n report .NET\nDescription\nThis application, being developed for \nStock house (Bhagirath palace)\n\nDelhi\n\n\nFollowing services:\n\n       \nEmployee Details\n\n       \nParty details\n\n       \nCustomer Details.\n\n       \nPayroll Management System.\n\n       \nAttendance Management System\n\n       \nExcise System and Stock details. And Chelan details.\n            \n\n       \n\nEnquiry system\n\n       \nReports\nThis system allows the employees to input goods, Enquiry information into a central database and generate all type of challan, enquiry, invoice, excise report.\n\nProject \nGlobaladmin.info (Shopping Gallery For Promotional Item)\nSoftware Used\nASP.NET\n\nWITH C# , Framework -2.0\nDatabase\nSQL SERVER 2000.\n\nOther Tools\n\nXML, Web service.\nRole\n\n(Coding, Functional testing, Report developing, Module integration)\nClient\n\nGo daddy (\nUSA\n).\nModule\n\nItem purchasing, Online Payment system.\nDescription\nhttp://www.globaladmin.info\n\nIt is a special site for purchasing promotional item which reduces the effort of each n every customer. From this site person can buy things online n they can get their goods as a home delivery. They can pay their bills through credit cards.\n\n\n\nProject \nERP(Multi User Environment)\nSoftware Used\nC# 2003, ASP.NET\n\n,Web Service \nDatabase\nSQL SERVER 2000.\n\nReports.\nCrystal\n report 9\n\nRole\n\nCoding(C#, T-SQL), Module ,Report Developer.\nClient\n\nOCL (ORISSA CEMENT LTD, Rajgunpur Orissa.)\nModule\n\nRaw Material, HR.\nDescription\nERP\n\nCreated Organization structured of enterprise according to the need of the Client, specifically in Raw Material and HR Segments. Also provided\nHelpful hand in creating different type of \nBusiness & Plain Reports\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nPERSONAL DETAILS:\nName\n                                       \n\n           \nAshes Kumar Sinha\nFather?s Name\n                         \n\n           \nDr. Shakti Kumar Sinha\nSex\n                                          \n\n           \nMale\nMartial Status\n                          \n\n          \nSingle\nNationality\n                               \n\n           \nIndian\nLanguages Known\n                   \n\n           \nHindi, English\nHobbies\n                                               \n\n           \nComputer Programming, Listening Music, Driving.\n\nDate:\n                                                                                                   \n(ASHISH KUMAR SINHA)','NIIT TECH. LTD',1,NULL,'2007-10-18',NULL,'2007-10-18','2010-06-10 12:14:22','2010-06-10',15,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(262,'Arunachalam s',NULL,NULL,NULL,'arunacheedgrgdgergralamdil@gmail.com',NULL,'44 22320425','0','919841681169','0','04639 279567','0','2008-04-29',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-10 12:14:22',15,'0',NULL,'200710/18/ATT16386.html','200710/18/DOC14018.doc','                                         \nRESUME\n          \n\nARUNACHALAM S\n                                               \narunacheedgrgdgergralamdil@gmail.com\n\nPh.no:o44-22320425\n                    \n                                  \nNo.16/40, \nEast Portion\nMobile no: +919841681169\n                 \n             \nKarpagga vinayagar \nKoil Street\n            \nAlandur\n-600016\n\nObjective\nTo be a part of a dynamic environment, to introduce innovative ideas in the industry and to be an effective team member with team spirit.\n\nEXPERIENCE SUMMARY \nOver 2+ years of Software Development Experience in Internet Technologies and Client Server Environment Good programming skills in .Net, SQL, Java Script, AJAX and HTML\n\nEducation\n\nCourse\nName of institute\nYear Of Passing\n\nB. Tech (Information Technology\n\nJayamatha Engineering\n      \nCollege\n\nMay 2005\n\n66\n\nHigher secondary\nMargoschis Higher Secondary School\n\nMar 2001\n\n73.2\n\nSoft Skills\n\nOperating system\nWindows 2000, Windows xp\nLanguages\nC#.NET, VB.NET\nWEB TECHONOLOGIES\nHTML, ASP.NET\nDatabase\nMS Access, SQL Server2000\nInternet Applications & Other Utilities\nXML, Java script, AJAX, Web Services\n\n\nArea of Interest\n     \n\n      \nOOPS Concepts\n\n      \nSQL \n\n      \nWeb Services\n                    \n                                              \n\n\n\n\n\n\nInternational Certification\n\n\n      \nBrain Bench\n certified \nASP.Net Developer, C# Developer\n\n      \nTranscript ID#: \n5812758\n\n\n  \n\n\nWorking Experience\nCurrently working as a Programmer Analyst in Cognizant Technology Solution from Feb 2007 to till now\nPreviously worked at GLINFOTECH pvt ltd as a Programmer Analyst From Jun 2005 to Jan 2007\n\nClient Description\n\nMorgan Stanley\n is a \nUS\n mutual fund company with over $135 billion in assets under management and over 7 million shareholder accounts. Its broad family of more than 60 funds allows investors to create diversified portfolios for almost any investment goal. The client has been in this business for over 40 years now. It offers a diverse product line that includes mutual funds, variable annuities and qualified retirement plans. It also provides award-winning shareholder services to fund investors and their financial advisors.\n\nProjects Experience\n\n1.\nTitle\n\nMorgan Stanley Project Management Office (MSPMO)\n\nTools Used\n\nASP.NET, C#. NET, \nAjax\n, SQL SERVER 2000\n\nDuration\n: 6 months\n\nDescription\n\nMSPMO is a Morgan Stanley Knowledge Portal developed\n\n\nshares the experience and knowledge gained by the members of Cognizant working with Morgan Stanley. With valuable information added by each project team member, this site is poised to grow and enriched with details which would help people working in Morgan Stanley teams carry out their activities better. It mainly deals with the proposals, projects, resource allocation and different metrics.\n\nThe entire application developed using ASP.net and SQL Server as back-end. The Resource Request Automation, which automates the entire life cycle of resource request, has been developed in ASP.NET and integrated with the MSPMO portal. The application also has Metrics module developed using ASP.NET.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n2.\nTitle\n\nCustomer Solutions\n\nTools Used\n: Asp. Net, C#. Net, SQL SERVER, Ms-Access\n\nDuration\n: 8 months\n\nDescription\n: This application is about creating a web-based questionnaire\n\nInterview that will be taken by people attending trade-shows. This is split into two, a C#.Net Win forms application and an ASP.Net web application.\nThe Winform application maintains Customer information, Customer related Project Information, Project Question and Answer data and the Question Programming data. These data are stored in a local Access 2000 database. Questions and possible answers for a question are created first. The questions have been classified into different categories such as ?Single Choice?, ?Multiple Choice?, ?Yes/No?, ?Ranking? and ?Open End?. ?Single Choice?, ?Multiple Choice? and ?Yes/No? type questions will have possible answers. Each possible answer to a question carries a weight-age point. Once the question and answers are created then the question sequence or flow can be created by the user represented by a Tree-view control. Questions can be added to the tree and re-arranged within the tree just by drag and drop.\nOnce the question flow has been created the user has been provided with a facility to create HTML pages for the questionnaire that can run locally on the browser. When all is fine a facility has been provided to upload this data stored locally in and Access 2000 database to a Web-site SQL Server database to be used by the ASP.Net application. \nThe ASP.Net Web page is invoked by a Magcard Swipe Winforms application. When a user swipes the card the ASP.Net page loads with the user information read from the Mag-card. Here the user can make changes if any and can proceed to the Interview page by clicking a button. The interview questionnaire page is created dynamically based on the user?s response to a question and the question flow/sequence logic created in the Winform application. User can quit interview any time just by clicking an ?Exit Interview? button displayed on every Questionnaire page.\n\n3.\nTitle\n\nPLT MAIL \n(PLTMail.com)\n\nTools Used\n\nASP.NET, C#. NET, \nAjax\n, SQL SERVER 2000\n\nDuration\n: 1 month\n\nDescription\n\nThis is FORUM about license plate any one can register in\n\nto the forum by their email address and post the message with some heading (license no.) , the email notification will send while register and post message. If any one reply to their posting an email notification is send to mail immediately.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n4.\nTitle\n\nPregnancy Calendar \n(BrillBaby.com)\n\nTools Used\n\nASP.NET, C#. NET, \nAjax\n, SQL SERVER 2000\n\nDuration\n: 1 months\n\nDescription\n\nIn this project the pregnant women can register their last \n\nMenstrual date and depending on the current date the child?s current status will be displayed. Also the current status of baby and mom will be displayed. Here no need to enter the date every time, the date enter during registration is stored in cookies and while enter into the site next time will load the current status of baby and mom from depends upon the date in the cookie.\n\n5.\nTitle\n\nRTI-DFD(parsing .txt files)\n\nTools Used\n: VB.net, Ms Access, Crystal Report \n\nDuration\n: 3 months\n\nDescription\n: There are four broadly defined functions to this project:\n\n1.\n      \nImporting (parsing) a text file created by the tab program at RTI-DFD. The file format will be either .txt or .prt.\n2.\n      \nRetrieving specific questions and answer in whole or part from the saved imported data into an organized table in Excel. Once the table is in an Excel table additional tools will help manipulate the data such as re-arranging columns/rows or sorting based on values.\n3.\n      \nAfter the data is in the desired arrangement, pre-defined graphics formats need to be automatically applied if this is to remain a table for reporting purposes. If the table is to be reported as a chart, then the data needs to be incorporated into predefined chart formats in either an Excel chart or a MS Graph chart. \n4.\n      \nReporting - These finished tables and charts need to then be automatically inserted into reports. \n\n6.\nTitle\n\nData Import Tool\n\nTools Used\n\nC#. NET, ASP.NET,SQL SERVER 2000\n\nDuration\n: 3 months\n\nDescription\n\nThis tool is used to parse huge amount of survey details\n\nusing DTS package and store it in a database. Then the survey details are split to corresponding tables. In this the webforms controls are created dynamically based on the table name in the config file also we have a option to INSER, DELETE, UPDATE and VIEW in datagrid by the dynamically created forms.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nPersonal Details\n\n            \n\nI am good at technical, managerial and human relation skills. Quick learner. Highly adaptive to working environments. Will be an effective team member with team spirit. High command of language and Communication skills.\n                                                                                      \nName \n                                    \n             \n\n   \nS. Arunachalam\n\nFather?s Name\n                     \n             \n\n   \nS. Shunmuga Sundram\n\nDate of Birth\n                        \n             \n\n   \n\nth\n Feb, 1983\n\nSex\n                 \n              \n          \n             \n\n   \nMale\n\nMarital Status\n                      \n          \n    \n\n   \nSingle\n\nNationality\n    \n                        \n              \n\n   \nIndian\n\nAddress\n                                \n              \n\n   \n26B,\nII-Issac Street\n                                                             \nNazareth-628617\n                                                             \nTutucorin dist.\nPhone\n                                    \n             \n\n    \n04639-279567,9841681169\n           \n\nHobbies\n                                \n              \n\n    \nPlaying Basket Ball, Playing\n\nCricket,\n                         \n                                                              \nListening music\n                         \n                                  \n                                                                                    \n                                    \n            \n\nDeclaration\n            \n            \nI do hereby declare that the particulars of information and facts stated above are true and correct and complete to the best of my knowledge and belief.\n\nDate:\n                                                \n          \nSignature:\n                \n                                                        \n\nPlace: CHENNAI.\n\n               \n                           \nName:\nARUNACHALAM S',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-18',NULL,'2007-10-18','2010-06-10 12:14:22','2010-06-10',15,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(263,'Archanaba P ',NULL,NULL,NULL,'arcdvdvhandvdva_jhadvdvla@india.com',NULL,'02752 242250','0',NULL,'0',NULL,'0',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2010-06-10 12:14:22',15,'0',NULL,'200710/18/ATT16387.html','200710/18/DOC14019.doc','Parmar Rajen K\nArchanaba P \n\n(B.C.A & M.C.A) Career Profile \nE-mail: \narcdvdvhandvdva_jhadvdvla@india.com\nPhone: (R):02752 242250 \n\nOBJECTIVES\n          \nWork in a challenging environment with total commitment for excellence and with the highest degree of professionalism. \n\nSKILLS\n          \nLanguages\n\n\n        \nC, C++, VC++, JAVA, Core JAVA, VB 6.0, VB.net, COBOL, Fortran, Assembly\n\nDatabase\n\n        \nSQL\n\nMS\n-Access, Oracle, SQL Server, SQL *Plus\nOperating\n\nSystems\n\n\n        \nWindows 9X/2000/XP, DOS 6.0, UNIX\nWeb Designing\n      \n\n        \nASP, ASP.net, HTML, FrontPage\n\n\n        \nGood Analytical Skills with Strong Interpersonal Skills.\n\n        \nAn enthusiastic individual with a Never Say Die Attitude.\n\n        \nGood Listening Ability and Patience.\n\n        \nHardworking.\n\n        \nQuick Learner.\n\n\nExperience\nCompany Name\nNew Tech Computer Centre,\nAndh Vidyalaya Road\n\n2, \nChitrakut\nPark\n\nSurendranagar,\nGujarat\n\nWorking From\n\nAugust 2005 till Date\n\nMy Responsibility :\n\n\n         \nReview of the system requirement specification\n\n         \nPrepare technical application documents\n\n         \nCode review \n\n         \nResponsible for Unit Testing, preparation of Test Cases and helping in System Testing.\n\n1.) Project:\n          \nAnalysis & Maintenance System for Gujarat Education Department\nSoftware:\n             \nAsp.NET with C#\nDatabase:\n           \nSQL Server 2000\n\n2.) Project:\n       \nSystem for Analysis & Maintaining of District Schools\nSoftware:\n             \nVB 6.0 \nDatabase:\n           \nOracle\n\n3.) Project:\n     \nRailway Reservation System\nSoftware:\n             \nASP, HTML\nDatabase:\n           \nOracle\n\nPROJECT DETAILS\nAnalysis & Maintenance System for Gujarat Education Department\nRole\nTeam Leader\nPlatform\nAsp.NET,C#,SQL SERVER 2000\nTeam Size\n\nDescription\n\n\nThis product developed for Gujarat Education Department and is used by\n    \nVarious DEO?s to improve the Education system in \nGujarat\n\n\n\nThrough this system they can search any record or printout any report\n                               \nwithin a minute by pressing one button.\n\n\nInserting the given data.\n\n\nRetrieval of the stored data according to user needs.\n\n\nDeletion of stored information as per the user requests.\n\n\nUpdating the stored information for which user demanding.\n\n\nChecking integrity rules.\n\n\nThe system will create various reports in well designed format which\n                              \ncan be printed out on A4 size paper.\n\n       \n\n\nSystem for Analysis & Maintaining of District Schools\nRole\nTeam Member\nPlatform\nVB 6.0, Oracle\nTeam Size\n\nDescription\n\n\nThis product developed for District Education office Surendranagar, and\n                                  \nis used by\n   \nDEO?s of S.nagar to improve the Education system in S.nagar.\n\n\nThrough this system they can search any record or printout any report\n                               \nwithin a minute by pressing one button.\n\n\nInserting the given data.\n\n\nRetrieval of the stored data according to user needs.\n\n\nDeletion of stored information as per the user requests.\n\n\nUpdating the stored information for which user demanding.\n\n\nChecking integrity rules.\n\n\nThe system will create various reports in well designed format which\n                         \n     \ncan be printed out on A4 size paper.\n         \n\n\nRailway Reservation System \nRole\nTeam Member\nPlatform\nAsp, HTML, Oracle\nTeam Size\n\nDescription\n\n\nThis product is developed for Online Reservation System.\n\n\nThrough this system one can get the information about the Indian Railway.\n\n\n\nBooked the ticket, can cancel the booked ticket, pay online for ticket, even\n                                 \ncan takeout the printout of their ticket any where from world.\n                                                       \n                                                      \n\n\nOne can know what is the status of their ticket such as waiting number,\n                               \nRAC number etc.\n\nACADEMICS\n                                                                        \nExamination\n\nSchool/college\nBoard/\nUniversity\nYear of Passing\n\n\nMCA\nIndira Gandhi National Open University\n(IGNOU)\nIndira Gandhi National Open University\n(IGNOU)\n2007\nWaiting \nfor Result\nADCA\n\n(IGNOU)\n\n(IGNOU)\n2006\n58.92%\nPGDCA\n\n\nIGNOU)\n\n(IGNOU)\n2006\n60.67%\nBCA\nC. U. Shah College of Comm. Mang. & Comp. Edu.\nSaurashtra\nUniversity\n2003\n55.33%\nH.S.C.\nR. P. P. Girls? High School, Surendranagar\nG.H.S.E.B\n\n2000\n68.83%\nS. S. C\nR. P. P. Girls? High School, Surendranagar\nG.S.E.B.\n1998\n69.29%\n          \n\n\nPERSONAL DETAILS\n               \nAddress\nH/99,\nG.I.D.C. Housing Plots,\nWadhwan\nCity\n ? 363035,\nDist.: Surendranagar.\nGujarat\n\n               \nDate of birth\n\nth\n July 1983.\n               \nGender\nFemale.\n               \nNationality\nIndian.\n\n\n\nDeclaration:\n                       \nI hereby declare that the above-mentioned information is correct up to my knowledge and I bear the responsibility for the correctness of the above-mentioned particulars.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n(Archana Jhala)',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-18',NULL,'2007-10-18','2010-06-10 12:14:22','2010-06-10',15,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(264,'Anpur sunil',NULL,NULL,NULL,'sufbfdbnil.nrdfbfdbpt@gmail.com','sunil.nrpt@gmail.com','09886355743','0','09886355743','0','91 9886355743','0','2007-01-28',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-10 12:14:22',15,'0',NULL,'200710/18/ATT16388.html','200710/18/DOC14021.doc','Resdex @ naukri.com\nAnpur Sunil\nBangalore \nsufbfdbnil.nrdfbfdbpt@gmail.com\n\nTelephone: 09886355743\n(M)\n\nD.O.B\n - 15 Jan 1982 \nModified on\n - 26 Sep 2007 \nAnnual Salary\n - INR 3 Lac(s) 20 Thousand \nTotal Years of Experience\n - 3 Year(s) 2 Month(s) \nCurrent Location\n - Bangalore \nPreferred Location\n - Anywhere in India \nM.Sc(IT) with 3+ years of experience in Dotnet platform\n\nTEXT RESUME \n\nANPUR SUNIL\nMobile\n: +91-9886355743 Email: sunil.nrpt@gmail.com\nPROFESSIONAL SUMMARY\n· 3+ years of experience as a Software Developer in MS .Net Technologies.\n· Good experience in ASP.Net, C#.Net, VB.Net.\n· Hands on experience in Web based and Windows based Application.\n· Extensive Hands-on Experience in Database Connectivity using ADO.Net.\n· Database skills with SQL Server.\n· Flexibility and adaptability in regards with new technologies and\nenvironments.\nEDUCATION DETAILS\n· Master of Science in Information Technology from Dr B.A.M University, \nAurangabad\n\n· Bachelor of Science in Computers from \nOsmania\nUniversity\n\nHyderabad\n\nPROFESSIONAL EXPERIENCE\n· Working as a Software Engineer for BMC Software, \nBangalore\n from Oct 2006 to till date.\n· Worked as a Software Engineer for Sritech Solutions, \nHyderabad\n from May 2004 to Sep 2006.\nSKILLS\nMicrosoft Technologies : ASP.Net, VB.Net, C#.Net, ADO.Net.\nOperating Systems : Windows98/2000/XP.\nWeb Tools : ASP.NET, XML, HTML, JavaScript.\nWeb Server : IIS.\nDatabases : \nMS-SQLServer\n\nMS\n-Access.\nLanguages : C, C++.\nScripting Technology : Java Script.\nPROJECTS\n#1. Project : \nEnterprise\n Resource Planning.\nRole : Developer.\nEnvironment : Winforms, C#, Sql Server 2000.\nDescription:\nThis is a windows based project. This project is broadly classified into different modules such as Sales, Purchase, HR, Stores, Customer Support and Accounts Modules. The HR Module comprises of generation of pay slip, managing leave account and generating leave forms. The Sales module deals with the details of the customers, Advances and invoice details. The Stores deals with the details of Item details, Indent, Purchase order, ordertovendors, materials issue entry, work orders, stock position. The Purchase module covered by this system include Vendor details, material details, Tender sorting, Purchase releasing etc. The Accounts Module details with the maintenance of transaction such as Sales, Purchase, and Bank. The Customer Support details with the customer complaints and tracking of complaints. For all the Modules, necessary reports are generated.\nResponsibilities:\nü Database connectivity through ADO.NET.\nü Coding and debugging.\nü Involved in Validations.\nü Involved in Unit Testing.\nü Creating a user friendly GUI.\nü Write stored procedures using SQL Server.\n#2. Project : Ventures Online Portal.\nRole : Software Engineer.\nEnvironment : ASP.Net, C#, Sql Server,IIS 5.0.\nDescription:\nThis portal provides unique facility to common people to search for commercial and Residential properties. In Builders point of view, Builders can register and utilize services like Add, Modified and Delete their ventures. Builders can add their Venture information like about Upload Building plans Elevations Location maps and us for each Venture. Builders Registrations are of Classic, Executive and gold based on Builders have to pay some service charge in the form of Check, DD etc. Once they registered with this system they have to pay services charges according to type of category selected then only they are allowed to post their details into this portal and also this portal provide common features like knowledge Bank, Software, E-Services and so on.\nResponsibilities:\nü Coding and debugging.\nü Involved in Validations.\nü Involved in Resolving Issues.\nü Designing of pages.\nü Involved in Unit Testing.\nü Involved in Code Review.\n#3. Project : Clinical Management Center.\nRole : Developer.\nEnvironment : Winforms, C#, Sql Server, Crystal Reports.\nDescription:\nThis project is used of maintaining the patient related information. By this project Patient Registration at the starting entry to Hospital, After the Registration, then we maintains the type of patient i.e. either Outdoor or Indoor and at what time the appointment is allotted to him. The Doctors report entry about the patient. In this either the patient required operation or not, if required, type of Operation. Billing, Delivery details etc.\nResponsibilities:\nü Communicating with database.\nü Involved in Coding and debugging.\nü Involved in designing of pages.\nü Generation of Reports using crystal reports.\nü Involved in Validations.\nü Involved in Unit Testing.\n#4. Project : Project Administration.\nRole : Developer.\nEnvironment : ASP.Net, VB.Net, Sql Server, IIS 5.0.\nDescription:\nThis project helps the company to track the projects undertaken by them. The project helps to enter all the details of the project such as the list of the members who will be involved in the project along with the activities they are to perform within a particular duration of time. At any time of the project the status of the work allocated to a particular user can be tracked along with the name of the project, its subject and the name of the user to whom it is allocated. Any changes requested by the customer can also be incorporated into the project.\nResponsibilities:\nü Involved in Coding and debugging.\nü Designing of pages.\nü Involved in Unit Testing.',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-18',NULL,'2007-10-18','2010-06-10 12:14:22','2010-06-10',15,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(265,'Ankur Bajhal Jain E',NULL,NULL,NULL,'ankurbajhal@rediffmail.com','nkurbwegtwertwetajhal@gmail.com','07692 220406','0','9890307764','0',NULL,'0','2008-04-29',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-10 12:14:22',15,'0',NULL,'200710/18/ATT16389.html','200710/18/DOC14023.doc','ANKUR BAJHAL JAIN E-MAIL: ankurbajhal@rediffmail.com\nAnkur Bajhal Jain\n                                       \n         \n              \n                   \n             \nEMAIL\n\n\nnkurbwegtwertwetajhal@gmail.com\n\n\n\n\n                                \n                \n                                                   \n                             \nContact\n: 9890307764(M)\n               \nKumar Samruddhi,\nNear Tingre Nagar Petrol Pump,\nVishrantwadi\nPune\n                                                              \n               \n\nCARRIER OBJECTIVE\n\n\n                                      \n\nI immensely value self-development and personal growth. I adapt well in new situation and like to interact with people. I am open to learning from my mistakes. My strengths are resilience and objective orient- ness. My greatest asset is my will power and devotion towards objective. The greatest satisfaction to me is a job done perfectly.\n\nSUMMARY\n\n\n        \nBE in Computer Science.\n     \nMicrosoft .NET-connected CRM product suite (MSCRM).\nMajor Skill Sets: ASP. Net, C, C++, C#,\n\nHTML, MSSQL.\n\nSKILL SETS\n\nRDBMS\n                                 \n\n\nMS SQL Server 2000\nInternet Technologies\n         \n\n ASP.Net, HTML, XML,\nInternet Languages\n             \n\n VBScript and JavaScript\nFront Ends \n                           \n\n Visual Basic 6.0, ASP.Net\nProgramming Languages\n    \n\n C, C++, C#\nOperating Systems\n              \n\n Windows NT, Windows 95, 98, 2000, XP\nERP SYSTEM\n                      \n: MSCRM\n\nSELF PROFILE\n      \n           \nI immensely value self-development and personal growth. I adapt well in new situation and like to interact with people. I am open to learning from my mistakes. My strengths are resilience and objective orient- ness. My greatest asset is my will power and devotion towards objective. The greatest satisfaction to me is a job done perfectly.\n\nWork Experience:\n\nCurrent Employer\n      \n\n\nSunflower Information Technologies Pvt. Ltd.\nFrom - To -\n                 \n\n\nDecember 26, 2005\n\n? Till Date\nDesignation\n                \n\n\nSoftware Engineer.\n\nProject Name\n\n: Document Management System\nTeam Size\n       \n: 4\n\nFront End\n              \n\nASP. Net,\n HTML, JavaScript\nBack End\n               \n\nC#.Net\nDatabase\n                \n\nVisual Studio 2005, Sql Server Express Edition 2005.\nProject Details\nDMS is a simple document management system for maintaining electronic files. This consists of all the basic functionalities like category management, document upload, assigning permissions for user to upload document, download\n\nmanagement etc.\nContribution\n         \n\n      \nDesigned the HLD for the same\n\n      \nDeveloped the class architecture for the retrieving values from database.\n\n      \nDeveloped the Business logic.\n\n      \nDeveloped the document upload form to maintain the user permissions.\n\n      \nDeveloped role based access functionality\n\n\n\nProject Name\n\n: Electronic Claims Processing\nTeam Size\n       \n: 7\n\nFront End\n              \n\nASP. Net,\n HTML, JavaScript\nBack End\n               \n\nC#.Net\nDatabase\n                \n\nVisual Studio 2005, Sql Server Express Edition 2005.\n\nAjax\nProject Details\nECP is related to the claim billing based on the HCFA 1500 standards. This is claim processing system. It takes the inputs from the user based on the those inputs and procedures (policy Numbers) the claims are processed and checked for the payments.\nContribution\n         \n\n      \nImplement the master page concept.\n\n      \nDesigned the template base UI as per the Client?s requirement.\n\n      \nDeveloped the Tree View and developed the various categories like Medicaid and Medicare.\n\n      \nDeveloped the input forms from the application.\n\n\n\nProject Name\n\n: eShoes Online (ASPDotNetStoreFront 6.0 ML)\nTeam Size\n       \n: 3\n\nFront End\n              \n\nASP. Net,\n HTML, JavaScript\nBack End\n               \n\nVB.Net,\nDatabase\n                \n\nSql Server Express Edition 2005.\n\nAjax\nProject Details\neShoes Online is a eCommerce project. It deals with selling of the variety of shoes. This project has been developed by using ASPDTSF .It perform all the basic functionality like selling shoes, selecting product. All the payments are done online using credit payments and Pay Pal .\nContribution\n         \n\n      \nDesigned the template base UI as per the Client?s requirement.\n\n      \nCustomized the Admin section of the project for adding related products in the project.\n\n      \nCustomized the image display at various stages of the projects.\n\n      \nImplemented the search screen for the products.\n\n\nProject Name\n\n\nEMS\n (Emergency Medical Services)\nTeam Size\n       \n: 8\n\n\nFront End\n              \n\nASP. Net.\n HTML, JavaScript\nBack End\n               \n\nC#\nDatabase\n                \n\nSql Server 2000.\nThird Party Controls (.Dlls)\nAjax\nProject Details\nEMS\n is an online medical service provider, which provides the online medical service to the users as doctors, hospitals. \nEMS\n maintains the record of all the incidents those occurs along the patient details and the medical services provided to those patients. It maintains all the basic billing of charges along with the primary aid charges and the ambulance charges.\nContribution\n         \n\n      \nDesigned the time sheet entry of the Incident along with the Incident Details.\n\n\n      \nDesign and developed the \nauthentication based role for the Patient details and billing.\n\n\n      \nPerform the various form type of validation as per the clients requirement.\n\n\nPrevious Employer\n     \n\n\nzSyndicate Software?s (Ignify Inc.)\nFrom - To -\n                 \n\n\nMarch 2005 ? \nDecember 23, 2005\nDesignation\n                \n\n\nSoftware Engineer.\n\nProject Name\n             \n\n\nAll Language Systems (ALS Inc.)\nTeam Size\n                   \n: 8\n\n\nFront End\n              \n\nASP. Net.\n HTML, JavaScript\nBack End\n               \n\nC#\nDatabase\n                \n\nSql Server 2000.\nProject Details\nALS is a mid sized \nERP\n based project. This project is developed on \nMSCRM\n platform using ASP.Net. ALTIMS provides the complex calculation of charges depending on the time. This system provides the generation of the invoices for the particular order. Those orders can be mailed to the particular client and can be faxed through this system.\nContribution\n         \n\n      \nDesign and Implementation of business objects and front-end. Implement the Business Logic for the Finalize Order and the Class for calculating the surcharges. Developed the stored procedures for updating and saving the finalized values. Designed the various API?s for data serializes to XML for consumption by the application. Implement the various merged code\n\n\n      \nDesign and developed the \nSearch Screen\n for the ALTIMS. Designed the various \nstored procedures\n for the search screens. Developed the validations using java script. Developed the C# code to manipulate the data with \ndatagrid\n\n\n\n      \nDesign and developed the various reports as purchase orders, letters, emails by using the \nCUBIZZ Software\n and merged codes using \nOmnirush\n Software.\n\nPrevious Employer\n     \n\n\nPDSYS Technologies Pvt. Ltd\nFrom - To -\n                 \n\n\nSeptember 2004 ? March 2005\nDesignation\n                \n\n\nTrainee Software Engineer.\n\n\nPROJECT\n                  \n\n\nOnline Classroom Study (Teachers Pal. Inc).\nTeam Size\n                   \n: 9\n\n\nFront End\n              \n\nASP. Net.\n HTML, JavaScript\nBack End\n               \n\nC#\nDatabase\n                \n\nSql Server 2000.\nThird Party Controls Used\nRad Tree View.\nUltra Web Controls.\nContribution\n         \nDesigned the various wizards for making the Reports on students. Also involved in the database designing and using the stored procedures. The major role is as a \nC# developer\n. This is implemented using \nASP.Net\n and \nCrystal\n reports\n\n\n\nEDUCATIONAL DETAILS\n\nDegree\n                         \n                          \n  \nUniversity\n                                           \n                \nPercentage\n\nB.E (Computer Sc.)\n               \n   \nVisveshwaraiah Technological\n         \n     \n                         \n      \n59.40%\n   \nUniversity, \nBelgaum\n       \n    \n(Karnataka)\n    \n\nH.S.S.C\n                                   \n   \nMadhya Pradesh Board\n                                                   \n      \n60.81%\n                                                \n   \nBhopal\n (M.P)\n\nS.S.C.\n                      \n\n              \n   \nMadhya Pradesh Board,\n                                                  \n      \n64.29%\n                                                                \n   \nBhopal\n (M.P.)\n\nPERSONAL DETAILS\nDate of Birth\n                        \n\n   \n30th Jan 1981\nSex\n                                         \n\n   \nMale\nNationality\n                            \n\n   \nIndian\nPermanent Address\n            \n\n  \nS/o Mr. S.K.Jain,\n                                     \n           \n    \nNear Big \nJain\nTemple\n\nMahaveer Ward, Seoni,\nDist.Seoni (M.P.) 480 661\n                                \n                \n    \nPhone No. (07692) 220406',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-18',NULL,'2007-10-18','2010-06-10 12:14:22','2010-06-10',15,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(266,'Bhagwan Das',NULL,NULL,NULL,'ddsvdvvas.bdvdvhagdvdvdvwan@gmail.com','das.bhagwan@gmail.com','91 0512 2408190','0','09313163378','0','919313163378','0','2008-04-29',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-10 12:14:22',15,'0',NULL,'200710/18/ATT16390.html','200710/18/DOC14024.doc','Resdex @ naukri.com\nbhagwan das\nC-266 Pandav Nagar New delhi New Delhi - 110092 \nddsvdvvas.bdvdvhagdvdvdvwan@gmail.com\n\nTelephone: 09313163378\n(M)\n 91 0512 2408190\n(R)\n\nD.O.B\n - 20 Jul 1982 \nModified on\n - 26 Sep 2007 \nAnnual Salary\n - INR 1 Lac(s) 80 Thousand \nTotal Years of Experience\n - 2 Year(s) 0 Month(s) \nCurrent Location\n - Delhi \nPreferred Location\n - Anywhere in Northern India \nMCA with 2 years and 0 months experiance in dot net technology\n\nTEXT RESUME \n\nBHAGWAN DAS\nMob. :- +919313163378 Address: C-266, ground floor\nEmail:- das.bhagwan@gmail.com Pandav Nagar New Delhi-110092\nSUMMARY: -I am MCA (2005) with 68.20% Marks and have 2+ year of experience in Software Development in Microsoft Technology (ASP.Net, C#.Net, VB.Net, Sql Server)\nCAREER OBJECTIVE\nSeeking a position to utilize my skills and abilities in information technology industry that offers security and professional growth while being resourceful, innovative and flexible.\nWORKING EXPERIENCE\n\n Working as a Software Developer in A1technology Pvt Ltd Gurgaon (A Leading USA based Software Company, MNC) from 22 Feb 2007.\n\n Worked as a Software Engineer in Nagsoft Soloution Pvt.Ltd \nDelhi\n From 25 OCT 2006 to 15 Feb 2007.\n\n Worked As a Software Programmer in NIC (National Informatics Centre) CGO Complex Lodhi road New Delhi from 18 July 2005 to 20 OCT 2006\nINDUSTRIALTRAINING\n\n Worked as a Software trainee under the last Semester project in NHPC (National Hydroelectric power corporation Ltd) Faridabad from 01 Feb 2005 to 31 May 2005\n\n Worked as a Software trainee under the summer training program in H.A.L. (Hindustan Aeronautic Limited) Kanpur, from 28th June 2004 to 24th July 2004.\nPROJECTS UNDERTAKEN\n1.IndiaTVNews:(URL:-http://www.planitwithus.com/indiatvnews/index.aspx) This software is used to keep records of the program name, Start Time, End Time. It contains Live TV, Archives, Anchors, Programs, and weekly Shows. There are 3 modules\n1.CMS Section:This section contains all the class files there are 7 classes each for a level and a DAL class, connection class, Universal class (level Universal), Link Validate class.\n2. Admin Section:This section used to enter the data to the database.It contains three sections\n2.1 Site Architecture:This section is used to set the property of the data according to Structure\n2.2 Banner Section:This contains the Entry page of banner.We can Add,Edit & delete Banner 2.3 Program:This contains Program name,Starttime, Endtime with Add,Edit & Delete options.\n3.User Section:Each page contains Five Common Controls\n3.1.Banner top:This control contains a Header banner according to the conditions.\n3.2.Menu upper:This Control contain the link of common Pages\n3.3.Left Menu:This Control shows the links to inside pages\n3.4.User poll:This control has an ASP page.\n3.5.Lower Menu:This is same as upper menu accept the conditions are differ\nTeam Members : Two\nSoftware Language s: ASP.NET (using C#. net) With SQL Server 2000\nClient :IndiaTvNews Delhi\nRole and Responsibility: Managing database, Asp.NET, Java Script, HTML, DHTML\n2. MYDhan:(URL:-http://www.Mydhan.com)\nThis software is used to provide the customer; clarity in terms of the right products to purchase that will fulfill the financial requirements. It helps the user to pursue the long-term financial goal. It also provides the information about maximizing the return on investments while reducing risk and also inflation-proof of investment income. The application is an independent advisor of insurance and mutual fund products.\nThe application is divided in two sections\nAdmin Section: The admin can add edit and delete the information of the application.\nUser Section: user can register himself and get the information about his investment.\nTeam Members : Two\nSoftware Languages: ASP .NET (using C#. net) with SQL Server 2000\nRole : Analysis, Design, Coding\n3. Personnel Information System :( http://Delserve/PIS/loginpassword.aspx)\nThis software is related to \nNational\nInformatics\nCenter\n. PIS keep the information like personnel details, academic details, salary details, previous postings, and training of the employees of the ministry. Details of the employees are needed for performance appraisal and number of leaves availed\nDue to the static nature of this setup further modification or updation of the information was difficult. To overcome this problem, this system is being planned. This will make the entire processing dynamic, fast and accurate. There are 5 modules in this project\n\n Admin Module:-This Module Contains Employees Details, Employees Education, Employees family and Employ training\n\n Transfer Module:-It Contain Employees Transfer, Employees reliving, Employees joining\n\n Master Entry Module:- This Module Contains Employees Department, Employees Designation, Employees Language, Employees Category, Employees Religion\n\n Leave Module:-This Contains Employees leave demand, Employees Leave approval\n\n Increment Module:-Contains Employees Increment yearly,Employees Increment monthly\nTeam Members : two\nSoftware Languages: ASP.Net (using VB.Net) with SQL Server 2000\nClient : National Informatics Center Delhi\nRole : Analysis, Design, Coding\n4.PayGini: In almost every big organization, managing people and resources have been a difficult task. For organizations with more than hundred or thousands of employees, managing each employee\n?s details, loans and advances, attendance, multiple shifts and overtime etc., is impossible without an efficient system. The proposed solution, named as ?PayGini? software package. There are 5 modules in this project\n\n Manage Employee and Company Details\n\n Manage Loans and Advances\n\n Manage Attendance, Multiple Shifts & Over Time\n\n Company Policy Database\n\n Future Modules: This contains payroll system to include PF, ESI, TDS, & Leave Rules\nTeam Members : three\nSoftware Languages: C#.Net with SQL Server 2000\nClient : National Informatics Center\nRole : Analysis, Design, Coding\nEDUCATION\nProfessional Qualification: MCA (2005) from \n?Havard Institute of Management\n\nTechnology Greater Noida (Affiliated to U.P.Technical\nUniversity, Lucknow). (Aggregate 68.20% marks).\nAcademic Qualification: B.Sc. (MATHS, CHEMISTRY) with 55.78%\nFrom \nC.S.J.M\nUniversity\n\nKanpur\n in 2001.\nIntermediate from H.N Inter College, \nKanpur\nU.\n P. Board with 71.20% in 1998.\nHigh School from V.N. Inter College, \nKanpur\nU.\n P. Board with 73.67% in 1996.\nSOFTWARE SKILLS\nOperating System : Window 9x /2000/XP\nProgramming Languages : ASP.NET, C#.NET, VB.NET, ASP 3.0, V.B, C, C++\nRDBMS : Sql Server 2000, MS-Access, Oracle 8i/9i\nWeb Technology : HTML, DHTML, Xml\nCOURSES UNDERTAKEN\n\n Hardware Course: Five-Weeks Certificate Course in \n?Computer Hardware Maintenance\n & Networking\n? from SISI (Small Industries Service Institute) Kanpur\n\n Accounting Package: Four-Weeks Certificate Course in \n?Business Ac\ncounting Professional\n? from SISI (Small Industries Service Institute), Kanpur.\nPERSONAL DETAILS\nFather\n?s Name\n : Shri Surya Bali\nPermanent Address : 110 \n?A? Safipur 1st Harjender Nagar\nKanpur 208007 (U.P) Tel.no: - 0512-2408190\nDate of Birth : 20 July 1982\nSex : Male\nMarital Status : Single\nNationality : Indian\nLanguages Known : English, Hindi\nHobbies : Playing Chess, Net Surfing & Making new friends\nACHIVEMENT\n\n Participated in \n?Akhil Bharti Sanskrit Gyan Pariksha? in Kanpur. and got 66% marks, reward a\nnd Certificate\n\n Participated in \n?Bharti Sikshan Mandal, Kanpur? and got third rank\n & Certificate in G.K\nSTRENGTHS\n\n Manageable and can work in any condition\n\n Responsible and teamwork spirit\n\n Analytical skill and hard working\nDECLARATION\nI hereby declare that information furnished above is to best of my knowledge and belief.\nDate: / /\nPlace: Bhagwan Das',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-18',NULL,'2007-10-18','2010-06-10 12:14:22','2010-06-10',15,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(267,'Balaji Rj',NULL,NULL,NULL,'rjbalsdvadvdsvdsvji79@rediffmail.com',NULL,NULL,'0','09900392561','0',NULL,'0','2003-04-30',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-10 12:14:22',15,'0',NULL,'200710/18/ATT16391.html','200710/18/DOC14025.doc','Resdex @ naukri.com\nBalaji RJ\nBangalore \nrjbalsdvadvdsvdsvji79@rediffmail.com\n\nTelephone: 09900392561\n(M)\n\nD.O.B\n - 03 May 1979 \nModified on\n - 26 Sep 2007 \nAnnual Salary\n - INR 15 Lac(s) 0 Thousand \nTotal Years of Experience\n - 7 Year(s) 6 Month(s) \nCurrent Location\n - Bangalore \nPreferred Location\n - United States \nTech Architect with H1 Visa Approval + MCAD and PSP/TSP Certified',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-18',NULL,'2007-10-18','2010-06-10 12:14:22','2010-06-10',15,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(268,'Bhavtosh Bhushan Bhardwaj',NULL,NULL,'Pune ','b3dvdsv_jdvdvvdob@LiveForBest.com',NULL,NULL,'0','9890 958 736','0',NULL,'0','2006-12-13',8,23,'2010-06-10 12:14:22',15,'0',NULL,'200710/18/ATT16392.html','200710/18/DOC14026.doc','BHAVTOSH BHUSHAN BHARDWAJ\nBhavtosh Bhushan Bhardwaj\nB. Tech. (Computer Engineering & I.T.)\nCurrent Add\n   \n\n\nFlat # A3/11 Hermes Heritage Phase 2, Shastri Nagar, Pune-14\nE-mail\n             \n\n\nb3dvdsv_jdvdvvdob@LiveForBest.com\nMobile\n                        \n\n\n\n9890-958-736\nD.O.B\n             \n\n\nJan. 1\nst\n 1980\n\nRESUME SUMMARY:-\n\n\n        \nExperience\n   \n\n 3+ year?s software application development experience in .\nNET\n Technologies.\n\n        \nTechnologies: \nWorked extensively for web application development using \nAjax\n 1.0, C#,\n\n                       \n        \nASP.\nNET\n(C#, VB.\nNET\n), JavaScript and SQL SERVER 2000, T-SQL.\n\n        \nOther skills\n\n\nStrong debugging, BACK-END/FRONT-END programming, DATABASE \n   \n     \nAdministration and optimization skills. Implemented SECURITY \n     \n        \nSETTINGS in the \n    \ndeveloped web applications.\n-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nTECHNICAL SKILLS EXPOSED TO\n\n\nNET\n Technology:\nVB.Net, C#, ASP. Net, \nADO\n.Net, Web Services, WPF,WCF,WWF, Visual Studio 2003, Visual Studio 2005\nWeb Technologies\nAjax\n 1.0, MS-Commerce Server 2000, \nHTML, XML, JavaScript, ASP (VB-Script)\nMS-SQL Server 2000:\nT-SQL, \nStored Procedures, Views, Triggers, XML Support, Indexes, Administration, Data Transformation Service (DTS), Optimizing Database Performance\nOther Programming Languages:\nC, C++, VB6, PL/SQL and Java\nOperating Systems\n\nWINDOWS 98,XP,2000\nOthers:\nAction Script (FLASH), Knowledge of Search Engine Optimization Techniques\n-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nPROFESSIONAL EXPERIENCE\n\nOrganization:\n -Irus Software Applications Pvt. Ltd., Pune\n       \n            \n                        \n            \nDec 2006 ---Till Date\nDesignation: - \nSoftware Engineer\n1.\n Project\n: SalesX (Desktop application and Web Version of Product)\n                  \nClient: -\n Product of the company\n                                                         \n         \n   \n       \nDuration: -\n\nDec: 2006- Till date\nRole & Responsibilities: - \nProgrammer, Team Member\nTechnology: - \nAjax 1.0, C#, ASP.\nNET\n\nADO\n.Net, SQL Server 2000, Visual Studio.Net2003 & 2005, XML, Infragistics controls\nDescription:\n\n A product of the company used for selling the products online on eBay by uploading through the application interface. It uses APIs provided from eBay to upload and manage uploaded items at eBay. Items of seller to be sold are stored in Everest Database from which application takes all the information of the items before uploading to eBay. Applications interact with Everest database to get the information of the items which can be uploaded as well as gets the information of the uploaded items from eBay, like the item status(sold , unsold, selling), customer?s feed back, upload listing fee etc. Applications also give the report of items depending upon different criteria.\nOrganization:\n - Sobha Renaissance IT Pvt. Ltd., \nBangalore\n            \n                 \n\n          \nFeb 2006 --- Dec 2006\nDesignation: - \nSoftware Engineer\n2.\n Project\n\nwww.banddigs.com\n\n                       \nClient: -\n Exstreme Solutions, \nU.S.A.\n                                                    \n            \n    \nDuration: -\n\nJune: 2006- Dec 2006\nRole & Responsibilities: - \nProgrammer, Team Member, Client interaction\nTechnology: - \nMS-Commerce Server, C#, ASP.\nNET\n\nADO\n.Net, SQL Server 2000, Visual Studio.Net, XML\nDescription:\n\n An e-commerce website for musical Bands, Fans, Corporate buddies or musical groups, Professionals in musical industry and related market and Industries. Application having the functionalities of user registration, profile editing, user search, dynamic home page publishing, personalization of home page, shopping cart. In personalization section the registered user can upload pictures and videos to be displayed on his home page and at other relevant pages after which they can preview their home page before publishing and on publishing their personalized settings are reflected in their published home page, which is then available to other users.\n\n3.\n\nProject\n\nwww.webhut.com.au\n\n                     \nClient: -\n WEBHUT, \nAustralia\n                                                  \n            \n    \nDuration: -\n\nFeb: 2006-May: 2006\nRole & Responsibilities: - \nProgrammer, Debugging, Enhancements, Project Deployment\nTechnology: - \nC#, ASP.\nNET\n\nADO\n.Net, SQL Server 2000, Visual Studio.Net\nDescription:\n\n A website of a web hosting Company which allows for direct sale and sale through call center agents of the WEBHUT. It sells different types of website packages at various rates. It has the functionality of checking dynamically the existence of domain names and domain registration processes.\n\nOrganization:\n - VSM Software Pvt. Ltd., \nBangalore\n   \n           \n             \n            \n           \nSept 2005 ---Feb 2006\nDesignation: - \nSoftware Engineer\n4.\n\nProject\n\nStudent Program Management System \nClient: -\n IIM, \nBangalore\n                                                                      \n            \n      \nDuration: -\n\nOct: 2005-Feb: 2006\nRole & Responsibilities: - \nProgrammer, Group Leader\nTechnology: - \nC#, ASP.\nNET\n\nADO\n.Net, SQL Server 2000, Visual Studio.Net\nDescription:\n\n An Intranet based Management system with access limitations to Administrative Level and concerned staff. This Management System that keeps the record of students registered Different programs available at the Institute, programs allotted to students, class/section details, all the academic details of all the batches per programm\ne. This automates and simplifies the functionality of record keeping and student management task, related to the concerned students & programs.\n\n5.\n\nProject\n\nSidus Performance System\nClient: -\n Sidus Infotech, \nBangalore\n                                                       \n            \n      \nDuration: -\n\nSep: 2005-Oct: 2005\nRole & Responsibilities: - \nProgrammer\n, Bug Fixing\nTechnology: - \nVB.Net, \nADO\n.Net, SQL Server 2000, Visual Studio.Net\nDescription\n: - \nAn Employee performance system which stores generates and calculates employee weekly, monthly and annually reports based on the employees performance which takes into consideration like (time taken for the task, estimated time, and other criteria depending upon the department of the employee.\n\nOrganization:\n - Alien SoftNet Technologies Pvt. Ltd., \nDelhi\n              \n          \n     \n          \nJune 2004 ---Aug 2005\nDesignation: - \nSoftware Developer\n6.\n\nProject\n\nPocket PC Application\n\nClient: -\n Ilium \nSoftware\n\nUSA\n                                                  \n            \nDuration: -\n\nMay: 2005?July: 2005\nRole & Responsibilities: - \nProgrammer\nTechnology: - \nC#, Fash6 for Pocket PC, Visual Studio.Net\nDescription: - \nThe application developed was intended to enhance the functionality of the pocket PC by introducing extra facilities through the application. \nThe features which were introduced through application and on which work was performed included \nFour Alarms, Analog and Digital Clock interfaces, Four Timers, World Clock.\n7.\n\nProject\n\nWenzohou Mgmt. System\nClient: -\n Wenzohou Chemical Regaents Co. Ltd, \nSpain\n                        \n            \n\nDuration: -\n\nOct: 2004 ?April: 2005\nRole & Responsibilities: -\nModule Leader, Programmer\nTechnology: - \nAsp.net (C#), \nADO\n.net, JavaScript, SQL Server 2000\nDescription: -\nAn Intranet based Record Management System with access limitations to Managerial level and Operation Level. The Management system included the modules: \nEnquiry module, Stock Module, Service Record Module and Client Record Module\n (payment, contract and Client-Info sub modules).\nIt contained the capabilities of keeping details (viz. Enquiry, Product, Service, Stock, etc.), expiration notification of customer contract, report generation, renewal of contract, Bill Payment Records, etc.\n\n8.\n\nProject\n\nwww.alfabetaindia.com\nClient: -\n Beeta Educational consultancy Pvt. Ltd.)\n        \n                        \n           \nDuration: -\n\nJune: 2004 ? Sep: 2004)\nRole & Responsibilities: - \nProgrammer, Team Member\nTechnology: - \nAsp.net (C#), \nADO\n.net, Flash, JavaScript, SQL Server 2000\nDescription: - \nA fully functional website of the Educational Consultancy which has various University links to fulfill the educational needs of students.\n\n-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nEDUCATIONAL QUALIFICATION\n\nQUALIFICATION\nUNIVERSITY / BOARD\nPERCENTAGE \nB. Tech. (Computer Engg. & IT)\nU.P.\nTechnical\nUniversity\n\nLucknow\n65%\nAISSCE (XII)\nC.B.S.E.\n73% (PCM 80%)\nAISSE (X)\nC.B.S.E.\n63%\n\nVocational Training and Projects: -\nSummer training: - BSNL \nTelephone Exchange on working, fault diagnosis, call switching and \nWLL\n Technology Basics.\nSeminar delivered on (\nVII\n Sem) - \nC# & .\nNET\n technology.\nMy\n Strengths:\n Practical, positive thinker, belief in miracles with proper effort and time utilization, self starter, fast learner.\n\n\n\n\nBHAVTOSH BHUSHAN BHARDWAJ','Irus Software Applications Pvt. Ltd',1,NULL,'2007-10-18',NULL,'2007-10-18','2010-06-10 12:14:22','2010-06-10',15,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(269,'Balachandar R',NULL,NULL,'Banglore',NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL,'0',NULL,'0','2007-12-13',8,25,'2010-06-10 12:14:22',15,'0',NULL,'200710/18/ATT16393.html','200710/18/DOC14027.doc','RAVINDRAN S SUBRAMANIAM\n\nOBJECTIVE\n\nTo work with an organization, where I will have the opportunity to learn and apply my technical skills and have the opportunity to develop in-depth knowledge of the software development life cycle.\n\nSkills Summary\n\n\n          \nStrong Application Developer with 2.2 years of experience in developing and implementing enterprise applications using \nVISUAL BASIC 6.0, \nC#, VB.NET, ADO.NET, ASP.NET\n\nwith databases like \nSQL Server 2000\n\nMS ACCESS\n and IIS 5.0.\n\n\n          \nExperience in designing \nuser interface\n\nwindows forms, web forms and database access\n in \nthree-tier environment\n\n\n\n          \nWorked in \nRDBMS environment \nand experience in database management in SQL Server.\n\n\n          \nUnderstanding of various phases of software development life cycle.\n\n\n          \nHas good communication and interpersonal skills, capability to learn fast and assume any responsibilities.\n\n\n          \nAbility to work well in a team and manage multiple projects at the same time. \n\n\n          \nHighly competent in Software design, development lifecycle, feasibility through testing and implementation. \n\n\nEDUCATION\n\nB.TECH (Computer Science)\n from \nVELLORE INSTITUTE OF TECHNOLOGY, \nUniversity\n\nIndia\n\n\nCERTIFICATION\n\nMicrosoft Certified Professional Developer in \nEnterprise\n Application (MCPD EA)\n\nMicrosoft Certified Professional in\n\n\n         \n.Net Framework 2.0 - Windows Based Client Development\n\n         \n.Net Framework 2.0 - Web Based Client Development\n\n         \n.Net Framework 2.0 - Distributed Application Development\n\n         \n.Net Framework 2.0 - Application Development Foundation\n\n         \nDesigning and developing enterprise application in .Net Framework 2.0\n\nMicrosoft Certified for Academic Project.\n\nREWARDS/ Recognition\n\nBest ?Achiever Award? \nat Entry Level from \nAccenture\n\nIndia\n during 2005 - 2006.\n?High Performance? \ndelivered work recognition from \nAccenture\n\nUK\n during 2006 - 2007.\n?Accenture Celebrate Excellency? \naward from \nAccenture\n\nIndia\n during 2006 - 2007.\n\n\n\n\n\nTRAINNING ATTENDED:\n\n    \n        \nTechnical Trainings\n at Accenture Service Pvt Ltd, \nBangalore\n\n\n          \n.Net Overview\n\n          \nC, C++, UNIX \n\n          \nXML Fundamentals \n\nSoft Skill\n\nTraining\n at Accenture Service Pvt Ltd, \nBangalore\n\n\n          \nTeam Working\n\n          \nVerbal Communication\n\n          \nPlanning and Prioritization \n\n\nTECHNICAL PROFICIENCIES\n\nEnvironment\n        \n\nMicrosoft VISUAL STUDIO.NET 2005, 2003\nProgramming Languages\n           \n                \n\nC#, VB.NET, ASP.NET, ADO.NET, AJAX, VB, VBA, ASP, XML, HTML, XHTML, DHTML, \n\nJava Script, VB Script and Web Services.\nRDBMS \n\n\nSQL Server 2000, Oracle 9i and MS Access 97, 2003\nMS Servers \n\nIIS 5.0\nReport Writers \n\nXML, XSLT\nWeb-designing Applications\n\nMicrosoft FrontPage and Microsoft Interdev 6.0.\n\n\nProfessional Experience\n\n\nORGANIZATION: ACCENTURE SERVICES Pvt Ltd\n\nINDIA\n\n                                                           \n   \n\nAccenture is a global management consulting, technology services and outsourcing organization.\n\nCLIENT: \n             \nROYAL\n\nSUNALLIANCE\n\nUK\n\n\nRoyal & SunAlliance has a proud heritage dating back almost 300 years. The Sun (established in 1710) \n       \nis the oldest insurance company still trading under its original name. The current Company structure was created in 1996 following the merger of two of the largest insurance companies in the \nUK\n, Royal Insurance and Sun Alliance.\n                                \n     \n           \n\nPROJECT: E- Business\n                     \n                                 \n                                             \n   \nJan 07 ? Present\n\nEnvironment\n        \n\n               \nEnterprise\n Web application interacting with different technologies\nLanguages\n           \n\n               \nASP.NET, SQL SERVER 2000, XML\nTeam Size\n            \n\n               \n\n\n\n\nPROJECT OVERVIEW\n\nROLES\n\n\n          \nInvolved in requirement collection, estimate, design, build and through out the end of SDLC.\n\n          \nDesigned and developed dynamic ASPX web pages using C# .NET, ASP.NET, XML, HTML and JavaScript.\n\n          \nWorked extensively with windows controls.\n\n          \nDefined and developed XML Web Services and reusable-Classes in order to interact with multiple applications. \n\n          \nCreated classes and objects to write the business logic in a separate assembly to isolate business from user interface.\n\n          \nWorked extensively with DataGrid, Treeview, Style sheets and other web controls.\n\n          \nHandled Custom Validations through the built - in Validation Controls using C#.Net and Client side JavaScript.\nDeveloped the architectural design of the database and involved in the performance issues. \n\n          \nDevelop Stored Procedures using SQL Server.\n\n\nPROJECT: FSA\n                                                                \n                     \n                        \n                            \nSep 06 ? Jan 07 \n\nEnvironment\n        \n\n               \nEnterprise\n application \n       \nLanguages\n           \n\n               \nVisual Basic 6.0 and Access 97\nTeam Size\n            \n\n               \n\n\nPROJECT OVERVIEW\n\n\nROLES\n\n\n          \nInvolved in Development phase of the application.\n\n          \nBetter knowledge in \napplication and the architectural design.\n\n          \nDeveloped user defined methods, class, ActiveX controls. \n\n          \nCreated user interface screens and worked extensively with the \nCrystal\n reports.\n\n          \nWorked with Stored Procedures, BI objects.\n\n          \nAnalysis on the performance issue of the application.\n\n          \nInvolved in the deployment process of the application.\n\n\nPROJECT : Reinsurance Controller\n           \n                                                                                                    \nJuly 05 ? Sep 06 \n\n\nEnvironment\n        \n\n               \nDesktop application in different location\n        \nLanguages\n           \n\n               \nVisual Basic for Application and MS Access 97\nTeam Size\n            \n\n               \n\n\nPROJECT OVERVIEW\n\n\nROLES\n\n\n          \nInvolved in analysis, design and development of the application.\n\n          \nGood \nunderstating of domain and understanding of application knowledge.\n\n          \nDefined and developed user defined methods. \n\n          \nCreated user interface screens and worked extensively with Activex controls in access 97.\n\n          \nDesigned application constrained complex SQL queries.\n\n          \nAnalysis on the performance issue of the application.\n\n          \nInvolved in the deployment process of the application.','ACCENTURE SERVICES Pvt Ltd',1,NULL,'2007-10-18',NULL,'2007-10-18','2010-06-10 12:14:22','2010-06-10',15,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(270,'Balaji.R',NULL,NULL,NULL,'balajidvedvcse@gmail.com',NULL,NULL,'0','09916136157','0',NULL,'0','2008-04-29',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-10 12:14:22',15,'0',NULL,'200710/18/ATT16394.html','200710/18/DOC14028.doc','                \n\nBALAJI.R\n\n\nEmail \nbalajidvedvcse@gmail.com\nbaververvla_csrve_2002@yahoo.\ncom\n\n\n\nContact Phone Number\n09916136157\n\n\nPermanent Address:\nBalaji.R\nA-3, Plot No 204,\nGatta Prabha, \nNational\nGames\nVillage\n, Koramangala,\nBangalore\n\n\n\nPersonal Data\nDate of Birth:\n\n07-Nov-1982\nPassport No: E9021093\n\nCurrent Location: \nBangalore\n\n\nProficiency and Skills\n\n    \n   \nExperienced in \nN-tier Architecture\n and full life cycle software\n            \nDevelopment, which includes Object Oriented approach.\n\n          \nWell versed in \n.Net framework\n and worked on \nASP.NET, C#.Net and \nADO\n. Net \nand \nstrong \nOracle\n database skills\n\n\n    \n  \nHighly skilled in GUI design and development of \nweb-based\n applications using \nASP, HTML and \nAJAX\n\n\n          \nExperienced in Client interaction, requirement analysis, application development, debugging, testing and implementation.\n\nEducation\n\n\n          \nBachelor of Engineering in Computer Science (B.E)\n from\n   \nBharathidasan University.Trichy.\n   \n\n\nI Class\n\nWork Experience\n\n\n    \nTotal IT Experience of around \n3.6\n years\n\n\n\n         \nWorking as a \nTechnology Specialist ? Associate \nin \nTech Mahindra \n(CMMI Level 5, PCMMI Level5, and BS7799)\n\nBangalore\n from April 2007 to till date.\n\n\n         \nWorked as \nSoftware Engineer\n in Nucleus Software Exports Ltd \n(CMM Level 5)\n, Noida from August 2004 to April 2007.\n\n\n         \nWorked as Intern in Ocean Solutions, Trichy from March 2004 to July 2004.\n\n\nCertifications & Awards\n\n\n         \nMicrosoft Certified Professional\n in Developing Web applications using Visual Studio.Net\n\n\n         \nAwarded \nNucleite of the month\n for July 2006 for commitment & reconciling BMW migration data with Finnone financial data with very stiff deadlines and pressure from client and also for handling the Lending Reconciliation team and client interaction very effectively.\n\n\nTechnical Skills\nProgramming Languages\nVisual Basic,\n C#,\n VB.NET\n\nDatabase\n\nOracle\n, SQL Server 2000, IBM DB2.\n\nWeb Technologies\nHTML, VBScript, Java Script, Oracle BI Publisher, ASP, \nASP.NET, XML\n\n\nGUI Tools\nVS.NET 2005\n\nVersion Controller\nVisual SourceSafe\n\nExposure To\nC++, PHP, BizTalk Server 2006, \nCrystal\n Reports.\n\nAreas of Interest\n\n          \nFinancial and Banking Domain.\n\n\n          \nResearch and Development.\n\n\n\n\n\nPROJECT EXPERIENCE\n\n\nConnected Services Framework (CSF) - Web Service and SOA Plug in\n\nEnvironment\n                \nASP.NET, C#, AJAX.NET, BizTalk Server 2006\nClient\n                           \nBritish \nTelecom\n\nUK\n\nProject Description\n\n                                        \nCSF provides a number of core services, including session management, identity management, and profile management. CSF also provides a service catalog Web service that is used to access a UDDI-based repository that contains definitions of all of the Web services associated with a particular application. CSF provides order handling and billing services referred to as standard business events that are used to connect your CSF-based services solution to your regular order handling and billing systems. \n         \nMicrosoft® Connected Services Framework (CSF) is an integrated, server-based software product which provides common service capabilities needed to connect and manage content services and networks. It builds, delivers, and manages services using a service-oriented architecture (SOA). For telecommunications operators and service providers, Connected Services Framework allows them to aggregate, provision and manages converged communications services for their subscribers across multiple networks and a range of device types.\n\nResponsibilities\n\n          \nManage user services across a broad array of devices (including third-party devices), such as cell phones, IP Networks and Sandboxes.\nRapidly connect legacy systems, proprietary processes, and standard technologies by using Web services.\nCombine the power of Web services with next-generation network services?including IP Multimedia Subsystems.\nInvolved in Design & Development of the new components to be introduced in the application\n\n         \nResponsible for fine-tuning the performance of the application and maintenance of the application by providing End-User Support.\n\n\nWindows To Operation (WTO)-Expense System (IPS & EERS)\n\nEnvironment\n                \nASP, ASP.NET, VB.NET, C#, AJAX.NET, Oracle, Windows 2000 and IIS 5.0\nClient\n                           \nShinsei Bank, \nTokyo\n\nJapan\n\nProject Description\n\nWindow To Operation ? WTO, is an Intranet application being used by Shinsei Bank for its business requirements. WTO includes 14 individual applications for Shinsei users, where a single login is required for accessing these applications.\nInvoice Processing System-IPS\n is a Queue based application that pays all the Expense for Shinsei Bank. This Solution facilitates Top Management to approve the Expenses. All the Domestic and International payments are done through the external systems.\nEmployee Expense Reimbursement-EERS\n is a Queue based application that reimburses all the expenses of Shinsei Bank Employees. Employees can raise their claims, which will undergo several approval process based on the quite a few criteria and will be finally paid to his account.\n\nResponsibilities\n\n            \n\n         \nResponsible for implementing the \nData Verification\n screen, which is used by senior officials for approving invoice payments.\nInvolved in development of \nVendor Custodian\n, which is used to make urgent payments which do not need approval before-hand.\nIdentifying the different \nRe-Usable Components\n in each layers are to be developed.\nInvolved in \nDesign & Development \nof the new components to be introduced in the application\nDesigned and Developed Web based UI using \nASP, ASP.NET, VB.NET and XML\n\n\n         \nResponsible for fine-tuning the performance of the application and maintenance of the application by providing \nEnd-User Support\n\n\nWindows To Operation(WTO)-Relationship Management System (RMS)\n\nEnvironment\n    \nASP.NET, C#, Oracle, Windows 2000 and IIS 5.0\nClient\n               \nShinsei Bank, \nTokyo\n\nJapan\n\nProject Description\n\nWindow To Operation - WTO\n, is an Intranet application being used by Shinsei Bank for its business requirements. WTO includes 14 individual applications for Shinsei Bank users, where a single login is required for accessing these applications.\nRelationship Management System-RMS\nis a back-office application that is used in Customer relationship management for Shinsei Bank. This gives solution for Customer data analysis, Grouping of customers based on their credits and assignment of Relationship Managers. \n\nResponsibilities\n\n            \nDeveloped the component, which is used to upload data from different sources.\nDesigned and Developed Web based UI using \nASP.NET, C# and XML\n\n\n         \nResponsible for implementing different \nSchedulers\n for the application.\n\nWindows To Operation(WTO)-Housing Loan (HL)\n\nEnvironment\n    \nASP, ASP.NET, VB.NET, Oracle, Windows 2000 and IIS 5.0\nClient\n               \nShinseiBank, \nTokyo\n\nJapan\n\nProject Description\n\nWindow To Operation - WTO\n, is an Intranet application being used by ShinseiBank for its business requirements. WTO includes 14 individual applications for ShinseiBank users, where a single login is required for accessing these applications.\nHousing Loan-HL\n is a Queue based application that processes the housing loan application for ShinseiBank.This gives solution for rapid loan processing with Third-Party Real Estate evaluation, Individual Credit Information Processing, Japan Loan Policies and Top Management Review. ShinseiBank bagged the Best Customer Support Award, 2005 for Housing Loan processing. ShinseiBank stays ahead of other Japanese banks for Housing Loan processing at the rate of 250 loan applications per day.\n\nResponsibilities\n\n            \n\n         \nInvolved in \nClient Meeting\n to understand the business requirement of the System.\nIdentifying the different \nRe-Usable Components\n in each layer are to be developed.\nDeveloped the component, which communicates with \nAccounting Opening System\n\nDeveloped the component to communicate with \nFlex Cube.\nInvolved in development of \nPolicy Matrix\n and \nDocument Matrix\n\nDesigned and Developed Web based UI using \nASP, ASP.NET, VB.NET and XML\n\n\n         \nResponsible for implementing \nWindows Level Security\n for the application\n\n         \nResponsible for fine-tuning the performance of the application and maintenance of the application by providing \nEnd-User Support\n\n\nWindows To Operation(WTO)-Cashless Teller (CT)\n\nEnvironment\n    \nASP, ASP.NET, VB.NET, Oracle, Windows 2000 and IIS 5.0\nClient\n               \nShinseiBank, \nTokyo\n\nJapan\n\nProject Description\n\nWindow To Operation - WTO\n, is an Intranet application being used by ShinseiBank for its business requirements. WTO includes 14 individual applications for ShinseiBank users, where a single login is required for accessing these applications.\nCashless Teller-CT\n is a Queue based application that processes the Teller transactions for ShinseiBank.This gives solution for safe handling of cash by bank tellers. The system automates the teller transactions for Deposits, Withdrawals and Funds Transfer. \n\nResponsibilities\n\n            \nIdentifying the different \nRe-Usable Components\n in each layer are to be developed.\nDesigned and Developed Web based UI using \nASP, ASP.NET, VB.NET and XML\n\n\n         \nResponsible for implementing \nDeposit module \nfor the application.\n\n         \nResponsible for fine-tuning the performance of the application and maintenance of the application by providing \nEnd-User Support\n\n\n\nCorporate Maintenance\nEnvironment\n                \nASP.NET, C#, XML, Windows 2000 and IIS 5.0\n                    \n\n                   \nThis is used to handle all network-based operations of a firm, which includes controlling all employees through network. It includes interaction between the various levels in an organization person can remotely log on in a LAN network and report his daily work. He can also work under another level, which is placed under the purview of top levels in the firm. For this also, a reporting by him is required. \n       \n                                               \n                 \nThe time sheet of the each employee is sent daily to the senior employer. By these the control of various jobs and their assignments to the employees in a LAN network can be controlled effectively .It also contains the HR unit, Technical level and Management level.',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-18',NULL,'2007-10-18','2010-06-10 12:14:22','2010-06-10',15,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(271,'Ashutosh',NULL,NULL,'Noida','ashutefefosh-mefefefefisra@hotmail.com','ashutosh-misra@hotmail.com','09971853422','0','09971853422','0',NULL,'0','2008-02-12',8,23,'2010-06-10 12:14:22',15,'0',NULL,'200710/18/ATT16395.html','200710/18/DOC14029.doc','Resdex @ naukri.com\nAshutosh \nAshutosh misra B-127/A Noida - 301201 \nashutefefosh-mefefefefisra@hotmail.com\n\nTelephone: 09971853422\n(M)\n\nD.O.B\n - 11 Mar 1980 \nModified on\n - 25 Sep 2007 \nAnnual Salary\n - INR 1 Lac(s) 70 Thousand \nTotal Years of Experience\n - 2 Year(s) 4 Month(s) \nCurrent Location\n - Noida \nPreferred Location\n - Anywhere in India \n2.4 Year exp. in ASP.Net With C#\n\nTEXT RESUME \n\nCURRICULUM VITAE\nCurrent Location : Noida\nContact Number: 9971853422\nEmail: ashutosh-misra@hotmail.com\nAshutosh Misra\nJob Profile:\nExperience in live commercial environment in Microsoft Technologies. Good exposoure of ASP.Net with C# in web application and socket programming, having good analytical skill and communication skill, Gethring requirement form client, client interaction, support to live project, modification of codes, taking sign off from client.\nProfessional Experience:\n1.Cleave Global e-Services Ltd. (Feb 2007 to Till Date)\nPresently I am Working in Cleave Global e-Services Ltd. My company is engage in web site and portal development with Business process outsourcing .The Company has developed expertise in handling projects such Floor Manager, Pay master.\nDesignation: Software Engineer.\nDuration: Feb 2007 to Till Date.\n2.Infoserve Technologies (Aug 2005 to Jan 2007)\nI did work with InfoServe provides project -specific services encompassing all phases of the software development life cycle. The company has developed expertise in handling projects of various kinds such as re-engineering, customized development and software integration.\nDesignation: Software Engineer.\nDuration: Aug 2005 to Jan 2007.\nTechnical Qualification:\nMCA from UP \nTechnical\nUniversity\nLucknow\n (U.P.) with 72.5 %.\nSkills:\n\n Language : VB6.0, VB.NET2005\n\n Web Technology: ASP, ASP.NET, HTML\n\n RDBMS : SQL Server2000\n\n Report Tools : Crystal Report\n\n Window : Win2000,WinNT\nProjects:\nWebsite : Extramarks.com\nRole : Team Member\nSkill Used : ASP.Net with C#, IIS Server, SQL Server 2000,\nTeam Size : 4 Members\nDescription: This is a portal for student and teenager .the aim of this portal is to provide sample paper and reference books question with there solutions for the CBSE student. It will provide chatting feature, communities feature, as well as game to the student.\nProject Name: Immigration\nOrganization : K.K. Overseas \nNew Delhi\nRole : System requirements analysis, System designing and development along with table formation in existing database\nTeam Size : 2 Members\nSkill Used : ASP.NET with C#, SQL Server 2000, Crystal Report\nDescription : K.K. Overseas. \nNew Delhi\n is the companies, which provide\nmanpower to overseas company this software, help them to manage the record of job seeker. Along with Status of Passport and other documents of job seeker, with reporting.\nProject Name: Canin Exprss Logistic Pvt.ltd\nOrganization : Canin Exprss Logistic Pvt.ltd ,\nKanpur\n\nRole : Team Member\nTeam Size : 2 Members\nSkill Used : ASP.NET with C#, SQL Server 2000\nDescription : This client is engage in courier service, it was a trouble for him,\nTo manage and maintain the data and status their day to day business routine .There are 4 major modules in this software, which helps to run the whole process of. These modules are given below:\nMaster Management\nAccount\nUtility\nMailers and Reports\nProject Name: Cadet Information System.\nOrganization : MCTE, \nIndore\n (M.P.).\nRole : Designing and Coding, Testing\nTeam Size : 4 Members\nSkill Used : ASP.Net with C#, SQL Server 2000, Crystal Report\nDescription : Cadet Information System software is a Client Server based Application for Cadets Training Wing, MCTE (Military College of Telecommunication Engineering) MHOW, and INDORE (M.P.)\nEducational Qualification:\nB.B.A Mahatma Gandhi Kashi VidhyaPeeth University.\nIntermediate U.P. Board Allahabad.\nHigh School U.P. Board Allahabad.\nPersonal Details\nName: Ashutosh Misra\nDOB: 11-March- 1980\nFather\n?s name:\n SRI. R.K.Misra\nLanguages: Hindi, English.\nMartial Status: Single\nPermanent Address: Plot No. 101A Janaki Nagar Colony\nVaranasi\n (U.P)\nDate: (Ashutosh Misra)\nPlace:','Cleave Global e-Services Ltd',1,NULL,'2007-10-18',NULL,'2007-10-18','2010-06-10 12:14:22','2010-06-10',15,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(272,'Ashutos',NULL,NULL,'Hyderabad','wrgww.ashbhbththhtutoshrg15n@yahoo.co.in','www.ashutosh15n@hotmail.com','040 27620167','0','9849573912','0',NULL,'0','2005-12-12',7,19,'2010-06-10 12:14:22',15,'0',NULL,'200710/18/ATT14020.html','200710/18/DOC14033.doc','CURRICULUM VITAE\nCURRICULUM VITAE\n\n\nASHUTOSH\n                                                     \nCONTACT NUMBER: 9849573912\n   \n#1-8-7, Sarvodaya Colony,\nChickkadpally , Hyderabad-20\nPhone: 9849573912 , 040 - 27620167\nEmail : \nwrgww.ashbhbththhtutoshrg15n@yahoo.co.in\n\n\n\nObjective\n\n\n     \nTo work with sincerity & dedication to achieve Quality & Professional results.\n\nSkills Overview\n\n\n        \nWorked in a variety of roles including programmer, designer and programmer-analyst.\n\n        \nExtensive experience with VB.NET, Visual Basic 6.0, VBScript, JavaScript, HTML and related technologies having focused heavily on ASP.NET,ASP3.0, COM, DCOM web application design, development, infrastructure design and integration for around \n2 years\n\n\n        \nExperience with leading teams. Extensive consulting and problem solving experience gained through the development of business applications for a broad range of industries. Possesses excellent communication skills in small and large group situations. Proven documentation and writing skills.\n\nExperience\n\n\n        \nWorking as a Software Engineer for Answerland IT Univ, \nHyderabad\n since June 2003.\n\n\n        \nIn the present position handling various responsibilities includes system/software requirements study, analysis, design, and programming.\n\n\nMajor Strengths\n\n        \nGood exposure to designing databases.\n\n        \nExcellent practical knowledge in development and implementation of web based projects.\n\n        \nExperience with full requirements to design process, and ability to handle projects independently.\n\n\n\nCompetencies and Focus\nCompetencies include development of web and client server based applications in:\n\n        \nVB .NET, Visual Basic 6.0\n\n        \nASP 3.0, ASP.NET,COM, DCOM\n\n        \nHTML, DHTML, XML\n\n        \nVBScript, JavaScript\n\n        \nIIS 5.0\n\n        \nOracle 8.0/8i, MS SQL Server and MS Access 2000\n\n        \nCrystal\n Reports, Data Reports\n\n        \nC, C++, C#\nEducation\n\n\n        \nMCA from Indira Gandhi National Open University (\nAurora\nDegree & PG\nCollege\n, Chikkadapally, \nHyderabad\n\n\n\n        \nBCA\n\nfrom Indira Gandhi National Open University (\nAurora\nDegree & PG\nCollege\n, Chikkadapally, \nHyderabad\n\n      \n                 \n\nOther Qualifications\n\n\n        \nProficiency Diploma in German (Deutsch) Language from Central Institute of English and\n\nForeign Language (CIEFL) \nHyderabad\n\n\n\nProfessional Experience\n\n\nDuration (6 months)\nClient: \nRiyad\nMedical\nCenter\nProject Title\n\n   \nAdvance\nMedical\nCenter\n (AMC)\nAMC is a clinic, which is based in \nRiyadh\n\nKingdom\n of \nSaudi Arabia\n. The application is operative in multiple health care domains like dermitology, cardiology etc. The application software is being developed for easing the billing operations of the clinic. The main modules include Front Office management, Billing, Finance and Administration. The application is compatible for both localized and English version. All the dates are handled using HIJRI calendar. \n\nSalient features of AMC include\nDual Language compatibility\n\n        \nIncorporation of Hijri calendar. \nUser level authentication for all the documents. \nSearch facility based on key value for all the screens. \nRole:\n   \nSystem Study, Design, Coding\nTeamSize: \n\nEnvironment:\nWindows 2000, SQL Server 2000,ASP.NET, VB.NET, \nCrystal\n Reports\n\n\n\nDuration (10 months)\nClient\n : Airport\n\nAuthority of India Limited\n\nProject Title\n\n   \nAir Trafficbilling and maintenance\n\nSystem (ATBMS)\n\nATBMS is an application software, to provide the complete information on Air Traffic Billing. The system manages information generated at various centers of activities at an Airport.. Data Consolidation Facility is provided through Import and export mechanism. The Central Server is located at the Corporate Headquarters at \nDelhi\n\nReport Generation Module of the system resides on the Central Server for Reports generation as per the requirement of the Corporate Headquarters. The system is integrated with Billing, Flight Movements Air Craft parts maintenance and Administration to achieve efficient resource planning for AAI (\nAirport Authority of India Limited\n). \n\nResponsibilities:\n Include Designing and Coding for Administration, Flight\nMovements Modules and Database Maintenance.\nRole:\n\n        \nCreated Databases from scratch, Designed Tables, Views, Triggers, Table spaces, Data files, Indexes, Cursors, Users, Maintained Database and other related design elements.\nTeam Size : \n\nEnvironment:\n Windows 2000, Oracle 8i, ASP.NET, Data Reports.\n\n\nDuration (6\n\nmonths )\nClient\n : ITC Limited\nProject Title\n\n   \nDealer\'s Management System\nDealer is the person who acts as a mediator between Industries and Wholesalers, i.e. dealer takes orders from the wholesaler and gives it to the industries. The dealer also takes the payment from the wholesalers regarding the transactions.\nResponsibility of the dealer is to generate orders to the industry, i.e. takes orders from the wholesaler and sends the same to industries. Then Industries will dispatch the items directly to the wholesalers according to their orders. The dealer needs not to maintain any stock. And dealer will receives the payments from wholesalers and pass it to the industry. Later industries will give the commission to dealer. \nThe Dealer also provides a single window provision to wholesalers. Some wholesalers need only one item, whereas some other wholesalers need different items from different industries. Instead of approaching different industries the wholesalers directly places the orders to Dealer and the dealer will take the responsibility to dispatch the orders to various industries. And the Industries also depends on the dealer for payments, they don\'t need to approach different wholesalers. Dealer will collect the payment and sends to the Industries and Industries will pay his commission later.\n\nTechnical Stuff:\n\n1. Window based authentication has been implemented.\n\n2. Server Side Controls Data Grid has been implemented.\n\n3. Cashing concept has been implemented.\nModules are used: \n\n1. Industries wise details, Industries wise bill.\n\n2. Whole seller wise details, Whole seller wise bill.\nTeam Size\n : 5\nRole:\n\nDeveloper and Designer\nEnvironment:\n\n\nWin 2003 server, ASP.NET, Oracle8i, Crystal Report .\n\n\n\nPersonal Details\n\nName\n                                       \n\n          \nAshutosh\nDate of Birth: \n                           \n\n           \n15th\n\nnovember, 1978\nFather\'s Name\n                          \n\n           \nShobha Kant Jha\nMarital Status\n                           \n\n           \nUnmarried\nPermanent Address\n                  \n\n           \nAshutosh,\nC/o L Vithal Rao,\nH. No. 1-8-7,\nSarvodaya Colony\n\nOpp.\nAurora\nDegree\nCollege\n), \nChikkadapally,\nHyderabad\n - 500020\nContact number\n       \n                 \n\n      \n     \n9849573912,\n\n040 - 27620167\nE-Mail Address\n                        \n\n           \nwww.ashutosh15n@hotmail.com\nLanguages Known\n                    \n\n           \nHindi, English, German (Deutsch)\n          \nPlace : \nHyderabad\nDate\n\n\n\n\nASHUTOSH)','Answerland IT Univ',1,NULL,'2007-10-18',NULL,'2007-10-18','2010-06-10 12:14:22','2010-06-10',15,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(273,'Ashutosh Panda',NULL,NULL,'Bangalore','sefk.asefefhutoefefsh@gmail.com','aef.paefefndefa@aol.in',NULL,'0','9900402164','0',NULL,'0','2008-02-12',8,23,'2010-06-10 12:14:22',15,'0',NULL,'200710/18/ATT14022.html','200710/18/DOC14034.doc','Debasis Mohapatra\nASHUTOSH PANDA\nE-Mail Id: \nsefk.asefefhutoefefsh@gmail.com\n\naef.paefefndefa@aol.in\n\nMobile No: +91-9900402164\n\nPROFILE :\n\n\n            \nHaving \n2.2years \nof IT Experience in \nDevelopment of Application Software.\n\n            \nExtensive knowledge in \n.NET Frame Work, C#, ASP.NET, ADO.NET\n\n\n            \nStrong knowledge of Object Oriented concepts.\n\n            \nWorking Knowledge on Database.\n\n            \nWell versed to GUI designing\n\n\n            \nGood command over Exception handling and Debugging.\n\n            \nExcellent analytical and programming skills\n\n\n            \nAbility to Work in-group as well as independently with minimal supervision.\n\n\nSKILL SET:\n\nProgramming Languages\n   \n\n           \nC#.NET, VB.NET, C, C++.\nDatabase\n                               \n\n           \nSQL Server 2000, Oracle9i & MS Access.\nTechnologies\n            \n            \n\n           \nASP.NET, ADO.NET, HTML, XHTML, Java Script. \n  \nWeb Server\n                           \n\n         \nIIS\nTools\n                                       \n\n           \nVisual Studio 2003/2005\nOperating Systems\n             \n\n         \nWindows 9x, 2K, XP.\n\nQUALIFICATION :\n\n\n            \nB.E \n\nElectronics & Telecom)\n from B.P.U.T, Orissa\n\nin\n\nthe\n\nyear of \n2005\nPROFESSIONAL EXPERIENCE :\n\n\n            \nCurrently Working for \nShellsoft Technologies\n\nBangalore\n\nas a Software\n Engineer\n\n\nPROJECT DETAILS :\n\nProject #1:\n   \nDream Bricks\n\nPlatform\n                  \n: Windows 2000\nLanguage/Tools\n        \n: ASP.NET 1.1, C#.NET, ADO.NET, CSS, Java Script\nDatabase\n                \n: SQL Server 2000\nWeb server\n              \n: IIS 5.0\n                  \nTeam Size\n               \n: 3\nDuration\n                  \n: On going\n\n\nProject Description\nThis is a properties based web project with lots of information regarding properties and services at different sites in \nIndia\n. Here users can buy/sale/or give their properties in lease online. It has properties tools such as EMI, area calculation, city description etc. It also provides information about bank loans. The functional specification of the project is in two parts user and admin. In user module it again divided into sub-modules. In the user area user has to search for properties by property type, price, city, region and location. User can search for real-estate agents as city wise. For searching properties user can register with filling all the necessary details or without registering also. In the Admin it consists with offer management, giving rights to user to perform specific task, change password, banner advertise management.\n\n\nResponsibilities\n\n            \nInvolved in Coding of module.\n\n            \nInvolved in Design of User Interface.\n\n            \nInvolved in Database connectivity.\n\n            \nInvolved in Unit Testing.\n\nProject#2:\n\ne-Cards\n\nPlatform\n                \n: Windows 2000\nLanguage/Tools\n      \n: ASP.NET, C#.NET, ADO.NET, CSS, Java Script\nDatabase\n              \n: SQL Server 2000\nTeam Size\n             \n: 4\nDuration\n               \n: 6 months\n\nProject Description\nThis Web based project is purely shopping of e-Greetings. Where shopping is for user need with online. The Functional specifications of the project are deals in two parts user area, and admin area. In the user area, users have to search for Greetings by category and card name, browse for Greetings by alphabetic name, view Greetings detail page and buy online. In online shopping, each Greetings details page will have functionality to add desired no?s to cart. Checkout shopping which can be edited. Get e-mail address. Give payment detail. Display payment conformation and display order id, simultaneously e-mail of order detail will send to user and a copy to admin. User to enter order id after successful buying session the system will now show the status. Admin area consists of four parts, Greetings catalogue management, order status update, offer management and change password.\n\nResponsibilities\n\n            \nInvolved in Coding and User Interface Designing.\n\n            \nInvolved in Unit Testing.\n\nProject #3:\n   \nTrack Biz Solution\n\n\nPlatform\n               \n: Windows 2000\n\nLanguage/Tools\n     \n: C#, ADO.NET\n\nDatabase\n             \n: SQL Server 2000\n              \n\nTeam Size\n            \n: 5\n\nDuration\n              \n: 8 months\n\n\nProject Description\nThis is completely automated software for an automobile dealer. This is a Window based application. This application is used to keep track of all purchase, sale, enquiry, service, account and attendance of employee. This project is divided into six modules vehicle purchase, inquiry and vehicle sale, spare purchase and sale, service, account, front office and attendance register. I have handled vehicle purchase, spare purchase, sale and inquiry. Once your entry is done it will show you about the stock in report. I have also have worked in account module to keep track of vehicle, spare - purchase and sold.\n       \n\nProject #4:\n   \nLearning Management Systems(LMS)\n\n\nPlatform\n                \n: Windows2000\n\nLanguage/Tools\n      \n: ASP.NET, C#.NET, ADO.NET, Java Script\n\nDatabase\n              \n: SQL Server 2000\n\nTeam Size\n             \n: 5\n\nDuration\n                \n: 7 months\n          \nProject Description\nLMS is web based e-learning management system enabling users to achieve high level of education through Intranet. This e-learning is a mode of instruction that is delivered electronically through web server. The main modules in LMS are admin, register, instructor and learner. The different activities involved are like creating syllabi, assignment entry, mail services, examination schedule.\n\n\nPERSONAL DETAILS :\n\nDate of Birth\n                   \n\n   \n12\nth\n Jun 1982\nFather?s Name\n                 \n\n   \nSusanta Ku. Panda\nNationality\n                      \n\n   \nIndian\nMartial Status\n                 \n\n   \nSingle\n\nPassport\n                         \n\n   \nValid Passport \nSex\n                               \n\n   \nMale\n      \nLanguages Known\n   \n          \n\n   \nEnglish, Hindi, Oriya and Kannada\n\n\nCONTACT DETAILS :\n\n           \n15,17\nth\nMain\n, AGOS Layout, Arehalli,\n           \nB.S.K 4\nth\n Stage, Bangalore-61.','Shellsoft Technologies',1,NULL,'2007-10-18',NULL,'2007-10-18','2010-06-10 12:14:22','2010-06-10',15,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(274,'Pradip sudke',NULL,NULL,NULL,'psnvddvvdvdetmdvail@rediffmail.com','pdvdvdvdvs3dvdsdvdvvd981@gmail.com','9422220027','0','9923177295','0',NULL,'0','2008-04-29',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-10 12:14:22',15,'0',NULL,'200710/18/ATT14013.html','200710/18/DOC14035.doc','R E S U M E\nR E S U M E\nFlat No. 76, Savant Vihar - Phase 2, \nOppo. Sarpodyan, Pune - 411001\nContact\n\n9923177295, 9422220027\nEmail: \npsnvddvvdvdetmdvail@rediffmail.com\n\n           \n  \n            \npdvdvdvdvs3dvdsdvdvvd981@gmail.com\n\n\n\n                                \nPradip Sudke\n\nSatyam - Software Engineer (2 yrs. exp,.NET)\nCDAC, B.E. MECH. 2004 (69%)\nFree Lancer during B.E. (BSNL, CG Ltd.)\n\nKEY SKILLS\nASP.NET, JavaScript, VB.NET, C#, Web Services, SQL Server 2005, Oracle 9i, BizTalk Server, XML, Visual Basic 6.0, Linux Programming, Visual Foxpro 6.0, C++, C\n\nWORK EXPERIENCE \nOrganization: Satyam Computer Services\nDesignation\n: Software Engineer\n Period: \nOct 05 ? April 07\n\nProject:\n CheckFree\nClient:\n CheckFree\nInvestment\n Services, \nUSA\nDomain:\n Finance\nDescription\n\nCheckFree develops markets and supports software applications used by financial institutions to process more than two-thirds of the 14 billion automated Clearing House transactions in the \nUnited States\n\nFunctions: \nShares management (for Managers, Investors) ? create, edit, display\nPortfolio strategies application to securities/shares accounts, intelligent suggestions based on historical & current market trading prices.\n               \n    \n\nRole:\n Team Member\nResponsibility:\n Complete SOA architecture Web Page development\nModule:\n Security (Shares) management\n\nTeam size:\n Module ? 15, Project - 126\nDev. Environment:\n ASP.NET, C#, VB.NET, SQL Server 2005, BizTalk Server 2006, XML\n\nFREE LANCER EXPERIENCE - DURING B.E. EDUCATION\nProject:\n\nAI based Bank Reconciliation\n (Nov 2002 - Aug 2003)\nClient:\n BSNL\nDomain:\n Finance\nFunction\n: AI based Bank Reconciliation of all BSNL transactions (Customer bills, Refunds, Funds Transfer, etc.) with various Banks. All possible human errors by BSNL & Bank Staff are considered. Any layman can operate because of easy interfaces, \nMarathi\n\nhelp & automated processes.\nImprovement:\nManual work of 80-100 hours is done within just 1-2 hours with accuracy.\nDev. Environment: \nVisual Basic 6.0, SQL Server\n\nProject:\n\nNavy Motor Shock Grade checking Software\n (Jan 2004 - March 2004)\nClient:\n\nCrompton Greaves Ltd.\nDomain:\n Machine Design & CAD\nFunction\n: Navy Motors have to be checked according to the Shock Grade standards to withstand explosions & sea waves. Software checks the motors, gives & prints sketches of deflections in various parts of the motor under severe conditions. \nImprovement:\n Manual work of 50-60 hours is performed within just 15-30 minutes.\nDev. Environment: \nVisual Basic 6.0, SQL Server\n\n\nProject:\n\nAyurveda\n\nAuto Diagnosis Software\n (July 2003 - Aug 2003)\nClient:\nPanchakarma\nHospital\n, Pune\nDomain:\n\nAyurveda \nHealthcare\nFunction:\nSanskrit \nshlokas \nfor specified number of Symptoms are searched by the software. Respective index of them help to get its solution from \nGranthas.\nImprovement\n: Manual work of 15-20 hours is done within just few seconds accurately.\nDev. Environment: \nVisual FoxPro 6.0\n\nProject:\n\nAuto Operations A/C & JS management\n (July 2005 - Sept 2005)\nClient:\n\nBSNL\nDomain:\n Finance\nFunction:\n Auto data entry & coordination with old softwares to take input or supply output data. Auto Cheque printing, CDR reports generations are possible by software.\nImprovement:\nManual work of 20-30 hours is completed in less than 1 hour.\nDev. Environment: \nVisual FoxPro 6.0\n\nProject:\n\nDimensional Analysis of Electric Motors \n(Nov 2004 - Jan 2005)\nClient:\n\nCrompton Greaves Ltd.\nDomain:\n Machine Design\nFunction:\n Dimensional Analysis is carried out of all the motors to check that they are meeting the Standards.\nImprovement:\nManual work of 15-20 hours is completed in less than 0.5 hour.\nDev. Environment: \nVisual FoxPro 6.0\n\nProject:\n\nContractors Billing\n (Dec 2002 ? Feb 2003)\nClient:\n\nBSNL\nDomain:\n Finance\nFunction:\n Software is used for Contractors\' Billing and making respective reports.\nImprovement\n: Manual work of 5 To 8 hours is performed within few minutes.\nDev. Environment: \nVisual FoxPro 6.0\n\nACADEMIC QUALIFICATION\nLevel\nUniversity\n/Board/\nCollege\nPassing Year\nMarks\nCDAC\nIACSD, Pune\n2005\n67.00 %\nB.E. Mech.\nPune\n2004\n69.07 %\nD.M.E.\nB.T.E.\n2001\n73.02 %\nH.S.C\nMaharashtra\n1999\n74.33 %\nS.S.C.\nMaharashtra\n1997\n84.26 %\n\nSPECIAL ACHIEVEMENTS\n          \nDipex Software Projects exhibition:\n          \nSecond prize for Shaft Designing Software with \n3D Graphical user interface in C\n like \nbuttons, text boxes, highlights, etc\n\nPERSONAL DETAILS\nDate of Birth:\n03/09/1981\nPassport Number: \nF5535607',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-18',NULL,'2007-10-18','2010-06-10 12:14:22','2010-06-10',15,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(275,'Piyush Kumar',NULL,NULL,NULL,'piyufgrfgrgshchd@gmail.com','piyufgfagfgsh_cfgrfhd@rediffmail.com','0172 2783765','0','09815703377','0','09872772315','0','2008-04-29',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-10 12:14:22',15,'0',NULL,'200710/18/ATT14030.html','200710/18/DOC14038.doc','PRADEEP KUMAR MISHRA\nPIYUSH KUMAR\n\n\nSeeking challenging managerial assignments in IT/projects involving Coding Installation, Configuration & Implementation with an organisation of Repute preferably as \nIT Sector as Technical writer Engineer\n\nCAREER SUMMARY\nCurrently working with \nKayako Infotech ltd(Jalandhar)\n as Technical writer. Kayako is one of the leading software company which provides the\n(Customer relationship management) CRM\n help desk software to the various clients globally.\n\nThe technical writer includes the application maintence of the Kayak Software i.e coding of various modules in the PHP and the Mysql,fixing the bugs of the various clients worldwide. Also handles the product documentation of the manuals and updating the kayako forums on various errors of the clients.\n\nTo assist the clients world wide using the product knowledge of various settings and documentation of the software upgrading various clients helpdesk.\n\n     \nTechnical Engineer:\n\n\n      \nProvide staff members with informal coaching and formal training in writing, editing, and desktop publishing as needed. \n\n      \nAll aspects of written presentation, to include: structure, organization, argument, tables and graphs, and matters of non-technical document content. \n\n      \nReview and comment on study design documents, outlines, reports, and presentations. \n\n      \nEdit (substantive edit or copy edit) documents Work Performed by Incumbent Troubleshooting pertaining to Performance, IT support, Networks, Application Conflicts and system Bugs.\n\n      \nAddressing queries regarding the Information System / Software & extending onsite support to the clients including maintenance of hardware / software.\n\n      \nInstalling, configuring and maintaining Operating Systems, Application Software, and Anti-Viruses & Hardware.\nUnderstanding the client technical environment and applications\n\n\nKey Responsibilities:\n\n      \nTechnical coordinate with Training to ensure consistent product messages in training\n                                \nmaterials and documentation.\n\n      \nTechnical one to install the company\'s products (Support Suite, esupport software), and provide feedback on the consistency of user interfaces across a product line.\n   \nOverview of editorial tasks :\n\n   \n\n) Check and verify all facts and references.\n\n    \nEnsure that every text and non-text element is correct. Accomplish this by: \n   \nTesting every example \n   \nChecking each non-text element for accuracy and ensuring it matches the text and is appropriate \n\nInvestigating any references to ensure they are correct and valid\n\n\nIn short, put yourself in the shoes of the intended reader and scrutinize every detail.\n\n\n2) \nEnsure consistency.\n\nConsistent terminology is an important element of a well-written book. If you encounter differences (command versus option, for example), determine which term to use and stick with it. \n\n3) \nAnswer all queries of a technical nature.\n\n\nThe technical editor is the backstop within the book team for all technical questions, issues, and requests for clarification. Therefore you must respond to every query with a response sufficient to meet the needs of the person asking the question.\n\n\n\n\nEnsure the work meets market and audience goals\n\n\n\n\n\n\nPrincipal Accountabilities\nAssists in establishing, monitoring, and reinforcing editorial standards to ensure that the department\'s publications are of the highest standard appropriate to their format and to cost and time constraints.\n\nSupports the Group Manager in his effort to ensure timely delivery of high-quality written product\ns.\n\n\nRich and insightful experience of \nOne year& \neleven\n months\n in Team Leading / Technical writer. \nSince Jul?05 with Real pc Pvt. Panchkula ltd. (India) also worked on the project setup of networking (installation of server, pc, LAN) at army headquarters CCSR Lucknow Signals Centre.\n\n\n      \nHave experience in working in various part time jobs like in Airtel, Spice for various promotions.\n\n      \nFirst rank in inter school nature quiz conducted by Environmental Society of CHANDIGARH in 1994.\n\n      \nReceived additional appreciation from the senior engineer of production group\n\nfor the\n\nexcellent work during the six weeks training, worked as coordinator for organizing a NATIONAL LEVEL TECHNICAL FESTIVAL (2002) conducted by M.MENGG.COLLEGE MULLANA.\n\n      \nCompleted a major project on Digital Water Level Controller for Six months\n\n      \nHave effectively handled numerous projects on IT ,Networking and System administration. \n\n      \nSkilled at mapping client?s requirements, custom designing solutions & troubleshooting for complex information systems management. \n\n      \nExcellent communication and interpersonal skills with abilities in resolving complex networking, hardware and software related issue.\nEMPLOYMENT HIGHLIGHTS\n\nSince Jul?05 with Real pc Pvt. Panchkula ltd. (India) also worked on the project setup of networking (installation of server, pc, LAN) at ARMY HEADQUATER CCSR LUCKNOW SIGNALS CENTRE.\n\n\n         \nWas responsible for handling the IT & Networking projects all over India Army Cantonment and solving the issues of the organization related to the networking, hardware, and IT support\n\nKey Deliverables \n\nNetwork Management\n\n      \nManaging the overall networking of computer systems involving design of network layouts, configuration and maintenance of application servers .\n\n      \nInstalling and maintaining network and data communication hardware and software environment.\n\nOperations management \n\n      \nDesigning Backup Strategy & ensuring scheduled / unscheduled backups as per the backup plan.\n\n      \nPlan and increase capacity for systems and communications to accommodate growth in a timely manner.\n\n      \nContribute to the ongoing development of technology infrastructure such that they develop in line with company organizational, technical and commercial requirements.\n\n      \nPlan for business continuity or disaster recovery, including Development, Operations, IT Security, and IT Services & help desk, and mission critical applications.\n\n\nCommenced career with CII as Supervisor from \n06?10?2003\n\nto\n\n06?11?2003\n\nPROJECTS UNDERTAKEN\n\n1.)Project\n\nTitle\n\n      \n\nRecovery of Hacked Linux Server.\n\n                                      \n\n\nProfile\n                     \n\nIt was the project in which there is client of the U.S, whose server is hacked by\n         \n\n                                 \nhacker\n\nand client was using our product(Support suit).\n                                   \n\n\nRole\n                        \n\nRecover the dump of the database through the RDB connection. Changing the files\n    \n                                 \nPermission in order to resolve the client issue so that he can us our product.\n\nTechnology\n             \n\n      \nPHP\n\n\nOperating System\n   \n\n   \nLinux\n\nDuration\n                  \n\n   \n6 weeks (March 2007 to April 2007)\n\nTeam size\n               \n\n   \n\n\nDatabase\n                \n\n   \nMysql\n\nTools Used\n             \n\n   \nPlesk ,Cpanel, RDC ,Vebex for GO to meeting.\n\nCompany Name\n      \n\nKayako Infotech Ltd\n\nResponsibility\n         \n\nTo coordinate with the team member making daily reports of the \nclient technical\n                    \n                                   \nSpecification.\n\nWorked on the various templates of the code of the php .\n                                          \n2.) Project Title\n\n  \n: Live response issue\n\nCompany\n: Ambientsolutions.com\n\nCountry\n\nUnited Kingdom\n\nDescription\n: Issue with chat. It says that client closed window or chat expired and it is happening with every chat.\nUrl: www.hiyasupport.com/admin\nUsername: kash\nPassword: enter\n\n\nResponsibility\n: Making report of the client update daily. Adding various codes to the application\n\nFile. Active role in resolving the new XML error and ASCII Unicode version upgrade error.\n\nTools \n  \n: Cuteftp, WHM,\nProgramming Language\n: PHP\n\nOperating system\n: Linux\n\nDuration\n: Two weeks\n\nTeam Size: 3\n\n                                                \n\nIT SKILLS\n\nProgramming languages\n             \n\n          \n\nC, C++.\nScripting Language\n     \n                \n\n   \n        \n\nPHP,\nHardware Skill\n                           \n\n          \n\nWindows 2000 Server (Networking),\nOperating System\n          \n           \n\n            \nWindows XP, 2000, RHCE\n LINUX\nMicrosoft Skill\n                           \n\n             \nDOT.NET (C#, VB.NET.ASP.NET) (Pursuing)\n                                              \n\nACADEMIC CREDENTIALS\n\n2005\n     \n            \nBachelor of Technology (Electronics & instrumentation) from Kurukshetra University \n2001\n                 \n12th from G.M Sr. Sec School, Chandigarh\n\n1999\n                 \n10th from G.M Sr. School Chandigarh\n\n\nPERSONAL DETAILS\n\nDate of Birth\n                  \n\n      \n     \n26\nth\n December 1983\nLanguages \n                    \n\n           \nEnglish, Hindi, and Punjabi\n          \nPhone\n                           \n\n           \n0172 -2783765\nMobile\n                           \n\n           \n09815703377,09872772315,09812338460,09899624700\nEmail\n                            \n\n            \npiyufgrfgrgshchd@gmail.com\n, piyufgfagfgsh_cfgrfhd@rediffmail.com\nAddress\n                        \n\n           \n#2565 Sector 19 C , \nChandigarh',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-18',NULL,'2007-10-18','2010-06-10 12:14:22','2010-06-10',15,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(276,'P Peruswamy',NULL,NULL,NULL,'pfberufdbbswadfbdfbmy20@gmail.com',NULL,'91 99 40 08','0',NULL,'0',NULL,'0','2007-10-29',8,NULL,'2010-06-10 12:14:22',15,'1','2010-06-21','200710/18/ATT14031.html','200710/18/DOC14039.doc','SRINIVAS\n\n\nPERUSWAMY\nMobile\n: +91 - 99 40 08 32 47\nEmail : \npfberufdbbswadfbdfbmy20@gmail.com\n\n\nOBJECTIVE\n                                                                                                                                              \n\nTo obtain a position in the product development arm of an IT company which offers a challenging work environment and utilizes my creativeness, experience and fast-adaptability capabilities for achieving the goals of the company.\n\n\nPROFESSIONAL SUMMARY\n\n3+ years\n of IT experience out of which \n2.5 years\n of experience is in Microsoft Dot Net Web Solution, Internet applications over Windows platforms and\n\n6 Months of experience in development of application in client server technology.\n\nTECHNICAL STRENGTHS\n\n\n       \nExperience in \nClient Interaction Skills\n\n\n\n       \nExpertise in \nMicrosoft Dot Net\n\nTechnologies\n\n? Asp.net and\n\nC# \n\n\n       \nKnowledge in \nDocumentation, Analysis and Database designing\n\n\n\n       \nExpertise in \nSQL Server 2000. \n\n\n\n       \nKnowledge in \nWeb Services\n\nPROFESSIONAL EXPERIENCE\n\n\n       \nPresently working as a \nSoftware Engineer\n with \nSify Ltd.\n\nChennai,\n from February 2006 to till date\n\n\n       \nWorked as a Programmer at \nZoniac software Pvt. Ltd., Chennai,\n from\n\nAugust 2004 to January 2006\n\n\n\nPROFESSIONAL QUALIFICATION\n\n\n       \n\nM.C.A from \nKakatiya\nUniversity\n, Andhra Pradesh.\n\nTECHNICAL EXPERIENCE\n. NET Technologies\nASP.NET, C#. NET, ADO.NET.\nDBMS and Related Tools\nMS-Access, MS SQL Server 2000.\nLanguage\nC, C++.\nOperating Systems\nWindows 95/98/2000/NT/XP/2003\nWeb Servers\nIIS 5.0\n\n\n\nPROFESSIONAL EXPERIENCE \n\n\n\nPROJECT #1: CBU Support System \n                                                     \n\n(May 2007 to Till Date)\n\nDescription\nNHT is selling their tractors through a Dealership network and their sales team manages this network where the frontline representative is called the Commercial Business Unit or CBU. Scope of the project is to automate this sales process, taking into accounts the business processes accomplished by the CBU and the Dealers. Essentially the objective of the project are\n\nManaging the CBU and Dealer activities, Managing the primary & secondary sales data for reporting & MIS purpose and Manage the primary payment collection data for reporting & MIS purpose\nClient \nNew \nHolland\n Tractors (\nIndia\n) Pvt. Ltd\nEnvironment\nC#. NET, ASP.NET, SQL Server2000, ADO.NET.\nRoles&Responsibilities\n\n\nClient Interaction\n\n\nDesigning and Development \n\nClient Requirement Analysis\n\nUnit Testing. \n\n\n\n\nPROJECT #2: \nOPTS\n\n                                                                 \n    \n(October 2006 to April 2007)\n\nDescription\nThis Project helps the students to prepare for their University \n   \nexams. Students can login to the application and they can give exams for the previous papers of any subject and student can attempt particular exam any number of times. Using this application student can see the previous attempts history like marks scored, correct answers and answer submitted by the student for a particular exam. The main objective of this application is to provide the assessment for the preparation before attempting the main exams. The user interface has multilingual support. The product will be launched in English and Japanese language. \nClient\n   \nNagase Corporation, \nJapan\n\n                    \nTeam size\n5 members\n                \nEnvironment\n                      \nC#. NET, ASP.NET, SQL Server2000, ADO.NET.\nRoles&Responsibilities\n\nClient Interaction\n\nDesigning and Development \nClient Requirement Analysis\nInvolved in Unit Testing\n\n\nPROJECT #3:\n\nNagase Head Quarter\n                                                      \n(Feb 2006 to Sep 2006)\n\nDescription\nThis project helps\n      \n  \n\n\nNagase Head Quarter users to see all the performance statistics of all HS schools operated by Nagase as well as the performance of individual students belongs to the schools. This is purely a statistical tool i.e. the logged in user can only view the statistics and it?s not possible for the user to update anything using this application. In Same way logged in user can see the statistics of the FS schools and students belongs to those schools of Areacounsellors and Prefectures under the control of logged in NHQ user. The user interface has multilingual support. The product will be launched in English and Japanese language. \n\nClient\nNagase Corporation, \nJapan\n\nDuration\n8 months \nTeam size\n3 members \nEnvironment\nC#. NET, ASP.NET, SQL Server2000\nRoles&Responsibilities\n\nClient Interaction\n\nDesigning and Development \nClient Requirement Analysis\nInvolved in Unit Testing \n\n\n\n\n\nPROJECT #4:\n\nOnline Room & Car Bookings System.\n               \n     \n\n(Aug 2005 to January2006)\n\nDescription\nThis site is divided into four modules Room Reservation, Car Booking, Hotel or Car Administrator and Site Administration. Room Reservation module allows the user to book the room(s) according to his requirement in the star hotels after checking the availability of room(s) on that day(s). Car booking module allows the user to book a cab or car to pickup or drop-off the user at the locations specified by the client on his required date & timings. Hotel Administrator can add or modify the hotel and rooms details. Car Administrator can create the car details. Site Administrator is having deals with the Hotel administrators and car administrators.\n\nClient\nSATCO\nDuration\n6 months \nTeam size\n2 members \nEnvironment\nC#. NET, ASP.NET, SQL Server2000, ADO.NET.\n         \nResponsibilities\nGUI design, Development, and Testing.\n\n\n\n\nPROJECT #5: AutoServer Information System \n                                  \n(March 2005 ? July 2005)\nClient\n               \n\n\n\nWeb Scion LLC. CT, \nUSA\nEnvironment\n      \n\n C#\n, ASP.NET and SQLServer 2000\nTeam size\n         \n\n\n\nRole\n                 \n\n: Team Member\n\n\n\nDescription:\n Web Based Appointment System facilitates the customers in scheduling online appointment for their vehicles. Search mechanism allows the user to select the services point by geographical region or the service details, which will be helpful in evaluating a vehicle of certain Made/model .The system mainly facilitates to the customer, Services provider & Administrator. The customer can log on to the site and can view the different services that are provided by the system and provider can use this system to update their services and appointment to the customer. The Admin can use this system to take important decisions regarding the service provide centers and to handle the system effectively. \n\nResponsibilities:\n GUI design, Development and Testing. \n\n\n\nPROJECT #6: IBSINDIA\n                                                 \n     \n\n(Aug 2004 ? January 2005)\nClient\n               \n\nICFAI\n\nINDIA\nEnvironment\n    \n\n ASP and SQL Server 2000\nTeam Size\n        \n: 2\nRole\n                 \n: Team Member\n\n\n\n\n\n1.\n Faculty Zone\n\n       \nThis system maintains and displays the various details of ICFAI faculty members from any centers all over India depending on privileges of user e.g. Appraisal systems to HR department and teaching and examination schedules, students interaction etc. to Academics Department. The process includes keeping the data of faculty members updated and showing it as of now basis. I am involved in gathering and analyzing requirements by meeting different level of users in different department of the organization, designed the module, helping programmers in coding and testing. My responsibility includes the maintenance and up gradation of the project. \n\n\n2. Online Student Registration\n       \n                  \nThis system maintains and displays the various details for semester registration like electives taken, fee structure etc. of all terms for students registered in \nICFAI\nBusiness\nSchool\n in any of the centers in \nIndia\n. The project helps in registering students online, making it a centralized process and provides information as of now basis. I was involved in analyzing requirements of the project, coding, and manual testing part of the project.\n\n3. Online Leave Application & Work-Load redistribution System\nThis system currently maintains the leave application and its status for ICFAI faculty members in \nHyderabad\n center and hence the related workload redistribution. It is currently done as a pilot project under my supervision, which is to be extended to all centers across \nIndia\n\n\nResponsibilities:\n\nDevelopment and Maintenance.',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-18',NULL,'2007-10-18','2010-06-10 12:14:22','2010-06-10',15,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(277,'Pallabi M',NULL,NULL,'Bhubaneswar','pal-mohdfvdfvanty@hotmail.com','pdval.dvvmodvandvty@gmail.com','91 6755 2220269','0','91 9861037402','0',NULL,'0','2007-10-13',8,24,'2010-06-10 12:14:22',15,'0',NULL,'200710/18/ATT14032.html','200710/18/DOC14040.doc','PALLABI MAHANTY\nPallabi M\n         \nM-12, BDA Colony, Khurda, Orissa, Pin-752055\nTelephone: (Cell) \n+91-9861037402\n\n(Res.) \n91-6755-2220269\nD.O.B ? \n\nnd\n September 1980\npal-mohdfvdfvanty@hotmail.com\npdval.dvvmodvandvty@gmail.com\n\n\n2.4yrs. of Application Software Development in .NET (ASP.NET, C#. NET) \n\n\nCAREER OBJECTIVE:\n            \nTo be a part of successful Team, that offers highly creative and challenging environment encouraging new ideas and providing a very good avenue for individual excellence and team effort.\nPROFESSIONAL SYNOPSYS:\n\n\n       \nHaving around \n2.4 Years\n Experience as a \nSoftware Engineer\n with extensive Knowledge in analysis, design, development and implementation.\n\n       \nGood Knowledge of \nSoftware Development Life Cycle (SDLC)\n\n\n       \nExtensively worked on the .NET tools like \nASP.NET, C#. NET.\n\n       \nGood expertise in RDBMS like \nMS SQL Server, Oracle.\n\n       \nHaving the \ngood knowledge of Web Service, XML\n\n\n       \nInterested to explore my self with new Technologies.\n\n       \nHave Good communication skills, interpersonal relations, hardworking and result oriented as an individual and in a team.\n\nPROFESSIONAL DETAILS:\n\n\n       \nPresently working as a \nSoftware Engineer\n in \nReM & MyAG, \nBhubaneswar\n, from \nNov. 2006 till Date\n\n\n       \nWorked as a\n Software Developer\n in \nNewgen Engineers\n\nBhubaneswar\n, from \nApril 2005 to Nov 2006\n\n\nACADEMIC CREDENTIALS:\n\n\n       \nMCA\n from Indira Gandhi National Open University (IGNOU), 2006.\n\n      \nB.Sc.\n from \nUtkal\nUniversity\n, Orissa.\n\nCERTIFICATIONS:\n\n\n       \nMicrosoft Certified Professional (\nMCP\n), Transcription ID: #3886541\n\n       \nIBM Certified \nE-Commerce\n Professional.\n\nIT SKILL SETS:\n\n          \nOperating System\n               \n: Windows XP\n          \nRDBMS\n                    \n: MS SQL Server 2000/2005,Oracle 9i\n          \nLanguages\n                        \n: C, C++\n          \nTechnologies\n                     \n: MS .NET 2.0(ASP.NET, C#. NET)\n    \n      \nInternet Technologies\n         \n: Java Script, HTML, DHTML, XML\n          \nPROJECT SUMMARY:\n\n#1 \nCareer Management Service\n\n      \nOrganization\n     \n: ReM & MyAG\n     \nTeam Size\n         \n: 7\n     \nTechnology\n       \n: ASP.NET 2005,C#. NET 2005,SQL Server 2000\nDescription\n        \n: C\nMS is a web portal where the recruiter and the jobseeker can\n   \nmeet their requirements. It?s different from other job portals in having a third party consultant who works as the interface for both of them while serving the best as per individual requirement. Posting new jobs, customization of current openings according to location, date, skill set, experience, Management of shot listed profiles according to company and interview scheduling, resume building are some of the USP of the project.\nResponsibilities\n\n\n\n   \nTaking active participation in System Analysis, URD, SRS design.\n\n   \nDesign, Coding.\n\n   \nUnit, Integration Testing.\n\n   \nProject Implementation.\n\n#2 \nHospital Management Solution\n\n     \nOrganization\n     \n: ReM & MyAG\n     \nTeam Size\n         \n: 5\n     \nTechnology\n       \n: ASP.NET 2005,C#. NET 2005,SQL Server 2000\nDescription\n        \n\nHospital Management Solution is a product, which caters most of the requirements of hospitals in India & Abroad. It primarily focuses on the modules like Patient Registration, Appointment Scheduling, Financial Accounting & Human Resource Management though the whole project consists of 24 modules and some sub modules. My individual module is Patient Registration. Online Appointment Scheduling, Different methods of patient registration, easy billing process, highlighting the visiting doctor according to the departments are some of the key features of the project.\nResponsibilities\n\n\n\n   \nSystem Analysis.\n\n   \nPreparation of URD, SRS.\n\n   \nDesign (Database, Form), Coding.\n\n   \nUnit, Integration Testing.\n\n#3 \nDWH Training Solution\n\n     \nOrganization\n     \n: ReM & MyAG\n     \nTeam Size\n         \n: 2\n     \nTechnology\n       \n: ASP.NET 2005,C#. NET 2005,SQL Server 2000\nDescription\n        \n: It is a web portal for registration of candidates for the Data Ware Housing Training. It caters both the registration of individual and corporate. It also facilitates the user to view the Brochure in .ppt format. The syllabus in the .PDF format is available in the portal. Search facility of the candidates already registered is also available.\nResponsibilities\n\n\n\n   \nSystem Analysis, Preparation of URD, SRS.\n\n   \nDatabase Design.\n\n   \nCoding.\n\n   \nUnit, Integration Testing.\n\n   \nImplementation.\n\n#4 \nGIMPEX INVENTORY MANAGEMENT\n\n     \nOrganization\n     \n: Newgen Engineers\n     \nTeam Size\n         \n: 4\n     \nTechnology\n       \n: ASP.NET 2003, C#. NET 2003,SQl Server 2000\nDescription\n        \n\nGIMPEX Pvt. Ltd. is leading ore Export Company of \nIndia\n. Basically it supplies Iron ore to various parts of \nIndia\n. The inventory management of the company is a challenge while it has various sources and many destinations and also a lot of stockyards. The application registers different contractors for a specific period for this export .ORE Percentage calculation, Stockyard management, Transport Management, Employee Assignment are some of the key modules of the project.\nResponsibilities\n\n\n\n   \nSystem Analysis, SRS preparation.\n\n   \nBack End, Front End Design.\n\n   \nCoding.\n\n   \nUnit, Integration testing.\n\n   \nDocumentation Preparation.\n\n#5 \nCall Monitoring System\n          \n     \nOrganization\n     \n: Newgen Engineers\n     \nTeam Size\n            \n: 5\n     \nTechnology\n       \n: ASP.NET 2003,VB.NET 2003,SQL Server 2000\nDescription\n        \n\nCall Monitoring System is an application mostly focusing on the customer care unit of computer vendors. This application fulfills the need of the computer vendors in recording different types of calls that normally comes from different types of customers. According to the queries of the customers and their complains and suggestions, it gives service.\nResponsibilities\n\n\n\n   \nFront End Design.\n\n   \nCoding.\n\n   \nUnit, Integration testing.','ReM & MyAG',1,NULL,'2007-10-18',NULL,'2007-10-18','2010-06-10 12:14:22','2010-06-10',15,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(278,'Nitin L',NULL,NULL,NULL,'nscitisacsan_leascuvsaca@yahoo.co.in',NULL,NULL,'0','09972882875','0',NULL,'0','2007-04-30',8,NULL,'2010-06-10 12:14:22',15,'1','2010-06-21','200710/18/ATT14036.html','200710/18/DOC14041.doc','<Please Type in your NAME here>\nNITIN L \n(M.E. (Computer) with 3+ exp. In .Net)\n                                   \n                                                                                   \n\nShree\nNivasa\nBuilding\n?(2nd\n\nFLR), \nMobile\n\n09972882875\n\nst\n Cross, 2\nnd\n Main, Near \nTrishul\nSchool\n\nEmail\n\nnscitisacsan_leascuvsaca@yahoo.co.in\n\nJ.P.Nagar 6\nth\n Phase,\n\n\n\nBangalore\n: 560078\n\n\n\n\nCAREER OBJECTIVE:\n\nI would like to contribute in the growth of a dynamic/progressive company using my Programming, Designing, Analytical and interpersonal skills. I enjoy working in a challenging environment, where I can utilize my experience/problem solving skills towards accomplishing major software projects.\n\nEXPERIENCE SUMMARY:\n\n\n         \nSecuring \n3+ years\n hand on experience in development of web based multi-tire application.\n\n         \nGood Understanding of \n\noftware \n\nevelopment \n\nife \n\nycle\n\n         \nStrong understanding of \n.Net Framework, ASP.net, ADO.net\n\nC#\n and \nMS SQL Server\n\n         \nGood at \nASP.Net 2.0\n\n         \nUnderstanding of \nWeb Service, Window Service \nand \nConsole application\n\n         \nAware of \nXML\n\nDesign Patterns, UML, \nJava Script \nand\n Remoting \n\n         \nSubmitted dissertation on \n\nCryptography Added Steganography?\n\nPROFESSIONAL EXPERIENCE:\n\nOrganization\n            \nDuration\n         \nDesignation\nSoftware information Solution\n(www.sisolindia.com)\nJune 2005 to till date\nSoftware Engineer\nRelative Solution\n(www.relativesolution.com)\nMay 2004 to Feb 2005\nSoftware Programmer\n\nTECHNICAL SKILLS:\n\nLanguages\n\n\nC#,\n\nVB 6.0\nFramework Knowledge\n\n.Net Framework\n\nWeb Technologies\n\nASP.net 2.0, ADO.net, HTML, Java Script,\n\nXML\nIDE\n\nVisual Studio .net \nApplication / Web Servers\n\nMicrosoft IIS\nRDBMS\n           \n\nMS SQLSERVER 2000, MS Access 2000\nOperating System\n\nWin XP professional, Win 2k Server\nOther \n\nMy Generation Tool\n\nEDUCATION HISTORY:\n\n\nDegree\nUniversity\nGrade\n\nM.E. (Computer Engg.)\n   \nD D University, Nadia, \nGujarat\n           \nSecond\nB.E. (Computer Engg.)\n\nNorth\nGujarat\nUniversity\n, Patan, \nGujarat\nDistinction\n     \nH.S.C\n   \nGSEB\nDistinction\n     \nS.S.C\n   \nGSEB\nDistinction\n\nPROJECTS:\n\nOrganization\n: Software Information solution, \nBangalore\n1.\n\nProject Name\n\nSDMS\n\n\n\n\n\nDuration\n\nFrom Jan 2007 to till date\n\n\n\n\n\nTools/Technology\n\nAsp.net \n\n2.0, C#, ADO.net, Window Service, Console Application ,SQL Server, IIS on Win Xp, My generation tool.\n\n\n\n\n\nDescription\n\n\noft \n\nocument \n\nanagement \n\nystem is especially designed to empower the presentation of soft documents. It retrieves the scanned image and converts into text file. The system also stands with optimized and intelligent recognition engine to search text from image. And also provide image navigation tool in case of searching from multiple images or inside single image. \nDifferent modules and their functionalities:\n\n      \nDocument management and text generation: \nIt retrieves specific types of scanned (printed or handwritten) image (or images in zip file) from remote location and apply strong OCR tool to generate text file from retrieved image. Store the generated contents in database. Also maintain all images as documents through out their life cycle.\n\n      \nSearch Engine: \nFacilitate the system to search text with different searching option from belonging images. Apply full-text indexing to make searching optimized and intelligent.\n\n      \nImage Navigation tool: \nProvide \noption to images navigate to first, last, next, previous, go to, zoom, email, print and download a document almost instantly.\n\n      \nAdministration:\n\nFacilitate the system to manage user information and various document information.\ndocuments.\n\n\n\n\n\nRole\n\nInvolved in LLD.\nInvolved in the design of Document management and text generation \nmodule\n\nAlso involved in the design of Administration module and Background Window service with Console application.\nInvolved in Search engine.\nDeveloped DAL layer, Business layer and \nASP\n.net pages.\nPeer-to-Peer Code Review, Unit Testing and Bug Fixing.\n        \n2.\nProject Name\n\nCASpeces\n\n\n\n\n\nDuration\n           \n\nFrom Feb. 2006 to Dec 2006\n\n\n\n\n\nTools/Technology\n\nAsp.net \n\n2.0, C#, Web Service, ADO.net, SQL Server, IIS on Win Xp,My Generation tool.\n\n\n\n\n\nDescription\n\n\nullen and \n\nssociates \nSpec\nification manage claimants with respective insurance companies. It provides services to different insurance companies. It provides facility to load new case when claimant comes with certain type of loss to belonging company. System also allows generating invoices as per the claim and company details. \n\nDifferent modules are described below:\n\n     \nAdministration:\n Provide functionalities to manage Users, Insurance Companies and Claim Adjusters.\n\n     \nPayment:\n Maintain the payment information regarding to the claim.\n\n     \nCase Load Log:\n Let the user to manage case information.\n\n     \nReport:\n Generate various kinds of reports like Adjuster Summary, Invoice Summary and Adjuster Invoice Summary. \n\n     \nInvoice: \nTo generate, maintain and print the Invoice information.\n\n\n\n\n\nRole\n\nInvolved in LLD.\nCompletely involved in the design of \nAdmin panel module\n\nInvolved in the design of Case Load Log module.\nDeveloped DAL layer and ASP.Net pages.\nPartially involved in design of Web Service.\nInvolved in Peer-to-Peer Code Review, Unit Testing and Bug Fixing.\n\n3.\nProject Name\n\nLMS\n\n\n\n\n\nDuration\n           \n\nFrom Aug. 2005 to Jan. 2006\n\n\n\n\n\nTools/Technology\n\nAsp.net\n\n2.0, C#,\n\nADO.net, SQL Server, IIS on WinXp\n\n\n\n\n\nDescription\n\n\neave \n\nanagement \n\nystem is designed for managing application, recommendation and sanctioning of leave requests as well as to keep track of the staff members as to where he/she is present at a particular moment. There are mainly three modules in this system, Leave Management, Person Tracking and the Daily Timings Record modules.\n\n\n\n\n\nRole\n\nInvolved in LLD.\nCompletely involved in the design of leave management and\nadmin functionality.\nDeveloped DAL layer, Business layer and ASP.Net pages.\nPeer-to-Peer Code Review, Unit Testing and Bug Fixing.\n\nOrganization\n: Relative solution, Nadiad, \nGujarat\n4.\nProject Name\n\nEIS\n\n\n\n\n\nTools/Technology\n\nC#, ADO.net, ASP.net, SQL Server, IIS on Win Xp\n\n\n\n\n\nDescription\n\n\nducation \n\nnformation \n\nystem: Strong and robust intranet based application provide various functionalities to students, faculties, non-teaching members and admin of the system. The main aim of EIS to make paper less institutional activities. Different modules are described below.\n\n\n      \nAdministration: \nPowerful module to provide admin level functionality such User and privileges management.\n\n      \nInformation: \nOriented to gather information about students, faculties, and available asset.\n\n      \nDocument Upload: \nFacilitates the faculties to upload assignments, notices, result of the test conducted, lecture notes, lecture planning in time and scheduled based manner.\n\n      \nFeedback and analysis: \nThis module provides online feedback functionality and generates performance result of faculty in particular subject in term.\n\n      \nReports: \nProvide facility to generate various kinds of reports.\n\n\n\n\n\nRole\n\n\n       \nInvolved in LLD.\n\n       \nDeveloped DAL layer as well as Business layer and ASP.net pages for site.\n\n       \nCompletely involved in the design of \nAdmin panel module\n\n\n       \nInvolve in Feedback Analysis module.\n\n        \nPeer-to-Peer Code Review, Unit Testing and Bug Fixing.\n\n   \n\nM E dissertation\n\nCryptography Added Steganography\n\n\n\n\n\nDuration\n           \n\nFrom Jun. 2004 to Apr. 2005\n\n\n\n\n\nResearch Area\n\nImage Steganography and Cryptography\n\n\n\n\n\nTools/Technology\n\nVB 6.0\n\n\n\n\n\nDescription\n\nCAS:\n   \n\nThis research oriented application designed for security aspect. \n\n\n       \nThis application allows user to hide text file (information containing file) inside the bitmap image file (Cover image).\n\nThe user can send the Stego image (information text file + cover image) on insecure channel.\n\n       \nI have used \nHigh Capacity Image Steganography Model \nto embed the text file in to cover image. This model work on texture information of image and provides \nhigh embedding capacity\n and \ninvisible image distortion.\n\n       \nI have also provided the extra security layer that first converts the text file into encrypted text using \nAdvanced Encryption Standard\n algorithm.\n\n       \nOnly the intended end user can extract the text file and then can decrypt that text file to have meaningful information\n\n\n\n\n\n\nPERSONAL QUALITIES:\n\n\n         \nEnthusiastic and committed to maintain quality and efficiency.\n\n         \nFast & self-directed learner, work effectively independently or as team player.\n\n         \nGood communication and problem solving skills.\n\n         \nEnjoy new challenges and willing to take on extra responsibilities to get work done.\n\nPERSONAL DETAILS:\n\nName \n\nLeuva Nitinkumar Bhagwandas.\nDate of Birth\n\nAug. 21\nst\n , 1982\nSex\n\nMale\nMarital Status\n\nDouble',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-18',NULL,'2007-10-18','2010-06-10 12:14:22','2010-06-10',15,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(279,'Neeraj Kumari',NULL,NULL,NULL,'neegnragngnjinfo@sify.com','togngnmergnginfo@sify.com','0120 4120287','0','9868048403','0',NULL,'0','2008-04-29',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-10 12:14:22',15,'0',NULL,'200710/18/ATT14037.html','200710/18/DOC14042.doc','Curriculum ?Vitae\nCurriculum ?Vitae\n                                                                        \n     \nCommunication Address\n\n                                                          \n    \nHouse no.9/648,Vasundhra\n                                                                        \n    \nGhaziabad\n\n\n 201012\n                                                                        \n     \nPhone:(0120)?4120287,M:-9868048403\n                                                                        \n     \nEmail Add\n\n\n\nneegnragngnjinfo@sify.com\n\n                                                                   \n              \ntogngnmergnginfo@sify.com\n\nNEERAJ \n\nKUMARI\n\n____________________________________________________________\n                                                                                   \n                                                                        \nObjective\n                 \n\n    \nTo work in challenging atmosphere to\n\nProfessional\nQualification excel in Performance & to ensure every step\n\nforward\n\nreducing the gap to perfection\n\nJob\n                       \n\n   \nSoftware Developer in TT-Tech \n\ndevelopment devision)\n    \nNoida UP \nINDIA\n\n\n(fom-may 2005) \nEXPERIENCE\n\n      \n2 year of experience in Software Development\n\n      \nWorking experience on ASP. Net, C#, VB.NET, SQL SERVER\n\n      \nResponsible for Developing Web Based applications using Microsoft.Net (C#, ASP.Net)\n\n      \nResponsible for Developing Window based applications using Microsoft Technologies (VB.Net),\n\n      \nCrystal Report, SQL Server2000\n\nTechnical Profile\n\n                        \nOperating System \n        \n\n     \nWindows 98, 2000 &XP/NT\nLanguages/Scripts\n         \n\n     \nC, C++, C#, VB.NET\nWeb Technologies\n        \n\n      \nASP.NET,HTML\nData Base\n        \n         \n   \n\n     \nMS-SQL Server 2000, Oracle/MS-Access\nOther Software Tools \n\n     \nHTML,XML,Flash,Word, and\n\nPower Point\n\nNET Skills\n\n      \nStrong understanding of \n.NET framework\n\n\n      \nASP.NET\n\nVB.NET, C#\n, Strong OOPS Concepts.\n\n       \nCan develop Both Windows and Web Applications.\n\nProfessional Qualification\n\n   \n\nMCA \nfrom IGNOU \n                                                            \n\n    \nDone \nPGDCA\n from IGNOU\n                                                            \n\n   \nDiploma \n.NET\n application and XML \n                                                            \n            \n\n    \nWeb Service (\nVB.NET, ASP.NET, C#, XML\n\n      \nFrom NIIT\n                                                                        \n\n    \nAnd \nSQL Server \n2000 from NIIT\nAcademic Qualification\n                   \n\n     \nB.Sc. (Zoology, Botany & Chemistry)\nIn\n\n1994 with 55% marks from\n   \nC.C.S.University, \nMeerut\n\n     \nM.A. (Economics) in 1997 with 54% \n      \nMarks from C.C.S.University, \nMeerut\nCurriculum Project & Research Summaries\n\nProject : # 1\nProject Name\n             \n\n      \nAutomation of Authorized Service Station [Hero Honda ]\nClient\n                          \n\n           \nAuthorized Service Station [Hero Honda Automobiles]\nOrganization\n               \n\n           \nTT-Tech\n\nNoida\nOperating System\n\n    \n\n           \nWindows 2000\nTechnology\n     \n     \n       \n\n\n          \nASP. Net, C#,\n MS SQL Server 2000\nDuration\n      \n          \n\n         \nIN Progress (Total duration - Eight Months)\nRole\n                \n             \n\n          \nDeveloper(form \nDesigning and Coding.\n\nDescription\nThis is a web-based application. \nProject is based on the requirement of Automobile Industry. It has three\n   \nmodules Sales, Spares and Service. This is fully web-based project.\n\nContribution\nAs a team member, I was responsible for \n\n        \nAnalysis of the specifications provided by the clients\n\n        \nDevelopment and Helping the Team\n\n        \nCoding using ASP.Net , C#,\n\nHTML,\n\nJavaScript\n\nProject : # 2\nHospital Management System\n         \nClient\n\n                        \n\n           \nVasundhara\nHospital\nGhaziabad\nOrganization\n               \n\n           \nTT-Tech Noida\nTeam Strength\n      \n\n        \nFour.\nDuration\n               \n\n         \nseven Months\n            \nLanguage/Technology\n\n   \nASP. Net, C#,\n MS SQL Server 2000\nPlatform\n      \n          \n\n         \nWindows XP\n\nRole\n                           \n\n           \nDeveloper\nDescription\n     \n            \n\n           \nMaintains the Records of Hospital\n\nReports Generation and Maintenance\nThis is fully web-based project\nProject : # 3\n                                    \nInventory Management Software\nProject Title\n                   \n   \n\n     \nPetrol pump?s inventory management Software\nLanguage/Technology\n\n\n. Net Technologies (VB.Net), SQL Server2000\n\nTeam Strength\n      \n   \n\n      \nFour.\nPlatform\n                \n   \n\n      \nWindows2003 (Server)\nDuration\n               \n   \n\n      \nNine Months\nDescription\n\n          \n   \n\n      \nProject is based on the requirement of Petrol pump. It is complete Automated Software for petrol pump, which contains complete inventory management of petrol pump, involving transaction module, employee module, stock module etc. It was a window-based project and Crystal Reports Generation.\nRole\n\n\n         \nI worked as a developer on this project and was an active member of the project team. I have assigned the job to developed Form-Design, Codes of Enterprises ?Transaction Module, Stock module and reporting part of these modules\n\nStrengths\n                                \n\n      \nKeen to learn new things & ready to accept challenges.\n\n      \nStrong fundamental knowledge of software development process including design, documentation, development, testing, debugging and maintenance of commercial applications\n\n\n      \nPatience and cooperation in teams.\n\n      \nAbility to convey technical concepts to non-technical audience.\n\n      \nFriendly Nature,Confident\n\n      \nFlexible to adjust in changing environment\nPersonal Profile\n\n\n          \nFather?s Name\n             \n\n           \nLate Shri Inder Singh Tomer\n            \nDate Of Birth\n                \n\n           \nAugust 15, 1975 \n            \nMarital Status\n               \n\n           \nUnmarried\n            \nAddress\n                       \n\n           \nHouse no.9/648,Vasundhra,\n                                                            \nGhaziabad\n, U.P. 201012\n            \nPhone \n\nNo.\n                  \n\n           \n(0120) ?4120287, M: -9868048403\n\n            \nSalary Expected\n         \n\n           \nNegotiable\n\n            \nThe above statements are true to the best of my knowledge and belief.\n\nDate: \nPlace: \nGhaziabad\n U.P.\n\n                                                                                                \n(NEERAJ KUMARI)',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-18',NULL,'2007-10-18','2010-06-10 12:14:22','2010-06-10',15,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(280,'Nagi R',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0','9848730365','0',NULL,'0','2007-09-28',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-10 12:14:22',15,'0',NULL,'200710/18/ATT14043.html','200710/18/DOC35079.doc','1+Years of Experience in Software Development\n\n\n        \n  \n\n            \nObjective\n\n\nAssociate with a progressive organization that gives me the scope to apply my knowledge and skills especially in the area of software development and to be a part of the team that dynamically work towards the growth of the organization\n\n\n                        \nSUMMARY\n\n\nHaving \n2.6+\n\nyears of experience in the IT Industry in Application Development on \n             \nMicrosoft .Net Platform\n\n       \nHaving Knowledge on Microsoft .NET Technologies.\n\n       \nHands on experience in WSE (web service enhancement) which provides security.\n\n       \nHands on Experience in Security issues in .net using WSE.\n\n       \nGood knowledge on creating \ntokens \nlike Username token, mutual certificate token.\n\n\n       \nFamiliar with .net framework 2.0 \n\n       \nSAML (Security Assertion Markup language) Specification usage in .net.\n\n       \nClear understanding of connected and disconnected architecture in ADO.net.\n\n                        \nPROFESSIONAL EXPERIENCE\n\n\n\n       \nWorking as software programmer in \nVarnar Softech Ltd\n, from October 2006 to till date.\n\n       \nWorked as software programmer in \nSparsh Communication Ltd\n\nHyderabad\n from January 2005 to October 2006.\n\n            \naCADEMIC PROFILE:\n\n\n       \nB.Tech \nfrom Jawaharlal Nehru Technological affiliated University, \nHyderabad\n in Computer Science Engineering.\n\n     \nskill set\n\n\nOperating Systems\n                       \n: MS-DOS, Windows\nLanguages\n                        \n          \n: C, C++, C#.net, VB.Net \nData Base\n                         \n          \n: SQL Server 2000/2005\nFront-end Tools\n                 \n          \n: Visual Studio.net\nSecurity Technology\n                     \n: WSE (in .net) \n                                                    \n\nSAML (Security Assertion Markup language) \n                                                \n\nSSL (security Socket Layer)\n         \nData access Technology\n     \n          \n: ADO.Net\nWeb technologies\n               \n          \n: C# with ASP.net, VB.net with ASP.net \nMarkup Languages\n              \n          \n: HTML, XML\nScripting Languages\n            \n          \n: JavaScript\nVersion Controller \n                        \n: Visual Source safe \n\n    \n\nproject handled\n\n\nProject 1:\nTitle\n    \n          \n  \n                 \n\n       \nFreshAdz\n       \nTeam Size\n      \n\n                  \n\n       \n\nRole\n    \n                   \n  \n                 \n\n       \nTeam Member \nTechnologies\n     \n                \n\n       \nC#.net 2.0, Asp.net 2.0, Sql server 2005\nOrganization\n                      \n\n        \nVarnar Softech Ltd, \nHyderabad\nOperating System\n    \n\n          \n\n       \nWindows 2000\n                      \n\nDescription\nFreshAdz is an advertising website where a viewer can find ads based on location. FreshAdz provides most valuable aspect of the e-business revolution, offering business the opportunity to save costs, increase revenues, improve productivity, and reengineer inefficient workflows/business processes. Goal is to build a network B2B portal where companies can find post there trade offers and maximize revenue. Application is packed with high end features to provide a very sound foundation, offers great earning potential. The site offers services such of quality control, customer care management, marketing and in-house management.\n\nA successful online presence can now be one that combines a company web site and vertically integrated industry-specific Portal consisting of many different products, services, solutions and modules reaching different media platforms and channels such as WEB and E-mail able to attract and retain much more unique visitors than any other single company web site.\n\nResponsibilities\n\n\n         \nInvolved in development of Employee management.\n\n         \nDisplaying the ads page according to the location.\n\n         \nWorking on the videos playing in the web site.\n\n         \nActively participated in development of business entity.\n\n         \nInteracted with developers to resolve application defects.\n\n         \nInvolved in Unit testing.\n\nProject 2:\nTitle\n    \n            \n                 \n\n       \nKamae search reports\nTeam Size\n      \n\n                  \n\n       \n\nRole\n    \n                   \n  \n                 \n\n       \nTeam Member \nTechnologies\n     \n                \n\n       \nC#.net 2.0, Sql server 2005\nOrganization\n                      \n\n        \nVarnar Softech Ltd, \nHyderabad\nOperating System\n    \n\n          \n\n       \nWindows 2000\n                      \n\n\n\n\n\nDescription\nThe basic idea of this project is to generate reports and search of an existing database. When the client wants to generate customized reports which is not possible by his existing application, kamae reports facilitates to generate reports without disturbing exiting database by saving data into application database itself.\n\nKamae Report Generator is to generate reports from any database supplied. It is a generalized tool designed to fit into any application. It should not have any dependencies on other modules of the application. It uses windows service for sending reports which is an optional service. Each user has got access roles and admin is super user. The application provides user friendly and efficient reporting to end user. \n\nResponsibilities\n\n\n         \nInvolved in front end design of kamea search reports.\n\n         \nDeveloped back ground worker process for report display.\n\n         \nActively participated in development of business entity.\n\n         \nDesign and developed system tray icon for notification.\n\n         \nInteracted with developers to resolve application defects.\n\n         \nStudying and review the use cases.\n\n         \nInvolved in Unit testing.\n\nProject 3:\nTitle\n    \n            \n                 \n\n       \nExciteHomeMedia\nTeam Size\n      \n\n                  \n\n       \n\nRole\n    \n                   \n  \n                 \n\n       \nTeam Member \nTechnologies\n     \n                \n\n       \nC#.net, ASP.net, Sql server 2000\nOrganization\n                      \n\n        \nVarnar Softech Ltd, \nHyderabad\nOperating System\n    \n\n          \n\n       \nWindows 2000\n                      \n\nDescription\nExcite Home media Entertainment is a website which is used for the cable TV operator?s management. The project keeps track of cable TV operator?s information, such as maintaining the geographical information across different places of all subscribers who are authorized and also keeps track of in-house management related to the company.\n\nIn this website they can able to manage their subscriber?s information, also keeps track of collections and billing of all customer?s information and company information. This website acts as a global one so that many users will maintain their own information. The reports provide efficient information for decision making\n\n\nResponsibilities\n\n\n         \nInvolved in Development of Customer information System.\n\n         \nInteracted with developers to resolve application defects.\n\n         \nDeveloped Business Entities for the application.\n\n         \nStudy and review the test cases.\n\n         \nInvolved in Unit Testing.\n\n\n\nProject 4:\nTitle\n    \n            \n                 \n\n       \nSAC\nTeam Size\n      \n\n                  \n\n       \n\nRole\n    \n                   \n\n\n                 \n\n       \nTeam Member \nTechnologies\n     \n                \n\n       \nC#.net, ASP.net 2.0, WSE 3.0, Sql server 2000\nOrganization\n                      \n\n        \nSparsh Communication Ltd, \nHyderabad\nOperating System\n    \n\n          \n\n       \nWindows 2003\n                      \n                          \nDescription\n\n\nSAC Compliance Gateway service that is an XML-based technology that incorporates cryptographic processes to provide robust authentication and compliance services. The Compliance Gateway technology allows SAC to provide a complete security infrastructure solution that can be customized to unique business policies across individual markets.\n\nThis technology and service model layers directly into an organization?s application and process infrastructure to enforce user and message authentication policies, and compliance requests for data access and collaborative design transactions.\n\nThe SAC model includes digital certificates, Secure ID tokens, smart card tokens, and even user-name password solutions that can also leverage any existing identity framework the organization has already deployed.\n\n\nThe SAC Compliance Gateway receives and begins to process the incoming transaction.\n\nUsers and messages are authenticated and validated, and are processed against the business policies that are created and managed by the organization.\n\nThese business policies dictate the compliance privileges and entitlements that the user has for the requested transaction. \n\n\nResponsibilities\n\n\n         \nInvolved in the design and analysis of the project SAC.\n\n         \nWorked on Web services enhancements (WSE 3.0).\n\n         \nCreated Mutual certificate token in the application.\n\n         \nCreated username token in the application.\n\n         \nAs a team member was given all the specifications and Created SAML token.\n\n         \nInteracted with developers to resolve application defects.\n\n         \nInvolved in Unit Testing.\n\n\nProject 5\n\n\nTitle\n                                 \n\n        \nStock picking\nTeam Size\n                         \n\n        \n\nRole\n                                 \n\n        \nTeam Member\nTechnologies\n     \n                \n\n       \nC#.net, ASP.NET, Sql server 2000\nOrganization\n                      \n\n        \nSparsh Communication Ltd, \nHyderabad\nOperating System\n    \n\n          \n\n       \nWindows 2000\n                 \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nDescription\n\n          \nA web site is all about to run an ongoing stock picking contest. The project consists of two parts: first is Contest playing and second the functional aspects of showing winners in three positions and retrieving stock prices. \n          \nThe contest part of it goes like this: A registered user can pick stocks from a list of pre selected stocks and save his picks. The system monitors the stock prices of the pre selected stocks during a trading day. At the end of a trading day, a winner is picked according to certain criteria.\n\nResponsibilities: \n\n\n         \nInvolved in User Interface designing and coding. \n\n         \nInteracted with developers to resolve application defects.\n\n         \nInvolved in Unit testing.\n\n     \npersonal profile\n\n\nName \n                     \n: T. Nagireddy.\nMartial Status\n          \n: Single.\n                  \nContact Number \n      \n: 9848730365.\nPermanent Address \n\n: Vengalrao nagar, Door No: 8-3-199/F,\n                             \n\nOpp.Saibaba\nTemple\n\nHyderabad\n\n                      \n      \n                                                                               ',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-18',NULL,'2007-10-18','2010-06-10 12:14:22','2010-06-10',15,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(281,'Mukesh Kumar',NULL,NULL,NULL,'mubfkdbgsdbesh17fb8@rediffmail.com',NULL,'09412384467','0','9891330162','0','9312558284','0','2008-04-29',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-10 12:14:22',15,'0',NULL,'200710/18/ATT35078.html','200710/18/DOC35080.doc','ASHU DUBEY Mobile- 9891330162, pp-09412384467\nMUKESH KUMAR\nSoftware Engineer\nExperience 2+ years\n\n\nD-336, Street No. 20\nWest Vinod\n Nagar \n\nNew Delhi-\n 110092\n\n\n\n\nMob.:\n\n9312558284\nEmail:\n\nmubfkdbgsdbesh17fb8@rediffmail.com\n\n\n                                                                           \nOBJECTIVE\n     \nTo work at a growth oriented position in a professionally managed and dynamic organization that provides opportunities for development and responsibilities to contribute toward organization?s success.\n\n\nSUMMARY\n        \n   \nSoftware professional with working experience of \n2+ years\n using Microsoft Technologies on window and web based applications. Having good aptitude for learning, adaptability to any environment, challenge, variety and pressure drive me to achieve results within the given time frame.\n\n\nWORK EXPERIENCE\n\n\n       \nCompany\n               \n\neTech online Pvt. Ltd., \nNew Delhi\n\n       \n\n     \nDesignation\n         \n: Software Engineer\n     \nPeriod\n        \n          \n: Sept. 2005 to till date\n\n       \nCompany\n               \n\nSR Infotech Pvt. Ltd., Gurgaon.\n\n\n              \nDesignation\n         \n: Software Engineer\n              \nPeriod\n        \n          \n: March 2005 to Sept 2005\n\n                                     \n\nQUALIFICATIONS SUMMARY\n\n\n       \nM.C.A.\n From \nIndira Gandhi National Open University\nin Dec. 2004\n\n\n       \nC.O.P.A.\n from \nI.T.I. Muzaffarnagar \n\n(U.P.)\n\n       \nB.Sc.(Maths)\n From \nC.C.S.University, \nMeerut\n in 1999\n\n\nSKILL SET\n\nLanguages \n              \n   \nC#, VB.NET, \nCrystal\n Reports\nInternet Technology\n   \nASP.NET, XML, HTML, JAVA-SCRIPT\nRDBMS \n                    \n   \nSQL Server 2000\nMethodology\n            \n   \nObject Oriented Modeling, IIS, .NET-Framework\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nPROJECT DETAILS\n\n1.\n   \nTitle:\n                           \neRetail\n\n\nundergoing\n\n                  \n\nPlatform & Tools\n\n\n   \nASP.NET, C#, SQL Server 2000 \n\nTeam size\n             \n\n   \n\n\nDuration\n              \n\n\n   \nJune 2007 to till now\n\nResponsibility\n\n  \n\n\n\n  \nResponsible for The Specification Design, backend \n                              \n         \nProgramming, Coding and Integration Testing.\n\nDescription:\n\neRetail software can handle the goods that sale to the customers or purchase from the venders. User can see the items available in the stock, And give the purchase order to the supplier. After that retailer set the MRP of that product that include freight charge, packaging pricing, margin. Then retailer sales item to the customer. Customers can payment by credit card, cheque and cash. \n\n\n2.\n       \nHR \nManagement SYSTEM \nPlatform & Tools\n     \n\n   \nC#, ASP.NET,\n\nSQL Server 2000 \nTeam size\n                \n\n   \n\nDuration\n                \n     \n\n\n   \n6 months\n\nDescription:\n This software handles data of Recruiters (Several companies) who are looking for suitable candidates for their vacancies, and will be most useful for Consultants for searching of matching Job with Jobseekers.\n                      \n\n3.\n      \nCollege Management Software\n\n          \nPlatform & Tools\n     \n\n\nVB.Net SQL Server 2000 \n          \n               \nClient\n\n                       \n\n\n\nU.C.E.R., \nAllahabad\n               \nModules\n                     \n\n\n1. \nAcademic \n2.\n Admission\n           \nTeam Size\n                \n\n\n\n        \nDuration\n                   \n\n\n8 months\nDescription: \nThis Project is basically used for all those college, which solves the entire function of Institute/college. Academic module as its name suggest handles all the related academic activity of the student & teachers. It provides the details of the subjects, examination, student marks, occasions, etc. Library Module maintains all the details of books, magazines, suppliers and also the details of bookbinder. In addition to this user can also issue/return the books and the system itself handles the condition of fine. \n\n\n\n4.\n      \nBUDGET MONITORING SYSTEM\n          \n\nPlatform & Tools\n   \n\n\nVB.Net, SQL Server 2000 \n      \nTeam Size\n              \n\n\n\n          \nClient\n                \n         \n\n\nTrident Corporation Limited, \nChandigarh\nDuration\n                \n\n\n6 months\nAbout\n\n\nThe Budget Monitoring System Software is software for monitoring the budget of any organization.\n\nThe software will maintain the total of the Budget allocations and the expenses incurred during the current financial year. The software will give all the functionality for monitoring the budgeted transactions. \n\n\nProject made in SR Infotech Pvt. Ltd.\n\n5.\n      \nLibrary Management Software \n          \nPlatform & Tools\n     \n\n\nvb.net, SQL Server 2000 \n          \n               \nClient\n\n                       \n\n\n\nNIFD, \nChandigarh\n           \nTeam Size\n                \n\n\n\n        \nDuration\n                   \n\n\n6 months\nDescription: \nThis software maintains all the details of books, magazines, suppliers and also the details of bookbinder. In addition to this user can also issue/return the books and the system itself handles the condition of fine. Hostel module gives the complete solution to handle the records of hostel facility provided by the institute\n\n\nPersonal Information\n          \nName\n             \n    \nMukesh Kumar\n          \nFather?s name\n\n   \nSri N.R.Saini\n          \nDate of Birth\n       \n     \n1st Oct 1978\n          \nSex\n                  \nMale \n          \nNationality\n          \nIndian \n          \nMarital Status\n\n     \nUnmarried\n          \nLanguage\n           \nHindi, English\n          \nHobbies\n            \nPlaying Cricket, Reading Newspaper, Watching movies. \nStrength:\n\n       \nAdopt any situation easily\n\n       \nRegular & punctuality\n\n\n\n\n\n            \nDATE:\n            \nPLACE:\n                                                                                  \nMUKESH KUMAR\n\n\n\n\n\n                   ',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-18',NULL,'2007-10-18','2010-06-10 12:14:22','2010-06-10',15,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(282,'Mudit Kumar',NULL,NULL,'NEW delhi','mdvdudit_26dvvadvugust@rediffmail.com',NULL,NULL,'0','9899422109','0',NULL,'0','2008-01-12',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-10 12:14:22',15,'0',NULL,'200710/18/ATT35081.html','200710/18/DOC35083.doc','Resume\nMUDIT KUMAR\n32-tilak khand, GIRINAGAR, KALKAJI, \nNEW delhi\nMOBILE\n 9899422109; E\n-mail \nmdvdudit_26dvvadvugust@rediffmail.com\n\n\nEXECUTIVE SUMMARY\n\n2.2 Years of \nworking experience in Application Development using Microsoft .NET Technologies. Currently working with \nA1 Technology\n Pvt. Ltd.\n\nNew Delhi\n as a Software Developer. \n\n\nTECHNICAL SKILLS\n\nDomains\nTechnologies / Tools / Languages\nLanguages\nC#,VB.NET,\n ASP.NET, Java Script ,Xml ,Html \nDatabase\nMS SQL Server \nReporting Tool\nCrystal Report \nOperating Systems\nWin 9x/xp, 2000,2003 Server\n\n\nPROFESSIONAL / ACADEMIC QUALIFICATIONS\n\n         \nM.C.A\n\nfrom U.P. technical University in 2005. \n\n         \nB.Sc.\n from \nPurvahchal\nUniversity\n, Jaunpur (U.P) in 2001.\n\n         \nXII\n from U.P. Board in 1998.\n\n         \n\n from U.P. Board in 1996.\n\nPROJECTS \n\nIn the reverse chronological order\n\n\n\n\n\n1.\n       \nOrderiton \n                                   \n                          \nFebruary ? 07 ?Till Date\n\nDescription\n\nOrderiton is a restaurant-based site using by \nU.S.\n people. This site keeps all the information about the registered merchant in this site. User of this site can see all the information about his favorite?s restaurant by entering area or name of that restaurant and can place online order for his items and pay money online. A new merchant can also be registered in this site. \nTo see this site click here.\n\nwww.orderiton.com\n\n\nCompany:\n                                           \nA1 Technology Pvt. Ltd\nClient:\n                                                   \nAndrew Cusmano, U.S.A\nTeam Size:\n                                         \n\nLanguages & Tools\n\n       \n          \n      \nC#, ASP.NET\nDatabase:\n                                            \nSQL Server \nRole:\n                                     \n                \nDeveloper\n\n2.\n       \nLunchHourSale \n                                       \n                          \nOctober ? 06 ?January? 07\n\nDescription\n\n\nIt?s an e-commerce site were the user can purchase one item in a speculated time. Which displays the product for a particular time? With in speculated time you have to place an order for that particular product. If either of the limits is over (time or product) accordingly the status is displayed. It also displays the next product to be sold. Apart from that this site is having the feature of Free Day where all remaining items are available for sale.\n\nTo see this site click here.\n\nwww.lunchhoursale.com\n\n\nCompany:\n                                           \nA1 Technology Pvt. Ltd\nClient:\n                                                   \nAkiva Tauber, U.S.A\nTeam Size:\n                                         \n\nLanguages & Tools\n\n       \n          \n      \nC#, ASP.NET\nDatabase:\n                                            \nSQL Server \nRole:\n                                     \n                \nDeveloper\n\n\n\n3.\n       \nDemand Management System \n                          \n\nApril ? 06 ?August? 06\n\nDescription\n\nThe Demand Management System (DMS) use between Accenture and his Business Leads or Client Partners to capture the details of a horizon/prospect or a confirmed contract. This tool will capture the details of a demand for seats from any of the verticals of the BPO operations. The demand could be raised from any of the verticals for a said number of seats, which could be demanded by the BL or client partner in a consolidated fashion for a shift at a particular location. \nThe BL can also define the ramp-up plan into the system. A provision is provided in the Contract creation wherein the month-wise break up of the total demand could be entered as well as day-to-day break up\n\n\nCompany:\n                                           \nEastern Software Systems (\nSEI CMM Level 5)\nClient:\n                                                   \nAccenture, Banglore\nTeam Size:\n                                         \n\nLanguages & Tools\n\n       \n          \n      \nC#, ASP.NET, \nCrystal\n Reports\nDatabase:\n                                            \nSQL Server \nRole:\n                                     \n                \nDeveloper\n\n\n\n4.\n       \nWarehouse Inventory Management System \n                \n     \nNov ? \n05 ? March ?06\n\nDescription: \nThis Application has developed for managing the inventory of warehouses. This software keeps all the record of product, which are coming in warehouses from their vendors or going from warehouses to their Channel Partner.\n\nCompany:\n                                           \nRsoftech Pvt. Ltd\n\nTeam Size\n\n                                          \n\nLanguages & Tools\n\n       \n          \n      \nVB.NET, \nCrystal\n Reports\nDatabase\n\n                                            \nSQL Server \nRole:\n                                     \n                \nDeveloper\n\n\n\n5.\n       \nComplaint Management Information System\n                   \nJuly ? 05 ? Oct ? 05\n\nDescription: \nIn this software the officer/staff members of the company can register their complaints about the computer related equipments online to the different maintenance vendors authorized by the company. There is a unique complaint number generated for each complaint. The person who registers the complaint can see the online status of the complaint by entering this number.\n\nCompany:\n                                           \nRsoftech Pvt. Ltd\nTeam Size\n\n                                          \n\nLanguages & Tools\n\n       \n          \n      \nC#, ASP.NET\nDatabase\n\n                                            \nSQL Server \nRole:\n                     \n                \n                \nDeveloper\n\n\n\n\n\n\n6.\n       \nIntraMEF \n                    \n\n               \n                                                \nJan ? 05 ? April ? 05\n\nDescription\n: The IntraMEF is a Website Developed for the employees of Ministry\n of Environment & Forests. This site provides all the information about all employees. Employee can view their Pay slip, and all other information.\n\nCompany:\n                                           \nNational\nInformatics\nCenter\nClient\n\n                                                   \nMinistry of Environment & Forests\nTeam Size\n\n                                          \n\nLanguages & Tools\n\n       \n               \nASP.NET\nDatabase\n\n                                            \nSQL Server \nRole\n                                                       \nTrainee\n\n\n\nPERSONAL DETAILS\n\nFather? Name\n                                 \nR.S.Lal Srivastav\nDate Of Birth\n                                     \nOctober 26, I983\nMarital Status\n                                    \nSingle\nHobbies\n\n                                              \nListening Music\n\n\n\n\nDate:\n                                                                                 \n                                                \n(Mudit Kumar)','A1 Technology Pvt. Ltd',1,NULL,'2007-10-18',NULL,'2007-10-18','2010-06-10 12:14:22','2010-06-10',15,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(283,'M Nadeem',NULL,NULL,NULL,'nfdbadfbfbeefdbm.bbbfbs@gmail.com',NULL,NULL,'0','9221045100','0',NULL,'0','2007-04-30',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-10 12:14:22',15,'0',NULL,'200710/18/ATT35082.html','200710/18/DOC35085.doc','M Nadeem\nM Nadeem\n302 / 305 Abis Manzil, \nArab Lane\n\nGrant Road\n (E) Mumbai ? 400 008\nnfdbadfbfbeefdbm.bbbfbs@gmail.com\nMobile\n: 9221045100\nPROFILE:\nA Senior Web Developer with a wide range of experience in both server and client side technologies. Able to work on my own initiative and as a part of a team. Dedicated to maintaining high quality standards. Good interpersonal skills and a productive team player.\nMAJOR ACHIEVEMENTS:\n\n        \nPromoted as Administrator for Gemini Bug tracking software.\n\n        \nPromoted as a Trainer in setting-up Sub Version Control System for newly recruits.\n\n        \nSolved cross-browser related problems.\n\n        \nDeveloped client side reusable components which are used in multiple projects.\n\n        \nSolved and handled major user interface markup (HTML, DHTML and JavaScript) related problems.\n\n        \nInitiated the design, user interface of many websites that has been developed.\nEXPERIENCE:\n2004 ? Date\n\nZeus Systems Pvt. Ltd.\n                           \nZeus is an e-learning solutions company. The company is majorly involved in live in-application simulations delivered over the internet.\n                        \nhttp://www.zeuslearning.com\n\n2005 ? Date\n\nContent Management Systems\nTechnology: \nMS-SQL 2005, AJAX, ASP.NET, C#, HTML, DHTML, CSS, JavaScript, XML, Photoshop, MS-Excel 2007.\n                        \nAug 07 ? Date\n           \nDiscovery Exploration CMS\n\nDiscovery Exploration CMS is used by Zeus and Discovery to track the status of the project. It is also used as a content delivery system where both parties upload, download and view the content. \nAjax\n enabled website for quick-page loading.\nResponsibilities and Achievements:\n\n        \nResponsible for designing a rough draft of the website using MS-Excel 2007, to get actual approval of the design and then use Photoshop to create graphics, icons of the website by coordinating with the graphic designer.\n\n        \nDeveloped a mail component for the website using .NET classes and C#, this component should send a notification mail to the parties whenever a new content is uploaded.\n\n        \nGuided freshers mostly in JavaScript, HTML and CSS, also took initiative to review their task. \n\n        \nSetup a bug tracking project in Gemini for tracking issues, bug and code review related to CMS.\n\n        \nPromoted as a Gemini Bug tracker Administrator.\n\n\nApr 07 ? Date\n            \nDestination Science CMS\n\nThis CMS majorly used by 4 - 5 companies across globe and by Internal Zeus. It is used for managing content developed by Zeus in English language. The final output of the product will be localized in Arabic language by another company. This company will use CMS as a source for localization. The website is Ajax-based for quick page loading and multi-browser supported.\n\nResponsibilities and Achievements:\n\n\n        \nMajorly participated at the time of designing the architecture of the website.\n\n        \nSolved and implemented the cross-browser related problem and also provided alternate solution to the team lead.\n\n        \nSuggested and implemented an error handling system at the initial stage of development.\n\n        \nDeveloped a generic class which changes the website CSS based on the server details for differentiating local v/s online CMS, This helped Zeus QA team to remove confusion as they have to do QA both local and online simultaneously.\n\n        \nDeveloped various admin maintenance utility which helped many team to remove repetitive task.\n\n        \nDeveloped a Bug Tracker with complex filter and sort criteria for the QA team. This feature helped the team to do their task quickly and more effectively.\n\n        \nDeveloped an Image Library module for Zeus content, graphic artist, and flash animators. This module contains hi-res images which can be used across or within teams.\n\n        \nCreated a utility which copies server data to the clipboard of the user.\n\nApr 06 ? Apr 07\n        \nBilli ? CMS Prentice Hall\nBilli is a feature-packed multifunctional Content Management System (CMS) that is being used to generate and manage the content intended for the CMS of a large publishing house.\n\nThe live CMS offers interactive training and evaluation in Microsoft Office 2007 products, using a simulation engine developed by Zeus Learning.\n\nResponsibilities and Achievements\n\n\n        \nImplemented \nAJAX\n for quick page-loading and easy web-based editing of content, using JavaScript on client side and C# and ASP.NET on server side. We?ve used http handler for processing \nAjax\n request.\n\n        \nSolely handled and manage CSS of the entire website. Also, developed graphics, icon for the site using Photoshop.\n\n        \nDeveloped a reusable components, menu and tree component which at present is used in other CMS site (Destscience and Discovery explorations).\n\n        \nDeveloped a common library class which is used to format Date, Name to title case etc?\n\n        \nResponsible for programming content module which act as a centralized coordination between authors, editors, technical reviewers, software developers, quality assurance teams, and audio vendors across five different organizations.\n\n        \nProgrammed SQL stored procedures used in content module such as Add, Edit, and Delete Content.\n\n        \nGuided team members in developing HTML markup, and solve HTML markup errors.\n\n2005 ? Date\n\nFlash Programmer\nTechnology: \nC#, MS-SQL, ASP.NET, BinHex Editor, Flash 9, Action Script 2.0, XML.\nDec 06 ? Feb 07\n       \nScience Sleuth ? Discovery\nScience Sleuth is a 100% web-based application from a desktop-based application. Its core is a flash-based engine which plays over 24 mysteries and each episode is driven by XML.\n\nResponsibilities and Achievements:\n\n        \nUnderstood and documented the binary file (pkt) structure using BinHex Editor.\n\n        \nResponsible to extract the data from binary file using C#, SQL and ASP.NET.\n\n        \nProgrammed a small website which was used by other programmers for reading, extracting data from the binary file and storing into the database and images on disk.\n\n        \nProgrammed an additional feature which creates XML file and store it on the website along with the other resources. This XML file later used by flash-based engine to load its resources and data.\n\n        \nProgrammed a Calculator in flash Action Script which is used as an interactive tool in the player.\n\nNov 06 ? Dec 06\n       \nFlash-based E-book \nThis application was developed for discovery targeting Kindergarten children; it is an electronic version of a printed book with features like navigating book by flipping pages, Zoom and Pan Tool, simple activities for children. \n\nResponsibilities and Achievements\n\n        \nResponsible to complete this project solely.\n\n        \nManage to complete this project before the deadline.\n\n        \nAble to learn and grasp Action Script 2.0 in 5 days prior the project.\n\n\nQUALIFICATIONS / EDUCATION:\n\n                        \nBachelor of Management Studies, \nMumbai\nUniversity\n                        \n2004, Major in Finance. \n                       ',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-18',NULL,'2007-10-18','2010-06-10 12:14:22','2010-06-10',15,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(284,'Megha Bansal',NULL,NULL,NULL,'mescsgha.bscansevscal.svemegs@gmail.com',NULL,'0124 2329135','0','9818485717','0','0124 2329135 95124','0','2007-04-30',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-10 12:14:22',15,'0',NULL,'200710/18/ATT35084.html','200710/18/DOC35087.doc','CURRICULAM VITAE\nMEGHA BANSAL\n\nAddress for Correspondence:\n                                 \n   \n\nE-mail: \nmescsgha.bscansevscal.svemegs@gmail.com\n\n\n  H.No. 380/16\n                                                \n    \n     \nPhone:\n 0124 - 2329135 (95124 from \nDelhi\n\n  Nai Basti                                                              \n              \n                     \nMobile\n\n9818485717\n  Gurgaon, Haryana -122001 \n\n\nOBJECTIVE\n\nTo hold a challenging and competitive position in an organization where I can enhance my skills and strengths and can prove my caliber in conjunction with company\'s goals and objectives.\n\nWORK EXPERIENCE\n\n& SKILL SET\nTotal Experience: 3+ years\nIT\n\nExperience: 2+ years(.NET Technology)\n\n    \n\n\n\nGood communication skills, fluency in English.\n      \n\n Good team working and planning skills \n      \n\n Adaptive to work in different conditions\n      \n\n Perseverance.\n      \n\n Innovative and creative.\n      \n\n Determination, patience, lively.\n      \n\n Create friendly atmosphere at workplace.\n      \n\n Easily understand new concepts and also a keen learner of new things.\n\n   \nClient Interaction Skills. \n\n\nTECHNICAL SKILLS\n\nLanguages\n                       \n: C, C++, Visual Basic, VB.NET(1.x, 2.0), C#.\nWeb Tools\n                        \n: ASP.NET(1.x, 2.0), XML, HTML.\nMethodology\n                     \n: Object Oriented Programming (OOPs), ADO.NET\nDatabase Management\n      \n\nSQL Server 2005, MS-Access 2005\nTools\n                                 \n: Dreamweaver 4,Photoshop 7\nOperating System\n         \n     \n\n\nWin-98, Win-XP\n\n        \n\n\nQ3 TECHNOLOGIES (present)\n\nDuration\n            \n\nfrom March 2006 till present\nProject Title\n      \n\nDevelopment of Core Services.\nEnvironment\n     \n\nASP.NET 2.0, C#, Sql Server 2005\nDescription\n\n    \n\nChemOffice and ChemOffice Ultra provides pleasant environment for the chemistry professionals to create new molecules or to setup a reactions, etc. ChemOffice gives best environment to store and to manage the chemical data. This enterprise application for development and deployment of scientific information is being used in chemical and pharmaceutical organizations. Using this application all the work can be automated. There are various features of this product like Registration of various chemical compounds, Inventory Management. \n                        \nCore services forms the basic of the all these major features running, and is the search method employed to get the result from the database. I?m creating these core services.\n                              \nIt?s a 3-tier architecture, which has a presentation layer, business layer \n\n                              \nand a Data Access Layer(DAL). Presentation layer calls Business layer (BL) via a web service, which in turn loads data access layer to perform the desired function from the database. This application works for any kind of backend database used (Sql Server 2005, Oracle 10g or MS-Aceess 2005). Depending on the user?s choice of the database, DAL objects establishes a connection with the database, and performs the required operations and return the data to BL which is returned to presentation layer via web service.\n                              \nThere is a single DAL.cs for every core service, which contain sql scripts for all the function to be performed. For the different database viz Oracle, Sql server or MS-Access, there are Database specific files which have few overridden functions, exclusive for the databases. \n                                                                                                                                                                        \nRole\n                   \n\n\n Software Developer\nTeam Size\n           \n\n\n\nResponsibilities Included:\nCoded the Business Logic Layer, Data Access Layer using Db Provider Factories and C# classes, for various core services viz. HitList Management Service, Form View service, Query Criteria, Data View Service.\nHave written sql scripts for all the functions in Data Access Layer for all the core services. \nHave added database specific files and written the overridden functions and also their corresponding sql scripts. \nGenerated the unit tests, provided by Visual Studio 2005, for the functions of BL and had checked them against any error.\nHave written serialization function for the XML data for the clob field in oracle and vice versa to deserialize them.\nHave designed the custom control for HitList Management Service.\nHave prepared a web service for the HitList Management service to be called by the mock presentation layer.\n\nS.R.INFOTECH\n   \n\nDuration\n            \n\nfrom Jul 2005 to Feb 2006 \n                                                                                         \nProject Title\n      \n\n\nCampus Pro?Institute Management Software\nEnvironment\n\n   \n\n ASP.NET(1.1) , C#, HTML, VB.NET (1.1)\nDatabase\n    \n       \n\n\nSQL Server 2003\nDescription\n\n      \n\n\nInstitute Management Software that maintains the details \n    \n     \n\nregarding the students studying in the school, their fee \n          \nstructure, faculty\n                          \n     \n     \nteaching in the school and every other details regarding \n  \n          \nschool management.\n          \nRole\n\n                 \n\n Software Developer.\nTeam Size\n         \n\n\n\n\n\nResponsibilities Included:\n                         \nInvolved in developing modules, Admission, Fees, Faculty, separately in ASP.NET with C# as code behind language, and VB.NET. \nDeveloped major forms in the modules.\nInvolved in testing and formatting of the modules.\nDeveloped the stored procedures used by the applications. \nHeld a key position in the team\n\nINFO VISION GROUP\n\nDuration\n        \n\n\n\nJun 2004-Jun 2005\nDesignation\n     \n\n\nTechnical Support Engineer\nJob profile\n      \n\n\nHave worked\n with OneTel Inbound process and dealing with queries \n                             \nrelated to setting up of dialup network connection and configuring outlook \n                             \nexpress and handling all the problems regarding internet\n\n\nAcademic Projects Undertaken\n\n\n1.) TRANSPORT MODULE\n\nC-DOT\n\nDescription\n                \n\nThe project deals in the study of CFITL (C-dot?s Fiber in the \nLoop\n).\n     \nvarious components of Fiber Access System, which forms the \n\n     \nbackbone for the delivery of advanced services that will make \n\n     \ncopper installation obsolete tomorrow, were studied.\nTeam size\n                \n  \n\n  \n\n                                                                                                         \nResponsibility \n           \n\n   \nHave prepared the documentation flow of the project for the \n                                          \ncompany.\n\n\n2.) VIDEO LIBRARY\n\nNIIT\n\nEnvironment \n           \n\nVisual Basic 6.0\nDatabase\n                \n\n\n: SQL Server 2000\nTeam Size\n                \n\n\n\nDescription\n          \n\n  \n\n\n\nVideo Library is a project that maintains the various details of a \n  \nvideo library like sale of cassettes, send on rent.\nResponsibility\n          \n\n   \nAnalysis, Design, Coding, testing of the project\n\n\nTRAINING DONE\n\nDone 6-weeks training in C-DOT, \nNew Delhi\n, June-July 2001.\nDone 8-weeks training in NIIT, Gurgaon, June-July 2002.\n\n\nFinal Semester Project:\n\n1.) REGISTRATION OF VEHICLE\n\nEnvironment\n            \n\n\n    \nVisual Basic 6.0\nDatabase\n                  \n\n\n    \nMS-Access\nTeam Size\n                 \n\n    \n\nDescription\n                \n\n\nThe project aims at developing of software for registration of vehicle.\nResponsibility\n            \n\n   \nAnalysis, Design, Coding, testing of the project\n\nEDUCATIONAL QUALIFICATIONS\n\n   \n\nB.E.(Computer Science) with 69.25% in 2003 from Lingaya?s \nInstitute\n of \nManagement\n and Technology, \nFaridabad\n (Haryana), affiliated to \nM.D.\nUniversity\n, Rohtak (Haryana).\n\n\nPassed XII with 66.7% in 1999 from \nMount Carmel\nSchool\n\nNew Delhi\n\n\n\nPassed X with 76.4% in 1997 from Lady of \nFatima\nConvent\nHigh School\n, Gurgaon (Haryana).\n\n   \n\n2 months certificate course in C++ from Excel Computers, Gurgaon\n\n   \n\n2 months course in Visual Basic from NIIT, Gurgaon\n\n   \n6 months course in .NET (VB.NET, ASP.NET, XML,C#,SQL Server) from NIIT, Gurgaon\n\n\nEXTRA CURRICULAR ACTIVITIES\n\n\n\nActive organizer of stage activities.\n\n Active participant in group discussions, seminars.\n\n   \nPresently reformatting the website \nwww.checklaptops.com\n and adding features like user login, security and role authentication, searching techniques, and improving the overall design of the website using ASP.NET 2.0 AND C#.\n\nPERSONAL DETAILS\n   \nDate of Birth\n          \n\n        \n22,Oct,1981\n   \nLanguages \n     \n   \n\n\n\n      \n\nEnglish, Hindi.\nHobbies\n              \n    \n\n       \nWriting\n\nphrases and thoughts, Anchoring stage shows.\n\nDate:\n\nPlace: Gurgaon\n                         \n                                                    \nMegha Bansal',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-18',NULL,'2007-10-18','2010-06-10 12:14:22','2010-06-10',15,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(285,'Ambika  s',NULL,NULL,'Chennai ','amcscbixsxka_sscsdancssdckari@yahoo.co.in','ambika_sankari@yahoo.co.in','0462 2521167','0','94438 52428','0','98411 65156','0','2007-04-14',8,24,'2010-06-10 12:14:22',15,'0',NULL,'200710/18/ATT35086.html','200710/18/DOC35088.doc','ARUNKUMAR\nAMBIKA S\n    \n                           \nNo 27/6, \nIndirani Street\n\nAyyavoo Colony,\n\nNear to MR Hospital,\nAminjikarai,\n      \nChennai ?600 029.\nEmail: \namcscbixsxka_sscsdancssdckari@yahoo.co.in\nMobile\n: 94438 52428, 98411 65156\n    \n\nPERSONAL DETAILS:\n\nFather?s Name \n                        \n\n         \n\nS.Madasamy\nDate-of-Birth\n                \n\n           \n28-12-1978.\nSex\n                              \n\n         \n\nFemale\nNationality\n                   \n\n        \n   \nIndian\n                          \nLanguages Known\n       \n\n         \n\nEnglish, Tamil\nE-mail\n                           \n\n          \nambika_sankari@yahoo.co.in\nPermanent Address\n     \n\n           \n461,J,Jeyanthi Nagar, VM.Chathram,Tirunelveli-627011,\n                                                \nTAMILNADU.\n   \nPH: 0462-2521167.\n\n\nOBJECTIVE:\nSeeking a position to utilize my skills and abilities in the Information Technology Industry that offers Professional growth while being resourceful, innovative and flexible.\n\nPERSONAL SKILLS:\n\n          \nComprehensive problem solving abilities\n\n          \nExcellent verbal and written communication skills\n\n          \nAbility to deal with people diplomatically\n\n          \nWillingness to learn\n\n          \nTeam facilitator\n\nEXPERIENCE SUMMARY:\n\n          \nHaving \nmore than 40 months\n of experience in software development\n\n          \nWorked as a Software Developer at \nNanda Solutions Pvt. Ltd.\n\n          \nWorking as a Software Developer at \nNittany Outsourcing Services.\n\nACADEMIC EXPOSURE:\n\n          \nMCA with 72% at \nManonmaniam\nSundaranar\nUniversity\n, Tirunelveli, Tamilnadu.\n\n          \nB.S.C with 70% at \nSadakathullah\nAppa\nCollege\n\nManonmaniam\nSundaranar\nUniversity\n, Tirunelveli, Tamilnadu.\n\nTECHNICAL CERTIFICATION:\n\n\n          \n1 Year Course in \nNIIT\n, which includes \nSQL Server 7.0 , VB 6.0 , C++ \n\n          \n4 Months Course in \nNIIT\n which includes \nXML,VB.NET,ASP.NET with C#\n\n          \nMCP\n Certified in \nVB.NET\n\nTECHNICAL ACUMEN:\n    \n            \nDatabases\nSQL Server 7, 2000\nProgramming Tools\nVisual Basic 6.0, Visual Basic.Net\nWeb based\nASP.Net\nScripting Languages\nPERL , PROCOMM, POWER TERM\nReport Generation Tool\nSeagate Crystal Reports\n\n\nPROJECT DETAILS:\n\nAt Nittany OutSourcing Services., Chennai\n\n1.\n\nAccounts Receivable Tools(AR Tools)\nTeam Size\n       \n\n           \n\nEnvironment\n   \n\n           \nMS SQL Server 2000 , Visual Basic .NET 2.0\n\n           \nThis application automates the Claim data entry process by reading the data from the text file , interpreting the data, validating and transferring it to the database.\n\nClaims are allocated and worked and finally sent to Insurance .\n\nResponsibilities : \n\n          \nCreated the PERL Script to extract the data from the text file and transfer the data to the database. \n\n          \nDesigned and Developed Upload Module, Process and Reallocation Module.\n\n          \nProvided support in generation of reports.\n\n2.\n\nWeb Scan Log\nTeam Size\n       \n\n           \n\nEnvironment\n   \n\n           \nMS SQL Server 2000 , Asp.Net 2.0\n\n           \nThis Application was developed for raising an Issue and responding to a raised Issue.\nBoth the Client and Company Person can raise an Issue to each other. A raised Issue can be closed only by whom it is created. Files are downloaded through FTP and displayed for the client. \n\nResponsibilities : \n\n          \nInvolved in Analysis and Documentation. \n\n          \nDesigned and Coded Login Screen, Calendar View, Raising and Responding to Issues. \n\n\n3. Velocity\nTM\n Billing Software :\nTeam Size: 6\nEnvironment: MS SQL Server 2000, Asp.Net 2.0\n\n            \nThis software covers a range of activities associated with a Medical Billing such as scheduling, charge entry, claim generation & transmission, cash posting, patient billing and AR Analysis. It employs extensive reporting & querying options and user-defined rules to ensure clean claim production and timely reimbursements. \n\nResponsibilities :\n\n          \nWorked towards developing higher versions of the software with focus on bug correction and optimization. \n\n          \nDesigned and Coded Master screens, Release Notes and Version Change module, Developed Time zone based production reports, Resolution module, worked on Reports module, Power Search module.\n\n          \nTesting and Documentation of the product \n\n\n4.\n\nNDS Admin Tool\nTeam Size: 4\nEnvironment: MS SQL Server 2000, Visual Basic .Net \n\nNDS Admin Tool is an administrative tool used by the HR and MIS teams to maintain Recruitment, Employee and Production Details related information. The software is used to store, track and analyze all administration and HR related data like employee details, team listing, transfers and deployment, attendance maintenance and activity tracking. It provides many reports, which help to monitor the daily production. \n\nResponsibilities :\n\n          \nDeveloped the activity tracking system used by all employees of the company on a daily basis.\n\n          \nWorked on leave tracking, transfer and swipe tracking reports.\n\n          \nWorked on Permission, resume master and HR letter formats module.\n\n\n5. Cost To Company (CTC)\nTeam Size: 1\nEnvironment: MS SQL Server 2000, Visual Basic.Net\n\nThis application was developed using Visual Basic.Net. The system is used for calculating the overall cost to the company of each project.\n\nThe reports generated by this application provide an accurate account of the contribution of each project to the company?s total CTC.\n\nResponsibilities : \n\n\n          \nDesigning and Development of the Project \n\n          \nProvided support in generation of periodical reports.\n\n\n6. Quality Audit\nTeam Size: 2\nEnvironment: MS SQL Server 2000, VB.Net 2.0\n\nDeveloped for the Quality Audit Team, this application enables error capture, communication and correction thereby contributing to improvement in quality of production. It also provides many reports for Error Analysis.\n\nResponsibilities : \n\n\n          \nDesigned and developed the Monthly Audit Plan and Internal Audit Module and master screens. \n\n          \nCreated Error Analysis and Monthly Plan deviation Reports.\n\n7.\n\nElectronic PD Upload Application\nTeam Size: 2\nEnvironment: MS SQL Server 2000, Visual Basic 6.0\n\nThis application automates the Patient Demographics data entry process by reading the data from the electronic text file, interpreting the data, validating and transferring it to the database.\n   \n\nResponsibilities : \n\n\n          \nCreated the PERL Script to extract the data from the electronic text file and transfer the data to the database. \n\n          \nWorked on back-end procedures and front-end forms for validation and modification of data as required.\n\n8.\n\nOptical Character Recognition (OCR)\nTeam Size: 3\nEnvironment: MS SQL Server 2000, Asp.NET\n\nThis is an application meant for the automation of the data entry process. Here the data is captured through OCR from a scanned image file. Thereafter it is formatted and made available to the user for Validation. The data is then validated by the users through the Audit screen and later uploaded into the System.\n\n9. Protraining\nTeam Size: 2\nEnvironment: MS SQL Server 2000, Asp.Net 2.0\n\nThis is an application meant for the training department. The project consists of screens for Trainers as well as trainees. The data entered by trainers is compared with the data entered by the trainees and reports are generated for errors made by the trainees.\n\nResponsibilities : \n\n\n          \nCreated the Screens used for trainers and data comparison reports. \n\n\n10. Nittany Administration Tool(NAT Tool)\nTeam Size\n       \n\n           \n\nEnvironment\n   \n\n           \nMS SQL Server 2000 , Visual Basic .NET\n\nThis Application is developed for the Production Department and for Administration. This Project is used for keeping track of the candidates attending the interviews and\n\nto have the details of each employee. File Allocation Module is responsible for classifying the scanned files to each departments . Report will be generated to keep track of the employees production. \n\nResponsibilities : \n\n          \nDeveloped Resume Master Module,Internal Audit Module,Error Capture Module.\n\n          \nDesigned File Allocation Module\n\n          \nProvided support in generation of periodical reports.\n\nAt Nanda Solutions Pvt. Ltd., Chennai\n\n11. Financial Accounting System (FINAS)\nTeam Size\n       \n\n           \n\nEnvironment\n   \n\n           \nMS SQL Server 7.0 , Visual Basic 6.0\n\nThis software is developed to prepare Challan, Journal, Day Book, Trial Balance and Balance Sheet. The entries in the Challan are automatically posted in the ledgers.\n\nBoth the Day Book entries and the challan entries are posted by a single data entry screen automatically .Final accounts like Income & Expenditure Statement, Trial Balance and Balance Sheet are provided. \n\nResponsibilities : \n\n          \nDesigning and Development of the Project \n\n          \nProvided support in generation of periodical reports.\n\n12. Automated Payroll System (APS)\nTeam Size\n       \n\n           \n\nEnvironment\n   \n\n           \nMS SQL Server 7.0 , Visual Basic 6.0\n\nAPS 1.0 is a Payroll Automation s/w. It helps to prepare salary bills. This Software helps to prepare salary bills very quickly and precisely. This System is used to prepare pay slip and maintain required Registers in the Special Village Panchayat\n\nOffices. \n\nResponsibilities : \n\n          \nDesigning and Development of the Project \n\n          \nProvided support in generation of periodical reports.\n\nDECLARATION:\n\nI hereby declare that the above written particulars are true to the best of my knowledge and belief.\n\n                                                                                                \nYours Sincerely,\n                                                                                    \n          \nM.Ambika Sankari.\n           ','Nittany Outsourcing Services',1,NULL,'2007-10-18',NULL,'2007-10-18','2010-06-10 12:14:22','2010-06-10',15,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(286,'Mahesh M',NULL,NULL,NULL,'mfbahfbefbsh_mirfbjfbe@yahoo.com',NULL,'91 8338 267508','0','9886541409','0',NULL,'0','2008-04-29',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-10 12:14:22',15,'0',NULL,'200710/18/ATT35089.html','200710/18/DOC35091.doc','RESUME\nMahesh M\n        \nH.No 59B,\n\nrd\nMain Road\n, Prashanth Extension,\nWhitefield Road\n\nBangalore-66,\nKarnataka\n\nIndia\n\nMobile\n: 9886541409\nPh ? 91 8338 267508\nE-mail: \nmfbahfbefbsh_mirfbjfbe@yahoo.com\n\n\n2+ years of Professional Experience of executing Web Applications using Microsoft Technologies.\n\n\nObjective:\n\nSeeking a competitive and challenging environment with scope for career advancement and exposure towards the progress of your esteemed company.\n\nACADEMIC QUALIFICATION\n\nBachelor of engineering, Information Science and Engineering, from \nA.M.C\nEngineering\nCollege\n\nBangalore\n under \nVishveshwariah\nTechnological\nUniversity\n\nBelgaum\n\n\nExamination Passed\n\n\nBoard \n\n   \nInstitution\n\n\nYear \n\n\n% of Marks\n\nBE(Info Science)\n\nVTU\n\nAMC Engg. College \nBangalore\n\n2005\n\n\n71.37%\n\nP.U.C\n\nP.U.Board\n\nG.I.B. Nipani\n\n2001\n\n\n73.16%\n\nS.S.L.C\n\nK.S.E.E.B\n\nS.K.H.S.Benadi\n\n1998\n\n\n70%\n\nSkill Set:\n\nOperating System: Windows 98, Windows 2000, Windows XP\nDatabase: MS-SQL Server 2000 and MS-Access. \nProgramming Languages: ASP.Net, VB.net, C# \n\n\n\nBrief Career\n\nPresent Organization\n\nAffiliated Computer Services, Inc. (ACS), ITPL \nBangalore\n\n(www.acs-inc.com)\nDuration: 1\nst\n August 2005 to till date\nDesignation: \nSystems Development Associate.\nResponsibilities: Analyzing, Designing & Developing of project\n\n\n\n\n\n\nProjects Worked: \n\n1. Learning Management System\nTeam: 4\nTechnology Used: C#, ASP.Net and MS-SQL Server.\nResponsibility: Developing of the project and also maintaining communication with clients during the period of project development.\nDescription:\n\nLMS is developed for tracking registration, grades, class scheduling, tests, test results and other administrative requirements of e-Learning. This can be used for people who involved in call centers, product support or in any place where e-Learning takes place. It had modules like Corporate Admin, learner, Developer, Editor. The major entity called Program which has number of courses that in turn contains lessons and Topics. These are composed by the Developer (The authorized person who conducts this training program). One of the features is to have Audio and Video merged with the training session. Learning Management System project is to build a framework using which a domain expert can build learning programs using rich media contents. And the Learner will assess the Programs online.\n\nLMS is a very user friendly application with a pleasant appearance.\n\nThe content available in LMS holds rich multi-media files like flash and other images. The LMS system is envisaged as having a four-tiered architecture\n\n\n2. Training log \nTeam: 4\nTechnology Used: C#, ASP.Net with MS-SQL Server\nResponsibility: Developing of the project and also maintaining communication with clients during the period of project development.\nDescription: To centralize the capture and reporting (billing) of training hours incurred in Customer Care sites. At the end of each day, trainers in customer care center from each location log into a Traninglog website where they could enter the names of the attendees for the day?s classes.\n\nEach day?s training log would capture the following information of class attended. Once a log has been completed by a Trainer, the log would be ?submitted? and an email notice should be sent to the Payroll Coordinator who would carry out their duties as it relates to moving the payroll hours in the Ultipro system and recording the number of payroll hours moved for the date of the class. All data would be stored in a SQL database when submitted. The PC would update the log with the number of payroll hours transferred from ?production? to ?training?.\n\nThe log would then compute the number of hours which could be reported as billable (billable training hours could not exceed the number of payroll hours for an employee for the day).\n\nThe PC would then submit the log to the Ops Manager for review and approval.\n\nUpon their final ?approval? of the log, the log would be locked and could not be edited.\n\nEach person who ?approved/submitted? the log would have their name appear on the log \n\n\n\nEnterprise\n Data Warehousing\n\nTeam: 6\nTechnology Used: VB 6.0 with MS-SQL Server\nACS is having many call centers across the \nUS\n. Call centers are handling calls which landing to their call center. Calls are distributed by the call center switch. This switch been customized to deliver the call details in the form of flat file (raw data) to each call center FTP site. The main objective of this project is to capture all these files to the centralized location to process the data. While collecting the data, it must make sure that there is no data loss or data addition etc. The entire process will be logged for the verification process. The named itself indicates that the application is used to generate various kinds of customer care reports. This project consists of two modules. \n\n1.\n    \nA windows based application designed using VB 6.0., and SQL Sever 2000, generates\n     \nvarious kinds of reports on user request in excel format.\n2.\n    \nIntranet application designed using Asp.net, SQL Server 2000 and \nCrystal\n reports, to view the customer care reports online.\n\n\n\n\n\nMy strengths and experiences\n\nA good team member.\nQuick Learner.\nGood command over spoken and written English.\n\n\n\n\n\nPERSONAL DETAILS\n\nNAME:\n                                           \nMahesh Mirje\n                    \nDATE OF BIRTH:\n       \n               \n\n22\nnd\n July, 1982\nFATHERS?S NAME:\n   \nMr.Annaso Mirje.\nSEX:\n                                               \nMale\n                                     \nNATIONALITY:\n                          \nIndian\nMARITIAL STATUS:\n\nSingle\nLANGUAGES KNOWN:\n            \nEnglish, Kannada, Hindi and Marathi.\nCAN READ:\n                 \nEnglish, Kannada, Hindi and Marathi.\nCAN WRITE:\n                               \nEnglish, Kannada, Hindi and Marathi.\n\nDECLARATION\n\nI hereby declare that the above information is true to the best of my knowledge and understanding.\n\n                                                                                                      \n             \nMAHESH MIRJE',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-18',NULL,'2007-10-18','2010-06-10 12:14:22','2010-06-10',15,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(287,'Jeeten Kumara',NULL,NULL,NULL,'jeetdvedvdndra.kdvudvmar11@gmail.com',NULL,NULL,'0','09810735800','0',NULL,'0','2008-04-29',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-10 12:14:22',15,'0',NULL,'200710/18/ATT35090.html','200710/18/DOC35092.doc','CURRICULUM VITAE\nCURRICULUM VITAE\n\nJeeten \n\nKumar\n     \n                                                                               \njeetdvedvdndra.kdvudvmar11@gmail.com\nA-388, New Ashok Nagar,\nNew Delhi-96\nMobile No\n-09810735800\n\nObjective:\n                                                                                                                   \nTo develop my career as a Software Engineer where I will be valuable team member, contributing quality ideas and work for an organization where there is an ample scope for individual as well as organizational growth in Software Design & Development.\n\nWork Experience:\n\nI have 2.0 years experience in the field of Web development using (Asp.Net, C#, Sql Server, JavaScript, Xml, Xsl, Html, Css).\n\nCompany Name\nJob Title\nDuties & Responsibility\nDuration\nInfoaxon Technologies Ltd.(H-189, Sec-63, Noida)\n\nwww.infoaxon.com\n\nSoftware Engineer\n(.Net)\nCoding\n\nusing C#, Asp.Net, HTML(Client Side validation,\n\ndynamic page creation, database design)\nAug, 2005- Till Date\n\n\nPrimary Skill Sets:\nProgramming Language\n\n: -C#, C++\nScripting Language\n                   \n: -Asp.Net, Java Script, Css, Html, Xml, Xsl, Ajax.\nOperating system\n                      \n: - Windows Server-2000, Windows- XP\nDatabases\n                                \n: - SQL Server 2000, Oracle 9i, MS Access\n\nSoftware Development Skills: -\nSoftware Development Skills: - Asp.Net, C#, JavaScript, SQL Server 2000, CSS, HTML, XML, XSL.\n\nProfessional Qualification:- \n      \nMSC (IT)\n from Sikkim Manipal University and Scored first division in 2007.\n      \nBSC (IT)\n from Sikkim Manipal University in 2004.\n\n     \nAcademic Qualifications:\n      \n\n          \nIntermediate (10+2) with Physics, Chemistry and Math from UP Board in 2001.\n          \nMatriculation (10\nth\n) from Bihar Board in 1999.\n\nPROJECT HISTORY\n\n\n\n   \nPROJECT-1\n\nProject Title\n                  \n: AgrHosting\nURL\n                             \n\n\nhttp://www.agrhosting.com/\nSoftware Tool\n              \n: Asp.Net, C#, HTML, CSS\nEnvironment\n                 \n: Windows 2000 Server\nDatabase\n                      \n: Sql Server 2000.\nRole\n                             \n: Dynamic page creation, Client side validation, Database\n\ndesigning.\nTeam Size\n                    \n: 2\n\nDescription:\n\nThis is complete package for Shopping Cart site. AGR offers Web Hosting, Domain Name Registration, Web Design, Email Services, Technical Training and Enterprise Network Solutions. There are two sections in this project: user, admin. Through admin section, admin can manage their home page like Hosting, Domain, Services, Support, Customer Orders, Shipping Module, Photo Gallery, and Static Page content using FCKeditor. On user section, user can browse products and can purchase products online through ?Paypal? Payment gateway integration.\n\n\n   \nPROJECT-2\n\nProject Title\n                  \n: Castrol BikeZone ? Site Builder ? Castrol India Limited.\nSoftware Tool\n              \n: Asp.Net, C#, HTML, CSS\nEnvironment\n                 \n: Windows 2000 Server\nDatabase\n                      \n: Sql Server 2000.\nRole\n                             \n: Dynamic page creation, Client side validation, Database\n\ndesigning.\nTeam Size\n                    \n: 5\n\nDescription:\n                \n\nhis is a web-based application for the Castrol India Limited to automate their franchisee through web application. The project uses Façade, Adapter and Factory Design Patterns.\n\n\n\n   \nPROJECT-3\n\nProject Title\n                  \n: Job Tracking System.\nSoftware Tool\n              \n: Asp.Net, C#, HTML, CSS\nEnvironment\n                 \n: Windows 2000 Server\nDatabase\n                      \n: Sql Server 2000.\nRole\n                             \n: Dynamic page creation, Client side validation, Database\n\ndesigning.\nTeam Size\n                    \n: 3\n\nDescription:\n                \nThis project has developed for Self Office that give the information about job status of each project and it also give information employee attendance\n\n\n\n   \nPROJECT-4\n\nProject Title\n                  \n: Shop Automation System.\nSoftware Tool\n              \n: Asp.Net, C#, HTML, CSS\nEnvironment\n                 \n: Windows 2000 Server\nDatabase\n                      \n: Sql Server 2000.\nRole\n                             \n: Dynamic page creation, Client side validation, Database\n\ndesigning.\nTeam Size\n                    \n: 2\n\nDescription:\n            \nThis project has developed for Medical Shop that give the information about how many medicine sale and how many in stock also give price and total amount information.\n\nPersonal Skills\n\n       \nComprehensive problem solving abilities, excellent verbal and written communication\n   \nskills, ability to deal with people diplomatically, willingness to learn, team facilitator.\n\nAchievements\n                 \nManagerial\n                                \n   \nSchool Leader\n                 \nExtra Curricular \nParticipated and registered meritorious performance as team member in various sports and games at school\n\n             \nPersonal Details\n\n\n   \nName\nJeetendra kumara\n    \n\n\nFather?s Name\nIndrasan Thakur\n   \nDate of birth\n10-May-1983\n   \nGender\nMale\n   \nMarital Status\nSingle\n   \nPersonality\nActive & Self Starter\n   \nHobbies\nReading computer books & about latest technology, Troubleshooting hardware and software, watching movie.\n   \nLanguages Known\nEnglish, Hindi\n    \n\n   \nNationality\nIndian\n\nDECLARATION: \n\nI hereby declare that all the above information is the true and correct to the best of my knowledge and belief.\n    \nPlace:\n                                                                                       \nSignature:',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-18',NULL,'2007-10-18','2010-06-10 12:14:22','2010-06-10',15,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(288,'K.V.Rao',NULL,NULL,NULL,'vsufbbbarfbafbokcfbfse@gmail.com',NULL,NULL,'0','91 9866368040','0',NULL,'0','2008-04-29',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-10 12:14:22',15,'0',NULL,'200710/18/ATT35093.html','200710/18/DOC35098.doc','subbarao\n                                    \n                     \n\nRESUME\n\nK.V.Rao\n\n       \n                                           \n                  \nMobile\n: +91-9866368040\n                                                \n\nrd\n Floor, #8-3-231/b/5, Plot No: 205,\n                           \n   \n     \n\n-mail\n\nvsufbbbarfbafbokcfbfse@gmail.com\nKrishna\n Nagar,\nYousufguda,\nHyderabad\n: - 500045\n\n                     \n   \n\nExperience Summary:\n\n\n         \n2+ Years of experience in the development of VB.NET, ASP.NET, C#.NET, web services and Enterprise Applications\n\n\n\n         \nExtensive knowledge of Client/Server and Web based applications\n\nPossessing knowledge and development experience in MS-Access, SQL Server 2000.\nExceptionally well organized, quick learner and willing to work hard to achieve employer objectives.\n\nSTRENTHS:\n\n         \nAbility to work effectively in a fast-paced, high volume, deadline-driven environment.\n\n         \nAbility to work in both team environment as well as Independent\n\n         \nGood written and verbal communication skills & inter-personal skills.\n\nEducational Qualification:\n\n2001 ? 2005\n\n\n\n      \nB.E\n\n\nComputer Science and Engineering\n),\n                       \n    \n\nAnna\nUniversity\n\n\nProfessional Experience\n\n\n\nWorking as Software Engineer in \n\nINTEQ Software Private Ltd.\n, JubliHills\n\nHyderabad\n         \n  \n\nFrom May 2005 to till date\n\nTechnical Expertise:\n\nOperating Systems\nWindows NT/2000/2003, Windows XP, 98, 95\nProgramming Languages\nC, C++.\nScripts\nHTML, Java Script\n. Net Frame work\n\n\nLanguage\nVisual C#, Visual Basic\nWeb Application\nASP. Net\nOthers\nWindows Services, Web Services\nEnvironment\nVisual studio. Net\nDatabases\n\nSQL Server 2000, MS ?Access, Transact SQL\n\n\nROJECTS PROFILE:\n\n         \nPROJECT \n#1\n                                                                      \n               \n          \n\nFeb 2006\n to till date\n            \n            \nProject Title\n                   \n\n\n\nEZCAP .NET\n\nClient\n                            \n\n   \nMZI Health Care.\nTeam Size\n                     \n\n   \n30\nEnvironment\n                  \n\n   \nMS.NET,\nASP.NET with VB.NET and ADO.NET \nDatabase\n                       \n\n   \nSQL SERVER 2000\nRole\n                              \n\n   \nDeveloper.\n\n\nPROJECT DESCRIPTION\n\n\nEZ-CAP is a fully integrated system that supports and manages day-to-day business operations of healthcare organizations such as HMOs, MSOs, PHOs, IPAs, specialty service organizations, medical groups, hospitals and government sponsored health plans. It has over 16 integrated modules including Benefit Enrollment and Eligibility administration, Claims processing and Adjudication, Authorizations, Capitation, Case Management,\n\nProviders,\n Internet Connectivity. EZ-CAP literally means the \nEasy\n\n\nlaims\n\n\ndministration and \n\nayment\n system with a comprehensive set of functionality including, eligibility and benefit tracking, provider maintenance and fee schedules, claims, authorizations, HIPAA ANSI EDI and referrals.\nThe main application is written with Gupta SQLWindows and is client server based application. It requires client installations at every place. The clients need to install new updates and the organization faces high maintenance cost. In order to be competitive and meet the customer expectations the management felt that product enhancement, modifying the existing features and migration to new technologies is of prime importance.\nAs a result it is decided to move away from Gupta and transition the product fully into Visual Studios 2005.net and SQL Server 2000 database. The current .NET Migration project will improvise on its current capabilities and features suiting to the different business lines HMOs, PPOs and POSs and make the product HIPAA compliant. The .Net application will follow browser based architecture\n\n\n\nMODULE NAME:\n\n          \nPROVIDERS\n\n        \n                             \n\n\nMODULEDESCRIPTION:\n\nThis module provider plays an important role in this project. Because providers help in efficient interactions among policy holders, vendors, medical groups, hospitals, MZI Health Care organization. It corroborate in creating records for each contracted provider that includes his/her contacts payments and demographic information. This assigns default emoluments to providers based on services or range of services provided.\nThis provider also includes information about venders. The vender file contains account information regarding provider?s provider groups, suppliers or any payment receiving entity .The information entered here is used to print checks. A vendor record is required for each provider in the provider file; however, more than one provider may be assigned to same vendor.\n\n\nThis module is divided into.\nProviders.\nProvider details.\nVendors.\nWith Hold Sets and Tables.\nCodes.\n                            \nRESPONSIBILITIES\n\n\n         \nAs a Team Member\n\n         \nInvolved in designing, coding and unit testing.\n\n   \n   \nInvolved in designing and storing data into database\n\nMODULENAME\n: -\n           \nELIGILIBITY\n                  \n                             \n\nMODULEDESCRIPTION\n\n\nThe eligibility module contains the detailed information of the each member assigned to the medical group. This section contains information on manually edited eligibility data. EZ-cap also uses eligibility data to calculate member?s months and provider caption payments automatically. This module enables us to\n\ncreate detailed record about each health plan member, Store additional information about the health plan?s\n\nsubscribers, Terminate and re-roll members, Transfer members to another health plans/options. Undo options and correct errors.\nMore over the above module is divides into following modules.\nMembers.\nHistory Transactions.\nUndo Last Transactions.\nCorrecting Errors.\nSubscribers.\nCodes Eligibility Types\n\n                             \nRESPONSIBILITIES\n\n\n         \nAs a Team Member.\n\n         \nInvolved in designing, coding and unit testing.\n\n   \n   \nInvolved in designing and storing data into database.\n\n       \nPROJECT\n#2\n                                          \n                              \n           \n\nMay 2005\n to Jan 2006\n\nProject Title\n                   \n\n  \nEmployees Daily Work Activities Recording (EDWARD)\n                     \nTeam Size\n                     \n\n   \n\nEnvironment\n                  \n\n   \nMS.NET1.0,\n ASP.NET with C#.NET and ADO.NET\nDatabase\n                       \n\n   \nSQL SERVER 2000\nRole\n                              \n\n   \nDeveloper.\n\n\n\nPROJECT DESCRIPTION:\n\nThe EDWARD website is maintained in the intranet. The functionality of the website has been divided into two categories. They are Admin Module and User Module. In admin level the employee details, authentications, update, delete, Add project, modules, work allocation, and request acceptance is mainly done. The admin can accept the requests and responds with appropriate steps. He can view the work activities in date, month, year by using simple and advance search. Client module has privileges the work activity like uploading burgs, personal problems and leaves request are to be submitted to the admin. Reports are also generated on the bases of employee call projects on the bases of the activities.\n\nAttendance of each employee is generated as a report for every month on the last day of the month and wages allotted according this base. The images required by the employee can be uploaded and downloaded to and from the server.\n                                      \nRESPONSIBILITIES:.\n\n         \nInvolved in designing, coding and unit testing.\n\n         \nInvolved in designing and storing data into database.\n\nACADEMIC PROJECT\n\n                                                                           \nDec 2004 to Apr 2005\n\n\nProject Title\n                   \n\n   \nWEBMART.\n                     \n                   \nTeam Size\n                     \n\n   \n4.\nEnvironment\n                  \n\n   \nMS.NET1.0,\nASP.NET with VB.NET and ADO.NET. \nDatabase\n                      \n\n   \nSQL SERVER 2000.\n\nPROJECT DESCRIPTION:\n\n\nWeb Mart? is an expensive portal development to case the shopping and shipping across the net. The functionality of the web site has been divided into two categories Admin and customer.\n\nThe entire project has been divided into various modules like administrator, shopping cart, products catalog, products directory, products items, checkout, mail services and help. Admin category is mainly divided into three categories. They are catalog administration, general administration and security administration. Each category will have different roles all this role are maintained my administrator. In customer category it will provided an account, when user logs on to the site, views all the current products directories with product items and their rates. At last payments has provided by two options by credit card or pay on delivery.\n                 \n\n\n\n                                             \n                                                             \nK.V.SubbaRao.',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-18',NULL,'2007-10-18','2010-06-10 12:14:22','2010-06-10',15,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(289,'Jatin Praja',NULL,NULL,'Bangalore ','jaefewtin_s_peffrajefapatefi@yahoo.com',NULL,NULL,'0','91 9900415925','0',NULL,'0',NULL,8,24,'2010-06-10 12:14:22',15,'0',NULL,'200710/18/ATT35094.html','200710/18/DOC35099.doc','Jatin S Prajapati\nJatin \n\nPraja\n\nAddress:\n\n\n86, 2\nnd\n E? \nMain Road\n\n                    \nE-Mail : \njaefewtin_s_peffrajefapatefi@yahoo.com\n                \n\nth\n Block, Koramangala,\n                  \nPhone : +\n91 9900415925\n                \nBangalore\n ? 560095\n                       \nGender: \nMale\nDate of Birth :\n    \n15/10/1983\n                   \n\n\nOBJECTIVE\n     \nTo work honestly & sincerely towards responsibilities taken & achieving goals\nAnd grow positively in the organization I work.\n\nEDUCATION\nCourse\nUniversity / Board \nYear\nPercentage\nM.Sc. (I.T)\n*V.N.S.G.U,\nSurat\n     \n2006\n67.23%\nB.sc.(I.T)\n*V.N.S.G.U,\nSurat\n     \n2004\n66.07%\n12\nth \nCommerce\n**GSEB\n     \n2001\n75.00% \n10\nth\n**GSEB\n     \n1999\n67.43%\n\n\n   \nV.N.S.G.U ? \nVeer\nNarmad\nSouth\nGujarat\nUniversity\n** GSEB ? \nGujarat\n Secondary Education Board\n\nTECHNICAL SKILLS\nTechnology\n.NET ( ASP.NET, C#.NET ,VB.NET) , ASP\n\nDevelopment Tools\nVisual Studio 6, Visual Studio .NET 2003, Code Smith Templates.\nScripting\nHTML, JavaScript.\nDatabases\nSQLServer 2000, MS Access, MySql, Oracle.\nPlatforms\nWindows NT/2000/98, UNIX, Linux Red Hat 9.0\nOther Skills\nUML, XML.\n\n\n\nACADEMIC PROJECTS\n\n\n\nPayroll cum Attendance System\n\nI have developed the Generalized Payroll Cum attendance system as. That satisfy the need of the organization including employee Information system , Leave management, Earning, Tax and deduction calculation, Region configuration, Payslip Engine and Various reports etc.\n\n\nPlatform/Software/Tools: \nASP.NET, VB.NET, MS SQL 2000, Win XP\nDuration:\n 6 Months\n\nMembers:\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nContent Management System\n\n( CMS )\n\n\nCMS is generalized Content Management System, Using this system we can change the content of the site, and we can add or delete static pages in website. we can also add new links to existing menu and also add content to newly created pages. These all functionality can be managed by Admin side.\n\nPlatform/Software/Tools: \nASP.NET, C#.NET, MS SQL 2000, Win XP\nDuration:\n 2 Months\n\nMembers:\n\n\n\nOnline Shopping & Catalogue \nMobile\n Application \n\nAs a part of the 7\nth\n semester project work, I worked on developing online shopping cart and Catalogue mobile application.\n\nAn e-Commerce based application, developed in 3-tier architecture. There are 3 layers\n(Business Layer, Data Access Layer, Presentation Layer) makes the application modular & reusable. This site provides all the facilities that a typical Online shopping site provides today. \n\nThe Catalogue Mobile application displays Catalogue and Items with their\n\nimages.\n\nPlatform/Software/Tools: \nC#.NET,ASP.NET,SQL SERVER 2000, XML, WIN2000\nDuration:\n 2 Months\n\nMembers:\n\n\n\nSohagia Tours & Travel PVT. LTD.\nAs a part of the final semester project work for B.Sc.(I.T.) Degree Course, I \nworked on developing a website for a Tours & Travel Company.\n\nA Website for a Travel agent who is member of FOREX & IATA. The site contains information about all the Hotels, Airlines, Visiting places by people can contact the firm and make Reservations and the web also provides current FOREX rates.\nPlatform/Software/Tools:\n ASP, MS Access -2000 , Photo Shop 7.0.\nDuration:\n 2 Months\n\nMembers:\n\n\n\nSEMINARS DELIVERED\n\n         \nUML (Unified Modeling language)\n\n         \nBRD ( Blu Ray Disc )',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-18',NULL,'2007-10-18','2010-06-10 12:14:22','2010-06-10',15,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(290,'Jagadees Jupalli',NULL,NULL,'Visakhapatnam','jagadeesh.jupalli@gmail.com','jagadeesh_jupalli@yahoo.co.in','91 891 2504655','0','9866886903','0',NULL,'0','2007-04-14',8,23,'2010-06-10 12:14:22',15,'0',NULL,'200710/18/ATT35095.html','200710/18/DOC35100.doc','JAGADEESWARARAO JUPALLI\nCareer Objective\nTo work in a challenging position in an organization that celebrates and rewards creativity, and fresh thinking where innovative ideas are always appreciated and to enhance my working knowledge, ability and skills.\nProfessional Summary\nOverall experience of \n3 years as a Software Engineer\n, involved in the development and implementation stages of various projects.\n\n          \nHaving experience in \n.Net 2.0, .Net 1.1, \nASP.NET, C#, VB.NET, ADO.NET, \nWeb Services,\n SQL Server, Windows operating systems.\n\n          \nAble to work under strict deadlines.\nTechnical Skills\nTechnologies\n               \n\n\n.Net 2.0, .Net 1.1, ASP.Net, C#, VB.Net, ADO.Net\nRDBMS\n                       \n\n\nMS-SQL Server\nWeb Technologies\n        \n\n\nHTML, XML, Web Services\nDevelopment Tools\n      \n\n\nVisual Studio 2005, Visual Studio 2003, Visual Studio 6, \n                                     \nMS Access\nProfessional Experience\nCurrently Working as Software Programmer in \nSamudra Software Pvt. Ltd.\n Since Oct 2004 to till date. URL: http://www.samudrasoftware.com/\nEducation\n\n          \nMaster of Science in Information Systems, 2004, Andhra university\n\n          \nBachelor of Computer Applications, 2001, Andhra university\nCertifications\n\n          \nDiploma in Information Systems Management\n\n\n\nOverall Technical Skills\nLanguages\n\nASP.NET 2.0, C# 2.0, \n\nVB.NET 2.0, C++\nTechnologies\n\nASP.NET, ADO.NET, ASP, XML\nDevelopment Environments\n\nVisual Studio .Net 2005, \nDream weaver\nDatabases\n\nSQL Server 2005/2000, MS Access\nMarkup\n\nHTML, XML, CSS\nOperating Systems\n\nWindows NT/2000/XP\n\nPROJECT SUMMARY\n\nProject# 1\nProject Name:\n          \nShared Parenting Calendar Software.\nClient:\n                    \nFront Porch Software, LLC\n\nEnvironment:\n\n          \nASP.NET 2.0, C# 2.0, SQL Server, IIS\nTechnical Environment:\nC#, ASP. NET 2.0, \nADO\n. NET 2.0, SQL Server 2005, Visual Studio 2005\nProject Description: \nwww.sharedground.com\n                          \nThe Shared Ground\nis designed especially for divorce and family law attorneys, courts, arbitrators, mediators, and counselors who develop many diverse Parenting Plans for clients. Contained within the Shared Ground program are default settings that reflect many typical and standard-parenting plans approved by courts and are set to distribute time equitably between two primary caregivers. Defaults may be used or a custom designed parenting plan may be created.\n                          \nOur calendar wizards guide you through each step as you enter recurring events like school schedules, holidays and birthdays. You can use the defaults or choose to enter your own dates and times. Vacation time and special occasions can even be planned a year in advance. When you\'re finished, view the calendar as a weekly or monthly schedule.\n                \nThe calendar displays any schedule conflicts, allowing time to coordinate with the other parent or caregiver. A percentage calculator is also included to display the percentage of time each child is with parent.\n\nRole: Software Engineer\nTeam size: 2\n\nResponsibilities: \n\n          \nClients? communication regarding the nature of the information process or computation needs. \n\n          \nCreating Web Forms using ASP.NET, MS Visual Studio .NET, HTML, CSS.\n\n          \nImplementing the web application using three-tiered architecture.\n\n          \nImplemented Web User Interface, Business logics, and Data Access Components.\n\n          \nImplemented with C#, ASP.NET, ADO.Net and SQL Server 2005 as back-end database.\n\n          \nDesigned and implemented relational database, and stored procedures, views, and triggers.\n\nProject# 2\nProject Name:\n          \nBack Office Maintenance Software for Stock Exchange.\nClient:\n                    \nSurya Shakti India Financial Pvt. Ltd.\n\nA leading financial service consultant and share broker in \nAndhra Pradesh\n\nIndia\n\n\nTechnical Environment:\nC#, ASP. NET, \nADO\n. NET, SQL Server 2000, Visual Studio\nProject Description:\n                                    \n                          \nBack Office Maintenance Software is an Exhaustive share broker Solution with matchless perfection for any share broker. The current system organizes and automates the back office work of Surya Shakthi India Finance Ltd. This project maintains the details of share purchases and sales of shares and to offer the customers the best Customer service.\n                          \nThe main purpose of this project is to track the daily share purchases, sales, Cash and Share deposits, Withdrawals and transfers by all the users. Set and calculate commission values, late fee etc. generate Monthly and Capital Gains Reports. Intimating the user about the share holdings, price fluctuations etc. in that week through News Letters.\n\nRole: Software Engineer\nTeam size: 4\n\nResponsibilities: \n\n          \nClients? communication regarding the nature of the information process or computation needs. \n\n          \nUnderstanding the business requirements and implementing the solution.\n\n          \nCreating Web Forms using ASP.NET, MS Visual Studio .NET, HTML, CSS.\n\n          \nImplementing the web application using three-tiered architecture.\n\n          \nImplemented Web User Interface, Business logics, and Data Access Components.\n\n          \nImplemented with C#, ASP.NET, ADO.Net and SQL Server 2000 as back-end database.\n\n          \nDesigned and implemented relational database, and stored procedures, views, and triggers.\n\n          \nInvolved in Testing and maintaining the applications.\n\n          \nMaking presentations to the users and offering solutions that they would be interested in.\n\nProject# 3\nProject Name:\n          \nGreat\nValley\nPublication Management System\nClient:\n                    \nGreat Valley Center?, \nUSA\nTechnical Environment:\nVB.NET, ASP. NET, \nADO\n. NET, SQL Server 2000, Visual Studio\n\nProject Description:\n          \nhttp://www.greatvalley.org/\n\n                     \nDeveloped an web application to manage the details of all the books Published by the Great Valley Publications and other publishers; and to provide different search options to users.\n\nThe modules of the project include: (1) Admin - Publication Management System (2) Public - Publication Management System.\n\nAdmin module:\nThe Admin module is classified into Content Administration and System Administration. Through content Administration, The administrator can add new publication and edit existing publication. The \nSystem Administrator\n, can \nAdd\n new Content Administrator and also monitor the work done by Content administrators.\n\nPublic module:\nThe Public module facilitates the users with search options such as simple, advanced and keyword search.\n\nRole: Software Engineer\nTeam size: 4\n\nResponsibilities: \n\n\n          \nInvolved in requirement gathering.\n\n          \nCreating Web Forms using ASP.NET, MS Visual Studio .NET, VB.NET, HTML, CSS.\n\n          \nInvolved in retrieving data using ADO.NET with VB. NET, ASP.NET.\n\n          \nProgramming in .Net environment using VB.NET in 3-tier architecture.\n\n          \nClient Communication.\n\n          \nTesting.\n\nProject# 4\nProject Name:\n          \niLrn Hub\n (Offshore Support)\nClient:\n   \n       \n          \nThomson\n\nHigher Education\n\nUSA\n   \n\nThe \nThomson Corporation\n is a leading global provider of integrated information solutions to business and professional customers.\n\nTechnical Environment:\nC#, ASP. NET, \nADO\n. NET, XML SQL Server 2000, Visual Studio\nProject Description:\n          \nhttp://ilrnhub.brookscole.com\n\n                           \niLrn Hub is a dynamic, powerful online project management software which tracks all the ongoing projects. It maintains the details of all the Clients and the projects under production. With an user friendly interface. \n\nSmartClient communication module:\nThis module will manage all the contacts of users on project basis. It displays the details off all the users and provides various options. Such as exporting the view to a spread sheet for offline verification and/or computation, the Alerts feature allows the users to create an e-mail alert notify when there are changes to the items. Alert frequencies can be adjusted i.e. alerted immediately when there is a change, or daily or weekly summary messages.\n\nProduction Management module: \nThis module is used to keep track of all the projects under production. This is used by all the users listed in the SmartClient communications and each user can view only the projects assigned to them. It maintains all the details about the project such as Project contacts, Announcements, Events, Issue Tracker, Links, Tasks, General Discussion and Shared Documents. The alert and the export to spread sheet features are applied for all these items. \n\nMy information module:\nUsed to view or update the information stored about the user. To manage the list of documents or other items in this site for which user receive alerts.\n\nRole: Software Engineer\nTeam size: 4\n\nResponsibilities: \n\n          \nDeveloped User interfaces using ASP.NET Forms.\n\n          \nInvolved in coding and testing.\n\n          \nCreated Web Forms using ASP.NET, MS Visual Studio .NET, HTML, CSS.\n\nProject# 5\nProject Name:\n          \nShipping Information System.\nEnvironment:\n\n\n        \nASP.NET, VB.NET, SQL Server 2000, IIS 5.0 \nProject Description:\n            \n                           \nIt is an Online (Dynamic) Information System which is useful for Employees of Marine Department (Research and Planning) to know the Details of Ships entered the \nPort\n of \nVisakhapatnam\n. It maintains the details of Vessel, Vessel Owner, Cargo, Agents, Berthing, Arrival, Departure, Shifting Information of the vessel and to calculate the \nTurn Round Time\n (TRT) of the vessel.\n\nRole: Software Engineer\nTeam size: 2\n\nResponsibilities: \n\n          \nInvolved in requirement gathering.\n\n          \nCreating Web Forms using ASP.NET, MS Visual Studio .NET, HTML, CSS.\n\n          \nUsed ADO.NET to establish database connectivity and data manipulation.\n\n          \nImplementing the site in 3-tier architecture.\n\n          \nUnderstanding the business requirements and implementing the solution.\n\n          \nMaking presentations to the users and offering solutions that they would be interested in.\n\n          \nClient Communication.\n\n          \nTesting.\n\n\n\n\nPersonal Details:\n\nDate of Birth: \n19-August-1981\n\nAddress:\n\n# 2-41-11, \n                 \nPlot No: 18/XI, \n                 \nM.V.P. Colony, \n                 \nVisakhapatnam\n\n                 \nA.P, \nIndia\n\n\nContact Numbers:\n   \n     \nMobile\n ? 9866886903\n                \nResidence - +91-891-2504655\n\n     \n                                    \n\nEmail Address: \n        \n              \njagadeesh.jupalli@gmail.com\n\n             \njagadeesh_jupalli@yahoo.co.in\n\n                           ','Samudra Software Pvt. Ltd',1,NULL,'2007-10-18',NULL,'2007-10-18','2010-06-10 12:14:22','2010-06-10',15,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(291,'Kumar sahu',NULL,NULL,'Hyderabad','goeeffvidvnd31dv83@yahoo.co.in','godsvidsvndsvds2dv0@rediffmail.com',NULL,'0','91 9948292045','0',NULL,'0','2008-04-13',8,24,'2010-06-10 12:14:22',15,'0',NULL,'200710/18/ATT35096.html','200710/18/DOC35101.doc','RESUME\n\n\n\n\n\nKumar Sahu \n\n  \n\n                                           \nE-mail\n\n   \ngoeeffvidvnd31dv83@yahoo.co.in\n               \ngodsvidsvndsvds2dv0@rediffmail.com\n\n                              \n      \n    \nPlot No 143, H.No. 143,\n                                       \nOld\n\nVASAVI \n\nNAGAR,\n                                  \n                                  \nKARKHANA\n                                  \n   \n   \n\nSec-Bad-500015\n                 \n                             \nMobile\n: 91-9948292045\n\n\n\n\nCareer Profile\n    \n\nAn application developer with around \n\n\nyears\n of progressively responsible experience in a reputed organization, I possess expertise in developing client-server applications using Sql Server (2000), .Net and Asp.net. I have developed projects at my own responsible\n\n\n\nProfessional Summery:\n\n\n      \nExpertise in working Client/Server technologies using Sql Server (2000), C# .Net, Asp.Net.\n\n      \nExpertise in Project Deployment using 2 tier and 3tier Architecture.\n\n      \nExpertise in developing Web Technologies.\n\n      \nExpertise in implementing 3-tier architecture.\n\nTechnical Proficiency\n\n\nOperating System\n        \n: Windows XP/2000/2003\nLanguage\n                     \n: C#, Asp.Net, Vb.Net, C, C++\nWeb Technologies\n       \n: HTML, ASP.Net\nRDBMS\n                       \n: Sql Server 2000\n\nEducational details\n\n\n\n      \nMCA, \nSession 2003-2005, with\n First Division from UtkaL University, Orissa.\n\n      \nBCA \nwith\n First Division from North Orissa University, Orissa in the year 2003.\n\n      \nIntermediate\n (+2 Science) with\n First Division from C.H.S.E, Orissa in 2000\n\n\n      \nH.S.C.\n(10\nth\n) with \nSecond Division from B.S.E, Orissa in the year 1998\n\n\n\nProfessional Training and Certification \n\n\n\n\n\n  \nGNIIT from NIIT, \nHyderabad\n\n\n\n\n\nProfessional Experience\n\n\n\n\n      \nPresently working in \nE-Velociti Software Solutions\n, Hyderabad\n as\n Team Member\n\nthis deals with software development and provides IT solutions to Domestic and International clients since 1st Aug 2005 to till date.\n\n   \n      \n\nProjects profile (Continues?.)\n                                                            \nVISA (Virtual Information System for Audit Department) \n\nO/S\n      \n\n: Win XP/2003\nTechnologies: SQL Server (2000),\nC#.net \nRole\n       \n\n\n: Team Member\nTeam Size:12\nClient\n\nState Audit dept, Govt. Of Andhra Pradesh\n\n\nDescription:\n\nThis application is for the State Audit department, Cyber bad, Govt. Of Andhra Pradesh, India for atomizing the manual/traditional process for overall activity done by the Department to improve their productivity, management and efficiency as the Honorable CM of Andhra Pradesh and the Govt. of Andhra Pradesh already taken up the initiative to utilize the power of IT in every area to the maximum extent.\n\n            \nIt is a Enterprise-level application based on n-tier architecture and consist of 7 modules \n[Admin, Audit, Registers/Reports, PIS Establishment, Accounts, LB Accounts, MISC\n] provides a rich set feature to perform and manage starting from daily to monthly, quarterly and annual activities related to audits, internal accounts, local bodies accounts, managing and tracking personal information?s related to employees, payroll management, generating performance and progress reports etc. It has 2 types of interface (Windows and Web Based).\n\nRole: \n\n        \nDesigning the User Interface (Fronted)\n\n        \nImplementing Business Logic.\n\n        \nFinding Out Solutions\n\n        \nResponsible for Web Based work.\n\n    \n  \nDatabase programming Procedures/Triggers\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nDev. Of \nwww.hiresstudios.com\n (Press and Media Comp.) - \nUSA\n\nO/S\n       \n: Win XP Professional\nTechnologies\n: SQL Server(2000), C#.Net, ASP.NET, IIS 5.0.\nRole: Team Member\nTeam Size:12\nClient:U.S.A\n\nDescription:\nwww.hiresstudios.com\n\nis an e-commerce, B2B and B2C portal to bring customers, employees and the press, media and advertising company (Hires Studios) together by providing a better way to place orders for getting various objects for printing and advertising based on the specific requirement sets of clients. It provides a means for customization of the various offerings and a range of products like customized business cards, invitation cards, Flyers, Postcards, Posters as well as custom jobs (prints). ). It allows the customers to submit their templates, logos, images and other files, which has to use for the ordered product for printing. It stores detailed information about individuals seeking various products as well as customization information about the product with payment information.\n\nRoles:\n       \n\n        \nDesigning the User Interface (Fronted)\n\n        \nImplementing Business Logic.\n\n        \nFinding Out Solutions\n\n        \nResponsible for Web Based work.\n\n        \nDatabase programming (Procedures / Triggers)\n\n                  \n\nClosure Module Version 1.2 (The BANC724 TBA-2 Closure Version)\n\nO/S\n        \n: Win XP\nSoftware\n\n:C#.net, Sql Server 2000\nRole\n      \n: Designing, and Coding.\nTeam Size: 8\nRole :Team Member\nClient: Central Bank Of \nIndia\n\n\n\nDescription: \nTypically this module is design to receive all the transaction related information ones a day after all the transactions are over.\n\nThe information is carried over to databases relating to a consistent transaction.\n\nThe service provided by this module can be tailored to banking operation carried out by Managerial Staff.\n\nThis also allows an integrated picture of the customers business on daily operations which are being updated in Centralized Database System for the safe, secure and consistent operation.\n\nThis consists of 9 modules.\n\n         \nChecking cash denomination.\n\n         \nChecking daily transaction.\n\n         \nChecking same day outward clearing.\n\n         \nChecking next day outward clearing.\n\n         \nChecking inward clearing.\n\n         \nWriting Master Transaction.\n\n         \nWriting Closing Balance.\n\n         \nUpdating Debit / Credit Balance.\n\n         \nDay successfully closed.\n\nBesides it gives messages on error report, pending authorization, account opened but no transaction, reading signature file and exceptional error message BRCP.\n\n\nCheque Book Module\n           \n\nO/S: Windows 2000 \nEnterprise\n Server\nTechnologies: C#.Net, Sql Server 2000\nTeam Size: 8\nRole :Team Member\nClient: V.S.B\n\n\n\nDescription:\n\n      \nThis module is one of the BANC724 branch modules - which deal with all the cheque book related issues, which makes it possible to perform cheque book operation like real time transactional unit which consists of following modules.\n\n\n        \nCheque Book Stocks\n\n        \nCheque Books Issues Single\n\n        \nStop/Revoke Cheque Leaf\n\n        \nStop/Revoke Batch\n\n        \nCheque Book Cancellation \n\n        \nCheque Books Reports\nRole:\n\n        \nCheque Book Issued \n\n        \nCheque Book Stopped\n\n        \nLoose Leaves list\n\n        \nList of Cheque in stocks\n\n\n\n\nPersonal Details:\n\n\nPERSONAL DETAILS:\n\n                \nFather?s Name\n             \n\n   \nDhirendra Nath Sahu\n            \nDate of Birth\n                 \n\n   \n30-05-1983\n            \nPassport\n                       \n\n   \nApplied?. yet to come\n            \nGender\n                         \n\n   \nMale\n            \nMarital Status\n               \n\n   \nSingle\n            \nAddress \n                      \n\n   \nPlot No. 143, Old Vasavi Nagar\n\n             \n                                 \n   \n, Karkhana, Secunderabad ? 15\n\nReferences:\n\n\n1)\n\n\nGurubrata Panda, Sr. Software Engineer, \nNess\n Technologies\n       \nMail:\n\ngurubrata.panda@ibs.ness.com\n\n\n                               \n                                \n   \n                                    \nGovind Kumar Sahu\n                                                     \n                                                                                                                               \n                                    \n                  \n                                                                                  \n                           \n                                                                                             ','E-Velociti Software Solutions',1,NULL,'2007-10-18',NULL,'2007-10-18','2010-06-10 12:14:22','2010-06-10',15,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(292,'G Janardhan',NULL,NULL,'Bangalore','g_jadvdvnadvrsdveddvdy@yahoo.co.in','g_janareddy@yahoo.co.in','08592 9959821702','0','9886136274','0',NULL,'0','2007-12-13',8,24,'2010-06-10 12:14:22',15,'0',NULL,'200710/18/ATT35097.html','200710/18/DOC35102.doc','Resdex @ naukri.com\nG janardhan \nmaratha halli,banglore banglore \ng_jadvdvnadvrsdveddvdy@yahoo.co.in\n\nTelephone: 9886136274\n(M)\n 91 08592 9959821702\n(R)\n\nD.O.B\n - 23 Jun 1979 \nModified on\n - 26 Sep 2007 \nAnnual Salary\n - INR 3 Lac(s) 60 Thousand \nTotal Years of Experience\n - 3 Year(s) 8 Month(s) \nCurrent Location\n - Bangalore \nPreferred Location\n - Anywhere in South India \nm.c.a with 3 years experience\n\nTEXT RESUME \n\nG.janardhan Reddy\nE-mail: g_janareddy@yahoo.co.in\nMobile\n: 9886136274,9959821702\nPROFESSIONAL SUMMARY\n\n??\n 3+ Years of extensive experience in Microsoft Technologies.\n\n??\n Strong in Software Development Life Cycle.\n\n??\n Qualitative experience of handling, managing & delivering multiple development projects to suit\nthe clients? requirements.\n\n??\n Strong communication, collaboration & team building skills with proficiency at grasping new\ntechnical concepts quickly and utilize the in a productive manner.\n\n??\n Well Versed with ASP.NET and C#.\n\n??\n Good knowledge in .NET Framework, ADO.NET.\n\n??\n Expertise in Web development using ASP. Net.\n\n??\n Experience in developing Web User Controls and custom controls\nTECHNICAL SKILLSET\nMicrosoft Technologies : ASP.NET and C#\nOperating Systems : Windows NT/98/2000/XP\nRDBMS : SQLServer2000\nScripting Languages : Java Script, VBScript\nTools : Microsft Visual Source Safe, VS.Net\nWeb Servers : IIS 6.0\nEDUCATIONAL BACKGROUND\n\n??\n M.C.A in madras university with 61%.\n\n??\n B.s.c(c.s) in nagarjuna university with 55%.\nPROFESSIONAL EXPERIENCE\n\n??\n Working as Software Engineer in econcept technologies, \nBangalore\n from june 2005 to till Date.\n\n??\n Worked as a Software Developer in bs talent solutions, \nBangalore\n from jan 2004 to june 2005.\nProjects\nProject #1\nTitle : E.KATS\nClient : \nKUWAIT\n STOCK EXCHANGE\nEnvironment : .NET\nDatabase : SQL Server 2000\nLanguages : ASP. Net, C#. Net\nRole : coding and development\n\n??\n Description:\n\n??\n Electronic Kuwait Automated Trade System (e.KATS) will provide automated trading facility for Kuwait Stock in this project terminal are BT,BAT,VOT,MOP.this is for \nKuwait\n stock exchange.all transactions are online.\nRoles and Responsibilities:\n\n??\n Involved in Coding.\n\n??\n Connecting database through ADO.NET.\n\n??\n Unit Testing\nProject #2\nTitle : COMPUTERRAZATION VEHICLE REGISTRATION.\nClient : ORIENTAL INSURANCE COMPANY.\nEnvironment : ASP.NET,C#.NET,SQLSERVER\nDatabase : SQL Server 2000.\nLanguages : C#. Net, Web Forms.\n\n??\n Description:\n\n??\n The main objective of this project is to register the new vehicles into insurance system and display thepremium dates and renewal dates of vehicles.this project also contains the information about thepolicyholders information.this project is used for generate the reports for customer wise.this project veryion to optimize and centralized their transaction very easily\nRoles and Responsibilities:\n\n??\n Involved in Coding.\n\n??\n Connecting database through ADO.NET.\n\n??\n Unit Testing\n\n??\n Project #3\nTitle : MEDENT\nClient : ELECTROCARE SOLUTIONS INC(USA)\nEnvironment : .NET\nDatabase : SQL Server 2000\nLanguages : ASP.NET,C#.NET,SQLSERVER2000\n\n??\n Description:\n\n??\n Medent is medical billing software .medent is used to store patient information,charged made to patient bythe doctor,claiming the charges to the insurance company and patient,payment made by the insurance companyand patient and rporting facility to view different types of reports and ledgers\nRoles and Responsibilities:\n\n??\n Involved in Coding.\n\n??\n Connecting database through ADO.NET.\n\n??\n Unit Testing .\nProject #4\nTitle : MEDICAL SERVICES.\nClient : NIJAM HOSPITAL,HYDERABAD\nEnvironment : .NET\nDatabase : SQL Server 2000\nDescription:\n\n??\n It maintains a list of doctors department wise along with details of the doctors.it maintains a list ofvarious departments that exist in the hospital along with the details of doctors heading thosedepartments.the principal advantage of this project is that by just selecting the name of a desease from thelist of deseases it would automatically generating the symptoms of the desease and the list od medicinessuggested by the doctor and there is a provision for removing symptoms that are not observed in a patient fora particular desease .since all the symptoms that confirms a deasease may not be observed in a patient.\nRoles and Responsibilities:\n\n??\n Involved in Coding.\n\n??\n Connecting database through ADO.NET.\n\n??\n Developed Data Access Components using Stored Procedures.\n\n??\n Unit Testing .\nProject #5\nTitle : SMART BANK.\nClient : MAHAVEER CO OPERATIVE URBAN BANK\nDatabase : SQL Server 2000\nDescription:\n\n??\n smart bank is a product designed and developed for complete automation of bank front office and backoffice operations of ant bank using clent/server architecture .it consists of modules like savings bankaccount,current account,overdraft(clean od,secured od,occ-open cashcredit),bills,cash,clearing,loans,deposits,cash management and locker management.it also consists of moduleslike fixed deposits,term deposits,and recurring deposits.reports of diverse nature are to be generated fromtime to time.\n\n??\n The broad areas are as follows savings& current bank accounts ,overdrafts(clean od,securedod,occ-open cash credit,ksc-key shut credit),demand drafts,clearing(outward clearing,inwardclearing)deposits(term deposits,cumulative deposits and recurring deposits),cash management,lockermanagement,bills for collection,loans(gold loans,agriculture loans,demand loans,vehicle loans\nRoles and Responsibilities:\n\n??\n Involved in Design and Coding.\n\n??\n Connecting database through \nADO','econcept technologies',1,NULL,'2007-10-18',NULL,'2007-10-18','2010-06-10 12:14:22','2010-06-10',15,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(293,'Garima C',NULL,NULL,NULL,'grfgrarimfgera.chargndrrga1rg010@gmail.com',NULL,'01126686699','0','91 9911636584','0',NULL,'0','2008-04-29',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-10 12:14:22',15,'0',NULL,'200710/18/ATT35103.html','200710/18/DOC35105.doc','Abhinaw Dixit\n\nGarima C\nContact No : +91 - 9911636584\nE-\nmail: grfgrarimfgera.chargndrrga1rg010@gmail.com\n\n\nRESUME SUMMARY\n\nHaving over 2 years of I.T. experience in the field of software development comprising Product & Application development. I have worked on Microsoft Technologies primarily on ASP.Net,C# and MS SQL Server. A strong team player with exposure to working in a team environment, have the ability to learn & deliver quickly & I am willing to acquire new skills in the field of software development.\n\nobjective\n\nTo obtain a challenging position in the area of Software Development where my skills, creativity and experience can be used to development of high quality products & services.\n\nQUALIFICATIONS\n\n\n        \nMCA from IGNOU, \nNew Delhi\n in 2005.\n\n        \nBA from \nMeerut\nUniversity\n in 2000.\n\nTechnical skills\n\nLanguages\n                                         \n: C# , SQL\nRDBMS\n                                              \n: MS SQL Server. Oracle\nInternet Technologies\n                       \n: HTML, ASP. Net, Java Script\nDevelopment Tools\n                           \n: VS.Net\nOperating System\n                             \n: WindowsNT/2000\nData Access Tool\n                             \n\nADO\n\nNET\nVersion Control tool\n                          \n\nVisual Source Safe\n\n\n\nProfessional EXPERIENCE: September 2006 - PRESENT\n\nCMC\n PVT \nLTD\n\nNew Delhi\n\nIndia\nWorking as a Software Developer\n    \n\n\n\nPROJECT DETAILS \n\nProject 1\n:-\n\nProject Name:-CPIS(Computerized Project Information System)\n   \nClient:-\n          \n\nNATIONAL HIGHWAY\n AUTHORITY OF \nINDIA\n\n\n\nProject description:-\n\nThe \nComputerized Project Information System\n is the online project monitoring system proposed by National Highway Authority of India to monitor the currently running projects at their Project Implementation Unit. The architecture provides the solution to automate the process of Planning, Monitoring and tracking of Different Project Of National Highways Authority of India .\n                        \nWeb Forms\n: - Web form part of CPIS includes and maintain all the \nInformation from Detailed Project report study, Tender of Project, Contract Award, Monitoring, start of Construction and then maintenance of the Roads. Further it is divided into Three Phases.\n\na.)\n   \nPre-Construction Phase:- This part of web Forms maintains captures all the pre bid activity, activity of contract award, procurement of Supervision Consultant, DPR-Consultant, and Civil works Contractor.\nb.)\n   \nConstruction Phase:- This part of web Forms maintains captures all the information related with Construction of Highways.\nc.)\n    \nPost-Construction Phase:- This part of web Forms maintains, captures all the information related with Maintenance of Highways\n\nRole and Responsibilities:\n\n\n        \nDeveloped \nWeb Forms using\n\nASP.\nNET\n\nHTML, \nCSS\n\n\n        \nUsed Java Script as a client side scripting Language.\n\n        \nCoding of \nBusiness Logic Layer in C#.\n\n        \nUsed \nADO\n\nNET\n for Database Connection.\n\n\n        \nUsed SQL Server as RDBMS. \n\n        \nWrote \nStored Procedures and triggers in T-SQL for implementing business rules\n\n        \nWorked on \nSQL Server Reporting Services\n\n\n        \nInteracting \nwith client regarding the changes and maintenance\n..\n\n         \nInvolved in \nProduction, Enhancements and Maintenance of the Application\n\nTools Used:\n\n                        \nPresentation Layer\n               \n: ASP.Net, HTML, JAVA SCRIPT\n                     \nBusiness Logic Layer \n: C#\n                        \nData Layer\n                             \n: MS SQL Server\n                        \nDevelopment Tools\n               \n: Visual Studio .Net\n   \n                        \nServer\n                                     \n: IIS 5.0\n                     \nData Access Tool\n                    \n\nADO\n\nNET\n                     \nVersion Control Tool\n                \n: VSS\n\n                      \nReporting Services \n                \n: SQL Reporting Services.\n\nProject 2\n:-\n\nProject:-E-Rolls(Electronic Electrol)\nClient:-Election Commision of \nIndia\n\nProject description\n\nPreparation of the voter?s list is the key ingredient in the elections. The main purpose of the application is to bring the states? voter list in all the languages under a single database.The application has the following parts:-\n\n1)\n     \nSchema Creation:-Creates the database and the database schema\n2)\n     \nData Porting:-Ports the states English/Vernacular data into the Oracle structure\n3)\n     \nCleaning and Unicode conversion:-Applise cleaning rules that are required to convert ISCII/ISFOC data into Unicode\n4)\n     \nGeneration of reports:-Reports depicting problems in the voter list are generated.\n5)\n     \nReverse Dictionary Creation:-Dictionary creation on the basis of names obtained after applying the simplication routines on the voter?s name.\n6)\n     \nGrouping Application:-Clubbing of simplified names into a single group so as to form one group for various distinct names on the basis of certain well defined algorithms.\n\nThe application provides the functionality through an easy to use GUI in a Client-Server environment.\n\nRole and Responsibilities:\n\n\n        \nUsed Oracle10g as RDBMS. \n\n        \nInteracting \nwith client regarding the changes and maintenance\n..\n\n         \nInvolved in \nProduction, Enhancements and Maintenance of the Application\n\n\n\nTools Used:\nPresentation Layer\n               \n:Win Forms\n    \n                        \n\nDatabase\n                              \n: Oracle10g\n                        \nDevelopment Tools\n               \n: Visual Studio .Net\n   \n                        \nServer\n                                     \n: IIS 5.0\n                     \nData Access Tool\n                    \n\nADO\n\nNET\n                     \nVersion Control Tool\n                \n: VSS\n\n                        \nReporting Tools\n                     \n\nCrystal\n Reports\n                      \nProfessional EXPERIENCE:\n                \nSeptember 2005 ? AUGUST 2006\n\nTotal Software Pvt Ltd\n\n\nEducation Software\n\n             \n\nThis is the web-based portal for the school and colleges, which involves maintaining the MIS for School/ College. This solution includes several activities of school/ College comprising of creation of Report cards of students, General administration, Admission procedure, Content Management, Internal Assessments and Online assessment for the inter and intra school activities & functions.\n\nResponsibilities\n: I was involved in development of the different modules consisting of coding, low-level designing and Unit testing of the module.\n\nTools Used:\n\n                        \nPresentation Layer\n   \n: ASP.Net, C#\n                        \nData Layer\n                 \n: MS SQL Server\n                        \nDevelopment Tools\n   \n: Visual Studio .Net\n   \n                        \nServer\n                         \n: IIS 5.0\n                     \nData Access Tool\n        \n: ADO.NET\n     \n                          \nProject \n\nDuration\n: 9 Months\n                                                 \n\nProject Role\n: Software Engineer\n\nPERSONAL DETAILS \n\n\n        \nLocal Address\n                 \n: H8/1,First Floor, Malviya Nager ,\nNew Delhi\n\n        \nMartial Status\n                  \n: Unmarried\n\n        \nDate of Birth\n                    \n: 10th October \n\n1979.\n\n        \nSex\n                            \n       \n: Female\n    \n\n        \nLanguages\n                       \n: English, Hindi\n\n        \nPassport No\n                    \n: B09010641 \n\n        \nAlternate Contact No\n      \n:01126686699\n\n\nGarima Chandra\n                                                                                                      \n    \n              ',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-18',NULL,'2007-10-18','2010-06-10 12:14:22','2010-06-10',15,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(294,'E Mohanty',NULL,NULL,NULL,'elowerggergra.moergghrganty9gr9@gmail.com',NULL,NULL,'0','91 9886918394','0',NULL,'0','2008-04-29',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-10 12:14:22',15,'0',NULL,'200710/18/ATT35104.html','200710/18/DOC35106.doc','Srikanta Kumar Barik\nE Mohanty\n\n\n\n\nEmail ID: elowerggergra.moergghrganty9gr9@gmail.com\n\n\nMobile\n: +91? 9886918394\n\n\nTechnical Experience\n\n?2+ Years of experience as a Software Professional.\n?Good application development skills using \n.NET\n\nFramework\n\nC#, ADO.NET, ASP.NET\n\nVB.NET\n\nSQL Server 2000,XML, IIS\n and\nJavaScript\n\n?Knowledge of \nObject Oriented programming (OOPS) \n\n?Good working knowledge of Internet languages like \nHTML, XML, \nand\n JavaScript\n\n?Knowledge about\n\nWeb Service & Remoting\n\n\nWorked with \nindexes, Stored Procedures\n and\n Triggers\n\n?Highly dedicated team player backed by independent thinking and Proficient at\nimplementing \n\nand managing new software technology.\n\n\nObjective\n\n\nTo work in a challenging and dynamic environment towards a successful career in the software industry by making the best out of my abilities and interpersonal skills. I want to see myself as an active contributor to a team of ambitious people and thereby enhance my knowledge and personality.\n\n\nEmployment Summary\n\n\nWorking as software engineer in CGI Netvorks (Banglore) from may 2005 to till date.\n\n\nEducational Profile\n\n\nB.E from \nBPUT\nUniversity\n (Orissa) in 2005 scoring 75%.\n\nTechnical Skills\n\n\nOperating Systems\n    \n:Windows 2000/XP\nLanguages\n               \n:C# 1.1\nWeb Programming\n     \n:ASP.Net 1.1 and XML\nDatabases\n             \n\n:SqlServer2000\nScripting\n                 \n:Java Script\nSource control\n         \n:Visual source safe\n\nProjects Handled:\n\n\n1.#IBS- RD:Finance/Banking Domain\n\n\nCurrent module\n         \n     \n\nApplication System\nSoftware Platform\n     \n     \n: ASP. Net, C#,XML, ADO.NET and SQLServer2000\nTools\n                      \n     \n: VSS 6.0\nWeb-server\n             \n     \n: IIS 6.0\nArchitecture/Framework\n    \n\n\n3-Tier, MVC\n\n\nApplication System:\n\n\nThis module helps to automate the process of new Recurring Deposit proposal and helps the Bank Executive to Enter, Retrieve and Check data of the person who has applied for RD account as well the renewal of an existing RD account. This Application sub System captures the customer details including the personal, nomination, tenure and mode of interest payment details.\n\nDescription:\n\n\nThe project, Recurring Deposit, is developed for our client, who keeps track of the Administrator, Executive, Report handling and \nCreating RD\n account of customer. The Recurring deposit is a part of the different deposit schemes available in a bank. This scheme deals with the deposit, which is done in a regular interval.\nModules included are application system, deposit process system, payment system, closure system, customer interaction, user interaction, product administration and accounting interface and management system.\n\nResponsibilities:\n\n\n\n         \nAnalyzing the design pattern given to us.\n\n         \nInvolvement in Coding the user Interface.\n\n         \nImplemented client side validations and involving in peer reviews.\n\n2.#CIA-OMI: Finance/Insurance Domain\n\n\nSoftware Platform\n     \n     \n\n\nASP. Net, C#.Net,XML, ADO.NET and SQLServer2000\nTools\n                      \n     \n:VSS 6.0\nWeb-server\n             \n     \n:IIS 6.0\nArchitecture/Framework\n     \n\n3-Tier, MVC\n\n\nDescription:\n\n\nThe Overseas Mediclaim Insurance (OMI) Policy is issued to persons undertaking bonafide trips abroad, which will not involve any manual labor. OMI provides indemnity for expenses incurred for medical treatment for illness, diseases contracted or injury sustained during overseas travel, which is primarily in the nature of an emergency and without which the Insured is not able to leave the overseas country due to being medically incapable of traveling. OMI also provides travelers with in-flight Personal Accident and Loss of Passport benefits and the additional coverage?s of loss of checked baggage, delay of checked baggage and personal liability. An OMI is offered to business and holiday travelers.\n\nProposal Sub-System:\n\n\nThe proposal Sub-System deals with the person going abroad. It is the User Interface, which captures all the details including Policy period, Policy amount, and Premium amount and about Generation of Policy number.\n\nResponsibilities:\n\n\n\n         \nAnalyzing the design pattern given to us.\n\n         \nInvolvement in Coding the user Interface.\n\n         \nImplemented client side validations and involving in peer reviews.\n\n3.#\n Insurance\n\nDomain# AI-CIA (Automobile Insurance)\n\nModule Handled\n        \n    \n\nApplication System\nSoftware Platform\n     \n    \n: ASP. Net, VB.Net, ADO.NET and SQLServer2000\nTools\n                      \n    \n: VSS 6.0\nWeb-server\n             \n    \n\n\nIIS 6.0\nArchitecture/Framework\n    \n\n3-Tier, MVC\n\n\nDescription\n\n\n\nAutomobile Insurance is a web-enabled centralized application that automates Automobile insurance. This sub system provides the Registration and Renewal of the Automobile Insurance Policy.The Proposal or Renewal Sub System: The Proposal or Renewal Sub System deals with the Registration of a new Automobile Insurance or Renewal of the existing policies.\nThe functionalities handled are:\noCustomer\nThe sub module is used to register the Customer details.\nInsured Objects. This module is used to capture the details and condition of the object to be insured.Fraud Detection\n\nVDR(Variation Detailed Report)Used to analyze the previous history of the Customer and the vehicle.\noPremium calculation:\nBased on parameterized inputs generated thru proposal system, Premium amount is computed.\noPolicy Preparation:\nThe policy document containing the perils, validity etc is generated.\n\nResponsibilities:\n\n\n\n         \nAnalyzing the design pattern given to us.\n\n         \nInvolvement in Coding the user Interface.\nImplemented client side validations and involving in peer reviews.\n\n\nPersonal Profile:\n\n\nGender\n                    \n:Female.\nMarital Status\n          \n:Single.\nFather?s Name\n          \n\nNiranjan Mohanty.\nLanguages Known\n     \n:English, Hindi, and Oriya.\n\nShould you feel convinced as regards the achievements stipulated, May please contact \n\nme to be across your table to justify my worth for the position applied for, I shall be grateful.\n\n\n\n\nDate:\n    \n                                                                                             \nElora Mohanty',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-18',NULL,'2007-10-18','2010-06-10 12:14:22','2010-06-10',15,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(295,'D Naga',NULL,NULL,'Hyderabad','dfefn.ganewfdheffaewfm@gmail.com',NULL,NULL,'0','919949231287','0',NULL,'0','2007-11-12',10,34,'2010-06-10 12:14:22',15,'0',NULL,'200710/18/ATT35107.html','200710/18/DOC35108.doc','CURRICULUM VITAE\nCURRICULUM VITAE\n\nD Naga \n                                       \n       \n                                                                                      \nE-mail: \n\ndfefn.ganewfdheffaewfm@gmail.com\n     \n         \nMobile\n\n\n+919949231287\n\n                                    \n    \n        \nProfile:\n                  \nI have 2+ \nyears \nof experience in IT industry with expertise in .NET Technologies and would like to add my skills to a team that designs and develops successful software that leads the industry in functional and technical achievement. \n\nAbility to work in a team & a flair for learning new things are my strong points\n\nProfessional Summary:\n\n\n      \nExposure in Functional and technical design Specifications.\n\n      \nExperience in Asp.Net, VB.Net, C\n#.Net, ADO.Net, SQL Server.\n\n      \nStrong Understanding of Object Oriented Programming & Application Design.\n\n      \nProficiency in Database programming using ADO.Net.\n\n      \nExperience in writing stored procedures, data retrieving.\n\nExperience:\n\nCurrently working as a Software Engineer in \nPromatrix Solutions\n\nHyderabad\n since\nMay 2005 to till date.\n\nEducation Qualification\n\n\n      \nM.Sc (\nI E\n\nfrom\n\nBharathidasan\nUniversity\n, Trichy with \n86%\n in 2005\n      \nBSC (Computer Science\n\nfrom \nAndhra\nUniversity\n with \n68%\n in 2003\n\nTechnical Exposure: \n\nOperating System\n                   \n\n           \nWindows XP/2000, MS-DOS\nLanguages\n                              \n\n           \nC, C++, C#, VB.NET\nWeb Technologies\n                  \n\n           \nASP.NET 2.0, ADO.NET, Web Services\nDatabases\n                               \n\n           \nMS Access, SQL-Server\nIDE\n     \n                                    \n\n            \nVisual Studio 6.0\n\nAcademic Achievement:\nGot \nGold Medal\n for \nUniversity Topper\n in \nM.SC., (IE)\n from \nBharathidasan\nUniversity\n in \n2005\n\n\nProject Details:\n\nProject#1\n\nProject Title \n               \n\n\n         \nPMS \nTechnologies\n              \n\n         \nC#.Net, VS.Net, Asp.Net, Window?s Xp\nClient\n             \n             \n\n\n         \nCipra Pharmaceuticals \nDatabase\n   \n                  \n\n\n   \n      \nSql Server\nTeam size\n      \n              \n\n\n          \n\nRole\n                \n                        \n\n\n         \nTeam Member\n\n         \nI was responsible for designing and coordinating the development of this system. I was also responsible for helping the development of all modules.\nDescription\n   \n\nThis project deals with call centre campaign .Admin creates managers, centres and agents. Admin has privilege to modify the database. Admin observes billing approval status. Manager creates agents and views status of agents. Manager has creation permissions but hasn\'t modifications. Agents will interact with people and take orders from them and send these orders to Manager. Manager maintains the information of the clients and generates the reports\n\n\nResponsibilities:\nInvolved in web page designing and coding\nInvolved in security management by using ASP. Net\n\nProject#2\n\nProject Title\n                \n\n         \n360EHS\nURL\n                          \n   \n\n\n\n\n      \n\n\n\nhttp://www.360ehs.com\nTechnologies\n              \n\n        \nAsp.Net, C#, VS.Net, Window?s Xp\nClient\n                          \n\n       \n\nEssential Health Supplies, US\nWeb Server\n                 \n\n         \nSql Server\nTeam size\n                    \n\n        \n\n\nRole\n                            \n\n         \nTeam Member\nI am not only responsible for designing and coordinating the development of this system but also responsible for helping the development of all modules.\n\nDescription:\n\nThe site main aim is to provide online shopping of the products related to Medical, Dental and Long Term care. This site enables the user requests fro a product and if user interested to buy a product.\n\n360EHS.com Essential Health Supplies, as the name suggests it provides complete supply solution to the various sectors of the Health care.\n\nThe user has to register with the site by providing the necessary details.\n\nOnce the user registers he can start using the 360ehs to get the complete solution on ehs. \n\nThere is a facility fax service in this site to send fax message to the supplier who supplies products.\n\nResponsibilities:\n\nInvolved in My fax Web Services Integration, Pay pal Payment Gateway Integration\n   \nInvolved in Coding\nInvolved in web page designing\n\nProject#3\n\nProject Title \n               \n\n\n         \nElite Global\nTechnologies\n              \n\n         \nC#.Net, VS.Net, Asp.Net, Window?s Xp\nClient\n             \n             \n\n\n         \nElite Global\nURL\n                                \n\n      \n   \nWWW.Eliteglobal.com\n   \nDatabase\n   \n                  \n\n\n         \nSql Server 2000\nTeam size\n      \n              \n\n\n        \n  \n\nRole\n                \n                        \n\n\n         \nTeam Member\n\nDescription\n   \n\n   \nTraveling world wide has become a common thing today.\n   \nElite Global aims to offer services and products for those who value excellence in service and luxury more than budget.\n\nIn order to create a wider customer base Elite Global will offer a membership categorized according to budget and value.\n\nThis web application provides the services for booking of cars or hotels enabling them to utilize their time for their actual purpose of traveling and make it joyful.\n\nResponsibilities:\nInvolved in security management by using ASP. Net.\nInvolved in Coding of the project.\n\nProject#4\n\nProject Title \n               \n\n\n         \nArk Hospitals\nTechnologies\n              \n\n         \nC#.Net, VS.Net, Asp.Net, Window?s Xp\nClient\n             \n             \n\n\n         \nArk Hospitals\nDatabase\n   \n                 \n\n\n         \nSql Server\nTeam size\n      \n              \n\n\n          \n\nRole\n                \n                        \n\n\n         \nTeam Member\n\nI am not only responsible for designing and coordinating the development of this system but also responsible for helping the development of all modules.\n\nDescription\n   \n\nThis is a computer enabled portable equipment system for effective maintenance of clinic and it provides better information and services for users. The main aim of this project is to maintain clinic, employee, patient, patient information reference details and also useful to manage all administration activities of the clinic.\nIt has been divided into three modules. It contains registration schedules, appointment and patient information. This project also have different reports for convenience of user to take decisions over all activities such as giving appointments to patients to a particular doctor through mails and all the activities.\n\nResponsibilities:\nInvolved in security management by using ASP. Net.\nInvolved in Coding of the project.','Promatrix Solutions',1,NULL,'2007-10-18',NULL,'2007-10-18','2010-06-10 12:14:22','2010-06-10',15,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(296,'Chintan V',NULL,NULL,'Mumbai','chssaiscntsacan_vscascschi@yahoo.com','chintan_vashi@yahoo.com','91 000000','0',NULL,'0',NULL,'0','2