 this project, this project also \n                     \nContains administrator module, which is fully dynamic. \nResponsibilities\n\nInvolved in Database Design, Coding for Complete \nWorking on \n                                         \nAgents\nmodule, administration Module \n\n\n. Projects Title\n\n       \nDaily Production Update System\nClient\n\n         \nSMARTech Interactive (P)\n Ltd., \nIndia\nLanguage\n   \n: ASP.NET, C#\n    \n   \n     \n   \nDatabase\n        \n: SQL Server 2000\nEnvironment\n: Windows XP\n                \nTeam Size\n      \n: Two\n\nDescription\n     \n\n    \nThis project was targeted to develop a Intranet site for\n\n                      \nSMARTech Interactive (P) LTD. \nAnd provide facility\n\n\nto feed daily project progress of employee. In this Intranet web application every employee login with his/Her ID/Password and feed his work progress against assigned project. And Super Admin Module can facilitate to super admin to get the information about every employee and his/her performance. When a Employee feed project progress, a copy of this update is sent to the client by mail. This project also contains administrator, In Administration module proves facility to maintain client, project, users/employees and the project assign to which person. And Progress report of every Employee.\n\nResponsibilities\n\n    \nInvolved in Database Design, Coding for Complete \nWorking on agents\n module, administration Module.\n\n\n\n. Projects Title\n\n       \nShopping Cart\nClient\n\n         \nIn-house Project \n\nLanguage\n   \n: ASP.NET, C#\n    \n   \n     \n   \nDatabase\n        \n: SQL Server 2000\nEnvironment\n: Windows 2000 advance server\n      \nTeam Size\n       \n: Three\n\nDescription\n        \n\n This project was targeted to develop a site to user and other one s sec the all information about the company history, product, new product, store, press information and other ones. In this two type of user first general user and second \nRetailer. And also the store kippers registered store, and \nall visitors Enquiry of all product, store, store location, suppliers, and all new/special product\n, product category and product item and admin. Do type related work just like modified, delete and get permission to other one?s do the related work. And also the details about the company employee with deg. also.\n\nResponsibilities\n\n    \nInvolved in Database Design, Coding for Complete \nWorking on agents\n module, administration Module and Report.\n\n\nPersonal Details:\nFather?s Name \n            \n\n           \nSri. Krishana Singh\n            \nDate of Birth\n     \n            \n\n           \n01 Dec,1982\n            \n            \nGender\n             \n            \n\n           \nMale\n            \nMarital Status\n    \n           \n\n           \nUnmarried\n            \nNationality\n                    \n\n           \nIndian\n            \nLanguage known\n          \n\n           \nEnglish & Hindi\n            \nPermanent address\n      \n\n          \nS/0 Sri Krishana Singh\nShastrinagar, Road no-02\nJail \nPress Road\nGaya\n\nBihar\n) .\n\nHobbies:\n\n        \nSolving Puzzles and Playing Comp. game that extensively involves strategy at the back of mind.\n\n\n         \nListening Light instrumental music and Devotional songs.\nI hereby assure that all the information mentioned above are true to the best of my knowledge and belief.\n\n\n\n\nDate:\n   \n??????????. \nPlace:\n\n??????????.\n                                                               \nApplicant?s sign:..?????????.???..?',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-18',NULL,'2007-10-18','2010-06-10 12:14:22','2010-06-10',15,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(298,'Alok sinha',NULL,NULL,'New Delhi','alodscsdacdsvk.sdsdcvsdsacsdcviscnha@hotmail.com',NULL,'09999658257','0','91 99 99658257','0','06540 285340','0','2008-04-13',10,33,'2010-06-10 12:14:22',15,'0',NULL,'200710/18/ATT17981.html','200710/18/DOC17984.doc','Resdex @ naukri.com\nAlok Sinha\nB-45,Gopalpura Colony, Post Office Mugma, Dhanbad - 828204 \nalodscsdacdsvk.sdsdcvsdsacsdcviscnha@hotmail.com\n\nTelephone: 09999658257\n(M)\n 91 99 99658257\n(R)\n\nD.O.B\n - 26 Mar 1983 \nModified on\n - 26 Sep 2007 \nAnnual Salary\n - INR 2 Lac(s) 20 Thousand \nTotal Years of Experience\n - 2 Year(s) 2 Month(s) \nCurrent Location\n - Delhi \nPreferred Location\n - Anywhere in India, Anywhere in Northern India, Anywhere in South India \nB.Tech(CSE) having 2 years of experience in .Net and Microsoft Technology\n\nTEXT RESUME \n\nCURRICULUM VITAE\nAlok Kumar Sinha (B. Tech)\nCorrespondence Address: Email: 1) alok.sinha@hotmail.com\nRoomNo-k/301, HNo-14 , 2) meetalok_2004@yahoo.co.in\nBer Sarai, Oppsite Old JNU Campus,\nNew Delhi-16 Tel #: - 09999658257\nObjective: To associate with the reputed industry and work for the organization\n?s growth\n & progress with my whole energy, ability, knowledge, dedication and sincere efforts.\nSkills: C, C++, Vb.Net, C#, Java Script and \nADO\n. Net, Asp. Net, Sql Server 2000 and 2005 , \nCrystal\n report, PL\\SQL, Oracle 9i.\nExperience: 2 year and 2 months as Software Engineer and getting the requirements from the clients for developing the software and develops the projects. I take care of the timely delivery of quality software.\nI am presently working as Web Developer in Nethuesindia- futuristic software solutions, NN Mall, Rohini Sector-3, \nNew Delhi\n since 10th August 2007.\nI was previously working as Software Engineer in Dwon Technologies, \nBehind\nBhikaji\nCama\nPalace\n, and \nNew Delhi\n since 5th July 2005 to 9th August 2007\nEducation:\nB. Tech from Dehradun Institute of Technology in Computer Science & Engineering (2001-05) from \nU.P\nTech\nUniversity\n with 63%.\n12th from De Nobili School, Mugma, (affiliated to ICSE) in the year 2000 with 75.5%\n10th from De Nobili School, Mugma, (affiliated to ICSE) in the year 1998 with 82.5%\nProjects:\n1)Project Name: www.123supercart2.com\nSite : www.123supercart2.com\nResponsibilities: Designing of database, Coding and development of the software.\nTechnical Skills used: C#, ASP. Net 2.0, SQL Server2005, and \nAdo\n. Net.\nDescription of the project: It deals with the online shopping of products and placing their orders. User gets logins to view their orders placed and their status. The project is of n tier architecture. It is built in C# , ASP.Net, Ado.Net and SQLServer2005.\n2)Project Name: Quality Control Forum\nSite : www.qcforum.in\nResponsibilities: Designing of database, Coding and development of the software.\nTechnical Skills used: C#, ASP. Net , SQL Server2000, and Ado. Net.\nDescription of the project: It deals with the quality standards present in different industries. User gets logins to view the queries posted by different members and their solutions. In this quality related jobs are displayed and members can apply to the different jobs posted. It is a system which increases the efficiency of the management by searching the different quality standards prevailing in the different organization.. The project is of n tier architecture. It is built in C# , ASP . Net, Ado. Net and SQLServer2000.\n3)Project Name: www.onslogistics.in\nSite : www.onslogistics.in\nResponsibilities: Designing of database, Coding and development of the software.\nTechnical Skills used: C#, ASP. Net , SQL Server2000, and Ado. Net.\nDescription of the project: It deals with the ONLINE tracking of goods and cargo of customers and their updated status of the goods forwarded. It deals with online tracking of customer orders and maintain the details of the goods and their shipments. User gets logins to view the shipment of the goods and their updated status. It is an automated system, which increases the efficiency of the management. The project is of n tier architecture. It is built in C# , ASP . Net, Ado. Net and SQLServer2000.\n4)Project Name: Project Management System\nResponsibilities: Designing of database, Coding, Testing and documentation of the Software\nTechnical Skills used: C#, ASP. Net , SQL Server2000, Crystal Report and Ado. Net.\nDescription of the project: It deals with the project handling and maintenance of the projects in the Company. It also deals with establishing the milestone for the project and jobs completed by the developers in given time and schedule. It is an automated system, which increases the efficiency of the management. The project is of n tier architecture. It is built in C#, Ado. Net , Crystal Report and Sql Server2000.\n5)Project Name: ONSLOGISTICTS ACOUNTING AND BILLING SOFTWARE\nResponsibilities: Designing of database, Coding, Testing and leading the team of the software developer to deliver a quality product.\nTeam Size: Three (3) members.\nTechnical Skills Used: Vb.net, Sql Server2000, Crystal Report and Ado. Net.\nDescription of the project: It deals with Acounting and billing system of the company and Tracking the transactions of goods and cargo. The project is of n tier architecture. It is built in Vb. net, Ado. Net , Crystal Report and Sql Server2000.\n6)Project Name: IMS (Inventory Management System)\nTeam Size: Three (3) members.\nResponsibilities: Designing, Coding, Testing and documentation of the IMS.\nTechnical Skills used: VB.Net2003, Sql Server2000, Crystal Report and Ado. Net.\nDescription of the project: It deals with the Inventory Management System. The project is of n tier architecture. It is built in VB. Net, Ado. Net, Crystal Report and Sql Server2000\nComputer skills\nProgramming Languages - C, C++, C#, Vb.Net, Ado.Net, Asp.Net, Crystal\nReport , SQL Server, Oracle, PL\\Sql, Microsoft Visio.\nSubjects -Software Engineering, Database, Operating System\nConcepts and data structure.\nOperating Systems - MS-DOS, Windows 2k, 9X Series and XP\nPackages - MS Word, MS PowerPoint, MS Access, Ms Excel\nExtra Curricular Activities\n§ Member of Indian Society for Technical Education.\n§ Lead the CSE team in cricket tournament in college.\nHobbies\nMy hobbies are reading books on computer concepts, playing cricket, football, badminton, chess & video games.\nStrengths\nPositive attitude.\nI am eager to learn new things and try to implement in the project only if the quality of the project gets improved.\nI am a good team member and a good team leader.\nI am ready to accept challenges.\nPersonal Details\nFather\n?s name\n : Late: Anil Kumar Sinha\nDate of Birth : 26TH March 1983.\nPermanent Address : Village+PO: Lalpur, Dhanbad \n? 828129\nPhone (residence) : 06540 285340\nAlok Kumar Sinha','Nethuesindia- futuristic software solutions',1,'2.2','2007-12-14',NULL,'2007-10-18','2010-06-10 12:14:22','2010-06-10',15,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(299,'Ankur Bajhal',NULL,NULL,'Pune ','nkudfgvrbwegtwertwetajhal@gmail.com',NULL,'07692 220406','0','9890307764','0',NULL,'0','2008-04-13',8,23,'2010-06-10 12:14:22',15,'0',NULL,'200710/18/ATT17982.html','200710/18/DOC17985.doc','ANKUR BAJHAL JAIN E-MAIL: ankurbajhal@rediffmail.com\nAnkur Bhaji\n                                      \n         \n          \n                   \n             \nEMAIL\n\n\nnkudfgvrbwegtwertwetajhal@gmail.com\n\n\n\n\n                                \n                \n                                                   \n                             \nContact\n: 9890307764(M)\n               \nKumar Samruddhi,\nNear Tingre Nagar Petrol Pump,\nVishrantwadi\nPune\n                                                              \n               \n\nCARRIER OBJECTIVE\n\n\n                                      \n\nI immensely value self-development and personal growth. I adapt well in new situation and like to interact with people. I am open to learning from my mistakes. My strengths are resilience and objective orient- ness. My greatest asset is my will power and devotion towards objective. The greatest satisfaction to me is a job done perfectly.\n\nSUMMARY\n\n\n        \nBE in Computer Science.\n     \nMicrosoft .NET-connected CRM product suite (MSCRM).\nMajor Skill Sets: ASP. Net, C, C++, C#,\n\nHTML, MSSQL.\n\nSKILL SETS\n\nRDBMS\n                                 \n\n\nMS SQL Server 2000\nInternet Technologies\n         \n\n ASP.Net, HTML, XML,\nInternet Languages\n             \n\n VBScript and JavaScript\nFront Ends \n                           \n\n Visual Basic 6.0, ASP.Net\nProgramming Languages\n    \n\n C, C++, C#\nOperating Systems\n              \n\n Windows NT, Windows 95, 98, 2000, XP\nERP SYSTEM\n                      \n: MSCRM\n\nSELF PROFILE\n      \n           \nI immensely value self-development and personal growth. I adapt well in new situation and like to interact with people. I am open to learning from my mistakes. My strengths are resilience and objective orient- ness. My greatest asset is my will power and devotion towards objective. The greatest satisfaction to me is a job done perfectly.\n\nWork Experience:\n\nCurrent Employer\n      \n\n\nSunflower Information Technologies Pvt. Ltd.\nFrom - To -\n                 \n\n\nDecember 26, 2005\n\n? Till Date\nDesignation\n                \n\n\nSoftware Engineer.\n\nProject Name\n\n: Document Management System\nTeam Size\n       \n: 4\n\nFront End\n              \n\nASP. Net,\n HTML, JavaScript\nBack End\n               \n\nC#.Net\nDatabase\n                \n\nVisual Studio 2005, Sql Server Express Edition 2005.\nProject Details\nDMS is a simple document management system for maintaining electronic files. This consists of all the basic functionalities like category management, document upload, assigning permissions for user to upload document, download\n\nmanagement etc.\nContribution\n         \n\n      \nDesigned the HLD for the same\n\n      \nDeveloped the class architecture for the retrieving values from database.\n\n      \nDeveloped the Business logic.\n\n      \nDeveloped the document upload form to maintain the user permissions.\n\n      \nDeveloped role based access functionality\n\n\n\nProject Name\n\n: Electronic Claims Processing\nTeam Size\n       \n: 7\n\nFront End\n              \n\nASP. Net,\n HTML, JavaScript\nBack End\n               \n\nC#.Net\nDatabase\n                \n\nVisual Studio 2005, Sql Server Express Edition 2005.\n\nAjax\nProject Details\nECP is related to the claim billing based on the HCFA 1500 standards. This is claim processing system. It takes the inputs from the user based on the those inputs and procedures (policy Numbers) the claims are processed and checked for the payments.\nContribution\n         \n\n      \nImplement the master page concept.\n\n      \nDesigned the template base UI as per the Client?s requirement.\n\n      \nDeveloped the Tree View and developed the various categories like Medicaid and Medicare.\n\n      \nDeveloped the input forms from the application.\n\n\n\nProject Name\n\n: eShoes Online (ASPDotNetStoreFront 6.0 ML)\nTeam Size\n       \n: 3\n\nFront End\n              \n\nASP. Net,\n HTML, JavaScript\nBack End\n               \n\nVB.Net,\nDatabase\n                \n\nSql Server Express Edition 2005.\n\nAjax\nProject Details\neShoes Online is a eCommerce project. It deals with selling of the variety of shoes. This project has been developed by using ASPDTSF .It perform all the basic functionality like selling shoes, selecting product. All the payments are done online using credit payments and Pay Pal .\nContribution\n         \n\n      \nDesigned the template base UI as per the Client?s requirement.\n\n      \nCustomized the Admin section of the project for adding related products in the project.\n\n      \nCustomized the image display at various stages of the projects.\n\n      \nImplemented the search screen for the products.\n\n\nProject Name\n\n\nEMS\n (Emergency Medical Services)\nTeam Size\n       \n: 8\n\n\nFront End\n              \n\nASP. Net.\n HTML, JavaScript\nBack End\n               \n\nC#\nDatabase\n                \n\nSql Server 2000.\nThird Party Controls (.Dlls)\nAjax\nProject Details\nEMS\n is an online medical service provider, which provides the online medical service to the users as doctors, hospitals. \nEMS\n maintains the record of all the incidents those occurs along the patient details and the medical services provided to those patients. It maintains all the basic billing of charges along with the primary aid charges and the ambulance charges.\nContribution\n         \n\n      \nDesigned the time sheet entry of the Incident along with the Incident Details.\n\n\n      \nDesign and developed the \nauthentication based role for the Patient details and billing.\n\n\n      \nPerform the various form type of validation as per the clients requirement.\n\n\nPrevious Employer\n     \n\n\nzSyndicate Software?s (Ignify Inc.)\nFrom - To -\n                 \n\n\nMarch 2005 ? \nDecember 23, 2005\nDesignation\n                \n\n\nSoftware Engineer.\n\nProject Name\n             \n\n\nAll Language Systems (ALS Inc.)\nTeam Size\n                   \n: 8\n\n\nFront End\n              \n\nASP. Net.\n HTML, JavaScript\nBack End\n               \n\nC#\nDatabase\n                \n\nSql Server 2000.\nProject Details\nALS is a mid sized \nERP\n based project. This project is developed on \nMSCRM\n platform using ASP.Net. ALTIMS provides the complex calculation of charges depending on the time. This system provides the generation of the invoices for the particular order. Those orders can be mailed to the particular client and can be faxed through this system.\nContribution\n         \n\n      \nDesign and Implementation of business objects and front-end. Implement the Business Logic for the Finalize Order and the Class for calculating the surcharges. Developed the stored procedures for updating and saving the finalized values. Designed the various API?s for data serializes to XML for consumption by the application. Implement the various merged code\n\n\n      \nDesign and developed the \nSearch Screen\n for the ALTIMS. Designed the various \nstored procedures\n for the search screens. Developed the validations using java script. Developed the C# code to manipulate the data with \ndatagrid\n\n\n\n      \nDesign and developed the various reports as purchase orders, letters, emails by using the \nCUBIZZ Software\n and merged codes using \nOmnirush\n Software.\n\nPrevious Employer\n     \n\n\nPDSYS Technologies Pvt. Ltd\nFrom - To -\n                 \n\n\nSeptember 2004 ? March 2005\nDesignation\n                \n\n\nTrainee Software Engineer.\n\n\nPROJECT\n                  \n\n\nOnline Classroom Study (Teachers Pal. Inc).\nTeam Size\n                   \n: 9\n\n\nFront End\n              \n\nASP. Net.\n HTML, JavaScript\nBack End\n               \n\nC#\nDatabase\n                \n\nSql Server 2000.\nThird Party Controls Used\nRad Tree View.\nUltra Web Controls.\nContribution\n         \nDesigned the various wizards for making the Reports on students. Also involved in the database designing and using the stored procedures. The major role is as a \nC# developer\n. This is implemented using \nASP.Net\n and \nCrystal\n reports\n\n\n\nEDUCATIONAL DETAILS\n\nDegree\n                         \n                          \n  \nUniversity\n                                           \n                \nPercentage\n\nB.E (Computer Sc.)\n               \n   \nVisveshwaraiah Technological\n        \n      \n                         \n      \n59.40%\n   \nUniversity, \nBelgaum\n       \n    \n(Karnataka)\n    \n\nH.S.S.C\n                                   \n   \nMadhya Pradesh Board\n                                                   \n      \n60.81%\n                                                \n   \nBhopal\n (M.P)\n\nS.S.C.\n                      \n\n              \n   \nMadhya Pradesh Board,\n                                                  \n      \n64.29%\n                                                                \n   \nBhopal\n (M.P.)\n\nPERSONAL DETAILS\nDate of Birth\n                        \n\n   \n30th Jan 1981\nSex\n                                         \n\n   \nMale\nNationality\n                            \n\n   \nIndian\nPermanent Address\n            \n\n  \nS/o Mr. S.K.Jain,\n                                     \n           \n    \nNear Big \nJain\nTemple\n\nMahaveer Ward, Seoni,\nDist.Seoni (M.P.) 480 661\n                                \n                \n    \nPhone No. (07692) 220406','Sunflower Information Technologies Pvt. Ltd.',1,NULL,'2007-10-18',NULL,'2007-10-18','2010-06-10 12:14:22','2010-06-10',15,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(300,'Chennuru ',NULL,NULL,'Bangalore','chganga00@gmail.com','chfvfgavfvfvngafvfv00@gmail.com',NULL,'0','91 9959655838','0',NULL,'0','2006-12-13',8,24,'2010-06-10 12:14:22',15,'0',NULL,'200710/18/ATT17983.html','200710/18/DOC17986.doc','Resdex @ naukri.com\nchennuru \nchganga00@gmail.com Hyderabad - 516105 \nchfvfgavfvfvngafvfv00@gmail.com\n\nTelephone: 9959655838\n(M)\n\n(R)\n\nD.O.B\n - 06 May 1981 \nModified on\n - 26 Sep 2007 \nAnnual Salary\n - INR 4 Lac(s) 0 Thousand \nTotal Years of Experience\n - 3 Year(s) 2 Month(s) \nCurrent Location\n - Hyderabad \nPreferred Location\n - Anywhere in India \n.NET DEVELOPER with 3 yrs exp.\n\nTEXT RESUME \n\nHyderabad, INDIA\nChganga00@gmail.com\nMobile: +91 9959655838\nCHENNURU GANGAIAH\n________________________________________\nOBJECTIVE: A young, enthusiastic and dedicated hard worker with excellent computing and communication skills, aiming for an innovative, challenging, responsible and rewarding career in the field of Software Technology, which gives professional and career satisfaction.\nSummary:\n\n Over all 3 years of professional experience in Microsoft Technologies and played major role as a Module Lead.\n\n Have successful track record in Analysis, Design, Development, Testing, Maintenance, Support and Implementation of software applications for the Telecommunication and Higher Education Industries.\n\n Have worked with client system analysts in preparation of Business Requirement Documents.\n\n Good exposure towards the web interaction and database interaction applications.\n\n Worked extensively in SQL Server - Oracle queries, Stored Procedures using SQL Developer.\n\n Conducted peer reviews.\nEXPERINCE DETAILS: 3 Years\nOrganization : Real Soft Technologies, Bangalore\nPosition : .NET Consultant\nFrom : June, 2004\nTo : Till Date\nQUALIFICATIONS:\n\n Bachelor of Science, from S.V.University, Thirupati, A.P.\nPRIMARY COMPUTING SKILLS: Microsoft VS.NET & SQL Server\n\n OBJECT ORIENTED LANGUAGES : C#, VB.NET, C++\n\n PROCEDURAL LANGUAGES : C, COBOL, Basic, FoxPro\n\n DATABASE SYSTEMS : SQL Server Database, MS Access\n\n WEB DEVELOPMENT TOOLS : ASP.NET, VBScript, XML, HTML\nProjects:\n1. Managerial Information System (MIS)\nSoftware : VB.NET, ASP.NET\nDuration : 6 Months\nDatabase : SQL Server 2000\nRole : Design, Development, Unit Testing\nDescription:\nThis Application automates the Office work of the Company/Organization. This contains Transactions and Reports of departments like Marketing, Finance & Accounts, R&D, Production, Stores and Purchase, Vendor and HRD. This focus on processing, verifying and Authorizing of Messages/Files, which are transferred among these departments and this also provides mails transferring among the authorized employees. This Project is divided into modules like Transactions, Reports. This Project is meant to computerize the activities of company top management tasks. in this project we developed the reports like bank statements ,year wise billing details of products and customers ,analysis of production and marketing.\n2. Trivitron Trade Accounting System\nClient : M/S Trivitron Medical Systems Pvt. Ltd\nDuration : July 2005 \n? June 2006\nRole : Team Member\nSoftware : Windows 2003, C#, ASP.Net, SQLServer2000\nOverview:\nInternet presence and web-based trading has become the keywords for the success of Modern Corporate houses all over the world and M/S Trivitron Group of companies is no exception to this. The Trivitron Group houses 2 major and 2 upcoming sister-concerns that together contribute to a whooping n-Croce turnover for the Group as a whole. While Trivitron Medical Systems Pvt. Ltd. (TMS) and Trivitron Diagnostics (TDL) are trading with specifications in importing High-End Critical Care & Ultrasound Medical Equipments & providing technical, marketing and sales support to a vast 150 plus satisfied customers, Trivitron Consultancy Services and Metropolis Chain of labs form the upcoming two some.\nThis software takes care of the following modules:\n\n Order Processing Management and related Supply-Chain issues.\n\n Financial Analysis & Accounting System.\n\n Payroll Management System and other Employee related issues.\n\n Service Call Management System & Sales Call Management System.\n\n Management Information System and Budgeting, Forecasting activities\nResponsibilities: As a Software Engineer I have done Unit Testing, Integration Testing,\nand Bug Fixing\n3. Smart Vehicle Booking System\nTechnologies Used : .NET & SQL Server\nTeam Size : 6\nDescription:\nThe main aspect of this project to make easy the Business calculations and generating required reports effectively for a Vehicle Booking System. This maintains a huge data for their operations. This also facilitates some security aspects by allowing a super user to give permissions on different operations to different other users.\n\n Efficient mathematical calculations for Bill generations.\n\n Security is provided by giving privileges to the users.\n\n Backup and restore facility for data.\n\n Reports generation for various criteria\n\n Help available with the application.\nPersonal Details:\nData of Birth : June, 1981\nGender : Male\nMarital Status : Married\nLanguages Known : English, Hindi & Telugu','Real Soft Technologies',1,NULL,'2007-10-18',NULL,'2007-10-18','2010-06-10 12:14:22','2010-06-10',15,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(301,'Sukanta Kumar',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'sufbfbkant_jedfbfbvna2002@yahoo.com',NULL,'0','09841930478','0',NULL,'0','2008-04-29',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-10 12:14:22',15,'0',NULL,'200710/18/ATT17827.html','200710/18/DOC17988.doc','Resdex @ naukri.com\nsukanta kumar \nsukant_jena2002@yahoo.com RAJGANGPUR - 770017 \nsufbfbkant_jedfbfbvna2002@yahoo.com\n\nTelephone: 09841930478\n(M)\n\nD.O.B\n - 18 May 1983 \nModified on\n - 25 Sep 2007 \nAnnual Salary\n - INR 2 Lac(s) 0 Thousand \nTotal Years of Experience\n - 2 Year(s) 2 Month(s) \nCurrent Location\n\nBangalore\n\nPreferred Location\n - Anywhere in \nIndia\nPlsql Developer having 2+ years of expe in Oracle application\n\nTEXT RESUME \n\nSUKANTA KUMAR JENA Mobile no: 09841930478\nMail:sukant_jena2002@yahoo.com\nSUMMARY\nÂ· Having around over 2+years of experience in software development using oracle.\nÂ· Experience in Application Development using oracle tools (SQL,PL/SQL, Reports, Forms) and other related technologies.\nÂ· Experience in development of live projects in Developer 2000 and Oracle 8i.\nÂ· Experience in development of live projects in Ramco ERP (e.Application).\nÂ· Having good domain knowledge and working experience in HRMS product.\nÂ· A self-motivated and results-driven professional with strong analytical ability backed by technical knowledge. Has a strong communication and team skill.\nÂ· Currently Working in Ramco System Ltd as a Programmer\nEDUCTIONAL QUALIFICATION\nBachelors of Engineering in Information Technology, Padmanava College of Engineering, Sambalpur University, Orissa, India\nTECHNICAL SKILLS\nOperating Systems : Windows NT/2000/XP.\nLanguages : PL/SQL\nDevelopment Tools : Developer 2000\nDatabases : Oracle 8i/9i\nReporting Tools : Oracle Reports 6i\nERP : Oracle Applications (PO & AOL) and Ramco e. Applications (HRMS)\nTools : Toad 7.3.0, SQL*Loader, Discoverer, Ramco Virtual Works\nPROFESSIONAL EXPERIENCE\nCurrent Employer: Sheltec Software (India) Pvt ltd, Bangalore July 2005 â\n?? till Date\nContractor: Ramco System Ltd, Chennai, India Oct 2006 â\n?? till Date\nClient : ITC-WELCOMGROUP, (ITC) New Delhi (July 2007 to till date)\nModule : HRMS (APPRAISAL)\nRole : Analyzing, Coding and Debugging\nTools : Ramco HRMS, PL/SQL, RVW\nDescription: ITC Hotel Division is one of top companies in India for Hotels. The project was developed ITC Hotel Div for implementing appraisee appraisal details.Their appraisal are of three types BSC, NBSC and Others. Based on Appraisal type they are maintain their appraisee details. As a programmer I was involved in these following areas.\nResponsibilities:\nÂ· Involved in Writing Procedure, Function for Appraisal Component.\nÂ· Involved in Bug fixing and Testing for the same.\nÂ· Involved in Supporting Work from Offshore.\nClient : Competent Software Ltd, (CSW) \nNew Delhi\n (Feb 2007 to Jun 2007)\nModule : HRMS (Leave, Payroll, Production Planning)\nRole : Developer, Debugger and Tester\nTools : Ramco HRMS, SQL Server 2005\nDescription: Competent Software Pvt. Ltd. (CSW) incorporated in 1992, is in the Business Process Outsourcing (BPO) space. The company headquartered in New Delhi with full fledged units at Noida and Gurgaon is engaged in the development of electronic databases for clients in North America.CSW provides businesses of all sizes with a complete range of services including data conversion services and data analysis services. These intelligent services allow the customers to maximize the value of their IT expenditure and the unique methodology provides exceptional speed, efficiency, accuracy, and of course a very high returns on investment. I was responsible for these areas.\nResponsibilities:\nÂ· Involved in Writing Procedure, Function for leave Component.\nÂ· Involved in Bug Fixing for payroll, leave, Source to transmission, Production Planning Component.\nÂ· Extensively involved in Review and Testing for the same.\nClient : \nSingapore\n Health Services, (Sing Health) \nSingapore\n (Sep 2006 to Jan 2007)\nModule : HRMS\nRole : Developer and Debugger\nTools : Ramco HRMS, PL/SQL\nResponsibilities:\nÂ· Involved in Writing Procedure, Function for Employee Induction and leave Component.\nÂ· Involved in Bug Fixing for payroll, leave, Employee Induction, Reimbursement Component.\nÂ· Extensively involved in Review and Testing for the same.\nClient : South India Corporation Limited (Jun 2006 to Aug 2006)\nModule : AOL, \nPO\nRole : Developed Reports.\nTools : Oracle Applications 11i, Oracle 9i, SQL * Loader\nÂ· Reports Customization of Purchase Order Detail Report in Purchasing.\nÂ· Developed New Report Which give the stock of particular item on a particular date and as well as quantity received only without deliver.\nÂ· AOL activities like Creation of Users, Responsibilities, and Value sets, Enabling Flex Fields etc.\nÂ· Registration of Forms and Reports\nClient : Aurobindo Pharma ltd, \nHyderabad\n (Jan 2006 â\n?? May 2006)\nTools : SQL, PL/SQL, 8i, Reports 6i\nRole : Analyzing, Coding and Debugging\nDuration : 5 months\nTeam Size : 5\nDescription:\nAPL is one of top ten pharmaceutical companies in \nIndia\n in bulk drugs. As a Developer I was Preparating of Reports in accordance with the User requirements, Development of Forms and Reports in Oracle Forms/Reports 6i.\nPayroll system was designed for providing Employee database, Attendance Maintenance, Leaves Maintenance, Loans and Advances, Bonus, Saving Schemes. This was developed on Oracle-8i with developer 2000 as front end.\nResponsibilities:\nÂ· Implemented various packages, PL/SQL procedures.\nÂ· Designed and Developed Forms as per client requirements.\nÂ· Generation of Reports as per requirement.\nClient : Jyoti Pvt Ltd, BBSR (July 2005 â\n?? Dec 2005)\nTools : Oracle 8i, Forms 6i, Report 6i\nRole : Developer\nDuration : 6 Months\nTeam Size : 7\nDescription:\nThe project was developed for Jyoti Pvt Ltd. Before implementing the project they faced problems with legacy system to maintain the inventory details. So this project was to solve all the problems met by the company. Here complete details about the Items and the stocking details were maintained. Depending on the previous months sale and keeping a base month sales the order level and re-order level was calculated so that, they can manufacture the at required level. This data was very helpful for managers and admin departments. Various flexible features which involve Quotation analysis, rising purchasing orders and receiving. It also gives complete information of On-hand-Quantity and on hand avalibilty.\nResponsibilities:\nÂ· Created table in database using Oracle-8i.\nÂ· Writing the procedures,functions,packages,database triggers in PL/SQL\nÂ· Involved for designing various application forms using form 6i.\nÂ· Generating various Reports using report 6i.\nÂ· Extensively involved in review and testing for the same.\nPersonal Details:\nName : Sukanta Kumar Jena\nMail id : sukant_jena2002@yahoo.com\nDate of Birth : 18th May 1983\nSex : Male\nMarital status : Single\nNationality : Indian',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-18',NULL,'2007-10-18','2010-06-10 12:14:22','2010-06-10',15,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(304,'Chinmaya Kumar',NULL,NULL,NULL,'chidvgnmasdcvya_bedvdvhdvra@yahoo.co.in',NULL,NULL,'0','91 9916589230','0',NULL,'0','2008-04-29',NULL,NULL,'2010-06-10 12:14:22',15,'0',NULL,'200710/18/ATT17993.html','200710/18/DOC17994.doc','Srikanta Kumar Barik\nChinmaya Kumar\n\n\n\n\nEmail ID: chidvgnmasdcvya_bedvdvhdvra@yahoo.co.in\n                          \n\n\nMobile\n: +91? 9916589230\n    \n\nTechnical Experience\n   \n?2+ Years of experience as a Software Professional.\n\n?Good application development skills using \n.NET\n\nFramework\n\nC#, ADO.NET, ASP.NET\n\nSQL Server 2000,XML,XML Parsing, IIS\n and\n JavaScript\n\n?Knowledge of \nObject Oriented programming (OOPS) \n\n?Good working knowledge of Internet languages like \nHTML, XML, \nand\n JavaScript\n\n?Knowledge about\n\nWeb Service\n\n\nWorked with \nindexes, Stored Procedures\n and\n Triggers\n\n?Highly dedicated team player backed by independent thinking and Proficient at\n\nimplementing\n\nand managing new software technology.\n\nObjective\n\n\nTo work in a challenging and dynamic environment towards a successful career in the software industry by making the best out of my abilities and interpersonal skills. I want to see myself as an active contributor to a team of ambitious people and thereby enhance my knowledge and personality.\n\nEmployment Summary\n\n\nWorking as software engineer in CGI Netvorks (Banglore) from may 2005 to till date. \n\nEducational Profile\n\n\nB.E from \nBPUT\nUniversity\n,2005, Orissa.\n                                                                \n\nTechnical Skills\n\n\nOperating Systems\n    \n:Windows 2000/XP\nLanguages\n               \n:C# 1.1\nWeb Programming\n     \n:ASP.Net 1.1 and XML\nDatabases\n               \n:SqlServer2000\nScripting\n                 \n:Java Script\nWeb Server\n             \n:IIS 6.0\nSource control\n         \n:Visual source safe\n\n\nProjects Handled:\n\n\n\n#IBS- RD:Finance/Banking Domain\n\n\nCurrent module\n         \n\nApplication System\nSoftware Platform\n     \n: ASP. Net, C#,XML, ADO.NET and SQLServer2000\nTools\n                      \n: VSS 6.0\nWeb-server\n             \n: IIS 6.0\n\n\n\n\n\nApplication System:\n\n\nThis module helps to automate the process of new Recurring Deposit proposal and helps the Bank Executive to Enter, Retrieve and Check data of the person who has applied for RD account as well the renewal of an existing RD account. This Application sub System captures the customer details including the personal, nomination, tenure and mode of interest payment details.\n\nDescription:\n\n\nThe project, Recurring Deposit, is developed for our client, who keeps track of the Administrator, Executive, Report handling and \nCreating RD\n account of customer. The Recurring deposit is a part of the different deposit schemes available in a bank. This scheme deals with the deposit, which is done in a regular interval.\n\nModules included are application system, deposit process system, payment system, closure system, customer interaction, user interaction, product administration and accounting interface and management system.\n\n\n\nResponsibilities:\n   \n\n\nAnalyzing the design pattern given to us.\nInvolvement in Coding the user Interface \nImplemented client side validations and involving in peer reviews.\n\n#NIS-CCD: Intranet Business\n\n\nCurrent module\n        \n\nBackground process\n\nSoftware Platform\n     \n\n\nASP. Net,C#.Net,Windows Services,ADO.NET and SQLServer2000\nTools\n                      \n:VSS 6.0\nWeb-server\n             \n:IIS 6.0\nTeam size\n                \n:Fourteen\n\nDescription:\n\n                                                          \nThe project is developed for our client, needs to purchase E-mail ids from E-mail providers like Yahoo, Rediff, etc. Validates the E-mail ids using GIS & stored in database, information about there product to be sent to the customers through there E-mails, there is a possibility for bounce back and it needs to be tracked, and for the bounce customers letters need to be posted.\nThe project is divided into two modules.\nModule1\n\nBackground process designed about product information (details).\nModule2\n\nForeground process designed to purchase E-mail ids, sending mails to ids about the\n             \ndetails of\n\nproduct.\n\n\nResponsibilities:\n\n\nAnalyzing the design pattern given to us.\nInvolvement in Coding the user Interface \nImplemented client side validations and involving in peer reviews.\n         \n\n\n\n\n WebWorld Management:Telecomm Domain\n\nModule Handled\n        \n\nTransaction System\nSoftware Platform\n     \n: ASP. Net, C#.Net, ADO.NET and SQLServer2000\nTools\n                      \n: VSS 6.0\nWeb-server\n             \n\n\nIIS 6.0\nTeam size\n                \n: Fourteen\n\n\nDescription\n\n\n\nWith the advent at the computer, all the procedures appeared to be very simple\nThe most utilization of this technology has been done in the areas at the reliance base group. The makes an attempt to automate the whole transaction of the web world. In this project the Customer can navigate the menu clients and the prices of the product respectively. The objective of this project is to control the whole transaction system of the web world.\n\n\nResponsibilities:\n\n\nAnalyzing the design pattern given to us.\nInvolvement in Coding the user Interface \nImplemented client side validations and involving in peer reviews\n\n\nPersonal Profile:\n\n           \n                                                                                                        \nGender\n                    \n:Male.\nMarital Status\n          \n:Single.\nFather?s Name\n          \n\nShyama sundar Behera.\nLanguages Known\n     \n:English, Hindi, and Oriya.\n\nShould you feel convinced as regards the achievements stipulated, May please contact me to be across your table to justify my worth for the position applied for, I shall be grateful. \n\n\n\n\n\nDate:\n   \n                                                                        \nChinmaya Kumar Behera \n                 ',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-10-18',NULL,'2007-10-18','2010-06-10 12:14:22','2010-06-10',15,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL),(306,'Kannan',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'91 80 41467451','0','9916926980','0',NULL,'0',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2010-06-11 09:37:07',15,'0',NULL,'200711/13/DOC3493.html','200711/13/DOC3493.html','p.MsoNormal {margin-left:37.5pt;} \n\n\nRegards,\n--------------------------------------------\nKannan.V.K.G\n+91 9916926980 [Mobile]\n+91 80 41467451[Office]',NULL,1,NULL,'2007-11-13',NULL,'2007-11-13','2010-06-11 09:37:07','2010-06-11',15,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',NULL);
